ent in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":25,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JP-nhmhiJzbRxgmW7ZkqE","name":"Under The Peepal Tree - 2025 ","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":50,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"30","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 15:24:31.731769+00', '2026-01-30 20:28:08.035178+00'), ('1eab44ba-d542-4c49-8a4a-03d94912714b', 'bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC007","name":"Aditi Agrawal","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Cb73uw1eXuKxYPk00KLh5","name":"Fast Trek","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/20RXwry3EXy3sPLfxYQuD.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/zWdhcJPKqUcSpHWln765g.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/uFXITGyJ0tx1D2xttrdC9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Fast-Trek successfully combined adventure with social responsibility. The event helped raise funds and awareness for underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases, contributing toward a meaningful medical cause.\\n\\nIt also strengthened teamwork and bonding among students from different departments, encouraging interaction beyond academics. Participants benefited physically and mentally through the trekking experience, promoting fitness, confidence, and resilience.\\n\\nOverall, the event was impactful, well-organized, and memorable, leaving participants with a sense of fulfillment while supporting a noble cause.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Fast-Trek was organized as a social impact initiative combining adventure with a meaningful cause. The primary objective of the project was to raise funds and awareness to support underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases, helping contribute toward their medical care and well-being.\\n\\nThe event began early in the morning at 7:30 AM, with all registered participants assembling at the designated departure point. Volunteers ensured a smooth check-in process, followed by a brief orientation session. During this session, participants were given safety guidelines, trek instructions, and an overview of the social cause associated with the event. This helped create awareness and instill a sense of purpose among everyone involved.\\n\\nParticipants then traveled together by bus to the scenic trekking destination at Huthridurga Hills. The trek was designed to be both enjoyable and manageable, encouraging teamwork, endurance, and a spirit of adventure. Throughout the journey, volunteers and coordinators were stationed at various points to guide participants, ensure safety, and provide assistance whenever required.\\n\\nThe natural beauty of Huthridurga Betta added to the overall experience, allowing participants to connect with nature while being part of a charitable initiative. The trek also served as a platform for students from different streams and years to interact, collaborate, and build camaraderie outside the classroom environment.\\n\\nTo ensure the comfort and well-being of all attendees, breakfast and lunch were arranged at the trek location. Adequate rest breaks, hydration points, and first-aid support were also provided, reflecting the organizers’ emphasis on safety and participant care.\\n\\nOverall, Fast-Trek was not just a recreational outing but a well-coordinated social service event that successfully blended fitness, fun, and philanthropy. It fostered community spirit among students while contributing to a noble cause, making the event both impactful and memorable for everyone involved.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Qm0OQzwUuoily55M9aS5z","name":"SDG Photo Competition \"Through the Eyes of Youth\"","slNo":2,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/_9p9cJBhrZifw9swp9kIT.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/gXiUxa7EllWMacB637FTU.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/0bAcpHtnxO0A6R0aP0RVk.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully increased awareness and understanding of all 17 Sustainable Development Goals among participants. It encouraged students to think critically about real-world problems and how these global goals address issues like poverty, inequality, environmental protection, and human well-being.\\n\\nParticipants developed empathy, social consciousness, and a stronger sense of responsibility toward society. The activity also enhanced creativity and communication skills by allowing students to express serious global issues through stories and images.\\n\\nBy engaging young minds in meaningful reflection, the event fostered a deeper connection with sustainable development and inspired participants to contribute, even in small ways, toward building a more inclusive, equitable, and sustainable world.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The event was organized to promote awareness about the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and encourage participants to understand global challenges and their role in creating a better future. Students were asked to choose any one SDG, upload a related photograph, and write a short story explaining its importance and real-world relevance.\\n\\nThis activity provided a creative platform for participants to express social issues through visuals and storytelling. Each entry reflected different aspects of sustainable development such as poverty, education, health, gender equality, clean energy, climate action, and more. By combining photography with narrative writing, the event aimed to make global goals more relatable and emotionally impactful.\\n\\nOverall, the event served as an educational and awareness-driven initiative that connected creativity with social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dTi95pfBwtOg8A1FeBlQV","name":"MUSKAAN","slNo":3,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/E5pNrv9pbSCITwCM4UR7u.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/W7jRSCuuo7dg3zJ0Gyfes.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-11-23","duration":5,"outcomes":"The Muskaan initiative successfully spread happiness and appreciation among the beneficiaries, making them feel seen, valued, and respected for their everyday contributions. The distribution of useful items provided practical support while also delivering emotional encouragement and recognition.\\n\\nFor the participants, the event fostered empathy, gratitude, and a deeper understanding of social responsibility. It encouraged students to acknowledge the importance of kindness and to recognize the dignity of labor in their daily lives.\\n\\nOverall, Muskaan created a positive social impact by promoting compassion, generosity, and community bonding, leaving both the beneficiaries and volunteers with a lasting sense of fulfillment and shared humanity.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-11-19","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Muskaan was a heartfelt social initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE from 19th to 23rd November 2023 with the aim of expressing gratitude toward individuals who quietly contribute to our daily lives. The event focused on appreciating workers and support staff who often go unnoticed despite their essential role in society.\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, participants collected and distributed essential items such as food, clothes, books, and gifts as a token of appreciation. More than just material support, the project was designed to spread positivity, kindness, and recognition for the dignity of labor. By acknowledging their efforts, the event aimed to make these individuals feel valued and respected.\\n\\nMuskaan served as a reminder that small acts of gratitude can create a meaningful emotional impact and strengthen the bond between communities.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LzS-Zpgi8LkOJTL-QMuH5","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/e0Vwi9omnk__Vj5itH-EO.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/d-_0QfCPD8ZEslj3MJBYW.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/kqFAtqDl0bLjNoU55eG7K.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-12-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"Uptown Junk successfully promoted environmental sustainability by encouraging participants to reuse and repurpose waste materials creatively. The event helped spread awareness about waste management and demonstrated how discarded items can be transformed into useful products through innovation.\\n\\nFor volunteers, the event enhanced organizational, communication, and teamwork skills while providing hands-on experience in managing a large-scale campus activity. Participants developed problem-solving abilities, creativity, and a deeper understanding of sustainable practices.\\n\\nOverall, the event made a positive impact by combining learning, fun, and environmental responsibility, fostering a culture of innovation and sustainability among students.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-14","hoursSpent":18,"description":"Uptown Junk was a two-day flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 14th and 15th December, designed to combine creativity, teamwork, and sustainability in an engaging format. The event blended an adventurous treasure hunt with a Best-Out-of-Waste competition, encouraging participants to think innovatively while promoting environmental awareness.\\n\\nThe event began with a treasure hunt across the college campus where participants solved clues to earn “Rota money.” This was later used to collect waste or discarded materials, which teams creatively transformed into useful and innovative models. The competition tested participants on creativity, practicality, teamwork, and presentation skills. The final models were judged based on ideation, creation, presentation, and future utility, with the top three teams being rewarded.\\n\\nAs a volunteer, I contributed by assisting in event coordination, guiding participants during the treasure hunt, managing materials, and supporting the smooth execution of the competition. The event successfully created an energetic and collaborative atmosphere while spreading awareness about the importance of recycling and sustainable practices.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2LWwFRP9beMwhxgk2qcB1","name":"Secret Santa","slNo":5,"place":"Sri Sai Sneha foundation","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/jNJ4dYRQfJyGL3LRPvbUX.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/xW8oOg88i_xQnG-xYr8hk.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/bXRLn2VtSq2Nhc90o9Rqk.png"],"endDate":"2023-12-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The “Secret Santa” initiative successfully brought joy, excitement, and a sense of belonging to children across the four orphanages. The festive celebration helped create a cheerful environment where the children could momentarily forget their challenges and experience the warmth of care and companionship.\\n\\nThe interactive activities such as games, storytelling, music, and dance encouraged social engagement and boosted the children’s confidence and happiness. The thoughtful distribution of gifts ensured that each child felt valued and remembered during the holiday season, strengthening their emotional well-being.\\n\\nOverall, the project made a meaningful difference by spreading compassion, building human connections, and creating lasting memories for both the children and the volunteers, truly reflecting the spirit of generosity and service.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-25","hoursSpent":6,"description":"In December 2023, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a heartwarming social outreach initiative titled “Secret Santa”, aimed at spreading joy and companionship to underprivileged children during the Christmas season. The project brought together more than 150 volunteers who visited four orphanages — Sri Sai Sneha Foundation, Sneha Jyoti Orphanage, Jana Seva Orphanage, and Chinmayi Foundation — on Christmas Day to celebrate with the children.\\n\\nThe event was designed to create a festive and inclusive atmosphere through a variety of engaging activities. Volunteers organized games, storytelling sessions, music, and dance, encouraging active participation and interaction with the children. These activities helped build a sense of connection, happiness, and belonging, making the celebration lively and memorable.\\n\\nIn addition to entertainment, the volunteers distributed thoughtful gifts as part of the “Secret Santa” concept, ensuring each child felt valued and remembered during the holiday season. The initiative focused not only on material support but also on emotional well-being by sharing time, care, and positive experiences.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PNCv4jDPlPGyGXu-ZZ7bz","name":"Fist Full","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/Kgkm3f7mbBaxPJ_-lJpXN.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-19","duration":96,"outcomes":"The Fist Full initiative successfully provided essential food supplies to organizations that care for underprivileged children, helping ensure access to nutritious meals and basic support. The collected donations contributed to reducing food insecurity for many beneficiaries and supported institutions working toward child welfare and education.\\n\\nFor volunteers, the project fostered a strong sense of empathy and social responsibility. Participating in the logistics and distribution process helped build teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills while also creating a deeper awareness of the challenges faced by vulnerable communities.\\n\\nOverall, the project created a meaningful social impact by combining collective effort with compassion, demonstrating how small individual contributions can come together to make a significant difference in the lives of those in need.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-10-16","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Fist Full was a large-scale humanitarian initiative carried out by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Rotary Club of Bangalore Spandana, District 3191, from 16th October 2023 to 19th January 2024. The project was built around the simple yet powerful idea of donating a “fistful” of essential food grains to support underprivileged children and communities.\\n\\nThe initiative was conducted in two phases. In the first phase, substantial quantities of rice, various types of dal, and wheat flour were collected and donated to Advaya Educational and Charitable Trust. In the second phase, additional food supplies were gathered and provided to Sai Gurukul School, Bengaluru, which supports underprivileged children by offering free education, meals, and basic necessities.\\n\\nAs a volunteer, I contributed by assisting in the collection, sorting, packing, and distribution of food items. The project emphasized teamwork, compassion, and the importance of community support in addressing hunger and food insecurity.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1Mg_ZQwu_bnXAX0JT03b9","name":"Fask Trek 2.0","slNo":7,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/Gyu6IJjI1UmVGASZPtaFy.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/WcvJrizwDhqDMd18LCm3K.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/jm5hEbvQK1BTxvb34nobA.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Fast Trek 2.0 successfully promoted environmental awareness and responsible tourism by encouraging participants to actively engage in cleanliness and conservation efforts during the trek. The initiative contributed to maintaining the natural cleanliness of Kunagalu Betta Hills and highlighted the role individuals can play in preserving the environment.\\n\\nFor volunteers, the event provided valuable experience in event coordination, teamwork, and leadership while strengthening a sense of social and environmental responsibility. Participants gained a deeper appreciation for nature and the importance of sustainable practices.\\n\\nOverall, Fast Trek 2.0 was a meaningful and impactful initiative that effectively combined adventure, community participation, and environmental stewardship, leaving a lasting positive impression on both participants and volunteers.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Fast Trek 2.0 was a flagship social and environmental initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th January 2024. The event combined adventure with environmental responsibility, focusing on a cleanliness drive during a trekking expedition to promote awareness about environmental conservation.\\n\\nThe event commenced early in the morning, with participants assembling at 7:30 AM and receiving detailed safety instructions and event guidelines before departure. The trek took place at the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills, where participants not only experienced the beauty of nature but also actively contributed to preserving it through cleanliness efforts.\\n\\nAs a volunteer, I assisted in coordinating participants, ensuring adherence to safety protocols, guiding trekkers along the route, and supporting the cleanliness drive during the trek. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 75 individuals, creating a vibrant and energetic atmosphere while reinforcing the importance of protecting natural ecosystems.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":18,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_ZAZwMoJX3dlTCGvuMMrt","name":"Literary Team Rotaract RVCE","slNo":8,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/JccaBLAH6dFRnWv9Kv6c9.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/uN1RATrClRWDU4P8NEopp.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-26","duration":126,"outcomes":"Being part of the Literary Team strengthened my writing, editing, and communication skills, enabling me to convey ideas clearly and creatively for different audiences. I gained practical experience in drafting formal reports, promotional content, and event documentation.\\n\\nThe experience also enhanced my teamwork, time management, and coordination abilities, as I worked closely with event organizers and other team members to deliver quality content within deadlines.\\n\\nOverall, this role contributed to my personal and professional growth while allowing me to play an important part in documenting and promoting the social service initiatives of the Rotaract Club of RVCE.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-11-22","hoursSpent":24,"description":"As a member of the Literary Team of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, I contributed to the written and communication aspects of various social service, cultural, and community outreach initiatives conducted by the club. My role involved drafting event reports, writing descriptions for projects, preparing social media captions, and assisting in creating formal content for documentation and promotion.\\n\\nThe literary team played an important role in presenting the club’s initiatives in a clear, impactful, and professional manner. Through structured and meaningful content, we helped increase awareness, participation, and engagement for various events while also maintaining proper documentation of the club’s activities.\\n\\nThis role allowed me to support Rotaract’s mission through effective communication and storytelling, ensuring that the impact of each initiative reached a wider audience.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1de3u-BmIDZuluiJyzxHg","name":"Paperdrive","slNo":9,"place":"Rajarajeshwari Nagar","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/htLvUfb9jOLGclmMRoGAB.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Paper Drive successfully gathered a substantial quantity of recyclable materials, which helped generate resources for charitable organizations and reduced environmental waste. The initiative contributed to promoting sustainable practices and responsible recycling within the community.\\n\\nFor volunteers, the event strengthened teamwork, communication, and organizational skills while fostering a deeper sense of social responsibility and environmental awareness. Participants gained firsthand experience in community engagement and understood how small individual efforts can collectively create a meaningful impact.\\n\\nOverall, the Paper Drive was a successful outreach program that combined environmental sustainability with social service, leaving a positive impact on both the community and the student volunteers involved.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The Paper Drive, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 23rd June 2024, was a large-scale community service initiative aimed at promoting recycling and supporting charitable causes. The event brought together more than 400 student volunteers who actively participated in collecting used books, papers, and other waste materials from various areas across Bangalore.\\n\\nVolunteers went door-to-door and visited local businesses early in the morning to gather donations. The collected materials were then directed toward charities and NGOs, where they could be recycled or reused to support social welfare initiatives. The drive not only focused on material collection but also encouraged community members to contribute to sustainable waste management practices.\\n\\nAs a volunteer, I participated in the collection process, coordinated with residents and shop owners, and assisted in sorting and organizing the donated materials. The initiative highlighted the importance of responsible waste disposal and collective community effort.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GEbRvueG0JR4SIPfQEZg5","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/xHrfoMbNszCv857RxB0CH.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/hSbgfOrX3_cSweHfaILus.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/csPdqmfVSvtA38_5cKMg6.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp successfully collected a significant number of blood units, directly contributing to saving lives and supporting hospitals in meeting medical emergencies. The initiative also helped spread awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and dispelled common myths associated with it.\\n\\nFor volunteers, the event strengthened teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills while fostering a deep sense of social responsibility and compassion. Participants gained a greater understanding of the impact of community-driven health initiatives.\\n\\nOverall, the camp made a meaningful difference by promoting a culture of voluntary service and reinforcing the importance of contributing to public health and well-being.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":14,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th June 2024, was a health-focused social service initiative aimed at saving lives through voluntary blood donation. The camp was conducted at the Biotech Quadrangle inside the RVCE campus and encouraged students and staff to contribute to a noble medical cause.\\n\\nThe event was designed to raise awareness about the importance of blood donation and to ensure a sufficient blood supply for hospitals and patients in need. Proper medical supervision, safety measures, and post-donation care were arranged to ensure a safe and comfortable experience for donors. Refreshments and participation certificates were also provided to appreciate the donors’ contribution.\\n\\nAs a volunteer, I assisted in organizing the event, guiding donors through the registration process, managing crowd flow, and ensuring smooth coordination between participants and the medical team. The event reflected the spirit of service and humanitarian responsibility.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nN8Hie1fVXJjp4NuUpkr_","name":"Design Team Rotaract RVCE","slNo":11,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/GxIGC2NgXp6iEP0w5Sgly.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bbfd5a96-28b6-4705-8bc7-5481fdd800d2/x2B-oEFcdt-js4pTGyVQ2.png"],"endDate":"2024-08-28","duration":246,"outcomes":"Being part of the Design Team enhanced my creative, technical, and communication skills, particularly in graphic design, visual storytelling, and digital content creation. I gained hands-on experience in using design tools and learned how effective visuals can influence audience engagement and event participation.\\n\\nThe role also improved my time management, teamwork, and coordination skills, as I worked closely with event coordinators and other club members to meet deadlines and deliver designs for multiple events.\\n\\nOverall, this experience helped me grow both personally and professionally while contributing to the promotion and success of meaningful social service initiatives conducted by the Rotaract Club.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-12-27","hoursSpent":48,"description":"As a member of the Design Team of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, I contributed to the visual and creative aspects of various social, cultural, and community service events conducted by the club. My role involved designing posters, social media creatives, event banners, certificates, and promotional materials that helped in effective communication and outreach.\\n\\nThrough this role, I supported multiple initiatives by ensuring that event information was presented clearly, attractively, and professionally, thereby increasing engagement and participation. The design team played a crucial role in building the club’s visual identity and promoting its activities across digital and offline platforms.\\n\\nThis experience allowed me to combine creativity with communication while contributing to the successful execution and visibility of Rotaract events.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":16,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 03:22:13.830394+00', '2026-01-31 11:23:41.597763+00'), ('21daa076-6028-4170-82b5-88709894293c', '1d99b29b-1bca-486b-843a-54458037499f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22BT001","name":"Amith B","period":"2022-2026","department":"Biotechnology","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"7-wlDtcT-l9qP0Fb8mhA5","name":"FAST TREK 2.0","slNo":1,"place":"Kunagalu Hills","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":48,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9IzEyVr9hFcJXb-QZmzBu","name":"VISION","slNo":2,"place":"New National PU College","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":60,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fhKmxODGC-DMJlXSzV9Ui","name":"PAPER DRIVE","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":48,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pTNksYzOD9d0lprJamXsx","name":"BLOOD DONATION CAMP","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":64,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":16,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3zSGs-9GJ4QwJuVvtSxR7","name":"NAIVEDYAM 3.0","slNo":6,"place":"Banashankari","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-10-19","durati