, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HxZHXq3XX5T2AotI6AvUg","name":"UPTOWN JUNK","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-29","duration":2,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"2025-11-28","hoursSpent":24,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Y95NaCksEQF8kYx-GtIjx","name":"Eye-check up camp","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"2024-06-14","hoursSpent":8,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Regular Health Check up","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 11:07:47.889366+00', '2026-02-01 11:57:03.814584+00'), ('21db3ceb-5bd5-40da-b1ae-6ed70013244b', '72f796dc-58ff-4f0e-95f4-0e64d583d45c', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"8DY1J8B0xAmkcDvVLo9ij","name":"222222","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/72f796dc-58ff-4f0e-95f4-0e64d583d45c/6kckGbgzY-yP4P0NnzdEF.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/72f796dc-58ff-4f0e-95f4-0e64d583d45c/f_G-Ok4MraTTM27XsXXkw.png"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/72f796dc-58ff-4f0e-95f4-0e64d583d45c/FLYf8DN-eUitRV6X_yX3R.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 13:27:33.818725+00', '2026-01-30 13:27:33.818725+00'), ('225869d1-d663-4640-a953-c9bdf83c3973', 'e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC169","name":"Tejaswi Kulkarni","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"DSFbPpVVWdG-KpT-BcUsQ","name":"Echolore","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/SUvEue0gRmntw0PbbkyZb.png"],"endDate":"2025-09-18","duration":5,"outcomes":"Through this event, I enhanced my creative and expressive writing skills while gaining a deeper understanding of storytelling rooted in culture, emotion, and social themes. I developed the ability to articulate ideas clearly and impactfully, built confidence in presenting original thoughts, and cultivated an appreciation for folklore, motherhood, and environmental narratives. The experience also reinforced the importance of using words as a powerful medium for awareness and positive change.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-09-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"I participated in Echolore, a creative writing event organized by Rotaract RVCE, where I submitted an original essay inspired by themes of mothers, children, folklore, and the deep connection between humanity and the Earth. Through this event, I expressed emotions, cultural narratives, and social reflections using storytelling as a medium. My participation and successful submission earned me 4 activity points, recognizing my creative effort and engagement in literary expression.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ol7PCQr-APHUFilf23pHo","name":"FISTFULL 2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this initiative, I developed a stronger sense of social responsibility and awareness of food insecurity issues affecting vulnerable populations. I gained insight into the impact of individual contributions when combined with collective action, understanding how small efforts can scale into meaningful social change. The experience strengthened values of empathy, compassion, and civic engagement, while also enhancing my appreciation for structured social service initiatives. Additionally, it reinforced the importance of consistent participation in community welfare programs and encouraged me to actively contribute to sustainable and socially impactful causes in the future.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in Fist Full, a social welfare initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November. The initiative aimed to combat hunger and food insecurity by encouraging students to contribute essential food grains. As part of this drive, I donated 5 kg of rice, contributing to the collective effort to support underprivileged communities. The donation drive involved systematic daily collections and emphasized student participation in addressing real-world societal challenges.","aicteMapping":"Food Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/E0wCefVqeFfBfPB0fpVsx.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MgwO3faQ6p4aktNip_Xz_","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this initiative, I developed a deeper understanding of the social, ethical, and cultural implications of female foeticide and the long-term impact of gender imbalance on society. The experience strengthened my awareness of gender equality issues and reinforced the importance of advocacy and public participation in driving social change. I gained insight into how awareness campaigns and collective action can influence mindsets and promote social responsibility. The walkathon also enhanced my sense of civic duty, empathy, and commitment toward supporting causes that uphold human dignity, equality, and justice, motivating me to actively engage in initiatives that contribute to a more inclusive and equitable society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in the Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025. The walkathon was conducted with the objective of spreading awareness about the critical issue of female foeticide and emphasizing the importance of gender equality and the value of the girl child in society. The event witnessed the active participation of over 350 individuals, including students, faculty members, and parents, who came together in solidarity to support the cause. The walkathon commenced from the RVCE campus in the early hours of the morning and featured impactful placards, meaningful slogans, and a collective atmosphere of unity and purpose.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/FBdZyn_Ekr1PunY8OW0g5.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1ao_sNzcyDiSjbH1iK3Bo","name":"FISTFULL 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/aYfk4xNes_G9DbS7rzgTy.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this initiative, I developed a deeper sense of social responsibility and an increased awareness of issues related to hunger, nutrition, and community health. I gained insight into how individual contributions, when combined with large-scale participation, can lead to significant and measurable social impact. The experience strengthened my values of empathy, compassion, and civic engagement while enhancing my understanding of organized community service initiatives. It also reinforced the importance of active student involvement in social welfare programs and motivated me to continue contributing to sustainable initiatives aimed at improving the well-being of underprivileged communities.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in Fist Full, a standalone community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the support of Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted on 02/11/25. The initiative was focused on addressing hunger and improving food security by mobilizing students to donate essential food grains for community welfare. As part of this initiative, I contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, supporting the larger collective effort to combat food scarcity. The drive involved structured and systematic collection processes and witnessed large-scale student participation, highlighting the effectiveness of organized social service efforts. The collected food grains were distributed to multiple beneficiary organizations, including temples, hospitals, foundations, schools, and nearby anganwadis, ensuring support reached diverse sections of society. This initiative reinforced the importance of community-driven action in addressing societal challenges related to nutrition and welfare.","aicteMapping":"Food Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/ahsj7-vrOZpDSHMV77Hyi.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KsBrgb0SnEzv2o3GxPNEl","name":"T Shirt for Smiles","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this initiative, I developed a deeper understanding of social responsibility and the importance of contributing to community welfare through collective efforts. I gained insight into how even indirect forms of participation, such as financial or material support, can play a significant role in the success of social initiatives. The experience strengthened my sense of empathy, compassion, and civic awareness, while reinforcing the value of supporting causes that focus on the well-being and happiness of underprivileged children. It also motivated me to remain actively engaged in charitable initiatives and to contribute consistently toward meaningful social impact.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in the “T-Shirt for Smiles” community service initiative organized by Kannada Sangha, conducted on 07/07/2024. The initiative was aimed at supporting children residing at Prajkirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram, Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru, by encouraging students to contribute through the purchase of T-shirts as a form of donation. By purchasing a T-shirt, I actively supported the cause and contributed to the overall objective of spreading happiness and providing assistance to underprivileged children. The initiative promoted student involvement in social welfare activities and emphasized the importance of contributing in accessible and impactful ways. Through this initiative, students collectively worked towards creating a positive and compassionate environment for the children through support, care, and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/TJcG6h2jYpXT4-pIX4i5s.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WcsuNANoUXhSnK5AF7hUE","name":"Buy a Shirt , Plant a Tree","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this initiative, I developed a greater awareness of environmental sustainability and the role individuals play in protecting natural resources. The experience reinforced the importance of adopting environmentally responsible practices and contributing to long-term ecological balance through simple yet meaningful actions such as tree plantation. I gained insight into how collective student participation can create a significant positive impact on environmental conservation efforts. The initiative strengthened my sense of responsibility toward nature and motivated me to continue engaging in activities that promote sustainability, environmental protection, and community well-being.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in the “Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” community service initiative organized by Kannada Sangha on 07/07/2025. The initiative was designed to promote environmental awareness and encourage individual responsibility toward sustainability among students. As part of the event, students who purchased a T-shirt were provided with a tree sapling along with guidelines on proper planting and care. By purchasing the T-shirt and receiving a sapling, I actively contributed to the initiative’s objective of fostering eco-friendly practices and promoting green habits within the student community. The distribution of T-shirts and saplings was carried out within the college campus, making participation accessible and impactful while reinforcing the importance of personal involvement in environmental conservation.","aicteMapping":"Planting Tree","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/ZN9gdxGMN4rdw40jjHLQg.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4PSEP5ToirJKWtxf2pUmj","name":"Lakshya 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this event, I developed improved focus, hand-eye coordination, and mental discipline, which are essential skills both in sports and academic pursuits. The experience enhanced my understanding of precision-based sports and the importance of calm decision-making under controlled pressure. I gained exposure to the fundamentals of air rifle shooting, including posture, aim, and trigger control, while also learning the value of patience and consistency. The event strengthened my appreciation for structured sporting activities as a means of personal development and stress management.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in Lakshya – 10m Air Rifle Shooting Event, organized by NCC RVCE in collaboration with Kadamba Sports, conducted on 26th and 27th April 2025 at RV College of Engineering. The event was designed to promote discipline, focus, and precision while providing students with an opportunity to experience shooting sports in a structured and supervised environment. Open to students of all experience levels, the event encouraged participation by emphasizing skill development, concentration, and mental control rather than prior expertise. ","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/Jq9_Y3Ot2L9jeXfCHrYlt.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PWzM4NtbLuDCav6Jg-v86","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this initiative, I developed a deeper understanding of the educational challenges faced by underprivileged children in rural areas and the role community-driven initiatives play in bridging these gaps. The experience strengthened my sense of social responsibility and empathy toward marginalized communities, particularly in the context of access to education. I gained insight into how organized donation drives and collaborative efforts between educational institutions and non-profit organizations can create large-scale and sustainable impact. ","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in Project Pustak (Pusthaka – 2024), a stationery kit distribution program jointly organized by Rotaract Club of RVCE, RV College of Engineering, and Pranav Foundation, conducted from 24th May to 6th August 2024. The initiative aimed to support underprivileged children studying in rural government schools by addressing the lack of basic educational resources such as notebooks and geometry boxes. As part of this project, stationery kits were distributed to students from 1st to 10th standard, ensuring age-appropriate academic support. The initiative reached multiple rural regions across Karnataka, benefiting students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds who often face challenges in continuing their education due to the unavailability of essential learning materials.","aicteMapping":"Book Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/bejvW1x7Nge0_rqsotOBQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"l_ByfCY-r5fKm94Gv_vK9","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this initiative, I developed a stronger awareness of the challenges faced by underprivileged children in accessing basic educational resources. The experience reinforced the importance of education as a foundation for long-term social development and highlighted how individual financial contributions can create meaningful and measurable impact when combined with collective efforts. I gained insight into the role of organized donation drives in supporting educational equity and learned the value of social responsibility and empathy in community engagement. The initiative motivated me to continue supporting educational and welfare-oriented programs that contribute to inclusive growth and sustainable societal progress.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in Project Pustak, an educational support initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, aimed at promoting access to quality education for underprivileged children. The initiative focused on collecting donations to provide essential learning resources such as books, stationery, and other academic materials to students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds. Through this project, contributors were encouraged to support education in a structured and impactful manner by choosing donation tiers aligned with activity points. ","aicteMapping":"Book Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/v-pBr3z8ZSvCY7Q5EvyBj.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jHnejqxFsDln2fnGow7la","name":"Rush Hours 4.0","slNo":10,"place":"Respective Homes","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-11-15","duration":6,"outcomes":"Through my participation in RUSH HOURS 4.0, I developed enhanced skills in teamwork, time management, creative thinking, and leadership. The event improved my ability to perform under time constraints and adapt to competitive environments while maintaining focus and consistency. I gained greater awareness of pressing social and environmental issues through poster creation and plantation activities, reinforcing the importance of responsible citizenship. The talent-based and influencer-themed tasks helped build confidence, communication skills, and creative expression.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-11-10","hoursSpent":5,"description":"I participated in RUSH HOURS 4.0, the fourth edition of a mega community service and professional development event organized with the objective of engaging students beyond their routine academic schedules while fostering creativity, teamwork, and social awareness. The event was conducted over five days and included a pre-event task to generate enthusiasm, followed by eight main competitive tasks designed in an elimination-based format. With participation from 250+ students, the event combined learning, competition, and societal contribution in an engaging manner. Participants competed in teams, with each task leading to progressive eliminations, and their performance was tracked through regular updates on an event dashboard and leaderboard.","aicteMapping":"Planting Trees","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/9Yenxir4mkTv30A0tQRxb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iKoY6PCs931vbAw9wod9D","name":"UTPT India Quiz 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the India Quiz, I strengthened my general knowledge, analytical abilities, and problem-solving skills while performing under time-bound conditions. The quiz enhanced my awareness of India’s historical, cultural, and contemporary developments and improved my ability to recall information quickly and accurately. Additionally, participating in a national-level event boosted my confidence and exposure to competitive academic environments. Overall, the experience contributed positively to my intellectual growth and reinforced the importance of continuous learning and awareness as an engineering student.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in the India Quiz conducted as part of Under The Peepal Tree 2025, a national-level quiz fest organized by RV College of Engineering, held from 23rd to 25th May, 2025. The quiz aimed to test and enhance participants’ knowledge of India across diverse domains including history, culture, governance, current affairs, and national heritage. The event provided a competitive yet intellectually stimulating platform, encouraging analytical thinking, quick decision-making, and awareness of India’s socio-cultural landscape. Participants from various institutions across the country actively took part, making the event a rich learning experience and a celebration of knowledge at the national level.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e54ca50f-8bb0-46c8-a29d-9e0768d26196/sJeEQnzNFqcKFIG0VdPfJ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"S Praveen","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 19:47:37.199261+00', '2026-01-31 04:58:33.002117+00'), ('228c5566-fe23-4ca0-9b5a-950567cfb60c', '17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS058","name":"Sankalp Chaudhary","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"xj16McirlIf0_7PWFklSM","name":"Fist Full","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/SgXAq3jnR4kwLbuCLIV-D.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant quantity of rice through the contribution of 5 kg from each participant. It helped provide food support to underprivileged communities and addressed issues related to hunger and food insecurity. The drive created awareness about the importance of sharing and social responsibility among students. \\n\\nOverall, the initiative made a meaningful social impact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and humanitarian service on campus.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the aim of supporting the underprivileged and promoting social responsibility among students. In this drive, students and volunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, symbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of food to those in need. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and hunger faced by many sections of society. It encouraged participants to share resources selflessly and develop a habit of giving back to the community. \\n\\nThe drive also strengthened values of empathy, kindness, and unity among the students. The collected rice was planned to be distributed to needy communities through charitable organizations. The drive witnessed enthusiastic participation, showcasing strong teamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided students with an opportunity to actively engage in social service activities. The initiative highlighted how even small contributions can collectively create a significant positive impact. \\n\\n","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/IYj76u-1_u-E4jzqTTpFx.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oERlK7zdB0SnvBwRpo0wu","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/VRsYo1e4t5cmCoesZoXrK.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-02","duration":-1,"outcomes":"The overwhelming response from participants highlighted the deep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service and social responsibility. The event fostered a sense of camaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of teamwork and determination. \\n\\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, encouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while giving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the bond between students and the community but also showcased how small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful social change.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants. \\n\\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/0E106CVCypm7XjAtd7gIw.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KUDthDQjjT_4hQi60yjlm","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/w0gLCCS_vapBfDBEfX6Ja.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The overwhelming response from participants highlighted the deep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service and social responsibility. The event fostered a sense of camaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of teamwork and determination. \\n\\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, encouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while giving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the bond between students and the community but also showcased how small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful social change.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants. \\n\\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/vEsqVZSFI7-spQ1J1Y9bm.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cVPoAARmM3Rk-x6YM68MH","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/3lKZvPcgxuHqA-JoZl3k5.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged rural students by providing them with essential educational materials and school supplies. The initiative created a meaningful impact by ensuring needy students received textbooks, stationery, and other learning resources required for a better education experience. \\n\\nWith effective fund collection and proper utilization, the event reflected strong community participation and social responsibility. The collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranava Foundation strengthened the reach of this initiative, helping improve access to education and creating a positive learning environment for students.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of approximately Rs. 100 to 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which was used to procure and donate mission-needed supplies such as severe deserving students. \\n\\nThe collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. The Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranava Foundation procured essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/Qs51waEEr1e21j5XiWmry.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nD1e03fqoypSDI9ZAW8MA","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/SvNFJmi7qzEQaPZR7lxDP.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-25","duration":4,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged rural students by providing them with essential educational materials and school supplies. The initiative created a meaningful impact by ensuring needy students received textbooks, stationery, and other learning resources required for a better education experience. \\n\\nWith effective fund collection and proper utilization, the event reflected strong community participation and social responsibility. The collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranava Foundation strengthened the reach of this initiative, helping improve access to education and creating a positive learning environment for students.\\n\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of approximately Rs. 100 to 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which was used to procure and donate mission-needed supplies such as severe deserving students. \\n\\nThe collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. The Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranava Foundation procured essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/EGwKUHeqtQUlzdJCYDV89.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3EzDAt01uIHRHr12vlMab","name":"Discom Volunteer for Cultural Fest","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":4,"outcomes":"Completed","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-03","hoursSpent":24,"description":"I was actively involved as part of DISCOM, the event security\\ndepartment for the cultural fest 8th Mile. My responsibilities\\nincluded crowd regulation, access control, coordinating with\\norganizers, and ensuring smooth movement across venues. I\\nhelped maintain safety protocols, managed peak-hour footfall,\\nand contributed to the seamless execution of events throughout\\nthe fest.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/CFRrXWiTX4NtNQfTxjFpk.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1KF_dlUWX_DOJdtTPzQy1","name":"Broseph Shikshana Vedike (BSV) Programme","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-04","duration":44,"outcomes":"COMPLETED","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-01-20","hoursSpent":32,"description":"I taught underprivileged students at a government school,\\nfocusing on building their foundational understanding through\\nsimple explanations and interactive learning. This experience\\nhelped me develop patience, adaptability, and effective\\ncommunication skills. Teaching in a real classroom environment\\nincreased my empathy, confidence, and sense of social\\nresponsibility while deepening my appreciation for the impact of\\neducation at the grassroots level.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":35,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/17be83a8-ae24-4cc4-935b-dd4d02b10615/VAD2Oo6ia0Wl_Lky9yVjb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:31:20.794686+00', '2026-01-30 08:20:19.897628+00'), ('250753c2-6611-4689-8eba-8788c177a4b2', 'c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD062","name":"VIPUL S","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"sP8d-dVFUZ_3tyL99XmK0","name":"UTSARGA 2024","slNo":1,"place":"In and around RVCE  Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The \\nactivity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and \\ncompleting the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the \\nmarathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on \\npromoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on February 4th, 2024, \\nfrom 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages \\nstudents and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based \\nregistration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create \\nawareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness \\nactivity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community \\nimpact.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rHcgo6Aa3qM3h3l_wBIDS","name":"AEC Plantation 1","slNo":2,"place":"Bengaluru University","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-03-22","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the AEC Plantation, I contributed to the enhancement of \\nthe Bio Park''s natural environment and developed a practical understanding of reforestation \\ntechniques. The activity helped me realize the importance of individual contributions to \\nenvironmental sustainability and the role of the youth in combating climate change at a local \\nlevel. I gained hands-on experience in manual labor and teamwork while coordinating with \\npeers to ensure the successful planting of saplings. Overall, the experience strengthened my \\ncommitment to environmental responsibility and provided a meaningful connection to nature.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-22","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The AEC Plantation 1 was an environmental conservation initiative focused on improving \\ngreen cover. Held at the University Bio-Park campus, near the Gandhi Research Centre, \\nparticipants worked under the guidance of student organizers to plant saplings and learn \\nabout local biodiversity. The event aimed to promote environmental stewardship among \\nengineering students and address local ecological concerns through direct action. Activities \\nincluded preparing the soil, planting various species of trees, and understanding the long-term \\nmaintenance required for successful reforestation efforts. This hands-on experience not only \\nenhanced the aesthetic appeal of the area but also instilled a sense of shared responsibility among \\nthe students. By actively engaging in the physical labor of afforestation, participants recognized \\nthat combating climate change begins with small, local steps.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/M65yj7L-vxjORpXMq7BtK.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MVaDEUeHb9ibIZIO1VX86","name":"FAST TREK 2.0","slNo":3,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by \\nactively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense \\nof environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by \\nreporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped \\nimprove my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Kunagal Betta Hills, and \\nit also enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group \\nof participants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved \\nmy fitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature. \\nFurthermore, witnessing the tangible impact of sustainable tourism taught me how recreational \\nactivities can be effectively combined with social responsibility to preserve our heritage sites.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated \\nto preserving the environment. Armed with waste collection bags, the student volunteers \\ndiligently cleared plastic waste and litter along the trail, ensuring the natural beauty of \\nthe hills was restored. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus to \\nthe trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the \\nadventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all \\nattendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagal Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding \\nsuccess, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750 \\nindividuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s \\nvibrant atmosphere.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/PMU9pAAmUGpSFMVENZK7D.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ryM-d1-345vxTbRu41qmP","name":"PAPER DRIVE 2024","slNo":4,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Paper Drive, I actively contributed to a large-scale \\nresource mobilization effort that benefited multiple charitable organizations. The experience \\nof going door-to-door helped me develop better interpersonal and communication skills while \\ninteracting with diverse residents and business owners. I gained a deeper understanding of \\ncommunity involvement and the practical logistics of managing waste materials for a social \\ncause. This activity also reinforced my commitment to environmental sustainability and social \\nresponsibility. Overall, the initiative provided a meaningful platform to address social issues \\nthrough collective student engagement and volunteerism.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":8,"description":"On 23rd June 2024, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a \"Paper Drive\" involving over \\n400 student volunteers who collected books, papers, and waste materials across various areas \\nof Bangalore. Volunteers started early in the morning, going door-to-door and visiting local \\nbusinesses to gather donations. The primary objective was to collect resources for charities \\nand NGOs to support their initiatives and assist people in need. Beyond resource collection, \\nthe drive served as a community awareness program to foster social responsibility among \\nboth the participants and the residents of Bangalore. Crucially, the drive also served a major \\nenvironmental purpose by diverting tons of paper waste from landfills and channeling it into \\nproper recycling streams, thereby promoting sustainable waste management practices among \\nthe local residents.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/gHg7f6WyOhYQPFjkf1R9H.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Vq6bmtJ_v-QC0bIr5hxpq","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in this awareness campaign, I gained a comprehensive \\nunderstanding of the electoral process and the critical importance of youth participation \\nin democracy. The activity helped me realize how an informed electorate is the backbone \\nof a progressive nation. I developed better civic awareness and learned about the ethical \\nresponsibilities associated with casting a vote. Additionally, engaging with the campaign \\nimproved my communication skills as I helped spread awareness to my peers about voter \\nregistration and democratic rights. Overall, the experience instilled a deeper sense of patriotism \\nand social responsibility, motivating me to remain an active and informed citizen.","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The \"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye\" (My First Vote for the Country) was an awareness-driven \\ninitiative organized by NSS RVCE to encourage and educate first-time voters on the importance \\nof electoral participation. The activity focused on highlighting the role of the youth in \\nshaping the nation''s future through their democratic right to vote. Participants were engaged \\nin discussions regarding the voting process, the significance of informed decision-making, \\nand the impact of individual votes on national governance. The campaign aimed to foster a \\nsense of civic duty among students and ensure they are prepared to contribute responsibly to \\nthe democratic process. To make the session interactive, students actively participated in an \\nonline quiz designed to test their knowledge of the Indian Constitution and electoral history. \\nFurthermore, the event concluded with a collective pledge-taking ceremony, where young voters \\nformally committed to exercising their franchise ethically, thereby reinforcing the spirit of \\ndemocracy on campus.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/sxg8YsuaeBC1cnvh7G6B5.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xa_cwTZcAIRPeIF4ZNY8b","name":"CHEELA MELA","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2026-01-02","duration":379,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the Eco bag Initiative, I successfully crafted 200 newspaper \\nbags, directly contributing to the reduction of single-use plastic in local markets. This \\nactivity helped me develop a practical understanding of sustainable alternatives and the \\nimportance of community-driven environmental solutions. I gained hands-on experience in \\nmanual crafting and learned how small, collective efforts can lead to a significant social impact. \\nAdditionally, managing the production of a large quantity of bags improved my discipline, time \\nmanagement, and commitment to social service. Overall, the experience strengthened my sense \\nof environmental responsibility and civic duty toward creating a more sustainable community.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-20","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Eco bag Initiative, also known as \"Cheela Mela,\" was a sustainability-focused project \\norganized by NSS RVCE in collaboration with EMPRI. The primary goal was to craft newspaper \\nbags to be distributed to street vendors at K R Market, providing a biodegradable alternative to \\nplastic and supporting a greener environment. Participants were tasked with crafting durable \\npaper bags following specific guidelines to ensure they were suitable for commercial use. \\nThe initiative allowed students to contribute to environmental preservation through hands-on \\nvolunteerism, either by crafting bags onsite at the Environment Lab or at home. To ensure the \\nbags were sturdy enough for daily use, participants followed a structured video tutorial that \\ndemonstrated the precise folding and pasting techniques required. The completed batches were \\ncollected at the Environment Lab in the Civil Department, symbolizing a collective effort to \\nturn waste paper into a valuable, eco-friendly resource for the city''s vendors.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/qH9ln2vLbdjUXyZIHkC1G.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Er6ern984MDsdxviqH9X8","name":"CHEELA MELA(Extra)","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained practical exposure to sustainable alternatives by \\nlearning and demonstrating the process of making eco-friendly paper bags from recycled \\nnewspapers. Actively interacting with visitors and vendors improved my communication and \\npublic engagement skills while spreading awareness about the harmful effects of single-use \\nplastics. The workshop strengthened my sense of environmental responsibility and reinforced \\nthe importance of responsible waste management and sustainable living. Additionally, working \\nalongside fellow volunteers enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills. Overall, the activity \\nincreased my awareness of sustainability practices and gave me a sense of satisfaction in \\ncontributing to a positive environmental impact within the community.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-20","hoursSpent":3,"description":"NSS RVCE, in collaboration with EMPRI, organized a Paper Bag Workshop as part of the \\nPlastic Drive Awareness campaign at the Kadale Kayi Parishe. The event aimed to reduce the \\nuse of single-use plastics by teaching visitors and vendors how to make eco-friendly paper \\nbags using recycled newspapers. Volunteers demonstrated the process, interacted with the \\npublic, and spread awareness about the environmental impact of plastic waste. The activity \\nencouraged sustainable practices, promoted responsible waste management, and motivated the \\ncommunity to adopt reusable and biodegradable alternatives. The workshop helped create a \\npositive environmental impact and strengthened awareness on sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/nVAnWbjW5vqf5io6bk0uv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"I73gacEtjjaGA2p4YLKaP","name":"FIST FULL 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-21","duration":7,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in this donation drive, I contributed directly to community \\nwelfare by supporting the collection of essential food items for those in need. I gained a \\nstronger sense of social responsibility and empathy by being part of an initiative that emphasized \\nsolidarity and helping others through collective effort. The activity also helped me understand \\nhow even small individual contributions can lead to large-scale impact when students come \\ntogether for a cause. Furthermore, being involved in the collection process gave me practical \\ninsight into the logistics of resource mobilization and the importance of organized packaging in \\nhumanitarian relief efforts. Overall, this experience strengthened my awareness of community \\nservice and reinforced the importance of actively participating in welfare-oriented initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":3,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore \\nSpandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily \\ncollections in the Civil Department. Student volunteers played a crucial role in meticulously \\nweighing, packing, and segregating the donations to ensure they were ready for immediate \\ndistribution to the partner beneficiaries. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with \\nthe total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. \\nThe collected grains were subsequently distributed to orphanages and care homes, directly \\naddressing the issue of hunger in the community. This initiative highlighted the power of small \\nefforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare \\nand solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/4T91PDtqv9abEb_eM_REG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DZ-jBE4jH71ZQ-r3tmVw6","name":"Human Elephant Conflict","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The session emphasized the importance of coexistence between humans and wildlife, \\nshowcasing how timely alerts, improved safety equipment, and local community involvement \\ncan significantly reduce conflict-related risks. Participants gained a deeper understanding of \\nground-level conservation challenges and the critical role of technology and awareness in \\nwildlife protection. Overall, the activity sensitized students toward environmental responsibility \\nand the need to support initiatives that safeguard both forest personnel and wildlife.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":2,"description":"As part of the Elephant Conflict Mitigation project, NSS RVCE organized an awareness \\nand interaction session in collaboration with the Adavi Alert Foundation (AAF). The session \\nwas conducted by Mr. Pavan Joshi, who provided valuable insights into the growing issue \\nof human–elephant conflict (HEC) in India and the need for sustainable, technology-driven \\nsolutions.\\nDuring the talk, Mr. Pavan Joshi explained the mission and work of the Adavi Alert Foundation, \\nwhich focuses on protecting frontline forest staff and reducing HEC through tactical equipment, \\ndetection technology, and community-based proactive measures. He highlighted key initiatives \\nsuch as the use of early warning and detection systems, distribution of high-power torches and \\nprotective gear, and support extended to anti-poaching camp staff operating in high-risk forest \\nzones.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/dVYFbU8mXqZX4epPKM3Hg.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"O87caX3JyXRtNspVlUHmD","name":"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, participating students developed a stronger sense of \\nenvironmental responsibility by directly contributing to tree plantation efforts. The initiative \\nincreased awareness about the importance of afforestation and individual actions in combating \\nenvironmental degradation. Students were motivated to adopt sustainable habits and take \\nownership of nurturing the saplings they received. Overall, the drive successfully fostered \\neco-conscious behavior, encouraged community participation, and made a positive contribution \\ntoward environmental sustainability, thereby justifying the allocation of AICTE activity points \\nfor student involvement.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Kannada Sangha, R.V. College of Engineering, organized the community service initiative \\n“Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” to promote environmental awareness and sustainable practices \\namong students. As part of this drive, students who purchased the event T-shirt were provided \\nwith a tree sapling along with clear guidelines on proper planting and care. The distribution \\nof T-shirts and saplings was conducted within the college campus, encouraging students to \\ntake personal responsibility for contributing to a greener environment. The initiative aimed to \\ncombine participation with action by motivating students to actively engage in afforestation and \\nenvironmental conservation.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/L-PnmwM8Ehfj0ZXSdfGhQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_g5PlDBw89mpmuqyfwR7t","name":"UTPT INDIA QUIZ 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Indi-Genius Quiz, I enhanced my knowledge of Indian \\nculture, history, and traditions through a competitive and interactive learning experience. The \\nevent helped improve my critical thinking, recall ability, and time-based decision-making skills \\nwhile working collaboratively in a team. Participation also strengthened my confidence in \\nexpressing ideas and responding under pressure during quiz rounds. Overall, the quiz served \\nas an enriching academic and cultural experience that combined learning, teamwork, and \\nco-curricular development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Indi-Genius Quiz, organized by RV Quiz Corp, was conducted as part of UTPT 2025 on \\n23rd May 2025 at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The quiz was designed \\nto celebrate India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage through an engaging and \\ncompetitive format. The event covered a wide range of topics including Indian history, Mughal \\narchitecture, epics such as the Mahabharata and Ramayana, festivals, regional cuisines, and \\ncultural traditions. Conducted in teams of up to three members, the quiz provided participants \\nwith an interactive platform to test their knowledge, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills \\nwhile experiencing the diverse essence of India in an intellectually stimulating environment.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/bLsPYXUBa_te47-xOAXE9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-JmW4ypEpvPyvnyS1qZCO","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Blood Donation Camp, I developed a stronger sense of social responsibility and awareness about the importance of contributing to society’s healthcare needs. The experience enhanced my understanding of humanitarian service and the impact a single act of donation can have on saving lives. It also helped build empathy, confidence, and a willingness to participate in future social welfare activities. Overall, the camp was a meaningful and enriching experience that combined community service, awareness, and personal growth through a noble cause.","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was organized as a social responsibility initiative to promote voluntary blood donation and raise awareness about the importance of saving lives through timely medical support. The camp brought together students, faculty members, and volunteers in a collective effort to contribute to the healthcare needs of the community. Medical professionals supervised the entire process, ensuring safety, hygiene, and proper screening of donors. Participants were educated about the benefits of blood donation, eligibility criteria, and the critical role donated blood plays in emergency treatments, surgeries, and for patients with serious medical conditions. The event fostered a spirit of compassion, social service, and community involvement while providing a well-coordinated and supportive environment for all donors.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/x5NH7BjUdhwCHVz89d1oK.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EIBsmdNDd6KBNX7haDFba","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz","slNo":13,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Round 1 of the Viksit Bharat Quiz 2024, I gained a clearer \\nunderstanding of India’s key achievements, development initiatives, and long-term vision of \\nbecoming a developed nation by 2047. Attempting the time-bound digital quiz enhanced my \\ngeneral awareness, analytical thinking, and ability to perform accurately under time constraints. \\nThe competitive format helped improve my focus, quick decision-making, and familiarity with \\nnational policies and progress across various sectors.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz 2024 (formally the Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge) was the introductory \\nstage of a national competition designed to engage India’s youth in the vision of a \"Developed \\nIndia\" by 2047. It served as Round 1 of the Viksit Bharat Young Leaders Dialogue, testing \\nknowledge of India’s landmark achievements and progress. Format: A digital, time-bound \\ncontest hosted on the MY Bharat platform. Participants had to answer 10 questions in 300 \\nseconds. Engagement: Nearly 20 lakh (1,952,749) participants took part in the challenge.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/TEbOsXHtR6rNcRarMZy2e.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Uz80hhjxF9j_YpxvKcnwF","name":"ECO WALK","slNo":14,"place":"JP Nagar","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Eco Walk, I developed a deeper appreciation for nature and a stronger awareness of environmental conservation. The experience helped reduce stress, improved mindfulness, and encouraged me to adopt more eco-friendly habits in daily life. Observing the peaceful environment and listening to birds enhanced my sense of connection with the natural world. The event also promoted physical well-being through light exercise and fostered a sense of responsibility toward protecting the environment. Overall, the Eco Walk was a refreshing and meaningful experience that combined health, learning, and environmental consciousness.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-01-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Eco Walk was organized as an environmental awareness activity aimed at promoting appreciation for nature and encouraging sustainable living practices. The walk was conducted in the early morning at JP Nagar, providing participants with a refreshing opportunity to experience the natural surroundings in a calm and pollution-free environment. During the walk, we observed greenery, fresh morning air, and the soothing sounds of birds chirping, which created a serene and rejuvenating atmosphere. The event highlighted the importance of conserving biodiversity, protecting urban green spaces, and maintaining ecological balance. It served as a platform to connect with nature while understanding the role individuals can play in environmental protection.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/vIm2OPQkaI5ioYuTHmpQo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HZDwYMptzyLZDTeJxCINx","name":"FAST TREK 3.0","slNo":15,"place":"Ramnagara","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by \\nactively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense \\nof environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by \\nreporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped \\nimprove my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Kunagal Betta Hills, and \\nit also enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group \\nof participants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved \\nmy fitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature. \\nFurthermore, witnessing the tangible impact of sustainable tourism taught me how recreational \\nactivities can be effectively combined with social responsibility to preserve our heritage sites.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated \\nto preserving the environment. Armed with waste collection bags, the student volunteers \\ndiligently cleared plastic waste and litter along the trail, ensuring the natural beauty of \\nthe hills was restored. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus to \\nthe trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the \\nadventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all \\nattendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagal Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding \\nsuccess, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750 \\nindividuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s \\nvibrant atmosphere.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c694e7de-ca6d-47c5-a3bb-d6b3a9b45243/CEAz3d58xCrnfvVIj5SdL.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","de