photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":40,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Kendaganna Swamy","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 19:30:55.110517+00', '2026-02-01 19:56:32.343478+00'), ('269866f1-b7b9-43e1-b10e-a6cfdb7a5b3b', '1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS179","name":"Sathwik Chandra","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"1MRCMocBj7A1Qpy7B_SGL","name":"Fast Trek","slNo":1,"place":"Kaurava Kunda Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/Snmb9_EFPOkhKVvud-Wpr.jpeg"],"endDate":"2022-12-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced participants’ physical endurance, confidence, and stress management abilities while fostering leadership, coordination, and teamwork skills. It also encouraged a sense of environmental awareness and responsibility among students, strengthened peer relationships, and provided a memorable experiential learning opportunity outside the classroom.","semester":"1","startDate":"2022-12-15","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Fast Trek was a one-day trekking event organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on December 15, 2022, to the scenic Kaurava Kunda Hills near Bengaluru. The event aimed to promote adventure, physical fitness, and team bonding among students through a fast-paced trek across challenging rocky trails and natural landscapes. Participants enjoyed panoramic views from the hilltop while engaging in teamwork and mutual support throughout the journey, making it a refreshing break from routine academic life.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/pJYSN1zDlLCgP9ssaaMvD.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iARhSLfAvgLGQYi6JrVmf","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/iFhQ48-SN0vsqWvIFYxLt.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive achieved strong participation from the RVCE community, resulting in a significant collection of blood units that were handed over to the Lion’s Blood Center for use in local hospitals. The event heightened awareness about the importance of regular blood donation, strengthened community engagement, and inspired many first-time donors to commit to future drives, while reinforcing values of empathy, altruism, and public health responsibility among students and staff.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Blood Donation Drive was a campus-wide social initiative organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Lion’s Blood Center on June 6, 2023. The drive aimed to encourage students, faculty, and staff to contribute to community health by donating blood, fostering a culture of compassion and civic responsibility within the college. Participants registered, underwent health screening, and donated blood under the supervision of trained medical professionals in a safe and supportive environment, reinforcing the spirit of service and collective contribution toward saving lives.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to health care by donating blood to blood camps.","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/-MOXzvSkq9IrwZE27D1GD.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uJjJD0SK4m-s5-4-44czC","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":3,"place":"Kormangala Residential Area","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/ZNMKI059Fv-HxTImy4dhf.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-10","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Paper Drive successfully collected a substantial amount of waste paper, which was then sorted and sent for recycling, reducing landfill contributions and supporting sustainable resource use. The campaign increased awareness about waste segregation and recycling among students and residents, inspired continued participation in environmental initiatives, and strengthened RVCE’s commitment to community service and ecological stewardship.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-10","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Paper Drive was a sustainability initiative organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) to collect waste paper from student residences and nearby communities, aiming to promote environmental responsibility and recycling awareness. Volunteers went door-to-door to gather old newspapers, notebooks, and other recyclable paper materials, encouraging participants to reduce waste and support eco-friendly practices. The drive fostered teamwork among student volunteers and helped build stronger connections between the college and local residents while contributing to a cleaner, greener campus and neighborhood.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/SaUtJY0PZgXApurt1dTeh.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yzsIeDGMHRblj9o_uAQKI","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/CiZnb6FWnLLWiu5yUQQ2e.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully mobilized financial support for children’s education, enabling access to essential learning materials and academic opportunities. The initiative fostered a strong sense of empathy, social awareness, and responsibility among participants, while promoting the value of collective contribution. It also inspired continued student involvement in educational and philanthropic initiatives aimed at creating a positive and lasting impact on society.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Project Pustak was a donation drive organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) with the objective of supporting children’s education by raising funds for educational resources and learning support. Under this initiative, each participant contributed ₹350 per person, collectively helping provide books, stationery, and educational assistance to underprivileged children. The camp encouraged students to actively participate in social upliftment and understand the importance of equal access to education, reinforcing RVCE’s commitment to social responsibility and community development.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/wa_t8RP84K3qUaa9JueVk.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uTW8sUtgKomWpAnUmz9I7","name":"Akshara","slNo":5,"place":"Mount Caramel School","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/O0Cyotq_jg7OHEDpo1Hcv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-10-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative helped improve students’ understanding of basic concepts, boosted their confidence in learning, and encouraged curiosity and regular study habits. For the college volunteers, Akshara enhanced teaching, communication, and leadership skills while fostering empathy and social responsibility. Overall, the program contributed to educational empowerment at the grassroots level and strengthened the bond between RVCE students and the local community.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-10-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Akshara was a community outreach initiative organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) in which college students volunteered to teach children from 1st to 5th standard. The program focused on providing academic support in core subjects such as mathematics, science, and languages through interactive lessons, simple explanations, and engaging activities. By bridging the gap between formal schooling and personalized learning, Akshara aimed to strengthen foundational concepts while creating a supportive and motivating learning environment for young students.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/8GtMmwW_QFyN-k_IGSIvQ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4dO6dy3uN0UtgbVPmbbKa","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"Rajarajeshwari Nagara","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully increased awareness about the importance of regular physical activity and healthy living among participants. It helped build stamina, mental resilience, and a spirit of perseverance, while also strengthening camaraderie and collective participation. Utsarga Marathon inspired continued engagement in fitness-oriented and socially driven initiatives, reinforcing RVCE’s culture of holistic student development.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-25","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Utsarga Marathon was a fitness and social awareness event organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) with the objective of promoting physical well-being, endurance, and community participation among students. The marathon brought together participants from the RVCE community to run in support of a larger cause, encouraging a healthy lifestyle while fostering discipline, determination, and teamwork. The event created an energetic and motivating atmosphere, uniting students in a shared commitment to fitness and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/P9rSgLQVkgOyLTGUVsh-C.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ClOxnkHu4DaYSnz6dN-6p","name":"Plantation Drive","slNo":7,"place":"Devikarani Roerich Estate","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/qFt4iHTSGO5_3ji4w6Sr2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The plantation drive resulted in the successful planting of numerous saplings, contributing to long-term environmental benefits such as improved greenery, soil stability, and ecological balance. It also increased environmental awareness among participants, instilled a sense of responsibility toward nature, and encouraged continued involvement in sustainability initiatives, reinforcing RVCE’s commitment to environmental protection and community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-25","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Plantation Drive was an environmental sustainability initiative conducted by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) at Devikarani Roerich Estate on 25th May 2024. The drive focused on planting saplings and promoting ecological conservation, with active participation from students and volunteers who worked together to restore green cover and enhance biodiversity in the area. The event emphasized the importance of environmental stewardship and hands-on involvement in conservation efforts, allowing participants to connect with nature while contributing positively to the ecosystem.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/FsYv0jWwXHI3BGYFX9V0D.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KsgDF3yhj8VsuMMtQ_a7p","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/6h98XL-WYpKfwdNZCDWDb.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The camp witnessed enthusiastic participation and resulted in the successful collection of a substantial number of blood units, directly contributing to lifesaving treatments for children at the institute. It raised awareness about the critical need for regular blood donation, motivated first-time donors, and strengthened the sense of empathy, civic responsibility, and community service among participants, making the initiative both impactful and meaningful.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Blood Donation Camp was a social service initiative organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on June 28, 2024, in collaboration with the Indira Gandhi Institute of Child Health. The camp aimed to support pediatric healthcare by encouraging students, faculty, and staff to voluntarily donate blood for children in need of medical care. The event was conducted in a well-organized and hygienic setting, with proper medical screening and supervision by healthcare professionals, reflecting RVCE’s commitment to social welfare and community health.","aicteMapping":"Contributing to the healthcare sector by donating blood.","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/DfOmlBoscnRxWQy23BgTV.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5Xl9U_aDq3Zoh0Issnprs","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/WHujhPIbuSn50RrZrpyFs.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-02-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully generated funds that were utilized to support children’s learning needs and improve access to quality educational resources. The initiative fostered empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility among participants, while encouraging continued involvement in educational and philanthropic activities that contribute to long-term societal development.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-02-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Project Pustak was a donation initiative organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) aimed at supporting children’s education by collecting contributions of ₹350 per person. The project focused on providing educational resources such as books, stationery, and learning materials to underprivileged children, thereby promoting equal access to education. Through this initiative, students actively participated in a meaningful social cause, reinforcing the importance of collective effort and educational empowerment.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/KnpnmBCwTAR-Fo6bbD_V2.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZnebW-Y3JZAxF9VD992M0","name":"Female Feoticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":10,"place":"Rajarajeshwari Nagara","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/vyoneIFahFSndbsqRS0fL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon successfully raised awareness about the harmful consequences of female foeticide and reinforced the values of gender equality and social justice among participants. It encouraged meaningful discussions, strengthened social consciousness, and motivated individuals to become advocates for the rights and dignity of the girl child, leaving a lasting impact on attitudes and awareness within the community.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was a social awareness initiative organized on 11th May 2025 with the objective of sensitizing students and the public to the importance of protecting the girl child and promoting gender equality. The walkathon brought together participants who walked in solidarity, carrying messages and slogans that highlighted the social, ethical, and legal issues surrounding female foeticide. Through active participation, the event aimed to spread awareness, challenge deep-rooted social biases, and encourage collective responsibility toward building a more inclusive society.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/wr7SqzZDW3YaB6bLev1qC.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"X0jt6To067dfhGRw47VRN","name":"Fist Full","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/ql7-OBpJme5LfD9SkZNl2.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-12-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully collected a substantial quantity of rice, which was distributed to families in need, helping address food insecurity. It raised awareness about hunger and basic necessities, fostered a spirit of sharing among participants, and reinforced the importance of community-driven efforts in supporting vulnerable sections of society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-15","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Fist Full was a social service initiative focused on supporting underprivileged families through food donation, wherein participants contributed 5 kg of rice per person. The initiative emphasized the idea of collective giving, encouraging students and volunteers to make small yet meaningful contributions that could create a significant impact when combined. Through organized collection and distribution, the drive promoted compassion, empathy, and a strong sense of social responsibility within the community.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/1da39e16-fd7b-483c-ab1a-4b3142a4216a/YL7KGexnlxqK4QyDnl-5u.jpeg","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Krishnappa H K","designation":"Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 20:18:47.967289+00', '2026-02-01 18:00:59.246593+00'), ('278cb022-1bbb-40d5-9a93-3e36ffc8313b', '5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD024","name":"K.M.S Siddharth","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"3Tyy8J7xYjMXZShEsvntG","name":"AKSHARA ","slNo":1,"place":"Vishwabharathi High Scool","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/FGQWFn04cky3bmDZbS_kn.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the initiative was a meaningful experience that refined my ability to\\ncommunicate effectively. By conducting a session for a class of students, I learned how to\\nadapt my presentation style to be more interactive and accessible, ensuring that concepts were\\neasily understood. Managing the classroom dynamics, even for a single session, taught me\\nthe importance of patience and engagement in the learning process. Furthermore, this direct\\ninteraction provided personal insight into the educational disparities faced by these students,\\nfostering a deeper sense of social responsibility and a genuine appreciation for the effort required\\nin the teaching profession.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE held skill development sessions in eight Bangalore schools,\\nbenefiting over 1000 underprivileged students. Targeting financially modest backgrounds,\\nthe sessions enhanced academic understanding and provided essential skills. Schools visited\\nincluded BET Convent, Sai Sri Vidya Chethana, Vishwa Bharathi High School, Kengeri High\\nSchool, Government Model Primary School, Nehru Memorial School, Priyadarshini Vidhya\\nKendra School, and Mount Carmel English School. The initiative used interactive methods\\nfor curriculum-based learning to ensure relevance and engagement. Volunteers gained valuable\\nexperience as teachers, fostering appreciation for the profession and addressing educational\\ndisparities. This initiative underscored the power of volunteerism and the need for quality\\neducation for all.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/VIbYQM8WBvMO0tpKt4Mnl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"njKo6PXpWlBt6PPIeQKK-","name":"DATA REMIX","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/18dtJPohrldTFLW4g-tsH.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Data Remix, I significantly enhanced my technical proficiency in data analysis and visualization by interpreting complex datasets under time constraints. The competition improved my ability to derive actionable insights and present technical findings to an expert panel. By working on solutions aligned with the UN’s Sustainable Development Goals, I developed a deeper understanding of how to integrate sustainable thinking into business innovation and technological progress. Additionally, working in a team environment strengthened my collaborative skills and my ability to think holistically about real-world challenges. Overall, the experience bridge the gap between academic learning and practical industry applications in the field of AI and Data Science","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The DHI DAY was a technical event organized by Team DHI, a student initiative from the to develop sustainable business solutions aligned with the UN’s Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The event aimed to promote a advancement with environmental and technological sustainability. Department of AIML at RVCE, in collaboration with GE Healthcare. The flagship event, \"Data Remix,\" was a two-phase competition focused on Data Analysis and Business Innovation. In the first phase, teams of up to four students used provided pre-processed datasets to create data visualizations and present inferences to a panel of judges. The second phase required students revolutionary mindset that balances technical","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/D0SZzFdJpWP-ta9JjWDpH.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eZhT-6DgHUz6tOphjJXDz","name":"FAST TREK","slNo":3,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/mcgpFXDehzaybAsWHkSjz.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through the Fast-Trek event, I gained firsthand experience in contributing to a meaningful social cause while actively engaging in a well-organized community event. The trek enhanced my awareness of social responsibility, encouraged teamwork and interaction with fellow participants, and provided a refreshing break that improved physical endurance and mental well-being. Being part of Fast-Trek also helped me appreciate the impact that collective effort can have in supporting underprivileged children with heart diseases, making the experience both personally enriching and socially rewarding.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was to provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the participants boarded the bus to the trek location with great enthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with basic information of the event. The trek was a great success as all the participants had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of Huthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very memorable journey. Breakfast and lunch was provided at the trek location for all the participants.","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/GRDILxka-MQlsATB0CIQf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OYJCVWIk7ME1K-DhS8FVO","name":"FAST TREK 2.0","slNo":4,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/MXaBf-nR_-Z60a5PizIPu.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense of environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by reporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped improve my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Kunagal Betta Hills, and it also enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group of participants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved my fitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated to preserving the environment. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus to the trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the adventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all attendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagal Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding success, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750 individuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s vibrant atmosphere.","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/VND5dyPJeDvDgMTqRFzm6.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6Uamrw4dQN49aQCUxPGLZ","name":"Paper Bag Extra","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/K48IVs7Q4OQaGyf288GtD.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed awareness about environmental sustainability and the importance of reducing plastic waste. Gained hands-on experience in contributing to a community-oriented, eco-friendly initiative. Strengthened a sense of social responsibility and environmental consciousness. Encouraged sustainable habits and community participation through collective effort. If","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-01-29","hoursSpent":5,"description":"NSS, RVCE organized a community development initiative focused on promoting environmental awareness and sustainable practices. As part of the activity, paper bags were made as an eco-friendly alternative to plastic bags. The initiative aimed to encourage responsible consumption, reduce plastic usage, and spread awareness about environmental conservation through simple, practical action.","aicteMapping":"12","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/ELWWbUaSBQyHHMkhp4x80.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6kHa2Kc4EHZ7Z51xfKuH8","name":"SDG PHOTOGRAPHY 2023","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/ypE1MEayzsuMLMVr2BkYe.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"I enhanced my creativity and photography skills by capturing meaningful visuals that represent real-world issues aligned with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The competition helped me develop stronger observation and storytelling ability, as I learned to express social and environmental messages through impactful photographs. It also increased my awareness of SDG-related challenges and encouraged me to think critically about how youth can contribute to positive change. Overall, the activity gave me confidence in presenting my perspective creatively, improved my visual communication skills, and motivated me to engage more actively in socially responsible initiatives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Organized by the IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter,it is an SDG-themed photography competition titled “Through the Eyes of Youth!” designed to encourage students to creatively capture and present real-world perspectives through photography. The competition provides a platform for youth to express their interpretation of the world, focusing on themes aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Open to all RVCE students and students from other IUCEE Student Chapters, the event promotes creativity, awareness, and storytelling through visual media. Participants are invited to submit impactful photographs that reflect social, environmental, or developmental issues, thereby using art as a tool for communication and change. The competition also includes an exciting prize pool of ¹ 3500, motivating students to actively participate, showcase talent, and contribute towards SDG awareness through their unique lens.","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/IvREt_uJzfTh2PgT48TbZ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dEN3s8mrzIXbkl90Kf8iR","name":"PROJECT PUSTAK","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/8CGkgdSWoS--vgT44JQar.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in Project Pustak, I gained a strong sense of social responsibility and satisfaction from contributing towards the education of underprivileged rural students. I understood the real impact that even small contributions can create when combined for a meaningful cause. This activity helped me develop empathy and awareness about the difficulties faced by students who lack basic school resources. I also gained exposure to community service initiatives and learned the importance of teamwork and collective effort in successfully carrying out a donation-based project. Overall, the experience was rewarding as it allowed me to support a noble cause and contribute directly to creating a better learning environment for deserving students.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students living in rural areas. Under this project, a contribution was collected from each donor, and the funds raised were used to procure and donate much-needed educational materials. The collected amount was utilized to purchase resources such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other important school supplies that help create a better and more supportive learning environment for deserving students. The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, undertook the responsibility of procuring and distributing these essential supplies to ensure meaningful educational support for the beneficiaries.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/IaKK1YP9z6mYgNlrClh48.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nUxbv6oy4VBveGHJMxikR","name":"SDG PHOTOGRAPHY 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/ib_4lF3_FEfkq3rqH8vf1.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"I enhanced my creativity and photography skills by capturing meaningful visuals that represent real-world issues aligned with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The competition helped me develop stronger observation and storytelling ability, as I learned to express social and environmental messages through impactful photographs. It also increased my awareness of SDG-related challenges and encouraged me to think critically about how youth can contribute to positive change. Overall, the activity gave me confidence in presenting my perspective creatively, improved my visual communication skills, and motivated me to engage more actively in socially responsible initiatives","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Organized by the IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter,it is an SDG-themed photography competition titled “Through the Eyes of Youth!” designed to encourage students to creatively capture and present real-world perspectives through photography. The competition provides a platform for youth to express their interpretation of the world, focusing on themes aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Open to all RVCE students and students from other IUCEE Student Chapters, the event promotes creativity, awareness, and storytelling through visual media. Participants are invited to submit impactful photographs that reflect social, environmental, or developmental issues, thereby using art as a tool for communication and change. The competition also includes an exciting prize pool of ¹ 3500, motivating students to actively participate, showcase talent, and contribute towards SDG awareness through their unique lens","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/ZO4SFZzbFY6lGCar2eCn3.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"U8u7fvGQ7K5-sETmE5-eH","name":"UTSARGA 2024 ","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/N5pvWRW-Pjq2KRYZIh0qL.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based registration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create awareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness activity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community impact.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/BsVAyoOdQjYb--D3RphLN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Q4yGC0Mi0wmmfyjl81shl","name":"UTSARGA 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/Fy5Ya9RNkEHgqn5kZ8s4C.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need. Overall, this activity contributed both to my NSS activity progress and my personal development.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on April 6th, 2025, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based registration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create awareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness activity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community impact.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/CAJyoFf_eFx-tCE3DR9lv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yZqY233uh_WZycis8OLzw","name":"ACM India Summit 2024","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/bUKGtE7mULgRmK9CCKP1w.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/Xu-Q-JjOF-Wxx1WbSCOh3.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the ACM India Summit 2024 provided me with valuable exposure to national-level academic and professional discourse in computer science and related fields. The event enhanced my understanding of current research directions, industry practices, and technological advancements through expert sessions and discussions. It also helped me build professional connections, encouraged collaborative thinking, and strengthened my appreciation for the role of academic and technical communities such as ACM in advancing knowledge and innovation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-09","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The ACM India Summit 2024 was a national-level academic and technical event hosted at RV College of Engineering in collaboration with the ACM India Council. Conducted over two days, the summit brought together students, faculty members, researchers, and industry professionals from across the country. The event featured expert talks, panel discussions, and knowledge-sharing sessions focused on emerging trends in computing, research, and technology. It served as a platform for meaningful interaction, learning, and exposure to advancements shaping the future of the computing domain.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/E6OUjo0KkCRTVrYvFF6un.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jPkJwybvwqviN2ZUDN-eH","name":"ACM GEN AI HACKATHON","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/-IkVKHYA8HcD9CoaESSTE.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"As a volunteer for the GenAI Hackathon (powered by EDOCK) held on 29th November 2024 at RVCE, I gained valuable experience in event coordination and student management by supporting the smooth execution of the hackathon. I developed strong communication and teamwork skills by interacting with participants, guiding them when required, and coordinating with the organizing team to ensure timely flow of activities. This volunteering opportunity also improved my leadership, responsibility, and problem-solving abilities, especially while handling on-spot requirements during the event. Additionally, being part of a technology-focused hackathon enhanced my exposure to Generative AI innovations and strengthened my understanding of how collaborative events encourage creativity, innovation, and real-world solution building. Overall, the experience helped me grow professionally by building organizational skills and giving me practical experience in managing a large student-driven technical event.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The GenAI Hackathon, powered by EDOCK, was successfully organized at RV College of Engineering on 29th November 2024 at the DTL Huddle. The event served as a dynamic platform for students to explore and apply advanced concepts in Generative Artificial Intelligence, focusing on innovative solutions that enable machines to generate content, simulate human-like interactions, and address complex real-world challenges. The hackathon witnessed enthusiastic participation from students who showcased their creativity and technical expertise by developing innovative prototypes within a limited timeframe. Overall, the event encouraged collaborative learning, problem-solving, teamwork, and innovation, creating an enriching experience that promoted emerging AI technologies and their transformative impact across industries","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5eee8389-9653-4aa2-9f51-9d0ad3dae38f/IpUlXhzRO-fPiNrV_vrLG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 08:56:56.462126+00', '2026-02-01 14:03:40.684762+00'), ('27a48f44-5666-47a5-9f38-84fdabeacf85', 'da1e5518-29a6-40a2-8d66-8a796d3bde68', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23IS105","name":"Samkit Samsukha","period":"2023-2027","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"QwMBKbGMJpDQ5GUti4Yo_","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":1,"place":"BT Quadrangle","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-12-01","duration":2,"outcomes":"","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-11-30","hoursSpent":8,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Design Thinking Abilities","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"32BBrAptlAlw0t-1Gv9V8","name":"Under The Peepal Tree","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-PQRltWd-qzHR457gjIn6","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":3,"place":"BT Quadrangle RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/da1e5518-29a6-40a2-8d66-8a796d3bde68/Ih12NWT82pyAEHJ3Tr3Y_.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Donated a unit of blood, potentially helping save multiple lives.\\n\\nContributed to strengthening blood bank reserves for emergency medical needs.\\n\\nSupported the Rotaract Club of RVCE in its mission of community service and social responsibility.\\n\\nHelped raise awareness about safe and voluntary blood donation among students and the community.\\n\\nReinforced values of empathy, civic responsibility, and humanitarian service.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"On 28th June 2024, I voluntarily donated blood during a Blood Donation Drive organized by the Rotaract Club of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE). The initiative was conducted with the aim of supporting hospitals and patients in need of timely and lifesaving blood transfusions, while also spreading awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.\\n\\nBlood donation is a vital humanitarian activity that plays a significant role in strengthening the healthcare system, particularly during medical emergencies, surgeries, and for patients with critical health conditions. By participating in this drive, I contributed to a meaningful social cause and supported the Rotaract Club’s efforts in promoting service above self and community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Blood Donation Camp","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/da1e5518-29a6-40a2-8d66-8a796d3bde68/ZwxEOhRLyZpkE6D4PU7VS.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dfiValSd-Qs_d7AUTK4lj","name":"Walkathon - Alzheimers Day","slNo":4,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0IOomipuPbM6vELsAVRj5","name":"8th CSITSS","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"","hours