,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4bG9pwrPRFMwTtpy4b0Vh","name":"Fast Trek 4.0","slNo":24,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Prof. Rashmi R","designation":"Assistant Professor, Dept of ISE"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 04:39:17.111463+00', '2026-02-01 05:05:59.287243+00'), ('27c5afee-db2c-4e45-b835-c6026397d97e', 'e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV065","name":"Nagesh Kadappa Betageri","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"bUL2TVfJX9FFvE97J8z-E","name":"Adamya Chetana Plantation Drive","slNo":1,"place":"Jnanabharathi ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Environmental Impact: Contribution to increased green cover and improved local ecology through tree plantation and care.\\nSustainability Awareness: Enhanced understanding of environmental responsibility and sustainable practices.\\nCommunity Engagement: Active involvement in a large-scale, community-driven environmental movement.\\nSocial Responsibility: Demonstrated commitment to ecological conservation and civic duty.\\nRecognition: Formal acknowledgment for participating in a nationally recognized, consistent green initiative.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The program marks a major milestone—372 consecutive Green Sundays—highlighting consistent community engagement in environmental conservation. The participant, Nagesh K B\\nfrom R V College of Engineering, actively contributed to this eco-friendly initiative, supporting Adyamya Chetana’s mission of promoting sustainability, biodiversity, and environmental\\nawareness.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/01-5OV25D1dPFNvjV4q7O.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3 - 4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LOJNkLLzXeygXdfR6ftnG","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye ","slNo":2,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye initiative has a profound impact by empowering first-time voters with the knowledge and confidence to participate in the electoral process. It fosters a sense of civic responsibility and awareness, encouraging informed decisionmaking. The campaign enhances youth engagement in democracy, leading to a more inclusive and representative electoral process. By inspiring active participation, it lays the foundation for a lifelong commitment to voting and strengthens the democratic fabric of the nation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-13","hoursSpent":16,"description":"The Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye initiative is a powerful campaign aimed at empowering first-time voters to actively engage in the democratic process. Recognizing that young voters form a significant portion of the electorate; the initiative seeks to educate them about the value of their vote and its impact on shaping the nation’s future. The core objective of the event was to instill a sense of responsibility and national pride among students who are eligible to vote for the first time. The theme, Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye, emphasized the power of a single vote and how young citizens can contribute to the country’s progress by exercising their electoral rights\\nresponsibly. The campaign emphasizes the critical role of voting as a fundamental right and a civic duty, inspiring young citizens to make informed decisions at the ballot box. It includes\\ninteractive workshops, informational sessions, and creative outreach strategies to demystify the voting process, address common misconceptions, and highlight the significance of every\\nindividual vote in driving national progress. “Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” was more than just a campaign; it was a call to action. The event successfully instilled a sense of civic duty\\namong the youth, reminding them that active participation in democracy begins with a single step: casting your first vote.\\nThrough educational, creative, and motivational activities, the event made a meaningful impact, empowering students to become informed, responsible, and proud voters of India.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/23Pk7f-I2G7tamwW534mg.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1 - 2 ","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"U3BzTXxxHxAdZr4TtlxhS","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"24","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/cCDmcprlQ64rxHd4tQT2B.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility\\nand gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":80,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my\\nphysical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote\\nsocial responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating anpositive change in society. Thiscause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causesin the future.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5 - 6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HGAs_RBED7aLc7I9nZefd","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"25 ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/OOEN7HlACxT2fDp0uP9ct.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility\\nand gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":144,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my\\nphysical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote\\nsocial responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating anpositive change in society. This cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5 km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causes in the future.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":36,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/intxsouPo3DFVtciwK77w.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7 - 8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"O--S-fCMLblYywwud6pLU","name":"Kannada Sanga","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/SHHpCfVicd69f6fd3vCD9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"Efficient Coordination: Successfully collected and managed Kannada Sangha T-shirts for participants.\\n\\nOrganizational Skills: Improved planning, record-keeping, and distribution management skills.\\n\\nTeamwork & Communication: Enhanced interaction with students and Kannada Sangha coordinators.\\n\\nCultural Promotion: Contributed to strengthening Kannada identity and visibility during events.\\n\\nResponsibility & Leadership: Demonstrated accountability in handling collective resources.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-07-02","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The activity involved collecting and organizing Kannada Sangha T-shirts for members and participants of Kannada Sangha events. This task required coordination with students, maintaining records of requests, ensuring correct sizes and quantities, and distributing the T-shirts efficiently. The activity supported the smooth conduct of Kannada Sangha programs\\nand helped promote unity, cultural identity, and active participation among members.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/WCfSVvGGBEEDKCWWtT9p_.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9 - 10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3MbStWHB7Io2Y32awPIWC","name":"Fist Full","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/HiBWnrEBlQGUWY0PMyfEO.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the donation drive held at the RVCE campus was the successful collection of essential food items to support underprivileged communities. The initiative helped address\\nbasic nutritional needs and contributed to food assistance efforts. It fostered a sense of social responsibility and empathy among students while encouraging active participation in\\ncommunity service. The activity also strengthened awareness about the importance of collective effort, demonstrating how small contributions can create a meaningful and positive impact on society.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-13","hoursSpent":40,"description":"A contribution of 2 kg of toor dal was made during the donation drive held at the RVCE campus. The initiative was organized with the objective of supporting food assistance programs. It aimed\\nto extend help to underprivileged communities through essential supplies. The drive encouraged student participation in social welfare activities. It highlighted the importance of collective\\nresponsibility toward society. Food grains collected were intended for meaningful community support. Such initiatives help address basic nutritional needs. They also promote empathy and humanitarian values. The campus environment fostered a spirit of service unity. Students were motivated to contribute in practical ways. The activity emphasized giving back to society. It reflected the role of educational institutions in social development. Small contributions together create a larger impact. The drive served as a reminder of social accountability. Overall, the initiative strengthened awareness about community welfare.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/8MIaDJ-CDfB_PMJpCyLe1.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11 - 12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IDKjuv_K5wVnLhhl1ejhQ","name":"8th Mile Discom","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/ZNPSTyvJNMPpJM7Pmy0T7.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"Gained hands-on experience in event management\\nDeveloped leadership and teamwork skills\\nImproved communication and coordination abilities\\nLearned time management and problem-solving under pressure\\nEnhanced confidence in handling responsibilities\\nUnderstood the importance of discipline and teamwork in large-scale events\\nBuilt strong connections with peers and organizing members","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":60,"description":"8th Mile is a flagship cultural and technical fest organized by our college with the objective of promoting creativity, teamwork, leadership, and student engagement. The event brought\\ntogether students from various departments to participate in a wide range of cultural, technical, and fun-filled activities. It served as a platform for students to showcase their talents, enhance interpersonal skills, and experience large-scale event management. The fest witnessed enthusiastic participation, vibrant performances, competitive events, and smooth coordination among organizing teams. It played a significant role in fostering unity, innovation, and a festive spirit across the campus.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e33025af-61d2-4d9c-ba6a-f482d13c32a3/u1p2MBnfr9ku4uZuONUgH.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13 - 14","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Prof. Shashi Kiran C. R","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 18:07:22.66025+00', '2026-01-29 20:05:10.582425+00'), ('29d10ac9-91fe-4c01-8b5c-91c318416854', 'c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC171","name":"Thilak S","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"yGtVW9ig8gP7SM0E3vjuh","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Drive successfully contributed a significant number of blood units to the Rashtrotthana Blood Centre, directly supporting lifesaving medical treatments for numerous patients. The initiative fostered a deep sense of social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among the participants. It strengthened the institutional linkage with healthcare organizations and underscored the college''s commitment to societal well-being, creating a lasting positive impact on community health.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Rashtrotthana Voluntary Blood Donation Drive was a critical community health initiative organized in collaboration with the Rashtrotthana Blood Centre, a government-recognized institution. The primary objective was to augment the regional blood bank''s repository to meet the urgent demands arising from medical emergencies and routine procedures. This flagship humanitarian endeavor encouraged eligible students and staff to participate in the noble act of blood donation, emphasizing the profound impact of a single donation on saving countless lives. Participants, including donor Thilak S (Blood Group A+), underwent rigorous preliminary screening to ensure donor safety and blood quality. The event was conducted under strict medical supervision, aligning with national health guidelines. It served as a powerful platform to raise awareness about the constant need for safe blood and to inculcate a spirit of selfless service and civic responsibility among the student body. The collected units were systematically processed and stored by the Rashtrotthana Blood Centre for equitable distribution to patients in need, thereby strengthening the healthcare infrastructure of the community.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/0wDd1KH4YDURB_yRhxNg7.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XY5viN9eWwa70qhCx7MJt","name":"BGS Global Hospitals Voluntary Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The drive successfully augmented the blood inventory of BGS Global Hospitals, directly aiding their attempt to save precious lives. It fostered a sense of civic duty and altruism within the student body, validating the institution''s commitment to social welfare. The event successfully bridged the gap between academic institutions and healthcare providers, ensuring that vital resources are available for patients in critical need.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"This Voluntary Blood Donation Camp was organized at R.V. College of Engineering in strict coordination with the Department of Transfusion Medicine, BGS Global Hospitals (Super Specialty Quaternary Care). The initiative was conceived to address the perennial demand for quality blood components essential for trauma care, surgeries, and chronic treatments. Acknowledging that \"blood of the desired quality can only be provided by voluntary donors,\" the drive mobilized the student community to participate in this life-saving mission. Donor Thilak S (Blood Group A+, Donor ID: 0383/23) stepped forward to contribute, embodying the spirit of the event''s motto: \"Give the gift that costs nothing to give\". The collection process was managed by the BGS medical team under rigorous aseptic conditions to ensure donor safety and sample integrity. This camp served not only as a logistical exercise in blood collection but also as a moral imperative to instill a habit of regular voluntary donation among the youth, thereby fortifying the region''s medical emergency response capabilities.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/ryZIJ4XCzv5yQUvmoSLHb.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IfjWsIU3UK1v-uk0h5WOq","name":"Fist full","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/WdpoCzPACuEDDG6ZEB8iK.jpeg"],"endDate":"0025-10-27","duration":-730484,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event enabled effective collection and distribution of food grains to support\\nvulnerable communities. It promoted social responsibility, empathy, and active student\\nparticipation. The initiative strengthened collaboration between the institution and community\\nservice organizations while creating a lasting social impact","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-27","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Fist Full event was a flagship community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club\\nof RVCE under Rotary Bangalore South, with the objective of combating food insecurity and\\nsupporting vulnerable communities. Conducted from 17th to 22nd November 2025, the event\\nencouraged collective social responsibility by involving students in contributing essential food\\ngrains. Each participating student donated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, transforming small\\nindividual contributions into a large-scale humanitarian effort. The initiative was aligned with\\nRotary’s Community Service avenue, specifically focusing on the theme of Fighting Disease\\nthrough nutritional support. A total of 2146 students actively participated, demonstrating\\nstrong student engagement and awareness toward social causes. The collected food grains\\nwere systematically sorted, recorded, and prepared for distribution to ensure transparency and\\neffective utilization","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-B4tG_z9jmhqUBAU7gdZI","name":"8th Mile – Production Design & Stage Management","slNo":4,"place":"campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/ZE8BDpW-GR_zfV8xxBu9t.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-12","duration":3,"outcomes":"The production design was lauded for its grandeur and technical precision, significantly enhancing the visual appeal of the fest. The seamless execution of the stage setup provided a world-class platform for performers and was a key factor in the event''s massive footfall. The initiative honed the student''s skills in project management, spatial design, and collaborative problem-solving under pressure.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-10","hoursSpent":35,"description":"8th Mile, the annual techno-cultural extravaganza of RVCE, is a confluence of art, technology, and culture. For the 2024 edition, the Production Design team was tasked with conceptualizing and executing the visual identity of the main stage and peripheral events. As a core member of the production design crew, Thilak S played a pivotal role in the \"Aesthetic Visualization and Structural Fabrication\" sector. The work involved translating the fest''s theme into tangible stage elements using sustainable materials and innovative joinery techniques. Responsibilities included drafting 3D layout plans for the main arena, overseeing the carpentry and metalworks teams, and ensuring the structural integrity of the backdrop props. The design philosophy integrated dynamic LED mapping with static art installations to create an immersive experience for the audience. The team worked tirelessly over 72 hours to erect a 40-foot main stage structure that withstood high wind loads and supported heavy audio-visual equipment. This role required acute attention to detail, crisis management during live setups, and seamless coordination with the logistics and technical committees to ensure a glitch-free visual spectacle.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0QeNnnUidHoEMLUk7UovA","name":"Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-04-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully fostered awareness about physical fitness and social\\nresponsibility among participants.\\nIt contributed directly to supporting educational opportunities for children in need through\\ncollective donations.\\nThe event strengthened community bonding by uniting students, faculty, and the public under\\na shared cause of compassion and change.","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-04-02","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon, a spirited initiative that brings together fitness, compassion, and social\\nresponsibility. Scheduled for February 4th, 2024, at R V College of Engineering, this marathon is\\nmore than just a run—it is a collective movement towards meaningful change. With the inspiring\\ntheme “Help a Child Change the World”, the event aims to promote health and well-being while\\ncontributing towards the education of underprivileged children. Participants can choose between\\n5 km and 10 km runs, making it accessible to all age groups and fitness levels. By taking part,\\nevery runner becomes a catalyst for hope, proving that small steps taken together can create a\\nlasting impact on society","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/PwbrU45bFvYsRcMoZB0Cy.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QDGHm1YSJRcrVMf379Xta","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2023","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully mobilized substantial resources for child development initiatives, directly impacting the lives of beneficiaries. For the participant, it served as a rigorous exercise in discipline and perseverance, reinforcing the vital link between physical well-being and social activism. The event fostered a spirit of unity among the student fraternity and highlighted the institution''s dedication to holistic nation-building.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2023 was the flagship philanthropic sporting event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of RVCE, anchored by the profound motto \"Help a Child, Change the World\". This marathon was not merely a test of physical endurance but a synchronized movement of solidarity aimed at uplifting underprivileged children. Thilak S (10 KM Category) was among the dedicated participants who braved the course, transforming every step into a stride for social justice. The event, held under the aegis of the G20 India presidency and Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav, galvanized the youth to champion the cause of child welfare. The logistical framework involved meticulous route planning, hydration management, and crowd control, all executed to professional standards. By participating in the grueling 10 KM category, the student demonstrated exceptional physical resilience and an unwavering commitment to the ethos of \"Not Me, But You,\" thereby amplifying the message of community service through personal example.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/xO1AzvHZob_Iy5bx8rRKe.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IM9ok-Y6iiseEHwPE2lsx","name":"Indian Red Cross Society Voluntary Blood Donation Drive","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The drive significantly bolstered the blood bank inventory of the Indian Red Cross Society, ensuring the availability of life-saving blood for patients in need. It successfully promoted the culture of voluntary donation among the youth and reinforced the importance of community health support systems. The participant''s contribution was formally recognized, serving as an inspiration for peers to engage in similar humanitarian activities.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":2,"description":"This voluntary blood donation drive was organized in association with the Indian Red Cross Society, Karnataka State Branch, an organization renowned for its humanitarian motto \"Through Humanity to Peace\". The event was designed to address the critical shortage of blood components required for emergency medical interventions and surgeries. Thilak S participated in this noble cause, donating blood (Group B Pos) on 30th October 2025, thereby directly contributing to the state''s healthcare reserves. The certificate of appreciation acknowledges this selfless gesture as instrumental in \"saving precious lives\". The drive was conducted with high standards of medical safety and hygiene, ensuring the well-being of all donors. By stepping forward to donate, the participant demonstrated a profound commitment to societal welfare and exemplified the core values of compassion and civic duty advocated by the Red Cross.","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/mapGv6JFHMdPif6da0QKY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zjwlT1ILE9iS4wZC9J3MB","name":"\"T-Shirt for Smiles\" – Kannada Sangha Community Initiative","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The \"T-Shirt for Smiles\" initiative successfully generated vital funds and resources for the Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust, directly improving the quality of life for the resident children. It fostered a spirit of generosity and cultural responsibility within the college, reinforcing the ethos that student activism can be a powerful force for social good.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Organized by the Kannada Sangha of RVCE, the \"T-Shirt for Smiles\" campaign was a heartfelt community service initiative designed to support the Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram in Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru. The event''s primary mission was to extend financial and emotional support to underprivileged children, aiming to \"bring joy\" to their lives through structured activities and donations. Thilak S (1RV22EC171) actively participated in this philanthropic drive, contributing to the fundraising efforts that provided essential resources to the orphanage. The initiative was not merely a donation drive but a collective expression of empathy, where the student body united to address the needs of vulnerable sections of society. By supporting this cause, the participant demonstrated a commendable commitment to social welfare, helping to transform a simple contribution into a significant impact for the children at the Anathashram.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/rJxZOQeTd2SKia1E0GN6n.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zdzSK-VX6T59pap4gLEVS","name":"Energy Swaraj Foundation – Energy Literacy Training","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed a strong conceptual foundation in sustainable energy systems and environmental responsibility. Acquired the ability to evaluate energy usage patterns and propose efficiency improvements. Built awareness to support informed decision-making toward clean and renewable energy adoption.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Completed a structured Energy Literacy Training covering energy generation, consumption, and wastage. The course provided an in-depth analysis of carbon footprints and the environmental impact of conventional energy sources. Thilak S successfully completed the 12-module curriculum, learning strategies to minimize energy usage and adopt sustainable consumption practices. The training offered insights into alternative and renewable energy solutions, specifically focusing on solar energy adoption and dispelling common misconceptions about its viability. It emphasized pathways to achieve carbon neutrality, equipping the participant with the knowledge to contribute effectively to climate change mitigation.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/7QVSwF9AIqOrFz5aiz3Ej.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EVYEMcITvd0dJvGDvcg0U","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The dedication of the participants was instrumental in empowering underprivileged students, directly contributing to their educational continuity. The initiative strengthened the link between the institution and grassroots community welfare, helping the participant develop a deeper awareness of social challenges and the impact of collective philanthropy.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. Organized by the Pranav Foundation in collaboration with the Rotaract Club of RVCE, the event mobilized students to bridge the educational resource gap. Thilak S (1RV22EC171) actively participated in this drive, making a generous donation that helped sponsor a stationery kit for a student in a Government School. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase textbooks, backpacks, and other vital resources to create a conducive learning environment. This initiative was not just about material aid but about empowering rural students and fostering a sense of global solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/OqcdzWB1PcWDiVQANP7W9.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CFQHNN54YxmFnGFh9hrLb","name":"Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2025 – India Quiz","slNo":11,"place":"campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"Strengthened general awareness, reasoning, and analytical skills through high-pressure quizzing rounds. Gained exposure to a national-level competitive academic environment and interacted with a diverse pool of talent. The participation underscored the value of extracurricular academic engagement.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participated in the \"India Quiz\" at Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2025, a national-level quiz fest organized to test knowledge on diverse domains including Indian culture, history, and current affairs. The event fostered a competitive spirit and encouraged critical thinking, requiring participants to engage in rapid problem-solving and knowledge application under time constraints. Thilak S competed against peers from various institutions, demonstrating analytical ability and a strong grasp of the country''s heritage and modern developments. The fest provided a platform for intellectual exchange and interdisciplinary learning, reinforcing the importance of general awareness in holistic student development.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c42a274c-a204-48d0-9ce6-8b3eeeeab5bd/RWG1hYcRbJOdPquQtTNKo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"S Praveen","designation":"assistant professor, ECE dept"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr. Ravish Aradhya ","designation":"HOD, ECE dept"},"evaluator2":{"name":"Dr K M Ajay","designation":"associate professor, civil dept"}}}', '2026-01-29 20:38:20.516153+00', '2026-01-30 07:14:35.239712+00'), ('29e6bf2c-93c1-46ba-94aa-2dc03897c6b0', '2705c2ff-72be-4209-a6dd-978af15996b6', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"DEEPAKKUMAR M N","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"MaHBEnbTQyEaGlmkfaT6Q","name":"KANNADA SANGHA","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2705c2ff-72be-4209-a6dd-978af15996b6/X1IZy2p3MAeJlO80gObMp.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-12-10","duration":21,"outcomes":"NOTHING","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-20","hoursSpent":80,"description":"PD HEADS\\t\\t\\nNikhita Jakkappa Biradar \\t1RV22CV068\\t60\\nSadiq S Muddapur\\t1RV22CV091\\t60\\nRahul\\t1RV22CV081\\t60\\nYuvaraj K T\\t1RV22EE065 \\t60\\nTarun H S\\t1RV22EE057\\t60\\nDeepakkumar M N \\t1RV22AS013\\t60\\nKarthik Devadiga\\t1RV22CY032\\t60","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2705c2ff-72be-4209-a6dd-978af15996b6/OGZoZ6rtKeUu1I45_FAod.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 13:48:50.516402+00', '2026-01-29 13:52:00.379396+00'), ('2a998ae5-eb9e-4a78-ad8e-071c270ff3c1', '5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC029","name":"Avani Ramesh","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"sbgrdBe0opvllOWfdS98b","name":"TEDxRVCE : Resonating Chords","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/x_QXM_NmcpNRBjKL7iBMB.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event enriched students’ perspectives by exposing them to interdisciplinary ideas, real-life success stories, and societal challenges. It fostered inspiration, self-reflection, and motivation to pursue passion-driven and socially responsible career paths. Students gained insights into leadership, creativity, mental well-being, governance, entrepreneurship, and the importance of perseverance and innovation. The activity enhanced communication skills, critical thinking, and cultural awareness while encouraging personal growth and lifelong learning. Overall, TEDxRVCE 2023 contributed significantly to the holistic development of students and aligned with AICTE’s objectives of experiential learning and personality development.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-08","hoursSpent":6,"description":"TEDxRVCE 2023, themed Resonating Chords, was a full-day intellectual and cultural event organized on June 8, 2023, at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The event featured an eminent lineup of speakers from diverse domains, each sharing unique life experiences, professional journeys, and ideas aimed at inspiring students and fostering holistic development.\\nThe event commenced with an inspiring talk by Mr. Rishi Raghavan, who shared his journey in local governance and community leadership, emphasizing the role of youth participation, grassroots initiatives, and responsible leadership in driving societal transformation. His talk highlighted how dedication and vision can bring meaningful change even without a traditional political background.Ms. Andaleeb Wajid, a renowned author and self-published writer, spoke about her journey from being a novice writer to a successful author with over forty published books. She provided insights into self-publishing, perseverance, and balancing personal responsibilities with professional aspirations, motivating students to pursue creative passions despite challenges.\\nMr. Nishit Sharma, a travel filmmaker, self-taught cinematographer, and content creator, shared his experiences of choosing passion over conventional career paths. Through his journey as an IIT graduate who embraced storytelling through cinematography, he emphasized authenticity, creativity, and the transformative power of visual media in shaping narratives and careers. The artistic dimension of the event was further enriched by Vidwan Sujay Shanbhag, who narrated his life journey in the field of art and music. He spoke about the challenges and rewards of pursuing art as a profession, highlighting the dedication, discipline, and perseverance required to achieve self-sustainability through creative pursuits. The event concluded with an enlightening session by Shri D. P. Nagendra Kumar, a former government officer and key contributor to the implementation of the Goods and Services Tax (GST) in India. His talk provided students with valuable insights into public policy, economic reforms, and the importance of governance, helping them understand the rationale and impact of GST on the Indian economy.","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/h9iXQ21U5VLCqqNSxQUva.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1RljzHKOLOoKZLk1jGXJ2","name":"Paper Drive - 2023","slNo":2,"place":"Attiguppe and Vijayanagar residential ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/hvOv1wCtN4IMbYQAS_gnk.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/tpYGZ4K0H3pLknC5Dw4m7.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in this community service initiative, I gained firsthand experience in teamwork, social responsibility, and large-scale event coordination. The activity made me aware of how sustainable practices like recycling can be effectively used to support social welfare causes. I developed a stronger sense of empathy toward underprivileged communities and understood the importance of collective action in bringing about meaningful change. This experience motivated me to actively engage in future community development activities and contribute responsibly to society.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The event witnessed overwhelming participation from over 500 student volunteers who came together to contribute towards economic and community development. The volunteers assembled at Kriyakalpa, RVCE at 8:00 AM and were transported by buses to various localities across Bengaluru. Over a duration of approximately nine hours, the volunteers collected more than 7 tonnes of newspapers, books, magazines, and other waste paper materials. The collected items were sold to paper vendors, and the funds generated through this initiative were donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation to support the welfare of orphaned and underprivileged individuals. The event not only promoted recycling and environmental responsibility but also demonstrated the power of collective effort in driving social impact.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/Tig8YefU9b4Ah_WRrck8u.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fBFW1mDVE0aREPsGFbZqy","name":"One Student One Plant","slNo":3,"place":"Residence","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/PwTeOT6iF56KRWw3sb_Gd.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the One Student One Plant initiative, I became more aware of the importance of plants in sustaining life and maintaining ecological balance. The activity encouraged me to reflect on my personal responsibility toward environmental conservation and sustainable living. By documenting and understanding the significance of the plant I chose, I developed a deeper connection with nature and a sense of accountability in nurturing it. This experience motivated me to adopt environmentally responsible practices and actively contribute to initiatives that promote sustainability.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":"One Student One Plant was an environmental awareness and sustainability initiative organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, conducted from 11th July 2023 to 14th July 2023. The activity aimed to promote environmental responsibility and ecological awareness among students by encouraging individual participation in plantation and reflection. As part of the initiative, each student was required to plant or adopt a plant and submit a photograph along with a brief description of the plant, including its significance, benefits, and the role it plays in supporting the environment and human life. The activity emphasized the importance of greenery, conservation of natural resources, and the responsibility of individuals in protecting the environment.","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability and Climate Action","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/XSeQ_EkecNA7vE0_IEV-H.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LgMw0ZDwKRQu4-SGOawWM","name":"Project Pustak -2023","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/I3LeJrREi9hwL9ic1J6mx.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-22","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative positively impacted underprivileged students by providing them with essential educational materials, thereby supporting their academic continuity and motivation to learn. It fostered a sense of social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among student volunteers. The activity also enhanced awareness about educational inequality and the importance of collective efforts in promoting inclusive and equitable education.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-22","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a social outreach initiative aimed at supporting the education of underprivileged students in rural areas by providing them with essential school supplies and learning resources. Project Pustak is a meaningful and humanitarian initiative focused on bridging the educational resource gap faced by underprivileged students residing in rural communities. As part of this initiative, a contribution of Rs. 100 was collected from each willing donor, forming the basis for procuring essential educational materials. The collected funds were judiciously utilized to purchase and distribute items such as textbooks, notebooks, stationery kits, school bags, and other basic academic necessities. By ensuring access to these fundamental resources, the initiative aimed to create a supportive and conducive learning environment for students, thereby encouraging continued education and reducing barriers to learning. The project reflects a strong commitment to social responsibility and inclusive education.","aicteMapping":"Social Outreach","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/hEsdGaerOetPXSzaV3De1.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jPw5XjB7FjyHIj6MuMVol","name":"Through the Eyes of YOUth","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/gLqN1a37pgDoh1m0jZEPw.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The SDG Photography Event, \"Through the Eyes of YOUth\", enhanced students’ awareness of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals by encouraging them to creatively interpret real-world sustainability challenges through photography and storytelling. The activity promoted critical thinking, observation, and digital media literacy while fostering a strong sense of social responsibility and environmental consciousness. It also provided an interdisciplinary platform for students to express ideas, engage collaboratively, and develop leadership and evaluation skills through peer involvement. Overall, the event contributed to campus-wide sustainability sensitization and aligned with AICTE and institutional objectives for holistic and experiential learning.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The SDG Photography Event, Through the Eyes of YOUth was held at RV College of Engineering. The event received an overwhelming response, with participation from more than 550 students who expressed their creative interpretations of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\\nParticipants contributed meaningful photographs accompanied by narratives that promoted awareness of sustainable development. All submissions were reviewed through a structured two-stage evaluation process. In the first stage, 98 exceptional entries were shortlisted by the Activities and Events Prefects under the supervision of the Social Media Prefects. The shortlisted submissions were then assessed by designated Committee Officers in the final round to identify the most noteworthy contributions.\\n","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability and Climate Action","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/wBbzOmhCDqXgny_8XXhIN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iRdFUsDqH9pD2cttX5EOW","name":"Energy Literacy Training Program by Energy Swaraj Foundation","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/2eozDV4RcFx5BR4qF89fv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":11,"outcomes":"The completion of the Energy Swaraj Foundation course enhanced students’ awareness and understanding of climate change, sustainable energy practices, and individual responsibility in environmental conservation. Students developed energy literacy and gained practical insights into reducing carbon footprints through the Avoid–Minimize–Generate approach. The activity fostered a sense of social and environmental responsibility, encouraging students to adopt sustainable lifestyles and advocate for renewable energy solutions. It also strengthened their understanding of global sustainability challenges, policy-level interventions, and community-driven climate action, thereby contributing to their holistic development as responsible engineers and citizens.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-21","hoursSpent":24,"description":"As part of sustainability and climate awareness initiatives, students successfully completed an online certification course offered by the Energy Swaraj Foundation (ESF), a not-for-profit organization dedicated to climate correction and aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The course was founded on the principles articulated by Prof. Chetan Singh Solanki, emphasizing the concept of Energy Swaraj—localized, sustainable, and responsible energy consumption and generation.\\nThe course introduced students to the global challenge of climate change, the impact of excessive carbon-based energy usage, and the urgent need for collective action. Core concepts such as the AMG framework (Avoid–Minimize–Generate) were explored in detail, highlighting practical ways to reduce energy consumption, optimize usage, and adopt renewable energy sources, particularly solar energy. The curriculum also covered sustainable living principles, energy literacy, distributed energy production, and the role of individuals in climate correction. Through structured learning modules, real-world case studies, and awareness-driven content, the course encouraged students to rethink energy usage and adopt environmentally responsible practices in daily life.\\n","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability and Climate Action","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/PVWGofQqgfIZW-iG8R9AA.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tYCBuDuKCo9a0odcboSDj","name":"Utsarga Marathon - 2024","slNo":7,"place":"Rajarajeshwari Nagar","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/OgN1TckyzVlqD7DO0FTQk.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in the Utsarga Marathon 2024, I developed a greater sense of social responsibility and awareness of the role individuals can play in supporting underprivileged children. The event motivated me to contribute toward a meaningful social cause while also emphasizing the importance of physical fitness and discipline. I experienced a strong sense of community camaraderie and teamwork, which reinforced the value of collective effort in bringing about positive social change. This activity encouraged me to remain actively involved in community service and socially driven initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024 was a charity marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) wing of RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru, with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The event aimed to support the education, healthcare, and overall welfare of underprivileged children while promoting fitness and community engagement. The marathon featured 5 km and 10 km race categories, attracting wide participation from students, faculty members, athletes, and the general public. Through strong community involvement and enthusiastic participation, the event successfully created awareness about social responsibility and philanthropy while encouraging a healthy and active lifestyle.","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme (NSS) Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/vHwH0fIlt-SHQBXpnpMzR.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rPW_oqPVKm_3E-tu7zEH_","name":"Project Pustak - 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/HSYRQdSSotPQSKoCxZfKp.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in Project Pustak, I developed a deeper sense of social responsibility and awareness of the educational challenges faced by underprivileged students in rural areas. The activity helped me understand how collective contributions, even in small amounts, can create a meaningful impact on society. I gained satisfaction from contributing to an initiative that promotes inclusive education and supports the academic growth of deserving students. This experience motivated me to actively engage in community service and reinforced the importance of empathy, collaboration, and responsible citizenship.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Social Outreach","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/Ghz06tcRqH4AswwUZ8zHS.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"y0mOi3JaO15z1ZVnq5F_S","name":"TEDxRVCE : Tomorrow''s Tapestry","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/W-NfesRFarGVwUPnVE6V0.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"By attending TEDxRVCE 2024: Tomorrow’s Tapestry, I gained valuable insights into diverse fields and contemporary issues through the experiences and ideas shared by the speakers. The event enhanced my critical thinking and broadened my perspective on topics such as mental well-being, technology, governance, creativity, and societal responsibility. It inspired me to reflect on my own ideas and aspirations while motivating me to engage in meaningful discussions and innovative thinking. Overall, the experience contributed to my personal and intellectual growth and encouraged a mindset of curiosity, openness, and lifelong learning.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"TEDxRVCE 2024, themed Tomorrow’s Tapestry, was an intellectually stimulating event organized to promote dialogue, curiosity, and the exchange of ideas across diverse domains. The event featured an accomplished lineup of speakers including professionals from fields such as mental health advocacy, storytelling, artificial intelligence and law, grassroots governance, cybersecurity, and creative arts. Through engaging talks, discussions, performances, and interactive experience zones, the event aimed to connect past experiences with future possibilities. Conducted at the IEM Auditorium, RVCE, the program provided participants with exposure to thought-provoking perspectives and encouraged meaningful discourse on contemporary social, technological, and human-centric challenges.","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/RhJ90b6oTf8gPO9bgO3d0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FpDg5OqQUPpVCZnyLalCP","name":"Fistfull - 2024","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/hx1_Lsd1fLddyjMGrUwde.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the “Fist Full” initiative, I became more aware of the issue of hunger and the importance of contributing to community welfare. The activity strengthened my sense of empathy and social responsibility, as I realized how small individual contributions can collectively create a significant impact. I gained satisfaction from being part of a large-scale humanitarian effort and was motivated to actively engage in future social service initiatives. This experience reinforced the value of compassion, unity, and responsible citizenship.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-27","hoursSpent":10,"description":"“Fist Full” was a social outreach and hunger-relief initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November 2024. The initiative aimed to combat hunger and support food security by encouraging students to contribute essential food grains. As part of the drive, students were invited to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily collections organized at the Civil Department. The initiative witnessed an overwhelming response, resulting in the collection of more than 6,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal from over 1,750 students. The collected food grains were directed toward community welfare efforts, highlighting the impact of collective action in addressing basic human needs.","aicteMapping":"Social Welfare Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/pFH81u2_uZ9Z2p4ZkNLPl.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EVcwcve75W_5Fjb6MhuJd","name":"Utsarga Marathon - 2025","slNo":11,"place":"Rajarajeshwari Nagar","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/wbYhtaEWe-2l6AvmwaVDn.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in UTSARGA 2025, I developed a stronger sense of social responsibility and awareness of the challenges faced by underprivileged children. The event motivated me to contribute to a meaningful social cause while also emphasizing the importance of physical fitness and discipline. I understood how collective participation in such initiatives can create a positive impact on society. The experience encouraged me to actively engage in community service activities and reinforced the value of empathy, teamwork, and responsible citizenship.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"UTSARGA 2025 is the flagship charity marathon organized by NSS RVCE, conducted on April 6, 2025, at the RV College of Engineering campus, Bengaluru. The event was organized with the objective of supporting the education, healthcare, and overall welfare of underprivileged children while promoting social responsibility and physical well-being among students. The marathon featured 5 km and 10 km race categories, encouraging wide participation from students and the community. Registration fees collected from participants were directed towards charitable causes benefiting underprivileged children. The event, supported by Elegant Builders & Developers as the title sponsor, successfully combined fitness, community engagement, and philanthropy, offering participants an opportunity to contribute to society while earning activity points.","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme (NSS) Activities","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/00XsjlJgAsr3-9Vt4b9Hq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3fkkWXh4Qm2piP0aBNXCT","name":"Project Pustak - 2025","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/ogaahbHvDVPudV6FGAwI_.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my involvement in Project Pustak, I gained a deeper appreciation for the importance of education in shaping lives and communities. The activity strengthened my sense of social responsibility and empathy toward underprivileged students who lack access to basic learning resources. I understood how collective efforts and small contributions can make a meaningful difference in promoting education and equality. This experience motivated me to actively participate in community service initiatives and reinforced the value of giving back to society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is an educational outreach initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of supporting underprivileged students by providing them with essential school supplies. The activity focused on spreading the message “Education is a gift, pass it on, change a life!” and encouraged students and donors to contribute towards improving access to education. Funds were collected through voluntary donations using digital platforms, and the initiative aimed to procure and distribute learning materials such as books, stationery, and other academic essentials. The activity promoted social responsibility among students while creating awareness about the importance of education as a tool for empowerment and long-term societal development. This activity facilitated the supply of stationary kits to 5,500+ underprivileged children.\\n","aicteMapping":"Social Outreach","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/LLoBB4dzPlLPqdN5CEifS.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Gq0Dhl4DXoAkDXzL7Sy2P","name":"Fistfull - 2025","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/zxj8DTqeBBfTSu21x-HHT.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in Fistfull 2025, I developed a deeper understanding of food insecurity and its impact on vulnerable communities. The activity strengthened my sense of empathy and social responsibility, as I witnessed how individual contributions could collectively support large-scale humanitarian efforts. I gained satisfaction from contributing to institutions involved in feeding, healthcare, and elder care, and the experience motivated me to actively participate in future community service initiatives. This activity reinforced the values of compassion, teamwork, and responsible citizenship.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Fistfull 2025 was a large-scale community service initiative organized to combat food insecurity and support health and care institutions through collective student participation. Conducted under the Community Service avenue with a focus on Fighting Disease, the initiative was carried out with the support of Rotary Bangalore Spandana. The project was based on a simple yet impactful model, wherein each participating student contributed either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal.\\nThe initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2,146 students, resulting in the collection of substantial quantities of essential food grains. The collected rice and dal were distributed to multiple beneficiary institutions engaged in daily mass feeding programs, elder care, education, and healthcare services. Beneficiaries included Hanuman Temple’s daily mass feeding program, Pruthvi Foundation Blind Boys Hostel, Amrutavani Vridh Seva Samithi, Sai Ashraya Hospital, Sai Satguna Sangraha Trust School, Nele Foundation, and nearby anganwadis. The distribution was carried out on 2nd December 2025, when representatives of the beneficiary institutions, along with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, visited the RVCE campus to receive the donations. The initiative reinforced RVCE’s commitment to social welfare and community engagement.\\n","aicteMapping":"Social Welfare Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5ad8bc2d-73ee-4f4f-91dc-d6122588e3bd/JzcTvGZ2QCC3q9BSD0uXK.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Rohini S. Hallikar","designation":"Assistant Professor, ECE Department, RVCE"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 02:48:55.847111+00', '2026-01-31 03:47:40.752199+00'), ('2b6346ec-c698-4b2e-9fce-bd2291b82c2b', '3e821853-1d08-4993-b3b6-402d0342dc2f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS033","name":"Manish S Raj","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"UCub-byMQZVWGAvx-wabi","name":"FAST-TREK 2023","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hilla","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e821853-1d08-4993-b3b6-402d0342dc2f/c0vCU1xJdda8BBLIY2dsK.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e821853-1d08-4993-b3b6-402d0342dc2f/saA4LSgeBIlvIiYZVqQR_.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e821853-1d08-4993-b3b6-402d0342dc2f/SKNlknWE8MvDJ-CJ1w0tj.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully raised awareness about environmental cleanliness and sustainable practices among participants.\\nEncouraged active student participation and fostered a sense of social responsibility.\\nStrengthened teamwork, leadership, and coordination skills through group trekking activities.\\nPromoted physical fitness, mental well-being, and stress relief among students.\\nEnhanced the visibility and impact of the Rotaract Club’s community-oriented initiatives.\\nDelivered a memorable and enriching outdoor experience, strengthening students’ connection with nature.\\n","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":20,"description":"FAST TREK 1.0 was a flagship trekking and social responsibility initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 23rd February 2023. The event combined adventure with\\nenvironmental consciousness through a cleanliness drive conducted during the trek. Participants assembled early in the morning and traveled to the trekking site after being briefed on safety protocols and event guidelines. The trek through the scenic Huthridurga Hills provided students with an opportunity to experience nature while actively contributing to its preservation. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 750 students, creating a vibrant and energetic atmosphere while promoting teamwork, discipline, and environmental awareness.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"d6bVnUCR1CjjZki75S1Ow","name":"RUSH HOURS 4.0","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e821853-1d08-4993-b3b6-402d0342dc2f/4wQqqA3VcGvbY6SXxsmj0.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-23","duration":9,"outcomes":"The 4th version of the mega-event helped the participants to come out of\\ntheir stressful routine and boredom, and also welcomed the juniors into the college.\\nHelped juniors in making new groups and interacting with club members and organisers of the club","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-15","hoursSpent":30,"description":"Rush Hours 4.0 was a major community service and professional development mega-event\\norganized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE between July and December 2023. Designed to\\nwelcome juniors and alleviate student stress, the project engaged over 250 participants in a\\nfive-day competition featuring eight distinct tasks.\\nThe participants run for their positions as each task led to the elimination of a certain number of teams with 250+ participants; participating actively, followed by regular updates through event dashboard and leader board. The event was a huge\\nsuccess with the participants contributing to society along with having fun in this process. \\nKey activities included:\\nBrainwave Blazers: A general knowledge quiz focusing on Rotary and college\\nhistory.\\nSpectrum Spark: A creative poster-making challenge addressing social issues like\\nchild labor and global warming.\\nBlossom Bonanza: A three-day environmental initiative where participants planted\\nand nurtured saplings.\\nTalent Showcases: Tasks like \"Minute Master\" and \"Echoverse Extravaganza\"\\nencouraged participants to share unique skills and motivational content.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"toChk0kFj3Z8e6J6tHPtw","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e821853-1d08-4993-b3b6-402d0342dc2f/DRa66_-gDLcUOf1tUHlet.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness regarding the importance of\\nphysical fitness and community service among participants. \\nIt helped develop discipline, endurance, teamwork, and a sense of social responsibility. \\nParticipation in the marathon strengthened the understanding of how individual effort can contribute to broader community welfare and encouraged continued involvement in NSS-led initiatives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) with the objective of promoting community\\nparticipation, health awareness, and social responsibility. The\\nevent encouraged students to actively engage in a long-distance marathon that symbolized commitment towards physical fitness and collective well-being. Through structured coordination and volunteer participation, the activity aimed to highlight the importance of an active lifestyle while fostering a sense of service towards society. The marathon also served as a platform to create awareness about community health initiatives and the role of youth in contributing to social development.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:40:47.720952+00', '2026-01-29 18:33:59.65862+00'), ('2c3a9f45-2c06-4dd4-a202-da6657c78c95', '4eac6c0b-5a70-4a76-9142-ef5786410cbb', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:17:35.628854+00', '2026-01-30 07:17:36.71505+00'), ('2c9b5992-7fd5-481c-b3cf-03b5d54249c6', '3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS189","name":"Shreya Chakote","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Jg-Vc7g-7nO0tl8nlDw6A","name":"Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT 2023) – Sci-Biz Quiz","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"I gained insights into how scientific and technological concepts are applied in real-world business scenarios. The activity helped improve my problem-solving ability, quick decision-making, and understanding of interdisciplinary applications.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participated in the Sci-Biz quiz event conducted as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT 2023), a national-level quiz fest held at RV College of Engineering. The quiz focused on testing knowledge at the intersection of science, technology, and business, encouraging analytical thinking and interdisciplinary awareness.","aicteMapping":"Cultural / Co-curricular Activities (Quiz / Competitions)","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/KNXbhbuEuL5bUOy5WJBle.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0eIX5xjJMB8ra8pfq2wXq","name":"Rush Hours 5.0 – Rotaract Club of RVCE","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"I developed teamwork and coordination skills while working under time-bound challenges. The event improved my creativity, adaptability, and ability to actively participate in multi-day competitive activities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Participated in Rush Hours 5.0, a five-day inter-collegiate competitive event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. The event consisted of multiple creative and problem-solving tasks conducted over consecutive days, encouraging teamwork, innovation, and active engagement through structured challenges.","aicteMapping":"Co-curricular / Extracurricular Activities (Club Activities / Competitions)","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HxDe2YXM8wbUoDLS5aSRj","name":"FAST-TREK – Rotaract Club of RVCE","slNo":3,"place":"Huthridurga Hills, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/XqOUK6hNIkYreOXMN8dQc.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of social responsibility and community service. The activity helped me understand how student-led initiatives can contribute meaningfully to social causes while also improving teamwork, coordination, and leadership skills.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Participated in FAST-TREK, a flagship community service event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. The event involved a guided trek aimed at raising funds to provide financial assistance to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The activity combined social responsibility with teamwork and outdoor engagement.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/m1Xd3q5oYMJ-JfKhYvvYI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hSCMhfYQlMsX_jC5usKI8","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of social responsibility and the impact of collective efforts in addressing educational inequalities. This activity helped me develop a sense of empathy, teamwork, and an understanding of how organized student initiatives can contribute meaningfully to community development.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students from rural areas. Funds were collected through voluntary contributions from donors and members, which were used to procure textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other necessary educational materials. The project focused on supporting education and improving access to basic learning resources for deserving students.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract Club of RVCE","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GyVT_Lh4OpbFBd9-_ahxn","name":"FISTFULL","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/vZXs47_lGWRORa1X3NmAy.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/C59G616DunCP4RW0z63Md.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of consistency and dedication in social service activities. The initiative helped me understand how structured volunteer efforts over an extended period can create meaningful social impact while improving teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Fist Full is a community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, aimed at making a tangible and lasting social impact. The event was conducted over a two-week duration and involved coordinated efforts by Rotaract volunteers to support social welfare initiatives. The activity emphasized collective responsibility, service to society, and sustained volunteer engagement.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract Club of RVCE","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6VSVbhd24qRV4NZRyceh_","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of social responsibility and collective action in addressing community issues. The marathon reinforced discipline, perseverance, and the value of contributing towards social causes while promoting physical fitness and civic awareness.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participated in the Utsarga Marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, under the 5 KM category. The marathon was conducted to promote social awareness, community participation, and commitment towards a worthy social cause. The event encouraged students to actively contribute to societal well-being through physical participation and service-oriented engagement.","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme RVCE","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Pn9H123mAibtJvCFe0Vm1","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":664743,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of social responsibility and collective action in addressing community issues. The marathon reinforced discipline, perseverance, and the value of contributing towards social causes while promoting physical fitness and civic awareness.","semester":"6","startDate":"0205-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participated in the Utsarga Marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, under the 5 KM category. The marathon was conducted to promote social awareness, community participation, and commitment towards a worthy social cause. The event encouraged students to actively contribute to societal well-being through physical participation and service-oriented engagement.","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme RVCE","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EYzN1JUd2jxpUuwRGMqk5","name":"Farmathon 2024","slNo":8,"place":"Art of Living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/Yrk448-djjh56ZpEZS2Xu.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/8UlsjvfAQfwBzlifI6P2j.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained awareness about sustainable farming practices and the role of agriculture in societal well-being. The activity helped me understand the importance of community participation in addressing agricultural and environmental issues and encouraged a sense of social responsibility.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-16","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Participated in Farmathon 2024 organized at the Art of Living, which focused on creating awareness about sustainable farming practices and the importance of agriculture. The event included an informative talk on farming, highlighting challenges faced by farmers and the need for sustainable agricultural methods. This was followed by a march to promote awareness and solidarity towards the farming community. The event concluded with community dining, encouraging interaction and collective participation.","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme RVCE","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"O5ZtC_-lKMAhMU_mWDDmB","name":"Rush Hour 4.0 ","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/gYngap5a091SiSBOa1_GS.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3995fa3e-c37c-4944-87df-eec0fcdb1897/hsl0UbAhd0G471TJ6ZiN5.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-02","duration":2,"outcomes":"I developed teamwork, leadership, creativity, and time-management skills while contributing to socially relevant causes. The event enhanced my ability to balance responsibility with innovation and encouraged active participation in community-oriented initiatives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-01","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Rush Hours 4.0 was a five-day community service and professional development event organized with the objective of fostering social awareness, creativity, teamwork, and leadership skills among students. The event began with a pre-event task to build interest and engagement, followed by eight structured tasks. Each task involved elimination rounds, encouraging healthy competition among teams. Over 250 participants actively took part in the event, with regular progress updates shared through an event dashboard and leaderboard. The event successfully combined social responsibility with enjoyment, and the top five teams were recognized with OTT subscriptions and other rewards.","aicteMapping":"ROTARACT CLUB OF RVCE","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MtckVSF8ngZYFo91dazyd","name":"","slNo":10,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"","hoursSpent":5,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"glxMp2f_aLybm8lhTTwBC","name":"spark","slNo":11,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 18:32:46.327173+00', '2026-01-29 18:32:47.166232+00'), ('2f15c3dd-1dbe-4810-89c5-77e0011d560b', 'ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS132","name":"NITHIN GOWDA L","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"K2xIPoEsyWKhGO7yGDL2t","name":"Trekking","slNo":1,"place":"Kunagalu betta","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/WSRv-lfOpJBT8_hHtkRdf.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fast Trek 2.0 event achieved several significant outcomes that extended beyond a simple recreational outing. By successfully mobilizing over 750 participants, the Rotaract Club of RVCE demonstrated an impressive ability to foster large-scale student engagement and community spirit. One of the most tangible results was the direct environmental impact made through the integrated cleanliness drive, which ensured the preservation of the Kunagalu Betta Hills ecosystem and raised ecological awareness among the youth.\\n\\nFurthermore, the event prioritized participant well-being by effectively disseminating comprehensive safety protocols, ensuring that a high-volume adventure remained secure and organized. The day concluded as a resounding success, not only providing students with a memorable experience in nature but also reinforcing the club''s reputation for executing high-impact, flagship social initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Fast Trek 2.0 event was a major flagship initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on January 28th, 2024, which successfully blended outdoor adventure with environmental responsibility. The day began early at 7:30 AM as over 750 enthusiastic students boarded buses bound for the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills. Before the trek officially commenced, organizers conducted a comprehensive briefing to disseminate safety instructions and event particulars to all attendees.\\n\\nAs the participants traversed the picturesque landscape, the journey doubled as a cleanliness drive aimed at preserving the natural environment. This dual-purpose mission created a vibrant atmosphere where students could enjoy breathtaking views while actively contributing to a social cause. Ultimately, the event was a resounding success, leaving participants with a memorable experience rooted in community spirit and ecological stewardship.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8vF2563IHQotcoA3qzJfM","name":"Buy a shirt plant a tree","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/-iUixzJ98xe5O3Xk7D3hf.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The \"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree\" initiative led to several key outcomes focused on environmental impact and student recognition at R V College of Engineering. By linking the purchase of a T-shirt to the distribution of a tree sapling, the Kannada Sangha successfully encouraged students to take personal responsibility for environmental sustainability. This approach not only promoted widespread environmental awareness across the campus but also resulted in the direct distribution of saplings along with actionable guidelines on planting and care.\\n\\nA major administrative outcome of the event was the formal proposal to award students for their civic engagement through the AICTE activity point system. Specifically, the initiative sought to grant 15 activity points to each participating student, acknowledging their involvement in an environmentally conscious effort. To facilitate this, the organizers compiled a comprehensive report and a participant list to ensure that the students'' contributions were officially recognized by the Dean of Student Affairs.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The provided document is a formal letter addressed to Dr. B.M. Sagar, the Dean of Student Affairs at R V College of Engineering, regarding a community service initiative titled \"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree\". Organized by Kannada Sangha, the event was designed to promote individual responsibility and environmental awareness among the student body.\\n\\nThe core of the initiative involved providing a tree sapling to every student who purchased an event T-shirt, along with specific guidelines on how and where to plant it. Both the distribution of the T-shirts and the saplings took place directly on the college campus. The primary goal was to inspire students to personally contribute to environmental sustainability.\\n\\nAs a result of this environmentally conscious effort, the organizers are requesting the grant of AICTE activity points for the participating students. The letter proposes awarding 15 activity points to each student who participated in the initiative. To support this request, a brief report on the event''s execution and a list of participating students with their recommended points are attached to the document.","aicteMapping":"social awarenss","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1tBks4iI6eu4nKVOLOE3W","name":"MARATHON","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/-YqSDg7oat94Aub6uua_C.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE resulted in several impactful outcomes that benefited both the participants and the broader community. By successfully managing a large-scale athletic event, the club promoted a culture of physical health and endurance among the student population, encouraging individuals to adopt more active lifestyles. This mobilization of a diverse group of runners also strengthened the sense of campus unity, providing a shared platform for students to connect outside of a traditional academic setting.\\n\\nBeyond the immediate fitness benefits, the marathon served as a significant leadership and logistical milestone for the organizers. The event’s success demonstrated the club''s capability to coordinate complex safety protocols, volunteer management, and route planning for hundreds of people. Furthermore, by aligning the run with a specific social or charitable cause, the marathon raised substantial awareness and potentially gathered resources for important community issues, reinforcing the idea that collective effort can drive tangible social change.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-27","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a marathon as a flagship event to promote physical fitness and community engagement. This large-scale initiative brought together hundreds of participants, including college students and fitness enthusiasts, to run for a common cause while fostering a spirit of health and wellness within the campus community. The event successfully combined a high-energy athletic challenge with a vibrant atmosphere, encouraging participants to push their limits while building connections with their peers.\\n\\nThe primary outcomes of the marathon included a significant increase in health awareness and a demonstrated commitment to community involvement among the student body. By coordinating such an extensive event, the club showcased its strong leadership and organizational capabilities, ensuring a safe and motivating environment for all runners. Additionally, the event served as a platform for social impact, often tying the run to specific charitable causes or awareness campaigns, further solidifying the club''s role in driving meaningful collective action.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2iEXMV7MEkuJuAWJF2DAi","name":"Blood donation Camp","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/rn1y8fdsCeLASvmn6AB1h.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp resulted in several critical outcomes that directly benefited the local healthcare system and the campus community. The most immediate impact was the collection of a significant volume of blood units, which provided a vital resource for local hospitals and emergency medical services to assist patients in need of transfusions. This direct contribution helped stabilize local blood supplies and potentially saved numerous lives by ensuring that life-saving resources were available for medical emergencies.\\n\\nFrom a community perspective, the initiative successfully raised awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and dispelled common myths surrounding the process. By engaging a large number of first-time donors among the student body, the event fostered a long-term culture of altruism and civic responsibility. Additionally, the event served as a platform for the Rotaract Club of RVCE to strengthen its collaborative ties with medical professionals and healthcare organizations, demonstrating a high level of logistical excellence in managing health-sensitive volunteer activities.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The blood donation camp organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE served as a vital community health initiative, successfully bridging the gap between willing donors and medical institutions in need of life-saving resources. By creating a safe and professional environment on campus, the event encouraged a large number of students and faculty members to contribute to a critical social cause. This initiative not only addressed the constant demand for blood units but also educated the participants on the health benefits and the procedural safety of regular donation.\\n\\nThe primary outcomes of the camp included the collection of a significant volume of blood units, directly contributing to local blood banks and emergency medical supplies. Beyond the tangible medical impact, the event fostered a profound sense of civic duty and altruism within the student body, empowering individuals to save lives through a simple yet powerful act of service. Additionally, the successful execution of the camp strengthened the club''s partnership with healthcare organizations and reinforced its commitment to addressing essential public health needs through organized volunteer efforts.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nkAwTriiqL8EFR3E3znn4","name":"blood donation camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/1N5CnlzL-mQUIgWyC3AnJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp resulted in several critical outcomes that directly benefited the local healthcare system and the campus community. The most immediate impact was the collection of a significant volume of blood units, which provided a vital resource for local hospitals and emergency medical services to assist patients in need of transfusions. This direct contribution helped stabilize local blood supplies and potentially saved numerous lives by ensuring that life-saving resources were available for medical emergencies.\\n\\nFrom a community perspective, the initiative successfully raised awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and dispelled common myths surrounding the process. By engaging a large number of first-time donors among the student body, the event fostered a long-term culture of altruism and civic responsibility. Additionally, the event served as a platform for the Rotaract Club of RVCE to strengthen its collaborative ties with medical professionals and healthcare organizations, demonstrating a high level of logistical excellence in managing health-sensitive volunteer activities.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The blood donation camp organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE served as a vital community health initiative, successfully bridging the gap between willing donors and medical institutions in need of life-saving resources. By creating a safe and professional environment on campus, the event encouraged a large number of students and faculty members to contribute to a critical social cause. This initiative not only addressed the constant demand for blood units but also educated the participants on the health benefits and the procedural safety of regular donation.\\n\\nThe primary outcomes of the camp included the collection of a significant volume of blood units, directly contributing to local blood banks and emergency medical supplies. Beyond the tangible medical impact, the event fostered a profound sense of civic duty and altruism within the student body, empowering individuals to save lives through a simple yet powerful act of service. Additionally, the successful execution of the camp strengthened the club''s partnership with healthcare organizations and reinforced its commitment to addressing essential public health needs through organized volunteer efforts","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ct4bfkeGdsN6SX7WVBatU","name":"Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/1oKBD2vF1WVJDwcXfjXGW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE resulted in several impactful outcomes that benefited both the participants and the broader community. By successfully managing a large-scale athletic event, the club promoted a culture of physical health and endurance among the student population, encouraging individuals to adopt more active lifestyles. This mobilization of a diverse group of runners also strengthened the sense of campus unity, providing a shared platform for students to connect outside of a traditional academic setting.\\n\\nBeyond the immediate fitness benefits, the marathon served as a significant leadership and logistical milestone for the organizers. The event’s success demonstrated the club''s capability to coordinate complex safety protocols, volunteer management, and route planning for hundreds of people. Furthermore, by aligning the run with a specific social or charitable cause, the marathon raised substantial awareness and potentially gathered resources for important community issues, reinforcing the idea that collective effort can drive tangible social change","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-01-27","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a marathon as a flagship event to promote physical fitness and community engagement. This large-scale initiative brought together hundreds of participants, including college students and fitness enthusiasts, to run for a common cause while fostering a spirit of health and wellness within the campus community. The event successfully combined a high-energy athletic challenge with a vibrant atmosphere, encouraging participants to push their limits while building connections with their peers.\\n\\nThe primary outcomes of the marathon included a significant increase in health awareness and a demonstrated commitment to community involvement among the student body. By coordinating such an extensive event, the club showcased its strong leadership and organizational capabilities, ensuring a safe and motivating environment for all runners. Additionally, the event served as a platform for social impact, often tying the run to specific charitable causes or awareness campaigns, further solidifying the club''s role in driving meaningful collective action.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wTEpzAdoEXArxH-48HzSr","name":"Blood Donation camp","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/MBlDzrZlW-zMWpBjuSPH4.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp resulted in several critical outcomes that directly benefited the local healthcare system and the campus community. The most immediate impact was the collection of a significant volume of blood units, which provided a vital resource for local hospitals and emergency medical services to assist patients in need of transfusions. This direct contribution helped stabilize local blood supplies and potentially saved numerous lives by ensuring that life-saving resources were available for medical emergencies.\\n\\nFrom a community perspective, the initiative successfully raised awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and dispelled common myths surrounding the process. By engaging a large number of first-time donors among the student body, the event fostered a long-term culture of altruism and civic responsibility. Additionally, the event served as a platform for the Rotaract Club of RVCE to strengthen its collaborative ties with medical professionals and healthcare organizations, demonstrating a high level of logistical excellence in managing health-sensitive volunteer activities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The blood donation camp organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE served as a vital community health initiative, successfully bridging the gap between willing donors and medical institutions in need of life-saving resources. By creating a safe and professional environment on campus, the event encouraged a large number of students and faculty members to contribute to a critical social cause. This initiative not only addressed the constant demand for blood units but also educated the participants on the health benefits and the procedural safety of regular donation.\\n\\nThe primary outcomes of the camp included the collection of a significant volume of blood units, directly contributing to local blood banks and emergency medical supplies. Beyond the tangible medical impact, the event fostered a profound sense of civic duty and altruism within the student body, empowering individuals to save lives through a simple yet powerful act of service. Additionally, the successful execution of the camp strengthened the club''s partnership with healthcare organizations and reinforced its commitment to addressing essential public health needs through organized volunteer efforts.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FLLm-W02pAMkVEqQvl_Zu","name":"project pustak","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/pOmQcOH97gUVIhQ8BMoVi.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-09-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcomes of Project Pustak 2025 focused on bridging educational gaps and rewarding student philanthropy through a structured partnership between the Pranav Foundation and the Rotaract Club of RVCE. The most direct result of the initiative was the successful sponsorship of stationery kits for students at a Government School, ensuring that underprivileged children received the necessary supplies to support their daily learning and academic growth.\\n\\nIn addition to the social impact, the project facilitated formal academic recognition for the donors within the RV College of Engineering community. By participating in this charitable effort, students were awarded 10 AICTE Activity Points, which contribute to their mandatory non-academic credit requirements. Furthermore, each donor received a Certificate of Appreciation co-signed by the Dean of Student Affairs, providing them with official documentation of their commitment to community service and social responsibility.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-11","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The primary outcomes of Project Pustak 2025 centered on providing essential educational support and fostering a culture of student philanthropy. By collaborating with the Pranav Foundation and the Rotaract Club of RVCE, the initiative successfully sponsored stationery kits for students at a Government School. This direct contribution addressed the immediate needs of underprivileged children, ensuring they had the basic tools required for their education.\\n\\nBeyond the charitable impact, the project provided significant academic incentives for the participating college students. Each donor was officially recognized for their generous contribution with the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points, which supports their formal degree requirements. Additionally, every participant received a Certificate of Appreciation signed by key leadership figures, including the Dean of Student Affairs at RVCE, validating their commitment to community service and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xPBWRvVSo74IMXVhgvsB_","name":"No to Drugs","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/tswSY4WJ2p4DhP9HnhImU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The pledge serves as a powerful catalyst for behavioral change, encouraging individuals to adopt a healthier lifestyle and stay away from illegal substances. Participants often become ambassadors of awareness, sharing their e-certificates on social media platforms to inspire their peers and community members to take a similar stand against drug abuse. This collective action helps to de-stigmatize the conversation around addiction and strengthens the resolve of the youth to remain creative and productive members of society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-05","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Narcotics Control Bureau, under the Ministry of Home Affairs and in association with MyGov, issued an official certificate to Nithin Gowda L on March 5, 2024, to commemorate his commitment to a drug-free lifestyle. By taking the ''Say Yes to Life, No to Drugs'' pledge, he has formally committed to consciously cooperating in efforts to stop drug abuse and maintaining a healthy life away from illicit substances. This certification serves as a formal acknowledgment of his personal pledge toward civic responsibility and the promotion of a healthier society","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5hC3EEQJMH_2kgTkkqbJP","name":"Quiz","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/Pe-NfZfJVpM1Lzf_9uaYJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of the quiz is the deepening of a participant''s understanding of the fundamental principles of Indian democracy and the constitutional framework. By engaging with the material, participants become better informed about their rights and responsibilities as citizens, which is crucial for making empowered decisions in the electoral process. This initiative specifically targets \"young changemakers\" to foster a sense of civic duty and encourage active participation in governance, effectively turning them into \"democracy champions\".","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The \"Quiz on India''s Democracy\" was a national-level digital initiative organized by the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting in collaboration with MyGov. Designed specifically to engage young citizens and first-time voters, the quiz aimed to deepen the public''s understanding of India’s democratic fundamentals and the electoral process. By testing knowledge on the Constitution and the evolving democratic framework of the nation, the initiative encouraged participants to become more informed and active \"democracy champions\".\\n\\nThe outcomes of this initiative focused on both educational empowerment and civic motivation. By successfully completing the timed assessment, participants like Nithingowdal received an official Certificate of Appreciation from the CEO of MyGov, which serves as a formal acknowledgment of their efforts to learn about the country’s governance. Beyond individual recognition, the quiz served as a massive outreach tool for the \"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye\" campaign, successfully fostering a sense of patriotic duty and awareness among the youth ahead of major national events like the 18th Lok Sabha Election.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3gkRYoyE79KmK59PAzKvx","name":"Har Ghar Tiranga","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/T7LWEhhrAEL4PwPGUKFHL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The \"Har Ghar Tiranga\" campaign, a key part of the Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav, resulted in a widespread surge of national unity and personal connection to the Indian flag. By encouraging citizens to hoist the Tiranga at home, the initiative successfully moved the flag from a purely institutional symbol to one of personal identity and pride. One of the most significant socio-economic outcomes was the massive demand for flags, which empowered local Self-Help Groups (SHGs) and boosted the livelihoods of thousands of women across the country who were involved in their production.\\n\\nIn terms of digital and civic engagement, the campaign saw millions of participants uploading selfies with the flag, which served to mobilize the youth and create a massive, shared digital tribute to the nation. For students at institutions like RVCE, a tangible outcome of obtaining this official Certificate of Appreciation is its eligibility for AICTE activity points, allowing them to translate their civic participation into academic credit. Ultimately, the initiative fostered a deeper understanding of the Flag Code of India and historical literacy regarding the nation''s freedom struggle, turning patriotism into an active, lived experience for millions.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The \"Har Ghar Tiranga\" initiative is a national campaign launched by the Ministry of Culture as part of the Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav celebrations to mark India''s independence. The primary goal of the movement is to encourage citizens to bring the National Flag home and hoist it, transforming the relationship with the flag from a purely formal one to a more personal and symbolic connection with the nation.\\n\\nAs a digital component of this campaign, the government created a platform for citizens to share their participation by uploading a selfie with the National Flag. This certificate was awarded to Nithin Gowda L in formal appreciation for successfully participating in this initiative. By documenting their involvement, participants like Nithin contribute to a collective digital tribute that showcases national unity and patriotic pride on a massive scale","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wonY4plzXfqIF-y1jHvem","name":"Teaching school Children","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/qPaQfP17oLg8XR9_akXZZ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-01-21","duration":49,"outcomes":"The teaching engagement at Vidyanikethan Public School resulted in significant academic and professional outcomes for Nithin Gowda L. Primarily, the completion of 80 hours of service directly facilitates the acquisition of AICTE Activity Points, which are a mandatory requirement for his engineering degree at RV College of Engineering. This involvement satisfies the institutional goal of encouraging students to contribute to the academic improvement of local schools and the broader community.\\n\\nBeyond the formal academic credits, the project served as a practical platform for developing essential leadership and communication skills. By interacting effectively with students and delivering sincere, disciplined instruction, Nithin was able to bridge the gap between his technical education and real-world societal needs. This experience also contributed to his personal growth by enhancing his interpersonal skills and emotional intelligence, as he had to adapt his teaching style to ensure it was beneficial and accessible to his students.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":80,"description":"the official certification from Vidyanikethan Public School, Nithin Gowda L completed a significant teaching engagement totaling 80 hours over a 10-day period as part of his academic and AICTE activity requirements. During this time, he was actively involved in instructing and interacting with students, displaying a sincere and disciplined approach that was noted as being highly beneficial to the school''s learners. This experience allowed him to apply his academic knowledge in a practical setting, enhancing his communication and interpersonal skills while contributing to the school''s educational environment.\\n\\nThe outcomes of this teaching activity are substantial, providing both immediate impact and long-term professional benefits. By dedicating 80 hours to the school, Nithin has fulfilled a significant portion of the mandatory AICTE Activity Points required for his engineering degree, which specifically rewards students for helping local schools achieve better academic results and encouraging higher enrollment. Professionally, this role serves as an exercise in leadership and societal commitment, helping to bridge the gap between technical knowledge and real-world application. Furthermore, such interactions often lead to improved soft skills and emotional intelligence, as the student must adapt complex concepts for younger audiences, thereby reinforcing their own understanding of the subject matter.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":100,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/ReVYfTQG7fYP5MWI8tQR8.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ujMbf8xlI03R00L8iO_iI","name":"Nasha Mukht Bharat Abhiyaan","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ac97cea3-0066-4183-b79e-ea544dff36be/HilwCadYtu8F6bpiBr0D0.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of participating in the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan initiative extend from personal commitment to significant academic and social impact. By taking the formal \"Say no to drugs\" pledge, individuals like Nithin Gowda L actively contribute to the national vision of a drug-free India, fostering a culture of health and sobriety within their communities. This public commitment serves as a catalyst for personal behavioral change and encourages others to adopt a similar stance against substance abuse, effectively turning participants into ambassadors for a healthier society. Furthermore, for students at institutions like RVCE, a tangible academic benefit of this certification is the ability to claim AICTE activity points, which are essential for fulfilling non-academic degree requirements and gaining official recognition for their civic contributions.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The provided document is a formal certificate from the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan, an initiative by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, Government of India. It officially recognizes that Nithin Gowda L has taken the \"Say no to drugs\" pledge on August 14, 2025. By accepting this certificate, the recipient has committed to consciously staying away from drug abuse and maintaining a sober, healthy lifestyle. This certification serves as a testament to an individual''s personal dedication to community well-being and their participation in a national movement to create a drug-free society.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"DR. Jyothi Shetty","designation":"Associate Professor Department of CSE"},"evaluator1":{"name":"DR. Uma B V","designation":"professor Department of ECE"},"evaluator2":{"name":"DR. Raviraj Kusanur","designation":"Professor Department of Chemistry"}}}', '2026-02-01 16:08:25.331212+00', '2026-02-01 18:25:06.202663+00'), ('308d6584-bafc-4acb-b96c-7b38f115a991', 'dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22AS012","name":"CHARAN S L","period":"2022-2026","department":"Aerospace Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"l-lUAjy53ASmlei0GP-3x","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/T_McN1i1Def5bCr1laJcb.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Description of the activity\\tThe Blood Donation Camp 2023 was organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering in association with the Lions Club of Bangalore South as part of a social outreach initiative. The camp was conducted on 6 June 2023 within the RVCE campus to ensure accessibility and encourage voluntary participation among students and staff. \\nThe activity began with participant registration and preliminary health screening, which included basic checks such as hemoglobin level, blood pressure, and general health assessment to determine donor eligibility. Post-donation care and instructions were provided to all donors to ensure their well-being.\\nThe event aimed to raise awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its critical role in saving lives during medical emergencies, surgeries, and long-term treatments. By organizing the camp within the campus, the initiative successfully integrated social responsibility into the academic environment, encouraging students to contribute meaningfully to society beyond classroom learning.\\n\\n\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Description of the activity\\tThe Blood Donation Camp 2023 was organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering in association with the Lions Club of Bangalore South as part of a social outreach initiative. The camp was conducted on 6 June 2023 within the RVCE campus to ensure accessibility and encourage voluntary participation among students and staff. \\nThe activity began with participant registration and preliminary health screening, which included basic checks such as hemoglobin level, blood pressure, and general health assessment to determine donor eligibility. Post-donation care and instructions were provided to all donors to ensure their well-being.\\nThe event aimed to raise awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its critical role in saving lives during medical emergencies, surgeries, and long-term treatments. By organizing the camp within the campus, the initiative successfully integrated social responsibility into the academic environment, encouraging students to contribute meaningfully to society beyond classroom learning.\\n\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Blood Donation Program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/whMXXKeEPZWb8y7F8_bWp.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eexQC2W4wQodhVZD0BkhS","name":"KANNADA HABBA-2023","slNo":2,"place":"Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/LaN8Kyrg1BNHd564cSiD_.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-15","duration":32,"outcomes":"This activity helped me develop teamwork and coordination skills by working across food service, production design,\\nand logistics teams. I gained hands-on experience in event management and learned to handle responsibilities\\nefficiently under time constraints. The experience improved my communication and problem-solving abilities.\\nOverall, it enhanced my organizational skills and understanding of collaborative event execution.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-05-15","hoursSpent":60,"description":"I actively participated in the organization of the Kannada Sangha College Fest, conducted at R.V. College of\\nEngineering on 15-06-2023, and contributed for a total duration of 30 working days. My responsibilities included\\nserving meals and managing food distribution for participants and volunteers, ensuring smooth and hygienic service. I\\nwas also part of the production design team, where I assisted in the preparation and setup of the main stage. In\\naddition, I worked with the logistics team to support planning, coordination, and on-ground execution, contributing to\\nthe successful and efficient conduct of the fest.","aicteMapping":"COLLEGE FEST","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/w-icIrzpB0_O0VqR8RYL-.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"U5Rell01P_fddJdR5xySU","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":3,"place":"Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/yUgvZtva7x_9QxJm5nJL6.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE was a tremendous success, collecting around 800 units of blood and significantly contributing to local hospitals and blood banks. The initiative fostered a strong sense of social responsibility and compassion among participants while promoting awareness about the importance of regular blood donation. The event not only helped save numerous lives but also strengthened the spirit of community service within the RVCE fraternity and I am a proud donor.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":40,"description":"On 28th June 2024, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a large-scale Blood Donation Camp in collaboration with leading hospitals and blood banks. The event witnessed an overwhelming response from students, faculty, and staff, resulting in the successful collection of around 800 units of blood.\\nThe initiative aimed to promote the spirit of humanitarian service and raise awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. Prior to donating, all participants underwent a medical screening to ensure safety and eligibility. The camp maintained high standards of hygiene and medical supervision, ensuring a smooth and secure donation process for everyone involved.\\n The event witnessed an overwhelming response from students, faculty, and staff, resulting in the successful collection of around 800 units of blood.\\nThe initiative aimed to promote the spirit of humanitarian service and raise awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. Prior to donating, all participants underwent a medical screening to ensure safety and eligibility. The camp maintained high standards of hygiene and medical supervision, ensuring a smooth and secure donation process for everyone involved.\\n","aicteMapping":"Blood Donation Program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/NPtH_huZPnGIrU9GWJZZH.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Qq6GgWVpdWOytFKF_P8OZ","name":"KANNADA HABBA-2024","slNo":4,"place":"Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/FChaAytDkRtbCJK7L0zyG.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-20","duration":32,"outcomes":"This activity enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through involvement in food service, production design, and logistics. I gained practical experience in managing responsibilities during large-scale events. The experience improved my communication, time management, and problem solving abilities. \\nOverall, it helped me understand effective planning and execution of cultural events.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-05-20","hoursSpent":80,"description":"I actively participated in the organization of Kannada Habba-24, conducted at R.V. College of Engineering on 20-06-2024, and contributed for a total duration of 30 working days. My responsibilities included serving meals and managing food distribution for participants and volunteers. I was also involved in the production design team, assisting in the preparation and setup of the main stage. \\nAdditionally, I worked with the logistics team to support coordination and smooth execution of the event.","aicteMapping":"COLLEGE FEST","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/SKcNm-QT0IsL33nYEHfGZ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"70D1Ccqfc0Rtjxd1vnzsh","name":"AEROMANIA-2024","slNo":5,"place":"Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/RpvAcdesvOWL4yQFRHtBU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-21","duration":3,"outcomes":"This activity helped me gain hands-on experience in organizing and managing a department-level technical fest. I developed strong teamwork, leadership, and coordination skills through event planning and execution. The experience enhanced my communication and problem-solving abilities while handling real-time challenges. \\nOverall, it improved my understanding of systematic event management and collaborative work.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-19","hoursSpent":40,"description":"I actively participated in organizing and conducting the Department of Aerospace Engineering technical fest, AEROMANIA–2024, held at R.V. College of Engineering during 19th, 20th, and 21st December 2024. I contributed for a total duration of 20 working days as part of the organizing and volunteering team. \\nMy responsibilities included planning and conducting technical events, coordinating participants, managing event schedules, and providing on-ground support to ensure smooth execution of the fest. I also assisted in overall coordination and logistics required for the successful conduct of the department fest.","aicteMapping":"DEPARTMENT FEST","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/dca5ec2e-11ea-46d9-947f-b02621a1f033/-VSMK