"startDate":"2024-12-25","hoursSpent":12,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nVDDjcfRRs0_pG6lYz4X4","name":"Human–Elephant Conflict Awareness","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":5,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Wk-hFMlq2FzhxQlrD5w7g","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 ","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community Awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-31","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"W0QxBbIVWAcGFQetDpsVa","name":"Project Pusthak 2025","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":40,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"32-33","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_UiXNlO76oxRLAF_NKqwy","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"34-36","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 19:06:18.645614+00', '2026-02-01 19:45:50.455648+00'), ('4157f9c1-58ed-4486-9e75-aa5b5a668f4c', '99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC151","name":"Snehal Patil","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"sgoYv1l49pmLHnevIaKVM","name":"School Visit For Education ","slNo":1,"place":"Govt School Pattengere","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/SFaQexVWjpyTQRU6cI5Bd.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/SsjVn3C4niFUHoy-K6waq.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/PxNf20Ii__jPTSQhi-gHD.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity had a positive impact on the participating school children by significantly increasing their interest in learning through creative and interactive methods. Students actively engaged in the activities, which helped improve their self-expression, confidence, and enthusiasm towards education. The use of informal teaching approaches made learning enjoyable and accessible, reinforcing concepts beyond traditional classroom instruction.\\n\\nFrom the volunteers’ perspective, the initiative offered valuable exposure to community service and grassroots-level educational challenges. It strengthened skills such as teamwork, communication, leadership, and empathy while fostering a deeper understanding of social responsibility. Overall, the activity successfully contributed to social outreach objectives, encouraged educational engagement among school children, and supported the holistic development of both the beneficiaries and the student volunteers involved.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-20","hoursSpent":5,"description":"As part of the Republic Day outreach initiative, student volunteers from RV College of Engineering conducted a structured educational visit to a Government School with the objective of promoting inclusive and engaging learning practices among school children. The initiative was aimed at supplementing conventional classroom teaching by introducing interactive and experiential learning methods that could spark curiosity, sustain attention, and encourage active participation among students from diverse academic backgrounds.\\n\\nThe visit was carefully planned to create a welcoming and stimulating learning environment where students could freely express their ideas and creativity. Volunteers facilitated a series of age-appropriate, hands-on activities such as art and craft exercises, collaborative group games, storytelling sessions, and interactive discussions. These activities were designed not only to make learning enjoyable but also to strengthen foundational cognitive skills, enhance verbal and non-verbal communication, and promote teamwork and peer interaction.\\n\\nBeyond academic engagement, the initiative placed strong emphasis on the development of moral values, social awareness, and ethical behavior. Volunteers interacted closely with the children to highlight the importance of education, discipline, cooperation, and mutual respect in personal growth and societal progress. Through positive role modeling and mentorship, the volunteers aimed to inspire students to pursue learning with confidence and enthusiasm.\\n\\nAdditionally, the outreach activity served as a meaningful platform for the volunteers to gain first-hand exposure to grassroots-level educational challenges faced by government school students. It encouraged empathy, leadership, and social responsibility among the participating engineering students while reinforcing the role of youth in community development. Overall, the initiative successfully bridged the gap between academic institutions and the local community, contributing to the holistic development of both the beneficiaries and the volunteers.","aicteMapping":"Satva","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ppb-JHuLbkta15WqrYCRV","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye 2024","slNo":2,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/dD5aKUpj0CKAOOraFYkFc.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the initiative reinforced the importance of exercising one’s democratic right to vote and highlighted the role of youth in strengthening India’s electoral system. Taking the national pledge fostered a sense of responsibility and commitment toward active participation in democratic processes and ethical civic behavior.\\n\\nThe quiz component enhanced knowledge of India’s constitutional principles, electoral mechanisms, and democratic institutions. Overall, the activity contributed to increased civic awareness, political literacy, and informed citizenship. It also encouraged conscious and responsible participation in national democratic exercises, supporting holistic development beyond academic learning and earning 4 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye 2024 was an online national-level civic awareness initiative organized by the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting, Ministry of Education, and the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports. The program was conducted with the objective of encouraging young citizens, especially first-time voters, to actively participate in the democratic process and understand the importance of voting in a constitutional democracy.The event included an online pledge-taking ceremony emphasizing ethical voting practices, citizen responsibility, and informed decision-making. Participants also engaged in a structured quiz designed to test and enhance awareness of India’s democratic framework, electoral process, constitutional values, and the significance of civic participation. The initiative aimed to strengthen democratic awareness among youth and promote responsible citizenship through digital engagement.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0n2uUNSbHjCW4Kdg15rPI","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/hSXYElMtUOmgiKNi6myx5.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/e5N4WZG4cOgg5ItFHL_qk.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successful participation in the marathon reinforced the importance of maintaining physical fitness alongside academic responsibilities. Completing the 5 km run helped build endurance, mental resilience, and self-discipline, while also highlighting the role of an active lifestyle in overall well-being.\\n\\nThe event strengthened awareness about social causes supported by the NSS and emphasized the responsibility of youth in contributing to community welfare. Participation encouraged empathy, teamwork, and a service-oriented mindset, demonstrating how fitness-based initiatives can be effectively used as platforms for social change. Overall, the activity contributed to holistic student development by integrating health, social awareness, and civic engagement, and was formally recognized through the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The 5-Kilometer Charity Marathon 2024 was a social awareness and fitness initiative conducted under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. The marathon was organized with the objective of promoting physical fitness, social responsibility, and community participation among students while addressing pressing societal issues through collective action.\\n\\nThe event was centered around the theme of creating positive social impact by combining health awareness with service to society. Participants took part in the 5 km run as a symbolic commitment to causes such as child welfare, education for the underprivileged, and social inclusion. The marathon emphasized the idea that individual effort, when combined with collective participation, can contribute meaningfully to societal development. By encouraging students to engage in both physical activity and social outreach, the initiative fostered a sense of discipline, perseverance, and civic duty.\\n\\nIn addition to its social and fitness objectives, the marathon also served as a platform to promote unity, discipline, and collective responsibility among students from diverse academic backgrounds. The event encouraged active participation, punctuality, and adherence to organized guidelines, reflecting the core values of the National Service Scheme. By bringing together a large number of student volunteers for a common cause, the initiative fostered a sense of camaraderie and teamwork, reinforcing the idea that sustained social change is driven by collaborative effort and community involvement.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yXqT7Nx3CPUetIprAX4Vx","name":"Inkspire 2024 ","slNo":4,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/qVqKP1GesvBozlJq6EENY.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully fostered creative expression and enhanced social awareness among participants. By engaging with topics of public importance, students developed a deeper understanding of how storytelling can influence opinions, inspire empathy, and drive positive social change.\\n\\nParticipation in Inkspire 2024 strengthened critical thinking, written communication, and analytical skills. The inclusive nature of the event ensured that diverse voices were heard, respected, and appreciated, creating a supportive environment for intellectual and creative growth. Featuring selected works on public platforms boosted participants’ confidence and motivated them to use creative mediums responsibly and effectively.\\n\\nOverall, the activity contributed to the holistic development of students by integrating creativity with social consciousness and ethical reflection. It reinforced the importance of literature as a medium for awareness and advocacy while promoting cultural inclusivity and student engagement. Participation in Inkspire 2024 was formally recognized through the award of 3 AICTE Activity Points, adding value to students’ extracurricular involvement and service-oriented learning experiences.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-10-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Inkspire 2024 was a literary and creative writing initiative organized to encourage thoughtful expression, critical thinking, and social awareness through the medium of storytelling. The activity was designed to provide participants with a meaningful platform to explore, reflect upon, and articulate perspectives on socially relevant and contemporary themes such as sustainability, public health, social equality, education, and ethical responsibility.\\n\\nParticipants were invited to submit original literary works across multiple genres, including essays, poems, short narratives, and reflective pieces. Submissions were accepted in English, Hindi, and Kannada, thereby promoting linguistic inclusivity and cultural diversity. This multilingual approach enabled participants from varied backgrounds to express their ideas authentically while fostering mutual respect for different languages and perspectives.\\n\\nThe initiative emphasized the role of creative writing as a powerful tool for communication and advocacy. Selected entries were featured across the club’s magazine, blog, and official social media platforms, ensuring wider visibility and engagement beyond the campus community. By showcasing student voices publicly, the event encouraged dialogue, reflection, and awareness on important social issues.\\n\\nAdditionally, Inkspire 2024 aimed to nurture creativity, originality, and responsible expression among students. It encouraged participants to think beyond academic constraints, engage in meaningful discourse, and contribute constructively to discussions that extend into society at large.","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sh1mjy4bQZl-nvXX5wBtS","name":"Fistfull 2024 ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/lrm0cdH3EAHSB8VfGayHl.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-10","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative resulted in the successful collection of approximately 6700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal, demonstrating strong student participation and commitment to social welfare. The donated food grains were distributed to multiple beneficiary institutions, including humanitarian homes, orphanages, hospitals, and elderly care centers, thereby contributing directly to food security for individuals in need.\\n\\nParticipation in FistFull 2024 strengthened values of compassion, social responsibility, and collective action among students. The activity highlighted how sustainable, grassroots-level efforts can address essential societal needs such as nutrition and care. Overall, the drive had a meaningful social impact while contributing to the holistic development of students and was formally recognized through the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-10","hoursSpent":2,"description":"FistFull 2024 was a community-oriented donation drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the aim of addressing food insecurity and supporting vulnerable sections of society. The initiative encouraged students to voluntarily set aside a small portion of food grains—specifically rice or toor dal—from their daily meal preparations and contribute it towards a collective donation for a noble cause.\\n\\nThe activity emphasized the philosophy that consistent, small individual contributions can lead to large-scale social impact when carried out collectively. Students actively participated by donating grains over the course of the drive, fostering a sense of responsibility, empathy, and awareness about hunger-related challenges faced by many communities. The collected food grains were systematically aggregated and prepared for distribution to institutions serving underprivileged populations.","aicteMapping":"Rotract ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7-TeDo72fi0ghzZyO6WZR","name":"Project Pustak -2024 ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/oAuINDL60vVdvRxVYLqu0.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in Project Pustak 2025 contributed directly to supporting the educational needs of underprivileged government school students by enabling access to essential learning materials such as books and stationery kits. This assistance helped reduce resource gaps faced by students from economically weaker sections and promoted continuity in their academic activities.\\n\\nThe initiative provided meaningful exposure to social responsibility and community engagement beyond the academic environment. By being part of a structured social outreach program organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, it reinforced the importance of collective action and institutional support in addressing societal challenges, particularly in the education sector.\\n\\nAdditionally, the activity encouraged personal growth by fostering empathy, civic awareness, and ethical responsibility. It highlighted how individual contributions, when aligned with organized initiatives, can create measurable social impact. The participation was formally recognized through the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points, adding value to extracurricular involvement and holistic student development.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social outreach initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with Pranav Foundation and supported by RV College of Engineering.\\nThe initiative aimed to support the education of underprivileged government school students by sponsoring essential learning materials such as books, notebooks, and stationery kits.\\n\\nAs a participant, I contributed financially towards the initiative, directly enabling the sponsorship of a complete stationery kit for a government school student. The project emphasized the importance of community responsibility, educational equity, and student participation in social development activities.","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oPBw0eE3yl0PMcptlvXxR","name":"Project Pustak -2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/BQZXGqHLnwMu4k49cYB4-.png"],"endDate":"2025-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative played a meaningful role in enhancing the learning environment of government school students by ensuring the availability of basic educational materials. Access to these resources supported students in participating more effectively in classroom activities and reduced dependency on limited school provisions.\\n\\nEngagement in Project Pustak 2025 fostered a deeper understanding of social challenges related to education and economic disparity. It promoted awareness of how organized, small-scale interventions can collectively create a positive and sustainable impact on society, especially in the context of primary education.\\n\\nFrom a personal development perspective, the activity strengthened values such as empathy, community involvement, and ethical responsibility. Participation in an institutionally recognized outreach program also contributed to holistic student development and was formally acknowledged through the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a student-led educational support initiative undertaken by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with Pranav Foundation. The program focused on strengthening foundational education for students from government schools by providing them with essential academic resources, including textbooks and stationery supplies.\\n\\nThrough voluntary contribution, the initiative enabled the sponsorship of learning kits for school children from underprivileged backgrounds. The activity highlighted the role of student communities in addressing educational inequality and encouraged socially responsible participation alongside academic pursuits.","aicteMapping":"Rotract ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"edki1IzvRNFR0yutje2k0","name":"Utsarga Marathon - 2025 ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/43iiDvV1D5OIi6eaWF9kV.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/QT_CfHffzApXUsRCLxuWA.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the Utsarga Marathon 2025 led to the successful completion of the 5 km run, reinforcing the importance of physical fitness, stamina, and mental resilience. The activity promoted awareness of healthy living practices and encouraged students to incorporate regular physical activity into their daily routines.\\n\\nThe marathon also played a significant role in supporting a noble social cause by channeling student participation towards community welfare initiatives. It strengthened social awareness, empathy, and a sense of responsibility among participants, highlighting how organized student efforts can contribute to meaningful societal change. Overall, the activity supported holistic student development by integrating fitness, social consciousness, and volunteer service, and was formally recognized with the award of 15 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 was a 5-kilometer charity marathon organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru, with the primary objective of promoting physical fitness, social responsibility, and community engagement among students. The event was designed to encourage students to step beyond classroom learning and actively participate in initiatives that contribute to societal well-being while emphasizing the importance of a healthy and active lifestyle.\\n\\nThe marathon focused on raising awareness about critical social issues such as child welfare, inclusive education, and the need to support underprivileged and marginalized communities. By taking part in the run, students demonstrated solidarity with these causes and symbolically committed themselves to creating positive change through collective action. The initiative reinforced the message that individual effort, when combined with community participation, can lead to meaningful and sustainable social impact.\\n\\nIn addition to its social objectives, the marathon served as a platform to instill values of discipline, perseverance, and self-motivation among participants. Completing the 5 km run required physical endurance and mental resilience, encouraging students to challenge their limits and develop a strong sense of determination. The event also fostered teamwork and camaraderie, as participants motivated and supported one another throughout the course.\\n\\nFurthermore, the structured and well-coordinated nature of the marathon reflected the core principles of the National Service Scheme, particularly volunteerism, unity, and service to society. The initiative strengthened the bond between students and the broader community, inspiring participants to continue engaging in service-oriented activities beyond academic responsibilities. Overall, Utsarga Marathon 2025 successfully integrated health awareness, social consciousness, and civic engagement, contributing to the holistic development of the students involved.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MkChVzavPL4Wuk8yn5T2B","name":"UTPT QUIZ ","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/qDshkcwFDn4RYpXJ1MlC8.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the UTP Quiz 2025 significantly enhanced analytical abilities, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills. Engaging with a diverse set of questions broadened participants’ understanding of national and global issues, strengthening general awareness and intellectual curiosity.\\n\\nThe competition also promoted confidence, time management, and collaborative learning in a competitive academic environment. By participating in a national-level quiz, students gained valuable exposure to large-scale academic events, contributing to personal growth and academic enrichment. Overall, the activity encouraged continuous learning, healthy competition, and knowledge-based engagement, and was formally recognized through the award of 5 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"India Quiz at Under the Peepal Tree (UTPT Quiz) 2025 was a national-level quiz competition conducted as part of the Under the Peepal Tree cultural and academic festival. The event was organized with the objective of promoting intellectual engagement, knowledge sharing, and awareness of India’s rich heritage, history, culture, and contemporary developments. Conducted from 23rd to 25th May 2025, the quiz brought together participants from diverse academic backgrounds across the country.\\n\\nThe competition tested participants on a wide range of topics including Indian history, polity, culture, science and technology, current affairs, and general knowledge. Through multiple rounds of structured questioning, the quiz encouraged analytical thinking, logical reasoning, and quick decision-making. The event provided an interactive and competitive platform that emphasized learning through challenge while fostering academic excellence and healthy competition among students.","aicteMapping":"Quizcorp club","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TiXktWg8rQzigUyiF4l3A","name":"Echolore ","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/XvfnrZ_JCVXSbVSLxQZ-R.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event brought a positive change by inspiring participants to think deeply about social and environmental issues. Echolore was more than a storytelling event .It was a space to celebrate imagination, empathy and the impact that thoughtful writings can have on society. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-16","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V.C.E. organized Echolore, an event celebrating storytelling on themes of Saving Mothers & Children, Environment and Folklore, Participants shared their creative pieces in the form of essays, poems, articles and prose in different languages like English, Hindi, or Kannada, using creativity and  care to express their ideas. The event provided a platform for participants to share their voices and reflect on how stories can make a difference in the world. Through their writing, contributors connected with one another and discovered new ways to express their thoughts and feelings.  ","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sXkYlWTt-vncS7JXb7EEf","name":"Fistfull 2025 ","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/n3-TP2iS9JkfZySh2Wj0y.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"FistFull 2025 witnessed substantial participation, leading to the collection of approximately 2146 kg of rice and 2516 kg of toor dal. The collected food grains were distributed to multiple beneficiaries, including humanitarian temples, foundations, hospitals, and service organizations such as Amrutvani Old Age Home, Seva Samithi, Sai Aashraya Hospital, Sai Satguna Sangram Trust, and Nele Foundation, among others.\\n\\nThe initiative significantly contributed to addressing food and nutritional needs across several care institutions. It also enhanced students’ understanding of social service, teamwork, and ethical responsibility. By actively participating in a sustained community outreach effort, students developed empathy and civic awareness while contributing to a measurable social cause. The activity supported holistic student development and was acknowledged with 10 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"FistFull 2025 was a continuation and expansion of the FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to further strengthen efforts toward hunger relief and community support. Building upon the success of the previous year, the event encouraged students to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal voluntarily to support health care institutions and social welfare organizations.\\n\\nThe drive focused on mobilizing student participation through awareness campaigns and coordinated collection efforts. By simplifying the contribution process and emphasizing the importance of shared responsibility, the initiative promoted inclusivity and active engagement. The event reinforced the idea that student-led service initiatives can play a vital role in supporting essential care services and improving the quality of life for marginalized communities.","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"idH8r1w9b0N78yJcyKVkJ","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walk ","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE  Global Tech Park","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/w_8oRY0Z10IhlC56vdTuW.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/99e484bd-f571-4d35-b66f-bee024ea05e6/WY9co76QkEDcwvZhyjClw.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the walkathon significantly contributed to increasing awareness about the social, ethical, and long-term consequences of female foeticide. The initiative helped sensitize participants and the broader campus community to the importance of protecting the rights of women and girls, while reinforcing the need for sustained collective efforts to build a more just and equitable society.\\n\\nThe event fostered strong community engagement and encouraged students to reflect on their roles as responsible citizens. By being part of an organized awareness campaign, participants gained insight into how non-violent, community-driven initiatives can influence public perception and promote social reform. The walkathon demonstrated the effectiveness of youth participation in addressing social issues and advocating for positive change.\\n\\nOn an individual level, the activity enhanced values such as empathy, social awareness, civic responsibility, and ethical consciousness. It encouraged students to actively engage with societal challenges and contribute meaningfully beyond academic pursuits. Participation in this institutionally recognized outreach initiative supported holistic personality development and was formally acknowledged through the award of 15 AICTE Activity Points, strengthening students’ extracurricular profiles alongside their academic achievements.","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon – “Walk for Her, Walk for Change” was a socially impactful awareness initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, in association with Bangalore Hospitals, with institutional support from RV College of Engineering. Conducted on 11th May 2025 at the RVCE campus in observance of Mother’s Day, the walkathon was aimed at addressing the critical social issue of female foeticide and promoting the principles of gender equality, dignity, and respect for women.\\n\\nThe event served as a collective platform for students, faculty members, and volunteers to actively participate in advocating for the rights of the girl child. By engaging participants in a peaceful and symbolic walk, the initiative highlighted the importance of societal accountability in eliminating gender-based discrimination and deep-rooted social biases. The walkathon emphasized awareness, education, and community participation as essential tools in bringing about long-term social change.\\n\\nThrough coordinated participation and public engagement, the event conveyed strong messages supporting inclusivity, women’s rights, and ethical responsibility. It also reinforced the role of educational institutions and youth-led organizations in initiating meaningful conversations around sensitive social issues and inspiring proactive civic involvement beyond academic boundaries.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 05:52:19.610237+00', '2026-01-30 19:36:10.178026+00'), ('43468903-06e3-489f-9d25-af4dcdb9de26', 'e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC193","name":"Balasai Anish Ponnaluri","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"-DEdxO-TYj_8tiR6Dcsys","name":"Under the Peepal Tree 2023","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/1-BWvldgYYbHzLrq6HblJ.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/DqEL7xwFowPy1PEzqGyGK.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"Awareness of Indian Knowledge Systems, Indian cultural heritage, and the nation’s rich diversity was fostered through this engaging and thought-provoking quiz. Serving as a platform to explore and appreciate the vast historical, artistic, and intellectual contributions of India, the quiz allowed participants to marvel at the depth of our nation’s legacy. It not only instilled a sense of pride in India''s unique traditions but also emphasized the importance of preserving and promoting its cultural and historical treasures for future generations.\\nThe quiz covered a wide range of topics, from ancient scriptures and architectural marvels to modern scientific advancements rooted in traditional knowledge. Participants were encouraged to delve into India''s diverse linguistic, artistic, and philosophical heritage, gaining insights into the remarkable continuity of Indian civilization over millennia. The experience went beyond testing knowledge; it sparked meaningful discussions and curiosity about lesser-known aspects of Indian heritage, fostering a deeper connection with the country’s roots.\\nAdditionally, organizing an event of such a grand scale was an invaluable experience, providing deep insights into event planning, coordination, and execution. The process involved meticulous attention to detail, teamwork, and problem-solving, offering a wealth of learning opportunities in event management and large-scale logistics. Coordinating multiple aspects, such as quiz structure, participant engagement, and seamless execution, required strategic thinking and adaptability. From handling registrations to ensuring smooth transitions between quiz rounds, every step contributed to the development of leadership, communication, and organizational skills. This experience not only enriched knowledge but also reinforced the significance of collaboration and efficient management in successfully conducting large-scale intellectual events.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Under the Peepal Tree ''23, RV QuizCorp’s flagship annual quiz competition, stands as a grand celebration of knowledge and curiosity, bringing together some of the brightest minds from premier institutions across India. This prestigious event serves as a platform for intellectual exchange, fostering a spirit of healthy competition and learning among students from esteemed colleges such as IIT Madras, NIT Surathkal, NIT Trichy, RVCE, BMSCE, PES University, and MIT Manipal, among others. With a legacy of excellence, Under the Peepal Tree ''23 transformed into a melting pot of intellect and talent, where participants engaged in thought-provoking challenges across multiple domains.\\n\\nThe competition featured a diverse array of quizzes, each meticulously curated to cater to a unique area of interest, ensuring an engaging and immersive experience for all attendees. From deep explorations of India''s rich heritage to the strategic nuances of sports and game theory, Under the Peepal ''23 offered something for every quiz enthusiast.\\n\\nAs a key segment of RV QuizCorp’s flagship quiz fest, Indigenius (the India quiz) celebrated the vast and diverse cultural heritage of India. Designed to test participants on their knowledge of Indian history, traditions, arts, and the Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS), this quiz brought to light intriguing and lesser-known facts about the country. From the architectural marvels of ancient India to its modern scientific achievements, Indigenius encouraged participants to develop a deeper appreciation for India’s legacy while fostering a sense of national pride and curiosity.\\n","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/E1dBXv648hp0i2IL40aBt.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ceFEesMx62-0L-e5AuFl-","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":2,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/QkHzxroNG2LM4JZxHXLa3.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event served as a powerful demonstration of collective social impact. By the end of the day, hundreds of kilograms of waste were successfully removed from the Kunagalu Betta ecosystem. Beyond the physical cleanup, the outcome was measured in the shift in student perspectives; the event fostered a culture of \"clean trekking\" that participants are likely to carry into future adventures. The sheer scale of participation (750+ individuals) also provided a massive boost to the club’s visibility, proving that high-energy adventure is one of the most effective ways to mobilize the youth for a social cause.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Fast-Trek 2.0 is a premier flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, designed to bridge the gap between student life and environmental stewardship. The journey began at 7:30 AM, where a massive cohort of over 750 students gathered, representing a significant portion of the college''s active student body. The trek targeted the Kunagalu Betta Hills, a location chosen for its challenging elevation and ecological importance.\\n\\nThe core philosophy of the event was \"Leave No Trace.\" Before the ascent, organizers conducted a rigorous safety briefing, ensuring all participants were equipped with the knowledge and tools—such as eco-friendly waste bags and gloves—to conduct a cleanliness drive along the trail. As participants traversed the picturesque landscape, they weren''t just trekking for fitness; they were actively restoring the trail by collecting non-biodegradable waste, effectively turning a recreational activity into a large-scale environmental intervention.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/WyOIJylcIzEafjqq4RybN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"x3Ke6s6nRij0dEtvFWc0h","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/0_Zaqb9DXLvBaHaHA6_9g.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon achieved significant success in fostering a unified community spirit centered around wellness. By involving both the campus community and the public, the event broke down social barriers and created a shared experience of endurance and achievement. Key outcomes included a measurable increase in health consciousness among participants, many of whom committed to long-term fitness routines following the event. Furthermore, the marathon successfully raised the profile of preventative healthcare, utilizing its platform to distribute information on nutrition and routine health check-ups. The high turnout from faculty and local citizens underscored the event''s reach, positioning the institution as a leader in community health advocacy and inspiring a sustainable movement toward a healthier, more active society.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is a high-impact community health initiative designed to bridge the gap between academic life and physical well-being. Organized with the goal of promoting a \"Fitness First\" culture, the marathon brings together a diverse demographic, including students, faculty members, and the general public. The event is structured not just as a race, but as a comprehensive health awareness campaign. From the early morning warm-up sessions led by professional trainers to the strategically placed health stations along the route, every element of the marathon is designed to educate participants on the importance of cardiovascular health, mental resilience, and the long-term benefits of an active lifestyle. The event serves as a platform to challenge sedentary habits and encourages participants of all fitness levels to take a proactive step toward their personal health goals.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/fj4G55Q4ts8zkLhjZQoiJ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eGiDwfI0Bxdy2rZop3YXO","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/ZRUeUKM7lxjYBAkfShGvo.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of the campaign was a measurable increase in voter readiness and literacy. By participating in the quiz, thousands of students moved from a state of \"civic apathy\" to \"civic engagement,\" gaining the confidence to navigate the registration and voting process. The campaign successfully created a social ripple effect, where first-time voters became ambassadors within their own families and peer groups, encouraging others to exercise their franchise. Ultimately, the project’s success lies in its ability to transform the first vote from a routine task into a significant rite of passage for young Indian citizens, ensuring a higher and more informed voter turnout.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The \"Mera Phale Vote Desh Ke Liye\" (My First Vote for the Country) campaign is a strategic nation-building initiative aimed at the Gen-Z demographic. Recognizing that first-time voters often feel disconnected from complex political processes, this campaign uses gamified learning—specifically through a high-stakes Awareness Quiz—to make electoral education accessible and engaging.\\n\\nThe campaign utilizes a mix of digital storytelling and campus-level engagement to explain the \"why\" behind the vote. The quiz covers essential topics such as the history of the Election Commission of India (ECI), the significance of the VVPAT, and the power of the individual vote in a parliamentary democracy. By moving away from dry, textbook-style lectures and toward interactive competition, the campaign meets young voters where they are—on social media and in vibrant college environments—to instill a sense of ownership over the country’s democratic future.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/grFDhB1fpClDc7pCmzXGO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ld-TcUTWz8g5eP5Ec8f3h","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/8FJxZe3nkYwX5vJLIi9fC.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-24","duration":366,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of Project Pustak was the tangible empowerment of hundreds of students who began their academic year with renewed confidence and the necessary resources to succeed. By providing high-quality supplies, the project led to a noticeable increase in classroom engagement and attendance among the beneficiaries. From a community perspective, the initiative successfully fostered a culture of empathy and collective responsibility, with donors receiving direct updates on how their contributions translated into educational tools. Beyond the physical kits, the long-term impact lies in the psychological boost given to the children, instilling in them a sense that their education is valued by society. The project has laid a sustainable foundation for future drives, strengthening the bond between the institution and the community it serves.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a targeted social intervention program dedicated to ensuring that financial constraints never stand in the way of a child''s education. The initiative focuses on the fundamental belief that every student deserves a level playing field, starting with the essential tools for learning. By mobilizing a community of donors, the project raises funds specifically to purchase and distribute comprehensive school supply kits—including notebooks, textbooks, stationery, and backpacks—to underprivileged children in local government schools and low-income communities. The campaign goes beyond simple charity; it is a structured effort to reduce school dropout rates by removing the immediate economic burden of \"back-to-school\" expenses on families. Through transparency and direct impact, Project Pustak creates a bridge between those with the means to give and the bright young minds who need support to unlock their full potential.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/SAZJFO7ZGiBLb-A-1YHbC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LKnBA_RU-aGNUYVYniscv","name":"ROS Skill Lab","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-14","duration":5,"outcomes":"The lab’s success was measured by the shift in the students'' confidence; participants who walked in curious but cautious left with the ability to architect their own robotic frameworks. The primary outcome was the creation of a peer-to-peer technical community where students felt comfortable troubleshooting together, effectively lowering the barrier to entry for advanced robotics. Beyond the certificates, the tangible impact was seen in the sophisticated simulations and hardware interactions successfully executed by the end of the program. By mastering the industry-standard ROS2, students didn''t just gain a line on their resumes—they gained the digital literacy required to contribute to global open-source projects, ensuring they are ready to step into the workforce not just as observers, but as creators.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-10","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The ROS Skill Lab was envisioned as more than just a technical workshop; it was a deep dive into the \"brain\" of modern robotics. Recognizing that the Robot Operating System (ROS/ROS2) can be an intimidating frontier for many, the lab was designed to be a collaborative sanctuary where students could transition from theoretical coding to seeing their logic come to life. The sessions moved beyond dry slides, placing students in a hands-on environment where they wrestled with nodes, topics, and message-passing interfaces. The atmosphere was one of high-energy problem solving—a space where the hum of cooling fans and the occasional \"eureka\" moment defined the day. By breaking down the complexities of ROS2, the lab aimed to humanize the technology, making it accessible to aspiring engineers who want to build the autonomous systems of tomorrow.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/Hllz4FmVwOnA874SZg4cy.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"osjiGcARtGL4h4ZR-7NRW","name":"National Eye Donation Fortnight","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/xUNKEUKZCE_JHyW_OyWNx.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-08","duration":12,"outcomes":"The campaign’s impact was felt in the staggering number of eye donation pledges signed, representing a significant shift in community mindset and a breaking of long-standing social taboos. By humanizing the cause, the initiative moved beyond mere awareness to genuine commitment, creating a registered database of future donors that will one day change lives. The outcome was a more empathetic campus culture, where participants walked away with a deeper understanding of their power to provide a \"second sight\" to those in need. Ultimately, the fortnight succeeded in creating a lasting ripple effect, as students took these conversations home to their families, effectively turning a two-week event into a lifelong mission of compassion and hope.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The National Eye Donation Fortnight was an initiative rooted in the profound idea of leaving a legacy of sight. Moving away from clinical statistics, the campaign focused on the human stories of transformation—how a single decision can move someone from a world of darkness into a world of color and light. The event created a space for open, heart-to-heart conversations, dispelling the myths and fears that often surround organ donation. Through emotional storytelling and interactive sessions, students and faculty were invited to see eye donation not as a medical procedure, but as a final, selfless gift to humanity. The highlight of the fortnight was the Solemn Pledge, a quiet, powerful moment where individuals committed to giving the gift of vision, turning a collective awareness drive into a series of deeply personal promises.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/eiGp5TdAL-lZId6V0eZ1I.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YcoCWsEuAWupY0A46RyLg","name":"Vikasit Bharat Quiz","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/FB1dCKBSlHmXtQTRk5-G4.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully mobilized an unprecedented wave of youth engagement, with millions of young citizens participating from every corner of the country. The primary outcome was a significant rise in civic awareness and national pride, as students moved from being passive observers to informed stakeholders in India''s development story. Beyond the digital certificates and prizes, the quiz identified a massive cohort of \"Young Leaders\" who moved on to pitch actionable ideas to national leadership, bridging the gap between grassroots aspirations and government vision. Ultimately, the project succeeded in fostering a forward-looking mindset, ensuring that the youth are not just waiting for the future to arrive, but are actively equipped with the knowledge to build it.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz was more than just a test of facts; it was a digital gathering of the nation’s young architects, designed to align their personal dreams with the country''s roadmap toward 2047. Hosted on platforms like MyGov and MY Bharat, the quiz served as an entry point into the \"Viksit Bharat Young Leaders Dialogue,\" turning the abstract concept of a \"developed nation\" into a tangible, shared goal. It challenged participants to look beyond the present and explore India’s milestones in technology, sustainability, and social equity. By gamifying the vision for the future, the initiative humanized the policy-making process, making every student feel that their understanding of the country''s trajectory is the first step toward leading its transformation.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/YpuhWDeIQRSYfAQ-U_Qe1.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"71HY_gb-wpWgBbLrcSF_P","name":"CSITSS","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/0ED-nYTueVfRkDyWMOIbJ.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"The conference''s success was etched in the global knowledge exchange it facilitated, bridging the gap between international industry standards and local academic research. One of the most significant outcomes was the professional elevation of the participants; through diverse technical tracks and the prestigious Best Ph.D. Thesis Award, the event served as a high-stakes launchpad for the next generation of researchers. By integrating voices from around the world, CSITSS 2024 solidified a research culture that prioritizes inclusive technology, ensuring that advancements in 5G, robotics, and automation remain accessible and ethical. Ultimately, the outcome was the creation of a lasting international network, proving that the most powerful \"system\" in technology is the human connection behind it.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-07","hoursSpent":16,"description":"The 8th IEEE International Conference on CSITSS 2024 at RVCE was more than a technical gathering; it was a vibrant \"melting pot\" of global innovation aimed at solving the planet''s most pressing challenges. For three days in November, the campus became a global crossroads where veteran researchers from Florida and Germany walked alongside eager students, all united by the theme of Sustainable Solutions. The conference didn''t just stay in the clouds of high-level theory; it delved into the tangible—from AI in healthcare and green electronics to the ethics of cyber-physical systems. The atmosphere was charged with a spirit of \"interdisciplinary curiosity,\" where a breakthrough in quantum mechanics could spark a conversation about renewable energy at the next table, humanizing the often-isolated world of academic research into a shared journey toward a better future.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/z8o0OcH1JUZQ0VhnDN6yd.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rjpbmjSWb_MiYdrUgfX2b","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/GNKjNRlFbR15us1vf-FYa.png"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of Rush Hours 5.0 was the cultivation of resilient teamwork and radical creativity under pressure. By utilizing a gradual elimination process, the event successfully kept motivation high, ensuring that every task was met with the participants'' best efforts. Beyond the rankings, the project provided a vital platform for students to forge new collaborations and showcase skills—ranging from strategic thinking to artistic expression—that often go untapped in a traditional academic setting. The final announcement of the top three teams served as a celebration of consistency and collective imagination, leaving the entire participant body with a sense of accomplishment. Ultimately, the event strengthened the campus community, proving that healthy competition is one of the most effective ways to foster genuine human connection and shared growth.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Rush Hours 5.0 was a high-spirited, five-day marathon of creativity and wit organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. Far from a standard competition, it was designed as a gauntlet of interactive challenges that pushed more than 450 participants to think on their feet and work in tight-knit teams. The journey was a rollercoaster of emotions, starting with the digital adrenaline of an online treasure hunt in Cyber Chase and moving into the heart of advocacy with Capture the Cause, where teams used art to speak on social issues. From film-inspired performances in Beyond the Frame to the tactile craftsmanship of DIY Wear It!, the event humanized the competitive spirit by celebrating individual passions and diverse talents. The intensity culminated in The Social Showdown, where the digital and physical worlds collided, forcing teams to become storytellers and influencers to win their way to the top.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/Mfwdj-Zlr-AdxWMhIyTcB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HyZ3mZufNRbA_QrprAibg","name":"School Genesis","slNo":11,"place":"Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/n16fgUtbzvJXexwwhogsv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-31","duration":-273,"outcomes":"The program successfully bridged the gap between high-level engineering and foundational school education, sparking a measurable interest in STEM fields among the participants. By providing a comprehensive introduction to core robotics concepts, the initiative empowered students with the confidence to explore technical disciplines they might have previously found intimidating. The outcome was not just a transfer of knowledge, but the cultivation of a \"maker mindset,\" where students learned to approach problems with the curiosity of an engineer. For Team Astra Robotics, the project served as a powerful reminder of the impact of peer-to-peer mentorship, reinforcing their commitment to community outreach and the democratization of technical education.","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-10-01","hoursSpent":32,"description":"The School Genesis Outreach Program was a heartfelt initiative by Team Astra Robotics, a student-led research club from RVCE, designed to ignite a passion for technology in the next generation. Moving beyond textbook learning, the team conducted intensive workshops across five different schools, aiming to demystify the world of engineering for young students. Each session was humanized through interactive, hands-on experiences where complex topics like electronics, embedded systems, automation, and control systems were brought to life through practical demonstrations. For seven hours a day over a two-day span at each location, the team acted as mentors, guiding students through experiments and problem-solving exercises that transformed abstract STEM concepts into tangible, exciting realities.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/dmVhY799kjI_vtHTh7Aid.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FRi2KwDQGRnWwCKsplZlz","name":"Under the Peepal Tree 2025","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/9OK975b1Qe_jqcCQ8sFgI.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"The fest was a resounding success, drawing an impressive cumulative turnout of more than 1,500 participants over the three-day period. Beyond the thrill of competition, the key outcome was the significant enhancement of civic and cultural awareness among students, who engaged deeply with topics like electoral processes, renewable energy initiatives, and the Indian Constitution. The event successfully equipped participants with knowledge that extended far beyond their standard academic curriculum, introducing them to critical national initiatives such as Start-up India and the Digital Literacy Mission. Ultimately, UTPT ''25 solidified its reputation as a prestigious fixture in the quizzing calendar, leaving participants with a renewed passion for lifelong learning and a deeper connection to the diverse intellectual landscape of the country.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":16,"description":"Under the Peepal Tree 2025 was organized as a vibrant intellectual fest designed to foster curiosity and camaraderie through the art of quizzing. The event aimed to bridge the gap between academic theory and real-world knowledge, offering a platform for students from across India to showcase their expertise in disciplines ranging from Science and Business to Culture and History. Over three dynamic days in May, the fest featured a series of meticulously organized quizzes, including the Indi-Genius Quiz, which celebrated India''s rich cultural tapestry, and the Varun Krishnamurthy Memorial Game Theory, a sports quiz dedicated to honoring the legacy of a late alumnus. By including open events like Magnum Open, which invited professionals and alumni alongside students, the fest humanized the competitive experience, turning it into a cross-generational exchange of ideas and a true \"festival of the mind\".","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/EMOtj9jVb8p5eXU1H7t53.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dGUysQM25jbmlfW-SZHP0","name":"FISTFUL","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/iyJu2AfRDl65VqTflvtq6.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"The project witnessed an overwhelming response, with 2,146 students stepping forward to contribute. This collective empathy resulted in a massive haul of food grains that was strategically distributed to several care-based institutions. The outcomes were life-changing for the beneficiaries:\\n\\n    Massive Nutritional Support: A total of 4,300 kg of rice and 2,900 kg of dal was distributed across six major institutions and local anganwadis.\\n\\n    Direct Impact: Beneficiaries included the Hanuman Temple Daily Mass Feeding Program, the Pruthvi Foundation Blind Boys Hostel, and hospitals like Sai Ashraya, ensuring that daily meals remained uninterrupted.\\n\\n    Strengthened Community Bonds: The event culminated in a meeting between the beneficiaries and Dr. KN Subramanya, Principal of RVCE, reinforcing a long-term commitment to social responsibility.\\n\\nUltimately, Fistful proved that when individual small acts are multiplied by thousands, they create a substantial wave of relief, positively impacting the health and dignity of countless individuals.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Fistful was a standalone community service project organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to tackle the urgent issue of food insecurity through simple, collective action. The initiative was built on a powerful, human-centric principle: that every student has the capacity to make a tangible difference. In collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, the project asked participants to contribute a \"fistful\" of hope in the form of essential staples—specifically 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. What made this project unique was how it transformed the student body into a massive, decentralized supply chain of nutrition. It wasn''t just about a donation; it was about thousands of individuals coming together to ensure that the most vulnerable members of society—children, the elderly, and patients—had a warm meal waiting for them.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e7e927e6-6c4f-4728-92bc-cfdab02e64da/5FRTlOnQ4XaVapMtEKytH.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 14:11:17.609232+00', '2026-01-31 02:59:45.5379+00'), ('436621b1-38cd-4164-b6ff-7c9d984b3e39', '0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI006","name":"ASHRAY A PAI","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"rkcMamme7dOKOAtwoz9Wr","name":"ROTARACT Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"R.V. College of Engineering, Bengaluru – 560059","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/dsm-ZAAznKbSmm8LXcJN9.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/9cfo8pF6nJ8M00inplYIC.jpeg"],"endDate":"2022-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Contributed directly to public healthcare by donating one unit of blood.\\n\\nDeveloped a strong sense of social responsibility and civic duty.\\n\\nGained awareness about blood donation protocols, safety standards, and post-donation care.\\n\\nUnderstood the impact of individual contributions in lifesaving medical interventions.","semester":"2","startDate":"2022-06-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The activity involved voluntary blood donation conducted in collaboration with the Blood Centre of Victoria Hospital, Bangalore Medical College & Research Institute, under the Government of Karnataka. The event was organized at R.V. College of Engineering, where participants underwent preliminary health screening followed by the safe donation of one unit of blood. The initiative aimed at supporting emergency medical needs and promoting awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation in saving lives.","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility / Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/SGKH3FexOcmwUvVoCZhdY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"r2OZ_hsuwktYmkVvva5Xe","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON – NSS Initiative","slNo":2,"place":"R.V. College of Engineering, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/zu55b8E_X03ncSDfPOO2W.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Actively contributed to a community-oriented social cause.\\n\\nDeveloped awareness of civic responsibility through NSS activities.\\n\\nPromoted physical fitness and disciplined participation.\\n\\nStrengthened commitment toward volunteering and social service.\\n\\nEarned officially recognized NSS activity points.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"UTSARGA Marathon was a social outreach initiative organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at R.V. College of Engineering. The event aimed to promote social responsibility, physical well-being, and community engagement, aligned with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The marathon encouraged student participation for a social cause and reinforced the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges.","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility / Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/zWHZ02tKniCfL7Jhpo-eg.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1BeF9WzMj9-H-qjTZ18b-","name":"Energy Literacy Training Program","slNo":3,"place":"Online (Energy Swaraj Foundation – National Program)","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/DFClp-Ti_a9gI_tFmV81Z.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/GBpHYtQUJ1AsEbYMsXYAj.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Gained comprehensive understanding of energy systems and sustainability principles.\\n\\nDeveloped awareness of carbon footprint reduction and energy efficiency practices.\\n\\nLearned practical approaches for adopting renewable and solar energy solutions.\\n\\nImproved environmental responsibility and long-term sustainable thinking.\\n\\nBuilt a strong foundation in energy literacy aligned with global sustainability goals.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-30","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The Energy Literacy Training Program, conducted by the Energy Swaraj Foundation, was a structured educational initiative spanning 12 modules focused on energy awareness and sustainability. The program covered topics including energy generation and consumption, carbon footprint, environmental impact, energy wastage reduction, renewable and alternative energy solutions, solar energy adoption, and pathways to achieving carbon neutrality. The training aimed to build foundational knowledge and responsible attitudes toward sustainable energy usage.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values / Environmental Sustainability","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/B4W6Jk492ozero3KncPuC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"er1xD_INBvqfKTvLMuJFT","name":"NSS FAST TREK 2.0 ","slNo":4,"place":"Trek Location: Kunagalu Betta Hills, Karnataka  ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/5P3oByDCwaMGCoBEbwTN9.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/ajvaqT5AouW1Evw-YVhye.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/Yk4javQpLu14bsEB1ZRWr.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/IfcxlxJK-53pZFSXR8gfq.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Actively contributed to environmental conservation through a cleanliness drive.\\n\\nDeveloped awareness about sustainable practices and ecological preservation.\\n\\nEnhanced teamwork, leadership, and community participation skills.\\n\\nGained exposure to organizing and participating in large-scale social initiatives.\\n\\nPromoted physical fitness alongside social responsibility.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"FAST TREK 2.0 was a flagship social initiative conducted by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, combining environmental responsibility with student engagement. The event involved a large-scale trekking activity at Kunagalu Betta Hills, integrated with a cleanliness drive aimed at preserving natural ecosystems. Participants were briefed on safety protocols and environmental ethics prior to the trek. The initiative witnessed participation from over 750 students and volunteers, fostering collective action toward sustainability, physical well-being, and civic responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility / Community Engagement","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/-YAfjBZ5n54ansbz2D4sm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"B3rNL5HeJjfWIPqOxCoS0","name":"ROTARACT Blood Donation Camp ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/uD11_onVd2sdp-IZ_TLyr.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/4NAiARkMvaUc6tXkLiJ1K.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/s0Yaak_8q7GRh5Zzg6EQR.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Contributed directly to healthcare and lifesaving medical support.\\n\\nReinforced commitment to social service and community welfare.\\n\\nGained awareness of blood donation standards and transfusion safety.\\n\\nDemonstrated consistent participation in socially impactful activities.\\n\\nStrengthened ethical responsibility and volunteer mindset.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The activity involved voluntary blood donation at Rashtrothana Blood Centre, a government-recognized regional blood transfusion centre in Bengaluru. The participant donated blood after undergoing mandatory medical screening, adhering to all safety and hygiene protocols. The initiative supported emergency medical requirements and contributed directly to saving lives, reflecting social responsibility and civic awareness.","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility / Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/YrItn4QNn4-P416DjIPQO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"j0moM3duw8CUlsjJXlxX6","name":"ROTARACT Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":6,"place":"R.V. College of Engineering, Bengaluru – 560059 ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/CiMiBXKaK7utgEJ9SrLtJ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/VwuKdsVm2vkclJYJv6PvQ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/TFWDSZOz8fQh16P2Vpiyb.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/Cn0qFByj5cCd4CgWO7IH2.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed strong awareness about gender equality and the social impact of female foeticide.\\n\\nActively contributed to a large-scale social awareness campaign.\\n\\nEnhanced civic responsibility and ethical consciousness.\\n\\nGained experience participating in mass social mobilization initiatives.\\n\\nStrengthened teamwork and leadership through community engagement.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":6,"description":"On the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11 May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized the Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon to highlight the critical social issue of female foeticide and promote the value of the girl child in society. The event witnessed participation from over 350 individuals, including students, faculty members, and parents. The walkathon featured impactful placards, slogans, and collective participation aimed at educating the public and inspiring action against gender","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility / Community Engagement","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/dppIKE-RXMmPUzdVso4aQ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IxCp9tR8WiRLki5saQW8b","name":"Plant a Tree – Environmental Sustainability Driv","slNo":7,"place":"R.V. College of Engineering, Bengaluru – 560059 ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/dGhmhwBdvvw73boDRjXqp.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/JgBFO-ne93Of6UMVjgqEy.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/BraGPKm0VKUj_Ibjo68RL.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed awareness about environmental sustainability and green initiatives.\\n\\nEncouraged individual accountability through active tree plantation.\\n\\nGained understanding of practical methods to contribute toward ecological balance.\\n\\nStrengthened civic responsibility and participation in community-driven initiatives.\\n\\nReinforced the importance of sustainable practices in everyday life.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The “Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree” initiative was a community service and environmental sustainability program organized by Kannada Sangha, R.V. College of Engineering. The event aimed to promote environmental awareness and individual responsibility toward sustainability. As part of the initiative, students who purchased an event T-shirt were provided with a tree sapling along with clear guidelines on plantation and care. The distribution and awareness activities were conducted within the college campus, encouraging students to actively contribute to ecological preservation through direct action.","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/4hWz1DyVcC7c8Lrl_Dtvg.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ccV4oT4K_C-CVYk2VJ6JQ","name":"ROTARACT FISTFUL","slNo":8,"place":"R.V. College of Engineering, Bengaluru ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/03F87XZ29IIQciy585rNe.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/Ep-Y4WQQKacQx_qO_ZInW.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/4hqmMU2WTw4GAcrIr3Z5F.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/lwfPW2vf4mUb9SlGmoofK.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Contributed directly to addressing food insecurity and community nutrition.\\n\\nDeveloped strong social responsibility and empathy toward vulnerable populations.\\n\\nLearned large-scale coordination and execution of community service projects.\\n\\nGained exposure to impact-driven volunteering supported by Rotary institutions.\\n\\nStrengthened teamwork, leadership, and civic engagement skills.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":12,"description":"FISTFUL was a standalone community service project organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to combat food insecurity and support health and care institutions. The initiative encouraged collective student participation, where each participant contributed either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. With support from Rotary Bangalore Spandana, the project successfully collected and distributed large quantities of essential food grains to beneficiary organizations including hospitals, shelters, schools, temples, and anganwadis. The project transformed individual contributions into a large-scale nutritional support system for vulnerable communities.","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility / Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/_XF0kC7noLOugG0qmwSEI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"n6gbIR0UHbxnWm9P-y6sV","name":"ASTRA Robotics School Genesis Workshop ","slNo":9,"place":"St. Claret’s School, Bengaluru ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/NvB7znFcgqYuzyw3JppvE.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/H7HrwBiG7jEmXC9GWXinJ.png"],"endDate":"2025-09-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Delivered hands-on STEM education to school students.\\n\\nStrengthened understanding of core engineering concepts through teaching.\\n\\nDeveloped communication, leadership, and technical mentoring skills.\\n\\nGained experience in outreach-based technical program execution.\\n\\nRepresented RV College of Engineering in an external academic engagement.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-09-25","hoursSpent":15,"description":"The School Genesis Workshop was a technical outreach initiative conducted by Astra Robotics under the School Genesis Outreach Program. The workshop was held at St. Claret’s School and aimed to introduce school students to core engineering concepts through hands-on exposure. Sessions covered fundamentals of electronics, embedded systems, automation, and control systems. The initiative focused on bridging the gap between theoretical learning and practical application while fostering early interest in engineering and robotics. The event involved extensive preparation, logistics planning, and interactive delivery by the student team.","aicteMapping":"Professional Development / Technical Outreach","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/rr4NqV-9ZtmKQweKDiQiO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3peTFChJycdH7nB8nWiwW","name":"ROTARACT Blood donation camp","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/yHhnWaBRycGGJv5ObaSIy.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed a strong sense of social responsibility and civic engagement.\\n\\nGained awareness about the blood donation process, eligibility criteria, and safety standards.\\n\\nUnderstood the role of voluntary blood donation in supporting emergency and healthcare needs.\\n\\nContributed directly to a life-saving initiative benefiting society.\\n\\nEnhanced empathy, ethical values, and commitment towards community service.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Participated in a voluntary blood donation camp organized in collaboration with the Indian Red Cross Society at the RVCE campus. The activity aimed at supporting healthcare services by collecting safe blood from eligible donors and promoting awareness about the importance of regular blood donation. The event followed standard medical protocols, including donor screening, hygienic collection procedures, and post-donation care, ensuring donor safety and efficiency. The initiative contributed to humanitarian service and community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Voluntary blood donation / saving precious lives","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0b2d1c57-8935-4aba-a138-f893f3614006/Z4MCc6d_C3L_iixqO1r2n.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:15:12.137045+00', '2026-01-30 19:18:31.747741+00'), ('43d633c3-e5dc-4900-b9cb-df86c460f980', '6b276a60-9d0b-4b42-b1cc-e2b0f8377eca', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23CS049","name":"ArushI Vaidya","period":"2023-2027","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"vZZtlWC3YV0T-si1l7utE","name":"Mera vote desh ke liye","slNo":1,"place":"Voting centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6b276a60-9d0b-4b42-b1cc-e2b0f8377eca/ZM2-O2XP7ytPt1ZtajQRU.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":367,"outcomes":"Increased Voter Awareness: Young citizens gained a clear understanding of the voting process, electoral rights, and the importance of informed and ethical voting.\\nHigher Youth Participation: The campaign encouraged first-time voters to actively participate in the 18th Lok Sabha elections.\\nStrengthened Democratic Values: Students developed a stronger sense of civic responsibility and respect for democratic institutions.\\nEnhanced Engagement Through Creativity: Activities like blogs, podcasts, quizzes, debates, and cultural events boosted interest and participation among youth.\\nLeadership and Social Responsibility: NSS volunteers and participants built leadership skills, teamwork, and a commitment to nation-building.\\nInformed Decision-Making: The initiative promoted critical thinking, helping young voters evaluate issues and candidates responsibly.\\nInstitutional Impact: Colleges and institutions created a culture of electoral awareness and sustained civic engagement beyond the campaign period.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"(Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye) is a nationwide initiative launched by the Ministry of Education through the National Service Scheme (NSS) and other partner organizations to encourage youth aged 18 years and above to participate in voting. The campaign aims to help young citizens understand the importance of voting, practice ethical and informed voting, and actively contribute to the nation’s development.\\nKey Highlights:\\nObjective: To motivate and raise awareness among young voters—especially first-time voters—to actively participate in the 18th Lok Sabha elections.\\nRole of NSS: NSS units organize oath-taking ceremonies, seminars, and rallies across colleges and institutions to promote voter participation.\\nActivities: The campaign features a variety of creative and engaging activities such as blog writing, podcasts, essays, quizzes, debates, rallies, and cultural events like Battle of Bands.\\nSignificance: The initiative fosters a sense of responsibility toward the electoral process, strengthens participation in democracy, and inspires youth to see themselves as “architects of the nation’s future.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RMAYBzBiKSg4OsA_2qg6k","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"1","startDate":"","hoursSpent":3,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 07:20:23.52785+00', '2026-01-31 07:24:56.423217+00'), ('4506ffd5-899b-4ca6-8768-ddcaa2bb90b8', '89b688d9-c767-4eca-ad6d-79d146a4a5dc', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC137","name":"Shashwat Jha","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"KI81GPsiOoax2aV5yC1-L","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/89b688d9-c767-4eca-ad6d-79d146a4a5dc/rrmRz4SXEdnslbPCOACcU.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Project Pustak initiative resulted in successful student participation and meaningful resource mobilization to support the education of underprivileged children. The funds collected through the campus drive enabled the procurement of books, stationery, and essential learning materials, directly contributing to improved access to education for beneficiaries. Additionally, the activity enhanced social awareness among students, encouraging a sense of responsibility toward community welfare. The initiative strengthened the culture of volunteerism within the campus and demonstrated the effectiveness of student-led efforts in driving positive social change, thereby fulfilling both educational and social objectives of the program.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-29","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak was a social outreach initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) with the objective of supporting the education of underprivileged children. The drive was conducted within the college campus and aimed at collecting monetary contributions to provide essential learning resources such as books, stationery, and other educational materials. Information regarding the initiative, including its purpose, donation tiers, and deadline, was officially communicated to students through institutional email, ensuring wide participation and awareness across the campus.\\n\\nThe event encouraged students to contribute according to predefined donation tiers, with activity points awarded as a form of recognition for social responsibility and community engagement. This structured approach not only motivated participation but also helped instill a sense of accountability and social awareness among students. The initiative successfully highlighted the importance of equal access to education and demonstrated how small individual contributions can collectively make a significant impact.\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/89b688d9-c767-4eca-ad6d-79d146a4a5dc/WH0ikI-D1cv-1RvRGqUCy.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"k8CQr9SVF9S1qN0N1a2P0","name":"UTSARGA","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/89b688d9-c767-4eca-ad6d-79d146a4a5dc/hyD8vRhp5gFUHVauPtskY.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The successful execution of UTSARGA ’25 resulted in heightened awareness and meaningful engagement among students toward social causes related to child welfare. The marathon helped generate support and resources for initiatives aimed at improving educational opportunities and healthcare access for underprivileged children. Additionally, participation in the 5 km run promoted physical fitness, teamwork, and perseverance while fostering a sense of empathy and social responsibility. Overall, the event strengthened student involvement in community service and highlighted the role of youth-led initiatives in driving positive social change.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"UTSARGA ’25 was a flagship marathon organized by NSS RV College of Engineering (RVCE) with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The event aimed to promote social responsibility while raising awareness and support for underprivileged children, focusing on key areas such as education, healthcare, and overall welfare. Information regarding the marathon, including registration details and extended deadlines, was communicated to students through official channels, encouraging active participation from the college community.\\n\\nThe marathon was conducted within and around the RVCE campus, with the activity commencing at approximately 7:00–7:30 AM. Participants, including students and volunteers, took part in various running categories, and I actively participated by completing a 5-kilometer run for the cause. The early-morning start emphasized discipline, fitness, and commitment, while the campus-based route ensured safety and inclusivity. The event successfully combined physical activity with a strong message of social impact, reinforcing the importance of collective action for community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Help a Child, Change the World","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/89b688d9-c767-4eca-ad6d-79d146a4a5dc/s7JH6pS9tu9q8OU7ZQoCa.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 10:53:54.49898+00', '2026-02-01 11:09:02.94526+00'), ('451162b9-f4dd-4b4f-90d3-42bf95e6062a', '65041fcf-888f-4257-ba14-b57edade73f1', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evalua