Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HzxST-FhNlyEB4QNJiedm","name":"Sweden India Quiz","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/-cTSNH0_5mugnPiK0xEqQ.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/9Q2L5_7hE1cv7KD9BI2ba.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/Vp2N8yZXY_CEYl9g4sOYL.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/PSqhFs3Osl9_7y1Le3e2g.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Vast amount of knowledge concerning sustainability, peace and harmony, \\ncutting edge scientific developments and life of numerous Nobel Prize \\nawardees was gained.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-10-16","hoursSpent":50,"description":"The Embassy of Sweden, in collaboration with RVCE and Xpress Minds \\nEdutainment, conducted the Sweden-India Nobel Memorial Quiz 2024 at the \\nIEM Auditorium. This prestigious event covered various topics including the \\nlife of Alfred Nobel, the Nobel Prize, Swedish innovations, and sustainability \\nin Indo-Swedish relations. \\n \\nStudents of prominent institutions of South India namely PESU, NITK, Christ \\nUniversity, NLSIU, NIMHANS, etc. participated in the event. ","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kT5VK7fvvNalVz3BZKGkb","name":"CSITSS 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/QGtD7X94-GqGsWr2-zPGM.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/QSG3rtYXx_ffb0F7h24-y.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/mZ7Li4nK2hnBEF8ej5PDo.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/C6hQ96Vawnb8oG4F4tOa1.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"We learnt to use novel technologies to work with bulk certificate creation and how technology can assist in ease of manual process.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-07","hoursSpent":100,"description":"The 8th International Conference on Computational Systems and Information Technology for Sustainable Solutions [CSITSS - 2024] will bring together leading academics, researchers, industry representatives and postdoctoral researchers from around the world to share their knowledge and research experience in the fields of green electronics, renewable energy, robotics and automation, photonics, artificial intelligence, cyber-physical systems, quantum mechanics and computer science from November 7 to 9, 2024.\\n\\nWe volunteered for certificate generation for all authors, reviewers, session chairs and so on.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"F1yUZ1QXiVUT5GMdrtki3","name":"Industry Visit to  Raichur and  Yeramarus  Thermal Power  Stations ","slNo":6,"place":"Yeramarus Thermal Power Plant Raichur","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/2O_Ax9pvSeUa017kjQjkH.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/uEvXJd1M4Per7PFSldqVS.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/56x7v-0wCD54523aAFVdH.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-07","duration":-29,"outcomes":"The visit improved practical understanding of thermal power \\ngeneration and strengthened the ability to relate theoretical \\nconcepts to industrial operations. It enhanced awareness of plant \\nsafety, system integration, and operational challenges while \\nfostering interest in core engineering applications. The activity \\ncontributed to professional exposure, industry readiness, and \\ninformed career perspectives in the power and energy sector. ","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-07","hoursSpent":50,"description":"The industry visit to Raichur and Yeramarus Thermal Power \\nStations, organized by SPARK – IUCEE RVCE Student \\nChapter, was conducted to provide practical exposure to power \\ngeneration systems. During the visit, students observed the \\noperational aspects of thermal power plants, including fuel \\nhandling, boiler operations, turbines, generators, and control \\nsystems. The visit enabled interaction with plant professionals and \\nhelped bridge the gap between classroom theory and real-world \\nindustrial practices. This hands-on exposure enhanced \\nunderstanding of large-scale power plant functioning, safety \\nprotocols, and engineering applications in the energy sector.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RzKJ2tzVQCj7U602-qRtT","name":"Environmental Day Quiz","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/-InXX-F3M41Ok5QDX0ufZ.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/6KUpZl7Yd0HN78ocm1wkt.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event signifies the students'' proactive involvement in \\naddressing pressing global challenges, aligning with the \\nemphasis on holistic education and socially responsible \\ninitiatives promoted by AICTE. This not only encourages student \\nleadership and teamwork but also reinforces the importance of \\nintegrating environmental considerations into academic and \\nextracurricular activities.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Environmental Day Quiz organized by students of the \\nSPARK, the IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter, was a \\ncommendable initiative that promoted environmental awareness \\nand education. Students were involved in framing questions for \\nconduction of Quiz and students of SPARK actively involved \\nthemselves in conducting quizzes by visiting each and every \\nclass and awarding the winners with a Plant Sapling, thereby \\nspreading the awareness of being globally and environmentally \\nresponsible citizens. The quiz served as a platform for students to \\nshowcase their knowledge and understanding of crucial \\nenvironmental issues, fostering a sense of responsibility towards \\nsustainability.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LymC1YiYPhmACiidfsbSf","name":"Infosys Visit ","slNo":8,"place":"Infosys Campus Mysore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/qBqtctMbm3DcPTHQ0MxLb.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/6GpAczUQoR8DPT6bcYYbt.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/bTAnL3AUsSRfI3_M-NzD5.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bff40d1b-b1b3-4ad5-8044-ce2abc2ae03e/KmTKnPKei2z-aH1RVAbqg.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":1,"outcomes":"The visit was a valuable experiential learning opportunity. This \\nevent provided students with firsthand exposure to the corporate \\nenvironment and the latest technological advancements at one of \\nIndia''s leading IT companies. By touring the Infosys campus, \\nstudents gained insights into real-world applications of their \\nacademic knowledge, witnessed industry best practices, and \\ninteracted with professionals in the field. This aligns with \\nAICTE''s vision of promoting industry-academia collaboration to \\nensure that students are well-prepared for the dynamic demands \\nof the professional world, fostering a holistic and experiential \\napproach to engineering education.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-31","hoursSpent":50,"description":"A visit to Infosys Mysore Campus was planned by the senior \\nmembers of SPARK, the IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter. It \\nmainly aimed to explore the Campus and get a feel for the \\ncampus environment and facilities. Connect with Industry \\nExperts and interact with them to gain insights into campus life \\nand culture. Exploring the wide variety of opportunities to build \\nin the career and discuss potential future contributions and ways \\nto support the students to excel in quality and perseverance.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 17:43:29.647523+00', '2026-01-29 19:06:48.748111+00'), ('4d50e6ad-ccad-445a-87f9-dc8afbc576ae', '39645530-c54b-4bbd-9a0f-2e4a4af1521c', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22BT019","name":"Hima Bindu Attel","period":"2022-2026","department":"Biotechnology","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"rUKOrWjMUUQTlnk2DqoyQ","name":"Fast Trek ","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE - Hutridurga hill","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/39645530-c54b-4bbd-9a0f-2e4a4af1521c/3UfLdXdnWRuphmaIEbs55.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improved physical fitness, stamina, and endurance among participants\\n\\nEnhanced teamwork, cooperation, and group coordination skills\\n\\nDevelopment of leadership, discipline, and problem-solving abilities\\n\\nIncreased awareness about nature conservation and environmental responsibility\\n\\nExposure to historical and geographical significance of Hutridurga Hills\\n\\nBoosted confidence, stress relief, and overall mental well-being","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":9,"description":"The FAST Trek activity was conducted on 12th February 2023 at Hutridurga Hills, a historically significant hill fort located near Bengaluru. The trek was organized as part of the FAST (Fitness and Adventure Student Training) initiative to promote physical fitness, teamwork, endurance, and environmental awareness among students.Participants undertook a guided trek along rugged trails and steep rocky paths leading to the summit of Hutridurga fort. The activity involved navigating natural terrain, maintaining group coordination, and following safety guidelines under the supervision of coordinators. Along with physical exertion, the trek also provided exposure to the region’s historical significance, natural biodiversity, and scenic landscapes.The event encouraged students to step out of their comfort zones, build resilience, and experience adventure-based learning while fostering camaraderie and leadership qualities.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2g23miFwHloW_3XYRAtFU","name":"Inno-Quest:Ideathon Competition","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/39645530-c54b-4bbd-9a0f-2e4a4af1521c/rT5VoXASFPZcbtjPz402I.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness of challenges related to women’s employment and empowerment\\n\\nEncouraged development of innovative and sustainable solutions for women’s workforce participation\\n\\nEnhanced problem-solving, critical thinking, and social responsibility\\n\\nImproved teamwork, leadership, and presentation skills\\n\\nFostered an inclusive mindset and sensitivity toward gender equality\\n\\nMotivated students to contribute toward women-centric entrepreneurial and employment initiatives","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-17","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Inno-Quest: Women Empowerment Ideathon was conducted on 17th July 2023 at RV College of Engineering with the objective of promoting innovative ideas focused on enhancing women’s employment, skill development, and economic independence. The competition provided a platform for students to brainstorm and propose solution-driven concepts addressing challenges faced by women in education, workforce participation, entrepreneurship, and access to opportunities. Participants presented their ideas before an evaluation panel, emphasizing feasibility, social impact, and sustainability. The event fostered awareness of gender equality while encouraging socially responsible innovation.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/39645530-c54b-4bbd-9a0f-2e4a4af1521c/Af7Iggi7rEJil-HgdEIMu.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 13:37:58.293502+00', '2026-01-29 14:24:00.309714+00'), ('4db02f45-9525-44b2-b316-f82dde20e6eb', '55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD066","name":"Dhanyashree Krishnamurthy","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"MoyzeQZe_aAusTZhbNj6u","name":"Akshara","slNo":1,"place":"Mount Carmel","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/xrPND7wSVK47B9b6o2V1f.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the initiative was a meaningful experience that refined my ability to\\ncommunicate effectively. By conducting a session for a class of students, I learned how to\\nadapt my presentation style to be more interactive and accessible, ensuring that concepts were\\neasily understood. Managing the classroom dynamics, even for a single session, taught me\\nthe importance of patience and engagement in the learning process. Furthermore, this direct\\ninteraction provided personal insight into the educational disparities faced by these students,\\nfostering a deeper sense of social responsibility and a genuine appreciation for the effort required\\nin the teaching profession.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE held skill development sessions in eight Bangalore schools,\\nbenefiting over 1000 underprivileged students. Targeting financially modest backgrounds,\\nthe sessions enhanced academic understanding and provided essential skills. Schools visited\\nincluded BET Convent, Sai Sri Vidya Chethana, Vishwa Bharathi High School, Kengeri High\\nSchool, Government Model Primary School, Nehru Memorial School, Priyadarshini Vidhya\\nKendra School, and Mount Carmel English School. The initiative used interactive methods\\nfor curriculum-based learning to ensure relevance and engagement. Volunteers gained valuable\\nexperience as teachers, fostering appreciation for the profession and addressing educational\\ndisparities. This initiative underscored the power of volunteerism and the need for quality\\neducation for all.","aicteMapping":"Basic education and literacy","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/lVdEZwtAzgKc5w7U6keGz.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yiWOpi0NzOKf_7hTnu8Go","name":"ACM India Summit","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/uZksw7b2B3n0oL1_KKrQL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in organizing the ACM India Summit 2024 provided the RVCE ACM Student Chapter members with significant exposure to leadership and large-scale event managerment at a national level. The organizing team gained hands-on experience in planning, coordination, stakeholder communication, and logistical execution while collaborating with ACM India Council, BMS College of Engineering, and participants from premier institutions across the country. The event enhanced professional networking with industry experts searchers, and academicians, strengthened teamwork and problem-solving skills, and improved organizational, communication, and time-management abilities. Overall, the experience contributed to the holistic development of student volunteers and reinforced their capacity to successfully manage high-impact technical and academic events.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":10,"description":"RVCE ACM Student Chapter in collaboration with BMS College of Engineering hosted the ACM India Summit 2024 on 20th and 21st December. This national-level event organized by the\\nACM india Council brought together esteemed speakers and attendees from premier institutions across the country. The summit featured technical talks by renowned experts, panel discussions about cutting-edge technological advancements, poster presentations showcasing innovative research and cultural performances along with gala dinner.","aicteMapping":"Professional development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/iVWt8PWBR9djvxmQsGSi9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sHLP74gXJP91tMgGprgx9","name":"Collection Drive","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/LfNAWVa_tW2cu3pFM1DM0.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The drive received an encouraging response from the community, resulting in the collection of a significant number of usable clothes. These items were successfully distributed to underprivileged individuals and local shelters. The initiative helped meet basic clothing needs while fostering awareness about compassion, reuse, and community support.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-09","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A clothes collection drive was organized to collect gently used and new clothing for individuals and families in need. The drive invited community members to donate items such as shirts, pants, dresses, jackets, and children’s clothing. Collection points were arranged at accessible locations, and volunteers assisted in sorting and organizing the donated items.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/GyyuEv7XvS1mZHnQAHCTJ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"H0cZKpr8h9IAmyBnyxyPA","name":"Data Remix","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/_0gEhmkmh-0T7aOij4w2F.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Encouraged a holistic approach, combining technical advancements with sustainable thinking, promoting a revolutionary mindset that considers both environmental and technological aspects in business and technology. The initiative  inspired us students to advance sustainable development while embracing technological progress","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Data Remix is an event comprising Data Analysis and Business Innovation in which students of teams of up to 4 people, will be competing for the ultimate prize. This event comprises 2 phases, the prior consists of data analysis and data visualization, in which students will be given pre processed data sets and tools to provide information and inferences for the available data\\nThe event involves students using provided datasets to create data visualizations, presenting their findings to judges including Dr. Satish Babu, Dr. Arulalan Rajan, and Dr. Prasad Sudhakar. The second phase focuses on students developing sustainable solutions aligned with the UN''s Sustainable Development Goals.","aicteMapping":"Community service and Professional development","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/jJJO0FMEB_PJXFuzHzRg-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sEiNh3fiGvapOZHiMBcyy","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":5,"place":"Narayangiri Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/7NFUI-JISIcJdBWKVclHb.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Fast Trek 3.0, I gained a strong sense of environmental responsibility by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive and contributing to preserving\\nthe natural beauty of Narayangiri Hills. The trek helped me improve my physical stamina and endurance by completing the trails, while also teaching me discipline and consistency\\nthrough early-morning participation. I also developed better teamwork and coordination skills by trekking along with a large group and supporting others throughout the journey. Overall, the\\nevent gave me a memorable experience of bonding, collective effort, and personal achievement, leaving me feeling accomplished, motivated, and inspired.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":7,"description":"Fast Trek 3.0, the biggest flagship event of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, took place on 12th January 2025 at the scenic Narayangiri Hills, bringing together over 500 enthusiastic participants from the college. This adventure-packed event combined trekking\\nwith a meaningful cleanliness drive, reinforcing the club’s commitment to environmental responsibility. The trek began early in the morning, with participants embarking on a\\nthrilling journey through the rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills. Amidst breathtaking views, the team actively engaged in cleaning the surroundings, collecting litter, and promoting\\neco-consciousness. The event not only contributed to preserving the natural beauty of the hills but also instilled a sense of responsibility among students. Beyond the cause, Fast Trek 3.0 fostered incredible team bonding, as participants supported and motivated one another throughout the trek. Laughter, shared experiences, and the collective effort to make a difference created an unforgettable experience. The event concluded on a high note, with participants feeling both accomplished and inspired.","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/TbIypwZ0G7VAGXA-yh1re.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vPvO9E97bEa9h96AbaqK2","name":"Fast Trek","slNo":6,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/vS0teqQgID-o70o3Bhi7q.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense of environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by reporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped\\nimprove my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Huthridurga Hills, and it also enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group of\\nparticipants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved my fitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated to preserving the environment. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus\\nto the trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the adventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all\\nattendees. Traversing the picturesque Huthridurga Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding success, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750\\nindividuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s vibrant atmosphere.\\n","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/k4N1J-vqVhdapPmxUWtEe.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2RBa7xm3LaOnqv5IW_LOW","name":"GenAI Hackathon","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/laj9H3Z6M5MNfkqM0g5RQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"As a volunteer for the GenAI Hackathon (powered by EDOCK) held on 29th November 2024 at RVCE, I gained valuable experience in event coordination and student management\\nby supporting the smooth execution of the hackathon. I developed strong communication and teamwork skills by interacting with participants, guiding them when required, and\\ncoordinating with the organizing team to ensure timely flow of activities. This volunteering opportunity also improved my leadership, responsibility, and problem-solving abilities,\\nespecially while handling on-spot requirements during the event. Additionally, being part of a technology-focused hackathon enhanced my exposure to Generative AI innovations and\\nstrengthened my understanding of how collaborative events encourage creativity, innovation, and real-world solution building. Overall, the experience helped me grow professionally\\nby building organizational skills and giving me practical experience in managing a large student-driven technical event.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-15","hoursSpent":6,"description":" The GenAI Hackathon, powered by EDOCK, was successfully organized at RV College of Engineering on 29th November 2024 at the DTL Huddle. The event served as a dynamic platform for students to explore and apply advanced concepts in Generative Artificial Intelligence, focusing on innovative solutions that enable machines to generate content, simulate human-like interactions, and address complex real-world challenges. The hackathon witnessed enthusiastic participation from students who showcased their creativity and technical expertise\\nby developing innovative prototypes within a limited timeframe. Overall, the event encouraged collaborative learning, problem-solving, teamwork, and innovation, creating an enriching\\nexperience that promoted emerging AI technologies and their transformative impact across industries.","aicteMapping":"Professional development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/Yx8kUyAWcELeKkaMiDV0e.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"daQuJ285qgspXTlM3mS2C","name":"Indi-Genius : The India Quiz","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/Ns6J9GDVPAk20aBrQ6d63.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Indi-Genius Quiz, I enhanced my knowledge of Indian culture, history, and traditions through a competitive and interactive learning experience. The\\nevent helped improve my critical thinking, recall ability, and time-based decision-making skills while working collaboratively in a team. Participation also strengthened my confidence in\\nexpressing ideas and responding under pressure during quiz rounds. Overall, the quiz served as an enriching academic and cultural experience that combined learning, teamwork, and\\nco-curricular development.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Indi-Genius Quiz, organized by RV Quiz Corp, was conducted as part of UTPT 2024 on 7th June 2024 at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The quiz was designed\\nto celebrate India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage through an engaging and competitive format. The event covered a wide range of topics including Indian history, Mughal\\narchitecture, epics such as the Mahabharata and Ramayana, festivals, regional cuisines, and cultural traditions. Conducted in teams of up to three members, the quiz provided participants\\nwith an interactive platform to test their knowledge, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills while experiencing the diverse essence of India in an intellectually stimulating environment.\\n","aicteMapping":"Professional development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/62RiARK5IqcQRxQYZ64sQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0Qy84UloJYHZtBe9dAUyb","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/_GyAJy6ko_FZrDyC0UhhE.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The drive received active participation from the community and resulted in the collection of a substantial amount of recyclable paper. The collected paper was sent to authorized recycling facilities, helping reduce waste and conserve natural resources. The drive successfully raised awareness about responsible waste management and reinforced the importance of sustainable practices within the community.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":7,"description":"A paper collection drive was organized to promote recycling and environmental awareness. The initiative encouraged participants to donate used paper materials such as old notebooks, newspapers, magazines, office papers, and cardboard. Collection points were set up at convenient locations, and volunteers helped in collecting, sorting, and bundling the paper for recycling.","aicteMapping":"Environment Protection & Sustainability","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/BuA9S0KxKAisMOIkBxhl9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MpPfG1pMFdIieeId7ByOS","name":"“Through the Eyes of Youth\" an SDG photo competition","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/hLP0eZstmLIIPSOEJNp9Q.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"I enhanced my creativity and photography skills by capturing meaningful visuals that represent real-world issues aligned with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The competition\\nhelped me develop stronger observation and storytelling ability, as I learned to express social and environmental messages through impactful photographs. It also increased my awareness of SDG-related challenges and encouraged me to think critically about how youth can contribute to positive change. Overall, the activity gave me confidence in presenting my perspective\\ncreatively, improved my visual communication skills, and motivated me to engage more actively in socially responsible initiatives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Organized by the IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter,it is an SDG-themed photography competition titled “Through the Eyes of Youth!” designed to encourage students to creatively capture and present real-world perspectives through photography. The competition provides a platform for youth to express their interpretation of the world, focusing on themes aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Open to all RVCE students and students from other IUCEE Student Chapters, the event promotes creativity, awareness, and storytelling through visual media. Participants are invited to submit impactful photographs that reflect social, environmental, or developmental issues, thereby using art as a tool for communication and change. The competition also includes an exciting prize pool of 3500, motivating students to actively participate, showcase talent, and contribute towards SDG awareness through their unique lens.\\n","aicteMapping":"Professional development","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/hThLO-on4PLrcQrILCg91.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"F7JiNqWLbZ2fOvA-Avz9y","name":"India quiz - 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/lOF3OiUzk43YbU4aO0ALu.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/j-B9Lh0vG7vf89zHBXam1.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Indi-Genius Quiz, I enhanced my knowledge of Indian culture, history, and traditions through a competitive and interactive learning experience. The\\nevent helped improve my critical thinking, recall ability, and time-based decision-making skills while working collaboratively in a team. Participation also strengthened my confidence in\\nexpressing ideas and responding under pressure during quiz rounds. Overall, the quiz served as an enriching academic and cultural experience that combined learning, teamwork, and\\nco-curricular development.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Indi-Genius Quiz, organized by RV Quiz Corp, was conducted as part of UTPT 2025 on 23rd May 2025 at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The quiz was designed\\nto celebrate India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage through an engaging and competitive format. The event covered a wide range of topics including Indian history, Mughal\\narchitecture, epics such as the Mahabharata and Ramayana, festivals, regional cuisines, and cultural traditions. Conducted in teams of up to three members, the quiz provided participants\\nwith an interactive platform to test their knowledge, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills while experiencing the diverse essence of India in an intellectually stimulating environment","aicteMapping":"Professional development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/d8vxCsFndNOIDq2j5h6Eg.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LkRDH7ElXLyIs2ls7xSwb","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/k2tfYPFr577pEEghTm_2x.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-05-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in Project Pustak, I gained a strong sense of social responsibility and satisfaction from contributing towards the education of underprivileged rural students. I understood the real impact that even small contributions can create when combined for a meaningful cause. This activity helped me develop empathy and awareness about the difficulties faced by students who lack basic school resources. I also gained  exposure to community service initiatives and learned the importance of teamwork and collective effort in successfully carrying out a donation-based project. Overall, the experience was rewarding as it allowed me to support a noble cause and contribute directly to creating a better learning environment for deserving students.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-05-12","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students living in rural areas. Under this project, a contribution was collected from each donor, and the funds raised were used to procure and donate much-needed educational materials. The collected amount was utilized to purchase resources such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other important school supplies that help create a better and more supportive learning environment for deserving students. The Rotaract\\nClub of RVCE, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, undertook the responsibility of procuring and distributing these essential supplies to ensure meaningful educational support for\\nthe beneficiaries.\\n","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/9EtazL_hicZZMjuAaDadF.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tOz7afIv0DfzTpPqime-L","name":"Rush Hours 4.0","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/0wqSzC1-nTpz3F5fZWZm_.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-11-29","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event was a huge success with the participants contributing to society along\\nwith having fun in this process. The top 5 teams were rewarded with OTT\\nsubscriptions and other prizes.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-11-25","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The 4th edition of the mega-event provided participants a refreshing break from their routine, helping them overcome stress and boredom while warmly welcoming juniors into the college. This five-day community service and professional development project began with a pre-event task to spark interest, followed by eight main tasks designed with an elimination format. With over 250 active participants, the event featured regular updates through an event dashboard and leaderboard.\\n\\nThe tasks included Brainwave Blazers, a time-based online quiz testing general knowledge of Rotary, Rotaract, and the college; Spectrum Spark, a poster-making activity on social and environmental issues; Blossom Bonanza, a three-day plantation drive; Minute Master Showcase, a 60-second talent presentation; and Echoverse Extravaganza, where participants creatively imitated inspirational social media influencers to spread positivity and motivation.","aicteMapping":"Community service and Professional development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/Z5CvjA_MMvktlKy1oYItZ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"VAoqbAHI2B8iNWNzNv9hn","name":"Tanuja Screening","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/g2Er_WCWeHsYLqb5mzNY9.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Motivation for students to work hard and succeed in life.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Screening of “Tanuja”, which is a movie on Tanuja, a young girl, who made news when she travelled 400 km to appear for the NEET examination on 14/10/2020. She was supported by Hon. CM, B. S. Yediyurappa and the minister of health and family welfare Dr. Sudhakar to acquire Medical education","aicteMapping":"Awareness drive","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/hLCjSx0V95CjfdgC4Qmrj.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"e4MzkxCSRiyuCN_UWCF3j","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/BjVVKpRP70D8954a8KYwj.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-12-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"Uptown Junk successfully provided participants with a fun and engaging platform to relieve stress while enhancing teamwork, problem-solving, and creativity. The treasure hunt sharpened strategic thinking and coordination, while the “Best Out of Waste” activity encouraged innovation, sustainability, and effective presentation skills. Overall, the event fostered leadership, creativity, and environmental awareness among budding Rotaractors.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-12-14","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Continuing the legacy of the flagship events of Rotaract Club of RVCE, Uptown Junk was conducted to ease the college stress and bring in the competitive spirits of all the budding Rotaractors. The event began with an adventurous treasure hunt where participants solve clues hidden in the college premises to collect Rota money, and buy junk in exchange of the Rota money. This was followed by a competition of best out of waste to test the abilities and creativity of the participants. The top 3 teams with most innovatory models were rewarded. The models were evaluated on the basis of four factors namely, Ideation, Creation, Presentation and Utility in future.","aicteMapping":"Environment Protection & Sustainability","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/EMfPbH3vqVgclf5okOVuu.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-30","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DMhrB_dGDOlzpfUV4LSYJ","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":16,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/dgb5A7iDw87ZgZI0akJLy.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in Project Pustak, I gained a strong sense of social responsibility and satisfaction from contributing towards the education of underprivileged rural students. I understood the real impact that even small contributions can create when combined for a meaningful cause. This activity helped me develop empathy and awareness about the difficulties faced by students who lack basic school resources. I also gained exposure to community service initiatives and learned the importance of teamwork and collective effort in successfully carrying out a donation-based project. Overall, the experience was rewarding as it allowed me to support a noble cause and contribute directly to creating a better learning environment for deserving students.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students living in rural areas. Under this project, a contribution\\nwas collected from each donor, and the funds raised were used to procure and donate much-needed educational materials. The collected amount was utilized to purchase resources\\nsuch as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other important school supplies that help create a better and more supportive learning environment for deserving students. The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, undertook the responsibility of procuring and distributing these essential supplies to ensure meaningful educational support for the beneficiaries.\\n","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/qZD6wBKEkbZGyQ0F8TJNm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"31-32","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ekEZBCUtef-Px51yiTADM","name":"World Alzheimer''s Day Walkathon","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/GAqt3rOTco7fFwU5UnlY2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-09-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon effectively raised awareness about Alzheimer’s disease and highlighted the need for compassion, understanding, and timely medical intervention. Participants gained valuable insights into mental health issues and the importance of community involvement in supporting affected individuals. The event fostered social responsibility, empathy, and collective action among Rotractors, reinforcing their commitment to public health awareness.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-09-21","hoursSpent":6,"description":"In observance of World Alzheimer’s Day, NSS RVCE organized a Walkathon to spread awareness about Alzheimer’s disease and emphasize the importance of mental health and early diagnosis. The walkathon witnessed active participation from students and volunteers who walked together within the campus, carrying placards and slogans to educate the public about the symptoms, challenges, and impact of Alzheimer’s on individuals and families.","aicteMapping":"Awareness drive","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/A7-IpKr8FcBYaOLF513tF.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"33-34","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"L-W3q4x7sr9HkOPM9mOuh","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":18,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/1GnTR9WquJuyOk8z9hZD0.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need. Overall,\\nthis activity contributed both to my NSS activity progress and my personal development.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on April 6th, 2025,\\nfrom 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based\\nregistration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create awareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness activity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community impact.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/55610c45-0f09-446d-bb36-4a180476b487/6VsTXha3cncgegen0ru7E.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"35-36","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 16:32:00.246466+00', '2026-02-01 16:32:35.226568+00'), ('4fda32b0-a30f-4676-a674-0dd85cd56e1d', '6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC178","name":"Veer Porwal","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"sT6uaoges3x3O7DdVNNqm","name":"Plantation Drive","slNo":6,"place":"Adamya Chetana","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/Eo7Y5zCTnBdMGMhffhlU9.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/Xtn_C1KshyYQVrvDcGJp8.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I gained hands-on experience in environmental conservation and developed a stronger sense of social responsibility. The event improved my teamwork and volunteering skills while also creating awareness about sustainable living and the long-term benefits of afforestation for urban environments.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in a plantation drive organized at Adamya Chetana, Bengaluru, with the objective of promoting environmental sustainability and increasing green cover in the city. The event involved planting saplings, learning about organic farming practices, and understanding the importance of native plant species in maintaining ecological balance. Volunteers worked collaboratively under guidance to ensure proper planting techniques and post-plantation care, making the drive both educational and impactful.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AY5ksPrhs2Ne036HN9tmX","name":"Mera phale vote desh keliye","slNo":3,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/3vPRFNn0Yvxz3unvuhVlz.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program enhanced awareness of democratic values and electoral responsibility among students. It instilled a sense of patriotism and accountability, motivating participants to become responsible voters and encourage democratic participation within their communities. ","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The activity Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye was conducted to encourage first-time voters to actively participate in the democratic process. It aimed to create awareness about the importance of voting,constitutional rights, and civic duties of citizens. Participants took a formal pledge to exercise their voting rights responsibly and ethically. The activity emphasized the role of youth in shaping the future of the nation through informed and conscious electoral participation. ","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZLnIVBb-Mo0Lqn8jkwyi8","name":"Utsarga : Publicity","slNo":3,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/bd6nB-WuE675MG8PMAZfL.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"This role helped me improve my communication and interpersonal skills while gaining experience in event publicity and crowd engagement. I also developed confidence in public interaction and learned how awareness campaigns contribute to the success of large-scale social and fitness-oriented events.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated as a publicity volunteer for the Utsarga Marathon, where I was involved in promoting the event and spreading awareness among the public. My role included engaging with participants, explaining the purpose of the marathon, encouraging registrations, and helping increase visibility through on-ground interactions and coordinated outreach activities. The experience required clear communication and active coordination with the organizing team to ensure effective promotion.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CCiqbiNw7UtEeDbaX2og3","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":6,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/ko3y8AK00K9ClKP7K0Bf-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed a strong sense of empathy and civic responsibility. It enhanced my organizational and teamwork skills while also increasing my awareness about healthcare initiatives and the impact of community participation in emergency medical support.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I actively participated in a blood donation camp organized to promote awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its role in saving lives. The event involved coordinating donors, assisting the medical team during registration and screening, and ensuring a smooth and comfortable donation process. The camp created a sense of social responsibility and encouraged people from different backgrounds to contribute to a meaningful cause.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nIdWLKnHu34-MkyeOQ8PF","name":"Utsarga : Certificate and registration","slNo":6,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/CieydOEM2-0zwIKX2h1sU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"This experience improved my organizational and coordination skills while teaching me the importance of accuracy and responsibility in event management. I also gained confidence in handling participants professionally and learned how backend operations play a crucial role in the success of large-scale events.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-02-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I volunteered in the certificate distribution and registration team during the Utsarga event, where I was responsible for managing participant registrations, verifying details, and issuing certificates efficiently. The role required handling participant queries, maintaining accurate records, and coordinating with the organizing team to ensure smooth crowd flow and timely completion of the process.","aicteMapping":"Community Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wUfUWZyEjoUqJi2LD0Msp","name":"RUSH HOURS 4.0","slNo":8,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/UV0_pc1ps7QyBVYu4tX3b.png"],"endDate":"2023-11-30","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event was a major success, encouraging teamwork, creativity, leadership, and social responsibility among participants. Along with enjoying the competitive experience, students contributed positively to society through awareness campaigns and environmental activities. The structured format and continuous participation kept enthusiasm high throughout the event, and the top five teams were rewarded with OTT subscriptions and other prizes, making Rush Hours 4.0 both impactful and memorable.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-11-26","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Rush Hours 4.0 was a five-day community service and professional development mega-event designed to help participants take a break from their stressful routines while also giving juniors an energetic welcome to college life. The event began with a pre-event task to build excitement and interest, followed by eight competitive tasks where teams ran for positions and faced eliminations after each round. With over 250 participants actively involved, the event maintained strong engagement through regular updates via an event dashboard and leaderboard. The tasks included quizzes, creative poster making, plantation drives, talent showcases, and influencer-inspired challenges, combining fun with social awareness.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xF2tQVHcUpJ374kiIx5Jh","name":"UPTOWN JUNK","slNo":8,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/x2I6fBoq20hURw7L0Eu-7.png"],"endDate":"2023-12-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"Participation in Uptown Junk promoted creativity, innovation,\\nand environmental awareness by encouraging participants to turn waste materials into useful models. The event strengthened\\nteamwork, leadership, and problem-solving skills through the\\ntreasure hunt and building phases. It also emphasized\\nsustainability and responsible resource usage. Overall, the event\\nprovided a fun and enriching platform that boosted creativity,\\nreduced stress, and reinforced the values of teamwork and\\ninnovation.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Uptown Junk was a flagship two-day event organized by the\\nRotaract Club of RVCE, combining a treasure hunt with a bestout-of-waste challenge to encourage teamwork, creativity, and stress relief. The event began with teams solving clues across the campus to earn “Rota money,” which was used to purchase junk materials. Participants then created innovative models from waste items, showcasing sustainability and creativity. Overall, the event was a fun and engaging experience filled with enthusiasm, collaboration, and learning.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"SbIb6XMtt7Wb9gWCJhmtV","name":"Road Safety","slNo":9,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/ZDUSIrbvC3gRDVrXTuS-o.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"This experience helped me understand the real-world impact of road safety initiatives and improved my communication and public engagement skills. It also strengthened my sense of civic responsibility and highlighted how small awareness efforts can contribute to safer roads and better compliance with traffic regulations.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in a road safety awareness activity aimed at educating the public about traffic rules, safe driving practices, and the importance of pedestrian safety. The event involved interacting with commuters, distributing awareness material, and conveying key messages related to helmet use, seat belts, speed limits, and accident prevention. The activity focused on creating a sense of responsibility among road users and reducing the risk of accidents through awareness.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"piKLRMJr6JWTmGIfszL1c","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":11,"place":"Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/GPkgiTLwQYiCuaGFeSFOF.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Paper Drive successfully promoted community service and\\nenvironmental awareness by collecting a large amount of books, papers, and recyclable materials to support NGOs and underprivileged communities. The initiative encouraged reuse and recycling, contributing to sustainable waste management.\\nParticipants developed teamwork, leadership, and social responsibility while engaging with the community. Overall, the event highlighted the power of collective student effort and made Paper Drive 2024 a meaningful and impactful initiative.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The Paper Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 23rd June 2024 to promote social responsibility and environmental sustainability by collecting books, papers, and recyclable materials for NGOs and underprivileged communities. Over 400 student volunteers participated, conducting door-to-door collections across Bangalore and encouraging citizens to donate reusable resources. The collected items were segregated for proper distribution and recycling, making the drive a meaningful initiative reflecting Rotaract’s commitment to service and sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OwbCVjVs9efc3-6yMyHcr","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":12,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/nTVVr4zxqfItpN9RC333K.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp had a positive impact by providing\\nblood for patients needing urgent medical support, with donations sent to the Kidwai Research Institute. The activity promoted humanitarian values, teamwork, and social responsibility among volunteers. Overall, it was a fulfilling experience that highlighted the importance of community service in saving lives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"With the inspiring motto “Donate Blood Today, Save a Life\\nTomorrow,” I had the opportunity to volunteer in the Blood\\nDonation Camp organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on\\n28/06/2024. The camp was conducted with the objective of\\nsupporting patients in need and promoting awareness about the\\nimportance of voluntary blood donation.\\nAs a volunteer, I assisted in coordinating the event by guiding\\ndonors, supporting the registration process, and ensuring a smooth flow of activities. The camp was organized in a safe and\\nprofessional manner with proper medical supervision. The blood\\ncollected during the drive was sent to the Kidwai Research\\nInstitute to help needy patients suffering from various diseases.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bIdDIXPCGqVqZZKZKGabo","name":"ACM India Summit 2024","slNo":12,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/SqnWEWrgaZ-RhFff7Whcg.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-21","duration":2,"outcomes":"This experience strengthened my organizational, leadership, and teamwork skills while exposing me to large-scale professional event management. It also provided valuable networking opportunities with industry experts and academicians, enhanced my understanding of emerging technological trends, and encouraged active participation in professional and technical communities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-20","hoursSpent":8,"description":"I was involved in the organization and volunteering activities for the ACM India Summit 2024, hosted at RV College of Engineering in collaboration with BMS College of Engineering. The national-level event brought together experts, researchers, and students from across the country and featured technical talks, panel discussions on emerging technologies, poster presentations, cultural performances, and a gala dinner. As part of the ACM Student Chapter RVCE, the activity involved coordination, planning, and smooth execution of event-related responsibilities.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZZx3InfamCLlCoOMdFaIK","name":"India quiz at Under The Peepal Tree 2025","slNo":13,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/WWymHv_TUo1OhhT1LngR5.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"This event helped enhance my general knowledge, presence of mind, and analytical thinking skills. It also improved my confidence in competitive quizzing and provided an opportunity to interact with like-minded participants in a relaxed and intellectually enriching atmosphere.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in the India Quiz 2025 conducted at Under The Peepal Tree, which focused on testing knowledge related to Indian history, culture, current affairs, and general awareness. The quiz provided an engaging and intellectually stimulating environment, encouraging participants to think critically, recall facts quickly, and collaborate effectively during the rounds. The informal yet competitive setting made the learning experience enjoyable and interactive.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cke_vV2GGkQPa8taSQViJ","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":14,"place":"Kempegowda Nagar , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/OvqD47WfnH1GSslFA46ee.png"],"endDate":"2025-06-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me develop empathy, teamwork, and organizational skills while understanding the real-life impact of community-driven healthcare initiatives. It also strengthened my sense of civic duty and highlighted the importance of regular blood donation in saving lives.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in a blood donation camp organized at Kempegowda Nagar, Bengaluru, aimed at creating awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and supporting emergency medical needs. The event involved assisting in donor coordination, registration, and ensuring a smooth and safe donation process in collaboration with the medical team. The camp encouraged community participation and promoted a culture of compassion and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gf6eZYMCNmoPREkYAsIW-","name":"Nasha Mukta Bharatha","slNo":15,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/6SXdc8Qd4fy_mCN8O4o_9.png"],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me develop a deeper understanding of social issues related to substance abuse and strengthened my communication and public outreach skills. It also increased my sense of social responsibility and highlighted the importance of awareness programs in creating a positive and lasting impact on the community.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in the Nasha Mukta Bharatha awareness program, which focused on spreading awareness about the harmful effects of drug and substance abuse. The event involved interacting with the public, conveying key messages on addiction prevention, healthy lifestyle choices, and the importance of seeking help and support. The initiative aimed to educate people, especially youth, and encourage a drug-free and responsible society.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OlXBEoJp0XmbiZNYja3Hy","name":"8th Mile","slNo":15,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6d775bae-19af-40a8-98d3-d374ab247ceb/qTTbE1vnRJwnbBAEtNp0n.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"This experience enhanced my event management, teamwork, and leadership skills. It also improved my ability to handle responsibilities under pressure, communicate effectively, and adapt to real-time challenges, making it a valuable learning experience in large-scale event organization.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":15,"description":"I was part of the organizing team for the 8th Mile college fest, where I contributed to planning and coordinating various activities and events. My responsibilities included managing logistics, assisting with event scheduling, coordinating with participants and volunteers, and ensuring the smooth execution of programs throughout the fest. The event brought together students from different departments, creating a vibrant and energetic campus atmosphere.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:21:56.854076+00', '2026-01-30 17:49:09.738968+00'), ('500bf784-63ea-4088-ab4b-0496c9ddb5f8', '7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC031","name":"Aviral Jain","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"R33gTOkfFncs4X2OnTB9d","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/3Y363RaEvMmv_UVTEzW0h.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The camp successfully contributed to meeting critical blood requirements for hospitals and emergency care. It also increased awareness about voluntary blood donation and encouraged a spirit of social responsibility among students and staff.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was successfully organized at our college with the objective of promoting social responsibility and awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. The camp was conducted in collaboration with certified medical professionals who ensured a safe, hygienic, and well-managed donation process. Students, faculty members, and staff actively participated in the event, demonstrating compassion and a strong sense of community service. Prior to donation, all participants underwent basic health screening, and proper post-donation care was provided. The camp not only helped meet the critical demand for blood in hospitals but also educated participants about the life-saving impact of donating blood. The event fostered teamwork, empathy, and a spirit of humanitarian service among the college community.","aicteMapping":"10","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/ldWQFAl4iBqoeQMfNUKnX.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"e927MefVFIHjA0VFY2K_e","name":"UTSARGA Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/5zjktEdg9VEG8NmoupfaA.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully promoted health, fitness, and social responsibility while generating meaningful support for children’s education. The collective participation and contributions helped fund educational initiatives, directly impacting the lives of underprivileged children and reinforcing the message that community effort can create lasting change.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is more than just a marathon;  it''s a celebration of health, fitness, and charity. Your participation is crucial in guaranteeing the marathon''s successful execution and making it a memorable event for everybody along the journey. \\n\\nYour involvement goes beyond mere physical activity; it symbolises commitment to reshaping a child''s future. The motto of this marathon, ''Help a child, Change the world,'' encapsulates our mission. Every contribution directly impacts providing education to those in need, altering a child''s life path, and fuelling educational initiatives for deserving children.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/970yhx1O5GnJdFBJq2j_d.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0LeMQZVzYoXnGVD7xaI55","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":3,"place":"Apartments in the area","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/nUdD8pgJq46VrjXlW0k87.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"The paper drive resulted in a significant collection of recyclable materials that supported the initiatives of charities and NGOs. It increased awareness about community participation and social responsibility while highlighting the positive impact of student engagement in addressing societal issues.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The students started early morning, going door to door and visiting businesses to gather donations. Their efforts resulted in a significant collection of materials which aims to help charities and NGO''s in order to support their initiatives and assist people in need.\\nThe paper drive not only aimed to provide resources for charitable organizations but also raised awareness about community involvement. The event was a resounding success, showcasing the power of student engagement in addressing social issues and fostering a sense of responsibility among participants and the residents of Bangalore.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/SX1zEvGpJMLAS2HiCATlX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Jc4QAli8Qfy5bjB8y1cBk","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":4,"place":"RVE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/Zu2tyavrRMthjKiEuROwK.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"The camp successfully contributed to meeting critical blood requirements for hospitals and emergency care. It also increased awareness about voluntary blood donation and encouraged a spirit of social responsibility among students and staff.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-06-26","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was organized in the college premises to highlight the importance of voluntary blood donation and its role in saving lives. The initiative received active participation from students and faculty members, showcasing a strong sense of social commitment. The camp was conducted under the supervision of trained medical professionals who ensured proper screening and safe donation practices. Through this activity, participants gained awareness about blood donation while contributing positively to the healthcare needs of the community. The event successfully promoted values of compassion, responsibility, and service among the college community.","aicteMapping":"10","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/KfYsM4qXFVhPEmvbBaWNs.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"v_9Uxwga3e1S216VxuRW1","name":"FistFull","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/w6Xp-oW-mW5rbuXzSgoUX.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The drive resulted in the successful collection of large quantities of essential food grains, demonstrating strong student participation and collective responsibility. It reinforced the impact of small individual contributions in addressing community needs and strengthened the institution’s commitment to social welfare and solidarity.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Students were encouraged to donate 5kg of rice r 2kg of toor dal, with daily collections in the Civil department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6700+kg of rice and 800+kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students . This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive a significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"12","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/dlN-FB0bEMwqzdr-Xpy8v.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7x4Z898Enr8RhNZqGOJ-o","name":"UTSARGA Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/hHdUChUX5A3JyeJyvBmxl.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully promoted health, fitness, and social responsibility while generating meaningful support for children’s education. The collective participation and contributions helped fund educational initiatives, directly impacting the lives of underprivileged children and reinforcing the message that community effort can create lasting change.","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is more than just a marathon;  it''s a celebration of health, fitness, and charity. Your participation is crucial in guaranteeing the marathon''s successful execution and making it a memorable event for everybody along the journey. \\n\\nYour involvement goes beyond mere physical activity; it symbolises commitment to reshaping a child''s future. The motto of this marathon, ''Help a child, Change the world,'' encapsulates our mission. Every contribution directly impacts providing education to those in need, altering a child''s life path, and fuelling educational initiatives for deserving children.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/zz73TCHK71eplcK9_uAzg.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DcnYNjz3dStYFb3zC7af3","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/OR51d_wUjF1Md1K9gHfoC.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-22","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative helped bridge the educational resource gap for underprivileged students by providing essential learning materials. It improved their preparedness for academic activities and promoted equal learning opportunities across different age groups.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Project Pustak was launched with the aim of supporting underprivileged children who, although provided with school uniforms through government aid, often lack access to basic academic tools. This gap places many students at a significant disadvantage. The distribution included two types of kits tailored for different age groups: students in grades 1 to 5 received kits with four notebooks (two ruled, two unruled) along with a stationery kit, while students in grades 6 to 10 received four notebooks (two ruled, two unruled) and a geometry box.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/QeHfKF2Ewh_6iC3_a3N2K.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_fPk7oFp7bApdwiXGDc-9","name":"FistFull","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/XLG4mhJ23Inu2hE2qhlMV.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"These contributions directly supported institutions engaged in daily feeding programs, elder care, education, and healthcare, ensuring sustained nutritional assistance and contributing to better health outcomes for beneficiaries. The remaining contributions were given to nearby anganwadis.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-21","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing essential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted in the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions that serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups.","aicteMapping":"12","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/6jPLUgEmpj2s3-yeVoXN9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YPaBz6bsoLep6d1PUaG_6","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/dkOYymevAWd3qXfCTFdXF.jfif"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The camp successfully contributed to meeting critical blood requirements for hospitals and emergency care. It also increased awareness about voluntary blood donation and encouraged a spirit of social responsibility among students and staff.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was successfully organized at our college with the objective of promoting social responsibility and awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. The camp was conducted in collaboration with certified medical professionals who ensured a safe, hygienic, and well-managed donation process. Students, faculty members, and staff actively participated in the event, demonstrating compassion and a strong sense of community service. Prior to donation, all participants underwent basic health screening, and proper post-donation care was provided. The camp not only helped meet the critical demand for blood in hospitals but also educated participants about the life-saving impact of donating blood. The event fostered teamwork, empathy, and a spirit of humanitarian service among the college community.","aicteMapping":"10","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/OHvC_YRtd_vda0CpEwTZ5.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QoW1KMCDEMbtX2K9B5MPR","name":"Photgraphy","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/QeI5y_8DrjZQyYCEG00Dh.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Amazing pictures and visual representation of real life problems were addressed.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"SDG Photography Contest organized by SPARK and demonstrated\\nexceptional creativity in promoting the Sustainable Development Goals","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/Bu7JD5cjT-bl7O68fgeIB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KhAcnzVGfyo9fmpEIcDS4","name":"Secret Santa","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/Qs5J_LmOs2NYPKRP22-ag.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Secret Santa event concluded on a joyful, heartwarming, and deeply fulfilling note, leaving lasting smiles on the faces of the children and a strong sense of satisfaction among the volunteers. The combination of gift distribution, cake-cutting celebrations, and meaningful interaction ensured that the children experienced the warmth, happiness, and inclusiveness of Christmas in its truest sense.\\n\\nOrganised by the Rotaract Club of R V College of Engineering, Secret Santa stood out as a meaningful and impactful community service initiative that beautifully blended festive celebration with social responsibility. The enthusiastic participation of volunteers, the cheerful response of the children, and the heartfelt appreciation from the NGOs collectively made the event a memorable and enriching Christmas experience for everyone involved, reinforcing the club’s commitment to service, empathy, and community bonding.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-09","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Secret Santa event was conducted on 25th December, coinciding with Christmas Day, and involved coordinated visits to five NGOs across the city. Volunteers were carefully divided into groups to ensure smooth execution, effective coordination, and meaningful engagement at each location. This structured approach allowed volunteers to spend quality time with the children without rushing activities, ensuring that every interaction felt personal and heartfelt. The NGOs visited included Samartha Trust, Anand Marg Children’s Home, Swavalambi Trust, Sree Manukula Charitable & Educational Trust, and Suprabha Educational & Charitable Trust.\\n\\nAt each NGO, volunteers distributed Christmas gifts to the children, making sure that every child received a present and felt valued. This was followed by a joyful Christmas celebration that included cutting the Christmas cake together with the children, symbolising unity, sharing, and festive togetherness. The cake-cutting moments were filled with excitement, laughter, and cheer, creating memories that extended beyond material gifts.\\n\\nIn addition to this, volunteers engaged the children through interactive games, group activities, and the singing of Christmas carols. These activities encouraged participation, boosted confidence, and brought out genuine smiles and laughter among the children. The festive music, cheerful conversations, and playful interactions transformed each visit into a lively and heartwarming celebration. The consistent presence of volunteers dressed in festive colours further enhanced the Christmas spirit, making the celebrations feel immersive and special rather than formal or routine outreach programmes.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7de73f46-e49e-4f68-9d73-3e4db590db3a/MsIfQON7dVdb-ldEimDqR.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 02:19:20.254597+00', '2026-01-31 05:51:38.139594+00'), ('5107a54a-ccda-489e-be9e-6126420148b8', 'c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65', '{"student":{"usn":"RV22EC109","name":"Pancham Rai","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"f3r1HVASYcRc0ci6SpHOi","name":"SDG  Photography Competition","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/4h1xFhBv10L5GmWM2PS26.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-25","duration":4,"outcomes":"The photography competition enhanced students'' creative expression, visual storytelling abilities, and awareness of global sustainability issues through the lens of the 17 Sustainable Development Goals. It fostered critical thinking about environmental and social challenges while developing participants'' photography skills and artistic sensibilities.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-22","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This photography competition centered on the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), challenging participants to capture and communicate the essence of all 17 SDG themes through visual storytelling. The event was organized by SPARK prefects and drew participation from students across various ability\\nenhancement courses. Throughout the competition, students demonstrated their creative vision and awareness of global sustainability issues, presenting compelling photographic interpretations of themes ranging from poverty alleviation to climate action. The organizers were actively involved in all aspects of the event, including publicity, coordination, evaluation, and shortlisting entries, thereby developing essential leadership, management, and communication skills.","aicteMapping":"Student Development Activity / Co-curricular Activity / Event Organization","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/o9FpjYLXqukJ0i58xuKhj.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"v7rfGEZADlmi3z9art3VF","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/ErQYOwjUVCBof3199pVGq.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive successfully cultivated a culture of social responsibility and humanitarian service among participants. Students gained firsthand experience in contributing to critical healthcare needs while developing empathy and awareness about the ongoing requirement for blood supplies in medical emergencies and treatments.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This blood donation drive was organized in collaboration with the Indira Gandhi Institute of Child Health, Bangalore, as part of a voluntary community service initiative. The camp provided students and staff an opportunity to contribute to society by donating blood to the Blood Transfusion and Immunohaematology Unit, which serves critical healthcare needs in the region.\\n\\nThroughout the event, participants demonstrated compassion and social responsibility by voluntarily stepping forward to donate blood. The drive was coordinated with healthcare professionals from the institute, ensuring proper medical protocols and safety standards were maintained. This initiative not only addressed the urgent need for blood supplies in healthcare facilities but also raised awareness about the importance of regular blood donation in saving lives.","aicteMapping":"Social Service / Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/h-ytqm1MD0ZBOMe2IjYTF.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"u65JOirzxphT5gsZXsob5","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025 successfully instilled values of community service, social responsibility, and active citizenship among participants. Students gained practical experience in collective action for social causes while developing physical fitness and mental resilience through the marathon challenge.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"This community service initiative was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering, focusing on active participation in the Utsarga Marathon 2025. The event provided students an opportunity to engage in meaningful community service while promoting health, fitness, and social awareness.\\n\\nParticipants demonstrated their commitment to social causes by taking part in this marathon, which brought together the college community for a common purpose of service and solidarity. The NSS Programme Officers coordinated the event, ensuring effective organization and maximum student engagement. This initiative aligned with the NSS philosophy of community development and youth empowerment through experiential learning.","aicteMapping":"Sports, Fitness & Wellness Activity","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/Af7XfzTSKbn0J18MhnKyd.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GbUCDLpUui0zOST14gXpn","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp successfully cultivated values of altruism, civic responsibility, and humanitarian service among participants. Students gained firsthand experience in contributing to critical public health needs while developing a deeper understanding of the life-saving importance of voluntary blood donation.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This blood donation camp was organized in collaboration with the Karnataka Sarkara Sparsha Gona Sangha (Government Blood Bank), located at Victoria Hospital, Bangalore. The initiative provided students and staff an opportunity to contribute to the critical need for blood supplies in government healthcare facilities serving the community.\\n\\nThroughout the event, participants voluntarily came forward to donate blood, demonstrating compassion and social responsibility. The camp was conducted with proper medical supervision and adherence to safety protocols established by the government blood bank. This initiative addressed the ongoing requirement for blood in emergency medical situations, surgeries, and treatment of various health conditions.","aicteMapping":"Social Service / Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/KuVF2sOmLXaTQZMOJ6au0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CXFEp6JEegd0Fs904ynj6","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp successfully instilled values of\\ncompassion, humanitarian service, and social responsibility\\namong participants. Students gained meaningful experience in\\ncontributing to life-saving healthcare initiatives while developing\\na deeper appreciation for the critical role of blood donation in\\nmedical emergencies and treatments.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This blood donation initiative was organized in partnership with\\nthe Indian Red Cross Society, Karnataka State Branch, as part of\\na humanitarian service activity. The camp provided participants an\\nopportunity to contribute to the noble cause of saving lives through\\nvoluntary blood donation, aligning with the Red Cross mission of\\n\"Through Humanity to Peace.\"\\nThroughout the event, students and staff demonstrated\\ncompassion and social responsibility by voluntarily donating\\nblood to support the critical healthcare needs of the community.\\nThe camp was conducted under the supervision of Indian Red\\nCross medical professionals, ensuring adherence to international\\nstandards and safety protocols. This initiative addressed the\\nongoing demand for blood supplies in hospitals and medical\\nemergencies across Karnataka.","aicteMapping":"Social Service / Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/IGrxaR7G3LlJNDSDHKXnG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8gy43hWIDGaxZ7bvgBdIa","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully fostered values of community service, social commitment, and active citizenship among participants. Students gained practical experience in combining physical fitness with social causes, developing both personal wellness and a sense of civic responsibility.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":10,"description":"This community service initiative was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering, featuring participation in the Utsarga Marathon with a focus on the K5 KM category. The event provided students an opportunity to engage in meaningful community service while promoting fitness, wellness, and social awareness for a worthy cause.\\n\\nParticipants demonstrated their dedication to social responsibility by actively taking part in this marathon, which combined physical activity with community engagement. The NSS Programme Officers coordinated the event, ensuring effective organization and encouraging maximum student participation. This initiative embodied the NSS philosophy of \"Not Me, But You,\" emphasizing service to society and youth empowerment through experiential learning.","aicteMapping":"Sports, Fitness & Wellness Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/N8fota6ac1U51z74eFDXG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"16xlTbZGVKCu5nkm_z3mY","name":"Energy Literacy Training Program","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-19","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Energy Literacy Training successfully enhanced students''\\nunderstanding of energy conservation principles and sustainable\\npractices. Participants gained comprehensive knowledge about\\nrenewable energy technologies, energy-efficient systems, and\\npractical strategies for reducing energy consumption in daily life.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-18","hoursSpent":24,"description":"This energy conservation initiative was organized in collaboration\\nwith the Department of Electrical and Electronics (EEE) at RVCE,\\nfocusing on comprehensive Energy Literacy Training. The\\nprogram aimed to raise awareness about sustainable energy\\npractices and empower students with knowledge and skills to\\npromote energy efficiency in their communities.\\nThroughout the training, participants engaged in learning about\\nvarious aspects of energy conservation, renewable energy\\ntechnologies, and sustainable practices. The initiative covered\\ncritical topics including energy auditing, efficient resource\\nutilization, and the importance of reducing carbon footprint.\\nStudents were exposed to practical approaches for implementing\\nenergy-saving measures in residential, institutional, and industrial\\nsettings.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/dlrBDSlFMLZjkEsPTiYJK.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"36","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ACd7DoJRRIXGCzvXjEZfA","name":"FistFull","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-25","duration":9,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event successfully cultivated values of empathy,\\ngenerosity, and social responsibility among participants. Students\\ngained meaningful experience in grassroots-level community\\nservice while developing organizational and coordination skills\\nthrough the collection and management of food donations.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This community service initiative was organized by the Rotaract\\nClub of RVCE under the theme \"Unite for Good,\" featuring the\\nflagship event \"Fist Full\" scheduled to commence on November\\n1st, 2025. The program focused on collecting essential food items,\\nspecifically 5 kg rice and/or 2 kg Toor Dal, from students to\\nsupport underprivileged communities.\\nThe donation collection phase ran from November 17th to\\nNovember 25th, 2025, providing students ample opportunity to\\ncontribute voluntarily to this noble cause. The initiative aimed to\\naddress food security challenges while fostering a spirit of\\ncompassion and social responsibility among the college\\ncommunity. Students actively participated in collecting,\\norganizing, and managing the donations under the coordination of\\nRotaract Club members.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/RrejYoHw1W5NnPRZUoYLi.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"56","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gq7EuQFSRHnz-ZKz52OuQ","name":"FistFull","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-22","duration":8,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event successfully cultivated values of empathy,\\ngenerosity, and civic responsibility among participants. Students\\ngained hands-on experience in organizing and executing a large-scale humanitarian initiative while developing essential skills in teamwork, coordination, and community engagement.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This community service initiative was organized by the Rotaract\\nClub of RVCE under the motto \"Strength in Unity, Power in\\nPurpose,\" featuring the event \"Fist Full\" conducted from\\nNovember 18th to November 29th, 2024. The program focused on collecting essential food supplies to support underprivileged\\ncommunities, embodying the spirit of humanitarian service and\\nsocial responsibility.\\nThroughout the event duration, students voluntarily participated in the collection and organization of food donations, demonstrating  compassion and commitment to making a positive impact on society. The initiative was carefully coordinated by Rotaract Club members who managed logistics, publicity, and participant engagement to ensure the success of the campaign.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/gNq4TzvRxr9oglu1qVa7h.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Plb6BnNSC2G2F38A-EJdS","name":"Utsarga Marathon Volunteering","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon volunteering experience successfully\\ninstilled values of selfless service, teamwork, and organizational\\nexcellence among participants. Students gained practical\\nexperience in event management, crisis handling, and public\\ninteraction while developing essential soft skills including\\ncommunication, leadership, and problem-solving abilities.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"This community service initiative was organized under the\\nNational Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering,\\nfocusing on volunteering activities for the Utsarga Marathon. The event provided students an opportunity to contribute to\\ncommunity welfare through active volunteer service, supporting\\nthe successful execution of this large-scale marathon event.\\nThroughout the marathon, student volunteers played crucial roles in various aspects of event management including registration,\\nparticipant coordination, hydration station management, route\\nguidance, crowd control, and logistical support. The NSS\\nProgramme Officers coordinated the volunteer deployment,\\nensuring comprehensive coverage of all event requirements.\\nVolunteers demonstrated dedication, responsibility, and teamwork while facilitating a smooth and safe marathon experience for all\\nparticipants.","aicteMapping":"Student Development  Activity / Co- curricular Activity /  Event Organization","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/pitQoXnUYgpScCEjq5ugr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"35","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"p-DX6aW9diYd16SorrWzp","name":"Nasha Mukth Bharat Pledge","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-08-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Nasha Mukth Bharat Abhiyaan successfully cultivated\\nawareness about drug abuse prevention and fostered a strong\\ncommitment to healthy living among participants. Students gained\\nvaluable knowledge about the physical, mental, and social\\nconsequences of substance addiction while developing a sense of\\npersonal and collective responsibility toward creating a drug-free\\nsociety.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This awareness and pledge initiative was organized under the\\nNational Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering as\\npart of the Nasha Mukth Bharat Abhiyaan (Drug-Free India\\nCampaign). The program aimed to create awareness about the\\nharmful effects of drug abuse and substance addiction while encouraging students to actively commit to a healthy, addiction-\\nfree lifestyle.\\nThroughout this initiative, students participated by taking the\\nofficial Nasha Mukth Bharat pledge through the government\\nportal, formally committing to stay away from drugs and harmful\\nsubstances. Participants also pledged to inspire and influence\\nothers in their families, peer groups, and communities to adopt\\nsimilar values. The activity was coordinated by NSS volunteers\\nwho facilitated registration, guided students through the pledge\\nprocess, and ensured proper documentation of participation.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c718f1f1-e014-42ee-9960-b3a0473fda65/XFIQ5-fT2LZu88bwkBBdn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr Kiran V","designation":"Counsellor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr. H. V. Ravish Aradhya","designation":"Head of Department"},"evaluator2":{"name":" NCC/NSS officer/DSA/Dean CAT","designation":" "}}}', '2026-01-31 06:08:34.088858+00', '2026-02-01 10:39:07.775042+00'), ('52c63ba5-e6d2-4172-b3d4-462ffd9