nd writing emails to students and teachers encouraging them to participate in the event.","aicteMapping":"Helped club organize a marathon","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/573bD_ox_Yll_IZO2fl4w.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9_Vz-0Uom0majN6WwOgbC","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/Q8TBgmS6WtxxFddV-K03p.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event improved physical endurance, mental resilience, and self-discipline among participants. It also enhanced awareness about health, teamwork, and social responsibility, contributing to overall personality development.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Utsarga Marathon was organized to promote physical fitness, healthy lifestyle habits, and community participation among students. The event encouraged active involvement in sports and emphasized the importance of discipline, endurance, and social awareness.","aicteMapping":"Raising funds","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/HboC4kELorzWz-L2mcuu1.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ga09a9PA2TX8xVooNXZvz","name":"Lakshya 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/oYUdPB6SbxEBhjQO2uy6F.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity improved focus, hand–eye coordination, and mental discipline among students. It also reinforced the importance of safety awareness, patience, and self-control, contributing to overall personality development.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":2,"description":"A shooting sports activity was organized where students were given the opportunity to aim and shoot at distant targets under controlled and supervised conditions. The event focused on concentration, discipline, and adherence to safety rules.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/AY49smcrBJkrg649Kilzi.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lWSgO2g7Lqp5qrKcM-EwZ","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/EZl9Zc-w8Gl-6p_feICPU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity developed social responsibility, empathy, and awareness about educational inequality. It also enhanced teamwork, organizational skills, and active involvement in initiatives supporting inclusive education.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Project Pusthak was a social outreach initiative aimed at collecting and distributing books to students in underprivileged and rural areas. The project encouraged knowledge sharing and promoted access to education through community participation.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/zbnQ1XNI13sfOnsmlkxsm.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RMqmy_W0DqOevpRV2kOFK","name":"Mega Plantation","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced environmental consciousness, social responsibility, and teamwork among students. It encouraged sustainable practices and active involvement in initiatives focused on environmental protection.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-25","hoursSpent":5,"description":"A Mega Plantation Drive was organized to promote environmental sustainability and increase green cover through mass participation of students. The event aimed to create awareness about ecological balance and the importance of tree plantation.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/uDTnhesO0JkdEOIkOHi6Q.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GRCGheasXYuUmQIOHSNNQ","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/JBFLWzdiLgxU3V0C3LwLh.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The activity fostered social responsibility, empathy, and awareness of rural needs among students. It encouraged community service, collective participation, and a sense of compassion towards economically disadvantaged sections of society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The “Fist Full” initiative was organized to encourage students to contribute essential food grains by donating 2 kg of toor dal or 5 kg of rice. The collected food items were distributed in rural areas to support underprivileged communities and promote social welfare.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/iOIPgNP_EYtEJuRIFgc-T.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wTJexZk9BQnRZ1TIewDE0","name":"Internship at a Non profit Youth Led Organization ","slNo":11,"place":"Maiti Labs","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-11-18","duration":110,"outcomes":"The internship enhanced understanding of climate action, sustainability practices, and social responsibility. It helped develop professional skills such as teamwork, communication, time management, and practical exposure to working in a non-profit organization.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-01","hoursSpent":80,"description":"I did an internship at Maiti Labs, a non-profit youth-led organization working on climate action. The internship involved contributing to sustainability initiatives and supporting organizational activities over a period of more than 80 hours.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24c93be0-4012-46d7-8c01-5ba305d7008d/UMNA_DNqwQnDJi5bZIsOq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 15:55:15.446842+00', '2026-01-30 18:06:41.788617+00'), ('53dbc63a-a96a-4793-a17d-ce1f77b51ea9', 'aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22ME038","name":"Bhuvan Krishna Reddy P","period":"2022-2026","department":"Mechanical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"tLkI92DiW2_Xmclp-sv81","name":"Shaurya (8th Mile)","slNo":1,"place":"RV College of Engineering ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/oitCbz1ZLFJ9We8gtF4lv.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/IukDDtCgsUJ3An8QLv_s5.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-17","duration":13,"outcomes":"The event created awareness about NCC training and values, encouraged active participation, and fostered teamwork, confidence, and leadership skills among students.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Shaurya (8ᵗʰ Mile 2023) was the flagship NCC event conducted during the college fest. The event included challenges for NCC cadets from various institutions as well as college students, introducing them to NCC-based activities such as weapon training, code and decoding, and obstacle training. The event aimed to promote discipline, leadership, and physical fitness.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":25,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/nR1gChiacsu9zFkbKNkWM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mTGnjklJjW5EI2zJhgjDc","name":"TSC-1","slNo":2,"place":"Siddhaganga Institute of Technology","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/TuudEQSEJYav79wxVPhxL.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/w744ua1HtG1unr9-AD-j3.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-12","duration":11,"outcomes":"The Thal Sainik Camp provided the cadets with intensive exposure to rigorous military training and competitive activities, significantly enhancing their physical fitness, mental resilience, and tactical skills. Participation in various events improved their discipline, leadership abilities, teamwork, and decision-making under pressure. The camp also boosted the cadets’ confidence, sense of responsibility, and competitive spirit, contributing effectively to their overall personality development and preparedness for future leadership roles.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-02","hoursSpent":140,"description":"NCC RVCE cadets participated in the Thal Sainik Camp (TSC) conducted for a duration of 10 days at Siddaganga Institute of Technology. The camp focused on advanced military-oriented training, including weapon training, firing practices, obstacle training, drill, and physical training. Cadets were also evaluated through various competitive events such as drill competitions, map reading, and field craft activities. The camp aimed at developing high standards of discipline, physical endurance, leadership qualities, competitive spirit, and overall personality development among the cadets.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":35,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/mnJz2B8LG-eRrk-vuPO_e.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MfsRVSPJ6SHOdmdLnJ6A9","name":"Major Trek and Cleanliness Drive\\t","slNo":3,"place":"Chikkamagaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/MSRNjsZDFSxxNUaPDEuEP.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/P_jhBjm_xYVkhnxvx26h4.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":3,"outcomes":"Outcome\\tThe Swatch Bharat and Plantation Drive at Narasimha Parvatha resulted in clean trekking trails and the planting of over 100 geotagged saplings to enhance the green cover. It raised awareness among locals and trekkers about cleanliness and environmental conservation. The cadets demonstrated leadership and responsibility by adopting saplings for ongoing care. The event inspired sustainable practices, fostered teamwork, and promoted the importance of maintaining\\necological balance, leaving a lasting positive impact on the environment and participants alike.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-01-26","hoursSpent":30,"description":"NCC RVCE cadets organized a Swatch Bharat and Plantation Drive at Narasimha Parvatha from January 26th to 28th. The event aimed to promote cleanliness and environmental conservation in the Western Ghats. Cadets cleaned trekking trails, collected waste, and ensured its proper disposal to preserve the area''s beauty. A plantation drive was conducted, during which geotagged saplings were planted and assigned to cadets for care. Small teams interacted with locals and trekkers to raise awareness about sustainability. The initiative successfully combined adventure with environmental responsibility, leaving a lasting impact on participants\\nand nature alike.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":7.5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/9-oeOsXEIypmwJoRBTWQh.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"r20sgpCgOyM8gd7OXljuY","name":"Major Trek and Cleanliness Drive","slNo":4,"place":"Gokarna","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/VLe2DEXuIGUHOcm5WMFMj.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/JAFTp9ARMFskWMhoJ8KGE.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":3,"outcomes":"The Swatch Bharat and Plantation resulted in clean trekking trails and the planting of over 100 geotagged saplings to enhance the green cover. It raised awareness among locals and trekkers about cleanliness and environmental conservation. The cadets demonstrated leadership and responsibility by adopting saplings for ongoing care. The event inspired sustainable practices, fostered teamwork, and promoted the importance of maintaining ecological balance, leaving a lasting positive impact on the environment and participants alike.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-10","hoursSpent":30,"description":"NCC RVCE cadets organized a Swatch Bharat and Plantation Drive at Gokarna from January 10th to 12th. The event aimed to promote cleanliness and environmental conservation in the beaches. Cadets cleaned trekking trails, collected waste, and ensured its proper disposal to preserve the area''s beauty. A plantation drive was conducted, during which geotagged saplings were planted and assigned to cadets for care. Small teams interacted with locals and trekkers to raise awareness about sustainability. The initiative successfully combined adventure with environmental responsibility, leaving a lasting impact on participants and nature alike.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":7.5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/gFM4CUUu9uYdlqZGUDDPi.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HpJ14AeywLxMWg2L4FGkq","name":"CATC - RMS","slNo":5,"place":"Rasthriya Military School","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/9YEdp9Rticalh_CkD5NhD.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/l6ado9i9K0PFElY4YmaVP.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-05-17","duration":10,"outcomes":"The camp significantly improved physical endurance, discipline, and leadership qualities among the cadets. NCC RVCE cadets showcased outstanding performance by winning multiple medals in group song, group dance, and volleyball events, bringing laurels to the unit and fostering team spirit and confidence.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-05-08","hoursSpent":140,"description":"NCC RVCE cadets participated in the Combined Annual Training Camp (CATC) conducted for a duration of 10 days at Rashtriya Military School. The camp included regular parade training, physical training, drills, and various inter-unit competitions such as group song, group dance, and sports events including volleyball. The camp aimed at enhancing discipline, leadership, teamwork, and overall personality development of the cadets.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":35,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/aa83bd10-08dd-4963-94ab-9fc63e483aa7/zxsYedXDrsyIc-tQAZRFo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:47:23.411118+00', '2026-01-29 18:41:35.702503+00'), ('55661034-d996-44da-bfb0-392b328da86e', '85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD022","name":"Kiran R Aithal","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"UbIw-eu4oA0Cno4UrwiOU","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/8Rp170uu3HsW6QrxpZYEa.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in Project Pustak, I gained a strong sense of social responsibility and satisfaction from contributing towards the education of underprivileged rural students. I understood the real impact that even small contributions can create when combined for a meaningful cause. This activity helped me develop empathy and awareness about the difficulties faced by students who lack basic school resources. I also gained exposure to community service initiatives and learned the importance of teamwork and collective effort in successfully carrying out a donation-based project. Overall, the experience was rewarding as it allowed me to support a noble cause and contribute directly to creating a better learning environment for deserving students. ","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students living in rural areas. Under this project, a contribution was collected from each donor, and the funds raised were used to procure and donate much-needed educational materials. The collected amount was utilized to purchase resources such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other important school supplies that help create a better and more supportive learning environment for deserving students. The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, undertook the responsibility of procuring and distributing these essential supplies to ensure meaningful educational support for the beneficiaries. The initiative went beyond mere material distribution; it served as a significant morale booster for the students, encouraging them to pursue their studies with renewed vigor. Volunteers visited the schools personally to hand over the kits, fostering a sense of solidarity and community connection between the college students and the rural youth. This hands-on engagement provided the team with deep insights into the challenges faced by government schools while highlighting how collective student efforts can effectively bridge the gap in educational resources.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/-wDv4RCUTAMKUHyujdb0K.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NA9xQw0ZKqyXHYFoHtzr3","name":"Utsarga 2023","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/W29wZQnaWJ2c5BePcTmXq.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need. Overall, \\nthis activity contributed both to my NSS activity progress and my personal development. Moreover, the experience tested my mental resilience, teaching me to push past physical fatigue to reach the finish line. It also provided a unique platform to network with like-minded peers who share a commitment to fitness and social welfare, reinforcing the habit of maintaining a healthy lifestyle.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on April 6th, 2025, from 6:00 AM  at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based registration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create awareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness activity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community impact. The event witnessed a vibrant atmosphere filled with enthusiasm as hundreds of participants, including faculty and local residents, gathered at the starting line to champion the cause. Volunteers were strategically stationed along the route to ensure safety, manage hydration counters, and cheer on the runners, creating a supportive and energetic environment. The proceeds from the registration fees were directly channelled towards educational NGOs, ensuring that every step taken by the runners translated into a tangible opportunity for an underprivileged child.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/ftiXZO5bNhzV4cEMmU27j.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wInecwgVN3qbHaZYf4QH3","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":3,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/jHxD68sEsSjdApdnq6gfT.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense of environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by reporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped improve my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Kunagal Betta Hills, and it also enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group of participants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved my fitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature. \\nFurthermore, witnessing the tangible impact of sustainable tourism taught me how recreational activities can be effectively combined with social responsibility to preserve our heritage sites.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated to preserving the environment. Armed with waste collection bags, the student volunteers diligently cleared plastic waste and litter along the trail, ensuring the natural beauty of the hills was restored. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus to the trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the adventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all attendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagal Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding success, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breath taking landscapes. Over 750 individuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s vibrant atmosphere.","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/_18-ISzHuDCRI5L4Bz5wS.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Vr5dP-wuFh_u2NGWdSzK9","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/xEuoYY0rcHXaMDPgSZGp6.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in this donation drive, I contributed directly to community welfare by supporting the collection of essential food items for those in need. I gained a \\nstronger sense of social responsibility and empathy by being part of an initiative that emphasized solidarity and helping others through collective effort. The activity also helped me understand \\nhow even small individual contributions can lead to large-scale impact when students come together for a cause. Furthermore, being involved in the collection process gave me practical \\ninsight into the logistics of resource mobilization and the importance of organized packaging in humanitarian relief efforts. Overall, this experience strengthened my awareness of community service and reinforced the importance of actively participating in welfare-oriented initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":10,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. Student volunteers played a crucial role in meticulously weighing, packing, and segregating the donations to ensure they were ready for immediate distribution to the partner beneficiaries. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. The collected grains were subsequently distributed to orphanages and care homes, directly addressing the issue of hunger in the community. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/Lwy4pSGjTSCWvTXkhKSIb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xpZQDsqEU0a_Kt7DNJzMo","name":"Swachhata Pakhwada 2023 ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/3LgwnkyY3gdIvgS9rnUyK.png"],"endDate":"2023-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Swachhata Pakhwada, I gained practical experience in community service by actively contributing to cleaning and maintaining the campus environment. This activity strengthened my sense of responsibility toward hygiene and public cleanliness and helped me understand the importance of environmental stewardship. I also developed teamwork and coordination skills by working with other volunteers and students to complete the drive effectively. Participating in this drive also instilled a long-term behavioural change in me regarding waste management. I became more conscious of my own ecological footprint and encouraged my peers to adopt a ''zero-litter'' approach in their daily lives, ensuring the impact of the campaign extended beyond just a single day. Overall, the initiative increased my awareness about cleanliness as a social duty and motivated me to continue participating in activities that contribute positively to society and the environment.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-10-01","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Swachhata Pakhwada was organized on October 1st as an important cleanliness initiative aligned with the Swachh Bharat Abhiyan. The event was graced by the presence of the AICTE Chairperson, who delivered an inspiring speech emphasizing the importance of hygiene, cleanliness, and social responsibility. Volunteers, along with Rotaract members and students, actively collaborated to clean the college premises and surrounding areas. Armed with brooms, gloves, and waste collection bags, the student volunteers were divided into teams to ensure comprehensive coverage of the designated areas. Special emphasis was placed on waste segregation at the source, separating dry recyclables from organic waste to promote sustainable disposal practices. The program aimed to promote cleanliness on campus while strengthening community spirit and encouraging students to participate in socially responsible initiatives.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/H3D9oyxJrb50GJwafeMG9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"53d4ZGGPlP0C1Xuu4OFsI","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/cTX-53CMQcy0EwE1W8deY.png"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Rush Hours 5.0, I significantly improved my ability to work effectively within a team under the pressure of a multi-day competitive environment. The diverse range of tasks helped me refine my problem-solving and strategic thinking skills, particularly during the fast-paced \"Cyber Chase\" and the \"Social Showdown\" engagement rounds. I also gained experience in creative communication and social awareness by developing content for social causes and DIY challenges. Furthermore, the elimination-based structure of the event taught me the importance of consistency, discipline, and adaptability. Overall, the activity provided a rewarding experience that enhanced my organizational skills, boosted my confidence in presenting creative ideas, and strengthened my peer-to-peer networking within the college community. Additionally, navigating the digital challenges honed my digital literacy and taught me how to leverage technology for effective storytelling and audience engagement, a skill crucial in today''s tech-driven world.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":16,"description":"Rush Hours 5.0 was a high-spirited, five-day event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE that brought together over 450 participants for a series of interactive and competitive challenges. The event was designed to foster teamwork, problem-solving skills, and healthy competition through a gradual elimination process that kept teams motivated. Participants engaged in diverse tasks including \"Cyber Chase\" (an online treasure hunt), \"Capture the Cause\" (social issue awareness through art), \"Beyond the Frame\" (performance-based videos), \"DIY Wear It!\" (crafting accessories), and \"The Social Showdown\" (social media engagement). This multi-day initiative provided a dynamic platform for students to showcase their creativity, technical expertise, and collaborative spirit. The event’s seamless integration of digital platforms for the treasure hunt and social media campaigns required participants to effectively utilize various software tools, successfully bridging the gap between technical proficiency and creative expression.","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/1ZI-NcQNN27mjUoF20duI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pPTbSWT-K8bkC5r4f9XBa","name":"Utsarga 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/RTbAi-gsG8o89zRMzf-8Q.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need. Beyond the physical benefits, the event fostered a strong sense of community spirit as I ran alongside peers united for a common cause. It reinforced the importance of consistency in my fitness regime and demonstrated how sports platforms can be effectively utilized to drive positive social change.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on February 4th, 2024, \\nfrom 6:00 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based registration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create awareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness activity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community impact. The event was marked by high energy and enthusiastic participation from the student body and local \\ncommunity. Volunteers managed the route efficiently, providing water stations and medical aid, ensuring a safe run for everyone. The collective effort resulted in a significant contribution to the partner NGOs, successfully fulfilling the event''s dual goal of fitness and philanthropy.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/jOxRvq8nr6pAa8RoEtOjr.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RLzRK4_HdhRHHEpB7zdBI","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/8WrMSeXAAOPUd7QYcGDJ1.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in this awareness campaign, I gained a comprehensive understanding of the electoral process and the critical importance of youth participation in democracy. The activity helped me realize how an informed electorate is the backbone of a progressive nation. I developed better civic awareness and learned about the ethical responsibilities associated with casting a vote. Additionally, engaging with the campaign improved my communication skills as I helped spread awareness to my peers about voter registration and democratic rights. Overall, the experience instilled a deeper sense of patriotism and social responsibility, motivating me to remain an active and informed citizen.","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The \"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye\" (My First Vote for the Country) was an awareness-driven initiative organized by NSS RVCE to encourage and educate first-time voters on the importance of electoral participation. The activity focused on highlighting the role of the youth in shaping the nation''s future through their democratic right to vote. Participants were engaged in discussions regarding the voting process, the significance of informed decision-making, and the impact of individual votes on national governance. The campaign aimed to foster a sense of civic duty among students and ensure they are prepared to contribute responsibly to the democratic process. To make the session interactive, students actively participated in an online quiz designed to test their knowledge of the Indian Constitution and electoral history. Furthermore, the event concluded with a collective pledge-taking ceremony, where young voters formally committed to exercising their franchise ethically, thereby reinforcing the spirit of democracy on campus.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/rx-47oUJ0Bmd3gj7ttwAi.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Sf3hd-3mRAerJIhv20lAm","name":"Data Remix","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/O4B9-HEj1kGN90vUZkfkS.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Data Remix, I significantly enhanced my technical proficiency in data analysis and visualization by interpreting complex datasets under time constraints. The competition improved my ability to derive actionable insights and present technical findings to an expert panel. By working on solutions aligned with the UN’s Sustainable Development Goals, I developed a deeper understanding of how to integrate sustainable thinking into business innovation and technological progress. Additionally, working in a team environment strengthened my collaborative skills and my ability to think holistically about real-world challenges. Overall, the experience bridge the gap between academic learning and practical industry applications in the field of AI and Data Science.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The DHI DAY was a technical event organized by Team DHI, a student initiative from the Department of AIML at RVCE, in collaboration with GE Healthcare. The flagship event, \"Data \\nRemix,\" was a two-phase competition focused on Data Analysis and Business Innovation. In the first phase, teams of up to four students used provided pre-processed datasets to create data \\nvisualizations and present inferences to a panel of judges. The second phase required students to develop sustainable business solutions aligned with the UN’s Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The event aimed to promote a revolutionary mindset that balances technical advancement with environmental and technological sustainability. Operating under the theme ''Clash of Companies,'' the competition simulated a real-world corporate environment where participants acted as business analysts for assigned organizations. The presence of industry experts from GE Healthcare as judges added a layer of professional rigor, offering students a unique opportunity to receive constructive feedback on their analytical models and strategic proposals.","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/tu8yaMqFb76mFx0RcmIUB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"V0VHTgiM1TiIRU1h8xCrF","name":"Cheela Mela","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/ZQlFjb8a69aPRurf5xhUV.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the Eco bag Initiative, I successfully crafted 200 newspaper bags, directly contributing to the reduction of single-use plastic in local markets. This activity helped me develop a practical understanding of sustainable alternatives and the importance of community-driven environmental solutions. I gained hands-on experience in manual crafting and learned how small, collective efforts can lead to a significant social impact. Additionally, managing the production of a large quantity of bags improved my discipline, time management, and commitment to social service. Overall, the experience strengthened my sense of environmental responsibility and civic duty toward creating a more sustainable community.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-20","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The Eco bag Initiative, also known as \"Cheela Mela,\" was a sustainability-focused project organized by NSS RVCE in collaboration with EMPRI. The primary goal was to craft newspaper bags to be distributed to street vendors at K R Market, providing a biodegradable alternative to plastic and supporting a greener environment. Participants were tasked with crafting durable paper bags following specific guidelines to ensure they were suitable for commercial use. The initiative allowed students to contribute to environmental preservation through hands-on volunteerism, either by crafting bags onsite at the Environment Lab or at home. To ensure the bags were sturdy enough for daily use, participants followed a structured video tutorial that demonstrated the precise folding and pasting techniques required. The completed batches were collected at the Environment Lab in the Civil Department, symbolizing a collective effort to turn waste paper into a valuable, eco-friendly resource for the city''s vendors.","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/v9Ow_MTkvchxViEWm3K5N.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hfUni6PvPhUZLLsakdPj-","name":"Paper Drive 2024","slNo":11,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/lt289SU6GE7dq0vaLnCkc.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Paper Drive, I actively contributed to a large-scale resource mobilization effort that benefited multiple charitable organizations. The experience of going door-to-door helped me develop better interpersonal and communication skills while interacting with diverse residents and business owners. I gained a deeper understanding of community involvement and the practical logistics of managing waste materials for a social cause. This activity also reinforced my commitment to environmental sustainability and social responsibility. Overall, the initiative provided a meaningful platform to address social issues through collective student engagement and volunteerism.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":10,"description":"On 23rd June 2024, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a \"Paper Drive\" involving over 400 student volunteers who collected books, papers, and waste materials across various areas of Bangalore. Volunteers started early in the morning, going door-to-door and visiting local businesses to gather donations. The primary objective was to collect resources for charities and NGOs to support their initiatives and assist people in need. Beyond resource collection, the drive served as a community awareness program to foster social responsibility among both the participants and the residents of Bangalore. Crucially, the drive also served a major environmental purpose by diverting tons of paper waste from landfills and channelling it into proper recycling streams, thereby promoting sustainable waste management practices among the local residents.","aicteMapping":"10","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/giuKaTq-1Z4WTMjs77EuA.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NYYfzv-UqAz86yHQXezJZ","name":"AEC Plantation 1","slNo":12,"place":"Bengaluru University ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/P6HIeEKOrCPnS7UWRpMAD.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-22","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the AEC Plantation, I contributed to the enhancement of the Bio Park''s natural environment and developed a practical understanding of reforestation techniques. The activity helped me realize the importance of individual contributions to environmental sustainability and the role of the youth in combating climate change at a local level. I gained hands-on experience in manual labour and teamwork while coordinating with peers to ensure the successful planting of saplings. Overall, the experience strengthened my commitment to environmental responsibility and provided a meaningful connection to nature.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-22","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The AEC Plantation 1 was an environmental conservation initiative focused on improving green cover. Held at the University Bio-Park campus, near the Gandhi Research Centre, participants worked under the guidance of student organizers to plant saplings and learn about local biodiversity. The event aimed to promote environmental stewardship among engineering students and address local ecological concerns through direct action. Activities included preparing the soil, planting various species of trees, and understanding the long-term maintenance required for successful reforestation efforts. This hands-on experience not only enhanced the aesthetic appeal of the area but also instilled a sense of shared responsibility among the students. By actively engaging in the physical labour of afforestation, participants recognized that combating climate change begins with small, local steps.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/ZkgtTnBheuaklHIlupp5G.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"SoVjqqps38xyb8uep0h-o","name":"Nasha Mukta Bharat Abhiyan","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/sNQgnVV2qwYRc2_Yjv9TN.png"],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in this pledge-taking ceremony, I have formally committed to a drug-free lifestyle and gained a deeper understanding of the societal impact of substance abuse. This \\nactivity reinforced my sense of personal and social responsibility toward maintaining a healthy environment within the college campus and the broader community. I learned about the significance of national health initiatives and how individual commitments contribute to the overall goal of a \"Khushaal Bharat\" (Prosperous India). Overall, the experience instilled a \\nstronger sense of discipline and motivated me to advocate for healthy, addiction-free living among my peers.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The \"Nasha Mukta Bharat, Khushaal Bharat\" (Drug-Free India, Prosperous India) initiative was an awareness program organized by NSS RVCE to combat drug abuse among the youth. As part of this national campaign by the Government of India, participants took a formal pledge to \"Say No to Drugs\" and committed to staying away from drug abuse to lead a healthy and sober lifestyle. The activity aimed to create a strong moral stance against substance abuse within the student community and promote the values of health, sobriety, and national prosperity. The session also included an interactive discussion on the detrimental effects of addiction on mental and physical well-being, fostering open dialogue among peers. To mark the occasion, every participant who took the pledge received a digital certificate from the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, serving as a lasting reminder of their commitment to the cause.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/QvlYU2ZmMt7Gku3XJPudE.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oEVsfF4bXmuu5F_PTWvXm","name":"Paper Drive 2023","slNo":14,"place":"Vijayanagar","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/PaXWOYiXFy3GoK512WGYz.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the Paper Drive, I contributed to a massive resource-gathering effort that successfully collected over 7 tonnes of recyclable paper. I gained hands-on experience in large-scale event logistics and community outreach while working alongside a diverse team of 500 volunteers. The activity helped me develop stronger communication and interpersonal skills as I interacted with the public to gather donations for a social cause. Most importantly, I learned how coordinated student initiatives can directly translate into financial support for charitable organizations like the Nele Narendra Foundation. Overall, the experience reinforced my understanding of community development and the positive impact of environmental recycling on social welfare.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Paper Drive was a mega event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to support orphanages and underprivileged individuals. With the support of over 500 volunteers, the team \\nassembled at Kriyakalpa, RVCE at 8:00 AM before being transported to various localities across Bengaluru. Over the course of 10 hours, volunteers collected more than 7 tonnes of old newspapers, books, magazines, and waste papers. The primary objective of the drive was to raise funds by selling these collected materials to paper vendors, with all proceeds donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation for the welfare of the needy. Beyond the fundraising aspect, the drive fostered a strong connection between the students and the city''s residents, as volunteers went door-to-door to spread awareness about the cause. The massive collection effort also contributed \\nsignificantly to environmental sustainability by ensuring that tons of paper waste were sent for recycling rather than ending up in landfills.","aicteMapping":"10","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/85a192c8-89b7-4275-a14e-4de7e3e43c33/yy6x0SEP8CgwAJnn186FI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-30","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Prof. Rajatha","designation":"  Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Evaluator 1","designation":" "},"evaluator2":{"name":"Evaluator 2","designation":" "}}}', '2026-01-30 13:42:24.340427+00', '2026-01-31 15:10:10.30756+00'), ('58a59133-3fe1-40a8-960c-cd9abddc30fa', '8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22AI027","name":"Mishael Abhishek Zakkam","period":"2022-2026","department":"Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"4zi5ZZCBi-hHKHwYz89nS","name":"Fast-Trek","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/d-fjyUw5UDcah4ujWUkZR.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/xpxaIgHPomPNoO_cyGeDj.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in FAST TREK was a highly rewarding experience, especially being part of a large and enthusiastic group of over 750 students. The scale of the event created a strong sense of unity and excitement among all participants, making the trek both engaging and memorable. The cleanliness drive conducted during the trek at Huthridurga Hills helped us become more aware of the importance of responsible tourism and environmental conservation, as we actively contributed to keeping the natural surroundings clean. The event was well organized, with smooth transportation, clear instructions, and constant support from volunteers, which allowed us to focus on enjoying the trek without any confusion or safety concerns. Overall, the experience not only provided a refreshing outdoor adventure but also encouraged personal growth, teamwork, and a deeper sense of responsibility toward the environment.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"FAST TREK, a flagship event conducted by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 12th February 2023, was an enriching experience that combined environmental responsibility with physical fitness and adventure. As a participant, the day began early at 7:30 AM, when all registered members assembled on campus and boarded the buses arranged by the organizing team to travel to Huthridurga Hills, a scenic trekking destination near Bengaluru.\\n\\nUpon arrival, we were welcomed by the organizing volunteers and provided with a detailed briefing on the trekking route, safety precautions, and the purpose of the event. The board members and volunteers ensured that all participants were aware of the environmental goals of the trek, particularly the cleanliness drive aimed at preserving the natural beauty of Huthridurga Hills. Safety instructions, including hydration, pacing, and group movement, were clearly communicated, which helped us feel confident and well-prepared for the trek ahead.\\n\\nAs we began the ascent, the volunteers actively guided different groups along the trail, ensuring that everyone stayed on the designated paths and moved at a safe and comfortable pace. The coordination between teams was evident, as any logistical or participant-related issues were handled promptly through continuous communication. Along the way, participants took part in collecting litter and maintaining the cleanliness of the trekking area, reinforcing the event’s core message of environmental awareness.\\n\\nOverall, FAST TREK was a well-organized and impactful experience that allowed us, as participants, to contribute meaningfully to nature conservation while also enjoying a physically engaging outdoor activity. The professionalism and dedication of the Rotaract Club of RVCE made the event both memorable and successful.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1ca0Jjrxr-pF1dGTzEi0-","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/JLgIh1gAdPk0pAcrkqMJH.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The camp received an encouraging response from students and faculty, resulting in the successful collection of a significant number of blood units. The initiative helped strengthen awareness about the continuous need for blood in hospitals and emergency care. It instilled a sense of empathy, civic responsibility, and social commitment among participants. Overall, the event reinforced the value of collective effort in supporting healthcare systems and serving the community.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp organized in 2023 was a community-oriented initiative aimed at promoting voluntary blood donation and spreading awareness about its importance in saving lives. The event was conducted with the support of certified medical professionals and volunteers who ensured a safe, hygienic, and well-regulated donation process. Participants were guided through registration, medical screening, donation, and recovery procedures in a structured manner. The camp created a supportive environment where students and staff could contribute to a noble cause while learning about health, responsibility, and social service.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LeBDvNVNQtetLgw9fmmBp","name":"DHI Day- Data Remix","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/sv6iH76lU1lS-bBt2m18A.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/6VYCCtKpk1An1euiebc6F.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event witnessed active participation from students across multiple semesters of RV College of Engineering, reflecting strong engagement with interdisciplinary learning and innovation. DHI DAY successfully fostered analytical thinking, teamwork, and practical application of data science concepts while encouraging solutions aligned with the United Nations’ Sustainable Development Goals. From an organizational standpoint, the event strengthened coordination, leadership, and event management skills among the core team and volunteers, particularly in handling large-scale academic events under strict time constraints. The collaboration with GE Healthcare added significant industry relevance, enhancing the overall impact of the event. The successful execution of DHI DAY established a strong foundation for future technical initiatives by Team DHI and reinforced the department’s commitment to experiential learning and sustainable innovation.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":16,"description":"DHI DAY was a technical event organized by Team DHI, the technical club initiative by the students of the Department of Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning at RV College of Engineering, in collaboration with GE Healthcare. The event was conducted on 6th March 2024 and was structured to promote data-driven thinking, business innovation, and sustainable technological solutions. The program began with an expert speaker session hosted by GE Healthcare in the IEM Auditorium from 9:00 AM to 1:00 PM, followed by the flagship competition, Data Remix, conducted from 1:30 PM to 6:30 PM. Data Remix was designed as a multi-phase competition involving teams of up to four participants, where students worked on data analysis and data visualization using provided datasets. The event emphasized real-world problem solving, with participants presenting insights and optimization strategies to a panel of esteemed judges, including industry professionals and faculty members. Throughout the event, the organizing team coordinated logistics, participant management, judging schedules, and smooth transitions between sessions to ensure seamless execution.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jaJstDrNiGPkF8D1PoMc1","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/V3NzWYHuPPxSWGvJ-fYt4.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The camp witnessed active participation and demonstrated the willingness of students to contribute toward a meaningful social cause. It helped participants understand the medical and social importance of blood donation and reduced common fears and misconceptions associated with it. The event enhanced teamwork and volunteer coordination while strengthening the institution’s role in community welfare. Overall, it contributed to building a compassionate and socially responsible student community.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp held in 2024 focused on strengthening community health support by encouraging voluntary and ethical blood donation among students and staff. The event was conducted in collaboration with trained medical personnel who ensured strict adherence to safety and hygiene standards. Volunteers coordinated participant flow, assisted donors, and maintained smooth operations throughout the camp. The initiative aimed to create awareness about the life-saving impact of blood donation while fostering a culture of service and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0aRvmlyi-eZBHHtu5OkBs","name":"Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/zLWuZlfzzH2XgGTe1xZ6T.png"],"endDate":"2024-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Taking the pledge under the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan strengthened my awareness of the physical, mental, and social consequences of substance abuse. It reinforced my commitment to maintaining a healthy lifestyle and encouraged me to act as a responsible citizen who can positively influence peers and the community. The initiative also instilled a sense of accountability and moral responsibility, emphasizing that collective individual actions are essential in building a drug-free society. Overall, the activity promoted self-reflection, social consciousness, and alignment with national efforts toward public health and youth empowerment.","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-08-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":"As part of the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan, I took a pledge on 14th August 2025 committing to say no to drugs and substance abuse. This initiative aimed to raise awareness about the harmful effects of drug addiction and to promote a healthy, responsible, and addiction-free lifestyle among individuals, especially the youth. By taking this pledge, I consciously acknowledged the importance of personal discipline, mental well-being, and social responsibility in contributing to a drug-free society. The activity served as a reminder of the role individuals play in shaping a healthier nation through informed choices and positive behavior.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gkRdVSmI9pIYyzLUqhz97","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/VlPBcplH8Op0TuDQsWukV.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/EOv7sAjukX5330BhNBHi-.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The Fist Full initiative received an overwhelming response from the student community, resulting in the collection of over 6,700 kg of rice and more than 800 kg of toor dal, donated by approximately 1,750 students. This large-scale participation highlighted the effectiveness of collective action in addressing societal challenges such as hunger. The project reinforced values of empathy, responsibility, and community service among participants, while also strengthening collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Rotary Bangalore Spandana. Overall, the initiative demonstrated how small individual contributions can come together to create significant social impact, further reinforcing RVCE’s commitment to community welfare and social responsibility.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Fist Full was a socially impactful initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November. The project aimed at addressing hunger and food insecurity by encouraging students to contribute basic food essentials as part of a collective effort toward social welfare. Students were invited to donate either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily collection drives carried out at the Civil Department. The initiative was structured to make participation simple and accessible, allowing a large number of students to contribute meaningfully. Through consistent coordination and volunteer support, the project successfully mobilized the student community toward a shared humanitarian goal, reflecting the spirit of service and solidarity promoted by the institution.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3azB_BOXial16p3gLNITV","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":7,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/5huuQkYlYUaFn0ZVN5cPU.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The UTSARGA Marathon successfully created awareness about social responsibility and community service while promoting a healthy and active lifestyle among students. The event encouraged participants to adopt fitness as a regular habit and understand the importance of contributing to meaningful social causes. Through their involvement, students developed a strong sense of discipline, perseverance, teamwork, and civic responsibility. The marathon also strengthened community engagement and highlighted the impact of collective participation in social welfare initiatives. Overall, the activity supported the holistic development of students and aligned with the objectives of NSS and AICTE in fostering socially responsible and health-conscious individuals.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The UTSARGA Marathon was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, as a social service and fitness-oriented initiative aimed at promoting community welfare and social responsibility. The event encouraged students to actively participate in a marathon conducted for a worthy cause, emphasizing physical fitness, discipline, and commitment to societal development. Participants \\ncompeted in different distance categories, including the 5 km category, demonstrating enthusiasm and dedication toward the objective of the event.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"81djdtFcP-c_Cgu0duPrJ","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/eWvf07_MXf4PNvRy8WG0_.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-26","duration":5,"outcomes":"The activity successfully contributed to improving access to \\neducational resources for underprivileged rural students. It \\npromoted social responsibility, empathy, and community \\nengagement among the volunteers involved. By supporting \\nstudents with essential learning materials, the initiative helped \\nreduce barriers to education and encouraged continued schooling. \\nThe project aligned with the objectives of experiential learning \\nand community development by creating a positive social impact \\nwhile fostering a sense of civic duty among participants. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":2,"description":"\\nProject Pustak was a social outreach initiative aimed at providing \\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in \\nrural areas. The activity involved mobilizing voluntary \\ncontributions from donors, with a nominal amount collected from \\neach participant to support the cause. The funds raised were \\nsystematically utilized to procure necessary educational materials \\nsuch as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other basic \\nlearning resources. The initiative focused on addressing \\neducational inequity by ensuring that students had access to \\nessential supplies required for a conducive learning environment. ","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/IhJabzfK8xo4tq7lLODvC.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wI0iaXT3GXpujnnXWjuHN","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/-XFK1ANmn5ZJ8iXNmCL5c.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully encouraged students to participate in humanitarian service, strengthening awareness about the role of blood donation in emergency medical care. It helped develop a sense of responsibility, empathy, and social consciousness among participants. The coordinated efforts of volunteers and donors resulted in a well-executed event that contributed positively to the healthcare needs of the community. The camp reinforced the idea that small individual actions can make a life-saving difference.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp conducted in 2025 was organized to support healthcare institutions and promote a culture of selfless service among the student community. The event followed a systematic process involving donor registration, health screening, supervised donation, and post-donation care. Medical professionals ensured the safety of all donors, while volunteers facilitated smooth coordination and maintained a positive and encouraging environment. The camp emphasized the importance of regular blood donation as a vital contribution to public health.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Jq40WbXqr2YVYDgC7-pOZ","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/-EKSK4S79hJkS5Qlurn-7.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/vag5s_ngr8bvGlmOOy631.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/tXT4ysLFVp4VSz0fkBDVG.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/9dLCnEyWNxTB3UB4yjgZh.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"Participating in Fist Full helped me develop a deeper understanding of food security issues and the role students can play in creating social impact. The initiative reinforced values of empathy, social responsibility, and collective action, as I witnessed how contributions from a large number of students came together to support disadvantaged groups, including children, the elderly, and patients in need. The experience also strengthened my sense of civic duty and encouraged continued involvement in community-oriented activities. Overall, the initiative demonstrated the power of small, consistent actions in driving meaningful change and contributing to the well-being of society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in Fist Full, a community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of addressing food insecurity through collective student contribution. The initiative encouraged students to donate either 5 kilograms of rice or 2 kilograms of toor dal, making it a simple yet impactful way for individuals to support vulnerable communities. As a participant, I found the concept meaningful as it transformed small individual contributions into a larger effort aimed at supporting health and care institutions. The event created a sense of shared responsibility among students and highlighted the importance of community service in addressing societal challenges such as hunger.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"name":"8th Mile Team","place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/boVZWe97IwlWkbsKcn4le.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8a0fdda7-a7e1-42d0-9dc0-4b444daabb72/erCDzSMpBE3IBKS-ATCfe.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"The collective dedication and coordinated efforts of the Core Team and Volunteers resulted in the successful execution of the 8th Mile initiative, demonstrating strong organizational discipline and teamwork. The experience significantly enhanced students’ leadership, communication, time management, and problem-solving skills while working under real-world constraints. Active involvement in planning and execution improved participants’ confidence and sense of responsibility, preparing them for future professional and organizational roles. The initiative also strengthened student–faculty collaboration and contributed to holistic development by promoting teamwork, accountability, and experiential learning. Overall, the program stood as a meaningful learning platform that aligned with the institution’s vision of academic excellence and character building.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":50,"description":"The 8th Mile Committee was a large-scale student-driven initiative organized at RV College of Engineering with the objective of fostering leadership, teamwork, and experiential learning through coordinated event planning and execution. The Core Team and Volunteers worked under the guidance of the Steering Committee, Staff Coordinators, and Student Convenors to ensure the smooth functioning of the initiative. The committee was responsible for handling multiple aspects of the event, including logistics, communication, participant management, cultural coordination, documentation, and real-time problem solving. Continuous interaction with faculty coordinators and administrative authorities ensured that all processes followed institutional guidelines and maintained professional standards. The collaborative efforts of the team enabled seamless planning, effective execution, and successful completion of all assigned responsibilities, making the initiative a well-organized and impactful student-led event.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":20,"certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23"},{}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Somesh Nandi","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 07:37:46.580824+00', '2026-02-02 05:38:11.432764+00'), ('58d7824e-7e40-4b5a-96e5-38c011dc5ac4', 'b702c130-e362-41d8-a0ec-921e2189607a', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:59:30.095739+00', '2026-01-31 15:58:02.187325+00'), ('5b8492ea-3ad6-4b8a-9ada-b192e4e28be2', '62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY048","name":"S Jeevan","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"l_B8U6gegCp1gnSMG0mPa","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh  Keliye ","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/dr1hpIHMVpbAcoyjfJsZE.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/t5OLKZ8Hpvk00n_JYXUkW.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity successfully enhanced awareness among students regarding the importance of voting and active participation in the democratic process. It helped students recognize voting not only as a right but also as a fundamental responsibility of every citizen.\\n\\nA significant number of students expressed interest in registering themselves as voters and gaining a better understanding of their electoral rights and duties. The program encouraged young individuals to become informed and responsible voters, thereby contributing to the strengthening of democratic values in the nation.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) unit organized an awareness activity titled “Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” with the objective of encouraging young voters to understand the importance of voting and active participation in the democratic process. The program aimed to motivate first-time voters to exercise their voting rights responsibly and to spread awareness about the value of each vote in building a strong and progressive nation.\\n\\nThe activity was conducted on the college campus, where NSS volunteers educated students about the voter registration process, the role of elections in a democracy, and the importance of informed voting. The session emphasized how youth participation plays a crucial role in strengthening democratic values.\\n\\nVarious awareness methods were used to engage students effectively, including speeches, poster displays, slogan writing, and interactive discussions. Volunteers highlighted key themes such as responsible citizenship, ethical voting practices, and the power of youth in shaping the future of the country.\\n\\nThe event also provided a platform for students to share their views on democracy and their responsibilities as citizens. Participants actively interacted with the volunteers and clarified their doubts regarding the voting procedure. Overall, the activity successfully increased awareness and inspired students to become conscious, responsible voters.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/_Lf-2mkZ0LuXgwFyReVg1.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hoLMxOLZPFUjHCR0cCnZo","name":"Through The  Eyes of  You(th) by  IUCEE -  SPARK","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/dJvXlUKHNhXdaL1edqbEi.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"Enhanced awareness among students about the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and their practical relevance.\\n\\nEncouraged creative expression through photography as a tool for social impact.\\n\\nImproved students’ observation skills, storytelling ability, and visual communication.\\n\\nInspired participants to think critically about environmental and social challenges.\\n\\nStrengthened youth engagement in sustainability and responsible citizenship.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Through The Eyes of You(th) was a photography-based awareness initiative conducted under IUCEE SPARK, aimed at encouraging students to express their perspectives on global and social issues through visual storytelling. The event centered around the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), motivating participants to observe their surroundings critically and capture meaningful images that highlight sustainability, environmental protection, and social responsibility.\\n\\nStudents were given a specific time frame to take photographs representing themes such as climate action, life on land, gender equality, and responsible consumption. Each participant submitted their photograph along with a brief explanation describing the message and SDG connection behind their work. The submissions were evaluated by a panel of judges based on creativity, relevance, storytelling, and impact.\\n\\nThe activity provided a platform for youth to voice their ideas artistically while linking local realities to global developmental goals.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/BtT62XL11HXSnYR8g5GvK.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tZw1EyI2oIL-U1rvtf9qi","name":"Campus Cleanup","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The campus environment became noticeably cleaner and more organized.\\n\\nStudents developed a stronger sense of responsibility toward maintaining cleanliness in shared spaces.\\n\\nAwareness about waste segregation and sustainable practices increased among participants.\\n\\nThe activity encouraged teamwork, discipline, and community service.\\n\\nIt reinforced the importance of environmental protection and civic responsibility in daily life.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-27","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized a Campus Cleanup Drive to promote cleanliness, environmental responsibility, and community participation among students. The activity aimed to instill the values of hygiene, waste management, and sustainable living while creating a cleaner and healthier campus environment.\\n\\nNSS volunteers, along with student participants, carried out a systematic cleanup of various areas of the campus, including classrooms surroundings, pathways, gardens, and common spaces. Students collected litter such as plastic waste, paper, and other non-biodegradable materials. The waste was segregated into biodegradable and non-biodegradable categories to spread awareness about proper waste disposal practices.\\n\\nVolunteers also interacted with fellow students and staff, emphasizing the importance of maintaining cleanliness in public spaces and reducing single-use plastics. The activity highlighted the message that individual responsibility plays a major role in environmental conservation.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/zfG4wIDJPvJDDqLFOjRpC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Rk6Lb0ZpFD-yTmWZFMuzf","name":"Fastrek 2.0","slNo":4,"place":"Kunigal Betta","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/JMF3PwYQgCdNBzlI6tsk2.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Encouraged Fitness & Adventure: Promoted physical activity and appreciation for outdoor exploration.\\nEnvironmental Awareness: Strengthened understanding of sustainable practices and nature conservation.\\nWaste Management & Cleanup: Over 20 kg of waste was collected and properly disposed of, reducing pollution on the trail.\\nCommunity Bonding: Fostered teamwork, leadership, and camaraderie among students.\\nSocial Responsibility: Reinforced the idea that collective small actions can create meaningful environmental impact.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fast Trek 2.0 was an adventure-based social initiative organized by Rotaract RVCE with the objective of promoting environmental conservation, physical fitness, and community engagement. The event combined trekking with a cleanliness drive, encouraging students to explore nature responsibly while contributing to its preservation.\\n\\nThe initiative witnessed participation from 750+ students across various departments, making it one of the largest student trekking events of the academic year.\\n\\nPrior to the event, organizers conducted an awareness campaign on eco-friendly trekking practices, waste management, and biodiversity conservation. Participants were also given a safety briefing covering trekking routes, precautions, and emergency procedures.\\n\\nThe trek commenced at 7:30 AM, with participants traveling by bus to Kunagalu Betta, a scenic hill known for its rich biodiversity and panoramic views. Before starting the trek, biodegradable waste bags were distributed, encouraging participants to collect plastic and litter found along the trail.\\n\\nThe trek covered approximately 6 km of rocky terrain, greenery, and viewpoints. A midway sustainability session reinforced the “Leave No Trace” principle and the importance of protecting natural ecosystems.\\n\\nAt the summit, a collective cleanliness drive was conducted where students gathered non-biodegradable waste. Post-trek, the collected waste was segregated into recyclable and non-recyclable categories and disposed of responsibly. The event concluded with a certificate distribution ceremony recognizing the efforts of volunteers and participants.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/KZ_O8nN0AT4Y4e5yemC7s.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_fDpZ6evScMD3GLnKTtjN","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully promoted awareness about physical fitness and the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle.\\n\\nParticipants developed improved stamina, discipline, and motivation to engage in regular exercise.\\n\\nThe event fostered unity, teamwork, and a spirit of collective participation among students and volunteers.\\n\\nIt strengthened social responsibility by encouraging students to be part of community-centered initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The UTSARGA Marathon 2024 was organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) as a community-oriented initiative aimed at promoting physical fitness, endurance, and social responsibility among students. The event brought together NSS volunteers, students, and members of the community to participate in a 5 km marathon, encouraging the adoption of a healthy and active lifestyle.\\n\\nThe marathon served as a platform to create awareness about the importance of regular exercise, mental resilience, and self-discipline. NSS volunteers were actively involved in planning and executing the event, managing registrations, guiding participants along the route, and ensuring safety measures were followed throughout the program.\\n\\nBeyond being a sporting activity, the marathon highlighted the values of teamwork, commitment, and community engagement. It reflected NSS’s mission of developing socially responsible individuals through meaningful participation in activities that contribute to both personal growth and societal well-being.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/o_06rd5UV4grSllnYqIqW.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GQvBAtgIEkp0XvR0mx0eq","name":"DHI Day-Data Remix","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced students’ understanding of data analysis, data visualization, and decision-making using real datasets.\\n\\nEncouraged innovative thinking by integrating business optimization with sustainable development goals.\\n\\nImproved teamwork, communication, and presentation skills among participants.\\n\\nProvided practical exposure to solving real-world problems using data-driven approaches.\\n\\nReinforced the importance of sustainability and responsible technological innovation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"DHI Day – Data Remix was organized by Team DHI, Department of Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning (AIML), RV College of Engineering, as a technical and innovation-driven event focused on data analytics, visualization, and sustainable business solutions. The event was conducted as part of DHI Day and brought together students from various semesters to apply data-driven thinking to real-world problems.\\n\\nThe event was conducted in multiple phases. In the initial phase, participants were provided with pre-processed datasets and relevant analytical tools to perform data analysis and generate meaningful visualizations. Students worked in teams of 3 to 4 members, encouraging collaboration, problem-solving, and critical thinking.\\n\\nThe second phase focused on business innovation and optimization, where teams used their analytical insights to propose solutions aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Participants presented their findings and solutions to a panel of judges comprising faculty members, who evaluated the teams based on creativity, analytical approach, clarity of visualization, and relevance to sustainability.\\n\\nThe event concluded with final presentations, result announcements, and prize distribution. DHI Day – Data Remix successfully blended technical learning with sustainability-focused innovation, providing students with hands-on exposure beyond classroom academics.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/v7poAkpR4UJy3VuTZlz6I.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZOxCiAxU8aJZ7fCZhriL_","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/_2NcRYVNP0zoUlz-GjmIW.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":" \\nA significant number of books and study materials were collected and redistributed to students in need.\\n\\nUnderprivileged children received access to learning resources, supporting their academic growth.\\n\\nStudents developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility toward educational equity.\\n\\nThe activity promoted the values of sharing, sustainability (reuse of books), and community service.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2024 was a social initiative organized to promote education access and literacy among underprivileged children. The project focused on collecting and distributing educational materials such as textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery to students from economically weaker sections of society.\\n\\nStudents actively participated by donating books and study materials that were in good condition. Volunteers sorted, categorized, and packed the collected materials based on age group and academic level to ensure effective distribution. The resources were then provided to government schools, community learning centers, and children from low-income families who lacked access to adequate learning materials.\\n\\nThe initiative highlighted the importance of sharing knowledge resources and reducing educational inequality. It encouraged students to contribute meaningfully toward building a more educated and empowered society.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/sXdAqJIBht1lILj2E7uL7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-EH9Z7AwThhHR97EHkWns","name":"Through The  Eyes of  You(th) by  IUCEE -  SPARK ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/UQ9sjKERlLJu8rAF6JU2g.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-19","duration":36,"outcomes":"The initiative enhanced students’ awareness of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and their relevance to real-world challenges.\\n\\nParticipants developed stronger creative thinking and visual storytelling skills through photography.\\n\\nThe activity improved students’ ability to observe social and environmental issues from a critical perspective.\\n\\nIt encouraged youth engagement in topics related to sustainability, social responsibility, and environmental protection.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-14","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Through The Eyes of You(th) was a photography-based awareness initiative conducted under IUCEE SPARK, designed to encourage students to express their perspectives on global and social issues through visual storytelling. The event was aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), motivating participants to observe their surroundings thoughtfully and capture impactful images reflecting themes such as sustainability, environmental conservation, and social responsibility.\\n\\nStudents were given a defined time frame to take photographs representing SDG themes including climate action, life on land, gender equality, and responsible consumption. Each participant submitted their photograph along with a brief write-up explaining the concept and SDG relevance behind their image. The entries were evaluated by a panel of judges based on creativity, relevance to SDGs, storytelling quality, and overall impact.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/8ihv53UndUilP9VdH7Amx.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9bhDsGdK63tUI0xgM1Q0M","name":"Fistful 2024","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/-dd_WqE3-7I_82Dv7mwAE.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected, helping address food insecurity among vulnerable communities.\\n\\nThe donated food grains supported nutrition programs in old age homes, hospitals, schools, anganwadis, and institutions for visually challenged children.\\n\\nStudents developed a stronger sense of empathy, social responsibility, and awareness of hunger-related issues.\\n\\nThe initiative demonstrated the power of collective effort, where small individual contributions created a large social impact.\\n\\nIt promoted the values of service, compassion, and community engagement among participants.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI District 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program focused on reducing food insecurity and supporting underprivileged sections of society. The initiative followed a simple yet powerful concept where each participating student donated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, turning small individual contributions into a collective effort with significant impact.\\n\\nThe drive received overwhelming support, with participation from over 2,100 students, leading to the collection of a large quantity of essential food grains. As part of this initiative, I personally contributed 2 kg of toor dal, which was added to the overall collection. The donated food grains were then distributed to various beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding programs, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes, hospitals, trust-run schools, and nearby anganwadis. These supplies helped strengthen existing nutrition programs benefiting children, senior citizens, patients, and economically disadvantaged communities.\\n\\nThe distribution was carried out in a systematic and well-coordinated manner, with beneficiary institutions collecting the food supplies directly from the campus under the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The initiative focused on creating a sustainable and community-driven impact, emphasizing long-term support rather than short-term relief.\\n\\nOverall, the FistFull initiative made a meaningful contribution toward addressing hunger and nutritional challenges among vulnerable populations. It enhanced students’ awareness of social issues and fostered values such as empathy, responsibility, and civic engagement. The event highlighted how united student participation can create large-scale positive change and strongly reflected the principles of service, compassion, and community development upheld by Rotaract and Rotary.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/r8DtIAiKhcUtuzdjFRzUm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zDWsIuttbVu64Lq05ehmb","name":"Plog Run along  Vrishabhavati  Valley ","slNo":10,"place":"Bengaluru University","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/fmR-x4EsJ-haikEVSUMXv.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"A considerable amount of plastic and non-biodegradable waste was collected, contributing to a cleaner environment along the Vrishabhavati Valley.\\n\\nParticipants developed greater awareness about pollution, waste segregation, and sustainable disposal practices.\\n\\nThe activity successfully combined physical fitness with environmental responsibility.\\n\\nStudents strengthened their sense of civic duty toward maintaining public spaces and protecting urban ecosystems.\\n\\nThe event promoted eco-friendly habits and encouraged continued participation in environmental conservation initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"A Plog Run was organized along the Vrishabhavati Valley at Bengaluru University with the objective of promoting environmental cleanliness, physical fitness, and social responsibility. Plogging — a combination of jogging and picking up litter — was adopted as a practical and engaging method to address pollution while encouraging an active lifestyle.\\n\\nStudents and volunteers participated enthusiastically, jogging along the valley stretch while collecting plastic waste, wrappers, and other non-biodegradable materials found along the route. Participants were provided with gloves and waste collection bags to ensure safety and effective segregation of waste.\\n\\nThe activity aimed to raise awareness about improper waste disposal, the importance of maintaining clean natural surroundings, and the responsibility of individuals in protecting urban ecosystems. It also highlighted the need to preserve water bodies and green zones such as the Vrishabhavati Valley, which are often affected by pollution and human activities.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/2hcRH_5qFwFsJkRMxHwNx.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5LGuyuVsT2dLAk81gjl8e","name":"Vikasit Bharat","slNo":11,"place":"MyGov Portal","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"A significant amount of plastic and non-biodegradable waste was removed from the Vrishabhavati Valley area.\\n\\nParticipants developed increased awareness about environmental pollution and proper waste disposal practices.\\n\\nThe activity successfully combined physical fitness with environmental responsibility.\\n\\nStudents strengthened their sense of civic duty toward protecting public spaces and natural ecosystems.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"A Plog Run was conducted along the Vrishabhavati Valley at Bengaluru University to promote environmental cleanliness, physical fitness, and social responsibility. Plogging — jogging while collecting litter — served as an engaging approach to tackle pollution while encouraging an active lifestyle.\\n\\nStudents and volunteers participated by jogging along the valley stretch and collecting plastic waste, wrappers, and other non-biodegradable materials. Gloves and waste collection bags were provided to ensure safety and proper segregation.\\n\\nThe activity created awareness about responsible waste disposal, the importance of maintaining clean natural surroundings, and the need to protect urban ecosystems, water bodies, and green zones affected by pollution and human activity.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/gsHzMn64663bx2r1WeTa_.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YarjYkXpZbDXq1KJFIRxl","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Encouraged Fitness & Adventure: Promoted physical activity and appreciation for outdoor exploration.\\n\\nEnvironmental Awareness: Strengthened understanding of sustainable practices and nature conservation.\\n\\nWaste Management & Cleanup: Over 20 kg of waste was collected and properly disposed of, reducing pollution on the trail.\\n\\nCommunity Bonding: Fostered teamwork, leadership, and camaraderie among students.\\n\\nSocial Responsibility: Reinforced the idea that collective small actions can create meaningful environmental impact.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The UTSARGA Marathon, conducted by the National Service Scheme (NSS) on 06 April 2025, was a major community-focused initiative designed to promote physical fitness, social awareness, and overall well-being. The event brought together students, NSS volunteers, and community members for a 5 km run, highlighting the importance of an active lifestyle in developing a healthy and responsible society.\\n\\nThe marathon acted as more than just a sporting event — it served as a medium to spread awareness about health, endurance, self-discipline, and community participation. NSS volunteers were actively involved in planning and executing the event, managing logistics, ensuring participant safety, and maintaining smooth coordination throughout the program. The initiative reflected NSS’s dedication to shaping socially responsible individuals through practical engagement beyond classroom learning.\\n\\nThe event saw energetic participation and successfully created a sense of unity, determination, and collective spirit among participants. Taking part in the 5 km marathon encouraged students to recognize the value of physical fitness in maintaining overall health and mental strength. The experience symbolized commitment, perseverance, and enthusiastic involvement.\\n\\nOverall, the marathon strengthened qualities such as teamwork, discipline, and social responsibility among students. It also supported the core objective of NSS — holistic development — by combining physical wellness with community service, thereby contributing to both personal growth and the betterment of society.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/lY67RPBbCiV9Z0mDGIUVx.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CFzYlbzxNCEb5P9-HrGyj","name":"Encanto Activity","slNo":13,"place":"RV Dental College","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-20","duration":2,"outcomes":"Students developed a stronger sense of social responsibility and community service.\\n\\nThe event promoted teamwork, leadership, and active participation among youth.\\n\\nParticipants fostered empathy, inclusiveness, and awareness about contributing to society.\\n\\nIt provided a platform for students to engage in meaningful, service-oriented activities.\\n\\nThe initiative reinforced the values of collaboration, compassion, and social harmony","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-19","hoursSpent":0,"description":"ENCANTO was a social impact event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE (R.I. District 3191) with the aim of promoting community engagement, teamwork, and social responsibility among students. The event brought together enthusiastic participants to take part in meaningful service-oriented activities while fostering collaboration and leadership.\\n\\nDesigned as a multi-activity initiative, ENCANTO involved organized tasks and interactive sessions that emphasized compassion, inclusivity, and collective effort. The program reflected Rotaract’s mission of creating a tangible and lasting social impact while strengthening unity among youth.\\n\\nVolunteers actively contributed to the planning, coordination, and execution of the event, ensuring its smooth conduct. Through structured activities and teamwork, participants experienced the value of service, empathy, and cooperation. The event encouraged students to move beyond academics and actively engage in initiatives that support community welfare and social harmony.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/tHTcGJQYIS5szDn15TOBz.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hEA5QIJXWQLmgiu8Xq8eQ","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/Ivp8jtIKoUL4WjvZPCYyc.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"A substantial number of books and study materials were collected and distributed to students in need.\\n\\nBeneficiary children received improved access to educational resources, supporting their learning.\\n\\nStudents developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility toward educational equity.\\n\\nThe initiative promoted sustainability through the reuse and redistribution of books.\\n\\nThe activity strengthened community engagement and the spirit of service among participants.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was an educational outreach initiative aimed at promoting literacy and supporting students from underprivileged backgrounds by providing essential learning resources. The project focused on collecting textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery items from students and distributing them to children who lacked access to adequate educational materials.\\n\\nVolunteers actively participated in the collection drive, encouraging students to donate books in good condition. The collected materials were carefully sorted based on subject, age group, and academic level to ensure their usefulness to the recipients. These resources were then distributed to government schools, community learning centers, and children from economically weaker sections.\\n\\nThe initiative highlighted the importance of sharing knowledge, reducing educational inequality, and promoting the reuse of books as a sustainable practice. It also encouraged students to view education as a powerful tool for social development.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/J5ODZkeQB_FCb4w45BMX8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-30","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"J7tXv0GjZNxI78T53ey2-","name":"Vintage Car","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/KiPaav41Fa9sm8a7RkUuC.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Students gained exposure to automobile history and vintage engineering.\\n\\nThe event fostered curiosity and appreciation for classic vehicle design and technology.\\n\\nIt encouraged social interaction and strengthened bonding among participants.\\n\\nStudents developed a better understanding of the importance of preserving automotive heritage.\\n\\nThe rally provided a blend of learning, recreation, and cultural enrichment.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Vintage Car and Bike Rally was organized by NSS RVCE as an engaging event celebrating automotive heritage while bringing students together for a unique and enjoyable experience. The rally featured an impressive collection of classic cars and vintage motorcycles, giving participants the opportunity to witness iconic vehicles known for their timeless design, engineering excellence, and historical significance.\\n\\nThe event created a lively and enthusiastic atmosphere as students explored the vehicles, interacted with owners, and learned about the evolution of automobile technology. Conducted as a fun-filled morning activity, the rally combined recreation with awareness about the importance of preserving vintage machines as part of cultural and technological history.\\n\\nBeyond entertainment, the event encouraged social interaction, appreciation of mechanical innovation, and community engagement among students. It served as a refreshing break from routine academic activities while still offering an educational and culturally enriching experience.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/62ccbdd8-0619-4a7b-8432-d885c341b9b2/evR06MuwUNOiDWcHgsUIY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"31-32","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 04:36:11.884713+00', '2026-01-30 05:53:33.392611+00'), ('5c925239-2a85-4167-a280-5a2ef3b3ac2a', 'b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC021","name":"Apurva Ashok Patil","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"pe70uKtHpXSH_bicVdj1w","name":"Biofuel Day Essay Competition and Model Making","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/fceFPY_CZ91gCK_OnE7KS.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ understanding of biofuels and their importance in achieving sustainable energy goals. It helped improve research skills, critical thinking, and effective written communication. The essay writing competition also strengthened awareness of environmental responsibility and encouraged students to actively engage in discussions related to renewable energy and sustainability. Participation in the event contributed to NSS activity points and reinforced the importance of academic involvement in addressing real-world environmental challenges.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-08","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The International Biofuel Day Essay Writing Competition organized by NSS RVCE on 8th August was an educational initiative aimed at creating awareness about renewable energy sources and sustainable development. The activity provided a platform for students to express their understanding and perspectives on biofuels, their environmental benefits, and their role in reducing dependence on fossil fuels.\\n\\nParticipants were encouraged to research current biofuel technologies, their applications, and their impact on environmental sustainability. Through essay writing, students critically analyzed the significance of biofuels in addressing global energy challenges and climate change. The competition fostered analytical thinking, technical writing, and awareness of eco-friendly energy solutions.\\n\\nThe event was conducted in a structured manner following the prescribed guidelines, with attendance recorded for all participants. Overall, the activity contributed to enhancing knowledge about sustainable energy practices while promoting responsible and informed citizenship among students.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/nGb0xT30Uu_XP3bBzaiXv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"enyQ7wUqGevK_AxaaQsHU","name":"Cheela Mela","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/kBOvtDPc8nof1uoCkQxEN.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"The activity resulted in the successful creation and collection of a significant number of paper bags, contributing directly to reducing plastic usage during the Kadale Kayi Parishe. Participants developed awareness about sustainable alternatives to plastic and the importance of recycling and waste management. The workshop enhanced participants’ sense of social and environmental responsibility while promoting active community involvement. Additionally, students earned NSS activity points based on their contribution, reinforcing the value of sustained participation in social and environmental initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Paper Bag Workshop for Kadale Kayi Parishe was organized by NSS RVCE in collaboration with Youth For Seva from 11th to 22nd November 2024. This initiative aimed to promote environmental sustainability by encouraging the use of eco-friendly alternatives to plastic bags, particularly for local festivals and markets such as Kadale Kayi Parishe.\\n\\nAs part of the activity, participants crafted paper bags using old newspapers, thereby practicing waste reuse and recycling. The workshop provided flexibility, allowing participants to prepare the bags either onsite at the Environment Lab, Civil Department, during the designated time or offsite at their convenience and submit them within the specified duration. Through this hands-on activity, students actively contributed to reducing plastic usage while supporting a greener and cleaner environment.\\n\\nThe initiative fostered environmental awareness, creativity, and social responsibility among participants. By engaging students in a simple yet impactful activity, the workshop highlighted how small sustainable practices can collectively lead to meaningful environmental change.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/CptuNDhrDemH4bIcm2iNs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4Uiv2xdMpB81PvD-i666G","name":"Energy Literacy Training Program","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/w_UPGusNCsGwed3Je-GGd.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":31,"outcomes":"The Energy Literacy Training Program significantly enhanced participants’ understanding of energy systems, sustainability, and climate responsibility. It empowered students to make informed decisions regarding energy conservation and encouraged them to practice and promote energy-efficient habits within their families and communities. The successful completion of the training strengthened awareness of renewable energy solutions and environmental stewardship. Additionally, participants received certification and were eligible for the allocation of activity points, motivating continued involvement in sustainability-driven initiatives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-01","hoursSpent":25,"description":"The Energy Literacy Training Program was conducted under the initiative of the Energy Swaraj Foundation, as part of the Energy Swaraj Mission, and facilitated through the Urja Energy Swaraj Club, RV College of Engineering®, Bengaluru. The program aimed to create awareness about energy usage, climate change, and sustainable energy practices among students.\\n\\nThe training comprised multiple modules that covered essential topics such as energy generation, consumption patterns, energy wastage, carbon footprint, environmental impact, and alternative renewable energy sources, including solar energy. The program emphasized correcting common misconceptions related to energy usage and encouraged participants to adopt responsible and sustainable energy practices in daily life.\\n\\nStudents were required to dedicate approximately 20–24 hours to complete the training modules successfully. Upon completion, participants submitted the course certificate for verification. The initiative served as a social cause, focusing on spreading energy awareness within the community and promoting environmentally conscious behavior.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/LyV3bvKbFnzMcwbW3O6zD.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"twRcbk_zNUaqYbqrPZ83y","name":"Gandhian Principles(Essay Writing)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/JXLcsOHy3WuCei6eEEJGB.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ understanding of Gandhian principles and their relevance to modern sustainable development goals. It helped improve critical thinking, ethical reasoning, and written communication skills. The competition encouraged participants to reflect on value-based living and social responsibility. Participation in the event contributed to earning NSS activity points and reinforced the importance of integrating moral values with contemporary societal and environmental challenges.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-09","hoursSpent":2,"description":"An Essay Writing Competition on Gandhian Principles was organized by NSS RVCE in association with the Centre for Gandhian Principles and Value Based Education, RV College of Engineering®, Bengaluru, on 9th December 2024 at the IEM Auditorium. The activity aimed to encourage students and faculty to reflect on Mahatma Gandhi’s philosophies and their relevance to sustainable development goals in the modern era.\\n\\nThe competition provided a platform for participants to articulate their thoughts on the topic “Sustainable Goals in Gandhiji’s Views”, emphasizing ethical living, social responsibility, environmental sustainability, and value-based development. Participants were required to write and submit the essay on the spot, ensuring active engagement and original expression of ideas.\\n\\nThrough this activity, participants explored Gandhian values such as simplicity, self-reliance, non-violence, and sustainability, and analyzed their applicability in addressing contemporary global challenges. The event fostered critical thinking, ethical awareness, and effective written communication.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/YZ-y7AN7bBE4-XW7TS3Q7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2nHVCRoJQgoAMsA5xqehH","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/wvDvbiAnPXF640pKndDUc.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The Fist Full initiative successfully mobilized student participation and resulted in the collection of a substantial quantity of food grains for social welfare purposes. The activity strengthened awareness about food security and social inequality among participants. It fostered a sense of responsibility, teamwork, and empathy while reinforcing the impact of collective effort in community service. Participation in the event was formally recognized, and eligible students were awarded AICTE activity points, encouraging continued engagement in social and humanitarian initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Fist Full 2024 was a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE during the period from 15th November to 29th November 2024. The activity was aimed at addressing food insecurity and promoting social responsibility among students through collective community participation.\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, participants contributed food grains in small quantities (“a fist full”), symbolizing how small individual contributions can collectively create a significant impact. Rotaract volunteers coordinated the collection, organization, and distribution process, ensuring that the contributions reached the intended beneficiaries effectively.\\n\\nThe event emphasized values such as compassion, empathy, and social solidarity. It encouraged students to actively participate in humanitarian efforts and understand the importance of addressing societal challenges such as hunger through sustained and collaborative action. The initiative reflected the Rotaract Club’s commitment to community service and inclusive development.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/p_UhK_IdSPPYKXmYn79ea.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1V14TypZOmPOFcdndb_AO","name":"One Student-One Plant: Green","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity successfully increased awareness about the importance of plant adoption and environmental sustainability. Participants developed a sense of responsibility toward nurturing plants and maintaining green spaces in their surroundings. The initiative promoted eco-friendly habits and encouraged long-term commitment to environmental care. Overall, the activity reinforced the idea that individual actions play a vital role in protecting and preserving the environment.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-11","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A Plant Adoption and Awareness Activity was organized to promote environmental consciousness and encourage individuals to adopt sustainable and eco-friendly practices. The initiative motivated participants to bring greenery into their living spaces by adopting an indoor plant of their choice, such as a succulent, houseplant, or herb.\\n\\nParticipants were required to select a plant that suited their personal space and preferences and take a photograph with the adopted plant. The activity emphasized personal involvement and responsibility towards nurturing plant life. Participants then submitted their details along with the photograph through an online submission form, ensuring structured participation and documentation.\\n\\nThe activity aimed to create awareness about the importance of plants in maintaining ecological balance, improving air quality, and fostering a sustainable lifestyle. By encouraging individual participation, the event highlighted how simple actions can collectively contribute to environmental conservation.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/g3r6mf_RZzNPM5VWi7Z8e.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sz2mjUIGf574XDv1g1fVz","name":"Paper Drive 2023","slNo":4,"place":"Vijayanagar and Attiguppe","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/WIQhlpUkFO6XUkLboY12X.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully generated funds for charitable causes \\nthrough recycling while promoting environmental sustainability. \\nIt also strengthened students’ teamwork, leadership, and \\ncommunity engagement skills, fostering a strong sense of social \\nresponsibility.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The Paper Drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 24th \\nJune 2023 was a commendable community initiative aimed at \\npromoting recycling and supporting social welfare. Volunteers, \\nincluding college students, faculty members, and local residents, \\ncollected old newspapers, magazines, and books across \\nBengaluru. The collected materials were sold, and the proceeds \\nwere donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation, which supports \\norphaned children. The event not only generated essential funds \\nfor a noble cause but also fostered a spirit of environmental \\nresponsibility and community engagement.\\n\\nAdditionally, the drive \\nraised awareness about recycling and sustainable living. As \\nvolunteers interacted with residents, they educated them on the \\nbenefits of recycling and reducing paper waste. This outreach \\nhelped in still a collective sense of responsibility for adopting eco\\nfriendly practices. The collaborative effort demonstrated the \\nimpact of collective action, strengthening community bonds and \\nhighlighting the power of volunteerism in addressing social issues. \\nThe Paper Drive’s success reflected how small individual actions, \\nwhen combined, can bring about meaningful societal change. ","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/2Gh4JVPxdgUjl9IuNMUa5.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LQKGGadPMYA4swdDnsQTn","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/eZo2qx4uamRQd5-eyPdjC.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project successfully generated sufficient funds to procure and distribute essential school supplies to underprivileged students, thereby supporting their educational needs. It contributed to creating a more conducive learning environment for the beneficiaries and reinforced the importance of education in social development. Participants developed a strong sense of social responsibility, empathy, and teamwork. The successful execution of Project Pustak demonstrated the positive impact of collective action and volunteerism, and participants were duly recognized with activity points for their contribution.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak was a social service initiative undertaken by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 24th May 2024, with the objective of supporting the education of underprivileged students from rural areas. The project focused on collecting funds to provide essential school supplies to students who lack access to basic educational resources.\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, contributions of ₹100 or ₹350 were collected from compassionate donors. The funds collected formed the basis for procuring necessary educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, school bags, and other learning essentials. The initiative was carried out in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, ensuring proper utilization of funds and effective distribution of resources to the beneficiaries.\\n\\nProject Pustak highlighted the importance of collective effort in addressing educational inequality and emphasized the role of students in contributing to social upliftment. The initiative reflected a strong commitment to community service and the promotion of education as a fundamental right.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/E2A1p6iEr8XgJMw7_-L8X.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_F7z4C2xjMJN-5dyvvieX","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"Over 6700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal were collected, \\nhighlighting the strength of collective effort and the power of \\ncommunity support in addressing food insecurity. The event \\ndemonstrated how unified action, driven by empathy and a shared \\nsense of purpose, can make a tangible impact in providing \\nessential resources to those in need. More than just a charitable \\ninitiative, it instilled a sense of social responsibility among \\nparticipants, inspiring many to continue engaging in philanthropic \\nactivities. By showcasing the transformative potential of \\ncommunity-driven efforts, the event reinforced the importance of \\nsustained contributions and collaboration in building a more \\nequitable and compassionate society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with Rotary \\nBangalore Spandana, successfully launched the \"Fist Full of Rice \\n& Dal\" initiative, a week-long charitable drive designed to \\ncultivate the spirit of giving and provide much-needed support to \\nunderprivileged communities. This unique initiative encouraged \\nthe students and staff of RVCE to set aside a fistful of rice and dal \\nduring their daily meal preparation as a simple yet powerful \\ngesture of generosity. The drive garnered remarkable \\nparticipation, resulting in the collection of over 6700 kg of rice \\nand 800 kg of toor dal, a testament to the collective compassion \\nand social responsibility of the RVCE community. To broaden \\nparticipation and make giving more accessible, the initiative also \\noffered an option to donate fixed quantities of 5 kg of rice or 2 kg \\nof toor dal. This flexibility enabled more individuals to join the \\ncause, reinforcing the idea that everyone can contribute \\nmeaningfully regardless of the size of their donation. The \\noverwhelming response reflected the strength of unity and the \\npower of collaborative action in addressing food insecurity.  \\nThrough this initiative, students not only helped meet the \\nimmediate nutritional needs of vulnerable communities but also \\ndeveloped a deeper sense of empathy and responsibility. The \\nsuccess of \"Fist Full of Rice & Dal\" demonstrated how small, \\nmindful contributions can collectively drive significant social \\nchange, inspiring a culture of ongoing charity and communal. ","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/OG-EH2CU1ikIFScV3aacX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"N5BcZb4YshGNfkXXrBr5Q","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/287ux2nz9ENlVlDc7YtsE.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-26","duration":5,"outcomes":"The initiative improved access to basic educational resources for \\nunderprivileged students, contributing to a better learning \\nenvironment. It also fostered social responsibility, empathy, and \\ncommunity engagement among student volunteers involved in \\nplanning and execution.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a social initiative aimed at supporting \\nunderprivileged students in rural areas by providing essential \\nschool supplies. Funds collected through donor contributions of \\n₹100 or ₹350 were utilized to procure textbooks, stationery \\nitems, backpacks, and other learning resources. The project was \\ncarried out by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with \\nPranav Foundation to promote equitable access to education. ","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/GvXmwc1dUU8g68AAgrAC0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DI-KNaI9RqHzt9N77sdvw","name":"UTPT 2024","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/FuFub2soxzMUEQELPcAzS.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ general awareness, critical thinking, and quick decision-making skills. It encouraged continuous learning and curiosity about national and global topics. Participation in the quiz contributed to intellectual development and confidence-building. Successful participation in the event was recognized with a Certificate of Participation, making participants eligible to claim 5 AICTE activity points, thereby motivating engagement in academic and co-curricular enrichment activities.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz was conducted as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2024, a national-level quiz fest, held from 07th to 09th June 2024. The event aimed to promote awareness and knowledge about India’s culture, history, heritage, governance, and contemporary developments through an engaging quiz-based format.\\n\\nThe quiz provided participants with an opportunity to test and enhance their general knowledge, logical thinking, and analytical skills. By participating in this intellectually stimulating competition, students were encouraged to stay informed about national and global issues while fostering a spirit of healthy competition.\\n\\nThe activity was conducted in an organized manner and participants were evaluated based on their knowledge and problem-solving abilities. The event served as an effective platform for learning beyond the classroom in an interactive and enjoyable way.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/KYX4xOdUV3XhdQcA-E0iz.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"suh7r19DUZMwsys9tXxEJ","name":"SDG Photography Contest","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/omfjV0K3pLcQNnCmbdOS2.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-19","duration":6,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ understanding of the Sustainable Development Goals and their relevance in everyday life. It helped develop creative thinking, observational skills, and visual communication abilities. The contest encouraged participants to engage meaningfully with global sustainability issues and express them innovatively. Participation in the event was recognized with the awarding of 5 AICTE activity points, reinforcing the value of creativity-based learning and social awareness initiatives.","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-11-14","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The SDG Photography Contest 2024 was organized by SPARK with the objective of promoting awareness about the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through creative visual expression. The activity encouraged participants to use photography as a medium to highlight social, environmental, and developmental challenges aligned with the SDGs.\\n\\nParticipants captured and submitted photographs that reflected themes such as sustainability, environmental protection, social responsibility, and inclusive growth. The contest provided a platform for students to creatively communicate powerful messages related to global development goals while combining artistic skills with social awareness.\\n\\nThrough this initiative, students were motivated to observe their surroundings critically and interpret real-world issues through a sustainable development lens. The activity successfully blended creativity with purpose, reinforcing the importance of visual storytelling in driving social change.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/fMjNAq1dPZbz0g11L34xW.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6yf29cD5e_hJC7wOJjHAR","name":"Tanuja Movie Screening","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/jZ8xAQm9AKLoqGfKuF9PT.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity deeply inspired participants by reinforcing the values of determination, resilience, and self-belief. It helped students understand the critical role of teachers, parents, and society in nurturing young talent and supporting educational aspirations. The screening motivated participants to pursue their goals without fear of obstacles and encouraged empathy toward students from underprivileged backgrounds. Overall, the activity fostered moral awareness, social responsibility, and a positive mindset among students.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"A live screening of the inspirational film “Tanuja” was organized by NSS RVCE on 14th July 2023. The screening aimed to motivate students by showcasing a real-life story of determination, resilience, and social support in the face of adversity.\\n\\nThe film narrates the journey of Tanuja, a young girl from a financially disadvantaged farmer’s family, who traveled nearly 400 kilometers to appear for the NEET examination on 14th October 2020. Despite numerous challenges, she successfully secured a medical seat in Karnataka. The story also highlights the pivotal roles played by her teacher Mr. Pradeep Ishwar, senior journalist Mr. Vishweshwar Bhatt, and public representatives who ensured her timely arrival at the examination center.\\n\\nThe screening emphasized the importance of mentorship, societal support, and encouragement in shaping students’ academic journeys. It conveyed a strong social message on perseverance, empathy, and collective responsibility, inspiring students to face challenges with confidence and courage.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/QGFiYWaNHLaP-bVJvYea5.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uylyp6VvH9Cwl5_igxwWQ","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge","slNo":14,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/0Ryt2Zo4GN-Gvq0PvfQAg.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The quiz enhanced participants’ understanding of India’s development agenda and the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047. It improved awareness of government initiatives, national policies, and long-term planning. The activity encouraged informed citizenship and active engagement in nation-building efforts. Successful participation in the quiz contributed to earning 2 AICTE activity points, motivating students to take part in national-level educational and awareness programs.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge was a nationwide online initiative launched by the Government of India with the objective of engaging youth in understanding India’s progress, governance, and long-term vision of becoming a developed nation by 2047. The activity was promoted by NSS RVCE to encourage student participation in national development–oriented programs.\\n\\nThe online quiz consisted of 10 time-bound questions designed to assess participants’ awareness of India’s developmental milestones, government initiatives, and future goals. Participants registered on the official Viksit Bharat portal, followed the prescribed guidelines, and completed the quiz within the allotted time. Upon completion, participants documented their participation by submitting a screenshot containing their name and reference ID.\\n\\nThe activity served as an interactive platform to enhance civic awareness and foster a sense of responsibility toward national development among students.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/3tFobiLxxRyUIOaBoSNwq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zH7k8_OuwJVp3gbq3LoB9","name":"SDG Photography Contest 2025","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/d789Q_001ifkkwzlNnI_n.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ understanding of the Sustainable Development Goals and their relevance in everyday life. It helped develop creativity, observational skills, and visual communication abilities. The contest encouraged participants to think critically about social and environmental issues and express their perspectives innovatively. Participation in the event was recognized through a Certificate of Participation, reinforcing the importance of creative contributions toward sustainability and social responsibility.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The SDG Photography Contest was organized by SPARK, RV College of Engineering®, with the objective of promoting awareness about the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through creative visual expression. The activity encouraged students to use photography as a medium to highlight social, environmental, and developmental issues aligned with the SDGs.\\n\\nParticipants captured and submitted original photographs that reflected themes related to sustainability, environmental protection, social responsibility, and inclusive development. The contest provided a platform for students to creatively communicate impactful messages and demonstrate how visual storytelling can contribute to social awareness and change.\\n\\nThrough this activity, participants engaged with real-world sustainability challenges, combining creativity with purpose. The initiative successfully emphasized the role of art and innovation in addressing global development goals.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/CHgrqbBVbOEBaYPP99XGI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EkpmeHJphRcHTwpa-ord8","name":"TEDxRVCE 2023: Resonating Chords","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ critical thinking, listening skills, and exposure to diverse perspectives. It inspired intellectual curiosity, creativity, and personal growth. Attending the TEDx event encouraged participants to reflect on ideas that drive innovation and positive change in society. Participation in the event was recognized with the awarding of 3 AICTE activity points, reinforcing the importance of intellectual and cultural engagement beyond the classroom.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-08","hoursSpent":3,"description":"TEDxRVCE 2023: Resonating Chords was an intellectual and inspirational event organized at RV College of Engineering as part of the globally recognized TEDx platform. The event aimed to provide a space for the exchange of innovative ideas, personal stories, and thought-provoking perspectives across diverse domains.\\n\\nThe session featured speakers who shared insights, experiences, and ideas designed to inspire, educate, and provoke meaningful reflection among the audience. Participants attended the event to engage with ideas worth spreading and to gain exposure to contemporary thought leadership and creative expression.\\n\\nThe event emphasized curiosity, open-mindedness, and lifelong learning, making it a valuable academic and cultural experience for students.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/7FXlNLfJ-QXDlZ4sg35aI.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OQNDvdlR2K3NffITPJe7V","name":"Secret Santa 2025","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/rPAgKM8nGeutBaqd_hDhi.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity brought happiness and emotional support to the children by making them feel valued and included during the festive season. It strengthened participants’ sense of empathy, compassion, and social responsibility. Volunteers gained firsthand experience in community service and learned the importance of contributing selflessly to society. The initiative reinforced the spirit of volunteerism and demonstrated how small acts of kindness can create a meaningful and lasting impact on the lives of others.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Secret Santa was a charity-based social service initiative organized by NSS RVCE with the objective of spreading joy, compassion, and inclusivity among underprivileged children. The activity was conducted in collaboration with an NGO that supports children from economically disadvantaged backgrounds and special needs institutions.\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, volunteers collected gifts, stationery items, clothes, and essential supplies through contributions from students. The event was organized around the Christmas season, incorporating celebrations, interactive activities, and the spirit of giving. Volunteers engaged with the children through games, conversations, and festive interactions, creating a warm and joyful environment.\\n\\nThe initiative emphasized empathy, social responsibility, and the importance of sharing happiness with those in need. By combining celebration with service, the activity highlighted the value of human connection and community involvement.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0435529-dfa6-45fa-8e7d-14b722129f20/f-AvTAxfTusDnn_JTPJid.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 13:41:50.778533+00', '2026-01-30 21:03:50.177911+00'), ('5d58bd22-1b1d-4f57-b173-a06a6967aad8', '6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS173","name":"Samarth D Gothe","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"xZytci2fefjGO-DqHaKKE","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/h39zqFc-KGKhnt6qt1B4M.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/LJkKGcwNsixcUrUcC91eC.png"],"endDate":"2022-02-04","duration":-702,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s education programs. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and learning resources to underprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its fundraising goals, amassing contributions that will sustain classroom initiatives for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students from local underserved communities.\\n\\nBeyond the financial gains, the marathon left an indelible impression on all involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from first-time runners conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz amplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and encouraging future involvement.\\n\\nUltimately, it redefined the act of running as a meaningful pursuit, not only for personal health and endurance, but for forging a brighter, more inclusive future. The Utsarga Marathon exemplified how community-driven events can \\ncreate ripple effects of change, empowering children to dream big and succeed while fostering a culture of giving back.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-08","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, took place on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM across the Bengaluru campus. Under the theme \"Help a Child Change the World,\" it celebrated health, fitness, and education support for underprivileged children. Months of planning ensured smooth logistics with sponsor-backed medals, T-shirts, and refreshments along tree-lined routes.\\n\\nOver 500 runners, including RVCE students, faculty, alumni, and locals from Karnataka, gathered at dawn. They chose between a 5 km fun run (Rs. 399) or 10 km challenge (Rs. 449), with all donations funding school supplies and tuition. Warm-ups, cheers, live music, banners, and photo booths created festive energy.\\n\\nVolunteers in high-visibility vests managed water stations, medical aid, and crowd control with enthusiasm. They helped runners adjust to long conditions, ensuring safety and inclusivity. Heartwarming scenes featured friends jogging together, families cheering from sidelines, and visitors spectating.\\n\\nRunners crossed the finish line to roaring applause, greeted with finisher medals and personalized certificates. Top age-group performers received special trophies, sparking friendly rivalries. On-site announcements celebrated winners, fueling real-time excitement around the charitable core.\\n\\nThe event proved transformative, blending physical challenge with philanthropy. It promoted wellness while instilling purpose through unity. Individual strides wove into widespread positive change for children''s futures.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/cQceLMuODZLtphquxKbt9.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QhPHsrRebmftUdgn5_iUd","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/9LgIg05kkAApaQTnS3S4z.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/f7tsEIQvt_67xzqZTZJxz.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s education programs. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and learning resources to underprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its fundraising goals, amassing contributions that will sustain classroom initiatives for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students from local underserved communities.\\n\\nBeyond the financial gains, the marathon left an indelible impression on all involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from first-time runners conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz amplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and encouraging future involvement.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, was held on February 4, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM across the RVCE campus in Bengaluru. Conducted under the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the event aimed to promote health and fitness while supporting the education of underprivileged children. Careful planning and sponsor support ensured smooth logistics, with medals, T-shirts, refreshments, and a well-marked route enhancing the overall experience.\\n\\nOver 500 participants—including students, faculty, alumni, and runners from across Karnataka—took part in the marathon. Participants could choose between a 5 km fun run or a 10 km competitive run, with all proceeds directed toward educational support such as school supplies and tuition fees. The campus came alive with warm-up sessions, cheering crowds, music, banners, and photo booths, creating a lively and motivating atmosphere.\\n\\nNSS volunteers efficiently managed water stations, medical aid, and crowd control, ensuring safety and inclusivity throughout the event. Runners were welcomed at the finish line with applause, finisher medals, and certificates, while top performers received special trophies. The marathon successfully blended physical endurance with social responsibility, inspiring unity and generating meaningful impact toward improving children’s futures.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/ftkvMWV4veYutEW5rax_O.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FtwzkFwtq2Nct_Z9Mcxt2","name":"Walkathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/ELGo7Xt9MSyE0wkOX5E5m.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/OoAcTVijelDXhzmrx7ocD.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon successfully sensitized participants and the wider campus community to the critical issue of female foeticide and the need for gender equality. The event helped participants develop a deeper understanding of the social, ethical, and moral responsibilities involved in protecting the rights of women and ensuring a balanced and just society.\\n\\nThe walkathon encouraged students to move beyond academic learning and actively engage in social causes, fostering values such as empathy, leadership, teamwork, and civic responsibility. It strengthened community bonding by bringing together students, faculty, and families for a shared purpose, thereby reinforcing the spirit of collective action.\\n\\nFrom an organizational perspective, the event enhanced the visibility and impact of the Rotaract Club’s service initiatives and demonstrated the effectiveness of awareness-based activities in driving social change. Overall, the walkathon left a lasting impression on participants, motivating them to continue advocating for social justice and contributing meaningfully to nation-building efforts.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, sponsored by Rotary Bangalore South (R.I. District 3191), on the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025, at the RV College of Engineering campus. The event was conducted with the objective of addressing the serious social issue of female foeticide and spreading awareness about the importance of gender equality and the protection of the girl child.\\n\\nThe walkathon witnessed the participation of over 350 individuals, including enthusiastic students, committed faculty members, and supportive parents. Participants gathered in the early hours of the morning and walked together along a planned route within the campus, holding placards and banners carrying strong messages against female foeticide and gender discrimination. The use of impactful slogans and visual messages helped draw attention to the cause and encouraged dialogue among onlookers.\\n\\nThe walkathon created a powerful sense of unity and purpose, highlighting the collective responsibility of society in eliminating social evils. By organizing the event on Mother’s Day, the Rotaract Club emphasized the emotional and social significance of respecting and protecting women and girls. The activity served as an effective platform to educate, inspire, and mobilize the community towards positive social change.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/UIZKL18AJ6G5RX6y_12KA.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OXmYaTlm4hnm5S009yknT","name":"Fistfull 2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/3XgyNfdoeqRdZYjU4kz1A.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/kIAvMLekuSGJP4yLLZ9Oq.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The \"FIST FULL\" event resulted in the collection of large quantities of rice and toor dal, benefiting multiple service organizations and spreading hope and nourishment to many, while actively engaging students in social service.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a heartwarming event titled \"FIST FULL\" from November 15th to November 29th, 2024, rallying the campus community to combat hunger and spread kindness in a simple yet profound way. This two-week initiative invited students, faculty, and staff to make a daily pledge: set aside a fistful of rice or toor dal from every home-cooked or hostel meal. These small contributions accumulated into bulk donations, with participants encouraged to deliver 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal by the event''s end.\\n\\nThe beauty of \"FIST FULL\" lay in its accessibility; no grand gestures required, just a mindful handful per meal to symbolize shared empathy. Collection points sprouted across RVCE hostels, mess halls, and common areas, manned by enthusiastic Rotaract volunteers who weighed donations, shared uplifting stories, and tracked progress on a public leaderboard. QR codes linked to a digital pledge tracker, allowing participants to log their daily fistfuls and see the growing total in real-time.\\n\\nEngagement soared as word spread through posters, WhatsApp groups, and cafeteria announcements, drawing hundreds into the fold. Families joined remotely, mailing contributions, while creative twists emerged: dorm challenges for \"fistful relays\" and recipe shares using toor dal. Volunteers hosted mini-awareness sessions, discussing local hunger statistics and how staples like rice and dal sustain underprivileged families, turning donations into teachable moments.\\n\\nBy November 29th, the collection drive overflowed with sacks of grains, ready for distribution to nearby shelters and orphanages. Heartfelt thank-you notes from recipients were shared back with donors, closing the loop on impact. \"FIST FULL\" proved that consistent small acts multiply into waves of change.\\nThis remarkable initiative highlighted how individual kindness combines to create significant societal impact, reinforcing compassion and social responsibility among RVCE students. It left a lasting blueprint for future drives, showing that a fistful of generosity can fill hearts and stomachs alike.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/NzYiJuwHvmwSrNtZusHRB.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Mf2NSK7LS9aT_ZI8QSI_N","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/udRxUYey8I-Nswe6Vr-cM.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/4JXbq80V9ClE7WPys80aS.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The “FIST FULL” event concluded with the successful collection of large quantities of rice and toor dal, which were distributed to multiple service organizations, shelters, and orphanages, providing essential nourishment to those in need. The initiative effectively transformed small, daily contributions into a significant humanitarian effort, spreading hope and food security across the community. At the same time, it actively engaged students in meaningful social service, deepening their awareness of hunger-related issues and reinforcing values of empathy, responsibility, and collective action within the RVCE campus.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE conducted a compassionate initiative titled “FIST FULL” from November 17th to November 21st, 2025, with the aim of combating hunger through collective effort. Students, faculty, and staff were encouraged to contribute a fistful of rice or toor dal from every home-cooked or hostel meal, transforming small daily acts into meaningful support for those in need.\\n\\nThe initiative stood out for its simplicity and accessibility, requiring no monetary contribution—just mindfulness and empathy. Participants were motivated to accumulate and submit 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal by the end of the drive, reinforcing the idea that consistency in small actions can lead to significant outcomes.\\n\\nCollection points were established across RVCE hostels, mess halls, and common areas, where Rotaract volunteers actively managed donations and engaged contributors. The use of QR codes and a digital pledge tracker allowed participants to log daily contributions and view real-time progress, while posters, announcements, and social media outreach helped spread awareness across the campus.\\n\\nBy November 21st, the drive had gathered large quantities of food grains ready for distribution to nearby shelters and orphanages. Sharing heartfelt messages from beneficiaries brought the initiative full circle, highlighting its impact. “FIST FULL” successfully fostered a sense of compassion and social responsibility among RVCE students, proving that even a fistful of generosity can make a lasting difference.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/vtQPdVrYjdbdtiSsaIHfa.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"W1shiWlf7RCM_zWU67VYu","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/v7UCH51nQA9Kfu8K7mzwj.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp helped participants understand the life-saving importance of\\nvoluntary blood donation and dispelled common myths associated with it. It fostered empathy,\\nsocial responsibility, and a spirit of selfless service among students and staff while increasing\\nawareness about health, eligibility, and safe donation practices. The event reinforced the value of\\ncommunity service and encouraged participants to actively contribute to humanitarian causes.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized a Blood Donation\\nCamp with the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and creating awareness\\nabout its importance in saving lives. The camp was conducted on the college campus in\\ncollaboration with certified medical professionals and a recognized blood bank, ensuring a safe,\\nhygienic, and well-regulated donation process. Students, faculty members, and staff actively\\nparticipated in the event, reflecting a strong sense of social responsibility and community\\nservice. Prior to donation, all participants underwent proper registration and medical screening\\nto determine eligibility, and donors were educated about the benefits of blood donation and\\nthe common myths associated with it. The blood collection was carried out under expert\\nsupervision following standard medical protocols, and donors were provided with refreshments\\nand acknowledgment for their contribution. The event resulted in the successful collection of\\na significant number of blood units, which will aid hospitals and patients in need. Overall,\\nthe Blood Donation Camp was a meaningful initiative that strengthened humanitarian values,\\nencouraged selfless service, and highlighted the active role of the Rotaract Club of RVCE in\\ncontributing to society.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/aaijfxXLdPdwo5PzRbtZ-.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oxaI4UxTOy_mvRqpg2ucD","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/n1eALeMWQLQ0B1tFbnHCx.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/qo85eSLBm_WghZguWqPyO.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-31","duration":8,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged rural students by providing them with essential educational materials and school supplies. The initiative created a meaningful impact by ensuring needy students received textbooks, stationery, and other learning resources required for a better education experience. With effective fund collection and proper utilization, the event reflected strong community participation and social responsibility. The collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranava Foundation strengthened the reach of this initiative, helping improve access to education and creating a positive learning environment for students.","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of approximately Rs. 100 to 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which was used to procure and donate mission-needed supplies such as severe deserving students.\\nThe collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed other Rs. 100 or Rs. 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranava Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/HzLtud7U7KfiXcSB_s9Ng.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZWfKpD8DNjmd4cMWkqL3H","name":"INTEL HACKATHON X E-SUMMIT","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/HlnJPudAyLRGb6aZ9aFiB.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/tM3PqdFBKOpZ3FMYWfd23.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Intel Hackathon X E-Summit effectively enhanced participants’ understanding of artificial intelligence through practical exposure and collaborative learning. The event encouraged innovation, problem-solving, and technical skill development by engaging students in hands-on coding challenges and real-world applications of AI. Participants gained insights into emerging AI trends while benefiting from peer interaction and networking opportunities. The hackathon successfully aligned with sustainable development goals by promoting quality education and innovation-driven growth, leaving participants better equipped for future technological challenges.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-08","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Intel Hackathon, organized by E-Cell, was a pioneering workshop on artificial intelligence, centered on themes of open innovation and exploration. Participants, from beginners to AI enthusiasts, engaged in coding challenges, hands-on activities, and networking, delving into the latest AI trends and advancements. Aligned with SDG 9 (Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure) and SDG 4 (Quality Education), this hackathon demonstrated E-Cell''s dedication to fostering a collaborative environment for learning and technological growth. It empowered participants to explore AI''s potential, contributing to the development of skills essential for future breakthroughs in technology and innovation.","aicteMapping":"Innovation / Technical Skill","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/c99vC2Ro1CZqmNp9XnOF2.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tapnIXhpSukskbJhhZvbz","name":"World Entrepreneurship Day","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/zKziPCzh-xF7IH5hZlXXh.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/gP2efeiiDi-GDOfEK4dmV.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-08-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"World Entrepreneurship Day successfully inspired students by exposing them to real-world entrepreneurial experiences and industry perspectives. The panel discussion provided valuable insights into startup challenges, opportunities, and leadership, helping students develop a practical understanding of the entrepreneurial ecosystem. The event strengthened participants’ motivation, resilience, and innovative mindset, reinforcing the role of entrepreneurship in driving personal growth and societal impact.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-21","hoursSpent":4,"description":"World Entrepreneurs'' Day was celebrated at RV College of Engineering with great enthusiasm with the event organized by the vibrant E-Cell RVCE. The event brought together aspiring entrepreneurs, industry veterans, and students to foster a spirit of innovation and enterprise within the campus. A key event highlight was a panel discussion featuring Arvind Prakash Singh, Founder and CEO of SuperBolt, and Shreesha Sridhar, Chairperson of ProjectX Labs. These distinguished guests shared their invaluable insights into the startup ecosystem, discussing the challenges and opportunities faced by modern entrepreneurs. Their experiences and advice gave students practical knowledge and inspiration, igniting a deeper passion for entrepreneurship. The session was informative and motivational, reinforcing the importance of resilience, innovation, and leadership in the entrepreneurial journey.","aicteMapping":"Entrepreneurship Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6cb94d39-efd1-4130-a35e-f70c0623fe27/_DcAZgQ0K67THjKD6kwpv.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 05:31:10.949364+00', '2026-01-31 05:32:50.633667+00'), ('5d6c33e9-9e56-4a4a-b8ac-425a4b62b94d', '81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY045","name":"Prajwal U","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"YEjjdGjwrMzvqM-u1Vlq-","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp successfully collected a substantial quantity of blood units, which were added to the local blood bank’s inventory and will support patients in need of transfusions during emergencies and medical treatments. The event raised awareness among participants and the wider community about the importance of voluntary blood donation, helping dispel myths and encourage future donor participation. It also fostered a strong sense of community engagement, social responsibility, and solidarity among students and volunteers involved in the initiative","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"I participated in a blood donation activity as part of the AICTE Social Service initiative. By voluntarily donating blood, I contributed to supporting patients in need and promoting awareness about the importance of blood donation in society. This activity helped me develop a sense of social responsibility, empathy, and commitment toward community welfare and public health.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/_9JdRXMziT--U8yE5y7Mo.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"51N-HWKKbLtwyEArJ913I","name":"Through the Eyes of You(th) by IUCEE-SPARK","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"Increased student awareness and understanding of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\\n\\nEncouraged creative expression and critical thinking through visual storytelling.\\n\\nEnabled students to connect real-world social and environmental issues with global sustainability goals.\\n\\nEnhanced students’ observational, technical, and narrative photography skills.\\n\\nFostered a sense of social responsibility and environmental consciousness among participants.\\n\\nProvided a platform for students to communicate impactful messages on sustainability to a wider audience.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Here’s a clean, polished paraphrase with the same meaning and a slightly more formal academic tone:\\n\\n**Outcome**\\nThe *“Through the Eyes of Youth”* event was a photography competition focused on the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Organized by IUCEE-SPARK, the initiative encouraged students to use visual storytelling to draw attention to major global issues and possible solutions. The competition offered a creative platform for participants to present their views on sustainability, environmental protection, and social responsibility through photography.\\n\\nStudents were given one week, from 7th to 13th August 2023, to capture photographs aligned with any of the 17 SDGs, covering themes such as climate action, gender equality, responsible consumption, and life on land. Each submission was required to convey a clear and impactful message related to sustainability or a significant social concern, accompanied by a brief description explaining the concept and intent behind the image.\\n\\nEntries were evaluated by a panel consisting of faculty members and professional photographers, based on creativity, narrative strength, technical excellence, and relevance to the SDGs. Overall, the activity effectively combined artistic expression with social awareness, motivating students to engage more deeply with their surroundings and relate local issues to global development goals.\\n","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/2QH0MU0j8UVZdMlzM84eG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"th6mp2hTu-TFIXr25BSVw","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness about the importance of regular exercise, fitness, and a healthy lifestyle.\\n\\nEncouraged active participation from students and community members, strengthening social connections.\\n\\nHelped participants develop resilience, discipline, and goal-setting skills.\\n\\nPromoted teamwork, motivation, and sportsmanship.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The marathon, organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), was designed to promote physical fitness, healthy living, and active community participation. The event attracted students, faculty, and local residents who came together to participate in long-distance running across a carefully planned route within the city. The marathon emphasized endurance, stamina, and perseverance, while also encouraging participants to push their personal limits and set achievable goals.\\n\\nIn addition to its focus on fitness, the marathon served as a platform for social engagement, allowing participants to connect with fellow community members and promote a sense of unity. NSS volunteers played a key role in organizing the event, managing logistics, ensuring safety, and motivating participants. The marathon also highlighted NSS’s broader mission of fostering leadership, teamwork, and social responsibility among students, demonstrating how physical activity can be effectively combined with community service initiatives.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/B7B5dqOUw8GBjtNWzP5fg.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qYR1YLXGVa4ZW5mOpzuim","name":"DHI Day-Data Remix","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced students’ understanding of data analysis, data\\nvisualization, and decision-making using real datasets.\\nEncouraged innovative thinking by integrating business\\noptimization with sustainable development goals.\\nImproved teamwork, communication, and presentation\\nskills among participants.\\nProvided practical exposure to solving real-world\\nproblems using data-driven approaches.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"DHI Day – Data Remix was organized by Team DHI, Department\\nof Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning (AIML), RV\\nCollege of Engineering, as a technical and innovation-driven event\\nfocused on data analytics, visualization, and sustainable business\\nsolutions. The event was conducted as part of DHI Day and\\nbrought together students from various semesters to apply data-\\ndriven thinking to real-world problems.The event was conducted\\nin multiple phases. In the initial phase, participants were provided\\nwith pre-processed datasets and relevant analytical tools to\\nperform data analysis and generate meaningful visualizations.\\nStudents worked in teams of 3 to 4 members, encouraging\\ncollaboration, problem-solving, and critical thinking.The second\\nphase focused on business innovation and optimization, where\\nteams used their analytical insights to propose solutions aligned\\nwith the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\\nParticipants presented their findings and solutions to a panel of\\njudges comprising faculty members, who evaluated the teams\\nbased on creativity, analytical approach, clarity of visualization,\\nand relevance to sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/CgEPY8BW8yiwQcnTIFgiT.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tddEqTvdp24UsU6o-y8wh","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"A significant number of books and study materials were\\ncollected and redistributed to students in need.\\nUnderprivileged children received access to learning resources,\\nsupporting their academic growth.\\nStudents developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of\\nresponsibility toward educational equity.\\nThe activity promoted the values of sharing, sustainability\\n(reuse of books), and community service.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2024 was a social initiative organized to promote\\neducation access and literacy among underprivileged children.\\nThe project focused on collecting and distributing educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery\\nto students from economically weaker sections of society.Students\\nactively participated by donating books and study materials that\\nwere in good condition. Volunteers sorted, categorized, and\\npacked the collected materials based on age group and academic\\nlevel to ensure effective distribution. The resources were then\\nprovided to government schools, community learning centers, and\\nchildren from low-income families who lacked access to adequate\\nlearning materials.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/Odd5AwwvmYzWU4Fk6yNOd.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Y1TTR4saQVR0PNjSUXKFw","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Collected blood units to support hospitals and patients in need, directly contributing to life-saving efforts.\\n\\nRaised awareness among participants about the importance and impact of voluntary blood donation.\\n\\nEncouraged social responsibility, empathy, and community service among students and local residents.\\n\\nProvided Rotaract members with organizational and leadership experience in managing public health initiatives.\\n\\nPromoted a culture of voluntary giving, health consciousness, and civic engagement in the community.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The blood donation camp, organized by Rotaract, aimed to promote social responsibility, health awareness, and community service among students and local residents. The event brought together volunteers and donors at a designated venue, following all medical safety protocols to ensure a smooth and secure process. Participants were educated about the importance of blood donation, its life-saving impact, and the role it plays in supporting hospitals and patients in need.\\n\\nThe camp also served as an opportunity to instill a sense of civic duty and empathy among young individuals. Rotaract members coordinated logistics, registration, health checks, and post-donation care, ensuring a safe and efficient experience for all donors. Beyond collecting blood, the initiative sought to raise awareness about voluntary blood donation as a regular social practice, highlighting how small individual contributions can have a profound impact on the community.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/_NFaa-Bm1U5y0ekpn4GQY.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cIQWIfxufMHWx5Qg-X3TI","name":"FistFul-2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-29","duration":13,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected,\\nhelping address food insecurity among vulnerable\\ncommunities.\\nThe donated food grains supported nutrition programs in\\nold age homes, hospitals, schools, anganwadis, and\\ninstitutions for visually challenged children.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of\\nRVCE in association with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI\\nDistrict 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program\\nfocused on reducing food insecurity and supporting\\nunderprivileged sections of society. The initiative followed a\\nsimple yet powerful concept where each participating student\\ndonated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, turning small individual\\ncontributions into a collective effort with significant impact. The\\ndrive received overwhelming support, with participation from\\nover 2,100 students, leading to the collection of a large quantity\\nof essential food grains. As part of this initiative, I personally\\ncontributed 2 kg of toor dal, which was added to the overall\\ncollection. The donated food grains were then distributed to\\nvarious beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding\\nprograms, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes,\\nhospitals, trust-run schools, and nearby anganwadis. These\\nsupplies helped strengthen existing nutrition programs benefiting\\nchildren, senior citizens, patients, and economically\\ndisadvantaged communities. The distribution was carried out in a\\nsystematic and well-coordinated manner, with beneficiary\\ninstitutions collecting the food supplies directly from the campus\\nunder the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The\\ninitiative focused on creating a sustainable and community-\\ndriven impact, emphasizing long-term support rather than short-\\nterm relief.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/5C4Mf4kB-oCe_Z0vvqOk2.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YsCJnVpGNJM4aBFpyN6sM","name":"Utsarga Marathon-2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"Promoted physical fitness, mental resilience, and overall well-being among participants.\\n\\nStrengthened community engagement and student participation in socially responsible initiatives.\\n\\nEncouraged perseverance, discipline, and personal challenge through long-distance running.\\n\\nEnhanced teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills among NSS volunteers.\\n\\nReinforced NSS’s vision of combining individual development with service to society.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-13","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The second marathon, conducted under the NSS, aimed to promote fitness while also raising awareness about societal and community issues. The event saw enthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and local residents, all coming together to engage in a long-distance run along a pre-determined route, supported by volunteers at checkpoints and hydration stations.\\n\\nThe marathon not only tested the endurance and perseverance of participants but also encouraged them to adopt a disciplined lifestyle, highlighting the connection between personal health and overall well-being. Through this event, NSS volunteers emphasized teamwork, leadership, and social responsibility by coordinating logistics, ensuring safety, and motivating participants throughout the run. Additionally, the marathon served as a platform to foster unity, collective effort, and active civic engagement, reflecting NSS’s mission of integrating personal development with community service and social awareness.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/sFsMAfUlUAhyV1n9d-EoG.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"v5GWzwzDhUolA0XLkF56T","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully collected blood units to aid hospitals and patients, directly contributing to life-saving efforts.\\n\\nEnhanced awareness among participants about the significance of voluntary blood donation.\\n\\nFostered a culture of social responsibility, empathy, and community participation.\\n\\nProvided Rotaract members with hands-on experience in organizing and managing health-related community initiatives.\\n\\nMotivated participants to adopt voluntary blood donation as a regular practice, promoting long-term community health benefits.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-20","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The blood donation camp, conducted by Rotaract, was organized to promote health awareness, community service, and the spirit of volunteerism. The event provided a safe and well-structured environment where students, faculty, and local residents could donate blood under professional medical supervision. Detailed briefings were given to all participants about the donation process, eligibility criteria, and the critical need for regular blood supply in hospitals.\\n\\nThe initiative aimed to instill a sense of social responsibility and empathy among participants while fostering active community involvement. Rotaract members played a key role in managing registrations, health screenings, and post-donation care, ensuring a smooth and efficient process. The camp also served as an educational platform to encourage long-term voluntary blood donation habits, emphasizing how individual contributions collectively save lives and strengthen community health resilience.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/QSU1_mLchk-ePds63oXg5.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hfp12yWU-lrM6zQIjvlq7","name":"Project Pusthak ","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"A substantial number of books and study materials were collected and redistributed to children in need.\\n\\nUnderprivileged students gained access to essential educational resources, supporting their academic progress.\\n\\nParticipating students developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility toward educational equity.\\n\\nThe initiative reinforced values of sharing, sustainability through the reuse of books, and active community service.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social initiative aimed at enhancing access to education and promoting literacy among underprivileged children. The project centered on collecting and distributing educational resources, including textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery, to students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds.\\n\\nStudents actively contributed by donating books and study materials in good condition, while volunteers organized, categorized, and packed the items according to age group and academic level to ensure effective distribution. The collected resources were then provided to government schools, community learning centers, and children from low-income families who otherwise lacked access to essential learning materials.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/9cVbiAo-F_Uzb4-DMhPdT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GX2ewdKZNbFY-woHljz_c","name":"FistFull 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2026-11-21","duration":370,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected, addressing food insecurity among vulnerable populations.\\n\\nDonations supported nutrition programs in schools, anganwadis, hospitals, old age homes, and hostels for visually challenged children.\\n\\nEncouraged mass participation, with over 2,100 students contributing to the collective effort.\\n\\nFostered social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among participants.\\n\\nHighlighted the impact of small individual contributions when combined for a larger social cause.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI District 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program aimed at reducing food insecurity and supporting underprivileged communities. The initiative was based on a simple yet impactful concept: each participating student contributed either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. These small individual contributions combined to create a substantial collective impact.\\n\\nThe campaign received overwhelming support, with over 2,100 students participating and helping to collect a significant quantity of essential food grains. As part of this effort, I personally donated 2 kg of toor dal, which became part of the overall collection. Volunteers organized the collection, after which the food supplies were systematically distributed to various beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding programs, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes, hospitals, trust-run schools, and local anganwadis.\\n\\nThe donated rice and dal strengthened ongoing nutrition programs, benefiting children, senior citizens, patients, and economically disadvantaged communities. The distribution process was well-coordinated, with beneficiary institutions collecting the supplies directly from the campus under the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The initiative emphasized a sustainable, community-driven approach, aiming for long-term support rather than temporary relief.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/rToSLMkO1x2vxinfv4cpE.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NHl4JjmtQOQwuim9JqGq_","name":"Vikasith Bharath Quiz ","slNo":12,"place":"MyGovPortal","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity significantly enhanced participants’ knowledge of\\ngovernment policies, flagship initiatives, and the collective\\nresponsibilities of citizens in nation-building. It encouraged\\ncritical thinking about socio-economic challenges and solutions\\nwhile promoting informed decision-making and civic awareness.\\nThe quiz motivated participants to stay updated with national\\ndevelopments and inspired a sense of responsibility toward\\ncontributing positively to the vision of a developed India.\\nOverall, the initiative supported the development of socially\\naware, informed, and proactive individuals aligned with the\\nideals of Viksit Bharat.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz, conducted through the MyGov\\nplatform, was an awareness-oriented initiative aimed at\\neducating participants about the vision of Viksit Bharat and\\nIndia’s journey towards inclusive and sustainable development.\\nThe quiz focused on key national priorities such as economic\\ngrowth, technological advancement, social welfare schemes,\\ngovernance reforms, and citizen participation in nation-building.\\nParticipating in the quiz helped enhance understanding of\\ngovernment initiatives and future development goals, while\\nencouraging informed and responsible citizenship. The activity\\ncontributed to increased awareness about India’s progress and\\nreinforced the importance of youth involvement in shaping the\\nnation’s future.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/81587448-9f57-40eb-922d-8b47effade73/HD0YsPKYHqcHzjirHuuAa.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"24-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:29:50.003735+00', '2026-01-29 18:23:12.180108+00'), ('5f497fd5-9533-4bc2-93a3-8699707bb8a6', 'a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS024","name":"Ankit Patil","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"7p0AJvxEtSFFSBbWP4jBh","name":"Kannada Habba-2023","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/olaDshC6U2pcQOPwo5ZWO.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-06","duration":6,"outcomes":"The event successfully celebrated Kannada culture through mass singing, fostering regional\\npride and cultural unity among the student body.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-01","hoursSpent":40,"description":"On 05-02-2024, the Kannada Sangha of RV College of Engineering organized the \"Koti Kanta\\nGaayana\" event to celebrate the richness of Kannada culture and language. This mass singing\\nevent was part of a state-wide initiative to unite people through the power of music and shared\\nheritage. Students gathered in large numbers to sing iconic Kannada songs, creating a vibrant\\natmosphere of regional pride and unity.\\nThe event served as a prelude to the Kannada Rajyotsava celebrations, instilling a sense of\\nbelonging and cultural identity among the students. Participants, regardless of their linguistic\\nbackground, joined in the chorus, celebrating the inclusive spirit of Karnataka. The air resonated\\nwith melodies that paid tribute to the land, its poets, and its history.\\nGururaj Basavaraj Ghatigennavar actively participated in this cultural extravaganza. Beyond just\\nsinging, the event was a pledge to preserve and promote the local language and culture in an\\nincreasingly globalized world. It provided a refreshing break from academic routines, allowing\\nstudents to connect with their roots and celebrate the artistic legacy of the state.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/bXg6QGa2UkShM8w9Bg1kM.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MiF96N0uVDCS5ZM0xv5JD","name":"Fist full 2025","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/dRcbYhSk-LQWapCJT1CL5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"Fistful exemplifies the power of collective action driven by empathy and social\\nresponsibility. What began as a simple contribution from each student culminated in a\\nsubstantial supply of essential food grains, positively impacting multiple institutions and\\ncountless beneficiaries.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fistful was a standalone community service project designed to combat food insecurity\\nand support health and care institutions through collective student participation. The\\ninitiative was built on a simple yet impactful principle - every participating student\\ndonated either 5 kilograms of rice or 2 kilograms of dal. With the support of Rotary\\nBangalore Spandana and under the Community Service avenue focusing on Fighting\\nDisease, the project transformed individual contributions into large-scale nutritional\\nsupport for vulnerable communities.\\nEvent Description\\nThe Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each\\ncontributing essential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This\\ncollective effort resulted in the successful collection and distribution of food grains to\\nmultiple beneficiary institutions that serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients,\\nand disadvantaged groups.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8_VxYGfIy3A_L_G8EY6Jx","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/JU66BPZbzHKpkJs5vY6sM.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s education\\nprograms. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and learning resources to\\nunderprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its fundraising goals, amassing contributions\\nthat will sustain classroom initiatives for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students\\nfrom local underserved communities. Beyond the financial gains, the marathon left an\\nindelible impression on all involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from\\nfirst-time runners conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz\\namplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and encouraging future\\ninvolvement. Ultimately, it redefined the act of running as a meaningful pursuit, not only\\nfor personal health and endurance, but for forging a brighter, more inclusive future. The Utsarga\\nAICTE Activity Points 7 Department of Computer Science","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, took place on April 6th, 2025, from 6:00\\nAM to 10:30 AM across the Bengaluru campus. Under the theme \"Help a Child Change the\\nWorld,\" it celebrated health, fitness, and education support for underprivileged children.\\nMonths\\nof planning ensured smooth logistics with sponsor-backed medals, T-shirts, and refreshments\\nalong tree-lined routes. Over 500 runners, including RVCE students, faculty, alumni, and\\nlocals from Karnataka, gathered at dawn. They chose between a 5 km fun run (Rs. 399) or 10\\nkm\\nchallenge (Rs. 449), with all donations funding school supplies and tuition. Warm-ups, cheers,\\nlive music, banners, and photo booths created festive energy. Volunteers in high-visibility\\nvests managed water stations, medical aid, and crowd control with enthusiasm. They helped\\nrunners adjust to long conditions, ensuring safety and inclusivity. Heartwarming scenes\\nfeatured\\nfriends jogging together, families cheering from sidelines, and visitors spectating. Runners\\ncrossed the finish line to roaring applause, greeted with finisher medals and personalized\\ncertificates. Top age-group performers received special trophies, sparking friendly rivalries.\\nOn-site announcements celebrated winners, fueling real-time excitement around the charitable\\ncore. The event proved transformative, blending physical challenge with philanthropy.\\nIt promoted wellness while instilling purpose through unity. Individual strides wove into\\nwidespread positive change for children''s futures.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/d09YlMgoGxAwc71GPY0Ug.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AxSUS-U4If7ekHPAwaGPE","name":"Kannada Sangha : Buy a Tshirt,plant a tree","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/50Dz1cxeuF5TG1EYwRywI.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity successfully encouraged students to actively participate in environmental\\nconservation through tree plantation. It increased awareness about the importance of planting\\nand nurturing trees and promoted sustainable living practices. Participants developed a sense of\\nenvironmental responsibility and commitment towards protecting nature. Overall, the initiative\\ncontributed to fostering eco-conscious behavior among students.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":5,"description":"“Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” was an environmental awareness initiative organized by\\nthe Kannada Sangha with the objective of promoting sustainability and environmental\\nresponsibility among students. The activity aimed to encourage active participation in tree\\nplantation while creating awareness about the importance of preserving ecological balance.\\nAs part of the initiative, participants received saplings along with T-shirts, symbolizing\\nthe commitment to environmental conservation. Students were guided on proper planting\\ntechniques, sapling care, and the long-term benefits of tree plantation. The activity emphasized\\nthe role of individual efforts in combating environmental challenges such as deforestation and\\nclimate change.\\nThrough this initiative, students were motivated to adopt eco-friendly practices and contribute\\ntowards a greener and more sustainable future. The event successfully combined awareness with\\naction, making environmental conservation an engaging and meaningful experience.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/B12AMMzldBdVHdG_7wSkW.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8b91ml78pX1ai_r6vCpSk","name":"Kannada Sangha Activity-2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/FBl8-pu2tEw2H4oHUnQ3o.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-02","duration":4,"outcomes":"Ethnic Day successfully brought the campus together in a celebration of traditional culture,\\nfostering inclusivity and student bonding","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":12,"description":"On 02-12-2024 the campus of RV College of Engineering transformed into a vibrant tapestry\\nof colors and traditions for \"Ethnic Day,\" organized by the Kannada Sangha. This event was a\\ngrand celebration of diversity, encouraging students to step away from their daily western attire\\nand embrace traditional Indian clothing. The atmosphere was electric, filled with the energy of\\nstudents showcasing the rich sartorial heritage of various regions.\\nThe event was not merely about dressing up; it was a cultural exchange that highlighted\\nthe pluralistic nature of the student community. From silk sarees to panche, the campus\\nbecame a living exhibit of Indian tradition. The Kannada Sangha curated the event to ensure\\nit was a respectful and joyous celebration of identity, bringing students together in a spirit of\\ncamaraderie.\\nAnkit Patil participated as a volunteer, contributing to the smooth\\norganization of the festivities. Volunteers helped manage the crowds, organize cultural\\nperformances, and ensure the day proceeded without a hitch. The event strengthened the cultural\\nfabric of the college, creating lasting memories and reinforcing the importance of celebrating\\none''s heritage.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/NaNTNbSrOIYitYR1p5_eI.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uVF0kPIGgLx_Y9MUxh2tX","name":"Blood Donation Camp (2024)","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp (2024) successfully contributed to\\nstrengthening the blood supply for medical needs, thereby\\nsupporting healthcare institutions and patients in need. The\\nactivity reinforced awareness about the importance of voluntary\\nblood donation and helped instill a sense of social responsibility\\namong participants.\\nThe initiative encouraged healthy individuals to actively\\nparticipate in humanitarian causes and demonstrated how\\ncollective action can save lives. Overall, the camp played a\\nmeaningful role in promoting community health, compassion, and\\nresponsible citizenship.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp (2024) was conducted as a\\nhumanitarian initiative aimed at supporting healthcare services\\nand saving lives through voluntary blood donation. The activity\\nwas carried out in association with Rashtrrothana Blood Centre, a\\nRegional Blood Transfusion Centre recognized by the\\nGovernment of Karnataka.\\nAs part of this camp, participants voluntarily donated blood,\\ncontributing directly to the availability of safe blood for patients\\nrequiring transfusions during medical emergencies, surgeries, and\\ncritical treatments. The initiative emphasized the importance of\\nregular blood donation as a vital social responsibility and\\nhighlighted how individual contributions can have a significant\\nimpact on public health.\\nThe camp also served as an awareness-driven activity,\\nencouraging students to overcome misconceptions related to blood\\ndonation and motivating them to participate in life-saving efforts.\\nBy engaging youth in such initiatives, the activity promoted values\\nof empathy, civic duty, and service to humanity.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/hFECK7Y8wVpEF2F5DL5xq.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GOVKj2lt2fuOc-EVAvPV4","name":"Blood Donation Camp (2023)","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-29","duration":24,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp witnessed active participation from\\nstudents and staff members, resulting in the successful collection\\nof blood units to support medical emergencies and patient care.\\nThe activity helped raise awareness about voluntary blood\\ndonation, reduced hesitation among first-time donors, and\\nreinforced the importance of collective responsibility towards\\nsociety. Overall, the camp contributed positively to public health\\nawareness and humanitarian service within the college\\ncommunity","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was conducted by the Rotaract Club\\nof RVCE in collaboration with Lions Blood Centre, Bangalore,\\nwith the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and\\nsupporting the healthcare needs of the community. The camp\\naimed to encourage students and staff to actively participate in\\nhumanitarian service by donating blood for patients in need.\\nThe activity focused on creating awareness about the importance\\nof regular blood donation, its role in saving lives, and addressing\\nthe constant demand for blood in hospitals and emergency\\nsituations. Participants were educated about the blood donation\\nprocess, eligibility criteria, and safety measures followed during\\ndonation. By organizing the camp within the college premises, the\\ninitiative ensured greater participation and accessibility for\\ndonors.\\nThe event emphasized social responsibility and compassion,\\nmotivating individuals to contribute to society through voluntary\\naction. Such initiatives help foster a culture of service and\\nempathy among students while strengthening community health\\nsupport systems.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/He09bX6274RDyP7RRr6_w.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CYlZ5zvPGvo_mR7m0HvBP","name":"Blood Donation Camp (2025)","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp (2025) successfully contributed to the\\ncollection of blood units required for medical treatment and\\nemergencies, thereby supporting healthcare institutions and\\npatients in need. The activity reinforced awareness about the\\nimportance of voluntary blood donation and encouraged\\nresponsible citizenship among participants.\\nThe initiative helped foster a sense of empathy and social\\nresponsibility while demonstrating how collective action can save\\nlives. Overall, the camp made a meaningful contribution towards\\ncommunity health and humanitarian service.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp (2025) was conducted as a\\nhumanitarian and community-oriented initiative aimed at\\nsupporting healthcare services and saving lives through voluntary\\nblood donation. The activity was carried out in association with\\nthe Indian Red Cross Society, Karnataka State Branch, with the\\nobjective of strengthening the availability of safe blood for\\nmedical emergencies and patient care.\\nAs part of the camp, participants voluntarily donated blood,\\ncontributing directly to life-saving efforts for patients requiring\\ntransfusions. The initiative emphasized the importance of regular\\nblood donation as a social responsibility and highlighted how\\nindividual participation can make a significant impact on public\\nhealth and emergency healthcare systems.\\nThe camp also served as an awareness-driven activity,\\nencouraging students to understand the value of blood donation\\nand motivating them to actively participate in humanitarian\\ncauses. By engaging youth in such initiatives, the activity\\npromoted compassion, civic duty, and service to humanity.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/EqHiICmiZNqOxt_pDhn2z.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WgZlqyPd-bf5SzkYtqesC","name":"Project Pustak (2024)","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/3JkfJ7v0mxhYEKClx0wgW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak (2024) successfully supported underprivileged\\nstudents by providing them with essential educational materials\\nrequired for effective learning. The initiative created a meaningful\\nimpact by helping students gain access to textbooks, stationery,\\nand other school supplies that contribute to improved academic\\nengagement and continuity in education.\\nThe activity also fostered a strong sense of social responsibility\\nand community involvement among participants. The\\ncollaboration between the Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranav\\nFoundation enhanced the reach and effectiveness of the initiative,\\nreinforcing the role of student-led efforts in contributing positively\\nto society and promoting inclusive education.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable community service initiative\\naimed at supporting underprivileged students by providing them\\nwith essential educational materials and school supplies. The\\ninitiative was organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of\\nEngineering in collaboration with Pranav Foundation, with the\\nobjective of improving access to basic learning resources for\\nstudents from economically weaker sections.\\nAs part of this initiative, funds were collected through voluntary\\ncontributions from donors, typically ranging between ₹100 and\\n₹350 per individual. The collected amount was efficiently utilized\\nto procure essential educational materials such as textbooks,\\nnotebooks, stationery kits, school bags, and other necessary\\nlearning resources. These supplies were intended to create a\\nconducive learning environment for students studying in\\ngovernment and rural schools.\\nThe project focused on ensuring transparency in fund utilization\\nand maximizing the impact of contributions by directly converting\\ndonations into tangible educational support. Through collective\\neffort and organized execution, Project Pustak emphasized the\\nimportance of social responsibility, educational equity, and\\ncommunity participation in addressing gaps in access to education","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/KBtvtUmdu4qtWywFZeS_T.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HkaNMIrvTxHEMhaPJpFw0","name":"Project Pustak (2025)","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-26","duration":5,"outcomes":"Project Pustak (2025) successfully created a positive social impact\\nby providing essential educational supplies to students who\\nrequired academic support. The initiative helped reduce resourcerelated\\nbarriers to learning and enabled beneficiaries to continue\\ntheir education with adequate materials.\\nThe activity strengthened the spirit of community service among\\nparticipants and highlighted the effectiveness of organized\\nplanning and transparent distribution. It also promoted awareness\\nabout the importance of education and social contribution,\\ndemonstrating how collective effort and compassion can lead to\\nsignificant and sustainable change in society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Project Pustak (2025) is the second phase of a community service\\ninitiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of\\nEngineering in collaboration with Pranav Foundation. The\\ninitiative was aimed at supporting the education of\\nunderprivileged students by providing them with essential school\\nsupplies and learning materials.\\nAs part of this donation drive, funds were collected through\\nvoluntary contributions from students and donors. These funds\\nwere carefully utilized to procure essential educational materials\\nsuch as notebooks, textbooks, stationery kits, pens, pencils,\\ngeometry boxes, school bags, and other required study resources.\\nThe collected supplies were distributed to students from\\ngovernment and economically weaker sections to ensure\\ncontinuity in their education without financial constraints.\\nThe initiative focused on bridging educational resource gaps faced\\nby underprivileged children and emphasized the importance of\\nequal learning opportunities. By transforming small individual\\ncontributions into meaningful educational support, Project Pustak\\n(2025) reinforced the role of student-led initiatives in promoting\\nsocial responsibility and educational equity.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/3bFNHd8htIX0Xr-QSE6Az.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"taxgWicl-piQ2XK0O7f6r","name":"Nasha Mukth Bharat","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-08-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"The pledge initiative effectively promoted awareness and individual responsibility towards\\ndrug-free living, contributing to the larger goal of a healthier, addiction-free India.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Nasha Mukth Bharat Abhiyaan (NMBA) is a nationwide initiative launched by the Ministry of\\nSocial Justice & Empowerment to build a drug-free India. The campaign focuses on spreading\\nawareness about the harmful effects of substance abuse, especially targeting vulnerable districts\\nand youth through various programs such as awareness generation, counselling, treatment, and\\nrehabilitation. It engages educational institutions, communities, and stakeholders to promote\\na healthy, addiction-free society. As part of this campaign, participants were invited to take\\nan online pledge to stay away from drugs and harmful substances, encouraging personal\\ncommitment and inspiring others. The pledge was accessible via the NMBA official website,\\nreinforcing the Abhiyaan’s mission of creating a disciplined, drug-free youth population for\\nnational development","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/9IqR36UiuFohV5hP5daM6.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yQQa00ojm2at-ZOytTRKu","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Keliye - Pledge","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The campaign successfully mobilized first-time voters to pledge their participation in the\\ndemocratic process, strengthening civic responsibility.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"RV College of Engineering participated in the nationwide \"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Keliye\" (My\\nFirst Vote for the Country) campaign. This initiative was a significant voter awareness drive\\ntargeted at first-time voters within the student populace. The primary objective was to instill a\\nsense of civic duty and encourage active participation in the democratic process.\\nStudents gathered to take a solemn pledge to exercise their franchise in the upcoming elections.\\nThe campaign emphasized the power of a single vote in shaping the nation''s future. It was\\nan educational session where students were reminded that voting is not just a right but a\\nresponsibility towards nation-building.\\nAnkit Patil was among the participants who took the pledge. The event\\ncreated a buzz about the electoral process, aiming to combat voter apathy among the youth. By\\nintegrating this pledge into campus life, the college reinforced its commitment to producing not\\njust skilled engineers, but responsible and engaged citizens of India.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a1ead4f9-d063-420a-a475-ef5d6e528fbc/69CcoPFnO6i557bPBiZ5j.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 17:45:34.96379+00', '2026-01-29 18:53:55.520896+00'), ('623166cf-06f0-4ac4-894c-d453cde82da5', 'ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS007","name":"Ananya Kishore Bharani","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"dVsnjkPSVwV2-1zhRddxX","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. ","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/TeG3owzu-0ce-64-ojOkB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"y9FI2Uya_jcOGVNKh1fh6","name":"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz (UTPT) 2023- QuizCorp, RVCE ","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-07-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the event was highly positive, as it strengthened participants’ understanding of Indian knowledge systems and instilled pride in the nation’s heritage. The quiz also promoted analytical skills, teamwork, and intellectual engagement. Overall, Indi-Genius: The India Quiz emerged as a successful and impactful academic event, reinforcing values of cultural awareness, lifelong learning, and national consciousness among students.impactful academic event, reinforcing values of cultural awareness, lifelong learning, and national consciousness among students.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-15","hoursSpent":7,"description":"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz, conducted as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2023, was a national-level quiz fest aimed at promoting Indian knowledge systems, culture, heritage, and intellectual traditions among students. Held from 14th to 16th July 2023, the event provided a platform for participants across the country to engage with India’s rich historical, scientific, philosophical, and cultural legacy in an interactive and competitive format.\\nThe quiz was designed to encourage curiosity, critical thinking, and appreciation for indigenous knowledge systems while fostering a spirit of healthy competition. Through thought-provoking questions and engaging rounds, the event successfully blended learning with fun, making it an enriching academic experience for all participants.\\nParticipation in Indi-Genius contributed significantly to increasing awareness about India’s contributions to various fields of knowledge. The event emphasized the importance of preserving and promoting traditional wisdom alongside modern education, aligning with the broader vision of UTPT to reconnect youth with India’s intellectual roots.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/zdBMaGDXKyq02i9L6bhsZ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nl45V_BMGC-I3jO-4l2zN","name":"Azadi Ka Kalotsav – Independence day Program","slNo":3,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/7U27VVKtXmciE77hZ5da8.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/-W_nwch5-gmVlCDgU1lGQ.png"],"endDate":"2024-08-15","duration":22,"outcomes":"The outcome of Azadi Ka Kalotsav was highly meaningful, as it strengthened patriotic values and cultural awareness among participants and the audience alike. The program successfully highlighted the importance of respecting India’s diverse traditions while standing united as a nation. Participating in the dance performance was a deeply enriching experience, fostering a strong sense of national pride, discipline, teamwork, and respect for both Karnataka’s cultural identity and India’s collective heritage.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-25","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Azadi Ka Kalotsav was an awareness-driven patriotic program conducted on Independence Day at the Manekshaw Parade Ground during the grand flag hoisting ceremony. The event was organized to commemorate India’s freedom struggle, celebrate national unity, and showcase the country’s rich cultural diversity. It aimed to instill a sense of patriotism, respect, and responsibility among citizens, particularly the youth, encouraging them to actively contribute to the nation’s progress.\\nAs part of the cultural segment of the program, I participated as a dancer, performing alongside fellow dancers to express respect for Karnataka’s heritage and India’s unity in diversity. The performance symbolized the harmony between regional culture and national identity, using dance as a medium to honor the sacrifices made by freedom fighters and to celebrate the spirit of independence. Through coordinated movements, traditional expressions, and patriotic themes, the performance conveyed pride in both state and country.\\nThe event was impactful in bringing together students, dignitaries, and the public in a shared moment of national pride. The cultural performances added emotional depth to the ceremony, reinforcing the message that freedom is preserved not only through remembrance but also through cultural expression and unity.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KlcCBdUnMGvmQfot6-OSa","name":"CSITSS 2024 IEEE Conference","slNo":4,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/P5QW_imrOXB4e_qBaKtvr.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"The dedication and enthusiasm were pivotal in the successful execution of this large-scale event. The active involvement ensured high standards of organization and smooth operation across all sessions, providing a professional and enriching experience to researchers, faculty members, and participants.\\n\\nThe event successfully fostered scientific dialogue, provided a platform for knowledge sharing, and promoted research innovation in various fields. Furthermore, the hybrid structure allowed broader participation, increasing the outreach and impact of the conference.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-07","hoursSpent":3,"description":"CSITSS 2024 IEEE Conference was held at RV College of Engineering from 7th November, 2024 to 9th November, 2024, focusing on scientific advancement, societal impact, and collaborative research and innovation. The conference witnessed over 350 research papers being submitted across 11 different tracks, reflecting the diversity and depth of academic contributions.\\n\\nAs part of the community work, the volunteers actively participated in every phase of the conference organization. Volunteers contributed to key tasks, including documentation, planning, organizing logistics, and managing both offline and online sessions. For the first time, the conference adopted a hybrid model, featuring 48 impressive sessions that combined both offline and online modes, facilitating broader participation despite geographical constraints. Volunteers ensured smooth coordination during the event, provided assistance to speakers and participants, managed session schedules, and helped overcome technical and logistical challenges.\\n","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Z8u-2aI8TGAyKM5j4w2jW","name":"Viksit Bharat - Quiz ","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/MmWnAIWC-4oPZtaXiwbJR.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The quiz successfully enhanced participants’ awareness of India’s development vision and encouraged critical thinking on nation-building. It motivated students to stay informed, responsible, and actively involved in contributing to India’s growth and progress.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz was an awareness-oriented initiative aimed at engaging students in understanding India’s vision for a developed nation. The quiz promoted knowledge on national development goals, innovation, governance, sustainability, and active citizen participation, encouraging youth to contribute meaningfully to the country’s progress.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"H2N7XYxM_BgquXqi2iHqg","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":6,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/-OvA-7fhELmSNg67amMsO.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/dabc_UMpsNBXA-nrIY8rZ.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully promoted awareness about social responsibility and the importance of collective action for societal well-being. Participation in the marathon encouraged a healthy lifestyle, fostered a sense of community involvement, and contributed toward earning activity points. The experience was motivating and reinforced the values of fitness, perseverance, and social awareness.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 was a social awareness and fitness-oriented event conducted to promote health, community participation, and social responsibility. The marathon aimed to encourage individuals to contribute towards meaningful social causes while adopting an active and healthy lifestyle. Participants from diverse backgrounds came together to run in support of initiatives focused on the welfare of underprivileged communities, especially children.\\nI participated in the marathon as a runner, completing the run along with other participants as part of the event. Taking part in the marathon provided an opportunity to actively engage in a cause-driven initiative while promoting physical fitness and discipline.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/DIGI2Urca9KzdcDQX_DUr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hdbeaWQxkNi8K8uk5jyxl","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye ","slNo":7,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/t-3ugQ2RS6_uwbf2TUSkD.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The \"Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye\" event was successful in creating awareness among young voters about their electoral rights and the importance of participating in the democratic process. It helped demystify the voting procedure and encouraged many first-time voters to register and actively engage in upcoming elections.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-08","hoursSpent":1,"description":"NSS RVCE organized an online event titled \"Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye\", aimed at encouraging and empowering young and first-time voters to actively participate in the democratic process. The event was designed to raise awareness about the importance of voting and to educate aspiring voters on their rights and responsibilities as citizens of the country.\\nThrough this initiative, participants were provided with important information in the form of quiz about the voting process. It also provided resources and guidance via the official platform:\\nhttps://www.mygov.in/mera-pehla-vote/\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"u1xA3qi_LamcmofSQpQut","name":"UTPT 2024","slNo":8,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The quiz successfully enhanced participants’ understanding of India’s heritage and current developments while fostering analytical thinking and intellectual engagement. Participation in Indi-Genius helped strengthen awareness, confidence, and appreciation for India’s diverse knowledge systems, making it a meaningful academic and cultural experience.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz, conducted as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2024, was a national-level quiz fest designed to celebrate India’s rich heritage, culture, history, and contemporary knowledge. The event aimed to promote awareness of India’s intellectual and cultural legacy while encouraging critical thinking and curiosity among students from across the country.\\nI participated in the quiz as a participant, engaging in various rounds that tested knowledge across multiple domains related to India. The event provided an interactive platform for learning, discussion, and healthy competition, making the experience both educational and engaging.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/pfpWtBR0p02VT2x_3MiWt.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NB1lz-ZiKmSdnmytaHDap","name":"Fistfull","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/rQbrL2-ijx6PNR0_y3k5S.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative received an overwhelming response from students, leading to the successful collection of large quantities of food grains. The event effectively raised awareness about hunger-related issues and highlighted the importance of collective responsibility and compassion. Participation in Fist Full fostered a sense of social responsibility and contributed towards meaningful community service while earning activity points.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-16","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Fist Full was a social welfare initiative conducted by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana from 15th to 29th November. The initiative focused on addressing hunger and food insecurity by encouraging students to contribute essential food grains such as rice and toor dal, reinforcing the idea that small individual contributions can collectively create a significant social impact.\\nAs part of the initiative, students were invited to donate food grains during the collection drive conducted on campus. I participated in the event by contributing to the donation drive, supporting the cause of combating hunger and aiding community welfare efforts.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mGp9kOUGw6Sr0mYmfP_HC","name":"RUSH HOURS 5.0","slNo":10,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/Gfum_2NepbjydX2OqFBfm.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/WRWtBI35W9xsvBgvHMHBj.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/Ua1813crfBb8T_hsLFqO2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event was successfully conducted with active participation from numerous teams. My team performed consistently across the rounds and secured 2nd place overall, demonstrating strong teamwork, creativity, and problem-solving abilities. Participation in Rush Hours 5.0 enhanced skills such as collaboration, strategic planning, and creative thinking, while also contributing to activity points and providing a rewarding competitive experience.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Rush Hours 5.0 was a five-day interactive competition organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE from 17th to 21st March 2025, designed to foster creativity, teamwork, problem-solving skills, and healthy competition among students. The event featured a series of engaging challenges conducted over multiple days, providing participants with opportunities to showcase strategic thinking, artistic expression, and collaboration.\\nI participated in the event as part of a team, taking part in various creative and competitive tasks conducted across the five days. The challenges encouraged innovation, adaptability, and consistent performance, making the experience both intellectually stimulating and enjoyable.\\n","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"q1gmeuaJUJ5gn6mWUJ4JX","name":"RUSH HOURS 4.0","slNo":11,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/iI6XKkoVROMy1_L9ZYYlN.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/Jf71Lmss2wLoEy3RikINK.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/H1mzMQcpxOXgB00-HZ2X2.png"],"endDate":"2023-11-30","duration":6,"outcomes":"The event was successfully conducted with enthusiastic participation from students across the campus. Participation in Rush Hours 4.0 enhanced skills such as time management, creative thinking, and social awareness. The experience was enjoyable and enriching, contributing to personal development and earning activity points.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-11-25","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Rush Hours 4.0 was a multi-day interactive mega event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, designed to engage students through a mix of creative, intellectual, and social-awareness activities. The event aimed to provide a refreshing break from routine while encouraging teamwork, creativity, and personal skill development through a series of structured challenges conducted over several days.\\nI participated in the event as a participant, taking part in the various tasks designed to test general knowledge, creativity, social awareness, and individual talents. The activities offered an engaging platform to learn, collaborate, and express ideas while actively contributing to a positive and energetic event environment.\\n","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jV_xhM1zexf01Wsxev67P","name":"Through the eyes of youth-SDG competition","slNo":12,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce2ef68d-016c-4ea5-96e1-7e1dbbcd67ca/yvrs6NzY-BSovVpQ7dBQY.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The competition successfully raised awareness about the SDGs and encouraged youth to reflect on real-world issues through a creative lens. My entry was recognized for its relevance and clarity, and I secured the Runner-up position. The experience enhanced my understanding of sustainability concepts, improved visual communication skills, and reinforced the importance of youth involvement in achieving global development goals.","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Through the Eyes of the Youth – SDG Competition was an awareness-oriented event conducted by SPARK IUCEE, aimed at encouraging students to creatively interpret and present the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The competition required participants to submit a photograph representing any chosen SDG, along with a written explanation describing how and why the image related to the selected goal. The event promoted visual storytelling, critical thinking, and awareness of global sustainability challenges.\\n\\nI participated in the competition by submitting a photograph aligned with a specific SDG, supported by a clear explanation connecting the visual elements to the goal’s objectives and impact. The activity provided an opportunity to express perspectives on sustainability through creativity and thoughtful interpretation.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Poornima Kulkarni","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr.Rajalakshmi Mudbidre","designation":"Assistant Professor and Associate Dean "},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:22:31.40369+00', '2026-01-30 07:27:01.579837+00'), ('63ffcc92-f4ee-4a07-a587-70ea58ae84f6', '15ce0e24-c1e1-4b7b-80b9-2a3a07194128', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"Tejas Pattar","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 16:21:40.271176+00', '2026-01-30 17:04:05.418451+00'), ('669c8718-97ee-44a5-aa42-3591f4e0277c', 'f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS066","name":"Sithij Shetty","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"uYEKOiqA0mQ5zi16tL6K_","name":"FAST-TREK","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/-ASF98k38Da_xOTF1wa3H.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/Qv5FNVYyYvjjGSS1zk0YT.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/VYp4lyI2H9gqjPm-Hn7iS.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully raised awareness about environmental cleanliness and sustainable practices\\namong participants.\\n• Encouraged active student participation and fostered a sense of social responsibility.\\n• Strengthened teamwork, leadership, and coordination skills through group trekking activities.\\n• Promoted physical fitness, mental well-being, and stress relief among students.\\n• Enhanced the visibility and impact of the Rotaract Club’s community-oriented initiatives.\\n• Delivered a memorable and enriching outdoor experience, strengthening students’ connection\\nwith nature.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":20,"description":"FAST TREK 1.0 was a flagship trekking and social responsibility initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 23rd February 2023. The event combined adventure with environmental consciousness through a cleanliness drive conducted during the trek. Participants assembled early in the morning and traveled to the trekking site after being briefed on safety protocols and event guidelines. The trek through the scenic Huthridurga Hills provided students with an opportunity to experience nature while actively contributing to its preservation. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 750 students, creating a vibrant and energetic atmosphere while promoting teamwork, discipline, and environmental awareness.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JWz2qr3tne7x44-tbPE02","name":"Utsarga Marathaon 2023","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/YH4vEGvQiCUagzW2YOpCL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully raised funds to support needy children and social welfare initiatives.\\n• Promoted awareness about child welfare and the importance of community contribution.\\n• Encouraged physical fitness and a healthy lifestyle among participants.\\n• Increased student and volunteer engagement in social service activities.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2023 was a flagship fundraising event organized by NSS RVCE with the theme “Help a child, change the world.” The marathon was conducted on 4th June 2023 and\\naimed to support needy children through funds raised from participant registrations. Participants were given the option to run either 5 km or 10 km, encouraging individuals of varying fitness levels to take part. The event combined physical fitness with social responsibility, motivating students and volunteers to contribute their time and effort toward a noble cause. All participants were provided with Utsarga T-shirts, certificates of participation, medals of recognition, and refreshments, making the event both meaningful and well-organized.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vYfRYD59_W-q8ExzqkKFf","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/UT5CLo_a5KpYJbwwxPOs_.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/ImJU34iLiNR1imkG9jABg.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully collected blood units to support hospitals and patients in need.\\n• Increased awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.\\n• Encouraged students to participate in life-saving humanitarian activities.\\n• Promoted a sense of social responsibility and empathy among participants.\\n• Strengthened collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Lions Club of Bangalore\\nSouth.\\n• Recognized and motivated donors through certificates, appreciation badges, and AICTE activity points.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with the Lions Club of Bangalore South on 6th June 2023 at the RVCE campus. The event aimed to promote voluntary blood donation and create awareness about the importance of blood donation in saving lives. Students, staff, and volunteers actively participated in the camp, contributing to this humanitarian cause. Proper medical supervision and post-donation care were ensured, with refreshments provided to all donors. Participants were also recognized with certificates of participation and appreciation badges, and AICTE activity points were awarded as a mark of respect for their selfless contribution.","aicteMapping":"Social Service and Community Development","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FpjqjBJQ9fUYsJBY7QQD-","name":"FAST TREK 2.0","slNo":4,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/70C4u4dzfaG-fax2gdu30.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/D11donlCloQMONlm-xfOW.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/1ltUWHaXepsao2WI5Xs3f.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully raised awareness about environmental cleanliness and sustainable practices among participants.\\n• Encouraged active student participation and fostered a sense of social responsibility.\\n• Strengthened teamwork, leadership, and coordination skills through group trekking activities.\\n• Promoted physical fitness, mental well-being, and stress relief among students.\\n• Enhanced the visibility and impact of the Rotaract Club’s community-oriented initiatives.\\n• Delivered a memorable and enriching outdoor experience, strengthening students’ connection with nature.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":40,"description":"FAST TREK 2.0 was a flagship trekking and social responsibility initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th January 2024. The event combined adventure with environmental consciousness through a cleanliness drive conducted during the trek. Participants assembled early in the morning and traveled to the trekking site after being briefed on safety protocols and event guidelines. The trek through the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills provided students with an opportunity to experience nature while actively contributing to its preservation. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 750 students, creating a vibrant and energetic atmosphere while promoting teamwork, discipline, and environmental awareness.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"S8wI5rJGxFl8EfeUhOfJ8","name":"DHI Day","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/95kmdT_tu15nFV3U7xpOA.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/ZRA7LUHtYEeIKes5ak0JA.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Enhanced students’ practical skills in data analysis and data visualization using real-world datasets\\n• Promoted teamwork, problem-solving, and critical thinking through competitive collaboration\\n• Encouraged sustainable and responsible innovation aligned with the UN Sustainable Development Goals\\n• Provided exposure to industry perspectives through interaction with GE Healthcare professionals\\n• Improved presentation and communication skills by pitching technical and business ideas to expert judges\\n• Fostered a holistic approach combining technology, business strategy, and environmental sustainability\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":12,"description":"DHI Day was a technical and innovation-focused event organized by Team DHI, the student technical club of the Department of AIML, RV College of Engineering, in collaboration with GE Healthcare on 6th March 2024. The event began with an expert speaker session hosted by GE Healthcare, followed by the flagship competition Data Remix. Data Remix was structured as a two-phase challenge where student teams worked on data analysis, data visualization, and business innovation using pre-processed datasets. Participants presented insights and visualizations to a panel of faculty judges and later proposed sustainable, technology-driven business solutions aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. The event concluded with final presentations, evaluation, result announcements, and prize distribution, encouraging interdisciplinary learning, innovation, and sustainability-oriented thinking among students","aicteMapping":"Intellectual & Knowledge Enhancement","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hpGPgWze1lTqaKMev2iMw","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye","slNo":6,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/2ZPhDVm5Fg5WL3PlsB0CU.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-03-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Increased awareness about the importance of voting and democratic participation among first-time voters\\n• Encouraged students to take personal responsibility in nation-building through informed voting\\n• Strengthened understanding of constitutional rights and civic duties\\n• Motivated participants to influence peers positively and promote voter participation\\n• Fostered a sense of national pride and democratic accountability","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-05","hoursSpent":16,"description":"The Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye initiative was a national-level voter awareness activity aimed at encouraging first-time voters to actively participate in the democratic process during the 2024 General Elections. As part of this initiative, participants took a pledge to exercise their right to vote responsibly and contribute towards building a strong and developed India. The activity emphasized the importance of informed voting, civic responsibility, and motivating fellow citizens to engage in the electoral process. Through this pledge, students reaffirmed their commitment to democratic values and national development by recognizing voting as a powerful tool for shaping the future of the country.","aicteMapping":"Civic Engagement & National Awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YmEWBH5fGbkqaN2q-CX1g","name":"Matrubhasha Diwas – Echoes of India","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/LZ_VCY_N78bxyWg4eVtNu.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/ySqaxXCPRdYUdUx2RIVD9.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/jzJp8NS_G182PYu5rqYkN.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Promoted awareness and appreciation of India’s linguistic and cultural diversity\\n• Encouraged multilingualism and cultural sensitivity among students\\n• Fostered a sense of unity in diversity through artistic expression\\n• Enhanced teamwork, leadership, and collaboration among participants and volunteers\\n• Provided a platform for students to express cultural identity through music\\n• Contributed to the preservation of traditional and folk music heritage","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-08","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Matrubhasha Diwas – Echoes of India 2025 was a cultural celebration organized by the Alaap Music Club of RV College of Engineering on 8th April 2025 to promote India’s rich linguistic and cultural heritage. The event featured musical performances of folk and traditional songs in multiple Indian languages such as Kannada, Tamil, Telugu, Marathi, Bengali, and Hindi, reflecting the theme of Unity in Diversity. The initiative aligned with the objectives of NEP 2020 by encouraging multilingualism and cultural awareness in educational spaces. Through music, the event provided a platform for students to reconnect with their roots, celebrate mother tongues, and foster inclusivity and cultural sensitivity within the campus community.","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jKQa-MWCwKWDgw783jveb","name":"CAT Student Induction ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/1B_wfIUpClu64Dc0Mm9C2.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/GfR2writm2zWXhI5Gj_33.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Helped first-year students transition smoothly into university life\\n• Promoted social interaction, confidence building, and communication skills\\n• Encouraged peer learning and mentorship through senior–junior interaction\\n• Fostered a sense of inclusivity, teamwork, and campus engagement\\n• Enhanced leadership, coordination, and organizational skills among volunteers","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-28","hoursSpent":16,"description":"The CAT Student Induction Program was conducted at RV College of Engineering for first-year students during the academic year 2024–2025. Senior students actively contributed to planning, coordinating, and conducting various cultural and interactive sessions as part of the induction process. These activities included debates, creative arts, dance, presentations, quizzes, and interactive sessions aimed at easing the transition of first-year students into university life. The program focused on creating a welcoming, inclusive, and engaging environment while helping new students build confidence, communication skills, and a sense of belonging within the campus community.\\n","aicteMapping":"Leadership and Organizational Development","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Vha-k7v_z2YLmvuOfvR_C","name":"TEDx RVCE – Mosaic of Minds","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/ePSclBPrSVpRrP9toN4m2.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/bCGyrCsXITLnspf-L-myq.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Promoted awareness and dialogue on sustainability, environmental conservation,\\nand civic responsibility.\\n• Exposed students to real-world insights from experts in sustainable architecture\\nand environmental journalism.\\n• Encouraged youth engagement with the United Nations Sustainable\\nDevelopment Goals.\\n• Reinforced eco-friendly practices through the distribution of sustainable,\\nbiodegradable goodies.\\n• Strengthened leadership, coordination, and event-management skills among\\nstudent organizers.\\n• Established TEDxRVCE 2025 as a benchmark for student-led, socially\\nimpactful initiatives on campus.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-09","hoursSpent":40,"description":"TEDxRVCE 2025, themed “Mosaic of Minds,” was organized as a full-day intellectual engagement platform focusing on sustainability, environmental awareness, and civic responsibility. Held on 9th June 2025, the event brought together\\nstudents, academicians, and distinguished speakers to explore ideas that address pressing global and societal challenges. The event was the result of over a month of structured planning and coordination by the organizing team, ensuring seamless\\nexecution and high-quality audience engagement.\\nThe event featured insightful talks by Mr. Nikhil Isaac, who discussed sustainable architecture and future-ready urban design aligned with SDG 11 (Sustainable Cities and Communities), and Mr. Gopikrishna Warrier, senior environmental journalist at\\nMongabay India, who highlighted the role of storytelling in conservation, aligning with SDG 13 (Climate Action) and SDG 16 (Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions).\\nEco-conscious initiatives, including the distribution of seed pencils and seed balls as sustainable goodie bags, further reinforced the event’s commitment to environmental\\nresponsibility.","aicteMapping":"Professional Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Y198Mk-_j329W3sIqzUhG","name":"RV Geeks 3.0- Coding Contest","slNo":10,"place":"RV PU College","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/aiHOGlU4bIcZ7H0rI5Mgw.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/tW4Xg0SE5V18pW65Y23vW.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/tC0JDtKXcZrQNZ5VVApps.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-08","duration":7,"outcomes":"A total of 122 students got an opportunity to showcase their skills and enthusiasm for technology. The progressive rounds ensured a funnel approach to selecting top talent, with 67 students advancing to the second round and 39 finalists competing in team-based challenges. Through these rounds, participants gamed hands-on experience with different programming languages and tools. The event helped build confidence in technical problem-solving and fostered a sense of community and healthy competition among aspiring coders. Additionally, the exposure and interaction with the department\\nand club members provided valuable mentorship and inspiration to students considering careers in STEM.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-02","hoursSpent":60,"description":"RV GEEKS 3.0 was a dynamic and intellectually engaging coding competition organized in collaboration with the Department of Computer Science at RVPU and the Coding Club of RVCE, spanning over three exciting days—28th April, 2nd May, and\\n8th May the event provided a vibrant and competitive platform for young minds to explore and demonstrate their skills in logical reasoning, analytical thinking, and\\nprogramming. The competition was thoughtfully structured into multiple rounds; each designed to progressively challenge and elevate the participants'' abilities. With a mix of individual and team-based tasks, RV GEEKS 3.0 successfully fostered a spirit of innovation, collaboration, and enthusiasm for technology among the students.\\nThe primary purpose of RV GEEKS 3.0 was to ignite interest in computer science and coding among pre-university students. The competition aimed to:\\n• Encourage logical thinking and problem-solving skills.\\n• Provide exposure to real-time debugging and coding environments.\\n• Promote teamwork and collaboration in software development.\\nBridge the gap between school-level academics and university-level technical challenges\\nThe event was exclusively designed for students currently pursuing their Second Pre- University (II PU) course. It was open to students from all academic streams, ensuring inclusive participation.\\nKey takeaways:\\nEnhanced Problem-Solving Skills: Exposure to logical reasoning. aptitude, and debugging challenges helped participants sharpen their analytical thinking.\\nHands-On Programming Experience: Practice with real coding questions in languages like Python, Java, and C++ improved technical proficiency.\\nTeam Collaboration: Final round encouraged teamwork and communication through collaborative coding tasks.\\nExposure to Competitive Coding: Participants experienced a structured, multi-round competition format that simulates real-world coding challenges.\\nConfidence Boost: Successfully progressing through rounds boosted self-belief and technical confidence.","aicteMapping":"Professional Skill Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GIo1c5bxebayVxm2vkEbm","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/ZASx1MsJaJT5xe8Z5I6MS.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-26","duration":5,"outcomes":"• Provided essential stationery kits to underprivileged school-going children.\\n• Supported educational continuity and learning among economically disadvantaged students.\\n• Positively impacted the lives of over 5,500 children through community support.\\n• Encouraged social responsibility and active participation among contributors.\\n• Strengthened the Rotaract Club of RVCE’s commitment to education-focused service\\ninitiatives.\\n• Recognized and appreciated contributors for their meaningful involvement in the cause.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of supporting the education of underprivileged children. Through this\\nproject, essential stationery kits were distributed to school-going children from economically disadvantaged backgrounds. The initiative successfully reached over 5,500 children during\\nthe year, aiming to reduce barriers to education and encourage consistent learning. The project emphasized the importance of collective contribution and community involvement in\\nempowering young minds and promoting educational equity.","aicteMapping":"Social Service and Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6on2yNqON7a83HburgYOQ","name":"Club Showcase Day","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/BXAWHDcQmqMRgRD7ceMDZ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/SMu_LyuYWpQzARk2qmZsL.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/W6AleFEjRDiweIQl4k1UE.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-08-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Provided a platform for students to showcase musical talent and creativity\\n• Promoted cultural participation and artistic expression on campus\\n• Encouraged student engagement and collaboration across disciplines\\n• Fostered a sense of community, belonging, and inclusivity\\n• Enhanced confidence, performance, and teamwork skills among participants\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-28","hoursSpent":20,"description":"Club Showcase Day was a cultural showcase event organized by the Alaap Music Club at RV College of Engineering on 28th August 2025. The event aimed to present the musical talent, creativity, and cultural contributions of the club to the campus community. Through a series of live musical performances spanning classical, semi-classical, contemporary, fusion, and band formats, the showcase highlighted the diversity and artistic excellence of student performers. The initiative provided a platform for students to express themselves creatively, foster peer engagement, and encourage wider participation in cultural activities within the institution.","aicteMapping":"Student Engagement and Leadership","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JmJ7iVkSrd03zgqfWNuQB","name":"FISTFULL","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/furl-x0JOwSUtmdnWR8Rc.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f5ce8565-ad19-4296-9b8c-bc108b784673/mDI8GFJrGWrpIQ1M2JtQz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully collected essential food grains from student contributors.\\n• Encouraged active student participation in social welfare activities.\\n• Promoted values of compassion, sharing, and social responsibility.\\n• Created awareness about food security and community support.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fist Full was a flagship social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of supporting food security and encouraging community participation. The event\\nwas scheduled to commence on 1st November 2025, with the donation collection phase running from 17th November 2025. As part of the initiative, students voluntarily contributed either\\n5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. The event aimed to promote empathy, social responsibility, and collective contribution among students while addressing the needs of underprivileged\\ncommunities. Proper coordination and planning ensured smooth execution of the donation drive within the campus.","aicteMapping":"Social Service and Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Raghavendra Prasad SG","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:41:30.481533+00', '2026-01-31 07:10:15.935455+00'), ('6708ae42-1ba5-400e-9bdb-93bbd508ac3b', '721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IM060","name":"Tejas Pathak","period":"2022-2026","department":"Industrial Engineering and Management","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"btBG6xLi-c80TA9qYjgly","name":"Rotaract Fistful","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/TtHP-qdg7SOo5PXSI2af4.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":" The initiative witnessed overwhelming participation from students, resulting in the collection of approximately 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by over 1,750 students. This large-scale contribution highlighted the power of collective effort in addressing hunger and reinforced Rotaract Club of RVCE’s commitment to community welfare and social responsibility. The project successfully transformed small individual contributions into a significant impact for underprivileged communities.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Fist Full was a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 17th to 22nd November 2025. The activity focused on combating hunger by encouraging students to donate either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, mobilizing the campus community to contribute essential food grains for the needy.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/HdgoGIcFUQ69X0BQZiivs.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6SZqQYldmO-mPLOhfV-IS","name":"FAST TREK 2023","slNo":2,"place":"Huthridurga Hills ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/G87fXtnu5GgMXGy4smsrA.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully achieved its intended social and experiential objectives. Through active participation and collective effort, the initiative helped raise awareness and financial support for underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases, reinforcing the spirit of social responsibility among the participants. The well-organized trek, coupled with clear safety instructions and proper logistical arrangements, ensured a safe and enjoyable experience for everyone involved. The scenic surroundings of Huthridurga Betta added to the overall enthusiasm and positivity, making the journey both refreshing and memorable. Overall, the event strengthened teamwork, promoted physical well-being, and contributed meaningfully to a noble cause, leaving a lasting impact on both the beneficiaries and the participants. The provision of breakfast and lunch ensured comfort and sustained energy levels, allowing participants to fully enjoy the experience without logistical concerns. The scenic landscape, combined with shared challenges and achievements during the trek, created memorable moments and strengthened interpersonal bonds.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":9,"description":"The social cause behind the project was to provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the participants boarded the bus to the trek location with great enthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with basic information of the event. The trek was a great success as all the participants had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of Huthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very memorable journey. Breakfast and lunch were provided at the trek location for all the participants","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/SawPrhVjw5PIsS5OMIeF4.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0ElFT8rNDrI7NHLAo2MAO","name":"BEEHIVE Case Study Competetion","slNo":3,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/3UWQhXTvpqfU7UfkcnTiS.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-01-20","duration":4,"outcomes":"Our team emerged as the winner of the Stock Market Competition 2023, reflecting our strong analytical capabilities, strategic planning, and effective teamwork. The experience significantly enhanced my practical understanding of stock market operations, including interpreting market indicators, evaluating investment opportunities, and managing portfolios under competitive conditions.\\nAdditionally, the activity helped me develop essential professional skills such as financial analysis, data-driven decision-making, teamwork, leadership, communication, and time management. Participating in this competition boosted my confidence in applying financial and management concepts to real-world scenarios and provided valuable exposure to competitive environments. Overall, the event was a highly enriching learning experience that complemented my academic background and contributed to my personal and professional development.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-17","hoursSpent":12,"description":"BEEHIVE is a case study competition organized by the Department of Industrial Engineering and Management, designed to foster analytical thinking, problem-solving skills, and industry-oriented decision making among students. The competition provides participants with real-world, multidisciplinary problem statements that reflect challenges faced in operations, supply chain, strategy, data analytics, and systems optimization. Through BEEHIVE, students work in teams to analyze complex scenarios, apply industrial engineering concepts, and propose innovative, feasible solutions within a limited timeframe. The event emphasizes structured thinking, data-driven analysis, and effective communication of ideas through professional presentations. Overall, BEEHIVE serves as a platform to bridge theoretical knowledge with practical application, encouraging collaboration, creativity, and competitive excellence in the field of industrial engineering and management.\\n","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/vmcGIdRt6wISYk1yFKV7_.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ibi4uuXOhJfYcwNyy1spD","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2023","slNo":4,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/HEJOqNahjxE5nJYMCWHvo.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon 2023 resulted in multiple positive outcomes spanning physical, social, and personal development among participants. One of the primary outcomes was the promotion of health and fitness, as students actively engaged in endurance-based physical activity, enhancing stamina, discipline, and overall well-being. Participation encouraged students to adopt healthier lifestyles and recognize the importance of regular physical exercise.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2023 was a socially driven fitness and awareness event organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. Conducted on 4th June 2023, the marathon aimed to combine physical fitness with a meaningful social cause under the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The event encouraged students to actively participate in community-oriented initiatives while promoting a healthy and disciplined lifestyle. The marathon included multiple distance categories, allowing participants to engage based on their physical endurance and interest. Registrations were conducted in an organized online manner, ensuring transparency and accessibility. Participants were guided through clear registration procedures, including payment verification and individual enrolment, which emphasized accountability and proper documentation. The event was held at the RV College of Engineering campus, providing a familiar and safe environment for participants. Through this initiative, NSS RVCE successfully created a platform that fostered social responsibility, physical well-being, and student engagement. The event reflected the NSS motto of “Not Me, But You” by encouraging students to contribute their time and effort toward a noble cause. Overall, the Utsarga Marathon stood as a well-coordinated initiative that blended fitness, service, and social awareness, reinforcing the importance of youth participation in nation-building and community welfare.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/y6DUMo6f9x1eNS1mckya5.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8lcDI0KilQBSss1ckUTDa","name":"Rotaract Blood Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/cU4C1G3e5sIThO16_zvGi.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"From a participant’s perspective, the Rotaract Blood Donation Camp was a highly meaningful and fulfilling experience. Donating blood created a sense of pride and satisfaction, as participants felt they were directly contributing towards a cause that saves lives. The event also helped students understand the importance of regular blood donation and the critical role it plays in supporting patients during surgeries, accidents, and medical emergencies.\\nFor many, the camp served as an opportunity to overcome hesitation or fear related to blood donation, especially for first-time donors. The professional guidance and support\\nfrom volunteers and medical staff made the process comfortable and reassuring. Participants also became more informed about health screening, eligibility criteria, and post-donation precautions, adding to their awareness and confidence.\\nOverall, the camp strengthened empathy, promoted community service, and encouraged participants to continue supporting humanitarian initiatives in the future.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Rotaract Blood Donation Camp was a socially impactful event organized with the objective of promoting the importance of voluntary blood donation and encouraging students to contribute towards saving lives. The camp served as a platform to spread awareness about the continuous need for blood in hospitals and emergency situations, and highlighted how a single donation can make a significant difference.\\nThe event was conducted in a well-organized and hygienic manner with the support of\\ntrained medical professionals. Proper arrangements were made for registration, screening, donor\\nassistance, and post-donation care, ensuring a safe and smooth experience for all participants. Volunteers played an active role in managing crowd flow, assisting donors, and maintaining discipline throughout the camp.\\nOverall, the Rotaract Blood Donation Camp successfully created awareness, motivated first-time donors, and encouraged a spirit of social responsibility among students through meaningful community service.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/5u1Z09kPOSpX9XrgRL01o.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qe1-BxFpdDcgvz6wHZJex","name":"Case Study Workshop","slNo":6,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The TQM workshop resulted in a strengthened understanding of Total Quality Management principles such as continuous improvement, process efficiency, and customer satisfaction. Participants gained insight into the broader role of sustainability and social responsibility in achieving long-term excellence, recognizing that quality extends beyond organizational processes to societal impact. The workshop also encouraged the adoption of environmentally responsible practices, including planting and nurturing plants, fostering a holistic mindset that integrates quality, ethics, and sustainability in both professional and personal contexts.","semester":"7","startDate":"2026-12-13","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The TQM Workshop was primarily focused on the principles and applications of Total Quality Management, emphasizing continuous improvement, customer satisfaction, and employee involvement across organizational processes. Alongside quality management concepts, the workshop also highlighted the importance of sustainability and social responsibility as integral components of long-term excellence.\\n\\nAs part of this broader perspective, participants were encouraged to promote environmental practices such as planting and nurturing plants, drawing a parallel between quality improvement in organizations and sustainable improvement in society. This approach reinforced the idea that TQM extends beyond operational efficiency to include ethical, environmental, and community-oriented initiatives, fostering holistic and responsible management practices.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3pLipnDZEtbAbTEc1S8hA","name":"Under the Peepal Tree - India Quiz","slNo":7,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/sD43-FyXrLe4J9GWuMcTR.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"From a participant’s perspective, taking part in the UTPT India Quiz was a highly exciting and intellectually rewarding experience. The quiz encouraged participants to think critically, make quick connections, and apply knowledge beyond textbooks, especially in topics related to Indian culture and national events. The competitive environment and the high standard of questions helped improve awareness, confidence, and recall ability.\\nThe event also provided an opportunity to interact with quiz enthusiasts from different teams, making it a great platform for networking and learning. Participating in a well-known quiz fest like UTPT gave students exposure to a national-level quizzing experience and inspired many to explore quizzing further as a serious skill and hobby. Overall, the quiz enhanced both general knowledge and analytical thinking while delivering an enjoyable and memorable experience.\\n","semester":"","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Under the Peepal Tree (UTPT) is the flagship quiz festival hosted by RV QuizCorp, RV College of Engineering, and is recognized as one of the most prestigious student-run quizzing events in India. As a part of this quiz fest, the India Quiz is a major event that celebrates India’s rich diversity through questions spanning culture, history, politics, sports, cinema, geography, literature, and current affairs. The India Quiz is designed to test not just factual knowledge, but also awareness and connection with “all things Indian,” making it engaging and competitive for participants from different backgrounds. The event attracts high participation due to its challenging question quality, professional quizmastering, and the energetic atmosphere created by the organizers. Overall, the\\nUTPT India Quiz is a highly anticipated event that contributes to RVCE’s legacy of excellence in collegiate quizzing.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/VTLum4x6rK19qa6eOpTtE.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iBv4LL61qngj0_yWU1yQb","name":"","slNo":8,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JsO69eAIsqfJjE2oRhqPY","name":"EDU-VITALITY (IEEE ComSoc)","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/721f018d-b057-482d-971d-e2261c1d7c5a/PiXu-hP8K0Md1K1u-SqeQ.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":2,"outcomes":"The EDU-VITALITY event resulted in enhanced awareness of emerging technologies in communication systems, artificial intelligence, and industry-driven engineering practices. Participants gained valuable insights from experts from academia and industry, particularly on bridging the gap between theoretical learning and real-world applications. The workshop helped strengthen technical knowledge, encouraged interdisciplinary thinking, and provided exposure to current industry expectations and career pathways. Overall, the event contributed to improved professional readiness, networking opportunities, and motivation to pursue innovation and continuous learning in the field of engineering.","semester":"","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The EDU-VITALITY event was a two-day educational workshop held on June 7th–8th, 2024 at RV College of Engineering, organized by IEEE ComSoc in association with RVCE and the IEEE ComSoc Bangalore Chapter, with industry collaboration from Intel Technology India. The program focused on enhancing academic and industry readiness by exposing participants to emerging trends in communication technologies, artificial intelligence, and engineering education. Through expert talks, interactive sessions, and knowledge sharing by industry professionals and academicians, the event aimed to bridge the gap between academia and industry, promote technical excellence, and inspire students to engage with cutting-edge technological advancements.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9gDANBGWvdlJyL23xNlyh","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":10,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on\\n11th May 2025, coinciding with Mother’s Day, with the objective of raising awareness about\\nthe issue of female foeticide and promoting the value of the girl child in society. The walkathon\\nbegan early in the morning from the RVCE campus and involved participants marching\\ntogether\\nwith placards and slogans advocating gender equality and social justice. served as a powerful platform to amplify the message of social equality and reinforced the\\nRotaract Club of RVCE’s commitment to driving meaningful social change.","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on\\n11th May 2025, coinciding with Mother’s Day, with the objective of raising awareness about\\nthe issue of female foeticide and promoting the value of the girl child in society. The walkathon\\nbegan early in the morning from the RVCE campus and involved participants marching\\ntogether\\nwith placards and slogans advocating gender equality and social justice.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 14:09:27.150306+00', '2026-01-29 17:48:53.173571+00'), ('67c4f3b3-aa32-48ad-8094-9df3d1f8cd11', '24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV052","name":"Maktumsab Imamasab Mulla","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"rxGf8zyD0oCIE-HGwFgfF","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"24","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/LTnYu0Qu3pbEaRTuMQn8b.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility and gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that myefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my physical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating anpositive change\\nin society. This cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5 km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced\\nmy belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causes in the future.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/zutyKkzkkYpU10RCZXZ14.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2kN8KF8kEwWwTYUCb7Yii","name":"Cheela Mela paper bag","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/IcVhwN-NF7NPjtmm2q2oX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"The activity created awareness among students about the harmful effects of single-use plastics on the environment.NSS volunteers gained hands-on experience in making eco-friendly paper bags using recyclable materials. It encouraged the adoption of sustainable alternatives to plastic bags among students and the local community. The activity strengthened the spirit of social responsibility and environmental stewardship in line with the NSS motto “Not Me But You”.Students developed teamwork, creativity, and practical skills through group participation.The initiative contributed to waste reduction and recycling practices on campus.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The NSS unit at RV College of Engineering organised the Paper Bag Making activity as part of its ongoing efforts to promote environmental awareness and sustainability on campus and in the surrounding community. Volunteers from the NSS unit gathered recyclable materials, such as old newspapers and waste paper, and were trained in making eco-friendly paper bags using simple tools and techniques. The primary aim of this initiative was to encourage the reduction of single-use plastic by demonstrating a practical, biodegradable alternative. During the activity, NSS volunteers worked in groups to create paper bags, learning hands-on skills in sustainable crafting while understanding the environmental impact of plastic pollution.\\nThese paper bags were later distributed or shared with local vendors and community members, coupled with awareness discussions on the importance of switching from plastic to paper solutions. The project reinforced the NSS motto of “Not Me But You” by combining skill development with civic responsibility and environmental stewardship\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/njqaqSUcOyHrrYLETW_Xc.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EsryptFue91uS1WLllsWi","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"25","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/0ua_5R_SHBpBMuE43RTGC.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility and gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my physical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating anpositive change\\nin society. This cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5 km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continuecontributing to similar causes in the future.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/P9xJfS6RovvO6yVufjO-q.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qQk66UIltfx5tannsFFX0","name":"Kannada Sangha T-shirt","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/FBA5vyMhq7t0B2CaDAZU5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity successfully instilled a sense of pride and respect for the Kannada language and culture among students of RV College of Engineering.It helped in strengthening Kannada bhimana by encouraging students to openly express their love for Kannada through the T-shirt campaign..The initiative promoted unity and cultural bonding among students from diverse linguistic and regional backgrounds on campus. Students became more aware of Karnataka’s cultural identity and heritage, fostering inclusivity and cultural appreciation. Through the “Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” concept, the activity also enhanced environmental awareness and social\\nresponsibility among participants\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-27","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Kannada Sangha T-shirt activity at RV College of Engineering (RVCE) was a campus event organized by the Kannada Sangha to promote both Kannada cultural pride and environmental responsibility among students. As a part of this initiative, the club introduced a campaign titled “Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” in which students were encouraged to purchase specially designed Kannada Sangha T-shirts. Each participant who bought the T-shirt also received a tree sapling, along with guidelines for planting and nurturing it, to personally contribute to environmental sustainability by planting the sapling in their neighbourhood or community. The event was structured so that students engaged in cultural pride and social responsibility together, and efforts were made to award AICTE activity points for participation to acknowledge student involvement\\nThe Kannada Sangha itself is a long-standing student club at RVCE, dedicated to celebrating and preserving Kannada language and culture through various programmes and events, helping both Karnataka locals and non-Kannadiga students connect with the state’s linguistic heritage\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/fnI_oZpSn23jkWWn9N5F3.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"J60EwbTREu8Z7Ah7IYd-i","name":"Fistfull","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/wJfjBS5DYdfaagM7zvd2D.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the donation drive held at the RVCE campus was the successful collection of essential food items to support underprivileged communities. The initiative helped address basic nutritional needs and contributed to food assistance efforts. It fostered a sense of social responsibility and empathy among students while encouraging active participation in community service. The activity also strengthened awareness about the importance of collective effort, demonstrating how small contributions can create a meaningful and positive impact on society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-13","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A contribution of 2 kg of toor dal was made during the donation drive held at the RVCE campus.\\nThe initiative was organized with the objective of supporting food assistance programs.\\nIt aimed to extend help to underprivileged communities through essential supplies.\\nThe drive encouraged student participation in social welfare activities.\\nIt highlighted the importance of collective responsibility toward society.\\nFood grains collected were intended for meaningful community support.\\nSuch initiatives help address basic nutritional needs.\\nThey also promote empathy and humanitarian values.\\nThe campus environment fostered a spirit of service and unity.\\nStudents were motivated to contribute in practical ways.\\nThe activity emphasized giving back to society.\\nIt reflected the role of educational institutions in social development.\\nSmall contributions together create a larger impact.\\nThe drive served as a reminder of social accountability.\\nOverall, the initiative strengthened awareness about community welfare.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/d8Gqvhv9oODhbvmLdPGuL.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DxpV4ZmWQhkhHY91pz7s7","name":"Yes+ Workshop","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/_MBnwfNBcSpsipbcTQtaM.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-16","duration":4,"outcomes":"The outcome of this activity was increased awareness and understanding of mental health and emotional well-being among participants. It helped develop practical skills for stress management, mindfulness, and self-regulation, contributing to improved mental clarity and emotional balance. The program empowered youth to recognize the importance of mental health in daily life and encouraged them to share this awareness within their communities, supporting the objectives of the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative. Overall, the activity fostered personal growth, social responsibility, and a positive approach toward holistic well-being.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-13","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The activity involved voluntary participation at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, during the academic year 2025–26 through the YES+ (Youth Empowerment Seminar for Students) program. The initiative focused on creating awareness about the importance of mental health and well-being in alignment with the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative of the Government of India. Conducted under the guidance of The Art of Living organization, the program emphasized stress management, mindfulness, and emotional balance while empowering youth with practical life skills. The experience contributed to personal development, social awareness, and an understanding of mental health as a key component of holistic well-being, while also encouraging active involvement in national-level humanitarian and educational initiatives.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/Y-R0VQqZdsc5xEE9CP5Hs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7kW2zhHkYxXt6QkX5kjks","name":"Yes+ service","slNo":7,"place":"Art of living centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/yKvAYUbhZ5Zc0U0WHs8Iu.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the Gaushala activity was increased awareness about the importance of conserving and protecting indigenous cow breeds of India. Participants gained an understanding of animal welfare practices, sustainable agriculture, and the ecological benefits associated with native cattle. The initiative fostered a sense of responsibility, compassion, and respect for animals while encouraging active involvement in environmental conservation and traditional practices that support rural and agricultural sustainability.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-21","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The activity involved voluntary participation at the Gaushala initiative conducted at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, during the academic year 2025–26. The program focused on the conservation, care, and nurturing of indigenous cow breeds of India, highlighting their cultural, ecological, and agricultural significance. Through this initiative, awareness was created about traditional cow-rearing practices, sustainable agriculture, and the importance of protecting native breeds. The activity encouraged responsibility toward animal welfare and environmental sustainability while fostering values of compassion, service, and respect for nature among participants.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/VbrH_yuch9A4CYZDdd9MT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mtuPAlfFfme4864YLYHP_","name":"Yes+ service","slNo":8,"place":"Art of living Centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/q6VKD6yAXqxy-3JYVXFFq.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of the Community Kitchen activity included enhanced awareness of the importance of hygiene, teamwork, and discipline in large-scale food service operations. Participants developed a sense of responsibility and cooperation while contributing to the efficient preparation and distribution of meals. The activity fostered values of selfless service, compassion, and equality, while also strengthening practical skills related to organization, coordination, and community engagement.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-27","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The activity involved active participation in the Community Kitchen initiative at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, during the academic year 2025–26. The program focused on supporting the preparation and distribution of food on a large scale, where participants assisted in cutting vegetables, cooking support, serving meals, setting up the kitchen area, and ensuring proper cleaning and hygiene. The initiative highlighted the importance of teamwork, time management, and discipline in efficiently managing community food services. It also emphasized values of selfless service, equality, and compassion by contributing to the provision of nutritious meals for a large number of people, while strengthening a sense of social responsibility and community engagement among participants.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/24e4abc4-12b4-4873-98a6-903d1aabebc7/APjC1jIQgcUYTyGHquJdI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Venugopal G","designation":"asst professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 12:48:53.216728+00', '2026-01-29 17:08:46.57385+00'), ('6858c40a-df4b-42cf-ab27-df8f6e322516', '97a4bd32-af77-436b-9392-314912d57403', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22BT004","name":"ANANYA S PADASALGI","period":"2022-2026","department":"Biotechnology","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 11:03:41.131792+00', '2026-01-30 11:03:41.131792+00'), ('68a5dd0b-2e8d-4a42-9463-5878917b5b21', '58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC184","name":"Vipul Shivakumar Joshi","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"3Snmh34PvCIRZTnjXQg2t","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 ","slNo":1,"place":"Around RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/vY2VqypWbCrzFwtp8ZkD3.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event promoted physical fitness, empathy, and social awareness among participants. It\\nstrengthened teamwork, leadership, and volunteerism while fostering a sense of fulfillment\\nthrough contribution to a meaningful social cause. Additionally, the marathon encouraged\\na spirit of unity and collective responsibility, inspiring participants to actively engage in\\ncommunity service initiatives. The experience reinforced the importance of sustained individual\\neffort in creating a positive and lasting social impact. Participants, reinforcing the spirit of\\nteamwork and determination. The well-organized event featured\\nstructured routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance,\\nensuring a smooth and safe experience for all runners.\\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign,\\nencouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while\\ngiving back to society. ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is a 5-kilometer charity marathon that symbolized a commitment to health,\\nfitness, and social responsibility, while contributing meaningfully toward shaping a child’s\\nfuture. Guided by the theme “Help a Child, Change the World,” the event emphasized the\\nrole of collective effort in supporting education for underprivileged children. The marathon\\nfeatured both 5 km and 10 km run categories, encouraging inclusive participation across varied\\nfitness levels. With an impressive turnout of over 1,650 participants, including students, faculty\\nmembers, and external runners, the event reflected strong community involvement and social\\ncommitment. The presence of esteemed dignitaries such as the Principal, Vice-Principal, Dean\\nof Student Affairs, and Dean of Academics added significance and reinforced the values of\\nservice, leadership, and civic responsibility upheld by NSS RVCE. The event was meticulously\\norganized with the coordinated efforts of nearly 200 dedicated\\nvolunteers, structured into specialized teams managing publicity, registrations, route\\ncoordination, refreshments, hospitality, and logistics.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/Y2MmQLav8P55HtiUYHZV4.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UAGrj2TT22YokTImNYM_G","name":"Project Pustak - 2024","slNo":2,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/df0e2EMg0hPFh9hQCewMz.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak 2024 was conducted in collaboration with the Rotaract Club of RVCE through an online mode. The initiative aimed to promote the value of education by engaging participants virtually and coordinating efforts to support learning and knowledge-sharing activities, ensuring wider reach and effective participation despite geographical limitations.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-05","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2024 was conducted in collaboration with the Rotaract Club of RVCE through an online mode. The initiative aimed to promote the value of education by engaging participants virtually and coordinating efforts to support learning and knowledge-sharing activities, ensuring wider reach and effective participation despite geographical limitations.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/R-62s57fzKpNurtErGsrM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"odguuxmD8C4CxmhyoD4FU","name":"World Space Week 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/iA4REZRp4gjND-mXDk_I_.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-10","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event enhanced students’ technical, creative, and problem solving skills while deepening their understanding of the role of space technology in addressing climate change. It also inspired innovation, interdisciplinary thinking, and sustained interest in space and climate-related research and applications.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-10-09","hoursSpent":0,"description":"World Space Week 2024 was celebrated on October 9th and 10th, focusing on the theme ‘Space and Climate Change.’ Team Antariksh organized events including a Payload Design Hackathon, where participants worked on designing a CubeSat payload based on given constraints, a Solid Rocket Motor Workshop that offered hands-on experience in building a solid rocket motor, and an Art Competition (online submissions) themed around space and climate change, organized in collaboration with Sattva,the Arts club of RVCE.\\n","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/JDDHzzLTT5useLdeM1fFT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Sel5PwgpLPWp7gm5wqR77","name":"IEEE MTTs Event","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/JfJK_YvrMJiFLvWcfShf0.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event provided students with valuable exposure to advanced antenna research and emerging trends in 5G and 6G technologies. It also enhanced their organizational, teamwork, and leadership skills through hands-on involvement in managing a large technical event.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Members of the IEEE MTT-S Student Branch Chapter volunteered for the IEEE–IETE collaborative event titled “Innovations in Active and Passive Antenna Systems for 5G and 6G Mobile Communication” held on 28/11/2024. The event brought together eminent academicians and industry experts to discuss cutting-edge advancements in antenna technologies for next-generation communication systems, with participation from 130 attendees across Karnataka. Student volunteers actively supported the event through responsibilities such as invitation coordination, materials management, venue setup, and catering arrangements, ensuring smooth and professional execution of the workshop. ","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/zjFsMX4eDSZ1prEIbWKmn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"k-OitzJUgmBxOZjov2DnT","name":"Fistfull - 2024 ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/2i3NUhKQYe3eg_BeeVpvg.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-10","duration":1,"outcomes":"6700+ kg of Rice and 800+ kg of Toor Dal was collected. The donation phase held on 10th Dec\\n2024. Seven NGOs namely,\\n1) A.I.R Humanitarian Homes.\\n2)Pruthvi Foundation.\\n3)Sai Aashraya Super Specialty Hospital.\\n4)Amrutavani Old Age Home.\\n5)Sneha Jyothi Orphanage.\\n6)Hanuman Temple.\\n7) Nele Foundation were benefitted with tons of rice and hundreds of kilos of Toor Dal.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-10","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fistfull 2024 was a hunger alleviation and food donation drive aimed at addressing food insecurity among underprivileged communities. The initiative encouraged students to donate\\nessential food grains, reinforcing the belief that small individual contributions, when combined, can create a significant and lasting social impact. The drive witnessed enthusiastic participation from students across various departments, reflecting a strong sense of empathy, social responsibility, and collective commitment toward community welfare. The activity served as a platform to sensitize students to the realities of food scarcity and the importance of sustainable humanitarian efforts. Through coordinated collection and distribution, the drive strengthened the spirit of volunteerism and demonstrated how organized student participation can effectively support vulnerable sections of society","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"C874ll6tgi5z4aZeIt_5u","name":"IEEE MTTs and AP-s DL","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/83ds4hNexXPieJ64aHNWK.png"],"endDate":"2025-06-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The workshop enhanced participants’ understanding of advanced antenna concepts and emerging research trends in wireless and satellite communications. It also inspired students to pursue innovation and research in antenna technologies while\\nstrengthening industry–academia interaction. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"An IEEE Distinguished Lecturer (DL) Workshop on Advanced Antenna Technologies was conducted at RV College of Engineering, Bangalore, organized jointly by the IEEE AP-S Bangalore Chapter and IEEE MTT-S RVCE Student Chapter. The workshop featured eminent IEEE Fellows and experts who delivered technical talks on satellite and ground antenna systems, hybrid UTD-ECM solutions, polarization in electromagnetics, and open-source 5G testbeds. The event saw active participation from around 100 students, researchers, and professionals, providing a strong platform for knowledge exchange and interaction with leading academicians and industry specialists. ","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/93LxiStuLAl60-fKpkSQI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Z76_6lX3va-GemMMIFhry","name":"Utsarga Marathon - 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/JIcVz-bg-3VKc6vVjtSDB.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully completed the 5km marathon run and helped in contributing towards a noble cause. Participants demonstrated strong enthusiasm and commitment, reflecting a growing awareness of the importance of maintaining a healthy\\nlifestyle and contributing to social causes. Overall, the Utsarga Marathon 2025 made a positive and lasting impact by combining fitness, awareness, and service, reinforcing the role of youth\\nas active contributors to a healthier and more socially responsible society .\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Participated in a 5-kilometer charity marathon that celebrated health and physical fitness while offering a meaningful opportunity to make a social impact. The event symbolized a\\ncommitment to reshaping a child’s future through collective action. Guided by the theme “Help a Child, Change the World,” the marathon emphasized the role of individual effort in supporting education for underprivileged children, where every step taken contributed toward a larger social cause.Conducted under the aegis of the National Service Scheme (NSS), the marathon brought together students, faculty members, alumni, and members of the public from diverse backgrounds to collectively run for a cause. The event effectively spread awareness about the importance of physical fitness, youth engagement, and community service. Utsarga Marathon 2025 fostered an energetic and inclusive environment, reinforcing the values of unity, service, and social responsibility, while inspiring participants to actively contribute toward nation-building and sustainable social development. ","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/B1wWG1oMRrIFL8GHTnWDY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t3FA0M89aeK0MrC3OSrak","name":"Project Pustak - 2025 ","slNo":8,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/WS6SvpJBwyqqySFqx6BO-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project resulted in increased awareness about educational opportunities and the value of continuous learning. It encouraged effective digital participation and strengthened coordination and communication among volunteers. The initiative also highlighted the potential of online collaboration in delivering impactful educational and community-driven programs.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was organized in association with the Rotaract Club of RVCE and conducted through an online platform. The initiative aimed to support educational development by creating virtual opportunities for learning, interaction, and awareness. It emphasized inclusivity and accessibility, allowing participants from diverse backgrounds to engage effectively.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Qd3kjnljdk89zRnEYeEBZ","name":" Fistfull – 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/oROJAxv5xqackPNAUevqJ.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Took part in a noble cause. Overall, 2146 students donated 4370 kg of rice and 2516 kg of dal and helped 7 beneficiaries such as: Hanuman Temple (1300 kg), Pruthvi Foundation\\n(900 kg), Amrutavani Vridh Seva Samithi (900 kg), Sai Ashraya Hospital (2000 kg), Sai Satguna Sangrama Trust (800 kg), Nele Foundation (900 kg) and nearby anganwadis. The collective effort resulted in the successful collection and distribution of food grains to the above listed beneficiaries. The project transformed individual contribution into large scale nutritional contribution to vulnerable communities. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized the FistFull initiative as a voluntary community service event aimed at addressing food insecurity and supporting health and care institutions. Under this initiative, students were encouraged to contribute 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, fostering a spirit of social responsibility and collective participation among the student community. The event was conducted with the support of Rotary Bangalore under the Community Service Avenue, with its primary area of focus being Fighting Disease. By ensuring the availability of essential food supplies, the initiative sought to indirectly promote health, nutrition, and well-being among vulnerable populations residing in care and healthcare institutions.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"G1LPHe-mtgQ3vdfS8yKyg","name":"Kannada Habba","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/58010599-0aa4-4321-982d-73d6f14d6a82/K6Wh4Z2GCL9kQuEPlKTg0.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully strengthened appreciation for Kannada language and culture among students. It enhanced cultural engagement, teamwork, and organizational skills of the volunteers while providing a vibrant platform to celebrate regional identity and unity within the institution.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Kannada Habba was organized in association with the Kannada Sangha, RVCE, to celebrate and promote the rich cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event showcased various aspects of Kannada language, traditions, and culture through well-coordinated activities, encouraging active participation from students and fostering cultural awareness on campus","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. S Praveen","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 20:47:41.94884+00', '2026-01-31 03:27:27.81814+00'), ('68ccf851-2c2b-4d7c-8c69-852492d0b566', 'b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV001","name":"Abhijit Dutta","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"ih9y8YlcDEejoYsOn6KSm","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/tlsWdYe4MlPjzpt_UntS8.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon concluded with significant social, organizational, and\\ncommunity-oriented outcomes. The event successfully mobilized more than 500 participants,\\ndemonstrating strong public engagement and widespread support for the cause of helping\\nunderprivileged children.\\nThe marathon also strengthened the culture of volunteerism, teamwork, and civic responsibility\\nwithin the NSS RVCE community, as volunteers efficiently managed logistics, safety measures,\\nhydration points, route coordination, and participant support. The structured execution of the\\nrun enhanced event management, planning, and leadership capabilities among organizers.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, a flagship community welfare initiative conducted by NSS RVCE, was\\norganized with the central theme “Help a Child, Change the World” emphasizing support for\\nunderprivileged children requiring educational and healthcare assistance.\\nThe event commenced at 7:00 AM with systematic registration, verification, and distribution of\\nevent shirts, badges, and participation materials, creating uniformity, identity, and enthusiasm\\namong attendees. Pre-event announcements, energy sessions, and safety briefings were\\nconducted to ensure preparedness and smooth coordination. Medical teams, hydration points,\\nvolunteers, and emergency response units were strategically stationed along the route to\\nmaintain participant safety and well-being.\\nThe Marathon officially began at 9:00 AM and witnessed active participation from over\\n500 individuals, including students, faculty members, and fitness enthusiasts. The carefully\\nplanned route encouraged inclusivity and accessibility, offering a balance of challenge and\\nengagement for runners of varying fitness levels. Throughout the event, NSS volunteers\\nfacilitated crowd management, route guidance, and awareness messaging, reinforcing the\\nevent’s social objective.\\nBeyond promoting physical fitness and recreational involvement, the marathon aimed to create\\nconsciousness about the struggles faced by underprivileged children and the importance of\\ncollective community action in addressing them. The event fostered social responsibility,\\nvolunteerism, compassion, teamwork, and civic participation within the campus community\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PquNF1PdmP7s_gdsmw6jv","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/Qria3pj-3NXaLqgNqSEDp.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp was very successful and received a good response from students,\\nteachers, and local community members. Many volunteers came forward to donate blood, and\\na significant number of blood units were collected. The event helped raise awareness about\\nthe importance of donating blood regularly and motivated others to participate in future drives.\\nIt also built a sense of social responsibility, compassion, and teamwork among participants.\\nOverall, the camp contributed to saving lives and supporting the healthcare system. The camp\\nwas a great success, with many volunteers donating blood and spreading awareness about its\\nimportance. The event helped in collecting several units of blood that will benefit patients in\\nneed. It also inspired participants to contribute to humanitarian causes and highlighted the value\\nof selfless service. Overall, the Blood Donation Camp strengthened the spirit of compassion,\\nresponsibility, and community welfare among all participants.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Blood Donation Camp is an organized event where volunteers donate blood under the\\nsupervision of medical professionals. It is conducted to collect blood for hospitals and blood\\nbanks, promote awareness about blood donation, and encourage people to contribute to society.\\nThe camp ensures safety, proper hygiene, and medical screening for all donors. The blood\\nis collected safely by trained medical staff using sterile equipment. Such camps also include\\nawareness programs to educate people about the importance of blood donation and how one\\ndonation can save several lives. A Blood Donation Camp was organized to collect blood from\\nvoluntary donors and create awareness about the importance of blood donation. The camp was\\nconducted in collaboration with a local hospital and medical professionals, who ensured all\\nsafety and hygiene measures. Students, teachers, and community members actively participated\\nin the event. The main aim of the camp was to help save lives, promote social responsibility,\\nand encourage regular blood donation.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6B6w3nbcpp0mxTVMkxDEl","name":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/xHENhWMKnsg07V7ggnpMz.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The MyGov Quiz on India’s Heritage successfully increased students’ awareness and\\nunderstanding of India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage. Participants gained\\ndeeper knowledge about monuments, freedom fighters, festivals, art forms, literature, and\\nancient scientific achievements. The activity promoted learning through fun and healthy\\ncompetition, improving teamwork and quick-thinking abilities. It also instilled a sense of\\npatriotism, pride, and respect for the nation’s traditions and values. Overall, the quiz inspired\\nstudents to stay connected to their roots and appreciate India’s diverse heritage","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-05","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The MyGov Quiz on India’s Heritage was organized to enhance students’ knowledge about\\nIndia’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage. The quiz included questions about\\nmonuments, freedom fighters, festivals, art forms, literature, and scientific achievements of\\nancient India. Students participated enthusiastically, showing their interest and pride in the\\ncountry’s glorious past. The event aimed to promote awareness of India’s diverse heritage and\\ninstill a sense of patriotism among young learners. The quiz helped students gain deeper insight\\ninto India’s history and cultural values. It encouraged learning through fun and competition,\\nstrengthening teamwork and quick-thinking skills. Participants developed greater respect and\\npride for the nation’s traditions and achievements. Overall, the MyGov Quiz on India’s Heritage\\nsuccessfully inspired students to stay connected to their roots and celebrate India’s rich legacy.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pw98HaIfLxTNpx1vwOx6j","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/XJIY9sk2dvb8lOth7eNTx.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-03-25","duration":9,"outcomes":"Rush Hours 5.0 was a high-spirited event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, bringing together participants for five days of interactive challenges. The event aimed to foster teamwork, problem-solving skills, and healthy competition\\namong the participants. With engaging tasks lined up for each day, it provided a platform for creativity and collaboration.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":6,"description":"With more than 450 participants, Rush Hours 5.0 was a n exciting five-day event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, designed to engage participants in a series of creative and competitive tasks. Each day featured a unique challenge, and based on their performance, some teams faced elimination. The gradual elimination process added intensity and kept the teams motivated to give their best. On the final day, the top three teams, who demonstrated consistent performance and creativity, were announced as the winners.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"SYwJvuTNuTk8wmm7ukoit","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/5RDItSb55tPauTkBO-ZpY.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"The project successfully collected and distributed a large number of books to government school\\nstudents. It brought smiles and encouragement to the children and helped improve their interest\\nin studies.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social outreach initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged\\nstudents studying in Government Schools. As part of this activity, a stationery kit containing\\nessential study materials was sponsored and donated to one student. The initiative focused on\\nencouraging education and reducing the financial burden on economically weaker students by\\nproviding them with basic academic resources. This activity promoted social responsibility,\\ncommunity service, and awareness about the importance of equal access to education. In\\nrecognition of this contribution\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1OPVUwsG_7wSqgxi552d7","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/KCC9McocRU-4vo8cqjL1u.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/2DHepdhlwXLWPNvbAZNPq.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon successfully raised awareness about female foeticide and the importance of\\nvaluing the girl child. It encouraged participants to take a stand against gender discrimination\\nand promoted social responsibility through collective action.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":7,"description":"On the occasion of Mother''s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized\\na Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon with the aim of shedding light on the grave issue\\nof female foeticide and promoting the value of girt children in society. The event witnessed\\nan overwhelming participation of 350+ individuals, including enthusiastic students, dedicated\\nfaculty members, and supportive parents who came together to walk for a cause that truly\\nmatters. The walkathon began in the early hours of the morning from the RVCE campus and\\nwas marked by thought-provoking placards, powerful slogans, and an atmosphere of solidarity.\\nThe event served as a platform to educate and inspire change, urging everyone to take a stand\\nagainst gender-based violence and discrimination even before birth. The Rotaract Club of RVCE\\nextends heartfelt gratitude to all participants for their support and commitment to this impactful\\ncause\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CL7KqKApJlAx48TjQqVal","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/WQp4LylmGbeTQkYGKqe7c.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp was very successful and received a good response from students,\\nteachers, and local community members. Many volunteers came forward to donate blood, and\\na significant number of blood units were collected. The event helped raise awareness about\\nthe importance of donating blood regularly and motivated others to participate in future drives.\\nIt also built a sense of social responsibility, compassion, and teamwork among participants.\\nOverall, the camp contributed to saving lives and supporting the healthcare system. The camp\\nwas a great success, with many volunteers donating blood and spreading awareness about its\\nimportance. The event helped in collecting several units of blood that will benefit patients in\\nneed. It also inspired participants to contribute to humanitarian causes and highlighted the value\\nof selfless service. Overall, the Blood Donation Camp strengthened the spirit of compassion,\\nresponsibility, and community welfare among all participants.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Blood Donation Camp is an organized event where volunteers donate blood under the\\nsupervision of medical professionals. It is conducted to collect blood for hospitals and blood\\nbanks, promote awareness about blood donation, and encourage people to contribute to society.\\nThe camp ensures safety, proper hygiene, and medical screening for all donors. The blood\\nis collected safely by trained medical staff using sterile equipment. Such camps also include\\nawareness programs to educate people about the importance of blood donation and how one\\ndonation can save several lives. A Blood Donation Camp was organized to collect blood from\\nvoluntary donors and create awareness about the importance of blood donation. The camp was\\nconducted in collaboration with a local hospital and medical professionals, who ensured all\\nsafety and hygiene measures. Students, teachers, and community members actively participated\\nin the event. The main aim of the camp was to help save lives, promote social responsibility,\\nand encourage regular blood donation.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zuR3uch5XWw-EGZboqUja","name":"Fistfull 2025 ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b8e3b04d-c9fc-438b-b00d-f191725be39f/2BMx_a07B6iQtoLrMFvKf.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"Fistful exemplifies the power of collective action driven by empathy and social responsibility.\\nWhat began as a simple contribution from each student culminated in a substantial supply of\\nessential food grains, positively impacting multiple Institutions and countless beneficiaries.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing\\nessential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted\\nin the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions\\nthat serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:26:57.653344+00', '2026-01-30 07:50:07.043323+00'), ('69d03a2b-cc7a-4878-9504-19db4a51a368', 'e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23EI405","name":"Shidesh S","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"pL-x9jV7TQ2dRgP38RgpK","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/LaHdPfHFti6Se-ReZ42mg.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/t9yGvioF5bdfT3uHkneQb.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":2,"outcomes":"This activity increased my awareness about the importance of blood donation in saving lives and supporting healthcare systems. It helped me develop empathy, humanitarian values, and a strong sense of social responsibility. I gained knowledge about donation procedures and safety measures while improving teamwork and cooperation skills. The experience boosted my confidence and motivated me to continue contributing to social welfare initiatives in the future.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-27","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I voluntarily participated in the Blood Donation Camp organized to support healthcare needs and save lives. This activity helped me understand the importance of social responsibility and the role of individuals in serving society. The camp was well organized with proper medical supervision and safety procedures, ensuring a safe donation process. Through this experience, I gained awareness about blood groups, donor eligibility, and the importance of timely donations during emergencies. The activity encouraged teamwork and coordination among volunteers and highlighted how a single donation can benefit multiple patients. Overall, this experience was meaningful and motivated me to actively participate in future social service activities.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/eS1mnOPchhHKNxTn9TcO7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lsXKzah862zFLfmjtiNOQ","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/7S--ltjZ64b2G-UPGKvMg.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/f9PK2Ic4O1w5gCj_FxuHE.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/5Myci_tV2v2dqfLmZsOtb.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/oUZVmvN4kEhGZUZzgrFRX.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon improved my awareness of physical fitness and healthy living habits. It enhanced stamina, endurance, and mental resilience while developing self-discipline and time management skills. Participation also encouraged teamwork, positive competition, and confidence building. Overall, the experience motivated me to maintain an active lifestyle and focus on overall personality development.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I participated in the Utsarga Marathon 2024, which was organized to promote physical fitness, discipline, and social awareness. The event encouraged students to adopt a healthy lifestyle by focusing on physical and mental well-being. Participation helped me develop endurance, perseverance, and self-discipline. The marathon promoted unity, teamwork, and sportsmanship while creating awareness about the importance of regular exercise. The well-organized event provided a motivating environment that improved stamina, reduced stress, and encouraged goal-oriented behavior. Overall, this activity contributed positively to my personal development.","aicteMapping":"Physical Fitness, Sports & Health & Wellness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/9gTvGGIDqDYKuo-1IZu6L.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UpAfS6bKxgn_aj45LjJ5_","name":"Unchained","slNo":3,"place":"RCCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/b5gAil4xUqRQg46gtMwDH.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/22KOD3vqVJ3A_ujrszZ17.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me gain awareness about social responsibility and community engagement. It improved my teamwork, leadership, communication, and coordination skills. I also learned the importance of mental well-being and positive lifestyle practices. The experience increased my self-confidence and encouraged active participation in social and personal development activities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-30","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I participated in the event “Unchained” organized by the RAAG Club in collaboration with The Art of Living, which focused on personal well-being, self-expression, and mental clarity. The program included interactive sessions that encouraged mindfulness, emotional balance, and self-awareness. It promoted teamwork, discipline, and active participation while helping me improve communication and interpersonal skills. The event created a positive and inclusive environment and enhanced my confidence and social responsibility. Overall, this activity was a meaningful learning experience beyond academics.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness & Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/ReGdP_iH0IDGlKjVyJVPL.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ucJAWsJIOLjROjF03e1oi","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/OsfhOS9ab6M45Tj3Cy8Ig.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/F1ABiyW2MlzpGWpBWjv5-.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/jiRN4Wo-W3YrWRrnEdw-7.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/hMOVNhlG51lfO-U30OPUG.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon helped improve my physical endurance and overall fitness awareness. It strengthened teamwork, discipline, and self-motivation while promoting health and wellness. Participation also improved time management skills and boosted confidence through social interaction. Overall, the event contributed to my physical and personal development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I participated in the Utsarga Marathon 2025 and successfully completed all the required event criteria. This activity promoted physical fitness and encouraged active participation in health-oriented events. It helped me understand the importance of maintaining discipline, motivation, and consistency in achieving fitness goals. The event also strengthened teamwork and coordination among participants. Overall, this experience enhanced my physical endurance and encouraged a healthy lifestyle.","aicteMapping":"Physical Fitness, Sports  & Health & Wellness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/30Y-dAlfGS0YijcNhBvIX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xB267T1ODYKt7GY2Rbw9_","name":"Secret Santa","slNo":5,"place":"Sree Manukula Charitable","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/INjQU-aLk3Q5ISA7XU27k.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/eeVA4hp4_zoOz5j7Z-TO-.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/1N7Wq1SMd2QVubhpYejvP.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped develop empathy, compassion, and a strong sense of social responsibility. It encouraged teamwork, volunteerism, and leadership skills while promoting the importance of sharing and generosity. The experience created emotional satisfaction and awareness about giving back to society, contributing to overall personality development.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-12-25","hoursSpent":15,"description":"I participated in the Secret Santa activity organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to spread happiness during the Christmas season. The event aimed to bring joy to underprivileged children by collecting and distributing gifts such as toys, cakes, and educational supplies. Volunteers personally interacted with children and distributed the collected items. This activity promoted kindness, compassion, generosity, and social responsibility among students. Overall, the experience was joyful, meaningful, and socially impactful.","aicteMapping":"Social Service ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/kHTuGjFz_B4cifBXs94-e.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wJFzB_7IFqZyfBThngp-9","name":"Walkathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/3fGlf6fUAtDJU_yhyJL7K.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/NOlJuJsenw6i3GYE5lgm-.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon increased awareness about health and fitness while improving physical endurance and stamina. It encouraged students to adopt healthy routines and strengthened teamwork and collective responsibility. The event enhanced mental strength, motivation, and social awareness, contributing to holistic personal development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":12,"description":"I participated in the Walkathon 2025 organized to promote physical fitness and social awareness. The event encouraged students to actively engage in walking activities and adopt healthy lifestyle habits. It helped improve stamina, mental strength, discipline, and self-motivation. The walkathon promoted unity and collective participation while creating awareness about maintaining physical well-being. Overall, this activity was an enriching and motivating experience.","aicteMapping":"Health Awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/Q-Q7Ap-RVnmlD3U1kQj4p.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rTjbMyqaZ-M3Vd3NFeJQj","name":"Fist Full","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/dsvlv6Uy4W5aIMLPVMlO6.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"This activity increased awareness about hunger and food wastage while encouraging compassion and ethical responsibility. It strengthened teamwork and cooperation skills and promoted the importance of sharing food. The experience provided personal satisfaction and reinforced community service values, contributing to social and moral development.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":12,"description":"I participated in the Fist Full social service activity, which focused on reducing hunger and minimizing food wastage. Students contributed food items that were collected and distributed to underprivileged people. The activity promoted compassion, social responsibility, and awareness about hunger issues in society. Teamwork and coordination played an important role throughout the event. Overall, this initiative had a positive social impact and provided a meaningful service experience.","aicteMapping":"Social Service & Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/llkXqZ3gVABhZleX_7Tim.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rc88e0WZW6YQqVPY8eq34","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/JWNRn31S_sBZTD0JYEfsg.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/lJVGnzcdjwJIJ4YfniEpp.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/NLUD_L4LeHOhvAH6tbkgE.png"],"endDate":"2025-03-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity increased awareness about the importance of blood donation and encouraged voluntary participation. It helped develop social responsibility, humanitarian values, and confidence in contributing to community service. Participants gained knowledge about safety and health practices while supporting patients in need. Overall, the experience strengthened civic responsibility and ethical development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-20","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I participated in the Blood Donation Camp 2025 organized by NSS RVCE to support hospitals and patients in need of blood. Students and volunteers actively took part in the donation drive under the supervision of medical professionals, ensuring a safe and hygienic process. The event created awareness about voluntary blood donation and promoted humanitarian values. Participants learned about health standards and eligibility criteria for donation. Overall, this activity was meaningful and life-saving in nature.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2b950d4-248d-40af-9434-638904010e70/kbkBzcH2E34V_9YFZO0PS.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Anand Jatti","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 11:02:28.950831+00', '2026-02-01 15:16:04.42989+00'), ('69e13a4a-5215-4fae-9274-53132043e880', '51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI058","name":"Thommandru Sai Krishna Sree","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"dzu880FqhKceot_Tb9WC1","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/bD2icH_XyrP_EZSHCi2vv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event had the successful collection of numerous blood units, directly contributing to the local blood bank reserves to aid patients in critical need. Participating in this drive provided a practical understanding of the shortage of medical resources and the importance of voluntary donation. ","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"On the morning of June 6, 2023, a voluntary blood donation camp was organized at the RVCE campus to encourage student participation in healthcare initiatives. The event was set up with a structured flow, beginning with a mandatory registration and a thorough medical screening where doctors checked vitals such as blood pressure and hemoglobin levels to ensure donor eligibility. As a donor, I proceeded through these checks before being guided to the donation area, where medical professionals managed the blood collection process with care and hygiene. The session concluded with a mandatory observation period where donors were given refreshments with appreciation badge to stabilize our energy levels before returning.","aicteMapping":"Blood Donation Activity","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/Wv2wU8JSsF2NnnM1xUvIQ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EkO70KyTbTa3QywgYVErr","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":2,"place":"Banashankari","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/JSlQRkBWRYbDLcj0ZgTAZ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"My participation contributed to the collective effort of collecting over 7 tonnes of recyclable paper, the proceeds of which were donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation. This intense 9-hour drive gave me hands-on experience in community mobilization and teamwork. It was rewarding to see how our physical effort could be converted into financial aid for a welfare organization, and the experience instilled in me a deeper appreciation for social service and environmental sustainability through recycling.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":9,"description":"I participated as a volunteer in the mega newspaper collection drive, assembling with fellow students at Kriyakalpa, RVCE at 8:00 AM. After the initial briefing, I traveled by bus with my team to a designated locality in Bangalore to execute the collection phase. My role involved going door-to-door to request and collect old newspapers, books, and magazines from residents, explaining the charitable cause to them. The activity spanned over nine hours, during which I assisted in gathering, carrying, and loading the materials for transport, working continuously to ensure we maximized our collection for the day.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/oMe5So-hdfXBA2MNTO4HZ.jpeg","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QUNFNmj1TcmmOBbDNyLx5","name":"Tanuja Movie Screening","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/31kmFvk2cElmfUuef830C.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The film served as a powerful case study in perseverance, grit, and the importance of never giving up on one''s educational aspirations, regardless of the odds. For many of us, it was an eye-opener regarding the privileges we often take for granted compared to students in rural areas. The event sparked post-screening discussions about the role of mentorship and government support in education. On a personal level, watching the film instilled a renewed sense of determination in me to face academic challenges with resilience, reinforcing the belief that \"where there is a will, there is a way.\"","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The screening of the Kannada movie Tanuja was organized on campus to provide students with a cinematic experience that was both entertaining and educational. The event began with a brief introduction by the faculty coordinator, who highlighted the film''s relevance to student life and its basis on a true story. The movie follows the gripping journey of a young girl from a rural background who battles systemic hurdles, technical glitches, and the COVID-19 pandemic restrictions to appear for the NEET examination. The auditorium was packed with students and staff, and the atmosphere quickly shifted from casual to intense as the narrative unfolded. The screening was immersive, with the audience visibly moved by the protagonist''s struggle and the realistic portrayal of the support she received from her teacher and state administration.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/OSbPkiYmGskLzuLE-deZ1.jpeg","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JQExJ49TOzZ7IMqOck0uo","name":"Indi-Genius:The India Quiz","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/gMPQvajmlZMdx29hwuxyS.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"The Indi-Genius quiz competition successfully enhanced participants'' knowledge and\\nappreciation of India''s cultural heritage, historical achievements, and contemporary\\ndevelopments. Students gained comprehensive insights into various aspects of Indian\\ncivilization while developing strong research skills, general awareness, and intellectual curiosity\\nabout their nation.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":"This intellectual competition was organized as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2023,\\nfeaturing \"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz,\" a national-level quiz fest held from July 14th to 16th,\\n2023. The event provided students an opportunity to showcase their knowledge about India''s rich\\ncultural heritage, history, geography, achievements, and contemporary developments through\\nan engaging and competitive format.\\nThroughout the three-day quiz fest, participants engaged in rigorous rounds of questioning\\nthat tested their comprehensive understanding of Indian civilization, traditions, innovations,\\nand contributions to global culture. The quiz was designed to celebrate India''s diversity and\\nintellectual legacy while fostering healthy academic competition among students from across\\nthe nation. The Cultural Activities Team coordinated the event with support from associate\\nsponsors and global education partners, ensuring high standards of organization and participant\\nexperience.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/1hXVtueEDlYUI_D6Ea7RH.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lJQeygdUCvuvnx0hbSeNR","name":"Wall as Your Canvas: Mural Painting Workshop","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/tLAqUg_KhpOrM_KO8UbNP.png"],"endDate":"2023-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of this project is the aesthetic revitalization of the campus, establishing a permanent visual landmark that inspires creativity and resilience. For me personally, the experience fostered a strong sense of ownership and accomplishment; seeing the mural daily serves as a tangible reminder of our collective effort. Beyond the immediate beautification, the mural stands as a lasting legacy of our batch''s collaborative spirit, continuing to inspire future students to embrace change and express their creativity long after we have graduated.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-12-06","hoursSpent":7,"description":"I participated in a creative campus initiative to transform a neglected wall into a vibrant piece of abstract art featuring a girl skateboarding. The project was designed to rejuvenate the space and infuse it with energy, using the dynamic imagery of skateboarding to symbolize freedom, empowerment, and the breaking of stereotypes. Working alongside fellow students, I contributed to the painting process, where we translated these themes into a colorful visual narrative. The activity involved collaborative planning and hands-on artistic work to turn a dull structure into a lively canvas that reflects the progressive values of our institution.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/qohxEPB5r9g7pgTwmxfgb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rSN8ssrOEqOhDYZGa1IKS","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":6,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/uNoIyJQT5XELUG9o9sDiN.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/iIPYz_hdtNTBkKjM2kAlP.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Fast Trek 2.0 successfully fostered environmental consciousness and adventure spirit among over 750 participants. Students gained valuable experience in outdoor activities while developing a deeper appreciation for natural landscapes and the importance of preserving pristine environments. The integrated cleanliness drive instilled practical habits of responsible outdoor behavior and environmental care.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":12,"description":"On January 28, 2024, I participated in \"Fast Trek 2.0,\" a flagship adventure and environmental conservation event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. We assembled at 7:30 AM to board buses to Kunagalu Betta Hills, creating an atmosphere of excitement and anticipation among the 750+ participants. Before the ascent began, I attended a mandatory briefing session where safety protocols and route details were explained. The event was unique as it integrated a standard trekking expedition with a cleanliness drive; while navigating the challenging terrain and enjoying the scenic landscapes, I actively collected litter and plastic waste along the trail, ensuring the path was left cleaner than we found it.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/RSn44CpmqnlFTclr0igTH.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EmdBwlv31z8A1HBA2Cuhq","name":"Utsarga Marathon Volunteering","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/OT1a00nmEzn9T0lkTsBeu.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of my contribution was the creation of a comprehensive visual archive that served as the official documentation for the event. These photographs were utilized for post-event publicity, social media updates, and future promotional materials for NSS RVCE, helping to amplify the message of the charity drive. On a personal level, this role sharpened my technical skills in sports and event photography, specifically in capturing fast-moving subjects and candid emotions. It gave me a unique perspective on the event, allowing me to contribute to the cause by preserving the memories and hard work of the volunteers and participants.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":12,"description":"On February 4, 2024, I volunteered for the Utsarga Marathon, the flagship charity run organized by NSS RVCE under the theme \"Help a child, change the world.\" The event hosted over 2,000 participants competing in 5 km and 10 km categories, with dignitaries like Mr. Y M Uppin present for the flag-off. Assigned to the Photography team, my role was to document the entire event visually. I was stationed at key vantage points along the route and near the stage to capture high-energy moments, from the adrenaline of the start line to the determination on the runners'' faces and the prize distribution ceremony. My responsibility involved staying mobile to cover different angles, ensuring that the scale of the crowd and the spirit of the cause were effectively immortalized through my lens.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/Dzn-zYUVZY2pluJU4GjAL.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7_eo85x1qQPtzCjHNyfOS","name":"Inde-genius Quiz","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/wAgO3n6jFYDFWwId2YZmW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"The Indi-Genius quiz competition successfully enhanced participants'' knowledge and\\nappreciation of India''s cultural heritage, historical achievements, and contemporary\\ndevelopments. Students gained comprehensive insights into various aspects of Indian\\ncivilization while developing strong research skills, general awareness, and intellectual\\ncuriosity\\nabout their nation.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This intellectual competition was organized as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2023,\\nfeaturing \"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz,\" a national-level quiz fest. The event provided students an opportunity to showcase their knowledge about India''s\\nrich\\ncultural heritage, history, geography, achievements, and contemporary developments through\\nan engaging and competitive format.\\nThroughout the three-day quiz fest, participants engaged in rigorous rounds of questioning\\nthat tested their comprehensive understanding of Indian civilization, traditions, innovations,\\nand contributions to global culture. The quiz was designed to celebrate India''s diversity and\\nintellectual legacy while fostering healthy academic competition among students from across\\nthe nation. The Cultural Activities Team coordinated the event with support from associate\\nsponsors and global education partners, ensuring high standards of organization and participant\\nexperience.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/lTN85cl_c25ufDWjjEbUs.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OEVIqo2sop0fVkljYil2I","name":"Inkspire","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/Vjgveh8qPXSBX-W-FynrE.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-28","duration":4,"outcomes":"The event was a significant success, uniting 132 participants who used their words to advocate for positive change. Selected entries were given a platform through the club’s magazine and blog, with standout pieces featured on Instagram to amplify their reach. For me, the experience was empowering; it allowed me to refine my literary skills while demonstrating how creative expression can serve as a catalyst for social impact. Being part of this collective voice gave me a sense of purpose and accomplishment, reinforcing the value of using one''s talents to champion compassion and awareness.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-10-25","hoursSpent":6,"description":"I participated in \"Inkspire,\" a creative writing initiative held from October 25th to 28th, 2024, designed to harness the power of storytelling as a force for social change. The event invited students to explore and write about impactful themes such as sustainability, health, equality, and education. As a participant, I submitted an original piece (prose/poetry/article) in [English/Hindi/Kannada], engaging with the prompt to craft a narrative that highlighted these critical societal issues. The event was highly inclusive, encouraging diverse expressions by accepting entries in multiple languages and formats like flash fiction and creative non-fiction, thereby fostering a rich environment of creative diversity.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/2jxqNfPYYc5pX1LS2WrU3.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"muzeyyPZlHAKsuP6Q5ary","name":"Fist Full","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus`","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/LNXJORTqnQzP0jR1P8ULq.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-25","duration":20,"outcomes":"The initiative was highly successful in gathering significant quantities of food essentials, directly benefiting those in need and addressing local food security challenges. On a personal level, participating in \"Fist Full\" cultivated a strong sense of empathy and social responsibility, helping me understand the impact of collective community action. The experience provided me with practical insights into grassroots community service and allowed me to develop valuable organizational and coordination skills through the management of the donation drive. It served as a powerful reminder of how small individual contributions, when united, can create a substantial positive impact on society.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"I participated in the \"Fist Full\" community service initiative, a flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE under the theme \"Unite for Good.\" The campaign, which commenced on November 1st, 2025, aimed to combat food insecurity by mobilizing the student body to donate essential staples for underprivileged communities. The primary collection phase ran from November 17th to November 25th, 2025. During this period, I actively contributed to the drive by helping to collect and organize voluntary donations, specifically focusing on 5 kg bags of rice and 2 kg packets of Toor Dal. The event required coordinating with fellow students to ensure a steady flow of contributions and managing the logistics of storing the collected items efficiently.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/ArPuQWFoVq3C9SG0fOfLi.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vTm3QMBT4w0Nf4qRVxHn6","name":"Utsarga Marathon Volunteering","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/meJWBksOuTXs6RH9iiP_6.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The volunteering experience was instrumental in instilling values of selfless service and community engagement. It provided me with a practical platform to develop organizational excellence and crisis management skills in a high-pressure environment. By interacting with the public and managing various aspects of the marathon, I significantly improved my communication, leadership, and problem-solving abilities. The event highlighted the power of teamwork and gave me a profound sense of satisfaction in contributing to a cause that benefits the broader community.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I volunteered for the Utsarga Marathon, a large-scale community service initiative organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. The event was designed to promote community welfare and health through a mass participation run. As an NSS volunteer, I played a key role in the on-ground management of the event, working alongside fellow students to ensure its successful execution. My responsibilities included assisting with participant coordination, managing hydration stations, ensuring effective crowd control, and providing route guidance to runners. Guided by the NSS Programme Officers, we worked cohesively to handle the logistical requirements and ensure a safe, smooth experience for all attendees.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/IdMEwlX5fJelOxKCdqtoo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"L506hNLs-P4lOY8UFqLMj","name":"Fistfull","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/FAoPOwHjxh03c_Hc4zwvY.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-25","duration":9,"outcomes":"The event was a resounding success, effectively gathering essential food supplies to support those in need. Participating in this drive cultivated a deep sense of empathy, generosity, and social responsibility in me. Beyond the charitable impact, the experience provided me with practical lessons in grassroots community service. It also helped me develop key organizational and coordination skills as I worked with the team to manage the inventory of donations, reinforcing the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in \"Fist Full,\" a community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE under the theme \"Unite for Good.\" The event, which launched on November 1st, 2025, aimed to alleviate food insecurity in underprivileged communities. The core collection phase took place from November 17th to November 25th, 2025. During this period, I actively contributed by helping to mobilize, collect, and organize voluntary donations from the student body, focusing specifically on essential staples like 5 kg bags of rice and 2 kg packets of Toor Dal. My role involved coordinating with fellow students to manage the logistics of the collection drive, ensuring that the contributions were properly stored and ready for distribution.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/bOkevz7VaCcP6v5mV9wQh.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cB-QQa8pilUWekGOZfbjO","name":"SDG Photography","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/QdW25ralWl80pmq-ihTXC.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"Participating in this competition significantly enhanced my visual storytelling abilities and technical photography skills. It pushed me to think critically about environmental and social challenges and how to represent them artistically. Beyond the creative aspect, the event deepened my awareness of the UN''s Sustainable Development Goals, helping me understand the importance of advocacy through art. The experience fostered a sense of global citizenship and allowed me to contribute to the campus dialogue on sustainability.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":6,"description":"I participated in the photography competition organized by the SPARK prefects, which challenged students to visually interpret the 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The event required us to capture and submit photographs that communicated complex themes ranging from poverty alleviation to climate action through a creative lens. As a participant, I engaged in the process of identifying real-world subjects that aligned with these global goals, composing shots that told a compelling story, and submitting my entries for evaluation. The competition provided a platform to showcase creative vision while engaging with students from various ability enhancement courses.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/5AOPbi1VnAcxJsqaRCQSQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"USTihrZ58AanybS1c0-C5","name":"Energy LiteracyTraining","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/BJ9_PRsdCtX95mj46LRP0.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-19","duration":2,"outcomes":"The training successfully enhanced my understanding of energy conservation principles and the importance of sustainability in modern engineering. I gained comprehensive knowledge about renewable energy technologies and energy-efficient systems, along with practical strategies to reduce energy consumption in daily life. On a personal level, the program empowered me to become more conscious of my energy usage and provided me with the technical foundation to promote energy efficiency, fostering a lasting commitment to environmental stewardship.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-18","hoursSpent":40,"description":"I participated in the Energy Literacy Training, an initiative organized in collaboration with the Department of Electrical and Electronics (EEE) at RVCE to promote sustainable energy practices. The program was designed to equip students with the knowledge and skills necessary to advocate for and implement energy efficiency in our communities. Throughout the sessions, I engaged in learning about critical topics such as energy auditing, renewable energy technologies, and efficient resource utilization. The training provided practical exposure to methods for reducing carbon footprints and implementing energy-saving measures across residential, institutional, and industrial settings.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/B91kMJa64A-QMjP3olYkx.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QoERTBmXEwfpKVzN_TLPV","name":"8th Mile Volunteering","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/tONnMDcoqmjbX8eu3PCm0.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":4,"outcomes":"The initiative was a success, fostering a strong sense of responsibility and professional growth among all involved. For me personally, this experience provided invaluable hands-on training in event management and strategic planning. It allowed me to develop essential leadership qualities and organizational competencies that extend beyond the classroom. Working through the challenges of such a large-scale event sharpened my ability to coordinate effectively within a team and reinforced the importance of perseverance and collective effort in achieving community-focused goals.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-03","hoursSpent":50,"description":"On January 5th, 2026, I served as a volunteer for the large-scale community service initiative organized by the 8th Mile Committee at RV College of Engineering. Under the coordination of the Cultural Activities team, the event focused on planning and executing meaningful community engagement activities. My role involved working collaboratively with the Core Team to manage various aspects of the event, ranging from logistics and resource management to on-ground participant coordination. The initiative required a high level of dedication and time management, as we worked to ensure the seamless execution of the program while maintaining a strong focus on social impact and teamwork.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/51281a58-c24c-4ac9-a35d-05ca1b968513/JHzTJIxpY0uzZZTJHQiiX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 16:01:17.958839+00', '2026-02-02 06:56:20.76457+00'), ('69e90a89-01a6-42d5-ac67-7be19036b742', 'ea65681d-c9ce-4d36-ae62-f52073049169', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"nTQA8SEUtkN7EnbIRZMwM","name":"","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"awareness","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kHD1uwCmVMKgyBSga89q7","name":"activity","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"7","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 09:29:39.67639+00', '2026-01-30 06:57:19.28629+00'), ('6af447b5-cde2-41a8-ab0c-2e0241fb7e39', 'f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC180","name":"Vijay Kumar Prajapati","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"IkwvCckVRCDVfwPdwyHpH","name":"Discover Yourself","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Camous","photos":[],"endDate":"2022-12-18","duration":7,"outcomes":"Through the Discover Yourself series, you gained a deeper understanding of self-identity and mind management, learning to distinguish your inner self from external pressures. The sessions provided you with spiritual tools to cultivate emotional resilience and a positive mindset, teaching you how to balance technical ambitions with internal peace. Ultimately, you learned that by mastering your thoughts and aligning your actions with a clear sense of purpose, you can navigate life''s challenges with greater clarity and focus.","semester":"1","startDate":"2022-12-12","hoursSpent":14,"description":"The activity is designed as a journey toward self-awareness, moving beyond academic or professional skills to focus on the \"inner self.\" Conducted by S.P.A.R.K. (which stands for Spreading Positive Attitude and Relevancy of Knowledge) in collaboration with RV Institutions, these sessions bridge the gap between modern lifestyle challenges and ancient spiritual wisdom.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/TdqpgTViW79AQ68aCjqGW.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vujMxFsE7gRrrL0y--1W1","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/1sYwiIrJk_NB1ne6f23R4.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/OT4DkadZdOB2fq_USRCsh.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The \"Mera Pehla Vote desh ke liye\" campaign, driven by the National Service Scheme (NSS), successfully transformed campus energy into civic action. The primary outcome was a significant surge in electoral literacy and voter registration among first-time voters. By organizing pledge drives and awareness workshops, NSS volunteers effectively bridged the gap between youth and the democratic process, ensuring that students not only registered for their Voter IDs but also understood the value of ethical voting. This initiative cultivated a deeper sense of responsibility, empowering the younger generation to shape the nation''s future through informed and active participation in upcoming elections.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"\\nThe \"Mera Pehla Vote desh ke liye  \" campaign is a flagship initiative spearheaded by the Ministry of Education in collaboration with the National Service Scheme (NSS) to foster democratic participation among India’s youth. By leveraging the vast network of NSS volunteers, the program transforms educational campuses into hubs of electoral literacy. It focuses on sensitizing first-time voters about the power of their franchise and the importance of ethical voting. Through rallies, workshops, and digital pledges, the initiative bridges the gap between young citizens and the electoral process, ensuring that the \"Gen Z\" demographic contributes vibrantly to the nation''s democratic future.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/x9CRkYpFVsfNm09r9LR-r.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"r57N1D4sRsG7FE34_4JzG","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/PULdbkOx3Hvey7VhB4VkH.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/i223xNlzWDBgATLllDDDi.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AS5mN-hveJUqWR6Vd0vDh","name":"Plantation Drive","slNo":4,"place":"Sri Panchmukhi Ganesh Temple","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/cF-wRPDolGtLYlZ3j7bRc.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-07-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Plantation Drive successfully contributed to environmental sustainability through the planting of multiple saplings around the Sri Panchmukhi Ganesh Temple, directly enhancing local air quality and soil conservation. Beyond the ecological impact, the initiative fostered a strong sense of community and teamwork among participants, encouraging the adoption of eco-friendly practices. Furthermore, the activity served as a practical learning experience, deepening participants'' understanding of plant care and the critical importance of vegetation in maintaining ecological balance.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The activity aimed to contribute to environmental sustainability and increase the local green cover. Volunteers actively participated in digging pits, planting various indigenous saplings, and watering them. The drive also focused on raising awareness among the local community about the importance of afforestation in combating climate change and preserving biodiversity.","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/XihTCJAzO84AjesNAYLNa.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bojHxVwXg_Nh-_Ec3nHQQ","name":"SDG Photo Competition","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/OLw3jmtK2ueTbu8-v3mlI.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the SDG Photo Competition fostered a deeper global awareness of the 17 Sustainable Development Goals and their significance in building a better future. The activity enhanced creative expression and visual storytelling skills by challenging participants to interpret complex social themes through a camera lens. Furthermore, it sharpened critical observation, developing the ability to identify and document sustainability challenges and solutions within the local campus environment.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The event encouraged students to use photography as a medium to highlight critical global issues such as climate action, poverty, and sustainable living. Participants captured creative images that visually narrated stories related to these goals, fostering a deeper connection between artistic expression and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/76SOYX_kIlelLjm4D6xbs.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cmx6EApRWPMO-sbGru9EO","name":"Utsarga Marathon ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"From a participant’s perspective, the NSS Utsarga Marathon was an inspiring and memorable \\nexperience that contributed to both physical fitness and personal growth. Participating in the \\nmarathon helped students develop stamina, endurance, and discipline, while also reinforcing \\nthe importance of maintaining a healthy and active lifestyle.\\nThe event also created a strong sense of motivation and enthusiasm, as students ran together \\nwith a shared purpose and collective energy. It encouraged teamwork, boosted confidence, \\nand provided a refreshing break from academic routines. Additionally, being part of an \\nNSS-driven activity helped participants feel more connected to social initiatives and understand \\nthe importance of taking part in events that contribute to community spirit and awareness.\\nOverall, the marathon was not just a fitness event, but also a meaningful initiative that promoted \\nunity, responsibility, and a sense of achievement among the participants","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon was a vibrant and impactful event organized with the aim of \\npromoting fitness, discipline, and social awareness among students. The marathon served as \\na platform to encourage participants to step out of their routine and take part in an activity that \\nsupports both physical well-being and a positive social message.\\nThe event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students and volunteers, creating an \\nenergetic atmosphere throughout. Proper coordination was ensured through volunteer support, \\nroute planning, and overall event management, which helped in smooth execution and \\nparticipant safety. The marathon not only encouraged students to adopt a more active lifestyle \\nbut also strengthened the values of community participation, unity, and responsibility, which lie \\nat the core of NSS initiatives.\\nOverall, the NSS Utsarga Marathon successfully combined fitness and social purpose, making \\nit a meaningful event that left a positive impression on all participants.","aicteMapping":"RVCE Campus  ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/FzDtb4OECMUb5LOZmaZ7D.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Gc3UWGj8fno46rVgmnXS1","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":7,"place":"Social Cause ","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Participating in this drive provided significant insights into the logistical challenges of waste management and the power of collective community action. Through this experience, I developed strong leadership and communication skills by managing volunteer schedules and interacting with diverse groups of people to encourage participation. From an environmental standpoint, the activity resulted in the successful diversion of a substantial volume of paper from local landfills, directly contributing to the conservation of natural resources and a reduction in the community''s carbon footprint. Ultimately, this project reinforced my understanding of social responsibility and the practical application of sustainable development goals (SDGs) in a real-world setting.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-27","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The \"Paper Drive\" was organized as a strategic community service initiative to address the growing concern of paper waste and to promote a culture of recycling within the local area. The activity involved a systematic approach, starting with a week-long awareness campaign to educate participants on the importance of waste segregation. I coordinated the setup of multiple collection hubs and managed a team to oversee the intake of materials. Our primary focus was on collecting and sorting various paper products,ranging from old newspapers and discarded cardboard to office stationery,to ensure they were free from contaminants. Finally, I collaborated with local recycling partners to ensure that 100% of the gathered material was processed sustainably, bridging the gap between waste generation and responsible disposal.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f0e508a6-01e0-418c-af86-8bd7b94ca2e1/i_1hipKH6Sin2nKlM9z6e.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 04:12:15.396108+00', '2026-02-01 08:19:20.505998+00'), ('6b9e0e45-a254-4158-bf13-14b553c9af31', '6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV056","name":"MINGKILING PERTIN","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"R_P2McMzmw1xrtxHZToEP","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":1,"place":"R.V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/8pB28CbK1F_4SAj0tGAmL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"Fistful exemplifies the power of collective action driven by empathy and social responsibility. What began as a simple contribution from each student culminated in a substantial supply of essential food grains, positively impacting multiple Institutions and countless beneficiaries.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing essential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted in the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions that serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups","aicteMapping":"Community development and social development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8EohiEvdu0YECexFdQqd-","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RV. College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/Ks2Q-3zAI9gr4m0Wxp4-u.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon concluded with significant social, organizational, and community-oriented outcomes. The event successfully mobilized more than 500 participants, demonstrating strong public engagement and widespread support for the cause of helping underprivileged children.\\n\\nThe marathon also strengthened the culture of volunteerism, teamwork, and civic responsibility within the NSS RVCE community, as volunteers efficiently managed logistics, safety measures, hydration points, route coordination, and participant support. The structured execution of the run enhanced event management, planning, and leadership capabilities among organizers.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, a flagship community welfare initiative conducted by NSS RVCE, was organized with the central theme “Help a Child, Change the World” emphasizing support for underprivileged children requiring educational and healthcare assistance.\\n\\nThe event commenced at 7:00 AM with systematic registration, verification, and distribution of event shirts, badges, and participation materials, creating uniformity, identity, and enthusiasm among attendees. Pre-event announcements, energy sessions, and safety briefings were conducted to ensure preparedness and smooth coordination. Medical teams, hydration points, volunteers, and emergency response units were strategically stationed along the route to maintain participant safety and well-being.\\n\\nThe Marathon officially began at 9:00 AM and witnessed active participation from over 500 individuals, including students, faculty members, and fitness enthusiasts. The carefully planned route encouraged inclusivity and accessibility, offering a balance of challenge and engagement for runners of varying fitness levels. Throughout the event, NSS volunteers facilitated crowd management, route guidance, and awareness messaging, reinforcing the event’s social objective.\\n\\nBeyond promoting physical fitness and recreational involvement, the marathon aimed to create consciousness about the struggles faced by underprivileged children and the importance of collective community action in addressing them. The event fostered social responsibility, volunteerism, compassion, teamwork, and civic participation within the campus community\\n","aicteMapping":"Community development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1p24PKgZnPcrpZvsfJBUH","name":"Female Foeticide Walkathon","slNo":3,"place":"RV. College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/6i0PlXTmHA9ubVRTdePYC.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/yDCuWrOkm2f8CXURHoaLX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon successfully raised awareness about female foeticide and the importance of valuing the girl child. It encouraged participants to take a stand against gender discrimination and promoted social responsibility through collective action.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":7,"description":"On the occasion of Mother''s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon with the aim of shedding light on the grave issue of female foeticide and promoting the value of girt children in society. The event witnessed an overwhelming participation of 350+ individuals, including enthusiastic students, dedicated faculty members, and supportive parents who came together to walk for a cause that truly matters. The walkathon began in the early hours of the morning from the RVCE campus and was marked by thought-provoking placards, powerful slogans, and an atmosphere of solidarity. The event served as a platform to educate and inspire change, urging everyone to take a stand against gender-based violence and discrimination even before birth. The Rotaract Club of RVCE extends heartfelt gratitude to all participants for their support and commitment to this impactful cause","aicteMapping":"Community development and social development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ycOAHI9yjTU7EUT0Rba5a","name":"Utsarga Marthon 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RV College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/Z0L2I2Kz9YcKvJjMv9f4E.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon concluded with significant social, organizational, and community-oriented outcomes. The event successfully mobilized more than 500 participants, demonstrating strong public engagement and widespread support for the cause of helping underprivileged children.\\n\\nThe marathon also strengthened the culture of volunteerism, teamwork, and civic responsibility within the NSS RVCE community, as volunteers efficiently managed logistics, safety measures, hydration points, route coordination, and participant support. The structured execution of the run enhanced event management, planning, and leadership capabilities among organizers.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, a flagship community welfare initiative conducted by NSS RVCE, was organized with the central theme “Help a Child, Change the World” emphasizing support for underprivileged children requiring educational and healthcare assistance.\\n\\nThe event commenced at 7:00 AM with systematic registration, verification, and distribution of event shirts, badges, and participation materials, creating uniformity, identity, and enthusiasm among attendees. Pre-event announcements, energy sessions, and safety briefings were conducted to ensure preparedness and smooth coordination. Medical teams, hydration points, volunteers, and emergency response units were strategically stationed along the route to maintain participant safety and well-being.\\n\\nThe Marathon officially began at 9:00 AM and witnessed active participation from over 500 individuals, including students, faculty members, and fitness enthusiasts. The carefully planned route encouraged inclusivity and accessibility, offering a balance of challenge and engagement for runners of varying fitness levels. Throughout the event, NSS volunteers facilitated crowd management, route guidance, and awareness messaging, reinforcing the event’s social objective.\\n\\nBeyond promoting physical fitness and recreational involvement, the marathon aimed to create consciousness about the struggles faced by underprivileged children and the importance of collective community action in addressing them. The event fostered social responsibility, volunteerism, compassion, teamwork, and civic participation within the campus community.\\n","aicteMapping":" Community development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"V_Aph79RLiGhYjEQ6nrTj","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":5,"place":"RV College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/6EBECC9MxWIfY9LPq2BoJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project successfully collected and distributed a large number of books to government school students. It brought smiles and encouragement to the children and helped improve their interest in studies.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-14","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social outreach initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged students studying in Government Schools. As part of this activity, a stationery kit containing essential study materials was sponsored and donated to one student. The initiative focused on encouraging education and reducing the financial burden on economically weaker students by providing them with basic academic resources. This activity promoted social responsibility, community service, and awareness about the importance of equal access to education. In recognition of this contribution","aicteMapping":"Community development and social development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZtS8xE3M3GbSa2DiWLxnP","name":"Fistfull 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RV College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/Fr7TeF8zg-h8yOVNB_1zp.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-24","duration":10,"outcomes":"The FISTFULL initiative successfully mobilized large-scale student participation and generated significant food grain donations, with over 6,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal collected from more than 1,750 students. The activity strengthened the spirit of social responsibility, compassion, and community service among students. It demonstrated the impact of collective effort in addressing hunger and supporting vulnerable communities. Participants developed greater awareness of social issues and the importance of contributing toward societal welfare. Overall, the initiative created a meaningful social impact by promoting solidarity and reinforcing the values of generosity and service","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":20,"description":"FISTFULL was a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana from 15th to 29th November. The project aimed to combat hunger and support the underprivileged by encouraging students to donate food grains. Students were motivated to contribute either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal as part of the donation drive. Daily collections were carried out in the Civil Engineering Department, receiving enthusiastic participation from the student community. The collected food grains were later distributed to needy sections of society through Rotary Bangalore Spandana, ensuring proper utilization for community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Community development and social development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t_X1l3HxNCPYFzPHQTIWj","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":7,"place":"RV College of Engineering ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/L0n0AuYTC9tDSAYYQzBuI.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp was very successful and received a good response from students, teachers, and local community members. Many volunteers came forward to donate blood, and a significant number of blood units were collected. The event helped raise awareness about the importance of donating blood regularly and motivated others to participate in future drives. It also built a sense of social responsibility, compassion, and teamwork among participants. Overall, the camp contributed to saving lives and supporting the healthcare system. The camp was a great success, with many volunteers donating blood and spreading awareness about its importance. The event helped in collecting several units of blood that will benefit patients in need. It also inspired participants to contribute to humanitarian causes and highlighted the value of selfless service. Overall, the Blood Donation Camp strengthened the spirit of compassion, responsibility, and community welfare among all participants.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Blood Donation Camp is an organized event where volunteers donate blood under the supervision of medical professionals. It is conducted to collect blood for hospitals and blood banks, promote awareness about blood donation, and encourage people to contribute to society. The camp ensures safety, proper hygiene, and medical screening for all donors. The blood is collected safely by trained medical staff using sterile equipment. Such camps also include awareness programs to educate people about the importance of blood donation and how one donation can save several lives. A Blood Donation Camp was organized to collect blood from voluntary donors and create awareness about the importance of blood donation. The camp was conducted in collaboration with a local hospital and medical professionals, who ensured all safety and hygiene measures. Students, teachers, and community members actively participated in the event. The main aim of the camp was to help save lives, promote social responsibility, and encourage regular blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Social & Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"m32B8s34BH5bYmJ95x35o","name":"Human Elephant Conflict Awareness ","slNo":8,"place":"RV College of Engineering ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/oZbovqSMgDF0A4lbEMSMu.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Save the Elephant Seminar successfully enhanced participants’ understanding of the importance of elephant conservation and wildlife protection. Students gained knowledge about elephant behavior, their ecological role, and the threats they face due to poaching and habitat loss. The seminar encouraged awareness of government and NGO initiatives for wildlife conservation and forest preservation. It inspired students to actively participate in environmental protection activities and spread awareness in their communities. The event also fostered respect for animals and promoted the need for peaceful coexistence between humans and wildlife. Overall, the seminar proved to be an informative and impactful initiative toward biodiversity and environmental conservation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Subject:\\nSeminar on Human–Elephant Conflict: Coexistence and Conservation\\nContent:\\nA seminar on Human–Elephant Conflict was organized to create awareness about the growing challenges arising from interactions between human populations and elephant habitats. The session focused on the causes of conflict such as habitat fragmentation, agricultural expansion, and urbanization, along with their impact on both human safety and elephant conservation. Experts and speakers discussed real-life case studies, mitigation strategies, and sustainable solutions including habitat corridors, early warning systems, and community involvement. The seminar encouraged participants to understand the importance of coexistence, responsible land use, and conservation-driven policies, fostering a sense of environmental\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"539EObNr-Q57xIrRiTNVL","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":9,"place":"RV college of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/vIPAZvnPAp5q1yV4CnZRI.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":2,"outcomes":"Uptown Junk successfully promoted creativity, innovation, and sustainable practices among participants. Students developed teamwork, leadership, and resource management skills while working under competitive conditions. The event increased awareness about waste reuse and environmental responsibility. It strengthened bonding within the student community and encouraged collaborative learning. Overall, the event created a fun yet meaningful learning experience by combining competition, sustainability, and innovation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Subject: Uptown Junk – A Two-Day Festival of Creativity and Sustainability\\nContent:\\nUptown Junk was a two-day flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th and 29th November 2024, designed to promote creativity, teamwork, and sustainable thinking among students. The event featured engaging activities such as a “Treasure Hunt” and a “Best Out of Waste” competition, where teams were challenged to innovate using auctioned materials and Rota money. With participation from over 400 students, the event created a vibrant platform for hands-on learning, problem-solving, and collaboration. Evaluated by esteemed judges including DRR Rtr. Abhay Lohia, Rtr. Disha, Rtr. Bhumika, Rtr. Shreya, and IPP Rtr. Satej, the competitions highlighted the importance of resourcefulness and environmental responsibility. Uptown Junk successfully blended fun with purpose, fostering a strong sense of community, innovation, and sustainability within the college.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Sustainability and innovation","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"m-udUe-tDZhghmeubSKGV","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz","slNo":10,"place":"RV College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/gqDSQGT_0FncFGZGLneN7.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The MyGov Quiz on India’s Heritage successfully increased students’ awareness and understanding of India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage. Participants gained deeper knowledge about monuments, freedom fighters, festivals, art forms, literature, and ancient scientific achievements. The activity promoted learning through fun and healthy competition, improving teamwork and quick-thinking abilities. It also instilled a sense of patriotism, pride, and respect for the nation’s traditions and values. Overall, the quiz inspired students to stay connected to their roots and appreciate India’s diverse heritage","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The MyGov Quiz on India’s Heritage was organized to enhance students’ knowledge about India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage. The quiz included questions about monuments, freedom fighters, festivals, art forms, literature, and scientific achievements of ancient India. Students participated enthusiastically, showing their interest and pride in the country’s glorious past. The event aimed to promote awareness of India’s diverse heritage and instill a sense of patriotism among young learners. The quiz helped students gain deeper insight into India’s history and cultural values. It encouraged learning through fun and competition, strengthening teamwork and quick-thinking skills. Participants developed greater respect and pride for the nation’s traditions and achievements. Overall, the MyGov Quiz on India’s Heritage successfully inspired students to stay connected to their roots and celebrate India’s rich legacy.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qyD-llzrUL54MzEhMX8DF","name":"Workshop on Sir M Vishweshwaraiah Rain Water Harvesting Theme Park","slNo":11,"place":"Sir M Vishweshwaraiah Rain Water Harvesting Theme Park","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6fcd3583-cd17-49a9-b6b5-b1e6e2c0e31e/yv8oAxr3LgYsx3FhiVFTM.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improved understanding of environmental management, sustainability, and climate change issues. Gained awareness about conservation practices, pollution control, and eco-friendly approaches, strengthening my sense of environmental responsibility.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-08","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Participated in an environmental awareness and education workshop focused on sustainable practices, environmental protection, and policy aspects. Gained knowledge on environmental management strategies, conservation techniques, and the role of individuals and communities in addressing environmental challenges. Developed better understanding of climate change issues, pollution control measures, and eco-friendly lifestyle practices. The activity enhanced my awareness, responsibility towards the environment, and ability to apply sustainable concepts in academic and real-life contexts.","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Venugopal.G","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 09:18:55.073647+00', '2026-01-30 09:27:06.739391+00'), ('6c49a78c-541e-426c-ac74-69eec94e4b9d', '6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS135","name":"PAVAN SHIVAKUMAR","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"UcMMEvQibk7h3jhd4Fxy_","name":"Mera Phale vote Desh Keliye","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/rYONEKZnpglzicbOsGeTk.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/-GoWCC0ygUeQ1ok4yveSN.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The “Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye” initiative successfully encourages first-time voters to participate actively in the electoral process. It creates awareness about voting rights and strengthens democratic values among youth. The program helps reduce voter apathy and motivates young citizens to make informed choices. It also increases overall voter turnout by building confidence in RV college of Engineering® Bengaluru AICTE activity points new voters. Overall, the initiative promotes responsible citizenship and\\nsupports a stronger, more participatory Democracy.\\n","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The \"Mera Pehla Vote, Desh Ke Liye\" initiative by the Indian government is a significant campaign aimed at encouraging first- time voters to actively participate in the democratic process and exercise their fundamental right to vote. Recognizing the importance of youth involvement in shaping the nation''s future, this program seeks to instill a deep sense of responsibility, civic duty, and national pride among young citizens who are eligible to vote for the first time. By engaging with the youth and educating them about the electoral process, the initiative emphasizes the power of voting in a democracy and the impact it has on governance, policy-making, and overall national development.\\n\\nAs a part of this initiative, individuals take a pledge, committing themselves to vote responsibly, make informed choices, and support leaders who work towards the progress and well-being of the country. Awareness programs, workshops, and interactive sessions are often conducted to familiarize first-time voters with the importance of their participation and the role they play in strengthening democratic institutions. The campaign also leverages social media, educational institutions, and community engagement programs to reach a wider audience, ensuring that young voters are motivated and well-prepared to take part in the electoral process. By fostering a culture of informed and responsible voting, \"Mera Pehla Vote, Desh Ke Liye\" serves as a crucial step in empowering the youth and reinforcing the principles of democracy, ensuring that every vote contributes to the nation’s growth and stability. Outcome The “Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye”\\n","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/zlgpnYtfY2T8KeJT1NsMT.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bE9_bMkxLkZwKM6Eo_u8W","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON 2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/jkgrvfonlHKNE0dzP8d0R.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/lNRokblr73WcLqXMhL_X8.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":18,"outcomes":"Volunteering for the Utsarga Marathon provided a meaningful opportunity to actively contribute to community service and social responsibility. Through involvement in event coordination and on-ground support, the activity helped develop teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills. The volunteers played a key role in ensuring the smooth conduct of the marathon by assisting participants, managing logistics, and supporting hydration and safety arrangements.\\n\\nThe experience strengthened a sense of empathy and civic responsibility, as the event aimed at channeling its proceeds toward noble causes such as supporting underprivileged communities, healthcare initiatives, and environmental sustainability projects. Volunteering in the marathon also promoted awareness about the importance of physical fitness and collective action for social good. Overall, the activity reinforced the values of selfless service, discipline, and community engagement among volunteers while contributing to the successful execution of a large-scale social initiative.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-18","hoursSpent":28,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants.\\n\\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well- marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/vARFoBgdQGXic2rq_fwHX.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ye9O7gjbyVWZ5X0dPsswo","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/f8hEdBkBHmAvzt4-xgtVY.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/c9L3YeV9wDVXEQQT9eoC1.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of RVCE, successfully blended fitness, community engagement, and philanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to contribute to a meaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With enthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful reminder of the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges. Runners contributed through their registration fees, which were directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to educational and environmental projects.\\nThe overwhelming response from participants highlighted the deep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service and social responsibility. Beyond the physical endurance required to complete the marathon, the event fostered a sense of camaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of teamwork and determination. The well-organized event featured structured routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance, ensuring a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Additionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, encouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while giving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the bond between students and the community but also showcased how small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful social change.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants.\\n\\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well- marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/wbEw4pfVzgdhlTt0uCaLl.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nCWdrnyXGNLEdyyftXMct","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/BW8L89UumriNNwiUH_oCz.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/yYmY83JrHZkn8T5tkkoP1.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-05-31","duration":8,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged rural students by providing them with essential educational materials and school supplies. The initiative created a meaningful impact by ensuring needy students received textbooks, stationery, and other learning resources required for a better education experience. With effective fund collection and proper utilization, the event reflected strong community participation and social responsibility. The collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranava Foundation strengthened the reach of this initiative, helping improve access to education and creating a positive learning environment for students.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":25,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of approximately Rs. 100 to 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which was used to procure and donate mission-needed supplies such as severe deserving students.\\nThe collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed other Rs. 100 or Rs. 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranava Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/eor4dXxYWZbWBPN0GuMUs.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dawVNLsYaljT6B3bg0OFY","name":"EYE DONATION FORTNIGHT","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/O0PPtghYpcH0Ibln_Dxyy.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/UQbI7DAAdYTBc7Dc_BrLV.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-09-08","duration":12,"outcomes":"The Eye Donation Fortnight had a significant positive impact on both the participants and the community. The event successfully increased awareness among students and the public about the importance of eye donation and its role in giving the gift of sight to visually impaired individuals. Many people were motivated to pledge their eyes, thereby contributing to the long-term goal of reducing corneal blindness.\\n\\nFrom an NSS perspective, the event helped volunteers develop a strong sense of social responsibility and empathy towards societal issues. Active participation in awareness activities improved the communication skills, leadership qualities, and teamwork abilities of the volunteers. It also reinforced the importance of youth involvement in community-oriented programs.\\n\\nOverall, the event strengthened the role of NSS at RV College of Engineering as a platform for service and civic engagement. The successful execution of the Eye Donation Fortnight reflected the dedication of NSS volunteers towards nation-building activities and social welfare, while also fulfilling the objectives of NSS in promoting selfless service among students.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-28","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Eye Donation Fortnight was organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of RV College of Engineering as part of its commitment to community service and social responsibility. The event aimed to create awareness about eye donation and highlight its importance in preventing avoidable blindness. It was conducted in association with recognized organizations working in the field of eye care and donation.\\n\\nDuring the event, NSS volunteers actively participated in awareness activities such as pledge drives, interpersonal interactions, and information dissemination among students and the general public. The initiative focused on educating people about corneal blindness, the eye donation process, and the role of timely donation in restoring vision. Volunteers also addressed common myths and misconceptions related to eye donation and encouraged individuals to pledge their eyes.\\n\\nThe Eye Donation Fortnight provided NSS volunteers with an opportunity to engage directly in social service while upholding the NSS motto, “Not Me, But You”. Through this initiative, students contributed meaningfully towards a humanitarian cause and strengthened the outreach efforts of NSS at RVCE.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/0qNKOdNRa1EessEAPM7ZY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1PswHktC4-EUiFGs5oCvK","name":"FistFull","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/3dEHxts2GDz_fLvRS2oj5.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/SHA7_SvAUEG5d8ODp2pUy.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant quantity of rice through the contribution of 5 kg from each participant. It helped provide food support to underprivileged communities and addressed issues related to hunger and food insecurity. The drive created awareness about the importance of sharing and social responsibility among students. Participants developed empathy, teamwork, and a strong sense of community service. Overall, the initiative made a meaningful social impact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and humanitarian service on campus.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":30,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the aim of supporting the underprivileged and promoting social responsibility among students. In this drive, students and volunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, symbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of food to those in need. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and hunger faced by many sections of society. It encouraged participants to share resources selflessly and develop a habit of giving back to the community.\\n\\nThe drive also strengthened values of empathy, kindness, and unity among the students. The collected rice was planned to be distributed to needy communities through charitable organizations. The drive witnessed enthusiastic participation, showcasing strong teamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided students with an opportunity to actively engage in social service activities. The initiative highlighted how even small contributions can collectively create a significant positive impact. Overall, the Fist Full Drive successfully reinforced the spirit of service, compassion, and social responsibility within the campus.\\n","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/bdPeTgoy787G9V9CsfJ3s.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qN_0HvVYYHZb-tNZ_h3VK","name":"Vikasit Bharath Quiz","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/71rzkymJZjUqXk8fUsNNn.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/WrrdZzMSCV0vNgVbRt1xT.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the Vikasit Bharat Quiz significantly enhanced the awareness of students regarding India’s developmental vision and contemporary national issues. The activity helped participants gain a broader understanding of government initiatives, economic reforms, technological innovations, and sustainable development practices that contribute to the nation’s progress.\\n\\nThe quiz strengthened analytical thinking and decision-making skills by challenging participants to apply their knowledge in a competitive environment. It also instilled a sense of patriotism and responsibility among students, encouraging them to actively contribute to society beyond academics.\\n\\nFrom an NSS perspective, the activity successfully promoted the values of informed citizenship, social responsibility, and youth engagement in national development. Overall, the Vikasit Bharat Quiz proved to be an impactful educational initiative that reinforced the role of students as responsible citizens committed to the vision of a developed and inclusive India.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Vikasit Bharat Quiz was organized under the aegis of the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering (RVCE) with the objective of creating awareness among students about India’s vision for holistic national development. The quiz focused on key themes such as economic growth, technological advancement, social welfare initiatives, sustainability, governance reforms, and India’s long-term development goals.\\n\\nThe event encouraged active participation from students across departments and served as an interactive platform to test and enhance their knowledge about national policies, government initiatives, and the role of youth in nation-building. By participating in the quiz, students were motivated to stay informed about current affairs and understand how individual responsibility contributes to the collective progress of the country.\\n\\nThe quiz was conducted in a structured and transparent manner, promoting healthy competition, critical thinking, and teamwork among participants. It aligned with the core objectives of NSS by fostering social awareness, civic responsibility, and informed citizenship among young engineers.","aicteMapping":"Comunity Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dbI9S_H7VM-iYA_9-4k6l","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON 2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/bpbjIJGT-VXf1jLMHyhRk.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/Hr9N5p8dhTa5vRtWpKFdW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s education programs. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and learning resources to underprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its fundraising goals, amassing contributions that will sustain classroom initiatives for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students from local underserved communities.\\n\\nBeyond the financial gains, the marathon left an indelible impression on all involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from first-time runners conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz amplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and encouraging future involvement.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, was held on 6th April, 2025, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM across the RVCE campus in Bengaluru. Conducted under the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the event aimed to promote health and fitness while supporting the education of underprivileged children. Careful planning and sponsor support ensured smooth logistics, with medals, T-shirts, refreshments, and a well-marked route enhancing the overall experience.\\n\\nOver 500 participants—including students, faculty, alumni, and runners from across Karnataka—took part in the marathon. Participants could choose between a 5 km fun run or a 10 km competitive run, with all proceeds directed toward educational support such as school supplies and tuition fees. The campus came alive with warm-up sessions, cheering crowds, music, banners, and photo booths, creating a lively and motivating atmosphere.\\n\\nNSS volunteers efficiently managed water stations, medical aid, and crowd control, ensuring safety and inclusivity throughout the event. Runners were welcomed at the finish line with applause, finisher medals, and certificates, while top performers received special trophies. The marathon successfully blended physical endurance with social responsibility, inspiring unity and generating meaningful impact toward improving children’s futures.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/Qfb01JeMttajG_ZdwNqUo.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Z615L8hnn69MAnlLcUYf_","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/bT0VVHFDjKTgyBfCav4tQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged rural students by providing them with essential educational materials and school supplies. The initiative created a meaningful impact by ensuring needy students received textbooks, stationery, and other learning resources required for a better education experience. With effective fund collection and proper utilization, the event reflected strong community participation and social responsibility. The collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranava Foundation strengthened the reach of this initiative, helping improve access to education and creating a positive learning environment for students.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-04-23","hoursSpent":25,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of approximately Rs. 100 to 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which was used to procure and donate mission-needed supplies such as severe deserving students.\\nThe collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed other Rs. 100 or Rs. 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranava Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Community Drive","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/54jlB2nKWttSU20e_dX1N.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"A6LsRro8zYnLOyz20GIxD","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/0ODScR_7SB7WZ0MyNMx-J.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/8nTo2fd9Am927jeDNSA1F.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon successfully sensitized participants and the wider campus community to the critical issue of female foeticide and the need for gender equality. The event helped participants develop a deeper understanding of the social, ethical, and moral responsibilities involved in protecting the rights of women and ensuring a balanced and just society.\\n\\nThe walkathon encouraged students to move beyond academic learning and actively engage in social causes, fostering values such as empathy, leadership, teamwork, and civic responsibility. It strengthened community bonding by bringing together students, faculty, and families for a shared purpose, thereby reinforcing the spirit of collective action.\\n\\nFrom an organizational perspective, the event enhanced the visibility and impact of the Rotaract Club’s service initiatives and demonstrated the effectiveness of awareness-based activities in driving social change. Overall, the walkathon left a lasting impression on participants, motivating them to continue advocating for social justice and contributing meaningfully to nation-building efforts.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, sponsored by Rotary Bangalore South (R.I. District 3191), on the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025, at the RV College of Engineering campus. The event was conducted with the objective of addressing the serious social issue of female foeticide and spreading awareness about the importance of gender equality and the protection of the girl child.\\n\\nThe walkathon witnessed the participation of over 350 individuals, including enthusiastic students, committed faculty members, and supportive parents. Participants gathered in the early hours of the morning and walked together along a planned route within the campus, holding placards and banners carrying strong messages against female foeticide and gender discrimination. The use of impactful slogans and visual messages helped draw attention to the cause and encouraged dialogue among onlookers.\\n\\nThe walkathon created a powerful sense of unity and purpose, highlighting the collective responsibility of society in eliminating social evils. By organizing the event on Mother’s Day, the Rotaract Club emphasized the emotional and social significance of respecting and protecting women and girls. The activity served as an effective platform to educate, inspire, and mobilize the community towards positive social change.","aicteMapping":"Awareness drive","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/4Z-G3Sutr9J-iCerrsJlY.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-27","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Tgq4p-yBz8H6LBY6VEi8-","name":"Nasha Mukta Bharatha","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/IvDGPdVLYRx40SEIz2gUQ.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/BpjIA_7SyOGFcqZEXT8dH.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Nasha Mukta Bharat activity successfully sensitized participants to the serious consequences of substance abuse and encouraged them to make informed and responsible life choices. The initiative helped students understand the social, psychological, and economic impact of addiction, thereby strengthening their awareness and moral responsibility as citizens.\\n\\nThe activity fostered a sense of discipline, self-control, and social commitment among NSS volunteers. It also reinforced the role of youth as change-makers in spreading awareness and influencing peers and communities toward healthier living. Overall, the program effectively contributed to NSS objectives by promoting social awareness, responsible behavior, and active participation in national development initiatives.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Nasha Mukta Bharat activity was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) as part of the Government of India’s nationwide initiative to combat substance abuse and promote a drug-free society. The program aimed to create awareness among students and the community about the harmful effects of alcohol, tobacco, and drug addiction on physical health, mental well-being, families, and society at large.\\n\\nAs part of the activity, NSS volunteers actively participated in awareness-oriented initiatives such as pledge-taking, poster displays, interaction sessions, and dissemination of key messages highlighting the dangers of substance abuse. The event emphasized preventive measures, the importance of self-discipline, and the role of youth in building a healthy and responsible society. Through collective participation, the program reinforced the message of adopting positive lifestyles and staying away from addictive habits.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"28-29","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"y1aUX3u2xmKGm7K3rWbGU","name":"FistFull 2025","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/a4sbyrIg1LL3xfVH2Daq0.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6f097755-3458-40b6-95c2-87af14c8c148/BQ0ludr8irS9MQaOxms_R.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant quantity of rice through the contribution of 5 kg from each participant. It helped provide food support to underprivileged communities and addressed issues related to hunger and food insecurity. The drive created awareness about the importance of sharing and social responsibility among students. Participants developed empathy, teamwork, and a strong sense of community service. Overall, the initiative made a meaningful social impact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and humanitarian service on campus.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":30,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the aim of supporting the underprivileged and promoting social responsibility among students. In this drive, students and volunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, symbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of food to those in need. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and hunger faced by many sections of society. It encouraged participants to share resources selflessly and develop a habit of giving back to the community.\\n\\nThe drive also strengthened values of empathy, kindness, and unity among the students. The collected rice was planned to be distributed to needy communities through charitable organizations. The drive witnessed enthusiastic participation, showcasing strong teamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided students with an opportunity to actively engage in social service activities. The initiative highlighted how even small contributions can collectively create a significant positive impact. Overall, the Fist Full Drive successfully reinforced the spirit of service, compassion, and social responsibility within the campus.","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"30-31","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 13:21:47.375076+00', '2026-01-31 04:20:09.725336+00'), ('6cacffad-615d-4bec-9695-ee2b8c58452d', '44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV085","name":"Rohan C","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"1RQd2sHpUXEhMywkzwF5h","name":"Project Pustak-2024(Rotaract)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/yTm8umqFIfA2SM1en1WX9.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/2K1JaoZ_mSAHqOEs3hvbr.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/0B2rciR67y0SrPuIzAb-C.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully translated collective goodwill into tangible educational support for \\nunderprivileged rural students. By mobilizing small but meaningful contributions of Rs. 100 \\nand Rs. 350 from donors, the initiative generated sufficient funds to procure essential school \\nsupplies such as textbooks, stationery, backpacks, and related learning materials. This directly \\nreduced the financial burden on economically disadvantaged families and improved students’ \\naccess to basic educational resources. The collaboration between the Rotaract Club of RVCE \\nand Pranav Foundation ensured transparent fund utilization and effective on-ground execution, \\nultimately fostering a more inclusive and supportive learning environment for rural students and \\nencouraging school attendance and engagement.\\nProject Pustak highlights the power of collective action, showing that modest individual \\ncontributions can create a significant social impact when pooled together. It demonstrates the \\nimportance of structured collaboration between student organizations and NGOs to achieve \\nefficient implementation and accountability. The project also reinforces key lessons in social \\nresponsibility, leadership, project planning, and resource management. Most importantly, it \\nemphasizes that education-focused interventions, even at a grassroots level, can play a crucial \\nrole in bridging inequality and empowering communities for long-term development.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies \\nto underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was \\ncollected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and \\ndonating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently \\nutilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and \\nother vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous \\ncontributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial \\nfunds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school \\nsupplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NdE86rWdQXB10uRT5eVRU","name":"Project Pustak-2025(Rotaract)","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/XnlwQAjZU_9k8rfsn24bf.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/9xQNovp7zlLmFOs7PRuyt.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/-ipGT3X60BrJ0ZOdW2Zzn.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-16","duration":8,"outcomes":"Project Pustak stands as a highly impactful, well-executed social initiative that successfully \\nbridged a critical educational resource gap for underprivileged students in government schools. \\nThrough a structured, two-phase approach, the Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with \\nthe Pranav Foundation, demonstrated how organized student-led efforts can translate intent \\ninto measurable results. Phase-1 achieved exceptional community engagement by mobilizing \\n1,022 college students and raising ¹3,50,000, reflecting strong trust, transparency, and collective \\nresponsibility within the RVCE ecosystem. The project’s recognition by UGRAM further \\nreinforced its credibility and societal relevance.\\nIn Phase-2, the collected funds were efficiently converted into large-scale on-ground impact. \\nThe July 2025 distribution drive resulted in the assembly and delivery of 5,500 complete \\nschool kits containing 24,000 notebooks, 3,250 stationery kits, and 2,250 geometry boxes \\nacross 12 government schools. The kits were thoughtfully designed based on students’ age \\ngroups, ensuring relevance and usability. With the participation of volunteers, faculty members, \\nand collaborators, the initiative directly enabled thousands of children—who otherwise lacked \\nbasic academic tools despite having uniforms—to actively participate in classroom learning. \\nThe project therefore contributed not only to improved access to education but also to \\nbetter attendance, engagement, and dignity for students from economically disadvantaged \\nbackgrounds.\\nProject Pustak offers several important takeaways. First, it highlights the power of collective \\naction—small individual contributions, when organized effectively, can create large-scale social \\nchange. Second, it demonstrates the value of phased project execution, where fundraisingplanning, and implementation are clearly separated, ensuring accountability and efficient use \\nof resources. Third, the initiative underscores the importance of collaboration between student \\nbodies, NGOs, and faculty to achieve sustainable and credible outcomes.\\nFrom a learning perspective, the project builds leadership, teamwork, ethical responsibility, and \\nproject management skills among student organizers and volunteers. It also shows how aligning \\nsocial service with institutional frameworks—such as activity points and certification—can \\nencourage participation without diluting the core humanitarian objective. Most importantly, \\nProject Pustak reinforces a fundamental lesson: addressing basic educational needs is one of \\nthe most effective ways to reduce inequality and empower future generations, and student-led \\ninitiatives can play a decisive role in driving meaningful, scalable social impact.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-09","hoursSpent":40,"description":"from April 23rd to 30th, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation. Recently recognized and \\nappreciated by UGRAM, the project aims to support the education of underprivileged children \\nby providing them with essential learning materials, Phase-1 focused on raising funds from \\ncollege students, and the response was overwhelming. The club successfully raised a remarkable \\nsum of ¹3,50,000 from contributions by 1,022 students during this phase, showcasing the spirit \\nof generosity and collective action within the RVCE community. For the students who donated \\nRs. 350, a certificate will be provided as a proof for 10 Activity Points. The funds collected \\nwere used in Phase-2 of the project, which involved the distribution of stationery kits and books \\nto children in government schools. The project reflects the club''s commitment to promoting \\neducation and reducing resource gaps for students in need.\\nThe Rotaract Club of R.V.C.E. hosted the event Project Pustak from 22nd-26th July 2025. \\nProject Pustak''s first distribution phase, conducted in collaboration with Pranav Foundation, \\nwitnessed the participation of 58 individuals, including 17 volunteers and 3 faculty members. \\nThrough generous donations collected in the first phase, essential educational supplies were \\ndistributed by faculty and participants to ensure underprivileged students received necessary \\nacademic materials such as notebooks, stationery kits, and geometry boxes. In total, 24,000 \\nnotebooks, 3,250 stationery kits, and 2,250 geometry boxes were assembled into 5,500 school \\nkits and distributed across 12 government schools in diverse locations.\\nProject Pustak was launched with the aim of supporting underprivileged children who, although \\nprovided with school uniforms through government aid, often lack access to basic academic \\ntools. This gap places many students at a significant disadvantage. The distribution included \\ntwo types of kits tailored for different age groups: students in grades 1 to 5 received kits with \\nfour notebooks (two ruled, two unruled) along with a stationery kit, while students in grades 6 \\nto 10 received four notebooks (two ruled, two unruled) and a geometry box.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4CcHDZFhw2hZmJ_z4KmrY","name":"Utsarga-2024(NSS Marathon)","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/CZWv9md_4nVd72kToqhuE.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/r8GbU6E6EIJ6fJ7lWYPSV.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-04-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully combined physical fitness with social impact, creating a \\nmeaningful platform for community engagement. By organizing the event at R V College of \\nEngineering, the initiative motivated students and participants to adopt healthier lifestyles while \\ncontributing to a larger humanitarian cause. The marathon helped raise awareness and support \\nfor educational initiatives aimed at underprivileged children, reinforcing the idea that individual \\nparticipation can directly contribute to social development. The provision of AICTE activity \\npoints further encouraged active involvement, ensuring strong participation and institutional \\nrecognition of social responsibility.\\nThis initiative demonstrates that social causes can be effectively integrated with fitness and \\nrecreational activities to drive wider participation and impact. It highlights the value of \\nholistic development—balancing physical well-being with empathy and civic responsibility. \\nParticipants learn that social change does not always require complex interventions; consistent \\neffort and collective participation can make a tangible difference. The marathon also fosters \\ndiscipline, teamwork, and a sense of purpose, reinforcing the role of students as active \\ncontributors to societal progress while nurturing both body and mind.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-04-02","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is a social and fitness-oriented event organized at R V College of \\nEngineering on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM. The marathon is designed \\nto promote physical well-being while fostering social responsibility among participants. More \\nthan just a running event, it carries a strong humanitarian message under the theme “Help a \\nChild Change the World.”\\nParticipants are encouraged to take part not only to celebrate health and fitness but also to \\ncontribute to a meaningful cause, as every step taken supports initiatives aimed at providing \\neducation to underprivileged children. By combining endurance, enthusiasm, and empathy, the \\nUtsarga Marathon creates a platform where students and participants actively engage in social \\nchange while earning 10 AICTE activity points for their involvement.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"S0Rjjryd-IUF3OnKlGMrN","name":"Utsarga-2025(NSS Marathon)","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/_XAoT8UY3m3cTYkjs1prV.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/4ieD5CsGCAWj0vuGYfR1K.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"UTSARGA ’25 successfully served as a comprehensive platform that integrated fitness, social \\nresponsibility, and cultural celebration. By bringing together students and members of the wider \\ncommunity at RV College of Engineering, the marathon generated awareness and support for \\nunderprivileged children in the areas of education, healthcare, and welfare. The dual-distance \\nformat enabled inclusive participation, while the cause-driven nature of the event transformed \\nphysical effort into meaningful social contribution. The cultural elements associated with Ram \\nNavami further enhanced participant engagement and community bonding. Overall, the event \\nstrengthened collective commitment toward social upliftment while promoting healthy lifestyles \\nand active citizenship.\\nUTSARGA ’25 highlights how social causes can be effectively amplified through engaging, \\nlarge-scale events. It demonstrates the importance of integrating physical well-being with \\nempathy and civic duty, showing that social impact can be achieved through participatory and \\ninclusive activities. Participants gain lessons in discipline, teamwork, and social awareness, \\nwhile understanding that individual effort—when combined with a shared purpose—can \\ncontribute to meaningful change. The initiative also reinforces leadership, organizational skills,\\nand cultural sensitivity, underscoring the role of educational institutions in nurturing socially \\nresponsible and well-rounded individuals.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-04","hoursSpent":60,"description":"UTSARGA ’25 is the flagship marathon organized at RV College of Engineering, dedicated \\nto the social cause “Help a Child, Change the World.” Scheduled on April 6, 2025, the event \\naims to mobilize students and the wider community to support underprivileged children through \\ninitiatives focused on education, healthcare, and overall welfare.\\nThe marathon features two categories—5 KM and 10 KM—encouraging participation \\nfrom individuals with varying fitness levels. By combining physical endurance with social \\ncommitment, the event promotes healthy lifestyles while fostering empathy and civic \\nresponsibility. Participants receive a comprehensive experience including a T-shirt, certificate, \\nmedal, breakfast, refreshments, and electrolyte juice, ensuring both motivation and well-being \\nthroughout the event.\\nIn addition, as the event coincides with Ram Navami, traditional refreshments such as \\nKosambari and Fruit Panaka are served, adding a cultural and celebratory dimension to the \\nmarathon. UTSARGA ’25 thus stands as a holistic initiative that blends fitness, social service, \\nand cultural values, while also recognizing participant involvement through the award of 15 \\nAICTE activity points.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"j18XByozeNF61_NOosU0V","name":"CHEELA MELA (NSS)","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/EcF7jN4drQRxds0hXkXyz.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/Yx7KNl890bTWqsOSyOoKk.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants developed practical skills in making eco-friendly paper bags using newspapers and recyclable materials.\\n Increased awareness about plastic pollution* and the importance of sustainable alternatives among students.\\nA significant number of paper bags were produced and made available for use during the Kadale Kayi Parishe, helping reduce single-use plastic consumption.\\n Students gained a sense of social responsibility and community involvement by contributing to an environmentally beneficial cause.\\n The activity promoted the principles of Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle reinforcing environmentally conscious behavior.\\n Strengthened collaboration between NSS RVCE and Youth For Seva*, fostering teamwork and volunteerism.\\n Encouraged participants to adopt eco-friendly practices in their daily lives beyond the workshop.","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-11-11","hoursSpent":80,"description":"NSS RVCE, in collaboration with Youth For Seva, is organizing a Paper Bag Making Workshop as part of its initiative to support the Kadale Kayi Parishe and promote sustainable practices.\\n\\nThe workshop aims to address the growing concern of plastic pollution by encouraging the use of eco-friendly paper bags as an alternative to single-use plastics. Participants will be guided step-by-step in creating sturdy paper bags using old newspapers and recyclable paper, transforming waste materials into useful, environmentally responsible products.\\n\\nThrough this hands-on activity, students will gain practical skills in paper bag making while also developing awareness about waste reduction, reuse of materials, and environmental conservation. The paper bags produced during the workshop will be distributed and used during the Kadale Kayi Parishe, helping vendors reduce their dependence on plastic carry bags.\\n\\nThis initiative not only supports a traditional local fair but also reinforces the values of social responsibility, sustainability, and community engagement. By crafting paper bags for a cause, participants actively contribute toward building a cleaner, greener, and more sustainable environment*.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yzmKe-7Wly6jgcgh5nUe5","name":"Fist Full-2024(Rotaract)","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/ca9b7y_CYvNcj-szPqtYd.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/M9CVz84GcdM6uhYhDjTXh.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/S_zCUeqpnOf8rwqAnjqnU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The food donation drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary \\nBangalore Spandana resulted in a substantial and tangible contribution to community welfare. \\nWith the participation of over 1,750 students, the initiative successfully collected more than \\n6,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal. These essential food supplies could support a large \\nnumber of families and communities facing food insecurity, thereby directly addressing basic \\nnutritional needs. The scale of the response demonstrated strong student engagement and reflected the culture of empathy, generosity, and social responsibility fostered at RV College \\nof Engineering.\\nThis initiative clearly illustrates the power of collective action—small individual contributions, \\nwhen combined, can create a massive social impact. It reinforces the idea that meaningful \\nchange does not always require large individual sacrifices, but rather consistent and coordinated \\nefforts. Students involved gained valuable lessons in social responsibility, teamwork, leadership, \\nand community engagement. The drive also highlights how educational institutions can serve \\nas effective platforms for social initiatives, encouraging students to look beyond academics and \\nactively participate in addressing societal challenges such as hunger and food security","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-12","hoursSpent":40,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore \\nSpandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily \\ncollections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total \\namount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative \\nhighlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s \\ndedication to community welfare and solidarity","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DVKI7E8H_XcWqa4u1cexd","name":"Fist Full-2025(Rotaract)","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/Iz5miiD0vjaclR5n3_wKQ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/vhjMlU4_6g_xQw0WlpMcN.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/EK1Q5kL0uIbo6Ch1-3pTz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fistful initiative achieved a significant humanitarian impact through large-scale student \\nparticipation and collective contribution. With 2,146 students donating essential food \\ngrains—either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal—the initiative successfully mobilized substantial \\nresources to support multiple beneficiary institutions. These institutions, which provide daily \\nmeals to children, the elderly, patients, and other disadvantaged groups, were able to strengthen \\ntheir food supply and continue their service more effectively. The initiative directly contributed \\nto food security for vulnerable populations and demonstrated how coordinated student efforts \\ncan translate into meaningful, real-world impactThis initiative highlights the power of collective responsibility and consistency in social service. \\nIt shows that small, individual contributions, when aggregated, can address large societal \\nchallenges such as hunger and nutrition. Participants learned the value of empathy, community \\nengagement, and teamwork, along with the importance of taking initiative to support those in \\nneed. The Fistful initiative also reinforces the role of students and educational communities as \\ncatalysts for social change, proving that structured, well-organized efforts can create sustainable \\nand far-reaching outcomes for society.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-27","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing \\nessential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted \\nin the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions \\nthat serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"J2z8KCvIbPmzlyTCeU1jf","name":"Kannada Habba (PD)","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/hRuEH_AnD-GFaJw2BXflm.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/zM9l1LIGaSrretv1q_AGA.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/44f3deae-b7e1-4c10-b271-f993376e7ed7/DzVm1jdU86bW3ADKkKWEn.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-03","duration":4,"outcomes":"Promoted awareness and appreciation of Kannada language, culture, and heritage among students.\\nEnhanced leadership, teamwork, and organizational skills of the participating students.\\nProvided practical exposure in event management, coordination, communication, and problem-solving*.\\nEncouraged students to actively engage in cultural and co-curricular activities beyond academics.\\nStrengthened a sense of cultural identity, unity, and social responsibility among the student community.\\nSuccessfully organized a large-scale cultural event in a disciplined and professional manner, reflecting the students'' commitment and dedication.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-30","hoursSpent":60,"description":"Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha was organized by Kannada Sangha, R. V. College of Engineering on 04/12/2025 with the objective of promoting Kannada language, culture, literature, and heritage among students.\\n\\nThe event served as a cultural platform to celebrate the richness of Karnataka’s traditions through various performances, literary activities, and stage programs. The Kannada Sangha student team actively participated in planning, coordination, and execution of the event by working across multiple verticals such as Production Design, Operations, Content Creation, Stage Decoration, Discipline Committee, Hospitality, Public Relations, Technical Team, and Media Team.\\n\\nStudents contributed their time and effort in pre-event planning, stage setup, coordination with participants and guests, managing technical arrangements, maintaining discipline, and ensuring smooth conduct of the program. The collective teamwork and disciplined approach of the student volunteers played a crucial role in the successful and well-organized execution of Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:21:22.979821+00', '2026-01-29 19:02:38.008243+00'), ('6ccd36b5-c9df-444c-ac7c-9c7c311e053c', '5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS050","name":"ENAMADI SANATH GNANA YASHWITHA LAKSHMI","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"hRGEzQ2Wjcv28ik1Dqi1g","name":"Project Pustak 2023","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/n6fzsyhN1GvC-weBlaTef.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/eCNj3iSavEBQZkKL6DINR.png"],"endDate":"2023-12-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The dedication and perseverance of the volunteers were instrumental in empowering rural and \\nunderprivileged students, in line with achieving the club’s mission of making a tangible, lasting \\nimpact on society and fostering a sense of global solidarity.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-12-05","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative\\naimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students\\nresiding in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from\\neach compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring\\nand donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The\\ncollected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital\\nresources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\nTo summarize, Project Pustak is a noble initiative aimed to provide\\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rYe8MCNoJmCLG2CHHW06Y","name":"Environmental Day Quiz","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/v0OQXQws2Qcucstb9nJ4K.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/kvPXhsZSc-iQiSOcRjQv1.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QhzaKQCVeRt3Bm8bqu-Pc","name":"Sci-tech Quiz","slNo":3,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FDoee_iXG7C1QV7dIcg7T","name":"SDG Photgraphy","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/yM8KHI54Mhmfgbg5ZcDkr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sgMJe8WuqvUKWgkkpGFFf","name":"Infosys Visit","slNo":5,"place":"Infosys Campus Mysore","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-31","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ogU5B61ENofAVqY1wMrjM","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus Premises","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/aOvJgMbuTVG1Yme_O3ERL.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dcy_px5xRTChlTahZkeFD","name":"Campaign on Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/8COLXwDOIDfaE8OUebe_N.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/DM15Kt7aPJXhssUTfIt8X.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully increased awareness about the importance of voting and democratic \\nparticipation among students. Participants gained a better understanding of India’s electoral \\nsystem and the role of citizens in strengthening democracy. The initiative empowered young \\nvoters to make informed choices while reinforcing responsible and active citizenship.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"NSS RVCE organized “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye”, an online awareness initiative aimed \\nat encouraging young and first-time voters to actively participate in India’s democratic process. \\nThrough the MyGov platform, participants engaged in two key activities—taking the National \\nVoters’ Pledge and completing a quiz on India’s democracy. The event sought to educate students \\nabout their constitutional rights and responsibilities while fostering a sense of civic duty and \\nnational pride among the youth.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/75OImvLDApBWZEs_LL9ka.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"df3PyHkxqmkSHfHOmGCdw","name":"Uptown junk","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/7t79DNK-fxDKA_R0ag52S.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/sFGqrEL33y3cic95pJ-AK.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-14","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TQRMsf2wya0hLXGK5HvTR","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully fostered awareness about physical fitness and social \\nresponsibility among participants.\\nIt contributed directly to supporting educational opportunities for children in need through \\ncollective donations.\\nThe event strengthened community bonding by uniting students, faculty, and the public under \\na shared cause of compassion and change.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Utsarga Marathon, a spirited initiative that brings together fitness, compassion, and social \\nresponsibility. Scheduled for February 4th, 2024, at R V College of Engineering, this marathon is \\nmore than just a run—it is a collective movement towards meaningful change. With the inspiring \\ntheme “Help a Child Change the World”, the event aims to promote health and well-being while \\ncontributing towards the education of underprivileged children. Participants can choose between \\n5 km and 10 km runs, making it accessible to all age groups and fitness levels. By taking part, \\nevery runner becomes a catalyst for hope, proving that small steps taken together can create a \\nlasting impact on society.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/wJS5JmZIAUR4wB895qcAY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"A8hNUpjjPD1yrrfFwPXeG","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/_0fLGbvTov3kfl9AxQqdF.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/imjrv4pLq5NYtuxJQB-NH.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The dedication and perseverance of the volunteers were instrumental in empowering rural and \\nunderprivileged students, in line with achieving the club’s mission of making a tangible, lasting \\nimpact on society and fostering a sense of global solidarity.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-14","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative\\naimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students\\nresiding in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from\\neach compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring\\nand donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The\\ncollected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital\\nresources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\nTo summarize, Project Pustak is a noble initiative aimed to provide\\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zVEdS8yyRgNwrxZdauCAz","name":"India Quiz","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/7t7j8Og-18lrWfZSI6yIi.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1AydglvQ6SFwBNYhMI2BL","name":"Fist-full","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/76oeJd0ookGsmoxF36aaC.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/baicZNOJGD2a2fFGbF0Ku.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event enabled effective collection and distribution of food grains to support \\nvulnerable communities. It promoted social responsibility, empathy, and active student \\nparticipation. The initiative strengthened collaboration between the institution and community \\nservice organizations while creating a lasting social impact","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Fist Full event was a flagship community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club \\nof RVCE under Rotary Bangalore South, with the objective of combating food insecurity and \\nsupporting vulnerable communities. Conducted from 17th to 22nd November 2025, the event \\nencouraged collective social responsibility by involving students in contributing essential food \\ngrains. Each participating student donated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, transforming small \\nindividual contributions into a large-scale humanitarian effort. The initiative was aligned with \\nRotary’s Community Service avenue, specifically focusing on the theme of Fighting Disease \\nthrough nutritional support. A total of 2146 students actively participated, demonstrating \\nstrong student engagement and awareness toward social causes. The collected food grains \\nwere systematically sorted, recorded, and prepared for distribution to ensure transparency and \\neffective utilization","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dWaGcYzN2T3b80IFKsUOx","name":"Police Marshals","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/16dRIMyOHybet8ONtiVVh.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/swRVYEofGQxLKsGjpH8Iy.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"This initiative presents a non-violent, youth-led model of security and governance by fostering \\ncollaboration between educational institutions and law enforcement to combat cybercrime and \\ndrug abuse. It serves as a scalable global example of strengthening civil–police partnerships and \\nbuilding resilient, secure communities. The effort strongly aligns with SDG 16 by reinforcing \\npeace and institutional trust, and supports SDG 3 by promoting youth health and well-being \\nthrough substance abuse prevention.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":0,"description":"A high-profile civic engagement initiative organized collaboratively by NSS RVCE, the \\nBengaluru City Police, and Aarohana Foundation. The event focused on training student \\nvolunteers to become Police Marshals, thereby creating a structured youth force dedicated to \\nsocial responsibility. Key focus areas of the training and subsequent roles include combating \\ndrug abuse and preventing cyber crimes, culminating in a formal Capping Ceremony by the \\nPolice Department to recognize the volunteers as role models.\\nThis event cultivates profound civic responsibility and leadership skills among students by \\nplacing them in a formal partnership with law enforcement. Volunteers gain critical knowledge \\nabout real-world societal threats like cyber crime and drug abuse, making them informed and \\nproactive citizens. Being formally recognized as a Police Marshal elevates their status as positive \\nrole models within the community, encouraging a commitment to public service and safety \\nthroughout their lives.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6qjKoZ0EFPjUFtWtLWXkP","name":"Female Foeticide Awarness Walkathon 2025","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus Premises","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/3W23_JrF7r0HGZ79DHWwI.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/xUFG1MQTmUcKMulkwz9lu.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon effectively raised awareness about female foeticide and gender-based \\ndiscrimination among participants and the wider community. It encouraged meaningful \\ndialogue, inspired collective responsibility, and reinforced the importance of standing against gender injustice. The event fostered social consciousness and strengthened community \\nparticipation toward promoting equality and respect for the girl child.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-14","hoursSpent":0,"description":"On the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a \\nFemale Foeticide Awareness Walkathon to highlight the critical issue of female foeticide and \\npromote the value of the girl child in society. The walkathon began in the early hours of \\nthe morning from the RVCE campus and witnessed the participation of over 350 individuals, \\nincluding students, faculty members, and supportive parents. The event was marked by \\nthought-provoking placards and powerful slogans, creating a strong atmosphere of unity and \\nsocial responsibility while spreading awareness on gender equality and dignity.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/TxyCLT5VNGgMQ84Y0XDZs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"R7msAjvONw2gTl9kzrbRj","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus Premises","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 successfully combined fitness, charity, and community spirit, advancing \\neducational opportunities for needy children and fostering a sense of social commitment among \\nparticipants.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, was a significant event that celebrated \\nhealth, fitness, and charity. Scheduled to take place on April 6, 2025, at RV College of \\nEngineering, this marathon aimed to bring the community together to run for a cause that \\nextends beyond physical activity to making a lasting social impact. The event''s motto, \"Help a \\nChild, Change the World,\" emphasized the marathon’s mission to support educational initiatives \\nfor underprivileged children and transform their futures.\\nParticipants could choose between 5 km and 10 km race categories, with donations contributing \\ndirectly to providing education for children in need. Beyond the physical challenge, the \\nmarathon represented a collective commitment to social responsibility and charity-driven action, \\nmotivating involvement through both fitness and service.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/jYz3NqQ6c5dqRuHyh2ejG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fSOirHYMsN2bF0WEQzQq6","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":16,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/sEJVcmRs2rHhoCChqYfsQ.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5bf80466-3316-4ec7-8c21-0ce4535209b2/G8hRdbl6GJCUy3k-viDxS.png"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced participants’ teamwork, creativity, and strategic thinking \\nthrough diverse, skill-oriented challenges. It provided a dynamic platform for students to \\nshowcase their talents across multiple domains, including problem-solving, social awareness, \\nartistic expression, and digital engagement. Rush Hours 5.0 also strengthened student \\ninteraction and leadership skills, leaving a lasting impact by promoting collaboration, \\ninnovation, and healthy competition among participants.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Rush Hours 5.0 was a five-day interactive event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE from \\n17th to 21st March 2025, aimed at fostering teamwork, creativity, and problem-solving skills \\namong participants. The event brought together over 450 participants who engaged in a series of \\ninnovative and competitive tasks designed to encourage collaboration and healthy competition. \\nEach day featured a unique challenge, ranging from online problem-solving activities to \\ncreative and performance-based tasks, ensuring continuous engagement and enthusiasm. The \\nstructured elimination process added excitement and motivation, culminating in the selection \\nof top-performing teams on the final day.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 14:38:21.371924+00', '2026-02-01 16:55:59.107417+00'), ('6dab2044-c180-4dc0-a305-d0e08ac20086', 'b2635f53-dc76-44a7-8daa-6a05eb0aedc0', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC034","name":"Bhini Singh","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"k92VklPCkhvZfPsWDZa-T","name":"Mega Plantation Drive","slNo":1,"place":"Kanakpura Road","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b2635f53-dc76-44a7-8daa-6a05eb0aedc0/DHgEAk94_CL4DpBmBkvCX.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The Mega Plantation Drive resulted in the successful plantation of a large number of saplings, contributing to increased greenery and a healthier environment. The activity enhanced awareness among participants about environmental protection and the importance of sustainable living practices. Students developed a sense of ownership and responsibility by committing to nurture the planted saplings, ensuring their long-term growth. The drive reinforced the value of community participation in addressing environmental challenges and encouraged continued involvement in eco-friendly initiatives, creating a lasting positive impact on both the environment and the participants.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-25","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Mega Plantation Drive was organized as a large-scale environmental initiative aimed at increasing green cover and promoting ecological sustainability. Students, faculty members, and volunteers actively participated in planting saplings across designated areas . The drive focused on planting native and environment-friendly saplings to ensure better survival and long-term ecological benefits.\\nParticipants were guided on proper planting techniques, soil preparation, and the importance of regular watering and maintenance. The activity emphasized the critical role of trees in improving air quality, conserving biodiversity, preventing soil erosion, and mitigating the effects of climate change. Through collective participation, the plantation drive fostered environmental awareness, teamwork, and a sense of responsibility towards nature. The event highlighted how collective action can contribute meaningfully to environmental conservation and sustainable development, similar in spirit to other eco-centric initiatives documented in the report.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cxRVsJiMUVhNPXaW_vbTq","name":"School Genesis Workshop","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The School Genesis Workshops successfully created awareness and interest in engineering and robotics among school students by providing meaningful exposure to practical STEM concepts. Students demonstrated increased curiosity, engagement, and enthusiasm towards learning through hands-on experimentation and interactive discussions. The program effectively bridged the gap between classroom theory and real-world engineering applications, fostering early technical aptitude and problem-solving skills.\\nFor the student volunteers, the activity enhanced teamwork, leadership, communication, and teaching abilities while reinforcing social responsibility and community engagement. The outreach initiative strengthened the connection between the institution and the local education ecosystem, highlighting the positive impact of student-led technical outreach programs in promoting STEM education and inspiring future innovators.","semester":"4","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The School Genesis Workshops were conducted as part of an outreach initiative by Team Astra Robotics to inspire school students towards engineering, robotics, and STEM education. The workshops were held across five schools in Bengaluru, including VVS Bangalore, MES Kishore Kendra (Malleshwaram), Vidya Mandir Ind PU College (Malleshwaram), St. Claret (Jalahalli), and Base PU College. Each workshop was designed to provide students with an engaging introduction to core engineering concepts such as electronics, embedded systems, automation, and control systems.\\nThe sessions emphasized hands-on learning through live demonstrations, guided experiments, and interactive problem-solving activities that helped students connect theoretical concepts with real-world applications. The workshops were conducted over two days at each school, with sessions lasting approximately seven hours per day. Significant effort was invested in planning, outreach, kit preparation, and coordination to ensure effective delivery of the program. Through these interactive sessions, the initiative aimed to spark curiosity, build foundational technical awareness, and encourage young students to consider careers in engineering and technology, as documented in the official submission.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1wI7dNIUW1ewyooSvKoyw","name":"Fast-Trek 2.0","slNo":3,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"FAST TREK 2.0 witnessed active participation from a large number of students, reflecting strong enthusiasm and engagement in outdoor and social activities. The event promoted physical fitness, mental well-being, and stress relief while encouraging participants to appreciate and protect natural environments. Students developed teamwork, leadership, and discipline through collective trekking and adherence to safety protocols.\\nThe activity also strengthened social bonding among participants and highlighted the value of organizing large-scale events with a focus on environmental awareness and responsible recreation. Overall, FAST TREK 2.0 created a positive impact by blending adventure with social responsibility, leaving participants with a memorable experience and increased awareness of sustainable practices.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"FAST TREK 2.0 was a flagship trekking and social awareness event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th January 2024. The event combined physical activity with environmental consciousness, aiming to promote fitness, teamwork, and respect for nature. The trek was conducted at the scenic Kunti Betta hills, offering participants an opportunity to experience natural landscapes while engaging in a well-organized outdoor activity.\\nParticipants assembled early in the morning and were briefed on safety guidelines, trekking protocols, and environmental responsibility before the commencement of the trek. The event emphasized disciplined participation, safe trekking practices, and collective responsibility towards preserving the natural ecosystem. With enthusiastic involvement from a large number of students, the trek fostered a spirit of unity, adventure, and social engagement. The initiative successfully balanced recreation with awareness, reinforcing the importance of sustainable interaction with nature and community-driven participation.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lsXkFs-lsFc8jjO6z25KF","name":"Vikasit Bharat Quiz","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The activity improved participants’ awareness of India’s development initiatives and governance systems. It enhanced quick decision-making, digital literacy, and general\\nknowledge skills. The quiz motivated students to remain updated on national progress and inspired a sense of responsibility towards contributing to a developed and empowered India.\\n","semester":"","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge was an online knowledge-based competition organized through the MyGov Quiz platform to promote awareness about India’s development goals, government initiatives, and the vision of a progressive and self-reliant nation. The quiz included questions related to national programs, economic growth, social welfare schemes, innovation, and India’s future roadmap. Participants actively engaged in the digital quiz format, testing their general knowledge and understanding of national development efforts.\\nThe activity encouraged students to stay informed about public policies and contribute towards building a knowledgeable and responsible society.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:24:32.868345+00', '2026-01-30 21:36:32.467825+00'), ('6ea74c90-129f-46df-bb2b-b4f72fa07e29', '7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22AS032","name":"Moulik Jain ","period":"2022-2026","department":"Aerospace Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"SW6jt4LuK8l5xHPVRYPcj","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/Zj1WBgFC4FX6uH2qUXOch.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp witnessed an enthusiastic response from students, teachers, and community members. A large number of volunteers willingly donated blood, resulting in the collection of a substantial number of blood units. The event successfully raised awareness about the need for regular blood donation and motivated many participants to take part in similar initiatives in the future. It also fostered values such as compassion, teamwork, and social responsibility among those involved. Overall, the camp made a meaningful contribution to healthcare support and community welfare.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The camp is conducted to collect blood for hospitals and blood banks while also spreading awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. Strict safety protocols are followed, including medical screening, proper hygiene, and the use of sterile equipment to ensure donor safety.\\n\\nDuring the camp, trained medical staff safely collect blood using standardized procedures. Along with the donation process, awareness sessions are conducted to educate participants about how a single blood donation can help save multiple lives and support patients in critical need.\\n\\nThe Blood Donation Camp was organized in collaboration with a local hospital and medical experts who ensured all health and safety measures were maintained. The primary objective was to save lives, encourage social responsibility, and promote the habit of regular blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IV2AKOQrBM2SoyDRgBugm","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/o4waJbZFBb5AjZ86DPFfa.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The project successfully collected and distributed a significant number of books and learning materials to students in government schools. The initiative brought joy and motivation to the children and played a role in increasing their interest and engagement in academics.","semester":"6","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak focused on supporting underprivileged students studying in government schools. As part of this initiative, volunteers and students gathered and distributed books, notebooks, and essential stationery to the children. In addition to material support, engaging and interactive teaching sessions were organized to help students understand basic subjects in an enjoyable and effective manner. The primary objective was to encourage learning, strengthen academic foundations, and build confidence among the children. Overall, Project Pustak, in collaboration with Vision, helped highlight the importance of education and fostered stronger connections between students and the local community.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KWcTueGAg9tNPYW7H8fhT","name":"Fist Full","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/aOLenEXpvXR768cNUmkaT.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"Helps address food insecurity by providing essential food supplies to individuals and communities in need.\\n\\nPromotes a sense of social awareness and compassion among participants.\\n\\nHighlights how consistent small contributions can collectively lead to significant positive change.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"FIST FULL is an annual donation initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE that turns simple everyday contributions into a meaningful social impact. Participants are motivated to save a small portion of rice or toor dal from their daily meals and contribute it towards helping people in need. Through this collective act of kindness, the drive aims to spread happiness and promote a culture of empathy and generosity within the community.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/zZbrlfLXb6iyAZ8Vi6OdR.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MvxneyYwXoi4LUqF8Spta","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/VD119VNvfv3T8zq4j_8oL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp witnessed an enthusiastic response from students, teachers, and community members. A large number of volunteers willingly donated blood, resulting in the collection of a substantial number of blood units. The event successfully raised awareness about the need for regular blood donation and motivated many participants to take part in similar initiatives in the future. It also fostered values such as compassion, teamwork, and social responsibility among those involved. Overall, the camp made a meaningful contribution to healthcare support and community welfare.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The camp is conducted to collect blood for hospitals and blood banks while also spreading awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. Strict safety protocols are followed, including medical screening, proper hygiene, and the use of sterile equipment to ensure donor safety.\\n\\nDuring the camp, trained medical staff safely collect blood using standardized procedures. Along with the donation process, awareness sessions are conducted to educate participants about how a single blood donation can help save multiple lives and support patients in critical need.\\n\\nThe Blood Donation Camp was organized in collaboration with a local hospital and medical experts who ensured all health and safety measures were maintained. Students, faculty members, and individuals from the surrounding community actively took part in the event. The primary objective was to save lives, encourage social responsibility, and promote the habit of regular blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"h8V0iR0U74GTjzXwVrlsi","name":"Hult Prize 2025","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/wEXbwR89B1z9Yomby6wEn.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-18","duration":2,"outcomes":"Helped develop critical skills such as teamwork, leadership, communication, and problem-solving.\\n\\nMotivated students to think creatively about addressing global and societal challenges.\\n\\nRecognized student participation and achievement through eligibility for AICTE activity points.\\n\\nStrengthened the culture of entrepreneurship and social responsibility within the institution.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-01-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Hult Prize 2025 Regionals were conducted on 17th and 18th January 2025, providing a platform for students to present impactful ideas focused on sustainability and social innovation.\\n\\nThe event was organized to promote entrepreneurial thinking, problem-solving skills, and teamwork among students. Participants worked in teams to identify real-world problems and propose scalable solutions aligned with the objectives of the Hult Prize Foundation. Through mentorship, presentations, and evaluations by a panel of judges, students gained valuable exposure to startup culture, innovation, and responsible leadership.","aicteMapping":"E Cell","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/D-0erkLF8q_CLv1oWEoeg.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lHL-OJ75eSj2dd0peresV","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/P8Mvo1lP-j_U8P5Dau2cW.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Promotes empathy and a spirit of service among students and\\nparticipants.\\nStrengthens NSS engagement in impactful social initiatives.\\nContributes to long-term positive change in the lives of children\\nin need.","semester":"4","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"UTSARGA is the flagship marathon of NSS RVCE, organized\\nwith the vision “Help a Child, Change the World.” This initiative\\nstrives to support underprivileged children by promoting access to\\neducation, healthcare, and overall welfare, inspiring collective action\\nfor a brighter future","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fdxv2pQ-sYR-Q2BQctdEu","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7157ddbc-dacd-4914-963e-85cfe6fbdf34/V_FniUI91XSZ16JXDC2J6.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Encourages community participation and social responsibility\\nthrough collective action.\\nPromotes empathy and a spirit of service among students and\\nparticipants.\\nStrengthens NSS engagement in impactful social initiatives.","semester":"6","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"UTSARGA 2025 is the flagship marathon of NSS RVCE, organized\\nwith the vision “Help a Child, Change the World.” This initiative\\nstrives to support underprivileged children by promoting access to\\neducation, healthcare, and overall welfare, inspiring collective action\\nfor a brighter future.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 14:02:41.215003+00', '2026-02-02 07:53:38.530943+00'), ('6ec3c6cb-7999-4958-beff-28f19ef5961a', '643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD047","name":"PUNEETH B","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"2ywjwtvyu73U7ndQaxSm3","name":"FAST TREK 2.0","slNo":1,"place":"KUNAGALU BETTA","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/I8rL68LELM7UuoHF8iLAh.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by\\nactively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense\\nof environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by\\nreporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped\\nimprove my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Kunagal Betta Hills, and it\\nalso enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group of\\nparticipants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved my\\nfitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated to\\npreserving the environment. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus\\nto the trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the\\nadventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all\\nattendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagal Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding\\nsuccess, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750\\nindividuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s\\nvibrant atmosphere","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/Fwt70aqY5oDRfWOca-Wv1.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OcvuSiz5EFE2F6_Efj2Qw","name":"UTSARGA 2024","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/zPggrD1icJV1WzfXFwq1m.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The\\nactivity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and\\ncompleting the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the\\nmarathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on\\npromoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on February 4th, 2024,\\nfrom 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages\\nstudents and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based\\nregistration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create\\nawareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness\\nactivity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community\\nimpact.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/PlGF0gXydSO27M8gmaIcH.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"N-fYRGsT0EtcMx31RS774","name":"PAPER DRIVE","slNo":3,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/PLNXLgfmN8KjoTuRtOG-2.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Paper Drive, I actively contributed to a large-scale\\nresource mobilization effort that benefited multiple charitable organizations. The experience\\nof going door-to-door helped me develop better interpersonal and communication skills while\\ninteracting with diverse residents and business owners. I gained a deeper understanding of\\ncommunity involvement and the practical logistics of managing waste materials for a social\\ncause. This activity also reinforced my commitment to environmental sustainability and social\\nresponsibility. Overall, the initiative provided a meaningful platform to address social issues\\nthrough collective student engagement and volunteerism.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":8,"description":"On 23rd June 2024, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a \"Paper Drive\" involving over\\n400 student volunteers who collected books, papers, and waste materials across various areas\\nof Bangalore. Volunteers started early in the morning, going door-to-door and visiting local\\nbusinesses to gather donations. The primary objective was to collect resources for charities and\\nNGOs to support their initiatives and assist people in need. Beyond resource collection, the\\ndrive served as a community awareness program to foster social responsibility among both the\\nparticipants and the residents of Bangalore","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/T5SU3vO5ZuC06PzP5v5Hn.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BifeBLFPVtPx83w-8KQAG","name":"FIST FULL","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/gQA-duR1okv3k9Y9zQCxH.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in this donation drive, I contributed directly to community\\nwelfare by supporting the collection of essential food items for those in need. I gained a\\nstronger sense of social responsibility and empathy by being part of an initiative that emphasized\\nsolidarity and helping others through collective effort. The activity also helped me understand\\nhow even small individual contributions can lead to large-scale impact when students come\\ntogether for a cause. Overall, this experience strengthened my awareness of community service\\nand reinforced the importance of actively participating in welfare-oriented initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":" In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore\\nSpandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily\\ncollections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total\\namount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative\\nhighlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s\\ndedication to community welfare and solidarity.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/k0LADMxWzUQoDwIOcR22-.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Oo_Bj5LPouPe1Ubv_pudB","name":"CHEELA MELA","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/3BPwWI_b-8BGfV_hKgKLe.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the Eco bag Initiative, I successfully crafted 200 newspaper\\nbags, directly contributing to the reduction of single-use plastic in local markets. This\\nactivity helped me develop a practical understanding of sustainable alternatives and the\\nimportance of community-driven environmental solutions. I gained hands-on experience in\\nmanual crafting and learned how small, collective efforts can lead to a significant social impact.\\nAdditionally, managing the production of a large quantity of bags improved my discipline, time\\nmanagement, and commitment to social service. Overall, the experience strengthened my sense\\nof environmental responsibility and civic duty toward creating a more sustainable community","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Eco bag Initiative, also known as \"Cheela Mela,\" was a sustainability-focused project\\norganized by NSS RVCE in collaboration with EMPRI. The primary goal was to craft newspaper\\nbags to be distributed to street vendors at K R Market, providing a biodegradable alternative to\\nplastic and supporting a greener environment. Participants were tasked with crafting durable\\npaper bags following specific guidelines to ensure they were suitable for commercial use.\\nThe initiative allowed students to contribute to environmental preservation through hands-on\\nvolunteerism, either by crafting bags onsite at the Environment Lab or at home.\\n","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/KaePlbfIKvYsIv5LsiuTm.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"r5NSIAHWvCE9H7TMPEPka","name":"SDG PHOTOGRAPHY","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/bkrrpBkCYTywaA9-BLmv-.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-20","duration":35,"outcomes":"Students developed a better understanding of Sustainable Development Goals and their relevance in daily life. The activity enhanced creative thinking, observation skills, and social awareness among participants. It encouraged students to identify and highlight real-life problems and positive practices related to sustainability. Participants gained awareness of their role as responsible citizens in contributing toward a sustainable future. The activity promoted visual storytelling as an effective tool for spreading awareness and initiating discussions on global challenges.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-16","hoursSpent":8,"description":"As part of the AICTE initiative to promote awareness about the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), a photography activity was conducted to encourage students to observe, understand, and visually document real-world issues related to sustainable development.\\n\\nThe activity aimed to capture photographs that reflect social, environmental, or economic challenges and solutions aligned with one or more SDGs, such as quality education, clean water and sanitation, good health and well-being, sustainable cities, climate action, or responsible consumption.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/Zk9umWIwcdLzBpf1nRVaX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fKNUpd7BFTSJBNjZZt0d9","name":"INDIA QUIZ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/zygV7jXBcTNG_F3058g4b.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"The India Quiz helped students strengthen their general knowledge and awareness about India’s historical and socio-cultural aspects. It improved participants’ critical thinking, recall ability, and teamwork while promoting a sense of national pride and unity. The activity successfully motivated students to stay informed about the nation and contributed to their overall intellectual and personality development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":8,"description":"An India Quiz was conducted in the college with the objective of enhancing students’ knowledge about the country’s history, culture, geography, constitution, scientific achievements, and current affairs. The quiz provided an interactive platform for students to test and expand their understanding of India’s rich heritage and contemporary developments. It encouraged healthy competition and active participation, fostering curiosity and interest in national awareness through a structured and engaging format.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/aiAPr4U1kXcE5DV0ZNwMe.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ighAeWUj1aqxlOsi1Wm5_","name":"HUMAN ELEPHANT CONFLICT","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/GcztGsfX8i5Lq7VqkM3lV.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-02","duration":91,"outcomes":"The session emphasized the importance of coexistence between humans and wildlife,\\nshowcasing how timely alerts, improved safety equipment, and local community involvement\\ncan significantly reduce conflict-related risks. Participants gained a deeper understanding of\\nground-level conservation challenges and the critical role of technology and awareness in\\nwildlife protection. Overall, the activity sensitized students toward environmental responsibility\\nand the need to support initiatives that safeguard both forest personnel and wildlife.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":2,"description":"As part of the Elephant Conflict Mitigation project, NSS RVCE organized an awareness\\nand interaction session in collaboration with the Adavi Alert Foundation (AAF). The session\\nwas conducted by Mr. Pavan Joshi, who provided valuable insights into the growing issue\\nof human–elephant conflict (HEC) in India and the need for sustainable, technology-driven\\nsolutions.\\nDuring the talk, Mr. Pavan Joshi explained the mission and work of the Adavi Alert Foundation,\\nwhich focuses on protecting frontline forest staff and reducing HEC through tactical equipment,\\ndetection technology, and community-based proactive measures. He highlighted key initiatives\\nsuch as the use of early warning and detection systems, distribution of high-power torches and\\nprotective gear, and support extended to anti-poaching camp staff operating in high-risk forest\\nzones.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/uO9wOo4UAjoTH4t-ujAGi.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RuRdHqWwjSwKxV9iqVtvG","name":"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/Gve8mhmhnkOrqk2Uz5Gfb.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, participating students developed a stronger sense of\\nenvironmental responsibility by directly contributing to tree plantation efforts. The initiative\\nincreased awareness about the importance of afforestation and individual actions in combating\\nenvironmental degradation. Students were motivated to adopt sustainable habits and take\\nownership of nurturing the saplings they received. Overall, the drive successfully fostered\\neco-conscious behavior, encouraged community participation, and made a positive contribution\\ntoward environmental sustainability, thereby justifying the allocation of AICTE activity points\\nfor student involvement.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Kannada Sangha, R.V. College of Engineering, organized the community service initiative\\n“Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” to promote environmental awareness and sustainable practices\\namong students. As part of this drive, students who purchased the event T-shirt were provided\\nwith a tree sapling along with clear guidelines on proper planting and care. The distribution\\nof T-shirts and saplings was conducted within the college campus, encouraging students to\\ntake personal responsibility for contributing to a greener environment. The initiative aimed to\\ncombine participation with action by motivating students to actively engage in afforestation and\\nenvironmental conservation.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/s7mz_z548aMRP7cD5jPvk.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2PpERaup3s6d-_wutGDoR","name":"BUILD WITH GEN AI HACKATHON","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/pDDJvjThhm8XGoN3-cFk6.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"The hackathon enhanced students’ technical skills in Generative AI concepts, prompt engineering, and application development while strengthening their problem-solving and teamwork abilities. Participants gained practical experience in building AI-driven solutions and improved their confidence in applying emerging technologies to real-world challenges. The activity inspired innovation, creativity, and an entrepreneurial mindset, aligning students with industry-relevant skills and future technological trends.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The “Build with Gen AI” Hackathon was organized in the college to provide students with hands-on exposure to Generative Artificial Intelligence technologies and their real-world applications. The event encouraged participants to ideate, design, and develop innovative solutions using Gen AI tools and frameworks within a limited time frame. Through teamwork, problem-solving, and mentorship, students explored how generative models can be applied to domains such as healthcare, education, automation, and sustainability, fostering an environment of innovation and collaborative learning.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/KhPtzmBWsn3DNNe5WSyBC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"D5TRzVEyqVaefQNByc5ip","name":"VIKASIT BHARAT QUIZ","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/txQRhoPAK6KqPKbD2QAnM.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Round 1 of the Viksit Bharat Quiz 2024, I gained a clearer\\nunderstanding of India’s key achievements, development initiatives, and long-term vision of\\nbecoming a developed nation by 2047. Attempting the time-bound digital quiz enhanced my\\ngeneral awareness, analytical thinking, and ability to perform accurately under time constraints.\\nThe competitive format helped improve my focus, quick decision-making, and familiarity with\\nnational policies and progress across various sectors.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz 2024 (formally the Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge) was the introductory\\nstage of a national competition designed to engage India’s youth in the vision of a \"Developed\\nIndia\" by 2047. It served as Round 1 of the Viksit Bharat Young Leaders Dialogue, testing\\nknowledge of India’s landmark achievements and progress. Format: A digital, time-bound\\ncontest hosted on the MY Bharat platform. Participants had to answer 10 questions in 300\\nseconds. Engagement: Nearly 20 lakh (1,952,749) participants took part in the challenge.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/qO41YKo5NNcDqygOPeNm-.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XUsbSwoBIgpgxEaI9bUpi","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/ejJluMaOE5My1vHOQJZNQ.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":367,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” initiative, I developed\\na deeper understanding of the democratic process and the significance of voting in shaping the\\nnation’s future. By taking the voter’s pledge and engaging in awareness activities, my sense\\nof civic responsibility and commitment to active citizenship was strengthened. Participation in\\ncreative and digital outreach activities enhanced my communication skills, critical thinking, and\\nconfidence in expressing opinions on national issues. Interacting with peers during discussions\\nand competitions improved my teamwork and collaborative abilities. Overall, this campaign\\ninstilled a strong sense of patriotism, increased my awareness about electoral participation, and\\nmotivated me to responsibly exercise my right to vote as a first-time voter.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Mera Pehla Vote - Desh Ke Liye (My First Vote for the Country) was a nationwide voter\\nawareness campaign launched in early 2024 to encourage youth, particularly first-time voters,\\nto participate in the 18th Lok Sabha Elections. The campaign was a joint effort by the Ministry\\nof Education, the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting, and the Ministry of Youth Affairs,\\nwith endorsement from the Election Commission of India (ECI).\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/ADp9vkUo1WecM1aq7v-ZD.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0BT7Ii7cYXqah97_CpCF8","name":"NASHA MUKT BHARAT","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/okBwrN-LKXnc31yiewvtB.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in this pledge-taking ceremony, I have formally committed to a drug-free\\nlifestyle and gained a deeper understanding of the societal impact of substance abuse. This\\nactivity reinforced my sense of personal and social responsibility toward maintaining a healthy\\nenvironment within the college campus and the broader community. I learned about the\\nsignificance of national health initiatives and how individual commitments contribute to the\\noverall goal of a \"Khushaal Bharat\" (Prosperous India). Overall, the experience instilled a ","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-15","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The \"Nasha Mukta Bharat, Khushaal Bharat\" (Drug-Free India, Prosperous India) initiative was\\nan awareness program organized by NSS RVCE to combat drug abuse among the youth. As\\npart of this national campaign by the Government of India, participants took a formal pledge to\\n\"Say No to Drugs\" and committed to staying away from drug abuse to lead a healthy and sober\\nlifestyle. The activity aimed to create a strong moral stance against substance abuse within the\\nstudent community and promote the values of health, sobriety, and national prosperity","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/643bcfe1-6c0c-4c27-bf2a-ae713850283e/1ZbUYYthOxVz8Wm4Vpb0p.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 07:30:47.097403+00', '2026-02-01 07:33:23.197189+00'), ('6f9b7ca6-3eba-4ff2-8e3f-b8cef434b6f1', '2896c27b-3bed-4ce8-8ebb-124961d1351d', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI060","name":"Varun S","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"BTV0W6R9fM7J3pso6uETF","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE ","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"","hoursSpent":6,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:31:21.117687+00', '2026-01-30 08:31:21.117687+00'), ('707dc600-6a24-49b3-914f-b1198b511a03', '91bc83d0-6dc3-43f4-9e52-c43d0059a3fb', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:58:38.5551+00', '2026-01-30 08:58:39.577671+00'), ('716bee2d-691a-4215-80ca-d9c0d719da4a', '5cb14b00-6c68-4931-9f38-8ab578ac35b2', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 17:26:02.028596+00', '2026-02-01 10:58:25.266038+00'), ('7181b869-84ed-4948-b480-a92040fb35e1', '7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS052","name":"ROHIT SANGAN","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"CgRIcN40zMu3hFhwIYxhh","name":"Utsarga-2024(NSS Marathon)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024 successfully mobilized the student body and local community, \\nraising significant awareness and funds for child welfare while fostering a spirit of health and \\ncollective social responsibility","semester":"","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by NSS RVCE, was a prominent community event held \\non February 4, 2024, at the RV College of Engineering campus. Carrying forward the impactful \\nmotto \"Help a child - Change the world!\", the marathon was designed to promote physical \\nfitness while supporting a vital social cause.\\nParticipants were able to engage in two primary race categories which were the 5km run and \\nthe 10km run","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/LWc1x1hW3HOCaLeUWbKz5.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KP1fSBYDoGQ0FXB6ZtA38","name":"RVCE BADMINTON","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/tsNryA-R5tsYpMTpbLcft.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-07-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Sports play a vital role in college life as they help students maintain physical fitness, reduce academic stress, and develop essential life skills beyond the classroom. Regular participation in sports improves discipline, time management, teamwork, leadership, and resilience, while also boosting confidence and mental well-being.","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-07-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Momentum (RVCE) is the Annual Sports fest organised every year . various top colleges of karnataka are invited . we have been Winning Various titles across the state in different field of sports . We are the runners in VTU SOUTH ZONE conduted in SJBIT college and 3rd place in INTER ZONE held at PES Mandya","aicteMapping":"Volunteering and Organising Comittee","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-QtMLPXJ2qUaXH4DULuwC","name":"GEN-AI HACKATHON","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/78o-IuHMPbiw_xUdKfes4.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/y0XsyJHGwjtbrg_BxNBFf.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of a Gen AI hackathon include hands-on experience with generative AI tools, improved problem-solving and coding skills, stronger teamwork and communication abilities, and a deeper understanding of how AI can be applied to real-world problems. Participants also gain confidence in innovation, exposure to industry-relevant technologies, faster learning under pressure, and valuable experience in presenting ideas and solutions effectively.","semester":"","startDate":"2025-01-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"A Gen AI hackathon provides students with a unique opportunity to explore, build, and innovate using cutting-edge generative artificial intelligence technologies in a collaborative and time-bound environment. It encourages creative problem-solving, hands-on learning, and teamwork as participants design AI-driven solutions for real-world challenges, enhancing their technical skills, critical thinking, and adaptability. The outcome of a Gen AI hackathon is not just functional prototypes, but also improved confidence, exposure to industry-relevant tools, and a mindset of innovation that prepares students for future careers in AI and technology.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/H7ZHEZ9NoBuYdIdin5CjK.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ec5ZLAAZbYcjOl0HST_A1","name":"PAPER BAG ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/CEY4tQbvpwX_TEzPssgGC.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/5YGC5oisZQLIr6KtHBnnL.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/igR7cf7s751g3q5K5fhUf.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Outcomes and Key Takeaways \\nThe Paper Bag Making Initiative achieved notable success both in execution and in impact: \\n1. Massive Plastic Reduction Impact: By distributing approximately 4000 paper bags, \\nthe initiative significantly reduced the use of plastic at one of Bengaluru’s largest \\ntraditional fairs. Many stall owners replaced plastic bags with the distributed paper \\nbags during the fair days. \\n2. Real-World Sustainability in Action: This initiative translated classroom \\nknowledge into real-world impact, giving students a hands-on experience in \\nsustainability, logistics, and social outreach. \\n3. Positive Community Engagement: Local vendors and visitors warmly appreciated \\nthe students'' efforts. The personal interaction during distribution created meaningful \\nconversations around waste reduction. \\n4. Teamwork and Leadership Development: Participants experienced practical \\nproblem-solving, resource management, and teamwork, all within a tight timeline. \\nVolunteers emerged as leaders, managing sessions and on-ground distribution under \\nminimal supervision. \\n5. Recognition and Appreciation: The initiative received acknowledgment from both \\nKadlekai Parishe organizers and visiting dignitaries, setting a benchmark for future \\ncollege-led sustainability efforts at public events. \\n6. Values and Awareness: Students developed a stronger sense of environmental ethics, \\ncivic duty, and proactive citizenship through their involvement. \\n7. Scalable Model: The success of this initiative offers a replicable model for other \\ninstitutions looking to contribute to sustainability through similar grassroots action. \\n8. Points Earned: \\no Organizers: 15 points for every 50 bags made \\no Volunteers: 20 points (full-time), 15 points (part-time)","semester":"","startDate":"2024-11-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"As part of RVCE’s commitment to sustainability and civic responsibility, the Department of \\nISE organized a Paper Bag Making Initiative in November 2024. The activity was aimed at \\nsupporting the iconic Kadlekai Parishe, an annual groundnut fair in Basavanagudi, by \\nreducing the use of single-use plastic through the distribution of handmade paper bags. \\nA total of 97 student participants and 5 dedicated volunteers took part in creating over 4,000 \\neco-friendly paper bags. The initiative involved sourcing recyclable materials, conducting \\norganized bag-making sessions, and finally distributing the bags to vendors and visitors \\nduring the fair. \\nThe effort received recognition from local stall owners and fair organizers, who appreciated \\nthe sustainable alternative. The activity not only raised environmental awareness but also \\nfostered a sense of teamwork, responsibility, and civic engagement among participants.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Environmental Awareness Activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xdRoypKzQvZbi5EuTqc-1","name":"FIST FULL","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/sCjsKb8pGfqHGZDQhb2oG.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/D9wNaqH2yiQsbgn7BVBde.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the Fist Full activity organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE is a meaningful contribution toward reducing hunger and supporting underprivileged communities through collective student effort. It creates a strong sense of social responsibility, empathy, and awareness among participants, showing how small individual contributions can lead to a large social impact. Additionally, the activity strengthens teamwork, leadership, and community engagement among students while reinforcing the values of service, compassion, and sustainable social action.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-27","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fist Full is a community service initiative organised by the Rotaract Club of RVCE (RV College of Engineering) where participants contribute to fighting hunger by donating a “fistful” of staple food items such as rice or toor dal during the event period. The idea is simple but impactful: for every meal prepared, students set aside a portion of food grains and donate it to support those in need. In one recent edition of this drive, the club collected over 6700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal, which were distributed to multiple service organisations to benefit underprivileged communities. Through Fist Full, Rotaractors turn small acts into big impacts by promoting service, empathy, and collective responsibility among students and helping address food insecurity in the community.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"M-FaGWrUneDYGm_xJpBc_","name":"Kannada Sangha T-Shirt","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/jECRREDyjC7euLElXWpGO.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/jTPYpEn7jV9ugzCnDbuFb.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity created a positive and memorable experience for the children, bringing joy and encouragement to their daily lives. For the students, it fostered empathy, social responsibility, and awareness of societal challenges. It also helped develop teamwork, compassion, and a strong commitment to contributing meaningfully to the community.","semester":"","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The community service activity organized by Kannada Sangha involved a group of students visiting Prajakirana Seva Charitable Orphan Ashram at Kumbalagodu, Bengaluru. During the visit, students interacted closely with the children through engaging activities and extended support through donations. The initiative aimed to provide emotional support, care, and happiness while understanding the needs of underprivileged children.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ci2wz0tMx5giRZO5mONOf","name":"DATA - REMIX HACKATHON","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/2lO1VNkIDNCWs6z1_--Vj.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/lzKDabQE9Zs77U-na5DgP.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event enhanced students’ practical understanding of data analytics, visualization, and sustainable business innovation while encouraging teamwork and critical thinking. Participants gained exposure to real-world datasets, industry interaction, and expert evaluation, boosting their confidence and presentation skills. Overall, the activity promoted a holistic mindset by integrating technological advancement with sustainability and innovation.","semester":"","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"DHI Day, organized by Team DHI, the technical club initiative of the Department of AIML at RVCE, featured the event “Data Remix” in collaboration with GE Healthcare. The event focused on data analysis and business innovation, where student teams worked on real-world datasets to perform data analysis, visualization, and problem-solving across multiple phases. It included expert judging, sustainable development–oriented problem statements, and final presentations, providing students with a comprehensive technical and innovation-driven learning experience.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"52rR4ieCDJZMw_XU81kcD","name":"ANTI DRUG CERTIFICATE","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/KrW2pQ74VswOjoBo_Z08v.jpeg"],"endDate":"2022-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity helped create awareness among students about the physical, mental, and social consequences of drug abuse. It encouraged responsible behavior, self-discipline, and a strong commitment to staying drug-free. Overall, the initiative reinforced positive values, social responsibility, and conscious decision-making for a healthier future.","semester":"","startDate":"2022-01-13","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Drug Awareness activity was conducted as part of the AICTE initiative in association with the Narcotics Control Bureau under the theme “Say Yes to Life, No to Drugs.” Students participated by taking an official pledge against drug abuse and completing the required awareness certification process. The activity aimed to educate students about the harmful effects of drug use and promote a healthy, drug-free lifestyle.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/5fvVq89ttpsaoOaSSgeOh.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yBipgD3zoQJrPGGo1LS2j","name":"DESH KA VOTE","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/0IOGXyqnjQUinkryioy1z.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/NEe3KfnIMLSzIJrIWGXV1.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced students’ awareness of civic responsibility and encouraged conscious participation in democratic and social initiatives. It helped reinforce values such as responsibility, awareness, and informed citizenship. Overall, the initiative motivated students to actively engage in nation-building efforts while developing a sense of accountability and social commitment.","semester":"","startDate":"2024-03-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The E-Pledge and E-Quiz activity was conducted as part of a national awareness initiative to promote responsible citizenship and active participation in democratic processes. Students participated by taking an official pledge and completing an online quiz through a Google Form, followed by submitting the required e-certificates. The activity aimed to create awareness about civic duties, informed decision-making, and the importance of active involvement in national initiatives.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lqCfVuOfsUPNcyvInIzYi","name":"FIST FULL 1","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/lraFPfcsdhyu_3jRf-02N.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/9n3J6fBay9HskkFjFj3vD.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the Fist Full activity organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE is a \\nmeaningful contribution toward reducing hunger and supporting underprivileged communities \\nthrough collective student effort. It creates a strong sense of social responsibility, empathy, \\nand awareness among participants, showing how small individual contributions can lead \\nto a large social impact. Additionally, the activity strengthens teamwork, leadership, and \\ncommunity engagement among students while reinforcing the values of service, compassion, \\nand sustainable social action.","semester":"","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fist Full is a community service initiative organised by the Rotaract Club of RVCE (RV College \\nof Engineering) where participants contribute to fighting hunger by donating a “fistful” of staple \\nfood items such as rice or toor dal during the event period. The idea is simple but impactful: \\nfor every meal prepared, students set aside a portion of food grains and donate it to support \\nthose in need. In one recent edition of this drive, the club collected over 6700 kg of rice \\nand 800 kg of toor dal, which were distributed to multiple service organisations to benefit \\nunderprivileged communities. Through Fist Full, Rotaractors turn small acts into big impacts by \\npromoting service, empathy, and collective responsibility among students and helping address \\nfood insecurity in the community.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uUurYuBBAr3NX_Lv3Oza0","name":"Kannda Sangha Tshirt","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/8sF568t5cI0Z4t8-naeck.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-10","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity created a positive and memorable experience for the children, bringing joy and \\nencouragement to their daily lives. For the students, it fostered empathy, social responsibility, \\nand awareness of societal challenges. It also helped develop teamwork, compassion, and a strong \\ncommitment to contributing meaningfully to the community","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-06-10","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The community service activity organized by Kannada Sangha involved a group of students \\nvisiting Prajakirana Seva Charitable Orphan Ashram at Kumbalagodu, Bengaluru. During the \\nvisit, students interacted closely with the children through engaging activities and extended \\nsupport through donations. The initiative aimed to provide emotional support, care, and \\nhappiness while understanding the needs of underprivileged children.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XB-NFGSo5_7ir8wf5m5Tf","name":"Rashtriya Ekta Diwas essay and slogan writing","slNo":12,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/Xb2G7WgRzCVTOHVPN7tCy.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-10-31","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Rashtriya Ekta Diwas event successfully instilled a sense of national pride and unity among \\nthe students, encouraging them to reflect on the foundational leadership of Sardar Patel while \\nrewarding their participation with two AICTE activity points.","semester":"","startDate":"2023-10-31","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rashtriya Ekta Diwas (National Unity Day) celebrations, organized by NSS RVCE, were \\nheld on October 31st to commemorate the birth anniversary of Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel, the \\n\"Iron Man of India\". The event, centered on the theme of national integration, took place from \\n2:30 PM to 4:00 PM in the Environment Engineering Lab of the Civil Engineering Department.\\nThe primary activity was an Essay and Slogan Writing competition, where participants were \\nrequired to write a catchy, impactful slogan alongside an essay of up to 1000 words. To ensure \\nauthenticity and traditional engagement, all submissions were handwritten on A4 sheets within \\na 1.5-hour time limit, with the use of electronic gadgets strictly prohibited","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"arR51wIiJqnbtZzvW5179","name":"Science, Space and Technology Essay Competition","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7a2fcf73-139a-4406-9869-5f6c1b718fab/aMiCPsvbrUpyjLpB7eaaT.png"],"endDate":"2023-09-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Science, Space, and Technology Essay Competition successfully promoted technical \\nliteracy and national pride by providing a platform for students to analyze India''s lunar \\nachievements and future space endeavors, reinforcing the importance of aerospace innovation \\nin sustainable development.","semester":"","startDate":"2023-09-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Science, Space, and Technology Essay Competition was an initiative organized by NSS \\nRVCE in August 2023 to encourage intellectual engagement with India''s expanding role in \\naerospace. The competition invited participants to submit essays by September 1st, 2023, \\nfocusing on the theme of space exploration and its ethical or developmental implications. \\nTo ensure a high standard of academic rigor, the event enforced strict formatting guidelines, \\nincluding a 1000-word limit and a requirement for original, non-plagiarized content","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:56:29.209991+00', '2026-02-01 19:28:28.072308+00'), ('73bceaa4-5490-4053-9b32-fac5ad749765', '8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CH036","name":"Smitha Royals G R","period":"2022-2026","department":"Chemical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"re8Q4WGLkoHLKTGYBzPa0","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":1,"place":"Government High  School at Bidadi","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-08-06","duration":75,"outcomes":"Project Pustak significantly improves rural education by reducing the financial burden on families and boosting student enrollment. By providing essential supplies like textbooks and backpacks, the initiative enhances student confidence and academic performance, ultimately narrowing the urban-rural divide and empowering the next generation with the tools necessary for long-term success","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":20,"description":"Project Pustak is an inspiring initiative dedicated to equipping underprivileged students in rural areas with essential school supplies, fostering a conducive learning environment. Spearheaded by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in partnership with the Pranay Foundation, funds were raised through generous contributions of ₹100 or ₹250 from donors. The second phase of the project, executed in Devanahalli and Bidadi, Karnataka, saw faculty members and volunteers actively distributing educational materials such as textbooks, stationery, and backpacks. This effort, widely recognized for its impact, gained significant media attention, underscoring its transformative role in empowering underprivileged children and enhancing educational opportunities in the region.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/_xJhAduMWOQZn33c9md3X.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RHUAGcurBNwt6hVctkCWJ","name":"Graduation Day volunteering ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/uNeSxx5P96L_iynAJALdz.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-08-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating as a SPARK volunteer for the 14th Graduation Day facilitated the development of essential leadership and logistical skills. I mastered crowd and queue management in a high-pressure environment, ensuring the event’s success. This experience enhanced my professional communication while contributing to a significant institutional milestone.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-03","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The 14th Graduation Day at RV College of Engineering was a prestigious ceremony held on August 3, 2024, to honor the hard work and academic excellence of the graduating batch. Serving as a SPARK volunteer, I was integral to the event''s execution, focusing on professional crowd and queue management. These responsibilities were critical for maintaining order during such a high-profile milestone. The experience enhanced my ability to handle logistical challenges effectively while contributing to a seamless and celebratory atmosphere for students and their families.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to RV college of engineering ","pointsEarned":16,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/PPGd0SjbWJM6xBnf9OoHZ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oWOloPjphqFu-9qUdgfpl","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/eW-60JZbE0Z7C2-GdkrnV.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-04-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of this initiative are deeply impactful, as the proceeds are channeled into providing scholarships and essential medical aid for underprivileged children and those with specialized health conditions. By mobilizing thousands of participants, the event fosters a strong sense of social responsibility and empathy among the youth, creating a ripple effect of awareness regarding rural education and healthcare gaps. Ultimately, the marathon succeeds in transforming physical activity into tangible social change, empowering vulnerable children with the resources necessary for a brighter, more equitable future.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-04-02","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is a signature philanthropic event organized by the NSS unit of RVCE, aimed at uniting the community through the spirit of fitness and social service. Guided by the powerful motto, \"Help a Child—Change the World,\" the marathon serves as a high-energy platform where students, faculty, and professional runners participate in 5K and 10K events. Beyond the race itself, the marathon acts as a major fundraising vehicle designed to support marginalized communities, particularly focusing on child welfare, education, and healthcare initiatives for those in need.","aicteMapping":"Participated in utsarga marathon","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/CjxfUJDzBT2CYeib-Qyqi.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mLXPW2YMeD0VDsoMJvovx","name":"Treasure Hunt","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of the Treasure Hunt was the cultivation of critical soft skills, as the multi-round format required teams to demonstrate exceptional speed, accuracy, and quick decision-making under pressure. By navigating complex riddles and campus-wide physical challenges, participants significantly enhanced their collaborative problem-solving and logical reasoning abilities. Furthermore, the event successfully fostered a high level of student engagement and campus spirit, bringing together 360 students for a unique experiential learning activity that balanced competitive play with thematic entertainment.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-16","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Treasure Hunt – Squid Game Edition was a dynamic, multi-round competition that engaged 120 teams of three members each in a day of logic and physical challenges. Organized by the club Raag and inaugurated by its President, Utkarsh Nijhawan, the event began with an online preliminary quiz focused on logic and theme-based questions to shortlist participants for the on-campus stages. From there, 60 participants moved into the core Treasure Hunt, which featured five sub-rounds spread across the campus involving riddles and clue-chasing. The competition intensified as 20 teams were tasked with collecting 20 unique items under tight time constraints, leading to a final Squid Game-themed round for the top 7 teams to determine the winners.","aicteMapping":"Participated in treasure hunt","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/BGC-1nhW-YXjQslIAsswd.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"baN_7VIzVFV-305kkMP2T","name":"Treasure Hunt ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-01-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The events successfully sparked heightened awareness and knowledge regarding eco-friendly solutions among the participants. Students significantly enhanced their problem-solving skills, creativity, and resourcefulness by applying their knowledge in dynamic settings. The competitive structure of these hunts also fostered a practical understanding of sustainability and required participants to demonstrate speed, accuracy, and quick decision-making under pressure.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-01-25","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The first round of the Treasure Hunt event centered on Sustainable Technologies concluded successfully, sparking heightened awareness and knowledge about eco-friendly solutions. The second round, a Hunt using clues, challenged teams to apply their knowledge in a dynamic setting, enhancing problem-solving skills. In the third round, \"Beg, Borrow, Steal,\" students demonstrated creativity and resourcefulness by finding sustainable solutions and procuring necessary items, fostering a practical understanding of sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Participated in Treasure hunt","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/QHJjDGzbo2TL8L89GaBaX.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Q0zSWhRImRN9FlhbHR9FL","name":"Azadi ka kalothsav","slNo":6,"place":"Manikshaw parade ground","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/l_BXAP1IO9rRg3V97yXXg.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/mnaMc3EVhvW5S9sRAq22I.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-08-15","duration":32,"outcomes":"The outcomes of this grand event were multifaceted, primarily fostering a profound sense of national unity and civic pride among the 10,000 spectators in attendance. By integrating large-scale student performances, the festival successfully empowered the youth, providing them with a prestigious stage to engage with national history and the spirit of \"Azadi\". Additionally, the event achieved significant social impact by publicly honoring the families of organ donors, thereby raising community awareness for humanitarian causes alongside traditional patriotic celebrations","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"he Azadi Ka Kalothsav (often associated with the broader Amrit Kalotsav or national cultural festivals) held at the Manekshaw Parade Ground in 2024 served as a massive platform for patriotic expression and cultural heritage. The event was characterized by a grand ceremonial parade featuring approximately 35 contingents and over 1,150 members from various divisions, including the Indian Army, Air Force, and the Karnataka State Police. A major highlight of the celebration was the synchronized performance by over 750 students in a program titled \"Jayabharathi,\" alongside a specialized showcase by 400 children that highlighted regional social schemes and historical milestones. The atmosphere was further energized by high-skill displays, such as Mallakhamb by the Maratha Light Infantry and daring motorcycle stunts performed by the Corps of Military Police.","aicteMapping":"Participated in azadi ka kalothsav","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ifZE5r0XZpIQ2noNYdU_a","name":"Environmental Quiz","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/5aXkfnpHbr0bAlhAfFdfm.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Environmental Day Quiz, organized by the students of SPARK, the IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter, was a well-planned initiative aimed at promoting environmental awareness among students. The event was designed to engage participants through questions covering topics like climate change, conservation, and sustainable practices. This ensured the quiz not only tested knowledge but also encouraged students to reflect on global environmental challenges.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Environmental Day Quiz, organized by the students of SPARK, the IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter, was a well-planned initiative aimed at promoting environmental awareness among students. The event was designed to engage participants through questions covering topics like climate change, conservation, and sustainable practices. This ensured the quiz not only tested knowledge but also encouraged students to reflect on global environmental challenges.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/inI1H3ek7Ecr6PTwyD2bT.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TCyFcFnGs7B9Rg2UBNQow","name":"Industry visit to RTPS and YTPS","slNo":8,"place":"Raichur","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/VNIxeol_ZU7XZE7EfZZfl.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-02","duration":4,"outcomes":"The visit successfully bridged the gap between academic knowledge and practical applications, aligning with AICTE’s emphasis on industry-academia collaboration. Students attained a comprehensive understanding of industrial scale operations and thermal technology, which is essential for professional skill development. Participation also allowed students to earn AICTE Activity Points, acknowledging their proactive efforts in experiential learning.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-29","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The industrial visit to Raichur and Yeramarus Thermal Power Station, organized by students of SPARK, the IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter, was an educational initiative with significant learning outcomes. The students thoroughly planned the visit and actively involved themselves in contributing to its success and the attainment of its true potential. This event provided students with a firsthand experience of the practical aspects of power generation, offering insights into the functioning, technology, and operations of thermal power plants.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/UB37iAeqK-NqPKxVTlDj9.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ut7U1D6hcjFNittDSFpm5","name":"Through the eyes of youth- SDG","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/aoavtJwzEOhg1rVp0a06T.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":16,"outcomes":"The competition surpassed expectations and became a resounding success, thanks to the incredible contributions from talented participants. The entries not only showcased the artistic skills of the youth but also conveyed their deep passion for addressing the global challenges encapsulated by the SDGs. Each submitted photograph resonated with a compelling narrative, highlighting the power of visual storytelling.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-04","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter successfully organized Through the Eyes of Youth, an SDG-themed photo competition, from 7th to 13th August 2023, with enthusiastic participation from approximately 330 students, including 289 students from RV College of Engineering. The event aimed to engage young minds in exploring and creatively expressing their perspectives on the United Nations’ Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through photography. The competition encouraged participants to use the power of visual storytelling to highlight critical global challenges and inspire meaningful change. The top 25 participants advanced to the final round, where 8 participants received Special Mention awards, and the top 3 winners were announced during the closing ceremony on 19th August 2023.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8b3bd5b5-f572-40c7-9cdc-5f3a4f989ac8/59JMQJ1rE5SBw1bPcH_lQ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 16:55:58.993359+00', '2026-01-30 17:42:15.385527+00'), ('749945d7-5feb-4be8-9c57-03df95f2e27e', 'f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC067","name":"Harshit Thakkar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"2MxQMbLuZB-fK-KC7EN8l","name":"Paper Drive 2023","slNo":1,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/zzNL4VjMqh0SAvCsuL6LL.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event achieved substantial outcomes, witnessing overwhelming support from over 500 volunteers who participated in the drive. Through their dedicated efforts, the team managed to collect more than 7 tonnes of newspapers in just over 9 hours. The collected materials were sold to paper vendors to raise funds, and the proceeds were subsequently donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation to support its welfare activities","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Paper Drive was a significant event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on June 24, 2023, in Bengaluru. Functioning under the avenue of Community Services with a focus on Economic and Community Development, the initiative was designed to support orphanages and underprivileged individuals. To execute this, volunteers assembled at Kriyakalpa, RVCE at 8:00 AM before traveling by bus to various localities across the city to collect a wide variety of paper materials, including old newspapers, books, magazines, and waste paper","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/YGwSVYl3Hpa5bDJN2qcf2.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GO20RBiPIRDljkvC7rB1a","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/mtXq1vZ012flhW6jMQYps.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the NSS Utsarga Marathon was very positive, with a large turnout of participants who successfully raised awareness about social causes and community well-being. The event strengthened teamwork, encouraged a culture of fitness and social responsibility, and inspired many students to take part in future NSS initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon was organized to promote health, fitness, and social responsibility among students and staff. The event saw enthusiastic participation, spreading awareness about community welfare causes while fostering unity and a spirit of service among the participants.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/djd6fthw93hPQZKJvxLsl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9ooBcRvpGRVUmkYn4iiAj","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/TP_Pl7lw2-g6lHlAHpasw.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"these drives resulted in the collection of nearly 1,000 units of blood in a single academic year, making a tangible, life-saving impact on the community and supporting multiple hospitals in Bengaluru.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp is a flagship initiative of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, organized to address the critical shortage of blood units in the region and foster a spirit of civic responsibility among youth.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/XgtcjC9BUOsgtJ3WuiBHD.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9Lr4aFtlnR0IkNIaJ-5Wt","name":"School Genesis Workshops ","slNo":4,"place":"VVS, Bangalore ; MES Kishore Kendra, Malleshwaram, Bangalore ; Vidya Mandir Ind PU College, Malleshwaram, Bangalore ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/SvbWidJOcAGtKklSxn9Y3.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-08-24","duration":8,"outcomes":"Through this outreach, we aimed to bridge the gap between theoretical learning and practical application, fostering an early appreciation for engineering and robotics. The dedication of our team extended beyond the workshop days, with significant hours spent in planning, kit preparation, and ensuring a smooth execution.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-17","hoursSpent":60,"description":"Each workshop was structured to provide a comprehensive introduction to core engineering concepts, including electronics, embedded systems, automation, and control systems. Our team engaged students with practical demnonstrations, guided  xperiments, and problem-solving exercises designed to stimulate interest in STEM fields. The sessions spanned 7 hours per day for\\n2 days at each school, with multiple weeks of planning, outreach, and preparation.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/06C-XnW3a9-3XykUwgmcb.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oVPeLl09O3YF-FgGgScqe","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/-lZZsEB9GZ6p1HBiy5Nun.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The outcome was overwhelming, with over 1,750 students participating in the drive. Together, they collected more than 6,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal. This massive contribution was recognized widely, earning the club awards for \"Most Impactful Initiative\" and \"Best Flagship Project\".","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fist Full was a major community initiative held from November 15th to November 29th, 2024, in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana. The project was designed to combat hunger by encouraging students to donate specific food staples—either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal—with daily collection drives organized in the Civil Department.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/jIlnY7hLFK_VhnZiE6fV8.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5Q6tJhE38Zk5xjBS8JBPr","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":6,"place":"Narayangiri Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/vGwFcAMB9FBr2jS6Pmvqv.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event was a massive success, bringing together over 500 participants. Beyond the environmental impact of cleaning the trekking route, the event fostered strong team bonding and camaraderie among the students, blending adventure with a meaningful lesson in eco-consciousness.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fast Trek 3.0 took place on January 12, 2025, at the scenic Narayangiri Hills. As the club''s \"biggest flagship event,\" it combined an adventurous trek with a social cause, focusing on environmental responsibility through a cleanliness drive. Participants trekked through rugged trails while actively collecting litter to preserve the natural beauty of the hills.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/mOyebijfuGOd_Io7s_heK.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nthfyYQcQtjBVTjqp2wcN","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/OG6H1vvkbAy-iSrj4pCoj.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"From the funds collected via donations in the first phase, the supplies were distributed to the underprivileged students.\\nA total of 24,000 notebooks, 3250 stationary kits and 2250 geometry boxes formulated into 5500 kits were distributed across 12 schools in different locations.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Phase-1 focused on raising funds from college students, and the response was overwhelming. The club successfully raised a remarkable sum of ₹3,50,000 from contributions by 1,022 students during this phase, showcasing the spirit of generosity and collective action within the RVCE community. The funds collected will be used in Phase-2 of the project, scheduled for the coming months, which will involve the distribution of stationery kits and books to children in government schools. The project reflects the club’s commitment to promoting education and reducing resource gaps for students in need.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/ZK8o5oFOVoZYj01yq_Iu9.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gQmSD_tCu29tbnCo8ehpy","name":"School Genesis Workshop conducted at St. Clarets.","slNo":8,"place":"St. Claret","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/6QpVUuhTZVxWuO-W2723l.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-10-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this outreach, we aimed to bridge the gap between theoretical learning and practical application, fostering an early appreciation for engineering and robotics. The dedication of our team extended beyond the workshop days, with significant ours spent in planning, kit preparation, and ensuring a smooth execution.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Team Astra Robotics successfully conducted aworkshop at St Clarets on 25th of October between 9 AM and 5:30 PM. Including the several hours before the event to prepare amounts to 15+ hours of work in total. The workshop was structured to proide a comprehensive introduction to core engineering concepts, including electronics, embedded systems, automation, and control systems.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/uGaffweViH97H98Rprds3.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fWQxaIT3s3wOe5Pi0zTng","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/SkFxOfABoctT5rQrmhEBd.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"these drives resulted in the collection of nearly 1,000 units of blood in a single academic year, making a tangible, life-saving impact on the community and supporting multiple hospitals in Bengaluru.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp is a flagship initiative of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, organized to address the critical shortage of blood units in the region and foster a spirit of civic responsibility among youth.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/MMZsftvLs6LooS37g4Mum.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tWEgytosuvGA51kKChcth","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/_8dRsO3uF3pv1ZQaq7NqN.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":19,"outcomes":"The outcome was overwhelming, with over 1,750 students participating in the drive. Together, they collected more than 5000 kg of rice and 900 kg of toor dal. ","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-03","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fist Full was a major community initiative held from November 3rd to November 11th, 2024, in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana. The project was designed to combat hunger by encouraging students to donate specific food staples—either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal—with daily collection drives organized in the Civil Department.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f549e20d-c936-43fc-8f70-536615194b80/dukdqNsOT_7QlWCI2fwDH.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Sujatha D Badiger","designation":"Assistant Professor "},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 20:03:47.779613+00', '2026-01-31 07:07:13.669513+00'), ('74f0aa45-d62f-4f6e-b2bb-bdb52c410de8', 'de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC066","name":"Harshit Srinivasa","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"wKktxj_nYhHvNtQVZKa9e","name":"Lakshya 2025","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/D07SpY_-1rBi_iU380UC8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-27","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event was open to all students, irrespective of prior experience, encouraging inclusivity and active participation. Lakshya focused on improving focus, discipline, confidence, and goal-oriented thinking, aligning with the core values of NCC. Participants were motivated to test their abilities, sharpen their aim, and challenge themselves in a structured and supportive environment.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The event was open to all students, irrespective of prior experience, encouraging inclusivity and active participation. Lakshya focused on improving focus, discipline, confidence, and goal-oriented thinking, aligning with the core values of NCC. Participants were motivated to test their abilities, sharpen their aim, and challenge themselves in a structured and supportive environment.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/Qbacc7USg8oE0QkRu6Atc.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t1Je-vattlpCDgvtY9td9","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/86qeARCtMhxZr2vEljzRK.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"* Project Pustak creates meaningful change by channeling \\ndonations into impactful support for underserved \\ncommunities. Through the distribution of essentials like \\nfood, clothing, and educational resources, it fosters hope and \\nempowerment. \\n* The initiative emphasizes collective effort and compassion,\\npaving the way for a more inclusive and supportive society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-14","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Rotaract Club of RVCE organized Project Pustak, a charitable \\ninitiative focused on uplifting underserved and vulnerable \\ncommunities through meaningful donations and organized \\nresource-sharing. The main objective of the project is to provide \\ntimely support to people who lack access to basic necessities and to ensure that essential resources reach those who need them the most.Under Project Pustak, the club actively collects and distributes a wide range of items such as food supplies, clothes, footwear, blankets, stationery, books, educational materials, hygiene kits, and basic healthcare essentials.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/kups854FCfzqJcq4wZhpk.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ldJihqSnC71aG1XEfbRhz","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/HkU-U4gp1RWqH4q1n-sIQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-25","duration":2,"outcomes":"Project Pustak creates meaningful change by channelling \\ndonations into impactful support for underserved communities. \\nThrough the distribution of essentials like food, clothing, and \\neducational resources, it fosters hope and empowerment.\\nThe initiative emphasizes collective effort and compassion,\\npaving the way for a more inclusive and supportive society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":6,"description":"ROTRACT, RVCE organized the PROJECT PUSTAK, Project \\nPustak is a charitable initiative dedicated to uplifting underservedcommunities through donations and resource-sharing. By providing essentials like food, clothing, education materials, and healthcare supplies, the project aims to bring hope and relief to those in need. Rooted in compassion and collective effort, Pustak inspires individuals to contribute towards building a more inclusive and supportive society.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/8wgkjC5R7AAXuPajzDE8e.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IT8wpaA4X44IskyNSHVOt","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/TGo1-jGJsV7I5OGll8HLB.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The online awareness event engaged young voters, resulting in participants taking a formal pledge to exercise their democratic rights and encourage others to build a \"New India\".","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"An Online Event organized by NSS RVCE with a focus on engaging young and aspiring voters.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/d5h_OxBwo5vHx5LKhY0TQ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Yfo5Dwc810WgT7JsoBKpg","name":"Fistfull 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/6bzVePISR3UNYBH4Rrq16.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-18","duration":31,"outcomes":"This large-scale hunger combat initiative successfully collected over 5,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal from students to support community welfare and solidarity.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-09-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The “Fist Full” initiative by Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana encouraged students to donate rice or toor dal to support hunger relief. The drive collected significant contributions, highlighting student solidarity and RVCE’s commitment to community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/EE62RbbQCKlS_xR74oScB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"R_P7RxtVQQGHvKy5lFWQl","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/Fuja-bv2VLcYY0UMIyifW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"This large-scale hunger combat initiative successfully collected over 5,700 kg of rice and 800 \\nkg of toor dal from students to support community welfare and solidarity.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The “Fist Full” initiative by Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore \\nSpandana encouraged students to donate rice or toor dal to support hunger relief. The drive \\ncollected significant contributions, highlighting student solidarity and RVCE’s commitment to \\ncommunity welfare.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de32e236-9b2b-4071-bc1c-08f8a0ea4cba/NI-R8DG7jIhVPWqKgz5D2.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 06:34:58.101586+00', '2026-02-02 08:24:08.6584+00'), ('753991ca-7650-48cd-ac8d-476f3c3ca94b', '4b562559-9fac-4a28-8520-2e4702a80358', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 04:43:23.795681+00', '2026-02-01 08:07:15.436401+00'), ('75b6a55c-0598-4e64-8865-b080af9804a4', '9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI027","name":"Kushagra Chaturvedi","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"FsifRSNxCU-VvUMBcgdP-","name":"Anti-ragging skit for AICTE New Delhi","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/inC3MVb6iaH8Xrj0SmKso.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-09-18","duration":2,"outcomes":"The activity had a significant impact on the participants, fostering a strong sense of social responsibility and ethical conduct. By conceptualizing and performing a skit centered on anti-ragging, the students effectively communicated the psychological and legal consequences of ragging, promoting a safer and more inclusive campus environment. It promoted teamwork and collaboration, with members working closely to script, direct, and edit the video content for submission to AICTE. The initiative also sharpened communication and digital literacy skills, making the project a holistic learning experience that combined creative expression with a powerful message of empathy and student safety.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-09-17","hoursSpent":6,"description":"I actively participated in a social awareness initiative organized by the CARV team in compliance with AICTE New Delhi mandates. Our group conceptualized, scripted, and performed a video skit focused on the critical theme of Anti-Ragging to promote a safer campus environment. The project involved collaborative efforts in acting and production to effectively communicate the legal and ethical consequences of ragging. The finalized video was successfully submitted and uploaded to the official AICTE website as a student welfare resource. This creative activity required 2 hours of dedicated participation, contributing to institutional efforts in fostering a respectful and inclusive college culture","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/bncNasupKxpj_qGo1S6bk.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nCOcIZDLSHcRHOTrMht0t","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/C3Zc0nOWbi2xoc6iby5Uq.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"The outcome of Project Pustak was multidimensional, successfully combining social service with environmental responsibility. The drive resulted in the donation of a significant number of books to government schools, directly empowering students with the resources needed for their academic growth. The initiative also promoted sustainability by recycling scrap paper, the proceeds of which were utilized to purchase new stationery for the beneficiaries. For the volunteers, the event fostered strong organizational and teamwork skills while instilling a deep sense of empathy and community responsibility, making it a holistic service-learning experience. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 is a flagship literacy and sustainability initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to bridge the educational gap for underprivileged students. The activity involved a massive collection drive where volunteers gathered used textbooks, novels, and unused stationery from students and faculty members across the campus. Following the collection, the team engaged in a rigorous segregation process, sorting books by subject and grade, while identifying unusable paper for recycling. The usable resources were then packaged and distributed to government schools and orphanages, ensuring that quality educational materials reached those who needed them most.\\nThe usable books were packaged for distribution to government schools and orphanages, directly supporting underprivileged students who lack access to quality study materials. Simultaneously, the project enforced a \"zero-waste\" policy by identifying scrap paper and cardboard for recycling. The funds generated from selling this scrap were creatively reinvested to purchase brand-new stationery kits—including notebooks, pens, and geometry boxes—which were donated alongside the books. This initiative not only provided essential academic resources but also fostered a culture of recycling and community service among the student volunteers involved in the logistics and distribution\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/yxY8Xda922vcJHqdnwagO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ovkAFmr3S5lY0BCzrbaFr","name":"Nasha Muka Bharat Pledge","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/ISHz75bxixsQuJOh-t_FT.png"],"endDate":"2025-08-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"The immediate outcome of the Nasha Mukt Bharat Pledge was the sensitization of the student body towards the critical issue of drug dependence. The activity successfully instilled a sense of moral responsibility, encouraging participants to adopt a healthy lifestyle free from intoxicants. By verbalizing their commitment, students strengthened their resolve to resist peer pressure and societal triggers associated with drug use. The event fostered a supportive peer network, where students felt empowered to discourage drug abuse among friends and seek help if needed. Long-term, this initiative contributes to a positive campus culture that stigmatizes drug consumption while promoting empathy for those in recovery. The pledge also connected students to a larger national movement, making them feel part of a significant social cause. Participation in this activity was formally recognized, awarding students with 2 activity points, which reflects their engagement in value-based education and community welfare initiatives essential for their overall character development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The \"Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyan\" (Drug-Free India Campaign) pledge activity was organized to align the student community with the national objective of eradicating substance abuse. Organized under the directives of the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, this event aimed to create mass awareness about the devastating impact of drug addiction on youth and society. The activity involved a formal gathering where students, faculty, and staff stood united to take a solemn integrity pledge. We collectively vowed to abstain from all forms of narcotics and dedicated ourselves to preserving the health and well-being of our community. Beyond the recitation of the pledge, the session served as an educational platform, briefly highlighting the socio-economic consequences of addiction and the importance of mental resilience. By participating, students acknowledged their role as key stakeholders in nation-building, promising to spread the message of a drug-free life to their families and neighborhoods. The event underscored the college''s commitment to fostering a safe, healthy, and intoxicant-free campus environment, ensuring that the youth remain focused on their academic and professional growth without the hindrance of substance dependence.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness ","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/uhK5ojGctdy-sqm4tkzj1.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oe7N1gkIaRFKyT17ol9cc","name":"Female Feticide Walkathon","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/45fseSu7OYCszRfQOWJYT.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Female Feticide Awareness Walkathon successfully mobilized campus and local communities, registering over 300 participants and engaging multiple student clubs and partner NGOs. The event distributed informational leaflets, collected contact details for volunteer follow-up, and recorded commitments for future school outreach and counselling workshops. Immediate outcomes included increased awareness of legal protections and reporting mechanisms among participants, improved campus dialogue on gender equity, and stronger ties between Rotaract and local support services. The organizing committee documented logistics, safety measures, and volunteer roles to inform a post-event report and metrics for future initiatives. Social media coverage and campus announcements amplified the message beyond on-ground attendance. Student volunteers gained hands-on experience in event management, advocacy, and community engagement. The Walkathon established an action plan for follow-up activities — including educational sessions in nearby schools, partnership meetings with NGOs, and awareness drives across campus — ensuring sustained momentum to safeguard girls’ rights.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-14","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organised the Female Feticide Awareness Walkathon on 11 May 2025 at the CS Ground, RVCE, under the Avenue of Community Service, commemorating Mother’s Day. The event commenced at 6:00 AM and brought together students, faculty, neighbourhood residents, and family volunteers in a peaceful public demonstration against sex-selective practices. Registration (via QR code) entitled student volunteers to 15 activity points, and the walkathon was designated pet-friendly to encourage wider participation. Participants assembled at Kriyakalpa, RVCE, carried informational banners, and distributed leaflets detailing legal protections, reporting channels, and counselling resources. The programme included short addresses by club leaders and invited social activists, coordinated hydration and first-aid stations, and clearly marked route management handled by volunteer teams. Event chairs Rtr. Mukund Verma and Rtr. Tarun Pedada, under the guidance of President Rtr. Kushal Mandhyan, oversaw logistics and volunteer allocation. The initiative also initiated collaboration with local NGOs to plan follow-up workshops and school outreach. The Walkathon successfully fostered campus solidarity, amplified conversation on gender equity, and provided a platform for sustained advocacy.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social issues","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/rfVji5VERUJhBPuhmoa5N.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"N3ecGcNNsFj0lk_uL76al","name":"Blood donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/XbifkHZUuTFADueyRuq30.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of this blood donation activity was immediate and tangible, contributing directly to saving human lives. By donating a single unit of blood, I potentially assisted up to three different patients, as the blood is separated into red cells, plasma, and platelets. The event successfully raised awareness about the scarcity of blood supplies and the safety of the donation process, dispelling common myths among the student community. On a personal level, the experience instilled a profound sense of altruism and social responsibility. It also provided a free health check-up, offering insights into my own physical well-being. Receiving the Certificate of Appreciation from the Indian Red Cross Society served as a validation of this humanitarian effort. Furthermore, being part of this drive helped foster a culture of regular donation within the campus, inspiring peers to join future camps and collectively work towards a healthier, more resilient society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Participating in the Voluntary Blood Donation Camp was a significant act of community service aimed at bolstering the healthcare resources of our region. Organized by the Indian Red Cross Society, Karnataka State Branch, this drive was conducted on 1st February 2026 with the primary objective of replenishing blood banks to assist patients in critical care, surgeries, and emergency situations. As a donor, the process began with a mandatory registration followed by a preliminary medical screening to check vital parameters like blood pressure, hemoglobin levels, and weight, ensuring fitness for donation. Once cleared, I donated 350ml of blood under the supervision of qualified medical professionals who ensured a sterile and safe environment. The activity was not just about the physical act of giving blood but also involved understanding the constant need for blood components like plasma and platelets in hospitals. This initiative provided a practical platform to fulfill my civic duty, requiring approximately 2 to 3 hours of participation, including the post-donation observation period, and reinforced the importance of selfless contribution to society.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to health services / Community Service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/r2d1HodYl0hqsTVG07nyQ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ag9uYYOP9gb5xidVrYfMV","name":"Fist Full","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/SpuWXgikYMGWlM2edXG4-.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"Fist Full successfully mobilised campus resources and community goodwill to support vulnerable households. Immediate outcomes included establishment of efficient collection points, volunteer training in safe food handling and packing, and formal registration of volunteers who earned AICTE activity points. The drive strengthened partnerships with local NGOs and social service groups for timely distribution of collected staples. Student volunteers gained hands-on experience in event coordination, logistics and community outreach, improving the club’s operational readiness for future drives. Awareness of simple donation practices increased across campus, reflected in steady inflow at collection points after the formal launch. Organisers compiled a post-event summary documenting donations received, volunteer rosters, logistics costs, and partner contacts to measure impact and plan improvements. The campaign created a clear follow-up plan — routine donation drives, structured school/outreach programs, and expanded NGO collaborations — to sustain momentum and maximise food-security impact in the local community.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organised Fist Full from 3rd November – 21st November 2025, with the donation drive phase beginning on 17th November 2025. Conducted under the Avenue of Community Service and in collaboration with Rotary Club of Bangalore Spandana, the campaign encouraged students, faculty, and local residents to “save up a fistful” while cooking and donate staples — 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal — for families in need. The drive promoted simple, repeatable giving and campus-wide participation: registration via QR-code awarded 10 AICTE activity points to volunteers, while multiple designated collection points across the college facilitated donations and safe handling. Event logistics were overseen by Event Chair Rtr. Aditi Kallolkar (+91 70229 98075) and President Rtr. Pratham M P (+91 83901 24801), with volunteer teams managing collection, sorting, packing and coordination with partner NGOs. The campaign combined ease of donation with awareness-building about food security and community solidarity, inviting sustained engagement from students and neighbouring communities. Fist Full emphasised dignity in giving and created a repeatable model for campus-led food drives.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to community development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9381eb4d-0e93-4528-8014-407f27aab909/O_JNCraLDpr_K4GrtHNhv.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-02 06:27:13.14089+00', '2026-02-02 07:46:24.148409+00'), ('765f0f51-2113-4a3a-93b9-bded35a588cd', 'e791d1b9-8fe3-4957-acd6-0867b8ae586c', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS171","name":"sai varun konda","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"1uI5yCewf5UjZ8kz345tD","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2023","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s education programs. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and learning resources to underprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its fundraising goals, amassing contributions that will sustain classroom initiatives for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students from local underserved communities.\\n\\nBeyond the financial gains, the marathon left an indelible impression on all involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from first-time runners conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz amplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and encouraging future involvement.\\n\\nUltimately, it redefined the act of running as a meaningful pursuit, not only for personal health and endurance, but for forging a brighter, more inclusive future. The Utsarga Marathon exemplified how community-driven events can create ripple effects of change, empowering children to dream big and succeed while fostering a culture of giving back.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Description of the activity\\tThe Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, took place on June 4th, 2023, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM across the Bengaluru campus. Under the theme \"Help a Child Change the World,\" it celebrated health, fitness, and education support for underprivileged children. Months of planning ensured smooth logistics with sponsor-backed medals, T-shirts, and refreshments along tree-lined routes.\\n\\nOver 500 runners, including RVCE students, faculty, alumni, and locals from Karnataka, gathered at dawn. They chose between a 5 km fun run (Rs. 399) or 10 km challenge (Rs. 449), with all donations funding school supplies and tuition. Warm-ups, cheers, live music, banners, and photo booths created festive energy.\\n\\nVolunteers in high-visibility vests managed water stations, medical aid, and crowd control with enthusiasm. They helped runners adjust to long conditions, ensuring safety and inclusivity. Heartwarming scenes featured friends jogging together, families cheering from sidelines, and visitors spectating.\\n\\nRunners crossed the finish line to roaring applause, greeted with finisher medals and personalized certificates. Top age-group performers received special trophies, sparking friendly rivalries. On-site announcements celebrated winners, fueling real-time excitement around the charitable core.\\n\\nThe event proved transformative, blending physical challenge with philanthropy. It promoted wellness while instilling purpose through unity. Individual strides wove into widespread positive change for children''s futures.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e791d1b9-8fe3-4957-acd6-0867b8ae586c/CIxMucu5s95-f12Gt7WJA.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"crOHvCI0aT1Ptpcd6wAde","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Outcome\\tThe Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s education programs. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and learning resources to underprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its fundraising goals, amassing contributions that will sustain classroom initiatives for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students from local underserved communities.\\n\\nBeyond the financial gains, the marathon left an indelible impression on all involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from first-time runners conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz amplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and encouraging future involvement.\\n\\nUltimately, it redefined the act of running as a meaningful pursuit, not only for personal health and endurance, but for forging a brighter, more inclusive future. The Utsarga Marathon exemplified how community-driven events can create ripple effects of change, empowering children to dream big and succeed while fostering a culture of giving back.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Description of the activity\\tThe Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, took place on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM across the Bengaluru campus. Under the theme \"Help a Child Change the World,\" it celebrated health, fitness, and education support for underprivileged children. Months of planning ensured smooth logistics with sponsor-backed medals, T-shirts, and refreshments along tree-lined routes.\\n\\nOver 500 runners, including RVCE students, faculty, alumni, and locals from Karnataka, gathered at dawn. They chose between a 5 km fun run (Rs. 399) or 10 km challenge (Rs. 449), with all donations funding school supplies and tuition. Warm-ups, cheers, live music, banners, and photo booths created festive energy.\\n\\nVolunteers in high-visibility vests managed water stations, medical aid, and crowd control with enthusiasm. They helped runners adjust to long conditions, ensuring safety and inclusivity. Heartwarming scenes featured friends jogging together, families cheering from sidelines, and visitors spectating.\\n\\nRunners crossed the finish line to roaring applause, greeted with finisher medals and personalized certificates. Top age-group performers received special trophies, sparking friendly rivalries. On-site announcements celebrated winners, fueling real-time excitement around the charitable core.\\n\\nThe event proved transformative, blending physical challenge with philanthropy. It promoted wellness while instilling purpose through unity. Individual strides wove into widespread positive change for children''s futures.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e791d1b9-8fe3-4957-acd6-0867b8ae586c/OObb5TjoM8ArI8-VSuNyY.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rvxeGVGLVNKboZ77QIXlH","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Outcome\\tThe Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s education programs. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and learning resources to underprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its fundraising goals, amassing contributions that will sustain classroom initiatives for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students from local underserved communities.\\n\\nBeyond the financial gains, the marathon left an indelible impression on all involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from first-time runners conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz amplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and encouraging future involvement.\\n\\nUltimately, it redefined the act of running as a meaningful pursuit, not only for personal health and endurance, but for forging a brighter, more inclusive future. The Utsarga Marathon exemplified how community-driven events can create ripple effects of change, empowering children to dream big and succeed while fostering a culture of giving back.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Description of the activity\\tThe Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, took place on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM across the Bengaluru campus. Under the theme \"Help a Child Change the World,\" it celebrated health, fitness, and education support for underprivileged children. Months of planning ensured smooth logistics with sponsor-backed medals, T-shirts, and refreshments along tree-lined routes.\\n\\nOver 500 runners, including RVCE students, faculty, alumni, and locals from Karnataka, gathered at dawn. They chose between a 5 km fun run (Rs. 399) or 10 km challenge (Rs. 449), with all donations funding school supplies and tuition. Warm-ups, cheers, live music, banners, and photo booths created festive energy.\\n\\nVolunteers in high-visibility vests managed water stations, medical aid, and crowd control with enthusiasm. They helped runners adjust to long conditions, ensuring safety and inclusivity. Heartwarming scenes featured friends jogging together, families cheering from sidelines, and visitors spectating.\\n\\nRunners crossed the finish line to roaring applause, greeted with finisher medals and personalized certificates. Top age-group performers received special trophies, sparking friendly rivalries. On-site announcements celebrated winners, fueling real-time excitement around the charitable core.\\n\\nThe event proved transformative, blending physical challenge with philanthropy. It promoted wellness while instilling purpose through unity. Individual strides wove into widespread positive change for children''s futures.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e791d1b9-8fe3-4957-acd6-0867b8ae586c/6ZQ4AJhjoFPP4Ioc_RDvH.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"My-tazG6Sq5phkf24ySJN","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":4,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YyU0UqmaKeUG8a0EFlUA_","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":4,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xz1WSfjN1N1vUYyltP1Ny","name":"Positive Thinker","slNo":6,"place":"Outside Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-02-28","duration":28,"outcomes":"","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-01","hoursSpent":-12,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tC48nPYcb4W3GHKgJpp-z","name":"Discover Yourself","slNo":7,"place":"Outside Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2022-12-31","duration":31,"outcomes":"","semester":"1","startDate":"2022-12-01","hoursSpent":20,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"u-EBP_9e1p7DjqN-I4xK_","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fOZ14MEdaFzceu4_iGYv3","name":"SPARK “Through the Eyes of Youth”, an SDG Photo Competition","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"Outcome\\t330 students had participated from which 289 were from RV College of Engineering. Top 25 participants made it till the final round out of which 8 participants were declared as Special Mention and Top 3 winners were announced on 19th August, 2023.\\n\\nBy engaging in this competition, young people can make\\na significant impact on their communities, countries, and the world at large.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":16,"description":"Description of the activity\\tParticipants were informed to capture a picture relating to any one of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and explain how the picture is connected to the chosen goal through a meaningful story or description. They were asked to reflect on the importance of the selected SDG and provide their explanation within a limit of 150 words, ensuring clarity and relevance in their response.\\n\\nThe purpose of this activity was to encourage participants to think deeply about sustainable development issues and creatively showcase their understanding through visual storytelling. Since the SDGs serve as a framework for global progress, this task helped the youth engage with these goals in a personal way, motivating them to actively participate, contribute their ideas, and envision how they can play a role in shaping a better and more sustainable future.\\n","aicteMapping":"Competition","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1dRe1HpUXUIr4xaCwlSCy","name":"ACM Summit 2024","slNo":10,"place":"BMSCE Campus and RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-22","duration":3,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-20","hoursSpent":20,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PD7vHpTDMWyxz7cMiIzf3","name":"Volunteering at Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":11,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"4","startDate":"","hoursSpent":10,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"90v2t8Um_W-vSgiOUgWAB","name":"Rush Hours","slNo":12,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"","hoursSpent":1,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AlEDwlLa7gVMlYRIwjnWx","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":13,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:47:25.747826+00', '2026-01-30 15:44:42.594187+00'), ('78b49c5d-7316-4bbd-a903-26cfbdd5774e', 'b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CH009","name":"Darshana Manish Jain","period":"2022-2026","department":"Chemical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"c5z3gvdD8eSccwW9qsQyl","name":"Treasure Hunt 2023","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-01-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Organizing the event helped strengthen my leadership, event \\nmanagement, and coordination skills. It enhanced my ability to \\nplan activities, manage teams, and handle real-time challenges \\neffectively. The experience contributed to creating a positive and \\nenergetic atmosphere while fostering teamwork and student \\nengagement. ","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-01-25","hoursSpent":0,"description":"As a part of the Raag Team we organized the Treasure Hunt – \\nFun and Gaming Event, designed to promote teamwork, \\nproblem-solving, and active participation in an engaging and \\nenjoyable format. As the organizer, I was responsible for \\nplanning the event structure, designing clues and game flow, \\ncoordinating with the organizing team and volunteers, and \\nmanaging on-ground logistics. The event encouraged \\ncollaboration,  strategic  thinking,  and  enthusiasm  among \\nparticipants through interactive challenges ","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/PHfbqphRjXMyb0JyMD7Hh.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"15_BJvtQ4De2yVDuy3KDv","name":"Matrubhasha Diwas ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-02-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The celebration of Matrubhasha Diwas 2023 resulted in meaningful outcomes that strengthened cultural awareness and inclusivity within the institution. By highlighting the importance of mother languages, the event encouraged students and faculty to appreciate India’s linguistic diversity and heritage. With nearly 750 participants actively engaging in the procession, performances, and competitions, the program fostered a strong sense of community and unity. Overall, the event reinforced RVCE’s commitment to national initiatives that promote respect for cultural traditions and helped instill pride in the richness of India’s multilingual identity.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Matrubhasha Diwas 2023 was celebrated with great enthusiasm to highlight the importance of mother languages and India’s rich cultural diversity. The event began with a colorful procession where faculty, staff, and students carried placards promoting linguistic pride while dressed in ethnic attire representing different regions. This was followed by a series of performances in various mother tongues, including poetry recitations, songs, dances, and skits, all of which showcased the beauty and uniqueness of India’s multilingual heritage.\\n\\nIn addition to the main program, several pre-events were organized to encourage creativity and participation. These included a rangoli competition, a photography contest titled Capture the Moment, and a digital art contest called Digitalize Your Heritage. The celebration also featured a ramp walk and DJ show, blending traditional and modern elements to engage the audience. With nearly 750 participants, the event successfully fostered inclusivity and cultural pride, while awarding AICTE activity points to the organizing team and competition winners.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/7PfUVv9DPbreQufiGktVX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GQdfPGTJ91qM3Us8FFkt5","name":"Fast Trek","slNo":3,"place":"Huthridurga  hills ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/9w8SL5d8RBmz2_Fh-n4Ac.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants gained greater awareness of the healthcare challenges \\nfaced by underprivileged children with heart diseases, resulting in \\nincreased empathy and social consciousness among students. The \\nevent successfully generated financial support and community \\nengagement, directly contributing to child healthcare assistance. \\nThe activity promoted physical fitness, environmental \\nresponsibility, and mental well-being, while fostering stronger \\nbonds and a sense of belonging within the student community. \\nOverall, Fast-Trek reaffirmed the importance of youth \\ninvolvement in social welfare and inspired continued \\nparticipation in future community development initiatives","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Content: \\nFast-Trek, held on 12th February 2023 at Huthridurga Hills, was a \\nflagship outreach event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. \\nWith more than 400 enthusiastic student volunteers, the initiative \\nblended adventure, youth participation, and social responsibility. \\nThe primary objective of the trek was to generate financial \\nsupport for underprivileged children battling heart diseases, \\nemphasizing empathy, healthcare awareness, and collective \\naction. \\n \\nThe volunteers and coordinators guided the participants \\nthroughout the journey, ensuring comfort, discipline, and \\ninclusivity. The scenic terrain of Huthridurga Betta provided an \\nideal setting for students to connect with nature, overcome \\nphysical challenges, and develop resilience, cooperation, and \\nleadership skills. \\n \\nBeyond the physical activity, Fast-Trek encouraged students to \\nreflect on social welfare, community engagement, and the \\nimportance of supporting vulnerable sections of society. The \\nevent concluded successfully, strengthening the culture of \\nvolunteerism, compassion, and proactive youth involvement in \\ncommunity development. \\n","aicteMapping":"Economic and  Community  development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/jrbVZRdTf6EbrJfM7Nte5.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qCkmRkAkNG6pd7PtyX9SC","name":"Special School Event","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/GriAaqJs7pMCNPsHAeIJu.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-12-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project successfully promoted inclusivity in education by bridging gaps in accessibility for disabled students. It encouraged participants to think beyond conventional approaches, fostering innovation and problem-solving skills. The initiative also strengthened social responsibility among student volunteers, who gained valuable experience in designing solutions for real-world challenges. Overall, the event reinforced the institution’s commitment to holistic development, combining technical knowledge with compassion and community service.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-30","hoursSpent":7,"description":"A special science project was designed and implemented with the goal of supporting disabled students by making learning more accessible and engaging. The project focused on developing simple, innovative tools and demonstrations that could be easily understood and interacted with by students with different abilities. Faculty guided the initiative, while student teams worked collaboratively to design models and experiments that emphasized inclusivity in science education.\\n\\nThe event not only showcased technical creativity but also highlighted empathy and social responsibility. By tailoring scientific concepts to meet the needs of disabled students, the project created a platform where education and accessibility merged, ensuring that every learner could participate meaningfully in the learning process.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/gl3SD4UIBbmZSLJQrqWkQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WHMaN8DL3VCvdUaIJbxzf","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":5,"place":"Kengeri","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/79lLhM1ygV8qcOETwqrkp.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"he Paper Drive successfully diverted a significant amount of 8.17 tonnes waste paper from landfills and contributed to recycling efforts. It fostered environmental consciousness among both students and apartment residents, motivating them to adopt greener practices in daily life. The initiative also strengthened the institution’s outreach to the local community, showing how collective action can create meaningful environmental impact.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Paper Drive to promote sustainability and environmental responsibility. As part of the initiative, student volunteers collected waste paper from nearby apartments and residential areas. The collected paper was then sent for recycling, ensuring that resources were reused effectively and waste was minimized. The drive also included awareness efforts to encourage residents to adopt eco‑friendly practices and contribute to reducing paper waste.\\n\\nThis activity not only highlighted the importance of recycling but also gave students practical exposure to community engagement and environmental stewardship. By coordinating logistics, managing collection points, and interacting with apartment residents, the volunteers demonstrated teamwork and leadership while advancing the cause of sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/wiC_wJh5datJZ0-25noiM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ebix5zF1ijoTpinpSvXiz","name":"Skit on Anti-Ragging","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The anti‑ragging skit video successfully raised awareness about the dangers of ragging and reinforced the institution’s commitment to a ragging‑free campus. It provided a creative platform for students to express social responsibility while also developing skills in teamwork, scriptwriting, and video production. Uploading the video to the AICTE website amplified its impact, allowing the message to reach a wider audience and contribute to national efforts against ragging. Overall, the initiative combined community service, cultural expression, and innovation, making it a valuable activity under the AICTE Activity Points framework.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-19","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The CARV Hindi club prepared and recorded a skit on Anti‑Ragging, which was later edited into a video for upload on the AICTE website. The skit was performed in Hindi to ensure relatability and wider reach among students, dramatizing the harmful effects of ragging and emphasizing the importance of empathy, respect, and inclusivity in campus life. The video production involved scripting, rehearsals, filming, and editing, giving students hands‑on experience in creative media while also serving as a powerful awareness tool.\\n\\nBy presenting real‑life scenarios and resolutions, the video aimed to sensitize students to the consequences of ragging and highlight institutional policies that safeguard student welfare. Faculty mentors guided the process, ensuring that the final video aligned with AICTE’s objectives of promoting safe and inclusive educational environments.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/JHjY4xtUih-qpCuz8t0dt.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ioXQ4MhbACDlYN8a02jIA","name":"Fist Full","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-09-29","duration":-46,"outcomes":"The Fist Full drive successfully provided essential food supplies to rural schools and communities, directly supporting children’s nutrition and well‑being. It instilled a sense of social responsibility among participants, demonstrating how small acts of kindness can create meaningful impact when multiplied across a community. The initiative also strengthened the bond between RVCE and the wider society, reinforcing the institution’s commitment to service‑oriented activities.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized Fist Full, a donation drive where students and faculty contributed fistfuls of toor dal or rice. The collected grains were pooled together and distributed to underprivileged communities and schools in rural areas. The initiative was designed to encourage the spirit of giving, showing how even small, consistent contributions can make a significant difference in addressing hunger and nutritional needs.\\n\\nVolunteers coordinated the collection across campus and nearby residences, ensuring that the donations were properly gathered, packaged, and delivered to beneficiaries. The activity emphasized empathy, community engagement, and the importance of collective responsibility in supporting those in need.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/vaKnbWGW_0H-2h2QB3Wg7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EyTdjtRMQNpgx8B5qTpcK","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-06-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project successfully provided essential school kits to rural students, directly supporting their educational journey. It fostered a sense of empathy and social responsibility among participating students, who realized the impact of small contributions in creating meaningful change. The initiative strengthened the bond between RVCE and the wider community, while aligning with AICTE’s vision of holistic student development through service‑oriented activities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-06-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak was an initiative undertaken in collaboration with the Rotaract Club of RVCE to support education in rural areas. As part of the project, students contributed ₹350 each, which was pooled to provide essential school kits for children studying in underprivileged rural schools. The kits included basic learning materials such as notebooks, pens, pencils, and other essentials to ensure that students had the necessary resources to continue their education.\\n\\nThis effort reflected the institution’s commitment to social responsibility and community service. By participating in Project Pustak, students not only contributed financially but also became part of a larger mission to bridge educational gaps and empower rural children with access to learning tools.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/FhECTxPPi5ouoYbAEP3nP.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ryajtbK-2GS1a6EjSZuF9","name":"Vision","slNo":9,"place":"Kengeri","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/PDcaspDjAft7bbroQNXG_.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-06-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The counselling sessions helped high school students gain a better understanding of the diverse career options available to them and the steps required to pursue their chosen paths. It instilled confidence and motivation among the participants, encouraging them to aim higher and plan their education strategically. For RVCE students, the initiative fostered empathy, communication skills, and a sense of social responsibility. Overall, Vision strengthened the institution’s outreach to the community and contributed to building an inclusive and supportive educational ecosystem.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-15","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized Vision, a career counselling program aimed at guiding high school students from government schools in choosing their future academic and professional paths. The initiative focused on providing clarity about different streams of higher education, competitive exams, and career opportunities in science, engineering, medicine, commerce, and the arts.\\n\\nStudent volunteers and faculty mentors interacted with the school children through presentations, discussions, and Q&A sessions. The program emphasized the importance of self‑awareness, goal setting, and informed decision‑making, ensuring that students from rural and underprivileged backgrounds received equal access to career guidance resources.","aicteMapping":"Education / Literary Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/7HFv51h_IJ2r5lb5IXTQq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0r6cFYo0Qm9o4tl7NJOC8","name":"Fist full","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":19,"outcomes":"The Fist Full drive successfully provided essential food supplies to rural schools and communities, directly supporting children’s nutrition and well‑being. It instilled a sense of social responsibility among participants, demonstrating how small acts of kindness can create meaningful impact when multiplied across a community. The initiative also strengthened the bond between RVCE and the wider society, reinforcing the institution’s commitment to service‑oriented activities.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-03","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized Fist Full, a donation drive where students and faculty contributed fistfuls of toor dal or rice. The collected grains were pooled together and distributed to underprivileged communities and schools in rural areas. The initiative was designed to encourage the spirit of giving, showing how even small, consistent contributions can make a significant difference in addressing hunger and nutritional needs.\\n\\nVolunteers coordinated the collection across campus and nearby residences, ensuring that the donations were properly gathered, packaged, and delivered to beneficiaries. The activity emphasized empathy, community engagement, and the importance of collective responsibility in supporting those in need.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/UNaYgcjACcSD1pC5lNI-E.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"d7DCKYT0w1Q5lhNq2Fs6S","name":"Treasure Hunt","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Organizing the event helped strengthen my leadership, event \\nmanagement, and coordination skills. It enhanced my ability to \\nplan activities, manage teams, and handle real-time challenges \\neffectively. The experience contributed to creating a positive and \\nenergetic atmosphere while fostering teamwork and student \\nengagement. ","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-01-16","hoursSpent":0,"description":"As a part of the Core Team we organized the Treasure Hunt – \\nFun and Gaming Event, designed to promote teamwork, \\nproblem-solving, and active participation in an engaging and \\nenjoyable format. As the organizer, I was responsible for \\nplanning the event structure, designing clues and game flow, \\ncoordinating with the organizing team and volunteers, and \\nmanaging on-ground logistics. The event encouraged \\ncollaboration,  strategic  thinking,  and  enthusiasm  among \\nparticipants through interactive challenges ","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/7HvQay37F5n9CzG1890FP.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0gVUTt9bW4SVwgzfxZdti","name":"Matrubhasha Diwas","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-08","duration":31,"outcomes":"The celebration of Matrubhasha Diwas 2025 resulted in meaningful outcomes that strengthened cultural awareness and inclusivity within the institution. By highlighting the importance of mother languages, the event encouraged students and faculty to appreciate India’s linguistic diversity and heritage. With nearly 750 participants actively engaging in the procession, performances, and competitions, the program fostered a strong sense of community and unity. Overall, the event reinforced RVCE’s commitment to national initiatives that promote respect for cultural traditions and helped instill pride in the richness of India’s multilingual identity.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-08","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Matrubhasha Diwas 2025 was celebrated with great enthusiasm to highlight the importance of mother languages and India’s rich cultural diversity. The event began with a colorful procession where faculty, staff, and students carried placards promoting linguistic pride while dressed in ethnic attire representing different regions. This was followed by a series of performances in various mother tongues, including poetry recitations, songs, dances, and skits, all of which showcased the beauty and uniqueness of India’s multilingual heritage.\\n\\nIn addition to the main program, several pre-events were organized to encourage creativity and participation. These included a rangoli competition, a photography contest titled Capture the Moment, and a digital art contest called Digitalize Your Heritage. The celebration also featured a ramp walk and DJ show, blending traditional and modern elements to engage the audience. With nearly 750 participants, the event successfully fostered inclusivity and cultural pride, while awarding AICTE activity points to the organizing team and competition winners.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b3167d5a-56e1-402b-8a6b-bb277e7f72c4/JUVjAfyqizBQue6StrvVa.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 11:57:38.031745+00', '2026-01-31 06:42:29.552789+00'), ('79e10179-6aa6-4dff-95f4-c1866ab17f9c', 'a1719f1e-78b4-4aca-b65a-e768ea002738', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"pIk6BOOf9YiT5fgBwtlnv","name":"","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 17:12:39.02226+00', '2026-01-29 17:12:39.02226+00'), ('7ba3f92e-a14d-4fc5-97e4-402db6177180', '80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC069","name":"Harshitha B J","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"S5F3H_o1DZoLJ-6d4LsEX","name":"Eye Donation Fortnight","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/yvk1RN1EOHysUKDaSv54U.png"],"endDate":"2025-09-08","duration":12,"outcomes":"The National Eye Donation Fortnight campaign successfully raised awareness about the critical need for corneal donations and the transformative impact of eye donation on visually impaired individuals. Students gained comprehensive knowledge about the eye donation process, its significance, and the myths and misconceptions surrounding organ donation, developing a deeper appreciation for this humanitarian cause.","semester":"1","startDate":"2025-08-28","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This awareness and pledge initiative was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering as part of the National Eye Donation Fortnight observed from August 25th to September 8th across the country. The program aimed to promote the noble cause of eye donation and create awareness about the life-changing impact of corneal transplants for visually impaired individuals.\\nThroughout this campaign, students participated by registering as Sight Ambassadors through a simple SMS-based process, pledging to donate their eyes posthumously to give the gift of sight to someone in need. The initiative involved completing an online registration, receiving an official Sight Ambassador Certificate, and committing to advocate for eye donation within their circles of influence. NSS coordinators facilitated the registration process, guided participants through the steps, and ensured proper documentation of pledges.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/OOKRNGRE0_ak0VGXPuwdm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IXLeXyF1dCfzedD78Mfo1","name":"Mera Pehla Vote","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/vnlsVCIdLEK_7bEN5Nj1K.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-09","duration":4,"outcomes":"The Mera Pehla Vote - Desh Ke Liye campaign successfully enhanced voter awareness and civic consciousness among students and their extended social networks. Participants gained valuable experience in creating impactful digital content for social causes while developing skills in visual storytelling, video editing, copywriting, and social media management.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"This social media awareness campaign was organized under the initiative \"Mera Pehla Vote - Desh Ke Liye\" (My First Vote - For the Nation) in collaboration with AICTE, aimed at promoting voter awareness and encouraging first-time voters to exercise their democratic rights responsibly. The program focused on leveraging social media platforms to amplify the message of electoral participation and civic responsibility among youth.\\nThroughout this campaign, students actively created and shared engaging content including pictures, reels, podcasts, Instagram posts, and blogs about various voter awareness events and initiatives. Participants utilized multiple social media platforms to reach wider audiences, spreading awareness about the importance of voting, electoral processes, and responsible citizenship. The campaign was coordinated by respective clubs who facilitated content creation guidelines, provided necessary resources, and managed the submission process through designated upload links.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/-AIRMbOYfDX2KB_jtYzJM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Bg3gI9X9WF8zL1OR7fMYO","name":"SDG Photography Competition","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/V06SSn3EK6OhWLvPu8tjY.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-25","duration":4,"outcomes":"The photography competition enhanced students'' creative expression, visual storytelling abilities, and awareness of global sustainability issues through the lens of the 17 Sustainable Development Goals. It fostered critical thinking about environmental and social challenges while developing participants'' photography skills and artistic sensibilities.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-22","hoursSpent":4,"description":"This photography competition centered on the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), challenging participants to capture and communicate the essence of all 17 SDG themes through visual storytelling. The event was organized by SPARK prefects and drew participation from students across various ability enhancement courses.\\nThroughout the competition, students demonstrated their creative vision and awareness of global sustainability issues, presenting compelling photographic interpretations of themes ranging from poverty alleviation to climate action. The organizers were actively involved in all aspects of the event, including publicity, coordination, evaluation, and shortlisting entries, thereby developing essential leadership, management, and communication skills.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/whLlCYDLhPgP3LyWkvyMC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"blFYCd88qTtYMYpxwZ98a","name":"Energy Literacy Training Program","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/Bcyo6QLb3_49nIsHvvPW5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-19","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Energy Literacy Training successfully enhanced students'' understanding of energy conservation principles and sustainable practices. Participants gained comprehensive knowledge about renewable energy technologies, energy-efficient systems, and practical strategies for reducing energy consumption in daily life.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-18","hoursSpent":24,"description":"This energy conservation initiative was organized in collaboration with the Department of Electrical and Electronics (EEE) at RVCE, focusing on comprehensive Energy Literacy Training. The program aimed to raise awareness about sustainable energy practices and empower students with knowledge and skills to promote energy efficiency in their communities.\\nThroughout the training, participants engaged in learning about various aspects of energy conservation, renewable energy technologies, and sustainable practices. The initiative covered critical topics including energy auditing, efficient resource utilization, and the importance of reducing carbon footprint. Students were exposed to practical approaches for implementing energy-saving measures in residential, institutional, and industrial settings.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/5pSwm6HmoDs7cIEx9Wlkf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OCAdq-U3Ze7ZxCupXCNkv","name":"FistFull","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/4QS_qOuEWQVaXiXVPv9Uv.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-25","duration":9,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event successfully cultivated values of empathy, generosity, and social responsibility among participants. Students gained meaningful experience in grassroots-level community service while developing organizational and coordination skills through the collection and management of food donations.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This community service initiative was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE under the theme \"Unite for Good,\" featuring the flagship event \"Fist Full\" scheduled to commence on November 1st, 2025. The program focused on collecting essential food items, specifically 5 kg rice and/or 2 kg Toor Dal, from students to support underprivileged communities.\\nThe donation collection phase ran from November 17th to November 25th, 2025, providing students ample opportunity to contribute voluntarily to this noble cause. The initiative aimed to address food security challenges while fostering a spirit of compassion and social responsibility among the college community. Students actively participated in collecting, organizing, and managing the donations under the coordination of Rotaract Club members.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/ee8stpwu_OcrMPh0Kpmjc.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Xsyb9afKV6ZT_NYXunMqG","name":"FistFull","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/ngDX3KgC-YXdZtH50Z8L3.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-22","duration":8,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event successfully cultivated values of empathy, generosity, and civic responsibility among participants. Students gained hands-on experience in organizing and executing a large-scale humanitarian initiative while developing essential skills in teamwork, coordination, and community engagement.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This community service initiative was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE under the motto \"Strength in Unity, Power in Purpose,\" featuring the event \"Fist Full\" conducted from November 18th to November 29th, 2024. The program focused on collecting essential food supplies to support underprivileged communities, embodying the spirit of humanitarian service and social responsibility.\\nThroughout the event duration, students voluntarily participated in the collection and organization of food donations, demonstrating compassion and commitment to making a positive impact on society. The initiative was carefully coordinated by Rotaract Club members who managed logistics, publicity, and participant engagement to ensure the success of the campaign.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/W2lF9gmIOZBQZsmSgb1rI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"q5tXRN9KmMLxyCZ3q2sKs","name":"Utsarga Marathon Volunteering","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/nbciLYWTi_8H0J3h753XK.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-07","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon volunteering experience successfully instilled values of selfless service, teamwork, and organizational excellence among participants. Students gained practical experience in event management, crisis handling, and public interaction while developing essential soft skills including communication, leadership, and problem-solving abilities.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"This community service initiative was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering, focusing on volunteering activities for the Utsarga Marathon. The event provided students an opportunity to contribute to community welfare through active volunteer service, supporting the successful execution of this large-scale marathon event.\\nThroughout the marathon, student volunteers played crucial roles in various aspects of event management including registration, participant coordination, hydration station management, route guidance, crowd control, and logistical support. The NSS Programme Officers coordinated the volunteer deployment, ensuring comprehensive coverage of all event requirements. Volunteers demonstrated dedication, responsibility, and teamwork while facilitating a smooth and safe marathon experience for all participants.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/o3PW6J56XbQAHVgiyzl9Q.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wy-4LIxewzdPwYW3iUyXw","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/zfkbWGKaa_xUSaPRKzTia.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-27","duration":4,"outcomes":"The Paper Drive successfully cultivated values of environmental responsibility, community service, and social entrepreneurship among the 500+ student volunteers. Participants gained hands-on experience in organizing and executing a large-scale collection campaign while developing essential skills in logistics management, teamwork, and community engagement.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"This large-scale community service initiative was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on June 24th, 2023, under the avenue of Community Services with a focus on Economic and Community Development. The Paper Drive was conceived as a mega event to support orphanages and underprivileged communities while promoting environmental sustainability through waste paper recycling.\\nWith overwhelming participation from over 500 volunteers, the initiative involved systematic collection of newspapers, books, magazines, and waste papers from various localities across Bangalore. Volunteers assembled at Kriyakalpa, RVCE at 8:00 AM and were strategically deployed to different locations via buses to maximize collection efficiency. The project operated on a dual-purpose model: collected materials were sold to paper vendors to generate funds, with the proceeds donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation for welfare activities supporting underprivileged communities.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/uYe4E5ikzSZQhyPoZqplM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8W2Ae4mN1YWoB7NPvOH0T","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":9,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/b952EO3n14xKMF_mwnWUE.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Fast Trek 2.0 successfully fostered environmental consciousness and adventure spirit among over 750 participants. Students gained valuable experience in outdoor activities while developing a deeper appreciation for natural landscapes and the importance of preserving pristine environments. The integrated cleanliness drive instilled practical habits of responsible outdoor behavior and environmental care.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"This adventure and environmental conservation initiative was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on January 28th, 2024, as one of their flagship events. Fast Trek 2.0 combined outdoor adventure with environmental responsibility, featuring a trekking expedition to the picturesque Kunagalu Betta Hills with an integrated cleanliness drive focused on environmental preservation.\\nThe event commenced at 7:30 AM with participants enthusiastically boarding buses to the trekking site, filled with excitement and anticipation for the day''s adventure. Prior to embarking on the trek, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were thoroughly disseminated to all attendees to ensure a secure and organized experience. Over 750 individuals participated in this memorable journey through breathtaking landscapes, creating a vibrant and energetic atmosphere throughout the event.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/PBpvQookHB5HbUcAi8YGs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9xB5GM6lnblD3KtNXGDSb","name":"Indi-Genuius:The India Quiz","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/eEUv3suXfngEwzwdtvAif.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"The Indi-Genius quiz competition successfully enhanced participants'' knowledge and appreciation of India''s cultural heritage, historical achievements, and contemporary developments. Students gained comprehensive insights into various aspects of Indian civilization while developing strong research skills, general awareness, and intellectual curiosity about their nation.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This intellectual competition was organized as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2023, featuring \"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz,\" a national-level quiz fest held from July 14th to 16th, 2023. The event provided students an opportunity to showcase their knowledge about India''s rich cultural heritage, history, geography, achievements, and contemporary developments through an engaging and competitive format.\\nThroughout the three-day quiz fest, participants engaged in rigorous rounds of questioning that tested their comprehensive understanding of Indian civilization, traditions, innovations, and contributions to global culture. The quiz was designed to celebrate India''s diversity and intellectual legacy while fostering healthy academic competition among students from across the nation. The Cultural Activities Team coordinated the event with support from associate sponsors and global education partners, ensuring high standards of organization and participant experience.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/COuxQPNDSU8fvI-CLEVl7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xNmEQTQAyJDsUkzrKXRWz","name":"Har Ghar Tiranga","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/VQ7ewjF9-5Rz0PdlLcepD.png"],"endDate":"2025-08-16","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Har Ghar Tiranga campaign successfully fostered patriotic fervor and national pride among participants while strengthening their emotional connection to India''s independence and sovereignty. Students gained deeper appreciation for the significance of the National Flag as a symbol of freedom, unity, and the sacrifices made by freedom fighters.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-15","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This patriotic initiative was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering as part of the nationwide Azadi Ka Mahotsav celebration, featuring the \"Har Ghar Tiranga\" (Tricolor in Every Home) campaign on August 15th, 2025. The program aimed to encourage every citizen to proudly display the National Flag and celebrate India''s spirit of freedom, unity, and independence.\\nThroughout this campaign, students actively participated by hoisting the Tiranga at their homes, workplaces, or other suitable locations on Independence Day, demonstrating their patriotic pride and connection to the nation. Participants captured photographs with the National Flag and uploaded them through the official Har Ghar Tiranga portal, becoming part of a massive nationwide movement celebrating India''s independence. The NSS coordinators facilitated the registration process, guided students through participation steps, and ensured proper documentation through designated Google Forms.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/eFf0nxl0sONZuGxRLCo08.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6OlcVPQsE-GC2hxEUipBQ","name":"Human-Elephant Conflict Awareness","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/FDkpGFtKP6uLWuLTW_6k2.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-31","duration":4,"outcomes":"The Human-Elephant Conflict Mitigation project successfully enhanced students'' understanding of wildlife conservation challenges while developing practical skills in conservation technology and AI applications. Participants gained valuable hands-on experience in designing and implementing real-world solutions to complex environmental problems, bridging the gap between theoretical engineering knowledge and practical conservation needs.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"This innovative wildlife conservation project was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering, focusing on \"Collaborate on Human-Elephant Conflict Mitigation\" in partnership with the Adavi Alert Foundation and the Gaja Raksha Project. The initiative aimed to address the critical environmental challenge of human-elephant conflicts through technology-driven solutions combining conservation science with engineering innovation.\\nThe project featured comprehensive technical components including elephant detection systems, early warning mechanisms, AI integration for pattern recognition, real-time alert systems, and animal-friendly design principles. Students engaged in developing and implementing technological solutions to prevent human-wildlife conflicts while ensuring the safety of both human communities and elephant populations in affected areas. This hands-on initiative provided participants with practical exposure to conservation technology and real-world wildlife management challenges.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/ZICrcPl1oB3eGt0OmTebv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"T5vECoD2DwxFKVauJeXVx","name":"Tanuja Screening","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/o3lKLxosHPbZg9OkiVJoY.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"The screening of \"Tanuja\" successfully inspired and motivated students by showcasing that determination and perseverance can overcome even the most daunting obstacles. Participants gained profound insights into the realities faced by underprivileged students aspiring for quality education while developing deeper empathy for socio-economic challenges that many students encounter in their educational journeys.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":"This inspirational film screening event was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering, featuring the live screening of \"Tanuja,\" a powerful documentary showcasing an extraordinary story of determination, perseverance, and triumph against adversity. The film narrates the remarkable journey of Tanuja, a young girl from a poor farmer''s family who traveled 400 kilometers on October 14, 2020, to participate in the NEET exam, ultimately securing a coveted medical seat in Karnataka.\\nThroughout the screening, students witnessed an inspiring narrative that went beyond individual achievement to highlight the crucial roles of supportive educators, journalists, and public representatives in enabling student success. The story particularly emphasized the remarkable contributions of Tanuja''s teacher Mr. Pradeep Ishwar, senior journalist Mr. Vishweshwar Bhatt, and public representatives who facilitated her timely arrival at the examination center. The documentary presented a holistic view of how community support, dedicated mentorship, and personal determination can overcome socio-economic barriers to education.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/5qgu9zZSDE1tCFxa7JH1I.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9vLhB4Dl2IhKUSmNyXTsd","name":"8th Mile Committee","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/qV7IZ15ikE-Pu7Ij5toKO.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":4,"outcomes":"The 8th Mile Committee initiative successfully fostered teamwork, responsibility, and professional skills among Core Team members and volunteers. Participants gained invaluable hands-on experience in event management, strategic planning, and community engagement while developing essential leadership qualities and organizational competencies that extend beyond academic learning.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-03","hoursSpent":30,"description":"This large-scale community service initiative was organized by the 8th Mile Committee at RV College of Engineering on January 5th, 2026, under the coordination of the Cultural Activities team. The event involved comprehensive planning and execution of the 8th Mile program, which focused on conducting meaningful community engagement activities with a strong emphasis on teamwork, leadership, and social impact.The Core Team members and volunteers demonstrated exceptional dedication, coordination, and perseverance throughout the initiative, playing instrumental roles in the smooth planning and execution of the event. Their collective efforts ensured effective time management, participant engagement, and overall success of the program. The team worked collaboratively to organize various aspects of the event, from logistics and resource management to participant coordination and on-ground implementation.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/ozl-k48PQ5BibNDdsV-gr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-lIwrN5oclT5Dh3T6Zkgj","name":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/CjGMW787eOwkhb5Fu0up9.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-10","duration":10,"outcomes":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge successfully enhanced students'' knowledge and awareness about India''s developmental trajectory, governance frameworks, and the ambitious vision of achieving developed nation status by 2047. Participants gained comprehensive insights into government initiatives, policy reforms, infrastructure projects, and socio-economic programs driving national transformation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This nationwide digital quiz initiative was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering in collaboration with the Government of India''s MyGov platform, featuring the \"Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge.\" The program aimed to engage youth in exploring India''s developmental progress, achievements, and the visionary roadmap for transforming India into a developed nation by 2047, aligning with national aspirations and the Viksit Bharat mission.\\nThe online quiz challenge provided students an accessible platform to test and enhance their knowledge about India''s socio-economic development, governance initiatives, infrastructure advancements, technological progress, and policy frameworks driving national transformation. Participants engaged with 10 carefully curated questions within a specified time limit, covering various dimensions of India''s developmental journey and future vision. The quiz was designed to promote awareness about government initiatives, flagship programs, and the collective efforts required to achieve developed nation status.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80bf051b-18e4-48a3-9763-14553e6d6542/rQjo4YIdjceYa7ZnaOPjs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"31","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr.Sujata D. Badiger","designation":" Counsellor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr. H. V. Ravish Aradhya ","designation":"Head of Department"},"evaluator2":{"name":" NCC/NSS officer/DSA/Dean CAT","designation":" "}}}', '2026-01-29 16:42:57.37433+00', '2026-02-01 10:32:02.755579+00'), ('7d341f3e-53c3-44a7-a644-baffbafcf0cc', 'ce447b70-4609-4a2b-9ccd-0fa0e654bb3b', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CH006","name":"Anirudh Sharma","period":"2022-2026","department":"Chemical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"XMswC5v-WeSPR00C9ADro","name":"Treasure Hunt 2023","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce447b70-4609-4a2b-9ccd-0fa0e654bb3b/psyxZJWXxHs1FYRO3foDo.png"],"endDate":"2023-01-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"I developed skills in teamwork, event planning, and sustainable thinking. The event showed how\\ninteractive challenges can spread awareness about environmental responsibility.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-01-25","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Helped organize a Treasure Hunt event designed around sustainability and eco-friendly\\nsolutions. Participants solved clues, completed problem-solving challenges, and performed\\ntasks that required practical application of environmental awareness and resource management.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under social outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce447b70-4609-4a2b-9ccd-0fa0e654bb3b/taRyDQH0vJVxnWgsMru13.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DCZopQSApwAIcULTKsUfF","name":"Matrubhasha Diwas 2023","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-02-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned how to organize large cultural events involving hundreds of participants. The activity\\nimproved my leadership, coordination, and appreciation of India’s multilingual and cultural\\ndiversity.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-11","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Actively organized Matrubhasha Diwas to promote linguistic diversity and cultural heritage.\\nThe event included a campus procession, cultural performances, ethnic dress displays, poetry,\\nmusic, and competitions like Rangoli, Capture the Moment, and Digitalize Your Heritage.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under social outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce447b70-4609-4a2b-9ccd-0fa0e654bb3b/Az7S9kV7mPbxpQR00xqan.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"taafw0zAqIvoxj_77PA74","name":"Treasure Hunt 2024","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce447b70-4609-4a2b-9ccd-0fa0e654bb3b/zjZpL7efwreyi8mUoGzNc.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained experience in event coordination, teamwork, and sustainability awareness. The\\nactivity helped me understand how gamified learning can effectively promote environmental\\nresponsibility and problem-solving skills.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-17","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Organized and coordinated the Treasure Hunt event focused on sustainable technologies and\\neco-friendly practices. The event involved multiple rounds including clue-based challenges,\\nproblem solving, and a final “Beg, Borrow, Steal” round that required participants to apply\\nsustainability concepts in a practical environment.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under social outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce447b70-4609-4a2b-9ccd-0fa0e654bb3b/ZNVXFxHLirNZrHvGhqhZH.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_zqyZuUZhqPqNINKHQCht","name":"Blood Donation Drive – Indian Red Cross Society","slNo":4,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce447b70-4609-4a2b-9ccd-0fa0e654bb3b/kUmCKxY_nQxV5XGrhEgwz.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of voluntary blood donation in supporting healthcare systems. The\\nactivity increased my awareness of medical safety, social responsibility, and how individual\\ncontributions can have a direct impact on saving lives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Participated in a voluntary blood donation drive organized by the Indian Red Cross Society,\\nKarnataka State Branch. The activity involved blood donation, and awareness about the\\nimportance of voluntary blood donation in saving lives. The collected blood units were used\\nfor emergency medical needs, supporting hospitals and patients requiring transfusions","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-02 07:37:45.094248+00', '2026-02-02 07:58:10.796416+00'), ('7e786f26-5c02-4802-9583-8fbce359d156', '23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC183","name":"Vineeth Kumar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"izgXRs9GepXIUK7ybrOjC","name":"INNOVATEX X E-SUMMIT","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/_oNDQhwwaF_y8HvKDzCfM.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-10","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Innovatex event successfully enhanced participants’ entrepreneurial thinking, creativity, and problem-solving skills. Through the elimination round, teams learned to ideate under time constraints and adapt their business concepts to diverse themes, strengthening their ability to think critically and innovatively. The pitching round improved participants’ presentation, communication, and persuasion skills while exposing them to real-world evaluation by industry professionals. Overall, the activity provided valuable insights into the startup ecosystem, encouraged teamwork and confidence, and motivated aspiring entrepreneurs to further refine and pursue their innovative ideas.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-09","hoursSpent":18,"description":"Innovatex, organized by E-Cell, featured a dynamic two-round competition aimed at fostering innovation and entrepreneurial spirit among participants. The elimination round challenged teams to demonstrate creativity, adaptability, and quick thinking by integrating three unique themes provided on prompt cards into their business ideas. This round served as a litmus test for the most innovative teams, with only the top contenders advancing to the pitching round.\\n\\nIn the pitching round, selected teams had the invaluable opportunity to present their business ideas to esteemed judges, Anshav Jain and Bhaskar M G. This phase allowed teams to showcase the merits of their innovation and persuade the judges that their ideas deserved recognition and support. Through Innovatex, E-Cell provided a platform for aspiring entrepreneurs to refine their ideas, receive feedback from industry experts, and gain exposure to the competitive landscape of entrepreneurship.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/LiNz9G37nkmWHNlF53C-X.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"x0_HD_iLEeeIys-Y-TaRv","name":"BUSINESS MARATHON X E-SUMMIT","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/6uj345VA4V4K4uBlJB_X9.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-10","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Business Marathon (BM) successfully strengthened participants’ entrepreneurial mindset, strategic thinking, and collaborative skills. By working through structured frameworks such as Empathy mapping, SWOT analysis, and the Lean Canvas model, participants gained hands-on experience in transforming ideas into viable business solutions. The overnight format enhanced teamwork, time management, and problem-solving under pressure. Additionally, alignment with the Sustainable Development Goals encouraged participants to develop socially responsible and innovation-driven solutions, bridging the gap between academic concepts and real-world business challenges.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-09","hoursSpent":18,"description":"The Entrepreneurship Cell''s Business Marathon (BM) is an overnight event promoting innovation, teamwork, and entrepreneurial skills. Teams work through phases like Empathy, SWOT, and Lean Canvas to solve a business problem, culminating in a final pitch. BM aligns with SDGs particularly Goal 8 (Decent Work and Economic Growth) and Goal 9 (Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure), driving participants to bridge theory and practice, build critical thinking, and create sustainable business solutions.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/3d36fzxAJYawMqvfAJL95.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JZZfDwZvMkgmRdCcg7VbR","name":"MERGERS AND ACQUISTIONS X E-SUMMIT","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/VLu3xG-mDPOy1fxup8Or7.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-10","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event enhanced participants’ understanding of mergers and acquisitions by exposing them to real-world corporate strategies and financial decision-making processes. Participants developed analytical and strategic thinking skills through case-based learning and expert interactions. The sessions strengthened their grasp of valuation, risk assessment, and operational integration in M&A deals, while also preparing them for leadership roles by improving their ability to evaluate complex business scenarios and make informed strategic decisions.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-09","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The “Mergers and Acquisitions” event, organized by E-Cell, provided an in-depth exploration of corporate transactions, focusing on mergers, acquisitions, and strategic alliances. Participants gained valuable insights into the strategic, financial, and operational dynamics of M&A activities through interactive sessions, case studies, and expert discussions, equipping them with the knowledge and skills to navigate complex transactions. Aligned with SDG 8 (Decent Work and Economic Growth), the event fostered critical business and financial skills, preparing students for leadership roles in the corporate world and promoting a deeper understanding of strategic decision-making.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/a115QpkViHuAzjGsuTq4U.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_KZX7i7yDuWk2p3TEPl6g","name":"Speaker Sessions X E-SUMMIT","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/OMJPxJCy6LqWItnpzhsKr.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-10","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event successfully inspired participants by exposing them to diverse perspectives in creativity, storytelling, content creation, and entrepreneurship. Attendees gained practical insights from industry experts, enhancing their motivation, confidence, and creative thinking abilities. The sessions encouraged personal and professional growth while equipping students with knowledge and inspiration to explore creative and entrepreneurial career paths.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-09","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Renowned speakers like Paritosh Anand, Arsh Goyal, Ishan Sharma, Arvind Prakash and San Kalra graced the event, sharing their expertise in content creation, story narration, motivation, and entrepreneurship. Their impactful presentations inspired and enlightened the audience, offering valuable insights into the realms of creativity, storytelling, and business. The event served as a platform for learning and empowerment, leaving attendees motivated and equipped with knowledge from these distinguished artists. The event became a rich source of inspiration, fostering learning and empowerment among attendees.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/ie6E8tVGIqWRT9HjaTaLR.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ot51NWjVX1snUM8gAiXPM","name":"INTEL HACKATHON X E-SUMMIT","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/naSZPDk5CXH9whb78iqdG.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Intel Hackathon successfully enhanced participants’ understanding of artificial intelligence through practical, hands-on learning experiences. Participants developed problem-solving, coding, and collaborative skills while gaining exposure to current AI trends and applications. The event fostered innovation-driven thinking, encouraged peer learning and networking, and equipped students with foundational skills necessary for future technological and industry-oriented advancements.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-08","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The Intel Hackathon, organized by E-Cell, was a pioneering workshop on artificial intelligence, centered on themes of open innovation and exploration. Participants, from beginners to AI enthusiasts, engaged in coding challenges, hands-on activities, and networking, delving into the latest AI trends and advancements.\\n\\nAligned with SDG 9 (Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure) and SDG 4 (Quality Education), this hackathon demonstrated E-Cell’s dedication to fostering a collaborative environment for learning and technological growth. It empowered participants to explore AI’s potential, contributing to the development of skills essential for future breakthroughs in technology and innovation.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/_CmYQf74uOXgReK7dIseN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zz-rezfJCAlTbO4rCY2PW","name":"PANEL DISCUSSION X E-SUMMIT","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/6FJJWPeSV8w7pZk39mB1e.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-09","duration":2,"outcomes":"The panel discussion enhanced participants’ understanding of emerging technology trends and their impact on entrepreneurship. Attendees gained strategic insights from industry experts, improving their awareness of innovation-driven opportunities and ethical considerations in the digital era. The session encouraged critical thinking, informed decision-making, and a forward-looking entrepreneurial mindset among participants.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-08","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The E-Summit 2024, a highly anticipated event in the tech and entrepreneurship domain, recently hosted a compelling panel discussion that brought together industry leaders, innovators, and experts. The panel, titled “Navigating the Future: Tech Trends and Entrepreneurial Opportunities,” delved into critical topics shaping the landscape of technology and entrepreneurship.\\n\\nThe E-Summit 2024 panel discussion provided a comprehensive and insightful exploration of key issues at the intersection of technology and entrepreneurship. Attendees gained valuable perspectives from industry leaders, fostering a deeper understanding of the challenges and opportunities that lie ahead in the digital age. The event successfully contributed to the ongoing dialogue surrounding innovation, ethics, and the future of technology-driven entrepreneurship.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/1rnQ-a0LMPSnjEnlndK1G.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"V4uZQHxrmYQoX9Crd_qmp","name":"STARTUP SAGA X EMBARK","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/uOzzSIIMA0X6pfx_RG0BV.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Two-Day Innovation Odyssey successfully strengthened participants’ entrepreneurial mindset by providing hands-on exposure to the complete startup lifecycle. Students enhanced their creativity, leadership, and problem-solving skills while gaining practical insights into social entrepreneurship, pitching, funding, branding, and scaling. The event fostered innovation-driven thinking, mentorship-based learning, and confidence among participants, equipping them to transform ideas into viable and impactful ventures.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-07-11","hoursSpent":18,"description":"A Two-Day Innovation Odyssey is a dynamic event designed to fuel the entrepreneurial spirit, with a focus on building impactful ventures through two flagship events: Startup Saga and Vision Venture.\\n\\nThe Startup Saga provides a unique platform for our budding entrepreneurs to showcase their innovative and socially sound ideas with the theme “Support Sphere: Social Entrepreneurship Saga.” By doing so, we helped to foster a culture of creativity, problem-solving, and leadership that will equip our students with the skills necessary to excel in the competitive world of entrepreneurship. Startup Saga immerses participants in the startup journey, offering workshops, panels, and mentorship sessions where founders and industry experts share insights on pitching, funding, branding, and scaling, aimed at guiding attendees from idea to launch.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/WCCSXz6I7liPbV-HDugyb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xUD-79TgoKRe3sSVZeie1","name":"VISION VENTURE X EMBARK","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/8M9GcAC-GkpWyFTTdRKUN.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Vision Venture successfully enabled participants to develop practical, user-centered, and sustainable solutions to real-world techno-social challenges. The activity strengthened participants’ skills in ideation, prototyping, testing, and product development while encouraging innovation aligned with sustainability goals. Through expert mentorship and hands-on learning, students gained confidence and technical insight to transform innovative ideas into viable, market-ready ventures.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-07-11","hoursSpent":18,"description":"A Two-Day Innovation Odyssey is a dynamic event designed to fuel the entrepreneurial spirit, with a focus on building impactful ventures through two flagship events: Startup Saga and Vision Venture.\\n\\nVision Venture provided a platform for all development enthusiasts to create sustainable solutions for techno-social problems worldwide. With its theme of “Eco Innovate,” the initiative inspires participants to leverage their product development skills and new technologies to solve societal challenges. Vision Venture, the product development challenge, empowers participants to bring their ideas to life by moving through ideation, prototyping, and testing phases, all while receiving expert guidance to create user-centered, sustainable, and market-ready solutions. Embark on Vision Venture promises a transformative experience for innovators looking to turn their visions into tangible ventures.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/08MNG3cC_fkRgQ2hRlpYe.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"x8CuRqtVf_9E_klbhxrcy","name":"World Entrepreneurship Day","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/FkG0dVF0x1k2yUcgW44lw.png"],"endDate":"2024-08-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The celebration of World Entrepreneurs’ Day successfully inspired students by providing real-world insights into the startup ecosystem through expert interactions. Participants gained practical understanding of entrepreneurial challenges, leadership, and innovation while being motivated to pursue entrepreneurial initiatives. The event strengthened students’ confidence, resilience, and passion for entrepreneurship, fostering a vibrant culture of innovation within the campus.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-08-21","hoursSpent":12,"description":"World Entrepreneurs’ Day was celebrated at RV College of Engineering with great enthusiasm with the event organized by the vibrant E-Cell RVCE. The event brought together aspiring entrepreneurs, industry veterans, and students to foster a spirit of innovation and enterprise within the campus. A key event highlight was a panel discussion featuring Arvind Prakash Singh, Founder and CEO of SuperBolt, and Shreesha Sridhar, Chairperson of ProjectX Labs. These distinguished guests shared their invaluable insights into the startup ecosystem, discussing the challenges and opportunities faced by modern entrepreneurs. Their experiences and advice gave students practical knowledge and inspiration, igniting a deeper passion for entrepreneurship. The session was informative and motivational, reinforcing the importance of resilience, innovation, and leadership in the entrepreneurial journey.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/ACrfBU2LX14XXL3tIdOkU.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"r47xjVJXobrJJ4usSJjGr","name":"Exuberance","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/eA7wWBMfxHKilE5-jO5o5.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-18","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event successfully strengthened participants’ strategic thinking, negotiation, and real-time decision-making abilities through hands-on business simulations. Participants enhanced their teamwork, adaptability, and problem-solving skills while gaining confidence in pitching and public speaking. Exposure to market dynamics and networking with peers and industry experts further improved their business acumen and preparedness for entrepreneurial and corporate challenges.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-01-17","hoursSpent":18,"description":"Exuberance, Chaos to Creation was an intense business-oriented event designed to test strategic thinking, negotiation skills, and decision-making in real-time scenarios. Exuberance provided participants with a real-world business experience, enhancing their strategic thinking, negotiation, and decision-making skills. Teams developed persuasive pitches, bid strategically for assets, and built strong business models under pressure. The event improved problem-solving, teamwork, and adaptability while boosting confidence in public speaking and presentations. Participants also gained insights into market dynamics and entrepreneurial challenges.\\n\\nAdditionally, it fostered networking opportunities, connecting them with peers and industry experts. Overall, Exuberance sharpened business acumen and nurtured future entrepreneurs.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/23cc24eb-af00-4213-ad8a-674838379e80/7ot7W8kPBePvH1-1dTjr7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 06:03:50.678474+00', '2026-01-30 20:08:38.570762+00'), ('81b68648-e1f7-4743-9509-cbcd71edcbf3', '256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CH024","name":"RAJESHWARI","period":"2022-2026","department":"Chemical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"LHrXoRXM5awjPApniYUgF","name":"FASTREK ","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/661-MYZX039bjWgFoixIu.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project aimed to provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event began at 7:30 AM with participants traveling to Huthridurga Betta, where safety instructions were given. The trek was successfully conducted from 9:30 AM to 1:00 PM, and breakfast and lunch were provided at the location. The event concluded by early evening, leaving participants with a memorable experience","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was to\\nprovide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from\\nheart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the\\nparticipants boarded the bus to the trek location with great\\nenthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided t o all along with basic\\ninformation o f the event. The trek was a great success a s all the\\nparticipants had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of\\nHuthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very\\nmemorable journey. Breakfast and lunch was provided at the trek location of all the participants","aicteMapping":"Participated in trek ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/u309_vAWu3y0UshYQd69T.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1 ","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RJVyxV_Fnt_sPSm_aP1k6","name":"Graduation day volunteering ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/8Riq1fqkheXeFd3QUi9bT.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-08-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating as a SPARK volunteer for the 14th Graduation Day facilitated the development\\nof essential leadership and logistical skills. I mastered crowd and queue management in\\na high-pressure environment, ensuring the event’s success. This experience enhanced my\\nprofessional communication while contributing to a significant institutional milestone.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-03","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The 14th Graduation Day at RV College of Engineering was a prestigious ceremony held on\\nAugust 3, 2024, to honor the hard work and academic excellence of the graduating batch.\\nServing as a SPARK volunteer, I was integral to the event''s execution, focusing on professional\\ncrowd and queue management. These responsibilities were critical for maintaining order\\nduring such a high-profile milestone. The experience enhanced my ability to handle logistical\\nchallenges effectively while contributing to a seamless and celebratory atmosphere for students\\nand their families.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to RV college of engineering ","pointsEarned":16,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/ao97W3lkZsRtFsp1y4wno.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9Z84T3FYe_TlOb1IHBdQq","name":"Treasure Hunt ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/q5GGAQw7LX9Gy6i8vDq7_.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of the Treasure Hunt was the cultivation of critical soft skills, as the multi-round format required teams to demonstrate exceptional speed, accuracy, and quick decision-making under pressure. By navigating complex riddles and campus-wide physical challenges, participants significantly enhanced their collaborative problem-solving and logical reasoning abilities. Furthermore, the event successfully fostered a high level of student engagement and campus spirit, bringing together 360 students for a unique experiential learning activity that balanced competitive play with thematic entertainment.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-16","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Treasure Hunt - Squid Game Edition was a dynamic, multi-round competition that engaged 120 teams of three members each in a day of logic and physical challenges. Organized by the club Raag and inaugurated by its President, Utkarsh Nijhawan, the event began with an online preliminary quiz focused on logic and theme-based questions to shortlist participants for the on-campus stages. From there, 60 participants moved into the core Treasure Hunt, which featured five sub-rounds spread across the campus involving riddles and clue-chasing. The competition intensified as 20 teams were tasked with collecting 20 unique items under tight time constraints, leading to a final Squid Game-themed round for the top 7 teams to determine the winners.","aicteMapping":"Participated in Treasure Hunt","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/7bENnYPz6rZ8KFo6hG6Hd.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8VHGvlahUcTXb_DZfOUCR","name":"Utsarga Marathon ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-04-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of this initiative are deeply impactful, as the proceeds are channeled into\\nproviding scholarships and essential medical aid for underprivileged children and those with\\nspecialized health conditions. By mobilizing thousands of participants, the event fosters a\\nstrong sense of social responsibility and empathy among the youth, creating a ripple effect of\\nawareness regarding rural education and healthcare gaps. Ultimately, the marathon succeeds\\nin transforming physical activity into tangible social change, empowering vulnerable children\\nwith the resources necessary for a brighter, more equitable future.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-04-02","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is a signature philanthropic event organized by the NSS unit of RVCE,\\naimed at uniting the community through the spirit of fitness and social service. Guided by the\\npowerful motto, \"Help a Child—Change the World,\" the marathon serves as a high-energy\\nplatform where students, faculty, and professional runners participate in 5K and 10K events.\\nBeyond the race itself, the marathon acts as a major fundraising vehicle designed to support\\nmarginalized communities, particularly focusing on child welfare, education, and healthcare\\ninitiatives for those in need.","aicteMapping":"Help child ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/dd_0jp370L4cYursxbOqf.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"a5KCyhC7_O4fKEuhRiHEo","name":"Treasure Hunt ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/Zt_VFPvIeqh8z1ZOMVjdv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-01-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The events successfully sparked heightened awareness and knowledge regarding eco-friendly solutions among the participants. Students significantly enhanced their problem-solving skills, creativity, and resourcefulness by applying their knowledge in dynamic settings. The competitive structure of these hunts also fostered a practical understanding of sustainability and required participants to demonstrate speed, accuracy, and quick decision-making under pressure","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-01-25","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The first round of the Treasure Hunt event centered on Sustainable Technologies concluded successfully, sparking heightened awareness and knowledge about eco-friendly solutions. The second round, a Hunt using clues, challenged teams to apply their knowledge in a dynamic setting, enhancing problem-solving skills. In the third round, \"Beg, Borrow, Steal,\" students demonstrated creativity and resourcefulness by finding sustainable solutions and procuring necessary items, fostering a practical understanding of sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Participated in Treasure Hunt ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/qts8PTEkwqgL8OYafn9UU.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oYQxi4wTcBAXSnwaBFZ5G","name":"Treasure Hunt","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/AU5s45TCM-j8cfqjEn0Na.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants enthusiastically delved into clues and challenges, showcasing a keen\\ninterest in sustainable practices. The event effectively combined fun and\\neducation, fostering a sense of responsibility towards the environment among\\nparticipants. The overall event successfully blended education, teamwork, and\\nenvironmental consciousness","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-01-17","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The first round o f the Treasure Hunt event centered o n Sustainable Technologies\\nconcluded successfully, sparking heightened awareness and knowledge about eco-friendly solutions. The second round, a Hunt using clues, challenged teams t o\\napply their knowledge i n a dynamic setting, enhancing problem-solving skills.\\nIn the third round, \"Beg, Borrow, Steal,\" students demonstrated creativity and\\nresourcefulness by finding sustainable solutions and procuring necessary items.\\nfostering a practical understanding of sustainability. The event was totally\\nadventurous and exciting which gave an fair opportunity t o the participants. The\\nlast round was the most thrilling one as you have the time running behind you\\nand you have t o collect the following items. This event was also one of the first\\nevents for the freshers as they participated a lot and were joyful","aicteMapping":"Participated in Treasure Hunt ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FpcrCgY6CYdZoLsk0t5x0","name":"UNCHAINED","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/codtAvRiGzklaCMNNg0_8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"The “UNCHAINED: Say No to Drugs” event successfully raised awareness about the harmful effects of drug abuse and encouraged students to adopt a healthy, addiction-free lifestyle. The program promoted informed decision-making, empathy, and social responsibility through expert addresses, performances, and visual storytelling. Active participation from students, faculty, and dignitaries strengthened community engagement and reinforced a collective commitment to building a safer, drug-free campus environment.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Say No to Drugs” was an awareness program organized to educate students and staff about the dangers of drug abuse and the importance of leading a healthy, addiction-free life. The event began with a formal inauguration and lamp lighting by dignitaries, followed by insightful addresses from the Dean of Student Affairs and the Principal. A musical performance and an informative video effectively conveyed the emotional and social impact of drug addiction. The program concluded with motivating remarks from the Dean of Cultural Affairs, reinforcing the message of awareness, resilience, and collective responsibility toward building a drug-free community.\\n","aicteMapping":"Organised unchained ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/xHanIoydWYireKe1DMb62.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pSCoY48NqEL43ThjcViSO","name":"Matrubhasha Diwas ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/V6GQil8et_dn5U1X0yPOD.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Matrubhasha Diwas fostered a strong sense of unity, cultural pride, and inclusivity across the RVCE community. The event enhanced cultural awareness, strengthened inter-club collaboration, and encouraged active participation from students, faculty, and staff. Its vibrant performances and engaging activities created a memorable experience, reinforcing the spirit of togetherness and appreciation for India’s diverse linguistic and cultural heritage.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-08","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Matrubhasha Diwas was celebrated on 8 April 2025 with the theme “Unity in Diversity,” bringing together students, faculty, and staff in vibrant ethnic attire representing India’s cultural richness. The event began with a grand cultural parade led by the RAAG core team and administrative dignitaries, followed by the ceremonial lighting of the lamp. The campus was beautifully decorated, creating a festive and inclusive atmosphere. Cultural performances by Alaap, Footprints, CARV, and EvokE showcased music, dance, theatre, and fashion reflecting India’s linguistic diversity. Exciting competitions such as Mr. & Ms. Best Dressed and Best Dressed Department added enthusiasm and participation. The celebration concluded with a lively DJ Night, marking a memorable and unifying cultural experience for the RVCE community","aicteMapping":"Organised the Event","pointsEarned":18,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/Ai5IVxgL8HMqFVLavA_rA.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"VqLf-kw0QPwkErqCSUrSG","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":9,"place":"GOVERMENT SCHOOLS ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/DywEu3ppva8PlACPPMH5i.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-08-06","duration":75,"outcomes":"Project Pustak significantly improves rural education by reducing the financial burden on families and boosting student enrollment. By providing essential supplies like textbooks and backpacks, the initiative enhances student confidence and academic performance, ultimate arrowing the urban-rural divide and empowering the next generation with the tools necessary for long-term success.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Project Pustak is an inspiring initiative dedicated to equipping underprivileged students in rural areas with essential school supplies, fostering a conducive learning environment. Spearheaded by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in partnership with the Pranay Foundation, funds were raised through generous contributions of 100 or 250 from donors. The second phase of the project, executed in Devanahalli and Bidadi, Karnataka, saw faculty members and volunteer actively distributing educational materials such as textbooks, stationery, and backpacks. Thi ffort, widely recognized for its impact, gained significant media attention, underscoring its transformative role in empowering underprivileged children and enhancing educational opportunities in the region.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/_9NdQnVHFptRTU7J56n5c.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3fGQoy8w6w-m65ybOnDcX","name":"Paper Drive ","slNo":10,"place":"LOCAL APARTMENTS ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/qbnwbariXufF9UzeAyxnb.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Paper Drive led to the successful collection of a large quantity of reusable and recyclable materials, which were directed toward charities and NGOs to support their initiatives. The event increased awareness about community service and sustainability while fostering a strong sense of social responsibility and teamwork among student volunteers and local residents.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":5,"description":"On 23rd June 2024, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Paper Drive across Bangalore with the participation of over 400 student volunteers. The students collected books, papers, and waste materials from homes and businesses to support charities and NGOs. The drive successfully promoted community involvement, social responsibility, and awareness about collective efforts toward social causes.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contributing to NGO''s","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/qk58MsniPKEh_LYm1BQ8M.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tGfZWvLqM465XKbgEWU1C","name":"Induction Program","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Camous","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/8mhqxth6GavrB1FY2BdmS.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-08-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Induction Program organized by the RAAG Club of RVCE led to several positive outcomes for first-year students and the campus community. It helped freshers become familiar with the club’s culture, values, and opportunities, easing their transition into college life and fostering early interaction between juniors and seniors. The program encouraged active participation in extracurricular activities by highlighting leadership, teamwork, and personal development opportunities through RAAG. Its structured and engaging format increased student enthusiasm, strengthened community spirit, and enriched the overall campus experience at RVCE.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-29","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Induction Program organized by the RAAG Club of RVE played a vital role in helping first-year students smoothly transition into college life by familiarizing them with RAAG’s vision, activities, and working culture. It fostered strong interaction between juniors and seniors, encouraging mentorship, collaboration, and a supportive campus environment. The program highlighted the importance of balancing academics with extracurricular involvement while increasing awareness and enthusiasm for sports, cultural events, e-sports, and social initiatives. Additionally, it motivated freshers to explore leadership roles and teamwork, contributing to the development of communication, confidence, and organizational skills. Overall, the induction strengthened community spirit, enhanced campus vibrancy, and reinforced RAAG’s commitment to holistic student growth.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to RV college of Engineering ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256547a0-ca6b-477b-9aeb-f99861184cb1/fqK1_yl1BT1vAZeDcYy6r.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 05:13:01.36829+00', '2026-01-31 05:16:12.019882+00'), ('821c0d5f-cf43-455e-9caa-7a0b478dcc82', '5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS230","name":"VIBHAV SIMHA G","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"-JR6TqY3bcZGhrTdHSQUU","name":"Project Pustak 2023 – Rotaract Club, RVCE","slNo":1,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/a8SGMXGvdDmKtduZysS2y.png"],"endDate":"2023-01-31","duration":31,"outcomes":"Improved availability of textbooks and reading material at recipient schools; direct engagement with local education outreach; small but tangible positive effect on students’ learning resources.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-01-01","hoursSpent":80,"description":"Project Pustak was a Rotaract-led initiative to collect and distribute books and study-materials to under-resourced schools and students. Volunteers coordinated collection drives on campus, sorted and categorized donated books, and organized distribution to partner schools. The activity focused on improving access to reading material and supporting the learning environment for younger students.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/x-zLVfLk7O22MaZJDauwO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"F5hiFukPXwGcF-awjtYGa","name":"FAST TREK – Rotaract Club, RVCE","slNo":2,"place":"Hutridurga Betta","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/46gpLMAVSKIWswo-2cylf.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Raised funds / awareness for the specified social cause; volunteers gained event-management and field logistics experience; participants received AICTE activity points and recognition.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast-Trek was a Rotaract flagship outing combining community development goals and fundraising/awareness. Volunteers participated in the trek, supported logistics, and the club used the event to raise funds and awareness for underprivileged children (financial aid). The Rotaract documentation lists participants and their points and describes the project purpose and logistics.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/AkR4zNI3l7c0rEXx0kWhL.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6R7W87tZm8O3VRiXldfv_","name":"Organizing Team - Hack4Soc 2.0 – National Hackathon for Social Solutions (IEEE)","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/FUB70OOattOXj0bEqggxU.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":2,"outcomes":"Successful execution of a national-scale hackathon; platform for student innovation and social-impact prototypes; organisers earned 25 AICTE points and event experience in large-event coordination.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-03","hoursSpent":80,"description":"Hack4Soc 2.0 was a 24-hour national hackathon focused on social impact solutions (verticals mentioned included Generative AI, Fintech, Blockchain). As an organiser you were part of the core team handling event planning, logistics, participant coordination, judge coordination, and on-the-ground execution. The event documents describe goals such as leveraging technology for societal benefit and the event summary, and the organisers’ list names the core team and points allocation.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":25,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/b3xo-nnarIwyUxI0FyaLS.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"l0hEdr9E168k-LB9sDAr6","name":"Student Volunteer – Advance Design and Analysis Techniques (workshop / event)","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/cWWCYl-q7gppEcn5HgjCf.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"Hands-on exposure to advanced engineering design topics; improved event-support and technical facilitation skills","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-15","hoursSpent":50,"description":"Volunteer role at a technical workshop titled \"Advance Design and Analysis Techniques\". Duties likely included session support, registration desk, logistics, and assisting speakers or labs.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/pEtMmVoG35iHpfbajb1qg.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"snZtVc44j1ghXIxV6Lzmi","name":"Crack The Career Code – LinkedIn and Beyond (Career counselling / networking session)","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/qbYDBD4FkeOafPzLeKODR.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/cg1N6yDwLiPLi-DToKPj3.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improved career-readiness for attendees, practical LinkedIn tips and networking guidance, volunteer experience in career-event logistics","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":80,"description":"A career-counselling session focused on LinkedIn use and professional networking. Volunteer responsibilities usually include coordination, participant onboarding, and logistical support. The event aimed to improve employability awareness and practical professional networking skills.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/Bu_CAFMsF9yIRvkSzDI7H.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9WeaEx-rvGlNrwosoZPZb","name":"DHI Day – Team DHI, Dept. of AI&ML (Data Remix - Clash of Companies)","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/3w61Y_Gz9wq35z632-87y.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Practical exposure to data analysis and business-innovation thinking, judged presentations, bridging technical skills with sustainability-oriented problem solving","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":24,"description":"DHI Day combined an industry speaker session (GE Healthcare) and a student competition \"Data Remix - Clash of Companies\". Students used provided datasets to create visualizations and business innovations aligned with sustainability goals; judging panels included faculty","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/Ms-J4swkOC1YXTxJpf3TB.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oO9W4Ha2imm86EeTt93nY","name":"Project Pustak – Rotaract Club, RVCE (May edition)","slNo":7,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/xWqypDv4LXBM5uXrmPdDM.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased access to educational resources in beneficiary communities; event coordination experience","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":24,"description":"Similar to the earlier Project Pustak, this Rotaract-led edition involved collection, curation and distribution of books and educational material to needy students/schools. Volunteers handled logistics and distribution on the scheduled date.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/oUMTfOpX4vYtQg71KqcUp.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qAzCB7lddp-8LViefjahs","name":"India Quiz – General Knowledge Quiz on India (QuizCorp / Under The Peepal Tree 2024)","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/15yovCIXflEB8z76vW1M4.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Broader general-knowledge exposure","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":15,"description":"Participation in a national-level quiz fest (Under The Peepal Tree 2024) focused on general knowledge about India.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/ZafZPCCNoeI6DmTDFwJNb.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BKidCAP_5pMsaxEMykbEu","name":"Student Volunteer – CSITSS 2024 (8th International Conference on Computational Systems and IT for Sustainable Solutions)","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/iXL2BsXGeNe_RM-6sxuh0.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"Conference operations experience; networking with researchers and practitioners; improved event-management and technical coordination skills","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-07","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Volunteering for an international technical conference involved tasks such as documentation, website support, session coordination, registration desk, and on-site logistics across three days. The conference documentation states volunteers supported the conference for months (website team) and lists the points assigned to volunteers. The volunteer role provided exposure to large-scale academic event management and technical program execution.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/5Qkl6pZ5P86s9irtagRuW.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eh2Uck_0CW25GUjWHcXLh","name":"Government School Visit – Sattva Club, RVCE (volunteering to teach art and craft)","slNo":10,"place":"Govt School Forest Layout Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/CPv6bWr0U1rnJo-XSqwLN.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-01-20","duration":3,"outcomes":"Direct educational engagement with government-school children; improvement in students’ creative skills and classroom participation","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-18","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Sattva Club organized visits to a government school to volunteer in teaching art and craft activities. Volunteers planned simple lessons and engaged students in hands-on activities aimed at creativity, confidence-building and encouraging school participation.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/I1YaBxQa3LUHt8c8eGxS3.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ah2STfyRh4HMarRvaHfYq","name":"Auction to Analysis – IEEE Computer Society, RVCE (Data Analysis competition based on Mock IPL Auction)","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/pGhVck16vnHVpVrOQkp5O.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/CFbEE4-grASLvWxdNyfUk.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-11","duration":3,"outcomes":"Encouraged practical data-analysis skills and visualization techniques among participants; awarded prizes and saplings given to participants as part of a sustainability message","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-04-09","hoursSpent":80,"description":"Auction to Analysis was a data-analysis competition simulating an IPL-style mock auction. The event aimed to promote data-driven decision-making, strategic thinking, and presentation skills. Rounds included a quiz/trivia round, auction-bidding and strategy rounds, and a data-presentation round where teams used tools like Tableau and Power BI to present insights","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c53c607-dbef-4fc5-aa4f-c62ea7b76d08/UiScHQ121Eu_jnkVqC9I9.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":" ","designation":" "},"evaluator1":{"name":" ","designation":" "},"evaluator2":{"name":" ","designation":" "}}}', '2026-02-01 16:11:17.86752+00', '2026-02-01 17:56:48.149377+00'), ('8564f20e-5018-4dd3-a789-a5edbf72b324', 'c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI048","name":"Sayyam Jain","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"88S_SZRK1s_2xBhHUPiV0","name":"SPARK VOLUNTEERS FOR GRADUATION CEREMONY","slNo":1,"place":"Poornima Palace","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/bVUhpuFoigTF0hj3E3sCZ.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The volunteering activity resulted in the smooth and well-organized conduct of the graduation ceremony, ensuring a memorable experience for students, parents, faculty, and dignitaries. Volunteers gained valuable experience in event management, leadership, communication, and coordination skills. The initiative strengthened students’ sense of community service and institutional involvement while contributing to the successful completion of one of the most important events in the college calendar.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":32,"description":"SPARK Volunteers for the Graduation Ceremony is an institutional service activity in which students actively contributed to the successful organization and management of the college graduation event. The volunteering initiative involved providing support in various arrangements such as coordinating with staff, guiding graduates and guests, managing seating and entry procedures, assisting in stage and event logistics, and ensuring smooth execution of the ceremony. Through this activity, volunteers played an important role in maintaining discipline, hospitality, and overall event flow, showcasing teamwork, responsibility, and dedication towards supporting a significant academic milestone for the institution.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/sJGcq_DFlbYg_xSHTvZIw.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_x2ytgiemqobidzfQNTkg","name":"NSS UTSARGA MARATHON","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/O0gN53tuZyFuKf4guf8JS.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation promoted physical fitness, social awareness, and empathy. It provided an opportunity to contribute to a meaningful cause, reinforced the value of community service, and inspired a sense of responsibility toward supporting underprivileged children through collective action.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":40,"description":"I participated in UTSARGA ’24, a charity marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The event was conducted with the objective of supporting underprivileged children through a social cause–oriented initiative. It aimed to create awareness and encourage community involvement in contributing toward the welfare and development of children in need.\\n\\nThe marathon successfully promoted the importance of physical fitness along with social responsibility. It provided an opportunity for students to actively engage in a meaningful cause while fostering values such as compassion, empathy, and collective service. Participating in this event was a valuable experience, as it reinforced the significance of contributing toward positive social impact through community-driven efforts.","aicteMapping":"Public Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/Hw4lBUMDZ39TXtj-UY5NW.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BKHsK2w78NoccZslx7qSU","name":"INTEL HACKATHON X E-SUMMIT","slNo":3,"place":"DTL Huddle","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/E4U7R1lCZ7iHRo1ycDkjE.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants gained practical exposure to AI tools and concepts, enhanced their technical and problem-solving skills, and developed a deeper understanding of innovation-driven\\ntechnologies essential for future careers.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-08","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Intel Hackathon, organized by E-Cell, was a pioneering workshop focused on artificial intelligence, emphasizing open innovation and exploration. Participants ranging from beginners to AI enthusiasts engaged in coding challenges, hands-on activities, and collaborative learning sessions. The hackathon introduced participants to emerging AI trends, practical applications, and real-world problem-solving using technology. Aligned with Sustainable Development Goal 9 (Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure) and Sustainable Development Goal 4 (Quality Education), the event highlighted E-Cell’s\\ncommitment to fostering technological learning and innovation.","aicteMapping":"Innovation / Technical Skill","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/T21I4w3cOwVOu8V_3pGe-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"X9qC347nKBgHl1A4LUVrs","name":"FISTFULL","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/MoqXKIF4Ds6umV_Ro9xU_.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"Hunger Relief: A significant quantity of food grains was collected to support individuals and communities in need.\\nMass Participation: Over 1,750 students actively contributed, demonstrating strong social responsibility.\\nAwareness Creation: Increased awareness about food insecurity and the power of collective action.\\nCommunity Welfare: Strengthened the spirit of compassion, generosity, and solidarity among students.\\nPositive Social Impact: Showcased how small individual contributions can lead to meaningful societal change.\\nInstitutional Commitment: Reinforced RVCE’s dedication to community service and humanitarian initiatives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fistfull was an impactful food donation initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, aimed at combating hunger and supporting community welfare. The initiative encouraged students to contribute toward a noble cause by donating 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, emphasizing how small individual efforts can collectively create a large social impact. Daily collections were carried out at the Civil Department, and the drive received an overwhelming response from the student community. Over the course of the event, more than 1,750 students participated, resulting in the collection of approximately 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal. The initiative highlighted the importance of empathy, generosity, and collective responsibility toward addressing food insecurity. Fistfull successfully reinforced RVCE’s commitment to social service, community welfare, and solidarity through meaningful student engagement.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/AQFzX3ZWpUhji4m-b9k54.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YJVS3sPgy2QkEitohSUIf","name":"UPTOWN JUNK","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/ZKZPYLc1uoVAL6IQCq1QD.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Environmental Awareness: Increased awareness about sustainability, recycling, and responsible waste management.\\nBehavioral Change: Encouraged participants to adopt reuse and recycling practices in everyday life.\\nCreative Thinking: Fostered innovation by transforming waste materials into useful and artistic creations.\\nStudent Engagement: High participation and enthusiasm through interactive activities and the treasure hunt.\\nTeamwork & Collaboration: Promoted teamwork, problem-solving, and time management skills among participants.\\nPositive Impact: Reinforced the idea that sustainable practices can be engaging, practical, and impactful.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-28","hoursSpent":32,"description":"Uptown Junk was a creative and engaging sustainability initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of promoting environmental awareness and responsible waste management practices. The event aimed to demonstrate that sustainability can be both impactful and enjoyable by encouraging participants to view waste as a valuable resource rather than something disposable. The initiative involved hands-on activities where participants transformed discarded and recyclable materials into innovative art forms and useful creations. This creative approach helped reinforce the importance of reuse and recycling in reducing environmental harm. To further enhance engagement, a fun-filled treasure hunt was organized across the campus, where teams solved riddles related to sustainability while racing against time. Uptown Junk successfully brought students together in a collaborative and energetic environment, inspiring them to adopt eco-friendly practices in their daily lives. The event highlighted how creativity, teamwork, and enthusiasm can contribute to building a greener and more sustainable future.\\n","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/2IYwkwfP4puLvUGpWlWP7.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZNvziBIVy1PjxdZJ0bMc7","name":"NSS UTSARGA MARATHON","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/sGfh6Ti6yI_v08Lg_qFkH.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation promoted physical fitness, social awareness, and empathy. It provided an opportunity to contribute to a meaningful cause, reinforced the value of community service, and inspired a sense of responsibility toward supporting underprivileged children through collective action.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-04","hoursSpent":60,"description":"I participated in UTSARGA ’24, a charity marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The event was conducted with the objective of supporting underprivileged children through a social cause–oriented initiative. It aimed to create awareness and encourage community involvement in contributing toward the welfare and development of children in need.\\n\\nThe marathon successfully promoted the importance of physical fitness along with social responsibility. It provided an opportunity for students to actively engage in a meaningful cause while fostering values such as compassion, empathy, and collective service. Participating in this event was a valuable experience, as it reinforced the significance of contributing toward positive social impact through community-driven efforts.","aicteMapping":"Public Awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/3UTCOiUfwRzDg2rJIxPd6.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4ZjK4oXYknsxpf4ZmMG0L","name":"FEMALE FOETICIDE AWARENESS","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/Sv3N1cdHWKAu0zIgPWy8N.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased Awareness: Successfully raised awareness about the social, legal, and moral consequences of female foeticide among participants and the public.\\nCommunity Engagement: Over 350 individuals actively participated, demonstrating collective responsibility and social unity.\\nPromotion of Gender Equality: Reinforced the importance of valuing girl children and promoting gender equality in society.\\nSocial Sensitization: Encouraged participants to reflect on and challenge societal norms related to gender discrimination.\\nStudent Development: Helped students develop social responsibility, leadership, empathy, and civic awareness.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":60,"description":"On the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon with the objective of creating awareness about the grave issue of female foeticide and promoting the value of the girl child in society. The walkathon aimed to educate the public on gender equality and encourage collective responsibility in preventing discrimination against female children.\\nThe event witnessed over 350 participants, including students, faculty members, and supportive parents, who came together to stand against gender-based violence and injustice even before birth. The walkathon commenced in the early hours from the RVCE campus and was marked by impactful placards, thought-provoking messages, and powerful slogans that effectively conveyed the importance of protecting and empowering girl children.\\nThe walkathon served as a strong platform to spread awareness, inspire social change, and reinforce the message of equality, dignity, and respect for women. The active participation and unity displayed during the event reflected a shared commitment toward building a more inclusive society","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/EK9veNsAzEQv8qi54KkBI.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gpFwfWZ51NMbJf1-2lJDN","name":"FISTFULL","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/xp-BxMsORLMg3-Gu81QNi.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity achieved significant success with the active involvement of 2,146 students, showcasing strong collective commitment towards social welfare. A total of 4,370 kilograms of rice and 2,516 kilograms of dal were collected and distributed to multiple beneficiaries, including Hanuman Temple mass feeding program, Pruthvi Foundation (Blind Boys Hostel), Amrutavani Vidh Seva Samithi, Sai Ashraya Hospital, Sai Satguna Sangraha Trust School, Nele Foundation, and nearby anganwadis. The initiative provided vital nutritional support to underprivileged communities and institutions, contributing towards better health and food security. Overall, Fistful created a meaningful social impact while fostering empathy, teamwork, and civic responsibility among students.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fistful was a standalone community service initiative conducted with the objective of combating food insecurity and supporting vulnerable sections of society through collective student participation. Supported by Rotary Bangalore Spandana, the project was carried out under the Community Service avenue with a focus on “Fighting Disease” by ensuring nutritional assistance to those in need. The initiative followed a simple yet impactful model where every participating student contributed either 5 kilograms of rice or 2 kilograms of dal. By uniting individual contributions, the activity transformed into a large-scale effort to provide essential food supplies to health and care institutions, hostels, schools, and nearby anganwadis. The project emphasized compassion, social responsibility, and the importance of community-driven action.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/FvnqZco-RMd865joLAH1k.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kdXbZnXwWcIPMnbn46bR_","name":"PROJECT PUSTAK","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/6XTvfrZ9b5LqiZR5YIueA.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-22","duration":1,"outcomes":"The funds collected were successfully utilized to distribute educational supplies to underprivileged students. A total of 24,000 notebooks, 3,250 stationery kits, and 2,250 geometry boxes were combined into 5,500 complete kits and distributed across 12 government schools in different locations. The initiative significantly contributed to promoting education, encouraging learning, and supporting students with the resources required for their academic growth.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is an educational outreach initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged children studying in government schools. The project was carried out in phases, beginning with a large-scale fundraising drive within the RVCE student community. Through generous contributions, the club raised ₹3,50,000 from 1,022 students, demonstrating strong collective responsibility towards social development. The project focuses on reducing the educational resource gap by providing essential stationery and learning materials to students in need.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/M3fR9sY0ojtpdTtt5bIjq.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RadK2SxS574xMrAvEVQwd","name":"SDG PHOTOGRAPHY COMPETITION 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/yzPf4oWTldV1GHpJEVJuq.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"The competition successfully promoted awareness of the SDGs among youth and the wider community by encouraging participants to observe and document societal and environmental concerns through photography. It enhanced students’ creativity, social responsibility, and understanding of sustainable development issues. The activity fostered engagement in global development goals, motivated participants to think critically about real-life challenges, and contributed to building a sense of responsibility towards creating a more inclusive and sustainable future.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":20,"description":"Through The Eyes Of YOUth: SDG Photography Competition 2025 is an awareness-driven initiative that encourages young individuals to creatively capture and highlight real-world issues connected to the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The competition provides a platform for students to express their perspectives on global challenges such as poverty, education, gender equality, environmental protection, and social justice through impactful photography. By using visual storytelling, participants contribute to spreading awareness and inspiring positive action towards sustainable development in society.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c01c45f2-aacb-4ebe-bfb9-fe6e061786f9/DMUE3wrKtE9PSlWYOZb9A.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 12:46:51.209819+00', '2026-02-02 05:28:29.45509+00'), ('85b849c3-a37b-44f2-b7b6-6147c63c2c68', '42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS198","name":"Siri H","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"NyHIdhwEf5vtRRfNlekzg","name":"Fast Trek 2023","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/LhpFN2-AAJvQtEKUgfLRf.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/dNHrHTJtzh4i5oy461Ccj.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event promoted environmental awareness and instilled a sense of responsibility toward maintaining cleanliness in natural spaces. Participants developed teamwork, discipline, and endurance while enhancing their appreciation for nature. The initiative encouraged eco-friendly behavior, leadership, and coordinated volunteer participation. Overall, the trek contributed to physical well-being, stress relief, and community-oriented environmental action.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The social cause behind the project was to provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the participants boarded the bus to the trek location with great enthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with basic information of the event. The trek was a great success as all the participants had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of Huthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very memorable journey. ","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/vBEGxeq498K63cYZkqmf2.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cTWs5WvsyDuxfPBuSfijn","name":"Paper Drive 2023","slNo":2,"place":"Kengeri","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/ppUEndT9UCMmPJFU_siqA.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/vJCBgwGc9FCD5gzY0LaVw.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/UaSblyXOOoG-gQBArVIyQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The paper drive promoted environmental sustainability through recycling while simultaneously supporting social welfare. It instilled values of social responsibility, teamwork, and civic engagement among participants. Students developed coordination, organizational, and volunteer management skills while contributing to a meaningful cause. The initiative demonstrated how collective effort can create both ecological and economic impact, benefiting underprivileged sections of society and encouraging youth participation in community development activities.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Paper Drive on 24th June 2023 in Bengaluru as a community service initiative focused on economic and community development. With the support of over 500 volunteers, the drive involved collecting old newspapers, books, magazines, and other wastepaper materials from various locations across the city. Volunteers assembled at RVCE and were transported to different areas to carry out the collection efficiently. In just a few hours, more than 7 tones of paper were gathered. The collected materials were sold to paper vendors, and the funds raised were donated for the welfare of underprivileged communities through a charitable foundation, making the event both environmentally and socially impactful.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/mz8LGJwQM3I-ek9cHAfMV.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EzvSIVrqfGjZMGqpvY716","name":"Quiz Corp","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/bW5JRqQ1P-Kgi0g4UpkFJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The quiz enhanced participants’ knowledge of India’s heritage, scientific contributions, culture, and intellectual traditions while improving their analytical thinking, recall ability, and competitive aptitude. It fostered curiosity, interdisciplinary learning, and awareness of Indian knowledge systems. The event also strengthened quizzing skills such as quick reasoning, teamwork, and decision-making under time constraints, while encouraging academic engagement beyond the classroom. Participation was recognized with activity points, reflecting involvement in a national-level knowledge event.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":24,"description":"RV QuizCorp, the quizzing club of RVCE, hosted Under the Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2023, Asia’s largest quizzing fest, from 14th–16th July 2023 at the IEM Auditorium, RVCE. As part of this flagship fest, Indi-Genius: The India Quiz was conducted on 14th July 2023, celebrating India’s knowledge systems, heritage, history, and achievements. The quiz brought together bright minds from across the country, providing an engaging platform to test awareness, analytical thinking, and domain knowledge. The event promoted intellectual curiosity and competitive spirit among students, and participants were awarded activity points in recognition of their involvement and knowledge engagement.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/xeB-VJVhrLsA64aoejHQl.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"r74m3TOojw56rfRXVNuKz","name":"Infosys Visit","slNo":4,"place":"Infosys Mysore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/ZCRv1lSwyDdZzDtSFBg29.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":1,"outcomes":"This event provided students with firsthand exposure to the corporate environment and the latest technological advancements at one of India''s leading IT companies. By touring the Infosys campus, students gained insights into real-world applications of their academic knowledge, witnessed industry best practices, and interacted with professionals in the field. ","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-31","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The industrial visit to Infosys, Mysore campus, organized by students of SPARK, the IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter, was a valuable experiential learning opportunity. This event provided students with firsthand exposure to the corporate environment and the latest technological advancements at one of India''s leading IT companies. By touring the Infosys campus, students gained insights into real-world applications of their academic knowledge, witnessed industry best practices, and interacted with professionals in the field. Awarding AICTE Activity Points for participating in such industrial visits is justified as it recognizes students'' proactive efforts to bridge the gap between theoretical learning and practical industry applications. This aligns with AICTE''s vision of promoting industry-academia collaboration to ensure that students are well-prepared for the dynamic demands of the professional world, fostering a holistic and experiential approach to engineering education.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/LfFkUpafdtDLwINrGQp9C.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZqBzrPacrL1hjCvmTTgX5","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth SDG Photo Competition","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/GPWFGl9CcH86ziPivdl46.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"The competition enhanced students’ awareness of Sustainable Development Goals and encouraged them to reflect on real-world social and environmental issues. It strengthened creative thinking, visual storytelling, and communication skills. Participants developed a deeper sense of social responsibility and global citizenship while using art as a medium to convey impactful messages. The initiative fostered youth engagement in sustainability discourse and promoted innovative expression aligned with community and global development.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":168,"description":"The SPARK – IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter organized “Through the Eyes of Youth” SDG Photo Competition from 7th August to 13th August 2023, encouraging students to creatively represent the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through photography. Participants captured images linked to specific SDGs and submitted a short description explaining the relevance of their photograph. The competition witnessed large student participation and promoted awareness of global challenges such as sustainability, social equity, and environmental responsibility. Entries were evaluated, and outstanding contributions were recognized as winners and special mentions, highlighting innovation and meaningful storytelling through visuals.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/cjbmw5OuVsYdbMIkBmXrt.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"utnw2jmWXdv2ZijmxqQXj","name":"Rush Hours 4.0","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/rFdnilUG6jleBTe83Gqkm.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/j3jhYPtT8LzNwS6AYijg-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-18","duration":4,"outcomes":"Rush Hours 4.0 enhanced participants’ general knowledge, creativity, environmental awareness, and social responsibility through diverse hands-on activities. It encouraged teamwork, leadership, time management, and digital engagement skills while fostering confidence through talent expression. The plantation drive promoted environmental consciousness, and socially themed tasks-built awareness about important global and community issues. Overall, the event provided a balanced platform for personal growth, skill development, and meaningful contribution to society, while strengthening peer interaction and campus involvement.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-15","hoursSpent":96,"description":"Rush Hours 4.0, the fourth edition of the mega-event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, was designed to help participants break away from routine stress while welcoming juniors into college life through an engaging and socially driven experience. Conducted over five days, the event combined community service and professional development through a series of structured tasks. It began with a pre-event activity to build interest, followed by five major tasks including a time-based knowledge quiz, poster creation on social awareness themes, a plantation drive, a one-minute talent showcase, and a social media inspiration challenge. With more than 250 participants actively involved and regular updates via dashboards and leaderboards, the event blended learning, creativity, teamwork, and societal contribution in an interactive format. Top-performing teams were recognized with awards and subscriptions, making the initiative both impactful and motivating.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/YOJI6VbeA6tLZ2UYqYaFa.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-R9J9njmY4EnH6ezHVI1D","name":"HACK4SOC 2.0","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/RwNsJzt2uGteYmZCoG767.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":2,"outcomes":"I contributed to the smooth execution of the event by supporting coordination efforts and leading the design of posters and banners, helping enhance the event’s visibility and engagement. Overall, the hackathon fostered a strong culture of innovation, teamwork, and social responsibility among all participants.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-03","hoursSpent":48,"description":"This 24-hour hackathon focused on leveraging technology for societal benefit, encompassing three key verticals: Generative Al, Fintech, and Blockchain. Throughout the hackathon, students showcased their creativity and problem-solving skills, developing innovative solutions. The top three teams emerged victorious, each presenting innovative ideas. This flagship event not only provided a platform for learning and collaboration but also fostered a culture of innovation among the participants.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/pWr3X4ZzLwOX-ziKZpYRk.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"T7NVWAWMizaE1CjPImytB","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/Sv2QXdo6dm2_EU_SS2ZTK.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/esc29jPcyFqVAai9Z0re5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-12-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event enhanced problem-solving, creativity, and teamwork skills among participants while promoting environmental awareness through the reuse of waste materials. It encouraged innovative thinking and practical application of ideas, strengthening presentation and communication skills. Uptown Junk also fostered leadership, coordination, and a spirit of healthy competition, contributing to overall personality development and responsible citizenship.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-14","hoursSpent":48,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized Uptown Junk, a two-day flagship event conducted on 14th and 15th December, designed to reduce academic stress while fostering creativity and competitive spirit among students. The event combined an adventurous treasure hunt with a best-out-of-waste competition. Participants solved clues across the campus to earn in-event currency, which was used to collect recyclable materials. This was followed by an innovation challenge where teams created useful models from waste materials. The models were evaluated based on ideation, creativity, presentation, and practical utility, and the top teams were recognized for their innovative solutions.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/t4RRCP9HQalfEJxJWOqfE.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"37ns9lYs34o9jSVQG8wFe","name":"NSS Farmathon","slNo":9,"place":"Art of Living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/w6dG6xq-XOT2MkG1--FX2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-12-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"Farmathon significantly enhanced students’ awareness of rural development, environmental sustainability, and the value of collective community effort. Participants developed teamwork, \\nleadership, communication, and coordination skills while working in a structured volunteer environment. The activity fostered a strong sense of civic responsibility, empathy, and \\nrespect for natural surroundings. Students also improved their adaptability, discipline, and physical endurance through active field participation. Overall, the initiative promoted holistic development by combining social service, environmental consciousness, and experiential learning, encouraging continued youth involvement in community welfare and \\nsustainability-driven initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-21","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The NSS Unit of RVCE organized Farmathon on 23rd December 2023 as a rural outreach and community service initiative conducted near the Art of Living region, Kanakapura. The \\nevent was designed to engage students in field-based social service activities that promote environmental responsibility and sustainable practices. Volunteers reported early in the morning \\nat the college campus and were briefed on safety guidelines, event objectives, and assigned responsibilities before traveling to the venue. The program involved structured, hands-on tasks \\ncarried out in a rural setting, enabling students to contribute directly to community-oriented and environment-focused efforts. Emphasis was placed on discipline, teamwork, coordination, and responsible conduct throughout the event. By participating in organized outdoor service work, students gained exposure to real-world community engagement beyond academic settings, strengthening their connection with grassroots-level initiatives.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"npejz2Y43mQkw-esIPYHK","name":"Tech For Tomorrow ","slNo":10,"place":"Kengeri Govt PU College","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/2OVb_xV1N1z-jisetxJG7.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/tzhvMOkuu9aQYpGkVNYW3.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/i5HciYg07httB5HH-EEoY.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/rP73Y2J2M6gDwvJplD3ng.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Volunteering at this outreach session with IEEE SIGHT and the Frequency Club was a deeply rewarding experience that helped me grow both personally and professionally. Through guiding students from government pre-university colleges in Kengeri and Attiguppe, I learned how impactful clear communication and mentorship can be in shaping young minds and helping them make informed career choices. Interacting with 11th and 12th grade students improved my ability to simplify complex concepts, understand their aspirations and concerns, and provide meaningful guidance. The experience strengthened my leadership, empathy, and public speaking skills, while also reinforcing the importance of social responsibility and community-driven initiatives in education.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-16","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The IEEE SIGHT and Frequency Club members came together, identified government pre-university colleges in Kengeri and Attiguppe and upon receiving the necessary permissions,\\nheld the session on technology and career guidance for the students of the 11th and 12th grade. The session consisted of the many upcoming fields of technology, career guidance\\nwhich included top colleges and the entrance exams to be focused on followed by a demonstration of a few software and hardware projects that the volunteers have developed\\ntheir attending the event. RV College of Engineering\\nthemselves at college. The session was ended by collecting the student''s feedback on the session and the distribution of notebooks and pens.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/Wptzaovsy5KT1G2eK4fHW.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DNWODJkx_24ZfK45ODO5z","name":"Gen AI Hackathon ","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/WbD3ASyQ-Dy0Lqf9dW77z.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/E-yoM2VLJ_E_2BHCs46WZ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Gen AI Hackathon was a highly enriching experience that significantly contributed to my personal and technical growth. I learned how to work effectively in a team under time constraints, manage pressure, and convert ideas into practical solutions. The event enhanced my understanding of Generative AI concepts, problem-solving methodologies, and real-world application development. I also developed stronger communication, collaboration, and critical thinking skills through team discussions and presentations. Overall, the hackathon helped me build confidence, improve my innovation mindset, and gain valuable exposure to emerging technologies and interdisciplinary problem-solving.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The Generative AI Hackathon was a 24-hour innovation-driven event focused on leveraging emerging technologies for societal benefit. The hackathon brought together students from diverse backgrounds to ideate, collaborate, and build impactful solutions across key domains such as Generative AI, Fintech, and Blockchain. Participants worked in teams to identify real-world problems and develop technology-driven solutions within a limited time frame, promoting creativity, teamwork, and rapid problem-solving. The event also served as a learning platform where students enhanced their technical knowledge, explored cutting-edge tools, and engaged in collaborative innovation. The hackathon concluded with project presentations, evaluation by judges, and recognition of the top-performing teams, making it a successful flagship event that fostered a strong culture of innovation and learning.","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UasTtc05Z-7gVJI_5G7BT","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":12,"place":"Mediscope Blood Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/IXyKvgH5X7YUbMpIHnkL9.png"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the blood donation camp taught me the true value of empathy, social responsibility, and community service. I learned how small individual actions can collectively make a significant impact on saving lives. The experience helped me understand the importance of awareness, organization, and discipline in conducting humanitarian activities. It also strengthened my sense of compassion, teamwork, and respect for healthcare professionals and donors. Overall, the camp made me more socially conscious and reinforced the importance of contributing positively to society through selfless service.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-21","hoursSpent":24,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was organized with the objective of promoting social responsibility, community service, and awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. The camp provided a safe, hygienic, and well-organized environment where students, faculty, and volunteers came together to contribute to a life-saving cause. Medical professionals and trained staff conducted health screenings, ensured donor safety, and followed proper medical protocols throughout the process. The event also included awareness sessions on the benefits of blood donation and its critical role in emergency healthcare. The camp successfully encouraged voluntary participation, strengthened community engagement, and fostered a culture of compassion, responsibility, and humanitarian service among participants.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/kKQ8mNrcQ2qKtF3icaHHF.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6ZfWsAiuwA5SHaGqCChD8","name":"Workshop on Research Paper Writing","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/y2oGTe0DiC70RByo-46hT.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/-yy1T1lhWDhwqytVtzePX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The workshop enabled participants to gain a clear understanding of the essential components of research paper writing and the process of converting project work into publishable research. Students became more confident in structuring their papers, selecting appropriate keywords, conducting literature reviews, and presenting methodology and results effectively. The introduction to various research tools and publication guidelines further enhanced their preparedness for academic writing. The interactive Q&A session helped clarify individual doubts, ensuring that participants left with practical insights and improved readiness to begin their own research paper journey. ","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Department of Computer Science and Engineering, in association with CISSS CoE, RVCE, \\norganized a Workshop on Research Paper Writing on Friday, 28th November 2025, from 6:30 PM to 8:30 \\nPM. The workshop focused on the fundamentals of writing effective research papers, emphasizing the importance and relevance of research in academic and professional growth. Students were guided on how experiential learning activities and project work can be transformed into publishable research contributions.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/9HUCVcCYbMVHqFYT55OHq.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2Zxpqy_XUAMvBX4coTitO","name":"Red Cross Blood Donation Camp","slNo":14,"place":"Red Cross Bhavan","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/ezOMRqBDjrSmBzS3LGTSM.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the blood donation camp taught me the true value of empathy, social responsibility, and community service. I learned how small individual actions can collectively make a significant impact on saving lives. The experience helped me understand the importance of awareness, organization, and discipline in conducting humanitarian activities. It also strengthened my sense of compassion, teamwork, and respect for healthcare professionals and donors. Overall, the camp made me more socially conscious and reinforced the importance of contributing positively to society through selfless service.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":24,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was organized with the objective of promoting social responsibility, community service, and awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. The camp provided a safe, hygienic, and well-organized environment where students, faculty, and volunteers came together to contribute to a life-saving cause. Medical professionals and trained staff conducted health screenings, ensured donor safety, and followed proper medical protocols throughout the process. The event also included awareness sessions on the benefits of blood donation and its critical role in emergency healthcare. The camp successfully encouraged voluntary participation, strengthened community engagement, and fostered a culture of compassion, responsibility, and humanitarian service among participants.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/42d0049d-d5af-4c83-943d-1dd14f5614cc/uGsmkoUVX1N7f7V8lHOPh.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-30","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:56:18.5015+00', '2026-01-30 10:40:32.998198+00'), ('895f8999-a1de-4965-9582-dc50e5beffab', 'f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS002","name":"Adarsh Kamath","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"gw5_iB4dRVUGaDbMcnJAE","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":1,"place":"Kunagala Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/kLzoZZ2-F6pPm8Lev5TSM.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fast Trek 2.0 encouraged combining environmental impact, student engagement, and community building. The cleanliness drive during the trek significantly contributed to preserving the natural beauty of Narayangiri Hills, while also instilling a strong sense of eco-consciousness and responsibility among participants. Over 500 students not only experienced the thrill of trekking but also actively engaged in social impact, reinforcing the Rotaract Club’s commitment to sustainability. The activity fostered teamwork, bonding, and motivation, as participants supported one another throughout the journey, creating lasting memories and shared experiences. Ultimately, the event left students feeling accomplished and inspired, setting a benchmark for future initiatives by blending adventure, social responsibility, and camaraderie into a single impactful activity.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":9,"description":"Fast Trek 2.0, the biggest flagship event of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, took place on 28th January 2024 at the scenic Kungala Betta Hills, bringing together over 500 enthusiastic participants from the college. This adventure-packed event combined trekking with a meaningful cleanliness drive, reinforcing the club’s commitment to environmental responsibility. The trek began early in the morning, with participants embarking on a thrilling journey through the rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills. Amidst breathtaking views, the team actively engaged in cleaning the surroundings, collecting litter, and promoting eco-consciousness. The event not only contributed to preserving the natural beauty of the hills but also instilled a sense of responsibility among students. Beyond the cause, Fast Trek 2.0 fostered incredible team bonding, as participants supported and motivated one another throughout the trek. Laughter, shared experiences, and the collective effort to make a difference created an unforgettable experience. The event concluded on a high note, with participants feeling both accomplished and inspired. With its perfect blend of adventure, social impact, and camaraderie, Fast Trek 2.0 was a massive success, leaving a lasting impact on both the environment and the participants, setting a benchmark for future events.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/7ITvYuAdc-RDcM9uOf8MT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fWQqDfdci1bzjuM3bBEWE","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":2,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/8mso3xuwj6YVK5lNy0nQ6.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the marathon felt empowering, knowing that my involvement directly supported\\neducation for underprivileged children. The donations from the 5 km and 10 km runs are making\\na tangible difference in providing educational resources and opportunities. Along the way, I had\\nthe chance to meet and make new friends who shared the same passion for helping others. After\\ncompleting the race, I received a medal and a certificate, symbols of the effort put into both the\\nrace and the cause. It was an unforgettable experience to be part of such a meaningful event and\\nto run alongside others committed to helping change the world for the better.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, was a special event aimed at promoting health\\nand fitness while making a meaningful impact. I participated in the 5 km race, and the event\\nproved to be an extraordinary experience. The theme, \"Help a Child- Change the World,\" was\\nat the heart of the marathon, emphasizing the importance of education and social\\ncontribution. Every step I took was part of a larger mission to support children in need, helping\\nto pave the way for their brighter futures. The marathon took place on February 4th, 2024, at\\nR VCollege of Engineering, and it was an inspiring sight to see so many participants come\\ntogether for a shared cause. It was not just about running but about being part of a movement.\\nThe event provided 10 activity points to everyone involved,\\nmaking it not only a fitness challenge but also an opportunity to contribute to a great cause.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/65Iq5udK5mQJz_7496noP.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2l4nMBrVpM85wcjg8fCzn","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/RuE8UfdStgvlsq4WEWU1r.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully achieved its objective of supporting underprivileged students by ensuring access to essential educational resources. Through the collective contributions of donors, adequate funds were raised and efficiently utilized to procure textbooks, stationery, backpacks, and other necessary school supplies. These materials were distributed to students in rural areas, helping reduce financial barriers to education and enabling a more conducive learning environment. The project not only positively impacted the academic preparedness of the beneficiaries but also strengthened collaboration between the Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranav Foundation, while fostering social responsibility and community involvement among volunteers and donors.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a socially impactful initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged students in rural areas by providing essential educational resources. The project focused on addressing the lack of basic school supplies that often hinders the learning experience of students from economically weaker backgrounds.\\nTo fund the initiative, a contribution of ₹100 or ₹350 was collected from each donor. These funds were systematically pooled and utilized to procure crucial educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other learning essentials. The project was carried out through the collaborative efforts of the Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranav Foundation, ensuring that the collected resources reached deserving students effectively and responsibly.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/Ni0WlNbHUjB4-nf1O5QyA.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HObn6nPWxPeaSjydH58YV","name":"Under The Peepal Tree 2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/9--uaVQm656OzK0QLUPTI.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the India Quiz at Under The Peepal Tree 2024 resulted in enhanced general awareness, improved critical thinking skills, and greater confidence in competitive academic settings. The event provided valuable exposure to a national-level platform, allowing participants to engage with peers from diverse backgrounds and broaden their perspectives.\\nAs a recognition of participation, a certificate was awarded, which could be used to claim 5 activity points, reinforcing the value of involvement in cultural and academic initiatives. Overall, the event proved to be an enriching experience that contributed to intellectual growth, cultural awareness, and active engagement in co-curricular activities.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Under The Peepal Tree 2024 was a national-level quiz fest that celebrated India’s rich heritage, culture, history, and contemporary knowledge. As part of this event, the India Quiz was conducted from 7th to 9th June 2024, bringing together participants from across the country. The quiz provided a platform for students to test their awareness, critical thinking, and understanding of diverse topics related to India in a competitive and intellectually stimulating environment.\\nThe event encouraged learning beyond textbooks by fostering curiosity, analytical reasoning, and knowledge exchange among participants. Organized with a strong academic and cultural focus, the quiz promoted healthy competition while also enhancing students’ appreciation of India’s socio-cultural and historical landscape. Participation in such a national-level event contributed to holistic student development and academic enrichment.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/8WLTAKPN-44EhEmCXBoZO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JUOEHpfcYkTSt-UZOl5AV","name":"T-shirt For Smiles","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/35WbgYh2elwT0yuegIOAH.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The T-Shirt for Smiles activity led to increased social awareness and a strong sense of empathy \\namong students, highlighting the importance of giving back to the community. It successfully \\ngenerated funds that contributed to the welfare and happiness of the children at Prajakirana Seva \\nCharitable Trust Anathashram, bringing smiles and emotional support to their lives. The event \\nencouraged teamwork, volunteerism, and a culture of compassion among participants, while \\nalso helping students understand the impact of collective efforts in addressing social needs. \\nOverall, the activity strengthened students’ commitment to social responsibility and community \\nengagement","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":1,"description":"T-Shirt for Smiles was a student-driven social initiative aimed at combining creativity, \\ncompassion, and community service. Students were encouraged to purchase specially designed \\nT-shirts, with the proceeds from the sales dedicated to spreading happiness among the children \\nof Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram, located at Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru.\\nThe event emphasized the spirit of social responsibility and collective contribution, \\ndemonstrating how small individual actions can create a meaningful impact. The funds raised \\nwere used to support the needs and bring joy to the children at the anathashram, reinforcing \\nvalues of empathy, generosity, and inclusiveness among students. T-Shirt for Smiles successfully \\nfostered a culture of kindness and awareness, inspiring participants to actively engage in \\nhumanitarian efforts beyond the classroom","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/uWCPYYd1ArDFzr7Gt8qIp.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZD8uYZCVr1x6y9eiXkD9I","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/aOG-TgBWj5GWia54sJ9_u.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fist Full initiative received an overwhelming response from the student community, with participation from over 1,750 students. A total of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal were successfully collected during the drive, demonstrating the powerful impact of collective action. The contributions made a significant difference in addressing food insecurity and supporting those in need.\\nThe event strengthened students’ sense of empathy, responsibility, and community engagement, while highlighting the effectiveness of simple yet purposeful contributions. Overall, Fist Full stood out as a highly impactful initiative that promoted social awareness, unity, and the spirit of giving, leaving a lasting impression on both the participants and the beneficiaries.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Fist Full was a humanitarian initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November. The primary objective of the project was to combat hunger and support food security through collective student participation. The initiative encouraged students to contribute either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, emphasizing how small individual efforts can collectively address a significant social issue.\\nDaily collection drives were organized at the Civil Department, ensuring ease of participation and consistent engagement throughout the event duration. The project focused on raising awareness about hunger, community welfare, and the importance of solidarity, while actively involving students in a meaningful social cause. Through this initiative, the Rotaract Club reinforced its commitment to service, compassion, and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/2Jg2uBmlEircE3XUf3RMq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NbTDSpZ6MkB7aERcLU1_U","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":7,"place":"Narayangiri Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/GNP45Zyrb9I2BONGZg261.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/i4CYrX0vfYyhwY_7mt961.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/UDbwTbqIU1aRAql3HQZ6e.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fast Trek 3.0 encouraged combining environmental impact, student engagement, and community building. The cleanliness drive during the trek significantly contributed to preserving the natural beauty of Narayangiri Hills, while also instilling a strong sense of eco-consciousness and responsibility among participants. Over 500 students not only experienced the thrill of trekking but also actively engaged in social impact, reinforcing the Rotaract Club’s commitment to sustainability. The activity fostered teamwork, bonding, and motivation, as participants supported one another throughout the journey, creating lasting memories and shared experiences. Ultimately, the event left students feeling accomplished and inspired, setting a benchmark for future initiatives by blending adventure, social responsibility, and camaraderie into a single impactful activity.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":9,"description":"Fast Trek 3.0, the biggest flagship event of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, took place on 12th January 2025 at the scenic Narayangiri Hills, bringing together over 500 enthusiastic participants from the college. This adventure-packed event combined trekking with a meaningful cleanliness drive, reinforcing the club’s commitment to environmental responsibility. The trek began early in the morning, with participants embarking on a thrilling journey through the rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills. Amidst breathtaking views, the team actively engaged in cleaning the surroundings, collecting litter, and promoting eco-consciousness. The event not only contributed to preserving the natural beauty of the hills but also instilled a sense of responsibility among students. Beyond the cause, Fast Trek 3.0 fostered incredible team bonding, as participants supported and motivated one another throughout the trek. Laughter, shared experiences, and the collective effort to make a difference created an unforgettable experience. The event concluded on a high note, with participants feeling both accomplished and inspired.\\n\\nWith its perfect blend of adventure, social impact, and camaraderie, Fast Trek 3.0 was a massive success, leaving a lasting impact on both the environment and the participants, setting a benchmark for future events.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/9UZ4MWii4TYQx9-u8Tlky.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"40gJYA-1JpjTnjEhJOhQB","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":8,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/8kNVF-_9nK9OLoxqCYUyv.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the marathon was a truly empowering experience, as it was fulfilling to know that my effort directly contributed to supporting education for underprivileged children. The funds raised through the 5 km and 10 km runs are making a meaningful impact by helping provide essential educational resources and opportunities. Throughout the event, I had the opportunity to interact with and befriend like-minded individuals who shared a common commitment to social service. Upon completing the race, I was awarded a medal and a participation certificate, which served as a reminder of both the physical effort and the social cause behind the event. Overall, being part of such a purposeful initiative and running alongside others striving to create positive change made the experience memorable and deeply rewarding.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, was a meaningful initiative focused on promoting health and fitness while contributing to a noble social cause. I participated in the 5 km run, and the experience was both motivating and memorable. Centered around the theme “Help a Child – Change the World,” the marathon highlighted the importance of education and social responsibility. Each step taken during the run symbolized a collective effort to support underprivileged children and help shape a better future for them.\\nThe marathon was held on April 6th, 2025, at R V College of Engineering, and witnessing a large number of participants come together for a shared purpose was truly inspiring. The event went beyond physical endurance, fostering a strong sense of unity and social commitment among participants. The race commenced at 8:00 AM, and the energetic atmosphere, filled with enthusiasm and determination, made the experience even more special.\\nAll participants were awarded 15 activity points, making the event not only a fitness challenge but also a valuable opportunity to contribute to a meaningful cause. The marathon successfully emphasized its theme and promoted a healthy lifestyle. At the conclusion of the event, participants felt accomplished and fulfilled, and certificates were distributed in recognition of their involvement and contribution to the social initiative.","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/FTDF-FWDmwNVPfkORPCWu.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4b1qbVVNmlrNCYR4kNHb8","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/_OYI7rzBN0sPiuuQPGLsX.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak achieved significant success in terms of participation, impact, and social outreach. A total amount of ₹3,50,000 was successfully raised through contributions from 1,022 students, showcasing the strong spirit of unity and collective action within the RVCE community. The funds directly supported the distribution of essential educational materials, benefiting children from government schools and positively contributing to their learning experience.\\nThe initiative enhanced students’ understanding of social responsibility and the importance of education as a tool for empowerment. It also fostered a culture of empathy, volunteerism, and active citizenship among participants. Overall, Project Pustak made a meaningful contribution toward reducing educational disparities and reinforced the Rotaract Club’s commitment to promoting education and inclusive development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is the flagship educational initiative of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, launched with the objective of supporting the education of underprivileged children by providing them with essential learning materials. Phase-1 of the project was conducted from 23rd April to 30th April in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation. The initiative, which has been recognized and appreciated by UGRAM, focused on fundraising within the RVCE student community to bridge educational resource gaps faced by children from disadvantaged backgrounds.\\nDuring this phase, college students actively participated by contributing funds toward the cause, demonstrating strong social awareness and generosity. The response to the initiative was highly encouraging, reflecting the collective commitment of students toward educational upliftment and social responsibility. Contributors who donated ₹350 were acknowledged with a certificate that accounted for 10 activity points, motivating active participation while reinforcing the importance of service-oriented involvement.\\nThe funds raised in Phase-1 were later utilized in Phase-2 of Project Pustak, which involved the procurement and distribution of stationery kits and books to children studying in government schools. Through this initiative, the Rotaract Club of RVCE aimed to ensure access to basic educational resources and promote equal learning opportunities for students in need.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/INC02jVgzm2h9-KFtXE_O.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"e9eDLgxxnIWz_70mV4ovf","name":"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/X3VxUYPjpN-ZGA1qq92aW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree initiative significantly enhanced environmental awareness and social sensitivity among students, highlighting the crucial role of tree plantation in giving back to both the community and the planet. The activity successfully raised funds that supported tree-planting efforts while also contributing to the well-being and happiness of the children at Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram, creating a positive emotional and social impact.\\nThe event promoted teamwork, volunteerism, and a shared sense of responsibility, helping participants recognize how collective action such as planting trees can lead to long-term environmental and social benefits. Overall, the initiative strengthened students’ commitment to sustainability, social responsibility, and active community engagement.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree was a student-driven social initiative that blended creativity, compassion, and environmental responsibility. Students were encouraged to purchase specially designed T-shirts, with the proceeds supporting both a meaningful cause and the planting of trees, highlighting the vital role of afforestation in protecting the environment and ensuring a sustainable future. The initiative also extended its impact to the children of Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram in Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru, spreading joy while promoting ecological awareness.\\nThe event underscored the significance of collective action in addressing environmental challenges, demonstrating how small individual contributions can lead to long-term positive change for the planet. By linking tree plantation with social service, the initiative reinforced values of responsibility, empathy, and inclusiveness among students. Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree successfully fostered a culture of environmental consciousness and kindness, inspiring participants to take active roles in both environmental conservation and humanitarian efforts beyond the classroom.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f9a79410-3004-4305-a952-512a90aea71b/4MNFraZ65ZuwCCjXk094L.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 05:42:25.604007+00', '2026-01-31 07:07:32.794679+00'), ('8a5082a0-b17b-4ddc-9c2d-73896bb9fbec', 'd2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV114","name":"U SUJAL AHMED","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"psf__a2cts568itOpwA2N","name":"Utsarga marathon (NSS)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/LzCDyNjDTv287Y0NDpcHy.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/Hjcf82AoMT9qL7iAeNGcI.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp was successfully conducted and received a \\nhighly positive response from the RVCE community. The initiative \\nsignificantly raised awareness about the importance of voluntary blood \\ndonation and inspired many individuals to contribute selflessly to a \\nhumanitarian cause. A notable outcome was the participation of several \\nfirst-time donors, who were encouraged by the supportive and \\nwell-organized environment. \\nOn a personal level, being involved in this event enhanced my sense of \\nsocial responsibility and empathy toward others. The experience also \\nhelped me develop valuable skills such as teamwork, leadership, \\ncommunication, and coordination. As a team, we learned to manage \\nresponsibilities effectively and work together under time constraints. \\nOverall, the event strengthened the bond among volunteers, brought \\nrecognition to the institution, and reinforced the belief that collective efforts \\nby students can create a meaningful and lasting impact on society. ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-03","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in \\ncollaboration with BGS Hospitals, was a highly impactful initiative aimed \\nat fostering social responsibility within the student community. In the days \\nleading up to the event, the Rotaract team worked tirelessly to manage \\nlogistics, coordinate with medical professionals, and spread awareness \\nacross the campus. This preparation created a professional and welcoming \\nenvironment in the BT Quadrangle, where the spirit of service was evident \\nfrom the start. \\nOn the day of the camp, the campus saw a remarkable turnout as students, \\nfaculty, and staff came forward to contribute to this noble cause. The \\nmedical team from BGS Hospitals ensured a safe and efficient process, \\nguiding donors through screening and the donation procedure with \\nimmense care. The atmosphere was further uplifted by the dedication of \\nstudent volunteers who managed registrations and provided post-donation \\nsupport, making the experience particularly reassuring for those donating \\nfor the first time. \\nThe success of the camp was ultimately measured by the significant number \\nof blood units collected, which will serve as a vital resource for patients in \\nneed. Beyond the physical contributions, the event served as a powerful \\nreminder of the strength of collective action and the profound impact of \\nhumanitarian service. Being part of this initiative was a deeply fulfilling \\nexperience, leaving a lasting impression of the importance of community \\nspirit and our shared responsibility to save lives.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"M-kkhuBXOztzg9qa5ePCQ","name":"Utsarga marathon (NSS)","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/3K5RrfTPYsVDO0Sk5Edaz.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/WJEFzUCilPyL3OeUqSeWy.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The UTSARGA 2025 marathon was a resounding success, effectively \\nraising awareness for child welfare and strengthening the community \\nspirit within the RVCE campus. In recognition of their dedication to \\ncommunity service and social impact, participants were awarded AICTE \\nactivity points, reflecting their commitment to humanitarian causes. \\nBeyond the rewards, the event’s true outcome was the tangible support \\ngenerated for underprivileged children, reinforcing the belief that \\ncollective efforts truly have the power to change the world.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":60,"description":"UTSARGA 2025, the flagship charity run organized by the National \\nService Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, continued its \\nimpactful legacy of social service under the theme \"Help a Child, Change \\nthe World\". Building on the success of previous years, the initiative \\nremained a powerful platform for fostering social responsibility among \\nstudents while actively contributing to the welfare of underprivileged \\nchildren. By blending physical endurance with a noble humanitarian \\ncause, the event served as a vibrant reminder of how collective action can \\npave the way for a brighter future for those in need. \\nThe marathon witnessed an incredible surge of energy and participation as \\nstudents, faculty, and community members gathered to \"Run for Their \\nSmiles\". The atmosphere was one of unity and purpose, with participants \\nshowcasing deep empathy and solidarity with the children they were \\nsupporting. This year’s event emphasized not just the importance of \\nphysical fitness, but also the vital role that young innovators and engineers \\nplay in driving meaningful community development through selfless \\nservice and outreach. \\nThe initiative was meticulously coordinated by the NSS team to ensure a \\nsafe and successful experience for all participants, highlighting the \\ncollege''s dedication to holistic education and social commitment. By \\nparticipating in this marathon, the student body demonstrated that impact \\nis often measured in the miles run and the lives touched. The event \\nconcluded with a renewed sense of responsibility among the youth, \\nproving that simple yet dedicated initiatives like Utsarga hold the \\ntransformative power to create lasting change in society.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lIfQf_f9AynwfNDWWwk9w","name":"Project Pustak (Rotaract)","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/tCs-xNl1WAS8ZnzaNYTk7.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-16","duration":8,"outcomes":"Project Pustak stands as a highly impactful, well-executed social initiative that successfully \\nbridged a critical educational resource gap for underprivileged students in government schools. \\nThrough a structured, two-phase approach, the Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with \\nthe Pranav Foundation, demonstrated how organized student-led efforts can translate intent \\ninto measurable results. Phase-1 achieved exceptional community engagement by mobilizing \\n1,022 college students and raising ¹3,50,000, reflecting strong trust, transparency, and collective \\nresponsibility within the RVCE ecosystem. The project’s recognition by UGRAM further \\nreinforced its credibility and societal relevance.\\nIn Phase-2, the collected funds were efficiently converted into large-scale on-ground impact. \\nThe July 2025 distribution drive resulted in the assembly and delivery of 5,500 complete \\nschool kits containing 24,000 notebooks, 3,250 stationery kits, and 2,250 geometry boxes \\nacross 12 government schools. The kits were thoughtfully designed based on students’ age \\ngroups, ensuring relevance and usability. With the participation of volunteers, faculty members, \\nand collaborators, the initiative directly enabled thousands of children—who otherwise lacked \\nbasic academic tools despite having uniforms—to actively participate in classroom learning. \\nThe project therefore contributed not only to improved access to education but also to \\nbetter attendance, engagement, and dignity for students from economically disadvantaged \\nbackgrounds.\\nProject Pustak offers several important takeaways. First, it highlights the power of collective \\naction—small individual contributions, when organized effectively, can create large-scale social \\nchange. Second, it demonstrates the value of phased project execution, where fundraising,","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-09","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE proudly launched Phase-1 of its flagship initiative Project Pustak \\nfrom April 23rd to 30th, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation. Recently recognized and \\nappreciated by UGRAM, the project aims to support the education of underprivileged children \\nby providing them with essential learning materials, Phase-1 focused on raising funds from \\ncollege students, and the response was overwhelming. The club successfully raised a remarkable \\nsum of ¹3,50,000 from contributions by 1,022 students during this phase, showcasing the spirit \\nof generosity and collective action within the RVCE community. For the students who donated \\nRs. 350, a certificate will be provided as a proof for 10 Activity Points. The funds collected \\nwere used in Phase-2 of the project, which involved the distribution of stationery kits and books \\nto children in government schools. The project reflects the club''s commitment to promoting \\neducation and reducing resource gaps for students in need.\\nThe Rotaract Club of R.V.C.E. hosted the event Project Pustak from 22nd-26th July 2025. \\nProject Pustak''s first distribution phase, conducted in collaboration with Pranav Foundation, \\nwitnessed the participation of 58 individuals, including 17 volunteers and 3 faculty members. \\nThrough generous donations collected in the first phase, essential educational supplies were \\ndistributed by faculty and participants to ensure underprivileged students received necessary \\nacademic materials such as notebooks, stationery kits, and geometry boxes. In total, 24,000 \\nnotebooks, 3,250 stationery kits, and 2,250 geometry boxes were assembled into 5,500 school \\nkits and distributed across 12 government schools in diverse locations.\\nProject Pustak was launched with the aim of supporting underprivileged children who, although \\nprovided with school uniforms through government aid, often lack access to basic academic \\ntools. This gap places many students at a significant disadvantage. The distribution included \\ntwo types of kits tailored for different age groups: students in grades 1 to 5 received kits with \\nfour notebooks (two ruled, two unruled) along with a stationery kit, while students in grades 6 \\nto 10 received four notebooks (two ruled, two unruled) and a geometry box.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ADqlNfCCzSfQwGmHG_9EF","name":"Kannada Sangha T-Shirt-2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/UGeYraMtjlSHZsh0nsja0.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/FRcod0Lw5b1iVw95PVxz2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The visit to Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram resulted in a positive and meaningful \\nimpact on the children residing there. Through interactive activities and personal engagement, the students helped create a joyful and supportive atmosphere, bringing emotional comfort and a \\nsense of belonging to the children. The donations made under the “T-Shirt for Smiles” initiative \\nensured that the children received essential clothing, directly contributing to their well-being. \\nOverall, the activity strengthened the bond between the student community and the orphanage, \\noffering both material support and emotional encouragement to the children.\\nThis activity highlights the importance of social responsibility and empathy in shaping \\nwell-rounded individuals. It demonstrates how simple acts—such as spending time, engaging \\nin conversations, and making small contributions—can have a significant positive impact on \\nthe lives of underprivileged children. The experience also teaches teamwork, compassion, and \\ncommunity awareness, encouraging students to look beyond academics and actively participate \\nin social welfare. Most importantly, it reinforces the value of giving back to society and \\nunderstanding the role of individuals in creating a more inclusive and caring community.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":60,"description":"As part of a community service initiative organized by the Kannada Sangha, a group of \\nstudents visited Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram, Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru, on \\n07-07-2024. The primary objective of this visit was to extend support, care, and happiness to \\nthe children residing at the orphanage. The students actively engaged with the children through \\ninteractive activities, spending quality time to create a positive and joyful environment. In \\naddition to interaction, contributions were made in the form of donations, including support \\nthrough the “T-Shirt for Smiles” initiative, which aimed to provide essential clothing and \\nspread happiness among the children. This activity fostered social responsibility, empathy, and \\ncommunity awareness among the participating students while contributing meaningfully to the \\nwell-being of underprivileged children","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Arn_-EX3nD5U67YU8NpsZ","name":"Fist Full-2024(Rotaract)","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/i-knepiO6Cgdnb4O9wJeI.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/DKvm3w887nUlJBHf2jbGz.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/yK3KWTD7IYjjsG_FDRPzn.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The food donation drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary \\nBangalore Spandana resulted in a substantial and tangible contribution to community welfare. \\nWith the participation of over 1,750 students, the initiative successfully collected more than \\n6,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal. These essential food supplies could support a large \\nnumber of families and communities facing food insecurity, thereby directly addressing basic \\nnutritional needs. The scale of the response demonstrated strong student engagement and reflected the culture of empathy, generosity, and social responsibility fostered at RV College \\nof Engineering.\\nThis initiative clearly illustrates the power of collective action—small individual contributions, \\nwhen combined, can create a massive social impact. It reinforces the idea that meaningful \\nchange does not always require large individual sacrifices, but rather consistent and coordinated \\nefforts. Students involved gained valuable lessons in social responsibility, teamwork, leadership, \\nand community engagement. The drive also highlights how educational institutions can serve \\nas effective platforms for social initiatives, encouraging students to look beyond academics and \\nactively participate in addressing societal challenges such as hunger and food security","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore \\nSpandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily \\ncollections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total \\namount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative \\nhighlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s \\ndedication to community welfare and solidarity","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eW68MxP6_-yuIgenghRhw","name":"Fist Full-2025(Rotaract)","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/Dv9gM5z2l0a9XExH5rHAz.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/W-FnoajHfze1aNN5Z18vL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fistful initiative achieved a significant humanitarian impact through large-scale student \\nparticipation and collective contribution. With 2,146 students donating essential food \\ngrains—either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal—the initiative successfully mobilized substantial \\nresources to support multiple beneficiary institutions. These institutions, which provide daily \\nmeals to children, the elderly, patients, and other disadvantaged groups, were able to strengthen \\ntheir food supply and continue their service more effectively. The initiative directly contributed \\nto food security for vulnerable populations and demonstrated how coordinated student efforts \\ncan translate into meaningful, real-world impact. This initiative highlights the power of collective responsibility and consistency in social service. \\nIt shows that small, individual contributions, when aggregated, can address large societal \\nchallenges such as hunger and nutrition. Participants learned the value of empathy, community \\nengagement, and teamwork, along with the importance of taking initiative to support those in \\nneed. The Fistful initiative also reinforces the role of students and educational communities as \\ncatalysts for social change, proving that structured, well-organized efforts can create sustainable \\nand far-reaching outcomes for society.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-27","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing \\nessential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted \\nin the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions \\nthat serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CJGR0B2ki8WYA5VyuH2ko","name":"Chela mela (NSS)","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/VozuJEg4BdAIpg0iLCij3.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants developed practical skills in making eco-friendly paper bags using newspapers and recyclable materials. Increased awareness about plastic pollution and the importance of sustainable alternatives among students. A significant number of paper bags were produced and made available for use during the Kadale Kayi Parishe, helping reduce single-use plastic consumption. Students gained a sense of social responsibility and community involvement by contributing to an environmentally beneficial cause. The activity promoted the principles of Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle, reinforcing environmentally conscious behavior. Strengthened collaboration between NSS RVCE and Youth For Seva, fostering teamwork and volunteerism. Encouraged participants to adopt eco-friendly practices in their daily lives beyond the workshop.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":80,"description":"NSS RVCE, in collaboration with Youth For Seva, is organizing a Paper Bag Making Workshop as part of its initiative to support the Kadale Kayi Parishe and promote sustainable practices.\\n\\nThe workshop aims to address the growing concern of plastic pollution by encouraging the use of eco-friendly paper bags as an alternative to single-use plastics. Participants will be guided step-by-step in creating sturdy paper bags using old newspapers and recyclable paper, transforming waste materials into useful, environmentally responsible products.\\n\\nThrough this hands-on activity, students will gain practical skills in paper bag making while also developing awareness about waste reduction, reuse of materials, and environmental conservation. The paper bags produced during the workshop will be distributed and used during the Kadale Kayi Parishe, helping vendors reduce their dependence on plastic carry bags.\\n\\nThis initiative not only supports a traditional local fair but also reinforces the values of social responsibility, sustainability, and community engagement. By crafting paper bags for a cause, participants actively contribute toward building a cleaner, greener, and more sustainable environment.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EfQ4GYeg8Rk1Mr_31ZhEI","name":"Blood Donation Camp - 2023 ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/mdkaDhaQIlmnI5tGk_Ewn.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp was successfully conducted and received a \\nhighly positive response from the RVCE community. The initiative \\nsignificantly raised awareness about the importance of voluntary blood \\ndonation and inspired many individuals to contribute selflessly to a \\nhumanitarian cause. A notable outcome was the participation of several \\nfirst-time donors, who were encouraged by the supportive and \\nwell-organized environment. \\nOn a personal level, being involved in this event enhanced my sense of \\nsocial responsibility and empathy toward others. The experience also \\nhelped me develop valuable skills such as teamwork, leadership, \\ncommunication, and coordination. As a team, we learned to manage \\nresponsibilities effectively and work together under time constraints. \\nOverall, the event strengthened the bond among volunteers, brought \\nrecognition to the institution, and reinforced the belief that collective efforts \\nby students can create a meaningful and lasting impact on society. ","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in \\ncollaboration with BGS Hospitals, was a highly impactful initiative aimed \\nat fostering social responsibility within the student community. In the days \\nleading up to the event, the Rotaract team worked tirelessly to manage \\nlogistics, coordinate with medical professionals, and spread awareness \\nacross the campus. This preparation created a professional and welcoming \\nenvironment in the BT Quadrangle, where the spirit of service was evident \\nfrom the start. \\nOn the day of the camp, the campus saw a remarkable turnout as students, \\nfaculty, and staff came forward to contribute to this noble cause. The \\nmedical team from BGS Hospitals ensured a safe and efficient process, \\nguiding donors through screening and the donation procedure with \\nimmense care. The atmosphere was further uplifted by the dedication of \\nstudent volunteers who managed registrations and provided post-donation \\nsupport, making the experience particularly reassuring for those donating \\nfor the first time. \\nThe success of the camp was ultimately measured by the significant number \\nof blood units collected, which will serve as a vital resource for patients in \\nneed. Beyond the physical contributions, the event served as a powerful \\nreminder of the strength of collective action and the profound impact of \\nhumanitarian service. Being part of this initiative was a deeply fulfilling \\nexperience, leaving a lasting impression of the importance of community \\nspirit and our shared responsibility to save lives.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"169CuypH8LHUcFrtpznEZ","name":"Sports ","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/3gJqWnKO0z7crREFUq2-s.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/UjA0kQH48h81IhXjG_TFB.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-20","duration":3,"outcomes":"Clear understanding of momentum and its application in football\\nAbility to relate theoretical concepts to real-life sports situations\\nImproved analytical skills by observing player movements and ball behavior\\nEnhanced awareness of force, speed, and direction in gameplay\\nBetter appreciation of how physics improves performance and safety in sports","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-18","hoursSpent":20,"description":"This activity focuses on understanding and analyzing the concept of momentum through the game of football. It explains how momentum influences player movement, ball speed, direction changes, and impact during passes, tackles, and shots. Real-game situations are used to relate theoretical principles with practical applications, helping learners connect physics concepts with sports performance.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CEeiDsmbAZ1jOmK6xj5YT","name":"Vikasit Bharath Quiz (NSS)","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/nqCu-M_u3VXUmgrC0NIUv.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d2b56960-685a-4842-8baf-0a894f510bf2/q509w5qm6A5aVEOtsF1o7.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced awareness about India’s development initiatives and national vision\\nImproved knowledge of government schemes, policies, and achievements\\nEncouraged critical thinking and healthy competition among students\\nPromoted a sense of patriotism and social responsibility\\nStrengthened understanding of the role of youth in building a developed India","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Vikasit Bharat Quiz was conducted to create awareness among students about the vision of Vikasit Bharat (Developed India) and the nation’s progress in areas such as economy, infrastructure, technology, governance, and social development. The quiz encouraged participants to learn about government initiatives, national achievements, and future goals while promoting active participation, critical thinking, and civic responsibility.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:59:23.507536+00', '2026-01-29 19:26:49.386154+00'), ('8adcfd92-3759-4b4c-aa9e-70908a0ed824', '25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI014","name":"CHANDANA","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"GImRuIzjPjfEDUB8mBOid","name":"Science, Space and Technology Essay Competition","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE - Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/V9SUdvrrRTjWN_d7khpgZ.png"],"endDate":"2023-09-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The competition witnessed enthusiastic participation and showcased a wide range of insightful perspectives and creative thinking. Participants demonstrated strong research skills, clarity of thought, and a deep understanding of scientific concepts and technological developments. The event successfully enhanced scientific awareness, improved writing and analytical abilities, and inspired students to think innovatively about the role of science and technology in solving real-world problems.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-09-01","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Science, Space and Technology Essay Competition was organized to encourage students to explore, analyze, and express ideas related to advancements in science, space exploration, and emerging technologies. The competition aimed to foster scientific curiosity, critical thinking, and awareness of how technology shapes the future of humanity. Participants were invited to present well-researched essays highlighting innovations, challenges, ethical considerations, and future possibilities in the fields of science and space technology.","aicteMapping":"Technical Skill Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/ms4vn-1716mnNJFfPJzBb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rcGtYEsjMvecBrSj2tbNX","name":"Energy literacy Training Program","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE - online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/qh4N0WDekgygyPQIXguED.png"],"endDate":"2023-05-05","duration":9,"outcomes":"The training program significantly improved participants’ knowledge of energy systems and sustainable energy practices. Participants gained practical insights into energy conservation, renewable energy solutions, and responsible energy consumption. The program encouraged environmentally conscious behavior, enhanced decision-making related to energy usage, and motivated participants to contribute towards a more sustainable and energy-efficient future.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-04-27","hoursSpent":22,"description":"The Energy Literacy Training Program was conducted to create awareness and understanding of energy resources, energy conservation, and sustainable energy practices. The program focused on educating participants about different forms of energy, efficient energy usage, renewable energy technologies, and the importance of energy sustainability in addressing environmental and climate challenges. Through interactive sessions and real-world examples, the program aimed to build informed and responsible energy-conscious individuals.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/PTAuWMsnKDy8_tgcBcd2v.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"F_yXHL7WjcQ50QKRImlJu","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE  - online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/PZCqFJugXj3bwQeCst1yR.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-03-05","duration":3,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully increased awareness among first-time voters regarding the significance of their vote. Participants developed a better understanding of democratic values, the voting process, and the impact of informed voting on nation-building. The program instilled a sense of civic responsibility, boosted confidence among young voters, and motivated them to actively participate in the democratic process.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-03-03","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye is an awareness initiative aimed at educating first-time voters about the importance of voting in a democratic nation. The program focused on creating awareness about the electoral process, citizens’ rights and responsibilities, and the role of youth in strengthening democracy. It encouraged young voters to actively participate in elections and make informed, ethical, and responsible choices for the development of the nation.","aicteMapping":"Voting awareness in India","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/zEXSnw8UsECJFiDk72Abi.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QA2ywYvHLTCxQK8MUIgXQ","name":"Fast trek 2.0","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/Fa0HrYUMREh2wbEx08xF8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully improved participants’ technical skills, confidence, and collaborative abilities. Participants demonstrated increased critical thinking, effective communication, and a proactive approach to challenges. FAST-TREK 2.0 encouraged innovation, practical learning, and peer interaction, leaving participants better prepared for academic, technical, and professional challenges.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"FAST-TREK 2.0 was organized as an engaging technical and skill-development initiative aimed at enhancing participants’ problem-solving, analytical thinking, and teamwork abilities. The event combined learning with hands-on activities, challenges, and interactive sessions designed to strengthen technical knowledge, innovation, and adaptability in a fast-paced environment.","aicteMapping":"Student Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/CrWGZ_UCTWdg83ApLvYlX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iAKC_BUuHcs1PjE_ksmf4","name":"Police Marshall","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/3zIjzv6uawobO4ITzhVZo.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program successfully enhanced participants’ understanding of public safety, discipline, and community policing. Participants developed leadership skills, situational awareness, and confidence in handling real-life safety scenarios. The initiative strengthened coordination between citizens and police personnel, encouraged responsible citizenship, and contributed to safer and more organized public environments.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Police Marshall program was conducted to promote discipline, safety awareness, and cooperation between citizens and law enforcement. The initiative aimed to train participants in basic crowd management, traffic regulation assistance, public safety practices, and emergency response. It focused on developing a sense of responsibility, leadership, and civic duty while supporting police authorities in maintaining law and order during public activities and events.","aicteMapping":"Spreading Public awareness about drugs","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/KMTHcTnXWzp2Utzp34pLu.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6KzTBscetpV1gCP9QxRA3","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/mjGlm-4UCpgkkODxyB0uH.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon witnessed active participation and successfully motivated individuals to adopt healthier habits. Participants demonstrated enthusiasm, perseverance, and sportsmanship throughout the event. The initiative enhanced awareness about fitness and well-being, strengthened community bonding, and inspired participants to prioritize physical and mental health in their daily lives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized to promote physical fitness, mental well-being, and social awareness among participants. The event aimed to encourage a healthy lifestyle, endurance, and discipline while fostering a sense of unity and community participation. It also emphasized the importance of regular physical activity and collective responsibility towards health and wellness.","aicteMapping":"Health, Wellness & Sports","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/EULyGwrQrxb2yFEHu-xWK.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gcVZsjhvyWNr8S6sz642Q","name":"UTPT 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/JCBf7blCFht-V-vfOHU1X.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"UTPT 2025 successfully enhanced participants’ confidence, conceptual clarity, and time-management skills. Participants gained valuable experience in competitive assessment environments and improved their analytical and critical-thinking abilities. The program encouraged continuous learning, self-evaluation, and better preparedness for future technical and professional examinations.","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":6,"description":"UTPT 2025 was organized as a competitive and skill-enhancement initiative aimed at assessing and strengthening participants’ technical knowledge, problem-solving abilities, and analytical thinking. The program provided a structured platform for participants to test their understanding of core concepts, apply theoretical knowledge to practical scenarios, and prepare for academic and professional challenges.","aicteMapping":"Technical Skill Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/7MusCgdou9HKILauei2jL.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"P8__c1OSK-sg3pgRvjn-B","name":"Wall Painting & Plastic Awareness","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/u72To76W7JP4MRxlTBKeW.png"],"endDate":"2025-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully raised awareness about the harmful effects of plastic pollution and the importance of sustainable alternatives. Participants showcased creativity, teamwork, and social responsibility while conveying impactful environmental messages. The program fostered environmental consciousness, encouraged eco-friendly practices, and enhanced community engagement through visual storytelling.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Wall Painting & Plastic Awareness initiative was organized to promote environmental awareness and responsible behavior towards plastic usage through creative expression. The activity combined art with social responsibility, using wall paintings as a medium to communicate messages on reducing plastic waste, recycling, and protecting the environment. It aimed to engage participants and the public in meaningful dialogue about sustainable practices and environmental conservation.","aicteMapping":"Environment & Sustainability","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/U_K0m6a8s4k5vSao-iYZy.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OS_mIYUtUB3q6oXaT3mjt","name":"Walkathon Wild Life Conservation","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/hXYsgPmzKf_8lcd3e2ml2.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon successfully increased awareness about wildlife conservation and environmental protection. Participants demonstrated commitment and social responsibility while actively supporting the cause. The event strengthened community involvement, encouraged eco-conscious attitudes, and inspired participants to take meaningful actions towards the conservation of wildlife and natural habitats.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-10-02","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Walkathon – Wildlife Conservation was organized to raise awareness about the importance of protecting wildlife and preserving natural ecosystems. The initiative aimed to educate participants and the public about biodiversity conservation, threats to wildlife, and the role of individuals in safeguarding nature. Through collective participation, the walkathon promoted environmental responsibility, unity, and advocacy for wildlife conservation.","aicteMapping":"Environment & Sustainability","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/OFi9f-eg6iwSxO2obozXy.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"w2yIODqvio66nB4rnwMJD","name":"SDG Photography","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/IpdLvqKwiNSR1tx9cze2p.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/BkMlrmB0KNKL3HciaDowL.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully enhanced participants’ awareness of the SDGs and their relevance in everyday life. Participants demonstrated creativity, social sensitivity, and strong visual communication skills. The activity fostered critical thinking, encouraged responsible storytelling, and inspired participants to view sustainability issues from a more conscious and impactful perspective.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The SDG Photography initiative was organized to create awareness about the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through visual storytelling. The activity encouraged participants to capture photographs that reflect social, environmental, and economic issues aligned with the SDGs. It aimed to promote creativity, observation, and a deeper understanding of global challenges and sustainable development through the power of photography.","aicteMapping":"Sustainable Development Goals","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/qWlUMfvS5RbpshTBJH5Rl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pd-2-yNEvGefMFeG2Au9d","name":"Fist Full 24","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/yWPnsqnYJuuTSIdYHaloj.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The visit helped participants gain practical knowledge of sewage treatment operations and their significance in sustainable urban development. Participants developed awareness about water conservation, pollution control, and responsible waste management practices. The program successfully bridged theoretical concepts with real-world applications, fostering environmental responsibility and technical understanding among participants.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-16","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The STP (Sewage Treatment Plant) Visit at RR Nagar was organized to provide participants with practical exposure to wastewater treatment processes and urban sanitation systems. The visit aimed to enhance understanding of how sewage is treated, recycled, and safely discharged, highlighting the importance of environmental protection, public health, and sustainable water management. Participants were introduced to various stages of sewage treatment and the role of STPs in maintaining ecological balance.","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility & Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/UqEATf0eZdc77mj07HcYr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Sk9Ji3k3TkZAMWlR7HSs7","name":"Fist Full 25","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/Y-3SMwsRoxOXoaIbT4HZd.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully collected food grains and extended support to those in need. Participants developed a stronger sense of empathy, generosity, and social awareness. The program promoted community involvement, responsible citizenship, and the value of small contributions making a significant social impact.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-21","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Fist Full initiative was organized as a social outreach program to address hunger and promote compassion within the community. The activity encouraged participants to contribute a “fist full” of food grains as a symbolic yet meaningful act of sharing with the underprivileged. The initiative aimed to foster empathy, social responsibility, and collective effort towards reducing food insecurity.","aicteMapping":"Donation ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/3kRgLw3C_LUknFTfSH5eo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TuRHN6oRyFKnZD2Jn9R9J","name":"Secret santa ","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/vwe3QjPWYWH0lMbokdMqY.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/sXYAaf91XaN-60uEzXdSf.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully fostered happiness, camaraderie, and emotional connection among participants. It encouraged generosity, creativity, and participation while creating memorable experiences. The initiative enhanced team bonding, promoted a culture of kindness, and contributed to a positive and festive environment.\\n\\n\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-19","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Secret Santa event was organized to spread joy, positivity, and a spirit of togetherness among participants. The activity encouraged anonymous gift-giving as a way to promote kindness, surprise, and mutual appreciation. It aimed to strengthen interpersonal bonds, boost morale, and create a cheerful and inclusive atmosphere through simple acts of thoughtfulness.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25e5967e-895c-43ee-a7e2-99ae803ec87d/LKiX7Qz9qLPqSV22l1n7s.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-02 02:46:03.161166+00', '2026-02-02 05:38:33.717964+00'), ('8b4ac7eb-505c-4b98-9124-1c01fa600457', 'c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD046","name":"Prithiviraj N","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"2mXyQ8rMuXXz158OblM5m","name":"Fist Full Donation Drive","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/p2kxMQSeUxKJ0HVOtnz-1.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-12-01","duration":154,"outcomes":"The Fist Full donation drive had a significant social impact by contributing essential food resources to underprivileged individuals and communities. The activity helped strengthen the culture of volunteering and social service among students.\\nThrough participation in the event, I developed a deeper understanding of social issues such as poverty and food insecurity. The event enhanced my sense of responsibility towards society and encouraged me to actively participate in community-oriented initiatives.\\nAdditionally, the activity improved my awareness of teamwork and collective effort in achieving social goals. Overall, the event contributed to the development of values such as empathy, generosity, and civic responsibility","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The “Fist Full” event was organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering as a social service initiative aimed at collecting essential food items such as rice and toor dal from students. The objective of the event was to encourage students to contribute towards supporting underprivileged communities and promoting the spirit of social responsibility.\\nDuring the event, students voluntarily donated food grains, which were later distributed to people in need. The campaign fostered a sense of empathy and collective responsibility among participants. I actively participated in the event by contributing to the donation drive, thereby supporting the initiative to address food insecurity and community welfare.\\nThe event also helped in spreading awareness about the importance of sharing resources and contributing to social causes. It served as an effective platform for students to engage in meaningful community service activities.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"L9QCn1TBdPsnShIgWyeqx","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":2,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/3Bo-9i7hRmSTAnvCj5pvG.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity contributed to environmental conservation by promoting\\ncleanliness and preserving the natural beauty of the trekking area. It\\nstrengthened awareness about sustainable practices and responsible interaction\\nwith nature. Through this event, I enhanced my teamwork, leadership, and\\nenvironmental consciousness while experiencing a sense of accomplishment\\nthrough collective effort and social impact.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I participated in FAST TREK 3.0, a flagship event organized by the Rotaract\\nClub of RVCE at the Narayangiri Hills. The event combined trekking with a\\nsocial and environmental cause through a cleanliness drive aimed at preserving\\nthe natural surroundings. Participants undertook an early-morning trek through\\nthe rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills while actively engaging in collecting litter\\nand promoting eco-conscious behavior. The initiative emphasized\\nenvironmental responsibility alongside adventure and teamwork.","aicteMapping":"Environment Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HMxRue86wv9h5SJdsCj8C","name":"UTSARG Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/xOosyUSc9ARMfjrmMM0yU.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the marathon led to significant personal and social development. The event helped improve physical endurance, stamina, and overall fitness. It also strengthened mental resilience, discipline, and perseverance.\\nThrough this activity, I developed a greater appreciation for teamwork, community engagement, and the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle. The marathon also enhanced my awareness of social causes promoted by the NSS and motivated me to participate in similar activities in the future.\\nOverall, the event contributed to the development of qualities such as determination, self-motivation, and social responsibility.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in the UTSARGA Marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. The event was conducted with the objective of promoting physical fitness, social awareness, and community participation among students.\\nThe marathon encouraged students to actively engage in physical activities while spreading awareness about social responsibility and healthy living. I participated in the 5 KM category and successfully completed the run along with other participants.\\nThe event provided an opportunity to interact with students from different departments and fostered a sense of unity and teamwork. It also highlighted the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle and contributing towards community-driven initiatives.\\n","aicteMapping":"Public Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"w7muKzDLIHc8REK9Fh9wZ","name":"Project PUSTAK","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/75fZAxSMIi4it0I934E00.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative contributed towards improving access to basic educational\\nresources for underprivileged children, thereby supporting regular school\\nattendance and a better learning environment. The expanded outreach in 2024\\naimed to benefit more than 10,000 students, significantly amplifying the social\\nimpact of the program. Through my involvement, I developed a stronger\\nunderstanding of community engagement, social responsibility, and the role of\\ncollective action in addressing educational challenges faced by marginalized\\ncommunities.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in Project Pustak 2024 (Pusthaka – Stationery Kit\\nDistribution Program), a social service initiative jointly organized by RV\\nCollege of Engineering and Pranav Foundation. The project was aimed at\\naddressing the lack of basic stationery among children from underprivileged\\ncommunities studying in rural government schools. Observations from earlier\\noutreach highlighted that the absence of essential supplies such as notebooks\\nand geometry boxes led to irregular class attendance among students. Building\\non the successful implementation of the initiative in 2023, the 2024 edition\\nfocused on expanding its reach by mobilizing support, encouraging donations,\\nand connecting with potential contributors to distribute stationery kits to a\\nlarger number of beneficiaries.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TMXbegPb3beeXBBAnCuAz","name":"Dengue Awareness Program","slNo":5,"place":"JP Nagar, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/vUrbg9ItfCmFEN8ezLnjh.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program helped raise awareness among community members about dengue\\nprevention and general health practices, contributing to improved public health\\nconsciousness. It enabled effective dissemination of preventive measures to\\nreduce the risk of dengue outbreaks. Through this activity, I developed a better\\nunderstanding of public health issues, community engagement, and the role of\\nawareness programs in promoting societal well-being.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-09","hoursSpent":5,"description":"I participated in a Health and Dengue Awareness Program organized by NSS\\nRVCE in collaboration with the District Health Officer at JP Nagar. The\\nprogram was conducted to educate the community about dengue prevention,\\nhealth awareness, and hygiene practices. The activity involved awareness\\nsessions and interactions aimed at spreading knowledge about the causes,\\nsymptoms, preventive measures, and control of dengue, while emphasizing the\\nimportance of community participation in public health initiatives.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iaj6WitcPrikCGsRvyaCG","name":"Green Sunday","slNo":6,"place":"Kengeri, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/O7Bpusm1RnB9IoH8kqaOP.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity strengthened environmental awareness, ecological responsibility, and sustainable\\nliving values. It promoted community service, social responsibility, and commitment towards\\nenvironmental conservation. The programme contributed to personal development through\\nactive participation in green initiatives and responsible citizenship practices.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-26","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Green Sunday is an environmental sustainability initiative organized by Adyamya Chetana\\nunder the Smt. Girija Shastry Memorial Trust. I participated in the 439th Green Sunday\\nProgramme, which focused on tree planting, nurturing of saplings, and environmental\\nawareness. The programme aimed at promoting ecological responsibility, conservation of\\nnature, and community participation in environmental protection through consistent green\\ninitiatives and public engagement activities.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RgTbzTm-F9q8pqD2GNkOP","name":"Human Elephant Conflict","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/R0oTd98a61zrxBqEMsJ6S.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness about the challenges associated with human–\\nelephant conflicts and the importance of conservation-oriented technological\\ninterventions. It provided insights into sustainable solutions that support\\nwildlife protection while ensuring human safety. Through participation in this\\nevent, I developed a better understanding of environmental sustainability,\\nconservation technologies, and the role of innovation in addressing ecological\\nchallenges.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in an eco-conscious awareness event organized by NSS RVCE in\\ncollaboration with the Sustainability Development Cell (SDC), focusing on\\naddressing Human–Elephant Conflict. The event highlighted innovative and\\ntechnology-driven solutions for wildlife conservation, including elephant\\ndetection using images and videos, integrated with real-time SMS alerts to\\nprovide accurate location information. The program aimed to create awareness\\nabout wildlife protection, promote sustainable practices, and demonstrate how\\ntechnology can be leveraged to mitigate conflicts between humans and wildlife.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PE7YY9lninRSw7p3WbneC","name":"UTSARG Marathon","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/EkzuKC6A2bWyuunc2RqVd.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the marathon led to significant personal and social development. The event helped improve physical endurance, stamina, and overall fitness. It also strengthened mental resilience, discipline, and perseverance.\\nThrough this activity, I developed a greater appreciation for teamwork, community engagement, and the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle. The marathon also enhanced my awareness of social causes promoted by the NSS and motivated me to participate in similar activities in the future.\\nOverall, the event contributed to the development of qualities such as determination, self-motivation, and social responsibility.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in the UTSARGA Marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. The event was conducted with the objective of promoting physical fitness, social awareness, and community participation among students.\\nThe marathon encouraged students to actively engage in physical activities while spreading awareness about social responsibility and healthy living. I participated in the 5 KM category and successfully completed the run along with other participants.\\nThe event provided an opportunity to interact with students from different departments and fostered a sense of unity and teamwork. It also highlighted the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle and contributing towards community-driven initiatives.\\n","aicteMapping":"Public Awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EGmg_qi15U1pZSFNRZ1DB","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":9,"place":"Narayangiri Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/k--iiFUxjLWGSCLemxB7r.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity contributed to environmental conservation by promoting\\ncleanliness and preserving the natural beauty of the trekking area. It\\nstrengthened awareness about sustainable practices and responsible interaction\\nwith nature. Through this event, I enhanced my teamwork, leadership, and\\nenvironmental consciousness while experiencing a sense of accomplishment\\nthrough collective effort and social impact.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in FAST TREK 3.0, a flagship event organized by the Rotaract\\nClub of RVCE at the Narayangiri Hills. The event combined trekking with a\\nsocial and environmental cause through a cleanliness drive aimed at preserving\\nthe natural surroundings. Participants undertook an early-morning trek through\\nthe rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills while actively engaging in collecting litter\\nand promoting eco-conscious behavior. The initiative emphasized\\nenvironmental responsibility alongside adventure and teamwork.","aicteMapping":"Environment Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JKQufk1G-4rRg6RUluOCG","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/YtYB3MFIRsjUHTEFt7_gy.png"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The activity provided a platform for collaborative learning, creativity, and\\ncompetitive engagement among participants. It enhanced skills such as\\nteamwork, strategic thinking, communication, and creative problem-solving.\\nThrough participation in diverse tasks, I gained exposure to multidisciplinary\\nchallenges, improved adaptability, and strengthened my ability to work\\neffectively in team-based, high-pressure environments.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":null,"description":"I participated in RUSH HOURS 5.0, a five-day inter-collegiate competitive\\nevent organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. The event was designed to\\nfoster teamwork, problem-solving skills, creativity, and healthy competition\\nthrough a series of interactive challenges conducted over multiple days. Each\\nday featured a unique task that tested participants’ analytical thinking,\\ncreativity, collaboration, and performance skills across various domains\\nincluding digital problem-solving, social awareness, artistic expression, and\\ninnovation.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Xn7kfnSriOVvS9I-ewEOu","name":"Voluntary Blood Donation Drive","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/luMOyeEcm74TyIg_CNsps.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The voluntary blood donation activity resulted in meaningful social and personal impact. \\nThrough participation in the program, I developed a deeper understanding of the importance of humanitarian service and social responsibility. The activity enhanced my awareness of public health issues and the critical role that individuals can play in saving lives.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in a voluntary blood donation program organized by the Blood Transfusion and Immunohaematology Unit of the Kidwai Memorial Institute of Oncology, Bengaluru. The event aimed to encourage students and the public to voluntarily donate blood to support patients in need of critical medical care.\\nDuring the program, medical professionals ensured that all safety and hygiene protocols were followed. After a preliminary health check, I voluntarily donated one unit of blood. The event highlighted the importance of blood donation in saving lives and strengthening the healthcare system. It also served as a platform to create awareness about social responsibility and humanitarian service among participants.\\nThe blood donation drive successfully motivated individuals to contribute towards a noble cause and emphasized the role of youth in supporting community welfare and public health initiatives.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RZ7e3MkHUjmF1JJljG6GN","name":"Fist Full Donation Drive","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/Ig1VBkT6Sjxw1w7-Clutm.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"The Fist Full donation drive had a significant social impact by contributing essential food resources to underprivileged individuals and communities. The activity helped strengthen the culture of volunteering and social service among students.\\nThrough participation in the event, I developed a deeper understanding of social issues such as poverty and food insecurity. The event enhanced my sense of responsibility towards society and encouraged me to actively participate in community-oriented initiatives.\\nAdditionally, the activity improved my awareness of teamwork and collective effort in achieving social goals. Overall, the event contributed to the development of values such as empathy, generosity, and civic responsibility\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The “Fist Full” event was organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering as a social service initiative aimed at collecting essential food items such as rice and toor dal from students. The objective of the event was to encourage students to contribute towards supporting underprivileged communities and promoting the spirit of social responsibility.\\nDuring the event, students voluntarily donated food grains, which were later distributed to people in need. The campaign fostered a sense of empathy and collective responsibility among participants. I actively participated in the event by contributing to the donation drive, thereby supporting the initiative to address food insecurity and community welfare.\\nThe event also helped in spreading awareness about the importance of sharing resources and contributing to social causes. It served as an effective platform for students to engage in meaningful community service activities.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Edgk1Hbf3ktoyIagGIEa6","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c70d3394-7638-415b-b6bf-82ab2bc95fbf/3JcK6aPmEJiwA9UpfJ0b1.png"],"endDate":"2023-05-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative contributed towards improving access to basic educational\\nresources for underprivileged children, thereby supporting regular school\\nattendance and a better learning environment.Through my involvement, I developed a stronger\\nunderstanding of community engagement, social responsibility, and the role of\\ncollective action in addressing educational challenges faced by marginalized\\ncommunities.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-05-12","hoursSpent":null,"description":"I participated in Project Pustak 2023 (Pusthaka – Stationery Kit\\nDistribution Program), a social service initiative jointly organized by RV\\nCollege of Engineering and Pranav Foundation. The project was aimed at\\naddressing the lack of basic stationery among children from underprivileged\\ncommunities studying in rural government schools. Observations from earlier\\noutreach highlighted that the absence of essential supplies such as notebooks\\nand geometry boxes led to irregular class attendance among students. ","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 09:24:30.612726+00', '2026-02-01 10:40:02.944883+00'), ('8c1e80e1-73f4-42ba-bb7d-0aaceb48f03c', '2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS141","name":"Prajwal M Biradar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"SuyTKWkcfcma0JzCxqF_i","name":"Kannada Habba - Karnata","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":22,"outcomes":"Promoted awareness and pride in Kannada language and culture among students.\\nProvided a platform for students to showcase artistic and cultural talents.\\nStrengthened cultural unity and inclusiveness on campus.\\nEncouraged active participation in regional heritage activities.\\nEnhanced appreciation of Karnataka’s traditions and values within the RVCE community.\\nFostered teamwork and event management skills among Kannada Sangha volunteers.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-05-15","hoursSpent":11,"description":"Kannada Habba was a vibrant cultural celebration organized by the Kannada Sangha of RVCE \\nto promote and preserve Karnataka’s rich language, heritage, and traditions. The event brought \\ntogether students and faculty to celebrate Kannada literature, folk arts, music, and cultural \\npride.\\nThe program featured various performances including classical and folk dance, music, poetry \\nrecitations, skits, and speeches highlighting the significance of the Kannada language and \\nKarnataka’s cultural identity. Students actively participated in showcasing traditional art forms, \\ncostumes, and customs, creating an engaging and festive atmosphere across the campus.\\nKannada Habba served as a platform to encourage linguistic pride, cultural awareness, and \\nunity among students, while strengthening appreciation for regional heritage within the RVCE \\ncommunity.","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/QX-070euW127YM-UhFoPe.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iv6CW8Bh9fyM4zywxcI4n","name":"Campus Clean Up Drive","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced campus cleanliness and hygiene standards.\\nCreated awareness about waste segregation and sustainable practices among students.\\nEncouraged student participation in social and environmental service activities.\\nDeveloped teamwork, leadership, and civic responsibility among NSS volunteers.\\nReinforced the value of environmental conservation within the RVCE community.\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS initiatives in promoting social responsibility.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-13","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Campus Clean-Up Drive to promote \\nenvironmental awareness and encourage responsible waste management practices among \\nstudents. The initiative aimed to maintain a clean, hygienic, and eco-friendly campus \\nenvironment while fostering a sense of social and civic responsibility.\\nVolunteers actively participated in collecting litter, segregating waste, and ensuring proper \\ndisposal across different areas of the RVCE campus. The drive also educated students on \\nthe importance of cleanliness, sustainability, and adopting environmentally friendly habits in \\ndaily life. Through enthusiastic participation, the event successfully conveyed the message that \\ncollective effort is essential in maintaining a green and healthy campus.","aicteMapping":"Environmental  Sustainability","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/YmMHWHoEncPYgColHX2U2.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-hk7RVEDshgleXVxTDZJw","name":"Campus Clean Up Drive II","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced campus cleanliness and hygiene standards.\\nCreated awareness about waste segregation and sustainable practices among students.\\nEncouraged student participation in social and environmental service activities.\\nDeveloped teamwork, leadership, and civic responsibility among NSS volunteers.\\nReinforced the value of environmental conservation within the RVCE community.\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS initiatives in promoting social responsibility.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-27","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Campus Clean-Up Drive to promote \\nenvironmental awareness and encourage responsible waste management practices among \\nstudents. The initiative aimed to maintain a clean, hygienic, and eco-friendly campus \\nenvironment while fostering a sense of social and civic responsibility.\\nVolunteers actively participated in collecting litter, segregating waste, and ensuring proper \\ndisposal across different areas of the RVCE campus. The drive also educated students on \\nthe importance of cleanliness, sustainability, and adopting environmentally friendly habits in \\ndaily life. Through enthusiastic participation, the event successfully conveyed the message that \\ncollective effort is essential in maintaining a green and healthy campus.","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/tCs8BlI0it9us9VnbJM14.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"E_4qgd4BkDdgdquJMHL65","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed social responsibility and humanitarian values\\nGained awareness of blood donation procedures and safety protocols\\nContributed directly to public health and lifesaving efforts\\nEncouraged participation in future community service activities","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":3,"description":"A Voluntary Blood Donation Camp was organized at RV College of Engineering (RVCE), \\nBengaluru, in association with the Indira Gandhi Institute of Child Health, Government of \\nKarnataka. The objective of the camp was to promote social responsibility among students and \\nto support patients requiring blood for emergency and critical medical treatment, especially \\nchildren.\\nI voluntarily donated one unit of blood after completing the prescribed medical screening and \\neligibility procedures. The event was conducted in a safe and hygienic environment under the \\nsupervision of qualified medical professionals, emphasizing the importance of voluntary blood \\ndonation and community participation in lifesaving initiatives.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human  Values (UHV) &  Social Responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/ysJzfl17whxA5MqieacV5.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gSemxt7tPqXtpwFho5WSi","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus and   Outskirts","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Encouraged physical fitness and healthy lifestyle habits among students.\\nPromoted social awareness and participation in community-oriented causes.\\nDeveloped discipline, perseverance, and endurance through marathon participation.\\nStrengthened student engagement in NSS initiatives.\\nFostered a spirit of teamwork and motivation among participants.\\nEarned 10 activity points for active participation and commitment.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering organized the Utsarga \\nMarathon to promote physical fitness, social responsibility, and awareness towards meaningful \\ncommunity causes. The marathon encouraged students to actively participate in a \\nhealth-focused \\nand service-oriented activity that combined endurance, discipline, and commitment to social \\nwelfare.\\nParticipants took part in different distance categories, fostering enthusiasm for fitness and \\nteamwork. I actively participated in the 5 KM category of the Utsarga Marathon, demonstrating \\ncommitment toward health, perseverance, and support for a worthy social cause.\\nThe event successfully motivated students to adopt a healthy lifestyle while contributing to \\nNSS’s mission of community engagement and social consciousness.","aicteMapping":"Health & Fitness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/7RQobV14rdQfISjmFhD8I.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9GppOH-C0MktblOte4oYG","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus and Outskirts","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced physical fitness and mental endurance\\nDeveloped discipline, determination, and time management\\nStrengthened commitment toward community service\\nIncreased awareness about social responsibility through NSS initiatives\\nEncouraged active participation in future social and outreach programs","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The UTSARGA Marathon 2025 was organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV \\nCollege of Engineering (RVCE) with the objective of promoting community service, social \\nawareness, and physical well-being among students. The event aimed to encourage active \\nparticipation of youth in initiatives that support societal welfare and healthy lifestyles.\\nI actively participated in the marathon, demonstrating commitment toward community service \\nand social responsibility. The event fostered values such as discipline, perseverance, teamwork, \\nand self-motivation. In recognition of my participation and dedication, I was awarded 15 NSS \\nactivity points.","aicteMapping":"Health & Fitness ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/fk2_xTlxaesY2cLNRF8d0.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3mteX7EWwPXUaX4mqqOIp","name":"Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-03","duration":23,"outcomes":"Developed awareness about environmental sustainability and tree conservation\\nEncouraged responsible participation in eco-friendly initiatives\\nPromoted the habit of tree plantation and green practices\\nStrengthened social responsibility toward protecting the environment\\nInspired long-term commitment to sustainable living","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-11","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The “Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree” initiative was organized at RV College of Engineering (RVCE) \\nby Kannada Sangha with the objective of promoting environmental awareness and sustainable \\npractices among students. The activity aimed to encourage students to actively contribute toward \\nenvironmental conservation through tree plantation.\\nAs part of the initiative, students who purchased the event T-shirt were provided with a \\ntree sapling along with proper guidelines for planting and maintenance. The saplings were \\ndistributed within the college premises, motivating students to take personal responsibility for \\nenvironmental protection. The activity successfully combined awareness creation with practical \\naction toward sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Environmental  Awareness &  Sustainability","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/oAFww6106Jg02wZ64apqf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1zCdU3fKE5NTdBb9uLiEw","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Created awareness about the importance of voting among students.\\nEncouraged active participation in the democratic process.\\nPromoted responsible citizenship and national commitment.\\nStrengthened civic consciousness among youth.\\nReinforced the role of NSS in conducting awareness initiatives","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye was a voter awareness initiative conducted by the National Service \\nScheme (NSS), RVCE to promote civic responsibility and educate students about the \\nimportance \\nof voting in a democratic country. The program aimed to inspire young citizens to actively \\nparticipate in the electoral process and understand their role in nation-building.\\nThrough awareness sessions and pledge activities, participants were encouraged to register as \\nvoters, understand electoral procedures, and exercise their voting rights responsibly. The event \\nsuccessfully fostered a sense of patriotism and civic consciousness among students.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Programs","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/qGWhnCtB967Tzmmv_7aoF.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nni9LIbH-Ao-vOdfaS-RA","name":"Mega Plantation @Hosadurga","slNo":9,"place":"Hosadurga","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased green cover in the Hosadurga region through large-scale plantation.\\nPromoted environmental awareness among students and local residents.\\nEncouraged active student participation in eco-friendly community service.\\nDeveloped a sense of social and environmental responsibility among volunteers.\\nContributed to long-term ecological sustainability and environmental restoration.\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS environmental initiatives at RVCE.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-09","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Mega Plantation Drive at Hosadurga, \\nas part of its environmental sustainability and community outreach initiatives. The primary \\nobjective of the event was to enhance green cover, promote afforestation, and create awareness \\nabout environmental conservation among students and local communities.\\nNSS volunteers actively participated in planting saplings across identified areas in Hosadurga, \\ncontributing to soil conservation, ecological restoration, and long-term environmental \\nimprovement. The drive also encouraged students to take responsibility for protecting nature \\nand \\nemphasized the importance of tree plantation in reducing pollution and maintaining ecological \\nbalance.\\nThrough collective participation, the initiative successfully demonstrated the role of youth in \\nbuilding a greener and healthier society.","aicteMapping":"Environmental   Sustainability","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2658cd52-fc46-439b-a083-c53000a45720/5Cmt3C7-UL0CCrA1Okovu.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 16:11:32.669863+00', '2026-02-01 20:20:44.82149+00'), ('8e66f8d7-b562-4cf8-8f06-18a72c522e4d', '187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY025","name":"DHANYASHREE R","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"aPZ79iDIEixbTAZT9gI3W","name":"Biofuel day essay competition and model making ","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/C-p1C1eFkT-2LvsIAOU2Z.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I gained a better understanding of biofuels as a renewable and eco-friendly energy source. I learned how biofuels help reduce dependence on fossil fuels and minimize environmental pollution. The activity also improved my research skills, creative thinking, and writing ability. It taught me how to analyze a topic, structure my ideas logically, and express them confidently. Overall, this activity increased my awareness of sustainable energy solutions and motivated me to think responsibly about environmental conservation.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-08","hoursSpent":2.5,"description":"As part of International Biofuel Day, our department organized an Essay Writing and Model Making Competition. I actively participated in this activity, which was conducted to create awareness about biofuels and their importance in today’s world. The event encouraged students to explore alternative energy sources and understand their role in sustainable development. During the activity, I researched various types of biofuels, their sources, and their applications. This helped me organize my thoughts clearly and present them effectively through writing.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t5esQdGCdAURBzNu-0tB2","name":"Campus Cleanup Program ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/dyoi8HAPZ4X_9zNVpYp_E.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this campus cleanup program, I learned the importance of cleanliness and hygiene in our daily lives. I understood that maintaining a clean environment helps prevent diseases and creates a positive atmosphere for learning. The activity also taught me teamwork, discipline, and social responsibility. It made me realize that cleanliness is not only the duty of cleaning staff but also the responsibility of every individual. This program motivated me to practice cleanliness regularly and encourage others to do the same.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-13","hoursSpent":4,"description":"NSS organized a Campus Cleanup Program to promote cleanliness and environmental responsibility among students. I actively participated in this program along with my classmates. During the activity, we cleaned classrooms, corridors, open areas, and surroundings of the campus by collecting waste and disposing of it properly. The program aimed to create awareness about maintaining a clean and healthy environment within the college premises. All students worked together with great enthusiasm and teamwork, making the activity successful.","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kHyT7Ba_RbmpFo4OU3u6v","name":"Utsarga Marathon ","slNo":3,"place":"Near Sattva Global City ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/jlA9zvqQilCHbNrCRliy9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this marathon, I learned the importance of physical fitness and mental strength. Participating in the run helped me understand how regular exercise improves stamina, concentration, and overall health. The activity also taught me self-discipline, perseverance, and teamwork. It motivated me to include physical activities in my daily routine and realize that a healthy body leads to a healthy mind. Overall, the marathon was an inspiring experience that promoted unity and well-being.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of our college organized  Utsarga Marathon to promote fitness, health awareness, and social responsibility among students. I actively participated in this event along with many volunteers and students. The marathon was conducted within and around ( Near Sattva Global city ) the college premises, and it was organized in a disciplined and well-planned manner. The event encouraged students to adopt a healthy lifestyle and understand the importance of physical fitness.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/KS1jbCQRwwY5ZTBOyWeSR.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wBiw2HFup_GU5DEZEC6IG","name":"Mere Phale Vote Desh Keliye ","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/ByQwRUm2soJO6An0nFdw2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I learned that voting is a fundamental right and duty of every citizen. I understood how a single vote can contribute to shaping the future of our country. The program helped me realize the importance of being an informed and responsible voter. It also increased my sense of patriotism, civic responsibility, and commitment towards the nation. This activity motivated me to actively participate in elections and encourage others to vote responsibly.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Our college NSS unit organized an awareness program titled “Mere Pehle Vote Desh Ke Liye” to encourage students to understand the importance of voting. The program aimed to motivate first-time voters to actively participate in the democratic process. Volunteers spread awareness about voter registration, voting rights, and the role of youth in nation-building. The activity created awareness about responsible citizenship and democracy.","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"co3OQDth7SPf3PVXCjeD2","name":"Vision ","slNo":5,"place":"Panchasheela PU College ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/IJVHmM30rpRioU4nRTCyf.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this career guidance initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, I learned the importance of social responsibility and community service. Interacting with underprivileged students helped me understand the challenges they face in accessing proper career guidance and educational opportunities. I realized how right guidance at the right time can shape a student’s future and build confidence in their abilities. This activity improved my communication, leadership, and empathy skills, and taught me the value of motivating others. Overall, the experience inspired me to contribute positively to society and support students in achieving their educational and career goals.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a career guidance session for over 500 underprivileged students across eight schools and colleges. This initiative aimed to empower students by providing essential guidance and support to help them navigate educational and career paths. The schools and colleges visited included BET Convent, Mount Carmel English School, Ashwini Primary High School, Government PU College Kengeri, New National PU College, Panchasheela PU College, Nehru Memorial School, and Priyadarshini Vidhya Kendra School. By offering insights into various fields of study and career options, the Rotaract Club sought to inspire confidence and ambition in these students, encouraging them to pursue their dreams despite challenges.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FGMVBxOWCvMjtOKj7kOvx","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through Project Pustak, I learned the true value of empathy, social service, and collective responsibility. The activity helped me understand how even small contributions matters. I contributed Rs 350 that can make a meaningful difference in the lives of underprivileged students when combined for a good cause. I realized the importance of education and how access to basic school supplies can motivate students and improve their learning experience. This initiative also taught me the significance of teamwork, transparent fund utilization, and community collaboration. Overall, the project inspired me to actively participate in social welfare activities and contribute towards building a more inclusive and educated society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 ог Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/VAk0UlY6hXU5vekWff6ME.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rXTc0d0Nk_n6uxprTeGJy","name":"Mega Plantation ","slNo":8,"place":"Kanakapura Road ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/UhyMibya1y1fdyj89RjpM.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this mega plantation activity, I learned the importance of protecting the environment and conserving nature. I understood how planting trees helps in reducing pollution, improving air quality, and preserving biodiversity. The activity also taught me teamwork, responsibility, and commitment towards environmental conservation. It made me realize that small efforts like planting and nurturing trees can lead to long-term benefits for future generations. This program motivated me to adopt eco-friendly habits and actively contribute to a greener and healthier environment.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-25","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of our college organized a Mega Plantation Drive to promote environmental awareness and sustainability. I actively participated in this program along with other NSS volunteers. During the activity, saplings were planted in and around the campus and nearby areas. The main objective of the program was to increase green cover and create awareness about the importance of trees in maintaining ecological balance.","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8l8Y88YkLIS0u0u-LQdC4","name":"FistFull","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/b-TniBEzk6Dv3da-TRdmw.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"Through this food donation initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, I learned the importance of compassion, unity, and social responsibility. The overwhelming participation of students showed how small individual contributions can collectively create a massive impact. I understood the value of helping the underprivileged and addressing basic needs like food security.  Overall, it strengthened my belief in community welfare and motivated me to actively participate in social service initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_5kAb_cTxokP1PIkPCfei","name":"Inkspire","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/YdGSofVe2RfqzuwS19A_A.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-10-28","duration":4,"outcomes":"Through Inkspire, I learned the power of words in creating awareness and driving social change. The initiative helped me understand how storytelling can effectively address important themes such as sustainability, health, equality, and education. I also learned the value of creative expression and inclusivity, as participants were encouraged to write in multiple languages and formats. This activity enhanced my writing skills, critical thinking, and social sensitivity, and showed me how creative platforms can amplify meaningful voices. Overall, Inkspire inspired me to use creativity responsibly and contribute positively to society through thoughtful communication.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-10-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Inkspire was created to inspire compassionate storytelling, inviting participants to explore themes like sustainability, health, equality, and education. Writers submitted original prose, poetry, articles, creative non-fiction, and flash fiction in English, Hindi, and Kannada, fostering inclusivity and creative diversity. Selected entries were showcased in the club''s magazine or blog, while standout pieces were highlighted on Instagram, providing a platform for voices championing positive change. The event successfully united participants in using their words as a catalyst for social impact.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dG3Ke6qaO-L0IZDv_hiq1","name":"Police Marshal ","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/AsBsr9IkBii7zJWaKNukD.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this seminar, I learned the importance of traffic discipline, public safety, and civic responsibility. I understood how police marshals assist law enforcement in managing traffic and ensuring safety during emergencies and public events. The session helped me become more aware of traffic rules and the role of citizens in supporting law enforcement agencies. It also instilled a sense of responsibility, alertness, and respect for law and order. Overall, the seminar motivated me to follow safety rules and act as a responsible citizen.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) organized a seminar on the Police Marshal Program to create awareness about public safety, traffic management, and civic responsibility. The seminar was conducted by police officials and resource persons who explained the role and responsibilities of police marshals in maintaining law and order. Topics such as traffic rules, emergency response, crowd control, and the importance of citizen cooperation with the police were discussed. The session was informative and interactive, helping students understand the significance of discipline and safety in society.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"aLIlMAKHNfL8wz3iRfPhK","name":"Vikasit Bharath Quiz ","slNo":11,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/7eKUHgoLySyUEV5cljnHt.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through the Viksit Bharat Quiz, I gained a deeper understanding of India’s development goals and nation-building efforts. I learned about various government initiatives and the role of youth in contributing to a developed India. The activity improved my general knowledge, critical thinking, and awareness of current affairs. It also instilled a sense of patriotism, responsibility, and confidence, motivating me to actively participate in the country’s progress.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) organized the Viksit Bharat Quiz to create awareness among students about India’s development, government initiatives, and national progress. The quiz covered topics such as economic growth, digital development, education, infrastructure, and social welfare schemes. Students actively participated in the quiz, making the event informative, engaging, and competitive. The objective of the activity was to enhance knowledge about India’s vision for a developed nation.","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TcpTblmykRpG8Nu1JrpR9","name":"Rush Hours ","slNo":12,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/zbo4L2kZ-vilviXVBmr6x.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"Through Rush Hours 5.0, I learned the importance of quick thinking, problem-solving, and teamwork in competitive environments. Participating in the first task, Cyber Chase, helped me improve my analytical skills and ability to decode cryptic clues under time pressure. Although I was eliminated after the first task, the experience taught me the value of learning from challenges and setbacks. I realized that participation itself helps build confidence, adaptability, and resilience. The event also exposed me to the power of creativity, digital platforms, and social engagement, motivating me to improve my skills and perform better in future competitions.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":5,"description":"With more than 450 participants, Rush Hours 5.0 was an exciting five-day event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, designed to engage participants in a series of creative and competitive tasks. Each day featured a unique challenge, and based on their performance, some teams faced elimination. The gradual elimination process added intensity and kept the teams motivated to give their best. On the final day, the top three teams, who demonstrated consistent performance and creativity, were announced as the winners.\\n\\nTASK 1: Cyber Chase - A fast-paced online treasure hunt across social media platforms, testing teams'' problem-solving and strategic thinking as they raced to crack cryptic clues.\\n\\nTASK 2: Capture the Cause-Participants creatively addressed social issues through handmade posters or photographs, showcasing teamwork and artistic expression.\\n\\nTASK 3: Beyond the Frame Teams submitted performance-based videos inspired by films, featuring monologues, dances, or artistic imitations that reflected individual passion.\\n\\nTASK 4: DIY Wear It! A DIY fashion challenge where participants designed and submitted unique handmade accessories, highlighting creativity and craftsmanship.\\n\\nTASK 5: The Social Showdown Top teams promoted their content on social media platforms to gain likes and comments, competing for points based on engagement to win the final round.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sGZbx6gkI-N32HPnPIDa3","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":13,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through Project Pustak, I learned the true value of empathy, social service, and collective responsibility. The activity helped me understand how even small contributions, such as Rs.100 or Rs.350, can make a meaningful difference in the lives of underprivileged students when combined for a good cause. I realized the importance of education and how access to basic school supplies can motivate students and improve their learning experience. This initiative also taught me the significance of teamwork, transparent fund utilization, and community collaboration. Overall, the project inspired me to actively participate in social welfare activities and contribute towards building a more inclusive and educated society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-14","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 ог Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/cu82wkoLNMKE0pvU-fSwZ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tiE_RzeTT_5Boutw-wVX1","name":"Utsarga Marathon ","slNo":14,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/aqFpc5Y9hmZzY-F33FVEh.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this marathon, I learned the importance of physical fitness and mental strength. Participating in the run helped me understand how regular exercise improves stamina, concentration, and overall health. The activity also taught me self-discipline, perseverance, and teamwork. It motivated me to include physical activities in my daily routine and realize that a healthy body leads to a healthy mind. Overall, the marathon was an inspiring experience that promoted unity and well-being.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of our college organized  Utsarga Marathon to promote fitness, health awareness, and social responsibility among students. I actively participated in this event along with many volunteers and students. The marathon was conducted within and around ( Near Sattva Global city ) the college premises, and it was organized in a disciplined and well-planned manner. The event encouraged students to adopt a healthy lifestyle and understand the importance of physical fitness.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hmWlCWkzzd3QUzVInxM4_","name":"Nasha Mukta Bharatha ","slNo":15,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/SLw5Hb-qFXNqr4f4PMELO.png"],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through the Nasha Mukta Bharat program, I learned about the serious physical, mental, and social consequences of substance abuse. I understood the importance of self-control, awareness, and peer support in preventing addiction. The activity made me realize the role of youth in spreading awareness and supporting a healthy lifestyle. It strengthened my sense of social responsibility and commitment towards building a drug-free and healthier society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS) organized a Nasha Mukta Bharat awareness program to educate students and the public about the harmful effects of drug and substance abuse. The program aimed to spread awareness about leading a healthy and addiction-free life. Through talks, discussions, and awareness messages, the activity highlighted the importance of making responsible choices and promoting a drug-free society.","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Jg2yHt0ys53awTUY7sEFl","name":"Echolore","slNo":16,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/LgPTWBfE2sODaN0K-3PGA.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through Echolore, I learned the power of storytelling as a tool for awareness and social change. The event helped me understand how creative writing can effectively highlight important issues such as saving mothers and children, environmental protection, and cultural heritage. I also learned the value of empathy, imagination, and self-expression, as participants shared their thoughts in different languages and forms. This activity enhanced my creative thinking, communication skills, and social sensitivity. Overall, Echolore inspired me to use my creativity responsibly and contribute positively to society through thoughtful storytelling.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-16","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V.C.E. organized Echolore, an event celebrating storytelling on themes of Saving Mothers & Children, Environment and Folklore. Participants shared their creative pieces in the form of essays, poems, articles and prose in different languages like English, Hindi, or Kannada, using creativity and care to express their ideas. The event provided a platform for participants to share their voices and reflect on how stories can make a difference in the world. Through their writing, contributors connected with one another and discovered new ways to express their thoughts and feelings. The event brought a positive change by inspiring participants to think deeply about social and environmental issues. Echolore was more than a storytelling event - it was a space to celebrate imagination, empathy and the impact that thoughtful writings can have on society.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LLSjk4ZgUNF389nAHcdQL","name":"Voting Awareness Seminar","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/xUwcN7pANh2ngurw9Y251.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this seminar, I learned that voting is both a right and a responsibility of every citizen. I understood how each vote contributes to the future of the nation and the importance of making informed choices. The seminar increased my awareness about the electoral process and motivated me to actively participate in elections. It also strengthened my sense of civic duty, patriotism, and responsibility towards society.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-09","hoursSpent":2,"description":"A Voting Awareness Seminar was organized to educate students about the importance of voting in a democratic country. The seminar focused on creating awareness about voting rights, the election process, and the role of citizens in choosing responsible leaders. Resource persons explained the significance of informed voting and encouraged young voters to actively participate in elections. The session was informative and helped students understand their role in strengthening democracy.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":1,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5-DJsknJiVVb7emGNQbOZ","name":"Space, Science and Technology Essay Competition","slNo":18,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/nMo4dvVgROc86Z73ryU-e.png"],"endDate":"2023-09-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this essay competition, I gained a deeper understanding of the role of science and technology in shaping the future. I learned about recent developments in space research and how technological advancements contribute to national and global progress. The activity improved my research, analytical thinking, and writing skills. It also inspired curiosity, innovation, and a scientific mindset, motivating me to stay updated with advancements in science and technology.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-09-01","hoursSpent":3,"description":"An Essay Competition on Space, Science, and Technology was organized to encourage students to explore advancements in science and their impact on society. The competition provided a platform for participants to express their ideas on space exploration, scientific innovations, and technological development. Students researched various topics related to space missions, emerging technologies, and future scientific possibilities, which helped enhance their knowledge and interest in science.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive ","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wQwj39Vjm_ouGgknH8Bnc","name":"FistFull","slNo":19,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/187330a1-4fcb-48c5-8c66-4a18212bca39/QyMOUEOc1hoA4QlyX8p6h.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"Through Fistful, I learned the impact of collective effort in addressing serious social issues like food insecurity and health support. The initiative showed how small individual contributions, when combined, can provide meaningful nutritional aid to vulnerable communities. I understood the importance of community service, empathy, and social responsibility, especially in supporting health and care institutions. This activity also highlighted the role of youth participation in driving positive change. Overall, Fistful motivated me to actively contribute to initiatives that promote social welfare and public health.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fistful was a standalone community service project designed to combat food insecurity and support health and care institutions through collective student participation. The initiative was built on a simple yet impactful principle every participating student donated either 5 kilograms of rice or 2 kilograms of dal. With the support of Rotary Bangalore Spandana and under the Community Service avenue focusing on Fighting Disease, the project transformed individual contributions into large-scale nutritional support for vulnerable communities.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 05:36:37.463189+00', '2026-01-30 07:33:57.268706+00'), ('8ecd1acb-9778-47e3-86f4-9fad21482e30', 'f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD061","name":"Tarun H S","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"wmZ1NUBNsJdERgYRhfYw-","name":"PD Kannada Sangha","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/NbZ2WAF8gOw-nKprNC1Q5.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-02","duration":33,"outcomes":"Enhanced appreciation of Kannada culture and arts among students.\\n\\nShowcased creativity in stage production, design, and event management.\\n\\nStrengthened teamwork and collaboration within the Kannada Sangha.\\n\\nProvided a platform for students to perform and express cultural talent.","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-01-01","hoursSpent":18,"description":"Our campus recently came alive with the vibrant celebration organized by the Kannada Sangha, showcasing the rich cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event featured a stunning array of performances, including traditional dance, music, and skits, all brought to life through meticulous production and design efforts. The stage setup, lighting, and décor were thoughtfully crafted to reflect Karnataka’s cultural essence, while costumes and props added authenticity and visual appeal to each performance. The seamless coordination between performers and the production team created an immersive experience, engaging the audience from start to finish. This event not only celebrated language and art but also highlighted the creativity, teamwork, and technical skills involved in bringing a cultural vision to life on campus.","aicteMapping":"College Event and Co oridination","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/1wiXxoDlADtHIqdCUDcql.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MQCVkeKJAwpNdjMPeMpWM","name":"Pd kannda sangha","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/8Hkm-G20MXdL8ei5NHFCO.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-12","duration":12,"outcomes":"Enhanced appreciation of Kannada culture and arts among students.\\n\\nShowcased creativity in stage production, design, and event management.\\n\\nStrengthened teamwork and collaboration within the Kannada Sangha.\\n\\nProvided a platform for students to perform and express cultural talent.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":20,"description":"Our campus recently came alive with the vibrant celebration organized by the Kannada Sangha, showcasing the rich cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event featured a stunning array of performances, including traditional dance, music, and skits, all brought to life through meticulous production and design efforts. The stage setup, lighting, and décor were thoughtfully crafted to reflect Karnataka’s cultural essence, while costumes and props added authenticity and visual appeal to each performance. The seamless coordination between performers and the production team created an immersive experience, engaging the audience from start to finish. This event not only celebrated language and art but also highlighted the creativity, teamwork, and technical skills involved in bringing a cultural vision to life on campus.","aicteMapping":"College Event ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6Eug6afQx5oFmi2mQT1Nu","name":"PD kannda sangha","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/r2hVVdEYmLSqTx7BIXrVj.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/sL4E9ctFijJ-P6vNMNn8z.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/F8-Qm0fitNjQh3dUMVBIU.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/5MQ86KjUCxGNhBYbJZ2Y8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-01-18","duration":49,"outcomes":"Enhanced appreciation of Kannada culture and arts among students.\\n\\nShowcased creativity in stage production, design, and event management.\\n\\nStrengthened teamwork and collaboration within the Kannada Sangha.\\n\\nProvided a platform for students to perform and express cultural talent.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-12-01","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Our campus recently came alive with the vibrant celebration organized by the Kannada Sangha, showcasing the rich cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event featured a stunning array of performances, including traditional dance, music, and skits, all brought to life through meticulous production and design efforts. The stage setup, lighting, and décor were thoughtfully crafted to reflect Karnataka’s cultural essence, while costumes and props added authenticity and visual appeal to each performance. The seamless coordination between performers and the production team created an immersive experience, engaging the audience from start to finish. This event not only celebrated language and art but also highlighted the creativity, teamwork, and technical skills involved in bringing a cultural vision to life on campus.","aicteMapping":"College event","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XS0lT1n9CJun5YeHtCTur","name":"Fist Full","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/OJKjNu7WZRfX2-Rx3fVbL.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-27","duration":2,"outcomes":"Collected essential items and funds to support underprivileged individuals or local charities.\\n\\nRaised awareness among students about social responsibility and community service.\\n\\nStrengthened the sense of empathy, teamwork, and active participation in service-oriented activities.\\n\\nEncouraged ongoing engagement in Rotaract social initiatives.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-26","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club organized the “Fistful Donation” initiative on campus, aiming to extend a helping hand to those in need. Students and faculty actively contributed small donations, which collectively made a significant impact. The activity was designed to foster a culture of generosity, empathy, and social responsibility among participants. Through creative promotion and engagement, the initiative encouraged everyone to participate, highlighting how even modest contributions can bring meaningful change to the community.","aicteMapping":"Social Welfare","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5EEWEOALkc1eOimwG8q2G","name":"Akshara","slNo":5,"place":"Sai Sri Vidya Chetana","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/ljd7nDQzApPGvCWit6xX3.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-24","duration":18,"outcomes":"Over 1,000 underprivileged students benefited from enhanced academic understanding and essential skills.\\n\\nVolunteers gained hands-on teaching experience, developing communication and mentorship skills.\\n\\nImproved awareness of educational disparities and the importance of quality education.\\n\\nStrengthened community engagement and promoted the value of volunteerism among students.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Rotaract Cf ub of RVCE held skill development sessions in eight\\nBangalore schools, benefiting over 1000 underprivileged students.\\nTargeting financially modest backgrounds, the sessions enhanced\\nacademic understanding and provided essential skills. Schools visited\\nincluded BET Convent, Sai Sri Vidya Chethana, Vishwa Bharathi High\\nSchool, Kengeri High School, Government Model Primary School, Nehru\\nMemorial School, Priyadarshini Vidhya Kendra School, and Mount\\nCarmel English School. The initiative used interactive methods for\\ncurriculum-based learning to ensure relevance and engagement.\\nVolunteers gained valuable experience as teachers, fostering\\nappreciation for the profession and addressing educational disparities.\\nThis initiative underscored the power of volunteerism and the need for\\nquality education for all.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":14,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YHyalUjZffpNSm5ZL6Ufr","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":6,"place":"Hutridurga Betta","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/6TxxmjjZmkoUCnqvWCp82.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-01-24","duration":2,"outcomes":"FAST TREK 2.0 witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 750 students, making it a highly successful and impactful event. The cleanliness drive helped create awareness about environmental conservation and responsible tourism among participants. The trek fostered teamwork, physical endurance, and a sense of community while strengthening the club’s outreach and engagement. Overall, the event achieved its social, recreational, and organizational objectives, leaving participants with a memorable experience and a heightened sense of environmental responsibility.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-01-23","hoursSpent":10,"description":"FAST TREK 2.0 was a flagship trekking event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of promoting environmental responsibility along with adventure and fitness. The event included a cleanliness drive as its core social initiative, emphasizing the importance of preserving natural ecosystems. The trek commenced at 7:30 AM, with participants being briefed on safety measures and event guidelines before departure. The trekking route covered the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills, offering participants an engaging and refreshing experience amidst nature. The event was carefully coordinated to ensure participant safety, discipline, and environmental awareness throughout the journey.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":18,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1olfji8A5v8uc4r1IqR3I","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/ICv7MiXjYj_2ZMSCWcX6v.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon received enthusiastic participation from students, creating a strong platform for promoting physical fitness and social awareness. The event successfully fostered unity, discipline, and motivation among participants while highlighting the importance of giving back to society. It enhanced student engagement, volunteer coordination, and leadership skills, making the marathon a meaningful and impactful initiative. Overall, the event fulfilled its objectives by combining health, awareness, and community service in a single successful initiative.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-07-18","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Utsarga Marathon was an awareness-driven running event organized at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) with the aim of promoting fitness, social responsibility, and community engagement. The marathon encouraged participants to adopt a healthy lifestyle while supporting the spirit of selflessness and social contribution. Prior to the event, participants were briefed about safety guidelines, race rules, and the significance of the marathon. The event witnessed active involvement from students and volunteers, ensuring smooth coordination and disciplined execution throughout the run.","aicteMapping":"Awarness Program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/Zk8D1d--A_z0YinC5Efe-.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"08Oi0fjGlF7PvC6uZq6e6","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon received enthusiastic participation from students, creating a strong platform for promoting physical fitness and social awareness. The event successfully fostered unity, discipline, and motivation among participants while highlighting the importance of giving back to society. It enhanced student engagement, volunteer coordination, and leadership skills, making the marathon a meaningful and impactful initiative. Overall, the event fulfilled its objectives by combining health, awareness, and community service in a single successful initiative.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-02-02","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Utsarga Marathon was an awareness-driven running event organized at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) with the aim of promoting fitness, social responsibility, and community engagement. The marathon encouraged participants to adopt a healthy lifestyle while supporting the spirit of selflessness and social contribution. Prior to the event, participants were briefed about safety guidelines, race rules, and the significance of the marathon. The event witnessed active involvement from students and volunteers, ensuring smooth coordination and disciplined execution throughout the run.","aicteMapping":"Awarness Program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f6ee9118-1f8e-44e8-adfb-f8d551ea9ae7/DQdOB7GY_0K5IFIyZV_SS.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 20:40:53.978697+00', '2026-01-30 21:32:17.724342+00'), ('8f6cdbb6-de3b-4244-843b-0aa91c6edf54', 'e52efa8b-4900-4683-bcec-6fa069a4a7c5', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 00:16:15.965189+00', '2026-02-02 02:16:43.6395+00'), ('906af05b-d59b-4702-87ca-7cad9b6ead17', '25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC182","name":"Vinay Kumar K R","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"3IcW80ReADaRu3QELF3Ix","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Bengalurur","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/6fTCvPkOu6Ip7k_ldw-a-.JPG"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the blood donation activity enhanced awareness of public health issues and the\\ncritical role of voluntary blood donors in healthcare systems. The event encouraged a sense of\\ncivic duty and motivated students to contribute positively to society through responsible and\\nethical actions.\\nFurthermore, the experience strengthened values such as empathy, social commitment, and\\ncommunity service. It inspired participants to engage in future outreach and health-related\\ninitiatives, contributing to their holistic development beyond academics while reinforcing the\\nimportance of giving back to society.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The voluntary blood donation activity was conducted as a community service and social\\noutreach initiative in collaboration with BGS Global Hospitals. The activity aimed to support\\nhealthcare services by encouraging voluntary blood donation and promoting awareness about\\nthe importance of safe and timely blood availability. Students willingly participated in the blood\\ndonation camp, demonstrating social responsibility and humanitarian values.\\nThe program emphasized the role of youth in contributing to public health and saving\\nlives through voluntary efforts. Participants were guided through proper medical screening\\nprocedures and educated on the significance of regular blood donation. The initiative helped\\ncreate awareness about the continuous need for blood in hospitals and highlighted how\\nindividual contributions can make a meaningful impact on society.\\nAdditionally, the activity fostered a spirit of compassion, empathy, and service among\\nparticipants. By actively taking part in the blood donation drive, students reinforced the values of\\nselflessness and community engagement. The program successfully aligned with the objectives\\nof extension and outreach activities by integrating health awareness with social responsibility\\nwithin the academic environment.","aicteMapping":"Health & Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/1xwVfeT7ORjJ2eRN9GQFM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"10EZ4wvTxUAYzPHj_RF5m","name":"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree(Kannda Sangha)","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/sBjl4ep4dOgHHT_CRTTnu.jpg"],"endDate":"2026-07-07","duration":366,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully contributed to tree plantation and environmental conservation efforts. It created awareness among participants about the importance of afforestation and sustainable environmental practices. The activity encouraged eco-friendly and responsible behavior among students. Participants developed a sense of environmental responsibility and commitment towards sustainability. The program promoted green initiatives and reinforced the importance of collective efforts in protecting the environment.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The “Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” initiative was organized by Kannada Sangha with the objective of promoting environmental sustainability and encouraging eco-friendly practices among students and the community. The activity connected consumer participation with environmental conservation, where the purchase of a T-shirt directly contributed to planting a tree. This initiative helped spread awareness about the importance of afforestation and the need to conserve natural resources.\\n\\nParticipants actively took part in the program and gained awareness about the role of tree plantation in improving air quality, conserving biodiversity, and addressing climate change. The event emphasized sustainable lifestyle choices and highlighted how individual actions can collectively create a positive environmental impact. Trees were planted through authorized means, ensuring proper growth and long-term environmental benefits. The initiative successfully fostered environmental consciousness and social responsibility among participants.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/J2myg2w0aS4zAJoji4QPl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"snw8XBtM-TDoQOdlxmRFk","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE, Bengaluru","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-06","duration":6,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged students by providing them with essential educational materials. It created awareness about the importance of education and equal access to learning resources. The activity encouraged community participation and social responsibility among volunteers. Participants developed teamwork, organizational, and leadership skills while coordinating collection and distribution activities. The project contributed to reducing educational inequality and promoting inclusive and sustainable educational practices.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-05-01","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Project Pustak was organized with the objective of promoting education and supporting underprivileged students by providing access to learning materials. The initiative focused on collecting and distributing books and study resources to students from economically weaker sections. Participants actively contributed by donating textbooks, notebooks, and other educational materials, ensuring that they could be reused effectively.\\n\\nThe project emphasized the importance of education as a tool for social development and equal opportunity. Volunteers helped in sorting, organizing, and distributing the collected materials to ensure they reached deserving beneficiaries. The activity also created awareness about the value of sharing resources and reducing educational inequality. Through active participation, the project encouraged community involvement and a sense of social responsibility among volunteers. The initiative played a meaningful role in supporting students’ learning needs and promoting inclusive education.","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/4WJdM5MrDa5F_mZvpNI5o.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"brFq_u4QVIiyKlwA0LohR","name":"Kannda Habba - JAGADHVAHA","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/72a7gWGdl4gTvb78jUhqH.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-04","duration":31,"outcomes":"By participating in Kannada Habba Jagadvaha 2025, held on 4 December 2025, I gained\\na stronger appreciation for the cultural richness and linguistic heritage of Karnataka. The\\ncelebration emphasized the importance of preserving and promoting the regional language\\nthrough artistic expression and active community participation.\\nWitnessing the enthusiasm of fellow students in various performances and cultural displays\\nhelped me understand how traditions bring people together and strengthen cultural identity.\\nOverall, the event deepened my respect for Kannada culture and motivated me to remain\\nconnected to my roots while encouraging others to take pride in our shared heritage.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-04","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha 2025 was celebrated on 4 December 2025 at R.V. College\\nof Engineering (RVCE) with great enthusiasm to honor the Kannada language and the\\ncultural heritage of Karnataka. The event aimed to promote awareness, pride, and respect for\\nKannada traditions among students and faculty members. Organized as part of the college’s\\ncultural initiatives, the celebration brought together participants from diverse backgrounds to\\ncollectively experience and appreciate the essence of Karnataka’s rich legacy.\\nThe program featured a wide range of cultural activities showcasing the vibrancy of Kannada\\nculture. Students performed traditional and contemporary dance forms, folk and classical music,\\nskits, and poetry recitations in Kannada. These performances highlighted themes related to\\nKarnataka’s history, social values, and linguistic beauty. The stage décor, traditional attire, and\\nenthusiastic participation created an authentic cultural atmosphere, making the event engaging\\nand memorable for the audience.\\nOverall, Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha 2025 served as an effective platform for cultural\\nexpression and community bonding within the college. The event strengthened cultural\\nawareness, encouraged student participation, and reinforced the importance of preserving\\nregional language and traditions within a modern academic environment. It successfully\\nfostered unity, cultural pride, and respect for Kannada heritage among the RVCE community.","aicteMapping":"Institutional Activity – Cultural & Social Engagement","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/FmNlACOkAd2h9nGjO-gK5.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"L8KX_JN1xUChGrD3XLi5F","name":"Kannada Habba - GHARJANE ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/D6QM-iKRnt33BhnX-hkln.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-20","duration":32,"outcomes":"By participating in Kannada Habba – Gharjane, I gained a deeper appreciation for the richness\\nand significance of the Kannada language and Karnataka’s cultural heritage. The event helped\\nme understand how cultural programs play a vital role in preserving traditions and promoting a\\nstrong sense of cultural identity.\\nI also learned the importance of teamwork and active participation in organizing and celebrating\\ncultural events. Overall, the experience strengthened my cultural awareness and motivated me\\nto respect, preserve, and promote regional traditions.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-05-20","hoursSpent":80,"description":"Kannada Habba – Gharjane was celebrated on 20 June 2024 at R.V. College of Engineering\\n(RVCE) with the objective of promoting the Kannada language and the cultural heritage of\\nKarnataka. The event aimed to foster cultural awareness and instill pride in regional traditions\\namong students and faculty members. Participants from various departments came together,\\ncreating an inclusive platform to celebrate Karnataka’s rich linguistic and cultural legacy.\\nThe program featured a variety of cultural performances, including traditional and contemporary\\ndance forms, folk and classical music, skits, and Kannada poetry recitations. These activities\\nhighlighted the history, values, and artistic richness of Karnataka. The enthusiastic participation\\nof students, complemented by vibrant stage decorations and traditional attire, created an\\nengaging and authentic cultural atmosphere throughout the event.\\nOverall, Kannada Habba – Gharjane served as a meaningful cultural celebration that\\nstrengthened unity and cultural appreciation within the college community. The event\\nsuccessfully encouraged student participation, promoted respect for regional culture, and\\nreinforced the importance of preserving the Kannada language and traditions within an\\nacademic environment.","aicteMapping":"Institutional Activity – Cultural & Social Engagement","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/4waAtvL8fxtVFmx1d0Bpz.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QLuyZMsvrhHCQCxaKt0ee","name":"Kannada Habba - KARNATA","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/5ZeVmJgyOpw4v0FmbaeTh.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-15","duration":32,"outcomes":"Through participating in Kannada Habba, I gained a deeper understanding of the richness and\\nimportance of the Kannada language and Karnataka’s cultural heritage. The event helped me\\nappreciate traditional art forms, folk culture, and the historical values associated with them.\\nIt also emphasized the role of language in preserving cultural identity and connecting people\\nacross generations.\\nAdditionally, the program enhanced my sense of cultural pride and encouraged me to respect and\\npromote regional traditions. Participating alongside peers from diverse backgrounds improved\\nmy ability to collaborate effectively and strengthened my appreciation for cultural inclusivity\\nwithin an academic environment.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-05-15","hoursSpent":70,"description":"Kannada Habba was celebrated with great enthusiasm at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE)\\non 15 June 2023 to promote the richness of the Kannada language and the cultural heritage\\nof Karnataka. The event was organized by the college’s Kannada Sangha with the objective\\nof instilling pride in regional culture and encouraging students to connect with Karnataka’s\\ntraditions, literature, and values. Students and faculty from various departments actively\\nparticipated, making the celebration vibrant and inclusive.\\nThe program featured a variety of cultural activities that reflected the diversity of Kannada\\nculture. Traditional folk dances, classical and light music performances, skits, and poetry\\nrecitations in Kannada were presented by students. These performances highlighted themes\\nrelated to Karnataka’s history, social values, and linguistic beauty. The event also provided a\\nplatform for students to showcase their artistic talents while strengthening cultural unity among\\nparticipants from different backgrounds.\\nOverall, Kannada Habba at RVCE was a meaningful and memorable celebration that reinforced\\nthe importance of preserving and promoting the Kannada language and culture. The event\\nfostered cultural awareness, enhanced student engagement, and encouraged respect for local\\ntraditions within the academic environment. It successfully fulfilled its objective of celebrating\\nKarnataka’s heritage while strengthening the sense of community among students and faculty\\nmembers.","aicteMapping":"Institutional Activity – Cultural & Social Engagement","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/25076854-3728-49a4-8f63-77c77098288d/GGQAa4CQKEjXzKe8YLfnf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 16:07:05.126888+00', '2026-02-01 20:45:30.921526+00'), ('91295985-7943-4cec-bbc6-1faaeb4e2789', 'e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY033","name":"Khushal A","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"CTzKs8Fd6VrgQfuZBCJrq","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp successfully collected a substantial quantity of blood units, which\\nwere added to the local blood bank’s inventory and will support patients in need of transfusions\\nduring emergencies and medical treatments. The event raised awareness among participants\\nand the wider community about the importance of voluntary blood donation, helping dispel\\nmyths and encourage future donor participation. It also fostered a strong sense of community\\nengagement, social responsibility, and solidarity among students and volunteers involved in the\\ninitiative","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":null,"description":"By voluntarily donating blood, I contributed to supporting patients in need and promoting\\nawareness about the importance of blood donation in society. This activity helped me develop\\na\\nsense of social responsibility, empathy, and commitment toward community welfare and public\\nhealth.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/n_ZJWHOuEFPV9CLKVPnxn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"O8G6i8edY4rOJsxf2_iOE","name":"Through the Eyes of You(th) by IUCEE-SPARK","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"Increased student awareness and understanding of the United Nations Sustainable Development\\nGoals (SDGs).\\nEncouraged creative expression and critical thinking through visual storytelling.\\nEnabled students to connect real-world social and environmental issues with global\\nsustainability goals.\\nEnhanced students’ observational, technical, and narrative photography skills.\\nFostered a sense of social responsibility and environmental consciousness among participants.\\nProvided a platform for students to communicate impactful messages on sustainability to a wider\\naudience.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The *“Through the Eyes of Youth”* event was a photography competition focused on the\\nUnited Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Organized by IUCEE-SPARK, the\\ninitiative encouraged students to use visual storytelling to draw attention to major global\\nissues and possible solutions. The competition offered a creative platform for participants to\\npresent their views on sustainability, environmental protection, and social responsibility through\\nphotography.\\nStudents were given one week, from 7th to 13th August 2023, to capture photographs aligned\\nwith any of the 17 SDGs, covering themes such as climate action, gender equality, responsible\\nconsumption, and life on land. Each submission was required to convey a clear and impactful\\nmessage related to sustainability or a significant social concern, accompanied by a brief\\ndescription explaining the concept and intent behind the image.\\nEntries were evaluated by a panel consisting of faculty members and professional\\nphotographers, based on creativity, narrative strength, technical excellence, and relevance to\\nthe SDGs. Overall, the activity effectively combined artistic expression with social awareness,\\nmotivating students to engage more deeply with their surroundings and relate local issues to\\nglobal development goals.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/b0ELc4nIOcuw9C593B4it.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"VqEiZbxTb0rWLKRLz2hlw","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye ","slNo":3,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” initiative enhanced understanding of\\ndemocratic principles and the significance of electoral participation. It reinforced a sense of\\ncivic duty and responsibility toward contributing to the nation’s governance through informed\\ndecision-making.\\nThe activity encouraged political awareness, social responsibility, and active citizenship,\\nhighlighting the importance of youth engagement in democratic processes. It also reflects\\na commitment to upholding constitutional values and contributing positively to the nation’s\\ndemocratic framework.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” is a national voter awareness initiative aimed at encouraging\\nfirst-time voters to actively participate in the democratic process of India. The campaign focuses\\non educating young citizens about the importance of voting, constitutional rights, and civic\\nresponsibility in strengthening democratic governance.\\nBy participating in this initiative, the individual demonstrated awareness of the role of informed\\nvoting in shaping public policy, leadership, and national development. The program promotes\\nethical citizenship, political awareness, and responsible participation in elections, aligning with\\nIndia’s democratic values and electoral integrity","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/aJqvi3j0sMYcvoykQQU8C.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vHbdI2VS0alyRU-ShPh3k","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness about the importance of regular exercise, fitness, and a healthy lifestyle.\\nEncouraged active participation from students and community members, strengthening social\\nconnections.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The marathon, organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), was designed to promote\\nphysical fitness, healthy living, and active community participation. The event attracted\\nstudents, faculty, and local residents who came together to participate in long-distance running\\nacross a carefully planned route within the city. The marathon emphasized endurance, stamina,\\nand perseverance, while also encouraging participants to push their personal limits and set\\nachievable goals","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/dHq_2cYFgekaN2Kx66SqQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iVYZFOCDGxcm1mbWJWnit","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"A significant number of books and study materials were\\ncollected and redistributed to students in need.\\nUnderprivileged children received access to learning resources,\\nsupporting their academic growth.\\nStudents developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of\\nresponsibility toward educational equity.\\nThe activity promoted the values of sharing, sustainability\\n(reuse of books), and community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2024 was a social initiative organized to promote\\neducation access and literacy among underprivileged children.\\nThe project focused on collecting and distributing educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery to students from\\neconomically weaker sections of society..Students\\nactively participated by donating books and study materials that\\nwere in good condition. Volunteers sorted, categorized, and\\npacked the collected materials based on age group and academic\\nlevel to ensure effective distribution. The resources were then\\nprovided to government schools, community learning centers, and\\nchildren from low-income families who lacked access to adequate\\nlearning materials.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/DW0_xO3PGr8EHU98Mzwkn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tpOmwYLlBFc-wwgRlnZe-","name":"FistFul-2024 ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-29","duration":13,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected,\\nhelping address food insecurity among vulnerable\\ncommunities.\\nThe donated food grains supported nutrition programs in\\nold age homes, hospitals, schools, anganwadis, and\\ninstitutions for visually challenged children.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of\\nRVCE in association with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI\\nDistrict 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program\\nfocused on reducing food insecurity and supporting\\nunderprivileged sections of society. The initiative followed a\\nsimple yet powerful concept where each participating student\\ndonated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, turning small individual\\ncontributions into a collective effort with significant impact. The\\ndrive received overwhelming support, with participation from\\nover 2,100 students, leading to the collection of a large quantity\\nof essential food grains. As part of this initiative, I personally\\ncontributed 2 kg of toor dal, which was added to the overall\\ncollection. The donated food grains were then distributed to\\nvarious beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding\\nprograms, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes,\\nhospitals, trust-run schools, and nearby anganwadis. These\\nsupplies helped strengthen existing nutrition programs benefiting\\nchildren, senior citizens, patients, and economically\\ndisadvantaged communities. The distribution was carried out in a\\nsystematic and well-coordinated manner, with beneficiary\\ninstitutions collecting the food supplies directly from the campus\\nunder the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The\\ninitiative focused on creating a sustainable and communitydriven impact, emphasizing long-term support rather than shortterm relief.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/tyEKeQ-InkyN2ucKU12Ur.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Phn_XtR80nhL3PSGHe9qY","name":"Utsarga Marathon-2025 ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Promoted physical fitness, mental resilience, and overall well-being among participants.\\nStrengthened community engagement and student participation in socially responsible\\ninitiatives.\\nEncouraged perseverance, discipline, and personal challenge through long-distance running.\\nEnhanced teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills among NSS volunteers.\\nReinforced NSS’s vision of combining individual development with service to society","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The second marathon, conducted under the NSS, aimed to promote fitness while also raising\\nawareness about societal and community issues. The event saw enthusiastic participation from\\nstudents, faculty, and local residents, all coming together to engage in a long-distance run along\\na pre-determined route, supported by volunteers at checkpoints and hydration stations.\\nThe marathon not only tested the endurance and perseverance of participants but also\\nencouraged them to adopt a disciplined lifestyle, highlighting the connection between personal\\nhealth and overall well-being. Through this event, NSS volunteers emphasized teamwork,\\nleadership, and social responsibility by coordinating logistics, ensuring safety, and motivating\\nparticipants throughout the run. Additionally, the marathon served as a platform to foster unity,\\ncollective effort, and active civic engagement, reflecting NSS’s mission of integrating personal\\ndevelopment with community service and social awareness.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/FtHdm8In85wrhvr6mkG0q.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MffsPnRsr9ckzFDew_m4a","name":"FistFull 2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected, addressing food insecurity among\\nvulnerable populations.\\nDonations supported nutrition programs in schools, anganwadis, hospitals, old age homes, and\\nhostels for visually challenged children.\\nEncouraged mass participation, with over 2,100 students contributing to the collective effort.\\nFostered social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among participants.\\nHighlighted the impact of small individual contributions when combined for a larger social\\ncause.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary\\nBangalore Spandana (RI District 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program aimed\\nat reducing food insecurity and supporting underprivileged communities. The initiative was\\nbased on a simple yet impactful concept: each participating student contributed either 5 kg\\nof rice or 2 kg of dal. These small individual contributions combined to create a substantial\\ncollective impact.\\nThe campaign received overwhelming support, with over 2,100 students participating and\\nhelping to collect a significant quantity of essential food grains. As part of this effort, I personally\\ndonated 2 kg of toor dal, which became part of the overall collection. Volunteers organized the\\ncollection, after which the food supplies were systematically distributed to various beneficiary\\norganizations, including mass feeding programs, hostels for visually challenged children, old\\nage homes, hospitals, trust-run schools, and local anganwadis.\\nThe donated rice and dal strengthened ongoing nutrition programs, benefiting children, senior\\ncitizens, patients, and economically disadvantaged communities. The distribution process was\\nwell-coordinated, with beneficiary institutions collecting the supplies directly from the campus\\nunder the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The initiative emphasized a\\nsustainable, community-driven approach, aiming for long-term support rather than temporary\\nrelief.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/gIg35J2PRUhMXRr3OGekM.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"R145qV1oZ0xhjt8NMXo-t","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"A substantial number of books and study materials were collected and redistributed to children\\nin need.\\nUnderprivileged students gained access to essential educational resources, supporting their\\nacademic progress.\\nParticipating students developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility\\ntoward\\neducational equity.\\nThe initiative reinforced values of sharing, sustainability through the reuse of books, and active\\ncommunity service.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social initiative aimed at enhancing access to education and\\npromoting literacy among underprivileged children. The project centered on collecting and\\ndistributing educational resources, including textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery,\\nto students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/5Eb1OdKky4VEb923JpKU8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1xkS4K4MfMEhRKG8bNrNO","name":"Fight Against Drug Abuse Pledge ","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Awareness & Social Responsibility:\\nGained a deeper understanding of the consequences of drug abuse and the importance of\\nindividual responsibility in preventing substance misuse.\\nEthical Commitment:\\nDemonstrated a formal commitment to leading a drug-free life and promoting positive\\nbehavioral choices within society.\\nCivic Engagement:\\nActively participated in a Government of India–recognized public health and social awareness\\ninitiative.\\nPersonal Development:\\nReinforced values related to self-discipline, health consciousness, and ethical decision-making.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"This certificate is issued by the Narcotics Control Bureau (NCB), Ministry of Home Affairs,\\nGovernment of India, under the national awareness initiative “Say Yes to Life, No to Drugs”.\\nThe program is aimed at promoting drug-free lifestyles and spreading awareness about the\\nharmful physical, psychological, and social impacts of drug abuse.\\nBy taking this pledge, the participant formally commits to:\\nRejecting the use of narcotic drugs and psychotropic substances\\nActively supporting efforts to prevent drug abuse\\nEncouraging healthy, responsible, and lawful living\\nThe initiative aligns with India’s national strategy to combat substance abuse through preventive\\neducation, social responsibility, and youth engagement.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/uzz6QiyvvUFssW6qSQrDr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"B_2BH25zgx8Y6lU0Pbgpo","name":"Female Foeticide Walkathon","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participation in the walkathon strengthened awareness of the long-term social consequences of\\nfemale foeticide and reinforced the role of youth in addressing deeply rooted societal challenges.\\nThe event promoted empathy, civic engagement, and a sense of responsibility toward advocating\\ngender equality and women’s rights.\\nBy engaging in this initiative, the participant demonstrated commitment to social causes,\\ncollaboration with healthcare and service organizations, and alignment with national and global\\nefforts to eliminate gender discrimination. The experience also contributed to personal growth\\nby enhancing social awareness, ethical values, and community involvement","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"This Certificate of Participation was awarded for active involvement in the Female Foeticide\\nAwareness Walkathon, held on 11th May 2025 at RV College of Engineering. The event was\\norganized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with Bangalore Hospitals, with the\\nobjective of raising awareness about the critical social issue of female foeticide and promoting\\ngender equality.\\nThe walkathon aimed to educate participants and the broader community on the ethical, social,\\nand legal implications of gender-based discrimination, emphasizing the importance of valuing\\nand protecting the rights of the girl child. Through collective participation, the event fostered\\nsocial responsibility and encouraged individuals to actively contribute toward building an\\ninclusive and equitable society.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/mSKRD8mjvfOWkM_4SVG7c.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dP-auML3GqxTZ-S9wNUP-","name":"DHI Day-Data Remix ","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced students’ understanding of data analysis, data\\nvisualization, and decision-making using real datasets.\\nEncouraged innovative thinking by integrating business\\noptimization with sustainable development goals.\\nImproved teamwork, communication, and presentation\\nskills among participants.\\nProvided practical exposure to solving real-world\\nproblems using data-driven approaches.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-03","hoursSpent":0,"description":"DHI Day – Data Remix was organized by Team DHI, Department\\nof Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning (AIML), RV\\nCollege of Engineering, as a technical and innovation-driven event\\nfocused on data analytics, visualization, and sustainable business\\nsolutions. The event was conducted as part of DHI Day and\\nbrought together students from various semesters to apply datadriven thinking to real-world problems.The event was conducted\\nin multiple phases. In the initial phase, participants were provided\\nwith pre-processed datasets and relevant analytical tools to\\nperform data analysis and generate meaningful visualizations.\\nStudents worked in teams of 3 to 4 members, encouraging\\ncollaboration, problem-solving, and critical thinking.The second\\nphase focused on business innovation and optimization, where\\nteams used their analytical insights to propose solutions aligned\\nwith the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\\nParticipants presented their findings and solutions to a panel of\\njudges comprising faculty members, who evaluated the teams\\nbased on creativity, analytical approach, clarity of visualization,\\nand relevance to sustainability","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e43f4886-4d20-44b1-b120-aac1d7ae333b/hzT0v1heyP7mqw3Wlmbm9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"24-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 19:43:18.425064+00', '2026-01-31 03:41:03.344751+00'), ('91f9ba8c-80a4-4734-8259-463da7b725ff', 'ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD017","name":"Dhruva B A","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"FvjTdf38xGACxENckIndd","name":"Fast Trek 1.0","slNo":1,"place":"Hutridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/VPQzghttqrzJjFxvlLdcP.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Fast Trek 1.0, I gained a strong sense of environmental\\nresponsibility by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive and contributing to preserving\\nthe natural beauty of Hutridurga Hills. The trek helped me improve my physical stamina\\nand endurance by completing the trails, while also teaching me discipline and consistency\\nthrough early-morning participation. I also developed better teamwork and coordination skills\\nby trekking along with a large group and supporting others throughout the journey. Overall, the\\nevent gave me a memorable experience of bonding, collective effort, and personal achievement,\\nleaving me feeling accomplished, motivated, and inspired.\\n","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast Trek 1.0, one of the biggest flagship events of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, took place\\non 12th February 2025 at the scenic Hutridurga Hills, bringing together over 500\\nenthusiastic participants from the college. This adventure-packed event combined trekking\\nwith a meaningful cleanliness drive, reinforcing the club’s commitment to environmental\\nresponsibility. The trek began early in the morning, with participants embarking on a\\nthrilling journey through the rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills. Amidst breathtaking views,\\nthe team actively engaged in cleaning the surroundings, collecting litter, and promoting\\neco-consciousness. The event not only contributed to preserving the natural beauty of the\\nhills but also instilled a sense of responsibility among students. Beyond the cause, Fast Trek\\n3.0 fostered incredible team bonding, as participants supported and motivated one another\\nthroughout the trek. Laughter, shared experiences, and the collective effort to make a difference\\ncreated an unforgettable experience. The event concluded on a high note, with participants\\nfeeling both accomplished and inspired.\\n","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/KWJljL-BKcrZT9BrOi29a.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ze-cre_hPLWZZbbxzHRh0","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":2,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/4CyhfLy6UbPp8cSPXTXXD.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by\\nactively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense\\nof environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by\\nreporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped\\nimprove my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Kunagal Betta Hills, and it\\nalso enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group of\\nparticipants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved my\\nfitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated to\\npreserving the environment. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus\\nto the trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the\\nadventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all\\nattendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagal Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding\\nsuccess, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750\\nindividuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s\\nvibrant atmosphere.\\n","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/ZDHdwfz4R58DyMf5C62pb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YnV8livhY2AZMiwYRfRI4","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":3,"place":" Narayangiri Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/J6Ho4rt_V-UFXVetrxT0S.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Fast Trek 3.0, I gained a strong sense of environmental\\nresponsibility by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive and contributing to preserving\\nthe natural beauty of Narayangiri Hills. The trek helped me improve my physical stamina\\nand endurance by completing the trails, while also teaching me discipline and consistency\\nthrough early-morning participation. I also developed better teamwork and coordination skills\\nby trekking along with a large group and supporting others throughout the journey. Overall, the\\nevent gave me a memorable experience of bonding, collective effort, and personal achievement,\\nleaving me feeling accomplished, motivated, and inspired.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast Trek 3.0, the biggest flagship event of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, took place\\non 12th January 2025 at the scenic Narayangiri Hills, bringing together over 500\\nenthusiastic participants from the college. This adventure-packed event combined trekking\\nwith a meaningful cleanliness drive, reinforcing the club’s commitment to environmental\\nresponsibility. The trek began early in the morning, with participants embarking on a\\nthrilling journey through the rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills. Amidst breathtaking views,\\nthe team actively engaged in cleaning the surroundings, collecting litter, and promoting\\neco-consciousness. The event not only contributed to preserving the natural beauty of the\\nhills but also instilled a sense of responsibility among students. Beyond the cause, Fast Trek\\n3.0 fostered incredible team bonding, as participants supported and motivated one another\\nthroughout the trek. Laughter, shared experiences, and the collective effort to make a difference\\ncreated an unforgettable experience. The event concluded on a high note, with participants\\nfeeling both accomplished and inspired.\\n","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/2wE2vnwtqBLHo_vb5A42X.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-rAYKea0PBujDGz8ZenJL","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":4,"place":"Localities of Bangalore (Vijaynagar)","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/L30QtNuilq-RdCaQB4fVP.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this project, I learned the importance of teamwork, coordination, and community participation in achieving large-scale social goals. The experience showed me how effective planning, time management, and volunteer engagement can lead to impactful outcomes within a short span of time. I also gained insight into social responsibility and sustainability, understanding how simple collective actions like recycling newspapers, can generate funds for a meaningful cause and create a positive impact on society.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":" With an overwhelming support of 500+ volunteers, the students collected more than 7 tonnes of newspapers in just over 9\\nhours! The volunteers, registered for the event, assembled at Kriyakalpa, RVCE at 8:00 AM. Volunteers were taken to different localities of Bangalore by buses to collect all sorts of papers. The incentive behind this was to raise funds by selling the collected old newspapers, books, magazines, waste papers etc. to paper vendors, and donating the same amount for the welfare of the Nele Narendra Foundation.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/HaT_FNMoGEFEPT755tPk4.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZfXYhckJp6jYkhWPLU8C2","name":"Akshara","slNo":5,"place":"Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/rWV-zPA7qX_CGljVImPBo.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/_FDQeuuatlt-WpCY4V04l.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this initiative, I learned the value of education as a tool for social empowerment and the impact of volunteer-driven efforts in reducing educational disparities. The experience helped me develop communication, leadership, and teaching skills while fostering patience and empathy through direct interaction with underprivileged students. It also deepened my appreciation for the teaching profession and highlighted how interactive, curriculum-based learning can significantly improve student engagement and understanding.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE held skill development sessions in eight Bangalore schools, benefiting over 1000 underprivileged students. Targeting financially modest backgrounds, the sessions enhanced academic understanding and provided essential skills. Schools visited included BET Convent, Sai Sri Vidya Chethana, Vishwa Bharathi High School, Kengeri High School, Government Model Primary School, Nehru Memorial School, Priyadarshini Vidhya Kendra School, and Mount Carmel English School. The initiative used interactive methods for curriculum-based learning to ensure relevance and engagement. Volunteers gained valuable experience as teachers, fostering appreciation for the profession and addressing educational disparities. This initiative underscored the power of volunteerism and the need for quality education for all.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/fUjz0-ecRelIqcPEBOt1q.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bi7qp1Zp5CPtJAaDzRIhh","name":"Rush Hour 4.0","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/H1C4UEKzTqn-RyOyhb4Zo.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-11-29","duration":5,"outcomes":"From this project, I learned the importance of leadership, strategic thinking, and consistent engagement in managing large-scale events. The experience highlighted how well-structured tasks, healthy competition, and real-time updates through dashboards and leaderboards can keep participants motivated. It also reinforced the idea that community service can be made impactful and enjoyable when combined with creativity, teamwork, and effective event planning.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-11-25","hoursSpent":20,"description":" A community service and Professional development project which went on for 5 days and included a pre-event task to build interest among the participants followed by 8 main tasks. The participants run for their positions as each task led to the elimination of a certain number of teams; with 250+ participants; participating actively, Followed by regular updates through event dashboard and leader board. The event was a huge success with the participants contributing to society along with having fun in this process. The top 5 teams were rewarded with OTT subscriptions and other prizes. ","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/7K_cFd1Ib64T_uW3LSUFl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_HX6nYZFlRkANj3nLv522","name":"ACM Gen AI Hackathon","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/bBUKCw3vd8i2UKHmWh0OU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"As a volunteer for the GenAI Hackathon (powered by EDOCK) held on 29th November\\n2024 at RVCE, I gained valuable experience in event coordination and student management\\nby supporting the smooth execution of the hackathon. I developed strong communication\\nand teamwork skills by interacting with participants, guiding them when required, and\\ncoordinating with the organizing team to ensure timely flow of activities. This volunteering\\nopportunity also improved my leadership, responsibility, and problem-solving abilities,\\nespecially while handling on-spot requirements during the event. Additionally, being part of\\na technology-focused hackathon enhanced my exposure to Generative AI innovations and\\nstrengthened my understanding of how collaborative events encourage creativity, innovation,\\nand real-world solution building. Overall, the experience helped me grow professionally\\nby building organizational skills and giving me practical experience in managing a large\\nstudent-driven technical event.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-29","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The GenAI Hackathon, powered by EDOCK, was successfully organized at RV College of Engineering on 29th November 2024 at the DTL Huddle. The event served as a dynamic\\nplatform for students to explore and apply advanced concepts in Generative Artificial Intelligence, focusing on innovative solutions that enable machines to generate content, simulate\\nhuman-like interactions, and address complex real-world challenges. The hackathon witnessed enthusiastic participation from students who showcased their creativity and technical expertise by developing innovative prototypes within a limited timeframe. Overall, the event encouraged collaborative learning, problem-solving, teamwork, and innovation, creating an enriching experience that promoted emerging AI technologies and their transformative impact across industries.\\n","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/T2C_O6VJIdU6HV0xBGkVb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"y90pTiKyyT2a5_c72rsg6","name":"ACM Summit","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/-tVakrADyrPsn2EjLYsiy.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/qWcWsa6d5C_Kozq1G8ryS.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-21","duration":2,"outcomes":"From volunteering at ACM Summit 2024, I gained hands-on experience in event coordination, teamwork, and professional communication while ensuring the smooth execution of a large-scale technical summit. The role helped me develop problem-solving, time management, and leadership skills by handling real-time responsibilities and coordinating with organizers, speakers, and participants. It also enhanced my understanding of how major technical events are planned and executed, while providing valuable exposure to the professional computing community and strengthening my sense of responsibility and collaboration.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-20","hoursSpent":16,"description":"ACM Summit 2024, held collaboratively at RV College of Engineering (RVCE) and BMS College of Engineering (BMSE), was a flagship technical event that brought together students, professionals, and ACM members from across institutions. The summit featured a blend of technical talks, workshops, panel discussions, and interactive sessions led by industry experts and academic leaders, focusing on emerging technologies, research, and career development in computing. It served as a strong platform for knowledge sharing, networking, and collaboration, fostering innovation, technical excellence, and a deeper connection between students and the professional computing community.\\n","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/ZfggBAv9Za_WXjFqut1YR.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"30x80-lVs7yW9d6VSu7Xv","name":"UTSARGA 2024","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/8tdaH5qnfcKs5I23dZrCh.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need. ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based\\nregistration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create\\nawareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness\\nactivity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community\\nimpact.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/KUMcz6DFhO92kgoGVHsAv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"U0F_qhW-vYoUOELNc8AJV","name":"UTPT India Quiz 2024","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/0kOEqblLUSIHIyxtjXhNU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-01-07","duration":580,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Indi-Genius Quiz, I  enhanced my knowledge of Indian culture, history, and traditions through a competitive and interactive learning experience. The event helped improve my critical thinking, recall ability, and time-based decision-making skills while working collaboratively in a team. Participation also strengthened my confidence in expressing ideas and responding under pressure during quiz rounds. Overall, the quiz served as an enriching academic and cultural experience that combined learning, teamwork, and co-curricular development.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Indi-Genius Quiz, organized by RV Quiz Corp, was conducted as part of UTPT 2024 on 7th June 2024 at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The quiz was designed\\nto celebrate India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage through an engaging and competitive format. The event covered a wide range of topics including Indian history, Mughal\\narchitecture, epics such as the Mahabharata and Ramayana, festivals, regional cuisines, and cultural traditions. Conducted in teams of up to three members, the quiz provided participants\\nwith an interactive platform to test their knowledge, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills while experiencing the diverse essence of India in an intellectually stimulating environment.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/sN59huYnRO79CqJhQDqJu.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IgKhfzFPxKIf76vFP5tBO","name":"UTPT India Quiz 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/gSsY3GfcMumonFIJDp-ls.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-01-23","duration":246,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Indi-Genius Quiz, I enhanced my knowledge of Indian culture, history, and traditions through a competitive and interactive learning experience. The event helped improve my critical thinking, recall ability, and time-based decision-making skills while working collaboratively in a team. Participation also strengthened my confidence in expressing ideas and responding under pressure during quiz rounds. Overall, the quiz served as an enriching academic and cultural experience that combined learning, teamwork, and co-curricular development","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Indi-Genius Quiz, organized by RV Quiz Corp, was conducted as part of UTPT 2025 on 23rd May 2025 at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The quiz was designed\\nto celebrate India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage through an engaging and competitive format. The event covered a wide range of topics including Indian history, Mughal\\narchitecture, epics such as the Mahabharata and Ramayana, festivals, regional cuisines, and cultural traditions. Conducted in teams of up to three members, the quiz provided participants\\nwith an interactive platform to test their knowledge, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills while experiencing the diverse essence of India in an intellectually stimulating environment.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/fYWAOTpGKp6DW_lLQUmAo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WkwUFpPEl75kRiZUD2wcv","name":"Tanuja","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/UiLtUZy3asKmkCSyCt-et.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this activity, I learned the importance of perseverance, self-discipline, and resilience in overcoming socio-economic challenges. The story reinforced the belief that consistent effort, strong determination, and faith in one’s goals can break barriers and lead to success. It also highlighted the transformative power of education and inspired a deeper appreciation for equal opportunities and support systems that enable talented students from underprivileged backgrounds to achieve their dreams.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Tanuja is an inspiring movie that portrays the journey of a determined young girl from an economically disadvantaged background who dreams of becoming a doctor. Despite facing financial hardships, social challenges, and limited resources, Tanuja remains focused on her goal and works relentlessly toward academic excellence. Through perseverance, discipline, and self-belief, she overcomes obstacles and successfully qualifies in NEET. The movie highlights the power of education, resilience, and equal opportunity, sending a strong message about how dedication and hard work can transform lives, regardless of one’s circumstances.\\n","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/3PuY8hs4o0IHYyl_bgj-v.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"x5FfxxQVtkX6MV2qz43D3","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/LF2e-g-6-ZuobT-RM6ZS0.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/EntZ1KPFJDHnl1YlycR93.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this activity, I learned the value of social responsibility and empathy in contributing to public health and saving lives. The experience reinforced the importance of voluntary blood donation and raised awareness about how a simple act can have a significant impact on patients in need. It also fostered a sense of civic duty, confidence, and personal satisfaction in being able to support the community through a meaningful and life-saving initiative.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"This activity involved voluntary blood donation conducted at RV College, in collaboration with BGS Global Hospitals. By donating blood, the initiative aimed to support patients in need and contribute to saving lives through safe and quality blood supply. The event emphasized social responsibility, compassion, and the importance of regular voluntary blood donation. Participation in this drive reflected a commitment to community welfare and highlighted how individual actions can make a meaningful difference in healthcare and emergency support systems.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ae2e9fcd-db93-44fd-9d85-c8e9a894ffb8/ZbVw6yBcBu9YsxIIGzyi8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 17:42:42.460328+00', '2026-01-30 17:56:38.17072+00'), ('9205e0f0-92dc-49a8-819b-27a17a75b789', '45f175a0-c412-4d77-bed1-eaa234b21250', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-02 05:18:52.479573+00', '2026-02-02 05:18:52.970934+00'), ('93318760-3826-4970-862f-d852cbb17b42', 'a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC059","name":"G Shashank Bharadwaj","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"_RAC2RvAGdW4LF9fkySGe","name":"LAKSHYA 2025","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/XMTW4AX0YpHjvCh5dskXx.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-27","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event was open to all students, irrespective of prior experience, encouraging inclusivity and active participation. Lakshya focused on improving focus, discipline, confidence, and goal-oriented thinking, aligning with the core values of NCC. Participants were motivated to test their abilities, sharpen their aim, and challenge themselves in a structured and supportive environment.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The event was open to all students, irrespective of prior experience, encouraging inclusivity and active participation. Lakshya focused on improving focus, discipline, confidence, and goal-oriented thinking, aligning with the core values of NCC. Participants were motivated to test their abilities, sharpen their aim, and challenge themselves in a structured and supportive environment.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/tgHpf_Bi_qahWzY5dltsR.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iyzya2I-6n7GJ0Z3KucyC","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/L0yNloS2XWnZWs6EuJ9KR.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"* Project Pustak creates meaningful change by channeling \\ndonations into impactful support for underserved \\ncommunities. Through the distribution of essentials like \\nfood, clothing, and educational resources, it fosters hope and \\nempowerment. \\n* The initiative emphasizes collective effort and compassion,\\npaving the way for a more inclusive and supportive society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-14","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Rotaract Club of RVCE organized Project Pustak, a charitable \\ninitiative focused on uplifting underserved and vulnerable \\ncommunities through meaningful donations and organized \\nresource-sharing. The main objective of the project is to provide \\ntimely support to people who lack access to basic necessities and to ensure that essential resources reach those who need them the most.Under Project Pustak, the club actively collects and distributes a wide range of items such as food supplies, clothes, footwear, blankets, stationery, books, educational materials, hygiene kits, and basic healthcare essentials.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/knzwfAA7_YyEXDM-OJMXm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DU-E118ePCeo_CNN9kasJ","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/NmX2FurU5b-MzYePRVb6x.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-25","duration":2,"outcomes":"* Project Pustak creates meaningful change by channeling \\ndonations into impactful support for underserved communities. \\nThrough the distribution of essentials like food, clothing, and \\neducational resources, it fosters hope and empowerment.\\n* The initiative emphasizes collective effort and compassion,\\npaving the way for a more inclusive and supportive society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":6,"description":"ROTRACT, RVCE organized the PROJECT PUSTAK, Project \\nPustak is a charitable initiative dedicated to uplifting underservedcommunities through donations and resource-sharing. By providing essentials like food, clothing, education materials, and healthcare supplies, the project aims to bring hope and relief to those in need. Rooted in compassion and collective effort, Pustak inspires individuals to contribute towards building a more inclusive and supportive society.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/LQ7Hhqz0HU3D07CloEu5W.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ail49BFIZkR_oWLnAXrlP","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/Z1PRTev7LMW20qkzQR4sl.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-03-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The online awareness event engaged young voters, resulting in participants taking a formal pledge to exercise their democratic rights and encourage others to build a \"New India\".","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-03-05","hoursSpent":1,"description":"An Online Event organized by NSS RVCE with a focus on engaging young and aspiring voters.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/u1zpnuWVvGghYs-zfqin_.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DSio7mSJgL0cBE786IF8O","name":"Fistfull 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/r2oMxN9fjg822ilCIwvji.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-18","duration":31,"outcomes":"This large-scale hunger combat initiative successfully collected over 5,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal from students to support community welfare and solidarity.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-09-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The “Fist Full” initiative by Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana encouraged students to donate rice or toor dal to support hunger relief. The drive collected significant contributions, highlighting student solidarity and RVCE’s commitment to community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/85AX22kU_5Obk_ijj9EZp.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nGlTuGNjfCHF8RjO56kd1","name":"FistFull 2025","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/7OxbV3qJlIVe3eb0qOfB7.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"This large-scale hunger combat initiative successfully collected over 5,700 kg of rice and 800 \\nkg of toor dal from students to support community welfare and solidarity.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The “Fist Full” initiative by Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore \\nSpandana encouraged students to donate rice or toor dal to support hunger relief. The drive \\ncollected significant contributions, highlighting student solidarity and RVCE’s commitment to \\ncommunity welfare.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/a10b5a01-66ef-470a-8bbd-bcade4ebc551/dff9nfBDOrgUH2rWjRmIO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-02 06:38:09.528606+00', '2026-02-02 08:26:27.304964+00'), ('940e75b1-5ef9-45f3-bb3b-6f1838a62c01', '66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS215","name":"T Vinay","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"_8cTDxxCAMgO6vsOMTcnt","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/n_nDD-wznnBaM5wS1_xlL.png"],"endDate":"2023-05-13","duration":2,"outcomes":"Education is the key to unlocking opportunities and building a better future. Unfortunately, many children in rural areas lack access to basic school supplies, making it difficult for them to learn and grow. Project Pustak aims to bridge this gap and help these children realize their potential.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-05-12","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a noble initiative that aims to provide essential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas. With the generous donations, notebooks and geometry boxes will be brought, which will be donated to government schools.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/0Kg22hSM0VBtrizCf8Fnd.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eLZEEiR2vI08KvH0-TYPn","name":"SDG Photography Contest","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/-y1HdBR-Jyrf4-v1wB3G8.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-19","duration":2,"outcomes":"We got a chance to show what the world looks like to us and also a chance to win a prize pool of Rs. 2000.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"\\nAll the photographs must be original work.\\nSubmissions must align with only one of the 17 UN SDGs.\\nIndicate the SDG number with the logo linked to the photo and write a brief story/description \\n(between 100 - 150 words) explaining how the photo is linked to the respective SDG.\\nEach participant can submit one entry only.\\nOnly minimal editing is allowed.\\nThe top 25 shortlisted submissions (after the plagiarism Image check and relevance check) will \\nbe uploaded\\non the official Instagram page of SPARK.\\nThe submissions that receive the most likes (genuine) by the audience as of 19th November 2024 \\nat 23:59 will be\\nconsidered winners.","aicteMapping":"Eyes of Youth","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/S4SaAA8_Z9-ot1rRBDaPF.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"J02I1K9OZC0Hd36fpeok2","name":"Blood Donation Camps","slNo":3,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/df2AR6k7mZUU9yfjzf5pO.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Many patients require blood at crucial times, and my blood being O+ve, it can be used by anyone, hence donated my blood so that it can be used for a good purpose.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Donated my blood to the blood bank for a social cause. Every drop counts — one pint of blood can save up to three lives. This was our chance to give someone a second chance at life, right \\nhere on campus.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/I7WtLMmXyW3Oi6Uy7ysTs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1tLB8pNS84t1-BaybT7S3","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":4,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/Ir3Kg1ilwztaWjcDSlsLg.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Many patients require blood at crucial times, and my blood being O+ve, it can be used by anyone, hence donated my blood so that it can be used for a good purpose.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Donated my blood to the blood bank for a social cause. Every drop counts — one pint of blood can save up to three lives. This was our chance to give someone a second chance at life, right \\nhere on campus.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/4ss0EadcNDE6sBL5hJWbq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2kKEu7t5kam7y810ErEiF","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/5EbdXBX07Fb47tpeFrEbW.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Don''t Just Run, Be the Change!\\nThis is more than a marathon, it''s a MOVEMENT! Let''s spread the word, rally your squad, and run for a cause! Together, we light up the path to a brighter tomorrow. #NOTMEBUTYOU","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This isn''t your average run—it''s a celebration of vitality, wellness, and, most importantly, an opportunity to make a real impact. Your run isn''t just a jog; it''s a promise to reshape a child''s destiny. The theme, ''Help a Child Change the World,'' is our social heartbeat, and every stride you take directly fuels for those in need.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/ETBIXcO01JBIJpd3UNwuC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nZaL8kouR_3dyECqkFaON","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":6,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/DBEYcNi651Rb7CMdXLiiY.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Our contribution helped us participate in this meaningful initiative. Our involvement significantly contributed to the success of this cause.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This marathon is dedicated to the cause of \"Help a Child, Change the World.\" This initiative aims to support underprivileged children through education, healthcare, and welfare programs.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/gAPr-rSrJieaFd4KSsg-R.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nKx8DhwuL6gtgK85I4x4Y","name":"Cheela Mela Paper Bag Workshop","slNo":7,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/CBodsvqjBQGgB6Gd6osx-.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-22","duration":12,"outcomes":"Go green by creating newspaper bags and contribute towards a sustainable environment!","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"NSS RVCE, in collaboration with Youth For Seva, is organizing a paper bag workshop for the Kadale Kayi Parishe.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/4o9bsaNYAsTeBj67BWOcU.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JBEd9XI0tGsloGtO4msiq","name":"Project Pustak (Pushtaka 2024)","slNo":8,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/Xj1n6c5ev-bvAipcVUbQI.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/g4JoVDxSsPvcCaTzmYAWe.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Education is the key to unlocking opportunities and building a better future. Unfortunately, many children in rural areas lack access to basic school supplies, making it difficult for them to learn and grow. Project Pustak aims to bridge this gap and help these children realize their potential.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-01-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a noble initiative that aims to provide essential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas. With the generous donations, notebooks and geometry boxes will be brought, which will be donated to government schools. ","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/FNg6oPmtvZ5wsNaTBaDdW.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"SYDSPo3DNC23G_eqq9MDR","name":"FistFull","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/6-IF2LMyYxYQJ48NoI0d1.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A fistful of kindness can fill a heart and feed a soul. For every meal we prepare from November 15th to November 29th, set aside a fistful of rice or toor dal. By the end of the event, we''ll have gathered enough to bring a smile to someone in need!","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/_FjHTiLWXfqT8xbuGVIxa.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"z0e_p1HOTWMQFX5Q8x9dU","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":10,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/4jukOZ1axBhtYaUhjXxyN.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"We were able to learn how to trek across Hutridurga Hills and also learn about beautiful scenary of the environment and exercise through trekking across the Hutridurga Hills.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Are you exhausted after the CIEs?\\nIs EL prep tiring you out?\\nDone with the fast track exams?📚\\n\\nTighten your seatbelts and brace yourself for the most exciting trek of the year. We bring to you yet another opportunity to create a suitcase of memories. 🤩\\n\\nThe Rotaract Club of RVCE brings to you the most awaited event, so gear up to feel the rush! Introducing to you,\\n\\nFAST-TREK 2023⛰️🧗‍♂️\\n📍Venue: Hutridurga Hills\\n🗓 Date: 12/02/2023\\n\\nGet a chance to feel the cool air brush your face as the adrenaline rushes through your veins, as you trek along with your friends. Looking forward to an invigorating and a memorable day!","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/gW6zF1UtVimq92cvnJLHZ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IbRs2Yc89idrq-zNLkBE7","name":"Fist Full","slNo":11,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/o9o0rEyn_wZ5cT8Er9QbT.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":19,"outcomes":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing essential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted in the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions that serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-03","hoursSpent":2,"description":"A fistful of kindness can fill a heart and feed a soul. For every meal we prepare from November 3rd to November 21st, set aside a fistful of rice or toor dal. By the end of the event, we''ll have gathered enough to bring a smile to someone in need!","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/66db9ef1-786d-40cb-96be-a738f2e4700e/I9Xlzz4lmo-fVmlwzPW8N.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 11:01:47.667744+00', '2026-01-30 11:01:47.667744+00'), ('9467bc5d-1961-439f-a4ff-c85954a00880', '512b8177-e8ab-4035-b090-3057b14edccd', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IM031","name":"Manish Chavan","period":"2022-2026","department":"Industrial Engineering and Management","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"EpMEg87Qb1v_UI41UofQZ","name":"Stock Market Compitation 2023  (8th mile)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/512b8177-e8ab-4035-b090-3057b14edccd/ipoH3lPWM0b9AGcChujmH.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Our team emerged as the winner of the Stock Market Competition 2023, reflecting our strong \\nanalytical capabilities, strategic planning, and effective teamwork. The experience significantly \\nenhanced my practical understanding of stock market operations, including interpreting market \\nindicators, evaluating investment opportunities, and managing portfolios under competitive \\nconditions.\\nAdditionally, the activity helped me develop essential professional skills such as financial \\nanalysis, data-driven decision-making, teamwork, leadership, communication, and time \\nmanagement. Participating in this competition boosted my confidence in applying financial and \\nmanagement concepts to real-world scenarios and provided valuable exposure to competitive \\nenvironments. Overall, the event was a highly enriching learning experience that complemented \\nmy academic background and contributed to my personal and professional development.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-16","hoursSpent":6,"description":"As part of the college fest 8th Mile, I participated in the Stock Market Competition 2023, \\nconducted by the Entrepreneurship Cell (E-Cell), RVCE, on 15th June 2023. The competition \\nsimulated real-world stock market trading scenarios, requiring participants to analyze market \\ntrends, evaluate financial data, and make strategic investment decisions under time constraints. \\nThe event aimed to enhance financial literacy, decision-making ability, and understanding of \\nmarket dynamics among students. I participated as part of a team, actively contributing to \\nstrategy formulation and trade execution.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/512b8177-e8ab-4035-b090-3057b14edccd/vc_LjG27sYWDZSenkp__7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","de