oration and networking among Rotaractors.\\n\\nImproved students’ confidence, discipline, and professional outlook.\\n\\nFostered cultural appreciation and student engagement through extracurricular activities.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-19","hoursSpent":20,"description":"A two-day district-level conference was conducted from 19th–20th April 2025 to promote leadership development, professional skills, and inter-club interaction among students. The event included motivational sessions, idea-pitching activities, cultural programs, and networking opportunities, providing participants with a holistic learning and engagement experience.","aicteMapping":"Leadership Development Program","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9da0cbc6-8845-4fcf-b12e-4ed8d5fc95c8/bJC82ibznjUHSu5m-JXhK.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"La40-qEUcZvazyYcRGVrv","name":"Volunteered in Skill lab sessions","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9da0cbc6-8845-4fcf-b12e-4ed8d5fc95c8/7L-c0m1FLTWP9-M7eeLt6.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9da0cbc6-8845-4fcf-b12e-4ed8d5fc95c8/yZ8frK2BkfaFh2ZpHwKOw.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9da0cbc6-8845-4fcf-b12e-4ed8d5fc95c8/OQlvrq5UxQLVy1pe6MJkw.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-26","duration":6,"outcomes":"Skill Lab sessions were conducted for 4th semester B.E. students of CSE, CSE-CD, and CSE-CY from 21/04/2025 to 26/04/2025, organized by the Accelerate Club in collaboration with the Department of CSE. The sessions aimed to enhance students’ technical and practical skills, with a major focus on Cyber Security. Senior students from the B.E. CSE (CY) program actively mentored and guided juniors through hands-on learning activities.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-21","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Skill Lab sessions were conducted for 4th semester B.E. students of CSE, CSE-CD, and CSE-CY from 21/04/2025 to 26/04/2025, organized by the Accelerate Club in collaboration with the Department of CSE. The sessions aimed to enhance students’ technical and practical skills, with a major focus on Cyber Security. Senior students from the B.E. CSE (CY) program actively mentored and guided juniors through hands-on learning activities.","aicteMapping":"Student Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9da0cbc6-8845-4fcf-b12e-4ed8d5fc95c8/wYSMBU8N24q3reWf1OJjX.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"aPnJ4r-lO3GlXFHgCazYR","name":"Rotaract Female Foeticide","slNo":10,"place":"Around RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Importance of stopping female foeticide for a better society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":6,"description":"On the occasion of Mother day, Rotaract organised a walkathon to spread awareness to stop the female foeticide and discuss about its harmful impact on the society","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9da0cbc6-8845-4fcf-b12e-4ed8d5fc95c8/4lR4thT_pJkC8JTn3bFm5.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6lyfKLlcwCFpn-X7XPjyQ","name":"Rotaract Fist Full 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Contribute to betterment of the society in terms of Food","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Rotaract organised a Fist Full event to help the needy have their meals so that they can get nourished which would be a warm gesture from us students to the society","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/9da0cbc6-8845-4fcf-b12e-4ed8d5fc95c8/xyvxgA9Cog4pqDuXGAKko.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 19:51:20.286154+00', '2026-01-29 20:44:24.294389+00'), ('96364cf3-e804-4d05-bd25-3c465a4b741f', '8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS188","name":"SHREERAM SHIVABASU BADAGANDI","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"efCgIDszoP74ACQcaPFGr","name":"Mera Pehal Vote Desh Ke Liye","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/ng6W1FjPvJe2GaJuCnlR5.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-08","duration":3,"outcomes":"Participants gained clarity on the electoral process, voter eligibility, and the importance of informed decision-making during elections. The activity helped cultivate a sense of\\nownership toward democratic participation, particularly among first-time voters who often lack exposure to formal civic education. From a learning perspective, the initiative strengthened civic consciousness and encouraged critical thinking about governance, leadership, and public accountability. It also contributed to the development of communication and social responsibility by engaging students in discussions on national issues and democratic values. The activity aligned with AICTE’s emphasis on social awareness and ethical responsibility, highlighting the role of educational institutions in nurturing informed and responsible citizens. Overall, the initiative reinforced the idea that voting is not merely a right but a duty toward national progress, thereby contributing to the broader goal of participatory democracy.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":16,"description":"Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye was a voter awareness initiative conducted to encourage informed and responsible participation of first-time voters in the democratic process. The activity aimed to educate students about the significance of voting, electoral rights, and the role of youth in strengthening democracy. Organized under a structured outreach framework, the program focused on creating awareness regarding voter registration, ethical voting practices, and the long-term impact of electoral participation on governance and national development. The initiative included awareness sessions, informational outreach, and student engagement activities designed to simplify electoral concepts and address common misconceptions related to voting. Emphasis was placed on motivating eligible students to register as voters and exercise their franchise responsibly. Through organized communication and interaction, the program sought to instill a sense of civic duty and national responsibility among young citizens. By aligning democratic values with student participation, the activity successfully integrated civic education within the academic environment, reinforcing the importance of active citizenship as part of holistic student development.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/kVSOoHnfyCb5EnLnLvhEb.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fVBcTy4zxe8Plgpjq2Vn3","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/SWVywx_rFvOH2CRC5rHqf.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon helped me improve my physical fitness, stamina, and overall endurance. It also strengthened my mental resilience by pushing me to stay focused, motivated, and disciplined throughout the run. The event encouraged a healthy lifestyle and made me understand the importance of consistency and regular exercise. I also gained confidence and a sense of achievement by completing the marathon successfully. Additionally, it promoted positive community spirit and teamwork by bringing together many participants with a shared goal of fitness and awareness. Overall, it was an energetic and inspiring experience that motivated me to stay active and maintain a balanced lifestyle.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-02","hoursSpent":40,"description":"I participated in the Utsarga Marathon, which served as a platform to promote health, fitness, and community spirit. The event encouraged participants to maintain an active lifestyle, improve physical endurance, and develop mental resilience. Being part of this marathon helped me understand the importance of self-discipline, consistency, and determination. The experience was truly inspiring and energizing, and it motivated me to continue focusing on fitness and personal growth while contributing to a socially meaningful initiative.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/KNOZv20KEoNLbYu3q5Xd-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"VLFYAQ3zf53Q1o6K6n52X","name":"Campus Cleanup-II","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/cRbiasAq5g_uMSNt2zQGG.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-21","duration":-5,"outcomes":"Participating in the Campus Cleanup Drive at RVCE helped me understand the importance of maintaining cleanliness and hygiene in public spaces. It created awareness about proper waste disposal, cleanliness habits, and environmental responsibility. The activity improved my teamwork and coordination skills as we worked together to clean different areas of the campus effectively. It also developed a sense of discipline, civic responsibility, and motivation to keep the surroundings clean and green. Overall, the cleanup drive was a meaningful experience that encouraged me to contribute actively towards a healthier and more eco-friendly campus environment","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-27","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I actively participated in the Campus Cleanup Drive conducted at RV College of Engineering (RVCE), which aimed to promote cleanliness, hygiene, and environmental awareness among students. During this drive, we collectively worked to clean various areas of the campus, segregate waste, and maintain a neat and healthy environment. The activity taught me the importance of civic responsibility and sustainable practices such as proper disposal of waste and keeping public spaces clean. It also strengthened my teamwork and leadership skills through coordinated group efforts. Overall, the drive was a valuable experience that motivated me to contribute towards a cleaner and greener campus.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/6UzHej7L4KEobRu34HI0G.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9CHzEkSDFVvqwhEC5Xw9R","name":"Village Camp","slNo":4,"place":"Hosadurga","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/MkEpLxBzMkf5Vz0lmhUhe.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/mcelCuXRcX9NtJMKA6dO5.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-19","duration":6,"outcomes":"The NSS Village Camp organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) helped us develop a strong sense of social responsibility and the importance of serving society. Through various community activities and awareness programs, we gained practical exposure to rural life and understood real challenges faced by villagers. The camp improved our teamwork, leadership, and coordination skills as we worked together to complete tasks efficiently. It also enhanced our communication skills by interacting with local people and spreading awareness about cleanliness, hygiene, and healthy living. Overall, the camp was a meaningful experience that built discipline, confidence, and motivation to contribute towards community development and nation building.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-14","hoursSpent":160,"description":"I had the privilege of attending the NSS Village Camp conducted by RV College of Engineering (RVCE), which aimed at promoting social responsibility and community development. The camp involved active participation in several programs such as village cleanliness drives, awareness campaigns, interaction with villagers, and initiatives focused on health, hygiene, and education. This experience helped me gain real-world understanding of rural challenges and the importance of collective effort in improving society. It also improved my teamwork, communication skills, leadership qualities, and strengthened my commitment to contribute towards the betterment of the community.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":40,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/SxXH5f1C_Bhd4RqqjHUfO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"quieUphoepBp1vGONqzgA","name":"Kannada Sangha T-shirt","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/7dIE6sL-EZx9I8k8zCn1p.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Purchasing the Kannada Sangha T-shirt helped me contribute towards a student welfare initiative where the collected money is used to provide essential resources and support for students. It created a sense of social responsibility and encouraged me to support meaningful causes within the college community. This act also promoted unity, cultural involvement, and teamwork among students while motivating others to participate in such initiatives. Overall, it was a small but valuable step towards helping students and strengthening the spirit of collective support and development","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I purchased the Kannada Sangha T-shirt as a way of supporting a meaningful initiative that contributes towards student welfare. The money collected through this purchase is used to provide necessary resources and support for students, helping them in their academic and personal development. This small contribution reflects my responsibility towards society and my willingness to be a part of positive change within the student community. It also promotes unity, culture, and the spirit of helping others through collective effort.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/ooaRgMyotDheaHRF5KqDh.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mvlidLPSMUVap2zI6luPs","name":"Eye donation","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/BEZHIw3fFBpoDlypPrg1a.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-08","duration":12,"outcomes":"Taking the eye donation pledge helped me understand the importance of organ donation and its life-changing impact on people who suffer from vision loss. It developed a strong sense of humanity, social responsibility, and willingness to help others beyond my lifetime. This pledge also increased my awareness about the value of donating eyes and encouraged me to spread awareness among others to support this noble cause. Overall, it was a meaningful decision that reflects compassion and commitment towards improving the lives of people in need.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-08-28","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I took a pledge for eye donation, which reflects my commitment towards helping others and supporting a noble cause. By pledging to donate my eyes after my lifetime, I aim to contribute to restoring vision for someone in need and bringing light into their life. This pledge increased my awareness about organ donation and the importance of making a positive impact on society. It was a meaningful step that strengthened my sense of humanity, responsibility, and service towards the community.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/n1bWdccq_iBmgha3yfDKN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kBoESPKorWlyUmxNbbm7U","name":"Fist Full - 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/goiKl_AZuRvsu2n7DCxNU.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/K5rPYhojMbz60lfmwVLo6.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-08","duration":3,"outcomes":"Participating in the Fist Full program helped me understand the serious issue of hunger and food insecurity in society and the importance of taking small steps to reduce it. It developed a strong sense of empathy, humanity, and social responsibility, and made me realize that even a small contribution like donating 5kg rice can bring a positive impact in someone’s life. This initiative also encouraged me to be more mindful about food usage, avoid wastage, and respect the value of essential resources. Overall, it was a meaningful experience that motivated me to participate more in community service activities and contribute towards creating a better and more supportive society.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":40,"description":"I actively participated in the Fist Full initiative, where I donated 5kg of rice as a contribution towards supporting needy and underprivileged people. The main purpose of this initiative is to encourage students and individuals to donate a small portion of food grains from their side, which can later be collected and distributed to families facing food shortage. This program promotes the values of sharing, kindness, and social responsibility by ensuring that basic necessities like food reach the people who require it the most. Being part of this initiative gave me a sense of satisfaction, as I was able to contribute to a noble cause and support community welfare through a simple yet meaningful act.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/7MzeL1AI9mMTvZfLfEShQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZtzUiy4ICwrc0tnLFDZZG","name":"Gandhian Principle''s Essay","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/X_fqw1kNfaD4tSVLO8HBw.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Essay Writing Competition on Gandhian Principles helped me gain a deeper understanding of Mahatma Gandhi’s values such as truth, non-violence, simplicity, and service to society and their relevance in today’s world. It improved my writing, vocabulary, and research skills, while also enhancing my ability to think critically and express my ideas in a well-structured manner. This competition boosted my confidence in communicating my thoughts and encouraged me to follow ethical values like honesty, patience, and discipline in daily life. Overall, it was a valuable learning experience that strengthened my awareness of social responsibility and inspired me to contribute positively towards society.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-09","hoursSpent":8,"description":"I participated in an Essay Writing Competition on Gandhian Principles, which gave me an opportunity to understand and express the timeless values taught by Mahatma Gandhi such as truth (Satya), non-violence (Ahimsa), simplicity, self-discipline, equality, and service to society. Through this competition, I researched and reflected on how Gandhian ideals are still relevant in today’s world to promote peace, unity, and moral leadership. Writing the essay helped me improve my critical thinking and writing skills while also inspiring me to adopt positive values like honesty, patience, and responsibility in daily life. Overall, it was a meaningful and informative experience that strengthened my awareness about Gandhian philosophy and its importance in building a better society.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/WxhpBZllfAL4arhceZIiU.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"36qHDzaA3x8Ejk-R4fpD0","name":"Plog run for Vrishabhavathi Valley","slNo":9,"place":"Bangalore University Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/2Jxa84P-v8evtVDEXQlQW.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":2,"outcomes":"Through this plog run, I gained a stronger sense of social and environmental responsibility and understood the importance of proper waste disposal and reducing plastic pollution. The activity contributed to improving the cleanliness of Vrishabhavathi Valley and created awareness among participants about protecting water bodies and public spaces. It also improved my teamwork, coordination, and discipline as we worked together efficiently during the clean-up. Overall, the experience was motivating and meaningful, and it inspired me to adopt eco-friendly habits and participate in more community service and environmental conservation activities in the future.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-05","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I participated in the Plog Run for Vrishabhavathi Valley, where we actively took part in cleaning the valley area to promote environmental awareness and cleanliness. This initiative combined physical activity with social service, as we ran/walked while collecting waste such as plastic wrappers, bottles, and other litter that was polluting the surroundings. The drive was focused on maintaining the cleanliness of Vrishabhavathi Valley and encouraging people to take responsibility for protecting natural spaces. Being part of this activity helped me understand how community efforts can contribute towards reducing pollution and creating a cleaner and healthier environment.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/jjJW2VvGTucfoHPFQoX2Y.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RqTqbpEIfTuJhbmbBXLnf","name":"Police Marshal","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/m14tGl6BVbuVrlHnj9DjK.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-13","duration":-4,"outcomes":"Participating in the Police Marshal Program improved my awareness of public safety, discipline, and the role of police in maintaining peace and order. It enhanced my confidence, communication, and leadership skills by encouraging me to act responsibly and support people in following rules. This experience also helped me develop a stronger sense of social duty, punctuality, and coordination while working with others. Overall, the program motivated me to be more alert, respectful towards laws, and contribute towards creating a safer and more organized environment.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I participated in the Police Marshal Program, which is an initiative that promotes discipline, civic responsibility, and public safety awareness among students. Through this program, I learned the importance of supporting law enforcement in maintaining order and ensuring safety in public places. The activities included understanding basic rules related to traffic awareness, crowd management, and responsible behavior in public areas. Being part of this program helped me realize the value of being a responsible citizen and contributing positively to society by following rules and encouraging others to do the same.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/66C1yMhzfXffbXj_bjkdp.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Nqc38Ze0sH0aaII-NKc-z","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/AA8Hr4yQc8K4L4XSdgkTj.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/nUbq3blCQnvBhSiwaNQbm.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/gtqnTqn2TwXohmbqiJjeC.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/D95R_ym724PGMRSFrnY-4.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/AFadF0jv3H-n2UNLMLV0E.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-28","duration":5,"outcomes":"Participating in the Fist Full program helped me understand the importance of reducing food insecurity and supporting those who struggle to meet basic needs. It developed a strong sense of social responsibility and encouraged me to contribute to society through simple acts of donation. This experience also inspired compassion and empathy, reminding me that even small contributions like donating 5kg rice can make a big difference in someone’s life. Overall, it was a meaningful initiative that motivated me to participate in more community welfare activities in the future.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"I participated in the Fist Full initiative, where I donated 5kg of rice to support people in need. This activity aimed at helping underprivileged families by collecting food grains and distributing them to ensure no one suffers from hunger. Being a part of this initiative made me feel proud as I could contribute towards a meaningful social cause. It was a small effort from my side, but it had a valuable impact in supporting the community and promoting kindness and sharing.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8856754e-00a4-4f15-89de-d663515413eb/nOzV0AB2zo3sCI1NOCTTj.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 17:16:55.229131+00', '2026-01-29 18:40:35.289681+00'), ('96820983-4faa-4b07-9167-338e5daed90a', '7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC074","name":"Junaid Ahmed","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"tno4XMcB5xaKNF5ixG4ac","name":"“Say Yes to Life, No to Drugs” Pledge Initiative","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I became more aware of the serious consequences of drug addiction on physical health, mental stability, and social life. It strengthened my resolve to lead a healthy, drug-free life and to be mindful of my actions and choices. The activity also increased my sense of responsibility as a student to contribute positively to society and support initiatives that promote public health and well-being. Overall, it encouraged me to adopt positive values and to play a small but meaningful role in building a safer and healthier community.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"As part of the “Say Yes to Life, No to Drugs” initiative conducted by the Narcotics Control Bureau under the Ministry of Home Affairs, Government of India, I took a pledge to stay away from drugs and support a drug-free society. This activity helped me understand how drug abuse negatively affects not only an individual’s health but also families and society as a whole. By participating in this national awareness campaign, I consciously committed myself to making responsible choices and encouraging a healthy lifestyle. The pledge served as a reminder of the importance of self-discipline, mental well-being, and social responsibility, especially among students and youth.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values / Social & Community Development Activities","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/IQ3fdIH7uymD2JzzruxJS.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"heNeyXr_aA0cCUctKnTO7","name":"Voluntary Blood Donation Camp Participation","slNo":2,"place":"Gavipuram Guttahalli, Kempegauda Neger, Bengaluru","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-08-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I experienced a strong sense of social responsibility and personal satisfaction by contributing directly to public health and emergency care. It helped me realize the value of selfless service and the impact of individual efforts in saving lives. The activity also increased my awareness about health, blood groups, and the importance of regular voluntary blood donation. Overall, it strengthened my commitment to social service and inspired me to continue participating in community-oriented and humanitarian activities in the future.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-05","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in a voluntary blood donation drive conducted by Rashtrotthana Blood Centre, a government recognized regional blood transfusion centre in Karnataka. By donating blood, I contributed to an essential healthcare service that helps save the lives of patients in need, including accident victims, surgical patients, and those suffering from serious illnesses. This activity gave me a deeper understanding of the importance of blood donation and how a simple act can make a significant difference in someone’s life. It also encouraged me to overcome common fears and misconceptions related to blood donation and motivated me to contribute positively to society through responsible and compassionate action.","aicteMapping":"Social and Community Development Activities / Health and Wellness Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/KGD07J1Z2zX19OalEG7W_.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bRtYesASeLdIX93zicYbw","name":"Project Pustak 2025 – Educational Support Initiative","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"This activity helped me develop a stronger sense of social responsibility and empathy towards students who lack access to basic educational materials. It reinforced the importance of supporting education as a foundation for personal and societal growth. The experience was personally fulfilling, as it allowed me to contribute directly to a cause that promotes equal learning opportunities. Overall, the activity encouraged me to actively participate in social initiatives and motivated me to continue supporting community-driven educational programs in the future.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":48,"description":"I contributed to Project Pustak 2025, an initiative organized by Pranav Foundation in association with RV College of Engineering and Rotaract Club of RVCE. Through this activity, I supported the education of a government school student by sponsoring a stationery kit. The initiative focuses on helping underprivileged students by providing them with basic educational resources, encouraging learning, and reducing barriers to education. Being part of this activity made me realize how small contributions can have a meaningful impact on a child’s academic journey and overall confidence.","aicteMapping":"Social and Community Development Activities / Education Support Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/MCIsfsEAa-Nze79RdsHfs.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FxDv72JjTh1oVIedwplqY","name":"Project Pustak – Student Stationery Support Initiative","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-30","duration":7,"outcomes":"This activity helped me develop empathy and a deeper understanding of the challenges faced by students with limited educational resources. It strengthened my sense of social responsibility and reinforced the importance of contributing towards education and community welfare. The experience was personally rewarding and motivated me to remain actively involved in initiatives that promote equal access to education and support social development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":48,"description":"I took part in Project Pustak, an initiative organized by Pranav Foundation in collaboration with RV College of Engineering and the Rotaract Club. Through this activity, I contributed towards sponsoring a stationery kit for a student studying in a government school. The aim of the initiative is to support students from underprivileged backgrounds by providing them with essential learning materials and encouraging them to continue their education with confidence. Being involved in this activity made me realize how meaningful even a small contribution can be in shaping a child’s learning experience and future opportunities.","aicteMapping":"Social and Community Development Activities / Education and Literacy Support","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/ryxsORkTibeB-WtHqxCEM.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Vpf8w8o0F5TsyD9xc8tGd","name":"Paper Drive for Recycling and Social Welfare","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-25","duration":2,"outcomes":"The paper drive successfully collected a large quantity of waste paper from households, reflecting active community participation and concern for the environment. The funds generated from selling the collected paper were contributed to the Neela Narendra Foundation, directly supporting the needs of children in the orphanage. The activity increased awareness about sustainable living practices and strengthened my sense of responsibility towards both environmental conservation and social welfare. Overall, it reinforced the idea that small individual actions, when combined, can create a meaningful and lasting impact on society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-24","hoursSpent":24,"description":"I participated in the Paper Drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering on 24th June 2023. The main aim of this activity was to promote recycling while supporting a meaningful social cause. Volunteers, including students, faculty members, and local residents, came together to collect old newspapers, magazines, and unused books from different areas of Bengaluru. The collected paper was later sold, and the money raised was donated to the Neela Narendra Foundation, an organization that works for the welfare of orphaned children.","aicteMapping":"Social and Community Development Activities / Environmental Sustainability Activities","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/S0AtyfOaT0eTjcX-DDxuK.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BQ5eUuc0XDajnavDRtc_w","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye – Voter Awareness Program","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-08-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me gain a clearer understanding of the importance of voting and civic responsibility. It encouraged me to actively participate in the democratic process and motivated me to spread awareness among peers about the value of informed voting. The program strengthened my sense of responsibility as a citizen and highlighted the role of youth participation in building a strong and inclusive democracy.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-08-20","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in the “Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” voter awareness program organized by the NSS unit of RV College of Engineering. The activity was conducted with the objective of creating awareness about the importance of voting, especially among first-time voters. Through this program, students were educated about their rights and responsibilities as citizens and the role of voting in strengthening democracy. The initiative encouraged young voters to actively participate in the electoral process and understand how individual participation contributes to the development of the nation.","aicteMapping":"Social and Community Development Activities / Awareness Programs (NSS)","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/x4Rsy4NI0hnNgX1bsR3Uo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"puKE8kMlspDLcEchzRWOW","name":"India Quiz – Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"This activity helped improve my general awareness and critical thinking skills while boosting my confidence in participating in competitive academic events. It encouraged continuous learning and staying informed about national and global issues. The experience also strengthened my interest in co-curricular activities and motivated me to take part in more knowledge-based competitions in the future.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in the India Quiz conducted as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2024, a national-level quiz festival held from 7th to 9th June 2024. This activity provided a platform to test and enhance my knowledge on various topics related to India, including history, culture, current affairs, and general awareness. Participating in a national-level quiz helped me engage in healthy competition, improve my analytical thinking, and gain exposure to a wider academic environment beyond the classroom.","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities / Co-curricular and Intellectual Activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/ZOQS2__cb0YXUCgZTtLO_.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qlJAZtHBSPNcy4_0RS1t_","name":"GenAI Hackathon 2024 – Volunteering and Event Support","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me improve my teamwork, coordination, and communication skills while working in a collaborative technical environment. I gained valuable exposure to current trends in Generative AI and understood how hackathons encourage creativity, problem-solving, and innovation under time constraints. Volunteering for this event enhanced my leadership abilities and strengthened my interest in participating in and supporting technical and professional development activities in the future.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-15","hoursSpent":5,"description":"I volunteered for the GenAI Hackathon organized by the ACM Student Chapter of RV College of Engineering, held on 29th November 2024 at the DTL Huddle. The hackathon focused on Generative Artificial Intelligence and provided students with an opportunity to explore and apply emerging AI technologies to solve real-world problems. As a volunteer, I supported the smooth execution of the event by assisting organizers, coordinating with participants, and ensuring that the overall flow of the hackathon was well managed. Being part of this event gave me exposure to the practical aspects of organizing a large technical program while closely interacting with students working on innovative AI-based solutions.","aicteMapping":"Professional Development Activities / Technical and Innovation Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/-xES4oVffoEdhLAe_k7Ex.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jI68XaFPYoHKB_UNWw7ht","name":"Volunteering for “Unchained” – A Social Awareness and Well-being Event","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"This volunteering experience helped students develop a strong sense of social responsibility and empathy towards community needs. It enhanced essential soft skills such as communication, leadership, teamwork, and problem-solving through real-time coordination and interaction. Participants also gained practical exposure to event management and organizational skills, while becoming more aware of mental well-being and self-development, contributing positively to their overall personal and professional growth.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The activity involved volunteering for the event “Unchained”, organized by the RAAG Club in collaboration with The Art of Living. The event focused on promoting mental well-being, emotional balance, and social awareness among students and the community. As volunteers, students actively contributed to planning, coordination, crowd management, and smooth execution of the program. The experience encouraged students to step beyond academics and participate in meaningful social initiatives that create a positive and lasting impact on society.","aicteMapping":"Extension / Outreach Activities (Social Responsibility & Community Engagement)","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/9juDZmo9cQND_yIU7wq2h.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7o1dIaBNM6DVIIeuDWJPY","name":"Volunteering and Event Management for TEDxRVCE 2024 – “Tomorrow’s Tapestry”","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in TEDxRVCE enhanced students’ organizational, leadership, and communication skills through real-time coordination and teamwork. Volunteers gained practical exposure to large-scale event management and learned to work responsibly under deadlines and pressure. The activity also increased awareness about sustainability, social development, and innovative thinking, while fostering confidence, professionalism, and a sense of contribution toward meaningful academic and social initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-05-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"This activity involved active participation as a volunteer in TEDxRVCE 2024, an independently organized TED event aimed at encouraging dialogue, innovation, and awareness about future challenges and societal development. Volunteers were responsible for various aspects of event management, including planning, coordination, logistics, participant handling, and overall execution. The event also emphasized sustainability through initiatives such as the distribution of seed balls and discussions aligned with climate action goals. Through this experience, students contributed to creating a platform that connected ideas, social responsibility, and community impact.","aicteMapping":"Extension / Outreach Activities (Cultural, Innovation, and Sustainability-Focused Events)","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/0BDobHn6bsd18CWJhYIHy.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sxoXy-FefuU9PwiW7HnGJ","name":"ReSearchathon 2025 – Research-Driven Hackathon and Innovation Challenge","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/L3Dol41J0SxOqr6BI2RbR.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/63owWKgZMJZ4TvasQDNdN.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-16","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participation in ReSearchathon 2025 significantly enhanced students’ research aptitude, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities. Students gained hands-on experience in interdisciplinary collaboration, research documentation, and technical presentation. The activity bridged the gap between classroom learning and real-world applications, strengthened innovation-driven thinking, and exposed participants to academic publishing and expert evaluation. Overall, the event fostered a strong research culture, improved technical and communication skills, and motivated students to pursue impactful, research-oriented solutions.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-15","hoursSpent":12,"description":"ReSearchathon 2025 was a 24-hour offline research-focused hackathon organized by the Coding Club of RV College of Engineering, aimed at transforming innovative research ideas into practical, real-world solutions. Unlike conventional hackathons, this event uniquely combined research, implementation, and academic paper writing. Students worked in multidisciplinary teams under faculty mentorship to address high-impact problem statements across domains such as defence technology, healthcare, space technology, semiconductors, smart engineering, and open innovation. The event encouraged participants to apply theoretical knowledge, conduct in-depth research, and develop solutions with both academic and societal relevance.","aicteMapping":"Technical / Research & Innovation Activities (Hackathon, Research, and Skill Development)","pointsEarned":18,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7f0ccee3-1825-467e-87d6-9be51bf4801b/ulPsfklCydrfEe_hP6pU8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr.Sujata D. Badiger","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 16:40:44.325482+00', '2026-01-30 18:30:02.630352+00'), ('96f5992f-38e1-4732-84df-7cd98b18fdc2', '3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY057","name":"Tanisha Agarwal","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"7rI_6S2SGg9lq8BbyVega","name":"ACM India Chapter Summit","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE and BMSCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/UO3kSGzSxObZvqh6E5aVv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-21","duration":3,"outcomes":"Leading a multi-institutional event of this scale likely taught me the complexities of high-stakes stakeholder management and the art of cross-functional leadership.  Ultimately, my role as President and Event Head centered on community building, teaching you that the true success of such an initiative lies in fostering long-term collaborative networks and driving a unified vision across the entire ACM India landscape.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-19","hoursSpent":50,"description":"B.M.S College of Engineering(Anchor Venue) and R.V. College of Engineering, Bangalore, Karnataka, are excited to invite ACM Chapters from across India to the Annual ACM India Chapter Summit 2024. The event will be held on the 20th and 21st of December, 2024, in Bangalore.\\n\\nThe summit aims to foster collaboration, exchange knowledge, and explore innovative solutions to drive progress in computing. By bringing together ACM chapters across India, the event also seeks to strengthen the community, inspire meaningful societal contributions, and build lasting connections among Student, Professional, SIG and ACM-W Chapters.\\n\\nThe two-day event will feature technical talks, startup showcases, panel discussions, industry interactions, and various opportunities to network and engage.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":25,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/hgyWV1SWA34cwWaxjaroI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"V8jxG0JEsgD8K4ILjY5tv","name":"ACM Build with Gen AI Hackathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/5dRYwIrpClngMcIJmFHnJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"As the organizer behind this hackathon, I gained firsthand experience in rapid-cycle project management and the nuances of fostering a specialized technical community. I had to navigate the logistics of a physical, offline venue while managing a partnership between ACM RVCE and the Accelerate Club, which sharpened your ability to align different organizational goals toward a single vision.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The \"Build with GenAI\" Hackathon, organized by ACM RVCE and Accelerate Club at RV College of Engineering, was a 6-hour offline event held on November 29, 2024, focused on creating AI-powered solutions. The competition encouraged teams of 2-4 members to develop innovative applications, such as agriculture assistants, with a ₹6,000 prize pool. ","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AaNDHnpZVKx_aHNljsIqD","name":"TechTank Hackathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/dGdp5woIVWvVZeWBKX5SS.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-11","duration":5,"outcomes":"I learned that the real challenge of a 12-hour sprint isn''t the code, but the orchestration. I mastered how to synchronize technical development with business viability by forcing a bridge between developer grit and investor expectations. Managing this event taught me that \"market-ready\" isn''t just a buzzword; it’s the result of rigorous time-boxing and facilitating the right connections under pressure.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"TechTank 2025 at RVCE was a 12-hour, Shark Tank-inspired hackathon held in April 2025, with key activities occurring around April 7th to April 11th, 2025. Organized by GDG RVCE and ACM RVCE, the event focused on innovation and entrepreneurship, featuring workshops and pitching sessions for student projects. ","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"E2zwmeJj1Ard-be_e6J-M","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/NPej5RpBUIYUOjLNHmyb9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the power of targeted philanthropy and resource logistics. By contributing at a higher tier, I saw firsthand how individual capital when efficiently managed directly removes the physical barriers to education for rural students, transforming a small donation into a complete toolkit for learning.","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies t o underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which\\nserved as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materialssuch as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FCmEbg7KT6-CKaX44Z1jo","name":"Utsaraga Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"Around RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/LasRHIhmwDfBovk5mqTUo.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned that I’m capable of more than I thought, especially when there''s a good reason to keep running. Pushing through the miles for a cause like \"Help a Child\" showed me that fitness is way more rewarding when you''re running for someone else’s future, not just your own health.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-18","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by the NSS wing of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) and sponsored by Elegant Builders & Developers, was a flagship charity event focused on the theme \"Help a Child, Change the World\". Held in early 2024, the event aimed to support underprivileged children through education, healthcare, and welfare initiatives. ","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/N2NrKR_Qj-vbvjxOd41-C.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"G7tK5ete8qtaG0lBprWFa","name":"Fist Full","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE CAmpus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/OajyhMpBAvWDIFjK3l7PW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":13,"outcomes":"Provided food, supplies, and support to underprivileged children, often supporting institutions like Sai Gurukul School.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Fist Full is an annual charity initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE (in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana) where students donate a handful of rice or dal for every meal cooked, aiming to combat hunger by collecting essential food grains for underprivileged children. ","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HhRuUfn7_zHASgzReUwT1","name":"Rush Hours","slNo":7,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/V0LjZvQDaYU-LcO_5YGVB.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-11-29","duration":6,"outcomes":"I learned that I thrive in high-pressure, elimination-style environments. Competing against 250+ people over five days taught me how to stay consistent and perform under the heat of a live leaderboard. It wasn''t just about winning a prize; it was about proving I could handle a heavy workloadwhile making sure my efforts actually contributed something meaningful to society.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-11-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"A community service and Professional development project which went on for 5 days and included a pre-event task to build interest among the participants followed by 8main tasks. The participants run for their positions as each task led to the elimination of a certain number of teams; with 250+ participants; participating actively, Followed by regular updates through event dashboard and leader board. The event was a huge success with the participants contributing to society along with having fun in this process. The top 5 teams were rewarded with OTT subscriptions and other prizes.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GnpURj74-r3D28bQQlrys","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth: Photography","slNo":8,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learnt photography and stood 8th in the competition.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The SDG Photography Competition witnessed enthusiastic participation, with 568 registrants, including 23 from other IUCEE student chapters. The event featured three evaluation rounds, assessing creativity, relevance to SDGs, and technical quality. Expert judges shortlisted entries, highlighting sustainability through impactful visuals.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/uggNXyoXwJUI_KqV8hWLg.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EKbM9gMaeyTjdUF9zn9YJ","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/j_Tf9jUdtUjEkodRXAPbU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-12-28","duration":9,"outcomes":"Participants created functional or decorative items from waste materials, promoting eco-friendly practices. The event acted as a platform to develop professional skills, including teamwork, critical thinking, and the ability to pitch new, creative ideas.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-12-20","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Uptown Junk is an annual, flagship sustainability and creativity event hosted by the Rotaract Club of RVCE at RV College of Engineering. It features a campus-wide treasure hunt (Fortune Quest) followed by a \"Best Out of Waste\" competition, where teams use collected \"waste\" materials to create innovative, functional models, judged on sustainability and engineering ingenuity. ","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Hj94Mt3RBL41wUDVd6JlX","name":"ACM Speaker Session","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3d0a5204-9575-4239-b3e6-9b21e4d39caf/QPd7M-BHs8HG0R0NxvSpa.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"I also realized that as an ACM leader, my role is to give members a head start on \"AI-driven research,\" moving us past the old-school way of manual tab-juggling and into a workspace where the browser acts as a co-pilot that handles the grunt work while I focus on the high-level strategy.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Agentic Browser Workshop, held on October 28, 2025, was a specialized technical session organized by ACM RVCE in collaboration with Perplexity AI. Hosted at the Civil Seminar Hall, the event focused on the cutting-edge shift from traditional search engines to \"Agentic\" tools.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 03:26:50.387677+00', '2026-01-31 04:23:50.511543+00'), ('97280797-564c-413a-a634-3a65498dbeea', 'b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI028","name":"Kushal Mandhyan","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"ZiCkMGXLOfnIi0VjpzMt1","name":"Rotaract Design Team","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/xsFk4SFbLF8ATJmkYYMsx.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":263,"outcomes":"This experience strengthened my skills in graphic design, visual storytelling, and brand consistency while working under real-world deadlines. I developed the ability to quickly adapt designs to different audiences and formats, improved coordination and communication within a team setting, and gained practical experience in managing multiple design deliverables simultaneously. The creatives produced contributed to better event visibility, higher engagement across platforms, and a more professional and cohesive presentation of the club’s activities throughout the year.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-10-10","hoursSpent":80,"description":"As a member of the Design Team at the Rotaract Club of RVCE, I actively contributed for several months as an Organiser, supporting the club’s events and initiatives through visual communication. My responsibilities included designing event posters and banners, special-day creatives, certificates, annual magazine, and newsletters, ensuring each deliverable aligned with the club’s identity and objectives. Using Canva as my primary design tool, I collaborated closely with event leads to translate ideas into clear, engaging, and timely visual content that enhanced outreach and participation.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/rj3gnF2DBk4QCh5AGJqFU.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lJ72aaappqlXmDNSeBE_A","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":2,"place":"Kunagalu Betta","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/NzaKcNaGEY9g2xiHOV8E0.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":17,"outcomes":"The event successfully achieved high student participation and engagement while promoting awareness about cleanliness and environmental conservation. Participants not only enjoyed a memorable trekking experience but also actively contributed to maintaining the natural beauty of the location. The project strengthened teamwork, leadership, and coordination among the organizing members, and enhanced the club’s reputation for conducting impactful, well-organized events that blend recreation with a meaningful social cause.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-12","hoursSpent":72,"description":"Fast-Trek 2.0, was one of the flagship events conducted by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, aimed at combining adventure with social responsibility. The event brought together enthusiastic college students for an early-morning trek to the scenic Kunagalu Betta. Beginning at 7:30 AM, participants were transported to the trek location, where they were briefed with safety instructions and an overview of the event. A key highlight of the project was the cleanliness drive carried out during the trek, reinforcing the importance of environmental preservation while allowing participants to experience nature firsthand. The event was well-planned and smoothly executed, with essential arrangements such as breakfast and lunch provided to ensure participant comfort throughout the journey.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":18,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/rwc2rrv-E0FxjNO5gi7p2.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qeRY5UZZ1jIQU9-3FOh_r","name":"Paper Drive 2024","slNo":3,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/rVo1gwMYzCiFN7ljNETmg.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":53,"outcomes":"The initiative resulted in the successful collection of 8.17 tonnes of recyclable materials, directly benefiting multiple NGOs and charitable organizations. Beyond its tangible impact, the drive significantly raised awareness about recycling and sustainability among residents, while highlighting the power of student-led action in addressing social and environmental issues. For the organizing team, the project strengthened leadership, large-scale coordination, and community outreach skills, and further established RAC RVCE as an organization capable of executing high-impact, city-wide social initiatives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-02","hoursSpent":64,"description":"RaC RVCE’s Paper Drive was a large-scale social initiative aimed at promoting recycling and supporting social welfare organizations. The drive mobilized over 400 student volunteers who actively collected books, papers, and waste materials from residential communities across Bangalore, including areas such as Nagasandra, Koramangala, and Indiranagar. By reaching out to nearly 15,000 flats, the team efficiently coordinated logistics, volunteer deployment, and area-wise coverage to ensure maximum participation. The collected materials were systematically sorted and directed toward charities, NGOs, and orphanages, reinforcing the importance of responsible waste management and community involvement.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":16,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/0t2zXJmOZWYyXfXF_6dDq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fGBoAYaEk6gE2U0SVBGqI","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/SmN28aUtcJ76qt1vwSjd7.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":12,"outcomes":"The camp resulted in the collection of over 650 units of blood, making a significant contribution toward meeting critical healthcare needs and potentially saving hundreds of lives. Beyond the quantitative impact, the event fostered awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and strengthened collaboration between student bodies and established social organizations. For the organizing team, it enhanced skills in large-scale event management, stakeholder coordination, and social outreach, while reinforcing RaC RVCE’s commitment to impactful community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-17","hoursSpent":64,"description":"RaC RVCE organized a large-scale blood donation camp on June 28, 2024, in collaboration with the Indian Red Cross Society and Rotary Bangalore South, at the Biotech Quadrangle. Commencing at 9:00 AM, the camp was meticulously planned to ensure smooth donor flow, medical safety, and efficient coordination between volunteers and healthcare professionals. The event witnessed participation from Rotaractors, Rotarians, students, faculty members, and members of the local community, reflecting a strong spirit of collective responsibility and service. Over a span of nine hours, the initiative successfully facilitated voluntary blood donations in a well-organized and supportive environment.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":16,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/NccWp29bMkfSjQgkpftLD.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DcUzknbWmpwAlGFAW3dc1","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":5,"place":"Narayangiri Betta","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/pXdtoyiaXOz7XEgh_tWlo.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":59,"outcomes":"The event successfully promoted environmental responsibility while delivering a memorable and engaging outdoor experience to a large student audience. It strengthened awareness about cleanliness and sustainability, encouraged teamwork and social bonding among participants, and created a lasting sense of collective responsibility toward nature. From an organizational perspective, Fast-Trek 3.0 enhanced large-scale event management, volunteer coordination, and leadership skills, while further establishing the Rotaract Club of RVCE’s reputation for executing impactful, purpose-driven flagship events.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":72,"description":"Fast-Trek 3.0 was one of the flagship events organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, designed to blend adventure, environmental awareness, and student engagement. The trek to Narayangiri Hills attracted over 500 enthusiastic college students, offering them an opportunity to experience nature while contributing to a meaningful cause. Along the scenic trail, participants actively took part in a cleanliness drive, reinforcing the importance of sustainability and responsible tourism. The event was carefully planned to ensure safety, smooth coordination, and an enriching experience, allowing participants to enjoy breathtaking views while fostering a deeper connection with the environment.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":18,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/NREUAzUswBsbCoL-dhmGc.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FFIynrRLjZCWh4Np3NLE3","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":6,"place":"Pattanagere","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/NZV3PucVrMJvBukBf4AZb.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":14,"outcomes":"The walkathon successfully sparked conversations and raised awareness about the importance of valuing the girl child and confronting gender-based injustice. It created a strong on-ground presence that extended the message beyond the campus into the surrounding community. The initiative fostered collective social responsibility, strengthened volunteer coordination and event execution skills, and reinforced the Rotaract Club of RVCE’s commitment to addressing sensitive social issues through inclusive, community-driven action.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-28","hoursSpent":80,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon on 11th May 2025 to commemorate Mother’s Day and address the critical social issue of female foeticide. The walkathon commenced at RV College of Engineering and followed a planned route through the Pattanagere area before returning to campus, creating strong visibility within the community. With over 350 participants, the event was inclusive, pet-friendly, and open to all. Participants, along with volunteers, carried creative placards and raised impactful slogans throughout the walk, while a midway checkpoint helped engage and motivate attendees. The distribution of T-shirts and refreshments ensured comfort and encouraged active participation.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b48a674d-27f7-4983-9cfd-c6dcc62cb873/bCOVMH_JgmTO7vs5DWkDq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Anand Jatti","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 17:45:50.434195+00', '2026-01-30 22:01:12.063479+00'), ('97c2250a-cf9c-4636-8a18-cda9e38b9744', '319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI003","name":"Aditya Srinivas ","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"MUj3XCNG1q_gSJA3UtERq","name":"Fist Full ","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/5of8G8P-eq_Mb1-67mZwv.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":19,"outcomes":"The activity significantly enhanced social awareness and sensitivity toward issues of hunger\\nand inequality. It fostered empathy, ethical responsibility, and a strong sense of community\\nservice among participants. Engagement in Fist Full reinforced Universal Human Values such\\nas sharing, compassion, and service to society, while motivating continued participation in\\ninitiatives that promote social welfare, inclusivity, and sustainable community support.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-03","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Participated in Fist Full, a community-oriented food donation initiative aimed at addressing\\nhunger and food insecurity among underprivileged sections of society. The activity focused on\\ncollecting, organizing, and distributing food to individuals in need while creating awareness\\nabout responsible consumption and food wastage. Through direct involvement in outreach\\nand distribution efforts, the initiative emphasized compassion, empathy, and collective\\nresponsibility. It encouraged students to actively contribute to social welfare and understand\\nthe importance of humanitarian action in supporting basic human needs.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values (UHV) – Social Responsibility, Humanitarian Service & Community Welfare","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/QE-FyTKqmdp_RMh3Bbjca.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WBICUVucV9dAsqmjoH2-3","name":"Kaalnirnay","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-12-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness about climate change, environmental responsibility, and the need for sustainable practices in daily life. It strengthened communication and community engagement skills through participation in an awareness-driven initiative, and encouraged a more responsible attitude towards energy usage and climate action.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-12-11","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Climate Clock Distribution Event “Kaalnirnay”, an environmental awareness and climate action initiative aimed at sensitizing students and the community about climate change and responsible energy use. The activity involved supporting the distribution and communication of the Climate Clock concept, which highlights urgency for climate action and encourages responsible individual choices for sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Environmental awareness & climate action / Sustainability outreach","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/eYioPQrCUHOxGaM3ivt8v.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"v_-MhDIOIxdM3x8b5KkKu","name":"Tanuja Screening","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/ZyvBfgbVmwBdeGN3HOfo7.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity helped participants develop empathy, ethical awareness, and a deeper understanding\\nof social issues highlighted through the screening. It promoted reflective thinking, value-based\\nlearning, and responsible attitudes among students, aligning with the principles of Universal\\nHuman Values and fostering social consciousness.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Tanuja Screening was organized as an awareness-oriented activity to sensitize students\\ntowards important social and ethical issues through visual media. The screening aimed to\\ncreate understanding, reflection, and discussion among participants by presenting real-life\\ninspired themes related to human values, social responsibility, and individual awareness. The\\nactivity encouraged students to engage thoughtfully with the subject matter in an educational\\nenvironment.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values (UHV) – Social Awareness & Ethical Responsibility","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7a_YAdrgwcPuxidQojc3_","name":"Nasha Mukt Bharath Abhiyan","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/roMeW-XANtoW6a78N2vfD.jfif"],"endDate":"2025-11-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity significantly improved awareness regarding the dangers of substance abuse and its\\nimpact on individuals, families, and society. It fostered responsible attitudes, self-discipline, and\\ninformed decision-making among participants. The program strengthened civic consciousness\\nand reinforced Universal Human Values such as self-control, social responsibility, and ethical\\nliving. Participation in the initiative motivated students to actively support preventive measures\\nand contribute to national efforts aimed at creating a healthier and drug-free society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Participated in Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan, a nationwide awareness initiative launched by the\\nGovernment of India to address substance abuse and promote a drug-free society. The activity\\naimed to educate students and the community about the harmful physical, psychological,\\nand social effects of drug and alcohol addiction. Through awareness sessions, discussions,\\ncampaigns, and community interaction, the program emphasized prevention, early intervention,\\nand responsible behavior. It encouraged youth participation in spreading awareness, promoting\\nhealthy lifestyles, and supporting national efforts toward building a socially responsible and\\naddiction-free India","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/gDm4UZggkDQDFmDTNzBOg.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TsXbwqeZGigtNeKKFrfUA","name":"Sattva School Teaching ","slNo":5,"place":"Government School ","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-26","duration":9,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced teaching, communication, and interpersonal skills while deepening\\nunderstanding of grassroots-level educational challenges. It fostered empathy, patience, and a\\nsense of responsibility toward community development. Participation in the program reinforced\\nUniversal Human Values such as service, compassion, and commitment to inclusive education,\\nmotivating continued involvement in educational outreach and socially impactful learning\\ninitiatives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-18","hoursSpent":20,"description":"Participated in a teaching and educational outreach program at Satvaa School, aimed at\\nsupporting holistic learning and academic development of students through community\\nengagement. The activity involved assisting in classroom teaching, explaining concepts in a\\nsimplified manner, and supporting students in their learning process. It focused on creating\\nan inclusive and encouraging learning environment while emphasizing the importance of\\neducation, value-based learning, and ethical responsibility. The initiative promoted student\\ninvolvement in social service by contributing time and knowledge to strengthen educational\\nfoundations at the community level.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values (UHV) – Education Support, Social Responsibility & Community Engagement","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/E37lOeSvWWkRX-60X8kVC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mB4Yt7Vi-oKmfrRkEXbZJ","name":"SPARK \"Through the eyes of Youth\" - SDG Photography","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/tCJ37_-TqsWK78N7Z5lbz.jfif"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness of sustainable development challenges and strengthened the ability to critically observe and interpret societal issues. It fostered creativity, social sensitivity,\\nand a deeper understanding of the role of youth in addressing global concerns. Participation reinforced Universal Human Values such as responsibility, empathy, and ethical awareness,\\nwhile encouraging active engagement with sustainability-oriented initiatives through creative and meaningful expression","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Participated in SPARK – “Through the Eyes of Youth”, an SDG-focused photography initiative aimed at encouraging young individuals to visually capture and interpret real-world\\nissues related to the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. The activity provided a creative platform to document social, environmental, and developmental challenges through\\nphotography, promoting observation, critical thinking, and awareness. By translating societal issues into visual narratives, the initiative emphasized youth perspectives on sustainability,\\nresponsibility, and global citizenship while fostering creative expression aligned with social impact.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values (UHV) – Social Awareness, Sustainability & Creative Engagemen","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/uygAh4WtBEK-gRlMfDytQ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UHmTiHCufrOYQqk6Vw5ll","name":"Under the Peepal Tree - 2023","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced reflective thinking, ethical awareness, and interpersonal communication skills among participants. It encouraged empathy, openness to diverse perspectives, and a deeper understanding of societal issues. UTPT 2024 reinforced the importance of dialogue-driven learning and community interaction, strengthening value-based attitudes and responsible\\ncitizenship aligned with Universal Human Values.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Participated in Under the Peepal Tree - 2023, a value-based community engagement initiative aimed at fostering meaningful dialogue, reflection, and awareness on social, ethical,\\nand human-centric issues. The program provided an open platform for discussions, storytelling, and shared experiences, encouraging participants to engage thoughtfully with themes related to empathy, social responsibility, and collective well-being. The activity emphasized inclusive participation, respectful dialogue, and experiential learning rooted in Universal Human Values.","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values (UHV) – Social Awareness, Ethical Engagement & Community Interaction","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/MeiX7Sf3Xd1nzHpG-7IhT.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vYAiDh__GgSxqnlcQZ2uX","name":"Under the Peepal Tree - 2024 ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/kDhy5qRm7FWya4-DSZ7hd.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced reflective thinking, ethical awareness, and interpersonal communication skills among participants. It encouraged empathy, openness to diverse perspectives, and a deeper understanding of societal issues. UTPT 2024 reinforced the importance of dialogue-driven learning and community interaction, strengthening value-based attitudes and responsible citizenship aligned with Universal Human Values.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Participated in Under the Peepal Tree - 2024, a value-based community engagement initiative aimed at fostering meaningful dialogue, reflection, and awareness on social, ethical,\\nand human-centric issues. The program provided an open platform for discussions, storytelling, and shared experiences, encouraging participants to engage thoughtfully with themes related to empathy, social responsibility, and collective well-being. The activity emphasized inclusive participation, respectful dialogue, and experiential learning rooted in Universal Human Values.\\n","aicteMapping":"Universal Human Values (UHV) – Social Awareness, Ethical Engagement & Community Interaction","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/2AHJ8K_9Xgo8ghc_IyFpi.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nLgT_mLlyfWyqPVCLTecL","name":"Under the Peepal Tree - 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/g-oORZOgpMV0--CUo88aT.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced reflective thinking, ethical awareness, and interpersonal communication skills among participants. It encouraged empathy, openness to diverse perspectives, and a deeper understanding of societal issues. UTPT 2024 reinforced the importance of dialogue-driven learning and community interaction, strengthening value-based attitudes and responsible\\ncitizenship aligned with Universal Human Values.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Participated in Under the Peepal Tree - 2025, a value-based community engagement initiative aimed at fostering meaningful dialogue, reflection, and awareness on social, ethical,\\nand human-centric issues. The program provided an open platform for discussions, storytelling, and shared experiences, encouraging participants to engage thoughtfully with themes related to empathy, social responsibility, and collective well-being. The activity emphasized inclusive participation, respectful dialogue, and experiential learning rooted in Universal Human Values.","aicteMapping":"UNDER THE PEEPAL TREE (UTPT 2025) – Community Awareness & Value-Based Interaction Program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/K4AWzX_hAcVEPUniNJqj0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"j0l4OjB2A1YdmIErjTBoc","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2023","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced physical endurance, self-discipline, and awareness of the importance of regular fitness practices. It also promoted teamwork, motivation, and a sense of\\nsocial responsibility, reinforcing healthy living habits and value-based participation in community-driven initiatives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participated in the Utsarga Marathon 2023, a community-level event aimed at promoting physical fitness, mental well-being, and social awareness. The marathon encouraged individuals\\nto adopt a healthy lifestyle while fostering discipline, endurance, and collective participation for a social cause. The event emphasized the importance of fitness, perseverance, and active\\ncommunity engagement.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/319f74d8-d782-444b-a1a0-5d91715e7112/tiWwzjcMR6Avh0Amt6VHc.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr Anand Jatti ","designation":"Associate Professor "},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 17:44:18.135225+00', '2026-02-01 14:41:44.683611+00'), ('98243aa6-7daa-4d46-a1d0-bd658379e381', '2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC058","name":"Gaurav R","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"XKIo37tHCaB1KeZwkojLq","name":" Fast Trek","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/Asf0uGf409i7i719TTC8u.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/k-ULTVdynneAIAB-ZKC3F.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/3ecltHO4mCOH6Un_5Sevf.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fast Trek event successfully brought together adventure and a social cause, with 462 participants taking part enthusiastically. The trek aimed to raise funds to provide financial support to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases.\\n\\nThe event encouraged physical fitness, teamwork, and social responsibility among the participants. It also helped strengthen community bonding and created a memorable experience, as participants enjoyed the scenic beauty of Huthridurga Hills while contributing to a noble cause.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The event Fast Trek was organized by the Rotaract Club of R V College of Engineering with the objective of providing financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases.\\nThe event started at 7:30 AM. Safety instructions along with basic information about the event were provided to all participants before the trek commenced. The trek was a great success, as participants enjoyed the scenic surroundings of Huthridurga Hills and took part in a memorable journey for a noble cause. Breakfast and lunch were provided at the trek location for all the participants.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FsmoxVBxC3kquIfsRTVVV","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/MY0GKYYFKbSi1Si16tkXa.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project helped collect funds and books for underprivileged students, supporting their education needs.\\n\\nEssential study materials such as textbooks, stationery, and school bags were provided to students from rural areas.\\n\\nThe initiative increased awareness about the importance of education and the value of sharing resources.\\n\\nParticipants experienced the satisfaction of contributing to a meaningful social cause.\\n\\nThe event encouraged social responsibility and community service while allowing participants to earn activity points.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to support education for underprivileged students. The main aim of this initiative was to encourage people to donate books and funds so that children in need could access quality education. The theme of the project was “Education is a gift, pass it on, change a life!”\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, donors contributed Rs. 100 or Rs. 350, which was used to purchase essential educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, and school bags. A QR code was provided on the poster to make the donation process easy and accessible. The collected resources were used to help students from rural and underprivileged backgrounds. Participants received up to 10 activity points for their contribution.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FpwiD9EHwXy-Yay5HpkaM","name":"T-Shirt for Smiles","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/Hf7Kl-H_3mnYMhhrI2xpN.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"he initiative successfully generated financial support for Prajakirana Seva     Charitable Trust Anathashram, helping to meet the basic needs andwell-being of the children residing there. Beyond the monetary contribution, the activity instilled a strong sense of empathy, social awareness, and responsibility among participating students. \\nIt reinforced the value of collective effort, demonstrating how small individual contributions can create meaningful impact. The event also strengthened the connection between students and the community, while promoting a lasting culture of compassion and service.  \\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":4,"description":"From 01-07-2024 to 07-07-2024, Kannada Sangha organized a T-shirt purchase initiative for students, priced at ₹400 per student, with the primary objective of contributing to a charitable cause. The initiative witnessed active participation from students, who willingly purchased the T-shirts with the understanding that the collected amount would be used for the welfare of children in need.\\nThe total funds raised through this drive were donated to Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram, located at Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru. The initiative was carefully planned and executed with transparency, ensuring that all contributions directly supported the charitable institution and reflected Kannada Sangha’s commitment to social responsibility.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"80dy-ehsEJoSxGcGV_zxD","name":"Paper Bag","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/OO2lJIvEiLp-wLgLX511e.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/y38FL6FwhQRzeAYlqXtf0.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-22","duration":12,"outcomes":"Participants learned the importance of reducing plastic use and adopting eco-friendly alternatives.\\n\\nThe activity promoted creativity, teamwork, and environmental responsibility.\\n\\nA total of 110 paper bags were made and submitted by me, earning 11 activity points (10 bags = 1 activity point).\\n\\nThe collected paper bags were contributed for community use, supporting sustainability and environmental protection.\\n\\nThe event encouraged students to actively participate in social and environmental causes.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"NSS RVCE, in collaboration with Youth For Seva, organized a Paper Bag Workshop under the Cheela Mela initiative. The activity encouraged students to make eco-friendly paper bags using newspapers as an alternative to plastic bags. Participants crafted paper bags and submitted them at the Environment Lab during the scheduled time. As per the points system, 1 activity point was awarded for every 10 paper bags submitted. The workshop aimed to promote environmental awareness, creativity, and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":11,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"b51GKDbJSedTMS3rKtiNn","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/TCJB5l4ICwcoYZKXEgVAS.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/7F1oSeBkxp0LAK3rkcW6B.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/7DLgWeActmv9CxDTKtLnb.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":5,"outcomes":"The initiative helped collect a large quantity of essential food grains for the underprivileged.\\n\\nSeven NGOs benefited from the donations: A.I.R Humanitarian Homes, Pruthvi Foundation, Sai Aashraya Super Speciality Hospital, Amrutavani Old Age Home, Sneha Jyothi Orphanage, Hanuman Temple, and Nele Foundation.\\n\\nThe event promoted kindness, empathy, and social responsibility among students.\\n\\nStudents actively contributed to reducing hunger and supporting community welfare.\\n\\nThe program strengthened the spirit of service and unity among RVCE students","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-25","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, successfully organized the “Fist Full of Rice & Dal” initiative. RVCE students were encouraged to set aside a fistful of rice or dal during each meal preparation and donate it for a noble cause. The initiative received an excellent response from students, making the event a grand success.\\n\\nDuring the week-long collection phase, over 6700 kg of rice and more than 800 kg of toor dal were collected. The donation phase was held on 10th December 2024, and the collected food grains were distributed to several NGOs to support people in need.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8SgFpzpOz78wyYkDet0ru","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz 2024 ","slNo":6,"place":"Online Mode","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/qxFRFUOQDoG_MUV54P0iF.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/4WJOVoCsCjHUOVZ_7zMwB.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The “Viksit Bharat Quiz 2024” was very successful as it helped spread awareness and information about India’s development. The event had many positive outcomes:\\n\\n1. Knowledge Building: Participants gained valuable knowledge about India’s growth, development, and achievements. They also learned about various government schemes and policies supporting the nation’s progress.\\n\\n2. Encouraging Patriotism: The quiz inspired a sense of patriotism and national pride among participants and motivated them to contribute to India’s growth and development.\\n\\n3. Healthy Competition: The event promoted healthy competition, encouraging participants to perform better and strive for excellence.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"With pride, NSS-National Service Scheme brought to the table \"Viksit Bharat Quiz 2024\"-a national quiz competition that aimed at testing their knowledge about India''s growth, development, and progress. On 1st December, the event witnessed an overwhelming response with more than 100 enthusiastic participants from diverse backgrounds.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"I7IdJt8o9-28LxdMBA85o","name":"UTSARGA Marathon 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/ieedAzlVksJ6VtqV1YTcG.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/8cCj9cWWNoRfSfp7MOTFe.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/LfVlZy57MY7chpEfXCT9A.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"It was a really good experience for the participants and the volunteers as well. This built friendships between the participants and the volunteers. This event also emphasized the importance of physical activity in daily life and how does this impact our health and mind.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The UTSARGA Marathon 2025 was organized by the NSS Club of RVCE. The event began with on-spot registration, where participants collected their UTSARGA T-shirts, badges, and labels. The participants then assembled at the RVCE cricket ground, with 5 km runners on one side and 10 km runners on the other.\\n\\nThe program started with warm-up exercises from 6:00 to 6:30 AM, followed by speeches from the Principal, Vice Principal, Chief Guest, and Major Raghavendra. After this, the marathon was officially flagged off.\\n\\nParticipants ran and jogged around the campus and nearby areas, with water and fruit juice provided along the route. After completing the run, participants collected their certificates, results were announced, and breakfast was served at the Cauvery Hostel mess. The event concluded with participants taking photos at the photo booth.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"P1zHGwagF6FNVKn0kn7BQ","name":"71st Wildlife Week Walkathon","slNo":8,"place":"Vidhana Soudha to Lalbagh","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/JXljwSD44zIYEXNy47Ic9.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/z_EvjPKx4_Nc5mBpeHSDy.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/dHQsX5usjjDsH_tyCm2jz.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The 71st Wildlife Week Walkathon created a strong impact by bringing together students, volunteers, environmental enthusiasts, and officials for a common cause of wildlife conservation. With over 200 participants, the event reflected active community involvement and growing environmental awareness.\\n\\nThe walkathon successfully:\\n• Raised awareness about human–wildlife coexistence and the need for conservation.\\n• Encouraged collaboration among government bodies, educational institutions, and social organizations.\\n• Motivated participants to adopt eco-friendly practices and protect biodiversity.\\n• Strengthened community engagement through a mix of educational messages and cultural activities.\\n\\nOverall, the event served as a meaningful platform to promote conservation values and reinforce collective responsibility toward protecting forests and wildlife.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-02","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The 71st Wildlife Week Walkathon was conducted on 2nd October 2025 from 6:00 am to 9:00 am in Bengaluru. It was jointly organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, NSS, and the Karnataka Forest Department.\\n\\nMore than 200 participants, including students and the public, took part enthusiastically. The event began with an inauguration near Vidhana Soudha, followed by a walkathon through city roads. Participants carried banners and placards to spread awareness about wildlife conservation and eco-friendly practices. The program successfully highlighted the importance of protecting wildlife and maintaining ecological balance.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"h0Fy_aCtSLauQGHeB9ZVb","name":"YES! + Program: Youth Empowerment Seminar followed by SEVA Activities","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fe9d23a-5dd9-4bc4-a648-966d04c9365a/1fhsVLjAHp5iQTEOL7b7y.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-27","duration":45,"outcomes":"After the workshop and SEVA, the students became very calm and got the right state of mind. This also inspired the students a lot. The SEVA activities also gave them an experience of how the Ashram kitchen works and the importance of togetherness and teamwork.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-13","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Day 1 (13th December 2024, 5:00 PM – 8:00 PM):\\nThe session was conducted by the Art of Living team. The program began with fun exercises, dances, and interactive activities to energize the students. The team explained the importance of mental health, energy levels, and the connection between the mind and body.\\n\\nStudents participated in games, riddles, and a Q&A session. After a short break, breathing exercises such as normal breathing, Ujjayi breathing, Bhastrika pranayama, and Sudarshan Kriya were practiced to improve focus and relaxation. The session ended at 8:00 PM.                                                                           Day 2 (14th December 2024, 4:00 PM – 8:00 PM):\\nThe session was conducted by the Art of Living team. The team revised the previous day’s activities and engaged students through fun exercises, games, and discussions on mental states, stress, and ego.\\nBreathing exercises such as normal breathing, Ujjayi breathing, Bhastrika pranayama, and Sudarshan Kriya were practiced to improve focus and relaxation. The session concluded at 8:00 PM.                                                                                                            Day 3 (15th November 2025, 4:00 PM – 8:00 PM):\\nThe session was conducted by the Art of Living team, where the activities from the previous two days were revised through fun exercises and discussions. The team explained different types of relationships, acceptance, responsibilities, and needs in daily life.\\nAfter a short break, students practiced breathing techniques such as normal breathing, Ujjayi breathing, Bhastrika pranayama, and Sudarshan Kriya to improve focus, calmness, and overall well-being. The session concluded at 8:00 PM.                    Day 4 (16th November 2025, 4:00 PM – 8:00 PM):\\nThe final session of the YES+ Program was conducted by the Art of Living team. Students practiced breathing techniques such as normal breathing, Ujjayi breathing, Bhastrika pranayama, and Sudarshan Kriya to improve focus, relaxation, and mental calmness.\\nThis session marked the conclusion of the YES+ program.          Day5 (23rd November 2025, 9:45 AM to 5:00 PM)\\nThe first SEVA activity at the Art of Living Ashram started at 9:45 AM. The students participated in a cleanliness drive near the large lake within the Ashram campus. This activity involved collecting dried leaves and sweeping the area to maintain a clean environment.                                                                                   After the lunch break, The students initially took part in community service work in the kitchen, which included peeling vegetables for dinner preparation.                                                           \\nDay6 (7th December 2025, 9:45am to 5:00pm)\\nIn the permaculture activity, we learned simple farming methods that work with nature. We learned about composting, mulching, and soil care. This activity helped us understand how to protect the environment.\\nAfter lunch, we helped in the kitchen by chopping vegetables (gobi). Later, we attended a meditation class, which helped us feel calm and relaxed.                                                                             \\nDay7(21st December 2025, 9:45 AM to 4:00 PM)\\nThe Gaushala Seva was a calm and peaceful activity. We helped by feeding the cows, cleaning the shelter, and taking care of their well-being. This activity taught us kindness and patience and helped us understand the importance of animals in nature and agriculture.\\nAfter lunch, the students did community service in the kitchen, which included peeling and chopping vegetables.                              Day 8(27th December 2025, 9:45 AM to 4:00 PM)\\nThe SEVA activity at the Art of Living Ashram started at 9:45 AM. The students learned to peel and chop vegetables such as carrots and radishes in the Art of Living kitchen until around 1:00 PM. Some students also helped with basic kitchen work and carrying work.\\nAfter the lunch break, the students returned to the kitchen and chopped the remaining vegetables along with other workers to prepare sambar.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":50,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Sujata D Badiger D","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 15:35:38.21957+00', '2026-02-02 06:52:59.129353+00'), ('9a1aeb1d-74dd-410c-9a3e-3ab0a7d1db0f', '799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC170","name":"Thandlam Mithila","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"G_eiU06snIrK5mzW35Njz","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event enabled effective collection and distribution of food grains to support \\nvulnerable communities. It promoted social responsibility, empathy, and active student \\nparticipation. The initiative strengthened collaboration between the institution and community \\nservice organizations while creating a lasting social impact","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Fist Full event was a flagship community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club \\nof RVCE under Rotary Bangalore South, with the objective of combating food insecurity and \\nsupporting vulnerable communities. Conducted from 17th to 22nd November 2025, the event \\nencouraged collective social responsibility by involving students in contributing essential food \\ngrains. Each participating student donated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, transforming small \\nindividual contributions into a large-scale humanitarian effort. The initiative was aligned with \\nRotary’s Community Service avenue, specifically focusing on the theme of Fighting Disease \\nthrough nutritional support. A total of 2146 students actively participated, demonstrating \\nstrong student engagement and awareness toward social causes. The collected food grains \\nwere systematically sorted, recorded, and prepared for distribution to ensure transparency and \\neffective utilization","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/KKkEHunQj8z3zMWFgxFPu.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6wsIMqLdkOeIVKfdpoRO2","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/NEQL373fjbW3KPiET7J2h.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"The dedication and perseverance of the volunteers were instrumental in empowering rural and \\nunderprivileged students, in line with achieving the club’s mission of making a tangible, lasting \\nimpact on society and fostering a sense of global solidarity","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative\\naimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital\\nresources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\nTo summarize, Project Pustak is a noble initiative aimed to provide essential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pZxHLWMuDzdmxNYFHzXpv","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 successfully combined fitness, charity, and community spirit, advancing \\neducational opportunities for needy children and fostering a sense of social commitment among \\nparticipants.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, was a significant event that celebrated \\nhealth, fitness, and charity. Scheduled to take place on April 6, 2025, at RV College of \\nEngineering, this marathon aimed to bring the community together to run for a cause that \\nextends beyond physical activity to making a lasting social impact. The event''s motto, \"Help a \\nChild, Change the World,\" emphasized the marathon’s mission to support educational initiatives \\nfor underprivileged children and transform their futures.\\nParticipants could choose between 5 km and 10 km race categories, with donations contributing \\ndirectly to providing education for children in need. Beyond the physical challenge, the \\nmarathon represented a collective commitment to social responsibility and charity-driven action, \\nmotivating involvement through both fitness and service.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/4Z7V2RMMULm2Pwppn_yJI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zhvWx9depyBox_6ba-v2L","name":"Female Foeticide Awarness Walkathon 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon effectively raised awareness about female foeticide and gender-based \\ndiscrimination among participants and the wider community. It encouraged meaningful \\ndialogue, inspired collective responsibility, and reinforced the importance of standing against","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":"On the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a \\nFemale Foeticide Awareness Walkathon to highlight the critical issue of female foeticide and \\npromote the value of the girl child in society. The walkathon began in the early hours of \\nthe morning from the RVCE campus and witnessed the participation of over 350 individuals, \\nincluding students, faculty members, and supportive parents. The event was marked by \\nthought-provoking placards and powerful slogans, creating a strong atmosphere of unity and \\nsocial responsibility while spreading awareness on gender equality and dignity","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/FpQ3hfbYcxeAn9jLPguDj.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FP7M4yeG5420zrQKlGoYa","name":"Energy Swaraj Foundation","slNo":5,"place":"Energy Swaraj Portal [Online]","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-10-18","duration":3,"outcomes":"Developed a strong conceptual foundation in sustainable energy systems and environmental responsibility.\\nAcquired the ability to evaluate energy usage patterns and propose efficiency improvements.\\nBuilt awareness to support informed decision-making toward clean and renewable energy adoption.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-10-16","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Completed a structured Energy Literacy Training covering energy generation, consumption, and wastage.Studied carbon footprint analysis and the environmental impact of conventional energy sources.Learned strategies to minimize energy usage and adopt sustainable consumption practices.Gained insights into alternative and renewable energy solutions, including solar energy.Understood pathways to achieve carbon neutrality and addressed common misconceptions about solar adoption.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/Pf2fYXbGRn0CuzsIufabZ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LE-Gkp-oeSPH1yE0rTeKV","name":"National-Level India Quiz – UTPT 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"Strengthened general awareness, reasoning, and analytical skills. Gained exposure to a national-level competitive academic environment. Earned certification contributing to recognized extracurricular activity points.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Participated in Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2024, a national-level India quiz fest. The quiz focused on Indian culture, history, current affairs, and critical thinking. Engaged in competitive problem-solving and rapid decision-making rounds. Demonstrated analytical ability and knowledge application under time constraints. Collaborated and competed with participants from institutions across the country.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/v-HX_1UYoNt1ZZKXEOxfC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tmSHbeFOABoSkqr6KH77C","name":"10m Air Rifle Shooting Event “Lakshya” – NCC RVCE","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-27","duration":2,"outcomes":"Improved marksmanship, focus, and hand–eye coordination. Developed discipline, patience, and stress management skills through competitive shooting. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Actively participated in the 10m Air Rifle Shooting Event “Lakshya” organized by NCC RVCE in collaboration with Kadamba Sports. Gained hands-on experience with standard air rifle equipment and shooting range safety protocols. Practiced precision shooting techniques including posture alignment, breathing control, and trigger discipline. Demonstrated focus, consistency, and mental composure under competitive conditions. Engaged in a structured sports activity promoting discipline, coordination, and concentration.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/yYCtm_iL2qlXNVVj_6Ikd.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"w5hWQeRVB-3U19FZRXuaH","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-08-06","duration":75,"outcomes":"Helped sponsor a stationery kit for a government school student. Developed awareness of grassroots educational challenges and social impact initiatives. Gained experience in community engagement and responsible citizenship.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Contributed to Project Pusthak, an educational outreach initiative by Pranav Foundation in collaboration with Rotaract and RVCE.\\nParticipated in fundraising efforts to support students from government schools. Collected a contribution of ₹350 toward sponsoring essential stationery kits. The initiative aimed to reduce educational resource gaps and encourage continued learning. Actively supported a cause focused on social responsibility and community development.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/36tA8ISZibAfb2tMg55Zl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IqilH6cqotKabdz7ni3G6","name":"Campaign on Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully increased awareness about the importance of voting and democratic \\nparticipation among students. Participants gained a better understanding of India’s electoral \\nsystem and the role of citizens in strengthening democracy. The initiative empowered young \\nvoters to make informed choices while reinforcing responsible and active citizenship","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-03","hoursSpent":3,"description":"NSS RVCE organized “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye”, an online awareness initiative aimed \\nat encouraging young and first-time voters to actively participate in India’s democratic process. \\nThrough the MyGov platform, participants engaged in two key activities—taking the National \\nVoters’ Pledge and completing a quiz on India’s democracy. The event sought to educate students \\nabout their constitutional rights and responsibilities while fostering a sense of civic duty and \\nnational pride among the youth.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/XguOkoflEb6_GS_RQq4yn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YExshoSk-IF7QsaWsAP8n","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-04-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully fostered awareness about physical fitness and social \\nresponsibility among participants.\\nIt contributed directly to supporting educational opportunities for children in need through \\ncollective donations.\\nThe event strengthened community bonding by uniting students, faculty, and the public under \\na shared cause of compassion and change.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-04-02","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon, a spirited initiative that brings together fitness, compassion, and social responsibility. Scheduled for February 4th, 2024, at R V College of Engineering, this marathon is more than just a run—it is a collective movement towards meaningful change. With the inspiring theme “Help a Child Change the World”, the event aims to promote health and well-being while contributing towards the education of underprivileged children. Participants can choose between 5 km and 10 km runs, making it accessible to all age groups and fitness levels. By taking part, every runner becomes a catalyst for hope, proving that small steps taken together can create a \\nlasting impact on society","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/GTPVcGVQzyvDOWYAq8SH2.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UPDwxK1rr3INQ0Gn6eRRu","name":"UTPT Quiz 2023","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"Enhanced critical thinking and analytical reasoning skills through competitive quiz rounds\\nImproved general awareness and subject integration across multiple knowledge domains","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Participated in Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2023, a national-level quiz fest organized by RV Institutions, held from 14th to 16th July 2023. The event focused on testing participants’ knowledge across diverse domains, encouraging analytical thinking, awareness of current affairs, and interdisciplinary learning. The quiz provided a competitive platform for students across India to engage in intellectually stimulating challenges and collaborative problem-solving.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/799383ac-f3cd-4acd-8aa9-5a2fbbddc461/8jX5iYXK5roomUhnE3pWG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 04:31:49.430448+00', '2026-01-30 05:06:00.178717+00'), ('9c2f180a-f271-47c0-aa03-6c4f2f79cf10', '567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC121","name":"Rahul Raj","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"lS8hW8CxwtCbqd3IhPL5H","name":"Fast-Trek 2023","slNo":1,"place":"Hutridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/PARY_LARui7qCZlRZ_-KL.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/lpPQFCQrCEuCZG6nKkPgB.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The trek was a great success as all the participants had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of Huthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very memorable journey. Breakfast and lunch were provided at the trek location for all the participants.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was to provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the participants boarded the bus to the trek location with with great enthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with basic information of the event.","aicteMapping":"Social cause  to provide financial aid to underprivileged children","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/vPrOC5beiLnO5T2NYFtjT.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TIwh4W636BpAy93B4M_IE","name":"Mera Vote Desh keliye","slNo":2,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/ByxxsJ6rQg9dNC9N2itjJ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/A4SAMETE-W2kkIXAOZZQM.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Supported by registering and spreading awareness.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Participated in Mera Vote Desh keliye to spread awareness among the public.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/wjNcgkIL6x7uw1sDOEB45.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"281a87HT80GNDvNmfWmII","name":"Pustak 2023","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-05-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-05-16","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak, a noble initiative aimed to provide\\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/eHsW8cpm-0YQ_Js8PpI05.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sEq5QSANg5w7sOEoT6VzE","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2023","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Gained awareness about the importance of blood donation and contributed to saving lives through voluntary service.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Participated in a blood donation camp to contribute towards community health and support patients in need.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/n7yXvtlAhfGEfzW-hCWRv.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"enGuo6HxAClOqxHKnPZl-","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/mgNazp2138Nyfh8nllyY0.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Collected money was given to orphans and needy children. Successfully completed the 5km run and contributed for a noble cause.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A community marathon event that had various categories across 5km and 10km. Winners were acknowledged with medals and prizes. Participants received certificates and medals.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/qqh4c9wcVoaQsxEVwB79h.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9lLa-TeKEBzvIA6nAifa2","name":"Pustak 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/rQA8rYmyrxlhiunAbMtbh.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Supported the education of deprived children by helping procure books, stationery, and learning materials, fostering a better learning environment.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantialamount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/lu9O4hpqIFYDSCQ00JgUw.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zNYSrN-WcpHiUqUN1Evt_","name":"FISTFULL 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"\"Fist Full,\" an impactful initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, was held from November 15-29. The first phase focused on combating hunger by inviting students to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":1,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with RotaryBangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/whYskZXWzO97hbl9Eh9Kf.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mql4BfYIu0R6RG75YKGDJ","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/4Mp8sRJfTMXv_hf9JIYYb.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/4FYls3CIT-HS22sslIhpj.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Collected money was given to orphans and needy children. Successfully completed the 5km run and contributed for a noble cause.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A community marathon event that had various categories across 5km and 10km. Winners were acknowledged with medals and prizes. Participants received certificates and medals.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/8B074RAONLVeKe18_CKsb.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"y9HwtXe4-T59HJNur3K0X","name":"Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased environmental awareness and measurable contribution to carbon reduction through tree plantation.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A sustainability initiative where every T-shirt purchase  ontributes to planting a tree, promoting eco-friendly consumer habits.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/567c3bef-5eee-490a-891f-55282844b4b6/1EvGhec8aQLXcI4Hs17WU.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ausHc_0c06WFRTshIvMcL","name":"Nasha Mukth Bharat Pledge","slNo":10,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-08-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced public awareness about the harmful effects of drugs and increased community participation in building a drug-free society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-15","ho