tive and uplifting environment for the children, fostering happiness and emotional well-being. The interaction helped in building confidence among the children by making them feel valued and cared for. Engaging games and shared celebrations encouraged social bonding and joyful participation. The distribution of sweets and goodies brought festive cheer and smiles to the children. The activity strengthened the spirit of empathy, compassion, and social responsibility among the Rotaract Club members. It provided an opportunity for students to understand the importance of community service. The event promoted teamwork and effective communication among volunteers. It reinforced the values of kindness and inclusivity. Overall, the activity contributed meaningfully to both personal growth and societal impact.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-11-12","hoursSpent":4,"description":"With the heartfelt desire to spread Diwali joy, the Rotaract Club of RVCE embarked on a meaningful visit to the Garden City Jeevitha Anath ashrama. The primary aim was to empower, support, and motivate the resilient young souls, inspiring them to move forward in life and reach their fullest potential. The day unfolded into a delightful celebration, marked by the joyous exchange of goodies and sweets with the children. The club members actively engaged in playing games, fostering a sense of camaraderie and fun-filled moments.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/48cd72ba-82e1-4261-8156-a25ac9e53cee/DNcQc-D0k7uiUynjI8KyV.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4i0bmAsRXX8Mp1ABgRLHE","name":"","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 11:46:44.741464+00', '2026-01-31 11:50:33.989602+00'), ('9d7e0167-fc46-463e-83cc-4d0c286a5b5b', '2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY037","name":"Mallikarjun M","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Qty-x9rW0mnTi3f9CyC7-","name":"Voting Awareness Seminar","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/YL1uVR8_UWyVMESrfI2l2.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness among students about the importance of voting and democratic values. Motivation of first-time voters to actively participate in elections. Enhanced understanding of electoral rights, responsibilities, and the voting process.\\nDevelopment of a sense of patriotism and social responsibility among participants. Encouraged students to become informed citizens and contribute positively to nation-building. Strengthened the idea that every single vote matters for the future of the country","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-09","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The event “Voting Awareness Seminar” was organized with the objective of creating awareness among students and citizens about the importance of voting in a democratic nation. The program aimed to motivate first-time voters to actively participate in the electoral process and understand their role in nation-building. The program successfully encouraged young voters to be informed, responsible, and proactive citizens who contribute to strengthening democracy.","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":1,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TmLPbBffDu3xxTMMRXp-m","name":"Mere Pehele Vote Desh keliye","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/MDlFD_9pRI1FPhAbBqT5H.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness among students about the importance of voting and democratic values. Motivation of first-time voters to actively participate in elections. Enhanced understanding of electoral rights, responsibilities, and the voting process.\\nDevelopment of a sense of patriotism and social responsibility among participants. Encouraged students to become informed citizens and contribute positively to nation-building.\\nStrengthened the idea that every single vote matters for the future of the country.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The event “Mera Pehle Vote – Desh Ke Liye” was organized with the objective of creating awareness among students and citizens about the importance of voting in a democratic nation. \\nThe program aimed to motivate first-time voters to actively participate in the electoral process and understand their role in nation-building. The program successfully encouraged young voters to be informed, responsible, and proactive citizens who contribute to strengthening democracy.","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/tZRd2Ga069tXUtYI4RKkJ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UJ3PL6LUexumdIl8zaell","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive at RVCE campus resulted in several meaningful outcomes. Most importantly, the donated blood will directly contribute to saving lives during medical emergencies, surgeries, and treatments. The initiative fostered a strong sense of social responsibility among students, encouraging them to actively participate in community welfare activities. It also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and inspired many to consider becoming regular donors. On a personal level, the experience brought a sense of fulfillment, empathy, and compassion, reinforcing the value of contributing to society in impactful ways.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at the RVCE campus. The event was conducted in a well-coordinated manner, with medical professionals ensuring safety and comfort throughout the process. It was a fulfilling experience to contribute towards saving lives and supporting the community. The initiative not only promoted social responsibility among students but also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Donation","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/6o3UEt4gniaXA1xPfdS26.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"B-H4X0dbmaKVtgRoN_ZkM","name":"Utsarga Marathon - Participant","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness among participants about the importance of physical fitness and maintaining a healthy lifestyle while strengthening interaction and bonding between students and the local community. It helped develop a strong sense of social responsibility, discipline, and volunteerism among students. Through active involvement in planning and execution, students improved their organizational, leadership, and teamwork skills. Overall, the program contributed positively to community well-being and encouraged continued participation in health-oriented and socially responsible activities.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized as a Community Development initiative with the objective of promoting health awareness, social responsibility, and community participation \\namong students and the general public. The event focused on encouraging physical fitness, discipline, and a sense of social commitment while spreading awareness about healthy lifestyles \\nand community well-being. Students, faculty members, and local community participants actively took part in the marathon. The program also aimed to instill values of teamwork, \\nleadership, and service towards society, aligning with the objectives of AICTE’s community engagement and social outreach initiatives.","aicteMapping":"Food and Malnutrition Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/wR5H4BSExNG7x76j_RVM0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wYf0hzZvX2I31tHlYB13f","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive at RVCE campus resulted in several meaningful outcomes. Most importantly, the donated blood will directly contribute to saving lives during medical emergencies, surgeries, and treatments. The initiative fostered a strong sense of social responsibility among students, encouraging them to actively participate in community welfare activities. It also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and inspired many to consider becoming regular donors. On a personal level, the experience brought a sense of fulfillment, empathy, and compassion, reinforcing the value of contributing to society in impactful ways.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at the RVCE campus. The event was conducted in a well-coordinated manner, with medical professionals ensuring safety and comfort throughout the process. It was a fulfilling experience to contribute towards saving lives and supporting the community. The initiative not only promoted social responsibility among students but also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/ASe1xgTGCObeDoxp5W052.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"I9zqeSp2bl0GqwMwjy0BZ","name":"Vikasit Bharath Quiz","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/QtWmhHq1TJY7sbbsC617m.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ understanding of India’s developmental roadmap and the role of citizens, especially youth, in nation-building. It improved awareness of government \\ninitiatives, current affairs, and socio-economic challenges. The quiz also helped develop critical thinking, teamwork, and competitive spirit among students, while fostering a sense of patriotism and responsibility towards contributing to a Viksit Bharat.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Activity was organized to create awareness among students about the Government of India’s vision for a developed nation (Viksit Bharat). The quiz focused \\non key themes such as economic growth, digital transformation, innovation, sustainability, infrastructure development, and social inclusion. It encouraged participants to learn about national policies, flagship schemes, and India’s long-term development goals through an interactive and engaging format.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"k8ufd1LFAnd51JUkp4njv","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive at RVCE campus resulted in several meaningful outcomes. Most importantly, the donated blood will directly contribute to saving lives during medical emergencies, surgeries, and treatments. The initiative fostered a strong sense of social responsibility among students, encouraging them to actively participate in community welfare activities. It also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and inspired many to consider becoming regular donors. On a personal level, the experience brought a sense of fulfillment, empathy, and compassion, reinforcing the value of contributing to society in impactful ways.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-20","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at the RVCE campus. The event was conducted in a well-coordinated manner, with medical professionals ensuring safety and comfort throughout the process. It was a fulfilling experience to contribute towards saving lives and supporting the community. The initiative not only promoted social responsibility among students but also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/Oo0gwsHew1R6_8wqhAFpK.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t4JXfPGdLqHIAv9de54k7","name":"Utsarga Marathon - Participant","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness among participants about the importance of physical fitness and maintaining a healthy lifestyle while strengthening interaction and bonding between students and the local community. It helped develop a strong sense of social responsibility, discipline, and volunteerism among students. Through active involvement in planning and execution, students improved their organizational, leadership, and teamwork skills. Overall, the program contributed positively to community well-being and encouraged continued participation in health-oriented and socially responsible activities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized as a Community Development initiative with the objective of promoting health awareness, social responsibility, and community participation \\namong students and the general public. The event focused on encouraging physical fitness, discipline, and a sense of social commitment while spreading awareness about healthy lifestyles \\nand community well-being. Students, faculty members, and local community participants actively took part in the marathon. The program also aimed to instill values of teamwork, \\nleadership, and service towards society, aligning with the objectives of AICTE’s community engagement and social outreach initiatives.","aicteMapping":"Community   Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/QphSw8dGn5hANlNR_3XhD.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tteo1ozFqhvs4_POKpgoW","name":" LAKSHYA","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event had several positive outcomes. Rifle shooting training helped in developing concentration, precision, and self-confidence, while also fostering teamwork and discipline. The plantation activity contributed to environmental conservation, adding greenery to the campus and spreading awareness about ecological responsibility. Together, these activities created a holistic experience that combined physical skill-building with social and environmental impact, leaving participants with a sense of accomplishment and responsibility towards society and nature.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in Lakshya, an event organized at RVCE that combined training in rifle shooting with a plantation drive. The program was designed to instill discipline, focus, and responsibility through shooting practice, while also promoting environmental awareness and sustainability through tree plantation. It was a unique blend of skill development and social contribution, encouraging students to engage in both personal growth and community welfare.","aicteMapping":"NCC","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/O4JbIDHbLZhF3-mkMo_4F.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-b-kTvJ6i_GlP6pcmypZ7","name":"PROJECT PUSTAK","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through Project Pustak, I learned the importance of social responsibility and community engagement. The activity highlighted how small interventions, such as providing basic \\nstationery, can create a significant impact on a child’s education. I gained a deeper understanding of the challenges faced by students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds and how lack of resources can affect attendance and learning outcomes. This initiative strengthened my sense of empathy, teamwork, and leadership, and reinforced the role of engineers and students in contributing positively to society beyond academics.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a joint initiative by the RV College of Engineering and the Pranav Foundation, aimed at supporting children in rural government schools. In 2024, the program made a meaningful impact by providing essential stationery like notebooks and geometry boxes to students from underprivileged communities. Many of these children, from economically disadvantaged families, often missed classes due to a lack of basic supplies. Pustak helps bridge this gap, ensuring every child has the tools they need to participate in their education.","aicteMapping":"Community  ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/6ycBTa0XV_2gO9zNkk8uP.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dBRdWGG-DGR1NJurS37KT","name":"Nasha Muktha Bharath","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/LYezYAV6uJTzXE7v9-Kro.png"],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity successfully increased awareness about substance abuse and its long-term impact on individuals and society. Participants gained a better understanding of the importance of \\nself-control, mental well-being, and healthy lifestyle choices. The initiative fostered a sense of social responsibility and encouraged students to act as ambassadors of a Nasha Mukta Bharat by spreading awareness among peers and the wider community. It also strengthened students’ commitment to personal discipline and community welfare.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Nasha Mukta Bharat Abhiyan activity was organized to create awareness among students and the community about the harmful effects of substance abuse and to promote a drug-free \\nlifestyle. The activity focused on educating participants about the physical, mental, and social consequences of addiction through awareness sessions, discussions, and interactive activities. Emphasis was placed on prevention, responsible decision-making, and the importance of maintaining a healthy and disciplined life.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/7iMpCddhmheIJbzKRy26V.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zzbXjnTEfOnbS2ZWGhzAl","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive at RVCE campus resulted in several meaningful outcomes. Most importantly, the donated blood will directly contribute to saving lives during medical emergencies, surgeries, and treatments. The initiative fostered a strong sense of social responsibility among students, encouraging them to actively participate in community welfare activities. It also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and inspired many to consider becoming regular donors. On a personal level, the experience brought a sense of fulfillment, empathy, and compassion, reinforcing the value of contributing to society in impactful ways.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at the RVCE campus. The event was conducted in a well-coordinated manner, with medical professionals ensuring safety and comfort throughout the process. It was a fulfilling experience to contribute towards saving lives and supporting the community. The initiative not only promoted social responsibility among students but also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/YoZt7m61LltE7XAkJ8gh6.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gvpcHbveU7uku6I402bq8","name":"Fist Full","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2ce0fe16-1ab5-4b9c-8312-41926285ea1d/YywMIcberx86rMMQjdebH.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The initiative received an overwhelming response, with over 4,370 kg of rice and 2,516 kg of toor dal donated by more than 2,146 students. The collected food grains contributed significantly to supporting underprivileged communities. The activity reinforced the impact of collective action and demonstrated how small individual contributions can lead to meaningful societal change. Participants gained a deeper sense of compassion, teamwork, and civic responsibility, strengthening RVCE’s commitment to community welfare and social solidarity.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"“Fist Full” is a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November. The initiative aimed to combat hunger and food insecurity by encouraging students to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. Daily collections were carried out in the Civil \\nDepartment, ensuring smooth coordination and participation. The drive witnessed enthusiastic involvement from students, reflecting a strong culture of empathy and social responsibility \\nwithin the campus.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 06:23:54.686196+00', '2026-01-30 06:23:55.642137+00'), ('9df37128-4972-4388-9287-013ecb4ac67c', 'e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD005","name":"Anant Tewari","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"eWRD9lHcKHZkGd098L3zv","name":"Under the Peepal Tree Quiz Fest 2025","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/DMy2T4T-1otvhGdJ4-GxV.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"A diverse group of more than 500 participants from across the nation was successfully attracted to the campus, fostering a high-intensity environment of intellectual exchange and academic networking. Significant contributions were made by twenty-one student organizers, whose dedication to the festival''s success was formally acknowledged by the institution. Large-scale event management skills, team coordination protocols, and public engagement strategies were refined by those involved in the execution phase. A total of 15 activity points were officially earned for the successful completion of these organizational duties.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":24,"description":"Detailed Description: The 2025 edition of \"Under the Peepal Tree\" (UTPT), which is widely recognized as the largest quizzing festival in Asia, was hosted and meticulously organized by RV QuizCorp, the official quizzing society of R.V. College of Engineering. The event was conducted over a three-day period from May 23rd to May 25th, 2025, within the specialized confines of the IEM Auditorium. Extensive logistical arrangements were overseen by the organizing team, involving the synchronization of technical infrastructure, the management of national-level participant registrations, and the curation of high-quality competitive content. Six distinct quiz categories—including Science and Technology, Arts and Literature, and Sports—were presented to challenge the intellectual breadth of all attendees.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/DUkFxng6mr_uD0YfVZu14.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2LRjL51m5fRJAaVtAczan","name":"Under the Peepal Tree Quiz Fest 2023","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/90zR0s7RHxiD82v6JEo3j.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"Intellectual engagement across a broad spectrum of academic disciplines was successfully facilitated for over 500 participants. The essential roles played by twenty-one student volunteers in maintaining the operational flow of the festival were formally recognized. Crisis management capabilities and collaborative teamwork were demonstrated during the four-day event duration. For the satisfactory performance of these volunteer responsibilities, 15 activity points were rewarded.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The 2023 iteration of the UTPT Quiz Fest was facilitated by RV QuizCorp between July 14th and July 17th, 2023. This prestigious national-level competition was hosted at the IEM Auditorium, where a tradition of intellectual excellence was continued through rigorous academic questioning and debate. Administrative support and volunteer services were provided to ensure that the influx of participants was handled with professional efficiency. Specialized quiz rounds in the domains of Science, Technology, Arts, Literature, and Sports were curated and executed to maintain the festival''s high competitive standards.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/VqbTPwYA4qQVtpZq34uRk.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FjkfWR-4TD5xScIdLg9th","name":"YES!+ Course","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/mr59B4vfzD4xN3eaEqa3w.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-03","duration":3,"outcomes":"Awareness regarding the critical importance of mental health and wellness was successfully acquired and subsequently imparted by the participant. Personal growth milestones and a heightened sense of social responsibility were achieved through the completion of the course modules. Formal validation of this achievement was provided by Rajeev Nambiar, Director of Art of Living Institutional Programs. A total of 10 points were awarded for the successful fulfillment of the course requirements.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":24,"description":"Participation in the YES!+ Course was undertaken from December 1st to December 3rd, 2024, at the RVCE Campus. This initiative was designed by the Art of Living International Center to empower young individuals through specialized educational workshops and humanitarian service modules. The course curriculum was aligned with the \"Har Ghar Dhyan\" initiative of the Government of India, focusing on the promotion of mental health and wellness among the student population. Techniques for stress management, emotional resilience, and leadership development were imparted to the participants during the seminar.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/70eQ75Kv7c1wgwyBJ0wv4.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yKTDBLXvVYS3rmqV-2QqH","name":"Community Kitchen","slNo":4,"place":"Art of Living International Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/CkOqPfUKEVtxLV0Yq-GsK.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Practical tasks, including the serving of food, the preparation of vegetables, and the maintenance of kitchen hygiene standards, were successfully executed. A practical understanding of humanitarian logistics and large-scale meal management was gained through this volunteer engagement. The center’s operational goals were supported by these efforts, which were formally appreciated in a letter of recognition. For this contribution to community welfare, 10 activity points were earned.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Hands-on community service was performed at the Art of Living International Center’s global headquarters on January 4th, 2025. This activity was facilitated through the YES!+ initiative, placing students in a high-capacity operational environment dedicated to humanitarian feeding programs. Large-scale food preparation and distribution protocols were followed to support the daily nutritional needs of the center’s community. The importance of collective effort and the dignity of manual labor were emphasized throughout the service period.","aicteMapping":"12","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/OLLV_AY_7hgDqtXAsg-3a.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lAQvoNc2KpYmnhutHz2XR","name":"Gaushala","slNo":5,"place":"Art of Living International Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/5N7E08aaYVMCRCDqTaBnX.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The conservation of native livestock breeds was directly supported through these volunteer efforts. Awareness of environmental impact and the intersection of traditional knowledge with modern sustainability was significantly increased. The successful completion of these conservation-based tasks was formally certified by the Art of Living leadership. A reward of 10 activity points was granted for this commitment to environmental and cultural preservation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-11","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Volunteer contributions were made to the Gaushala operations at the Art of Living International Center on January 11th, 2025. The conservation and raising of indigenous cows of India were prioritized during this activity, which was facilitated by the YES!+ youth empowerment framework. Participants were involved in the daily upkeep of the facility and were educated on the ecological significance of native livestock in sustainable agricultural practices. The preservation of biodiversity and traditional heritage was a central focus of the service provided.","aicteMapping":"7","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/HRZole7bsWC8oqtvKJYF0.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XD0HuRDQy3eeJB6fLaYm7","name":"Fist Full","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/7i_XdFA_hS0udFuwkO5_Q.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"A significant large-scale impact was achieved, with 2,146 students participating in the drive and a total of 4,370 kg of rice and 2,516 kg of toor dal being collected. Nutritional resources were distributed to multiple beneficiaries, including Sai Ashraya Hospital, the Pruthvi Foundation Blind Boys Hostel, and various anganwadis. The initiative successfully addressed local food insecurity through the organized efforts of the student body. For this contribution to the hunger relief program, 10 activity points were attained.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The \"Fist Full\" project, a flagship community service initiative, was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana in November 2025. Collective student action was utilized to combat hunger and food insecurity by gathering essential food grain donations. Voluntary contributions of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal were collected at the Civil Engineering Department. The project was classified under the \"Community Service\" avenue with a specific mandate to provide nutritional support to vulnerable demographics.","aicteMapping":"12","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/qFKgC3HxC7ynXZp3Tjl48.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YYxE3q7aJ_neKGwdapIqQ","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/7-YKChkwySKf4Y9FqkO4d.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improvements in physical stamina and endurance were gained through participation in the marathon. Personal development milestones, such as increased discipline and motivation, were achieved through the rigors of the event. Awareness of social contribution and the necessity of supporting children in need was successfully fostered. A total of 15 activity points were officially earned for this engagement in the NSS-led health and social awareness drive.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025 was organized by NSS RVCE on April 6th, 2025, to promote physical health, discipline, and social responsibility. A 5 km or 10 km run was encouraged for students and the public to raise awareness for education-related social causes. The event was held under the theme \"Help a Child, Change the World,\" connecting physical fitness with charitable contributions for the benefit of underprivileged children. All registration proceeds were dedicated to supporting initiatives that improve educational opportunities.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/uTy5p0JWTH4aKYWUXFhFk.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QRHil4H2thlOoMrQb8KOD","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/iOCA4apkJAlaEfWH1rGD7.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Vital school supplies, including textbooks, stationery items, and backpacks, were purchased and distributed using the funds gathered during the project. Deserving students in rural locations were directly supported, equipping them with the necessary tools for academic progression. The educational divide was effectively addressed through this student-led intervention. For the successful completion of these fundraising and resource procurement duties, 10 points were awarded.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"\"Project Pustak\" was executed on May 24th, 2024, as an initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation. The primary objective of the project was the provision of essential educational resources to underprivileged students residing in rural regions. Fundraising efforts were undertaken to procure school supplies, ensuring a more conducive learning environment for those in need. The belief that \"Education is a gift\" was central to the mission of the project.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/05HADiEoLFnHm-hc4Ls46.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"POpUEK_EYcP3E3qJ2VC9U","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2023","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/oG0tay4qgmktZhcz-Ehph.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Physical stamina and endurance were enhanced through participation in the marathon event. A sense of discipline was cultivated by the commitment to the early-morning run and its social objectives. Awareness of the impact of social contributions on the lives of children in need was successfully fostered. For the commitment shown toward this worthy cause, 5 activity points were rewarded.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The 2023 edition of the Utsarga Marathon was facilitated by NSS RVCE on June 4th, 2023. Fitness and social responsibility were promoted through the theme \"Help a Child, Change the World\". A donation-based registration model was utilized to encourage participation in 5 km and 10 km categories. The event served as a platform for creating awareness regarding the challenges faced by underprivileged children in accessing quality education.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e2ead273-f176-454e-a598-fc4d151741e2/QJa_l9AdAYBiGl5Q6DtDf.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 13:25:27.621454+00', '2026-01-31 15:09:58.803299+00'), ('9e729167-5a67-4f2b-a36e-9157972c81ee', '21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV089","name":"Sachin Reddy","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"vqFKbicOrEjfR4Syyn9VQ","name":"Utsarga marathon 2024","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/mA3YddwuXImvkWNiR2d15.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility and gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my efforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the\\ncommunity","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":80,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my physical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to\\nsociety in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating anpositive change in society. Thiscause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding.\\nKnowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of\\ncommunity service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causesin the future.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/lEmMpOTxHMcMN3nXoo-qQ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"h2HGjtbQlLyV77ZHJXUWR","name":"Utsarga Marathon 25","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/VcvTZ4KKe9DChB9y9ZoFa.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance\\nwith community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility and gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my efforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":144,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my physical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to\\nsociety in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating anpositive change in society. Thiscause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding.\\nKnowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of\\ncommunity service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causesin the future.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":36,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/EkuyH9Y974HiqvI81oIGh.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"W-6wc8Lj_kR_2dDSkDN3E","name":"Jagadhava Kannada Habba","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/jSP7svmtlWarfRqXcDPb5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness and appreciation of Kannada language and culture among students\\n\\nEncouraged active student participation in cultural and artistic activities\\n\\nStrengthened a sense of unity, pride, and regional identity\\n\\nEnhanced communication, confidence, and stage presence of participants\\n\\nPromoted respect for cultural diversity and traditional values\\n\\nCreated a memorable and enriching cultural experience for everyone involved","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":120,"description":"The Kannada Festival Celebration was organized to honor and promote the rich cultural heritage, language, and traditions of Karnataka. The event aimed to create awareness about the importance of Kannada language, literature, folk arts, and customs among students and staff. The celebration included various cultural activities such as Kannada songs, folk dances, skits, poetry recitations, and speeches highlighting the history and pride of Karnataka.\\n\\nStudents actively participated by wearing traditional attire, showcasing the diversity and beauty of Kannada culture. The program also emphasized unity, cultural identity, and respect for regional languages. Overall, the celebration served as a platform to encourage cultural expression and preserve Karnataka’s traditions in a joyful and engaging manner.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/3vmSysMDFePN1mb36URL8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kzRrz_DtlhnDKNOes8c2C","name":"8TH MILE","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/rFvDnk6hooqxwAB46lLEo.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":2,"outcomes":"Enhanced student engagement and participation across departments\\n\\nImproved leadership, teamwork, and organizational skills among students\\n\\nProvided a platform to showcase cultural, technical, and creative talents\\n\\nStrengthened interdepartmental bonding and campus unity\\n\\nBoosted confidence, communication, and event management skills\\n\\nCreated a lively, memorable, and enriching college experience","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-05","hoursSpent":80,"description":"8th Mile is an annual college-level cultural and technical festival organized to provide a vibrant platform for students to showcase their talents, creativity, and innovation. The festival featured a wide range of events including cultural performances, technical competitions, fun activities, and interactive sessions that encouraged student participation across various departments.\\n\\nThe event aimed to promote teamwork, leadership, and healthy competition while fostering an energetic and inclusive campus atmosphere. Students actively participated in organizing and managing the festival, gaining practical experience in event planning and coordination. Overall, 8th Mile served as a celebration of youth, creativity, and collaborative spirit within the college community.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/21d86d35-f2db-4ce3-a593-c1e6aadb6a15/Xib56usiqL7pQ2g6Zpb6m.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Prof.Ravikiran S Wali","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 21:37:42.413225+00', '2026-01-29 21:41:33.890798+00'), ('a016e0f9-413f-4cc3-ab8d-37b9dc61a724', '44ba49cf-0388-4b42-99bc