erpreviledged children","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-07-01","hoursSpent":50,"description":"It''s a marathon to help reduce weight and a fundraiser to help underprevilege children.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dMGCeZsCEx5r3ltv0zFNi","name":"Fist Full","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":32,"outcomes":"","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 06:52:16.537291+00', '2026-02-02 07:29:18.265921+00'), ('a01f75dc-c5ad-4992-a28b-59cb8e519c4e', '386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS067","name":"SOHAN RAJU M","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Pa01NnN4JhaDRiWUhHAr0","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":1,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/JTFFy0YHSjMJ-3pHPyH_-.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/3MIbzM0ZMJUNvjP61zvFl.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/6D7lVXIV4qEdBEMyn2O3a.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully raised awareness about environmental cleanliness and sustainable practices\\namong participants.\\n• Encouraged active student participation and fostered a sense of social responsibility.\\n• Strengthened teamwork, leadership, and coordination skills through group trekking activities.\\n• Promoted physical fitness, mental well-being, and stress relief among students.\\n• Enhanced the visibility and impact of the Rotaract Club’s community-oriented initiatives.\\n• Delivered a memorable and enriching outdoor experience, strengthening students’ connection\\nwith nature.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"FAST TREK 2.0 was a flagship trekking and social responsibility initiative organized by\\nthe Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th January 2024. The event combined adventure with\\nenvironmental consciousness through a cleanliness drive conducted during the trek. Participants\\nassembled early in the morning and traveled to the trekking site after being briefed on safety\\nprotocols and event guidelines. The trek through the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills provided\\nstudents with an opportunity to experience nature while actively contributing to its preservation.\\nThe event witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 750 students, creating a vibrant and\\nenergetic atmosphere while promoting teamwork, discipline, and environmental awareness.\\n","aicteMapping":"Environmental Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GFlrPYpKKjG5MK97yW4qu","name":"Kannada Sangha T Shirt","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/mmLHKLIvJdcGJGuQ3xD8i.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-09-04","duration":1,"outcomes":" Promoted environmental awareness and sustainable practices among students.\\n• Encouraged students to actively participate in tree plantation and conservation efforts.\\n• Fostered a sense of responsibility towards environmental protection.\\n• Increased student involvement in eco-friendly and socially responsible initiatives.\\n• Successfully distributed saplings with proper planting guidelines to participants.\\n• Strengthened the role of Kannada Sangha in organizing impactful community and\\nenvironmental activities.\\n• Fulfilled the criteria for awarding AICTE activity points to participating students.","semester":"7","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The “Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree” event was a community and environmental awareness\\ninitiative organized by Kannada Sangha on 07-07-2025 at R V College of Engineering. The\\ninitiative aimed to promote environmental responsibility among students by encouraging active\\nparticipation in tree plantation activities. As part of the event, every student who purchased a\\nT-shirt was provided with a tree sapling along with guidelines on how and where to plant it.\\nThe program was designed to inspire students to take personal responsibility for environmental\\nsustainability by planting and nurturing the saplings they received. The distribution of T-shirts\\nand saplings was carried out within the college campus, ensuring wide student participation and\\neffective execution of the initiative.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Environmental Awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"epvMCVR4-zTg4Iwp5BSDR","name":"T shirt For Smiles","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/QN6cNPfnLNa-CQEIsacSh.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-09-04","duration":1,"outcomes":" Brought happiness and emotional support to children residing in the orphanage.\\n• Encouraged students to actively participate in community service and social welfare\\nactivities.\\n• Strengthened values of empathy, compassion, and social responsibility among participants.\\n• Created awareness about the needs and challenges faced by underprivileged children.\\n• Fostered teamwork and a spirit of collective contribution among students.\\n• Successfully met the criteria for awarding AICTE activity points to participating students","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“T-Shirt for Smiles” and the Orphanage Visit was a community service initiative organized by\\nKannada Sangha on 07-07-2024. As part of this event, a group of students visited Prajakirana\\nSeva Charitable Trust Orphanage located in Kumbalagodu, Bengaluru. The primary objective of\\nthe visit was to support underprivileged children and bring joy to their lives through meaningful\\ninteraction. Students actively engaged with the children by participating in various activities\\nand contributing through donations and essential supplies. The initiative aimed to instill values\\nof compassion, empathy, and social responsibility among students while encouraging active\\ninvolvement in community service.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"n_OW7DI4JPnV7Ya_WGMhM","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2023","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/2hZ3C8NhtFInnBHSLuB_O.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/LwCpKU8-4Jc-7cj1Rb-uw.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully raised funds to support needy children and social welfare initiatives.\\n• Promoted awareness about child welfare and the importance of community contribution.\\n• Encouraged physical fitness and a healthy lifestyle among participants.\\n• Increased student and volunteer engagement in social service activities.\\n• Fostered a sense of empathy, responsibility, and collective effort among participants.\\n• Enhanced the visibility and impact of NSS RVCE’s flagship initiatives","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2023 was a flagship fundraising event organized by NSS RVCE with the\\ntheme “Help a child, change the world.” The marathon was conducted on 4th June 2023 and\\naimed to support needy children through funds raised from participant registrations. Participants\\nwere given the option to run either 5 km or 10 km, encouraging individuals of varying fitness\\nlevels to take part. The event combined physical fitness with social responsibility, motivating\\nstudents and volunteers to contribute their time and effort toward a noble cause. All participants\\nwere provided with Utsarga T-shirts, certificates of participation, medals of recognition, and\\nrefreshments, making the event both meaningful and well-organized.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"93NuxeeA40obnhdJOyrOs","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/vkwMicFQ9JFoybh78yZ3J.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully collected blood units to support hospitals and patients in need.\\n• Increased awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.\\n• Encouraged students to participate in life-saving humanitarian activities.\\n• Promoted a sense of social responsibility and empathy among participants.\\n• Strengthened collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Lions Club of Bangalore\\nSouth.\\n• Recognized and motivated donors through certificates, appreciation badges, and AICTE\\nactivity points.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with\\nthe Lions Club of Bangalore South on 6th June 2023 at the RVCE campus. The event aimed to\\npromote voluntary blood donation and create awareness about the importance of blood donation\\nin saving lives. Students, staff, and volunteers actively participated in the camp, contributing\\nto this humanitarian cause. Proper medical supervision and post-donation care were ensured,\\nwith refreshments provided to all donors. Participants were also recognized with certificates of\\nparticipation and appreciation badges, and AICTE activity points were awarded as a mark of\\nrespect for their selfless contribution.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Upfkztc2iBevS_86mfsEr","name":"Blood Donation Camp ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/PqqweTa9XxNejf8dww-6R.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully collected blood units to support hospitals and patients in need.\\n• Increased awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.\\n• Encouraged students to participate in life-saving humanitarian activities.\\n• Recognized and motivated donors through certificates, appreciation badges, and AICTE\\nactivity points.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with\\nthe Lions Club of Bangalore South on 28th June 2024 at the RVCE campus. The event aimed to\\npromote voluntary blood donation and create awareness about the importance of blood donation\\nin saving lives. Students, staff, and volunteers actively participated in the camp, contributing\\nto this humanitarian cause. Proper medical supervision and post-donation care were ensured,\\nwith refreshments provided to all donors. Participants were also recognized with certificates of\\nparticipation and appreciation badges, and AICTE activity points were awarded as a mark of\\nrespect for their selfless contribution.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"62u8hPVx7DUdDSc9fXHXQ","name":"Blood Donation Camp ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/g_zt12VtkwjwsgaSsvN7u.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"• The Rotaract RVCE Blood Donation Camp successfully bridged the gap between medical demand and voluntary supply \\n• It  Helps in collecting significant units to support local blood   banks .\\n• While instilling a deep sense of social accountability\\nand compassion in the student community.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with\\nthe Lions Club of Bangalore South on 30th October 2025 at the RVCE campus. The event aimed to\\npromote voluntary blood donation and create awareness about the importance of blood donation\\nin saving lives. Students, staff, and volunteers actively participated in the camp, contributing\\nto this humanitarian cause. Proper medical supervision and post-donation care were ensured,\\nwith refreshments provided to all donors. Participants were also recognized with certificates of\\nparticipation and appreciation badges, and AICTE activity points were awarded as a mark of\\nrespect for their selfless contribution.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BMIkO9A8b0nHWKrBODqVY","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/1ZhER1vMFZfSr49YphpT6.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully raised funds to support needy children and social welfare initiatives.\\n• Promoted awareness about child welfare and the importance of community contribution.\\n• Encouraged physical fitness and a healthy lifestyle among participants.\\n• Successfully combined fitness, charity, and community .\\n• It helps in  advancing educational opportunities for needy children and fostering a sense of social commitment among participants.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, was a significant event that celebrated health, fitness, and charity. Scheduled to take place on April 6, 2025, at RV College of Engineering, this marathon aimed to bring the community together to run for a cause that extends beyond physical activity to making a lasting social impact. The event''s motto, \"Help a Child, Change the World,\" emphasized the marathon’s mission to support educational initiatives for underprivileged children and transform their futures. Participants could choose between 5 km and 10 km race categories, with donations contributing directly to providing education for children in need. Beyond the physical challenge, the marathon represented a collective commitment to social responsibility and charity-driven action, motivating involvement through both fitness and service.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Mge5PqmgmdJEzk8RDb_Ac","name":"Fist Full","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/aNe361fvUDqQNlyTje3xo.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/5_vWOBNLGyWvrlDKqZX4b.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Collected essential food grains to support individuals and families in need.\\n• Promoted the value of kindness, sharing, and social responsibility among students.\\n• Encouraged sustained participation through simple and practical contribution methods.\\n• Increased student involvement in community service initiatives.\\n• Created awareness about food insecurity and the importance of collective effort.\\n• Successfully motivated participants through the provision of 10 AICTE activity points.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"It was a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to support\\nunderprivileged communities through food grain collection. The event encouraged participants\\nto set aside a fistful of rice or toor dal from every meal prepared between 15th November and\\n29th November, promoting a habit of mindful giving. Students contributed by donating either 5\\nkg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, making a meaningful impact through small but consistent efforts.\\nThe initiative aimed to foster compassion, social responsibility, and community involvement\\namong students while addressing food security needs in a simple yet effective manner.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_slsPmivnkEf_3R-jWr_U","name":"Fist Full.","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE CAMPUS","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/386eb3f8-81ea-4041-90c4-aceeb2431440/7FKX3bryRjZjysp9I19yK.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully collected essential food grains from student contributors.\\n• Encouraged active student participation in social welfare activities.\\n• Promoted values of compassion, sharing, and social responsibility.\\n• Created awareness about food security and community support.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fist Full was a flagship social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with\\nthe objective of supporting food security and encouraging community participation. The event\\nwas scheduled to commence on 1st November 2025, with the donation collection phase running\\nfrom 17th November 2025. As part of the initiative, students voluntarily contributed either\\n5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. The event aimed to promote empathy, social responsibility,\\nand collective contribution among students while addressing the needs of underprivileged\\ncommunities. Proper coordination and planning ensured smooth execution of the donation drive\\nwithin the campus","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 03:02:31.999949+00', '2026-01-30 03:02:33.06013+00'), ('a05f11bf-214c-49af-abef-dc8eaf3e6889', '106e1eba-63fc-4fd9-9bd7-dd406d8aaad1', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23CS411","name":"Nanthan S Shetty","period":"2023-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"VLlzpI4V6g8_FhM339_9p","name":"Green Sunday (Plantation Drive)","slNo":1,"place":"Bengaluru University Bio-Park Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-26","hoursSpent":6,"description":"","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"01-02","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Re3B5j94HbUf380ib_Ykf","name":"Vikasit Bha