 Awareness","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":4,"description":"","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iAsBD14_kDwHyPmHBktAR","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"23fiPouXQn3kpSR2sShrd","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"abVGaLlWbrFjUlo_4Z_Eh","name":"Nasha Mukta bharatha","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AP0eVCBq9iAuAazg_enpF","name":"FistFull ","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-27","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Jyoti Shetty","designation":"Associate, Professor Department of Computer Science Engineering"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr. Uma B V","designation":"Professor, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering"},"evaluator2":{"name":"Dr. Raviraj Kusanur","designation":"Professor, Department of Chemistry"}}}', '2026-01-30 03:14:08.601205+00', '2026-01-30 06:05:45.540673+00'), ('a0769eb7-d131-452b-95cc-7b98b65cb8f3', '8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI010","name":"Bhavik Bafna","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"RWmluEJkA8kk9030k4kAm","name":"INNOVATEX  x  E-SUMMIT","slNo":1,"place":"EC Seminar Hall, RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/5CpQAOPCNOOndPgdFwxTO.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-10","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event enhanced participants’ problem-solving abilities, creativity, and presentation skills. Students gained exposure to entrepreneurship, idea validation, and pitching techniques, while organisers developed leadership and coordination skills","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-09","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Innovatex, organized by E-Cell, was a two-round competition designed to promote innovation and entrepreneurial thinking among participants. The first round was an elimination round where teams were challenged to integrate three randomly assigned themes into their business ideas, testing their creativity, adaptability, and quick thinking. Based on their performance, the most innovative teams were shortlisted for the next stage.\\nIn the pitching round, selected teams presented their business ideas to the judges, Anshav Jain and Bhaskar M G. This round enabled participants to articulate the value of their innovations and receive constructive feedback from experienced professionals. The event provided a valuable platform for students to refine entrepreneurial skills and gain real-world exposure.\\n","aicteMapping":"Entrepreneurship/Innovation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/Fi16QLwzOjsOFa51cKKcC.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KU8-ELrJxpXqYslnF1ZRF","name":"BUSINESS MARATHON x E-SUMMIT","slNo":2,"place":"EC Seminar Hall, RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/NFu4YNNABXlqLj_hCpa5P.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-10","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants enhanced their problem-solving, critical thinking, collaboration, and pitching skills while gaining hands-on exposure to startup ideation, business model development, and structured entrepreneurial processes.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-09","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Business Marathon (BM), organised by the Entrepreneurship Cell, was an intensive overnight event designed to foster innovation, teamwork, and entrepreneurial thinking among participants. Teams progressed through structured phases such as Empathy Mapping, SWOT Analysis, and Lean Canvas to develop viable solutions to a given business problem, concluding with a final pitch presentation.\\nThe activity was aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, particularly Goal 8 (Decent Work and Economic Growth) and Goal 9 (Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure), encouraging participants to apply theoretical knowledge to real-world entrepreneurial challenges.","aicteMapping":"Entrepreneurship / Skill Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/o8a18YN28GfDjtabCKQh7.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"626yhu1xtQpRcy6zydWe4","name":"MERGERSAND ACQUISITIONS\\tx E-SUMMIT","slNo":3,"place":"Civil Seminar Hall,RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/RB0TNCKfI0p_VdWO-q51k.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-11","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants enhanced their understanding of corporate strategy, financial analysis, valuation concepts, and decision-making processes involved in mergers and acquisitions, gaining exposure to real-world business scenarios","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-10","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Mergers and Acquisitions event organized by the Entrepreneurship Cell provided participants with practical exposure to corporate transactions, focusing on mergers, acquisitions, and strategic alliances. Through expert talks, interactive discussions, and detailed case studies, students gained insights into the strategic, financial, and operational aspects of mergers and acquisitions. The activity was aligned with Sustainable Development Goal 8 (Decent Work and Economic Growth), enabling participants to understand how corporate restructuring and strategic decisions contribute to economic development and organizational growth.","aicteMapping":"Financial Literacy / Entrepreneurship","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/NMS-DJCellctFumhwmiBd.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fCSGXTVGWODEtnQ_LFgHF","name":"SPEAKER SESSIONS x E-SUMMIT","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/BQShsgmwYrIuApQOpxNeG.jpg"],"endDate":"0204-02-09","duration":-664953,"outcomes":"Participants gained valuable insights, motivation, and clarity on career paths in entrepreneurship and creative domains. The sessions enhanced students’ confidence, broadened their perspectives, and positively influenced their learning outlook","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-09-08","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Speaker Sessions at the E-Summit featured renowned personalities such as Paritosh Anand, Arsh Goyal, Ishan Sharma, Arvind Prakash, and San Kalra, who shared their experiences and insights on content creation, storytelling, motivation, and entrepreneurship. Through engaging and impactful talks, the speakers inspired students by providing practical knowledge and real-world perspectives, encouraging creativity, self-growth, and entrepreneurial thinking.","aicteMapping":"Leadership / Motivation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/kllVKJa9d3Q53gjt1wsyD.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CbB6lVyMUUDZtRzM4AhR0","name":"INTEL HACKATHON x E-SUMMIT","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/RRj0XEVULIgmu9o3IcEFc.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-09","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants gained practical exposure to AI tools and concepts, enhanced their technical and problem-solving skills, and developed a deeper understanding of innovation-driven technologies essential for future careers.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-08","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Intel Hackathon, organized by E-Cell, was a pioneering workshop focused on artificial intelligence, emphasizing open innovation and exploration. Participants ranging from beginners to AI enthusiasts engaged in coding challenges, hands-on activities, and collaborative learning sessions. The hackathon introduced participants to emerging AI trends, practical applications, and real-world problem-solving using technology. Aligned with Sustainable Development Goal 9 (Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure) and Sustainable Development Goal 4 (Quality Education), the event highlighted E-Cell’s commitment to fostering technological learning and innovation","aicteMapping":"Innovation / Technical Skill","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/N1hbvoT3qdiJ9GdjB2TKY.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LQqQrm8ocUUmatyBT6Q9M","name":"PANEL\\tDISCUSSIONS x E-SUMMIT","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/13bAJHHAFjQE2OJKAhGdI.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-09","duration":2,"outcomes":"Attendees gained a comprehensive understanding of future tech trends, entrepreneurial opportunities, and challenges, fostering critical thinking and strategic awareness in the digital age.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-08","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The E-Summit 2024 hosted a thought-provoking panel discussion titled “Navigating the Future: Tech Trends and Entrepreneurial Opportunities.” Industry leaders, innovators, and experts discussed emerging technologies, entrepreneurial challenges, ethical considerations, and future opportunities. The discussion provided a holistic view of the intersection between technology and entrepreneurship, offering valuable insights into innovation-driven decision-making and leadership.","aicteMapping":"Leadership / Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/zgp9LAQNTgn3MqP4dhpop.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5DtwYQfFpGOIPf9F_A_hv","name":"NSS Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"From a participant’s perspective, the NSS Utsarga Marathon was an inspiring and memorable experience that contributed to both physical fitness and personal growth. Participating in the marathon helped students develop stamina, endurance, and discipline, while also reinforcing the importance of maintaining a healthy and active lifestyle. The event also created a strong sense of motivation and enthusiasm, as students ran together with a shared purpose and collective energy. It encouraged teamwork, boosted confidence, and provided a refreshing break from academic routines. Additionally, being part of an NSS-driven activity helped participants feel more connected to social initiatives and understand the importance of taking part in events that contribute to community spirit and awareness.\\nOverall, the marathon was not just a fitness event, but also a meaningful initiative that promoted unity, responsibility, and a sense of achievement among the participants.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon was a vibrant and impactful event organized with the aim of promoting fitness, discipline, and social awareness among students. The marathon served as a platform to encourage participants to step out of their routine and take part in an activity that supports both physical well-being and a positive social message. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students and volunteers, creating an energetic atmosphere throughout. Proper coordination was ensured through volunteer support, route planning, and overall event management, which helped in smooth execution and participant safety. The marathon not only encouraged students to adopt a more active lifestyle but also strengthened the values of community participation, unity, and responsibility, which lie at the core of NSS initiatives. Overall, the NSS Utsarga Marathon successfully combined fitness and social purpose, making it a meaningful event that left a positive impression on all participants.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/9QacWuwEMIhswF-FUwwOm.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GRQfIgUOK6mdZ2r3s0fVh","name":"STARTUP SAGA x EMBARK","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/Q65GJUVum4-CU-zBQ4fsX.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-07-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants developed leadership, creativity, and problemsolving skills while gaining real-world exposure to startup ecosystems and social entrepreneurship","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-11","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Startup Saga, part of the Two-Day Innovation Odyssey under EMBARK, focused on nurturing entrepreneurial thinking with the theme “Support Sphere: Social Entrepreneurship Saga.” The event provided a platform for students to showcase innovative and socially impactful startup ideas. Participants engaged in workshops, panel discussions, mentorship sessions, and pitch presentations, gaining guidance on branding, funding, scaling, and launching startups.","aicteMapping":"Social Entrepreneurship","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/8gyL6PyywuHslvTTw73y6.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"f4vtaLKdiOiycOiOjxupX","name":"VISION VENTURE x EMBARK","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/9WyFGJR_7M7a26QFgwfYO.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-07-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants enhanced their product development, innovation, and sustainability-focused thinking, gaining hands-on experience in creating real-world solutions.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-11","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Vision Venture, conducted under EMBARK, was a product development challenge themed “Eco Innovate.” It encouraged participants to create sustainable solutions for techno-social challenges. Teams progressed through ideation, prototyping, and testing phases with expert guidance, focusing on user-centered and market-ready solutions. The event empowered participants to transform ideas into tangible innovations.","aicteMapping":"Innovation / Sustainability","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/A8LAVjCxhe5G7x9lWh1lQ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3Igj7eIwLbCAdFmKaPg8v","name":"WORLD\\tENTREPRENEURSHIP DAY","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/h_OEnk-SzCOIEv_joP7uf.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-08-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"Students gained practical entrepreneurial knowledge, inspiration, and motivation, reinforcing the importance of resilience, leadership, and innovation.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-21","hoursSpent":40,"description":"World Entrepreneurship Day was celebrated with enthusiasm at RVCE by E-Cell. The event featured a panel discussion with Arvind Prakash Singh, Founder and CEO of SuperBolt, and Shreesha Sridhar, Chairperson of ProjectX Labs. The speakers shared real-world experiences, startup challenges, opportunities, and insights into building resilient and innovative ventures.","aicteMapping":"Entrepreneurship Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/r9F4LIdzPxSNXLA-YEUW1.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5_STEV9f8cFLf5mhM4fQm","name":"IVS Group Vsit","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/JTZkTlU9vt2sWXSFt_Nyk.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants gained international exposure, insights into global startup ecosystems, and networking opportunities with investors and entrepreneurs.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-06","hoursSpent":28,"description":"The IVS Group Visit was a collaborative event involving RVCE, Campus Fund, and the IVS Group from Japan. The session included keynote addresses, presentations on Indo-Japanese startup ecosystems, a fireside chat, and startup pitch sessions by Indian and RVCE startups. The event concluded with a networking dinner promoting global collaboration.","aicteMapping":"Industry Interaction","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/OWeW23PLA3RyCok9wc2Ee.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nF7kynDk1yHX7t_dZc2kR","name":"Rotaract Blood Donation Camp ","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/revjXfppjdjDvKARv2cpN.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/clcBc_I9YnU_L-TcN5Xji.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"From a participant’s perspective, the Rotaract Blood Donation Camp was a highly meaningful\\nand fulfilling experience. Donating blood created a sense of pride and satisfaction, as\\nparticipants felt they were directly contributing towards a cause that saves lives. The event also\\nhelped students understand the importance of regular blood donation and the critical role it\\nplays\\nin supporting patients during surgeries, accidents, and medical emergencies.\\nFor many, the camp served as an opportunity to overcome hesitation or fear related to\\nblood donation, especially for first-time donors. The professional guidance and support\\nfrom volunteers and medical staff made the process comfortable and reassuring. Participants\\nalso became more informed about health screening, eligibility criteria, and post-donation\\nprecautions, adding to their awareness and confidence.\\nOverall, the camp strengthened empathy, promoted community service, and encouraged\\nparticipants to continue supporting humanitarian initiatives in the future.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Rotaract Blood Donation Camp was a socially impactful event organized with the\\nobjective\\nof promoting the importance of voluntary blood donation and encouraging students to\\ncontribute\\ntowards saving lives. The camp served as a platform to spread awareness about the continuous\\nneed for blood in hospitals and emergency situations, and highlighted how a single donation\\ncan make a significant difference.\\nThe event was conducted in a well-organized and hygienic manner with the support of\\ntrained medical professionals. Proper arrangements were made for registration, screening,\\ndonor\\nassistance, and post-donation care, ensuring a safe and smooth experience for all participants.\\nVolunteers played an active role in managing crowd flow, assisting donors, and maintaining\\ndiscipline throughout the camp.\\nOverall, the Rotaract Blood Donation Camp successfully created awareness, motivated\\nfirst-time donors, and encouraged a spirit of social responsibility among students through\\nmeaningful community service.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/bNSy6JkZb2-l0MvbdxZKK.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dXo6ex0i9bb9YANNCPffg","name":"WORKSHOP ON  AI AGENTS / AGENTIC AI","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/NV37xz7JP924n7Qknm6yV.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-01-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants gained hands-on AI exposure, understood agentbased systems, and learned how AI can revolutionize startups and product development.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-03","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The workshop introduced participants to autonomous AI agents capable of executing complex workflows. Students explored browser automation, voice AI models, MCP, workflow automation tools such as N8N, and real-time application development platforms. The session highlighted the entrepreneurial potential of AI agents in automating business processes.","aicteMapping":"Emerging Technology / Skill","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/0z5rRy2DfwiubNeVK8xxi.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"26-27","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AxWtRGYcMVCclD1Jp4c6k","name":"CORPORATE PARTNERSHIP WORKSHOP","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/TTp9deJ4WgxrltWuyxdZE.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-01-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants became confident in approaching sponsors, developing proposals, and securing partnerships essential for successful event execution.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-04","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The workshop on securing event sponsorships trained participants in identifying sponsors, crafting persuasive proposals, negotiating deals, and building long-term partnerships. It provided practical insights into corporate collaboration and event funding strategies.","aicteMapping":"Management / Leadership","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/TNFMxJGg9mzodR74IGBUE.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"28-29","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iMd85FITC2Aua5swXoyZi","name":"EXUBERANCE","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/VAo2TIo5pxi_4qToeghqG.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-01-18","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants enhanced strategic thinking, negotiation, teamwork, adaptability, and public speaking skills while gaining real-world business exposure.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Exuberance, themed “Chaos to Creation,” was a high-intensity business simulation event. Participants engaged in strategic bidding, negotiation, pitching, and business model creation under pressure, simulating real-world market dynamics","aicteMapping":"Business Simulation / Strategy","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/u15XBmlMy3HYPFuc_wLBD.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"30-31","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WCkaBIwbQjU7d5Tqwu473","name":"HULT PRIZE","slNo":16,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/Glgvz-mhg2JTrjxZjZHKG.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-01-18","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants strengthened innovation, pitching, and problemsolving skills, while winners received funding and mentorship to pursue real-world implementation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Hult Prize event provided a platform for teams to pitch sustainable and socially impactful business ideas. Judges evaluated feasibility, impact, and scalability, offering feedback, mentorship, and cash prizes to winning teams.","aicteMapping":"Social Innovation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/cqaN7VGciTIIthMIZ_Nm5.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"32-33","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rCJpBht_tPckAZhVeWYb_","name":"GROWW X E-CELL MASTERCLASS","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/bA0ni4djIsQpoSrnZ3Nbc.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants developed strong financial literacy, gained confidence in analyzing stocks and markets, and learned structured approaches to responsible investing and wealth creation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-04","hoursSpent":28,"description":"The Groww x E-Cell Stock Investing Masterclass was an interactive financial literacy initiative conducted in collaboration with Groww and IIIT Bangalore. The session aimed to empower students with practical knowledge of investing and long-term wealth creation. Participants were introduced to core concepts of stocks and mutual funds, along with structured methods to analyse company performance using tools such as the Piotroski Score and Graham Number.\\nThe workshop guided students in understanding macroeconomic trends, evaluating sectors, and making informed investment decisions. Expert-led discussions, real-world market insights, and hands-on exercises helped simplify complex financial concepts for beginners and aspiring investors. The session also offered exclusive goodies, certificates of participation, and priority access to future financial workshops, making it a holistic learning and engagement experience.\\n","aicteMapping":"Financial Literacy","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8c0d3228-7cad-4685-af65-fff012a22ca5/UIL0mTwk1v52DYSFcaB-i.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"34-35","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 03:49:09.798286+00', '2026-01-31 05:36:45.735337+00'), ('a0a63cfc-ac85-43e1-b0d0-6a5ecb6a28f5', '7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS228","name":"Vasanth K","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"UVXyzMneJwaJNggHFqlCz","name":"Hack4Soc","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/LFukYirZOhOJ7yAaB-lLB.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":2,"outcomes":"Gained hands-on experience in event coordination and volunteer management\\n\\nImproved teamwork, communication, and leadership skills\\n\\nDeveloped exposure to hackathon workflows, innovation culture, and problem-solving approaches\\n\\nLearned to handle real-time operational challenges in a technical event\\n\\nContributed to promoting technology-driven solutions for societal issues.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-03","hoursSpent":24,"description":"HACK4SOC 2.0 was a 24-hour national-level hackathon focused on leveraging technology for social impact. Organized by the IEEE RVCE Student Branch, the event challenged participants to develop innovative solutions across three key technical verticals: Generative AI, Fintech, and Blockchain.","aicteMapping":"Volunteer Work / Community & Social Development Activities","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/BPIc4Y5ofoFjg-P_VCHIm.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"P_59Oew94uv0174nM9j0l","name":"FistFull","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/NCj6DCQwA1K817AOxO8Ko.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"Developed a strong sense of social responsibility and community engagement\\n\\nImproved teamwork and coordination skills through group activities\\n\\nGained awareness of social issues related to food security and welfare\\n\\nEnhanced empathy, leadership, and interpersonal skills\\n\\nUnderstood the importance of student participation in social impact initiatives","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":336,"description":"FISTFULL is a community-oriented social initiative focused on addressing food-related issues and promoting social responsibility among students. As a participant, I actively contributed to the program by supporting its activities, collaborating with team members, and engaging in efforts aimed at helping the underprivileged and spreading awareness about social welfare and community service.","aicteMapping":"Community & Social Development / Volunteer Work","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/IQxJ5O8TzOkP_MBOz1BZ3.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rr2lPqUFbnkXkGcSgTCe8","name":"Fast-Trek","slNo":3,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/bD40ruh6tpnGqvl0S1dou.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/otvP5ZFZejrtS6dQCBJ0A.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improved physical fitness, stamina, and endurance\\n\\nDeveloped mental resilience and stress management skills\\n\\nEnhanced teamwork, coordination, and peer support\\n\\nGained awareness of the importance of health, fitness, and outdoor activities\\n\\nBuilt discipline, self-confidence, and perseverance","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Fast-Trek 2023 was a fitness and endurance-oriented trekking event aimed at promoting physical well-being, teamwork, and resilience among students. As a participant, I successfully completed the trek by actively engaging in the activity, following safety guidelines, and collaborating with fellow participants throughout the event.","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/4ggX5y2vpimUcG4BaRkU8.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"SxuLMw3_ODkZp5hyJxvpz","name":"QUIEEEZ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/z_M1IAclRiiYhlN8x3wrQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-07-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced general knowledge and subject awareness\\n\\nImproved logical thinking and analytical skills\\n\\nDeveloped quick decision-making and time management\\n\\nStrengthened teamwork and communication skills\\n\\nGained experience in healthy academic competition","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-07-09","hoursSpent":1,"description":"QUIZEEZ is a competitive quiz-based event designed to test participants’ knowledge, logical reasoning, and quick decision-making skills across various domains. As a participant, I actively took part in the quiz, demonstrating analytical thinking, teamwork, and subject knowledge in a competitive environment.","aicteMapping":"Technical & Non-Technical Competition","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"E1zKThqUxmIqEZN9apM__","name":"TechForTomorrow","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/awI4Xls_w-drETfCOzaGC.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Gained exposure to innovation-oriented problem solving\\n\\nApplied technical and analytical skills to real-world challenges\\n\\nEnhanced teamwork, communication, and presentation abilities\\n\\nDeveloped awareness of technology for social good\\n\\nImproved creative thinking and solution design skills","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-16","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Tech For Tomorrow is a technology-driven initiative focused on developing innovative solutions to address real-world and societal challenges. As a participant, I actively contributed by applying technical knowledge, problem-solving skills, and teamwork to propose or develop solutions aimed at creating a positive social impact.","aicteMapping":"Social Impact Activities","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/jmE7l1sn5r1KgV7bNULjR.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mPvj4mKmcseB6T0B6WvcA","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/C0I-AVmo1JQHBzb0EZMc6.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced creativity and innovative thinking\\n\\nImproved teamwork and collaborative skills\\n\\nGained experience in participating in large-scale campus events\\n\\nDeveloped communication and interpersonal skills\\n\\nEncouraged active involvement in cultural and extracurricular activities","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-28","hoursSpent":3,"description":"UPTOWN JUNK’24 was a student-centric creative and cultural event aimed at promoting innovation, creativity, and active participation in campus life. As a participant, I actively took part in the event, collaborating with peers and engaging in activities that encouraged creative expression, teamwork, and student engagement.","aicteMapping":"Extra-Curricular Activities","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"H3dmuam1VaSsI18W3eKxd","name":"UTPT Indie Genius","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/0KleEykx6tiMGX5VjCf6O.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"Gained exposure to national-level activities and participation\\n\\nImproved confidence and engagement beyond classroom learning\\n\\nDeveloped awareness of larger academic/social initiatives\\n\\nEnhanced self-motivation and participation skills\\n\\nEncouraged involvement in co-curricular and extra-curricular activities","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"This activity involved participation in a national-level event/initiative conducted at the India level, aimed at encouraging student involvement beyond academics. As a participant, I actively engaged in the program, demonstrating interest in learning, awareness, and broader academic or social engagement at a national platform.","aicteMapping":"Extra-Curricular Activities / National-Level Participation","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Dvsw3CKvcVnjB8-3Mwmf0","name":"Gen AI Hackathon","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/-JPBnAv7gGJZeTwaFuTvX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"Time constrained development.\\nGenerative AI knowledge.\\nTeam Work","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":0,"description":"This is the hackathon conducted by ACM based on Generative AI.","aicteMapping":"Technical Activity","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c0ee00b-3691-4dce-8796-773317b084ea/bCDeUhYFtqaiQkwVUV0De.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Shanta Rangaswamy","designation":"Professor and Head at the Department of CSE, RVCE"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr. Uma B V","designation":"The Dean, Student Affairs"},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 03:16:03.911757+00', '2026-01-31 15:20:03.080004+00'), ('a0d0fcd5-9d58-4526-a379-8e00c6cb2dba', '3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY008","name":"Aishwarya Gite","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"5eqrs90PSyHWwtHkZqN68","name":"Fast Trek","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/y5uJZDHmai6b2UrGwqC1i.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/tP0vjNJcU0qwUcv_6czoT.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Development of social responsibility and empathy\\nBeing part of a project aimed at providing financial aid to underprivileged children with heart diseases helped me understand the importance of giving back to society.\\n2.Understanding the power of collective action for social causes\\nThe event demonstrated how individuals coming together for a shared purpose can create meaningful change.\\n3.Enhanced awareness about healthcare inequalities\\nThe project helped me recognize the disparities in access to healthcare faced by underprivileged children.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The social cause behind the activity was to provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the participants boarded the bus to the trek location with great enthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with basic information of the event. The trek was a great  as all had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of Huthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very memorable journey.","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/v1tceDnrLWQi7-YkBDp9I.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nD22p3WUDjiDxmS5RAdc7","name":"Akshara","slNo":2,"place":"Kengeri and RR Nagar","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/r_rvh5_QEbqR7N-L9x5kt.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/1iuV-KcbjmVdVrajbhqh8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-10","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Improved access to quality education for underprivileged students\\nThe skill development sessions helped bridge the gap in educational resources for students from financially modest backgrounds.\\n2.Enhanced learning confidence among school students\\nThrough interactive teaching methods and personalized attention, students were encouraged to ask questions and clarify doubts.\\n3.Development of teaching and communication skills among volunteers\\nVolunteers gained first-hand experience by stepping into the role of teachers for a day.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-10","hoursSpent":8,"description":"With the zeal to give back to society and share the kind of learning experiences we ourselves always wished for as students, we volunteered to conduct skill development sessions in seven schools located in RR Nagar and Kengeri, Bangalore. The sessions were conducted for underprivileged students from financially modest backgrounds who are in need of access to quality education.\\nAs volunteers, we had the enriching experience of stepping into the role of teachers for a day, which gave us a deeper appreciation of the efforts involved in teaching. Through these sessions, we helped students better understand concepts relevant to their respective classes and standards, while also creating an interactive and supportive learning environment","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/6kfj45Ay9eKV64tsQ04ls.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_Z9JyDcjjHYmAjjudbymP","name":"Har Ghar Dhyan","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Improved awareness about mental health and mindfulness\\nThe session helped us understand the importance of mental well-being alongside physical health.\\n2.Enhanced ability to concentrate and manage stress\\nBy practicing guided meditation and concentration techniques, we realized the effectiveness of mindfulness in improving focus and managing academic and personal stress.\\n3.Development of a disciplined and calm mindset\\nThe activity emphasized the value of self-discipline, patience, and consistency.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-20","hoursSpent":5,"description":"With the intention of promoting mental well-being and self-awareness among students, we volunteered in the Har Ghar Dhyan activity, where an experienced coach conducted an interactive session on concentration, meditation, and yoga. The session focused on helping students understand the importance of mental calmness, self-discipline, and inner balance in their daily lives. Through guided meditation and simple yoga practices, the coach explained how regular practice can improve focus, reduce stress, and enhance overall mental health. As volunteers, we actively participated in the session and supported students in following the techniques taught, making the experience both informative and refreshing.","aicteMapping":"Health, wellness and well being","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/UNvOOdHjTBfAqGmbLp4tB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DwnrWCpYM773-tOab_wtk","name":"IEEE Ideathon - Empowering her bright future","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/yN08Q-dq4LoMPWu1kYsSi.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Enhanced understanding of women-centric social and technological challenges\\nThe ideathon helped us gain deeper insights into the social, economic, and technological challenges faced by women.\\n2.Development of innovative and problem-solving skills\\nParticipating in the ideathon strengthened our ability to analyze problems, brainstorm creative ideas, and design feasible solutions within a limited timeframe.\\n3.Boost in confidence and leadership abilities\\nPresenting ideas and collaborating with peers and mentors helped build confidence in expressing thoughts and taking initiative.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-17","hoursSpent":7,"description":"With the objective of promoting innovation, leadership, and confidence among women, we participated in the IEEE Ideathon – Empowering Her Bright Future. The ideathon provided a platform to identify real-world challenges faced by women and propose innovative, technology-driven solutions to address them. Through brainstorming sessions, mentoring, and idea presentations, the event encouraged critical thinking, creativity, and collaboration. As participants, we gained exposure to problem-solving approaches while contributing ideas focused on women empowerment, education, safety, health, and economic independence.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/XYVuoUWWB6znUImv8MxN8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BBPnjIimrod76PK3pfkv8","name":"SPARK –  Through the Eyes of Youth","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"1.Increased awareness about Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\\nThe competition effectively promoted awareness and understanding of the SDGs among students by encouraging them to interpret global issues through photography.\\n2.Development of leadership and event management skills\\nBeing involved in organizing the event enhanced our skills in planning, coordination, time management, and teamwork. Managing large-scale participation and multiple operational tasks strengthened our leadership and organizational abilities.\\n3.Enhanced sense of social responsibility\\nWorking on an SDG-focused initiative deepened our sense of responsibility toward societal and global challenges. It reinforced the importance of contributing to sustainable development through creative and educational platforms.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":25,"description":"SPARK – Eyes of Youth was an SDG-based photo competition aimed at creating awareness about the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) among students. The activity encouraged participants to observe social, environmental, and economic issues around them and represent these challenges through photography and meaningful visual narratives. By using creativity as a medium, the competition sought to inspire young minds to think critically about sustainability, social responsibility, and global development, while promoting ethical and original digital content creation.","aicteMapping":"Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) / Social Awareness","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/n8ISGtWljoKi0RcYOtTSq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0M2B6JwoSWCYD9EbkQNHP","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Improved awareness about India’s development vision\\nThe quiz helped participants gain a clearer understanding of India’s long-term development goals, including economic growth, infrastructure development, digital transformation, and social inclusion.\\n2.Enhanced knowledge of government initiatives and policies\\nParticipants became more informed about various national programs, reforms, and schemes that contribute to the vision of a developed India, strengthening their awareness as responsible citizens.\\n3.Encouragement of civic responsibility and national consciousness The activity fostered a sense of pride and responsibility toward the nation by motivating students to actively engage with topics related to governance, sustainability, and innovation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-01","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz was an awareness-based activity aimed at enhancing students’ understanding of India’s vision for development, governance, innovation, and nation-building. The quiz focused on themes such as Viksit Bharat 2047, government initiatives, technological advancement, economic growth, sustainability, and social progress. Through an interactive and knowledge-driven format, the activity encouraged students to stay informed about national policies and their role in contributing to India’s journey toward becoming a developed nation.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/WqvGyqf9olI-jsYy1FJ2a.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7R6XgBQ4ITag1hT_0Rmqj","name":"Induction Program and Recruitment","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Enhanced sense of belonging among incoming students\\nThe induction programme helped freshers feel welcomed and supported, reducing anxiety and encouraging a positive connection with the academic community from the beginning of their journey.\\n2.Improved awareness of academic and institutional resources\\nStudents gained clarity about academic structures, campus facilities, and support systems, enabling them to adapt more confidently to university life.\\n3.Development of leadership and mentoring skills\\nStudent involvement in the induction programme strengthened leadership, communication, and mentoring abilities by engaging in peer guidance and support.\\n4.Promotion of inclusivity and community building\\nThe activity encouraged interaction among students from diverse backgrounds, fostering inclusivity, cooperation, and mutual respect within the institution.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-10-01","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Participation in the Induction Programme for freshers was an activity aimed at welcoming newly admitted students and supporting their smooth transition into the academic environment. The programme focused on familiarizing freshers with the institutional culture, academic expectations, available resources, and student support systems. By fostering interaction and guidance, the activity promoted a sense of belonging, inclusivity, and community within the institution.","aicteMapping":"Student Development / Mentoring and Induction Activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/GVMdvLpNCoVSVpOzqF2nv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ERn5e-INl1heqnc569A5R","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":8,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/g_QWQ9wlEk5Zhx64aw_oy.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/-pxmTo0z4NOgQNHAVCOXi.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Enhanced environmental awareness and responsibility\\nThe activity helped participants understand the importance of cleanliness and environmental conservation, especially in natural and ecologically sensitive areas. It encouraged responsible behavior toward nature and reinforced the need for sustainable practices.\\n2.Promotion of civic sense and community responsibility\\nBy participating in a cleanliness-driven initiative, students developed a stronger sense of civic duty and accountability toward maintaining public and natural spaces.\\n3.Encouragement of physical well-being and active lifestyle\\nThe trek motivated participants to engage in physical activity, highlighting the importance of fitness and outdoor engagement as part of a healthy lifestyle.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Fast-Trek was an activity with an objective of promoting environmental responsibility and sustainable practices among students. The activity combined physical fitness and nature engagement with a cleanliness drive, emphasizing the importance of preserving natural ecosystems and maintaining ecological balance. It aimed to sensitize participants toward environmental conservation while encouraging active participation, teamwork, and responsible citizenship through experiential learning.","aicteMapping":"Environment and Sustainability / Cleanliness Drive","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/iy2f-pZkQ5-ER6qETZo1d.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XF3eGWSpVGPmkiRCvUHTU","name":"Fist Full","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Enhanced awareness about hunger and food insecurity\\nThe initiative helped participants understand the seriousness of hunger-related issues and the importance of ensuring food availability for underprivileged communities.\\n2.Development of empathy and social responsibility\\nContributing to the drive encouraged students to reflect on social inequalities and develop compassion toward individuals facing food scarcity.\\n3.Promotion of collective action for social good\\nThe activity demonstrated how small contributions, when combined, can lead to large-scale positive change, reinforcing the value of collective participation.\\n4.Strengthening community engagement and solidarity\\nThe initiative fostered a sense of unity among students, promoting cooperation and shared responsibility toward community welfare.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-25","hoursSpent":4,"description":"FISTFULL was a social welfare initiative aimed at addressing hunger and food insecurity within the community. The activity focused on encouraging students to contribute essential food grains, fostering a spirit of compassion, solidarity, and social responsibility. By promoting the idea that small individual contributions can collectively create a significant impact, the initiative emphasized community welfare, empathy, and sustainable support for those in need.","aicteMapping":"Social Welfare / Community Development Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/pIVKfZ83rBHFmx0X77Dt8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"g7lLzSKJLXtHGAYWtap1L","name":"Graduation Day Ceremony","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-08-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Development of responsibility and professionalism\\nVolunteering for a formal academic ceremony helped students understand the importance of discipline, punctuality, and professional conduct while handling assigned responsibilities.\\n2.Enhanced event management and coordination skills\\nThe activity strengthened organizational abilities through involvement in tasks such as crowd and queue management, improving coordination and time management skills.\\n3.Improved communication and interpersonal skills\\nInteracting with graduates, parents, faculty, and guests enhanced students’ ability to communicate clearly, respectfully, and confidently in a professional setting.\\n4.Strengthening of teamwork and collaborative spirit\\nWorking alongside fellow volunteers fostered cooperation, mutual support, and effective collaboration toward a common goal.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-08-03","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Volunteering for the 14th Graduation Day Ceremony of RV College of Engineering was an activity focused on supporting the smooth conduct of an important academic milestone. The activity aimed to install a sense of responsibility, discipline, and service among student volunteers while contributing to the effective organization of a formal institutional event. Through active involvement, the initiative emphasized teamwork, coordination, and commitment to institutional values.","aicteMapping":"Student Development / Institutional Support Activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/nXIIneWR-g3b37wf3q5WU.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Jvzg8qqsAVa4j2uUEPaVO","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Improved awareness of Sustainable Development Goals through visual learning\\nThe activity helped participants understand the relevance of the Sustainable Development Goals by connecting them to real-life situations through photography and visual storytelling.\\n2.Development of creative and critical thinking skills\\nInterpreting social, environmental, and economic issues through photographs enhanced participants’ ability to think creatively and critically while conveying meaningful messages.\\n3.Promotion of socially responsible use of photography\\nThe competition encouraged students to use photography as a medium for social awareness, reinforcing the role of creative expression in addressing global challenges.\\n4.Enhanced observation and perspective-building skills\\nParticipants developed a deeper sense of observation by identifying SDG-related themes in their surroundings and presenting them from unique perspectives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":4,"description":"SPARK – Eyes of Youth was a photography-based initiative centered on the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), designed to raise awareness among students through visual expression. The activity motivated participants to identify and capture social, environmental, and economic challenges in their surroundings, translating them into impactful photographs and visual stories. By integrating creativity with social awareness, the competition encouraged critical thinking on sustainability, global development, and social responsibility, while emphasizing originality and ethical practices in digital content creation.","aicteMapping":"Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) / Social Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/AeSL1R9rGmHDCMP9kJ0ZJ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xVgX4j2JbBl5jw_RYRDWY","name":"Gen AI Hackthon","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/1mFhBMXAk1jr6WFH7pKOL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Enhanced understanding of Generative AI concepts and applications\\nParticipants gained practical insights into Generative AI and its potential to create content, simulate intelligent interactions, and address complex problem statements.\\n2.Development of problem-solving and innovation skills\\nWorking under time constraints encouraged participants to think creatively, analyze challenges effectively, and design feasible AI-based solutions.\\n3.Improved technical and hands-on learning experience\\nThe hackathon strengthened students’ ability to apply theoretical knowledge to real-world scenarios, enhancing their technical competence in emerging technologies.\\n4.Strengthening teamwork and collaborative skills\\nTeam-based participation fostered effective communication, coordination, and collaboration, highlighting the importance of teamwork in technology-driven innovation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The GenAI Hackathon, powered by EDOCK, was a technical innovation activity designed to provide students with hands-on exposure to Generative Artificial Intelligence. The event aimed to encourage participants to explore emerging AI technologies and apply them to solve real-world problems through creative and technology-driven solutions. By offering a collaborative environment, the hackathon promoted innovation, critical thinking, and practical learning in a rapidly evolving technological domain.","aicteMapping":"Innovation, Startup & Entrepreneurship / Technical Skill Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/1AlrqQolUvTYJ1lMHnmyo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6GZL-lLuumR_4mMpCDbSy","name":"Design-A-Thon","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-25","duration":8,"outcomes":"1.Strengthened technical and practical knowledge\\nParticipants gained hands-on experience in applying core engineering concepts to real-world design challenges, improving their technical competence.\\n2.Development of design thinking and problem-solving skills\\nThe activity encouraged students to analyze problems systematically, ideate innovative solutions, and develop structured design approaches.\\n3.Exposure to industry-relevant practices and standards\\nCollaboration with an industry partner provided insights into professional workflows, expectations, and real-time problem-solving methodologies.\\n4.Enhancement of teamwork and collaboration skills\\nTeam-based participation promoted effective communication, coordination, and collaborative decision-making.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-18","hoursSpent":15,"description":"The Design-A-Thon was a technical and innovation-oriented activity aimed at enhancing students’ practical, analytical, and design-thinking skills through industry-aligned problem statements. The activity provided students with an opportunity to apply theoretical knowledge to real-world challenges, encouraging creativity, structured problem solving, and technology-driven design solutions. Through collaboration with industry experts, the event bridged the gap between academic learning and industry expectations.","aicteMapping":"Industry Interaction / Innovation & Skill Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/QWPwn00AVVJsmorWbHbrO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9DEYRBPkMN6dW6RH2qOOv","name":"Fist Full","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Increased awareness of food insecurity and social inequality\\nThe activity helped participants understand the seriousness of hunger-related issues and the importance of ensuring access to basic nutrition for vulnerable populations.\\n2.Development of empathy and humanitarian values\\nContributing to the initiative encouraged students to cultivate compassion and sensitivity toward disadvantaged communities.\\n3.Promotion of collective responsibility and social participation\\nThe initiative demonstrated how individual contributions, when combined, can lead to large-scale positive outcomes, reinforcing the power of collective action.\\n4.Encouragement of sustainable social support practices\\nBy focusing on food grains as essential resources, the activity highlighted practical and sustainable ways to support community welfare.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-21","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Fistful was a community service initiative designed to address the issue of food insecurity and hunger by mobilizing collective student participation for a meaningful social cause. The activity aimed to create awareness about the challenges faced by underprivileged and vulnerable communities in accessing basic nutrition, while encouraging students to actively contribute toward community welfare.The initiative was built on the principle that small individual contributions can collectively lead to a significant social impact. By promoting the donation of essential food grains, the activity emphasized sustainable and practical support for institutions and communities that serve children, the elderly, patients, and other disadvantaged groups.","aicteMapping":"Social Welfare / Community Service Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/n_gJHZfo2YEsY6-zANDc3.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JruHteU5CpT8p1R04-_Ah","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"1.Enhanced awareness of Sustainable Development Goals\\nParticipants gained a clearer understanding of the SDGs and their relevance to everyday life, strengthening awareness of global challenges and sustainable solutions.\\n2.Development of creative expression and visual storytelling skills\\nThe activity encouraged students to communicate complex social and environmental issues through photography, improving their creativity and storytelling abilities.\\n3.Strengthening of critical observation and analytical thinking\\nIdentifying and capturing SDG-related themes enhanced participants’ ability to observe their surroundings thoughtfully and analyze societal issues from multiple perspectives.\\n4.Promotion of ethical and responsible digital content creation\\nEmphasis on originality and plagiarism-free submissions reinforced ethical practices in photography and digital media usage.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The SDG Photography Event – Through the Eyes of Youth was an awareness-driven creative initiative aimed at promoting a deeper understanding of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The activity provided a platform for participants to observe, interpret, and reflect on social, environmental, and economic challenges through the lens of photography. By encouraging visual storytelling, the event highlighted the role of creativity in addressing global issues and fostering meaningful social awareness. The initiative sought to inspire students to connect global sustainability goals with real-life situations, enabling them to communicate powerful messages through images and narratives. Emphasis was placed on originality, ethical digital content creation, and thoughtful representation of SDG themes. ","aicteMapping":"Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) / Social Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e43190a-7075-47c4-a023-b060c5bd7c4f/lPTik-rFXoJ-s2_sPQLUq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Mohana","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Evaluator 1","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"Evaluator 2","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 20:05:04.4723+00', '2026-01-31 04:36:10.283826+00'), ('a1d1e9f2-da80-45b6-b1fb-4be53a1501f0', '70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY026","name":"DHARMIK J RAI","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"LcqxjrLuCiYgGx6nqU0fq","name":"Mera Pahle Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/4KFOQ4URpM_6h9DW3Lbub.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity significantly enhanced participants’ understanding of the electoral system, voting procedures, and the responsibilities associated with being an informed voter. It encouraged critical thinking about electoral choices, ethical voting practices, and the long-term impact of citizen participation on democracy. The initiative fostered civic awareness, strengthened commitment toward responsible voting, and inspired first-time voters to actively contribute to the democratic process and national development.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The Mera Pahle Vote Desh Keliye initiative was an awareness-oriented program aimed at educating and motivating first-time voters to participate actively in the democratic process. The activity emphasized the importance of voting as a fundamental right and duty, highlighting how informed electoral participation contributes to transparent governance and nation-building. It focused on strengthening awareness about democratic values, constitutional provisions, and the role of youth in shaping the country’s future.\\n\\nThe program also addressed practical aspects such as voter registration, ethical voting practices, and the significance of making informed choices during elections. By connecting individual voting decisions with larger national outcomes, the initiative encouraged young citizens to view voting as a meaningful responsibility rather than a mere formality.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/d1W4upvoetJunW_VxL7DG.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iytO_WpR130JxOVl006CM","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully collected blood units to aid hospitals and patients, directly contributing to \\nlife-saving efforts.\\n\\nEnhanced awareness among participants about the significance of voluntary blood donation.\\n\\nFostered a culture of social responsibility, empathy, and community participation.\\n\\nProvided Rotaract members with hands-on experience in organizing and managing \\nhealth-related community initiatives.\\n\\nMotivated participants to adopt voluntary blood donation as a regular practice, promoting \\nlong-term community health benefits.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The blood donation camp, conducted by Rotaract, was organized to promote health awareness, community service, and the spirit of volunteerism. The event provided a safe and well-structured environment where students, faculty, and local residents could donate blood under professional medical supervision. Detailed briefings were given to all participants about the donation process, eligibility criteria, and the critical need for regular blood supply in hospitals.\\n\\nThe initiative aimed to instil a sense of social responsibility and empathy among participants while fostering active community involvement. Rotaract members played a key role in managing registrations, health screenings, and post-donation care, ensuring a smooth and efficient process. \\n\\nThe camp also served as an educational platform to encourage long-term voluntary blood donation habits, emphasizing how individual contributions collectively save lives and strengthen community health resilience.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/jPu9P531qijC0T3M5vsZz.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pvn0z8eAYiAHSlduC2AMJ","name":"Utsarga Marathon - 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness about the importance of regular exercise, fitness, and a healthy lifestyle.\\n\\nEncouraged active participation from students and community members, strengthening social connections.\\n\\nHelped participants develop resilience, discipline, and goal-setting skills.\\n\\nPromoted teamwork, motivation, and sportsmanship.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The marathon, organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), was designed to promote physical fitness, healthy living, and active community participation. The event attracted students, faculty, and local residents who came together to participate in long-distance running across a carefully planned route within the city. The marathon emphasized endurance, stamina, and perseverance, while also encouraging participants to push their personal limits and set achievable goals.\\n\\nIn addition to its focus on fitness, the marathon served as a platform for social engagement, allowing participants to connect with fellow community members and promote a sense of unity. \\n\\nNSS volunteers played a key role in organizing the event, managing logistics, ensuring safety, and motivating participants. The marathon also highlighted NSS’s broader mission of fostering \\nleadership, teamwork, and social responsibility among students, demonstrating how physical activity can be effectively combined with community service initiatives.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/Vwo8wsoEQgI1mfN0lrzs7.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UybBK8hNm6QfWAq3FNTqe","name":"Project Pustak - 2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/pZpB7aF1zh6vO-Tip59OD.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-05-30","duration":7,"outcomes":"A substantial number of books and study materials were collected and redistributed to children in need.\\n\\nUnderprivileged students gained access to essential educational resources, supporting their academic progress.\\n\\nParticipating students developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility toward educational equity.\\n\\nThe initiative reinforced values of sharing, sustainability through the reuse of books, and active community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":null,"description":"Project Pustak was a social initiative aimed at enhancing access to education and promoting literacy among underprivileged children. The project centered on collecting and distributing educational resources, including textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery, to students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds.\\n\\nStudents actively contributed by donating books and study materials in good condition, while volunteers organized, categorized, and packed the items according to age group and academic level to ensure effective distribution. The collected resources were then provided to government schools, community learning centers, and children from low-income families who otherwise lacked access to essential learning materials.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/QjtCqlgrxJyMgq5ktMpeK.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"O_ulr7vj7t2HoCyfaMNJD","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Collected blood units to support hospitals and patients in need, directly contributing to life-saving efforts. \\n\\nRaised awareness among participants about the importance and impact of voluntary blood donation. \\n\\nEncouraged social responsibility, empathy, and community service among students and local residents. \\n\\nProvided Rotaract members with organizational and leadership experience in managing public health initiatives. \\n\\nPromoted a culture of voluntary giving, health consciousness, and civic engagement in the community.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The blood donation camp, organized by Rotaract, aimed to promote social responsibility, health awareness, and community service among students and local residents. The event brought together volunteers and donors at a designated venue, following all medical safety protocols to ensure a smooth and secure process. Participants were educated about the importance of blood donation, its life-saving impact, and the role it plays in supporting hospitals and patients in need.\\n\\nThe camp also served as an opportunity to instill a sense of civic duty and empathy among young individuals. Rotaract members coordinated logistics, registration, health checks, and post-donation care, ensuring a safe and efficient experience for all donors. Beyond collecting blood, the initiative sought to raise awareness about voluntary blood donation as a regular social practice, highlighting how small individual contributions can have a profound impact on the community.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/lZswR5YxD5mn2aY_zP3Qm.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DZfHZqeghmG5a5idwsm6n","name":"Fistfull - 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected, addressing food insecurity among vulnerable populations.\\n\\nDonations supported nutrition programs in schools, anganwadis, hospitals, old age homes, and hostels for visually challenged children.\\n\\nEncouraged mass participation, with over 2,100 students contributing to the collective effort.\\n\\nFostered social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among participants.\\n\\nHighlighted the impact of small individual contributions when combined for a larger social cause.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI District 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program aimed at reducing food insecurity and supporting underprivileged communities. The initiative was based on a simple yet impactful concept: each participating student contributed either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. These small individual contributions combined to create a substantial collective impact.\\n\\nThe campaign received overwhelming support, with over 2,100 students participating and helping to collect a significant quantity of essential food grains. As part of this effort, I personally donated 5 kg of rice, which became part of the overall collection. Volunteers organized the collection, after which the food supplies were systematically distributed to various beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding programs, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes, hospitals, trust-run schools, and local anganwadis.\\n\\nThe donated rice and dal strengthened ongoing nutrition programs, benefiting children, senior citizens, patients, and economically disadvantaged communities. The distribution process was well-coordinated, with beneficiary institutions collecting the supplies directly from the campus under the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The initiative emphasized a sustainable, community-driven approach, aiming for long-term support rather than temporary relief.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/PigBslGRg7nGi799oDhlN.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dM56jqNotVvs1cpY074Eb","name":"Utsarga Marathon - 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"Promoted physical fitness, mental resilience, and overall well-being among participants.\\n\\nStrengthened community engagement and student participation in socially responsible initiatives.\\n\\nEncouraged perseverance, discipline, and personal challenge through long-distance running.\\n\\nEnhanced teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills among NSS volunteers.\\n\\nReinforced NSS’s vision of combining individual development with service to society.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-13","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The second marathon, conducted under the NSS, aimed to promote fitness while also raising awareness about societal and community issues. The event saw enthusiastic participation from \\nstudents, faculty, and local residents, all coming together to engage in a long-distance run along a pre-determined route, supported by volunteers at checkpoints and hydration stations.\\n\\nThe marathon not only tested the endurance and perseverance of participants but also encouraged them to adopt a disciplined lifestyle, highlighting the connection between personal health and overall well-being. Through this event, NSS volunteers emphasized teamwork, leadership, and social responsibility by coordinating logistics, ensuring safety, and motivating participants throughout the run. Additionally, the marathon served as a platform to foster unity, collective effort, and active civic engagement, reflecting NSS’s mission of integrating personal development with community service and social awareness.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/RDxUwjS3W1ZV48ri-WE8c.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nBaiv5yrIgrrMgmPn8SlJ","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced student engagement and fostered a positive campus environment through recreational and skill-based activities. Participants developed essential soft skills such as teamwork, leadership, coordination, and quick decision-making in an informal setting.\\n\\nRush Hours 5.0 also strengthened peer interaction and promoted a sense of community among students. The event served as an effective stress-relief initiative while reinforcing the importance of balanced personal development alongside academic growth.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":null,"description":"Rush Hours 5.0 was an interactive event organized by Rotaract RVCE, featuring a variety of games and engaging activities designed to promote teamwork, creativity, and active participation among students. The event provided a lively platform for participants to take a \\nbreak from academic routines while engaging in fun yet meaningful challenges.\\n\\nThe activities included team-based games, problem-solving tasks, and interactive challenges that encouraged communication, strategic thinking, and collaboration. The event was well-structured and efficiently managed by the organizing team, ensuring smooth conduct and enthusiastic participation throughout.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/jFuRX4YL_JlMkC4zdrD3g.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fv86pqockR-GeXtTa0nxT","name":"Project Pustak - 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"A substantial number of books and study materials were collected and redistributed to children in need.\\n\\nUnderprivileged students gained access to essential educational resources, supporting their academic progress.\\n\\nParticipating students developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility toward educational equity.\\n\\nThe initiative reinforced values of sharing, sustainability through the reuse of books, and active community service.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":null,"description":"Project Pustak was a social initiative aimed at enhancing access to education and promoting literacy among underprivileged children. The project centered on collecting and distributing educational resources, including textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery, to students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds.\\n\\nStudents actively contributed by donating books and study materials in good condition, while volunteers organized, categorized, and packed the items according to age group and academic level to ensure effective distribution. The collected resources were then provided to government schools, community learning centers, and children from low-income families who otherwise lacked access to essential learning materials.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/Eaq_FGZsRw6gDb_QgqwHm.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ilpmNm0ibEZLMbtINHpCo","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully collected blood units to aid hospitals and patients, directly contributing to life-saving efforts. \\n\\nEnhanced awareness among participants about the significance of voluntary blood donation. \\n\\nFostered a culture of social responsibility, empathy, and community participation. \\n\\nProvided Rotaract members with hands-on experience in organizing and managing health-related community initiatives. \\n\\nMotivated participants to adopt voluntary blood donation as a regular practice, promoting long-term community health benefits.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The blood donation camp, conducted by Rotaract, was organized to promote health awareness, community service, and the spirit of volunteerism. The event provided a safe and well-structured environment where students, faculty, and local residents could donate blood under professional medical supervision. Detailed briefings were given to all participants about the donation process, eligibility criteria, and the critical need for regular blood supply in hospitals. \\n\\nThe initiative aimed to instill a sense of social responsibility and empathy among participants while fostering active community involvement. Rotaract members played a key role in managing registrations, health screenings, and post-donation care, ensuring a smooth and efficient process. The camp also served as an educational platform to encourage long-term voluntary blood donation habits, emphasizing how individual contributions collectively save lives and strengthen community health resilience.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/jhl4c9hyrdYgExd_vx9S4.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gaPicut9x017COyNP_UNp","name":"Fistfull - 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected, addressing food insecurity among vulnerable populations.\\n\\nDonations supported nutrition programs in schools, anganwadis, hospitals, old age homes, and hostels for visually challenged children.\\n\\nEncouraged mass participation, with over 2,100 students contributing to the collective effort.\\n\\nFostered social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among participants.\\n\\nHighlighted the impact of small individual contributions when combined for a larger social cause.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI District 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program aimed at reducing food insecurity and supporting underprivileged communities. The initiative was based on a simple yet impactful concept: each participating student contributed either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. These small individual contributions combined to create a substantial collective impact.\\n\\nThe campaign received overwhelming support, with over 2,100 students participating and helping to collect a significant quantity of essential food grains. As part of this effort, I personally donated 5 kg of rice, which became part of the overall collection. Volunteers organized the collection, after which the food supplies were systematically distributed to various beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding programs, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes, hospitals, trust-run schools, and local anganwadis.\\n\\nThe donated rice and dal strengthened ongoing nutrition programs, benefiting children, senior citizens, patients, and economically disadvantaged communities. The distribution process was well-coordinated, with beneficiary institutions collecting the supplies directly from the campus under the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The initiative emphasized a sustainable, community-driven approach, aiming for long-term support rather than temporary relief.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/H5QaG4L7_490dyX6qlwfS.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qCkjnJf1no4UI_46zfduF","name":"Drug-Awareness Campaign","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/RJ-6DeGvmKzR5NQm7my5p.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity significantly enhanced participants’ understanding of the harmful effects of drug abuse on individual health, families, and society. It encouraged responsible decision-making, self-discipline, and awareness of preventive measures while promoting a drug-free lifestyle. The campaign motivated participants to act as role models and spread awareness among peers and the community. Overall, the initiative supported the development of health-conscious, socially responsible, and proactive individuals committed to building a safe and drug-free society.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-28","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The Pledge No Drugs and drug awareness campaign was an awareness-oriented initiative aimed at educating participants about the harmful effects of drug abuse on physical health, mental well-being, and society. The campaign focused on issues such as substance addiction, its social, psychological, and legal consequences, as well as prevention strategies and healthy lifestyle choices. The activity emphasized the importance of collective responsibility and proactive participation in creating a drug-free and socially responsible community.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/1-J_av_NMKqOCLqqGk8ny.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"24-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"R4AKv5d2lIK4fZ5OeCWm6","name":"Quiz on India''s Democracy","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity significantly enhanced participants’ knowledge of India’s democratic system, constitutional principles, and civic responsibilities. It promoted critical thinking about democratic values, governance, and citizen participation while encouraging informed decision-making. Overall, the quiz strengthened democratic awareness and fostered a sense of responsibility toward active and ethical participation in the democratic process.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-05","hoursSpent":null,"description":"The quiz on India’s democracy was an awareness-oriented activity aimed at educating participants about the democratic framework of India, constitutional values, and the functioning of key democratic institutions. The quiz covered topics such as the Constitution of India, fundamental rights and duties, electoral processes, and the roles of the legislature, executive, and judiciary. The activity encouraged informed participation and deeper understanding of democratic governance.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/70a505de-6f09-4d83-93b4-d561e6f35c4d/DA_j-1vNc9OgFxLHF2eno.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"26-27","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"DR MOHANA","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 04:45:12.642825+00', '2026-01-30 19:19:19.704224+00'), ('a40ec03a-d645-4f08-83c9-9c63927261b3', '4f026596-c49e-4016-90a6-2323ca1a089d', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 03:21:09.871374+00', '2026-01-30 03:21:11.029653+00'), ('a47dcc22-2e3d-4a8d-b784-070ac2a1e814', '2001210b-7f66-4823-80fc-fd65488281b9', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC113","name":"PAVITRA","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"kEMskyiXlPQ5YYytRJHHX","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2001210b-7f66-4823-80fc-fd65488281b9/Xh2Eaeo6OEdjaCCN5vFBP.png"],"endDate":"2023-05-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully provided essential school supplies to\\nunderprivileged rural students, supporting their educational\\nneeds. The initiative promoted equitable access to learning\\nresources and improved the overall learning environment.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-05-17","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at\\nbringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students\\nresiding in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was\\ncollected from each compassionate donor, which served as the\\nfoundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to\\nthese deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently\\nutilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks,\\nstationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that\\ncontribute to a conducive learning environment","aicteMapping":"Community service/Social Innovation","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2001210b-7f66-4823-80fc-fd65488281b9/GaGB6lSslGMrFP0sbveGT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"un_-8dKu3oCCKpnQF-__f","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Blood Donation Camp on 6th June 2023 at the Biotech Quadrangle inside the RVCE campus. The event aimed to encourage voluntary blood donation and promote awareness about the importance of saving lives through blood donation. Students and faculty members actively participated in the camp, contributing to a noble cause. Refreshments were provided to donors to ensure comfort post donation, and participation certificates were awarded as a token of appreciation for their generous act. Additionally, donors were recognized with AICTE activity points for their contribution.","aicteMapping":"Community Service/Health & Wellness","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2001210b-7f66-4823-80fc-fd65488281b9/S2KNhEy0mgMX3QWaaxlbp.pdf","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TvE8Q0lx5UZQN54cgTXcj","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Blood Donation Camp on 28th June 2024 at the Biotech Quadrangle inside the RVCE campus. The event aimed to encourage voluntary blood donation and promote awareness about the importance of saving lives through blood donation. Students and faculty members actively participated in the camp, contributing to a noble cause. Refreshments were provided to donors to ensure comfort post donation, and participation certificates were awarded as a token of appreciation for their generous act. Additionally, donors were recognized with AICTE activity points for their contribution.","aicteMapping":"Community Service/Health & Wellness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2001210b-7f66-4823-80fc-fd65488281b9/lxLVBU0gRj2kqa097KftS.pdf","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:13:13.182856+00', '2026-02-01 16:56:24.104441+00'), ('a48a5f94-584c-4444-a29a-6b48f60b175b', 'fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS109","name":"Manoj Kumar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"HmulUZetEb0LR9bz0J4rt","name":"Volunteering for 14th Graduation Day Ceremony – 2024","slNo":1,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/ceSTmRY3qIpjoJn9fNQ5S.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-08-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"The volunteering experience enhanced students’ leadership, teamwork, and event management skills while contributing to the successful conduct of a major institutional ceremony. The activity aligned with the club’s mission of fostering responsibility, discipline, and social contribution among students, while providing meaningful support to the institution.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-03","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The 14th Graduation Day Ceremony – 2024 of RV College of Engineering was a significant academic event celebrating the achievements of graduating students. The ceremony, held on 3rd August 2024, was successfully facilitated with the support of dedicated student volunteers from the SPARK club (IUCEE – RVCE Student Chapter). The volunteers actively contributed by managing various responsibilities such as crowd control, queue management, and ensuring smooth coordination throughout the event. Their involvement played a crucial role in maintaining discipline, assisting attendees, and supporting the overall execution of the ceremony in an organized and efficient manner.","aicteMapping":"Institutional/Administrative Support","pointsEarned":11,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XtqHdTlZGJin3O4h0op0o","name":"FISTFULL – 2024 (Food Donation Drive)","slNo":2,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/ozxQQjLtOjBO7kOChLZXN.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The FISTFULL initiative successfully fostered social responsibility and humanitarian values among students while making a tangible impact on addressing hunger. The activity strengthened teamwork, civic awareness, and volunteerism, aligning with the institution’s and club’s mission of creating a positive and lasting societal impact.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"FISTFULL – 2024 was a meaningful social initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana. The event was conducted from 15th November to 29th November 2024 with the objective of combating hunger and promoting food security. Students were encouraged to contribute by donating 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. The initiative witnessed overwhelming participation, resulting in the collection of approximately 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal, contributed by over 1,750 students. The activity highlighted the collective power of student participation in addressing societal challenges and reinforced values of empathy, responsibility, and community service.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_CJz2s6JzcGukOgobo44r","name":"INKSPIRE – 2024 (Creative Writing & Storytelling Event)","slNo":4,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/xiAjrBqtArSA7TfqGr8Hu.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-10-28","duration":4,"outcomes":"INKSPIRE – 2024 successfully fostered creativity, critical thinking, and social awareness among students. The activity encouraged participants to communicate impactful ideas through writing, strengthened creative confidence, and reinforced the role of storytelling as a catalyst for social change, aligning with the club’s mission of meaningful community engagement.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-10-25","hoursSpent":1,"description":"INKSPIRE – 2024 was a creative and socially impactful initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE from 25th to 28th October 2024. The event aimed to empower participants to use storytelling as a medium for social change. With impactful themes such as sustainability, health, equality, and education, the initiative encouraged students to submit original prose, poetry, articles, creative non-fiction, and flash fiction in English, Hindi, and Kannada. The event promoted inclusivity and creative diversity, providing a platform for participants to express ideas that inspire positive societal transformation. Selected works were showcased through the club’s magazine or blog, while standout pieces were highlighted on Instagram, amplifying voices advocating meaningful change.","aicteMapping":"Cultural/Literary Activity","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DcFwVe-6qpEjo6eGC8Lhj","name":"NAAC Poster and PPT Preparation","slNo":4,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/ldsNjdb98pHcF57_ZuFZd.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-21","duration":2,"outcomes":"The activity significantly enhanced students’ skills in design, presentation, teamwork, and attention to detail. Their contribution played a crucial role in the successful representation of the institution during the NAAC visit. The experience also encouraged a culture of responsibility, excellence, and active participation in institutional activities, aligning with the objectives of quality assurance and continuous improvement.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-20","hoursSpent":12,"description":"As part of the preparations for the NAAC committee visit held on 20th and 21st November 2024, a group of student volunteers from SPARK actively contributed to the design and development of posters and presentations. These materials were instrumental in showcasing the institution’s achievements, key highlights, and compliance with NAAC accreditation standards. The students worked diligently under the guidance of faculty members, dedicating approximately 20 hours to the activity. Various design tools and platforms such as Canva, Microsoft PowerPoint, Google Slides, and Adobe Photoshop were used to create visually appealing, structured, and professional content that effectively represented the institution during the visit.","aicteMapping":"Institutional Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MtdvepQVsIHl0vJJbURQ7","name":"Project Pustak – 2024","slNo":5,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/j-PqR7ar2UbulLmShZvQC.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-08-06","duration":75,"outcomes":"The activity promoted social responsibility, empathy, and teamwork among students while making a tangible contribution to improving educational access for underprivileged children. Project Pustak reinforced the importance of community engagement and aligned with the club’s mission of creating a lasting positive impact on society.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":16,"description":"Project Pustak – 2024 was a noble community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Pranay Foundation. The project was conducted from 24th May to 6th August 2024 with the objective of providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas such as Devanahalli and Bidadi, Karnataka. Funds were raised through generous donor contributions and were utilized to procure educational materials including textbooks, stationery items, and backpacks. Faculty members and student volunteers actively participated in the distribution of these resources, helping to create a supportive and conducive learning environment. The initiative received media recognition for its impactful contribution toward fostering education in rural communities.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MRfvMxYsrWQ-WkXnsOWjb","name":"SDG Photography Event – “Through the Eyes of (YOU)TH” & SDG Honour Day","slNo":7,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/xBY5_0T949DHNujjA1ql3.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-18","duration":8,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced students’ awareness of social and environmental issues while encouraging creativity, critical thinking, and teamwork. It successfully used photography as a medium to engage youth in sustainability discourse and strengthened the culture of social responsibility and environmental consciousness among students, aligning with the institution’s community outreach and SDG objectives.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The SDG Photography Event “Through the Eyes of (YOU)TH” was organized by the SPARK–IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter and conducted from 11th November to 18th November 2024, followed by SDG Honour Day on 18th December 2024. The event aimed to promote awareness of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through creative visual storytelling. The initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation, with approximately 550 students registering from RVCE and IUCEE student chapters. SPARK prefects actively volunteered in organizing, coordinating, and evaluating submissions, working closely with faculty members to ensure a fair and comprehensive assessment process. The event concluded with SDG Honour Day, where certificates were distributed to all participants and prizes were awarded to top entries, recognizing excellence and innovation in photography.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tQfJYLme39B1FgQKKyCyt","name":"SPARK “Run For Wind” – Marathon","slNo":7,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/I74PBb6_KN7hrziNcDOY_.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully raised awareness about renewable energy and environmental sustainability while encouraging physical fitness and civic responsibility among students. The activity strengthened teamwork, discipline, and environmental consciousness, aligning with the institution’s commitment to sustainability initiatives and community engagement.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-05","hoursSpent":6,"description":"SPARK “Run For Wind” – Marathon was a sustainability-focused awareness event conducted on 5th June 2024 as part of Global Wind Week celebrations. The event was organized by Karnataka Renewable Energy Development Limited (KREDL) in collaboration with the Indian Wind Power Association (IWPA) and supported by SPARK, the IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter. The 4 km marathon was held at KREDL Headquarters, Nagarbhavi, with the objective of promoting renewable energy awareness and environmental responsibility. A total of 106 SPARK members actively participated in the marathon, contributing to both the execution and outreach of the event. Volunteers were also involved in participant coordination, registration through Google Forms, and promoting eco-friendly practices such as waste management and avoiding littering during the event.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FDw6OU8ESNg2QzsKkUfZl","name":"Industry Visit – RTPS & YTPS (Raichur & Yermarus Thermal Power Stations)","slNo":8,"place":"RTPS, Raichur, Karnataka and YTPS, Yermarus, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/u0F8UNGBh4IEEUAiYJPws.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-07-02","duration":4,"outcomes":"The industry visit enhanced practical knowledge, industry awareness, and technical understanding of power plant operations. It helped students gain real-world engineering exposure, strengthened analytical thinking, and aligned with AICTE’s objective of bridging the gap between academia and industry.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-29","hoursSpent":16,"description":"The Industry Visit to Raichur Thermal Power Station (RTPS) and Yermarus Thermal Power Station (YTPS) was organized by SPARK, the IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter, to provide students with practical exposure to large-scale power generation systems. During the visit, participants observed real-time operations, power generation processes, safety protocols, and control mechanisms involved in thermal power plants. The visit enabled students to correlate theoretical concepts learned in classrooms with real-world industrial applications, enhancing their understanding of energy systems and engineering practices.","aicteMapping":"Industry Exposure / Professional Development Activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mnpXNROalY_E1A-E9W1lI","name":"SPARK Induction Programme & Recruitment","slNo":9,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/arnDvavN8a-_vWqEc79wM.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity strengthened leadership, communication, and organizational skills among student volunteers. It also enhanced student engagement and contributed to building a strong and active student chapter within the institution.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-10-01","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The SPARK Induction Programme and Recruitment activity was conducted to welcome new members and introduce them to the objectives, structure, and functioning of the SPARK (IUCEE–RVCE) Student Chapter. Senior student members actively participated in organizing the induction session, coordinating recruitment activities, and guiding new entrants. The event helped familiarize students with leadership roles, teamwork, and the club’s community and professional initiatives.","aicteMapping":"Leadership & Student Engagement Activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KTU5UROfNocijKz2IWbuZ","name":"IASF (Indian Academy of Sciences Fellowship / Science Outreach Activity)","slNo":10,"place":"KLE, Hubli","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/jnuHQr6u83dDwTb0dtPwQ.jpg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced scientific awareness, critical thinking, and academic curiosity among students. It encouraged participation in science-driven initiatives and aligned with AICTE’s focus on community development, academic enrichment, and holistic student growth.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-02","hoursSpent":8,"description":"IASF was a science and academic outreach activity conducted with the objective of promoting scientific awareness, research interest, and academic excellence among students. The event provided a platform for interaction, knowledge sharing, and exposure to scientific initiatives and academic opportunities. Participants actively engaged in the sessions, gaining insights into research-oriented thinking, scientific temper, and the importance of community-oriented academic development.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wpYNPQFW9lwFINPBXsjiy","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye","slNo":11,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/fY9MrIKZOErvgWVxZzVQl.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity strengthened civic awareness, social responsibility, and democratic values among students. It motivated participants to actively engage in the democratic process and contributed to building informed and responsible future voters.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"“Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” was an awareness-driven civic engagement activity organized under NSS to encourage young citizens to understand the importance of voting and democratic participation. The event focused on spreading awareness about electoral rights, responsibilities of voters, and the significance of informed decision-making in a democracy. Students actively participated in awareness sessions and outreach activities aimed at promoting responsible citizenship among youth.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tmzXDFoU9Nk51rUXqQO6H","name":"Mega Plantation Drive @ Hosadurga","slNo":12,"place":"Hosadurga, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/9ClLai5cQufD7_tGybTVy.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced environmental consciousness, teamwork, and social responsibility among students. It contributed positively to sustainability efforts and reinforced the importance of active community participation in environmental protection.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-09","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Mega Plantation Drive at Hosadurga was organized under the NSS initiative with the objective of promoting environmental sustainability and increasing green cover in rural regions. Student volunteers actively participated in planting saplings and supporting afforestation efforts, contributing to ecological balance and environmental awareness. The activity emphasized the importance of conservation, sustainability, and collective responsibility toward protecting the environment.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bt56sI-92by4j_s6PhOoM","name":"Project Pustak – 2025","slNo":13,"place":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/XVh3NurtIGVSAcE-aIKbI.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"The activity contributed directly to improving educational access for underprivileged students and reinforced the values of empathy, social responsibility, and community engagement. It aligned with AICTE’s objectives of encouraging student participation in meaningful social outreach activities with tangible societal impact.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Project Pustak – 2025 was a community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation. As part of this initiative, students contributed towards supporting education for underprivileged children studying in Government Schools. Through a generous donation, a complete stationery kit was sponsored for one student, helping create a better learning environment and supporting access to essential educational resources. The initiative focused on promoting social responsibility and encouraging students to actively contribute toward inclusive education.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3J3-9BIQfLAosPKNNK_a3","name":"Shakthi Shiksha – Awareness Program for School Girls","slNo":14,"place":"Government School, Bengaluru, Karnataka","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fa312f5c-976b-4237-b640-6efa938625af/TV7L-URfEXU8nhsMEVjy2.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-12-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity contributed to empowering young girls through education and awareness, while also enhancing students’ sense of social responsibility, teamwork, and communication skills. It aligned with AICTE’s objectives of promoting community service, inclusivity, and holistic student development.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-23","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Shakthi Shiksha was a community outreach and awareness initiative organized by SPARK, the IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter, on 23rd December 2023. The program aimed at providing awareness to female students of Grade 7 and above on topics such as health, hygiene, and career guidance. Around 350 school girls were engaged through interactive sessions, games, and puzzles designed to promote learning and awareness in an approachable manner. Student volunteers actively participated in planning, coordination, and execution of the event, ensuring effective knowledge transfer and meaningful engagement.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Mohana","designation":"Associate professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 09:51:08.31379+00', '2026-01-29 09:52:54.928124+00'), ('a4da8f60-a6aa-43ab-b1fe-077d1846c599', '760d9206-01c5-4484-bc38-2c3c690d5247', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD007","name":"Anish Anand","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"MHxrmEJiQ4KQ1n6UsrLCv","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improved access to basic educational resources for underprivileged and rural students.\\nHelped create a more supportive and motivating learning environment.\\nEncouraged social responsibility, empathy, and sustained community engagement among student volunteers.\\nReinforced the importance of long-term commitment to educational upliftment initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-01","hoursSpent":90,"description":"Project Pustak is a social outreach initiative undertaken by the Rotaract Club with the objective of supporting the education of underprivileged students in rural areas. The activity involved collecting voluntary monetary contributions from students, which were utilized to procure essential educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other school supplies. The initiative was conducted over multiple academic years to ensure continuity and sustained impact. Through this project, student volunteers actively participated in donation drives and coordination efforts to ensure timely distribution of resources to the beneficiaries.","aicteMapping":"Community Service / Social Outreach","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/760d9206-01c5-4484-bc38-2c3c690d5247/2eKEvxjNLKvT0cLbIgLMD.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kf2UPCIHGsXjr4DJd-deo","name":"NSS Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-24","hoursSpent":3,"description":"","aic