ursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 16:07:26.88771+00', '2026-01-30 16:58:25.978775+00'), ('a7b9f410-cc85-449c-80b6-be9ce78de83b', '3b206d00-49e8-4062-b424-006ae74907ad', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 17:12:20.78316+00', '2026-01-29 17:12:21.812254+00'), ('a9ff8e9c-7de7-4912-a2fd-f2fc0f141e7f', '4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI035","name":"PEDADA TARUN","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"-WuFPpfsLgyxwTE4hJ9Xr","name":"Akshara","slNo":1,"place":"Kengeri Government School","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/gDo3pAlBpNThRdfH-h4k4.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/auBGwR5c6xO9XxKDTQ1fz.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The outcome of the Akshara event was highly positive and impactful:\\n•\\tEnhanced classroom learning: The sessions made learning more interactive and accessible for students, using creative teaching with real-life examples and visual aids.\\n•\\tImproved concept understanding: Students were able to grasp core concepts better due to simple explanations and engaging methods.\\n•\\tBoosted confidence and curiosity: The event focused not just on academics, but also on building student confidence and encouraging curiosity.\\n•\\tPositive student response: Students responded enthusiastically, showing that the efforts were both well-received and meaningful.\\n•\\tVolunteer impact: The experience was heartwarming and rewarding for volunteers, fostering shared joy and learning.\\n•\\tReach: A total of 8 schools were visited, amplifying the event’s educational reach.\\nOverall, the Akshara event resulted in a memorable day of learning, connection, and inspiration for both students and volunteers.\\n\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-14","hoursSpent":14,"description":"Held on 14th June, 2025, Akshara aimed to make classroom learning more interactive and accessible. Volunteers conducted sessions using creative teaching methods - incorporating real-life examples, visual aids, and simple explanations to help students grasp core concepts better. The focus was not just on academics, but also on building confidence and encouraging curiosity. The enthusiastic response from the students and the genuine efforts of the volunteers made this phase both impactful and heartwarming. It was a day of learning, connection, and shared joy - for both the students and the volunteers.\\nTOTAL SCHOOLS VISITED: 8\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/MG662EjDF1gioHwHfZrME.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xL7BOa4C9O81aW4L5JGJu","name":"NAIVEDYAM 3.0","slNo":2,"place":"Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/xn6L4Ww7a_ADroBMuSrbB.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/9ZSZZCJLhEnEzzW2JzfWJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"On 19th October 2024, the Rotaract Club of RVCE hosted Naivedyam 3.0, a food drive in Banashankari where 700 people were served meals utilizing 108 kg of rice. The event involved collaboration with 21 global clubs, including the Rotaract Clubs of Jayanagar, Narayani Mid Town,MGR, and People''s Campus.\\nMore than 600 people were fed by RaC JNC, RaC Orchards, RaC APSCE, and RaC NMIT-MBA. With contributions from these clubs, a total of 1,300 meals were provided across multiple locations. The initiative was a significant effort in promoting community welfaré and volunteerism.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-10-19","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Rotaract Club of RVCE conducted Naivedyam 3.0, a food drive, serving meals to more than 1300 people. The event was held in collaboration with 21 clubs across the globe, making it a successful community service initiative.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/g0I5iwS_fsAG8yvMiM9fB.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WW7YfFDpenY9UidrXbcgI","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/Q42QHufldHfmeJsmhbtWe.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/rtxfhqbVEXKNZ4udeWehk.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp was a remarkable success, with an impressive collection of 656 units of blood from generous donors. The event not only helped address critical medical needs but also fostered a strong spirit of empathy and social responsibility among participants. The overwhelming response highlighted the impact of collective goodwill, creating a lasting ripple of kindness and reinforcing the importance of service to humanity.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-24","hoursSpent":null,"description":"Description of the activity\\tOn 28th June 2024, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a blood donation camp that stood as a powerful testament to compassion, selflessness, and community service. ","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":16,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/Z_Vcm2_OonaepDb6Tb7Em.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"815cPoxLB3VDoM9TQBNgs","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":4,"place":"Narayanagiri Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/CTmrAlMtnFj2kjolM3mfG.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/JmyMAVdCB-VT2-etJhBPI.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/wj6Zo5-GwDkgwdFvEo2jr.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Outcome of the Fast Trek 3.0 event:\\n•\\tHigh Participation: Over 500 college students actively took part in the trek.\\n•\\tAdventure & Sustainability: The event successfully combined outdoor adventure with a sustainability mission, including a cleanliness drive at Narayangiri Hills.\\n•\\tEnvironmental Connection: Students explored and appreciated the natural beauty of the region, gaining a renewed sense of responsibility towards nature.\\n•\\tPositive Experiences: The scenic route offered breathtaking views and a refreshing, immersive experience for all participants.\\n•\\tCommunity Building: The day ended with students sharing stories, laughter, and memories, strengthening bonds and culminating in a truly memorable journey.\\nSummary:\\nFast Trek 3.0 motivated students to connect deeply with nature, promoted environmental stewardship, and left attendees with lasting memories and a greater sense of responsibility for preserving natural spaces.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Rotaract Club of RVCE organized one of its flagship events, Fast-Trek 3.0, which witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 500 college students. The event combined adventure with a meaningful purpose, encouraging students to connect with nature.\\nProject Description: Fast-Trek 3.0 organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE was an event that seamlessly combined adventure with a mission for sustainability. The trek to Narayangiri Hills was planned to encourage students to explore the natural beauty of the region while actively participating in a cleanliness drive. The scenic route offered breathtaking views, providing an immersive and refreshing experience for all. The day concluded with shared stories, laughter, and a renewed sense of responsibility towards nature, making it a truly memorable journey.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/43XM5gzYgd4VxzD5Aqd2U.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tr4YiK1KnTvHmWPJvQYZH","name":"Secret Santa","slNo":5,"place":"Various NGO''s","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/9swkM3coqdHaY5xPCI8X6.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/ledEBb9xcsqk5Ahs0vQRR.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/COZW-OIwX_mkp7ynkoMY_.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Outcome of the Secret Santa event:\\n•\\tSpread Joy: The event successfully brought happiness and festive cheer to underprivileged children in Bengaluru orphanages.\\n•\\tImpactful Giving: Gifts, toys, cakes, and educational supplies were distributed, making the holiday season memorable for the children.\\n•\\tCommunity Engagement: 88 participants (volunteers from RVCE) were actively involved, sharing time, games, and celebrations with the children.\\n•\\tReinforced Values: The initiative reinforced compassion, generosity, and the importance of giving back to the community.\\n•\\tPositive Experience: Both children and volunteers had a heartwarming and joyful Christmas, strengthening the spirit of collective effort and kindness.\\nSummary:\\nThe Secret Santa event created a positive impact by celebrating Christmas with children in need, fostering generosity and compassion, and making the day special for everyone involved.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-25","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Secret Santa event was a resounding success, spreading happiness and reinforcing the values of compassion and generosity. It highlighted the power of collective efforts in making a positive impact and served as a reminder of the importance of giving back to the community. For everyone involved, it was a truly Merry Christmas filled with love and joy.\\nProject Description: The Rotaract Club of RVCE hosted a heartwarming Secret Santa event on December 25, 2024, to celebrate Christmas with children in orphanages. This initiative aimed to bring joy and festive cheer to underprivileged children, making their holiday season memorable. The event was made possible through the generous contributions of RVCE students. The funds were utilized to purchase a variety of gifts and essential items, which were thoughtfully distributed to five different orphanages across Bengaluru on Christmas day. These gifts included toys, cakes, educational supplies, and other necessities that brought smiles to the faces of the children. Volunteers from the Rotaract Club spent the day with the children, engaging them in fun-filled activities, games, and festive celebrations.\\nNO. OF PARTICIPANTS: 88\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/7NymPpx9NIw7NzSB6HXNp.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0GMEI9Koms4Yc51dC3KDJ","name":"Raksha","slNo":6,"place":"Various NGO''s","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/RhJFJKHHRhZfoga5EEqVp.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Outcome of the Raksha event:\\n•\\tEmpowered Children: School children learned essential self-defense moves and situational awareness, gaining practical skills for personal safety.\\n•\\tBoosted Confidence: The event successfully helped instill confidence, preparedness, and quick-thinking in threatening situations.\\n•\\tHigh Engagement: The session was interactive, allowing kids to practice techniques and clarify doubts, resulting in enthusiastic participation.\\n•\\tPromoted Safety and Self-Reliance: Students became more aware of safety strategies and felt more self-reliant in emergencies.\\n•\\tPositive Impact: The initiative built a sense of preparedness among children, effectively promoting awareness and a proactive approach toward personal safety.\\nSummary:\\nThe Raksha event made a meaningful impact by equipping children with life-saving self-defense skills and boosting their confidence and awareness about personal safety.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-31","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE conducted an impactful event named Raksha, where volunteers taught school children essential self-defense techniques. The initiative aimed to instill confidence and create awareness among young students about personal safety.\\nProject Description: Raksha was organized on 24th May 2025 to empower school children by educating them on basic self-defence moves and situational awareness strategies. Volunteers demonstrated simple yet effective techniques that the kids could use in case of emergencies. The session was interactive, allowing students to practice and clarify doubts. The primary goal was to promote safety, self-reliance, and quick-thinking in threatening situations. The event received enthusiastic participation and helped build a sense of confidence and preparedness among the children.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/4PIviLbMPRNForegKzpJs.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4CnfdyCsTjD2aXNbGTux2","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/qt649sjH8cmWf-Zw8qnlp.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Increased Awareness: Successfully raised awareness about the social, legal, and moral consequences of female foeticide among participants and the public.\\n\\nCommunity Engagement: Over 350 individuals actively participated, demonstrating collective responsibility and social unity.\\n\\nPromotion of Gender Equality: Reinforced the importance of valuing girl children and promoting gender equality in society.\\n\\nSocial Sensitization: Encouraged participants to reflect on and challenge societal norms related to gender discrimination.\\n\\nStudent Development: Helped students develop social responsibility, leadership, empathy, and civic awareness.\\n\\nPositive Social Impact: The walkathon inspired dialogue and commitment toward preventing gender-based discrimination and violence.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"On the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon with the objective of creating awareness about the grave issue of female foeticide and promoting the value of the girl child in society. The walkathon aimed to educate the public on gender equality and encourage collective responsibility in preventing discrimination against female children.\\n\\nThe event witnessed over 350 participants, including students, faculty members, and supportive parents, who came together to stand against gender-based violence and injustice even before birth. The walkathon commenced in the early hours from the RVCE campus and was marked by impactful placards, thought-provoking messages, and powerful slogans that effectively conveyed the importance of protecting and empowering girl children.\\n\\nThe walkathon served as a strong platform to spread awareness, inspire social change, and reinforce the message of equality, dignity, and respect for women. The active participation and unity displayed during the event reflected a shared commitment toward building a more inclusive and just society.ffff","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/Xx10GJAF9dsZLgJ1vKcsM.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NJNrzT5_nYXYVHJ5eY4nE","name":"Eye Checkup Camp","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/-e6H-8UMqbbK6XY2NuM4G.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Accessible Healthcare: Provided free and high-quality eye check-ups to the RVCE community.\\n\\nHealth Awareness: Increased awareness about the importance of regular eye examinations and early diagnosis.\\n\\nPreventive Care: Enabled early identification of vision problems and guided participants toward timely treatment.\\n\\nProfessional Guidance: Participants received expert consultation and personalized eye care advice.\\n\\nPositive Participation: The camp saw strong engagement and appreciation from students, staff, and parents.\\n\\nSocial Impact: Contributed to improved health consciousness and well-being within the community.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Free Eye Checkup Camp on 23rd April 2025 in collaboration with Vasan Eye Care at the RVCE Health Centre. The camp was conducted with the objective of promoting awareness about eye health and the importance of regular eye examinations among the RVCE community.\\n\\nThe initiative was open to students, faculty members, non-teaching staff, and parents, ensuring wide accessibility to quality eye care services. Experienced professionals from Vasan Eye Care carried out comprehensive eye examinations, provided expert consultation, and offered guidance on maintaining good eye health.\\n\\nThe camp aimed to encourage preventive healthcare by facilitating early detection of vision-related issues and reducing the risk of long-term eye problems. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation, and several individuals were advised further medical treatment or corrective measures wherever necessary. The program concluded successfully with positive feedback from the participants.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/6dQcN_xAvs2M7kfrTGR0h.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7pHzMCElafn3CnR6NQoLA","name":"Paper Hearts","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/fRlHUVYZ7SudFXvDjf6BO.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Teacher Appreciation: Teachers felt valued and recognized for their dedication and contribution to student growth.\\n\\nStrengthened Student–Teacher Bond: The initiative fostered mutual respect and positive interaction between students and faculty.\\n\\nPromotion of Values: Encouraged gratitude, empathy, and respect among students.\\n\\nCreative Participation: Students actively engaged by designing handmade cards, showcasing creativity and sincerity.\\n\\nPositive Campus Culture: Contributed to a warm, respectful, and appreciative academic environment.\\n\\nSuccessful Celebration: The event was meaningful, memorable, and well-received by faculty and participants.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized “Paper Hearts – Honoring Our Teachers” to celebrate Teachers’ Day and express heartfelt gratitude to the esteemed faculty of RVCE. The event was dedicated to acknowledging the invaluable role teachers play in shaping the academic, personal, and professional growth of students.\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, club members presented each teacher with a rose, symbolizing admiration and respect, along with handmade greeting cards creatively crafted by the students. These thoughtful tokens served as a gesture of appreciation for the teachers’ unwavering dedication, commitment, and contributions to student development.\\n\\nThe event fostered a positive and respectful atmosphere on campus, strengthening student–teacher relationships and promoting a culture of gratitude, empathy, and mutual respect. The celebration was well-received and highlighted the importance of recognizing educators as pillars of society.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/F3IaaRLEzCNDadhahBxdk.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QXOtRiWYn5cTdmDebeb4N","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/Ki4jNRHDvOevZKSY7CLWL.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/5CxBNO83AKYQhxDOwRAkr.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":2,"outcomes":"Environmental Awareness: Increased awareness about sustainability, recycling, and responsible waste management.\\n\\nBehavioral Change: Encouraged participants to adopt reuse and recycling practices in everyday life.\\n\\nCreative Thinking: Fostered innovation by transforming waste materials into useful and artistic creations.\\n\\nStudent Engagement: High participation and enthusiasm through interactive activities and the treasure hunt.\\n\\nTeamwork & Collaboration: Promoted teamwork, problem-solving, and time management skills among participants.\\n\\nPositive Impact: Reinforced the idea that sustainable practices can be engaging, practical, and impactful.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Uptown Junk was a creative and engaging sustainability initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of promoting environmental awareness and responsible waste management practices. The event aimed to demonstrate that sustainability can be both impactful and enjoyable by encouraging participants to view waste as a valuable resource rather than something disposable.\\n\\nThe initiative involved hands-on activities where participants transformed discarded and recyclable materials into innovative art forms and useful creations. This creative approach helped reinforce the importance of reuse and recycling in reducing environmental harm. To further enhance engagement, a fun-filled treasure hunt was organized across the campus, where teams solved riddles related to sustainability while racing against time.\\n\\nUptown Junk successfully brought students together in a collaborative and energetic environment, inspiring them to adopt eco-friendly practices in their daily lives. The event highlighted how creativity, teamwork, and enthusiasm can contribute to building a greener and more sustainable future.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/uwZmhhQ_pUZVCioM3dT6M.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3h_IjIyixNeRwaWuFj83Y","name":"Fistfull","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/yw92jbY29DJfdJ-XnBDJW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"Hunger Relief: A significant quantity of food grains was collected to support individuals and communities in need.\\n\\nMass Participation: Over 1,750 students actively contributed, demonstrating strong social responsibility.\\n\\nAwareness Creation: Increased awareness about food insecurity and the power of collective action.\\n\\nCommunity Welfare: Strengthened the spirit of compassion, generosity, and solidarity among students.\\n\\nPositive Social Impact: Showcased how small individual contributions can lead to meaningful societal change.\\n\\nInstitutional Commitment: Reinforced RVCE’s dedication to community service and humanitarian initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fistfull was an impactful food donation initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, aimed at combating hunger and supporting community welfare. The initiative encouraged students to contribute toward a noble cause by donating 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, emphasizing how small individual efforts can collectively create a large social impact.\\n\\nDaily collections were carried out at the Civil Department, and the drive received an overwhelming response from the student community. Over the course of the event, more than 1,750 students participated, resulting in the collection of approximately 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal.\\n\\nThe initiative highlighted the importance of empathy, generosity, and collective responsibility toward addressing food insecurity. Fistfull successfully reinforced RVCE’s commitment to social service, community welfare, and solidarity through meaningful student engagement.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4a68f063-ee45-4d08-8599-a5cd6af8fae8/ooCBNXnwsgJVjUVi4ZB1I.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 13:07:30.637919+00', '2026-01-31 13:02:16.923671+00'), ('aaa331eb-488f-4da1-aeab-13ca185ec687', 'ce34c861-8dda-4669-8bca-a6435050e2d9', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS056","name":"Sanganna Motgi","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"8nVCccQ1sFp9gb2bVIcSG","name":"","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce34c861-8dda-4669-8bca-a6435050e2d9/otdtriID_u-6e3pijUbH1.png"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Kavitha S N ","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 10:55:42.738893+00', '2026-01-29 10:59:52.765494+00'), ('ab7cdec2-0d7e-4c7d-9827-4526cfcf17ce', 'e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY023","name":"Deekshith V","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"7XNIYR6IJBN3M2212etPF","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp successfully collected a substantial quantity of blood units, which \\nwere added to the local blood bank’s inventory and will support patients in need of transfusions \\nduring emergencies and medical treatments. The event raised awareness among participants \\nand the wider community about the importance of voluntary blood donation, helping dispel \\nmyths and encourage future donor participation. It also fostered a strong sense of community \\nengagement, social responsibility, and solidarity among students and volunteers involved in the \\ninitiative","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"By voluntarily donating blood, I contributed to supporting patients in need and promoting \\nawareness about the importance of blood donation in society. This activity helped me develop a \\nsense of social responsibility, empathy, and commitment toward community welfare and public \\nhealth.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/LbmxAKJznvcw4mcOD-8Pz.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3KxPjrA_2-bovmcXsE1Js","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye ","slNo":2,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” initiative enhanced understanding of democratic principles and the significance of electoral participation. It reinforced a sense of civic duty and responsibility toward contributing to the nation’s governance through informed decision-making.\\n\\nThe activity encouraged political awareness, social responsibility, and active citizenship, highlighting the importance of youth engagement in democratic processes. It also reflects a commitment to upholding constitutional values and contributing positively to the nation’s democratic framework.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” is a national voter awareness initiative aimed at encouraging first-time voters to actively participate in the democratic process of India. The campaign focuses on educating young citizens about the importance of voting, constitutional rights, and civic responsibility in strengthening democratic governance.\\n\\nBy participating in this initiative, the individual demonstrated awareness of the role of informed voting in shaping public policy, leadership, and national development. The program promotes ethical citizenship, political awareness, and responsible participation in elections, aligning with India’s democratic values and electoral integrity.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/QHD7grCAHpONvvEdjWjbD.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PKQ0smc0duFn3KaSvyweZ","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness about the importance of regular exercise, fitness, and a healthy lifestyle.\\nEncouraged active participation from students and community members, strengthening social \\nconnections.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The marathon, organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), was designed to promote \\nphysical fitness, healthy living, and active community participation. The event attracted \\nstudents, faculty, and local residents who came together to participate in long-distance running \\nacross a carefully planned route within the city. The marathon emphasized endurance, stamina, \\nand perseverance, while also encouraging participants to push their personal limits and set \\nachievable goals","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/kQMw4Nv6uioUGcLRdjjlV.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rgX3B18kEnQrBhIgfHVnQ","name":"Fight Against Drug Abuse Pledge","slNo":4,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Awareness & Social Responsibility:\\nGained a deeper understanding of the consequences of drug abuse and the importance of individual responsibility in preventing substance misuse.\\n\\nEthical Commitment:\\nDemonstrated a formal commitment to leading a drug-free life and promoting positive behavioral choices within society.\\n\\nCivic Engagement:\\nActively participated in a Government of India–recognized public health and social awareness initiative.\\n\\nPersonal Development:\\nReinforced values related to self-discipline, health consciousness, and ethical decision-making.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"This certificate is issued by the Narcotics Control Bureau (NCB), Ministry of Home Affairs, Government of India, under the national awareness initiative “Say Yes to Life, No to Drugs”.\\nThe program is aimed at promoting drug-free lifestyles and spreading awareness about the harmful physical, psychological, and social impacts of drug abuse.\\n\\nBy taking this pledge, the participant formally commits to:\\n\\nRejecting the use of narcotic drugs and psychotropic substances\\n\\nActively supporting efforts to prevent drug abuse\\n\\nEncouraging healthy, responsible, and lawful living\\n\\nThe initiative aligns with India’s national strategy to combat substance abuse through preventive education, social responsibility, and youth engagement.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/e__sPW-C7QfBQk7OCJwBl.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eI0I2VH2qgVyrQ2bl3Cs-","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"A significant number of books and study materials were\\ncollected and redistributed to students in need.\\nUnderprivileged children received access to learning resources,\\nsupporting their academic growth.\\nStudents developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of\\nresponsibility toward educational equity.\\nThe activity promoted the values of sharing, sustainability\\n(reuse of books), and community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak 2024 was a social initiative organized to promote\\neducation access and literacy among underprivileged children.\\nThe project focused on collecting and distributing educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery to students from economically weaker sections of society..Students\\nactively participated by donating books and study materials that\\nwere in good condition. Volunteers sorted, categorized, and\\npacked the collected materials based on age group and academic\\nlevel to ensure effective distribution. The resources were then\\nprovided to government schools, community learning centers, and\\nchildren from low-income families who lacked access to adequate\\nlearning materials.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/T1tREseEw10mpsdWYJ7XN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1aSi4KE6yKdyWMqjmE1ZA","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Collected blood units to support hospitals and patients in need, directly contributing to life-saving efforts.\\nRaised awareness among participants about the importance and impact of voluntary blood \\ndonation.\\nEncouraged social responsibility, empathy, and community service among students and local \\nresidents.\\nProvided Rotaract members with organizational and leadership experience in managing public \\nhealth initiatives.\\nPromoted a culture of voluntary giving, health consciousness, and civic engagement in the \\ncommunity.","semester":"4","startDate":"","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The blood donation camp, organized by Rotaract, aimed to promote social responsibility, health \\nawareness, and community service among students and local residents. The event brought \\ntogether volunteers and donors at a designated venue, following all medical safety protocols to \\nensure a smooth and secure process. Participants were educated about the importance of blood \\ndonation, its life-saving impact, and the role it plays in supporting hospitals and patients in \\nneed.\\nThe camp also served as an opportunity to instill a sense of civic duty and empathy among \\nyoung individuals. Rotaract members coordinated logistics, registration, health checks, and \\npost-donation care, ensuring a safe and efficient experience for all donors. Beyond collecting \\nblood, the initiative sought to raise awareness about voluntary blood donation as a regular social \\npractice, highlighting how small individual contributions can have a profound impact on the \\ncommunity.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/cmmUnLlrz6V_3diuY7bEQ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_gNicAefrz1QLUIG05a2n","name":"FistFull 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-29","duration":13,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected,\\nhelping address food insecurity among vulnerable\\ncommunities.\\nThe donated food grains supported nutrition programs in\\nold age homes, hospitals, schools, anganwadis, and\\ninstitutions for visually challenged children.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of\\nRVCE in association with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI\\nDistrict 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program\\nfocused on reducing food insecurity and supporting\\nunderprivileged sections of society. The initiative followed a\\nsimple yet powerful concept where each participating student\\ndonated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, turning small individual\\ncontributions into a collective effort with significant impact. The\\ndrive received overwhelming support, with participation from\\nover 2,100 students, leading to the collection of a large quantity\\nof essential food grains. As part of this initiative, I personally\\ncontributed 2 kg of toor dal, which was added to the overall\\ncollection. The donated food grains were then distributed to\\nvarious beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding\\nprograms, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes,\\nhospitals, trust-run schools, and nearby anganwadis. These\\nsupplies helped strengthen existing nutrition programs benefiting\\nchildren, senior citizens, patients, and economically\\ndisadvantaged communities.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/24wVAkpfhUUQDw2ocC1y1.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_yFgxgzPc0SzcWY8BxCwC","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"A substantial number of books and study materials were collected and redistributed to children \\nin need.\\nUnderprivileged students gained access to essential educational resources, supporting their \\nacademic progress.\\nParticipating students developed empathy, social awareness, and a sense of responsibility toward \\neducational equity.\\nThe initiative reinforced values of sharing, sustainability through the reuse of books, and active \\ncommunity service.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social initiative aimed at enhancing access to education and \\npromoting literacy among underprivileged children. The project centered on collecting and \\ndistributing educational resources, including textbooks, notebooks, storybooks, and stationery, \\nto students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/HkuKAQQ5OdiWJW1kaA5vt.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DWN7YJ7IyVeYsS_tw9OUy","name":"Female Foeticide Walkathon","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participation in the walkathon strengthened awareness of the long-term social consequences of female foeticide and reinforced the role of youth in addressing deeply rooted societal challenges. The event promoted empathy, civic engagement, and a sense of responsibility toward advocating gender equality and women’s rights.\\n\\nBy engaging in this initiative, the participant demonstrated commitment to social causes, collaboration with healthcare and service organizations, and alignment with national and global efforts to eliminate gender discrimination. The experience also contributed to personal growth by enhancing social awareness, ethical values, and community involvement.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":1,"description":"This Certificate of Participation was awarded for active involvement in the Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon, held on 11th May 2025 at RV College of Engineering. The event was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with Bangalore Hospitals, with the objective of raising awareness about the critical social issue of female foeticide and promoting gender equality.\\n\\nThe walkathon aimed to educate participants and the broader community on the ethical, social, and legal implications of gender-based discrimination, emphasizing the importance of valuing and protecting the rights of the girl child. Through collective participation, the event fostered social responsibility and encouraged individuals to actively contribute toward building an inclusive and equitable society.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/VbDJbLb25nXQZRDRxSoz-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Y-qTRC15FD6djD6h2Gtto","name":"Nasha Mukth Pledge","slNo":11,"place":"Online","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Participation in the Nasha Mukth Pledge enhanced awareness of the physical, psychological, and social consequences of drug abuse and reinforced the importance of preventive action at the individual and community levels. The activity strengthened a sense of civic responsibility and ethical commitment toward maintaining personal well-being and promoting healthy lifestyles.","semester":"6","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Nasha Mukth Pledge is a national awareness initiative undertaken under the guidance of the Narcotics Control Bureau (NCB), Ministry of Home Affairs, Government of India, aimed at promoting a drug-free and healthy society. By taking this pledge, the participant formally committed to rejecting the use of narcotic drugs and psychotropic substances and to consciously supporting efforts to prevent substance abuse.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Thz--RMYJCvXbzcqB4I7T","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-30","duration":14,"outcomes":"A substantial quantity of rice and dal was collected,\\nhelping address food insecurity among vulnerable\\ncommunities.\\nThe donated food grains supported nutrition programs in\\nold age homes, hospitals, schools, anganwadis, and\\ninstitutions for visually challenged children.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of\\nRVCE in association with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI\\nDistrict 3191), was a large-scale community outreach program\\nfocused on reducing food insecurity and supporting\\nunderprivileged sections of society. The initiative followed a\\nsimple yet powerful concept where each participating student\\ndonated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, turning small individual\\ncontributions into a collective effort with significant impact. The\\ndrive received overwhelming support, with participation from\\nover 2,100 students, leading to the collection of a large quantity\\nof essential food grains. As part of this initiative, I personally\\ncontributed 2 kg of toor dal, which was added to the overall\\ncollection. The donated food grains were then distributed to\\nvarious beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding\\nprograms, hostels for visually challenged children, old age homes,\\nhospitals, trust-run schools, and nearby anganwadis. These\\nsupplies helped strengthen existing nutrition programs benefiting\\nchildren, senior citizens, patients, and economically\\ndisadvantaged communities. The distribution was carried out in a\\nsystematic and well-coordinated manner, with beneficiary\\ninstitutions collecting the food supplies directly from the campus\\nunder the supervision of Rotaract and Rotary representatives. The\\ninitiative focused on creating a sustainable and community\\ndriven impact, emphasizing long-term support rather than short\\nterm relief.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/ww59TO-A7EsYJzOLHQxbA.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZZgWp9eI0yU2OiV_RJlLP","name":"Utsarga Marathon-2025","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"Promoted physical fitness, mental resilience, and overall well-being among participants.\\nStrengthened community engagement and student participation in socially responsible \\ninitiatives.\\nEncouraged perseverance, discipline, and personal challenge through long-distance running.\\nEnhanced teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills among NSS volunteers.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-13","hoursSpent":1,"description":"\\nThe second marathon, conducted under the NSS, aimed to promote fitness while also raising \\nawareness about societal and community issues. The event saw enthusiastic participation from \\nstudents, faculty, and local residents, all coming together to engage in a long-distance run along \\na pre-determined route, supported by volunteers at checkpoints and hydration stations.\\nThe marathon not only tested the endurance and perseverance of participants but also \\nencouraged them to adopt a disciplined lifestyle, highlighting the connection between personal \\nhealth and overall well-being. Through this event, NSS volunteers emphasized teamwork, \\nleadership, and social responsibility by coordinating logistics, ensuring safety, and motivating \\nparticipants throughout the run. Additionally, the marathon served as a platform to foster unity, \\ncollective effort, and active civic engagement, reflecting NSS’s mission of integrating personal \\ndevelopment with community service and social awareness.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e8124635-43f6-4a9a-a2d7-2ceb6ae6cb82/U-QnpYysxDq-CE-nn-Tia.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 15:40:54.415576+00', '2026-01-30 17:08:01.329577+00'), ('ad49c2e3-f58d-4f35-8608-abcc8bb947f6', 'ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS204","name":"Srivatsha N","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Cw4qKeuY5_MgMSjsUZBbI","name":"Problem-Based Learning","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/ePsiET1azuqihdn3knb3_.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced students’ understanding of Problem-Based Learning (PBL) as an effective and modern pedagogical approach. Participants gained practical insights into integrating real-world problems into the learning process, thereby improving critical thinking, collaboration, and problem-solving skills. The session encouraged students to move beyond rote learning and adopt a more hands-on, application-oriented mindset. Additionally, the event increased awareness of innovative teaching methodologies, motivating students to actively engage in self-driven and experiential learning.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-07-07","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The event organized by the students of SPARK, the IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter, featuring a talk on “Problem-Based Learning” by Sampada Pachaury, Director and Board Member of the IUCEE Foundation, was a valuable initiative promoting innovative pedagogical approaches. Ms. Pachaury’s expertise in problem-based learning contributed significantly to the educational enrichment of attendees, emphasizing the importance of hands-on, practical problem-solving in the learning process. By hosting such talks, students gain insights into contemporary teaching methodologies, thereby enhancing their overall educational experience. Awarding AICTE Activity Points for organizing this event is justified, as it recognizes the students’ proactive role in fostering educational innovation and creating opportunities for their peers to engage with progressive learning methods, aligning with AICTE’s commitment to promoting excellence in engineering education.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/wR776fAdlaK7jSG1JU9W9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Z4ays8ymEvCanT4mnRZsJ","name":"Under The Peepal Tree 2023","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/gylqMg6aLXS9PflEBGBwA.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-16","duration":3,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced students’ critical thinking, problem-solving abilities, and general awareness across a wide range of topics. Participants developed confidence in quick decision-making and logical reasoning while engaging in a competitive yet collaborative learning environment. The quiz also promoted peer interaction, teamwork, and intellectual curiosity among students from different academic backgrounds. Overall, Under the Peepal Tree contributed to the holistic development of students by encouraging continuous learning, active participation, and a strong culture of academic excellence within the institution, aligning with AICTE’s objectives of promoting student engagement and intellectual growth.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Under the Peepal Tree is a flagship quiz event organized at the college that brings together students from diverse disciplines to participate in an intellectually stimulating and competitive environment. The event is designed to encourage analytical thinking, general awareness, and interdisciplinary knowledge through multiple engaging quiz rounds. Conducted in an open and interactive setting, the quiz promotes curiosity, teamwork, and healthy competition among participants. By providing a platform for students to test their knowledge beyond classroom learning, Under the Peepal Tree plays a significant role in fostering a vibrant academic culture and enhancing student engagement across the campus.","aicteMapping":"Professional Society Activities","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/WC_2DDwvV5ukDef16kphd.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wW94CLYFTNMrNrlfTwnBs","name":"Infosys Visit","slNo":3,"place":"Mysore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/fAYPT-32QYcMusVctTtoo.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":1,"outcomes":"The industrial visit to the Infosys Mysore campus enabled students to gain practical exposure to a professional corporate environment and understand the functioning of a large-scale IT organization. Students developed insights into industry workflows, organizational culture, and the application of academic concepts in real-world scenarios. The visit enhanced their awareness of current technological trends, industry standards, and best practices, thereby improving their readiness for future professional roles. Overall, the experience helped bridge the gap between theoretical knowledge and practical industry requirements, contributing to the holistic development of students in alignment with AICTE’s objectives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-31","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The industrial visit to the Infosys Mysore campus, organized by students of SPARK, the IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter, was a valuable experiential learning opportunity. This event provided students with firsthand exposure to the corporate environment and the latest technological advancements at one of India’s leading IT companies. By touring the Infosys campus, students gained insights into real-world applications of their academic knowledge, observed industry best practices, and interacted with professionals in the field. Awarding AICTE Activity Points for participating in such industrial visits is justified, as it recognizes students’ proactive efforts to bridge the gap between theoretical learning and practical industry applications. This initiative aligns with AICTE’s vision of promoting industry–academia collaboration to ensure students are well-prepared for the dynamic demands of the professional world, fostering a holistic and experiential approach to engineering education.","aicteMapping":"Industry – Academia Interaction","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/0oryraB4dDBSWOZXLGw6W.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"VZQI0t5N4Dz5gYhDCKSj_","name":"Induction Programme & Recruitment","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/dQa1yFzCmf4o8b-6KswTO.png"],"endDate":"2023-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Induction Programme successfully helped freshers transition smoothly into the academic environment by providing essential information, guidance, and peer support. New students developed a sense of belonging and confidence, enabling them to adapt more effectively to university life and academic expectations. Student organizers enhanced their leadership, communication, and organizational skills while fostering an inclusive and supportive campus culture.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-10-01","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Participation in the Induction Programme for freshers by students of SPARK, the IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter, was a crucial initiative that fostered a sense of community and support within the academic institution. The event served as a warm welcome for incoming students, providing essential information, guidance, and a platform to acclimate to the university environment. Student organizers played a pivotal role in facilitating a smooth transition for the newcomers, aiding their integration into the academic community. Awarding AICTE Activity Points for involvement in the Induction Programme is warranted, as it recognizes students’ active contribution to the well-being and inclusivity of the academic community, aligning with AICTE’s goal of nurturing a holistic educational environment that prioritizes student engagement and support.","aicteMapping":"Student Development Activities","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/zGVdZ88TM5nNYBxlA3wbt.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9HqFZyONbV3xTXzhQ4AFQ","name":"IEEE Hack4Soc 2.0","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/c-GYC5bvWTqfYH1aINSmZ.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":2,"outcomes":"The hackathon significantly enhanced participants’ problem-solving abilities, technical proficiency, and innovation mindset. Students gained practical experience in rapid prototyping, system design, and collaborative development under real-world constraints. The event strengthened skills such as teamwork, time management, and effective communication while encouraging socially responsible engineering solutions. Additionally, participants were exposed to industry-relevant tools, frameworks, and development practices, improving their readiness for future technical and professional challenges.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-03","hoursSpent":24,"description":"IEEE Hack4Soc 2.0 was a 24-hour national-level hackathon organized at the college that brought together students to collaboratively develop innovative technology-driven solutions for real-world societal challenges. The event provided participants with an intensive, hands-on environment to ideate, design, and implement software and hardware solutions within a limited timeframe. Through continuous mentoring, team-based problem solving, and iterative development, students applied concepts from computer science, engineering, and emerging technologies to address practical problems. The hackathon fostered innovation, creativity, teamwork, and technical excellence while promoting the use of technology for social impact.","aicteMapping":"Technical & Innovation Activities","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/ixa8px3Nl7EurkxKJRM9A.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PaCjMJBhAl5K3vqkTzJuy","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":6,"place":"Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/OcxDq4ZJDptMGuXjhCL1P.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak was an initiative dedicated to supporting underprivileged children by providing essential educational resources such as books and study materials, helping to reduce barriers to learning. The project aimed to promote equal educational opportunities for students from economically weaker backgrounds and encourage their academic growth. Overall, Project Pustak created meaningful impact by combining educational support for children with hands-on community service for volunteers.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE launched “Project Pustak,” a community service initiative aimed at providing educational kits to underprivileged children. These kits included essential school supplies, books, and learning tools designed to empower students and create opportunities for a brighter future. The project sought to break down barriers to education, emphasizing the belief that education is a fundamental right and not a privilege.","aicteMapping":"Rural Outreach","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/hrNQFs9wh1_E-3LpylUxW.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"p5xWzWtuuvVrkd4dL_PDC","name":"Under The Peepal Tree 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/e6yFqjnozrMkDYGzM44qD.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced students’ critical thinking, problem-solving abilities, and general awareness across a wide range of topics. Participants developed confidence in quick decision-making and logical reasoning while engaging in a competitive yet collaborative learning environment. The quiz also promoted peer interaction, teamwork, and intellectual curiosity among students from different academic backgrounds. Overall, Under the Peepal Tree contributed to the holistic development of students by encouraging continuous learning, active participation, and a strong culture of academic excellence within the institution, aligning with AICTE’s objectives of promoting student engagement and intellectual growth.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Under the Peepal Tree is a flagship quiz event organized at the college that brings together students from diverse disciplines to participate in an intellectually stimulating and competitive environment. The event is designed to encourage analytical thinking, general awareness, and interdisciplinary knowledge through multiple engaging quiz rounds. Conducted in an open and interactive setting, the quiz promotes curiosity, teamwork, and healthy competition among participants. By providing a platform for students to test their knowledge beyond classroom learning, Under the Peepal Tree plays a significant role in fostering a vibrant academic culture and enhancing student engagement across the campus.","aicteMapping":"Professional Society Activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/8852XFhq3lfz3oSVpqxsr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Bhso-b1Md3aycY_U2Afic","name":"71st Wildlife Week Walkathon","slNo":8,"place":"Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/kdyVeNge3hVWkam1tdu3I.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"Engaged directly with government environmental initiatives. Gained awareness about the specific challenges facing Karnataka’s wildlife and the role of public solidarity in supporting the Forest Department’s conservation goals.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-02","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Participated in a major walkathon organized by the Karnataka Forest Department to commemorate the 71st Wildlife Week. The walk commenced from the iconic Vidhana Soudha and concluded at Lalbagh Botanical Garden. The event aimed to sensitize the general public about the importance of wildlife conservation and the protection of Karnataka’s rich biodiversity.","aicteMapping":"Environmental Activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/9aT_UgPNUWhGiJ8SFyl1Y.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NHLI6LZwO1TM0KLos6e7s","name":"Art of Living – YES+ Course","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/wrFcaSb4thpJpH42ILw5M.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/wKPJmNvqIytX-yyL3_2zH.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-30","duration":9,"outcomes":"The course enhanced practical techniques to manage stress, improve concentration, and maintain emotional well-being. It improved self-awareness, resilience, and the ability to stay calm under pressure. The program also emphasized the importance of mental health in leading a balanced and productive life.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-22","hoursSpent":12,"description":"On completing the YES+ Youth Empowerment Seminar conducted by the Art of Living, which included sessions on mental health awareness under the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative. The program involved guided meditation, breathing techniques, and interactive sessions focused on stress management, emotional balance, and self-awareness.","aicteMapping":"Mental Health Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/B8Mf2UMqpDXq-W7MJr43c.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yFXILvCsSGYDlRRmt0Bgg","name":"Art of Living –Community Kitchen & Cleanliness Seva","slNo":10,"place":"Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/yIGafhC2qKpLDxmL5Y83H.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/-KzkA8v-XaG8ZQospbGid.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"This initiative fostered teamwork, discipline, and a strong sense of social responsibility. It raised awareness about hygiene, public cleanliness, and the impact of small community efforts in creating a healthier environment for everyone.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"During the YES+ program at the Art of Living International Center, I volunteered in a community service initiative that included working in the community kitchen and participating in a cleanliness drive outside the ashram premises. The kitchen service involved supporting food preparation, serving meals, and maintaining hygiene, while the outdoor drive focused on collecting litter and promoting cleanliness in surrounding public areas. The activity highlighted the dignity of labor and the importance of civic responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/zwNCxMF3rEt3uWZRf1xuH.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"D4vyG5Y2qWmnGfSSrBXm4","name":"Art of Living – Permaculture & Soil Awareness Activity","slNo":11,"place":"Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/S02s7tCSztba0d50tbSVU.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/hy1ijlASyD4D05SgmC4Vr.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity increased awareness about sustainable farming, soil health, and environmental conservation. It reinforced the value of eco-friendly practices and the role of individuals in supporting a sustainable future.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-13","hoursSpent":7,"description":"As part of the YES+ initiative at the Art of Living International Center, I participated in a permaculture awareness activity aimed at promoting sustainable agricultural practices and soil conservation. The session focused on improving soil quality through natural methods and understanding the importance of ecological balance in food production. The initiative encouraged environmentally responsible practices for long-term sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/oxydZzwLlh-w4sxQGOme_.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FjhXMdwRRRofo6kJCpz-3","name":"Art of Living – Gaushala Service","slNo":12,"place":"Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/HKD8ogjEs9ktkhxVstYAq.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/HDyrn6TK3r3m3Ru7F8ys5.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The service deepened awareness about animal care, biodiversity, and sustainable agricultural practices. It reinforced compassion, responsibility, and the importance of maintaining harmony between humans, animals, and nature.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-21","hoursSpent":6,"description":"As part of the YES+ Youth Empowerment initiative, I participated in Gaushala service at the Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru. The activity focused on caring for indigenous cows through feeding assistance and maintaining cleanliness in the shelter. It emphasized the cultural, agricultural, and ecological significance of preserving native cattle breeds and promoting animal welfare.","aicteMapping":"Animal Care & Sustainability","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/9FVHb_A-XWWgsDtB6l2Mk.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8k2ZklQlhzi7HXOJyH273","name":"Art of Living – Horticulture Seva","slNo":13,"place":"Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/RdIdkgVjeDgXhlZ72N8YZ.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/X7ceVmXDH4fPl7TrzPg0S.png"],"endDate":"2026-01-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity strengthened awareness about environmental conservation and the importance of maintaining green spaces. It reinforced the value of sustainability, patience, and responsibility while contributing to a healthier and greener environment.","semester":"7","startDate":"2026-01-03","hoursSpent":7,"description":"As part of the YES+ Youth Empowerment Seminar at the Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, I participated in a horticulture service activity aimed at promoting environmental sustainability and ecological responsibility. The initiative involved watering plants, sowing seeds, and nurturing trees within the campus to support green cover and biodiversity. The activity fostered an atmosphere of environmental awareness and collective responsibility toward nature.","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ecb9a42c-a61f-467c-83e4-951fca0103a4/a3SdguqlBXRX3bGk6XtLD.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Neethu S","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:31:51.573287+00', '2026-01-31 04:22:25.731775+00'), ('aebfb871-3442-4a90-a527-2c193c1accd2', '510bdbae-1499-4cd5-ad0b-333c3790b89d', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY001","name":"Aarya Prasad Pai","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Q_aOnYzTT1NSqHhrUjISz","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The overwhelming response from participants highlighted the deep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service and social responsibility. The event fostered a sense of camaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of teamwork and determination. \\n\\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, encouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while giving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the bond between students and the community but also showcased how small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful social change.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants. \\n\\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond.\\n","aicteMapping":"Proceeds generated are donated to noble causes","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/510bdbae-1499-4cd5-ad0b-333c3790b89d/3KglKHo4xhr0ZpDw1Fy82.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XhAFBqNty5601Mwr5k1vV","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The overwhelming response from participants highlighted the deep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service and social responsibility. The event fostered a sense of camaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of teamwork and determination. \\n\\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, encouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while giving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the bond between students and the community but also showcased how small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful social change.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants. \\n\\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond.\\n","aicteMapping":"Proceeds generated are donated to a noble cause","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/510bdbae-1499-4cd5-ad0b-333c3790b89d/eeGQCYNPQglWsksUI4l15.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"E8hPYtwGs8tP5zX1RX19c","name":"Broseph Shikshana Vedike Student Volunteer Program","slNo":3,"place":"St. Broseph Foundation","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-02-17","duration":10,"outcomes":"The volunteering experience yielded significant outcomes in both personal growth and community impact. By bridging the educational gap for students at a local government school, the initiative helped foster a more inclusive learning environment and provided essential academic guidance to those in need. On a professional level, the program enhanced my ability to simplify complex concepts—a skill essential for effective technical communication—and strengthened my adaptability in diverse social settings. Furthermore, being recognized with 35 points by the institution underscores a demonstrated commitment to social responsibility and the ability to balance community-oriented projects alongside a rigorous academic schedule.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-02-08","hoursSpent":25,"description":"During the first phase of the Broseph Shikshana Vedike (BSV) Programme, I served as a student volunteer in a community initiative conducted by the St. Broseph Foundation. Between January and March 2025, I dedicated time to teaching underprivileged students at a local government school, focusing on academic support and social empowerment. For my consistent engagement over five days of instruction, I was awarded 35 points (7 points per day) by the Dean of Student Affairs at RV College of Engineering. This experience allowed me to contribute to educational equity while strengthening my communication and leadership skills within a diverse community setting.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":35,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/510bdbae-1499-4cd5-ad0b-333c3790b89d/g-nRjeJbYz96_S4yfkjfZ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ehrsVz1vYd6T5YfMQgY9m","name":"Discplinary Committee for 8th Mile RVCE","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":4,"outcomes":"The outcomes of serving on the 8th Mile Disciplinary Committee centered on developing high-stakes operational management and conflict resolution skills. By successfully overseeing crowd dynamics and maintaining campus decorum during one of the institution''s most attended events, I demonstrated the ability to lead under pressure and ensure the safety of a large, diverse population. This role sharpened my situational awareness and improved my ability to implement complex logistical protocols in real-time. Receiving 20 activity points further validates the success of these efforts, marking a tangible contribution to the college''s organizational excellence and the overall success of the cultural fest.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-03","hoursSpent":8,"description":"As a member of the Disciplinary Committee for 8th Mile, the flagship cultural fest of RV College of Engineering, I played a critical role in ensuring the safe and seamless execution of the large-scale event. My responsibilities included managing crowd control, monitoring event perimeters, and coordinating with campus security to maintain order throughout the festivities. By upholding safety protocols and managing high-pressure situations effectively, I contributed to a secure environment for thousands of attendees. For my dedication to campus safety and organizational integrity, I was awarded 20 activity points, reflecting my commitment to institutional service and teamwork.","aicteMapping":"Volunteered for college cultural events","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/510bdbae-1499-4cd5-ad0b-333c3790b89d/_Mff1E4CfHkAMXIRwSVyL.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"y8LepS_uDnnSzacRQbO3c","name":"FistFull Rice Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-09-10","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of this donation was the immediate provision of essential nutrition to families in need, contributing to the overall success of the Rotaract club’s hunger-relief goals. On a personal level, this experience reinforced the importance of social responsibility and consistent community engagement. It demonstrated how logistical coordination and student-led philanthropy can effectively address basic human needs, further cultivating a culture of empathy and civic duty within the student body.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-09-10","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in the \"Fistful of Rice\" donation drive, a community service initiative organized by Rotaract RVCE. By contributing 5kg of rice to the camp held on the RV College of Engineering campus, I joined a collective effort to combat local food insecurity and support underprivileged communities. This project focused on the power of small, individual contributions coming together to create a significant, large-scale impact on social welfare within the regional ecosystem.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/510bdbae-1499-4cd5-ad0b-333c3790b89d/myM0b6YLohk-MMMDA2_vn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OHq5RMhOW-gl2x0S__39u","name":"Fistfull Rice Donation Camp","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The outcome of this repeated contribution was the further scaling of the camp’s total food reserves, ensuring that a larger number of families received immediate nutritional support. On a personal level, this experience reinforced the value of long-term community engagement over one-time actions. It deepened my awareness of socio-economic disparities and demonstrated how organized, persistent collective efforts within a university ecosystem can provide a reliable safety net for those in need.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I continued my involvement with the \"Fistful of Rice\" initiative, a recurring social service drive organized by Rotaract RVCE. By contributing another 5kg of rice during the on-campus collection camp, I sustained my commitment to the club’s mission of gathering essential food supplies for local orphanages and marginalized communities. This repeat participation reflects a consistent dedication to grassroots humanitarian efforts and highlights the importance of student-driven action in addressing local food insecurity.","aicteMapping":"Food Donation Camp","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/510bdbae-1499-4cd5-ad0b-333c3790b89d/PyyoYIL91Yc2_QRaAWjvC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 06:56:25.800154+00', '2026-01-30 07:52:40.671484+00'), ('aec549e9-ca74-4ae1-9fad-8ee0109fe114', '2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23EC405","name":"Karthik S","period":"2023-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"JpqZj8eSzE6ldT4k0yf30","name":"Utsarga 2024 – NSS Club, RVCE","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/8zual8cyC54rxQ0hw9hOo.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of RVCE, successfully blended fitness, community engagement, and philanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to contribute to a meaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With enthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful reminder of the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges.\\nRunners contributed through their registration fees, which were directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or\\ncontributing to educational and environmental projects. \\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants.","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme (NSS)","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/tlKrsZ9T7zb5u8k813doe.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bQwNKJgnujGdNwseut0Zy","name":"Project Pustak 2024 – Rotaract Club, RVCE","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/YKe59SUf6Rm_65MLjDTX8.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/O3r8A0O-ZimyH4-_qeR7f.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged rural students by providing them with essential educational materials and school supplies. The initiative created a meaningful impact by ensuring needy students received textbooks, stationery, and other learning resources required for a better education experience. With effective fund collection and proper utilization, the event reflected strong community participation and social responsibility. The collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranava Foundation strengthened the reach of this initiative, helping improve access to education and creating a positive learning environment for students. \\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\nThrough the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds.Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Social Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/hlmE0KzFUg1BrgbfJm1fg.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pyyeAPwxUZyrscZSZ3Bnt","name":"Blood Donation Camp – Rotaract, RVCE","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/X6XvdZ4iYUzOUhs2qGbNW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE was a resounding success, fostering a spirit of compassion, generosity, and social responsibility within the campus. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and staff, all coming together to contribute to a noble cause that has the potential to save countless lives. By donating blood, the participants played a vital role in addressing the critical demand for blood in hospitals and medical facilities, thereby making a direct impact on healthcare and emergency situations.\\nThe event also served as an awareness drive, emphasizing the importance of regular blood donation and dispelling common myths associated with the process. Informational sessions and guidance from medical professionals helped participants understand how a single unit of donated blood can save multiple lives by assisting accident victims, patients undergoing surgeries, and individuals battling serious medical conditions. The presence of trained healthcare professionals ensured a safe and smooth donation process, making first-time donors feel comfortable and encouraged to make blood donation a regular practice.\\n\\n\\nThrough this initiative, the Rotaract Club of RVCE not only facilitated a significant contribution to blood banks but also inspired a culture of selfless service and humanitarianism within the college community. The overwhelming support and positive response reinforced the impact of collective efforts in bringing about meaningful change. By organizing such initiatives, the club continues to strengthen the values of empathy and social responsibility, motivating more individuals to step forward and contribute to the well-being of society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a blood donation camp on the campus of RV College of Engineering, aiming to encourage students and faculty to contribute to a lifesaving cause. The event was meticulously planned to ensure a smooth and efficient donation process, with medical professionals and volunteers assisting at every stage. Participants were first guided through a preliminary health check-up to determine their eligibility for blood donation, ensuring the safety of both the donors and the recipients. Once cleared, donors proceeded to the designated stations where trained medical staff facilitated the blood collection process in a hygienic and well-organized environment.\\nThe event not only provided an opportunity for individuals to donate blood but also helped raise awareness about the critical need for regular blood donations in healthcare. Informational sessions were conducted to educate participants on the benefits of blood donation, its impact on saving lives, and the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle to be a regular donor. Volunteers from the Rotaract Club played a crucial role in coordinating the event, assisting donors, and ensuring their comfort throughout the process. The camp witnessed an overwhelming response from students and faculty, reinforcing the spirit of humanitarian service within the RVCE community. Through this initiative, the Rotaract Club successfully contributed to replenishing blood banks while fostering a sense of social responsibility and compassion among the participants.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/FQqiwu8jif_psQQpsEMet.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QmhzyVyn6GuX6P7Nwbirx","name":"AZADI KA KALOSTAV - NSS Club, RVCE","slNo":4,"place":"Manekshaw Parade Ground, Bangalore ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/6l_xg-xUqmUKUeTmgzuzF.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/RxheR7a0p1iwX_-qO45iX.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/kneWrj_ZKKGyRDH3iuBU2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-08-15","duration":22,"outcomes":"The successful participation in AZADI KA KALOTSAV resulted in significant cultural, personal, and social outcomes. The event provided students with a unique opportunity to perform at a state-level national platform, thereby boosting confidence, stage presence, and cultural awareness. It strengthened appreciation for India’s traditional art forms and reinforced the importance of preserving indigenous cultural heritage.\\nStudents developed essential qualities such as discipline, teamwork, leadership, time management, and responsibility through rigorous rehearsals and coordinated execution. Exposure to professional choreographers enhanced artistic skills and provided valuable learning experiences. Additionally, participants became eligible for further prestigious opportunities such as National Integration Camp (NIC) and NSS Republic Day Camp (RDC) selections based on performance.\\nOverall, the activity instilled a deep sense of patriotism, social responsibility, and national pride among students. It strongly aligned with AICTE and NSS objectives by promoting holistic development, civic engagement, cultural awareness, and experiential learning beyond academics. The event successfully upheld RVCE’s reputation at the state level while contributing meaningfully to Independence Day celebrations.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-25","hoursSpent":70,"description":"AZADI KA KALOTSAV was a prestigious state-level cultural event conducted on the occasion of the 78th Independence Day of India on 15th August 2024 at the Manekshaw Parade Ground, Bengaluru. The event was organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, under the Government of Karnataka, and was held in the esteemed presence of the Honourable Chief Minister and the Governor of Karnataka, along with other dignitaries of the State Government.\\n\\nThe primary objective of the event was to celebrate India’s independence by showcasing the rich cultural heritage of Karnataka through traditional dance and folk art performances. Students from RVCE actively participated as performers and volunteers, representing the institution at a highly significant public platform. As proud RVCE students, participation in this event was considered both an honor and a responsibility, as it reflected the institution’s commitment to cultural preservation, national pride, and community service.\\n\\nThe cultural performances included a wide range of traditional dance forms such as Bharatanatyam, Dollu Kunita, Huli Kunita, Yakshagana, Veeragaase, Kudure Kunita, Peacock Dance, Nandi Kolu, Pyramid formations, and other folk representations. Students underwent disciplined practice sessions and coordinated performances under the guidance of experienced choreographers. The event emphasized unity in diversity and celebrated India’s freedom through art, discipline, and collective expression.","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme (NSS)","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NpMsV7tFlK9x7Z8gu5e6e","name":"Cheela Mela – NSS Club, RVCE","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/JcoCdnkK8phj4BW_ybL3f.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2fb3de2c-0c54-411f-abda-9155bc7cd313/DNoSdV10E6CRDw1x2M8n5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-20","duration":2,"outcomes":"In collaboration with Youth For Seva, students created handmade newspaper bags for the Kadale Kayi Parishe, promoting a \"go green\" initiative and a sustainable environment.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-19","hoursSpent":10,"description":"NSS RVCE, in collaboration with Youth For Seva, is organizing a paper bag workshop for the Kadale  Kayi Parishe. Go green by creating newspaper bags and contribute towards a sustainable environment!\\n","aicteMapping":"National Service Scheme (NSS)","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Prakash Biswagar","designation":"Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 05:03:24.919316+00', '2026-01-31 05:42:24.805615+00'), ('afc69400-30c3-451f-9d4b-c7571f4412fc', '359345ff-4073-46e2-a83d-e26706196d88', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23AI402","name":"k Preethi","period":"2023-2026","department":"Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"3dnzjcLfwcrp2HPi9fawJ","name":"Data Remix","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/359345ff-4073-46e2-a83d-e26706196d88/o_BiKKyLrQ72WmfCqbm36.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"DHI DAY promotes technical skills, creative problem-solving, \\nand sustainable innovation among participants. It empowers \\nstudents to integrate technology with sustainability, enhancing \\ntheir holistic thinking. Organizers and participants gain valuable \\nexperience in teamwork, technical expertise, and impactful \\nRV college of Engineering® Bengaluru \\nPoints earned \\ninnovation. The event also marks a successful collaboration \\nbetween academia and industry, inspiring future endeavors","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"DHI DAY, organized by Team DHI in collaboration with GE \\nHealthcare on 6th March 2024, is a landmark event for the AIML \\ndepartment of RVCE. The day includes a speaker session hosted \\nby GE Healthcare (9:00 am - 1:00 pm) and an engaging \\ncompetition, Data Remix (1:30 pm - 6:30 pm). Open to students \\nfrom all semesters, the event comprises two phases: data analysis \\nand visualization, and sustainable business innovation, aligned \\nwith the UN''s Sustainable Development Goals. Esteemed judges \\nwill evaluate presentations, fostering a blend of technical and \\nsustainable thinking. ","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/359345ff-4073-46e2-a83d-e26706196d88/sBorWMUEbmh1FPbFdszzN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 04:34:00.846336+00', '2026-01-31 04:44:00.049051+00'), ('b0b0cb66-9b0c-4769-a1a9-7197cc8c95e6', '3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY018","name":"Bhakti Vyas","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"GcIZIFFyEkKg4oahox0pn","name":"Blood donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/4R6aMpoYsDAQ6U5DRMiUk.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Many patients require blood at crucial times, and my blood being B+ve, it can be used by \\nanyone, hence donated my blood so that it can be used for a good purpose.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Donated my blood to the blood bank for a social cause. Every drop counts — one pint of blood \\ncan save up to three lives. This was our chance to give someone a second chance at life, right \\nhere on campus.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/a6dcsOE-lUod7a7UacyJg.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"f_DExod1cOR13MQ2zMHwa","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/JybkD0f3NLjrw6WxjRdHP.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-25","duration":2,"outcomes":"Education is the key to unlocking opportunities and building a better future. Unfortunately, \\nmany\\nchildren in rural areas lack access to basic school supplies, making it difficult for them to learn \\nand grow. Project Pustak aims to bridge this gap and help these children realize their potential","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a noble initiative that aims to provide essential school supplies to \\nunderprivileged students in rural areas. With the generous donations, notebooks and geometry \\nboxes will be brought, which will be donated to government schools. ","aicteMapping":"Social Service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/-jQ_AwNkjO_-B4K581J_0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vAn0k5iNV7S8LcF9y3nJN","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/Vym2vXYmd-7KKlzluXnEz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program increased awareness about the social and ethical impact of female foeticide among participants and the community.\\nIt motivated individuals to take a stand for the protection, respect, and empowerment of the girl child.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was organized to spread awareness about the importance of saving the girl child and promoting gender equality in society.\\nThe program aimed to encourage social responsibility and inspire collective action against female foeticide through active community participation.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/VOzSfG_YP9hYR89_d0D6P.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5M02-JCz4OzGCoU5lF67h","name":"Fist Full","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/emRT5I2Oj9-u49hYTx6kO.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":19,"outcomes":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing \\nessential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted \\nin the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions \\nthat serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-03","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A fistful of kindness can fill a heart and feed a soul. For every meal we prepare from November \\n3rd to November 21st, set aside a fistful of rice or toor dal. By the end of the event, we''ll have \\ngathered enough to bring a smile to someone in need!","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/Bbm0QTuMJBgviORWBocX-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Fsel6PIEXTRhEZiH0NCdP","name":"Fist Full","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/S6xjjdCiR9N42ZTf6ntQ-.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore \\nSpandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily \\ncollections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total \\namount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative \\nhighlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s \\ndedication to community welfare and solidarity.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":1,"description":"A fistful of kindness can fill a heart and feed a soul. For every meal we prepare from November \\n15th to November 29th, set aside a fistful of rice or toor dal. By the end of the event, we''ll have \\ngathered enough to bring a smile to someone in need!","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/A8URcqn6-UQScNOX9yzav.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"u9TDKGVYSyNj0dEB33ZBI","name":"SDG Photography Contest","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/359OiNQfStvU6PBEDA35k.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"The program enhanced awareness of global sustainability issues and encouraged participants to express social responsibility through creative photography.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The SDG Photography Contest organized by SPARK provided a platform to creatively showcase themes related to the Sustainable Development Goals through visual storytelling.","aicteMapping":"Sustainable Development Goals","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/lha6VcxyKxXrVdH74EOxm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PnXg_S1w_ne4hKa0ADc0V","name":"Secret Santa","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/2Y7hlBADuczj7TDs48mTr.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program created a joyful and inclusive atmosphere, strengthening bonds among participants. It successfully promoted empathy, happiness, and festive cheer within the campus community.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Secret Santa initiative to spread joy and kindness during the festive season through thoughtful gift-sharing. The event encouraged students to celebrate the spirit of giving while fostering togetherness and goodwill.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3c6e3004-4a3d-4970-ae35-2a36c13e4166/02u8bAuscvxLjoE1KadHz.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 17:14:03.637164+00', '2026-01-30 19:01:06.890516+00'), ('b0ec1e55-884e-4ee6-b507-2ace19bdea6a', '3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD030","name":"Mula Sohan","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"mE9r3q_dyKmH3oNaOGBSn","name":"AKSHARA","slNo":1,"place":"Vishwabharathi High Scool","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/FM8Jh9qkHvrnEqIB9hvhA.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the initiative was a meaningful experience that refined my ability to communicate effectively. By conducting a session for a class of students, I learned how to adapt my presentation style to be more interactive and accessible, ensuring that concepts were easily understood. Managing the classroom dynamics, even for a single session, taught me the importance of patience and engagement in the learning process. Furthermore, this direct interaction provided personal insight into the educational disparities faced by these students, fostering a deeper sense of social responsibility and a genuine appreciation for the effort required in the teaching profession.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE held skill development sessions in eight Bangalore schools, benefiting over 1000 underprivileged students. Targeting financially modest backgrounds, the sessions enhanced academic understanding and provided essential skills. Schools visited included BET Convent, Sai Sri Vidya Chethana, Vishwa Bharathi High School, Kengeri High School, Government Model Primary School, Nehru Memorial School, Priyadarshini Vidhya Kendra School, and Mount Carmel English School. The initiative used interactive methods for curriculum-based learning to ensure relevance and engagement. Volunteers gained valuable experience as teachers, fostering appreciation for the profession and addressing educational disparities. This initiative underscored the power of volunteerism and the need for quality education for all.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/MS4WPJEcFuBQ2P7flMdfv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9JJBCGONk_pzoocWWQ_nN","name":"UTSARGA 2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/OVgyOgZEhZY8e0dcX4iUy.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need. ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based registration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create awareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness activity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community impact.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/4Q_fhUSCEKhSwPTzMJphB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"37sXiZ9PXOpT5LNnWmHXn","name":"UTSARGA 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/CvF16eH02bau5PmlbzTWR.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"I gained improvement in physical stamina and endurance by participating in the marathon. The activity also helped me build discipline and motivation through early-morning participation and completing the run. Additionally, it increased my awareness of social contribution, since the marathon supported initiatives related to improving opportunities for children in need. Overall, this activity contributed both to my NSS activity progress and my personal development.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, is a marathon event focused on promoting health, fitness, and social responsibility. Scheduled to be held on April 6th, 2025, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM at R V College of Engineering (RVCE), the event encourages students and the public to participate in either a 5 km or 10 km run through donation-based registration. With the theme “Help a Child Change the World,” the marathon aims to create awareness and support for education-related social causes, making it more than just a fitness activity and instead a meaningful initiative that connects physical well-being with community impact.\\n","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/huvqCc9E6jqEwF2BT-RvC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EKGImXFteSCJYS1IbH0Dv","name":"PROJECT PUSTAK 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/3FkBouG5j6CMVWpJPptFn.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in Project Pustak, I gained a strong sense of social responsibility and satisfaction from contributing towards the education of underprivileged rural students. I understood the real impact that even small contributions can create when combined for a meaningful cause. This activity helped me develop empathy and awareness about the difficulties faced by students who lack basic school resources. I also gained exposure to community service initiatives and learned the importance of teamwork and collective effort in successfully carrying out a donation-based project. Overall, the experience was rewarding as it allowed me to support a noble cause and contribute directly to creating a better learning environment for deserving students.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students living in rural areas. Under this project, a contribution was collected from each donor, and the funds raised were used to procure and donate much-needed educational materials. The collected amount was utilized to purchase resources such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other important school supplies that help create a better and more supportive learning environment for deserving students. The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, undertook the responsibility of procuring and distributing these essential supplies to ensure meaningful educational support for the beneficiaries.","aicteMapping":"1","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/h59ScjtIu_wVC7epGvFch.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"j9HjJzwuQnobH72_j4LDU","name":"FAST TREK 2.0","slNo":5,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/7frOT1-4bLwec8qko5pXk.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of this activity, I gained meaningful experience in community service by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive during the trek, which strengthened my sense of environmental responsibility. I also developed better discipline and time management by reporting on time and following the event schedule starting from 7:30 AM. The trek helped improve my physical stamina and endurance while navigating the Kunagal Betta Hills, and it also enhanced my teamwork and coordination skills through interaction with a large group of participants. Overall, participating in this event gave me a sense of achievement, improved my fitness, and increased my awareness about maintaining cleanliness and protecting nature.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive during the trek, dedicated to preserving the environment. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus to the trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the adventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all attendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagal Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding success, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750 individuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s vibrant atmosphere.","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/zv_ee9AJxL_FjEvaN7jV_.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4oxEIUk91W4afyWOBlQUq","name":"FAST TREK 3.0","slNo":6,"place":"Narayangiri Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/Z2kFv9fHOfe0qzTF-Pdj8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Fast Trek 3.0, I gained a strong sense of environmental responsibility by actively taking part in the cleanliness drive and contributing to preserving the natural beauty of Narayangiri Hills. The trek helped me improve my physical stamina and endurance by completing the trails, while also teaching me discipline and consistency through early-morning participation. I also developed better teamwork and coordination skills by trekking along with a large group and supporting others throughout the journey. Overall, the event gave me a memorable experience of bonding, collective effort, and personal achievement, leaving me feeling accomplished, motivated, and inspired.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast Trek 3.0, the biggest flagship event of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, took place on 12th January 2025 at the scenic Narayangiri Hills, bringing together over 500 enthusiastic participants from the college. This adventure-packed event combined trekking with a meaningful cleanliness drive, reinforcing the club’s commitment to environmental responsibility. The trek began early in the morning, with participants embarking on a thrilling journey through the rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills. Amidst breathtaking views, the team actively engaged in cleaning the surroundings, collecting litter, and promoting eco-consciousness. The event not only contributed to preserving the natural beauty of the hills but also instilled a sense of responsibility among students. Beyond the cause, Fast Trek 3.0 fostered incredible team bonding, as participants supported and motivated one another throughout the trek. Laughter, shared experiences, and the collective effort to make a difference created an unforgettable experience. The event concluded on a high note, with participants feeling both accomplished and inspired.","aicteMapping":"4","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/0BOciM7CXE-5f3yIPmKS4.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_qSSN3Pj-d2rUMchiedny","name":"FIST FULL 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/q7RvOqxLdZyKWKxdSlbN_.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in this donation drive, I contributed directly to community welfare by supporting the collection of essential food items for those in need. I gained a stronger sense of social responsibility and empathy by being part of an initiative that emphasized solidarity and helping others through collective effort. The activity also helped me understand how even small individual contributions can lead to large-scale impact when students come together for a cause. Overall, this experience strengthened my awareness of community service and reinforced the importance of actively participating in welfare-oriented initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/uHbJsS9FFWiaQyJELXPxq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xcFplhQ922OsJjSc1qvnM","name":"FIST FULL 2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/ktvPxjEm2t4I6WfzvlmKv.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Fistful community service project, I contributed toward reducing food insecurity by supporting the collection of nutritional resources for vulnerable communities. This activity helped me develop a deeper understanding of social responsibility and the importance of collective action, as even a simple contribution like donating rice or dal became part of a large-scale support system for health and care institutions. I also gained awareness of how structured community service initiatives can effectively address real societal problems, and the experience strengthened my sense of empathy, gratitude, and commitment toward community welfare.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Fistful was a standalone community service project designed to combat food insecurity and support health and care institutions through collective student participation. The initiative was built on a simple yet impactful principle - every participating student donated either 5 kilograms of rice or 2 kilograms of dal. With the support of Rotary Bangalore Spandana and under the Community Service avenue focusing on Fighting Disease, the project transformed individual contributions into large-scale nutritional support for vulnerable communities.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/fSU6jaTGMTde282uHeiGN.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jqRpz2z1Qx_elGw1HU2wI","name":"ACM GEN AI HACKATHON","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/ng0lsHlcWb0im6H9iIywX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"As a volunteer for the GenAI Hackathon (powered by EDOCK) held on 29th November 2024 at RVCE, I gained valuable experience in event coordination and student management by supporting the smooth execution of the hackathon. I developed strong communication and teamwork skills by interacting with participants, guiding them when required, and coordinating with the organizing team to ensure timely flow of activities. This volunteering opportunity also improved my leadership, responsibility, and problem-solving abilities, especially while handling on-spot requirements during the event. Additionally, being part of a technology-focused hackathon enhanced my exposure to Generative AI innovations and strengthened my understanding of how collaborative events encourage creativity, innovation, and real-world solution building. Overall, the experience helped me grow professionally by building organizational skills and giving me practical experience in managing a large student-driven technical event.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The GenAI Hackathon, powered by EDOCK, was successfully organized at RV College of Engineering on 29th November 2024 at the DTL Huddle. The event served as a dynamic platform for students to explore and apply advanced concepts in Generative Artificial Intelligence, focusing on innovative solutions that enable machines to generate content, simulate human-like interactions, and address complex real-world challenges. The hackathon witnessed enthusiastic participation from students who showcased their creativity and technical expertise by developing innovative prototypes within a limited timeframe. Overall, the event encouraged collaborative learning, problem-solving, teamwork, and innovation, creating an enriching experience that promoted emerging AI technologies and their transformative impact across industries.","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/fSz-feH05gFus4IufKUPb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DCmai-vXJhvCuUg7brdxe","name":"SWACHHATA PAKHWADA 2023","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/WWSi56v0olXcy5rCB5P-p.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in Swachhata Pakhwada, I gained practical experience in community service by actively contributing to cleaning and maintaining the campus environment. This activity strengthened my sense of responsibility toward hygiene and public cleanliness and helped me understand the importance of environmental stewardship. I also developed teamwork and coordination skills by working with other volunteers and students to complete the drive effectively. Overall, the initiative increased my awareness about cleanliness as a social duty and motivated me to continue participating in activities that contribute positively to society and the environment.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-10-01","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Swachhata Pakhwada was organized on October 1st as an important cleanliness initiative aligned with the Swachh Bharat Abhiyan. The event was graced by the presence of the AICTE Chairperson, who delivered an inspiring speech emphasizing the importance of hygiene, cleanliness, and social responsibility. Volunteers, along with Rotaract members and students, actively collaborated to clean the college premises and surrounding areas. The program aimed to promote cleanliness on campus while strengthening community spirit and encouraging students to participate in socially responsible initiatives.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/c7RxcPYKNao6khotp_DhI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jsB2lwRwvvjcLihSt6z_8","name":"T Shirt for Smiles","slNo":11,"place":"Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/lAbdsx_zgvSqXva-RAobx.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the T-Shirt for Smiles and Orphanage Visit, I gained a deeper sense of empathy and social responsibility by directly interacting with the children and contributing to their well-being. The experience helped me understand the importance of giving back to society and supporting underprivileged communities through small but meaningful efforts. I also developed stronger communication and interpersonal skills by engaging with the children and participating in the activities conducted during the visit. Overall, the initiative gave me a sense of personal satisfaction and emotional growth, while reinforcing the value of kindness, service, and community involvement.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"T-Shirt for Smiles and Orphanage Visit was a community service initiative organized by Kannada Sangha on 07-07-2024. As part of this activity, a group of students visited Prajakarana Seva Charitable Nonatha Ashram located at Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru. The visit aimed to support and bring happiness to the children residing in the orphanage through meaningful interaction, participation in activities, and contributions in the form of donations. The initiative encouraged students to actively engage in social responsibility and contribute positively to the welfare of underprivileged children.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/zIT5AnnHaiisr14HzeELe.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7fjwX_7kB7ZYPDCI-P4zV","name":" SDG PHOTOGRAPHY 2024","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/tFbfG6I2AeOyn95sH_rFh.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"I enhanced my creativity and photography skills by capturing meaningful visuals that represent real-world issues aligned with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The competition helped me develop stronger observation and storytelling ability, as I learned to express social and environmental messages through impactful photographs. It also increased my awareness of SDG-related challenges and encouraged me to think critically about how youth can contribute to positive change. Overall, the activity gave me confidence in presenting my perspective creatively, improved my visual communication skills, and motivated me to engage more actively in socially responsible initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Organized by the IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter,it is an SDG-themed photography competition titled “Through the Eyes of Youth!” designed to encourage students to creatively capture and present real-world perspectives through photography. The competition provides a platform for youth to express their interpretation of the world, focusing on themes aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Open to all RVCE students and students from other IUCEE Student Chapters, the event promotes creativity, awareness, and storytelling through visual media. Participants are invited to submit impactful photographs that reflect social, environmental, or developmental issues, thereby using art as a tool for communication and change. The competition also includes an exciting prize pool of ₹3500, motivating students to actively participate, showcase talent, and contribute towards SDG awareness through their unique lens.","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/_qxXUQ_B1eBHxwaLJB0qB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TfTTVaviNnAlVyR2i3qti","name":" SDG PHOTOGRAPHY 2023","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/xoARvnW6FthwttbXFgcM7.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"I enhanced my creativity and photography skills by capturing meaningful visuals that represent real-world issues aligned with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The competition helped me develop stronger observation and storytelling ability, as I learned to express social and environmental messages through impactful photographs. It also increased my awareness of SDG-related challenges and encouraged me to think critically about how youth can contribute to positive change. Overall, the activity gave me confidence in presenting my perspective creatively, improved my visual communication skills, and motivated me to engage more actively in socially responsible initiatives.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Organized by the IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter,it is an SDG-themed photography competition titled “Through the Eyes of Youth!” designed to encourage students to creatively capture and present real-world perspectives through photography. The competition provides a platform for youth to express their interpretation of the world, focusing on themes aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Open to all RVCE students and students from other IUCEE Student Chapters, the event promotes creativity, awareness, and storytelling through visual media. Participants are invited to submit impactful photographs that reflect social, environmental, or developmental issues, thereby using art as a tool for communication and change. The competition also includes an exciting prize pool of ₹3500, motivating students to actively participate, showcase talent, and contribute towards SDG awareness through their unique lens.","aicteMapping":"5","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/xSUiaIwl7O6zLzpMvyluE.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tBkoApMvoZedcIoU6kF7x","name":"UTPT INDIA QUIZ 2024","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/WLCZB9c2LB1zYYlR_BURH.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/nojwB4c4RpZCl-cE9E7Gu.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"As an outcome of participating in the Indi-Genius Quiz, I enhanced my knowledge of Indian culture, history, and traditions through a competitive and interactive learning experience. The event helped improve my critical thinking, recall ability, and time-based decision-making skills while working collaboratively in a team. Participation also strengthened my confidence in expressing ideas and responding under pressure during quiz rounds. Overall, the quiz served as an enriching academic and cultural experience that combined learning, teamwork, and co-curricular development.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Indi-Genius Quiz, organized by RV Quiz Corp, was conducted as part of UTPT 2024 on 7th June 2024 at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The quiz was designed to celebrate India’s rich cultural, historical, and traditional heritage through an engaging and competitive format. The event covered a wide range of topics including Indian history, Mughal architecture, epics such as the Mahabharata and Ramayana, festivals, regional cuisines, and cultural traditions. Conducted in teams of up to three members, the quiz provided participants with an interactive platform to test their knowledge, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills while experiencing the diverse essence of India in an intellectually stimulating environment.","aicteMapping":"15","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3e1d4e6a-0629-4986-a7eb-0831c3d15243/ds3vgUEU4Is6_FiUYT2Z4.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Prof. Rajatha","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":" ","designation":" "},"evaluator2":{"name":" ","designation":" "}}}', '2026-01-29 18:29:58.360848+00', '2026-01-30 17:46:23.451008+00'), ('b1d46423-103c-4693-8178-bad744a02b57', '830ba299-8740-4bb5-9878-17f0ca2136ad', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22ME080","name":"Pranav Chandrashekhar Deshpande","period":"2022-2026","department":"Mechanical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"-V0q7W-P0-1msslemCIK-","name":"Rotaract Fastrek 1","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary outcome of my participation was contributing to a significant charitable initiative categorized under the area of \"Economic and Community Development\" . The specific goal of this project was to generate support and provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases . By dedicating my time to this cause alongside over 100 volunteers, I contributed to the club''s mission of creating a tangible, lasting impact on society and fostering a strong sense of solidarity . As a formal recognition of my active involvement and the successful completion of this social service activity, I was awarded 5 AICTE Activity Points .","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":6,"description":"I actively participated in \"Fast-Trek,\" a flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE (sponsored by Rotary Bangalore South) on February 12, 2023, situated at the scenic Huthridurga Hills (Huthridurga Betta) . The activity commenced early in the morning at 7:30 AM, where I joined other enthusiastic participants to board the designated transport to the trekking location . Upon arrival, I attended a briefing where essential safety instructions and event details were provided to ensure a secure experience before we embarked on the trek . The expedition itself was a memorable journey through the hills, offering a unique opportunity to engage with the environment and fellow students . throughout the duration of the event, the organizers provided logistical support, including breakfast and lunch at the trek site, ensuring the well-being of all participants .","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/830ba299-8740-4bb5-9878-17f0ca2136ad/O4wmNNbDdmUvqdhwpmUlf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:09:48.094381+00', '2026-01-30 04:29:28.540035+00'), ('b20ef6d4-d683-497d-9aae-abe6f198e526', '615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI052","name":"Shreesha Kumara K","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"dop1ax8-40LY9cboMR6f3","name":"Tanuja Screening","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/rkZmjWOEAzQA15qazfQ0C.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"From the movie Tanuja, I learned the importance of empathy, courage, and understanding the struggles faced by others in society. The film highlighted how human values and moral strength play a major role in overcoming difficult situations. It made me reflect on the responsibilities we have as individuals to support and respect others. Overall, the screening inspired me to think beyond myself and develop a more socially conscious and compassionate attitude.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized a movie screening of Tanuja as part of its social awareness activities. The event aimed to promote moral values, empathy, and responsibility among students through an engaging medium.\\n\\nTanuja highlights important social themes and encourages students to reflect on real-life challenges and human values. The screening helped create awareness and inspired students to think beyond academics and understand society better.\\n\\nMany students participated actively, and the movie served as an effective tool to spread meaningful messages. The activity supported the objectives of NSS by fostering social consciousness and motivating students towards positive community involvement.","aicteMapping":"Spreading the awareness of competitive exam","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rITQOuIrjO3D-nvig4-m0","name":"Campus Cleanup","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/L_OPOaVVIVMiaB-M3T12f.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Campus Cleanup drive resulted in a cleaner and more hygienic campus environment while creating awareness among students about the importance of cleanliness and proper waste disposal. It encouraged students to take responsibility for their surroundings and develop eco-friendly habits. The activity also promoted teamwork, discipline, and active participation in community service, reflecting the true spirit of NSS and contributing towards a healthier and greener campus.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-13","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized a Campus Cleanup drive to promote cleanliness, hygiene, and environmental responsibility among students. The activity aimed to create awareness about the importance of maintaining a clean and green campus.\\n\\nStudents actively participated in cleaning the surroundings, collecting waste, and ensuring proper disposal of litter in designated bins. The drive helped in improving the campus environment and encouraged everyone to adopt clean habits in daily life.\\n\\nThis initiative supported the Swachh Bharat mission and reflected the NSS spirit of service and community participation. Overall, the campus cleanup was a meaningful activity that instilled a sense of discipline, teamwork, and responsibility towards maintaining a healthy campus.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pYWx5u3zTgDGShEqRiz2L","name":"Mera pehla vote desh ke liye ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/BqhVLIgso2LPiEKMr9ckH.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The “Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” pledge activity created awareness among students about the importance of voting and active participation in democracy. It encouraged first-time voters to exercise their right responsibly and ethically. The initiative helped instill a sense of civic duty, patriotism, and commitment towards contributing to the nation’s development through informed and meaningful voting.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized a pledge-taking activity under the campaign “Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” to encourage students to participate actively in the democratic process. The objective of the event was to create awareness about the importance of voting and to inspire first-time voters to exercise their right responsibly.\\n\\nStudents took an oath to vote ethically, uphold democratic values, and contribute towards the progress of the nation. The pledge emphasized the role of youth in strengthening democracy and promoting informed decision-making during elections.\\n\\nThis initiative helped instill a sense of civic duty, patriotism, and responsibility among students, making it a meaningful step towards building an active and aware citizenry.","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RYpZkDCfWvm6ACEW-pNNL","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/_QZpGUb4RNNcVTkBH_s7m.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon helped promote awareness about physical fitness, healthy living, and social responsibility among students. It encouraged active participation, discipline, and teamwork while fostering a sense of unity and community service. The event motivated students to adopt a healthier lifestyle and reinforced the NSS spirit of contributing positively towards society.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized Utsarga Marathon, an event organized to promote health, fitness, and social awareness among students and the community. The marathon aimed to encourage a healthy lifestyle while spreading important messages of unity, discipline, and service.\\n\\nStudents took part with great enthusiasm, showcasing energy, teamwork, and commitment. The event also served as a platform to raise awareness about social responsibility and the importance of contributing towards a better society.\\n\\nThe Utsarga Marathon was a meaningful initiative that not only promoted physical well-being but also strengthened the spirit of community participation and NSS values among students.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"37E10wwPRn2HMqbcHaaAH","name":"Road Safety","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/OUfRpDdyAxYCLw6CfjcvS.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/Tp_h__LVnbClvO-AXSylO.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"The Road Safety Awareness program helped students understand the importance of following traffic rules and practicing safe behavior on roads. It also provided valuable knowledge on how to respond during accidents, handle injured individuals carefully, and offer basic first aid until professional help arrives. The activity encouraged students to become responsible and compassionate citizens, ready to support others in emergency situations and contribute towards a safer community.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized a Road Safety Awareness program to educate students and the public about the importance of traffic rules and safe travel practices. The activity aimed to promote responsible behavior on roads and reduce the risk of accidents.\\n\\nDuring the program, volunteers and participants were taught essential road safety measures such as wearing helmets, using seat belts, following speed limits, and avoiding distracted driving. Special emphasis was given on how to respond during road accidents. Students were trained on how to handle injured people carefully, provide basic first aid, and offer immediate support until medical help arrives. The session encouraged students to help accident victims with confidence and compassion.\\n\\nThis initiative helped create awareness, built a sense of responsibility, and motivated students to contribute towards a safer society by being alert, supportive, and socially conscious citizens.","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"H_sBT76XfAI-hzh2bX2oT","name":"Mega Plantation @ Hosadurga","slNo":6,"place":"Hosadurga","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/MbYte0V3BPXDrQ7f1W2fk.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/zLP-O4cHjn29qvRqvmw5d.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Mega Plantation Drive at Hosadurga resulted in increased awareness about environmental conservation and the importance of afforestation. It encouraged students to actively contribute towards creating a greener and healthier ecosystem. The activity promoted teamwork, responsibility, and commitment to protecting nature by planting saplings that will help reduce pollution, improve biodiversity, and maintain ecological balance in the long run.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-09","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) along with Indriya Foundation organized Mega Plantation Drive at Hosadurga as part of its environmental sustainability and community service initiatives. The activity aimed to promote greenery, increase tree cover, and spread awareness about the importance of protecting the environment.\\n\\nNSS volunteers actively took part in planting saplings in the designated area and learned the significance of afforestation in reducing pollution, conserving biodiversity, and maintaining ecological balance. The drive also encouraged students to take responsibility for nature and contribute towards building a healthier and greener future.\\n\\nThe Mega Plantation program at Hosadurga was a meaningful step towards environmental conservation and reflected the NSS commitment to social and ecological well-being.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PLWLkjEAGYaFJC8tkuuc3","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/vz8nNSne9i-WX_3WyN5VX.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp organized by Rotaract RVCE successfully promoted the importance of voluntary blood donation and helped meet the medical needs of patients in emergencies. It encouraged students to contribute towards saving lives through a noble cause. The activity fostered a spirit of compassion, social responsibility, and community service among participants while creating awareness about the value of regular and safe blood donation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) successfully organized a Blood Donation Camp as part of its social service and humanitarian initiatives. The camp aimed to encourage voluntary blood donation and create awareness about the importance of donating blood to save lives.\\n\\nStudents, faculty, and staff actively participated in the camp with great enthusiasm and a spirit of service. Medical professionals ensured that the donation process was safe, hygienic, and well-organized. Volunteers assisted in registration, guidance, and post-donation care, making the event smooth and effective.\\n\\nThe camp highlighted the value of compassion, community support, and the role of youth in contributing to society. Overall, the blood donation drive was a meaningful initiative that helped support healthcare needs and reflected the commitment of Rotaract RVCE towards social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sYjjXzr8JtZFRkZavAnTC","name":"Yoga Day","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/-1RSJlmsWLzlwTC7S2Jaw.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Yoga Day program helped students understand the importance of yoga for maintaining physical health and mental peace. It encouraged participants to adopt a healthier lifestyle by practicing asanas, breathing exercises, and meditation regularly. The activity promoted stress relief, improved concentration, and overall well-being, while reinforcing the NSS objective of holistic development among students.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-21","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized International Yoga Day to promote physical fitness, mental well-being, and a healthy lifestyle among students. The event aimed to create awareness about the importance of yoga in maintaining balance between body and mind.\\n\\nStudents actively participated in the yoga session, where they practiced various asanas, breathing exercises, and meditation techniques under proper guidance. The program highlighted the role of yoga in reducing stress, improving concentration, and enhancing overall health.\\n\\nThe celebration of Yoga Day was a meaningful initiative that encouraged students to adopt yoga as a regular practice and reflected NSS’s commitment towards holistic development and wellness.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LhovlcyvWrjiJJH0sQ8gm","name":"Yoga Day","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/FfJVM_E2hvR_54fzlg1Bj.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Yoga Day program organized by Rotaract RVCE helped students recognize the importance of yoga for physical fitness and mental well-being. It encouraged participants to practice yoga regularly to reduce stress, improve flexibility, and enhance concentration. The activity promoted a healthy and balanced lifestyle while reflecting Rotaract’s commitment towards holistic development and wellness among students.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-21","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized a Yoga Day program to promote physical fitness, mental wellness, and a healthy lifestyle among students. The event aimed to spread awareness about the benefits of yoga in maintaining balance between body and mind.\\n\\nParticipants took part in guided yoga sessions that included various asanas, breathing exercises, and relaxation techniques. The program emphasized the importance of yoga in reducing stress, improving flexibility, enhancing concentration, and boosting overall health.\\n\\nThe Yoga Day celebration was a meaningful initiative by Rotaract RVCE that encouraged students to incorporate yoga into their daily routine and highlighted the club’s commitment towards well-being and community development.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZsvBjpVPHEcq65tnmKl1E","name":"Kannada Sangha T-Shirt","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/LH-suMeq5DHAwYmxvLifo.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The purchase of the Kannada Sangha event T-shirt helped raise funds to support the welfare of children at the orphanage. It encouraged students to actively contribute towards a social cause through donations and meaningful participation. This initiative promoted a sense of responsibility, unity, and community service among students while supporting charitable efforts for the underprivileged.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"As part of the community service initiative organized by Kannada Sangha, RVCE, students actively contributed by purchasing the official event T-shirts. This initiative was undertaken to support the charitable activities conducted during the visit to Prajwalana Seva Charitable Trust orphanage.\\n\\nThe funds collected through the T-shirt sale were utilized to support the children residing in the orphanage by contributing towards their needs and welfare. By buying the T-shirt, students showed their involvement and commitment towards the cause and extended their support through donations.\\n\\nThis activity encouraged student participation in social service and reflected the spirit of unity, responsibility, and contribution towards community development.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-eGhMoITwtm5FRsZ88sXC","name":"Azadi ka Kalotsav","slNo":11,"place":"Manekshaw Parade Ground","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/yodYsPX8kvPqoK736A31c.png"],"endDate":"2024-08-15","duration":22,"outcomes":"The Azadi Ka Kalotsav celebration helped instill a sense of patriotism, unity, and national pride among students. It encouraged active participation in cultural activities that highlighted the importance of Independence Day and the sacrifices of freedom fighters. The event promoted cultural awareness, teamwork, and responsibility, reflecting the NSS objective of holistic development and nation-building among youth.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-25","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized Azadi Ka Kalotsav as part of the Independence Day celebrations to promote patriotism, cultural unity, and national pride among students. The event aimed to commemorate the spirit of freedom and honor the sacrifices made by freedom fighters.\\n\\nStudents actively participated in various cultural programs such as patriotic songs, dances, skits, and speeches highlighting the importance of independence and national integrity. The celebration provided a platform for students to showcase their talents while spreading messages of unity, responsibility, and love for the nation.\\n\\nAzadi Ka Kalotsav was a vibrant and meaningful initiative that strengthened cultural values, encouraged student involvement, and reflected the NSS commitment towards nation-building and holistic development.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gJTjkduQ7gNq0p9p9P86a","name":"Eye Donation Fortnight","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/v-y_4HxA61CLCXFQG518p.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-08","duration":12,"outcomes":"The Eye Donation Fortnight program successfully created awareness among students about the importance of eye donation and its role in restoring vision for the visually impaired. It helped clear misconceptions, encouraged students to pledge for this noble cause, and promoted values of compassion and social responsibility. The activity inspired participants to spread awareness and contribute towards building a more humane and supportive society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) observed Eye Donation Fortnight to create awareness about the importance of eye donation and to encourage students to support this noble cause. The activity aimed to educate participants on how eye donation can help restore vision and improve the lives of visually impaired individuals.\\n\\nDuring the program, students were informed about the process of eye donation, common myths, and the significant impact one donor can make by giving the gift of sight. Awareness messages were shared to motivate individuals to pledge for eye donation and spread the message within society.\\n\\nThis initiative helped promote humanitarian values, compassion, and social responsibility among students, contributing towards building an aware and supportive community.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"x7L8OVxg3a7vzP3lAmslB","name":"Fistfull","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/mcIbpJQKIh-INCHHFbGgE.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The FistFull initiative successfully collected food grain donations that were distributed to NGOs supporting needy individuals. It encouraged students to contribute towards a noble cause and understand the importance of helping society through simple yet impactful actions. The activity fostered unity, empathy, and a strong sense of social commitment among participants, reflecting the true spirit of Rotaract and community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE), in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, successfully organized “FistFull”, a meaningful community service initiative conducted from 15th to 29th November. The program aimed to support local NGOs by encouraging students to contribute essential food grains.\\n\\nStudents were invited to donate 2–5 kg of rice or pulses, which were collected and distributed to underprivileged communities. This initiative highlighted how small contributions from individuals can collectively create a significant impact in addressing food insecurity.\\n\\nThrough FistFull, Rotaract RVCE promoted the values of compassion, social responsibility, and community welfare while motivating students to actively participate in service-driven activities.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2bSSbHZVh3CyuV-YIdqDw","name":"Vikasit Bharat Quiz","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/eML0InPMziH-3UuUxrgIM.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Vikasit Bharat Quiz successfully increased students’ awareness about India’s development journey and future aspirations. It encouraged active learning, critical thinking, and participation in nation-building initiatives. The event motivated students to stay informed about national progress and inspired them to contribute positively towards the vision of a stronger and self-reliant India.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The NSS unit of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) organized the Vikasit Bharat Quiz as an awareness and knowledge-based initiative to encourage students to learn about India’s development goals and national progress. The quiz aimed to enhance understanding of the Viksit Bharat vision, focusing on topics such as innovation, economy, governance, sustainability, and India’s future roadmap.\\n\\nStudents actively participated with enthusiasm, making the event interactive and educational. The quiz provided a platform for students to test their knowledge, improve awareness about current national initiatives, and develop a sense of responsibility towards contributing to the nation’s growth.\\n\\nThis activity supported the objective of creating informed and socially aware youth committed to building a developed India.","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1xtOz3sGwlkIwhzgfexbh","name":"Fistfull","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/615e1ce8-3bb6-4a3b-aae4-fcd1380981d6/5PFlRHduIccoT7MF0dqfD.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"The FistFull initiative successfully provided large-scale nutritional support to multiple beneficiary organizations, ensuring sustained food assistance for vulnerable groups. It created strong awareness among students about food insecurity and inspired them to participate in meaningful social service. The activity promoted empathy, teamwork, and responsibility, highlighting how collective efforts can bring positive change in society. Overall, the initiative reflected the true spirit of community service and strengthened student involvement in nation-building activities.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE), supported by Rotary Bangalore Spandana, successfully organized FistFull, a community service initiative focused on combating food insecurity. The project encouraged students to donate essential food grains such as rice and dal, proving that even small individual contributions can collectively create a large social impact.\\n\\nThe event witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, who together collected around 4370 kg of rice and 2516 kg of dal. These food grains were distributed to various institutions including Hanuman Temple daily mass feeding program, Pruthvi Foundation Blind Boys Hostel, Amrutavani Vridh Seva Samithi, Sai Ashraya Hospital, Sai Sattgana Sangraha Trust School, and Nelo Foundation.\\n\\nThrough this initiative, students actively contributed to supporting daily meal programs for children, elderly people, patients, and other disadvantaged communities, reinforcing RVCE’s commitment towards social welfare and service.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:41:48.438631+00', '2026-01-30 10:16:46.946298+00'), ('b2a4dd24-bcbe-47db-ae52-738ce4fdac02', '2d90e56d-a675-48a9-b444-2a09e0f5e8d4', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS040","name":"Obbu Venkata Sai Nithin","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"AHvN1eJMrvIHFIF914IYy","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth” – SDG Photo Competition","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2d90e56d-a675-48a9-b444-2a09e0f5e8d4/oLAHR0xs3Y2wn_kymEkCS.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2d90e56d-a675-48a9-b444-2a09e0f5e8d4/UtO8nz9j4AKQmaSrYVNZy.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-01-13","duration":891,"outcomes":"Increased student awareness and engagement with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)\\n\\nEncouraged creativity and social responsibility through visual storytelling\\n\\nStrengthened student leadership, teamwork, and event management skills among organizers\\n\\nPromoted a culture of sustainability and social consciousness across the campus","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":8,"description":"A student-organized SDG-themed photo competition was conducted to raise awareness about sustainability and global development goals among campus students. The event encouraged creative expression, received large participation, and was successfully executed through coordinated efforts in publicity, content verification, and fair evaluation.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/2d90e56d-a675-48a9-b444-2a09e0f5e8d4/3JPE1zV3-8a1m_zMtSgkq.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Rekha B.S","designation":"Assistant Professo