inspired \\nresponsible citizenship, and motivated students to actively participate in the electoral process, \\nfostering a sense of national duty and commitment toward building a strong and inclusive \\ndemocracy","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":96,"description":"I participated in the AICTE initiative “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” by taking the official \\npledge to uphold democratic values and exercise my right to vote responsibly. The activity \\nemphasized the importance of informed voting, civic duties, and active youth participation in \\nstrengthening democracy, while encouraging first-time voters to contribute meaningfully to the \\nnation’s electoral process","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/SQQytWElfW2w6nt1N1io9.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"T4pypzFrebfegXIINprmE","name":"Say No To Drugs Pledge (NSS","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"The activity increased awareness about the harmful effects of drug abuse, reinforced responsible \\nbehavior among students, and strengthened collective commitment toward maintaining a safe, \\ndrug-free campus while fostering social responsibility and personal accountability","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-07","hoursSpent":72,"description":"I participated in the mandatory Drug Awareness E-Pledge conducted by NSS RVCE under the \\ndirectives of VTU and the Narcotics Control Bureau. By taking the online pledge, I committed \\nto promoting a drug-free campus, supporting awareness initiatives, and encouraging peers to \\nstand against drug abuse to help create a safe, healthy, and responsible academic environment","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/VRjEyE5vdUJb2spsaZhmy.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"W6E3tLf7SMgfmLNZQ89xN","name":"Eye Donation Fortnigh","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-08-28","duration":4,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness about eye donation, promoted empathy and social \\nresponsibility, and inspired participants to advocate for organ donation, contributing toward a \\nmeaningful cause that can restore vision and improve the quality of life for visually impaired \\nindividuals","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-25","hoursSpent":96,"description":"Eye Donation Fortnight – Sight Ambassador Initiative\\nI participated in the Eye Donation Fortnight campaign organized by NSS RVCE by registering \\nas a Sight Ambassador and pledging to donate my eyes after life. Through this initiative, I \\nsupported spreading awareness about eye donation, its life-changing impact, and encouraged \\nothers to consider contributing to this noble cause of restoring vision to those in need.","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/1xDAolsarsQPm36KyO2af.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IBgKLKt91O5ePlWQ7GnoH","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation promoted physical fitness, social awareness, and empathy. It provided an \\nopportunity to contribute to a meaningful cause, reinforced the value of community service, and \\ninspired a sense of responsibility toward supporting underprivileged children through collective \\naction","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":24,"description":"I participated in UTSARGA ’24, a charity marathon organized by NSS RVCE with the theme \\n“Help a Child, Change the World.” The event aimed to support underprivileged children through \\na social cause–driven run, encouraging fitness, compassion, and collective responsibility while \\ncontributing toward positive social impact","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/TnUK6pd_L6Grl3xfbsT3r.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nwTYj3YUZXCxoLpTCdsWN","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation strengthened my sense of social responsibility and empathy. It contributed directly \\nto healthcare support, raised awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation, and \\nencouraged a culture of service, humanity, and active community involvement among students.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-24","hoursSpent":24,"description":" I participated as a blood donor in the Blood Donation Camp organized by the Rotaract Club of \\nRVCE. By voluntarily donating blood, I contributed to saving lives and supporting healthcare \\nneeds. The initiative emphasized social responsibility, compassion, and the importance of \\nregular blood donation for community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/Ry-TWd0tQstxpx7QEu1nb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"SI0QaHFsmVIeYQJTAee-G","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation strengthened my sense of social responsibility and empathy. It contributed directly \\nto healthcare support, raised awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation, and \\nencouraged a culture of service, humanity, and active community involvement among students.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":24,"description":"I participated as a blood donor in the Blood Donation Camp organized by the Rotaract Club of \\nRVCE. By voluntarily donating blood, I contributed to saving lives and supporting healthcare \\nneeds. The initiative emphasized social responsibility, compassion, and the importance of \\nregular blood donation for community welfare","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/A6857MdKKMDpqMgnpEgkd.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jrfl_9bEgzpKj5IBOTrfc","name":"Marathon","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-12-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation promoted physical fitness, social awareness, and empathy. It provided an \\nopportunity to contribute to a meaningful cause, reinforced the value of community service, and \\ninspired a sense of responsibility toward supporting underprivileged children through collective \\naction","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-12-05","hoursSpent":24,"description":"I participated in UTSARGA ’23, a charity marathon organized by NSS RVCE with the theme \\n“Help a Child, Change the World.” The event aimed to support underprivileged children through \\na social cause–driven run, encouraging fitness, compassion, and collective responsibility while \\ncontributing toward positive social impact.","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/QUo0nUnCVAR2_PWbgeHrF.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8Oz-jG3ouM6D_tMj5AkOJ","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation strengthened my sense of social responsibility and empathy. It contributed directly \\nto healthcare support, raised awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation, and \\nencouraged a culture of service, humanity, and active community involvement among students","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-21","hoursSpent":24,"description":"I participated as a blood donor in the Blood Donation Camp organized by the Rotaract Club of \\nRVCE. By voluntarily donating blood, I contributed to saving lives and supporting healthcare \\nneeds. The initiative emphasized social responsibility, compassion, and the importance of \\nregular blood donation for community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/HJj9ioY323NeySEilMb0M.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"si3DKkpY8BM1APXLW3miM","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation fostered social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement. It helped \\nraise awareness about educational inequality, encouraged volunteering for social causes, and \\nprovided a rewarding experience by contributing directly to the learning and development of \\nunderprivileged children","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":168,"description":"I participated in Project Pustak, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, which aimed to \\nprovide educational kits to underprivileged children. The kits included essential school supplies, \\nbooks, and learning tools, helping support the education and growth of children in need. \\nMy involvement included contributing to the preparation and distribution of these kits and \\ninteracting with the children.","aicteMapping":"Social Cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/kCrf6JsElcP7MHr6ANSWw.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1JWVWR2XLZs53ItiXv00Q","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE ","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-06","duration":6,"outcomes":"Participation nurtured empathy, social responsibility, and community engagement. It provided \\na meaningful experience by contributing directly to children’s education, encouraged \\nvolunteering for social causes, and reinforced the importance of equitable access to learning \\nresources","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-01","hoursSpent":168,"description":"Project Pustak – Educational Kit Donation Drive\\nI participated in Project Pustak, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, by visiting schools to \\ndonate educational kits to underprivileged children. The kits included essential books, school \\nsupplies, and learning tools, aimed at supporting education and fostering opportunities for \\ngrowth among children in need.","aicteMapping":"Social cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f68c4e89-b410-4635-a1ba-c29157294142/EFZxUN0QAlgwwq1eBeL0K.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 21:51:23.569659+00', '2026-02-01 22:49:18.283008+00'), ('b4b226ec-1d40-44a3-974b-dde9ab3d9713', '38e98b03-bdae-4d56-978a-7e26f63edef0', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV107","name":"Sudeep R Sirur","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:00:48.718505+00', '2026-01-29 16:00:48.718505+00'), ('b602a70b-204c-450d-9cbb-9f62e99fab0d', '053e2140-0fcd-4e5f-a453-d9ed14337db7', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 14:03:56.648293+00', '2026-01-30 05:11:04.349128+00'), ('b606747f-d548-468b-b055-25bc5630ec5e', 'e421e5a7-e07d-4fba-a888-61bc448363aa', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI053","name":"Shreya Kulkarni","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"ff4FwCkr8AoLZ6YyKLyUw","name":"NSS UTSARGA Marathon","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully raised funds for social welfare activities while promoting a culture of fitness and community participation among students. The event strengthened the values of teamwork, leadership, and volunteerism as NSS members efficiently managed registration, logistics, crowd management, and awareness campaigns. Participants gained a sense of fulfillment by contributing to meaningful social causes, and the initiative helped build a stronger connection between the institution and the community. The successful execution of the marathon showcased the commitment of students toward social development and motivated more volunteers to engage in future NSS activities.","semester":"1","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Description of the activity\\tAn NSS Utsarga Marathon was organized as a fundraising initiative to support various social causes and welfare activities. The event aimed to create awareness about health, fitness, and community service while encouraging students and citizens to contribute toward societal development. Participants from different departments and local community members enthusiastically joined the marathon, showcasing unity, discipline, and social responsibility. The funds collected through registrations and sponsorships were allocated to support future NSS outreach activities and charitable initiatives, reinforcing the spirit of service among youth.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dEHXhE6A8sRYk5Qn752dA","name":"NSS Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp witnessed enthusiastic participation from students and staff, resulting in successful collection of blood units to support medical and emergency healthcare needs in the community. The activity helped in creating awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its role in saving lives. It also strengthened teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills among student volunteers. Participants gained firsthand experience in community service and developed a sense of empathy, civic duty, and social responsibility.","semester":"1","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"An NSS Blood Donation Camp was organized at the college premises near the Biotechnology Engineering Quadrangle. The primary objective of the event was to promote voluntary blood donation awareness among students and faculty and contribute to society by supporting emergency medical needs.\\nThe event was conducted in collaboration with a recognized blood bank/medical team, who managed the donation process and ensured proper safety and hygiene protocols.\\nStudents actively participated in various responsibilities such as registration, assisting donors, guiding participants, spreading awareness, and maintaining discipline at the venue. The initiative aimed to inspire the youth to contribute to life-saving social causes and encourage a culture of social responsibility on campus.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sklnBpI0l7dVIYNqhCtUe","name":"NSS UTSARGA Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon successfully brought together students and the community, generating widespread awareness and encouraging participation in social welfare-oriented initiatives. The event not only promoted fitness and healthy lifestyle habits but also reinforced teamwork, time management, and leadership skills among student volunteers. Participants experienced a deep sense of achievement by contributing to a meaningful purpose that extended beyond the race itself. Through this initiative, funds and awareness were raised to support future NSS activities and community service projects. Overall, the marathon strengthened the culture of volunteerism, social awareness, and public engagement within the college community.","semester":"3","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon was conducted as a major student-driven initiative aimed at promoting physical fitness, youth involvement in social causes, and spreading awareness about community welfare. The marathon served not only as a sporting event but also as a platform to encourage social responsibility by motivating participants to contribute toward noble causes. Students, faculty members, and community participants took part enthusiastically, reflecting unity and collective purpose. I actively contributed as a participant in the event by assisting in coordination tasks such as participant registration, route management, providing refreshments, cheering runners, and ensuring smooth execution throughout the event. The marathon symbolized the spirit of youth leadership and reinforced the idea that social development can be driven through sports-based engagement.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"klXbsrs3nZYO8AU9wkyWX","name":"Rotaract FIST FULL","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The initiative witnessed an enthusiastic response from the student community, with active participation from over 1,750 students. The collective effort resulted in the collection of more than 6,700 kg of rice and over 800 kg of toor dal, which were directed toward supporting hunger relief efforts. The successful execution of the project demonstrated the power of collective action and showcased how small individual contributions can lead to substantial social impact. Overall, “Fist Full” strengthened the culture of volunteering at RVCE and reaffirmed the institution’s commitment to societal development and humanitarian values.","semester":"4","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“Fist Full” was a social outreach initiative undertaken by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from November 15 to 29. The primary objective of the project was to address hunger and food insecurity by motivating students to donate essential food grain, either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. To ensure smooth participation, daily collection drives were organized in the Civil Department, making the process convenient and well-coordinated. Through this initiative, students were sensitized to social responsibility and encouraged to contribute meaningfully to community welfare through simple yet impactful actions.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pcFck8SoqhegGJI5mT33s","name":"FAST TREK 3.0","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Fast Trek 3.0 achieved significant success by creating a meaningful impact on both the environment and the participants. The cleanliness drive contributed to preserving the natural beauty of Narayangiri Hills, while also instilling a strong sense of environmental responsibility among students. The event encouraged collaboration, leadership, and teamwork, leading to enhanced bonding and shared experiences among participants. Overall, Fast Trek 3.0 left participants feeling accomplished and inspired, and it set a high benchmark for future Rotaract events by effectively combining adventure, social impact, and community engagement.","semester":"4","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fast Trek 3.0, the flagship event of the Rotaract Club of RVCE, was successfully conducted on 12th January 2025 at the scenic Narayangiri Hills. The event brought together over 500 enthusiastic participants from the college for an adventure-driven trekking experience combined with a purposeful cleanliness drive. Beginning early in the morning, participants traversed the rugged trails of Narayangiri Hills while actively engaging in cleaning the surroundings by collecting litter and promoting environmental awareness. The initiative effectively blended outdoor adventure with social responsibility, reinforcing the club’s commitment to environmental conservation and eco-conscious practices. Alongside its environmental focus, the trek fostered strong team spirit, as participants supported and motivated one another throughout the journey.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IM-ECojdqNZCKqo2DJaKm","name":"GENESIS Outreach Program ","slNo":6,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The Genesis Outreach Program successfully bridged the gap between theoretical classroom learning and real-world engineering applications, fostering early interest in STEM fields among school students. Participants gained hands-on exposure to robotics and engineering principles, which enhanced their curiosity, engagement, and conceptual understanding. The initiative reached a large and diverse group of students across multiple schools, creating a meaningful educational impact. Beyond the workshops themselves, the project demonstrated the dedication, teamwork, and organizational skills of Team Astra Robotics, with significant effort invested in planning, kit preparation, and execution. Overall, the outreach program strengthened the culture of STEM education and contributed positively to community engagement and technical awareness.","semester":"5","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Genesis Outreach Program was conducted by Team Astra Robotics, a student-led robotics research club, with the objective of inspiring school students to explore engineering and robotics through hands-on learning. As part of the initiative, interactive workshops were organized across five institutions in Bangalore, including VVS Bangalore, MES Kishore Kendra (Malleshwaram), Vidya Mandir Independent PU College (Malleshwaram), St. Claret (Jalahalli), and Base PU College. Each workshop was carefully structured to introduce core engineering concepts such as electronics, embedded systems, automation, and control systems. The sessions emphasized practical demonstrations, guided experiments, and problem-solving activities, and were conducted for approximately 7 hours per day over two days at each school, following extensive planning, outreach, and preparation by the team.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"L424mlxaxf_AjgzSW3AnM","name":"NSS UTSARGA Marathon","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon successfully brought together students and the community, generating widespread awareness and encouraging participation in social welfare-oriented initiatives. The event not only promoted fitness and healthy lifestyle habits but also reinforced teamwork, time management, and leadership skills among student volunteers. Participants experienced a deep sense of achievement by contributing to a meaningful purpose that extended beyond the race itself. Through this initiative, funds and awareness were raised to support future NSS activities and community service projects. Overall, the marathon strengthened the culture of volunteerism, social awareness, and public engagement within the college community.","semester":"6","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon was conducted as a major student-driven initiative aimed at promoting physical fitness, youth involvement in social causes, and spreading awareness about community welfare. The marathon served not only as a sporting event but also as a platform to encourage social responsibility by motivating participants to contribute toward noble causes. Students, faculty members, and community participants took part enthusiastically, reflecting unity and collective purpose. I actively contributed as a participant in the event by assisting in coordination tasks such as participant registration, route management, providing refreshments, cheering runners, and ensuring smooth execution throughout the event. The marathon symbolized the spirit of youth leadership and reinforced the idea that social development can be driven through sports-based engagement.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"q3BdYFjJoKsJPZq1OwsOT","name":"Project PUSTAK","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Outcome\\tThe Rotaract Project Pustak drive successfully gathered and distributed essential educational materials to deserving students, enabling them to pursue their studies with confidence and dignity. The activity helped bridge the learning resource gap for many children while spreading awareness about the importance of education and youth contribution toward social development. Through this initiative, I gained valuable exposure to community service and developed qualities such as empathy, responsibility, and social awareness. The project strengthened collaboration between volunteers and Rotaract members and encouraged continued involvement in educational support programs. Overall, the initiative created a positive impact by promoting equal learning opportunities and inspiring young minds to value and support education for all.","semester":"6","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Rotaract Project Pustak was an educational support initiative aimed at empowering underprivileged school children by providing them with academic materials and learning resources. As part of this campaign, students and volunteers contributed funds and books to help ensure that children from economically weaker backgrounds could continue their education without facing a shortage of basic study necessities. I actively took part in this initiative by donating educational supplies/monetary support, thereby contributing to the mission of promoting literacy and learning. The project was executed in collaboration with the Rotaract Club, which coordinated the collection and distribution process across various schools and community centers. This initiative served as a reminder of the power of collective effort in shaping a brighter and more educated future for children in need.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"O4sswQX0MgQk0uA9lUzPg","name":"Rotaract FIST FULL","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The initiative witnessed an enthusiastic response from the student community, with active participation from over 1,750 students. The collective effort resulted in the collection of more than 6,700 kg of rice and over 800 kg of toor dal, which were directed toward supporting hunger relief efforts. The successful execution of the project demonstrated the power of collective action and showcased how small individual contributions can lead to substantial social impact. Overall, “Fist Full” strengthened the culture of volunteering at RVCE and reaffirmed the institution’s commitment to societal development and humanitarian values.","semester":"7","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“Fist Full” was a social outreach initiative undertaken by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from November 15 to 29. The primary objective of the project was to address hunger and food insecurity by motivating students to donate essential food grain, either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. To ensure smooth participation, daily collection drives were organized in the Civil Department, making the process convenient and well-coordinated. Through this initiative, students were sensitized to social responsibility and encouraged to contribute meaningfully to community welfare through simple yet impactful actions.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mSFekTQ0zWgBx7Fz1fr6c","name":"GENESIS Outreach Program","slNo":10,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The workshop successfully bridged the gap between theoretical knowledge and practical application, fostering early interest in engineering and robotics among students. Participants gained hands-on exposure to fundamental engineering concepts, enhancing their understanding and engagement with STEM fields. The initiative demonstrated the dedication and teamwork of Team Astra Robotics, with more than 15 hours of collective effort contributing to a well-organized and impactful outreach program. Overall, the workshop created meaningful educational impact and strengthened the institution’s outreach efforts in promoting engineering awareness at the school level.","semester":"7","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"As part of the School Genesis Outreach Program, Team Astra Robotics conducted a hands-on engineering and robotics workshop at St. Claret’s on 25th October. The workshop was held from 9:00 AM to 5:30 PM and was designed to introduce school students to core engineering concepts such as electronics, embedded systems, automation, and control systems. The sessions focused on interactive learning through practical demonstrations, guided experiments, and problem-solving activities. In addition to the workshop hours, the team invested significant time in planning, kit preparation, and logistics to ensure smooth and effective execution of the program.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 05:33:12.843432+00', '2026-01-30 06:21:01.088723+00'), ('b60c5f88-bd94-4c4d-914a-a6118974900f', 'bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI025","name":"Harsha Vardhan N","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"7x0s7fyFc3jgBI7jcy1za","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/x7kGQLYqrTJC75YFtFlHL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp witnessed enthusiastic participation from students and staff, resulting in successful collection of blood units to support medical and emergency healthcare needs in the community. The activity helped in creating awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its role in saving lives. It also strengthened teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills among student volunteers. Participants gained firsthand experience in community service and developed a sense of empathy, civic duty, and social responsibility.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":24,"description":"An NSS Blood Donation Camp was organized at the college premises near the Biotechnology Engineering Quadrangle. The primary objective of the event was to promote voluntary blood donation awareness among students and faculty and contribute to society by supporting emergency medical needs.\\nThe event was conducted in collaboration with a recognized blood bank/medical team, who managed the donation process and ensured proper safety and hygiene protocols.\\nStudents actively participated in various responsibilities such as registration, assisting donors, guiding participants, spreading awareness, and maintaining discipline at the venue. The initiative aimed to inspire the youth to contribute to life-saving social causes and encourage a culture of social responsibility on campus.","aicteMapping":"Health & Welfare Activities","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/cr2RL0MpV-IQONL6seS0V.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6uI7Y_BTYin9ZtNbwkVOA","name":"NSS Utsarga Marathon","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/c5pMwjJj7UpWi1hed4cNE.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/cN8UBqaU9-NnB5n-ObodA.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/xtLzYCIG623C0Mf4mZ1oZ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/thlZswopT_qAFDD_FJwTj.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully raised funds for social welfare activities while promoting a culture of fitness and community participation among students. The event strengthened the values of teamwork, leadership, and volunteerism as NSS members efficiently managed registration, logistics, crowd management, and awareness campaigns. Participants gained a sense of fulfillment by contributing to meaningful social causes, and the initiative helped build a stronger connection between the institution and the community. The successful execution of the marathon showcased the commitment of students toward social development and motivated more volunteers to engage in future NSS activities","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":40,"description":"An NSS Utsarga Marathon was organized as a fundraising initiative to support various social causes and welfare activities. The event aimed to create awareness about health, fitness, and community service while encouraging students and citizens to contribute toward societal development. Participants from different departments and local community members enthusiastically joined the marathon, showcasing unity, discipline, and social responsibility. The funds collected through registrations and sponsorships were allocated to support future NSS outreach activities and charitable initiatives, reinforcing the spirit of service among youth.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness & Fitness Programs","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/fisIsmkhMnc1eFkC8vq8U.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FJ0gVygQxBn3yKw8MolcU","name":"Rotaract Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/1OrOhgGCniuL19srFYfhG.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Project Pustak initiative successfully enabled the Rotaract Club to distribute vital school supplies to deserving students, ensuring that financial limitations did not hinder their learning journey. Through their contributions, participants played an active role in encouraging education and improving academic accessibility for children in need. The activity strengthened social awareness, empathy, and philanthropic values among volunteers, while fostering a sense of satisfaction and civic duty. The initiative also reinforced collaboration between student groups and social organizations, inspiring continued involvement in educational support programs.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak 2024 was a social contribution initiative in which students supported the Rotaract Club’s mission to provide underprivileged school children with essential educational supplies, including notebooks, stationery, and textbooks. The activity aimed to encourage literacy, reduce educational inequality, and support young learners from economically weaker backgrounds. Students voluntarily contributed funds and resources as part of the campaign, demonstrating responsibility toward community welfare and youth empowerment through education. This initiative promoted the spirit of giving and emphasized the importance of collective support in building a stronger, educated society.","aicteMapping":"Educational Support & Literacy Promotion","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/mMM4yGKXl5BpI972GNIMp.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"S_P65WDtcghX-l3TUG8PX","name":"NSS – Adamya Chetana Green Sunday Plantation Drive","slNo":3,"place":"Pattangere","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/pVcpipku-b7dzOhlsQPQr.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/CY-LGLyxfaWCW-t39U-HE.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/36IJE2m27GMctIGdyy9xc.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/Kp1UNJGclBdDEwCH0akKW.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/j8K5hybKrFmPzOha--CaW.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/joyyFgbzT1sAoKmf6maqx.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Green Sunday Plantation Drive has significantly contributed to increasing green cover and improving environmental health in the surrounding communities. Through consistent weekly efforts, volunteers developed eco-friendly habits, learned plant care and maintenance skills, and cultivated a sense of commitment toward nature. The initiative encouraged community involvement, motivated residents to adopt tree-planting practices, and raised awareness about climate protection and natural resource preservation. The continued growth and survival of planted saplings symbolize the long-term positive impact of the activity, highlighting the dedication of students toward a cleaner, greener and more sustainable future.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-26","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The NSS – Adamya Chetana Green Sunday Plantation Drive is a year-long environmental initiative conducted every Sunday, aimed at promoting greenery and ecological conservation in the community. As part of this activity, volunteers visit various locations such as public parks, playgrounds, empty open spaces, and community gardens to plant saplings and nurture growing plants. Along with plantation, volunteers also engage in cleaning the areas, preparing soil beds, watering plants, and creating awareness among residents about the importance of environmental sustainability. This initiative fosters a strong culture of environmental responsibility and encourages youth participation in protecting and improving green spaces across the locality","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/W2ZLp2QnDb0wgFzUT8-Nv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7raKkOer6k0qhSZAxXjcB","name":"NSS Blood Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/WKoWEfaKig9051JkVdpju.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive received active participation from students and staff, resulting in successful collection of blood units for medical and emergency use. Through this activity, students gained awareness about the life-saving significance of blood donation while developing organizational, leadership, and communication skills. The campaign fostered a sense of social responsibility, compassion, and civic commitment among participants. The event strengthened the culture of community service on campus and encouraged more individuals to become regular voluntary blood donors.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The NSS Blood Donation Camp was organized as a humanitarian initiative to encourage voluntary blood donation and support healthcare needs in society. The camp was conducted in collaboration with medical professionals, who ensured proper screening, guidance, and safety measures for all donors. NSS volunteers assisted in donor registration, awareness campaigning, queue management, and providing refreshments and support to participants. The event emphasized the importance of voluntary blood donation and motivated students to contribute to saving lives through this noble act.","aicteMapping":"Health & Welfare Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/s07ZsxvIkLC-30Jqgdq3h.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gNb53uUaidwh23UYUj9RA","name":"Rotaract Fistful Donation Camp","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/MS_lDR77vjwJQoVzBb71Y.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fistful Donation Camp generated an impactful response, successfully gathering substantial quantities of rice and other grains that were distributed to several families in need, ensuring they received essential food support during difficult times. Through this activity, I learned the power of collective contribution and witnessed firsthand how even small gestures of kindness can create meaningful change in society. The initiative fostered values of compassion, charity, and empathy, strengthening the spirit of social service among students. It also enhanced team coordination and community engagement as volunteers collaboratively worked with the Rotaract Club to ensure smooth collection, packaging, and distribution of the donated supplies. The event proved to be a valuable learning experience and encouraged continued participation in future humanitarian efforts","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Rotaract Fistful Donation Camp was a social welfare initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged families by collecting staple food grains and distributing them to those facing food scarcity. As part of this noble cause, students were encouraged to contribute even a small quantity of grains, symbolizing the idea that a collective effort from many can bring significant change. I actively participated in this initiative by donating 5 kilograms of rice, demonstrating my commitment to helping the needy. The donation drive was conducted in collaboration with the Rotaract Club, which organized the logistics and outreach for the distribution drive. This activity not only encouraged students to contribute towards feeding the hungry but also helped build awareness about the importance of food security and social responsibility in our community.","aicteMapping":"Food Security & Humanitarian Relief Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/y2kwK69pWKxaI8xizThiT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"U9O56y3t_wt-Sl-CTL6jQ","name":"NSS Utsarga Marathon","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/n1MonyT04eX3UQFZkted8.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/NH_r_I1potCVrdpJd4ZZw.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/JXU5XUUBh6k7I0oWxvAmI.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon successfully brought together students and the community, generating widespread awareness and encouraging participation in social welfare-oriented initiatives. The event not only promoted fitness and healthy lifestyle habits but also reinforced teamwork, time management, and leadership skills among student volunteers. Participants experienced a deep sense of achievement by contributing to a meaningful purpose that extended beyond the race itself. Through this initiative, funds and awareness were raised to support future NSS activities and community service projects. Overall, the marathon strengthened the culture of volunteerism, social awareness, and public engagement within the college community.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The NSS Utsarga Marathon was conducted as a major student-driven initiative aimed at promoting physical fitness, youth involvement in social causes, and spreading awareness about community welfare. The marathon served not only as a sporting event but also as a platform to encourage social responsibility by motivating participants to contribute toward noble causes. Students, faculty members, and community participants took part enthusiastically, reflecting unity and collective purpose. I actively contributed as a participant in the event by assisting in coordination tasks such as participant registration, route management, providing refreshments, cheering runners, and ensuring smooth execution throughout the event. The marathon symbolized the spirit of youth leadership and reinforced the idea that social development can be driven through sports-based engagement.","aicteMapping":"Physical Fitness & Social Awareness Programs","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/vQ2FSCsxDUb3rrCvfA7E4.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rSpvdiXttPlN_HvbX73tu","name":"Rotaract Project Pustak","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/IyuKaoHvSGvHl0u57YUoN.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-30","duration":31,"outcomes":"The Rotaract Project Pustak drive successfully gathered and distributed essential educational materials to deserving students, enabling them to pursue their studies with confidence and dignity. The activity helped bridge the learning resource gap for many children while spreading awareness about the importance of education and youth contribution toward social development. Through this initiative, I gained valuable exposure to community service and developed qualities such as empathy, responsibility, and social awareness. The project strengthened collaboration between volunteers and Rotaract members and encouraged continued involvement in educational support programs. Overall, the initiative created a positive impact by promoting equal learning opportunities and inspiring young minds to value and support education for all.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Rotaract Project Pustak was an educational support initiative aimed at empowering underprivileged school children by providing them with academic materials and learning resources. As part of this campaign, students and volunteers contributed funds and books to help ensure that children from economically weaker backgrounds could continue their education without facing a shortage of basic study necessities. I actively took part in this initiative by donating educational supplies/monetary support, thereby contributing to the mission of promoting literacy and learning. The project was executed in collaboration with the Rotaract Club, which coordinated the collection and distribution process across various schools and community centers. This initiative served as a reminder of the power of collective effort in shaping a brighter and more educated future for children in need.","aicteMapping":"Educational Aid & Student Welfare Program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/FGXJbXgoBrT5ItSS8b3i8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MsToPgb8NRpX-hF1au6Bq","name":"Rotaract Female Foeticide Walkathon","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/cowYYZj7moz0UCv_t4SaJ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/GFozCMsAmuK6OsnrrF0JH.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon proved to be a resounding success, effectively drawing public attention to the alarming issue of gender-based injustice and the importance of valuing every life equally. The event not only raised awareness among participants and onlookers but also generated meaningful discussions on women’s rights and equality. The funds collected were productively channelled into the 8th Mile Event, showcasing how social awareness campaigns can also serve as a means to support larger community initiatives. Participants developed a deeper understanding of social sensitivity, empathy, and advocacy for women’s welfare. The initiative strengthened students’ leadership, communication, and teamwork skills while reinforcing their sense of civic and moral responsibility. Overall, the event stood as a powerful statement against social prejudice and a testament to youth-driven change.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The Rotaract Club organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon on 11th May 2025 to spread awareness about the critical social issue of female foeticide and to promote gender equality within the community. The event brought together students, faculty members, and local residents who participated in a purposeful walk holding banners and placards with impactful messages supporting the cause. The walkathon aimed to educate the public about the value of the girl child and the need to eradicate gender-based discrimination. In addition to creating awareness, the event served as a fundraiser, with proceeds being utilized to support the upcoming 8th Mile Event, thereby extending the impact of the initiative. As a participant, I actively contributed by helping in organizing, coordinating participants, and promoting the campaign through social media and word-of-mouth, demonstrating a commitment to social reform and women empowerment.","aicteMapping":"Gender Equality & Social Reform Campaign","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/vRQbZXchiT4c24fYx1H5a.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KxLB_dYHGWIYjoLzim_ig","name":"NSS World Alzheimer’s Awareness Walkathon ","slNo":10,"place":"Freedom Park, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/rQNkGm4etUc4q9iisOKOs.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/0YNALa1Ep9qHcNvBUHr3a.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/pUN0Qx4oJDuV23xSzG-Uc.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/oeyx3aERww_tzZeCaCY-6.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/Xs_NJ_1yvWwmWekcDTrmz.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/83B8H98V2dww2wD-_MVB0.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-09-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The World Alzheimer’s Awareness Walkathon successfully attracted widespread public attention and participation, making it a memorable and impactful event. The walk from Freedom Park to Vidhana Soudha served as a visible symbol of social concern and advocacy, encouraging open dialogue about mental health and dementia. Participants gained valuable insights into the challenges faced by Alzheimer’s patients and their caregivers, fostering a sense of understanding and empathy. The activity strengthened teamwork, discipline, and civic engagement among NSS volunteers, while enhancing their ability to organize and participate in large-scale awareness campaigns. Overall, the initiative contributed to building a more compassionate and informed community that recognizes the importance of mental health care and social responsibility.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-09-27","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The NSS World Alzheimer’s Awareness Walkathon was organized to spread awareness about Alzheimer’s disease and to show solidarity with individuals and families affected by it. The walkathon took place along a prominent route from Freedom Park to Vidhana Soudha, symbolizing a collective stride toward understanding and supporting mental health challenges in society. The event aimed to educate the public about early signs of Alzheimer’s, the importance of compassion toward patients, and the need for greater community involvement in dementia care. As an NSS volunteer, I actively participated in the walkathon by carrying awareness placards, engaging with bystanders to share information, and helping coordinate participants throughout the event. The initiative reflected the NSS’s mission of service to society while promoting health awareness and empathy for vulnerable populations.","aicteMapping":"Public Health Awareness & Disease Prevention Programs","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/5ZY0bI9--06ERuZqrUe_3.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KB9k6L_BN5aREWimb1a5k","name":"Rotaract Echolore Event","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/ZISP3zPygdyHqWdULPzt2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"Echolore successfully provided a creative space for students to voice their thoughts on social and environmental concerns while discovering the power of words to inspire change. The event nurtured literary and communication skills among participants, helping them develop confidence in expressing their ideas to a broader audience. It also strengthened social awareness by encouraging discussions around sustainability, maternal health, and cultural preservation. Participants experienced a deep sense of connection and purpose, realizing how art and storytelling can be tools for advocacy and empathy. Overall, the event promoted creativity, critical thinking, and civic sensitivity, aligning with the Rotaract Club’s vision of building socially conscious youth leaders.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-16","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V.C.E. organized Echolore, an event that celebrated storytelling and creative expression on meaningful social themes such as Saving Mothers and Children, Environment, and Folklore. The event encouraged participants to share their ideas and perspectives through various literary forms, including essays, poems, articles, and prose, in languages like English, Hindi, and Kannada. It served as a platform for students to use creativity and empathy to reflect on real-world issues, showcasing how storytelling can inspire awareness and social change. By engaging participants in the art of thoughtful writing, Echolore fostered a sense of imagination, compassion, and community consciousness while promoting social responsibility through artistic expression.","aicteMapping":"Environmental  & Sustainability Awareness","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/jAU9l72hWJP7NbrbBlDOq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Twk6l-m7IP1ZTJm8AtH3Q","name":"Rotaract Blood Donation Camp","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/wcQC_4zvWpGsv7717EzK8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp received an excellent response, with enthusiastic participation from students and staff, resulting in the successful collection of multiple blood units for hospitals and emergency medical use. The event not only helped fulfill an essential healthcare need but also educated participants about the value of voluntary blood donation and the role it plays in saving lives. Volunteers gained valuable experience in event coordination, teamwork, and public engagement, while donors experienced a sense of pride and compassion in contributing to a noble cause. Overall, the initiative strengthened the spirit of social service, empathy, and civic responsibility among students, while reinforcing the Rotaract Club’s ongoing mission of humanitarian support and community development.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Rotaract Blood Donation Camp was organized at the Biotechnology Engineering Quadrangle as a humanitarian initiative to promote voluntary blood donation and community health awareness. The event aimed to encourage students, faculty, and staff to contribute toward saving lives through safe and organized blood donation practices. Conducted in collaboration with certified medical professionals and local blood banks, the camp ensured proper medical screening, hygienic procedures, and post-donation care for all participants. As a volunteer, I actively assisted in organizing the event by helping with registration, guiding donors, managing logistics, and spreading awareness about the importance of regular blood donation. The activity reflected the Rotaract Club’s commitment to social welfare and service to humanity.","aicteMapping":"Community Health & Medical Support Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/jjnw0k42DEzvBZ2QgoI6k.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mlKMDnSlvy2EsrTkn-WeQ","name":"Rotaract Fistful Donation Camp","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/UCEBHfJeWIPRA6m4scvXd.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fistful Donation Camp successfully gathered a significant quantity of food grains, which were distributed to needy individuals and families, helping alleviate food insecurity in the local community. The initiative created awareness among students about the importance of sharing and contributing to social welfare, regardless of the size of their donation. It fostered teamwork, coordination, and humanitarian values among all participants, instilling a strong sense of social commitment and moral responsibility. The activity also reinforced the idea that consistent small acts of kindness can collectively bring about meaningful change. Overall, the donation camp strengthened community engagement and demonstrated the Rotaract Club’s ongoing dedication to social service and poverty alleviation.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Rotaract Fistful Donation Camp was organized as a charitable initiative to collect food grains and essential groceries from students and staff, which were later distributed to underprivileged families in need. The activity encouraged every participant to donate a small portion — even a handful — of rice, grains, or other essentials, symbolizing the idea that “little contributions can make a big difference.” The event promoted the spirit of generosity and social responsibility within the campus, inspiring students to understand the power of collective giving. I actively participated by donating food grains and assisting the Rotaract volunteers in collecting, sorting, and packaging the donated items. The drive reflected the values of compassion, empathy, and unity in addressing hunger and supporting the less fortunate sections of society.","aicteMapping":"Provision Food materials for underprivileged families ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/bfc38cad-08dd-4e13-97ee-fcb6a1e01436/XysEtNejfZOZ_AFQGKn2U.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"31","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 01:53:40.688017+00', '2026-01-30 18:39:42.050984+00'), ('b65fe465-33a2-4caa-b21d-2224706a295a', 'c0046e5f-a92b-4994-92a8-9d6ebccfd061', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CH004","name":"ANANTH RAM Y N","period":"2022-2026","department":"Chemical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"cS2bxJ3eK_6hOcnTwpbW_","name":"FAST-TREK 1.0","slNo":1,"place":"Hutridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c0046e5f-a92b-4994-92a8-9d6ebccfd061/zDBcbexB4yzV812wzB5nO.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c0046e5f-a92b-4994-92a8-9d6ebccfd061/VftgKqx2t38CfqlMEdmi3.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c0046e5f-a92b-4994-92a8-9d6ebccfd061/ROcw3_Jhkt50i7vEPczma.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Hutridurga Hills trek successfully combined environmental action with an enriching outdoor \\nexperience. The cleanliness drive helped restore portions of the trail and reduced litter, encouraging \\nmore responsible tourism. Participants left with a greater awareness of sustainability and a deeper \\nappreciation for heritage landscapes.\\nThe experience strengthened team spirit, discipline, and community involvement among students, \\ndemonstrating how purposeful initiatives can create long-lasting social and environmental value. \\nThe event concluded on a highly positive note, setting a strong precedent for future treks and service \\nactivities.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":10.5,"description":"As part of my ongoing commitment to environmental and social responsibility, I participated in the \\nFast Trek activity at Hutridurga Hills, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. The event aimed \\nto merge outdoor exploration with sustainable action, encouraging students to protect and preserve \\nnatural spaces while experiencing them firsthand.\\nThe day began early with volunteers assembling for a detailed briefing session. Organizers explained \\nthe safety guidelines, the route plan, and the significance of the cleanliness drive. With the group \\nenergized and prepared, we boarded the buses and made our way to the Hutridurga base.\\nHutridurga Hills, known for its rugged stone pathways, fortress remnants, and sweeping hilltop \\nviews, offered the perfect landscape for the trek. As participants ascended the trail, they actively \\nengaged in clearing the surroundings—collecting waste, removing plastic, and ensuring that the \\ntrekking path remained clean. The initiative encouraged everyone to adopt responsible trekking \\nhabits and reinforced the idea that preserving such heritage-natural sites is a shared duty.\\nBeyond the environmental impact, the trek brought students together. The climb, the scenic \\nstretches, and the shared responsibility fostered teamwork, communication, and a strong sense of \\ncamaraderie. Every participant contributed to the positive atmosphere of the event, making the \\nexperience memorable and impactful.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 10:31:53.146575+00', '2026-01-29 15:59:25.712507+00'), ('b69f1032-eb36-4047-9643-c14f64fa77b3', '3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"Chemical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"2ud1TrGidxV90tt5Ipw3w","name":"Matrubhasha diwas","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/HyS65nBylsagyTjzjPYBj.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/Tel5TNDV20zYLzts0LBo3.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-11","duration":4,"outcomes":"Matrubhasha Diwas celebrated with fervor, promoting linguistic diversity and cultural richness. The event fostered a sense of pride in native languages, encouraging unity through multilingual harmony. Participants engaged in various language-centric activities, fostering a deeper appreciation for linguistic heritage ","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-08","hoursSpent":20,"description":"RAAG hosted Matrubhasha Diwas, also known as International Mother Language Day, to promote the spread of mother tongues and a greater understanding of linguistic and cultural traditions. The main goal of the celebration was for students to participate and showcase the diverse culture and traditions of various states through their performances and ethnic-dresses. The stage was open to students, and approximately 350 people attended in the IEM auditorium and 400 in the MCA Quadrangle. Dr. KN Subramanya, Principal, and Dr. KS Geetha, Vice Principal, preceded the event. The event began with a Procession from the Admin Block to the IEM auditorium along with Dhol, all of the faculties, staff, and students carrying placards representing their respective states. Following that, linguistic music, dance, and poetry were performed in the IEM auditorium. Three pre-events were planned for students: Rangoli Competition(Offline on 10th Feb in MCA Quadrangle), Capture the Moment(Online) and Digitalize your Heritage(Online), to which they eagerly participated.","aicteMapping":"Volunteer ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WrJI-nujbY4xwdcJiFlMK","name":"Treasure hunt","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/9TelKKeW150Xwk573zuYj.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/75O1rcEoyHs5vBsJ3vqlF.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-01-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event effectively combined fun and education, fostering a sense of responsibility towards the environment among participants. The overall event successfully blended education, teamwork, and environmental consciousness ","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-01-25","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The first round of the Treasure Hunt event centered on Sustainable Technologies concluded successfully, sparking heightened awareness and knowledge about eco-friendly solutions. The second round, a Hunt using clues, challenged teams to apply their knowledge in a dynamic setting, enhancing problem-solving skills.\\nIn the third round, \"Beg, Borrow, Steal,\" students demonstrated creativity and resourcefulness by finding sustainable solutions and procuring necessary items, fostering a practical understanding of sustainability.","aicteMapping":"Club Volunteers ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"d74Zsnn15r0FtqIV2g3Td","name":"Treasure hunt","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/faAou7osKLWwHHOoY9XzK.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/1sjqmSEWMYSpyUDCZCHsj.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Team building and collectiveness for college and sustainable approach ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-17","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The first round of the Treasure Hunt event centered on Sustainable Technologies concluded successfully, sparking heightened awareness and knowledge about eco-friendly solutions. The second round, a Hunt using clues, challenged teams to apply their knowledge in a dynamic setting, enhancing problem-solving skills.\\nIn the third round, \"Beg, Borrow, Steal,\" students demonstrated creativity and resourcefulness by finding sustainable solutions and procuring necessary items, fostering a practical understanding of sustainability. The event was totally adventurous and exciting which gave an fair opportunity to the participants. The last round was the most thrilling one as you have the time running behind you and you have to collect the following items. This event was also one of the first events for the freshers as they participated a lot and were joyful.","aicteMapping":"Club Volunteers ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DFXWor4Kjx_TNyR9-CtDt","name":"Fast trek","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/ufqoEZ0l9S5dNexQmTMZI.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/0SmmIioVVEX5K2jQ535Ts.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Treking for a social cause","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The social cause behind the project was to provide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the participants boarded the bus to the trek location with great enthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with basic information of the event. The trek was a great success as all the participants had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of Huthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very memorable journey. Breakfast and lunch was provided at the trek location for all the participants.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iBlGp-w9_q1ZfrPPpNsVj","name":"Fistfull","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/MV8dgDaVLLUv6fg9tJ4Dj.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/c6PkhJ-mk5PuK82VZrSEV.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"A small help can create a great impact ","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":5,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Welfare and Solidarity ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"q_gZMjjGAFRQLi8iADYwm","name":"Fist full","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/_Bun0JxxVfAQWIRXV_zbB.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/Y281D3auXXjvL7gjFxMBX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":382,"outcomes":"Fistful was a standalone community service project designed to combat food insecurity and support health and care institutions through collective student participation.","semester":"7","startDate":"2024-11-01","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Fistful initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2146 students, each contributing essential food grains in the form of either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal. This collective effort resulted in the successful collection and distribution of food grains to multiple beneficiary institutions that serve daily meals to children, the elderly, patients, and disadvantaged groups.","aicteMapping":"Community service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mSLXqjmB8GxqHXv7ZioEH","name":"Unchained ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/FJW4x9O5Nh04RoMeoE_kg.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/3651f74a-1215-4243-9414-bcff2c969698/-w9Kyxouq4G10mzPOD9og.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"Spreading awareness among students and learning new ways to meditate ","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":13,"description":"Raag the Youth club of rvce organised a anti drug awareness campaign in the campus Iem auditorium with more than 200 participants in collaboration with Art of living with the help of musical and meditation activities ","aicteMapping":"Public awareness ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zSAzuLoUc09oZtgQJWDyj","name":"","slNo":8,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 21:38:56.36282+00', '2026-02-02 08:09:25.246046+00'), ('b74cc230-0d48-4da5-9421-3ceee3ca271e', '38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS169","name":"Sahil Santosh Naik","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"5IRtcDHtlpd_qmdhzTC4P","name":"Fast Trek","slNo":1,"place":"Kaurava Kunda Hills ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/SnCl-HZtuwj8S1vjHds5-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2022-12-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced participants’ physical endurance, confidence, and stress\\nmanagement abilities while fostering leadership, coordination, and teamwork skills. It\\nalso encouraged a sense of environmental awareness and responsibility among students,\\nstrengthened peer relationships, and provided a memorable experiential learning opportunity\\noutside the classroom.","semester":"1","startDate":"2022-12-15","hoursSpent":9,"description":"Fast Trek was a one-day trekking event organized by RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on\\nDecember 15, 2022, to the scenic Kaurava Kunda Hills near Bengaluru. The event aimed to\\npromote adventure, physical fitness, and team bonding among students through a fast-paced trek\\nacross challenging rocky trails and natural landscapes. Participants enjoyed panoramic views\\nfrom the hilltop while engaging in teamwork and mutual support throughout the journey, making\\nit a refreshing break from routine academic life","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/RBHH_whCFa5UR63gS4XK9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ur1DTmliBdUYm401SQ86s","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":2,"place":"Kudogahalli","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/rky7idfJC0Jr1p-w9Bb1p.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-08-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of community service and the impact of providing educational support at the grassroots level. I learned the value of teamwork, social responsibility, and how small efforts can contribute to improving access to education for children in rural communities.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-06","hoursSpent":9,"description":"I participated in Project Pustak, an initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation. The activity involved collecting funds and distributing essential school supplies such as textbooks, stationery, and backpacks to underprivileged students in rural areas, with the aim of supporting their education.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/9qGBcEJofXW_knDG0XyUn.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BireA3s0UoHXTHtLS49QN","name":"Fist Full","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/vyN4BDDiDTyuaTkM862qp.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully collected a substantial quantity of rice, which was distributed to\\nfamilies in need, helping address food insecurity. It raised awareness about hunger and basic\\nnecessities, fostered a spirit of sharing among participants, and reinforced the importance of\\ncommunity-driven efforts in supporting vulnerable sections of society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Fist Full was a social service initiative focused on supporting underprivileged families\\nthrough food donation, wherein participants contributed 5 kg of rice per person. The initiative\\nemphasized the idea of collective giving, encouraging students and volunteers to make small\\nyet meaningful contributions that could create a significant impact when combined. Through\\norganized collection and distribution, the drive promoted compassion, empathy, and a strong\\nsense of social responsibility within the community.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/4z45LU_Hp7lTCJuXFwmFT.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4Ww-UeYHCNhyweeQgwblp","name":"Utsarg Marathon 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/6WDvh2Lj608iho8ozRqZ8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of civic engagement and teamwork in community service. I learned how disciplined participation and social involvement can create a positive impact on society.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":9,"description":"I participated in Uttara Aarohana 2025 under the National Service Scheme (NSS) organized by RV College of Engineering. The activity focused on community service and social responsibility, encouraging students to actively contribute to societal development through collective efforts.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/_8kWewRyHgHL_MuEful1s.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QG00cSQ7YFoJy49RkL07k","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Pattanagere","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/lCBYiTEavJwPW5i0SBkeE.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I gained a deeper understanding of the seriousness of female foeticide and its long-term impact on society. I learned the importance of social responsibility and grassroots-level awareness in addressing deep-rooted social issues. The experience improved my communication and teamwork skills, and helped me understand how community engagement can bring meaningful change. It also reinforced the value of standing up for social justice and promoting equality through collective action.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"As part of the rural outreach program, I actively participated in the Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon conducted at RVCE Pattanagere on 14/05/2025. The walkathon aimed to educate and sensitize the public, especially in rural areas, about the social, ethical, and legal consequences of female foeticide. Participants walked through nearby localities holding placards, banners, and slogans promoting the protection and empowerment of the girl child. The activity involved interaction with community members to spread awareness about gender equality and the importance of supporting women’s rights and dignity in society","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/fV8aGDbf7ouvQyHpEdxtF.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Y8fWs9mj3rKGEglxB1-6U","name":"YES!+ Mental Health Awareness Volunteer Activity – Art of Living","slNo":6,"place":"Art Of Living International Centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/o5DCcDZb4k6sGpX_QYWid.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of mental well‑being and mindfulness in daily life. I learned how awareness programs can positively impact individuals and communities by promoting mental health and emotional balance.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-14","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I volunteered at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, as part of the YES!+ (Youth Empowerment Seminar) initiative. The activity involved acquiring and imparting awareness on the importance of mental health under the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative of the Government of India during the academic year 2025–26.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/fCrHmEcSoHsSYAuxgOjCV.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mxWfJfcuhZRthqNrlLbQL","name":"Horticulture Volunteer Activity – Art of Living","slNo":7,"place":"Art Of Living International Centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/jTT1QWLbXFMd7n9XpwGNR.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of environmental conservation and sustainable practices. I learned the value of patience, responsibility, and contributing to ecological well‑being through hands‑on service.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-23","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I volunteered at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, as part of the Horticulture initiative under the YES+ Youth Empowerment program. The activity involved nurturing plants and trees through watering, sowing seeds, and participating in plantation work.\\n","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/lUGLqKpUf32X4-TTD_xp1.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"p707VLrp4IyAvnjgmY0fH","name":"Community Kitchen: Art of Living YES+","slNo":8,"place":"Art Of Living International Centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/RiU3F3B_WhWjiJ2XEj5rt.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of selfless service and teamwork in community welfare. I learned discipline, responsibility, and the value of contributing my time and effort to support social service initiatives.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-07","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I volunteered at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, where I assisted in community kitchen activities such as serving food, cutting vegetables, setting up, and cleaning the kitchen. The activity was conducted as part of a youth empowerment initiative during the academic year 2025–26.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/eqN1KocfYnP95mxMMP3Bn.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XmJfBUlOWreK3dm1DYGWr","name":"Gaushala Volunteer Activity – Art of Living","slNo":9,"place":"Art Of Living International Centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/PbklWspJ7lAiRYr_dgowQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of preserving indigenous cattle and their role in sustainable agriculture and ecology. I learned the value of compassion, environmental responsibility, and community‑oriented service.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-21","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I volunteered at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, as part of the Gaushala initiative under the YES+ Youth Empowerment program. The activity focused on conserving and caring for indigenous Indian cows and supporting efforts related to their protection and well‑being.\\n","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/49HtsKF3GAtk3uJwqDRst.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Mi_iyKLfbiW1LGp4dvG0j","name":"Permaculture Awareness Volunteer Activity – Art of Living","slNo":10,"place":"Art Of Living International Centre","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/TDlKr-DQ5l5V575IuEBsQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-01-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the significance of sustainable farming practices and soil conservation. I learned how spreading environmental awareness can contribute to long-term agricultural and ecological sustainability.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2026-01-21","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I volunteered at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, as part of a Permaculture awareness initiative conducted through the YES+ Youth Empowerment program. The activity involved acquiring knowledge and creating public awareness on the importance of improving soil quality to enhance agricultural productivity.\\n","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/38f82f8e-0a7d-4fee-9075-92047cce9ceb/NH6pQOf2Sl_je-NzG7keG.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr H.K Krishnappa","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"Evaluator 1","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":" Evaluator 2","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 20:28:20.548941+00', '2026-02-01 08:22:13.487984+00'), ('b77c1c8c-76f7-402c-85a7-4b2fd306fd5d', '57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC187","name":"Vivek B R","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"5-DnxV8SzWf3V0i2_g1n9","name":"Blood Donation Camp ","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/LhNIz_W94PRrvzRwVWt_e.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/NiIWENsQh_sWcT_7Rs45A.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp successfully contributed to strengthening blood bank reserves, thereby supporting hospitals and healthcare facilities in meeting emergency and routine transfusion requirements. The initiative played a vital role in encouraging voluntary blood donation and increasing awareness about its importance in sustaining public health systems.\\n\\nParticipation in the camp reflected a strong commitment to social responsibility, empathy, and service to humanity among students. Donors gained a deeper understanding of healthcare challenges and the significance of selfless community service. The activity also fostered confidence and awareness regarding safe blood donation practices.\\n\\nOverall, the camp had a meaningful humanitarian impact while promoting ethical responsibility and civic engagement. Participants were formally recognized with certificates of appreciation, and the activity contributed to holistic student development, earning 6 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was a humanitarian health initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Lions Club of Bangalore South, with support from RV College of Engineering. Conducted on 06 June 2023, the camp aimed to promote voluntary blood donation and raise awareness about the critical role of blood banks in saving lives during medical emergencies.\\n\\nThe event was organized with a strong focus on safety, hygiene, and donor well-being. Qualified medical professionals from the Lions Blood Centre supervised the entire donation process, ensuring strict adherence to medical protocols and screening procedures. Participants were educated about the importance of regular blood donation, eligibility criteria, and the positive impact it has on patients requiring transfusions due to surgeries, accidents, or chronic illnesses. Post-donation care, including refreshments and rest facilities, was provided to ensure donor comfort and recovery.\\n\\nBeyond the act of donation, the camp served as a platform to instill a sense of social responsibility and humanitarian values among students. It encouraged voluntary participation and emphasized how individual contributions can collectively address critical healthcare needs within the community","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"seHyUdt2EDAbuZGRokCk_","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/kaaBUk-wNVjnEgK0ADF-E.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in Utsarga Marathon 2024 played a significant role in reinforcing the importance of maintaining physical fitness and adopting a healthy lifestyle. Successfully completing the 5 km marathon enhanced participants’ physical endurance, cardiovascular stamina, and mental resilience. The experience emphasized the value of regular physical activity in maintaining overall well-being and encouraged students to incorporate fitness-oriented practices into their daily routines.\\n\\nThe marathon also made a meaningful contribution toward a noble social cause centered on child welfare and education. Through active participation, students directly supported initiatives aimed at improving access to education for underprivileged children. The event helped raise awareness about educational inequality and demonstrated how fitness-based initiatives can be effectively used to support social development. This collective effort highlighted the strength of community participation in addressing societal challenges and promoting inclusive growth.\\n\\nOn a personal and interpersonal level, the activity fostered essential life skills such as empathy, perseverance, teamwork, and civic responsibility. Participants developed a deeper understanding of the importance of collaboration and mutual encouragement while working toward a common goal. Engaging in a volunteer-driven initiative strengthened social sensitivity and encouraged students to look beyond academic achievements toward contributing positively to society.\\n\\nOverall, Utsarga Marathon 2024 emerged as a well-balanced integration of physical fitness, social service, and personal development. The event contributed to the holistic growth of students by nurturing physical health, emotional maturity, ethical values, and social awareness. Participation and successful completion of the marathon were formally recognized through the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points, further enhancing the participants’ extracurricular profiles and reinforcing their commitment to service-oriented engagement.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 was a 5-kilometer charity marathon organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) with the objective of promoting physical fitness, social responsibility, and community engagement among students. The event was designed as a holistic initiative that combined health awareness with a strong commitment to social causes, encouraging participants to contribute meaningfully to society while maintaining personal well-being.\\n\\nThe marathon was conducted with the central theme “Help a Child, Change the World”, emphasizing the importance of supporting education and welfare initiatives for underprivileged children. By participating in the marathon, students symbolically pledged their support toward creating a positive and lasting impact on the lives of children in need. The event reinforced the idea that physical effort, when aligned with social purpose, can become a powerful tool for change.\\n\\nIn addition to promoting fitness, the marathon aimed to instill values such as discipline, perseverance, and determination. Completing a 5 km run required both physical endurance and mental resilience, motivating participants to challenge personal limits and develop self-confidence. The event environment fostered enthusiasm, motivation, and mutual encouragement, creating a strong sense of unity and camaraderie among participants.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dpe9W7Lgscw7uam_CMIDy","name":"Kannada Sangha Tshirt ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/U3Xe5aU5tvUx8guZb1fIj.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/pEGv3FhTmWlv1D6CtnyXN.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative provided both material support and emotional encouragement to the children at the orphanage, contributing positively to their well-being. Interacting directly with the children helped create a supportive and caring environment while reinforcing the importance of empathy and kindness.\\n\\nFor the participating students, the activity enhanced social awareness, civic responsibility, and community involvement. It encouraged meaningful engagement beyond academics and highlighted the impact of collective effort in addressing social needs. Overall, the initiative supported holistic student development and was recognized with the award of 5 AICTE Activity Points.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Kannada Sangha T-Shirt Initiative was a student-led social outreach activity organized by Kannada Sangha, aimed at supporting an orphanage through collective contribution and community engagement. The initiative encouraged students to participate by purchasing event T-shirts, with the proceeds directed towards welfare activities for orphaned children.\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, students visited an orphanage at Kumbalagodu, where they spent time interacting with the children and distributing essential items and donations. The activity promoted cultural unity while fostering social responsibility, compassion, and a sense of service among participants. Through this initiative, students were encouraged to contribute meaningfully to society while strengthening bonds within the campus community.","aicteMapping":"Kannada Sangha","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mTp0zNmdinmrT1I8i6Ld6","name":"ACM volunteer","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/-tGS2vaSynpSvDN6Os1Dt.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The summit provided exposure to emerging technologies, research trends, and professional networking opportunities. Volunteering enhanced organizational, communication, and teamwork skills while contributing to the successful conduct of a large-scale academic event. ","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-09","hoursSpent":6,"description":"ACM India Summit 2024 was organized at RV College of Engineering in collaboration with the ACM India Council, bringing together experts from academia and industry. As a \\nvolunteer, I assisted in event coordination, speaker sessions, participant management, and smooth execution of summit activities conducted on a national level. ","aicteMapping":"ACM","pointsEarned":7,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZzZJG_GPxSOYg8tqtnFu_","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":5,"place":" Kunagalu Betta Hills ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/WyAskffGGNFjJzde7fxHg.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/Hd6OThjwWWo6AdYrRCQTV.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in Fast Trek 2.0 significantly enhanced physical endurance, stamina, and overall fitness among students. The trekking experience encouraged participants to appreciate the importance of maintaining an active lifestyle and demonstrated how outdoor activities can positively contribute to both physical and mental well-being.\\n\\nThe event successfully fostered teamwork, cooperation, and leadership qualities as students supported and motivated one another throughout the trek. Facing natural challenges together strengthened problem-solving skills, confidence, and adaptability, contributing to holistic personal development.\\n\\nThe inclusion of an environmental cleanliness drive instilled a strong sense of ecological responsibility and awareness. Participants gained a deeper understanding of sustainable practices and the need to protect natural landscapes, reinforcing the concept of responsible citizenship and environmental stewardship.\\n\\nOverall, Fast Trek 2.0 proved to be a balanced blend of adventure, social responsibility, and community engagement. The activity strengthened bonds among students, promoted environmental consciousness, and supported experiential learning outside academics. Participation was formally recognized through the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points, adding significant value to students’ extracurricular and service-oriented profiles.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast Trek 2.0 was an outdoor experiential learning and adventure activity organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, aimed at promoting physical fitness, environmental awareness, teamwork, and student engagement beyond the classroom environment. The event involved a guided trek to the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills, providing participants with an opportunity to explore nature while engaging in meaningful group activity.\\n\\nThe trek was designed to encourage students to step out of their academic routines and experience the benefits of physical activity, endurance, and mental well-being through adventure-based learning. Participants navigated natural trails and rocky terrains, which required stamina, focus, and cooperation. The activity fostered resilience, determination, and adaptability as students worked together to complete the trek safely and responsibly.\\n\\nIn addition to adventure and fitness, Fast Trek 2.0 incorporated a strong social and environmental component. As part of the initiative, participants were encouraged to maintain cleanliness throughout the trekking route and surrounding areas, reinforcing the importance of environmental conservation and responsible tourism. The activity emphasized respect for nature and highlighted the role of youth in preserving natural ecosystems.\\n\\nThe event also served as a platform for strengthening interpersonal relationships among students. Through shared challenges and collective experiences, participants developed camaraderie, leadership skills, and mutual trust. The structured organization of the trek reflected Rotaract values of fellowship, service, and personal development, making the activity both recreational and purpose-driven.","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Vd_kamAd8BypQSU8GVmAi","name":"Inkspire 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/SRg6yxSjfHbOmqdRckK6S.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in Inkspire 2024 significantly strengthened creative thinking, written communication, and critical analysis skills among students. Engaging with socially relevant themes encouraged participants to develop a deeper understanding of contemporary issues and reflect on their roles as responsible and informed citizens.\\n\\nThe initiative also fostered confidence and motivation by providing recognition and visibility to student work. Featuring selected submissions on public platforms empowered participants to view storytelling as a meaningful tool for advocacy and societal engagement. The activity cultivated an environment of inclusivity, intellectual curiosity, and artistic appreciation.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-10-25","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Inkspire 2024 was a creative and socially driven literary initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, with the objective of encouraging students to engage with pressing societal issues through written expression. The event aimed to position storytelling as a powerful medium for reflection, dialogue, and advocacy by inviting participants to articulate their perspectives on themes of sustainability, public health, social equality, and education.\\n\\nThe initiative welcomed original literary submissions in English, Hindi, and Kannada, ensuring linguistic inclusivity and enabling participants from diverse cultural backgrounds to express themselves authentically. Contributions included essays, poems, reflective narratives, and creative pieces that demonstrated both artistic expression and social awareness. By offering a structured platform for creative writing, the event encouraged students to think critically, explore alternative viewpoints, and communicate ideas with clarity and purpose.\\n\\nSelected works were curated and showcased through the club’s official magazine, blog, and social media platforms, thereby extending the reach of student voices beyond the campus. This public dissemination reinforced the relevance of creative writing in shaping social conversations and highlighted the role of youth-led expression in driving awareness and positive change.","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KMDwn1VfH7CZS-gjjY1RE","name":"Utsarga Marathon - 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/VqqVqzkSQBJpNpaHKMx5w.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/YSIAVksICHGhJyQK4f6ih.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the Utsarga Marathon – 2025 significantly strengthened awareness about the importance of physical fitness and healthy living. Successfully completing the 5 km marathon enhanced participants’ stamina, endurance, and mental resilience, reinforcing the value of incorporating regular physical activity into daily life.\\n\\nThe marathon also contributed meaningfully to supporting a noble social cause focused on child welfare and education. By taking part in the event, participants helped raise awareness and support for initiatives aimed at improving the lives of underprivileged children. The activity highlighted the power of collective action and demonstrated how youth-driven efforts can generate tangible social impact.\\n\\nOn a personal level, the activity fostered qualities such as empathy, social awareness, perseverance, teamwork, and civic responsibility. Participants gained deeper insight into the importance of volunteerism and community service, encouraging long-term engagement with social causes. The experience strengthened leadership qualities and reinforced ethical responsibility among students.\\n\\nOverall, Utsarga Marathon – 2025 proved to be a successful integration of fitness, social consciousness, and civic engagement. The activity contributed to the holistic development of students by promoting physical health, emotional growth, and social responsibility. Participation and successful completion of the marathon were formally recognized with the award of 15 AICTE Activity Points, adding significant value to the students’ extracurricular and service-oriented profiles.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Utsarga Marathon – 2025 was a 5-kilometer charity marathon organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru, with the primary objective of promoting physical fitness, social responsibility, and active community engagement among students. The marathon was conceptualized as a holistic initiative that blended health awareness with a strong commitment to social causes, encouraging participants to contribute meaningfully to society while nurturing personal well-being.\\n\\nThe event was conducted with the central theme “Help a Child, Change the World”, which emphasized the importance of education, care, and support for underprivileged children. By participating in the marathon, students symbolically pledged their support toward initiatives aimed at improving access to education and creating opportunities for children from marginalized backgrounds. Each step taken during the run represented a collective effort toward social upliftment and long-term positive change.\\n\\nBeyond physical activity, the marathon served as a platform to instill values such as discipline, perseverance, self-motivation, and teamwork. The 5 km run required sustained physical endurance and mental resilience, encouraging participants to push beyond their comfort zones and develop determination and confidence. The shared experience fostered unity and camaraderie among students, reinforcing cooperation and mutual encouragement throughout the event.\\n\\nAdditionally, the structured organization of the marathon reflected the core principles of the NSS—selfless service, unity, leadership, and civic responsibility. The initiative motivated students to look beyond academic achievements and recognize their role as responsible citizens capable of contributing to societal development. Through active participation, students were encouraged to adopt a service-oriented mindset and continue engaging in community welfare activities beyond the marathon.","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Q2N2_5TH8WgJsf3zOvvxc","name":"Echolore ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/yAjdgLGeMmhLnGI43cpsL.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event brought a positive change by inspiring participants to think deeply about social and environmental issues. Echolore was more than a storytelling event .It was a space to celebrate imagination, empathy and the impact that thoughtful writings can have on society. ","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-16","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Rotaract Club of R.V.C.E. organized Echolore, an event celebrating storytelling on themes of Saving Mothers & Children, Environment and Folklore, Participants shared their creative pieces in the form of essays, poems, articles and \\nprose in different languages like English, Hindi, or Kannada, using creativity and care to express their ideas. The event provided a platform for participants to share their voices and reflect on how stories can make a difference in the world. \\nThrough their writing, contributors connected with one another and discovered new ways to express their thoughts and feelings.  ","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"00sDB-0hH-MNBZgBcDsg4","name":"UTPT QUIZ ","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/_sWn6okoEav2Azk-OIzoj.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in UTPT Quiz 2025 significantly enhanced analytical thinking, problem-solving skills, and general awareness among participants. Engaging with diverse and challenging questions helped broaden knowledge across multiple domains while strengthening the ability to think critically under pressure.\\n\\nThe event also improved confidence, concentration, and time-management skills by simulating a competitive academic environment. Interaction with participants from different institutions encouraged knowledge sharing and exposed students to varied perspectives and approaches to problem-solving.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-25","hoursSpent":4,"description":"UTPT Quiz 2025 was a national-level quiz competition conducted as part of the Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2025 fest at RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru, held from 23rd to 25th May 2025. The event was designed to promote intellectual engagement, critical thinking, and knowledge-based competition among students from diverse academic backgrounds across the country.\\n\\nThe quiz focused on testing participants’ understanding of a wide range of subjects, including Indian history, culture, polity, science and technology, current affairs, and general knowledge. Through a structured competitive format, the event encouraged participants to apply logical reasoning, analytical thinking, and quick decision-making skills under time-bound conditions. The quiz served as a platform for academic interaction, healthy competition, and collaborative learning.\\n\\nBy participating in a national-level quizzing event, students gained exposure to large-scale academic competitions and an opportunity to benchmark their knowledge and problem-solving abilities against peers from other institutions. The event emphasized learning through competition and fostered curiosity, awareness, and intellectual growth beyond the classroom environment.","aicteMapping":"Quizcorp club","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xE4mJfjcyodHmTIlcvHF2","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/dqpJPhuKLqtKkkqawTl1c.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative resulted in a substantial and impactful collection effort, with 2146 students collectively donating approximately 4370 kg of rice and 2516 kg of toor dal. The donated food grains were distributed to seven beneficiary institutions, including Hanuman Temple, Pruthvi Foundation, Amrutavani Vridh Seva Samithi, Sai Aashraya Hospital, Sai Satguna Sangrama Trust, Nele Foundation, and nearby anganwadis, thereby directly supporting individuals in need across multiple care sectors.\\n\\nFrom a student development perspective, participation in FistFull 2025 strengthened social awareness, civic responsibility, and a service-oriented mindset. Students gained firsthand experience in community engagement and collective action, reinforcing values of compassion and ethical responsibility. Overall, the activity contributed meaningfully to societal welfare while supporting the holistic development of students and was formally recognized with the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points, adding significant value to their extracurricular and service profiles.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"FistFull 2025 was a large-scale humanitarian donation drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of addressing food insecurity and supporting health care and social welfare institutions. Conducted on 17th November 2025, the initiative encouraged students to voluntarily contribute 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal as part of a collective effort to support vulnerable sections of society.\\n\\nThe activity was designed around the principle that small, consistent individual contributions can collectively lead to significant social impact. By involving students directly in the donation process, the initiative promoted awareness about hunger, nutrition, and the challenges faced by underprivileged communities, including patients, elderly individuals, and orphaned children. The collection process was systematically organized to ensure transparency, inclusivity, and active student participation.\\n","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HD_aFPaPi7MDlbXMfrtD0","name":"Project Pustak -2025 ","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/DXBXmWN3DMPAfkGqNoYx6.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully enabled the distribution of essential school supplies to underprivileged students, thereby improving their access to basic educational resources and supporting continuity in their academic activities. The contribution helped reduce resource gaps and positively impacted the learning experience of beneficiary students.\\n\\nFrom a student perspective, participation in Project Pustak – 2025 strengthened awareness of social responsibility and the importance of collective action in addressing educational challenges. The activity encouraged empathy, civic engagement, and community involvement, while contributing to holistic student development. The initiative was formally recognized through the award of 10 AICTE Activity Points, reinforcing the value of socially responsible participation alongside academics.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak – 2025 was a student-driven social outreach initiative aimed at supporting the educational needs of underprivileged government school students. The initiative focused on mobilizing financial contributions across the campus to procure essential academic resources such as notebooks, stationery items, school bags, and other basic learning materials required for effective schooling.\\n\\nThe collected resources were organized and distributed to students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds, ensuring that lack of basic supplies did not become a barrier to learning. The initiative emphasized community participation, educational equity, and sustainable support for primary education. By contributing to Project Pustak, students actively participated in a meaningful cause that linked social responsibility with educational development.","aicteMapping":"Rotract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xR2sDMtW6gxDWSP9XYSB-","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walk","slNo":12,"place":"Global Tech Park","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/57e41d40-9f85-40d2-b19e-ba1ea01124ed/JkfR7hzXK-pXmCx5q_lJt.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity successfully enhanced awareness among participants and the wider community regarding the importance of protecting the girl child and addressing deep-rooted gender discrimination. It helped sensitize students to the ethical, social, and human rights dimensions of female foeticide and reinforced the need for sustained advocacy and collective action.\\n\\nParticipation in the awareness walk fostered a strong sense of social responsibility, empathy, and civic consciousness among students. Being part of an organized advocacy initiative highlighted the power of youth engagement in driving social reform and demonstrated how community-oriented activities can create meaningful real-world impact.\\n\\nOn an individual level, the event encouraged active citizenship and strengthened values such as compassion, equality, and ethical responsibility. Overall, the Female Foeticide Awareness Walk contributed to holistic student development by integrating social awareness with civic participation. The activity was formally recognized with the award of 15 AICTE Activity Points, underscoring its significance as a meaningful and impactful social outreach initiative.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walk was a social awareness and advocacy initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in the month of May 2025, in observance of Mother’s Day, with the objective of addressing and eliminating the social issue of female foeticide. The event aimed to promote gender equality and emphasize the importance of protecting the rights, dignity, and lives of the girl child through collective student participation and public engagement.\\n\\nThe walkathon brought together students, volunteers, and faculty members to raise awareness about gender-based discrimination and the long-term societal consequences of female foeticide. By organizing a peaceful and symbolic walk, the initiative served as a platform for social advocacy, encouraging dialogue and reflection on ethical responsibility, social justice, and women’s empowerment. The activity reinforced the role of educational institutions and youth-led organizations in addressing sensitive social issues and influencing positive change through non-violent civic action.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 18:19:01.120365+00', '2026-01-30 19:16:01.536854+00'), ('b7bee80a-6970-433e-a4e5-66a5a02e050e', 'c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS213","name":"Swasti Sharma","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"ktKBAJ5069i3vUZsSCMRo","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/IkpRCp-Ga8FVSUp0cX8Wn.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Many patients require blood at crucial times, and my blood being O+ve, it can be used by anyone, hence donated my blood so that it can be used for a good purpose.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Donated my blood to the blood bank for a social cause. Every drop counts — one pint of blood can save up to three lives. This was our chance to give someone a second chance at life, right \\nhere on campus.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/CiPwu-LuAYFi4uR7Zjt1l.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"z1AkSfpqgdlYOGdSFeW0l","name":"Project Pustak ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/kOpuXUQoJecnOytb5Gz-b.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":8,"outcomes":"Education is the key to unlocking opportunities and building a better future. Unfortunately, many children in rural areas lack access to basic school supplies, making it difficult for them to learn and grow. Project Pustak aims to bridge this gap and help these children realize their potential.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Project Pustak is a noble initiative that aims to provide essential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas. With the generous donations, notebooks and geometry boxes will be brought, which will be donated to government schools.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/Fbldyv4Y-J0xj-avL8PRC.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Uv8pakyk7UYBeiq0saYtw","name":"Female Feticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/QjL0YdXAXx4enfVgpoz-_.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program increased awareness about the social and ethical impact of female feticide among  participants and the community.\\nIt motivated individuals to take a stand for the protection, respect, and empowerment of the girl child.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Female Feticide Awareness Walkathon is a community-driven initiative conducted by Rotract club dedicated to ending the practice of female feticide and celebrating the value of the girl child. Participants from all walks of life—students, professionals, and families—will gather to walk a designated 5km route, carrying placards and chanting slogans of empowerment. The event serves as a public demonstration of solidarity, aiming to break the silence surrounding gender-based discrimination before birth. Along the route, educational booths and speakers will highlight the legal, social, and ethical implications of sex-selective practices. By turning the streets into a platform for advocacy, the walkathon transforms a quiet social issue into a loud, collective demand for change.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/M6oUt3f9veiyxmLlXHYpq.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6EqIw-FDaEDe6Fs25vKtZ","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":4,"place":"Narayangiri Hills ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/V7b7YuotMUHnL10gCbf4c.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Resilience Building- Pushing yourself on a steep hill proves to your brain that you can handle discomfort, which translates into \"real-world\" confidence and nature Reset, even at high speeds, being away from screens and surrounded by the elements provides a massive mental health \"hard reset.\"","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":6,"description":"12th, 2025, at the scenic Narayangiri Hills. The event successfully brought together over 500 enthusiastic students for an adventure-packed journey through rugged and thrilling hill trails. Uniquely combining trekking with social impact, the initiative included a meaningful cleanliness drive to reinforce environmental responsibility. Participants actively engaged in collecting litter and promoting eco-consciousness while navigating the breathtaking views of the hillside.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QbXoOqu-4Gb6Cv3dhX-re","name":"FistFull","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/NzJ516Idgx-IbLQK1GJuP.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The project successfully reinforced RVCE’s dedication to community welfare and addressing food insecurity. The significant volume of food collected provided substantial support to hunger relief efforts through the collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":1,"description":"\"Fist Full\" was an impactful initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, held from November 15th to 29th. The project''s primary phase focused on combating hunger by inviting students to donate essential food staples. Students were encouraged to contribute specific quantities, namely 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal.\\nDaily collections were managed within the Civil Department to facilitate easy participation from the student body. The initiative highlighted how small individual efforts can collectively drive significant societal change and reinforce community solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Social Service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/QTahlPdQSyktXwPKVp40I.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-SzHyN563iwati8CGEAFh","name":"FistFull","slNo":6,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/wIUe4ou0kBR69n4sLswQ2.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"The drive received an overwhelming response, successfully collecting over 6,700 kg of rice. In addition to the rice, the student body donated more than 800 kg of toor daal. Massive student engagement was recorded, with over 1,750 students participating in the donation drive.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The project''s primary phase focused on combating hunger by inviting students to donate essential food staples. Students were encouraged to contribute specific quantities, namely 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal. Daily collections were managed within the Civil Department to facilitate easy participation from the student body.","aicteMapping":"Social Service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"JYMDlsu3ZPZS8wmq8yods","name":"Through the eyes of Youth ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/SWkMuk9E6_LzGVzEcrOOt.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"Enhanced social awareness and a sense of responsibility among all participating students.\\nFostered a sustainability-oriented mindset aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\\nIncreased awareness and understanding of international sustainability issues among the youth.\\nImproved participants'' artistic, observational, and visual storytelling skills through creative engagement platforms.\\nEncouraged critical thinking and the expression of social and environmental concerns.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The students were required to take a picture of their choice and map to to a SDG enhancing sustainability while also showcasing their talent and photography skills.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/-fRllOaBWpsQvjuo4l49m.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qGDetqIGahNc3wbG-RP59","name":"Secret Santa","slNo":8,"place":"Samartha Trust","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/jZi2AFAjhN71dgoT-B14v.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event brought immense happiness and excitement to the children, filling their day with joy and warmth. Participation in activities helped boost their confidence and social interaction. The celebration created meaningful memories that extended beyond material gifts. Volunteers experienced a deep sense of satisfaction by contributing positively to society. Overall, the event strengthened values of kindness, inclusion, and community bonding.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-25","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Secret Santa event was organized to spread joy among children in various NGOs during Christmas. Volunteers visited different organizations and distributed gifts to ensure that every child felt special and appreciated. The celebration included cake-cutting ceremonies that symbolized unity and togetherness. Interactive games, group activities, and Christmas carol singing were arranged to actively engage the children. Volunteers dressed in festive attire, creating a lively and cheerful atmosphere throughout the event.","aicteMapping":"Social Service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c707ecbe-ca57-427d-b6fd-4d6b318af94b/KUiZ6R4IjKlCb3wvdLYT3.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 17:38:01.826649+00', '2026-01-30 20:57:21.552786+00'), ('b81bed5f-86ee-4a69-a290-3bd519c82fa1', 'da1436ef-65fd-440d-b08a-95dcc9e8149e', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 04:48:44.324607+00', '2026-01-31 04:48:44.892652+00'), ('ba22c2b3-df6c-46b4-81c8-e6880332c18e', 'feefc575-4838-4d99-94c4-401ce2e9a5be', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22BT042","name":"Radni Chandrashekhar Degaonkar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Biotechnology","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"riJwqqUrFRDUnvPyd3k5p","name":"Environmental Day Quiz","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Environmental Day Quiz was successfully conducted and\\ncreated a strong impact by increasing awareness about\\nenvironmental issues and sustainability among participants. The\\nactivity encouraged students to think critically about ecological\\nchallenges and motivated them to adopt environmentally friendly\\nhabits in daily life.\\nThe event also strengthened teamwork and learning spirit among students while supporting SPARK’s goal of promoting\\ncommunity development and responsible citizenship. Overall, the quiz served as an effective awareness initiative by combining knowledge-sharing with student participation, making it a valuable extracurricular experience. \\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Environmental Day Quiz was organised by the students of\\nSPARK – IUCEE RVCE Student Chapter as a community\\ninitiative to enhance environmental awareness and education\\namong students. The quiz event focused on spreading knowledge about important environmental concepts, global sustainability issues, and eco-friendly practices that contribute to a greener future.\\nThe event encouraged participants to actively engage in learning through an interactive quiz format, which made the awareness campaign both informative and interesting. It served as a platform for students to showcase their knowledge while also understanding the importance of being environmentally\\nresponsible citizens. By conducting this initiative, SPARK\\nsuccessfully promoted sustainable thinking and inspired students to take small steps towards protecting the environment. ","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BtXqRM541g-Gaz2_E1BeR","name":"Through the Eyes of of Youth – SDG Photo Competition ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"The SDG Photo Competition successfully spread awareness about\\nsustainable development and encouraged students to reflect on\\nreal-world challenges through photography. With strong\\nparticipation and engagement, the event created a platform for\\nstudents to express innovative perspectives on social and\\nenvironmental issues. The well-managed coordination by the\\norganizing team ensured transparency and quality through\\nplagiarism checks, structured evaluation, and smooth handling of participant registrations. Overall, the competition strengthened the culture of SDG awareness within the campus and highlighted the importance of youth-driven initiatives for social change. ","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“Through the Eyes of Youth” is an SDG Photo Competition hosted by SPARK (IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter) to create awareness about the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) among students. The event was conducted from 7th August 2023 to 13th August 2023, witnessing participation from around 330 students, including 289 students from RV College of Engineering. The competition encouraged participants to submit meaningful photographs related to SDGs, promoting creativity along with social responsibility.\\nThe organizing team played a key role in ensuring the smooth\\nexecution of the event by managing publicity, participant profile\\nverification, digital content creation, and plagiarism checks to\\nmaintain originality and fairness. Due to the high number of\\nregistrations, the organizers actively coordinated for multiple days to make the event successful. The competition concluded with the announcement of the Top 25 finalists, Special Mentions, and Top 3 winners on 19th August 2023, making it a well-structured and impactful initiative. ","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xbAOer2H18LIPBrOSUcX_","name":"Rush Hours 4.0","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-11-20","duration":6,"outcomes":"This was a fun event that helped us come out of our stressful college life and have some fun by participating in various events and competing against various participants to win the game.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The 4th version of the mega-event helped the participants to Come out of their stressful routine and boredom, and also welcomed the juniors into the college with bang.\\nProject Description : A community service and Professional development project which went on for 5 days and included a pre-event task to build interest among the participants\\nfollowed by 8 main tasks. The participants run for their positions as each task led to the elimination of a certain number of teams; with 250+ participants; participating actively, followed by regular updates through event dashboard and leader board. The event was a huge success with the participants contributing to society along with having fun in this process.\\nThe top 5 teams were rewarded with OTT subscriptions and other prizes.\\nTASK 1: Brainwave Blazers\\nRUSH HOURS 4.0\\nThe quiz was a time based quiz conducted through Quizizz online platform with a time limit of 15 mins for 20 questions. The quiz tested the general knowledge of the participants. The\\nquestions were related to Rotary , Rotaract and college.\\nTASK 2 : Spectrum Spark\\nIn this task participants were asked to create handmade and digital poster based on the topics assigned to each team. The topics included: Child Labour, Dowry, Global Warming,\\nAddiction to electronic devices, Girl education, Save environment, etc\\nTASK 3: Blossom Bonanza\\nIts a plantation drive event where each member of the teams were asked to plant a sapling and nurture it. This task went on for three days where on the first day they planted the\\nsaplings and in the next two days they watered and groomed it. The participants were asked to upload videos of them doing the same once in the morning and once in the evening.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"P-wD9zQEqBVUA4ZMeLnKT","name":"UTPT Quiz","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"We gained a lot of knowledge about our country and the current affairs related to India. All in all, it was an enjoyable experience, and we had a lot of fun participating with our fellow batchmates and competing against them.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":"This was a quiz that was conducted by the Quizcorp club of RVCE. The theme of the quiz was All India Quiz, and it consisted of a lot of teams. The questions were based on general knowledge about our country and were moderately difficult in nature. It consisted of 2 rounds, wherein around 5 teams made it to the 2nd round, with one of them emerging as the winner.","aicteMapping":"Quiz","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/feefc575-4838-4d99-94c4-401ce2e9a5be/8toUsx6R7EJW45-AOv6Dt.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gbSVdASIQL-GdGMX48Chz","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":5,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive\\nduring the trek, dedicated to preserving the environment. Commencing at 7:30 AM, participants eagerly boarded the bus to the trekking site, brimming with enthusiasm for the day ahead. Prior to embarking on the adventure, comprehensive safety instructions and event particulars were disseminated to all attendees. Traversing the picturesque Kunagalu Betta Hills, the trek unfolded as a resounding success, offering participants a memorable journey amidst breathtaking landscapes. Over 750 individuals enthusiastically engaged in the trekking experience, contributing to the event''s vibrant atmosphere.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 11:18:51.879815+00', '2026-02-02 08:28:36.784189+00'), ('ba8bfa14-2d95-419e-aa0f-4f3e283d0c5d', 'de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC144","name":"Shreyas Aradhya K","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Nkm-lFba9HNb73-86B1qR","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2023","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/Ka4PgqG3PGddr7FzA_dnU.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp resulted in the successful collection of a substantial number of blood units, helping support local hospitals and save lives. It also enhanced awareness among \\nstudents about voluntary blood donation while fostering a strong sense of social responsibility and service.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was successfully organized at RVCE and BGS Hospital under the aegis of the National Service Scheme (NSS). The camp was conducted with the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and creating awareness about the importance of donating blood to save lives. \\nThe event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students, faculty members, and staff, reflecting the strong sense of social responsibility within the RVCE community. Qualified medical\\nprofessionals and trained volunteers ensured that the donation process was carried out in a safe, hygienic, and well-organized manner, adhering to all medical protocols.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4NWAEdXgGfN04UqgfHu3Y","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/VlrQuFwxKIxYx_xSSwRTl.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully promoted awareness about health, fitness, and social service. It fostered teamwork, discipline, and community engagement among students while motivating them to contribute towards a meaningful cause.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The NSS Unit of RVCE organized the flagship event “Utsarga Marathon 2024” at the RV College of Engineering campus. The event aimed to promote fitness, community participation, and contribution towards a noble social cause. The marathon was conducted from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM, witnessing enthusiastic participation from students and staff members. Participants\\nregistered in advance and gathered at the venue early in the morning, filled with energy and motivation. The event encouraged a spirit of unity, discipline, and social responsibility while highlighting the importance of physical well-being and service to society. Medals and participation certificates were awarded to recognize the efforts of the participants.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"g76k7oriS99sGXIkS3wKy","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Ke Liye ","slNo":3,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/-kiYow5UQrASAh43XWlI2.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Mera Pehla Vote - Desh Ke Liye campaign successfully enhanced voter awareness and civic consciousness among students and their extended social networks. Participants gained valuable experience in creating impactful digital content for social causes while developing skills in visual storytelling, video editing, copywriting, and social media management. ","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The social media awareness campaign was conducted under the initiative “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” in collaboration with AICTE to promote voter awareness and encourage first\\ntime voters to exercise their democratic rights responsibly. Students actively created and shared engaging content such as pictures, reels, podcasts, Instagram posts, and blogs to highlight the importance of voting, electoral processes, and responsible citizenship. By using multiple social media platforms, the campaign successfully reached a wide audience and inspired youth participation in democratic activities. The initiative also helped students develop creativity, communication, and digital outreach skills, while respective clubs supported participants with content guidelines, necessary resources, and managed submissions through designated upload links, ensuring smooth coordination and effective implementation. ","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qjHDeTeYWoRjwBJsl6_8z","name":"Independence Day Quiz in Collaboration with NSS, RVCE","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/j0TVbf3nOup-zNN94rA-w.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Independence Day Quiz helped enhance students’ awareness of India’s freedom struggle, constitutional values, and national heritage while promoting active participation and critical thinking. It encouraged teamwork and healthy competition among participants through an engaging learning experience. Overall, the activity fostered a strong sense of patriotism and social responsibility in line with the objectives of NSS.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"An Independence Day Quiz was successfully conducted in collaboration with NSS, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) as part of the Independence Day celebrations. The activity was aimed at promoting awareness among students about India’s freedom struggle, constitutional values, national symbols, and the contributions of freedom fighters. The quiz witnessed active participation from students across various disciplines and encouraged healthy competition, critical thinking, and patriotic spirit. Through this engaging and knowledge-based event, the initiative effectively combined learning with national pride, aligning with the objectives of NSS to foster civic responsibility and social awareness among students.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"InIB3qwn09XxWtqKBCDTY","name":"Blood Donation 2024","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/plJ0nH0nWHwmW4_1CaR44.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp resulted in the successful collection of a substantial number of blood units, helping support local hospitals and save lives. It also enhanced awareness among students about voluntary blood donation while fostering a strong sense of social responsibility and service. ","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":5,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was successfully organized at RVCE under the aegis of the National Service Scheme (NSS). The camp  was conducted with the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and creating awareness about the importance of \\ndonating blood to save lives. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students, faculty members, and staff, reflecting the strong sense of social responsibility within the RVCE community. Qualified medical professionals and trained volunteers ensured that the donation process was carried out in a safe, hygienic, and well-organized manner, adhering to all medical protocols. ","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UjUyGqxJ4AXlpzYNoqVgZ","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/JDj9-miQO-vqSE-2ghMbm.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The event successfully promoted student engagement in community service activities. It enhanced teamwork, organizational skills, and social responsibility among participants, contributing positively to co-curricular development. ","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized the event “FISTFUL” at  the Civil Engineering Department, RV College of Engineering, from 15th to 29nd November 2024. The event was conducted under the guidance of Faculty Coordinator Dr. Rajalakshmi Mudbidre. Student coordinators included Rtr. Pratham M Pimpalshende (President) and Rtr. Aditi Amit Kallolkar (Vice President and Event Chair). Fist Full was organized as a community-oriented initiative aimed at encouraging student participation in social service and collective responsibility. Students actively took part in the event activities conducted throughout the week, demonstrating teamwork, leadership, and commitment toward service-oriented goals. ","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"W_YfesDTGfBPEgzik3cGG","name":"Nasha Mukt Bharat Pledge ","slNo":7,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/0T8nmPn0IRpIe7TX4-C-Z.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-08-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity increased awareness among students regarding the physical, mental, and social consequences of substance abuse. It encouraged participants to adopt positive habits and commit to a drug-free way of life. The pledge reinforced a sense of social responsibility and collective action towards creating a healthier and safer society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Nasha Mukt Bharat Pledge was conducted to create awareness about the harmful effects of substance abuse and to promote a healthy, addiction-free lifestyle among participants. As part of the activity, students collectively took a pledge to abstain from drugs and actively contribute towards building a drug-free society. The initiative emphasized personal responsibility, social awareness, and the importance of making informed life choices, aligning with the national mission of Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"d9W09C_rcWIcv17zqSaOz","name":"IEEE MTTs and AP-s DL","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/vcjDtdsaTCyDn2WGoe-4E.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-06-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The workshop enhanced participants’ understanding of advanced antenna concepts and emerging research trends in wireless and satellite  communications.  It also inspired students  to pursue innovation and research in antenna technologies while strengthening industry–academia interaction. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-01","hoursSpent":6,"description":"An IEEE Distinguished Lecturer (DL) Workshop on Advanced Antenna Technologies was conducted at RV College of Engineering, Bangalore, organized jointly by the IEEE AP-S Bangalore Chapter and IEEE MTT-S RVCE Student Chapter. The workshop featured eminent IEEE Fellows and experts who delivered technical talks on satellite and ground antenna systems, hybrid UTD-ECM solutions, polarization in electromagnetics, and open-source 5G testbeds. The event saw active participation from around 100 students, researchers, and professionals, providing a strong platform for knowledge exchange and interaction with leading academicians and industry specialists. ","aicteMapping":"Volunteering","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Edfc7MVy2fgQcx9MUv2GS","name":"Skill Lab Conducted","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/Zi3C6zlzPj0kY22sFAhLd.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-23","duration":5,"outcomes":"Participants developed a strong foundational understanding of ROS and core robotics concepts. The hands-on sessions improved their practical skills in robot simulation, programming, and system integration. Overall, the Skill Lab enhanced technical confidence and sparked interest in robotics research and industry-oriented applications.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-19","hoursSpent":5,"description":"A Skill Lab was conducted for a duration of one week focusing on Robot Operating System (ROS) and robotics to provide participants with hands-on exposure to modern robotic frameworks and tools. The program covered fundamental concepts of robotics, ROS architecture, nodes, topics, services, and basic robot simulation and control. Through interactive sessions, practical demonstrations, and guided lab exercises, participants gained practical insights into developing, simulating, and understanding robotic systems, bridging the gap between theoretical knowledge and real-world applications.","aicteMapping":"Volunteering","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rPyOW9kLgiyEpS45N92Qg","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/liP5J-ySM3aMlxw1N8NW2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"A Blood Donation Camp was successfully organized at RVCE under the aegis of the National Service Scheme (NSS). The camp was conducted with the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and creating awareness about the importance of donating blood to save lives. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students, faculty members, and staff, reflecting the strong sense of social responsibility within the RVCE community. Qualified medical professionals and trained volunteers ensured that the donation process was carried out in a safe, hygienic, and well-organized manner, adhering to all medical protocols.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":5,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was successfully organized at RVCE under the aegis of the National Service Scheme (NSS). The camp was conducted with the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and creating awareness about the importance of donating blood to save lives. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students, faculty members, and staff, reflecting the strong sense of social responsibility within the RVCE community. Qualified medical professionals and trained volunteers ensured that the donation process was carried out in a safe, hygienic, and well-organized manner, adhering to all medical protocols.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ytPzUyTzGLX98IV-GACmp","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/de3e4e3c-d0ef-4a5a-b284-d8de0468a0e7/ZKStmNtGN8QifO4NXWLMs.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"The event successfully promoted student engagement in community service activities. It enhanced teamwork, organizational skills, and social responsibility among participants, contributing positively to co-curricular development.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized the event “FISTFUL” at the Civil Engineering Department, RV College of Engineering, from 15th to 29nd November 2024. The event was conducted under the guidance of Faculty Coordinator Dr. Rajalakshmi Mudbidre. Student coordinators included Rtr. Pratham M Pimpalshende (President) and Rtr. Aditi Amit Kallolkar (VicePresident and Event Chair). FISTFULL was organized as a community-oriented initiative aimed at encouraging student participation in social service and collective responsibility. Students actively took part in the event activities conducted throughout the week, demonstrating teamwork, leadership, and commitment toward service-oriented goals.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 15:16:23.54741+00', '2026-01-30 17:17:50.011547+00'), ('bbb638f7-af80-41ce-97e8-b22ab303c1d5', 'eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS139","name":"Posam Harshitha","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"6E6ulf4HFgjQLzCULODpV","name":"Project Pustak 2023","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/1RAnrIMGV0bU8l3mlbotP.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-05-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The dedication and perseverance of the volunteers were instrumental in empowering rural and underprivileged students, in line with achieving the club’s mission of making a tangible, lasting impact on society and fostering a sense of global solidarity.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-05-12","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative\\naimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students\\nresiding in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from\\neach compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring\\nand donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The\\ncollected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital\\nresources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\n\\nTo summarize, Project Pustak is a noble initiative aimed to provide\\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"g95_ylneJYRE8hYmaR7eM","name":"Biofuel Day Essay Competition","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/WQM-7N9OfCoHSsfpwVMW0.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event enhanced participants’ knowledge of biofuels, sustainable energy systems, and their environmental impact.\\nIt fostered critical thinking, creativity, teamwork, and practical problem-solving skills among students.\\nParticipants were motivated to adopt and advocate sustainable practices contributing to a cleaner and more energy-secure future.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-08","hoursSpent":3,"description":"NSS RVCE organized the International Biofuel Day Essay Competition and Model Making on 8th August to promote awareness about biofuels and their significance in achieving a greener and energy-secure future. The event provided a platform for students to express their understanding and ideas through essay writing while also encouraging innovation and practical learning through the development of biofuel-related working models. By combining intellectual discussion with hands-on creativity, the activity emphasized sustainability, environmental responsibility, and the role of youth in addressing global energy challenges.","aicteMapping":"Extra-Curriculars","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6bskb8k5717Bp7jJ0ThDp","name":"Fistfull 2025","slNo":4,"place":"Civil Engineering Department, R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/Lj43e25w1V-NAGO0ks4Fv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"The Fist Full event enabled effective collection and distribution of food grains to support vulnerable communities. It promoted social responsibility, empathy, and active student participation. The initiative strengthened collaboration between the institution and community service organizations while creating a lasting social impact","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Fist Full event was a flagship community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE under Rotary Bangalore South, with the objective of combating food insecurity and supporting vulnerable communities. Conducted from 17th to 22nd November 2025, the event encouraged collective social responsibility by involving students in contributing essential food grains. Each participating student donated either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, transforming small individual contributions into a large-scale humanitarian effort. The initiative was aligned with Rotary’s Community Service avenue, specifically focusing on the theme of Fighting Disease through nutritional support. A total of 2146 students actively participated, demonstrating strong student engagement and awareness toward social causes. The collected food grains were systematically sorted, recorded, and prepared for distribution to ensure transparency and effective utilization","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"P1-CU8jX2y3Otakamih_f","name":"Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":5,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/ZPadumnb8JUsy8IuZsJLp.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully raised awareness about environmental conservation and sustainable living among students.\\nIt motivated participants to actively contribute to a greener campus by planting and nurturing saplings.\\nThe event strengthened social responsibility while rewarding student participation with 15 AICTE activity points.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-03","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Kannada Sangha, RV College of Engineering organized the Environment Day initiative – “Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree” to promote environmental awareness and individual responsibility among students. As part of this meaningful campaign, every student who purchased the Kannada Habba 2025 T-shirt received a tree sapling along with guidelines for plantation, encouraging direct participation in sustainability efforts. The distribution of T-shirts and saplings was carried out within the college campus, aligning cultural celebration with environmental action and marking World Environment Day through a practical, impact-driven activity.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t-fEeLlUckntHrKncoCB8","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":6,"place":"Online","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/jB2Hshm3POqtKB57i3v3C.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced participants’ teamwork, creativity, and strategic thinking through diverse, skill-oriented challenges. It provided a dynamic platform for students to showcase their talents across multiple domains, including problem-solving, social awareness, artistic expression, and digital engagement. Rush Hours 5.0 also strengthened student interaction and leadership skills, leaving a lasting impact by promoting collaboration, innovation, and healthy competition among participants.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Rush Hours 5.0 was a five-day interactive event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE from 17th to 21st March 2025, aimed at fostering teamwork, creativity, and problem-solving skills among participants. The event brought together over 450 participants who engaged in a series of innovative and competitive tasks designed to encourage collaboration and healthy competition. Each day featured a unique challenge, ranging from online problem-solving activities to creative and performance-based tasks, ensuring continuous engagement and enthusiasm. The structured elimination process added excitement and motivation, culminating in the selection of top-performing teams on the final day.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sNypihq3GnKlERm2I0slU","name":"Female Foeticide Awarness Walkathon 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus Premises","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/DCSPhz4I9A6YSOS5C2jCK.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/v6ezUzTZPBTdVMBp2hpCa.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon effectively raised awareness about female foeticide and gender-based discrimination among participants and the wider community. It encouraged meaningful dialogue, inspired collective responsibility, and reinforced the importance of standing against gender injustice. The event fostered social consciousness and strengthened community participation toward promoting equality and respect for the girl child.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"On the occasion of Mother’s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon to highlight the critical issue of female foeticide and promote the value of the girl child in society. The walkathon began in the early hours of the morning from the RVCE campus and witnessed the participation of over 350 individuals, including students, faculty members, and supportive parents. The event was marked by thought-provoking placards and powerful slogans, creating a strong atmosphere of unity and social responsibility while spreading awareness on gender equality and dignity.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XyRuNh_INP9w_fNOy7dg-","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/U2vCklwAyk0CCNOYDMceW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"The dedication and perseverance of the volunteers were instrumental in empowering rural and underprivileged students, in line with achieving the club’s mission of making a tangible, lasting impact on society and fostering a sense of global solidarity.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative\\naimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students\\nresiding in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from\\neach compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring\\nand donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The\\ncollected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital\\nresources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\n\\nTo summarize, Project Pustak is a noble initiative aimed to provide\\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"n4E9vyeeSN9n_QdxYXDdi","name":"Fistfull 2024","slNo":9,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/StkLAipJwbWKPKr02pM-U.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The initiative received an overwhelming response, with 1750+ students participating and contributing approximately 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal. The collected food grains supported hunger-relief efforts and reinforced RVCE’s commitment to community welfare. The event fostered empathy, unity, and social awareness among students, leaving a lasting impact through collaborative service.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Fist Full was a community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November. The initiative aimed to combat hunger by encouraging students to contribute 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. Daily collections were organized in the Civil Department, ensuring systematic participation and smooth coordination. The event highlighted the importance of collective responsibility, demonstrating how small individual contributions can create meaningful social impact.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"e8OTr_wcBoTOBUda8xqsV","name":"Project Pustak 2024","slNo":12,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/VmirNHzAK3fufZHoTzxGq.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The dedication and perseverance of the volunteers were instrumental in empowering rural and underprivileged students, in line with achieving the club’s mission of making a tangible, lasting impact on society and fostering a sense of global solidarity.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative\\naimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students\\nresiding in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from\\neach compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring\\nand donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The\\ncollected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational\\nmaterials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital\\nresources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\n\\nTo summarize, Project Pustak is a noble initiative aimed to provide\\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Js7l5lzU5gR0dxvaESWpS","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":13,"place":"R V College of Engineering Campus Premises","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/hd_2byrWXYN8sCio_SGdV.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/9UCwbE1zasqRiGOrasUvz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 successfully combined fitness, charity, and community spirit, advancing educational opportunities for needy children and fostering a sense of social commitment among participants.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025, organized by NSS RVCE, was a significant event that celebrated health, fitness, and charity. Scheduled to take place on April 6, 2025, at RV College of Engineering, this marathon aimed to bring the community together to run for a cause that extends beyond physical activity to making a lasting social impact. The event''s motto, \"Help a Child, Change the World,\" emphasized the marathon’s mission to support educational initiatives for underprivileged children and transform their futures.\\n\\nParticipants could choose between 5 km and 10 km race categories, with donations contributing directly to providing education for children in need. Beyond the physical challenge, the marathon represented a collective commitment to social responsibility and charity-driven action, motivating involvement through both fitness and service.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uStU9DDncbKprAkmIyAtp","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":14,"place":"R V College of Engineering Campus Premises","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/VZm2Fit8S9QhVkZGsFFap.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully fostered awareness about physical fitness and social responsibility among participants.\\nIt contributed directly to supporting educational opportunities for children in need through collective donations.\\nThe event strengthened community bonding by uniting students, faculty, and the public under a shared cause of compassion and change.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Utsarga Marathon, a spirited initiative that brings together fitness, compassion, and social responsibility. Scheduled for February 4th, 2024, at R V College of Engineering, this marathon is more than just a run—it is a collective movement towards meaningful change. With the inspiring theme “Help a Child Change the World”, the event aims to promote health and well-being while contributing towards the education of underprivileged children. Participants can choose between 5 km and 10 km runs, making it accessible to all age groups and fitness levels. By taking part, every runner becomes a catalyst for hope, proving that small steps taken together can create a lasting impact on society.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8Kcmrt4W4Xs5me7JQNaPx","name":"Police Marshall","slNo":15,"place":"R  V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/ycMbQ5--GSGqWPD_fkj0f.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"This initiative presents a non-violent, youth-led model of security and governance by fostering collaboration between educational institutions and law enforcement to combat cybercrime and drug abuse. It serves as a scalable global example of strengthening civil–police partnerships and building resilient, secure communities. The effort strongly aligns with SDG 16 by reinforcing peace and institutional trust, and supports SDG 3 by promoting youth health and well-being through substance abuse prevention.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":3,"description":"A high-profile civic engagement initiative organized collaboratively by NSS RVCE, the Bengaluru City Police, and Aarohana Foundation. The event focused on training student volunteers to become Police Marshals, thereby creating a structured youth force dedicated to social responsibility. Key focus areas of the training and subsequent roles include combating drug abuse and preventing cyber crimes, culminating in a formal Capping Ceremony by the Police Department to recognize the volunteers as role models.\\n\\nThis event cultivates profound civic responsibility and leadership skills among students by placing them in a formal partnership with law enforcement. Volunteers gain critical knowledge about real-world societal threats like cyber crime and drug abuse, making them informed and proactive citizens. Being formally recognized as a Police Marshal elevates their status as positive role models within the community, encouraging a commitment to public service and safety throughout their lives.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5-b44u29tisBfK59IWAVK","name":"Through the eyes of Youth","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/uZFlwJhK7LblSIKFT5eB9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"The event enhanced participants’ awareness and understanding of the UN SDGs through hands-on creative engagement.\\nIt provided students with an opportunity to develop visual storytelling skills while expressing social responsibility.\\nThe competition successfully fostered youth participation, dialogue, and advocacy for sustainable development through art and innovation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":2,"description":"“Through the Eyes of You(th)!” is an SDG-themed photography competition organized by SPARK: The IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter, aimed at empowering students to creatively express their perspectives on global challenges defined by the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The event encourages participants to capture original photographs that reflect real-world issues such as sustainability, equality, environment, and social responsibility, and to complement their visuals with a meaningful narrative. By blending creativity with awareness, the competition serves as a platform for youth to voice their concerns, ideas, and hopes for a sustainable future through the powerful medium of photography.","aicteMapping":"Extra-Curricular Activity","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"aOnsK5GhHOVOPJtsu5NSG","name":"Campaign on Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/vQ_6C0VGfr9y_fEzWwYk6.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eafb682b-d442-41fb-a678-a6344a4a14b5/1MzXniq7S2Ze39Hig04cN.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully increased awareness about the importance of voting and democratic participation among students. Participants gained a better understanding of India’s electoral system and the role of citizens in strengthening democracy. The initiative empowered young voters to make informed choices while reinforcing responsible and active citizenship.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"NSS RVCE organized “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye”, an online awareness initiative aimed at encouraging young and first-time voters to actively participate in India’s democratic process. Through the MyGov platform, participants engaged in two key activities—taking the National Voters’ Pledge and completing a quiz on India’s democracy. The event sought to educate students about their constitutional rights and responsibilities while fostering a sense of civic duty and national pride among the youth.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 18:06:31.98904+00', '2026-01-29 18:09:25.535851+00'), ('bc9fb60e-8180-42fe-9a82-dbc7d450ed41', '2ff1ff41-b0d6-46f3-82f3-1b20efaca70c', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV24IS054","name":"Karthik K P","period":"2024-2028","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:24:56.909244+00', '2026-02-01 17:18:55.688221+00'), ('c3517f31-0f62-497f-8dea-dc500bcbfbe4', '6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI004","name":"Akshara Sridhara","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"YZxO8Ki6U1qlaYQdVYil4","name":"Tanuja Screening by NSS","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/XKM2M96THhNEdD-nG3ias.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The movie screening created a strong impact by increasing awareness among students about the ground realities of rural life and the importance of social responsibility. Participants developed a deeper understanding of rural challenges such as limited access to education, social inequality, and the need for collective community efforts. The activity helped students realize the role of youth and engineers in contributing to rural development through awareness, innovation, and service. It also highlighted the importance of empathy, ethical values, and active citizenship. Personally, the screening reinforced the idea that meaningful change begins with awareness and involvement, and it motivated students to actively participate in future NSS rural outreach programs with a more informed and sensitive perspective toward societal issues.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":8,"description":"NSS team of RV College of Engineering (RVCE), held a screening of the Kannada movie Tanuja was organised on 14th July 2023 at the RVCE campus. The activity was planned with the objective of spreading awareness about rural issues and sensitizing students to the social, economic, and cultural realities of rural India through a powerful visual medium. Tanuja was chosen for its strong social message and realistic portrayal of challenges faced by individuals and families in rural settings, including issues related to education, social responsibility, gender sensitivity, and community development. NSS volunteers and students actively participated in the screening, which was followed by informal discussions among participants to reflect on the themes presented in the film and their relevance to real-life rural conditions. The activity effectively used cinema as an educational tool to engage students emotionally and intellectually with the objectives of rural outreach.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/qop5zBgow-3ChZwR-23kZ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qwDvEnzH4XU8w2IfZMCAX","name":"Science, Space and Technology Essay Competition","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/wC-xKiFIOQC_3o3iurf59.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-11-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The essay competition successfully enhanced awareness about the significance of science, space research, and appropriate technologies in national development. It helped participants improve their research, analytical, and technical writing skills while encouraging critical thinking on how advanced technologies can be adapted for practical and inclusive use. Students gained insights into the societal impact of space and scientific innovations, particularly in areas such as communication, agriculture, disaster management, and rural development. The activity also reinforced the responsibility of future engineers to develop technologies that are sustainable, affordable, and beneficial to all sections of society. Personally, the competition fostered a deeper appreciation for the role of science and technology in solving real-life challenges and motivated participants to apply their technical knowledge toward socially relevant and impactful solutions.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-11-01","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Under NSS, RV College of Engineering (RVCE), a Science, Space and Technology Essay Competition was organised on 1st November 2023 at the RVCE campus as part of the initiative to promote appropriate technologies and scientific thinking among students. The competition aimed to encourage participants to explore the role of science and space technologies in addressing real-world problems, especially in the context of sustainable development and societal needs. Students from various departments participated by presenting essays that highlighted innovations in science and technology, applications of space research, and the importance of developing cost-effective, accessible, and locally relevant technologies. The activity provided a platform for students to express their ideas, research perspectives, and creative solutions while strengthening their understanding of how technological advancements can be aligned with social welfare.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/Z16VyGsMaqWRuWoDwpcdV.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"xu0whyPXfNtjeJ92URPIQ","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/0iekN9JjdF1M0RaJmy_zC.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully raised awareness about the significance of maintaining physical fitness and adopting healthy habits. Participants experienced the positive impact of collective physical activity and gained motivation to incorporate exercise into their daily routines. The event emphasized the strong connection between physical health, mental well-being, and productivity. It also helped inculcate values such as perseverance, teamwork, and self-discipline among participants. Personally, the marathon reinforced the understanding that health awareness initiatives play a vital role in shaping a proactive and health-conscious society, and it motivated students to act as advocates for fitness and well-being within their peer groups and communities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-02-03","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized by NSS, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on 3rd February 2025 at the RVCE campus as part of its initiative to spread awareness about health, fitness, and the importance of an active lifestyle. The marathon aimed to encourage students, faculty, and staff to prioritize physical well-being and mental health through regular physical activity. NSS volunteers played an active role in coordinating the event, ensuring smooth execution and enthusiastic participation. Through this health marathon, participants were motivated to understand the role of exercise in preventing lifestyle-related diseases, managing stress, and improving overall quality of life. The event also promoted unity, discipline, and community participation while reinforcing the message that health is a fundamental aspect of holistic development.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/MRUk0AdBad5EMxS2TtWFT.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jW9D9Q5eymmeANA9PQxyS","name":"Anti Drug Awareness Program","slNo":4,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The online quiz and pledge program effectively increased awareness about the serious consequences of drug abuse and the importance of prevention at an individual and societal level. Students gained factual knowledge about substance abuse laws, health impacts, and government efforts to address the issue. Taking the pledge created a sense of personal responsibility and moral commitment toward maintaining a drug-free lifestyle. The activity also demonstrated how digital platforms can be effectively used for large-scale awareness campaigns. Personally, the program emphasized the value of informed decision-making, self-control, and social responsibility, and motivated participants to actively support government initiatives by promoting healthy habits and positive influence among peers.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"An Anti-Drug Awareness Quiz and Pledge Program was organized by NSS, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on 4th March 2024 at the RVCE campus, as part of a national-level initiative by the Government of India. The program was conducted online through an official government portal, enabling students to actively participate in the awareness drive. The activity consisted of an online quiz designed to test and enhance students’ knowledge about drug abuse, its harmful effects, legal aspects, and preventive measures. Following the quiz, participants took an online pledge committing themselves to lead a drug-free life and to spread awareness within their communities. NSS volunteers encouraged maximum participation, reinforcing the importance of aligning student initiatives with national campaigns for social well-being.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/vpf9JKLzU03aqxB0G9opY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"97riwLxYCIom5sbcWqcIH","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye, Pledge to Vote","slNo":5,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/jG5G6buXzxOvfWTS8qkpl.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/TOuniBHukWLgz0PHmoR39.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program successfully enhanced awareness among students about the significance of voting and active citizenship in a democratic nation. Participants gained a clearer understanding of electoral rights, duties of voters, and the impact of informed voting on nation-building. The pledge instilled a sense of responsibility and commitment toward participating in elections with integrity and awareness. The activity also highlighted the effectiveness of digital platforms in reaching a large audience and promoting civic engagement. Personally, the program reinforced the importance of exercising one’s right to vote as a fundamental duty and motivated students to contribute positively to the democratic process by encouraging informed and responsible participation in future elections.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-05","hoursSpent":16,"description":"As part of its contribution to a national-level initiative of the Government of India, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized the “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” Online Quiz and Pledge Program on 5th March 2024 at the RVCE campus. The program was conducted online through an official Government of India portal with the objective of encouraging youth participation in the democratic process and promoting awareness about the importance of voting. The online quiz assessed participants’ knowledge of the Indian electoral system, constitutional rights, voting procedures, and the role of citizens in a democracy. Following the quiz, students took an online pledge to vote responsibly, uphold democratic values, and motivate others to actively participate in elections. NSS volunteers facilitated and promoted the activity to ensure wide student participation and alignment with the national campaign.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/nh3e-ybZNjTXyIemITwV_.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9-TdTJOJWToPRYlulg6om","name":"Quiz on Indian democracy","slNo":6,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program effectively enhanced students’ understanding of Indian democracy and the responsibilities associated with citizenship. Participants gained deeper insights into constitutional values, democratic institutions, and the importance of informed participation in elections and governance. The pledge fostered a sense of accountability and commitment toward protecting democratic ideals and practicing responsible citizenship. The activity also demonstrated how digital platforms can be effectively utilized to promote civic awareness on a large scale. Personally, the program reinforced the importance of democratic participation, respect for constitutional values, and the role of youth in strengthening the democratic foundation of the nation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"As part of its contribution to a national-level initiative of the Government of India, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized the “Quiz on Indian Democracy” Online Quiz and Pledge Program on 6th March 2024 at the RVCE campus. The program was conducted online through an official Government of India portal with the aim of strengthening awareness about democratic values, constitutional principles, and the functioning of the Indian political system. The online quiz covered key aspects of Indian democracy such as the Constitution, fundamental rights and duties, electoral processes, and the roles of citizens in governance. After completing the quiz, participants took an online pledge to uphold democratic values, respect the Constitution, and actively participate in democratic processes.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/zPI5mIc-P-kq2HUw-PgEl.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RMNcJsjgaE4CfZ7uvoh19","name":"Fistfull","slNo":7,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/UtjszOUvsbDcsfI9q-LV6.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/8r9qVHkRcf7JCUNIwOBXL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The initiative witnessed an overwhelming response, with over 1,750 students contributing to the collection of approximately 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal. The drive demonstrated the effectiveness of community-driven action in tackling critical issues such as hunger and food security. Participants gained awareness about food preservation, hygienic packaging, and the importance of reducing food wastage. For the volunteers, the project offered hands-on experience in coordination, logistics management, and collaboration with external organizations. Personally, the activity reinforced the understanding that even a “fistful” contribution, when multiplied by collective effort, can create a significant social impact and strengthen the spirit of empathy, unity, and service toward the community.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fist Full was an impactful social initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November 2024 at the RVCE campus. The first phase of the project focused on addressing hunger and food insecurity while creating awareness about the importance of food preservation, responsible storage, and proper packaging to minimize wastage. Students were encouraged to contribute 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, emphasizing how small, collective contributions can lead to large-scale social impact. Daily collection drives were conducted at the Civil Engineering Department, ensuring systematic aggregation and handling of the donated food grains. The initiative successfully mobilized student participation while reinforcing values of sharing, sustainability, and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/QosUqNS4w77gYMKQAjc0i.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"H9cCvrJUwIgki5bZzEyQw","name":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge (English)","slNo":8,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/MGoPCBpZm5hTmLOyv9L2P.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/Fpgc2FPAlPIxYXulvTIkl.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz effectively enhanced students’ understanding of India’s long-term development goals and the role of youth in achieving them. Participants gained insights into national policies, innovation-driven growth, sustainable development, and the importance of active citizenship. The pledge instilled a sense of responsibility, patriotism, and commitment toward contributing positively to the nation’s progress. The program also highlighted the effectiveness of digital platforms in engaging students with national initiatives in an interactive manner. Personally, the activity reinforced the belief that informed awareness, ethical conduct, and active participation by young citizens are essential in realizing the vision of Viksit Bharat, motivating students to align their academic and professional goals with national development priorities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-25","hoursSpent":8,"description":"As part of its contribution to a national-level initiative of the Government of India, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) conducted The Viksit Bharat Quiz, an online quiz and pledge program, on 25th January 2025 at the RVCE campus. The program was organized with the objective of creating awareness among students about the Viksit Bharat vision, focusing on India’s development goals, governance reforms, technological progress, sustainability, and citizen participation in nation-building. The activity was conducted through an official Government of India online platform, enabling large-scale student participation. The quiz tested participants’ knowledge on national development initiatives, constitutional values, innovation, and India’s roadmap toward becoming a developed nation. Following the quiz, participants took an online pledge committing themselves to contribute responsibly to the vision of a developed and inclusive India.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/CTxX3xsrLtRlYV9IuyWtO.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rpATa5EbbblQ3Ruk6zueU","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":9,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/jdo7J5fuAvju4l2GHpzgN.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-02-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon successfully raised awareness about the significance of maintaining physical fitness and adopting healthy habits. Participants experienced the positive impact of collective physical activity and gained motivation to incorporate exercise into their daily routines. The event emphasized the strong connection between physical health, mental well-being, and productivity. It also helped inculcate values such as perseverance, teamwork, and self-discipline among participants. Personally, the marathon reinforced the understanding that health awareness initiatives play a vital role in shaping a proactive and health-conscious society, and it motivated students to act as advocates for fitness and well-being within their peer groups and communities.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-02-08","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized by NSS, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on 3rd February 2025 at the RVCE campus as part of its initiative to spread awareness about health, fitness, and the importance of an active lifestyle. The marathon aimed to encourage students, faculty, and staff to prioritize physical well-being and mental health through regular physical activity. NSS volunteers played an active role in coordinating the event, ensuring smooth execution and enthusiastic participation. Through this health marathon, participants were motivated to understand the role of exercise in preventing lifestyle-related diseases, managing stress, and improving overall quality of life. The event also promoted unity, discipline, and community participation while reinforcing the message that health is a fundamental aspect of holistic development.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading Awareness on Health","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/esVpUmtxJwPrH2aEZ3zTI.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XDz0X-uoEodX4Ur8xDUBb","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":10,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/zuBvj7VyV4uXg0RQB1hEQ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/uqm6VgYBmq770WTdjkodF.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak had a meaningful social impact by directly addressing educational resource gaps faced by rural and underprivileged students. The initiative helped improve access to essential learning materials, contributing to better academic preparedness and motivation among beneficiaries. It also promoted the importance of community participation and collective responsibility in uplifting education standards. For the volunteers, the project fostered values of empathy, social responsibility, and leadership while offering practical experience in planning, fundraising, and collaboration with external organizations. Personally, the activity reinforced the understanding that even small individual contributions, when combined, can create a significant positive impact and play a crucial role in shaping the educational journey and future aspirations of young students.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative undertaken by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Pranav Foundation on 24th May 2024 at the RVCE campus. The project was aimed at supporting underprivileged students from rural areas by providing them with essential school supplies to encourage education and improve learning outcomes. As part of the initiative, a contribution of Rs. 100 or Rs. 350 was collected from compassionate donors, forming the financial foundation of the project. The funds collected were systematically utilized to procure educational resources such as textbooks, notebooks, stationery items, school bags, and other essential learning materials. Through this initiative, the Rotaract Club sought to create a supportive and inclusive learning environment for students who lack access to basic educational necessities, thereby motivating them to continue their education and aspire toward higher technical or vocational studies.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/tlUmBB6jK1uN4E6wyymxd.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OtAHGA7Nj4HNLFF2_m7L_","name":"Awareness Against Female Foeticide Walkathon","slNo":11,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/oTYuyxxzOFdXbdtzdkzzu.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/tzDGuqUovxSwufPI5tAQ8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon successfully raised awareness about the seriousness of female foeticide and its long-term impact on social balance and economic development. Participants gained a deeper understanding of gender equality, women empowerment, and the role of informed citizens in challenging social evils. The event encouraged open dialogue on women’s rights, legal provisions, and the importance of educating society to bring about sustainable change. For volunteers, the activity strengthened leadership, communication, and advocacy skills. Personally, the program reinforced the belief that awareness-driven initiatives and youth participation are crucial in addressing deep-rooted social issues and empowering women to contribute meaningfully to social and economic progress.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The Awareness Against Female Foeticide Walkathon was organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on 11th May 2025 at the RVCE campus, under the initiative of establishing an information-imparting platform for women and promoting their role in addressing social and economic issues. The walkathon aimed to create awareness about the social consequences of female foeticide and to promote gender equality, women’s rights, and the value of the girl child. Rotaract members and student participants took part in the walkathon carrying awareness messages and engaging in discussions that emphasized the importance of ethical responsibility, legal awareness, and societal change. The activity served as a strong visual and participatory campaign to sensitize the campus community and reinforce the need for collective action against gender-biased practices.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/hv0kCiD08h6yIAN9BvpBf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lsyHOX7sMH2UO96vGmigg","name":"India Quiz at Under The People Tree","slNo":12,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/KdXY7mdJvYYjfmt3L-mv6.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"The India Quiz successfully enhanced participants’ knowledge of India’s diverse tourism potential, including heritage sites, cultural practices, natural landscapes, and emerging tourist destinations. Students gained insights into how innovative methods such as quizzes, digital storytelling, and interactive engagement can promote tourism awareness effectively. The activity encouraged curiosity, teamwork, and analytical thinking while fostering pride in India’s cultural and historical richness. Personally, the quiz reinforced the understanding that tourism promotion is not limited to travel alone but can be strengthened through creative educational initiatives that inspire responsible tourism, cultural appreciation, and sustainable exploration of the country’s vast heritage.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The India Quiz was organized by Quiz Corp, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) as part of the cultural fest Under The People Tree (UTPT) 2025, held from 23rd to 25th May 2025 at the RVCE campus. The quiz was conducted with the objective of promoting tourism through innovative approaches by creating awareness about India’s rich cultural heritage, historical landmarks, geographical diversity, traditions, and lesser-known tourist destinations. The event adopted an engaging and interactive quiz format, encouraging participants to explore India beyond conventional tourism narratives. Through thought-provoking questions and creative rounds, the quiz highlighted how innovation, storytelling, and knowledge-sharing can play a vital role in enhancing tourism experiences and preserving cultural identity. The activity attracted enthusiastic participation from students and contributed to the festive and intellectually stimulating environment of UTPT 2025.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/DXYRtxtsxbi_Ko1jkRekK.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"np_gqazlv7FI8xw2fWV4F","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":13,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/1BFwJwm4Svl_zNXEjGlMt.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak created a meaningful impact by addressing the educational needs of underprivileged rural students and supporting their academic progress. The availability of essential learning materials helped improve students’ preparedness, confidence, and interest in education, thereby contributing to better academic performance and encouraging aspirations toward higher technical and vocational studies. The initiative also highlighted the importance of community involvement in educational upliftment. For the volunteers, the project fostered values of empathy, leadership, teamwork, and social responsibility, along with practical experience in fundraising, coordination, and collaboration with partner organizations. Personally, the activity reinforced the understanding that collective efforts and small individual contributions can bring about significant positive change and play a vital role in shaping the educational future of young learners.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative undertaken by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on 30th April 2025 at the RVCE campus, with the objective of supporting local schools to achieve better academic results and encouraging enrolment in higher technical and vocational education. The initiative focused on providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students from rural areas, thereby strengthening their learning foundation and academic motivation. As part of the project, a contribution of Rs. 100 or Rs. 350 was collected from compassionate donors, which formed the basis for the procurement of educational resources. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase textbooks, notebooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other essential learning materials that contribute to a supportive and conducive learning environment. The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, coordinated the procurement and distribution of these supplies to ensure maximum impact.\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/1HY97SL9O3ZNr2MJdTKsz.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4v6ToaEDgdy2Iub0koB6c","name":"Nasha Mukt Bharat, Kushal Bharat","slNo":14,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The program successfully increased awareness among students about the dangers of substance abuse and the importance of prevention. Participants developed a better understanding of the physical, psychological, and social impacts of drugs and alcohol. Taking the pledge instilled a sense of personal responsibility and commitment toward maintaining a healthy lifestyle. The activity also demonstrated the effectiveness of combining education and engagement to promote national campaigns and behavioral change. Personally, the initiative reinforced the importance of informed decision-making, peer influence in promoting positive choices, and the role of youth in contributing to a drug-free and socially responsible nation.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":8,"description":"As part of its contribution to a national-level initiative of the Government of India, RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized the Nasha Mukt Bharat, Kushal Barat, Say No To Drugs awareness program on 11th August 2025 at the RVCE campus. The initiative aimed to educate students about the harmful effects of substance abuse, including drugs, alcohol, and tobacco, and to promote a drug-free lifestyle. The program involved interactive sessions, awareness talks, and educational activities designed to highlight the health, social, and legal consequences of substance abuse. Participants were encouraged to take a pledge to abstain from drugs and to act as advocates for a Nasha Mukt Bharat, spreading awareness within their peer groups and communities. The initiative reinforced the government’s efforts to engage youth as responsible citizens in building a healthier and safer society.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/iaMM1a2-sbatps-1LzmFL.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oTGnJ9HTZkBt1EGj-fIWp","name":"Fistfull","slNo":15,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/4CewJeKGpH_Bl5ia-E4E4.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"The initiative received an overwhelming response, with 1,750+ students participating and donating approximately 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal. The program successfully addressed immediate food needs while creating awareness about food security, preservation, and responsible consumption. Volunteers gained experience in organization, coordination, and community engagement, while participants developed a stronger sense of social responsibility. Personally, the activity reinforced the understanding that small individual contributions, when combined, can create a significant impact, and highlighted the importance of youth participation in promoting community welfare and sustainable practices.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Fist Full was an impactful initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 1st to 17th November 2025 at the RVCE campus. The project focused on combating hunger and promoting awareness about food preservation and proper packaging. Students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily collection drives organized in the Civil Engineering Department. The initiative emphasized how collective small contributions can lead to meaningful societal change. Through this program, students learned about responsible food handling, storage, and the importance of minimizing wastage while actively contributing to community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6c91f813-7a2f-4e7e-8ba0-e613f2f0c419/Qs-Lzh4OjmoiMJ7JRPzbo.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Anand Jatti","designation":"Associate Professor, Dept. Of Electronics and Instrumentation Engineering"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-02 04:28:47.368706+00', '2026-02-02 07:03:35.884848+00'), ('c353bacf-fa99-4a95-a2ed-3c1d3f47362a', '6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY017","name":"Bandaru Jnyanadeep","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"8YdUg4m1NmMGkyITlZkLM","name":"Environmental day quiz ","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/lvDXBLRi04jBBDOuLXrpX.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Environmental Day Quiz was successfully conducted and created a strong impact by increasing awareness about environmental issues and sustainability among participants. The activity encouraged students to think critically about ecological challenges and motivated them to adopt environmentally friendly habits in daily life. The event also strengthened teamwork and learning spirit among students while supporting SPARK’s goal of promoting community development and responsible citizenship. Overall, the quiz served as an effective awareness initiative by combining knowledge-sharing with student participation, making it a valuable extracurricular experience.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Environmental Day Quiz organized by students of the SPARK, the IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter, was a commendable initiative that promoted environmental awareness and education. Students were involved in framing questions for conduction of Quiz and students of SPARK actively involved themselves in conducting quizzes by visiting each and every class and awarding the winners with a Plant Sapling, thereby spreading the awareness of being globally and environmentally responsible citizens. The quiz served as a platform for students to showcase their knowledge and understanding of crucial environmental issues, fostering a sense of responsibility towards sustainability. By organizing such events, students actively get engaged in promoting environmental consciousness among their peers and the broader community. Recognizing the effort and impact of organizing the Environmental Day Quiz, awarding AICTE Activity Points is justified as it signifies the students'' proactive involvement in addressing pressing global challenges, aligning with the emphasis on holistic education and socially responsible initiatives promoted by AICTE. This not only encourages student leadership and teamwork but also reinforces the importance of integrating considerations into academic  and environmental extracurricular activities.\\n","aicteMapping":"awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"W8_nhFVwlr1q_GkosGbVy","name":"Infosys Visit","slNo":2,"place":"Infosys Campus Mysore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/XhOm-Ljj3BJK1hr4OEBCK.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/0U3uzBDD3D3N3-mNrP2eA.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/C6FvI77vRDXM66ptEIavt.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/UF7LBSLso_YCZVU3XXmVZ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":1,"outcomes":"Outcome:\\nThe industrial visit to Infosys Mysore campus, organized by SPARK (IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter), proved to be an immensely enriching and transformative experience for all participating students. The visit successfully provided comprehensive firsthand exposure to a world-class corporate environment, allowing students to witness the operational excellence and cutting-edge infrastructure of one of India''s premier IT companies. Participants gained invaluable insights into how theoretical concepts taught in classrooms translate into real-world technological solutions and business applications. The campus tour offered students a glimpse into Infosys''s innovative work culture, state-of-the-art facilities, and advanced research and development initiatives, broadening their understanding of the IT industry''s scale and scope. Interactive sessions with industry professionals enabled students to learn about current technological trends, emerging career pathways, and the skills demanded by the corporate sector. Students observed industry best practices in software development, project management, and organizational workflows, which significantly enhanced their professional awareness and career readiness. The visit fostered networking opportunities, allowing students to connect with Infosys employees and alumni, potentially opening doors for future internships and employment prospects. This experiential learning opportunity ignited enthusiasm among participants about their future careers and motivated them to align their academic pursuits with industry requirements. The student organizers from SPARK demonstrated exceptional planning and coordination skills, ensuring seamless execution of the visit and maximum learning value for all attendees. In recognition of students'' proactive efforts in organizing and participating in this industry-academia bridging initiative, awarding AICTE Activity Points is highly justified, as it acknowledges their commitment to holistic learning beyond traditional classroom boundaries and aligns with AICTE''s vision of fostering experiential engineering education.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-31","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The industrial visit to Infosys, Mysore campus, organized by students of SPARK, the IUCEE-RVCE Student Chapter, was a valuable experiential learning opportunity. This event provided students with firsthand exposure to the corporate environment and the latest technological advancements at one of India''s leading IT companies. By touring the Infosys campus, students gained insights into real-world applications of their academic knowledge, witnessed industry best practices, and interacted with professionals in the field. Awarding AICTE Activity Points or participating in such industrial visits is justified as it recognizes students proactive efforts to bridge the gap between theoretical learning and practical industry applications. This aligns with AICTE''s vision of promoting industry-academia collaboration to ensure that students are well-prepared for the dynamic demands of the professional world, fostering a holistic and experiential approach to engineering education.","aicteMapping":"Activity 4 ","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-XjeSSqgc1EjhKVU34yZT","name":"ATAL Faculty Dvelopment Program on Cybersecurity for Industry 4.0","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/WMqhdl7jy-tQyVslYYP0P.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-10-14","duration":6,"outcomes":"Participation as one of the selected student volunteers in the AICTE–ATAL Faculty Development Program enabled the development of strong coordination, leadership, and program management skills through active involvement in the planning, conduction, and execution of the program alongside the HoD and Department Coordinator. The experience provided practical exposure to core cybersecurity concepts through conducting hands-on demonstrations on Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) attacks, SQL Injection (SQLi), and OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities for faculty participants, enhancing both technical competence and instructional communication skills. Additionally, the industrial visit to Dell Technologies Ltd. offered valuable insights into real-world cybersecurity operations and Industry 4.0 practices, strengthening the understanding of how academic knowledge aligns with industry requirements and professional cybersecurity standards.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-10-09","hoursSpent":30,"description":"1 of the 6 students selected as a volunteer for the Faculty Development Program(FDP) organized by AICTE training and learning academy (ATAL) , IQAC, EC-Council (Cybersecurity for Industry 4.0)\\n\\n- Assistance to HoD and Coordinator of Dept of CSE, RVCE in conduction, management and execution of the program.\\n- Included conducting hands on sessions for the faculty in demonstration of MITM attack, SQLi, OWASP top 10 vulnerabilities.\\n- Industry visit to Dell Technologies Ltd. and gained valuable insights.","aicteMapping":"Activity 5","pointsEarned":18,"certificateImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"aXN97fQxQ10NLT6Q8DIlu","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/wy2D5P7xrJGn7W243Vneu.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of RVCE, successfully blended fitness, community engagement, and philanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to contribute to a meaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With enthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful reminder of the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges. Runners contributed through their registration fees, which were directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants. Beyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond. ","aicteMapping":"Activity 14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/M_cB9IZ0WrTLothnYSMzS.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oyPPxCnSEtAaPt8x6VZwB","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/ftXjoqyaXBE2PN0ygxKn0.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/fzP3PxNmOhk1kt1LlJ1ma.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully supported underprivileged rural students by providing them with essential educational materials and school supplies. The initiative created a meaningful impact by ensuring needy students received textbooks, stationery, and other learning resources required for a better education experience. With effective fund collection and proper utilization, the event reflected strong community participation and social responsibility. The collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranava Foundation strengthened the reach of this initiative, helping improve access to education and creating a positive learning environment for students.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-25","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of approximately Rs.100 to 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which was used to procure and donate mission-needed supplies such as severe deserving students.The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed other Rs. 100 or Rs. 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranava Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Activity 14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/UOw7lgweuwgyVTnY8lhcC.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"96iMFsKua_h3YSLeaCXRG","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/EHaJeow9EXbLCoZRDpThu.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/HndcLqhhTT-_xDQqMzXmy.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant quantity of rice through the contribution of 5 kg from each participant. It helped provide food support to underprivileged communities and addressed issues related to hunger and food insecurity. The drive created awareness about the importance of sharing and social responsibility among students. Participants developed empathy, teamwork, and a strong sense of community service. Overall, the initiative made a meaningful social impact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and humanitarian service on campus. ","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the aim of supporting the underprivileged and promoting social responsibility among students. In this drive, students and volunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, symbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of food to those in need. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and hunger faced by many sections of society. It encouraged participants to share resources selflessly and develop a habit of giving back to the community. The drive also strengthened values of empathy, kindness, and unity among the students. The collected rice was planned to be distributed to needy communities through charitable organizations. The drive witnessed enthusiastic participation, showcasing strong teamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided students with an opportunity to actively engage in social service activities. The initiative highlighted how even small contributions can collectively create a significant positive impact. Overall, the Fist Full Drive successfully reinforced the spirit of service, compassion, and social responsibility within the campus.","aicteMapping":"Activity 14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/aacAqVx3fx9t3-p6_XkUh.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8up18JZJBQICg9EyFZHAd","name":"Gen AI HAckathon","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/Hu1r1GYzqWsjU1M6fWDkW.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/htt_A8MPOsWk4PQ8ItjWG.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-01-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The GenAI Hackathon achieved remarkable success, with enthusiastic participation from students who demonstrated exceptional creativity and technical acumen. Participants worked intensively within limited timeframes to develop innovative AI-driven solutions, showcasing their ability to translate theoretical concepts into functional prototypes. The event fostered a highly collaborative atmosphere where students formed dynamic teams, exchanged ideas, and leveraged each other''s strengths to overcome technical challenges. Beyond the technical achievements, the hackathon cultivated essential soft skills including effective teamwork, time management, and creative problem-solving. Students gained invaluable hands-on experience with Generative AI technologies, tools, and frameworks, significantly enhancing their practical skill sets. The positive response and quality of submissions demonstrated the event''s impact in inspiring the next generation of AI innovators. In recognition of their dedication and active participation, we recommended students receive AICTE activity points, providing formal acknowledgment of their efforts. This recognition serves not only to motivate participants but also to inspire broader student engagement in future technology-driven initiatives, creating a ripple effect of innovation within the academic community.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-15","hoursSpent":6,"description":"As the organizer of the GenAI Hackathon powered by EDOCK, I spearheaded a transformative educational initiative held on November 29th, 2024, at DTL Huddle. This event was meticulously designed to provide students with a practical platform to explore and implement cutting-edge Generative AI technologies. The hackathon served as a bridge between theoretical knowledge and real-world application, allowing participants to delve into an emerging field that is revolutionizing multiple industries. My role encompassed comprehensive event planning, from conceptualization to execution, including securing sponsorship from EDOCK, coordinating with the venue, managing participant registrations, and ensuring seamless logistics throughout the day. The event was structured to challenge students to harness the power of Generative AI—technology that enables machines to create original content, simulate human-like interactions, and solve intricate problems. By creating an environment that encouraged innovation and collaboration, I aimed to foster a learning ecosystem where students could push their creative and technical boundaries. The hackathon not only provided hands-on experience with AI tools but also cultivated essential skills such as rapid prototyping, team collaboration, and problem-solving under time","aicteMapping":"Activity 5 ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/pOr86nsb1U2usN7_zQYnm.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8jDqKGU0NTAbHqG1wAEQR","name":"Honey Well Hackathon Organizer","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/U1hvks9vUPZH7zxIKUsZC.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/2ZmfykAn-8KyL8twBe1Wf.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-25","duration":8,"outcomes":"The Design-A-Thon achieved exceptional success, delivering a meaningful and impactful learning experience for all participants. The volunteers from the Accelerate Club demonstrated outstanding dedication and professionalism, executing their responsibilities enthusiastically and ensuring the smooth conduct of both phases of the event. Their active involvement was instrumental in creating an engaging environment that facilitated effective learning and collaboration among participants. The Honeywell India team expressed high appreciation for the students'' efforts, congratulating them on their outstanding performance and the quality of design solutions presented. This positive feedback from industry professionals validated the effectiveness of our organizational approach and the caliber of student participation. Participants gained hands-on experience in tackling real-world design challenges, developed critical thinking and problem-solving abilities, and enhanced their understanding of industry expectations and standards. The event successfully fostered industry-academia collaboration, creating networking opportunities and potential career pathways for students. In recognition of the volunteers'' valuable contributions to making this event successful, we requested the allocation of AICTE Activity Points, acknowledging their dedication, hard work, and the significant role they played in delivering this impactful educational initiative.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-18","hoursSpent":6,"description":"As vice president of the Accelerate Technical Club in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, I played a pivotal role in organizing the Design-A-Thon, a prestigious collaborative event with Honeywell India Pvt. Ltd. This comprehensive initiative was strategically planned and executed in two distinct phases spanning from April 18th to April 25th, 2025. The event was meticulously designed with the primary objective of enhancing students'' technical and practical knowledge through real-world design challenges. My responsibilities encompassed coordinating with industry partner Honeywell India, managing logistics across both phases of the competition, mobilizing and coordinating volunteer teams from the Accelerate Club, and ensuring seamless execution throughout the event duration. The Design-A-Thon provided students with an invaluable opportunity to engage with industry-standard design problems, apply their theoretical knowledge to practical scenarios, and experience professional work environments. By facilitating this collaboration between academia and industry, we created a bridge that allowed students to understand corporate expectations, design methodologies, and innovation processes. The two-phase structure enabled participants to iterate on their designs, receive feedback, and refine their solutions, mirroring real-world product development cycles.","aicteMapping":"Activity 5","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/dyTJg6JPwq3ijLShfRzmi.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7lJ2ehwdI7KVxAxJiP_tZ","name":"Skill Lab","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/WkmGfF9wFfXpLWaXC5ROo.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-26","duration":6,"outcomes":"The Skill Lab sessions achieved remarkable success, creating a meaningful and impactful learning experience for all fourth semester participants. The volunteer team, primarily comprising 6th semester students from the B.E. CSE (CY) program, demonstrated exceptional dedication and commitment by actively mentoring and guiding their junior counterparts throughout the five-day program. Their hands-on approach to teaching and willingness to share knowledge was instrumental in ensuring the successful execution of all sessions. The peer-to-peer mentoring model proved highly effective, as junior students felt more comfortable asking questions and seeking clarification from seniors who had recently navigated similar learning challenges. Participants gained substantial technical knowledge, particularly in the Cyber Security track, developing practical skills that are directly applicable to industry requirements and future career opportunities. The sessions fostered a strong sense of community within the department, strengthening bonds between different batches and creating a collaborative learning culture. Students developed confidence in applying theoretical concepts to practical scenarios, enhanced their problem-solving abilities, and gained exposure to real-world security challenges. In recognition of the volunteers'' valuable contributions and exceptional dedication to mentoring their juniors, we requested the allocation of AICTE Activity Points, acknowledging their instrumental role in delivering this impactful educational initiative.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-21","hoursSpent":30,"description":"As vice president of the Accelerate Club, I contributed to organizing comprehensive Skill Lab sessions for fourth semester students across multiple Computer Science and Engineering programs, including B.E. (CSE), B.E. (CSE-CD), and B.E. (CSE-CY), conducted from April 21st to April 26th, 2025. This initiative was undertaken in collaboration with the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, with the primary objective of enhancing students'' technical and practical knowledge through hands-on learning experiences. The Skill Lab sessions were strategically designed to bridge the gap between classroom theory and industry-relevant practical skills. One of the major tracks during these sessions focused specifically on Cyber Security, a critical domain in today''s technology landscape. My role involved coordinating with department faculty, organizing session schedules across different specializations, managing resource allocation, and mobilizing senior student volunteers to serve as mentors and guides. As a 6th semester B.E. CSE (CY) student myself, I actively participated in mentoring and guiding junior students, sharing practical insights and technical expertise. The multi-day structure allowed for in-depth exploration of topics, providing participants with sufficient time to grasp complex concepts and develop practical competencies under expert guidance.","aicteMapping":"Activity 5","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/tNFcuBnHhLORK0ofTC6ii.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KIekCleyoGsF6RodMAAfu","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/bo_DcLjZxaPXA07L0-nzH.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/Ip8Yd9_I5zzZUxxr244v7.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant quantity of rice through the contribution of 5 kg from each participant. It helped provide food support to underprivileged communities and addressed issues related to hunger and food insecurity. The drive created awareness about the importance of sharing and social responsibility among students. Participants developed empathy, teamwork, and a strong sense of community service. Overall, the initiative made a meaningful social impact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and humanitarian service on campus. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the aim of supporting the underprivileged and promoting social responsibility among students. In this drive, students and volunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, symbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of food to those in need. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and hunger faced by many sections of society. It encouraged participants to share resources selflessly and develop a habit of giving back to the community. The drive also strengthened values of empathy, kindness, and unity among the students. The collected rice was planned to be distributed to needy communities through charitable organizations. The drive witnessed enthusiastic participation, showcasing strong teamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided students with an opportunity to actively engage in social service activities. The initiative highlighted how even small contributions can collectively create a significant positive impact. Overall, the Fist Full Drive successfully reinforced the spirit of service, compassion, and social responsibility within the campus.","aicteMapping":"Activity 14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/6605e786-fc50-4118-b7d7-d6f205325328/S_eIthqpq0UsR6Oae0fF9.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr Mohana","designation":"Associate Professor , Dept of CSE"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 12:27:44.664408+00', '2026-01-30 07:02:38.121258+00'), ('c5349b07-3595-4b10-9422-a1b7b52b4f40', '97b98877-6968-44bf-a178-b24bf92618ad', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 10:45:40.324269+00', '2026-01-29 10:45:40.324269+00'), ('c58669fd-8335-4228-a94f-11804e0f412a', '470220bd-0193-4de5-83ab-bc43aaf2b29c', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CH025","name":"JADHAVRAO RUTURAJ AJITRAO","period":"2022-2026","department":"Chemical Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"HPfTAtVo8i-FoqDowVImB","name":"Fast trek","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/470220bd-0193-4de5-83ab-bc43aaf2b29c/XYx9yT21uiAbgIX0VqyIt.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/470220bd-0193-4de5-83ab-bc43aaf2b29c/3oCNgjJBGW7TCpd8lEa24.png"],"endDate":"","duration":-738561,"outcomes":"\\nParticipants gained greater awareness of the healthcare challenges faced by underprivileged children with heart diseases, resulting in increased empathy and social consciousness among students. The event successfully generated financial support and community engagement, directly contributing to child healthcare assistance.\\nThe activity promoted physical fitness, environmental responsibility, and mental well-being, while fostering stronger bonds and a sense of belonging within the student community. Overall, Fast-Trek reaffirmed the importance of youth involvement in social welfare and inspired continued participation in future community development initiatives.\\n","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast-Trek, held on 12th February 2023 at Huthridurga Hills, was a flagship outreach event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. With more than 400 enthusiastic student volunteers, the initiative blended adventure, youth participation, and social responsibility. The primary objective of the trek was to generate financial support for underprivileged children battling heart diseases, emphasizing empathy, healthcare awareness, and collective action.\\n\\nThe volunteers and coordinators guided the participants throughout the journey, ensuring comfort, discipline, and inclusivity. The scenic terrain of Huthridurga Betta provided an ideal setting for students to connect with nature, overcome physical challenges, and develop resilience, cooperation, and leadership skills.\\n\\nBeyond the physical activity, Fast-Trek encouraged students to reflect on social welfare, community engagement, and the importance of supporting vulnerable sections of society. The event concluded successfully, strengthening the culture of volunteerism, compassion, and proactive youth involvement in community development\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EJiYnCE-SwyShR6VUBaWW","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon concluded with significant social, organizational, and community-oriented outcomes. The event successfully mobilized more than 500 participants, demonstrating strong public engagement and widespread support for the cause of helping underprivileged children.\\n\\nThe marathon also strengthened the culture of volunteerism, teamwork, and civic responsibility within the NSS RVCE community, as volunteers efficiently managed logistics, safety measures, hydration points, route coordination, and participant support. The structured execution of the run enhanced event management, planning, and leadership capabilities among organizers\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, a flagship community welfare initiative conducted by NSS RVCE, was organized with the central theme “Help a Child, Change the World” emphasizing support for underprivileged children requiring educational and healthcare assistance.\\n\\nThe event commenced at 7:00 AM with systematic registration, verification, and distribution of event shirts, badges, and participation materials, creating uniformity, identity, and enthusiasm among attendees. Pre-event announcements, energy sessions, and safety briefings were conducted to ensure preparedness and smooth coordination. Medical teams, hydration points, volunteers, and emergency response units were strategically stationed along the route to maintain participant safety and well-being.\\n\\nThe Marathon officially began at 9:00 AM and witnessed active participation from over 500 individuals, including students, faculty members, and fitness enthusiasts. The carefully planned route encouraged inclusivity and accessibility, offering a balance of challenge and engagement for runners of varying fitness levels. Throughout the event, NSS volunteers facilitated crowd management, route guidance, and awareness messaging, reinforcing the event’s social objective.\\n\\nBeyond promoting physical fitness and recreational involvement, the marathon aimed to create consciousness about the struggles faced by underprivileged children and the importance of collective community action in addressing them. The event fostered social responsibility, volunteerism, compassion, teamwork, and civic participation within the campus community\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/470220bd-0193-4de5-83ab-bc43aaf2b29c/Kk6GXRq2XMOmvLV_1jXEr.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KtbGX77JsZNrMQ4gr2s1J","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/470220bd-0193-4de5-83ab-bc43aaf2b29c/89l9yY_4uiUXE8P8OgVGO.jpg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The Paper Drive achieved remarkable social and environmental outcomes, collecting a total of 8.17 tonnes of recyclable waste, including books, papers, and other reusable materials from households and businesses across Bangalore. This substantial contribution was handed over to partnering charities and NGOs, enabling them to generate funds and strengthen ongoing welfare programs.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Paper Drive, conducted on 23rd June 2024, was a large-scale community welfare activity organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE. The initiative involved over 400 student volunteers who actively participated in collecting books, papers, and recyclable waste materials from households, institutions, and local businesses across various parts of Bangalore.\\n\\nThe primary objective of the event was to gather reusable and recyclable materials that could be contributed to charitable organizations and NGOs, enabling them to raise funds and support their social initiatives. The drive also aimed to promote environmental responsibility, recycling awareness, and community involvement among citizens. The activity received strong public response and resulted in a substantial collection of materials, showcasing the collective strength of student-driven service efforts.\\nThe Paper Drive served as a successful model of social engagement, sustainability, and youth leadership by addressing community needs, supporting welfare projects, and fostering a sense of responsibility among volunteers and residents of Bangalore.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/470220bd-0193-4de5-83ab-bc43aaf2b29c/EgQA9_GkFW4nKykjj-r4i.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8,9","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 14:01:02.269776+00', '2026-01-30 12:56:10.043539+00'), ('c6c91888-16c6-4522-8629-bd50ae91daea', '8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV019","name":"CHINMAYA R","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"NxTsFJAylvOvwu3oJbaYj","name":"Shaurya (8th Mile 2023)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/TEwUEDvZ8HkjVOvFHYCG3.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/4nM6_DDGs_ET9Np4TdNmQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-01-17","duration":958,"outcomes":"The event created awareness about NCC training and values, encouraged active participation, and fostered teamwork, confidence, and leadership skills among students.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-05","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Shaurya (8th Mile 2023) was the flagship NCC event conducted during the college fest. The event included challenges for NCC cadets from various institutions as well as college students, introducing them to NCC-based activities such as weapon training, code and decoding, and obstacle training. The event aimed to promote discipline, leadership, and physical fitness.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":25,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/bhe8v1HXuoFBZ0gq6md2B.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cZ9Xm7tR0eQNV0KZfv28h","name":"IGC-RDC","slNo":2,"place":"PRTC Thoranagallu, Bellary","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/273Ev1wYpRUeIAT2h-FNR.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-09-20","duration":10,"outcomes":"Inter-group competitions at the NCC RDC go beyond mere competition. They foster crucial life skills like teamwork, leadership, and discipline. Cadets learn to collaborate effectively, make strategic decisions, and perform with precision. These experiences boost confidence and prepare cadets for future challenges, making them well-rounded individuals with valuable skills applicable beyond their NCC journey.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-09-11","hoursSpent":140,"description":"Inter-group competitions are a cornerstone of the NCC Republic Day Camp. These competitions foster teamwork, camaraderie, leadership, and decision-making skills among cadets. They emphasize discipline, precision, and attention to detail, while also boosting confidence and self-esteem. Common competitions include drill displays, cultural performances, sports events, obstacle courses, line & flag area competitions, and individual excellence awards. These events are not solely about winning; they provide a valuable learning experience, fostering personal growth and developing essential life skills that will benefit cadets long after the camp concludes.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":35,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/Ry4oBKyaF_4BVuUl6sJLC.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lOtP-u42TKjLxEEY2zXnC","name":"CATC - RMS","slNo":3,"place":"Rashtriya Military School","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/rgG1cFc8NPnI_xH1hgTRa.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/DCBDeVWKbkYStqFjgi9qy.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-17","duration":10,"outcomes":"The camp significantly improved physical endurance, discipline, and leadership qualities among the cadets. NCC RVCE cadets showcased outstanding performance by winning multiple medals in group song, group dance, and volleyball events, bringing laurels to the unit and fostering team spirit and confidence.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-08","hoursSpent":140,"description":"NCC RVCE cadets participated in the Combined Annual Training Camp (CATC) conducted for a duration of 10 days at Rashtriya Military School. The camp included regular parade training, physical training, drills, and various inter-unit competitions such as group song, group dance, and sports events including volleyball. The camp aimed at enhancing discipline, leadership, teamwork, and overall personality development of the cadets.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":35,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/1x5SpU-juSXO1Mc3FIL84.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bsi_UpYFsP1dIBtoLIUEY","name":"Major Trek and Cleanliness Drive","slNo":4,"place":"Gokarna","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/SxmLw5f0M_i-vy4IqsrLG.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8fd02ae7-8127-4c82-b226-62edb3661d3e/2J6KOus6ZJBip3TKnwZF-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":3,"outcomes":"The Swatch Bharat and Plantation resulted in clean trekking trails and the planting of over 100 geotagged saplings to enhance the green cover. It raised awareness among locals and trekkers about cleanliness and environmental conservation. The cadets demonstrated leadership and responsibility by adopting saplings for ongoing care. The event inspired sustainable practices, fostered teamwork, and promoted the importance of maintaining ecological balance, leaving a lasting positive impact on the environment and participants alike.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-10","hoursSpent":30,"description":"NCC RVCE cadets organized a Swatch Bharat and Plantation Drive at Gokarna from January 10th to 12th. The event aimed to promote cleanliness and environmental conservation in the beaches. Cadets cleaned trekking trails, collected waste, and ensured its proper disposal to preserve the area''s beauty. A plantation drive was conducted, during which geotagged saplings were planted and assigned to cadets for care. Small teams interacted with locals and trekkers to raise awareness about sustainability. The initiative successfully combined adventure with environmental responsibility, leaving a lasting impact on participants and nature alike.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":7.5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Vinod A R","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 04:10:12.780148+00', '2026-01-30 15:17:25.046998+00'), ('cbff9191-0e8e-4d88-8c0b-c8c5468a6b75', 'ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS025","name":"Jeevan Kumar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"FOs0VNe0gBqDOay9LCPYL","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The blood donation activity contributed directly to societal healthcare support by increasing the availability of safe blood units for patients in need, including accident victims, surgical patients, and individuals with critical illnesses. It promoted awareness about the continuous demand for blood and the importance of voluntary donation in saving lives. Participation in the camp strengthened the sense of social responsibility, empathy, and civic duty among students. The initiative demonstrated how educational institutions can actively support community health systems through student participation. Overall, the event encouraged humanitarian values and motivated continued engagement in social service activities beyond academics.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"A blood donation camp was organized on 6/6/2023 at the campus of RV College of Engineering as part of a social welfare and public health support initiative. The camp was conducted under proper medical supervision with trained healthcare professionals to ensure safe and hygienic donation procedures. The objective of the drive was to encourage voluntary blood donation among students and staff and to contribute to emergency medical requirements in hospitals and blood banks. I actively participated in the camp as a voluntary donor and successfully donated blood. The program also included basic health screening before donation and awareness guidance about the benefits and safety of blood donation. The activity reflected student involvement in community-oriented service within the academic environment.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/4ZL6j7YCaMRq-wUCHv0kh.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"VrsDThq6enXkIDgRPciw-","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/p54iKtrqJbaCwDppJiego.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/uyouI0dkTx0uP2HX_luH7.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The activity contributed to societal welfare by supporting child empowerment initiatives through fundraising and awareness generation. It reinforced the importance of civic responsibility and demonstrated how community participation in structured events can create measurable social impact. Through this experience, I developed greater awareness of social causes related to child development and understood the value of contributing to society through participatory initiatives. I also learned the importance of physical discipline, goal setting, time management, and perseverance. The event strengthened my sense of social accountability and highlighted how individual effort, when combined with collective participation, can support meaningful humanitarian outcomes.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"I participated in the Utsarga Marathon conducted on 04/02/2024 under the social outreach theme “Run for a Cause – Help a Child, Change the World.” The event was organized as a structured charity and awareness marathon featuring two participation categories 5 km and 10 km to enable inclusive participation across different fitness levels. I completed the 5 km run category. The marathon functioned as a fundraising and advocacy platform to support child empowerment initiatives focused on education, welfare, and developmental opportunities for underprivileged children. The program integrated organized athletic participation with social contribution and promoted disciplined involvement, endurance, and civic engagement through a cause-oriented public event.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/gkSPKjqXEB4d7htqaDgRh.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ydoD7wuVNX0EqR_jb4kmM","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/AX0hAi-QTkzWT6iI_MnYe.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/3-mhGRfN_4QVB4qFpvGBR.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"The marathon supported child welfare efforts by mobilizing financial and social support through a participatory fundraising model. It enhanced awareness about the importance of sustained community support for child empowerment programs. From this activity, I learned the significance of consistency in social contribution and the impact of repeated participation in cause-driven initiatives. I improved my personal discipline, endurance capacity, and commitment toward goal completion. The experience also strengthened my teamwork spirit, civic consciousness, and long-term orientation toward socially responsible participation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"I participated in the Utsarga Marathon held on 06/04/2025 under the campaign message “Run for a Cause – Help a Child, Change the World.” The marathon was conducted as a formal social-impact event with two distance formats 5 km and 10 km designed to maximize outreach and participation. I took part in the 5 km category. The event combined organized endurance activity with philanthropic contribution, where participant registration and sponsorship support were directed toward child-centered welfare initiatives. It provided a structured platform for student and community engagement in social responsibility through fitness-based advocacy and fundraising.","aicteMapping":"Community Services","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3vrvmg8zre3pZiqjmNShY","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 PD","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/tjOHk4rKI8Xpd5aPXozmZ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/nsa6hQqyGGQOvbbxmQbId.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/hey4oixGgC7dYmAkFyhb9.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":5,"outcomes":"This activity supported the successful execution of a cause-driven public event by improving route clarity, participant guidance, and visual communication of the social message associated with the marathon. Proper signage and decoration enhanced participant safety, engagement, and awareness of the child empowerment theme promoted by the event. Through this involvement, I gained practical experience in event production planning, field execution, team coordination, and responsibility sharing. I developed skills in logistical organization, problem-solving during live setup conditions, and collaborative work management. The experience also strengthened my understanding of how well-planned production design contributes to the effectiveness and social impact of large community-oriented events.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-02","hoursSpent":0,"description":"I served as a member of the Production Design and Event Setup team for the Utsarga Marathon events conducted on campus, where I contributed to the planning and execution of visual and directional arrangements required for the smooth conduct of the run. The responsibilities included decorating marathon routes, placing directional and awareness banners, preparing thematic display elements, and assisting in overall campus decoration related to the event. The work involved coordination with organizing teams, on-site layout planning, material arrangement, and timely installation to ensure visibility, safety, and thematic consistency throughout the running path and gathering areas. The activity required structured teamwork, logistical coordination, and execution under time constraints to meet event readiness standards at RV College of Engineering campus.","aicteMapping":"Community Services","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dYkXWVTLPJu0IIX4DF4ur","name":"NSS Paper Bag Drive","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/X3LtU6rNpPkgQLDi-T00s.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":3,"outcomes":"This activity directly supported environmental sustainability by encouraging the reuse of waste newspapers and reducing dependence on plastic bags in local marketplaces. It promoted practical awareness of waste management and sustainable living practices through skill-based learning and community application. The distribution of paper bags to street vendors demonstrated how small, student-led initiatives can contribute to reducing plastic pollution at the grassroots level. The activity strengthened social responsibility toward environmental protection and highlighted the importance of eco-friendly alternatives in everyday commerce. On a personal level, I gained a useful sustainable craft skill, improved manual efficiency and productivity, and developed a stronger sense of community engagement through service-oriented environmental action.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-31","hoursSpent":0,"description":"I participated in a handmade paper bag making and distribution activity organized by the National Service Scheme unit of RV College of Engineering as part of an environmental sustainability and community outreach initiative. The objective of the program was to encourage eco-friendly alternatives to plastic carry bags by training students to reuse old newspapers and convert them into handmade paper bags instead of discarding them as waste. The workshop included step-by-step practical training on folding, pasting, edge reinforcement, and handle design to ensure the bags were durable and usable for vendors.\\n\\nAs part of the hands-on activity, I learned the complete manual process of paper bag preparation and personally produced 120 handmade paper bags using recycled newspapers. These bags were later distributed to local vendors participating in the Kadalekayi Parishe at Banashankari, where they were used by groundnut sellers as a sustainable packaging alternative. The initiative ensured that student volunteer work translated into direct real-world usage and environmental benefit.","aicteMapping":"Community Services","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mt6yQTJJEtJa1qDgbc9dD","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/dXk64uXjvgizfTHUvH7i3.png"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Project Pustak created meaningful societal impact by supporting underprivileged rural students with essential educational resources and thereby helping reduce barriers to learning. The initiative contributed toward improving access to textbooks, stationery, and school supplies, which are critical for sustaining academic participation and performance among economically weaker sections. My contribution of ₹350 formed part of a collective funding effort that demonstrated how small individual donations can aggregate into substantial educational support. The activity reinforced the importance of community-driven educational assistance and highlighted the role of student and service organizations in promoting social equity. It also strengthened my personal sense of civic responsibility, empathy, and commitment toward education-centered social welfare initiatives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak is a structured social outreach initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged students in rural areas by providing essential school supplies required for their education. The program was conducted through a collaborative effort by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with Pranav Foundation. As part of this initiative, voluntary contributions were collected from donors to build a dedicated educational support fund.\\n\\nThe collected funds were systematically utilized for procuring essential academic resources such as textbooks, notebooks, stationery kits, school bags, and other learning materials necessary for a supportive educational environment. The initiative followed an organized procurement and distribution process to ensure that the resources reached deserving students. The project demonstrated how structured student-led donation drives can be effectively converted into direct educational support for underserved communities.","aicteMapping":"Community Services","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/DpWM9Qr7eVaQohnuMdyag.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ciMZVbhfB48jhzeerJOmm","name":"Fist Full","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gbOg_a1N5eLrLLIVvPszs","name":"Kannada Habba 2025 - \"Jagadvaha\"","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/-MdHeVlEszvFMN_gipLcV.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ce92b7b4-3d73-4e9c-b741-a30de6feaafd/GwUe56ltWFaGWVXMRqnrG.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-04","duration":25,"outcomes":"Kannada Habba 2025 – “Jagadvaha” created meaningful societal impact by strengthening awareness and appreciation of Kannada language, traditions, and regional heritage among students from diverse academic and cultural backgrounds. The event emphasized the importance of preserving local culture in a modern, technology-oriented educational environment and encouraged students to actively participate in cultural continuity rather than being passive observers. The student-led execution of decorations and stage production reflected community collaboration and collective responsibility, demonstrating how shared cultural initiatives can build unity and mutual respect. By providing an inclusive platform for cultural expression within a large techno-cultural festival, the program helped bridge social and linguistic gaps across departments. It also highlighted that cultural identity and technological progress can coexist, reinforcing the idea of balanced societal development. Overall, the event nurtured values such as teamwork, volunteerism, and cultural responsibility, which are essential for positive social engagement beyond campus life.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-10","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Kannada Habba 2025, titled “Jagadvaha”, was organized as a major cultural segment of our college’s largest techno-cultural fest, 8th Mile. The event celebrated Kannada language, heritage, and artistic traditions through immersive visual themes, cultural symbolism, and student-driven creative execution. A unique highlight of this fest was that the entire campus decoration — including stage design, thematic installations, and cultural visual elements was fully conceptualized and executed by members of the Kannada Sangha, promoting student ownership and indigenous artistic expression. I actively contributed as a member of the Production Design Team, participating in planning, material selection, artistic layout, and on-site execution of decorative structures and stage aesthetics.\\n\\nFrom a societal perspective, the event played an important role in preserving and promoting regional language and culture among youth in a technology-focused academic environment. It encouraged cultural pride, community participation, and inter-department collaboration while demonstrating how traditional art and modern event execution can coexist. By enabling students to design and build cultural spaces themselves, the activity strengthened teamwork, cultural awareness, and respect for local heritage, contributing to social and cultural continuity within an educational ecosystem.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 09:40:00.619164+00', '2026-01-31 08:45:11.395139+00'), ('cd655eeb-bac1-420e-8790-321edf06dd51', 'd03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS056","name":"Sanganna Motgi","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"fO0__zHi-xc7IGL2w-mYZ","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/nus3MQQTdj0PtJn59TK9V.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation activity at RVCE had many positive outcomes. It helped collect blood units that can be used to save the lives of patients in hospitals during emergencies, surgeries, and treatments. The camp also created awareness among students about the importance of voluntary blood donation and encouraged many first-time donors like me to participate.\\n\\nPersonally, the activity helped me overcome fear and understand the value of helping others. It gave me a sense of responsibility toward society and increased my confidence. I felt proud that my small contribution could make a big difference in someone’s life.\\n\\nOverall, the event promoted teamwork, social service, and humanity among students while supporting the healthcare system with essential blood supplies.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Blood donation at the RVCE campus was a meaningful and memorable experience for me because it was my first time donating blood. The camp was organized on campus by student clubs like Rotaract along with medical teams from hospitals and blood banks. The area was well arranged with registration desks, health checkups, and donation beds.\\n\\nFirst, they checked my weight, hemoglobin level, and blood pressure to make sure I was fit to donate. The doctors and volunteers were very friendly and explained everything clearly, which made me feel comfortable and less nervous. The actual donation took only about 10–15 minutes and was almost painless.\\n\\nAfter donating, I was given some juice and snacks and asked to rest for a while. I felt proud and happy knowing that my small effort could help save someone’s life. Overall, it was a safe, well-organized, and satisfying experience, and I would definitely like to donate again in the future.","aicteMapping":"Social Service/Community Services","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_YqX4nmcl3sxQtw7bTvxZ","name":"T-Shirt for Smiles (Kannada Sanga)","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/2pYZ46sMCj2JinqivOrmO.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-09-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"he outcomes of the “T-Shirt for Smiles” initiative were significant both socially and personally. From a social perspective, the funds raised through T-shirt sales helped provide essential supplies and support to the children at Pragati Seva Charitable Trust. The donations contributed to improving their daily needs and overall well-being. Even small contributions from many students together created a meaningful difference in their lives.\\n\\nThe initiative also strengthened the bond between students and the community. It created awareness about the existence of orphanages and the importance of supporting underserved and vulnerable sections of society. By visiting the trust and interacting directly with the children, students developed a deeper understanding of social issues rather than just learning about them theoretically.\\n\\nOn a personal level, the activity had a strong emotional impact on me. It helped me develop empathy, compassion, and a stronger sense of social responsibility. I realized that contributing to society is not always about large efforts — even simple acts like participating in charity events can bring happiness to others. The experience also taught me the importance of sharing, kindness, and gratitude for what we have.\\n\\nAdditionally, it encouraged me to participate in more community service activities in the future. It inspired me to look for opportunities where I can give back to society and make a positive difference, however small it may be.\\n\\nOverall, “T-Shirt for Smiles” was not just a fundraising event but a valuable life experience that promoted humanity, social awareness, and service-mindedness, leaving a lasting impression on me.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-09-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Participating in the “T-Shirt for Smiles” initiative organized by Kannada Sanga at RV College of Engineering was a heartwarming and meaningful experience for me. Unlike regular college events that focus mainly on entertainment or competitions, this activity was centered around social service and charity. It combined a simple act — purchasing an event T-shirt — with a larger purpose of helping children in need, which made the initiative very special.\\n\\nAs part of the event, students contributed by buying specially designed T-shirts, and the funds collected were used to support children at Pragati Seva Charitable Trust – Anathashrama located at Kumbalagodu, Bengaluru. I really liked the idea that something as small as buying a T-shirt could be converted into a meaningful contribution toward someone’s well-being. It showed how small actions, when done collectively, can create a big positive impact.\\n\\nThe most memorable part of the activity was visiting the orphanage along with other students. When we reached the trust, we were warmly welcomed by the children and staff. Spending time with the children, talking to them, playing games, and interacting with them was a very emotional and eye-opening experience. Their energy, innocence, and smiles made the visit extremely special. Despite having limited resources, they were cheerful and content, which taught me an important lesson about gratitude and happiness.\\n\\nWe also distributed essential items and donations collected through the initiative. Helping arrange the materials and personally giving them to the children made me feel more connected to the cause. It did not feel like just a donation but rather a direct act of care and support. Talking to the children and understanding their daily lives helped me realize the challenges they face and how important such support activities are.\\n\\nThis experience helped me step outside my normal academic routine and look at life from a different perspective. It made me more empathetic and sensitive towards the needs of others. Overall, the activity was not only enjoyable but also emotionally fulfilling and deeply impactful.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uiRxCyLNJ9fGqpxQXflP9","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/gJAmGomup_IIYxEyTq4kb.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive resulted in the collection of many units of blood, which will be used to support patients during emergencies, surgeries, and medical treatments. Such camps help hospitals maintain an adequate blood supply and can potentially save many lives.\\n\\nThe activity also increased awareness among students about the importance of voluntary and regular blood donation. It encouraged teamwork, social involvement, and a spirit of service on campus. Personally, donating for the second time strengthened my sense of social responsibility and compassion toward others. It boosted my confidence and motivated me to continue participating in community service activities in the future.\\n\\nOverall, the event not only benefited society but also helped me grow personally by understanding the value of helping others through small but meaningful actions.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Donating blood at the RVCE campus for the second time was a very positive and reassuring experience for me. The blood donation camp was well organized by student clubs like Rotaract along with professional medical staff from hospitals and blood banks. The venue was neatly arranged with separate areas for registration, health screening, donation, and rest.\\n\\nThe process began with filling out a form followed by basic medical tests such as checking my weight, blood pressure, hemoglobin level, and overall health to ensure I was eligible to donate. Since this was my second donation, I felt more confident and relaxed compared to my first time. I already knew what to expect, so there was no fear or hesitation. The doctors and volunteers were friendly and explained each step clearly, which made the process smooth and comfortable.\\n\\nThe actual blood donation took about 10–15 minutes and was almost painless. After donating, I rested for a few minutes and was given refreshments like juice and snacks. I felt physically fine and mentally satisfied, knowing that my contribution could help someone in need. Overall, the experience was safe, organized, and very fulfilling.","aicteMapping":"Social Service/Community Services","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_F2mXgt1boYsmaw3CD0bf","name":"Utsarga Marathon ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/z9KdvY0DGSXV9ODRIC2Nj.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of participating in the UTSARGA Marathon were both personal and social. From a social perspective, the marathon was organized to support a worthy cause and promote awareness about community service and social responsibility. Events like these bring students together to contribute to society while promoting a healthy and active lifestyle. The collective participation of many students helps spread positive messages about fitness, unity, and service.\\n\\nOn a personal level, the marathon had a significant impact on me. It improved my physical stamina, endurance, and overall fitness. Running 5KM helped me understand the importance of regular exercise and maintaining a healthy lifestyle. It also taught me mental resilience, as completing the distance required determination and self-motivation.\\n\\nAdditionally, participating in such events increased my confidence and gave me a sense of achievement. It encouraged me to take part in more fitness and service-oriented activities in the future. I learned that stepping out of my comfort zone helps in personal growth and builds both physical and mental strength.\\n\\nOverall, my first UTSARGA 5KM marathon was a memorable experience that helped me grow stronger, more disciplined, and socially responsible, while contributing to a meaningful cause.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participating in the UTSARGA 5KM Marathon organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering was a completely new and exciting experience for me, as it was my first time running a marathon. Unlike other social service activities like blood or food donation, this event combined physical fitness with a social cause, which made it both challenging and meaningful.\\n\\nOn the day of the marathon, the campus was filled with energy and enthusiasm. Students gathered early in the morning, wearing sports attire and preparing themselves mentally and physically for the run. The environment was very motivating, with volunteers guiding participants, organizing the route, and ensuring safety arrangements. Seeing so many students come together for a common cause created a strong sense of unity and team spirit.\\n\\nSince it was my first time running a 5KM distance, I felt both excited and slightly nervous. I wasn’t sure how difficult it would be to maintain stamina throughout the run. As the marathon started, I began at a steady pace, focusing on controlling my breathing and conserving energy. The initial distance felt easy, but after a few kilometers, I started feeling tired and realized the importance of endurance and mental strength. However, the cheers from volunteers and fellow participants encouraged me to keep going without stopping.\\n\\nCompleting the 5KM run gave me a great sense of accomplishment. Crossing the finish line was a proud and satisfying moment because I had pushed myself beyond my comfort zone and successfully completed something I had never done before. It was not just a physical activity but also a test of determination, discipline, and perseverance. Overall, the experience was refreshing, challenging, and highly rewarding.","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Veq5DiPL7G_-uWcBRKiIV","name":"Fist Full ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/Cbp96WENKaVR1a3joeXQy.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The “FIST FULL” drive resulted in the collection of a large quantity of essential food grains, which will be distributed to underprivileged families and individuals in need. These contributions will help provide meals and reduce food insecurity for many households. Even small individual donations, when combined, create a significant positive impact on society.\\n\\nThe activity also raised awareness among students about hunger and the importance of sharing resources with those who are less fortunate. It encouraged a spirit of kindness, empathy, and social responsibility on campus. By participating, students understood that helping others does not always require big actions — even small efforts like donating a few kilograms of food can make a big difference.\\n\\nOn a personal level, this being my first time participating in such an initiative, it broadened my perspective about social service. It helped me develop compassion and gratitude for what I have. It also motivated me to take part in more community welfare activities in the future. This experience taught me that contributing regularly to such causes can create long-term positive change in society.\\n\\nOverall, the “FIST FULL” event was not just a donation drive but a learning experience that strengthened my sense of humanity, responsibility, and willingness to help others.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-17","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participating in the “FIST FULL” donation drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE was a unique and meaningful experience for me, as it was my first time taking part in a food donation activity of this kind. Unlike blood donation, which directly helps patients in hospitals, this initiative focused on supporting underprivileged families by collecting essential food grains like rice and toor dal. This made me understand another important side of social service — helping to fight hunger and ensuring basic needs for those in need.\\n\\nThe event was conducted in an organized manner at the Geotechnical Engineering Lab in the Civil Department during the scheduled collection hours. The volunteers were very welcoming and guided everyone through the process. Students were encouraged to contribute either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. I brought my contribution and handed it over at the collection counter, where it was properly recorded and stored along with other donations.\\n\\nSince it was my first time participating in such a drive, I initially didn’t realize how impactful even a small contribution could be. However, seeing many students coming forward with their donations and even making group contributions created a strong sense of unity and teamwork. The atmosphere was positive and service-oriented, and it felt good to be part of something that directly supports people’s daily needs.\\n\\nThis experience helped me step out of my routine academic life and think more about society and the struggles some people face for basic necessities like food. Contributing even a small quantity made me feel responsible and connected to the community. Overall, it was a simple yet deeply satisfying experience that introduced me to the value of food donation and community service.","aicteMapping":"Community Services","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sSmhm3YbVLZ19EfUV8EOE","name":" Kadale Kaayi Parishe","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/VMj_5GrCEFsvBAJuLwXik.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of this activity were significant both socially and personally. From a social and environmental perspective, the paper bags produced by students will be distributed to vendors at the Kadale Kaayi Parishe festival, helping reduce the usage of single-use plastic bags. This directly contributes to minimizing plastic waste, preventing environmental pollution, and promoting sustainable practices during a large public event.\\n\\nBy replacing plastic with paper, the initiative supports cleaner surroundings and encourages both vendors and customers to adopt eco-friendly habits. Since thousands of people attend the festival, even small changes like using paper bags can create a large positive environmental impact. The activity also spreads awareness among the public about the importance of recycling and reusing materials.\\n\\nOn a personal level, the activity helped me develop a stronger sense of environmental responsibility and social awareness. It taught me that contributing to society does not always require big actions — even small efforts like making paper bags from old newspapers can make a meaningful difference. It also improved my teamwork, patience, and creativity while working on the bags.\\n\\nAdditionally, participating in this initiative increased my understanding of sustainability and inspired me to adopt eco-friendly practices in my daily life, such as reducing plastic usage and reusing materials whenever possible. It motivated me to take part in more environmental and community service activities in the future.\\n\\nOverall, this paper bag–making drive was not just an activity but a valuable learning experience that combined service, sustainability, and social impact. It helped me grow into a more responsible and environmentally conscious individual while contributing positively to society.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-12","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Participating in the paper bag–making activity organized by Youth for Seva for the Kadale Kaayi Parishe festival was a very meaningful and enriching experience for me. Unlike other service activities such as blood donation or food donation, this initiative focused on environmental sustainability and creativity. It gave me an opportunity to contribute towards society in a simple yet impactful way by promoting eco-friendly practices.\\n\\nThe purpose of the activity was to replace single-use plastic bags with paper bags during the Kadale Kaayi Parishe festival at Basavanagudi, which is a well-known cultural and traditional event in Bangalore. Knowing that my small effort could help reduce plastic pollution during such a large public gathering motivated me to participate wholeheartedly.\\n\\nWe were asked to use old newspapers and recycled paper to make paper bags according to a standard template. At first, the process seemed simple, but when I actually started making the bags, I realized that it required patience, neat folding, proper alignment, and strong pasting to ensure the bags were durable. I learned how to measure the dimensions carefully, fold the paper correctly, and secure the edges so that the bags could carry items without tearing.\\n\\nDuring the activity, I worked along with my classmates, which made the experience more enjoyable and collaborative. We shared newspapers, helped each other with folding techniques, and tried to improve the quality and strength of each bag. The atmosphere was very positive and productive, and it felt good to see a pile of completed paper bags increasing steadily. It gave me a sense of satisfaction knowing that each bag we made would be directly used by vendors during the festival.\\n\\nThis activity also made me more conscious about environmental issues. While making the bags, I realized how easily we use plastic in our daily lives without thinking about its harmful effects. Creating eco-friendly alternatives with our own hands helped me understand the value of sustainability in a practical way.\\n\\nOverall, the experience was creative, educational, and socially responsible. It was not just about making paper bags but about understanding the importance of protecting the environment and contributing to the community through small, meaningful actions.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XnD2xh838Rk42fBRlIuQO","name":"Lakshya ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/Pf9qmfYfDn0WZCHn5KYlK.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-27","duration":2,"outcomes":"he Lakshya Shooting Challenge had several positive outcomes, both personally and skill-wise. From a learning perspective, the activity helped me understand the importance of concentration, precision, and patience. It taught me that even small movements or distractions can affect performance, and that maintaining focus is key to achieving accuracy.\\n\\nThe challenge also helped improve my mental discipline and self-control. By practicing steady breathing, calmness, and careful aiming, I developed better focus and coordination. These skills are not only useful in shooting but can also be applied in academics and daily life, especially in situations that require attention and careful decision-making.\\n\\nOn a personal level, participating in this activity boosted my confidence and encouraged me to try new experiences outside my comfort zone. Since it was my first time handling such equipment, I initially felt unsure, but completing the challenge successfully gave me a sense of accomplishment. It showed me that learning something new becomes easier with patience and practice.\\n\\nAdditionally, the event promoted sportsmanship and healthy competition among students. It provided a safe and professional platform to explore a unique sport, making campus life more engaging and diverse. It also highlighted the importance of safety, responsibility, and discipline while handling equipment.\\n\\nOverall, the Lakshya – 10M Shooting Challenge was not just a fun activity but a valuable learning experience that enhanced my focus, confidence, and mental strength. It encouraged me to participate in more skill-based and precision-oriented activities in the future.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Participating in the Lakshya – 10M Shooting Challenge on campus was a completely new and exciting experience for me. It was the first time I had ever tried target shooting, so I approached the activity with both curiosity and enthusiasm. Unlike regular sports events that focus mainly on physical strength or speed, this challenge emphasized focus, precision, patience, and mental control, which made it unique and interesting.\\n\\nThe event was organized in a professional and safe manner. Before starting, the instructors briefed us about the safety rules, proper handling of the equipment, and the correct shooting posture. They explained how to hold the rifle steadily, how to align the sights with the target, and how breathing control plays an important role in improving accuracy. This initial guidance helped me feel comfortable and confident even though I was a beginner.\\n\\nWhen I first held the rifle, I realized that shooting requires much more concentration than I had expected. Maintaining a steady aim, controlling hand movements, and focusing on the target simultaneously was challenging. During my first few attempts, my shots were slightly off-target because I was nervous and unfamiliar with the technique. However, with practice and guidance from the trainers, I slowly improved my stance and timing.\\n\\nOne of the most interesting parts of the experience was learning how mental calmness affects performance. I noticed that whenever I rushed or felt tense, my aim would drift. But when I stayed relaxed, controlled my breathing, and focused carefully, my shots were more accurate. This made me understand that shooting is not just about physical control but also about mental stability and discipline.\\n\\nAs the session progressed, I gained more confidence and started enjoying the challenge. Hitting closer to the center of the target gave me a strong sense of achievement. The environment was also very motivating, as other participants cheered and supported each other. Overall, the experience was thrilling, educational, and very different from any other activity I had previously tried on campus.","aicteMapping":"Sports and Extracurricular Activities or Physical Education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"v4xtCVQ5hMj_TVJU4ZZKz","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Capmus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/jJNiwgCBRk32xD-13tJoz.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of this activity were both social and personal. From a social perspective, the blood donation drive helped collect multiple units of blood that will be used in hospitals for emergencies, surgeries, accident victims, and patients undergoing treatments. Each unit of blood can potentially save several lives, so the collective contribution of students makes a significant difference to the healthcare system.\\n\\nThe drive also spread awareness among students about the importance of regular voluntary blood donation. Seeing repeat donors like me encouraged first-time donors to step forward and participate. It helped build a culture of service, empathy, and responsibility on campus.\\n\\nOn a personal level, donating blood regularly has had a strong impact on my mindset and character. It has helped me develop compassion, social responsibility, and the habit of giving back to society. Over time, it has increased my confidence and removed any fear related to medical procedures. Most importantly, it has become a healthy and positive habit in my life.\\n\\nBy donating for the third time, I realized that small, consistent actions can create a big impact. Instead of treating blood donation as a one-time event, I now see it as a regular contribution I can make to help others. This experience has motivated me to continue donating in the future and to encourage my friends and classmates to do the same.\\n\\nOverall, the activity benefited not only the community but also helped me grow personally, making me more aware, responsible, and committed to social service.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Donating blood at the RVCE campus for the third time was a very meaningful and fulfilling experience for me. Unlike my first donation, where I felt nervous, or my second, where I felt more comfortable, this time the entire process felt natural and familiar. Blood donation has gradually become a regular habit for me rather than a one-time activity.\\n\\nThe camp was organized efficiently by student clubs like Rotaract along with trained medical professionals from hospitals and blood banks. The venue was systematically arranged with separate counters for registration, medical screening, donation beds, and post-donation rest areas. Everything was well planned, creating a safe and hygienic environment for donors.\\n\\nAfter registering, I went through the routine health checkup which included checking my weight, hemoglobin level, blood pressure, and general fitness. Since I have donated before, I was confident about my eligibility and understood the importance of these tests for both donor and patient safety. I felt completely relaxed and mentally prepared.\\n\\nDuring the donation, I didn’t feel any fear or discomfort. Instead, I felt calm and proud that I was once again contributing to a noble cause. The process took about 10–15 minutes, and the medical staff ensured that I was comfortable throughout. After donating, I rested for a while, had juice and snacks, and interacted with other donors and volunteers. It felt less like a medical procedure and more like a positive community activity.\\n\\nBy the third time, blood donation has become something I genuinely look forward to. It no longer feels like a responsibility but rather a small act of kindness that I can regularly offer to society. Knowing that my blood might help save someone’s life gives me deep satisfaction and happiness.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CRjgg0ompz5f69g1RpRZh","name":"Fist Full","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Capmus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/SDXoXhuLSO00FR_8nxJ_B.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"The outcomes of participating in the “FIST FULL” drive for the second time were both social and personal. From a social perspective, the collected food grains will be distributed to underprivileged families, helping them meet their daily food requirements. When many students contribute regularly, the total quantity collected becomes substantial and can support numerous households. This shows how small individual efforts combine to create a large positive impact.\\n\\nThe drive also strengthened awareness on campus about food insecurity and the importance of sharing with those who are less fortunate. More students participated this time, and repeat donors like me helped motivate others to join. It helped build a culture of consistency in social service rather than treating it as a one-time activity.\\n\\nOn a personal level, participating for the second time helped me develop a stronger sense of commitment and empathy. I learned that service activities not only involve donating but also understanding logistics, teamwork, and responsibility. Facing small challenges, such as arranging the materials and managing time to deliver the donation, made me more disciplined and proactive.\\n\\nThis experience encouraged me to continue contributing to such initiatives regularly and to take on a more active role in future drives. Overall, the second participation deepened my understanding of social responsibility and reinforced the idea that consistent small actions can bring meaningful change to society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participating in the “FIST FULL” food donation drive for the second time at RVCE was a much more engaging and responsible experience compared to my first participation. During my first time, I simply contributed the required quantity of rice/toor dal and understood the importance of the initiative. However, this time, I was more aware of the purpose behind the drive and felt more involved in the entire process rather than just being a donor.\\n\\nThe collection took place at the Geotechnical Engineering Lab during the scheduled hours, and the arrangements were systematic with separate areas for receiving, checking, and storing the donated items. Since I had already experienced the event once, I knew what to bring and how the process worked, which made everything smoother. I also encouraged my friends and classmates to participate, explaining how even a small contribution could help families in need.\\n\\nThis time, I spent more time interacting with the volunteers and observing how the collected food grains were sorted and managed. Seeing the growing number of bags and packages made me realize the collective strength of student participation. It gave me a sense of teamwork and unity, as everyone was contributing towards the same social cause.\\n\\nAlong with the positive experience, I also noticed a few practical challenges. Carrying heavy bags of rice or dal from the hostel or home to the collection venue was physically tiring. During peak hours, there were small queues, and managing the crowd and organizing the materials required extra effort from the volunteers. Sometimes, proper packaging and labeling were needed to avoid confusion. Watching the organizers handle these challenges taught me that conducting such drives requires planning, coordination, and teamwork.\\n\\nOverall, my second experience felt more active and responsible. Instead of just donating, I felt like I was truly participating in a community service initiative and understanding the effort that goes into making it successful.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_5_u771xUSGHaPdhGv2o_","name":"Build with Gen AI","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/10AAspDLduz6Lx-UChNMv.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of the “Build with Gen AI” Hackathon were highly beneficial both technically and personally. From a technical perspective, the event enhanced my understanding of Generative AI concepts and their real-world applications. I gained hands-on experience in building AI-based solutions rather than just learning theory in classrooms. It improved my coding skills, logical thinking, and ability to apply knowledge practically.\\n\\nThe hackathon also helped me develop important soft skills such as teamwork, collaboration, and time management. Working in a team taught me how to divide responsibilities effectively, listen to different ideas, and combine strengths to achieve a common goal. Completing a project within a strict deadline improved my ability to work efficiently under pressure.\\n\\nAnother major outcome was the boost in creativity and problem-solving ability. Since the tracks were revealed on the spot, we had to think innovatively and come up with unique solutions quickly. This enhanced my analytical thinking and adaptability. I also became more confident in presenting ideas and communicating technical concepts clearly.\\n\\nFrom an academic and professional perspective, the activity added value through certificates and activity points, while also strengthening my profile for future internships and projects. More importantly, it inspired me to explore Generative AI further and motivated me to participate in more hackathons and technical competitions.\\n\\nOverall, the “Build with Gen AI” Hackathon was not just a competition but a valuable learning experience that improved my technical knowledge, teamwork skills, confidence, and innovation mindset, preparing me better for real-world challenges in technology.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Participating in the “Build with Gen AI” Hackathon organized by ACM RVCE and Accelerate under the CSE Department was an exciting and intellectually stimulating experience for me. Unlike social service or physical activities that I had previously taken part in, this event focused purely on technical skills, creativity, and problem-solving using Generative AI. It gave me an opportunity to explore cutting-edge technology in a competitive and collaborative environment.\\n\\nThe hackathon was conducted at the Design Thinking Huddle on campus, which created a very energetic and innovative atmosphere. Students from different branches and even other colleges participated, forming teams of 2–4 members. This diversity helped bring together different ideas, perspectives, and skill sets. Being part of a team made the experience more engaging because we could brainstorm, divide tasks, and work collaboratively to develop our solution.\\n\\nAt the beginning of the event, the problem statements and tracks were revealed, which added an element of surprise and excitement. We had to quickly understand the problem, identify a feasible idea, and plan how to implement it within the limited time of six hours. This required fast thinking, proper time management, and clear communication among teammates.\\n\\nDuring the development phase, we worked continuously on designing, coding, and testing our solution using Generative AI concepts. We explored tools and technologies such as AI models, APIs, and automation techniques to build something innovative and practical. There were moments when we faced technical challenges like debugging errors, integrating features, and optimizing performance. However, overcoming these obstacles through teamwork and logical thinking made the process even more rewarding.\\n\\nThe environment throughout the hackathon was very motivating. Seeing other teams actively building creative solutions pushed us to work harder and think more innovatively. Mentors and organizers were available to guide us whenever we were stuck, which helped us learn new approaches and improve our implementation.\\n\\nFinally, presenting our project in front of judges was a memorable part of the experience. Explaining our idea, demonstrating the working model, and answering questions improved my confidence and communication skills. Overall, the hackathon was intense, challenging, and extremely enjoyable. It felt satisfying to create something meaningful within a short time using advanced technology.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"o8fPoDf0jrO_OhhGclDrQ","name":"DATA Remix: Clash of Companies","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/d03ae4ee-daeb-4611-98a3-fe6a6f821bbc/Wke50BDIvt3lYuuU7ARGI.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcomes of participating in DATA Remix: Clash of Companies were highly beneficial both academically and personally. From a technical perspective, the event significantly improved my data analysis skills. I learned how to interpret raw datasets, clean and organize data, identify trends, and extract meaningful insights. This practical exposure strengthened my understanding of concepts like data visualization, problem-solving, and decision-making.\\n\\nThe activity also enhanced my critical thinking and analytical abilities. Instead of simply observing the data, I learned how to ask the right questions, identify gaps, and propose realistic solutions. This helped me understand how data can influence business strategies and drive improvements in performance and sustainability.\\n\\nWorking in a team helped me develop essential soft skills such as teamwork, collaboration, and communication. Coordinating with teammates, sharing ideas, and dividing responsibilities taught me how to work effectively in a group environment. It also improved my leadership and time-management skills, especially when working under deadlines.\\n\\nAnother important outcome was gaining awareness about the role of data in achieving Sustainable Development Goals. I realized that data analytics is not just about numbers but also about creating positive social and environmental impact. This broadened my perspective and encouraged me to think more responsibly while designing solutions.\\n\\nOn a personal level, the event boosted my confidence and motivated me to participate in more data-driven competitions and hackathons in the future. It also strengthened my interest in analytics and real-world problem-solving, which will be beneficial for my academic growth and future career.\\n\\nOverall, DATA Remix was not just a competition but a valuable learning experience that enhanced my technical knowledge, teamwork skills, and innovative thinking, while showing me how data can be used to create meaningful change in society.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Participating in DATA Remix: Clash of Companies was an exciting and intellectually enriching experience for me, as it combined data analytics, teamwork, and real-world problem-solving into a single competitive event. Unlike regular technical workshops or coding contests, this event focused on analysing datasets and making data-driven decisions, which gave me practical exposure to how companies use data to improve their performance and align with global goals like the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\\n\\nThe event was conducted at the Design Thinking Huddle, creating a professional and innovation-focused environment. Teams of 4–5 members were formed, and each team represented a company from a specific industry. This concept made the competition feel realistic, as we had to think not just like students but like analysts or decision-makers working for an actual organization.\\n\\nAt the beginning, each team was provided with exclusive datasets related to their assigned company. These datasets included various operational and performance-related information. Initially, the data looked large and complex, which was slightly overwhelming. However, as we began exploring and organizing it, we realized how much valuable information it contained.\\n\\nMy team divided the work among ourselves — some members focused on cleaning and preprocessing the data, others worked on analysis and visualization, while a few concentrated on identifying patterns and preparing solutions. We used logical reasoning and analytical tools to study trends, compare metrics, and detect inefficiencies. It felt like solving a real-life business problem rather than just completing an academic task.\\n\\nOne of the most interesting aspects was connecting our findings to the Sustainable Development Goals. We had to think beyond profit and performance and consider sustainability, resource optimization, and social impact. This added a meaningful dimension to our solutions and helped us understand the broader role of data in driving positive change.\\n\\nDuring the process, we faced several challenges. Cleaning the data, handling missing values, and interpreting large datasets required patience and teamwork. Time management was also important since we had to analyze the data, generate insights, and present our solutions within the given timeframe. Despite these challenges, the collaborative discussions and brainstorming sessions made the experience enjoyable and productive.\\n\\nFinally, presenting our insights and recommendations in front of judges was a valuable learning moment. Explaining our analysis, justifying our decisions, and answering questions improved my communication and presentation skills. Overall, the event was dynamic, challenging, and highly engaging, giving me hands-on exposure to practical data analytics.","aicteMapping":"Smart Technologies & Automation","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Kavitha S N ","designation":"Assistant Professor  "},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:03:19.168369+00', '2026-01-30 10:33:51.883329+00'), ('ce18862c-aecd-4df2-91f0-14e0a990e0ce', '8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC045","name":"Dhanush L","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"JXFkr-9-ZTC-4AFkz3eWq","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity helped in collecting blood for patients in need and \\ncontributed to saving lives. It also created awareness among \\nstudents about social responsibility and humanitarian values. \\nParticipants developed a sense of empathy, civic duty, and \\nunderstood the importance of contributing to society through \\nvoluntary service. The camp encouraged students to overcome \\nhesitation and actively participate in life-saving initiatives. It \\nstrengthened the spirit of teamwork and volunteerism among the \\nparticipants. Such programs inspire young individuals to become \\nresponsible citizens and motivate them to engage in future social \\nand health-related activities. The success of the camp reflected the \\ncollective effort and dedication of the organizers, volunteers, and \\nmedical staff. ","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The program emphasized the idea that a single unit of blood can \\nsave multiple lives, reinforcing the value of selfless service. \\nStudents from various departments came forward enthusiastically \\nto contribute to this noble cause. The organizers ensured proper \\ncoordination and time management, making the process smooth \\nand efficient. Informative sessions were conducted to educate \\nparticipants about eligibility criteria and post-donation care. The \\ncamp strengthened collaboration between the institution and \\nhealthcare professionals, promoting community engagement. Such \\ninitiatives play a vital role in building a healthy society and \\nencouraging youth participation in social welfare activities.","aicteMapping":"Community Health Initiative","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/56m7ar70auwg8rw_EJ2Jo.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8CcQPLBC5qOxJ1ORHxp1V","name":"Tanuja Screening","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Motivational Impact: The film deeply inspired participants by showcasing that dedication and hard work can help overcome financial and social obstacles. Students were motivated to pursue their academic goals with renewed determination.\\nAwareness Creation: The screening raised awareness about the difficulties faced by students from lower socio-economic sections in accessing quality education and preparing for competitive examinations like NEET.\\nEmpathy Development: Participants developed greater empathy and understanding towards classmates from diverse economic backgrounds, fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment.\\nCareer Guidance Insight: The film provided valuable insights into the NEET preparation journey, medical career paths, and the importance of proper guidance and resources for competitive exam aspirants.\\nSocial Responsibility: The activity encouraged participants to reflect on educational inequality and inspired discussions about how students can support each other and contribute to creating equal opportunities in education.\\nPositive Engagement: The screening witnessed enthusiastic participation and engagement, with students actively discussing the film''s themes and relating them to real-life challenges in their own educational journeys.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The screening featured a motivational film centered on the journey of a young girl from an economically disadvantaged background who aspires to crack the NEET (National Eligibility cum Entrance Test) examination to fulfill her dream of becoming a doctor. The film portrays her struggles, determination, and resilience in overcoming socio-economic barriers to pursue medical education.\\nPurpose: The film screening was organized to inspire students and create awareness about the challenges faced by underprivileged students in accessing higher education, particularly in competitive fields like medicine. It aimed to highlight the importance of perseverance, hard work, and educational opportunities regardless of one''s economic background.","aicteMapping":"Motivational for Students","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/lGIbNdmPdrqbYJwdLcgjQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6yxXUT2K171J-3DAwTdgX","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-12-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Substantial Collection: A significant quantity of old books, notebooks, newspapers, and paper materials was collected from multiple apartments, demonstrating strong community participation and support for the cause.\\nCommunity Engagement: The activity fostered meaningful interaction between volunteers and community members, creating awareness about sustainable waste management and the importance of reusing educational materials.\\nSupport to Children''s Homes: The donated books and paper materials provided valuable educational resources to children''s homes, supporting the learning and development of underprivileged children who may not have easy access to reading materials.\\nEnvironmental Awareness: The paper drive promoted environmental consciousness by encouraging recycling and reuse of paper materials, reducing waste, and contributing to sustainable practices within the community.\\nTeamwork and Collaboration: Volunteers developed teamwork, communication, and organizational skills through coordinating the collection drive, interacting with residents, and managing the sorting and distribution process.\\nSocial Responsibility: Participants experienced a sense of fulfillment and social responsibility by contributing to both environmental conservation and the welfare of underprivileged children through a single impactful activity.\\nCommunity Goodwill: The initiative strengthened the relationship between the Rotaract Club and the local community, creating goodwill and opening avenues for future collaborative social service projects.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-12-07","hoursSpent":6,"description":" The paper drive was a community service initiative aimed at collecting old books, newspapers, magazines, and other paper materials from residential apartments. The collected items were intended for donation to children''s homes to promote recycling, literacy, and support underprivileged children''s educational needs.\\nExecution: Volunteers visited various apartments in the locality to collect old books, notebooks, newspapers, and other paper materials that residents no longer needed. The collected materials were sorted, organized, and subsequently donated to children''s homes where they could be reused for educational purposes or recycled responsibly.\\nPurpose: The activity served a dual purpose—promoting environmental sustainability through paper recycling and supporting children''s homes by providing reading materials and educational resources to underprivileged children.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/HkLO16Un7abcru4roJu6P.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jR7ArrzhaiRHoaYU7eVIM","name":"Kannada Sangha Activity - 2023 ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-05","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event successfully celebrated Kannada culture through mass \\nsinging, fostering regional pride and cultural unity among the \\nstudent body. \\n \\nBeyond just singing, the event was a pledge to preserve and \\npromote the local language and culture in an increasingly \\nglobalized world. It provided a refreshing break from academic \\nroutines, allowing students to connect with their roots and celebrate \\nthe artistic legacy of the state.  ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"On 05-02-2024, the Kannada Sangha of RV College of \\nEngineering organized the \"Koti Kanta Gaayana\" event to \\ncelebrate the richness of Kannada culture and language. This mass \\nsinging event was part of a state-wide initiative to unite people \\nthrough the power of music and shared heritage. Students gathered \\nin large numbers to sing iconic Kannada songs, creating a vibrant  \\natmosphere of regional pride and unity. \\n \\nThe event served as a prelude to the Kannada Rajyotsava \\ncelebrations, instilling a sense of belonging and cultural identity \\namong the students. Participants, regardless of their linguistic  \\nbackground, joined in the chorus, celebrating the inclusive spirit \\nof Karnataka. The air resonated with melodies that paid tribute to \\nthe land, its poets, and its history.","aicteMapping":"Community   Service ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/LbLNv-gTGnSSXX3nhtQi3.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vWF1ou6v4JV4iQmICIfaV","name":"Utsarga Marathon  ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of \\nRVCE, successfully blended fitness, community engagement, and \\nphilanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to contribute to a \\nmeaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With \\nenthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and fitness \\nenthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful reminder of the \\nimportance of collective action in addressing societal challenges. \\nRunners contributed through their registration fees, which were \\ndirected toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivilege communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to \\neducational and environmental projects.   \\n  \\nThe overwhelming response from participants highlighted the \\ndeep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service \\nand social responsibility. Beyond the physical endurance required \\nto complete the marathon, the event fostered a sense of \\ncamaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of \\nteamwork and determination. The well-organized event featured \\nstructured routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance, \\nensuring a smooth and safe experience for all runners. \\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, \\nencouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while \\ngiving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the \\nbond between students and the community but also showcased \\nhow small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful \\nsocial change. ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National \\nService Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to \\npromote fitness, community engagement, and social \\nresponsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and \\nfitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a \\nregistration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the \\nproceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as \\nsupporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare \\ninitiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability \\nprojects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being \\nbut also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among \\nparticipants.  \\n  \\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of \\ngiving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals \\nto contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing \\nthe thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants \\ntake pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal \\nachievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. \\nOrganized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes \\nwellmarked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to \\nensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the \\nyears, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening \\nthe values of empathy and community service within RVCE and \\nbeyond. ","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/KbxRxner8fVYZyAqXpxPB.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zHZTdk56HkLPJhnSF2wUf","name":"DRUG AWARENESS E-PLEDGE   ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"  \\nThe activity increased awareness about the dangers of drug \\naddiction and its negative impact on health, career, and society. It \\nmotivated students to stay away from drugs and to spread \\nawareness among peers. The session helped students understand \\nthe long-term physical, psychological, and social consequences of \\nsubstance abuse. Interactive discussions encouraged students to \\nmake informed and responsible life choices. The program \\nreinforced the importance of a healthy lifestyle and self-discipline. \\nOverall, the activity played a significant role in shaping positive \\nattitudes and promoting a drug-free campus environment.  ","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The awareness program was conducted in association with the \\nNarcotics Control Bureau to educate students about the harmful \\neffects of drug abuse. The activity focused on highlighting the \\nphysical, psychological, and social consequences of substance \\naddiction. Students were informed about the importance of making \\nresponsible life choices and staying away from drugs. The program \\nencouraged students to take a pledge for a drug-free lifestyle. It \\nalso emphasized the role of youth in spreading awareness and \\nbuilding a healthy society. Interactive sessions and expert talks \\nhelped students clearly understand the legal, health, and social \\nimplications of drug abuse. The initiative motivated participants to \\nact as ambassadors of change within their peer groups and \\ncommunities. Overall, the program successfully reinforced \\nawareness, responsibility, and commitment toward maintaining a \\ndrug-free campus and society.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive  ","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/P_RbEsBw-DC5LJ4GZCyJX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"03zfyM0ATqvjPsSzabAh6","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity helped in collecting blood for patients in need and \\ncontributed to saving lives. It also created awareness among \\nstudents about social responsibility and humanitarian values. \\nParticipants developed a sense of empathy, civic duty, and \\nunderstood the importance of contributing to society through \\nvoluntary service. The camp encouraged students to overcome \\nhesitation and actively participate in life-saving initiatives. It \\nstrengthened the spirit of teamwork and volunteerism among the \\nparticipants. Such programs inspire young individuals to become \\nresponsible citizens and motivate them to engage in future social \\nand health-related activities. The success of the camp reflected the \\ncollective effort and dedication of the organizers, volunteers, and \\nmedical staff.  ","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The program emphasized the idea that a single unit of blood can \\nsave multiple lives, reinforcing the value of selfless service. \\nStudents from various departments came forward enthusiastically \\nto contribute to this noble cause. The organizers ensured proper \\ncoordination and time management, making the process smooth \\nand efficient. Informative sessions were conducted to educate \\nparticipants about eligibility criteria and post-donation care. The \\ncamp strengthened collaboration between the institution and \\nhealthcare professionals, promoting community engagement. Such \\ninitiatives play a vital role in building a healthy society and \\nencouraging youth participation in social welfare activities.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/1L0C9ZhtA9e5nTZE4jSKm.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LFv3gUSW0dWdFPxDHAWPF","name":"T-Shirt for Smiles(Kannada Sangha)  ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-09-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The “T-Shirt for Smiles” and orphanage visit was successfully \\ncarried out, making a positive impact on the children at Pragati \\nSeva Charitable Trust. The activity encouraged students to \\ncontribute towards a good cause while being actively involved in \\ncommunity service. The orphanage visit helped create awareness \\namong students about the importance of supporting underserved \\ncommunities and contributing to society beyond academics. ","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-07","hoursSpent":1,"description":"“T-Shirt for Smiles” is a social service and charity-based initiative \\norganized by Kannada Sanga, RV College of Engineering, where \\nstudents participated by purchasing a specially designed event \\nTshirt. The event aimed to combine student involvement with \\nmeaningful community service by raising contributions through T\\nshirt sales. As part of the initiative, a group of students visited \\nPragati Seva Charitable Trust – Anathashrama, located at \\nKumbalagodu, Bengaluru, to spend time with the children and \\nsupport them through donations and service activities.  \\n  \\nThe activity was organized with the intention of promoting \\nempathy, compassion, and social responsibility among students. \\nThe visit included interaction with the children, understanding \\ntheir needs, and offering support through various donated \\nessentials. This initiative not only strengthened the spirit of service \\nwithin the campus but also created a sense of connection between \\nstudents and the community.  ","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/j1qbVvVQiYoaZB4SCdNuB.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"x0OeaiugAZyqqBMo8HfWS","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of \\nRVCE, successfully blended fitness, community engagement, and \\nphilanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to contribute to a \\nmeaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With \\nenthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and fitness \\nenthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful reminder of the \\nimportance of collective action in addressing societal challenges. \\nRunners contributed through their registration fees, which were \\ndirected toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to \\neducational and environmental projects.   \\n  \\nThe overwhelming response from participants highlighted the \\ndeep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service \\nand social responsibility. Beyond the physical endurance required \\nto complete the marathon, the event fostered a sense of \\ncamaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of \\nteamwork and determination. The well-organized event featured \\nstructured routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance, \\nensuring a smooth and safe experience for all runners. \\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, \\nencouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while \\ngiving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the \\nbond between students and the community but also showcased \\nhow small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful \\nsocial change. ","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National \\nService Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to \\npromote fitness, community engagement, and social \\nresponsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and \\nfitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a \\nregistration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the \\nproceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as \\nsupporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare \\ninitiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability \\nprojects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being \\nbut also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among \\nparticipants.  \\n  \\nBeyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of \\ngiving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals \\nto contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing \\nthe thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants \\ntake pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal \\nachievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. \\nOrganized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes \\nwellmarked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to \\nensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the \\nyears, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening \\nthe values of empathy and community service within RVCE and \\nbeyond. ","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/rzOEJvOCqKApIFSeJClN5.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"llzXT5ZXyuvepdAEuaBBp","name":"Lakshya","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"Lakshya 2025 transcended the conventional shooting competition format by creating a\\nplatform that nurtured both individual talent and environmental stewardship. Participants\\nnot only developed valuable sporting skills but also became ambassadors of green initiatives,\\ncarrying the message of sustainability beyond the event itself.\\nThe dual focus on personal development and environmental awareness made this initiative\\nparticularly impactful, aligning with AICTE''s vision of holistic student development and\\nsocial responsibility.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Skill Development: Participants received training in shooting techniques, enhancing their focus, hand-eye coordination, and decision-making abilities under pressure.\\nDiscipline and Teamwork: The event promoted NCC values of discipline, responsibility, and collaborative learning through structured team activities and competitive exercises.\\nEnvironmental Integration: What distinguished \"Lakshya 2025\" was its unique integration of environmental consciousness with sports training. Each participant was provided with a sapling along with detailed planting and care instructions.\\nSapling Distribution Drive: Students were encouraged to plant their saplings within the college campus, making a personal commitment to environmental sustainability. This initiative successfully combined skill-building with ecological responsibility.\\n\\nImpact and Outcomes:","aicteMapping":"Encourage Plantation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/g_x9vaqkEUYxk9nv2sUZf.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WmCTwTnzuRi7Zi3zHOoeM","name":"Female Walkathon","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Wide Public Reach: The walk attracted significant public attention, effectively spreading awareness about female foeticide among diverse sections of the community including students, families, shopkeepers, and passersby.\\nSocial Awareness Creation: The initiative educated community members about the severity of female foeticide, its legal consequences under the Pre-Conception and Pre-Natal Diagnostic Techniques (PCPNDT) Act, and its detrimental effects on social balance and gender equality.\\nAttitude Change: The campaign prompted many individuals to reflect on deep-rooted gender biases and encouraged conversations about valuing the girl child equally, potentially influencing mindset changes within families and communities.\\nCommunity Engagement: Active interaction with the public during the walk facilitated meaningful discussions about gender discrimination, women''s rights, and the importance of female education and empowerment.\\nStudent Empowerment: Participants developed confidence in addressing social issues publicly and gained valuable experience in organizing awareness campaigns and communicating important social messages effectively.\\nVisibility to Social Cause: The use of impactful slogans, placards, and banners created strong visual messaging that resonated with observers and helped reinforce the campaign''s core message: \"Save the Girl Child\" and \"Daughters are Equal.\"\\nCollaborative Impact: The collective effort of volunteers demonstrated the power of youth participation in addressing critical social issues and inspired others to join similar initiatives promoting gender equality.\\nLong-term Awareness: The distribution of informational materials ensured that the message reached beyond the walk itself, creating lasting awareness that community members could share with their families and social circles.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"\\ni had an activity of a folm screing i attened that its a movie about agirl who is from lower class want to clear neet and become doctor soo give me the description and outcome of this ativity i want to enter in the report\\n\\n2:18 pm\\nI''ll help you write a description and outcome for this film screening activity for your report.\\n\\nActivity Description\\nActivity: Film Screening\\n\\nFilm Theme: The screening featured a motivational film centered on the journey of a young girl from an economically disadvantaged background who aspires to crack the NEET (National Eligibility cum Entrance Test) examination to fulfill her dream of becoming a doctor. The film portrays her struggles, determination, and resilience in overcoming socio-economic barriers to pursue medical education.\\n\\nPurpose: The film screening was organized to inspire students and create awareness about the challenges faced by underprivileged students in accessing higher education, particularly in competitive fields like medicine. It aimed to highlight the importance of perseverance, hard work, and educational opportunities regardless of one''s economic background.\\n\\nOutcome of the Activity\\nThe film screening proved to be highly impactful and achieved the following outcomes:\\n\\nMotivational Impact: The film deeply inspired participants by showcasing that dedication and hard work can help overcome financial and social obstacles. Students were motivated to pursue their academic goals with renewed determination.\\nAwareness Creation: The screening raised awareness about the difficulties faced by students from lower socio-economic sections in accessing quality education and preparing for competitive examinations like NEET.\\nEmpathy Development: Participants developed greater empathy and understanding towards classmates from diverse economic backgrounds, fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment.\\nCareer Guidance Insight: The film provided valuable insights into the NEET preparation journey, medical career paths, and the importance of proper guidance and resources for competitive exam aspirants.\\nSocial Responsibility: The activity encouraged participants to reflect on educational inequality and inspired discussions about how students can support each other and contribute to creating equal opportunities in education.\\nPositive Engagement: The screening witnessed enthusiastic participation and engagement, with students actively discussing the film''s themes and relating them to real-life challenges in their own educational journeys.\\nFeel free to modify this based on any specific details from the actual film or additional outcomes you experienced!\\n\\ngive the same for paper drive where it is arranged by rotract RVCE wheere we wnet to appartment and colleccted old books and papers and donated to chid homes\\n\\n2:38 pm\\nI''ll help you write a description and outcome for this paper drive activity for your report.\\n\\nActivity Description\\nActivity: Paper Drive (Community Service Initiative)\\n\\nOrganized By: Rotaract Club of RVCE\\n\\nObjective: The paper drive was a community service initiative aimed at collecting old books, newspapers, magazines, and other paper materials from residential apartments. The collected items were intended for donation to children''s homes to promote recycling, literacy, and support underprivileged children''s educational needs.\\n\\nExecution: Volunteers visited various apartments in the locality to collect old books, notebooks, newspapers, and other paper materials that residents no longer needed. The collected materials were sorted, organized, and subsequently donated to children''s homes where they could be reused for educational purposes or recycled responsibly.\\n\\nPurpose: The activity served a dual purpose—promoting environmental sustainability through paper recycling and supporting children''s homes by providing reading materials and educational resources to underprivileged children.\\n\\nOutcome of the Activity\\nThe paper drive successfully achieved its objectives and resulted in the following positive outcomes:\\n\\nSubstantial Collection: A significant quantity of old books, notebooks, newspapers, and paper materials was collected from multiple apartments, demonstrating strong community participation and support for the cause.\\nCommunity Engagement: The activity fostered meaningful interaction between volunteers and community members, creating awareness about sustainable waste management and the importance of reusing educational materials.\\nSupport to Children''s Homes: The donated books and paper materials provided valuable educational resources to children''s homes, supporting the learning and development of underprivileged children who may not have easy access to reading materials.\\nEnvironmental Awareness: The paper drive promoted environmental consciousness by encouraging recycling and reuse of paper materials, reducing waste, and contributing to sustainable practices within the community.\\nTeamwork and Collaboration: Volunteers developed teamwork, communication, and organizational skills through coordinating the collection drive, interacting with residents, and managing the sorting and distribution process.\\nSocial Responsibility: Participants experienced a sense of fulfillment and social responsibility by contributing to both environmental conservation and the welfare of underprivileged children through a single impactful activity.\\nCommunity Goodwill: The initiative strengthened the relationship between the Rotaract Club and the local community, creating goodwill and opening avenues for future collaborative social service projects.\\nYou can adjust any details to match your specific experience during the paper drive!\\n\\nsame thing for a walk conducted by rotract to spread awarness about female feouticide\\n\\n3:39 pm\\nI''ll help you write a description and outcome for this awareness walk activity for your report.\\n\\nActivity Description\\nActivity: Awareness Walk on Female Foeticide\\n\\nOrganized By: Rotaract Club of RVCE\\n\\nObjective: The awareness walk was organized to spread awareness about the critical social issue of female foeticide and its devastating impact on society. The initiative aimed to educate the public about gender equality, the importance of the girl child, and the legal and moral implications of sex-selective abortion.\\n\\nExecution: Volunteers participated in a planned walk through public areas, carrying placards, banners, and posters with impactful messages condemning female foeticide and promoting gender equality. The walk route covered key residential and commercial areas to maximize public reach and engagement. Participants also distributed informational pamphlets and engaged with community members to discuss the issue and its consequences.\\n\\nPurpose: The activity sought to create public awareness about the declining female sex ratio, challenge gender discrimination, advocate for the rights of the girl child, and encourage community members to take a stand against the practice of female foeticide.","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/_KqYwZJlWOgFS6slOTcQ4.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iEZo5l96sbbloMltARuZ6","name":"Project Pusthak","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-22","duration":1,"outcomes":"Project Pustak – Phase 2 successfully created a positive impact by \\ndistributing educational supplies to students who required support \\nfor their studies. The initiative strengthened the spirit of \\ncommunity service among participants and helped reduce \\nresource gaps faced by underprivileged children. Through \\norganized planning and efficient distribution, the drive ensured \\nthat contributions were effectively transformed into meaningful \\neducational assistance. The drive also promoted awareness about \\nthe importance of education and equal learning opportunities, \\nreinforcing the belief that every child deserves access to quality \\nresources. By transforming small donations into practical \\neducational support, the activity highlighted how collective \\ncontributions can bring significant change. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak – Phase 2 is a donation drive organized by the \\nRotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with Pranava \\nFoundation, to support education for underprivileged students. \\nThe initiative collected funds from donors and used them to \\nprocure and distribute essential school supplies such as notebooks, \\nstationery kits, geometry boxes, and other learning materials. The \\ndrive aimed to ensure that students from rural and underserved \\ncommunities had access to basic educational resources and better \\nlearning support.   \\n  \\n  As a part of this drive, funds were collected through generous \\ncontributions from donors and volunteers. These contributions \\nwere carefully utilized to procure essential items such as \\nnotebooks, textbooks, stationery kits, pens, pencils, erasers, \\ngeometry boxes, backpacks, and other required study materials. \\nThe collected supplies were then distributed to school-going \\nchildren who required support, ensuring that they could continue \\ntheir education without financial barriers. ","aicteMapping":"Community Service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/B3yPxXcJij8m9OrIlIFQv.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ChHHdgXZvjQiHfB3lnley","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation camp successfully collected blood units to \\nsupport patients in need and contributed to saving lives. The \\nactivity enhanced awareness among students about the importance \\nof voluntary blood donation and emergency medical care. \\nParticipants developed a strong sense of social responsibility, \\nempathy, and humanitarian values. The program motivated \\nstudents to actively engage in community service and encouraged \\nthem to participate in similar life-saving initiatives in the future.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":0,"description":"A blood donation camp was organized in association with the \\nIndian Red Cross Society, Karnataka State Branch, with the \\nobjective of supporting patients in need of blood and promoting \\nvoluntary blood donation. Students enthusiastically participated in \\nthe camp after undergoing basic health screening conducted by \\ntrained medical professionals. The activity was carried out in a \\ndisciplined, safe, and hygienic environment following all medical \\nguidelines. Donors were educated about the importance of blood \\ndonation and its role in saving lives during emergencies. The \\ninitiative encouraged social responsibility, humanitarian values, \\nand community service among students. The successful conduct of \\nthe camp reflected the commitment of the institution and students \\ntoward serving society and contributing to a noble cause. ","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/f8B-ReU-f9rZOkUDWXMFC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2vo5vnzJU0CbYbP-Ynv6P","name":"Fist Full","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"Substantial Food Collection: A significant quantity of rice and toor dal was collected through enthusiastic participation from students and staff, demonstrating strong community support for the welfare of orphaned children.\\nSupport to Orphanage: The donated food items provided essential nutritional support to the orphanage, helping ensure that children have access to regular, healthy meals and reducing the financial burden on the institution.\\nCommunity Participation: The campaign witnessed overwhelming response from the college community, with numerous students and faculty members contributing generously, reflecting collective commitment to social welfare.\\nAwareness About Food Security: The initiative raised awareness about food insecurity challenges faced by orphanages and other charitable institutions, encouraging participants to think about hunger and malnutrition issues in society.\\nCultivation of Empathy: Participants developed greater empathy and compassion towards orphaned and underprivileged children, understanding the importance of basic necessities like food in their daily lives.\\nSocial Responsibility: The activity reinforced the values of giving, sharing, and social responsibility among students, encouraging them to actively participate in community welfare initiatives.\\nTeam Coordination: Volunteers gained valuable experience in organizing large-scale collection drives, managing logistics, coordinating donations, and executing community outreach programs effectively.\\nSustainable Impact: The donation of staple food items ensured long-term utility, as rice and dal could be stored and used over an extended period, providing sustained support to the orphanage''s daily meal requirements.\\nPositive Campus Culture: The Fistful campaign fostered a culture of compassion and collective action on campus, inspiring students to look beyond academics and contribute meaningfully to society.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-20","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Objective: \"Fistful\" was a community service initiative aimed at collecting essential food\\nitems from students and staff to support orphanages. The campaign encouraged participants\\nto donate either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal (pigeon peas), which are staple food items, to\\nhelp provide nutritious meals to underprivileged children living in orphanages.\\nExecution: Volunteers organized collection drives across the college campus, motivating\\nstudents and faculty members to contribute food grains. The donations were systematically\\ncollected, recorded, and compiled. All the collected rice and dal were then packaged and\\ndelivered to a local orphanage to support their meal preparation and food security needs.\\nPurpose: The activity aimed to address food insecurity faced by orphanages, instill a sense of\\ncompassion and social responsibility among students, and demonstrate how small individual\\ncontributions can collectively make a significant impact on the lives of underprivileged\\nchildren.","aicteMapping":"To reduce hunger index","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/8bf9f35b-f898-42c9-81aa-dcc945bfc8b0/RfXbHMmJOc9Eeuaa8AD9E.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 09:56:36.4163+00', '2026-01-31 10:47:50.30593+00'), ('ce18bcee-10f9-4f6a-980a-e2361fc91c3c', 'fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS011","name":"Arnav Jain","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"FK-SkHLLdMrAgLlnD0_1_","name":"Health and Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"BGS Gleneagles Global Hospital, Kengeri","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/Q279zqr2L5yg30401RlyI.png"],"endDate":"2022-12-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"From the Health and Blood Donation Camp, I learned the importance of taking care of my health and the value of helping others through blood donation. I understood how donated blood can be life-saving for patients in emergencies and medical treatments. The event taught me social responsibility, compassion, and the need for regular health check-ups. Overall, the experience encouraged me to maintain a healthy lifestyle and actively participate in activities that benefit society.","semester":"1","startDate":"2022-12-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Health and Blood Donation Camp was organized by the NSS unit as a social service initiative to promote health awareness and encourage voluntary blood donation. The event aimed to educate students and the community about the importance of maintaining good health and the life-saving value of donating blood. Medical professionals and healthcare staff were invited to conduct health check-ups and guide participants throughout the camp.\\nDuring the event, basic health screenings such as blood pressure, weight, and general health assessments were carried out. Eligible participants voluntarily donated blood under proper medical supervision, ensuring safety and hygiene. The camp also included awareness sessions about healthy lifestyle habits, disease prevention, and the importance of regular medical check-ups. The event successfully created awareness about health care and highlighted how one small act like blood donation can save lives.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WLkycUxGgvvh130afbPxm","name":"Fast-Trek","slNo":2,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/_6LkB85q7w7Hhw5o4w7qp.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this fast trek, I learned the importance of combining social service with meaningful activities that bring people together for a good cause. I understood how participation in such events can help raise support for those in need while also promoting health and teamwork. The experience taught me compassion, responsibility, and the joy of contributing to a life-saving cause. Overall, the event inspired me to take part in more service-oriented initiatives and realize that even enjoyable activities can make a positive difference in society.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Fast trek was organized as a social service initiative with the noble cause of providing financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from heart diseases. The event combined adventure with service, encouraging participants to contribute to a meaningful cause while engaging in a healthy outdoor activity. The program began early in the morning at 7:30 AM, when all participants gathered and boarded the bus to the trek location with great enthusiasm. Before the journey began, safety instructions and basic information about the trek were clearly explained to ensure a secure and well-organized experience for everyone.\\n\\nThe trek took place in the scenic surroundings of Huthridurga Betta, where participants enjoyed the natural beauty and fresh environment. The journey was both exciting and memorable, allowing everyone to connect with nature while supporting a social cause. Breakfast and lunch were provided at the trek location, ensuring the comfort of all participants. The event was a great success, as it not only offered a refreshing experience but also helped raise support for children in need of medical care.","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Op8GZqRcTgl4aVjOlJToa","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/DwSPBR9HGgU4OE8tcGVww.png"],"endDate":"2023-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness regarding the importance of \\nphysical fitness and community service among participants. It \\nhelped develop discipline, endurance, teamwork, and a sense of \\nsocial responsibility. Participation in the marathon strengthened \\nthe understanding of how individual effort can contribute to \\nbroader community welfare and encouraged continued \\ninvolvement in NSS-led initiatives. ","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-04-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 was organized under the National Service \\nScheme (NSS) with the objective of promoting community \\nparticipation, health awareness, and social responsibility. The \\nevent encouraged students to actively engage in a long-distance \\nmarathon that symbolized commitment towards physical fitness \\nand collective well-being. Through structured coordination and \\nvolunteer participation, the activity aimed to highlight the \\nimportance of an active lifestyle while fostering a sense of service \\ntowards society. The marathon also served as a platform to create \\nawareness about community health initiatives and the role of \\nyouth in contributing to social development. ","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yY13MMLLl9xKQzz9Inyh6","name":"International Yoga Day","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/39mYXxuyMd3FJL-36Y0bF.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this event, I learned that yoga is very important for both physical and mental health. I understood how breathing techniques help reduce stress and improve focus, and how regular yoga can keep the body fit and the mind peaceful. The session also taught me discipline, patience, and the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle. Overall, it inspired me to include yoga in my daily routine for a better and more balanced life.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-21","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The NSS unit organized an awareness drive on the occasion of International Yoga Day to highlight the importance of yoga for a healthy body and peaceful mind. The event was conducted with active participation from NSS volunteers, students, and invited teachers. The program began with a brief introduction about the significance of Yoga Day and how yoga helps people manage stress in today’s busy lifestyle. Our teachers guided the session and demonstrated various yoga asanas and breathing exercises while students followed them with enthusiasm. Several yoga postures such as Tadasana, Vrikshasana, Bhujangasana, and Pranayama were practiced during the session. The teachers also explained the benefits of each asana and how regular yoga practice improves flexibility, posture, concentration, and overall well-being. The atmosphere was calm and disciplined, creating a positive environment for learning and relaxation. The event successfully spread awareness that yoga is not just physical exercise but a way to balance the body and mind.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qSzTVtmbkf96TvQ5ya515","name":"Har Ghar Dhyan","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/xVeoNy87S9Y-Oc5vmt0CU.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"From this event, I learned the importance of meditation in daily life. I understood how regular practice of deep breathing and mindfulness can reduce stress, increase focus, and create a positive mindset. The session also taught me patience, self-control, and the value of spending a few quiet moments with myself. Overall, the Har Ghar Dhyan program inspired me to practice meditation regularly for better mental clarity and emotional balance.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-21","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The NSS unit organized the Har Ghar Dhyan event as an awareness initiative to promote the importance of meditation for mental peace and emotional well-being. The program aimed to encourage students and community members to adopt meditation as a daily habit for a stress-free and focused life. NSS volunteers, students, and teachers actively participated in the session. The event began with an introduction explaining the meaning of “Har Ghar Dhyan,” emphasizing how meditation can bring positivity and balance into every home.\\nTrained teachers guided the participants through simple meditation techniques, including deep breathing, mindful awareness, and relaxation exercises. Everyone sat in a calm and quiet environment, focusing on their breath and thoughts. The teachers explained how meditation helps control negative emotions, improve concentration, and develop inner stability. The peaceful atmosphere of the session helped participants feel relaxed and refreshed. The event successfully spread awareness that meditation is a simple yet powerful tool for maintaining mental health and inner peace.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8sNgtXQsYsnQfqQ-ni88T","name":"Pusthaka Event","slNo":6,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/nMayiEfVvOIMdVpkWGq0F.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-22","duration":1,"outcomes":"From the Pusthaka Event, I learned the value of helping others and the importance of social responsibility. I understood how even small contributions from individuals can make a big difference in the lives of underprivileged students. The event taught me empathy, teamwork, and the joy of giving. I also realized that education is a basic right, and supporting someone’s learning journey is one of the most meaningful forms of service. Overall, this experience inspired me to take part in more community welfare activities and contribute towards creating equal educational opportunities for all.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-22","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Pusthaka Event was a commendable and noble initiative aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students living in rural areas. The main objective of the event was to support children who lack access to basic educational materials and to encourage them to continue their studies without difficulties. NSS volunteers played an active role in organizing and managing the event. A significant amount of contribution was collected from compassionate donors, which formed the foundation for procuring the required school supplies. The collected funds were effectively utilized to purchase educational materials such as notebooks, stationery, and other essential resources that help create a conducive learning environment. These materials were then distributed to deserving students, bringing smiles to their faces and motivating them to pursue their education with confidence. The event highlighted the importance of community support in building a better future for children through education","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BGhnhvAhX8GeSCADidyi4","name":"Induction Day Volunteering","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/kzpcP5vMNXEOlPDG1M8Bo.png"],"endDate":"2023-09-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"From the Rotaract Induction Session, I learned about the importance of youth involvement in community service and leadership activities. I understood how organized teamwork and dedication can bring positive change in society. The session also improved my awareness of different social initiatives and encouraged me to step forward, take responsibility, and contribute to meaningful causes. Overall, it inspired me to develop leadership qualities, communication skills, and a spirit of service toward the community.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-09-25","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Induction Session was organized as a welcoming and informative event for new college students. The session aimed to introduce them to the club’s mission, values, and various activities conducted throughout the year. A comprehensive overview of the club was presented to help students understand its purpose and the positive impact it creates in the community. A captivating video was shown, highlighting the major events and initiatives carried out during the year.\\nIn addition, a detailed PowerPoint presentation showcased the club’s achievements, projects, and community service contributions. The session was designed to inspire students to become active members and participate in meaningful social service activities. It concluded with an interactive question-and-answer segment, where students clarified their doubts and learned more about how they could get involved in future programs. The event successfully motivated many students to take interest in Rotaract activities.","aicteMapping":"Student Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OIJRw-q2xbsHDu86VQlFN","name":"Student Induction Programme","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/TF7BNwfTxLmzvINYrB7D0.png"],"endDate":"2023-10-31","duration":1,"outcomes":"From the NSS Induction Session, I learned about the importance of community service and the role of youth in nation-building. I understood how NSS activities help develop leadership qualities, teamwork, and a sense of responsibility toward society. The session increased my awareness of various social issues and motivated me to contribute my time and effort for the welfare of the community. Overall, it inspired me to become an active volunteer and participate in service-oriented activities for the betterment of society.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-10-31","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The NSS Induction Session was conducted as a welcoming and informative program for new college students. The session aimed to introduce them to the mission, objectives, and activities of the National Service Scheme. A detailed overview of NSS initiatives and community service programs was provided to help students understand the role of NSS in social development. A short video presentation showcased the highlights of various camps, awareness drives, and service activities carried out during the year.\\nA comprehensive PowerPoint presentation further explained the achievements of the NSS unit, including community outreach programs, health camps, environmental campaigns, and social awareness initiatives. The session was designed to inspire students to take part in meaningful service activities and develop a sense of social responsibility. It concluded with an interactive question-and-answer session, where students clarified their doubts and learned how they could actively participate in future NSS programs.","aicteMapping":"Student Development","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XPR8D33UKC-vIElW3RNL8","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/iCBI17Q6ayvuloxcCZ2qA.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of RVCE, successfully blended fitness, community engagement, and philanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to \\ncontribute to a meaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With enthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful \\nreminder of the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges. Runners contributed through their registration fees, which were directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to educational and environmental projects.\\nThe overwhelming response from participants highlighted the deep-rooted commitment of \\nRVCE towards community service and social responsibility. Beyond the physical endurance required to complete the marathon, the event fostered a sense of camaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of teamwork and determination. The well-organized event featured structured routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance, ensuring a smooth and safe experience for all runners.\\nAdditionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, encouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while giving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the bond between students and the community but also showcased how small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful social change.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants. Beyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. \\nThe event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in \\nknowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes well marked routes, \\nhydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values \\nof empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BZ3yRQ_d-YG4HGoqlwQTx","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":10,"place":"Nagasandra","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/7CMOIWuztUyp2nMaPIO1B.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"From participating in the Paper Drive, I learned the importance of teamwork, social responsibility, and environmental awareness. I understood how collective efforts can bring meaningful change and support those who are less privileged. The activity taught me the value of recycling, proper resource utilization, and community engagement. It also helped me develop communication skills, confidence, and a sense of empathy toward society. Overall, the experience inspired me to take part in more service activities and contribute positively to both society and the environment.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Paper Drive was organized as a meaningful social initiative aimed at supporting charitable causes through the collection of reusable and recyclable materials. The drive saw the enthusiastic participation of a large number of student volunteers who worked together to gather books, papers, and other useful materials from various areas. Volunteers began early in the morning, going door-to-door and visiting local establishments to request donations. Their dedicated efforts resulted in a significant collection of resources intended to assist charities and NGOs in their ongoing initiatives to help those in need.\\nBeyond material collection, the Paper Drive also focused on raising awareness about community involvement and social responsibility. The event highlighted how small contributions from individuals can collectively create a large impact. It served as a platform to encourage responsible waste management, recycling practices, and active participation in social service. The drive was a great success, reflecting the power of teamwork and the commitment of students toward addressing social and environmental issues.","aicteMapping":"Community development","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"I5uJZ7gLZvwd8NqDq8Hgf","name":"Water Analysis Event","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/kZQUhp3czLFMPCwrWQU8d.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"From the Water Analysis Event, I learned the importance of water quality in maintaining good health. I understood how contaminated water can cause diseases and why regular testing and purification are necessary. The activity increased my awareness about environmental protection and water conservation. It also taught me teamwork, responsibility, and the importance of scientific methods in solving real-life problems. Overall, the event inspired me to use water wisely and spread awareness about keeping our water sources clean and safe.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The NSS unit organized a Water Analysis Event with the objective of creating awareness about the importance of clean and safe water for health and the environment. The program focused on educating students and the local community about water quality, sources of contamination, and the need for regular monitoring. NSS volunteers actively participated in collecting water samples from different sources and assisting in the testing process under proper guidance.\\nDuring the event, basic water quality tests were conducted to examine parameters such as pH level, clarity, and the presence of impurities. The resource persons explained how polluted water can lead to various health problems and how simple preventive measures can help maintain water safety. The session also highlighted the importance of conserving water and protecting natural water bodies from pollution. The event successfully spread awareness about responsible water usage and the role of individuals in ensuring access to safe drinking water","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Y0mNbS23B0O3-YqK1OE0h","name":"SWACCHATA PAKHWADA","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/XVvFGnPu7-wz2eMmAOq6A.png"],"endDate":"2023-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"From the Swachhata Pakhwada event, I learned the importance of cleanliness and personal responsibility toward the environment. I understood how small actions like proper waste disposal and maintaining hygiene can prevent diseases and improve the quality of life. The activity also taught me teamwork, discipline, and the value of community service. Overall, the experience inspired me to follow clean habits and motivate others to contribute toward a cleaner and healthier society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-10-01","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Swachhata Pakhwada event was organized as an awareness and action initiative to promote cleanliness, hygiene, and environmental responsibility. The program aimed to encourage students and community members to maintain clean surroundings and understand the importance of sanitation in daily life. NSS volunteers actively participated in the campaign by taking part in cleanliness drives and awareness activities conducted in and around the campus and nearby areas.\\nDuring the event, volunteers cleaned public spaces, properly disposed of waste, and spread awareness about waste segregation and hygiene practices. Participants were educated about the harmful effects of littering and the importance of maintaining a clean environment for better health and well-being. The initiative emphasized that cleanliness is not only the responsibility of authorities but also of every individual. The event successfully promoted the message of a clean and healthy society through active participation and teamwork.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wDVQsRpcX7b91fvfOeo-l","name":"RENDEZVOUS WITH WRITING","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/nRXbCmbNJ8_gq2MYjltNM.png"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"From participating in “Rendezvous with Writing,” I learned the importance of expressing ideas and opinions on social issues through writing. The event helped me understand how powerful words can raise awareness and inspire change. I developed better thinking and communication skills while reflecting on real-world problems. It also taught me empathy, creativity, and the value of sharing perspectives. Overall, the experience motivated me to stay socially aware and use my voice to contribute positively to society.","semester":"4","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Rendezvous with Writing” was a creative literary event organized to provide participants with a platform to express their thoughts on various social service–related topics. Conducted over four dynamic days, the event encouraged students to reflect on important social issues and present their ideas through writing. The competition received an overwhelming response, with more than 80 submissions, showcasing a diverse range of perspectives and meaningful insights.\\nParticipants wrote on impactful themes such as women empowerment, mental health awareness, and income inequality. The event created a space for thoughtful discussion and dialogue within the community, highlighting the power of words in bringing social awareness and change. The winners stood out for their ability to present strong messages with clarity and creativity. Overall, the event successfully promoted social consciousness and encouraged students to use writing as a tool for expression and service","aicteMapping":"Student Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Gc4tOx08Enpss_p00VGJd","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/sVX1jwTgsO8SW4wbgfxkS.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"Participation in the Fist Full initiative enhanced my understanding of social responsibility and the seriousness of food insecurity faced by many communities. The activity demonstrated how small, consistent individual contributions can collectively lead to a large-scale impact. It helped me develop empathy toward underprivileged sections of society and strengthened my commitment to community welfare. The initiative also improved organizational and coordination skills through structured collection and teamwork, reinforcing the importance of solidarity, compassion, and service-oriented leadership.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fist Full was a humanitarian initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November. The primary objective of the project was to address hunger and food insecurity by encouraging students to contribute essential food grains for the underprivileged. As part of the initiative, students were motivated to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, symbolizing how small individual contributions can collectively create a significant social impact. Daily collections were systematically carried out at the Civil Department, RVCE \\ncampus, ensuring smooth coordination and participation.\\nThe project witnessed an overwhelming response from the student community, with over 1,750 students actively participating. In total, 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal were collected during the drive. The initiative not only provided substantial support toward combating hunger but also reinforced values of compassion, social responsibility, and community service among students. Fist Full stood as a strong example of collective effort driving meaningful societal \\nchange","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lCdstBemfgovgJ8rDJ0iz","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness  Walkathon","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/og7E6o8vbglKKEkQ_WqAB.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through participation in the Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon, I gained a comprehensive understanding of the social, ethical, and legal implications associated with female foeticide and its far-reaching consequences on society. \\nThe activity helped me recognize how deeply rooted gender bias and discrimination can begin even before birth, and how such practices disturb social balance and hinder societal progress. It reinforced the importance of gender equality, respect for human rights, and the urgent need to safeguard the dignity and life of the girl child.\\nThe walkathon also highlighted the power of collective action and community participation in addressing sensitive social issues. By engaging with a large and diverse group of participants, I learned how awareness initiatives can effectively influence public mindset, encourage dialogue, and inspire behavioral change. Carrying placards and slogans strengthened my ability to communicate social messages and advocate for justice and equality","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Engineering (RVCE) successfully organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon to highlight the serious social issue of female foeticide and to promote awareness about the importance and value of the girl child in society. The primary objective of this activity was to educate people and encourage collective responsibility in preventing gender-based discrimination even before birth.\\nThe walkathon commenced in the early morning hours from the RVCE campus and witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 350 individuals, including students, faculty members, and parents. Participants carried impactful placards and raised powerful slogans advocating gender equality and the right to life for every girl child. The atmosphere throughout the event reflected unity, awareness, and a strong commitment toward social change.\\nThe activity served as an effective platform to sensitize participants and the public about the consequences of female foeticide and the need for ethical and moral responsibility in society. \\nThrough this walkathon, the Rotaract Club of RVCE successfully conveyed the message of respect, equality, and dignity for women and girl children. The event concluded with a sense of accomplishment and gratitude, and the organizing team \\nexpressed sincere appreciation to all participants for their active involvement and support in making the walkathon impactful and meaningful.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/3_AWggGdjP6VJMtpYRZud.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FtKqI6SGK-h-oEIma-45F","name":"FistFull 2025","slNo":16,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/fbc88d30-1a69-4d9b-97d9-7a42417b7d95/dU_yEprdaYx9DirtHxvjU.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"Through participation in FISTFUL, I gained a deeper understanding of the issue of food insecurity and the crucial role that nutritional support plays in improving public health and overall well-being. The activity highlighted the power of collective action by demonstrating how small, consistent individual contributions can come together to create significant and meaningful societal impact. It helped me recognize the importance of addressing basic human needs such as food as a foundation for health, dignity, and social stability.\\nThe initiative also strengthened my sense of social responsibility and empathy toward underprivileged communities, motivating me to actively engage in community service. Working alongside fellow students enhanced my teamwork, coordination, and leadership skills, as effective organization and cooperation were essential for the success of the initiative.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"FISTFUL was a standalone community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) with the support of Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 17th to 22nd November 2025 at the Civil Engineering Department. The primary objective of the initiative was to combat food insecurity and address basic nutritional needs through collective student participation. By encouraging each student to contribute either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, the project emphasized how small, individual acts of generosity can come together to create a meaningful and large-scale social impact.\\nThe initiative witnessed enthusiastic participation from 2,146 students, resulting in the successful collection of 4,370 kg of rice and 2,516 kg of dal. These essential food grains were systematically distributed to a wide range of beneficiary institutions, including hospitals, hostels, elderly care homes, schools, and nearby anganwadis. The distribution ensured that \\nthe collected resources reached vulnerable sections of society such as children, the elderly, and patients, thereby supporting daily meal programs and contributing to improved health and \\nwell-being.\\nBeyond the material contribution, FISTFUL served as a powerful platform for nurturing values of empathy, compassion, and social responsibility among students. The initiative helped \\ncreate awareness about food scarcity and the importance of community-driven solutions to social challenges. It strengthened the spirit of volunteerism and reinforced the role of students \\nas responsible citizens committed to sustainable community service. Overall, the project demonstrated how organized collective action can effectively address societal needs and create a lasting positive impact.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ETN15ZMU8khQW_2DCFjFX","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE  Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through participation in the blood donation activity, I gained a deeper understanding of the critical importance of voluntary blood donation in saving lives and strengthening public health infrastructure. The experience helped me overcome initial hesitation and significantly boosted my confidence in contributing to medical and humanitarian causes. It made me more aware of how timely availability of blood can make a life-saving difference for accident victims, surgical patients, and individuals suffering from chronic illnesses.\\nI also developed a stronger sense of empathy and social responsibility toward patients and their families who depend on regular blood donations. The activity increased my awareness about health standards, blood group compatibility, donor eligibility, and the importance of organizing regular blood donation drives to maintain adequate blood reserves.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Blood Donation activity was a humanitarian initiative carried out in association with the Indian Red Cross Society, Karnataka State Branch, aimed at supporting healthcare services and saving lives through voluntary blood donation. As part of this activity, I voluntarily donated blood, contributing directly to emergency medical care and treatment for patients in need. \\nBlood donation plays a critical role in supporting hospitals, accident victims, patients undergoing surgeries, and individuals suffering from chronic illnesses.\\nThis activity emphasized the importance of social responsibility, compassion, and civic duty. By participating, I became part of a larger effort to strengthen the healthcare system and ensure the \\navailability of safe blood for critical situations. The initiative reflected the principle that a single act of kindness can have a life-saving impact and highlighted the role of youth participation in addressing public health challenges.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Poornima Kulkarni","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr. Rajalakshmi Mudbidre","designation":"Associate Dean Cultural Events"},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 13:48:59.707867+00', '2026-01-31 17:28:11.895938+00'), ('ce330040-544d-4606-b158-d7d455de965b', '0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV050","name":"MADHU K J ","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"rHSuW1val-exEhl5Y3R89","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"24","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/DrAZmwU6N2ZVpCyiCBVDA.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility\\nand gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":80,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my\\nphysical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical\\nchallenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating an positive change in society. This cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5 km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causes in the future.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/KgzBuKdOaHnjVkdYomGiA.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1 - 2 ","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1KXCkUKKV6oBKIRpMdv27","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"25","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/YNABLkYBR5maadgK3LprX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility\\nand gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":141,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category, which challenged my\\nphysical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating an positive change in society. This cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causes in the future.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":36,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/GUoUKtaKX0SOGd8b_Dzq2.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3 - 4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YDHrtRO9ago3Bcuhp-cpn","name":"Kannada Sangha  ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/g-As_3TNsD6jYj5ZG0nE8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"Efficient Coordination: Successfully collected and managed Kannada Sangha T-shirts for participants.\\nOrganizational Skills: Improved planning, record-keeping, and distribution management skills.\\nTeamwork & Communication: Enhanced interaction with students and Kannada Sangha coordinators.\\nCultural Promotion: Contributed to strengthening Kannada identity and visibility during events.\\nResponsibility & Leadership: Demonstrated accountability in handling collective resources.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-07-02","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The activity involved collecting and organizing Kannada Sangha T-shirts for members and participants of Kannada Sangha events. This task required coordination with students,\\nmaintaining records of requests, ensuring correct sizes and quantities, and distributing the T-shirts efficiently. The activity supported the smooth conduct of Kannada Sangha programs\\nand helped promote unity, cultural identity, and active participation among members.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/TPibZkGBrRQ3bfdNhsZx6.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5 - 6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"G3xA34pzA-LaCk6AifWzQ","name":"FistFull","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/OnfANE4CFJaRHkOoToQwT.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the donation drive held at the RVCE campus was the successful collection of essential food items to support underprivileged communities. The initiative helped address basic nutritional needs and contributed to food assistance efforts. It fostered a sense of social responsibility and empathy among students while encouraging active participation in\\ncommunity service. The activity also strengthened awareness about the importance of collective effort, demonstrating how small contributions can create a meaningful and positive impact on society.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-13","hoursSpent":40,"description":"A contribution of 2 kg of toor dal was made during the donation drive held at the RVCE campus. The initiative was organized with the objective of supporting food assistance programs. It aimed to extend help to underprivileged communities through essential supplies. The drive encouraged student participation in social welfare activities. It highlighted the importance of collective\\nresponsibility toward society. Food grains collected were intended for meaningful community support. Such initiatives help address basic nutritional needs. They also promote empathy and humanitarian values. The campus environment fostered a spirit of service unity. Students were motivated to contribute in practical ways. The activity emphasized\\ngiving back to society. It reflected the role of educational institutions in social development. Small contributions together create a larger impact. The drive served as a reminder of social accountability. Overall, the initiative strengthened awareness about community welfare.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/8mGd-tIHYYnsUnBxJLeUm.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7 - 8 ","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"G5IG6pC7TQvviWE9eJJiz","name":"8th Mile Vertical Volunteers ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/-D8DljBj9pP0MHPhFh4El.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"Gained hands-on experience in event management\\nDeveloped leadership and teamwork skills\\nImproved communication and coordination abilities\\nLearned time management and problem-solving under pressure\\nEnhanced confidence in handling responsibilities\\nUnderstood the importance of discipline and teamwork in large-scale events\\nBuilt strong connections with peers and organizing members","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":80,"description":"8th Mile is a flagship cultural and technical fest organized by our college with the objective of promoting creativity, teamwork, leadership, and student engagement. The event brought together students from various departments to participate in a wide range of cultural, technical, and fun-filled activities. It served as a platform for students to showcase their talents, enhance interpersonal skills, and experience large-scale event management.\\nThe fest witnessed enthusiastic participation, vibrant performances, competitive events, and smooth coordination among organizing teams. It played a significant role in fostering unity, innovation, and a festive spirit across the campus.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0c25c1db-5c0f-4a24-911e-74af8e7b2aac/WUm9L4jIYNujBi3-VO7am.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9 - 10","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Venugopal. G","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 18:36:06.629726+00', '2026-01-30 06:35:21.871729+00'), ('d092ce8b-0a5f-41f0-9d5e-8703482d17cf', '733adbc6-81ea-49ef-9d51-2aac48ea2097', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 06:28:56.939729+00', '2026-01-31 13:02:00.096029+00'), ('d0d8ce39-cbf1-4d98-a10a-34eb84789394', '29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS082","name":"Yashvanth B L","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"58tfZOEOhPPcEbdYgATXj","name":"Blood donation Camp - 2023","slNo":1,"place":"RV College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/FJwu0A6-FV-knW5w0lUsS.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation made a direct and meaningful contribution toward saving lives by supporting patients at Victoria Hospital who depend on timely and adequate blood transfusions during surgeries, accident-related treatments, and other critical medical emergencies. By voluntarily donating blood, Yashvanth actively supported the healthcare system in meeting urgent blood requirements, helping ensure that patients in critical conditions received safe, reliable, and timely medical assistance. In addition to addressing immediate medical needs, the initiative also served as a platform to raise awareness about the continuous importance of voluntary blood donation, inspiring and motivating more individuals to participate in such life-saving humanitarian efforts in the future.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":3,"description":"As part of a voluntary blood donation drive focused on encouraging social responsibility and humanitarian values, I donated one unit of blood on 06 June 2023 under the supervision of the Blood Centre of Victoria Hospital, Bangalore Medical College & Research Institute. The blood donation camp was organized at RV College of Engineering, providing a well-managed and accessible venue for students to participate in this life-saving initiative while strictly following all medical and safety protocols. The initiative aimed to support patients facing critical and emergency medical conditions who rely on timely blood transfusions for treatment and recovery, while also creating awareness about the constant need for voluntary blood donors. Through this activity, students were motivated to contribute selflessly to society, reinforcing the importance of compassion, community service, and a strong sense of humanitarian responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FrXhBrFtNLzmEANOMhZlO","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":2,"place":"Kengeri","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/dKSFgvDWFykmoRKd3Ple4.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/ykeBawmSkkUCh4mUwRxl6.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The collective efforts of the volunteers led to the successful collection of more than 7 tonnes of recyclable paper from various localities across the city. This significant quantity of waste paper was carefully sorted and later sold to authorized paper vendors, transforming recyclable materials into a valuable source of funds while promoting environmental sustainability.\\n\\nThe total amount generated through this initiative was donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation, with the aim of supporting the welfare and development of orphanages and underprivileged individuals. By converting waste into a meaningful resource, the initiative not only contributed to environmental conservation but also extended tangible social support to communities in need, reinforcing the values of compassion, responsibility, and community service.\\n\\n\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a large-scale Paper Drive on 24 June 2023 in Bengaluru as part of its Community Services initiative, with a strong focus on Economic and Community Development. The drive aimed to promote responsible waste management, environmental sustainability, and community involvement by encouraging the collection and recycling of old newspapers, magazines, books, and other waste paper materials across the city.\\n\\nMore than 500 enthusiastic volunteers gathered at RVCE and were deployed to various localities in Bengaluru to carry out the collection process. The volunteers worked tirelessly for over nine hours, actively engaging with households and local communities to spread awareness about the importance of recycling and sustainable practices. Through direct interaction and collective effort, the initiative fostered a strong sense of social responsibility while making a meaningful contribution toward environmental conservation and community welfare.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lEZb5-j6dSrbTNfhB_PEC","name":"BIOFUEL DAY ESSAY COMPETITION","slNo":3,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/82eYv5c8rN2OzUnDJwOh-.png"],"endDate":"2003-08-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The essay competition successfully fostered curiosity and awareness among students regarding sustainable fuel technologies and their relevance to future energy security. Participants gained deeper knowledge about the environmental and economic impact of biofuels, strengthening their understanding of sustainability practices. The event not only improved research and writing skills but also motivated students to contribute towards greener innovations, helping build a culture of environmental responsibility within the institution.","semester":"2","startDate":"2003-08-08","hoursSpent":3,"description":"On 8 August 2023, the Civil Engineering Department organized an “International Biofuel Day” Essay Writing Competition in room CE-205 from 2:00 PM to 4:30 PM, with the objective of encouraging students to examine the significance of sustainable energy in addressing pressing global environmental challenges. The competition provided participants with an opportunity to research and articulate their ideas on biofuels as an eco-friendly and renewable alternative to conventional fossil fuels, covering aspects such as their production processes, practical applications, and long-term benefits for society and the environment. Through this academic initiative, the event sought to enhance scientific awareness, promote informed discussion on renewable energy, and inspire students to think critically and creatively about sustainable solutions for a cleaner and more energy-secure future.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qI_pvALKtI1STASwq_09O","name":"Project Pustak - 2024","slNo":4,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/si_Ad-cM9s-9Dqm3prO-O.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/PdDGe_7LXm0rWQZvDjYzj.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"\\nThe generous contributions received from donors helped in accumulating substantial funds, which were effectively utilized to procure vital school supplies for deserving and underprivileged students. Through this meaningful initiative, the Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with Pranav Foundation, ensured that children from economically weaker backgrounds received the essential educational resources needed to pursue their studies with greater confidence and comfort. The project not only supported academic continuity but also promoted equal learning opportunities, while fostering values of compassion, social responsibility, and active community involvement among volunteers and contributors.\\n\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak, conducted on 24 May 2024 by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, was a charitable initiative focused on supporting underprivileged rural students by providing essential school supplies. The project aimed to reduce educational disparities and ensure access to basic learning resources for children from economically weaker backgrounds.\\n\\nDonors were encouraged to contribute ₹100 or ₹350, and the funds raised were used to purchase textbooks, stationery, backpacks, and other necessary materials. Through this effort, the initiative helped create a supportive learning environment for young students while reinforcing the importance of education in community development.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tCrSkOwwrIjnXI6Tyl_-u","name":"Blood donation camp - 2024","slNo":6,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/kaCZOT06J2GXJUYw7S4qK.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The contribution of blood on 28th June 2024 helped strengthen the emergency medical reserves of the Indian Red Cross Society, ensuring timely support for patients in need of transfusions. Each donor’s participation played a significant role in saving lives and supporting healthcare services, reinforcing the impact of individual action in public welfare. The event successfully promoted awareness about the necessity of regular blood donation and inspired more individuals to become recurring donors, ultimately fostering a culture of empathy and community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"On 28th June 2024, a voluntary blood donation drive was organized in collaboration with the Indian Red Cross Society, where participants came forward to donate blood to support medical needs and emergency requirements. The event encouraged healthy donors to contribute a unit of blood, highlighting the importance of blood availability for critical patients and accident victims. By participating in this initiative, donors demonstrated compassion and social responsibility, contributing to a humanitarian cause that directly saves lives.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RHwVs_VhJiz8FbvzulpBw","name":"Paper Drive 2.0","slNo":6,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/hRRttpVZofvgql7-iZaP9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-22","duration":12,"outcomes":"The workshop received an overwhelming response, and the paper bag contribution target was successfully achieved ahead of schedule. Students across departments demonstrated remarkable enthusiasm, contributing a large number of handcrafted bags that supported the zero-waste drive at the Parishe. With their collective effort, volunteers helped promote sustainable alternatives, reduce plastic usage, and spread environmental awareness within the community. The initiative served as a testament to the power of youth participation in social causes and strengthened the campus’ commitment toward a greener future.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-11","hoursSpent":30,"description":"The Cheela Mela Paper Bag Workshop was organized by NSS RVCE in collaboration with Youth For Seva to support the zero-waste initiative during the Kadale Kayi Parishe. Students crafted eco-friendly paper bags using old newspapers, either onsite in the Environment Lab or from home, and submitted them between 11th and 22nd November 2024. The activity encouraged sustainability, responsible waste management, and student participation, with an added incentive of 1 Activity Point for every 10 bags contributed. The workshop aimed not only to reduce plastic usage but also to engage the student community in environmental consciousness through hands-on action.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"onV1Yai1tL6rr2HCCLGXw","name":"Fist Full","slNo":7,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/KI67z--chrOPXxDq7dFbB.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-19","duration":5,"outcomes":"The initiative received an overwhelming response, with more than 1,750 students participating and collectively donating over 6,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal. The large volume of contributions showcased the success of the campaign in addressing hunger while reinforcing the spirit of solidarity within the student community. The collected food supplies significantly supported needy communities, reflecting RVCE’s commitment to social welfare and proving that collective small efforts can result in meaningful change.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Fist Full initiative, conducted from 15th to 29th November by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, aimed at combating hunger by motivating students to make small but meaningful contributions. Participants were encouraged to donate either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily collection points set up in the Civil Department. The campaign focused on fostering a culture of compassion and community support by demonstrating how small actions from individuals can lead to large-scale social impact.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RNgvdyAQmIwhiMgq7ro35","name":"Blood donation - 2025","slNo":8,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/IgbgsX-FIueHlxhtYKLn9.png"],"endDate":"2025-03-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"I actively participated in the drive and donated O +ve blood, contributing to the institute’s voluntary blood donation programme. This gesture helped support critical treatments for children requiring transfusions and added to the hospital’s emergency blood reserves. The certificate of appreciation was awarded as recognition of dedicated service, compassion, and commitment to social responsibility and healthcare support.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-20","hoursSpent":4,"description":"A voluntary blood donation drive was organized by the Blood Transfusion and Immunohaematology Unit of the Indira Gandhi Institute of Child Health to support patients in need of life-saving transfusions. The initiative encouraged students to participate in humanitarian service by donating blood and helping strengthen the institute’s supply for pediatric medical emergencies. As part of this noble cause, a camp was held at R.V. Engineering College, where donors contributed to public health by making safe and responsible blood donations.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PNCqs3Bly0a6zB13jLEss","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz","slNo":9,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/Y3kWV52gUAMtznEHbRQfg.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The quiz successfully increased awareness among students regarding India’s developmental milestones and future growth plans, helping them better understand the nation’s trajectory and their role in shaping it. By participating, students strengthened their general knowledge, civic awareness, and sense of national responsibility while earning 2 activity points from NSS. The event not only encouraged intellectual engagement but also inspired students to stay informed about national initiatives, fostering a spirit of active citizenship and informed youth participation in India’s progress.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz was an online nationwide initiative organized by the Government of India to engage youth in learning about India’s development, policies, and long-term vision for becoming a developed nation by 2047. Students from RV College of Engineering actively participated by registering on the official Viksit Bharat portal, reading the quiz guidelines, and answering 10 timed questions covering themes such as national progress, infrastructure, sustainability, governance, and technological advancements. Participants submitted a screenshot of their completion certificate and Reference ID through the NSS Google Form to record their participation and earn activity points\\n","aicteMapping":"Awareness Program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Fz4Sc8JDACrHppjLKQ8hT","name":"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree ","slNo":10,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/wV1HujzvXua5v_fd0p7Qb.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully encouraged students to take part in an environmentally responsible effort, strengthening their understanding of sustainability through direct involvement. A significant number of students purchased T-shirts and collected saplings, demonstrating strong participation and awareness. The activity helped foster a sense of community responsibility, as students took initiative to plant their saplings and contribute positively to the environment. Overall, the event met its objectives by raising consciousness about ecological conservation and engaging students in a meaningful, hands-on sustainability action.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The “Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” initiative was a community-service event organized by the Kannada Sangha of R. V. College of Engineering to promote environmental awareness and personal responsibility among students. As part of the event, every student who purchased a T-shirt received a tree sapling along with clear guidelines on how and where to plant it. The objective was to inspire students to actively contribute to environmental sustainability by planting and nurturing the saplings provided to them. The distribution of T-shirts and saplings was carried out on campus, ensuring smooth participation and engagement from a large number of students.\\n","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"22TQncLjjRGbKF3PWOCjh","name":"Blood donation camp - 2025","slNo":11,"place":"R V College of Engineering","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/29a581c9-1480-449d-9752-ba91839bd346/HBYxZuvStMBVnwTiqrMLa.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity was successfully completed, with students like Yashvanth B L donating blood and contributing directly to saving lives. The initiative helped increase awareness about the critical need for blood in emergencies and medical treatments, motivating more students to come forward for future donation drives. Participants were acknowledged by the Indian Red Cross Society with certificates of appreciation, reinforcing their commitment to community service. Overall, the event achieved its objective by instilling a spirit of volunteerism and promoting a culture of health, empathy, and civic responsibility among students.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The blood donation activity conducted on 30/10/2025 was organized in collaboration with the Indian Red Cross Society, Karnataka State Branch, to promote humanitarian service and voluntary contribution among students. As part of this initiative, eligible donors came forward to donate blood under the supervision of certified medical professionals, ensuring safety and proper medical procedures throughout the process. The event aimed to raise awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and its impact on saving lives, while also encouraging students to develop a sense of social responsibility and compassion toward the community.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 02:43:29.323853+00', '2026-01-31 06:29:20.097373+00'), ('d104bb04-cce8-46bb-b21e-84bcf51c5a4a', '80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI015","name":"Chirag Kumar Jaiswal","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"PIEhmeCKN0j3iakQXfKR3","name":"","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t7qH4dvtbxOCcPbZ2zR4c","name":"CSITSS 2024 ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/lofDicowgd1VLeyf2E1QN.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"The successful organization of CSITSS 2024 enhanced student participation, streamlined event management through the web portal, and contributed to the fulfillment of AICTE Activity Points by promoting technical, organizational, and leadership skills.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-07","hoursSpent":24,"description":"CSITSS 2024 was organized as a technical symposium aimed at providing a platform for students to showcase their skills, exchange ideas, and engage in knowledge-sharing through workshops, technical events, and competitions. I was actively involved in both the planning and execution phases, contributing to event coordination, scheduling, and participant management. In addition, I led the web development for the symposium, designing and maintaining the official website to handle event information, registrations, updates, and communication. The digital platform played a crucial role in ensuring smooth operations, wide outreach, and a professional representation of the event, in alignment with AICTE’s focus on technical skill development and co-curricular engagement.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/AYCuvMZUjDiBlqWh3wD26.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fPVxjHnV0WtsesEC1rEo3","name":"Project Pustak ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/yIlSVePKeay_GCBeC6K7d.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Rotaract Project Pustak drive successfully gathered and distributed essential educational materials to deserving students, enabling them to pursue their studies with confidence and dignity. The activity helped bridge the learning resource gap for many children while spreading awareness about the importance of education and youth contribution toward social development. Through this initiative, I gained valuable exposure to community service and developed qualities such as empathy, responsibility, and social awareness. The project strengthened collaboration between volunteers and Rotaract members and encouraged continued involvement in educational support programs. Overall, the initiative created a positive impact by promoting equal learning opportunities and inspiring young minds to value and support education for all.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Rotaract Project Pustak was an educational support initiative aimed at empowering underprivileged school children by providing them with academic materials and learning resources. As part of this campaign, students and volunteers contributed funds and books to help ensure that children from economically weaker backgrounds could continue their education without facing a shortage of basic study necessities. I actively took part in this initiative by donating educational supplies/monetary support, thereby contributing to the mission of promoting literacy and learning. The project was executed in collaboration with the Rotaract Club, which coordinated the collection and distribution process across various schools and community centers. This initiative served as a reminder of the power of collective effort in shaping a brighter and more educated future for children in need.\\n","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/4nAImWDFh-0WodoLzapQJ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AE-6esvU4_r4tuv_81m-V","name":"Hack4Soc","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/R9WINckaaPRtPp07C-Pyc.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":20,"outcomes":"The successful execution of Hack4Soc 2.0 resulted in nationwide participation, high-quality project submissions, and the development of impactful, socially driven technological solutions. The event established Hack4Soc as a flagship hackathon at RVCE, strengthened the IEEE RVCE Computer Society’s reputation, and demonstrated how a well-designed digital platform can significantly amplify outreach, engagement, and operational efficiency, ultimately fostering a strong culture of innovation and social responsibility among students.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-01-16","hoursSpent":60,"description":"Hack4Soc 2.0 was a national-level inter-college hackathon organized by the IEEE RVCE Computer Society, bringing together talented teams from institutions across the country to design and build impactful solutions for socially relevant and humanitarian problem statements. The event served as a platform for innovation, collaboration, and technical excellence, encouraging participants to apply their skills to real-world challenges and compete for top honors.\\n\\nI led the end-to-end development of the official event website, playing a key role in shaping the digital presence and outreach of the hackathon. The platform handled registrations, problem statement dissemination, event updates, and participant communication, ensuring a smooth and engaging experience for hundreds of users. The professional and user-friendly web interface significantly contributed to the visibility, credibility, and large-scale participation of the event, helping Hack4Soc 2.0 gain widespread recognition and setting a benchmark for future editions. The success of the platform and the event collectively fostered innovation and helped in empowering society through technology-driven solutions.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/TZXAsbsQyt2x1uFC2SsOs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"7hbxcw9OZRGZ8xNCCmFKN","name":"RVCExIITB CTF ‘24","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/aOtBY_G_2guLFkHCHYuu8.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/t1kz2V0EmLnaIE8KzCBHF.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-22","duration":15,"outcomes":"The CTF competition successfully strengthened the cybersecurity\\ncommunity by bringing together students from diverse\\nbackgrounds to collaboratively tackle real-world security\\nchallenges. Participants enhanced their problem-solving,\\nanalytical, and technical skills by working on practical scenarios\\ninvolving phishing scams, digital forensic investigations,\\ncryptographic analysis, and emerging blockchain security\\nconcepts. The event encouraged knowledge sharing, teamwork,\\nand healthy competition while raising awareness about\\ncybersecurity threats and defenses. Overall, the competition\\ncontributed to building a skilled and security-conscious student\\ncommunity, inspiring participants to pursue advanced learning\\nand careers in cybersecurity and helping promote a safer digital\\necosystem.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":60,"description":"RVCExIITB Capture The Flag ’24 was a national-level\\ncybersecurity competition organized by the Coding Club, RV\\nCollege of Engineering, consisting of an online preliminary\\nround held on 8th June 2024 and an offline final round conducted\\non 22nd June 2024 at the RVCE campus. The event witnessed\\nlarge-scale participation with 1834 teams from across India, out\\nof which 51 teams qualified for the offline finals. The CTF\\nfollowed a gamified format where teams solved challenges\\nacross multiple cybersecurity domains, testing skills in areas such\\nas ethical hacking, digital forensics, cryptography, OSINT, and\\nblockchain security. The competition aimed to foster a\\ncompetitive learning environment, promote cybersecurity\\nawareness, and identify talented ethical hackers, while being free\\nof cost to encourage wide participation.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/PfBPIv6aRzDOjnKZeH830.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HYeuu78ml3aiQvklGRoMZ","name":"CSITSS-2025","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/RQLElLlRaWxQRabYDtiog.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":3,"outcomes":"CSITSS-2025 achieved strong academic and professional outcomes. The conference upheld high scholarly standards with numerous peer-reviewed research paper presentations and expert talks, contributing to ongoing discussions in sustainable computational technologies. Participants gained exposure to global research practices and emerging technological trends, enhancing their academic and professional perspectives.\\nA key outcome was the development of operational and leadership skills among student volunteers. By coordinating sessions, managing technical logistics, and interacting with international delegates, volunteers strengthened their communication, teamwork, and problem-solving abilities within a professional academic setting. These experiences provided practical insight into large-scale conference organization and academic event management.\\nThe conference also fostered interdisciplinary collaboration and networking. Interactions among researchers, industry experts, and students encouraged knowledge exchange and potential research partnerships. The sustainability theme of the conference further amplified its societal relevance by highlighting technology-driven solutions for global challenges. Overall, CSITSS-2025 combined academic excellence, professional exposure, and skill development, leaving a lasting impact on participants and organizers alike.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-20","hoursSpent":48,"description":"The 9th IEEE International Conference on Computational Systems & Information Technology for Sustainable Solutions (CSITSS-2025) was held at RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru, from 20th to 22nd November 2025. Organized under the IEEE RVCE Student Branch in collaboration with international academic partners, the conference served as a global platform for researchers, academicians, industry professionals, and students to exchange ideas in the fields of computational systems, information technology, and sustainability-focused innovations. The event featured keynote talks, tutorials, plenary sessions, panel discussions, and multiple parallel technical paper presentation tracks.\\nThe conference emphasized interdisciplinary research and sustainable technological development. Its objectives included promoting research dissemination, fostering academia–industry interaction, encouraging global collaboration, and providing student volunteers with hands-on experience in organizing an international academic event. Over the course of three days, the program blended scholarly discourse with practical coordination, supported by a large team of student volunteers who managed logistics, registration, technical session flow, speaker coordination, and hospitality.\\nPre-conference preparations involved website development, scheduling, publication coordination, and technical setup. During the event, volunteers ensured smooth execution of tutorials, keynote sessions, and paper presentations, while post-conference activities included documentation, feedback compilation, and archival processes. The conference successfully created an environment of knowledge sharing and international collaboration while demonstrating effective large-scale academic event management.\\n","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/T1sdL97FLNal8v3Y08-D-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"g28PKU3Qrv9t3T-30dlKo","name":"Web Development Bootcamp","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/MqmlonK0MykB0RFpSgxWk.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/FZSjRcz8wHF1os2PNW0b_.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-23","duration":67,"outcomes":"The bootcamp delivered meaningful outcomes for both participants and organizers. Students gained a clear understanding of end-to-end web application development, from designing user interfaces to building backend services and managing databases. Hands-on exposure to tools like Git, React.js, Express.js, and MongoDB improved their technical confidence and readiness for real-world projects.\\nThe program also strengthened problem-solving, collaboration, and practical coding skills. Regular assignments and mentor feedback helped students develop structured thinking and debugging abilities. Many participants completed functional projects, giving them portfolio-ready experience and better preparation for internships, hackathons, and advanced technical work.\\nFor the Coding Club, the bootcamp enhanced leadership, teaching, and organizational experience among student coordinators. It expanded the club’s developer community and created a scalable framework for future training programs. The initiative reinforced a culture of peer learning and mentorship, contributing to a sustainable and supportive technical ecosystem within the institution. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-18","hoursSpent":80,"description":"The Web Development Bootcamp organized by the Coding Club at RV College of Engineering was an eight-week hybrid program aimed at introducing students to modern full-stack web development. Designed primarily for beginners, the bootcamp combined structured teaching with hands-on practice to ensure participants gained both theoretical knowledge and real-world skills. Sessions were conducted twice a week, balancing offline interaction with online flexibility. The curriculum covered the complete web development pipeline. Students began with Git, HTML, and CSS to understand the foundations of web technologies. They then moved on to JavaScript and frontend development using Tailwind CSS and React.js. In the later weeks, the focus shifted to backend development with Express.js and API integration, followed by database management using MongoDB. By the end of the program, participants had learned how to connect all layers to build a complete full-stack application. A strong emphasis was placed on experiential learning. Weekly assignments, mini-projects, and mentor guidance ensured students actively applied what they learned. The mentorship-driven approach provided personalized support and helped participants build confidence in problem-solving and development workflows. Overall, the bootcamp created a structured pathway for students to transition from beginners to capable web developers.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/PQArb5vjzRrSyG3FooqV7.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Psfa9UIorP5UzBOgrwCyb","name":"EY CATALYST PROGRAM - CODEATHON","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/CdHU70CL-pWLrqimUg8LR.png"],"endDate":"2025-02-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The EY Catalyst Program – Codeathon was an 8-hour strategic hackathon organized by the Coding Club of RV College of Engineering in collaboration with Ernst & Young (EY). The event was designed as a high-intensity, industry-aligned coding challenge that simulated real-world business problem solving. It also served as a preliminary assessment platform for EY’s recruitment process, providing students with direct exposure to corporate expectations and evaluation standards.\\nParticipants worked individually or in small teams to develop innovative software solutions addressing problem statements inspired by domains such as finance, data analytics, and automation-areas central to EY’s operations. The hackathon followed a structured format with periodic review checkpoints, where mentors provided technical guidance and evaluated progress. This ensured participants continuously refined their ideas and solutions under time constraints.\\nAt the end of the event, teams presented their solutions to a panel comprising EY professionals and faculty members. Projects were judged on technical feasibility, innovation, scalability, and user experience. The event created a professional, competitive learning environment that pushed students to apply classroom knowledge to real-world scenarios while strengthening coding, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills. Overall, the Codeathon functioned as both a learning experience and a bridge between academia and industry. \\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-02-13","hoursSpent":32,"description":"The EY Catalyst Program – Codeathon was an 8-hour strategic hackathon organized by the Coding Club of RV College of Engineering in collaboration with Ernst & Young (EY). The event was designed as a high-intensity, industry-aligned coding challenge that simulated real-world business problem solving. It also served as a preliminary assessment platform for EY’s recruitment process, providing students with direct exposure to corporate expectations and evaluation standards.\\nParticipants worked individually or in small teams to develop innovative software solutions addressing problem statements inspired by domains such as finance, data analytics, and automation-areas central to EY’s operations. The hackathon followed a structured format with periodic review checkpoints, where mentors provided technical guidance and evaluated progress. This ensured participants continuously refined their ideas and solutions under time constraints.\\nAt the end of the event, teams presented their solutions to a panel comprising EY professionals and faculty members. Projects were judged on technical feasibility, innovation, scalability, and user experience. The event created a professional, competitive learning environment that pushed students to apply classroom knowledge to real-world scenarios while strengthening coding, analytical thinking, and teamwork skills. Overall, the Codeathon functioned as both a learning experience and a bridge between academia and industry. \\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/iTOeAmVzzvPgbUEXreYRY.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2SaSzMkjEVHJ9q8BT__TV","name":"SKILL LAB x CODING CLUB - ECE","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/hcvQeHt4twKNKP1-oD5T3.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-23","duration":5,"outcomes":"The Skill Lab Series significantly improved students’ technical literacy and confidence in computing. Participants developed a working understanding of core software systems, programming fundamentals, and problem-solving techniques. Exposure to practical tools, coding platforms, and debugging exercises prepared them to independently pursue internships, interdisciplinary projects, and competitive programming opportunities.\\nA key outcome was increased confidence with coding and logical thinking. The mentorship-based model helped students overcome hesitation related to syntax, memory concepts, and algorithmic reasoning. Many students began exploring online coding platforms and continued practicing beyond the workshop, establishing a strong foundation for self-directed learning.\\nThe initiative also strengthened peer learning and interdisciplinary collaboration by connecting ECE students with mentors from computing backgrounds. This fostered a culture of knowledge sharing and early exposure to software-driven engineering applications. In the long term, the program contributes to improved employability, innovation readiness, and digital literacy among students, equipping them to integrate computing skills into future academic, industrial, and societal challenges. ","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-19","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Foundations of Computing – Skill Lab Series was a five-day intensive technical training program conducted from May 19 to May 23, 2025, at RV College of Engineering for second-semester ECE students. Organized by The Coding Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Skill Lab initiative, the program aimed to bridge the technological gap for students with limited prior exposure to core computing concepts. The sessions followed an immersive, hands-on format with three structured sessions each day, delivered across multiple labs to ensure small group learning and personalized mentorship.\\nThe curriculum covered foundational domains essential for interdisciplinary engineers, including Computer Networks, Operating Systems, Object-Oriented Programming in C++, Pointers and Standard Template Library (STL), and an introduction to Competitive Programming. Each topic combined theoretical understanding with practical demonstrations such as Linux command-line exercises, network simulation tools, coding challenges, and mini-projects. The pedagogy emphasized live coding, collaborative problem-solving, quizzes, and real-time debugging sessions to keep students actively engaged.\\nDesigned specifically for early-year ECE students, the program adopted a mentorship-driven approach where Coding Club members guided participants through learning pods and doubt-solving sessions. By creating an interactive and supportive environment, the Skill Lab ensured that students not only learned fundamental computing principles but also developed confidence in applying them to real-world technical problems.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/58iGq9E5gndEOTxQQBQVZ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qQrZKUBHnPVAtFzpyLP_Z","name":"ReSearchathon 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/d7RxjXtifVJU6yAZK64vx.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-16","duration":2,"outcomes":"ReSearchathon 2025 produced significant academic and skill-based outcomes. Participants enhanced their research abilities by working on real-world problems that required literature review, methodological design, and solution validation. The event helped students understand how research can be translated into practical, impactful innovations rather than remaining purely theoretical.\\nA major outcome was the development of interdisciplinary collaboration. Students from different domains worked together, combining technical knowledge with creative problem-solving. This collaborative approach strengthened teamwork, communication, and leadership skills, which are essential in both academic research and professional environments.\\nParticipants also gained exposure to evaluation processes similar to research conferences and innovation challenges, improving their presentation skills and technical articulation. The top teams were recognized for their exceptional contributions, motivating students to continue pursuing research and innovation. Beyond competition, the hackathon fostered a culture of research-driven thinking within the institution and encouraged students to apply their knowledge to solve pressing global challenges. Overall, ReSearchathon 2025 left a lasting impact by promoting practical research, innovation, and skill development among participants. ","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-15","hoursSpent":60,"description":"ReSearchathon 2025 was a 24-hour research-focused hackathon organized by the Coding Club of RV College of Engineering and held on 15–16 November 2025 in a hybrid format. The event aimed to transform innovative research ideas into practical solutions by bringing together students from diverse academic backgrounds and faculty mentors. Participants worked in teams of four, each guided by a mentor, and engaged in intensive problem-solving across domains such as Next-Gen Defense Technologies, Smart Sports & Engineering, Healthcare Innovations, Semiconductor Technologies, and Open Innovations for global challenges.\\nThe hackathon began with an online idea submission phase, where teams proposed research-driven solutions. Selected teams advanced to the offline final round, where they developed prototypes, refined methodologies, and validated their concepts through continuous mentorship and evaluation. The structure encouraged participants to integrate theoretical knowledge with real-world application, bridging the gap between academic learning and technological innovation. Evaluation criteria included innovation, feasibility, research depth, and real-world impact.\\nReSearchathon emphasized collaboration, research thinking, and interdisciplinary learning. Throughout the event, participants attended guidance sessions, technical reviews, and discussions that helped them strengthen their problem statements and solution frameworks. The event concluded with final presentations, recognition of top-performing teams, and reflections on research-driven innovation. Overall, ReSearchathon 2025 created a dynamic platform that nurtured creativity, analytical thinking, and solution-oriented research among students.\\n","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/80b2dfe9-d022-480c-9d64-d4679eed2523/ihkgyI27VoHc6ZS3jnFf0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 21:56:22.172774+00', '2026-02-01 07:28:19.415077+00'), ('d1eb5433-92d6-4734-870f-1a2a6c7a2e84', '6518a4a6-bac5-4bb5-81ac-e641b58166d0', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI013","name":"Chaheti Jha","period":"2022-2026","departmen