KBxKn1p9sp-j.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"SqVhD0SHW5bL-YbT6acHE","name":"Cumulative Event 2023","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-08-03","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants developed a strong sense of civic responsibility, leadership, and teamwork. The activities enhanced volunteer discipline, communication skills, and commitment to community welfare while promoting awareness of social, environmental, and ethical values.","semester":"5","startDate":"2023-08-02","hoursSpent":0,"description":"General NSS work involved active participation in routine National Service Scheme activities focused on community service, cleanliness, awareness programs, and volunteer support. The activities emphasized discipline, teamwork, and social responsibility among student volunteers","aicteMapping":"NSS","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5f418241-0432-47e8-a2a0-6cb58ae01695/VsHHCLqh8M7WVBoGBl42-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"U5poeSi4eIdoScwxkU59N","name":"Mera Pehla Vote - Desh Ke Liye","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-07","duration":4,"outcomes":"The pledge strengthened awareness about democratic rights and responsibilities, inspired \\nresponsible citizenship, and motivated students to actively participate in the electoral process, \\nfostering a sense of national duty and commitment toward building a strong and inclusive \\ndemocracy.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"\\nI participated in the AICTE initiative “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” by taking the official \\npledge to uphold democratic values and exercise my right to vote responsibly. The activity \\nemphasized the importance of informed voting, civic duties, and active youth participation in \\nstrengthening democracy, while encouraging first-time voters to contribute meaningfully to the \\nnation’s electoral process.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5f418241-0432-47e8-a2a0-6cb58ae01695/6S6id5uU4yGCyKlL9jvo_.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RSemjYUxXDz9AQVJqi9EB","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-07","duration":4,"outcomes":"Participation promoted physical fitness, social awareness, and empathy. It provided an opportunity to contribute to a meaningful cause, reinforced the value of community service, and inspired a sense of responsibility toward supporting underprivileged children through collective action.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"I participated in UTSARGA ’24, a charity marathon organized by NSS RVCE with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The event aimed to support underprivileged children through a social cause–driven run, encouraging fitness, compassion, and collective responsibility while contributing toward positive social impact.","aicteMapping":"Social awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5f418241-0432-47e8-a2a0-6cb58ae01695/xvZCs3rW8ejwoRhuJNJUG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"sphuqW46mEv1rU7Qvnb09","name":"BLOOD DONATION CAMP ","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-25","duration":6,"outcomes":"Increased awareness and positive attitude toward blood donation among the youth, promoting voluntary participation in life-saving initiatives.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-20","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized its flagship Blood Donation Camp as a pre-event of 8th Mile. The primary objective of the event was to encourage students to actively participate in the noble cause of saving lives through voluntary blood donation. Guided by the message “One pint of blood can save lives,” the camp motivated students to step forward, demonstrate compassion, and contribute meaningfully to society. The initiative also highlighted the importance of social responsibility and community service, fostering a spirit of empathy and civic duty among young individuals.","aicteMapping":"Social cause","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5f418241-0432-47e8-a2a0-6cb58ae01695/bqpztkX-Z4dvqn1dN1ePX.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YczR0j1KuJTALbEW_kHCB","name":"Quiz on Indian''s democracy","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-04-06","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants improved their knowledge of democratic principles, constitutional rights, and civic duties. The activity promoted critical thinking, awareness of national governance, and responsible citizenship while strengthening analytical and decision-making skills.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-04-05","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The quiz on Indian Democracy was conducted to enhance participants’ understanding of the Constitution, democratic values, and governance system of India. It encouraged active learning through an engaging and competitive question-answer format.","aicteMapping":"Social awareness","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5f418241-0432-47e8-a2a0-6cb58ae01695/hzjilLyzHiPl6YTBr0g8K.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iV1oOMCd_iKZzeeCOevuf","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-07","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participation promoted physical fitness, social awareness, and empathy. It provided an opportunity to contribute to a meaningful cause, reinforced the value of community service, and inspired a sense of responsibility toward supporting underprivileged children through collective action.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"I participated in UTSARGA ’25, a charity marathon organized by NSS RVCE with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The event aimed to support underprivileged children through a social cause–driven run, encouraging fitness, compassion, and collective responsibility while contributing toward positive social impact.","aicteMapping":"Social awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5f418241-0432-47e8-a2a0-6cb58ae01695/RBCfRwnAaaUto5_C6QYGl.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"S Praveen ","designation":"Assistant professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 11:46:46.990054+00', '2026-01-31 19:41:14.336013+00'), ('d35ba561-8e01-410e-ba24-ab243848553d', '65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS023","name":"Ishan Gupta","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"L7NRRb7-VlD5j60rRkALK","name":"SPARK “Through the Eyes of YOUth” – SDG Photography","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/qkJZ1nGSqZLFTnhUmX-mB.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I gained a deeper understanding of the Sustainable Development Goals and how real-world issues can be communicated effectively through photography and visual storytelling. The experience helped me think more critically about observing my surroundings, framing meaningful narratives, and expressing social and environmental concerns creatively. It also enhanced my ability to convey impactful messages using visuals, while encouraging a more conscious and empathetic perspective toward sustainability and community-driven challenges.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The event aimed to promote creativity and the knowledge of sustainable development goals through the art of photography and storytelling. Over the course of the event there were many participants submissions, reflecting the widespread engagement and excitement surrounding the initiative. ","aicteMapping":"Activity 14","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TJci5K2BdocR9-X_2MaCL","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024– NSS RVCE","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/7ShUsXECgrBQ_-9uyLHcd.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the Utsarga Marathon helped me understand the importance of social responsibility, community involvement, and collective action for a meaningful cause. The event reinforced values of discipline, perseverance, and teamwork while highlighting how individual efforts can contribute to larger social and charitable initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":40,"description":"5Km Marathon in and around RVCE campus for a worthy cause and charity.","aicteMapping":"Activity 15","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"o7WOQZfGEkKJoZaonJjJw","name":"Project Pustak 2024 – Rotaract Club, RVCE","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/WskyjY_b9Zju3Zsot60Ov.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through Project Pustak, I developed a strong sense of social responsibility and empathy toward underprivileged students. The activity helped me understand how collective efforts and structured resource allocation can directly improve access to education and create a meaningful impact in rural communities.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were eminently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Activity 1","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YfdlzguamTCmEGE7xwX1D","name":"Student Volunteer – CSITSS-2024","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/OTl8AWfoVOgpk-71mXiid.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"Volunteering at CSITSS-2024 enhanced my organizational, communication, and teamwork skills while giving me exposure to the structure and execution of a large-scale international academic conference. The experience helped me understand the importance of coordination and responsibility in facilitating knowledge exchange and research dissemination.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-07","hoursSpent":16,"description":"CSITSS 2024 Conference held at RVCE fueled scientific advancement, driving societal impact through collaborative research and innovation and witnessed 350+ research papers being submitted across 11 different tracks. To make this conference successful, numerous volunteers volunteered at every point right from documentation to planning and organizing. For the first time, the conference featured an impressive 48 sessions combining offline and online mode. Based on the work done, points have been allocated to the volunteers. Work consisted of managing sessions, giving guest introductions, and overall controlling the hall for that particular presentation session.","aicteMapping":"Activity 15","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"bLbzYtXYu7CdFJR_aVdQX","name":"Student Volunteer – Kadlekai Parishe 2024 (Eco-Conscious Initiative)","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/DgTYWhMs_M3huZbcYSbMH.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/H7OB1mqzGJKmGyBG1MzZf.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me develop environmental awareness and a sense of social responsibility by actively promoting sustainable alternatives to single-use plastics. It also strengthened my teamwork and planning skills through hands-on community engagement and practical implementation of eco-friendly solutions.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-12","hoursSpent":48,"description":"An eco-conscious community event aimed at promoting environmental sustainability and social responsibility. Students from the Department of Information Science and Engineering actively volunteered in the design, crafting, and distribution of handmade paper bags to reduce the use of plastic during the fair. The initiative focused on creating awareness about sustainable alternatives to single-use plastics while engaging with the local community.\\nThe activity encouraged teamwork, creativity, and hands-on learning, as students dedicated significant time and effort to planning and executing the initiative effectively. Through this effort, volunteers contributed to environmental awareness, community engagement, and the broader objectives of sustainable development.\\n","aicteMapping":"Activity 12","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ABh7gk_mNi_RIqMYudxoL","name":"Fist Full 2024– Rotaract RVCE","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/rOyjajlsASzHPYAFgi4oF.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"This initiative strengthened my sense of empathy and social responsibility by contributing directly to community welfare through collective action. It highlighted how organized participation and small individual contributions can come together to create a large-scale positive impact for those in need.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Activity 