rved as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were eminently utilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Activity 1","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"CBgQKEj7EckzOepXcV8cO","name":"Walk for Her – Walk for Change (Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon)","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/n6l_H1CnVMYnqxZzJkclb.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity helped me understand the importance of social awareness initiatives and the role of collective action in addressing deep-rooted social issues. It enhanced my sense of social responsibility and highlighted how simple initiatives can create meaningful impact in society.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":20,"description":"Walk for Her – Walk for Change was a social awareness walkathon organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering on Mother’s Day to raise awareness about female foeticide and the importance of protecting the girl child. The event encouraged collective participation to promote gender equality, social responsibility, and community awareness through a campus-based walkathon.","aicteMapping":"Activity 14","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"68z-k3z_0QLtEYnbs3m6U","name":"India Quiz – General Knowledge Quiz on India, UTPT, Quizcorp","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/s2Khk0dD03Ft097y9AzXR.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":3,"outcomes":"Participation in the India Quiz enhanced my knowledge of Indian history, culture, and Indian Knowledge Systems while improving my critical thinking, recall, and analytical skills in a competitive national-level setting.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-23","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Participation in the Indi-Genius: The India Quiz  at Under The Peepal Tree 2025, a national level quiz fest. The quiz promoted Indian Knowledge Systems","aicteMapping":"Activity 15","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Fkhn1xj0vmsqs10PNenpu","name":"Fist Full 2025– Rotaract RVCE","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/65ba9567-7040-4861-af71-bc9f9d382d73/XstMkkvuJDsj3-7Af6YGX.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"This initiative strengthened my sense of empathy and social responsibility by contributing directly to community welfare through collective action. It highlighted how organized participation and small individual contributions can come together to create a large-scale positive impact for those in need.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":10,"description":"In this initiative by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, students were encouraged to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor daal, with daily collections in the Civil Department. The drive garnered an overwhelming response with the total amount of 6,700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of toor dal donated by 1750+ students. This initiative highlighted the power of small efforts to drive significant societal change, reinforcing RVCE''s dedication to community welfare and solidarity.","aicteMapping":"Activity 15","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Rekha B.S","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:05:50.664731+00', '2026-01-30 08:59:30.245368+00'), ('d43271b0-1668-4c27-9295-0e7bd9f3cbd2', 'f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC157","name":"Sriman Reddy B","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"zkXxHu4H9srJL9vFrUA0j","name":"Kannada Habba - KARNATA","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/zhGWXD949aCccdi9w3rGs.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-15","duration":32,"outcomes":"Through participating in Kannada Habba, I gained a deeper understanding of the richness and importance of the Kannada language and Karnataka’s cultural heritage. The event helped me appreciate traditional art forms, folk culture, and the historical values associated with them. It also made me realize the role of language in preserving identity and connecting people across generations. Additionally, the program enhanced my sense of cultural pride and encouraged me to respect and promote regional traditions while working collaboratively with peers from diverse backgrounds.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-05-15","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Kannada Habba was celebrated with great enthusiasm at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) on 15 June 2023 to promote the richness of the Kannada language and the cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event was organized by the college’s Kannada Sangha with the objective of instilling pride in regional culture and encouraging students to connect with Karnataka’s traditions, literature, and values. Students and faculty from various departments actively participated, making the celebration vibrant and inclusive.\\n\\nThe program featured a variety of cultural activities that reflected the diversity of Kannada culture. Traditional folk dances, classical and light music performances, skits, and poetry recitations in Kannada were presented by students. These performances highlighted themes of Karnataka’s history, social values, and linguistic beauty. The event also provided a platform for students to showcase their artistic talents while strengthening cultural unity among participants from different backgrounds.\\n\\nOverall, Kannada Habba at RVCE was a meaningful and memorable celebration that reinforced the importance of preserving and promoting the Kannada language and culture. The event fostered cultural awareness, student engagement, and respect for local traditions within the academic environment. It successfully fulfilled its objective of celebrating Karnataka’s heritage while strengthening the sense of community among students and faculty members.","aicteMapping":"Event Management ","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/TT88qhfg8w9JTBTjyv5fI.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"v-DxYkuseo42yesR8whQu","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":2,"place":"Global Village Tech Park","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/QBRgDp7AkTxDJIahLxCIz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"By participating in the Utsarga Marathon 2025 organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), I learned the importance of combining physical fitness with social responsibility. The event helped me understand how collective effort and volunteering can contribute meaningfully to social causes, especially in supporting underprivileged communities. I also developed a sense of discipline, teamwork, and leadership by observing the coordination and dedication of NSS volunteers. Overall, the marathon strengthened my awareness of civic duty and motivated me to actively engage in community service initiatives.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025 was conducted on 6 April 2025 at R.V. College of Engineering under the aegis of the National Service Scheme (NSS) with the theme “Help a Child, Change the World”. This annual flagship charity marathon was organised to promote physical fitness, social responsibility, and community service among students and participants. NSS volunteers from the college worked throughout the preparatory phase to plan the route, manage registrations, and handle logistics, ensuring that the event ran smoothly and safely for all involved.\\n\\nThe marathon featured both 5 km and 10 km race categories, allowing students, faculty, and local participants to take part in an engaging run for a meaningful cause. Beyond fitness and sportsmanship, the event aimed to raise funds and awareness for underprivileged children, supporting initiatives related to education, healthcare, and basic welfare. Participants displayed enthusiastic involvement, cheering each other on and embodying the spirit of “service before self”, which lies at the heart of NSS activities.\\n\\nOverall, Utsarga Marathon 2025 was more than just a race—it served as a platform for social change and personal growth. Through this experience, participants developed a sense of empathy, teamwork, and civic engagement while contributing to a worthy cause. The marathon reflected the collective effort of the NSS RVCE team and the college community in promoting health, compassion, and social welfare, reinforcing the values of service and leadership among students.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/uGejMx6JAm_zO0oWYi4tG.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zQpofhvoNJHIkPU2-2IHa","name":"Kannada Habba - JAGADHVAHA","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/oC01YfUd1LI26mxmL2J3z.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-12-04","duration":31,"outcomes":"By participating in Kannada Habba Jagadvaha 2025, held on 4 December 2025, I gained a stronger appreciation for the cultural richness and linguistic heritage of Karnataka. The celebration made me realize the importance of preserving and promoting our regional language through artistic expression and community participation. Witnessing the enthusiasm of fellow students in performances and cultural displays helped me understand how traditions can bring people together and strengthen cultural identity. Overall, the event deepened my respect for Kannada culture and motivated me to stay connected to my roots while encouraging others to take pride in our shared heritage.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-04","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha 2025 was celebrated on 4 December 2025 at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) with great enthusiasm to honor the Kannada language and the cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event aimed to promote awareness, pride, and respect for Kannada traditions among students and faculty. Organized as part of the college’s cultural initiatives, the celebration brought together participants from diverse backgrounds to collectively experience and appreciate the essence of Karnataka’s rich legacy.\\n\\nThe program featured a wide range of cultural activities showcasing the vibrancy of Kannada culture. Students performed traditional and contemporary dance forms, folk and classical music, skits, and poetry recitations in Kannada. These performances highlighted themes related to Karnataka’s history, social values, and linguistic beauty. The stage décor, traditional attire, and enthusiastic participation created an authentic cultural atmosphere, making the event engaging and memorable for the audience.\\n\\nOverall, Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha 2025 served as an effective platform for cultural expression and community bonding within the college. The event strengthened cultural awareness, encouraged student participation, and reinforced the importance of preserving regional language and traditions in a modern academic environment. It successfully fostered unity, cultural pride, and respect for Kannada heritage among the RVCE community.","aicteMapping":"Event Management","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/hnqzYKtEP981Qkb0CgTC5.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GTbHgZf2TvQPNyawJUQ74","name":"Fist Full Event","slNo":4,"place":"Department of Civil Engineering , RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/dqTJeNXEjQ3X5MmTXuNFo.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"By participating in this Rotaract Club event, I learned the importance of social responsibility and the impact of even small contributions toward a larger cause. Donating 5 kg of rice made me realize how simple actions can directly help those in need when carried out collectively. The event also helped me understand the value of teamwork, organization, and empathy in service-oriented activities. Overall, it motivated me to actively participate in future social initiatives and contribute meaningfully to society beyond academics.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The first full-scale service event conducted by the Rotaract Club of RVCE marked an important step toward community engagement and social responsibility within the campus. The event focused on encouraging students to contribute essential resources for social welfare, emphasizing the value of collective action in addressing basic needs. Students actively participated by donating food items and essentials, reflecting a strong sense of empathy and responsibility toward underprivileged sections of society.\\n\\nAs part of the initiative, I contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, which was collected along with other donations for distribution to those in need. The event was well-organized by Rotaract volunteers, ensuring transparency, coordination, and proper handling of contributions. The initiative not only supported a meaningful cause but also created awareness among students about food security and the impact of small individual contributions when combined as a group effort.\\n\\nOverall, the event successfully highlighted the spirit of service and leadership promoted by the Rotaract Club at R.V. College of Engineering. It strengthened student involvement in social initiatives and laid a strong foundation for future Rotaract activities focused on sustainable community development and humanitarian service.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/wfu60ZhC40wY0ouRsCYVZ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"m4VxZtgIa0sdABnGuZC6l","name":"Kannada Habba - GHARJANE","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/vA36rQa7cbwrPBKub2T5f.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-20","duration":32,"outcomes":"By participating in Kannada Habba – Gharjane, I gained a deeper appreciation for the richness and significance of the Kannada language and Karnataka’s cultural heritage. The event helped me understand how cultural programs play a vital role in preserving traditions and promoting a sense of identity. I also learned the value of teamwork and active participation in organizing and celebrating cultural events. Overall, the experience strengthened my cultural awareness and motivated me to respect and promote regional traditions.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-20","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Kannada Habba – Gharjane was celebrated on 20 June 2024 at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) to promote the Kannada language and the cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event was organized with the objective of fostering cultural awareness and instilling pride in regional traditions among students and faculty. It brought together participants from various departments, creating an inclusive platform to celebrate Karnataka’s rich linguistic and cultural legacy.\\n\\nThe program featured a variety of cultural performances including traditional and contemporary dance forms, folk and classical music, skits, and Kannada poetry recitations. These activities highlighted the history, values, and artistic richness of Karnataka. The enthusiastic participation of students, along with vibrant stage decorations and traditional attire, created an engaging and authentic cultural atmosphere throughout the event.\\n\\nOverall, Kannada Habba – Gharjane served as a meaningful cultural celebration that strengthened unity and cultural appreciation within the college community. The event successfully encouraged student participation, promoted respect for regional culture, and reinforced the importance of preserving Kannada language and traditions in an academic environment.","aicteMapping":"Event Management","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f797181c-eaaa-4271-a38f-b372726e22b7/oUSIw4p3pNgKEB6_USgbx.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"S Praveen ","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 19:28:19.929395+00', '2026-01-30 20:42:03.042355+00'), ('d587d645-26ee-4c64-a353-1f3088b2f5e9', 'd2ea3a17-87b9-4224-b9cb-8c6a2a72d96a', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-02 06:15:52.09666+00', '2026-02-02 06:15:53.041847+00'), ('d7d23918-f9ea-4b58-b907-5fb34a5bdd03', '0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV072","name":"Pradeep S","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"MBvhQPgcfN8WfJ49qan7L","name":"Adamya Chetana Plantation Drive","slNo":1,"place":"Jnanabharathi ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Environmental Impact: Contribution to increased green cover and improved local ecology through tree plantation and care.\\n\\nSustainability Awareness: Enhanced understanding of environmental responsibility and sustainable practices.\\n\\nCommunity Engagement: Active involvement in a large-scale, community-driven environmental movement.\\n\\nSocial Responsibility: Demonstrated commitment to ecological conservation and civic duty.\\nRecognition: Formal acknowledgment for participating in a nationally recognized, consistent green initiative.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":12,"description":"The program marks a major milestone—372 consecutive Green Sundays—highlighting consistent community engagement in environmental conservation. The participant, Nagesh K B\\nfrom R V College of Engineering, actively contributed to this eco-friendly initiative, supporting Adyamya Chetana’s mission of promoting sustainability, biodiversity, and environmental\\nawareness.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/xxRT_Qcob1lcTh5v9SbIP.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1 - 2 ","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_HWUkIraaWpfcbgHHv66d","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye ","slNo":2,"place":"Online ","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye initiative has a profound impact by empowering first-time voters with the knowledge and confidence to participate in the electoral process. It fosters a sense of civic responsibility and awareness, encouraging informed decision making. The campaign enhances youth engagement in democracy, leading to a more inclusive and representative electoral process. By inspiring active participation, it lays the foundation for a lifelong commitment to voting and strengthens the democratic fabric of the nation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-13","hoursSpent":16,"description":"The Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye initiative is a powerful campaign aimed at empowering first-time voters to actively engage in the democratic process. Recognizing that young voters form a significant portion of the electorate; the initiative seeks to educate them about the value of their vote and its impact on shaping the nation’s future. The core objective of the event was to instill a sense of responsibility and national pride among students who are eligible to vote for the first time. The theme, Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye, emphasized the power of a single vote and how young citizens can contribute to the country’s progress by exercising their electoral rights responsibly. The campaign emphasizes the critical role of voting as a fundamental right and a civic duty, inspiring young citizens to make informed decisions at the ballot box. It includes interactive workshops, informational sessions, and creative outreach strategies to demystify the voting process, address common misconceptions, and highlight the significance of every\\nindividual vote in driving national progress. “Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” was more than just a campaign; it was a call to action. The event successfully instilled a sense of civic duty\\namong the youth, reminding them that active participation in democracy begins with a single step: casting your first vote.\\nThrough educational, creative, and motivational activities, the event made a meaningful impact, empowering students to become informed, responsible, and proud voters of India.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/J9YMR8Rwrd9V7mouD8Uia.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3 - 4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KPwGlOFA-HHwMZxc6oynZ","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"24 ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/ukwzJ5Zv_CTkPRDr54AV8.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility\\nand gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category, which challenged my physical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating an positive change in society. This cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causes in the future.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/VOqJNu2MJruqpNuFZQcpw.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5 - 6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OyVNvyOxUn3jlOf9tRNe8","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"25 ","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/-Rjew_pq5I-Tj7RtG1FLQ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility\\nand gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":144,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category, which challenged my\\nphysical endurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote\\nsocial responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating an positive change in society.\\nThis cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding.\\nKnowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and = teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continue contributing to similar causes in the future.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":36,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/DDUc2CYgYUNTozycYkBPN.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7 - 8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mJdW8Hyx66VcVc8IA0Dt3","name":"Kannada Sanga","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/mPaIC5M9P2tjGB27bT6uT.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"Efficient Coordination: Successfully collected and managed Kannada Sangha T-shirts for participants.\\n\\nOrganizational Skills: Improved planning, record-keeping, and distribution management skills.\\n\\nTeamwork & Communication: Enhanced interaction with students and Kannada Sangha coordinators.\\n\\nCultural Promotion: Contributed to strengthening Kannada identity and visibility during events.\\n\\nResponsibility & Leadership: Demonstrated accountability in handling collective resources.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-07-02","hoursSpent":60,"description":"The activity involved collecting and organizing Kannada Sangha T-shirts for members and participants of Kannada Sangha events. This task required coordination with students, maintaining records of requests, ensuring correct sizes and quantities, and distributing the T-shirts efficiently. The activity supported the smooth conduct of Kannada Sangha programs\\nand helped promote unity, cultural identity, and active participation among members","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/c4hCQ5qlrV4Rr-MrxS9b5.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9 - 10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PXOQ1V3SCVKO0WvWD05YR","name":"Fist Full ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/2ufGcJWZkRyY8LlAXWUIz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the donation drive held at the RVCE campus was the successful collection of essential food items to support underprivileged communities. The initiative helped address\\nbasic nutritional needs and contributed to food assistance efforts. It fostered a sense of social responsibility and empathy among students while encouraging active participation in\\ncommunity service. The activity also strengthened awareness about the importance of collective effort, demonstrating how small contributions can create a meaningful and positive impact on society.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-13","hoursSpent":40,"description":"A contribution of 2 kg of toor dal was made during the donation drive held at the RVCE campus. The initiative was organized with the objective of supporting food assistance programs.\\nIt aimed to extend help to underprivileged communities through essential supplies. The drive encouraged student participation in social welfare activities. It highlighted the importance of collective responsibility toward society. Food grains collected were intended for meaningful community support. Such initiatives help address basic nutritional needs. They also promote empathy and humanitarian values. The campus environment fostered a spirit of service unity. Students were\\nmotivated to contribute in practical ways. The activity emphasized giving back to society. It reflected the role of educational institutions in social development. Small contributions together create a larger impact. The drive served as a reminder of social accountability. Overall, the initiative strengthened awareness about community welfare.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/At8-tMkpohiJhnej6vPD7.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11 - 12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HN3NaooKW9Ag3f4HCSFtS","name":"Yes+ Workshop","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/I5Ausk-0P59u7FpRTkyLO.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of this activity was increased awareness and understanding of mental health and emotional well-being among participants. It helped develop practical skills for stress\\nmanagement, mindfulness, and self-regulation, contributing to improved mental clarity and emotional balance. The program empowered youth to recognize the importance of mental health\\nin daily life and encouraged them to share this awareness within their communities, supporting the objectives of the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative. Overall, the activity fostered personal growth,\\nsocial responsibility, and a positive approach toward holistic well-being.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-15","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The activity involved voluntary participation at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, during the academic year 2025–26 through the YES+ (Youth Empowerment Seminar for Students) program. The initiative focused on creating awareness about the importance of mental health and well-being in alignment with the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative of the Government\\nof India. Conducted under the guidance of The Art of Living organization, the program emphasized stress management, mindfulness, and emotional balance while empowering youth\\nwith practical life skills. The experience contributed to personal development, social awareness, and an understanding of mental health as a key component of holistic well-being, while also\\nencouraging active involvement in national-level humanitarian and educational initiatives","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/vS5zmphX5nH4ILaQ1t9Wl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13 - 14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zZQQb_atQvui7mcjImbIR","name":"Yes+ service","slNo":8,"place":"Art of living centre ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/MUr83em0j_zhbYApqQnsg.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of the Gaushala activity was increased awareness about the importance of conserving and protecting indigenous cow breeds of India. Participants gained an understanding\\nof animal welfare practices, sustainable agriculture, and the ecological benefits associated with native cattle. The initiative fostered a sense of responsibility, compassion, and respect for\\nanimals while encouraging active involvement in environmental conservation and traditional practices that support rural and agricultural sustainability.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-16","hoursSpent":40,"description":"The activity involved voluntary participation at the Gaushala initiative conducted at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, during the academic year 2025–26. The program\\nfocused on the conservation, care, and nurturing of indigenous cow breeds of India, highlighting their cultural, ecological, and agricultural significance. Through this initiative, awareness was\\ncreated about traditional cow-rearing practices, sustainable agriculture, and the importance of protecting native breeds. The activity encouraged responsibility toward animal welfare and\\nenvironmental sustainability while fostering values of compassion, service, and respect for nature among participants.\\n","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0ecfea54-b43d-4767-99b5-a87a40438006/MXzhPzRmKSulFytZtn-pw.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15 - 16","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Prof. Shashi Kiran C. R","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 20:06:39.404856+00', '2026-01-30 08:08:51.493638+00'), ('d8616aa7-77bd-42c0-a6c4-b8a140180a44', '0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV035","name":"Harsha Patil G C","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"wlozVYiPuektaguHsbHqB","name":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":1,"place":"online","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye initiative has a profound impact by empowering first-time voters with the knowledge and confidence to participate in the electoral process. It fosters a sense of civic responsibility and awareness, encouraging informed decisionmaking. The campaign enhances youth engagement in democracy, leading to a more inclusive and representative electoral process. By inspiring active participation, it lays the foundation for a lifelong commitment to voting and strengthens the democratic fabric of the nation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-13","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye initiative is a powerful campaign aimed at empowering first-time voters to actively engage in the democratic process. Recognizing that young voters form a significant portion of the electorate; the initiative seeks to educate them about the value of their vote and its impact on shaping the nation’s future. The core objective of the event was to instill a sense of responsibility and national pride among students who are eligible to vote for the first time. The theme, Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye, emphasized the power of a single vote and how young citizens can contribute to the country’s progress by exercising their electoral rights responsibly. The campaign emphasizes the critical role of voting as a fundamental right and a civic duty, inspiring young citizens to make informed decisions at the ballot box. It includes interactive workshops, informational sessions, and creative outreach strategies to demystify the voting process, address common misconceptions, and highlight the significance of every individual vote in driving national progress. “Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye” was more than just a campaign; it was a call to action. The event successfully instilled a sense of civic duty among the youth, reminding them that active participation in democracy begins with a single step: casting your first vote.\\nThrough educational, creative, and motivational activities, the event made a meaningful impact, empowering students to become informed, responsible, and proud voters of India.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/uXXESzzmIt-HWK90X_8oM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"blLZL0MUpVL8S6CxpzWr4","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/gSEXP_zI7uZTVGHs609On.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/VklqBcJGuPi4or34ftJip.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp held was a resounding success, both in terms of participation and the amount of blood collected. The camp successfully met its goal of increasing the local blood supply generous donors. The event helped raise significant awareness about the importance of regular blood donations and the vital role they play in saving lives. Many first-time donors expressed their appreciation for the smooth, wellorganized process and the educational materials provided during the event, which helped inform them about the significance of blood donation.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was successfully held on 6 June 2024 at RVCE, with the aim of collecting blood donations to support local hospitals and patients in need. The camp was organized by Rotaract in collaboration with blood banks and was open to all eligible donors. The event saw an overwhelming response from the students. The camp was fully equipped with all necessary medical facilities, and the process was managed by a team of experienced healthcare professionals who ensured the safety and comfort of all donors.\\n","aicteMapping":"Health Awarness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/TREoY0BHezNJuBNzSguFW.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HiWJKvD6bRwxhG2NrGaIU","name":"Police Marshal ","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/dqAGk_R0xBS4gDuEyNpYk.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced awareness among students regarding drug abuse prevention and cyber safety Students gained knowledge about their social responsibilities and civic duties Volunteers were\\nofficially recognized as Police Marshals, boosting leadership and confidence Encouraged youth participation in maintaining law, order, and social harmony Strengthened collaboration between students, police authorities, and social organizations\\nPromoted discipline, unity, and social responsibility through active involvement Participants received certificates and activity points, motivating continued NSS engagement","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Police Marshal Event was organized by NSS RVCE in collaboration with the Bengaluru City Police and Aarohana Foundation with the objective of promoting social responsibility and public safety among students. The event was conducted on 18th December 2024 at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The program aimed to create awareness among youth about drug abuse prevention, cyber crime awareness, and responsible citizenship. Officials from the police department addressed the gathering and shared valuable insights on current social challenges, legal awareness, and the role of students in maintaining law and order in society. A special highlight of the event was the Police Marshal Capping Ceremony, where selected NSS volunteers were formally recognized and honored as Police Marshals. This ceremony symbolized the trust placed in students to act as responsible citizens and role models within\\nsociety. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from students, all dressed in blue attire representing unity and discipline as per NSS guidelines. The session was interactive,\\ninformative, and motivational, encouraging students to actively contribute to building a safercommunity.\\n","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/e7UWPBDLzra8QN1slA3Tm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ArHCcS9JN5HMLzfuWGo7M","name":"Utsarga Marathon \"25","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/FBXqTOXxUk8nTxk8d0HTi.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/cOdd6Ss1rjzEIhkqfH_Td.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/qV7ffcEeLhJQJ_DJuirmL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participating in the Utsarga Marathon taught me the value of combining physical endurance with community service. The experience reinforced my commitment to social responsibility\\nand gave me a sense of accomplishment, knowing that my\\nefforts contributed to a meaningful cause. This event strengthened my belief in the NSS mission and motivated me to stay engaged in initiatives that benefit both my personal growth and the community","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was a significant event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering. I participated in the 5 km category,which challenged my physical\\nendurance and pushed me to connect with the core mission of NSS: contributing to society in a meaningful way. The marathon wasn’t just about running; it was about coming together with like-minded students, faculty, and other participants, all driven by a common purpose to promote social responsibility and community engagement. The atmosphere on the day of the marathon was energetic and filled with excitement. Everyone was motivated, not only by the physical challenge but also by the cause we were running for. Before the race began, the NSS program officers and college administration highlighted the impact of our participation, emphasizing how each step we took symbolized our commitment to creating anpositive change\\nin society. This cause gave me an extra push to perform well and stay focused throughout the 5 km course, even when the run started to get tough. Crossing the finish line felt incredibly rewarding. Knowing that my participation contributed to the NSS’s objectives made the experience even more valuable. The points awarded to each participant, including myself, served as a recognition of our effort and dedication to this cause. Participating in the Utsarga Marathon wasn’t just a personal achievement for me—it was an experience that underscored the importance of community service, physical fitness, and teamwork. This marathon has reinforced my belief in the NSS’s mission and has motivated me to continuecontributing to similar causes in the future.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/fZSzsacMqspuPNz50GxWF.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"e6xHPFhsYStSvCQhJtFDG","name":"Village Camp","slNo":5,"place":"Peraje, Coorg","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/FeQvvr14mMaWaMDMuvonQ.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/h1in5pgPBGE2m6f6n1VE3.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/xcNGz_bggeUKgGdRP2QVN.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-05-21","duration":7,"outcomes":"1)Enhanced Social Responsibility:\\nVolunteers developed a strong sense of duty towards society and understood real-life social challenges.\\n\\n2)Community Development:\\nAwareness programs and service activities positively impacted the villagers, especially in areas of cleanliness, health, and social awareness.\\n\\n3)Leadership and Teamwork Skills:\\nParticipants improved their leadership, coordination, and communication skills through group activities and fieldwork.\\n\\n4)Personality Development:\\nThe camp helped volunteers build confidence, discipline, and a service-oriented mindset.\\n\\n5)Practical Exposure:\\nStudents gained hands-on experience in organizing events, interacting with local communities, and managing responsibilities.\\n\\n6)Strengthened NSS Values:\\nThe camp reinforced the NSS motto “Not Me, But You”, encouraging selfless service and social commitment.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-15","hoursSpent":160,"description":"NSS RVCE organized a 7-day Special Camp from 15th May to 21st May 2025 at Peraje Village, Coorg, with the objective of promoting community development and nurturing social responsibility among students. The camp was exclusively organized for dedicated NSS volunteers, ensuring active participation and meaningful engagement throughout the program.\\n\\nThe camp focused on social awareness, community service, and personality development, aligning with the core values of the National Service Scheme. Volunteers participated in various activities such as village cleanliness drives, awareness programs on health, hygiene, education, and environmental conservation. The program also emphasized teamwork, leadership, discipline, and interaction with the local community.\\n\\nThe selection of participants was based on their previous NSS involvement and commitment, followed by personal interviews. Proper arrangements were made for accommodation, food, and transportation, ensuring a safe and productive environment. A Parent and Counsellor Consent Form (NOC) was mandatory, ensuring transparency and responsibility.\\n\\nThe camp provided an excellent platform for students to understand rural life, contribute to society, and develop empathy and leadership qualities while earning up to 40 NSS activity points.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":40,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/TAAm3dlyx-wZdzhvgU6aP.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kWaxcFjBxV-vffUgQODrF","name":"R V Instition Governer Event","slNo":6,"place":"Taj West End","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/6UPBNjvWZb3TDLLhOEp1w.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/A56QsTOGWSV9bNcbuDfVu.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-06-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event enhanced the participants’ understanding of sustainable development, policy-making, and governance frameworks at both national and global levels. NSS volunteers gained valuable exposure to expert opinions and interdisciplinary approaches toward sustainability. The interaction encouraged critical thinking, awareness of social responsibility, and motivation to actively contribute to sustainable initiatives. Overall, the event strengthened the volunteers’ knowledge, confidence, and commitment toward building a more sustainable and inclusive future.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-03","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The NSS RVCE unit participated in the Inaugural Session and Panel Discussion for the Release of the Sustainable Development Report (SDR) 2025, organized by O.P. Jindal Global University in collaboration with Rashtriya Shikshana Samithi Trust Institution. The event was held on 3rd June 2025 at Taj West End, Bengaluru and brought together academicians, policy makers, legal experts, and sustainability leaders from various sectors. NSS volunteers attended the inaugural session and engaged in insightful panel discussions focusing on sustainable development goals, global policy frameworks, academic governance, and legal perspectives. The presence of Shri Thaawarchand Gehlot, Hon’ble Governor of Karnataka, as the Chief Guest added significance to the event. The session provided volunteerswith an opportunity to understand real-world sustainability challenges and the role of institutions in achieving long-term development goals.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/BZXOVVTWIVn6H_im3rimW.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AbZqzT6WePsxR3zwNZttB","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/Whc0gukzhJGNjviUDWQ1R.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp held was a resounding success, both in terms of participation and the amount of blood collected. The camp successfully met its goal of increasing the local blood\\nsupply generous donors. The event helped raise significant awareness about the importance of regular blood donations and the vital role they play in saving lives. Many first-time donors expressed their appreciation for the smooth, wellorganized process and the educational materials provided during the event, which helped inform them about the significance of blood donation.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was successfully held on 30 OCT 2025 at RVCE, with the aim of collecting blood donations to support local hospitals and patients in need. The camp was\\norganized by Rotaract in collaboration with blood banks and was open to all eligible donors. The event saw an overwhelming response from the students. The camp was fully equipped with all necessary medical facilities, and the process was managed by a team of experienced healthcare professionals who ensured the safety and comfort of all donors.","aicteMapping":"Health Awareness","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/0f9bc832-aa9f-441e-954c-7e1cfa911cc4/dR5qFs-4fAVBOr-t5shlW.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. L.Durga Prashanth","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 21:24:46.04742+00', '2026-01-29 21:24:46.766737+00'), ('d89fc4c8-bf2d-4301-9c11-c5289ddc5efa', 'eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD004","name":"Anand Patil","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"Mcr58pXl8Vb2xldMF35zF","name":"Nasha Mukth Bharat ","slNo":1,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/-8Z3EOAiRLnPIXiDbUa_H.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-08-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"The pledge initiative effectively promoted awareness and individual responsibility towards drug-free living, contributing to the larger goal of a healthier, addiction-free India.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Nasha Mukth Bharat Abhiyaan (NMBA) is a nationwide initiative launched by the Ministry of Social Justice & Empowerment to build a drug-free India. The campaign focuses on spreading awareness about the harmful effects of substance abuse, especially targeting vulnerable districts and youth through various programs such as awareness generation, counselling, treatment, and rehabilitation. It engages educational institutions, communities, and stakeholders to promote a healthy, addiction-free society. As part of this campaign, participants were invited to take an online pledge to stay away from drugs and harmful substances, encouraging personal commitment and inspiring others. The pledge was accessible via the NMBA official website, reinforcing the Abhiyaan’s mission of creating a disciplined, drug-free youth population for national development.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/5Qb0dVokfRbwkL-LB0WKo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"k0lIXsb4jwhCVdUW0oqyN","name":"Mega Plantation @ Hosadurga","slNo":2,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/YOz5JbHIkcGWc_YT3YjCY.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"A large-scale plantation was completed in Hosadurga, aiding in soil conservation and ecological restoration in the region.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-09","hoursSpent":8,"description":"On June 9, 2024, the NSS unit of RVCE embarked on a major environmental expedition—the \"Mega Plantation @ Hosadurga\". This Community Development event required significant logistical planning and commitment, as students traveled to Hosadurga to execute a large-scale afforestation project. The initiative was aimed at restoring ecological balance in semi-arid regions.\\n\\n\\nUpon arrival, volunteers were assigned specific zones for planting. The terrain required physical endurance and teamwork to dig pits and plant saplings suitable for the local climate. The students worked tirelessly throughout the day, driven by the understanding that their efforts would help combat desertification and improve the local water table over time. The scale of this \"Mega\" plantation distinguished it as a high-impact event.\\n\\n\\nThis event was a profound learning experience, taking students out of their urban comfort zones and into rural landscapes that desperately need ecological intervention. It fostered a deep appreciation for rural environmental challenges and the importance of tree cover for soil conservation. The successful completion of the drive marked a significant milestone in the NSS unit''s annual calendar.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/elTVKCjJJ_f8zEQvIM0uV.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dD1af8HaeBBXOAf8SE4ES","name":"Kannada Sangha Activity - 2023","slNo":3,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/Yp6Xa5X0BUJOJBnUzDtVY.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-05","duration":5,"outcomes":"The event successfully celebrated Kannada culture through mass singing, fostering regional pride and cultural unity among the student body.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-01","hoursSpent":40,"description":"On 05-02-2024, the Kannada Sangha of RV College of Engineering organized the \"Koti Kanta Gaayana\" event to celebrate the richness of Kannada culture and language. This mass singing event was part of a state-wide initiative to unite people through the power of music and shared heritage. Students gathered in large numbers to sing iconic Kannada songs, creating a vibrant atmosphere of regional pride and unity.\\n\\n\\nThe event served as a prelude to the Kannada Rajyotsava celebrations, instilling a sense of belonging and cultural identity among the students. Participants, regardless of their linguistic background, joined in the chorus, celebrating the inclusive spirit of Karnataka. The air resonated with melodies that paid tribute to the land, its poets, and its history.\\n\\n\\nAnand Patil actively participated in this cultural extravaganza. Beyond just singing, the event was a pledge to preserve and promote the local language and culture in an increasingly globalized world. It provided a refreshing break from academic routines, allowing students to connect with their roots and celebrate the artistic legacy of the state.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/kQRWAvAxNQLFB-e0H1aUG.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BQMbJTm67L7biJMiKk9mS","name":"Paper Bag Making","slNo":4,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/lIRyIiWn3O45NZifv1sP6.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":10,"outcomes":"The workshop equipped students with the skills to create eco-friendly alternatives to plastic, promoting sustainability and waste reduction.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-24","hoursSpent":50,"description":"the NSS unit of RVCE organized a \"Paper Bag\" workshop under the category of Community Development. This creative and eco-friendly initiative was designed to campaign against the use of single-use plastics. Students gathered to learn the art of making durable bags out of old newspapers and other recyclable paper materials.\\n\\n\\nThe workshop was hands-on, with participants cutting, folding, and pasting to create functional bags. These bags were intended not just as a craft project, but as a practical alternative to plastic bags for distribution to local vendors or for use within the campus. The activity highlighted the concepts of \"Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle\" in a tangible way.\\n\\n\\nAnand Patil contributed his time and effort to this cause. The event fostered creativity while delivering a strong environmental message. It demonstrated that small, individual actions—like switching to a paper bag—can collectively contribute to a significant reduction in plastic pollution and a cleaner environment.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":17,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/9g0xfjGYR9LDWjGRw6cJ5.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Xn9ML7UPr0PrNwzOUa34E","name":"paper drive","slNo":5,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/CSkxfET8mVUptPJh0wRrR.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":" Rotaract Club of RVCE brought back the mega event\\nwith a bang to help orphanages/underprivileged people and bring a\\nsmile on their faces.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"With an overwhelming support of 500+ volunteers,\\nthe students collected more than 7 tonnes of newspapers in just over 9\\nhours! The volunteers, registered for the event, assembled at Kriyakalpa,\\nRVCE at 8:00 AM. Volunteers were taken to different localities of\\nBangalore by buses to collect all sorts of papers. The incentive behind\\nthis was to raise funds by selling the collected old newspapers, books,\\nmagazines, waste papers etc. to paper vendors, and donating the same\\namount for the welfare of the Nele Narendra Foundation.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/fx9gqFfOTPARbP6e87oZS.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EJsD_4KSgbcUXVRVAOzcT","name":"Utsarga Marathon  ","slNo":6,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/wxYta6L0ea_HrurRuxGjq.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/i0byuunhIYu4tu7zNVHeG.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/mpLjAuCR7qW4X99yfsMRP.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/D45nYyQUYleDhF1B8rETu.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon triumphantly raised substantial support for children''s  education programs. It channeled funds to provide books, scholarships, and  learning resources to underprivileged kids in need. The event achieved its  fundraising goals, amassing contributions that will sustain classroom initiatives  for months ahead and directly benefit dozens of students from local  underserved communities.    Beyond the financial gains, the marathon left an indelible impression on all  involved. Participants shared stories of personal growth, from first-time runners  conquering their fears to veterans inspiring newcomers. Social media buzz amplified the reach, with photos and testimonials drawing attention and  encouraging future involvement.    Ultimately, it redefined the act of running as a meaningful pursuit, not only for  personal health and endurance, but for forging a brighter, more inclusive future.  The Utsarga Marathon exemplified how community-driven events can create  ripple effects of change, empowering children to dream big and succeed while  fostering a culture of giving back. ","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon, organized by NSS RVCE, took place on February 4th,  2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM across the Bengaluru campus. Under the  theme \"Help a Child Change the World,\" it celebrated health, fitness, and  education support for underprivileged children. Months of planning ensured  smooth logistics with sponsor-backed medals, T-shirts, and refreshments along  tree-lined routes.    Over 500 runners, including RVCE students, faculty, alumni, and locals from  Karnataka, gathered at dawn. They chose between a 5 km fun run (Rs. 399) or  10 km challenge (Rs. 449), with all donations funding school supplies and  tuition. Warm-ups, cheers, live music, banners, and photo booths created festive  energy.    Volunteers in high-visibility vests managed water stations, medical aid, and  crowd control with enthusiasm. They helped runners adjust to long conditions,  ensuring safety and inclusivity. Heartwarming scenes featured friends jogging  together, families cheering from sidelines, and visitors spectating.    Runners crossed the finish line to roaring applause, greeted with finisher  medals and personalized certificates. Top age-group performers received  special trophies, sparking friendly rivalries. On-site announcements celebrated  winners, fueling real-time excitement around the charitable core.    The event proved transformative, blending physical challenge with  philanthropy. It promoted wellness while instilling purpose through unity.  Individual strides wove into widespread positive change for children''s futures.","aicteMapping":"Community  Development ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/R_hUrDaMxeDBKRgAnVYM0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IuGL5jxKUQQCW5IOnAqEV","name":"Project Pustaka - 2024","slNo":7,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/QODSF9P9eK8ZZH9s9Jjmg.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/JxFfmK1Fm51odE2M_udfr.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/W70zyjnTD_57_Ya_ciSkI.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-29","duration":6,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully bridged the educational resource gap for rural students by providing essential supplies like textbooks, stationery, and backpacks, directly fostering a more equitable and conducive learning environment. Through the strategic partnership between the Rotaract Club of RVCE and the Pranav Foundation, the initiative efficiently transformed tiered community donations into tangible academic tools that empower underprivileged youth.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential\\nschool supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial\\namount of Rs 100 or 350 was collected from each compassionate donor, which\\nserved as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to\\nthese deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to\\npurchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks,\\nand other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment.\\nThrough the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or\\nRs 350, the project garnered substantial funds.Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside\\nPranav Foundation will procure essential school supplies for the\\nunderprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/m0DVjgd8vx1j6trPTp0V9.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"UaFZcnQjKpmbf31WuI1cD","name":"Red Cross Humanity Blood Donation Camp","slNo":8,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/yvuR5G2wk6n0jlTzz6Mm-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully supported the Red Cross in their mission to provide safe blood to those in need, earning formal appreciation from the State Branch Chairman.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Voluntarily donated blood during the Karnataka State Branch drive. The activity focused on the Red Cross mission of \"Through Humanity to Peace,\" providing blood to government hospitals and underprivileged patients. This involved pre-donation health screenings and awareness about the importance of regular blood donation cycles.","aicteMapping":"Community Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/4t4FxpYdLSV9MM0TNpHo-.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"24-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5tdFgVI0ZWRzvocOgkfnF","name":"Project Pustak - 2025","slNo":9,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/MKF2AtNLZQR0miUuPChTa.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/rGkP26A955UNxtvKOqN9G.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-03","duration":4,"outcomes":"The dedication and perseverance of the volunteers were instrumental in empowering rural and underprivileged students, in line with achieving the club’s mission of making a tangible, lasting impact on society and fostering a sense of global solidarity.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":40,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs. 100 was collected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational \\nmaterials such as textbooks, stationary items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. \\n \\nTo summarize, Project Pustak is a noble initiative aimed to provide \\nessential school supplies to underprivileged students in rural areas. ","aicteMapping":"Rural Outreach","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/xakq85pZFXzCmpospKIJB.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"26-27","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hXZn5usd-qxiQAPurLrME","name":"Annual Voluntary Blood Donation Drive","slNo":10,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/cllAnrEJ5RF4bEoZoDYhh.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Reinforced the vital blood supply chain for the Red Cross and demonstrated consistent civic engagement.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Continued commitment to community health by participating in the 2025 donation drive. This consistent involvement highlights a dedicated effort toward social welfare and healthcare support. The donation process followed strict medical protocols, ensuring high-quality blood supply for the Bengaluru region.","aicteMapping":"Community Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/sQMXh9NyR0iSLiLhZ61zA.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"28-29","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TGL7jD0LXZoD86yePJ9pY","name":"Voluntary Blood Donation Drive","slNo":11,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/jYnD7IFYTUveGlEKb0cjs.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Contributed to saving lives through voluntary donation and helped promote a culture of altruism within the student community.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Participated in a campus-wide blood donation camp aimed at maintaining critical blood bank reserves. As an O Negative donor (Universal Donor), this contribution was vital for emergency medical procedures and quaternary care requirements. The drive emphasized the social responsibility of students in supporting the healthcare infrastructure.","aicteMapping":"Community donation","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/HmSwnEg7ik4H2nB-rriMl.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"30-31","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Vzk-FGWhI6APukqj-WMiA","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 – \"Help a Child, Change the World\"","slNo":12,"place":"BENGALURU","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/-hyxyB04mLrffO76UA18F.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The marathon successfully met its fundraising targets, providing critical support for children''s welfare projects. It significantly boosted the participants'' sense of civic duty and social empathy. By earning 15 AICTE activity points, students demonstrated their ability to balance physical endurance with a deep commitment to humanitarian service, making a tangible impact on the lives of future generations.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2025 was a flagship charity event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of RVCE. Held on April 6th, 2025, the marathon was centered around the theme \"Help a Child, Change the World,\" serving as a powerful initiative to support underprivileged children through dedicated education and healthcare funds.\\n\\nThe event successfully mobilized a large number of participants in both the 5 KM and 10 KM categories. More than just a fitness event, the marathon acted as a community-driven movement where every step taken contributed directly to the welfare of children in need. The registration proceeds were channeled into providing school supplies, medical aid, and better educational infrastructure for marginalized youth, reinforcing the institution''s commitment to social equity.\\n\\nVolunteers managed the entire lifecycle of the marathon, from the initial registration drive to on-ground coordination on the day of the race, ensuring that the mission of charity remained at the forefront of the event.","aicteMapping":"Awareness drive","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/eaea2d01-3fff-4603-9aed-094941e4753a/ZUjSIvzWUPGolh-qVSouW.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Srividya M S ","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:17:24.006268+00', '2026-02-02 07:25:21.613645+00'), ('d8b8eedf-fd15-4d48-8501-34f548ffb5df', 'df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CV055","name":"MAYANK MISHRA","period":"2022-2026","department":"Civil Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"nX9ZAXuF8Gaw7ZWsATx_T","name":"Uptown Junk 2024","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/hYpOHJeL5YO3_bUhtdItV.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":2,"outcomes":"Uptown Junk successfully promoted creativity, innovation, and sustainable practices among participants. Students developed teamwork, leadership, and resource management skills while working under competitive conditions. The event increased awareness about waste reuse and environmental responsibility. It strengthened bonding within the student community and encouraged collaborative learning. Overall, the event created a fun yet meaningful learning experience by combining competition, sustainability, and innovation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Subject: Uptown Junk – A Two-Day Festival of Creativity and Sustainability\\nContent:\\nUptown Junk was a two-day flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th and 29th November 2024, designed to promote creativity, teamwork, and sustainable thinking among students. The event featured engaging activities such as a “Treasure Hunt” and a “Best Out of Waste” competition, where teams were challenged to innovate using auctioned materials and Rota money. With participation from over 400 students, the event created a vibrant platform for hands-on learning, problem-solving, and collaboration. Evaluated by esteemed judges including DRR Rtr. Abhay Lohia, Rtr. Disha, Rtr. Bhumika, Rtr. Shreya, and IPP Rtr. Satej, the competitions highlighted the importance of resourcefulness and environmental responsibility. Uptown Junk successfully blended fun with purpose, fostering a strong sense of community, innovation, and sustainability within the college.","aicteMapping":"Economic and Community Development","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"b_hEhpDeiZfKQ4YuHSjzz","name":"Human Elephant Conflict Awareness","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/exYg1KZ94sfDQoFk5tRQ9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Save the Elephant Seminar successfully enhanced participants’ understanding of the importance of elephant conservation and wildlife protection. Students gained knowledge about elephant behavior, their ecological role, and the threats they face due to poaching and habitat loss. The seminar encouraged awareness of government and NGO initiatives for wildlife conservation and forest preservation. It inspired students to actively participate in environmental protection activities and spread awareness in their communities. The event also fostered respect for animals and promoted the need for peaceful coexistence between humans and wildlife. Overall, the seminar proved to be an informative and impactful initiative toward biodiversity and environmental conservation.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Subject: Seminar on Human–Elephant Conflict: Coexistence and Conservation\\nContent:\\nA seminar on Human–Elephant Conflict was organized to create awareness about the growing challenges arising from interactions between human populations and elephant habitats. The session focused on the causes of conflict such as habitat fragmentation, agricultural expansion, and urbanization, along with their impact on both human safety and elephant conservation. Experts and speakers discussed real-life case studies, mitigation strategies, and sustainable solutions including habitat corridors, early warning systems, and community involvement. The seminar encouraged participants to understand the importance of coexistence, responsible land use, and conservation-driven policies, fostering a sense of environmental","aicteMapping":"Social and cultural awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eQciOA9rXCwsWHzBPmgZy","name":"Rush Hours 5.0","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/4ueoE0iEuKJ70V-SVboSr.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-21","duration":5,"outcomes":"Rush Hours 5.0 concluded as a highly successful and engaging multi-day event, witnessing active participation from over 450 students. The structured elimination-based format sustained enthusiasm and healthy competition throughout the five days, motivating teams to consistently improve their performance. Participants demonstrated strong teamwork, creativity, and problem-solving abilities across diverse tasks ranging from digital challenges to artistic and social-media–driven activities. The event effectively fostered collaboration, strategic thinking, and confidence among students, while also providing a vibrant platform for creative expression. Overall, Rush Hours 5.0 strengthened peer bonding, enhanced co-curricular skills, and set a strong benchmark for future large-scale student\\nengagement initiatives by the Rotaract Club of RVCE.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-03-17","hoursSpent":15,"description":"Subject:\\nRush Hours 5.0 – A Five-Day Inter-College Challenge Event\\nContent:\\nRush Hours 5.0 was a dynamic five-day flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, designed to bring together students through a series of interactive, creative, and competitive challenges. With participation from over 450 students, the event aimed to foster teamwork, problem-solving skills, creativity, and healthy competition. Each day introduced a unique task, ranging from online treasure hunts and social awareness campaigns to performance-based and DIY creative challenges. The gradual elimination format added excitement and intensity, encouraging teams to consistently perform at their best. By blending digital engagement, artistic expression, and strategic thinking, Rush Hours 5.0 provided a vibrant platform for collaboration, innovation, and peer bonding, making it a memorable and impactful experience for all participants.\\n","aicteMapping":"Technical and Mental Awareness","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jJAT_BuK9xRZPtRQacrdu","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/mR7DL3dGbh-DcT2-atyHV.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon concluded with significant social, organizational, and community-oriented outcomes. The event successfully mobilized more than 500 participants, demonstrating strong public engagement and widespread support for the cause of helping underprivileged children.\\nThe marathon also strengthened the culture of volunteerism, teamwork, and civic responsibility within the NSS RVCE community, as volunteers efficiently managed logistics, safety measures, hydration points, route coordination, and participant support. The structured execution of the run enhanced event management, planning, and leadership capabilities among organizers.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"Subject:\\nUtsarga Marathon – NSS RVCE Flagship Social Event\\nContent:\\nThe Utsarga Marathon, a flagship community welfare initiative conducted by NSS RVCE, was organized with the central theme “Help a Child, Change the World” emphasizing support for underprivileged children requiring educational and healthcare assistance.\\nThe event commenced at 7:00 AM with systematic registration, verification, and distribution of event shirts, badges, and participation materials, creating uniformity, identity, and enthusiasm among attendees. Pre-event announcements, energy sessions, and safety briefings were conducted to ensure preparedness and smooth coordination. Medical teams, hydration points, volunteers, and emergency response units were strategically stationed along the route to maintain participant safety and well-being.\\nThe Marathon officially began at 9:00 AM and witnessed active participation from over 500 individuals, including students, faculty members, and fitness enthusiasts. The carefully planned route encouraged inclusivity and accessibility, offering a balance of challenge and engagement for runners of varying fitness levels. Throughout the event, NSS volunteers facilitated crowd management, route guidance, and awareness messaging, reinforcing the event’s social objective.\\nBeyond promoting physical fitness and recreational involvement, the marathon aimed to create consciousness about the struggles faced by underprivileged children and the importance of collective community action in addressing them. The event fostered social responsibility, volunteerism, compassion, teamwork, and civic participation within the campus community.\\n\\n","aicteMapping":"Social and cultural Awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"akSfe8FZnaxtQ9BpUHCKY","name":"Female Foeticide Walkathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/mKRqo2SSBBt4tjLSIn6h3.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"The walkathon successfully raised awareness about female foeticide and the importance of valuing the girl child. It encouraged participants to take a stand against gender discrimination and promoted social responsibility through collective action.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":6,"description":"On the occasion of Mother''s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon with the aim of shedding light on the grave issue of female foeticide and promoting the value of girt children in society. The event witnessed an overwhelming participation of 350+ individuals, including enthusiastic students, dedicated faculty members, and supportive parents who came together to walk for a cause that truly matters. The walkathon began in the early hours of the morning from the RVCE campus and was marked by thought-provoking placards, powerful slogans, and an atmosphere of solidarity. The event served as a platform to educate and inspire change, urging everyone to take a stand against gender-based violence and discrimination even before birth. The Rotaract Club of RVCE extends heartfelt gratitude to all participants for their support and commitment to this impactful cause","aicteMapping":"Social and cultural awareness","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/KIfc98SQp_usMw02lE_It.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rDHPyt8SfgNrvSAkTU1YK","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/C9ABf2QQhL1ZZtpu0aPVo.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-22","duration":6,"outcomes":"The Fist Full initiative concluded with outstanding social impact and community engagement. Contributions from more than 1,750 students resulted in the collection of over 6,700 kg of rice and 800+ kg of Toor dal, significantly supporting food distribution efforts for underprivileged communities. \\nFist Full successfully highlighted how collective small donations can create meaningful change, positively influence community welfare and reinforce the importance of sustained philanthropic action.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Subject:\\nFist Full – Hunger Relief and Community Donation Initiative by Rotaract Club of RVCE\\nContent:\\nThe FistFull initiative, conducted from 15th to 29th November, was a large-scale social welfare campaign organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana. The event aimed to address food insecurity by encouraging students to donate essential food grains, specifically 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. Daily collection points were set up in the Civil Department to ensure smooth coordination, accessibility, and consistent participation throughout the donation drive.\\nThe initiative received overwhelming support, with contributions from over 1,750 students, resulting in the collection of more than 6,700 kg of rice and over 800 kg of toor dal. These donated food grains were directed toward organizations supporting underprivileged communities, thereby helping reduce hunger and strengthen nutritional access. The campaign not only showcased the collective strength of student-led humanitarian efforts but also reinforced the importance of empathy, social responsibility, and community solidarity. Fist Full successfully demonstrated how small individual contributions, when united, can create meaningful and lasting societal impact.\\n","aicteMapping":"Community development and social development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RkCCCDWlaaElNMOIkSIcT","name":"YES!+ Course: Acquiring and imparting awarness on importance of mental health as per Har Ghar Dhyan Initative of Govt. of India","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/IQjxqw8yeUjF0qTFkQYJG.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/-O5Ob9aE92qHXR1fNRl4-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-16","duration":4,"outcomes":"The primary objective of this activity was to create awareness about the importance of mental health and to promote mental well-being among individuals and communities in alignment with the Har Ghar Dhyan Initiative of the Government of India. The activity aimed to educate participants about the significance of mental balance, stress management, and emotional health in daily life. It focused on encouraging the practice of meditation and mindfulness as effective tools for improving concentration, reducing stress, and enhancing overall quality of life.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-13","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This course focused on understanding the importance of mental health and promoting mental well-being among individuals and communities in alignment with the Har Ghar Dhyan Initiative of the Government of India. The program emphasized the significance of mental balance, emotional health, and stress management in daily life.\\nThe course provided basic knowledge about mental health awareness, common mental health challenges, and the role of mindfulness, meditation, and Dhyan (focused attention) in improving mental well-being. It highlighted how regular practice of meditation helps in reducing stress, improving concentration, emotional stability, and overall quality of life.\\nParticipants were trained to acquire awareness about mental health issues and impart this awareness to others through communication, guidance, and community interaction. The course also encouraged adopting a positive attitude, self-discipline, and healthy lifestyle practices to support mental wellness at individual and societal levels.","aicteMapping":"Mental and Social Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/5YOeyGVaq3jc5AqsbQ7uK.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YllwjeNIoHfR9EQy2MXOJ","name":"Activity Permaculture: Acquiring and  Creating awareness in the public on the importance of enhancing soil quality to produce  more agricultural yields","slNo":8,"place":"Art of Living International Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/K6AH8auu0_scXLuHl0on6.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary objective of this activity was to create awareness about the importance of soil health in increasing agricultural productivity through sustainable permaculture practices. The activity aimed to educate the public on natural methods of improving soil fertility and maintaining soil structure for long-term agricultural benefits. It also sought to promote environmentally friendly farming techniques that support sustainable yields while preserving natural resources. By spreading awareness and encouraging adoption of permaculture principles, the program aimed to contribute towards sustainable agriculture, environmental conservation, and improved food security.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-26","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This activity focused on the principles of permaculture with an emphasis on enhancing soil quality to improve agricultural productivity. The program involved acquiring knowledge about sustainable farming practices such as soil conservation, organic manure usage, composting, mulching, and natural methods to improve soil fertility. Participants also engaged in creating awareness among the public about the importance of healthy soil in achieving higher and sustainable agricultural yields. The activity highlighted the long-term benefits of soil health in promoting environmental sustainability, reducing dependency on chemical fertilizers, and supporting eco-friendly agricultural practices. Through interaction and awareness initiatives, the activity encouraged responsible and informed approaches towards sustainable agriculture.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/goG6uMmzV4SjFbLQcYFu9.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"VAfoF-FaVw1ZuIAye2ZAl","name":"Activity Horticulture: Nurturing plants and trees, watering, sowing seeds and plantation.","slNo":9,"place":"Art of Living International Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/uTDZ2gF8BAh0O0ND1VM6d.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/V3kP7R6NbKb0kDB409aPm.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The main objective of this activity was to promote environmental awareness and encourage active participation in green initiatives through horticultural practices. The activity aimed to develop understanding of the importance of plants and trees in maintaining ecological balance and supporting sustainable living. It also sought to instill a sense of responsibility towards nature by encouraging regular care, nurturing, and protection of plants. By engaging in watering, sowing, and plantation activities, the program aimed to foster environmental stewardship, discipline, and appreciation for sustainable environmental practices.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-07","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This activity focused on horticultural practices involving the nurturing and maintenance of plants and trees. The work included watering plants, sowing seeds, plantation of saplings, and basic care practices required for healthy plant growth. Participants gained practical exposure to the importance of greenery, soil care, and regular maintenance in sustaining plant life. The activity emphasized environmental awareness, sustainable practices, and the role of plants and trees in improving air quality, biodiversity, and ecological balance. Through hands-on involvement, the activity encouraged responsibility, patience, and respect for nature.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/5fQVCVBPF6aebgXSblmwa.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mX3up8Hf-r5g3hfTPbMfd","name":"Activity Gaushala: Conserving and raising indegenious cows of India.","slNo":10,"place":"Art of Living International Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/9XAERW_piTdytLFj6On20.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/CvzvZQsvcjj3VXq_BJ9oe.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/oF-t36yyi7BUzNSIBTHbl.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The main objective of this activity was to promote awareness about the conservation and sustainable rearing of indigenous cow breeds of India. The activity aimed to educate participants on the ecological, agricultural, and cultural importance of native cattle and their role in supporting organic farming and environmental sustainability. It also sought to instill a sense of responsibility and compassion towards animal welfare while encouraging community participation in preserving indigenous livestock. By engaging in Gaushala activities, the program aimed to develop respect for traditional practices, support rural sustainability, and contribute towards the long-term conservation of India’s native cow breeds.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-21","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This activity focused on understanding and supporting the conservation and care of indigenous cow breeds of India through active participation in Gaushala-related activities. The program emphasized the importance of native cattle breeds in maintaining ecological balance, sustainable agriculture, and rural livelihoods. Participants were exposed to the traditional methods of cattle care, feeding practices, cleanliness, and basic animal welfare. The activity also highlighted the significance of indigenous cows in producing organic manure, promoting natural farming practices, and preserving India’s cultural and agricultural heritage. Through hands-on involvement, the activity created awareness about the need to protect indigenous breeds from decline and encouraged responsible attitudes towards animal care and conservation.","aicteMapping":"Social and cultural development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/oCjvf7R4wm-Mj1yknWzhV.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"K_3YL1lDL_PjuK99Zwfga","name":"Activity Community Kitchen: Serving food, cutting vegetables, setting up and cleaning community kitchen","slNo":11,"place":"Art of Living International Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/jFDQ4MTeDd9xEqzeY3PHD.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/rY3Fe6e5OAhQR_-HWPBt-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"The primary objective of this activity was to contribute to community welfare by supporting the efficient preparation and distribution of food in a community kitchen. The activity aimed to develop a sense of social responsibility, teamwork, and respect for dignity in service. It also focused on creating awareness about food hygiene, cleanliness, and waste management while encouraging disciplined work practices. By participating in food preparation, service, and cleaning activities, the program sought to instill values of compassion, selfless service, and cooperation, while promoting the importance of community support systems in ensuring food security.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-27","hoursSpent":6,"description":"This activity involved active participation in a community kitchen, focusing on serving food and supporting essential kitchen operations. The work included cutting and preparing vegetables, assisting in cooking-related activities, setting up the kitchen area for service, distributing food in an organized manner, and maintaining cleanliness before and after food service. The activity emphasized the importance of teamwork, hygiene, time management, and discipline in large-scale food preparation and service. It also provided practical exposure to community service by addressing food needs and supporting inclusive access to nutritious meals. Through hands-on involvement, the activity encouraged empathy, cooperation, and social responsibility towards community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Cultural and social development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df21ceba-c313-48c3-91d9-bb924b9dc4fb/5M5Qnynhs0KITXo31qmO4.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Venugopal G.","designation":"Assistant Professor, Dept. of Civil Engineering"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 12:32:47.755648+00', '2026-01-29 23:24:06.099911+00'), ('d963e8d5-1cb2-49ef-9b74-d70cb1d479f2', 'c9579c01-7d08-4824-a742-88b9eb737a64', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS059","name":"Saran Karthik P","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":