s all the participants had a wonderful \\ntime surrounded by the scenic hills of Huthridurga Betta and \\nembarked on what would be a very memorable journey. ","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the participants boarded \\nthe bus to Huthridurga hills, which is the trek location with great \\nenthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with \\nbasic information of the event.","aicteMapping":"Economic and  community  development ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1ZXn5lsryUSXywgBKGUg-","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh K Liye","slNo":2,"place":"RV College of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Awareness of students to vote for the nation","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The event involves taking a pledge to vote, and a quiz on Indian \\nDemocracy for first-time voters.","aicteMapping":"Awareness  ","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8DoqGxUTZT8n8Jma3BHF9","name":"Voting Awareness Seminar","slNo":3,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-03-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Awareness of students to vote for the nation","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-03-09","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Event was to create awareness among student and teach them the importance of voting, The officials came from outside and took seminar for the students on \"Why Voting is important\".","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":1,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fLbR2n1SlXhTFRkY7YOS6","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":4,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"This marathon is a fundraiser to help underprivileged children.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is a marathon conducted by NSS RVCE. The \\ntheme of the marathon is \"Help a child, change the world\". The \\nlength of the marathon was 5km.","aicteMapping":"Community  Development ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qGm04qBZSqdEBAqpT3orz","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":5,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community  service","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"A27OjnEZSq-HCIgAXXx3E","name":"INDUSTRY VISITS  ORGANISED-RTPS  & YTPS","slNo":6,"place":"Raichur and  Yermarus ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-02","duration":4,"outcomes":"The industry visit enhanced students’ understanding of the \\npractical aspects of thermal power generation and reinforced \\ntheoretical knowledge related to power plant engineering. \\nStudents gained insights into real-world industrial operations, \\nsystem integration, safety standards, and environmental \\nconsiderations followed in thermal power plants. The visit \\nimproved students’ technical awareness, analytical thinking, and \\nappreciation of large-scale energy systems. It also motivated \\nstudents to explore industry-oriented learning and strengthened \\ntheir ability to relate academic concepts to practical engineering \\napplications, thereby contributing to their overall professional and skill development.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-29","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The industry visit to Raichur Thermal Power Station (RTPS) \\nand Yeramarus Thermal Power Station (YTPS) was organized \\nto provide students with practical exposure to the working of \\nlarge-scale thermal power plants. The visit was planned and \\ncoordinated by the student members of SPARK, the IUCEE\\nRVCE Student Chapter. During the visit, students were \\nintroduced to the complete process of thermal power generation, including coal handling, boiler operations, turbine functioning, condenser systems, cooling mechanisms, and power transmission processes. Interaction sessions with industry professionals helped students understand plant safety practices, operational challenges, maintenance procedures, and environmental management techniques. The visit aimed to bridge the gap between theoretical concepts learned in classrooms and their real-time industrial applications through experiential learning.","aicteMapping":"Community  service and  Professional  development ","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"njYCRdgc_IMi75VYtPgU5","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":7,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-12-15","duration":2,"outcomes":"The event enhanced students’ creativity, critical thinking, and \\nteamwork skills through interactive and hands-on activities. \\nParticipants developed problem-solving abilities, innovation \\nmindset, and presentation skills while working under time \\nconstraints. The activity also promoted sustainable thinking by \\nencouraging the reuse of waste materials for productive purposes. Overall, Uptown Junk contributed to holistic student development by fostering innovation, collaboration, and stress-free learning beyond academics.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-12-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":" Uptown Junk, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, was a \\ntwo-day student engagement event conducted on 14th and 15th \\nDecember. The activity combined a treasure hunt with a “best \\nout of waste” competition to promote creativity, problem-solving, teamwork, and stress relief through experiential learning. Participants engaged in clue-based tasks across the campus and utilized collected materials to design innovative models from waste. The event encouraged competitive spirit, innovation, and active participation while providing a platform for students to showcase creativity and practical thinking in a collaborative environment.","aicteMapping":"Community  Development ","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qP86Q9zHCb4uLC2HxTXWZ","name":"Fast TREK 2.0 ","slNo":8,"place":"Kunagalu  Betta Hills","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":" The activity enhanced students awareness of environmental \\nconservation and the importance of maintaining cleanliness in \\nnatural spaces. Participants developed teamwork, discipline, and a sense of collective responsibility while actively engaging in fitness-oriented and service-based activities. The trek encouraged healthy lifestyle practices and strengthened interpersonal skills through collaboration and shared experiences. Overall, Fast Trek 2.0 contributed to the holistic development of students by integrating adventure, environmental responsibility, and community service.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast Trek 2.0, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, was an \\nadventure-based social initiative designed to promote \\nenvironmental conservation, physical fitness, and community \\nengagement. The activity combined an organized trekking \\nexperience with a cleanliness drive, encouraging students to \\nexplore natural surroundings responsibly while practicing \\nsustainable and eco-friendly habits. Participants were sensitized \\nto environmental issues such as waste management, conservation of biodiversity, and responsible tourism through guided activities and volunteer coordination. The event provided students with an opportunity to engage in outdoor physical activity while contributing positively to environmental preservation.","aicteMapping":"Economic and  community  development","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AfslefQmYHJMLnuIwDPAQ","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":9,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The UTSARGA Marathon witnessed enthusiastic participation \\nand successfully fostered a spirit of unity, perseverance, and \\ncommunity involvement. Participants experienced improved \\nawareness of physical fitness and its role in overall well-being. \\nRunning  in the 5 km marathon reflected dedication, determination, and active participation in the event. \\nThe marathon strengthened the values of teamwork, discipline, \\nand social responsibility among students. It also reinforced the \\nmission of NSS in promoting holistic development by integrating \\nphysical wellness with community service, thereby contributing \\npositively to both individual growth and societal welfare.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":" The UTSARGA Marathon was organized by the National \\nService Scheme (NSS) on 04 February 2024 as a significant \\ncommunity development initiative aimed at promoting physical \\nfitness, social responsibility, and collective well-being. The event brought together students, volunteers, and members of the community to participate in a 5 km marathon, emphasizing the importance of an active lifestyle in building a healthier and more responsible society. \\nThe marathon served as a platform to spread awareness about \\nhealth, endurance, and discipline while encouraging students to \\nactively contribute to community-oriented activities. NSS \\nvolunteers played a key role in organizing and managing the \\nevent, ensuring smooth coordination, participant safety, and \\nadherence to event guidelines. The initiative highlighted NSS’s \\ncommitment to nurturing socially conscious individuals through \\nmeaningful engagement beyond academics.","aicteMapping":"Community Development ","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Fk8ifNmIDJiyTTASpN8zg","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":10,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":4,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DJs71LwZSbRFAxh8MroQ1","name":"FistFull","slNo":11,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-16","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative contributed to supporting nutrition programs for underprivileged communities and strengthened students’ sense of social responsibility and civic engagement. Participants developed awareness of social issues, empathy towards vulnerable sections of society, and an understanding of the importance of collective action. The activity reinforced the values of service, compassion, and community development among students.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-16","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The FistFull initiative, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE  in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana (RI District 3191), was a community service activity aimed at addressing food insecurity. The initiative encouraged student participation through the contribution of essential food grains, which were collectively pooled and distributed to beneficiary institutions such as orphanages, old age homes, hospitals, trust schools, and anganwadis. The activity focused on collective effort, organized distribution, and sustainable social impact through community participation.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"FBYiH40HH2AKxvI0HB0iy","name":"GEN-AI Hackathon","slNo":12,"place":"RV College Of Engineering","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"The hackathon enhanced students’ understanding of Generative AI concepts and strengthened their ability to apply AI techniques to practical problem scenarios. Participants developed skills in teamwork, critical thinking, time management, and innovative solution design. The event encouraged hands-on learning, improved technical confidence, and exposed students to industry relevant AI applications. Overall, the activity contributed to student''s professional development by promoting experiential learning, collaborative innovation, and readiness for emerging technology-driven challenges.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The GenAI Hackathon, powered by EDOCK, was organized to provide students with hands-on exposure to emerging technologies in Generative Artificial Intelligence. The event was conducted on 29th November 2024 at the DTL Huddle and offered participants an opportunity to apply theoretical knowledge to real-world problem statements within a limited timeframe. Students worked in teams to design, develop, and demonstrate innovative AI-based solutions, emphasizing creativity, technical skills, and practical implementation. The hackathon fostered a collaborative learning environment where participants engaged in ideation, coding, model development, and solution presentation, guided by problem-solving and innovation driven objectives.","aicteMapping":"Professional  Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ijMMstUuSrGhrsbDHX0LZ","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":13,"place":"Narayangiri  Hills","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity helped participants develop a sense of social responsibility, teamwork, and leadership. Students gained practical exposure to organizing and participating in community oriented initiatives, enhancing their communication skills, coordination abilities, and problem-solving mindset. The event fostered discipline, collaboration, and perseverance while encouraging students to actively engage in service-based learning. Overall, Fast Trek 3.0 contributed to the holistic development of students by strengthening ethical values, civic awareness, and professional skills.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Fast Trek 3.0 was organized as a student-driven initiative aimed at promoting social responsibility, teamwork, leadership, and community engagement among participants. The event was conducted on 12th January 2025 and involved structured activities that required coordination, perseverance, and active participation. The program aligned with the objectives of Rotaract by encouraging students to contribute meaningfully to society while developing interpersonal and organizational skills. Through active involvement, participants demonstrated commitment towards service-oriented goals and experiential learning beyond the classroom environment.","aicteMapping":"Economic and  community  development ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"31","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vCbNkrmHiG8Lhv51mV-ad","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":14,"place":"RV College Of Engoneering","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The UTSARGA Marathon witnessed enthusiastic participation and successfully fostered a spirit of unity, perseverance, and community involvement. Participants experienced improved awareness of physical fitness and its role in overall well-being.\\nRunning  in the 5 km marathon reflected dedication, determination, and active participation in the event. The marathon strengthened the values of teamwork, discipline, and social responsibility among students. It also reinforced the mission of NSS in promoting holistic development by integrating physical wellness with community service, thereby contributing positively to both individual growth and societal welfare.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":" The UTSARGA Marathon was organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) on 06 April 2025 as a significant community development initiative aimed at promoting physical fitness, social responsibility, and collective well-being. The event brought together students, volunteers, and members of the community to participate in a 5 km marathon, emphasizing the importance of an active lifestyle in building a healthier and more responsible society. \\nThe marathon served as a platform to spread awareness about health, endurance, and discipline while encouraging students to actively contribute to community-oriented activities. NSS volunteers played a key role in organizing and managing the event, ensuring smooth coordination, participant safety, and adherence to event guidelines. The initiative highlighted NSS’s commitment to nurturing socially conscious individuals through meaningful engagement beyond academics.","aicteMapping":"Community  Development ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"34","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 01:49:53.355193+00', '2026-01-31 06:55:14.76537+00'), ('e1f266ed-7061-4b82-9af4-0adc3cf72ba4', '18a97b5f-5257-4697-a924-5b408e1ceb37', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC038","name":"Chappidi Sai Sudheer","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"iGPwrHIkDfa1FY6tOF2-J","name":"","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GHCmiZkX7QG_2o7f037vk","name":"","slNo":2,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jS0ifBKFUE2nmSvgO3PF6","name":"Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":3,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/18a97b5f-5257-4697-a924-5b408e1ceb37/ldxwx5SVfP5vj3upfjg6T.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 16:59:19.708838+00', '2026-02-01 04:55:10.081488+00'), ('e2b089d3-0f16-471c-9076-4022054e75e2', '5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS068","name":"Subhranil Swar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"31u_J2KMPIAvl977eYb4g","name":"Swachh Bharat Abhiyan","slNo":1,"place":"JCI Hosur, Sipcot","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-04-20","duration":16,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of social responsibility and the impact that consistent community service can create. The experience strengthened my sense of discipline, teamwork, and time management while working toward a common social cause. It also deepened my understanding of cleanliness, public health awareness, and the role individuals play in contributing to societal development.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-04-05","hoursSpent":80,"description":"I participated in a social service initiative organized by Junior Chamber International Hosur SIPCOT, where I contributed 80 hours toward the Swachh Bharat Abhiyan. During this period, I actively took part in cleanliness drives and community-focused activities aimed at improving public spaces. The initiative emphasized discipline, teamwork, and civic responsibility. My efforts were formally recognized with a certificate of appreciation, acknowledging the time and commitment invested toward societal upliftment.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/P4uY1B1YEIDrNy2TYjeOn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9C5weNv5Pe1HSvovZ570L","name":"Enviromental and Climate change activity","slNo":2,"place":"Maiti Labs, Bengaluru","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-11-18","duration":110,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of environmental responsibility and how individual efforts contribute to larger climate action goals. The internship helped me develop consistency, accountability, and a strong sense of social commitment. I also gained experience in teamwork, communication, and working toward impact-driven objectives. Overall, it strengthened my awareness of sustainability challenges and the role youth can play in addressing them.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-01","hoursSpent":80,"description":"I completed an internship at Maiti Labs, a youth-led non-profit organization working toward climate action and sustainability. During the internship, I contributed to environmental awareness initiatives, community-focused projects, and impact-driven activities. The role involved consistent participation, coordination, and responsibility over more than 80 hours. This experience allowed me to actively engage in meaningful social work while supporting initiatives aimed at long-term environmental impact.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/s9quvP5FkzESxgogAdaoj.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WMp8eOsUjRaQ5DRYOeGRy","name":"10 m Air Rifle Shooting Event","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/AjenlnNTGNDgTgmxjUtTY.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of focus, patience, and controlled breathing through the 10 m air rifle shooting activity. The act of planting a sapling reinforced a sense of responsibility toward nature and sustainability. Together, the activity highlighted how discipline in sports and care for the environment both require consistency and commitment.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-30","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in a 10 m air rifle shooting activity, which focused on precision, discipline, and safety. Following the shooting session, I was given a sapling as a symbol of environmental responsibility and sustainability. I planted the sapling and documented the moment by taking a photograph. The photograph was later uploaded to the shared drive as part of the activity record. This experience combined sportsmanship with a meaningful gesture toward environmental awareness.","aicteMapping":"To promote discipline, responsibility, and sports culture in society.","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/-UiXZfK8eGnCNPDXou2Ux.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9LlSvNVa4UhudzGAolfmT","name":"Fast Trek 3.0","slNo":4,"place":"Narayangiri Hill","photos":[],"endDate":"2026-05-25","duration":0,"outcomes":"I learned the value of physical endurance, mental resilience, and perseverance while trekking through challenging terrain. The experience also strengthened my teamwork and coordination skills, as moving together was essential for a safe and successful trek. Spending time in nature helped me appreciate the importance of mindfulness, adaptability, and environmental respect.","semester":"5","startDate":"2026-05-26","hoursSpent":8,"description":"In April 2025, I took part in a trek to Narayan Giri Hills, which was both physically engaging and refreshing. The trek involved navigating uneven trails and gradual climbs, testing endurance and teamwork. Along the way, I experienced scenic views and a calm natural environment that offered a break from routine life. The trek helped build resilience, coordination, and a deeper appreciation for nature and outdoor activities.","aicteMapping":"To promote fitness, teamwork, and environmental awareness.","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/nKy8-D4ep9iyKhp2e1OQA.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"K6NkwT0A7lQy7LSfDSECm","name":"Carv Hindi - Acting Club","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of teamwork, commitment, and disciplined preparation while working toward a common goal. The experience improved my confidence, stage presence, and ability to perform under responsibility. It also taught me how cultural and creative contributions play a vital role in representing an institution professionally.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-03","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I was a part of the CARV-Hindi team that contributed during the NAAC visit at RV College of Engineering. I actively participated in the conceptualization, rehearsals, and final performance, which required dedicated preparation and teamwork. Our efforts aimed to create a meaningful impact and represent the institution positively. This contribution was formally acknowledged through a request for the allocation of activity points.","aicteMapping":"To promote culture, creativity, and social expression.","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/LPR4v8VfDuyR_DnL5T8ZT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rCZko5JY7czErXo75EisN","name":"Media Volunteering - 8th Mile","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"I learned how to work efficiently as part of a team in a fast-paced event environment. The experience improved my communication, coordination, and time-management skills while handling multiple responsibilities. I also gained practical exposure to leadership, problem-solving, and managing media tasks under pressure.","semester":"8","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I served as a volunteer and conducted activities as part of the Media Team for 8th Mile, our official college fest. I was involved in coordinating media coverage, capturing key moments, and managing content for documentation and promotions. The role required teamwork, quick decision-making, and effective communication under tight timelines. This experience enhanced my leadership skills and gave me practical exposure to event management and media operations.","aicteMapping":"To support collaboration, communication, and event culture.","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/nGZzuXWHNPWA3rCtIAp5s.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"84uglPacFLnxMdcCUAZsj","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the importance of social responsibility and how a small voluntary act can make a significant impact on saving lives. The experience increased my awareness about the blood donation process, safety measures, and healthcare ethics. It also reinforced values of empathy, community service, and civic responsibility.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I attended a blood donation camp organized to promote awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation. The camp was conducted in a well-organized and hygienic manner, ensuring the safety and comfort of all participants. Medical professionals guided donors through the process and carried out necessary health checks. The event highlighted the role of community participation in supporting healthcare needs and saving lives.","aicteMapping":"To support healthcare and save lives.","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5c3d6060-2510-4981-9cf9-f698f2cc7bd1/A-eYsw4sEgaLPHXbwCN2b.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 19:17:12.810986+00', '2026-02-01 19:26:52.439416+00'), ('e2e3ebb5-91cb-46f8-82ed-f31f0a2379aa', '75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI062","name":"Vinyas K S","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"P8PKqpm5LFkApYxWVVsKi","name":"Azadi Ka Kalotsav","slNo":1,"place":"Manekshaw Parade Ground","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/AO70QSDt6V25bLZeUEn-j.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/e4IJxtVaoY7PP0NLdLdGR.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/MIrn1WgJfy_5x0Zdtj_D0.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/Y6zNoHrFoAFYbfs_x1yXd.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-08-15","duration":22,"outcomes":"Awareness Generation:\\nThe dance effectively communicated the objectives and benefits of five government free schemes, helping in mass awareness through an engaging and non-verbal medium.\\n\\nCultural Representation:\\nThe fusion of different dance forms showcased India’s rich cultural diversity and reinforced the message of unity in diversity.\\n\\nSkill Development:\\nParticipants developed strong teamwork, leadership, discipline, time management, and coordination skills through rigorous 20-day practice sessions.\\n\\nConfidence and Exposure:\\nPerforming at a prestigious venue and in front of the Chief Minister and Governor boosted confidence and provided rare exposure to a state-level public event.\\n\\nInstitutional Recognition:\\nRVCE received recognition for its active student participation in a nationally significant celebration, enhancing the institution’s cultural and social engagement profile.\\n\\nSocial Responsibility:\\nThe event highlighted the role of youth in nation-building by using art to support government initiatives and promote public welfare.\\n\\nPersonal Growth:\\nParticipants experienced a strong sense of patriotism, responsibility, and pride, making the event a memorable milestone in their academic life.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-25","hoursSpent":120,"description":"Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav was a large-scale cultural dance event organized to celebrate the spirit of India’s freedom, national unity, and inclusive governance. The event aimed to spread public awareness about key government welfare initiatives through the powerful medium of dance and visual storytelling. Students from RV College of Engineering (RVCE) actively participated in this prestigious programme, contributing to both cultural representation and social awareness.\\n\\nA dedicated dance group was formed at RVCE, and the preparation phase spanned 20 continuous days. The practice sessions were conducted in multiple stages to ensure discipline, synchronization, and performance excellence. Initial rehearsals were held in classrooms for choreography development and coordination. As the performance scale increased, practices were shifted to the college ground, allowing the team to adapt to open-stage dynamics. The final rehearsals were conducted at the Manekshaw Parade Ground, simulating the actual event conditions and audience scale.\\n\\nThe dance performance was designed as a theme-based narrative, integrating multiple Indian dance forms to represent the diversity, culture, and unity of the nation. Classical, folk, and contemporary dance styles were blended to create a visually engaging and emotionally impactful performance. Each segment of the dance symbolically represented social development, national progress, and empowerment.\\n\\nA unique aspect of the event was the promotion of five free welfare schemes introduced by the government. Instead of conventional speeches, the awareness messages were conveyed through expressive movements, formations, and music, making them easily understandable and memorable for the audience. This creative approach ensured that the information reached people from different age groups and backgrounds effectively.\\n\\nThe final performance was held in the presence of distinguished dignitaries, including Honourable Chief Minister Sri Siddaramaiah and the Honourable Governor of the State. Performing before such eminent leaders added immense responsibility and pride to the participants. The event drew a large audience, including government officials, students, and members of the public, making it a high-impact public outreach programme.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/Y1ye5vmOYkxtnybwQNPR6.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_e8F5potrX1cPorUfoPAI","name":"Plantation Drive @ Hosadurga","slNo":2,"place":"Hosadurga","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/TNhUsyIkR9Wu_M73r5NQU.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/vDRX0BzKp511QnzgXtYgP.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Environmental Impact:\\nPlanting over 1,000 saplings in a single day significantly contributed to increasing green cover in the Kanakapura region and supporting local biodiversity.\\n\\nSustainability Awareness:\\nThe activity reinforced the importance of tree plantation and conservation, encouraging participants to adopt eco-friendly practices in daily life.\\n\\nCommunity Support:\\nActive assistance to local workers helped reduce manual workload and promoted collaboration between the team and the local community.\\n\\nTeamwork and Leadership:\\nCoordinating a large-scale plantation drive in one day enhanced skills such as planning, teamwork, time management, and leadership.\\n\\nSocial Responsibility:\\nThe event strengthened the sense of civic duty and environmental responsibility among participants.\\n\\nImmediate Plant Survival:\\nProper watering and planting techniques improved the chances of sapling survival, increasing the long-term success of the drive.\\n\\nPersonal Contribution:\\nPersonal involvement in planting and watering plants provided a strong sense of fulfillment and responsibility toward environmental conservation.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-09","hoursSpent":12,"description":"A large-scale plantation drive was actively undertaken near Hosadurga, Karnataka, with the objective of promoting environmental sustainability, increasing green cover, and supporting local ecological balance. The initiative was carried out as a team-based social responsibility activity, emphasizing hands-on participation and community engagement.\\n\\nThe plantation drive was completed in a single day, during which more than 1,000 saplings were planted across the identified area. The activity involved coordinated planning and efficient execution to ensure maximum coverage within a limited timeframe. Saplings of suitable native and fast-growing plant species were selected to improve survival rates and long-term environmental benefits.\\n\\nI personally participated in the plantation process, which included digging pits, planting saplings, and watering them immediately after planting to ensure proper soil settlement and initial nourishment. Special attention was given to watering the plants thoroughly, recognizing its importance in enhancing sapling survival during the early growth stage.\\n\\nAn important aspect of the drive was supporting and working alongside local workers from the Kanakapura region. The team assisted them in physically demanding tasks, shared responsibilities, and coordinated efforts to complete the plantation efficiently. This collaboration strengthened community involvement and fostered mutual respect between students and local residents.\\n\\nThe drive not only focused on planting saplings but also emphasized environmental awareness, highlighting the importance of afforestation, climate change mitigation, and sustainable land use. Participants were briefed on the long-term responsibility of plant care, encouraging continued monitoring and maintenance wherever possible.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/iML0x2ciWaJBPD7awRuox.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lVW2u69OvtSEB8F1hpM1X","name":"Road Safety Awareness","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/YEIb-bAvOIcikM9B8fuOq.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/0RtOpSHiznRwdxjaIoKZi.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/QHTMdlyZpAnbXluYfY0Zt.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"Improved Road Safety Awareness:\\nParticipants gained a clear understanding of traffic rules and the importance of responsible road behavior.\\n\\nLife-Saving Skills Development:\\nHands-on CPR and first aid training equipped participants with essential skills to respond effectively during road accidents.\\n\\nConfidence in Emergency Situations:\\nIndividual practice sessions increased confidence in handling accident scenarios and providing immediate assistance.\\n\\nAccident Preparedness:\\nParticipants learned systematic steps to follow during emergencies, reducing panic and improving response time.\\n\\nSocial Responsibility:\\nThe program encouraged participants to act as responsible citizens and first responders in their communities.\\n\\nPractical Learning Experience:\\nLive demonstrations combined with supervised practice ensured better retention and real-world applicability of knowledge.\\n\\nAwareness Multiplication:\\nParticipants were motivated to share road safety rules and first aid knowledge with peers and family, extending the program’s impact.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":10,"description":"A Road Safety Awareness Program was conducted with the objective of educating participants about traffic rules, accident prevention, and emergency response procedures. The program focused on creating awareness about responsible road behavior and equipping participants with life-saving first aid skills, particularly for accident situations.\\n\\nThe session began with a detailed explanation of traffic rules and regulations, including the importance of wearing helmets and seat belts, obeying traffic signals, speed limits, pedestrian safety, and the dangers of drunk and distracted driving. Real-life scenarios and common causes of road accidents were discussed to highlight how negligence and lack of awareness contribute to serious injuries and fatalities.\\n\\nA major component of the program was first aid and emergency response training. The instructors explained what immediate actions should be taken when an accident occurs, such as ensuring personal safety, assessing the victim’s condition, calling emergency services, and controlling bleeding. Special emphasis was placed on Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR), explaining when and how it should be administered.\\n\\nTo enhance practical understanding, live demonstrations were conducted, where trained professionals showed the correct techniques for CPR and basic first aid. After the demonstration, participants were given hands-on individual training, allowing each person to practice the procedures under supervision. This ensured proper posture, hand placement, and correct execution of life-saving techniques.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/Qv_BkPKFsLIS-X353sebU.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"X1KXFc560hCB7yh2n1I0D","name":"Female Foeticide Walkathon","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/_rW2mAu--J4RGaSU-bB9t.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/qvNJYKv8ctiFzJXjMtCkb.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/Ljn9V0YmcR5GXPXG_ROe6.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Public Awareness:\\nThe walkathon effectively raised awareness among the public about the seriousness of female foeticide and the need to protect the rights of the girl child.\\n\\nSocial Impact:\\nThe event encouraged people to rethink gender-based discrimination and promoted positive attitudes toward gender equality.\\n\\nYouth Participation:\\nActive involvement of students strengthened youth engagement in addressing critical social issues.\\n\\nCommunity Interaction:\\nDirect interaction with the public helped communicate messages in a relatable and impactful manner.\\n\\nPromotion of Ethical Values:\\nThe event reinforced values of equality, dignity, and respect for women in society.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was conducted by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) with the primary objective of creating public awareness about the social issue of female foeticide and the importance of gender equality. The event aimed to educate society on the ethical, social, and legal consequences of gender-based discrimination and to promote respect for the girl child.\\n\\nThe walkathon was organized in public areas to ensure maximum visibility and public engagement. Participants walked together carrying placards, posters, and awareness messages highlighting the importance of saving the girl child, equal rights for women, and the need to eliminate gender bias from society. Slogans and messages were used to communicate the seriousness of the issue in a peaceful and impactful manner.\\n\\nThe walkathon served as a platform to directly interact with the public and encourage people to reflect on the long-term societal consequences of female foeticide, such as gender imbalance and social inequality. Volunteers actively explained the purpose of the walkathon to bystanders, helping spread awareness in an approachable and meaningful way.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/Y0lflos7l-T65dX8S3ZUT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GfvmaynbRsKTDjvofqIU5","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/PNDutdkc1Z1Qn8z-rwQgu.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Support for a Social Cause:\\nThe marathon contributed toward providing assistance to a child in need, demonstrating the impact of collective effort.\\n\\nPromotion of Social Responsibility:\\nParticipants developed a stronger sense of empathy and civic duty through active involvement in a humanitarian initiative.\\n\\nEncouragement of Fitness and Well-being:\\nThe event promoted physical fitness while aligning health with social service.\\n\\nVolunteer Engagement:\\nNSS volunteers gained experience in event organization, leadership, and teamwork.\\n\\nCommunity Awareness:\\nThe marathon attracted public attention, helping spread awareness about social causes and charitable initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":10,"description":"NSS RVCE organized the Utsarga Marathon on 4th February 2024 with the noble objective of supporting a child in need through a social cause–oriented marathon. The event aimed to combine physical fitness with social responsibility, encouraging participants to contribute toward a meaningful humanitarian cause.\\n\\nThe marathon witnessed active participation from students, volunteers, and supporters who came together to run for a cause. Prior to the event, participants were briefed about the purpose of the marathon, highlighting how collective efforts and contributions could positively impact a child’s life. The event emphasized values of compassion, empathy, and selfless service.\\n\\nVolunteers from NSS RVCE played a key role in organizing and managing the event, including participant coordination, route management, safety arrangements, and crowd guidance. The marathon was conducted in an orderly and disciplined manner, ensuring participant safety while maintaining the spirit of social service.\\n\\nThrough this initiative, NSS RVCE successfully used a public platform to spread awareness about social responsibility and the importance of extending help to those in need.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/EDpvkdPlhpdeBe4yPDOaM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"p0a2QwLZih3BBjB1Wpyrf","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/AhbQRa4N4M_aF_O0P1weL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"A significant number of students and staff participated voluntarily, reflecting strong social awareness within the RVCE community.\\n\\nMultiple units of blood were successfully collected and handed over to the partnering blood bank for use in emergency and critical medical cases.\\n\\nThe camp helped create awareness about regular blood donation and motivated many first-time donors.\\n\\nRotaract members gained valuable experience in event management, teamwork, and community service.\\n\\nThe initiative strengthened RVCE’s commitment to social welfare and humanitarian service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE), in collaboration with a recognized blood bank and healthcare professionals, successfully organized a Blood Donation Camp on the college campus. The initiative aimed to promote social responsibility, humanitarian values, and awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation among students, faculty, and staff.\\n\\nThe camp was conducted in a well-organized and hygienic environment, following all medical safety protocols. Trained doctors, nurses, and volunteers ensured proper screening, counseling, and post-donation care for all donors. Rotaract members actively coordinated donor registration, crowd management, and awareness activities, ensuring a smooth and efficient process throughout the event.\\n\\nThe drive emphasized the message that a single unit of blood can save multiple lives, encouraging first-time donors to participate and helping dispel myths related to blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/KJT6tIIne4myN8FY05Yjf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NPoUz4K-r7sjwvFoTm4pN","name":"Fistful","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/r4KVjsVp8aQoe8Th11ak2.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/4HAkQOhImgMaH4hxZgnxu.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The Fist Full drive successfully collected essential food grains, including rice and toor dal, which were distributed to an orphanage to support the nutritional needs of underprivileged children. The event fostered a strong sense of compassion, generosity, and social responsibility among participants. It also enhanced teamwork and organizational skills among Rotaract members while strengthening RVCE’s commitment to community welfare and sustainable social initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Fist Full initiative was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE from 15th November 2024 to 29th November 2024 with the objective of addressing food insecurity and supporting underprivileged children. The drive encouraged students, faculty, and staff to contribute a fistful of food grains as an act of kindness and social responsibility.\\n\\nAs part of the campaign, participants were requested to donate either 10 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, depending on their capacity. The collection was carried out systematically over the two-week period, with Rotaract volunteers coordinating collection, storage, and documentation of the donated food items. Awareness was spread across the campus through announcements and peer interaction to maximize participation.\\n\\nThe collected food grains were later intended to be distributed to a local orphanage, ensuring that the contributions directly benefited children in need. The initiative promoted the values of sharing, empathy, and community service among students.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GQTkGy20gSBCzvj9fcx-R","name":"Yoga Day","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/JwI8KKHw7qQyYb8q93Ozw.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The International Yoga Day program helped participants understand the importance of yoga in maintaining physical fitness and mental well-being. Regular practice of yoga postures, breathing exercises, and meditation enabled students and staff to experience reduced stress levels, improved concentration, and better flexibility. The event encouraged participants to adopt yoga as a part of their daily lifestyle for long-term health benefits. It also strengthened the sense of discipline, mindfulness, and self-awareness among the attendees. Through this initiative, Rotaract RVCE successfully promoted a culture of wellness and holistic development within the campus community.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-21","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) organized the International Yoga Day celebration on 21st June 2024 at the RVCE campus. The event was conducted to promote physical fitness, mental well-being, and awareness about the importance of yoga in leading a healthy and balanced lifestyle.\\n\\nThe session was led by a certified yoga instructor who guided participants through various yogic practices, including asanas, pranayama, and meditation. Rotaract volunteers ensured active participation and proper coordination throughout the program. Students, faculty members, and staff enthusiastically took part in the session, following the instructions with discipline and focus.\\n\\nThe event highlighted yoga as an effective means to reduce stress, improve concentration, and enhance overall health, especially for students managing academic and personal responsibilities.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"G_ctbLlexopU-FIKPTCTX","name":"Campus Cleanup","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/CvbnviAjyq4Bd8v1eLU9N.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The clean-up drive resulted in a visibly cleaner and more hygienic campus, especially the college ground and nearby areas. The activity created awareness among students about the importance of cleanliness and environmental conservation. It encouraged a sense of social responsibility, teamwork, and discipline among the volunteers. The initiative also motivated students to maintain cleanliness on a regular basis, contributing to a healthier and more pleasant learning environment at RVCE.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-13","hoursSpent":6,"description":"A campus clean-up drive was conducted at RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on 13th January 2024 with the objective of maintaining cleanliness and promoting environmental responsibility among students. NSS volunteers actively participated in cleaning the campus premises and the surrounding areas of the college. The drive covered walkways, academic blocks, open spaces, and the entire college ground. Volunteers collected litter, segregated waste where possible, and ensured proper disposal. The activity emphasized the importance of hygiene, waste management, and collective responsibility in maintaining a clean and healthy campus environment.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/MNes7wa1ehPXCJZT3c4su.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"IWgE8eGnbJzbquVQUoJqR","name":"Tshirt for Smile and Orphanage Visit ","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/0yr24q7NCrMUJyUVeYNkx.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-07","duration":4,"outcomes":"The activities of Kannada Sangha resulted in multiple positive outcomes at both individual and institutional levels. The donation of surplus funds to an orphanage created a meaningful social impact and reinforced the importance of giving back to society. Members developed a strong sense of responsibility, empathy, and ethical decision-making through transparent fund management and charitable contribution. Active involvement in organizing Kannada Habba enhanced leadership, coordination, and teamwork skills among volunteers. The initiatives also strengthened cultural identity and pride in Kannada language and heritage within the campus. Overall, the activities contributed to the successful execution of a major cultural event at RVCE while promoting social awareness and community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The Kannada Sangha of RV College of Engineering (RVCE) actively carried out a combination of cultural, organizational, and social service activities, reflecting its commitment to promoting Kannada language and culture while contributing positively to society.\\n\\nAs part of its internal activities, the Kannada Sangha collected funds from its members for the purpose of designing and distributing Kannada Sangha T-shirts, which served as a symbol of unity, cultural identity, and pride in Kannada heritage. The fund collection process was carried out transparently and responsibly, ensuring that all necessary expenses related to the T-shirts were met.\\n\\nAfter the completion of the T-shirt distribution, the remaining balance amount was consciously allocated for social welfare. This surplus amount was donated to an orphanage, demonstrating the Sangha’s intention to extend support beyond campus activities and contribute meaningfully to the well-being of underprivileged children. Members personally took part in coordinating the donation, reinforcing values of empathy, compassion, and social responsibility.\\n\\nIn addition to the donation initiative, Kannada Sangha members played a crucial role in the planning and execution of the college cultural fest “Kannada Habba.” Volunteers actively assisted in various aspects such as event setup, stage management, coordination with performers, audience management, and smooth conduct of cultural programs. The fest provided a platform to showcase Kannada art, literature, music, and traditions, fostering cultural awareness among students from diverse backgrounds.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/5OYGlAUMmBqQokRKIXAPS.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4qeobTvOyUrOM5G-cl9xx","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Ke Liye","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/jqi0nPRrZdjxstNBxF2cT.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/0vNn5TdnfJhOiS8x1720I.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The campaign successfully increased awareness among first-time voters about the importance of participating in elections. Students gained clarity on the voting process and developed a sense of civic responsibility and national commitment. The initiative motivated young voters to register and actively participate in upcoming elections. Through this campaign, NSS RVCE effectively contributed to strengthening democratic values and encouraging informed and responsible voting among youth.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” campaign was organized at RV College of Engineering (RVCE) on 06th March 2024 by the Government, in collaboration with NSS RVCE, with the objective of encouraging first-time voters and young citizens to actively participate in the democratic process. The campaign aimed to create awareness about the importance of voting and the role of youth in strengthening democracy.\\n\\nThe event included awareness sessions explaining the voting process, voter registration, ethical voting practices, and the significance of informed decision-making. NSS volunteers actively guided students, especially new voters, on the responsibilities of being a citizen and the impact of each vote on the nation’s future. Informative messages, banners, and interactions were used to motivate students to exercise their voting rights without fear or influence.\\n\\nThe campaign emphasized that voting is not just a right but a responsibility, inspiring students to become active and responsible participants in democratic governance.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/gsc3z8RD8UpgdA2zkx2Le.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"24-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pd1xaOMiA7DU65PcrOnDQ","name":"Tanuja Movie Screening","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/gUqDPm6BcQI4AQe0dXL6o.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/URTu3XAJlcr9E8cpKvA1b.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The film screening successfully created awareness about the mental and emotional challenges faced by NEET aspirants. Participants developed greater empathy toward students undergoing academic pressure and understood the importance of mental health awareness and support. The event encouraged open conversations about stress management and responsible guidance for students. It also reinforced NSS RVCE’s role in promoting socially relevant issues and using creative approaches to educate the campus community.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"NSS RVCE organized a special screening of the film Tanuja on 14th July 2023 at the RVCE campus with the objective of creating public awareness about the challenges faced by NEET examination aspirants. The film highlights the intense academic pressure, emotional stress, and mental health struggles experienced by students preparing for highly competitive entrance examinations.\\n\\nThe screening was arranged as part of a social awareness initiative to encourage meaningful discussions on student well-being, mental health support, and the need for a balanced approach toward academic success. Students, faculty members, and staff attended the screening, which provided a realistic and emotional portrayal of the difficulties encountered by young aspirants.\\n\\nFollowing the screening, discussions were encouraged to help viewers reflect on the themes presented in the film, including parental expectations, societal pressure, and the importance of emotional support systems. Through this initiative, NSS RVCE used cinema as a medium to educate and sensitize the audience toward a critical social and educational issue.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DRI0WaOV_EYbeZtvMvUlF","name":"Yoga Day","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/JgBk-eVXXpSDFuQpcuxzU.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/75afc4cc-1967-49cb-99df-8ded4f9b477c/Q7HGlLTbTm7gH42IfWHGw.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Yoga Day event helped participants understand the significance of yoga in improving physical flexibility, concentration, and mental peace. The session encouraged students to adopt yoga as a regular habit for stress management and overall well-being. The initiative strengthened awareness about healthy living and reflected NSS RVCE’s commitment to holistic development and wellness on campus.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-21","hoursSpent":4,"description":"NSS RVCE organized the International Yoga Day program on 21st June 2004 at the RVCE campus with the aim of promoting physical health, mental well-being, and a balanced lifestyle among students. The event focused on spreading awareness about the importance of yoga in maintaining overall wellness and managing stress.\\n\\nParticipants were guided through various yoga asanas, breathing exercises (pranayama), and meditation practices under proper instruction. NSS volunteers coordinated the event and ensured active participation, discipline, and smooth conduct of the session. The program highlighted yoga as a traditional practice with long-term benefits for both physical fitness and mental clarity.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-30","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 17:10:46.948312+00', '2026-02-02 02:21:14.068721+00'), ('e541997d-6a09-4a71-badc-0b9b11a65638', '20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS205","name":"Srivishnu P N","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"_STjW0tJ52K7ZMakkJ4D7","name":"Infosys Visit","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-09-04","duration":5,"outcomes":"During the visit to Infosys, I learned how large IT organizations work in real time, including software development workflows, corporate culture, project management, and the importance of teamwork, communication, and industry-ready skills.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-08-31","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The industry visit to Infosys provided students with practical exposure to real-time IT infrastructure, software development practices, and enterprise-level project management. The visit helped bridge the gap between academic learning and industry requirements through interaction with professionals and observation of live systems.","aicteMapping":"AICTE Category: Industry Visit (Exposure to Industrial Operations & Technology)","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/Ln0Y_CfY75-ja05ofi-QW.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Iqot-A9XiJ5SUzVy301Q5","name":"Environmental Day Quiz ","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE ","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-12-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced students’ critical thinking, problem-solving abilities, and\\ngeneral awareness across a wide range of topics. Participants developed confidence in quick\\ndecision-making and logical reasoning while engaging in a competitive yet collaborative\\nlearning environment. The quiz also promoted peer interaction, teamwork, and intellectual\\ncuriosity among students from different academic backgrounds. Overall, Under the Peepal Tree\\ncontributed to the holistic development of students by encouraging continuous learning, active\\nparticipation, and a strong culture of academic excellence within the institution, aligning with\\nAICTE’s objectives of promoting student engagement and intellectual growth.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-12-09","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Under the flagship quiz event organized at the college that brings together\\nstudents from diverse disciplines to participate in an intellectually stimulating and competitive\\nenvironment. The event is designed to encourage analytical thinking, general awareness, and\\ninterdisciplinary knowledge through multiple engaging quiz rounds. Conducted in an open\\nand interactive setting, the quiz promotes curiosity, teamwork, and healthy competition among\\nparticipants. By providing a platform for students to test their knowledge beyond classroom\\nlearning,  plays a significant role in fostering a vibrant academic culture and enhancing student engagement across the campus.","aicteMapping":"Spread awareness about environment and best practices towards SDG''s.","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/BikJnkOGiykbbYmlv4fOI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Vx9iLa46mPGTcLsaNFIuh","name":"Industry Visit - RTPS and YTPS","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-04-05","duration":5,"outcomes":"From the visit to RTPS and YTPS power plants, I learned about thermal power generation, plant operations, safety measures, and how electricity is produced, controlled, and transmitted on a large scale, giving me practical insight into energy systems and industrial engineering.","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-04-01","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The visit to RTPS and YTPS Power Plants enabled students to understand large-scale power generation processes, plant operations, safety protocols, and control systems, offering valuable insight into industrial engineering and energy management practices.","aicteMapping":"the visit to RTPS and YTPS Power Plants enabled students to understand large-scale power generation processes, plant operations, safety protocols, and control systems, offering valuable insight into industrial engineering and energy management practices.","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/BWjlaRr1AsZ-z-LjWh0Eo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pXs9mSsiT6CDUYhKjE4Od","name":"Under The Peepal Tree 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event successfully enhanced students’ critical thinking, problem-solving abilities, and\\ngeneral awareness across a wide range of topics. Participants developed confidence in quick\\ndecision-making and logical reasoning while engaging in a competitive yet collaborative\\nlearning environment. The quiz also promoted peer interaction, teamwork, and intellectual\\ncuriosity among students from different academic backgrounds. Overall, Under the Peepal Tree\\ncontributed to the holistic development of students by encouraging continuous learning, active\\nparticipation, and a strong culture of academic excellence within the institution, aligning with\\nAICTE’s objectives of promoting student engagement and intellectual growth.","semester":"4","startDate":"2025-05-25","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Under the Peepal Tree is a flagship quiz event organized at the college that brings together\\nstudents from diverse disciplines to participate in an intellectually stimulating and competitive\\nenvironment. The event is designed to encourage analytical thinking, general awareness, and\\ninterdisciplinary knowledge through multiple engaging quiz rounds. Conducted in an open\\nand interactive setting, the quiz promotes curiosity, teamwork, and healthy competition among\\nparticipants. By providing a platform for students to test their knowledge beyond classroom\\nlearning, Under the Peepal Tree plays a significant role in fostering a vibrant academic culture\\nand enhancing student engagement across the campus.","aicteMapping":"Professional Society Activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/Wn6QvZW9ju4wflvzNyLnr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"P9l9HEewIF-flWaVQABpW","name":"IEEE Hack4Soc 2.0","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/dyHU5pp5c2iLx7iBa1R9z.png"],"endDate":"2023-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Induction Programme successfully helped freshers transition smoothly into the academic\\nenvironment by providing essential information, guidance, and peer support. New students\\ndeveloped a sense of belonging and confidence, enabling them to adapt more effectively\\nto university life and academic expectations. Student organizers enhanced their leadership,\\ncommunication, and organizational skills while fostering an inclusive and supportive campus\\nculture.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-10-01","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Participation in the Induction Programme for freshers by students of SPARK, the IUCEE–RVCE\\nStudent Chapter, was a crucial initiative that fostered a sense of community and support\\nwithin the academic institution. The event served as a warm welcome for incoming students,\\nproviding essential information, guidance, and a platform to acclimate to the university\\nenvironment. Student organizers played a pivotal role in facilitating a smooth transition for the\\nnewcomers, aiding their integration into the academic community. Awarding AICTE Activity\\nPoints for involvement in the Induction Programme is warranted, as it recognizes students’\\nactive contribution to the well-being and inclusivity of the academic community, aligning\\nwith AICTE’s goal of nurturing a holistic educational environment that prioritizes student\\nengagement and support.","aicteMapping":"Professional Society Activities","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/_DBNVgNwGoTE13zrvN7oo.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"aIj3R99nttgNqtVx1tSLm","name":"Tech tank","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-06-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Exposure to real world problems and tools used to overcome them. Learnt various techniques and got the opportunity to work with industry leading experts.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-01","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Attended a hackthon based on solving real world problems.","aicteMapping":"Participating in hackathons to solve real world challenges.","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/v1B2do00qvzESwtcWkDHB.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gCoqzjmbRD-W86_nEHseS","name":"Project Pusthak 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"Project Pustak was an initiative dedicated to supporting underprivileged children by providing\\nessential educational resources such as books and study materials, helping to reduce barriers\\nto learning. The project aimed to promote equal educational opportunities for students from\\neconomically weaker backgrounds and encourage their academic growth. Overall, Project\\nPustak created meaningful impact by combining educational support for children with hands-on\\ncommunity service for volunteers.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE launched \"PROJECT PUSTAK,\" a community service initiative\\naimed at providing educational kits to underprivileged children. These kits included essential\\nschool supplies, books, and learning tools designed to empower students and create\\nopportunities for a brighter future. The project sought to break down barriers to education,\\nemphasizing the belief that education is a fundamental right and not a privilege.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/pRknHAdhV5NYI47NE7cuN.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-CqRLPAGPS1-xBE5PPSc_","name":"Walkathon ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus , Vidhan Soudha - Cubbon Park","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed awareness about wildlife conservation and environmental protection.\\n\\nImproved sense of social responsibility and civic engagement.\\n\\nGained understanding of the importance of biodiversity and sustainability.\\n\\nEnhanced teamwork, participation, and community involvement skills.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-21","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Participated in a wildlife awareness walkathon organized from Vidhana Soudha to Cubbon Park.\\nThe event aimed to promote wildlife conservation and environmental responsibility.\\nActively contributed by spreading awareness among the public on protecting biodiversity.\\nThe activity enhanced social responsibility and environmental consciousness.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/Uhe9oeAlaOFfl9VvVxLJk.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ne6VD3u4IVNO0uBqjBpUo","name":"Art of Living – YES+ Course","slNo":9,"place":"Art of living International Center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/GEaZfub1g64RzRapa2rd9.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/f-n7HQMHqQnPUFYQGLidG.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-30","duration":9,"outcomes":"The course enhanced practical techniques to manage stress, improve concentration, and\\nmaintain emotional well-being. The course enhanced my self-awareness, resilience, and ability\\nto stay calm under pressure. It also emphasized the importance of mental health in leading a\\nbalanced and productive life.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-22","hoursSpent":6,"description":"On completing the YES+ Youth Empowerment Seminar conducted by the Art of Living, which\\nincluded sessions on mental health awareness under the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative. The program\\ninvolved guided meditation, breathing techniques, and interactive sessions focused on stress\\nmanagement, emotional balance, and self-awareness","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/q0xmCVoGWIsrc_0d6x49Z.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2NGg62Ok-y-3CMB_XphJU","name":"Art of Living – Horticulture Seva","slNo":10,"place":"Art of living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/0EFXQxgtXY8czlSqSgTdW.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/IJiNFcABtQa9sUIJ2GhUq.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity strengthened awareness about environmental conservation and the importance of\\nmaintaining green spaces. It reinforced the value of sustainability, patience, and responsibility\\nwhile contributing to a healthier and greener environment.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-21","hoursSpent":6,"description":"As part of the YES+ Youth Empowerment Seminar at the Art of Living International Center,\\nBengaluru, I participated in a horticulture service activity aimed at promoting environmental\\nsustainability and ecological responsibility. The initiative involved watering plants, sowing\\nseeds, and nurturing trees within the campus to support green cover and biodiversity. The activity\\ncreated an atmosphere of environmental awareness and collective responsibility toward nature.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/hyCtDoGZZ-4QMfXU2PHBh.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"t4JfQaLtEaROuOLdq6js4","name":"Art of Living –Community Kitchen & Cleanliness Seva","slNo":11,"place":"Art of living ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/v5-I1TaKYuv46EpwGBSt9.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"This initiative fostered teamwork, discipline, and a strong sense of social responsibility. It raised\\nawareness about hygiene, public cleanliness, and the impact of small community efforts in\\ncreating a healthier environment for everyone.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"During the YES+ program at the Art of Living International Center, I volunteered in a\\ncommunity service initiative that included working in the community kitchen and participating\\nin a cleanliness drive outside the ashram premises. The kitchen service involved food preparation\\nsupport, serving meals, and maintaining hygiene, while the outdoor drive focused on collecting\\nlitter and promoting cleanliness in surrounding public areas. The activity highlighted the dignity\\nof labor and the importance of civic responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/oOP5G0JweWmUq9u7k__oJ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"otXx4pp1BwXiGUxAC0UqC","name":"Art of Living – Gaushala Service","slNo":12,"place":"Art of living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/l00ntR1VR3qTGA9n_rjji.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/EewlNVIDKTiwVwkaovKla.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"The service deepened awareness about animal care, biodiversity, and sustainable agricultural\\npractices. It reinforced compassion, responsibility, and the importance of maintaining harmony\\nbetween humans, animals, and nature.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-21","hoursSpent":6,"description":"As part of the YES+ Youth Empowerment initiative, I participated in Gaushala service at the Art\\nof Living International Center, Bengaluru. The activity focused on caring for indigenous cows\\nthrough feeding assistance and maintaining cleanliness in the shelter. It emphasized the cultural,\\nagricultural, and ecological significance of preserving native cattle breeds and promoting animal\\nwelfare.","aicteMapping":"Participated in community service focused on cow welfare and Goshala maintenance.","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/xQQ-lySHQY1Xqiy-NWuif.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"95ovauWC199r9JGjCbIzi","name":"Art of Living –Permaculture & Soil Awareness Activity","slNo":13,"place":"Art of living International center","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/QwczSwCr68PwcslibTx0s.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/XieLt4U5Y3KmxJIB-hQtX.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-13","duration":2,"outcomes":"The activity increased awareness about sustainable farming, soil health, and environmental\\nconservation. It reinforced the value of eco-friendly practices and the role of individuals in\\nsupporting a sustainable future.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-12","hoursSpent":6,"description":"As part of the YES+ initiative at the Art of Living International Center, I participated in\\na permaculture awareness activity aimed at promoting sustainable agricultural practices and\\nsoil conservation. The session focused on improving soil quality through natural methods\\nand understanding the importance of ecological balance in food production. The initiative\\nencouraged environmentally responsible practices for long-term sustainability","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/20e85e9d-2b04-404e-b863-b11c015b7673/PWbe9c6IAkdcQqAlbAO6y.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Neethu S","designation":"Counsellor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 15:48:09.611927+00', '2026-01-31 14:11:07.533744+00'), ('e5a264de-6f66-47f6-ab55-8e37f48bef3c', 'e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS212","name":"Suyash Alva ","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"CqQB19D5pXvlz0G9RiBZx","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":1,"place":"Biotech Quadrangle","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/i6nB-dFiIbE22p9xZ2Xx4.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/vf5eN8oTi0ueD_B3WU-Ls.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-20","duration":4,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant\\nquantity of rice through the contribution of 5 kg from each\\nparticipant. It helped provide food support to\\nunderprivileged communities and addressed issues related\\nto hunger and food insecurity. The drive created\\nawareness about the importance of sharing and social\\nresponsibility among students. Participants developed\\nempathy, teamwork, and a strong sense of community\\nservice. Overall, the initiative made a meaningful social\\nimpact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and\\nhumanitarian service on campus.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of\\nRVCE with the aim of supporting the underprivileged and\\npromoting social responsibility among students. In this drive,\\nstudents and volunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice,\\nsymbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of food to those in\\nneed. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and\\nhunger faced by many sections of society. It encouraged\\nparticipants to share resources selflessly and develop a habit of\\ngiving back to the community. The drive also strengthened\\nvalues of empathy, kindness, and unity among the students. The\\ncollected rice was planned to be distributed to needy\\ncommunities through charitable organizations. The drive\\nwitnessed enthusiastic participation, showcasing strong\\nteamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided\\nstudents with an opportunity to actively engage in social service\\nactivities. The initiative highlighted how even small\\ncontributions can collectively create a significant positive\\nimpact. Overall, the Fist Full Drive successfully reinforced the\\nspirit of service, compassion, and social responsibility within\\nthe campus","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/b7_6VGzx6whzOg7ONDHK2.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nF3vNouuOzsLSfK8Sh1t3","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":2,"place":"Biotech Quadrangle","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/DDCoiGcIjpq3BWwZTcmLG.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/xxvfCBSxORtGukXg-ux88.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-23","duration":7,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant\\nquantity of rice through the contribution of 5 kg from each\\nparticipant. It helped provide food support to\\nunderprivileged communities and addressed issues related\\nto hunger and food insecurity. The drive created\\nawareness about the importance of sharing and social\\nresponsibility among students. Participants developed\\nempathy, teamwork, and a strong sense of community\\nservice. Overall, the initiative made a meaningful social\\nimpact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and\\nhumanitarian service on campus.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of\\nRVCE with the aim of supporting the underprivileged and\\npromoting social responsibility among students. In this drive,\\nstudents and volunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice,\\nsymbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of food to those in\\nneed. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and\\nhunger faced by many sections of society. It encouraged\\nparticipants to share resources selflessly and develop a habit of\\ngiving back to the community. The drive also strengthened\\nvalues of empathy, kindness, and unity among the students. The\\ncollected rice was planned to be distributed to needy\\ncommunities through charitable organizations. The drive\\nwitnessed enthusiastic participation, showcasing strong\\nteamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided\\nstudents with an opportunity to actively engage in social service\\nactivities. The initiative highlighted how even small\\ncontributions can collectively create a significant positive\\nimpact. Overall, the Fist Full Drive successfully reinforced the\\nspirit of service, compassion, and social responsibility within\\nthe campus.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/H5ZtsGSc8TDVIx89HT5n_.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Yijw8bvDDkc57XXNtqfRa","name":"DISCOM Core Committee","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/iUDF7HIxuC0wO6t2kzpgM.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/BpL3O-QjduyOMtF-7f4aB.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-20","duration":20,"outcomes":"Participation in the Disciplinary Committee (DISCOM) for 8th Mile provided valuable practical exposure to managing discipline and safety during a large-scale inter-collegiate cultural event. By actively monitoring venues and regulating crowd behavior, the committee contributed significantly to maintaining order and preventing disruptions, ensuring that events progressed smoothly without major incidents.\\n\\nThe role strengthened coordination and communication between multiple stakeholders, including event organizers, security personnel, volunteers, and participants. Effective collaboration enabled quick identification and resolution of on-ground issues, reducing delays and maintaining a structured flow of activities across different event locations and time slots.\\n\\nServing in DISCOM also enhanced leadership and decision-making abilities under high-pressure conditions. Handling conflicts, enforcing rules fairly, and responding to unexpected situations improved problem-solving skills and the ability to remain calm, authoritative, and objective in dynamic environments.\\n\\nOverall, the experience fostered a strong sense of responsibility, discipline, and professionalism. It provided hands-on learning in event governance, crowd management, and operational control, contributing to personal development while supporting the successful and safe execution of 8th Mile at RV College of Engineering.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":30,"description":"I was an active member of the Disciplinary Committee (DISCOM) for 8th Mile, RV College of Engineering’s flagship inter-collegiate cultural festival, which witnessed participation from multiple colleges and a large daily footfall. The role involved ensuring strict adherence to event rules and institutional guidelines to maintain discipline, safety, and smooth conduct across all venues.\\n\\nMy responsibilities included monitoring crowd behavior, managing entry and exit points, coordinating with security personnel and core organizing teams, and responding promptly to on-ground incidents involving participants, volunteers, and attendees. I also assisted in resolving conflicts, preventing rule violations, and handling emergency or high-pressure situations in real time. Close coordination with event heads ensured that disciplinary decisions were implemented fairly and efficiently without disrupting the flow of the event.\\n\\nAdditionally, I contributed to maintaining decorum during high-energy events and peak crowd hours, ensuring that performers, judges, and attendees could participate in a safe and well-regulated environment. The role demanded constant vigilance, quick decision-making, clear communication, and the ability to remain calm and authoritative in dynamic situations.","aicteMapping":"Disciplinary Committee","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/zTQYFAIbelm2c-Pd773PD.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"b0Nnx4tYMjWp3ty3c_eEP","name":"INTEL HACKATHON X E-SUMMIT","slNo":4,"place":"DTL","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/0j5PK0O_iS4mmmP7iIltq.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-09","duration":2,"outcomes":"Participants gained practical exposure to AI tools and concepts,\\nenhanced their technical and problem-solving skills, and devel\\u0002oped a deeper understanding of innovation-driven technologies\\nessential for future careers.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-02-08","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Intel Hackathon, organized by the Entrepreneurship Cell (E\\u0002Cell), was a pioneering, hands-on workshop designed to\\nintroduce participants to the rapidly evolving field of artificial\\nintelligence, with a strong emphasis on open innovation,\\nexperimentation, and collaborative problem-solving. The event\\nbrought together a diverse group of participants, ranging from\\ncomplete beginners to experienced AI enthusiasts, creating an\\ninclusive learning environment that encouraged peer learning and\\nknowledge exchange. Throughout the hackathon, participants\\nengaged in a series of coding challenges, guided hands-on\\nactivities, and interactive learning sessions that bridged the gap\\nbetween theoretical concepts and real-world implementation. The\\nworkshop exposed attendees to emerging AI trends, practical use\\ncases, and industry-relevant tools, enabling them to develop a\\ndeeper understanding of how artificial intelligence can be applied\\nto solve complex, real-world problems across domains.Beyond\\ntechnical skill-building, the hackathon fostered creativity,\\nteamwork, and critical thinking, as participants collaborated to\\nideate, build, and refine solutions under time-bound constraints.\\nBy emphasizing experiential learning, the event empowered\\nparticipants to gain confidence in applying AI technologies and\\nexplore innovative approaches to technological challenges.\\nAligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development\\nGoals, particularly SDG 9 (Industry, Innovation, and\\nInfrastructure) and SDG 4 (Quality Education), the Intel\\nHackathon reflected E-Cell’s commitment to promoting\\ntechnological literacy, innovation-driven education, and\\nsustainable skill development. The event served as a platform to\\ninspire young innovators, strengthen industry–academia\\nengagement, and contribute to the creation of a future-ready,\\ntechnology-enabled workforce.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/RpwaatvPhXbGqYINSVNPx.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2FIUy3qjrtv79D22o-1vn","name":"PANEL DISCUSSION X E-SUMMIT","slNo":5,"place":"EC Seminar Hall/ Main Stage","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/YlUQY7iWpvXp7wXBzrKZx.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants enhanced their problem-solving, critical thinking,\\ncollaboration, and pitching skills while gaining hands-on expo- sure\\nto startup ideation, business model development, and struc- tured\\nentrepreneurial processes.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-02-09","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The E-Summit 2024, a highly anticipated event in the tech and entrepreneurship domain, recently hosted a compelling panel discussion that brought together industry leaders, innovators, and experts. The panel, titled \"Navigating the Future: Tech Trends and Entrepreneurial Opportunities, \"delved into critical fopics shaping the landscape o technology and entrepreneurship. The E-Summit 2024 panel discussion provided a comprehensive and insightful exploration of key issues at the intersection of technology and entrepreneurship. Attendees gained valuable perspectives from industry leaders, fostering a deeper understanding of the challenges and opportunities that lie ahead in the digital age. The event successfully contributed to the ongoing dialogue surrounding innovation, ethics, and the future of technology-driven entrepreneurship.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/DYBHO9skexrmOQFy0WbXC.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ZZnBQ5PFPIBTM6ZVJVprP","name":"STARTUP SAGA X EMBARK","slNo":6,"place":"IEM AUDITORIUM/BT SEMINAR HALL","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/pLd-fD-_hPu7ydQZKD8hF.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Two-Day Innovation Odyssey successfully cultivated an entrepreneurial mindset among participants by exposing them to real-world startup challenges and solution-driven thinking. Students developed a deeper understanding of social entrepreneurship and learned how innovation can be leveraged to create both economic and societal impact.\\n\\nThe event enhanced participants’ practical skills in idea validation, pitching, teamwork, and strategic planning. Interaction with experienced entrepreneurs and industry experts provided clarity on startup fundamentals such as funding mechanisms, branding strategies, and scalability, enabling students to approach entrepreneurship with greater confidence and preparedness.\\n\\nAdditionally, the program fostered collaboration, leadership, and problem-solving abilities through group activities and mentorship-driven learning. Overall, the Innovation Odyssey equipped students with essential entrepreneurial competencies, inspired innovative thinking, and contributed to the development of future-ready innovators capable of thriving in a competitive startup ecosystem.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-07-11","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Two-Day Innovation Odyssey was a dynamic and immersive event designed to ignite and strengthen the entrepreneurial spirit among students, with a strong emphasis on building impactful and sustainable ventures. The program revolved around two flagship events—Startup Saga and Vision Venture—each crafted to provide participants with practical exposure to the entrepreneurial ecosystem.\\n\\nStartup Saga served as a unique platform for budding entrepreneurs to present innovative, socially responsible business ideas under the theme “Support Sphere: Social Entrepreneurship Saga.” The event encouraged participants to identify real-world societal challenges and propose viable startup solutions, fostering creativity, critical thinking, and leadership. Through idea pitching and evaluation, students gained hands-on experience in transforming concepts into structured entrepreneurial proposals.\\n\\nThe event further immersed participants in the complete startup journey through a series of workshops, expert panel discussions, and mentorship sessions. Founders, startup mentors, and industry professionals shared valuable insights on ideation, pitching techniques, funding strategies, branding, and scaling ventures. Vision Venture complemented this by guiding participants to refine their long-term vision, business models, and strategic planning, helping bridge the gap between innovative ideas and market-ready startups.","aicteMapping":"Facilitating 100% digitized money transactions","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/Crmsz0yog6wgiGLYQjrnO.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"f3LvuHgAZGF51deMsxjvB","name":"VISION VENTURE X EMBARK","slNo":7,"place":"BT SEMINAR HALL/ BT Quadrangle","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/dI7BSawc7vTu0nXwu56la.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"The Two-Day Innovation Odyssey, through its Vision Venture track, successfully encouraged participants to apply entrepreneurial and product development thinking to address real-world techno-social challenges. By focusing on the theme “Eco Innovate,” the event promoted sustainability-driven innovation and increased awareness of how emerging technologies can be used responsibly to create solutions with social and environmental impact.\\n\\nParticipants gained hands-on experience across the complete product development lifecycle, including ideation, prototyping, and testing. This practical exposure strengthened their ability to convert abstract ideas into functional, user-centered solutions while considering feasibility, sustainability, and market readiness. Expert mentoring throughout the process enhanced technical competence and design thinking skills.\\n\\nThe event also fostered collaboration, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities by encouraging teamwork and iterative development. Overall, Vision Venture empowered participants with the confidence, skills, and entrepreneurial mindset required to transform innovative concepts into viable ventures, preparing them to contribute meaningfully to the global innovation and startup ecosystem.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-07-11","hoursSpent":5,"description":"A Two-Day Innovation Odyssey is a dynamic event designed to fuel the entrepreneurial spirit, with a focus on building impactful ventures through two flagship events: Startup Saga and Vision Venture.\\nVision Venture provided a platform for all development enthusiasts to create sustainable solutions for techno-social problems worldwide. With its theme of\\n\"Eco Innovate,\" the initiative inspires participants to leverage their product development skills and new technologies to solve societal challenges. Vision Venture, the product development challenge, empowers participants to bring their ideas to life by moving through ideation, prototyping, and testing phases, all while receiving expert guidance to create user-centered, sustainable, and market-ready solutions. Embark promises a transformative experience for innovators looking to turn their visions into tangible ventures.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/DIi0QwjhB1KfIykitvVIl.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fb_UhezW5moKMbmMN-4Ba","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON 2024","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/_mNsN7gAi7cRQOc2Riqnc.jpeg"],"endDate":"2026-02-04","duration":732,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the\\nNSS of RVCE, successfully blended fitness, community\\nengagement, and philanthropy, creating a platform for\\nindividuals to contribute to a meaningful cause while\\npromoting a healthy lifestyle. With enthusiastic\\nparticipation from students, faculty, and fitness\\nenthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful reminder\\nof the importance of collective action in addressing societal\\nchallenges. Runners contributed through their registration\\nfees, which were directed toward a noble cause, such as\\nsupporting underprivileged","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National\\nService Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to\\npromote fitness, community engagement, and social\\nresponsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and\\nfitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a\\nregistration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the\\nproceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as\\nsupporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare\\ninitiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability\\nprojects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being\\nbut also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among\\nparticipants. Beyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes\\nthe spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for\\nindividuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while\\nexperiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon.\\nParticipants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond\\npersonal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in\\nneed. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon\\nincludes well- marked routes, hydration stations, and medical\\nassistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners.\\nOver the years, this initiative has gained widespread support,\\nstrengthening the values of empathy and community service\\nwithin RVCE and beyond","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/PYnldkQelhLGss9IgPuCc.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OayRBKf17R1msW-MAaxvH","name":"World Entrepreneurship Day","slNo":9,"place":"Chemical Seminar Hall","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/SPyZu6LETl6jFfSTG629p.png"],"endDate":"2024-08-22","duration":2,"outcomes":"The celebration of World Entrepreneurs’ Day significantly enhanced students’ understanding of the entrepreneurial ecosystem by exposing them to real-life startup experiences and industry perspectives. Interaction with experienced entrepreneurs helped bridge the gap between academic learning and practical business challenges, enabling participants to gain clarity on the opportunities and risks involved in entrepreneurship.\\n\\nThe panel discussion strengthened students’ awareness of essential entrepreneurial qualities such as innovation, resilience, and leadership. Insights shared by the speakers motivated participants to approach problem-solving with a growth mindset and to view failures as learning opportunities within the entrepreneurial journey.\\n\\nOverall, the event fostered a culture of innovation and enterprise on campus, inspiring students to explore entrepreneurship as a viable career path. It reinforced the role of entrepreneurial thinking in driving societal and economic progress, contributing to the holistic development of future innovators and leaders.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-08-21","hoursSpent":5,"description":"World Entrepreneurs'' Day was celebrated at RV College of Engineering with great enthusiasm with the event organized by the vibrant E-Cell\\nRVCE. The event brought together aspiring entrepreneurs, industry veterans, and students to foster a spirit of innovation and enterprise within the campus. A key event highlight was a panel discussion featuring Arvind Prakash Singh, Founder and CEO of SuperBolt, and Shreesha Sridhar, Chairperson of Project Labs. These distinguished guests shared their invaluable insights into the startup ecosystem, discussing the challenges and opportunities faced by modern entrepreneurs. Their experiences and advice gave students practical knowledge and\\ninspiao) nie F-depe Pasign La itepieheiship. The Session\\nwas informative and motivational, reinforcing the importance of resilience, innovation and leadership the entrepreneurial forme.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e1ecc90a-5406-4177-b5b1-0d39ae1bc116/V32Y_kMVAz2YalVs4w1ha.png","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 09:37:27.198932+00', '2026-01-30 16:18:38.338314+00'), ('e61e5df6-1815-49f8-b34d-afd5127f1f2b', '36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CD001","name":"Abhay GK","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Data Science","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"3xEZ3aBxhZvhbBp7HGRQq","name":"Fast Trek 2023","slNo":1,"place":"Hutridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/IOTujVYW6Q2W7jSWCVuAh.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/QhCViBwkWgkmUiTc84DjS.png"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through the Fast-Trek event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, I learned the importance of social responsibility and teamwork in organizing large-scale events. The experience highlighted how well-planned coordination, safety management, and participant engagement are crucial for the success of any social initiative. Additionally, being part of an event aimed at supporting underprivileged children strengthened my understanding of how student-led efforts can create meaningful social impact while fostering leadership, empathy, and organizational skills.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":15,"description":"Project Summary: Rotaract Club of RVCE conducted one of it''s\\nflagship events Fast-Trek. The event witnessed active participation\\nfrom college students.\\nProject Description: The social cause behind the project was to\\nprovide financial aid to underprivileged children suffering from\\nheart diseases. The event started at 7:30 AM, where all the\\nparticipants boarded the bus to the trek location with great\\nenthusiasm. Safety instructions were provided to all along with basic\\ninformation of the event. The trek was a great success as all the\\nparticipants had a wonderful time surrounded by the scenic hills of\\nHuthridurga Betta and embarked on what would be a very\\nmemorable journey. Breakfast and lunch was provided at the trek\\nlocation for all the participants.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gGhquEprt-acGazlxDywh","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/sdNMxT_gJGh8iUVmQatLv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The success of the camp was ultimately measured by the significant number\\nof blood units collected, which will serve as a vital resource for patients in\\nneed. Beyond the physical contributions, the event served as a powerful\\nreminder of the strength of collective action and the profound impact of\\nhumanitarian service. Being part of this initiative was a deeply fulfilling\\nexperience, leaving a lasting impression of the importance of community\\nspirit and our shared responsibility to save lives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":30,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp, organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in\\ncollaboration with BGS Hospitals, was a highly impactful initiative aimed\\nat fostering social responsibility within the student community. In the days\\nleading up to the event, the Rotaract team worked tirelessly to manage\\nlogistics, coordinate with medical professionals, and spread awareness\\nacross the campus. This preparation created a professional and welcoming\\nenvironment in the BT Quadrangle, where the spirit of service was evident\\nfrom the start.\\nOn the day of the camp, the campus saw a remarkable turnout as students,\\nfaculty, and staff came forward to contribute to this noble cause. The\\nmedical team from BGS Hospitals ensured a safe and efficient process,\\nguiding donors through screening and the donation procedure with\\nimmense care. The atmosphere was further uplifted by the dedication of\\nstudent volunteers who managed registrations and provided post-donation\\nsupport, making the experience particularly reassuring for those donating\\nfor the first time.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"N2nhB5I-2LfwqCCAOx_Rk","name":"Data Remix","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/U92-N9jUuH5nFYldLIeOg.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-10","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through the Data Remix event conducted during DHI Day, I gained hands-on experience in data analysis, data visualization, and interpreting real-world datasets to derive meaningful insights. The event enhanced my ability to communicate analytical findings effectively to a panel of experts and strengthened my understanding of how data-driven decision-making can be aligned with sustainable business practices. Additionally, working on solutions mapped to the UN Sustainable Development Goals helped me develop a holistic perspective that integrates technological innovation with environmental and social responsibility.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-10","hoursSpent":15,"description":"Data Remix is an event comprising Data Analysis and Business Innovation in which\\nstudents of teams of up to 4 people, will be competing for the ultimate prize. This event comprises\\n2 phases, the prior consists of data analysis and data visualization, in which students will be given\\npre processed data sets and tools to provide information and inferences from the available data.\\nThe event involves students using provided datasets to create data visualizations,\\npresenting their findings to judges including Dr. Satish Babu, Dr. Arulalan Rajan, and Dr. Prasad\\nSudhakar. The second phase focuses on students developing sustainable solutions aligned with the\\nUN''s Sustainable Development Goals. The goal is to encourage a holistic approach, combining\\ntechnical advancements with sustainable thinking, promoting a revolutionary mindset that\\nConsiders both environmental and technological aspects in business and technology. The initiative\\naims to inspire students to advance sustainable development while embracing technological\\nprogress.\\nThe teams would be making their final presentations of their Business Innovations and\\nOptimizations, which will be judged. Finally, the closing ceremony will be held during which the\\nVote of Thanks will be given by Dr. Satish Babu, followed by the results and the prize distribution\\nCeremony.\\nDHI DAY is the first event being held by team DHI, the core team & organizers have put\\nn great efforts to organize & prepare for this event. We request you to allot the core team members,\\norganizers and participants some activity points as per what you deem appropriate.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/bkEzv6Tiln9OacK9kVJId.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"llFN7T3lHPR9DdLDgFK0v","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":4,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/KCeVu-7zsmwsTGjvlm3Il.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"Beyond the physical run, UTSARGA ’24 served as a platform to\\nshowcase the critical role of youth in driving meaningful social change\\nthrough accessible yet impactful initiatives. The success of the marathon\\nreinforced the idea that simple acts of service can lead to significant\\npositive shifts in the lives of others. By participating, the RVCE\\ncommunity proved that when individuals unite with a shared vision, they\\ncan truly contribute to a world where every child is supported and\\nempowered.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-03","hoursSpent":20,"description":"UTSARGA ’24, a signature social service and outreach initiative\\norganized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of\\nEngineering, was held under the inspiring theme “Help a Child, Change\\nthe World”. Conducted on February 4th as a charity run titled “Run for\\nTheir Smiles – Marathon Miles,” the event sought to support\\nunderprivileged children while encouraging students to engage in social\\nwelfare. By integrating physical fitness with a noble cause, the initiative\\naimed to foster a culture of social responsibility and raise awareness\\nabout the profound impact of collective action on society.\\nThe event saw an active and enthusiastic turnout as students gathered\\nwith a unified purpose of humanitarian service. Through the miles\\ncovered during the run, participants expressed deep solidarity with\\nchildren in need, demonstrating values of empathy and unity. This\\ncollective effort showcased a strong commitment toward community\\ndevelopment and highlighted the power of the student body in\\nchampioning causes that extend far beyond the campus boundaries.\\n","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"aTJ20tirdDDyHRfTYEQ5w","name":"TEDxRVCE (Mosaic of minds)","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/vvc_1rjDX35TiLrqghS7k.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Ultimately, being part of Mosaic of Minds was a transformative\\njourney that went far beyond simple listening; it was about absorbing\\nconcepts with the potential to reshape one’s mindset and future path.\\nThe experience highlighted the profound power of curiosity and open\\ndialogue in driving creative innovation. It left a lasting impression,\\nserving as a powerful reminder that embracing new ways of thinking is\\nessential for both personal development and meaningful contribution to\\nsociety.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-09","hoursSpent":20,"description":"TEDxRVCE’s Mosaic of Minds was an intellectually stimulating\\nevent that brought together a diverse range of perspectives under the\\ntheme of \"Ideas Worth Spreading.\" Featuring a lineup of entrepreneurs,\\nscientists, artists, and visionaries, the event served as a vibrant platform\\nfor innovation and storytelling. The atmosphere in the auditorium was\\nelectric, filled with students and faculty eager to engage with\\ngroundbreaking insights that spanned across technology, sustainability,\\nand social change.\\nAttending the event with a full-day pass provided an immersive\\nexperience, allowing for a deep dive into back-to-back sessions of\\nthought-provoking and mind-bending talks. Each speaker challenged\\nconventional boundaries, offering fresh outlooks on personal growth\\nand global problem-solving. Beyond the stage, the event was\\nseamlessly organized to include interactive segments and networking\\nbreaks, which fostered a unique environment for exchanging ideas with\\nlike-minded peers and mentors.\\n","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fq8ylm7JiAQvkiYv174eV","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2025","slNo":6,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/b6XIC1clchcNenBhIS44J.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative was meticulously coordinated by the NSS team to ensure a\\nsafe and successful experience for all participants, highlighting the\\ncollege''s dedication to holistic education and social commitment. By\\nparticipating in this marathon, the student body demonstrated that impact\\nis often measured in the miles run and the lives touched. The event\\nconcluded with a renewed sense of responsibility among the youth,\\nproving that simple yet dedicated initiatives like Utsarga hold the\\ntransformative power to create lasting change in society","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":25,"description":"UTSARGA 2025, the flagship charity run organized by the National\\nService Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, continued its\\nimpactful legacy of social service under the theme \"Help a Child, Change\\nthe World\". Building on the success of previous years, the initiative\\nremained a powerful platform for fostering social responsibility among\\nstudents while actively contributing to the welfare of underprivileged\\nchildren. By blending physical endurance with a noble humanitarian\\ncause, the event served as a vibrant reminder of how collective action can\\npave the way for a brighter future for those in need.\\nThe marathon witnessed an incredible surge of energy and participation as\\nstudents, faculty, and community members gathered to \"Run for Their\\nSmiles\". The atmosphere was one of unity and purpose, with participants\\nshowcasing deep empathy and solidarity with the children they were\\nsupporting. This year’s event emphasized not just the importance of\\nphysical fitness, but also the vital role that young innovators and engineers\\nplay in driving meaningful community development through selfless\\nservice and outreach.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"goV6nKSNqsLkFM71Tw2Td","name":"Kannada Sangha T-Shirt and Plantation Drive","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/EaG-VzJQNsCAba9VwTOsi.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/FbE3yIKFdfzpoBEqbuSMu.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"This recent community service event organized by Kannada Sangha titled \"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree. \"This initiative was designed to promote environmental awareness and individual responsibility among students.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":25,"description":"As part of the event, every student who purchased a T-shirt was given a tree sapling along with guidelines on how and where to plant it. The idea was to inspire students to personally contribute to environmental sustainability by planting the saplings they received. The distribution of both T-shirts and saplings was carried out within the college campus.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gF_MtUmj0tl0jEaTiDeIv","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/ROueiBVAAAdT9uaai3Grh.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event witnessed a remarkable and enthusiastic turnout, as students from\\nacross various departments came forward to demonstrate their commitment to\\nhumanitarian service. This collective participation was not merely a logistical\\nsuccess but a powerful reflection of the compassion and unity prevalent within\\nthe RVCE community. Ultimately, SAMVEDNA – 2 served as a poignant\\ntribute to the nation’s martyrs, successfully transforming a day of\\nremembrance into a day of tangible action that will directly support patients in\\nneed and save lives","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-20","hoursSpent":20,"description":"SAMVEDNA – 2, a significant blood donation initiative organized by NSS\\nRVCE, was held as part of the International Blood Donation Awareness\\nCampaign to honor a profound historical milestone. The event solemnly\\ncommemorated the 94th Martyrdom Day of Shaheed Bhagat Singh, Rajguru,\\nand Sukhdev, seeking to channel the spirit of sacrifice exhibited by these\\nnational heroes into a modern act of service. By linking historical legacy with\\ncontemporary social welfare, the organizers aimed to inspire the student body\\nto contribute meaningfully to society through the selfless act of voluntary\\nblood donation.\\nThe primary objective of the initiative was to spread widespread awareness\\nabout the critical importance of blood donation as a life-saving service while\\ninstilling core values of empathy and social responsibility. To ensure a\\nprofessional and secure experience for all participants, the event was\\nconducted in close collaboration with the Mediscope Blood Centre. This\\npartnership guaranteed that the entire donation process was carried out in a\\nstrictly safe, hygienic, and well-supervised environment, meeting the highest\\nmedical standards and providing reassurance to both seasoned and first-time\\ndonors","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Acjxcs_TgOx_uwwqxXeBG","name":"Discom for 8th Mile 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/0PZT9V8pF2aGaq04XFUcD.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-12-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"By participating in 8th Mile 2025 as a Discom, I gained insight into the planning and execution of large-scale cultural events. I observed the importance of coordination among organizing teams, effective crowd control, time management, and adherence to safety protocols. The event also highlighted how teamwork, communication, and discipline contribute to the smooth functioning of high-energy public gatherings. Overall, the experience enhanced my appreciation for event management and the role","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-04","hoursSpent":50,"description":"By participating as member of Discom at 8th Mile 2025, I gained insight into the planning and execution of large-scale cultural events. I observed the importance of coordination among organizing teams, effective crowd control, time management, and adherence to safety protocols. The event also highlighted how teamwork, communication, and discipline contribute to the smooth functioning of high-energy public gatherings. Overall, the experience enhanced my appreciation for event management and the role such","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"i8tMxeFi13ne-pDbh0gDI","name":"Kannada Sangha T Shirt for Smiles","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/8Yyby71dOBEirrk3-zPl3.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/SRhBoRPAwA_L_lAlE5uVv.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"For students who bought T-shirt as part of \"T-Shirt for Smiles\" event 5 activity points are to be awarded","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-07","hoursSpent":20,"description":"On 07-07-2024 a group of students, visited Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Anathashram located at Kumbalgodu, Bengaluru. The visit aimed to support and bring joy to the children residing there through various activities and donations.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YuRuybFTDjFkiNrL1lyTj","name":"Build with Gen AI hackathon","slNo":11,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/36b0c725-1ab9-4537-9392-cb3e87cf8f22/6TOXVPqRn_H4YO-y5CMw6.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Build with Gen AI Hackathon was a technical innovation event focused on exploring the practical applications of Generative Artificial Intelligence. Participants worked in teams to ideate, design, and develop AI-driven solutions using modern generative models and tools. The hackathon encouraged problem-solving across domains such as automation, data intelligence, creative AI, and real-world productivity enhancements. Mentors and judges evaluated projects based on innovation, technical implementation, feasibility, and impact, providing valuable feedback to participants throughout the event.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":25,"description":"The Build with Gen AI Hackathon was a technical innovation event focused on exploring the practical applications of Generative Artificial Intelligence. Participants worked in teams to ideate, design, and develop AI-driven solutions using modern generative models and tools. The hackathon encouraged problem-solving across domains such as automation, data intelligence, creative AI, and real-world productivity enhancements. Mentors and judges evaluated projects based on innovation, technical implementation, feasibility, and impact, providing valuable feedback to participants throughout the event.","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Rajatha ","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 17:22:49.244126+00', '2026-01-29 19:36:21.666927+00'), ('e768023a-e7d9-4f71-a7b5-1a282cd2f3db', '823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY038","name":"Mayank Pritwani","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"x8y8jSpuT685Ja9ytynBj","name":"Fast trek 1.0","slNo":1,"place":"Huthridurga Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/o8HEY2fD42kgJ9DCyXn-g.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-02-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of physical fitness, teamwork, and discipline. It also created awareness about respecting nature and maintaining environmental cleanliness during outdoor activities.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-02-12","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Fast Trek 1.0 was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE as an outdoor trekking activity aimed at promoting physical fitness, environmental awareness, and teamwork among students. The event involved trekking through natural terrain while following safety instructions and maintaining discipline throughout the activity.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/PLeGua6oTACsPL7MgxuG0.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"3mMkiCr-hHfDyQuB_wszP","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":2,"place":"Kunagalu betta hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/BxOxVvHf_yIA3FcsbsZD1.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/ZOnhhG4PPllzGRLDd3hI5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed awareness about environmental conservation and the importance of maintaining cleanliness in natural spaces. The event improved my physical endurance, teamwork, and discipline. It also helped me understand the value of organized participation and collective effort in large-scale social and environmental initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Fast Trek was a flagship event organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with active participation from college students. The activity combined trekking with a cleanliness and environmental awareness drive. Participants were briefed on safety measures before the trek and followed structured guidelines throughout the event. The trek took place at Kunagalu Betta Hills, where students actively engaged in the activity while appreciating the natural surroundings. The event successfully promoted environmental responsibility, physical fitness, and community participation.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/10SLktLa0Cv-eJNueb0D3.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Bqh17PhC-kODnl8FHYq2j","name":"Eye Donation Fortnight","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/f18NnknPCsUr_kBZd9q7Z.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-08","duration":12,"outcomes":"This activity increased my awareness of organ donation and its impact on society. I learned how awareness campaigns can influence positive social change.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-08-28","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Eye Donation Fortnight was organized by NSS RVCE to spread awareness about the importance of eye donation. Volunteers educated students and staff about myths and facts related to eye donation and encouraged pledging.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/ct54moVvaVWuTIHhgBXe-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"R7rQrW9Mnj1blJ2QofMy8","name":"Fist Full","slNo":4,"place":"","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/B7NEZ5ntoa34Vn7ywsn7q.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"I developed a deeper sense of social responsibility and learned how collective efforts can address issues like hunger and malnutrition effectively.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":15,"description":"Fist Full 2025 continued the initiative of food donation to support underprivileged communities. The event encouraged student participation in social welfare activities and promoted empathy and compassion towards those in need.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/qFEWiH4QgZREsG1SCMcLR.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uKW7H4iJpMgjGxUzcrcW4","name":"Bangalore cube open 2024","slNo":5,"place":"VR mall","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/HVJrICtBS4ceSwiVpy0bA.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-22","duration":2,"outcomes":"This activity enhanced my organizational and teamwork skills. I also gained experience in managing events and interacting with participants from diverse backgrounds.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-21","hoursSpent":12,"description":"Bangalore cube open 2024 was organized by CubeX RVCE and involved planning, coordination, and volunteering for a competitive cubing event. The event aimed to promote logical thinking, problem-solving skills, and community engagement.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/M9Vx-TITkv2xUos8ffJA8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AXJ42kRtzA3h0JIIclk3E","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/1ysiB-X4rj3MnFdcguQMk.png"],"endDate":"2025-02-21","duration":15,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed a strong sense of social responsibility and empathy towards underprivileged students. The initiative helped me understand the importance of education as a fundamental right and how individual contributions can collectively create a positive impact on society. It also reinforced the value of participating in community-driven social initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-02-07","hoursSpent":15,"description":"Project Pustak was a social initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Pranav Foundation, aimed at supporting the education of underprivileged government school students. As part of this initiative, contributions were collected to sponsor stationery kits for school children. The project focused on promoting equal access to basic educational resources and encouraging students to contribute towards community welfare through meaningful social service.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/rKpXVyJhtjnZfWy3atKnr.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zm5kNHxEiTU41FlWTupno","name":"Art of Living – Awareness & Sustainability","slNo":7,"place":"Art of Living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/QogBE70u_P2MkBE-dMgeb.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I gained awareness about sustainable farming practices and the role of soil conservation in food security. It helped me understand how ecological balance can be maintained through responsible agricultural methods and community awareness.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-17","hoursSpent":9,"description":"This activity was carried out at The Art of Living International Center, Bengaluru, as part of the Youth Empowerment Seminar for Students. The activity focused on permaculture practices and creating public awareness about the importance of soil health and sustainable agricultural methods. Participants were involved in learning and spreading knowledge about improving soil quality to enhance agricultural productivity in an eco-friendly manner.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/Q5xg3BBiB5ODAIDAjdoQJ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MZRhtXathRfxs3RGxWQkg","name":"Art of Living – Community & Environmental Welfare","slNo":8,"place":"Art of living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/xE268cL9MRW0_jpjURXpu.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity enhanced my understanding of animal welfare and the importance of preserving indigenous species. It developed a sense of responsibility towards environmental sustainability and ethical treatment of animals.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-25","hoursSpent":9,"description":"The Gaushala activity was conducted at The Art of Living International Center with the objective of conserving and nurturing indigenous breeds of cows in India. The activity involved understanding the importance of native cattle, their care, and their contribution to sustainable agriculture and rural livelihoods.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/hWs3cSlg6NNxH98CNEMXU.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QBXT-dRJJRyzJRKTK9DQk","name":"Art of Living – Awareness Drive","slNo":9,"place":"Art of Living ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/45i_ikwYL58qbiabHUln4.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-08-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity helped me understand the importance of mental health and emotional well-being. I learned practical techniques to manage stress, improve focus, and maintain a balanced lifestyle, which are essential for both personal and academic growth.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-08-04","hoursSpent":9,"description":"The YES!+ Course was conducted under the Youth Empowerment Seminar initiative at The Art of Living International Center. The program focused on mental health awareness and well-being, aligned with the Har Ghar Dhyan initiative of the Government of India. It aimed to equip students with techniques for stress management, emotional balance, and positive thinking.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/tDCYrRLYHaUjAPuyncm_H.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1UY8OP_nLPlIKqro1GpKS","name":"Art of Living – Environmental Sustainability","slNo":10,"place":"Art of living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/q-7I4XKWyRGWcJAXJdwNW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-02-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed an appreciation for environmental conservation and greenery maintenance. It strengthened my understanding of the role of plantation and greenery in improving ecological balance and air quality.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-02-01","hoursSpent":9,"description":"The horticulture activity involved nurturing plants and trees at The Art of Living International Center. Participants took part in watering plants, sowing seeds, plantation activities, and maintaining green spaces. The initiative aimed to promote environmental conservation and sustainable living practices.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/16BLfeYuhMxDGAw4xP4sI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LoMFcJH4Z6Gkr93JmIzr4","name":"Art of Living – Community Development","slNo":11,"place":"Art of Living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/VRycKNHLlWoeGKTTwVKbU.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-01-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"This activity taught me the importance of teamwork, discipline, and service to society. It helped me understand how organized community efforts can efficiently support food distribution and social welfare initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-12","hoursSpent":9,"description":"The Community Kitchen activity was conducted at The Art of Living International Center, where volunteers actively participated in serving food, cutting vegetables, setting up the kitchen, and maintaining cleanliness. The initiative focused on service, teamwork, and supporting large-scale community food programs.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/uvzDbYQ6NT6er1i9gvtaj.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ac8oPouSLSI4wXH4mWSqk","name":"SDG Photography Contest","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/H_VTNGdwkT8LM3FrDEmmE.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-12-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"I learned about Sustainable Development Goals and how creative expression can be used to spread awareness about global issues.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-19","hoursSpent":5,"description":"This competition involved capturing photographs aligned with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. I submitted a photograph related to clean water and sanitation, highlighting the importance of water conservation.","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/823be3e0-663b-49cf-84c8-987375271b0f/Ad_I57wfEVT9TImq9XqaI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"24-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Minal Moharir","designation":"Professor and Program Co-ordinator CSE(CY)"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 15:40:08.08844+00', '2026-01-30 07:26:45.066488+00'), ('ea371bec-26ee-4a3c-8dc2-5d46d1646497', '4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS064","name":"Siddesh K R","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"P5Z5Gm1PaBFuJRs88P6gC","name":"Voluntary Blood Donation Camp","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the voluntary blood donation camp enhanced my understanding of social responsibility and the critical role individuals play in supporting public healthcare systems. The experience fostered a sense of empathy and humanitarian concern, highlighting how a simple act can have a life-saving impact.\\n\\nI also gained awareness about medical safety procedures, donor eligibility criteria, and the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle for regular blood donation. The activity strengthened my commitment to community service and motivated me to actively participate in future health-related and social welfare initiatives.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Voluntary Blood Donation Camp was organized in collaboration with the Indira Gandhi Institute of Child Health, Bengaluru, with the objective of promoting humanitarian values, social responsibility, and awareness about the importance of blood donation in saving lives. The initiative aimed to encourage students to actively contribute to the healthcare system and support patients in need of blood transfusions.\\n\\nAs a volunteer donor, I willingly participated in the camp and donated one unit of blood after undergoing the required medical screening procedures conducted by qualified healthcare professionals. The process followed strict medical and safety protocols to ensure donor well-being, hygiene, and compliance with health standards. Medical staff provided guidance on pre-donation preparation and post-donation care, ensuring a safe and informed experience.\\n\\nThe camp played a vital role in addressing the continuous demand for blood in hospitals, especially for children requiring emergency and critical care. Through this activity, participants were educated on the significance of regular blood donation, blood group compatibility, and the impact of timely donations in saving lives. The event also emphasized the ethical responsibility of individuals to contribute to society beyond academic pursuits.\\n\\nOverall, the blood donation camp served as a meaningful platform to instill empathy, compassion, and civic duty among students, reinforcing the values of selfless service and community welfare promoted by the National Service Scheme.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS – Health and Hygiene","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/wd2TMBvcIDbyR1guBM0CE.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3–4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"md5_k_VPcCyqFUfj4-Dcs","name":"Utsarga Marathon (5 KM)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through participation in the Utsarga Marathon, I gained a deeper understanding of the importance of community service and social responsibility. The event helped me develop discipline, perseverance, and teamwork while emphasizing the role of physical fitness in maintaining a healthy lifestyle.\\n\\nI also gained insight into how large-scale social events are organized and managed, including coordination, planning, and execution by NSS volunteers. The experience reinforced the values of volunteerism, leadership, and collective effort, encouraging me to actively contribute to similar social initiatives in the future.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-07","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is an annual flagship event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering, with the objective of promoting social responsibility, community participation, and physical fitness among students and the general public. The marathon was conducted with the inspiring theme of contributing towards a worthy social cause, emphasizing the importance of collective effort in addressing societal challenges.\\n\\nThe event featured multiple running categories, including a 5 KM run, and witnessed active participation from students, faculty members, and external participants. The marathon was meticulously planned and executed by NSS volunteers, ensuring smooth registration, route management, crowd control, hydration support, and post-run arrangements. Proper safety measures were implemented throughout the route to ensure the well-being of all participants.\\n\\nAs a participant in the 5 KM category, I actively took part in the marathon, demonstrating commitment towards social causes and community welfare. The event encouraged participants to adopt a healthy lifestyle while simultaneously raising awareness about social issues through physical engagement. The presence of college authorities and NSS coordinators further highlighted the significance of the event and reinforced the values of service, discipline, and teamwork.\\n\\nOverall, the Utsarga Marathon served as a platform to instill civic sense, promote volunteerism, and strengthen the bond between students and society. The event successfully combined fitness, service, and social awareness, making it a meaningful and impactful initiative under the NSS framework.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS – Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/K8KltSP0iAENSJRSaV4N6.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1–2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1bYv6ptcVPG4CMhoVJ-BS","name":"Food & DISCOM – Food and Malnutrition Awareness","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/0MoEjwmxA8yXS0ejQAGUM.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I gained a clear understanding of the causes and consequences of malnutrition and the importance of nutrition in maintaining overall health. The program enhanced my awareness of public health challenges related to food security and nutritional deficiencies.\\n\\nThe experience also strengthened my sense of social responsibility and motivated me to adopt and promote healthy dietary habits. It encouraged me to actively participate in community awareness initiatives aimed at improving public health and reducing food-related issues in society.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-15","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Food & DISCOM – Food and Malnutrition Awareness program was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) with the objective of creating awareness about nutritional deficiencies, food security, and the serious impact of malnutrition on public health. The activity aimed to educate students on the importance of balanced nutrition and responsible food consumption, particularly in the context of vulnerable communities.\\n\\nThe program focused on spreading awareness about different forms of malnutrition, including undernutrition and micronutrient deficiencies, and their long-term effects on physical and cognitive development. Volunteers actively participated in awareness sessions, discussions, and outreach activities designed to highlight the importance of nutritious diets, hygienic food practices, and reduction of food wastage.\\n\\nAs a participant, I was involved in understanding the societal challenges related to food distribution, nutritional imbalance, and public health awareness. The activity emphasized the role of students in promoting healthy eating habits and responsible consumption patterns within society. Informative sessions helped participants gain insights into government initiatives, community-level interventions, and the importance of collective efforts in addressing malnutrition.\\n\\nOverall, the program successfully reinforced the values of social responsibility and awareness towards public health issues. It encouraged participants to contribute meaningfully towards improving nutritional awareness and fostering a healthier society through informed actions.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS – Health and Nutrition Awareness","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5–6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dZc3ZxLXNI7slTGiED4Rq","name":"First Vote Awareness Program","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/V3OzO1H_qHQ01n8MmniNr.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed a clear understanding of the electoral process and the importance of voting in a democratic system. The program strengthened my awareness of constitutional rights and civic duties.\\n\\nThe experience encouraged me to become a responsible voter and motivated me to promote voter awareness among peers and within the community. It reinforced the values of democratic participation, ethical decision-making, and active citizenship.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-05","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The First Vote Awareness Program was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) with the objective of educating students about the importance of voting and active participation in the democratic process. The program aimed to create awareness among young and first-time voters regarding their constitutional rights and responsibilities as citizens of India.\\n\\nThe activity focused on explaining the significance of free and fair elections, the role of voters in a democratic nation, and the impact of informed voting on governance and societal development. Sessions were conducted to familiarize participants with the electoral process, voter registration procedures, and the importance of ethical voting practices. Emphasis was placed on encouraging youth participation to strengthen democratic values and civic engagement.\\n\\nAs a participant, I actively engaged in the awareness sessions and discussions, gaining insights into the functioning of democratic institutions and the power of an individual vote in shaping public policy and leadership. The program highlighted the role of educated youth in promoting democratic awareness and responsible citizenship within society.\\n\\nOverall, the First Vote Awareness Program served as an effective platform to instill democratic values, civic responsibility, and social awareness among students. It motivated participants to exercise their right to vote responsibly and to encourage others to participate actively in the democratic process.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS – Civic Engagement and Voter Awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WmFsEzdrmpXaAbl9Y5tNY","name":"Independence Day Unboxing Program","slNo":5,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/-lyK-33Fke77XserwngNf.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed a stronger sense of patriotism and appreciation for the sacrifices made during India’s freedom struggle. The program reinforced the importance of national unity, civic responsibility, and respect for democratic values.\\n\\nThe experience encouraged me to actively participate in national and social initiatives and strengthened my commitment to contributing positively to society as a responsible citizen.\\n","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-15","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Independence Day Unboxing Program was organized to commemorate India’s Independence Day and to instill a sense of patriotism, national pride, and civic responsibility among students. The activity aimed to encourage active participation of youth in national celebrations and to promote awareness about the values and sacrifices associated with India’s freedom struggle.\\n\\nThe program involved organized participation in Independence Day–related activities, highlighting the significance of unity, freedom, and responsibility as citizens of the nation. Through structured events and coordinated involvement, participants were encouraged to reflect on the contributions of freedom fighters and the importance of upholding constitutional values in modern society.\\n\\nAs a participant, I actively took part in the program and contributed to the celebration by engaging in the planned activities with discipline and enthusiasm. The event emphasized the role of young citizens in preserving national integrity and promoting social harmony. It also served as a reminder of the duties and responsibilities that come with the rights enjoyed in an independent nation.\\n\\nOverall, the Independence Day Unboxing Program provided a meaningful opportunity to connect with national values and to actively participate in a celebration that reinforces patriotism, unity, and respect for the nation’s heritage.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS – National Integration and Patriotism","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_ImDIik5_tSjizfkoucSX","name":"Inhouse Publicity – Citizen Responsibility Workshop","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/2NV_8F-K6I5XrUQo2eMTx.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Through this workshop, I gained a clearer understanding of civic responsibilities and the importance of ethical and responsible behavior in society. The activity enhanced my awareness of social duties and the role of citizens in maintaining harmony and public welfare.\\n\\nThe experience motivated me to actively engage in community-oriented initiatives and strengthened my commitment to contributing positively to society as a responsible and informed citizen.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-10","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Inhouse Publicity – Citizen Responsibility Workshop was organized with the objective of creating awareness among students about civic duties, social responsibility, and active citizenship. The workshop aimed to educate participants on the importance of responsible behavior in society and the role of individuals in maintaining social harmony and public order.\\n\\nThe program focused on key aspects of citizenship such as ethical conduct, respect for laws, participation in community welfare activities, and accountability towards society. Through structured sessions and discussions, students were encouraged to understand how their actions directly impact the community and the nation as a whole. Emphasis was placed on developing responsible attitudes and promoting positive social behavior.\\n\\nAs a participant, I actively took part in the workshop and contributed to the publicity efforts by supporting awareness dissemination within the campus. The activity highlighted the importance of informed and responsible participation in civic life and encouraged students to take proactive roles in social initiatives.\\n\\nOverall, the workshop successfully reinforced the values of civic consciousness, responsibility, and social engagement. It served as an effective platform to nurture responsible citizens who contribute positively to society beyond academic pursuits.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS – Civic Responsibility and Social Awareness","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"r4AnWP1S3lQ8S3JhcoNhU","name":"Kannada Habba (Gharjane)","slNo":7,"place":"RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/UH78aF90zUX_RfBsS_Koe.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-20","duration":101,"outcomes":"Participation in Kannada Habba 2024 enhanced my understanding and appreciation of Kannada culture, traditions, and language. The activity helped me develop teamwork, coordination, leadership, and organizational skills through active involvement in a large-scale cultural event.\\n\\nThe experience strengthened my cultural awareness and sense of belonging while motivating me to contribute to the preservation and promotion of regional heritage. It also improved my ability to collaborate with peers and manage responsibilities effectively in a group setting.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-12","hoursSpent":20,"description":"Kannada Habba 2024 was a major cultural event organized by the Kannada Sangha of RV College of Engineering with the objective of celebrating Karnataka’s rich linguistic, cultural, and artistic heritage. The event aimed to promote cultural awareness, unity, and pride among students while providing a platform for showcasing traditional and contemporary Kannada art forms.\\n\\nAs an active member and participant, I contributed to the successful planning and execution of various activities associated with Kannada Habba. The event involved extensive preparation, coordination, and teamwork, including stage arrangements, decorations, cultural programs, and volunteer management. Various competitions, performances, and cultural programs were conducted to engage students and faculty members from diverse backgrounds.\\n\\nThe event featured a wide range of cultural activities such as folk dances, music performances, theatrical presentations, literary events, and speeches highlighting the importance of preserving Kannada language and culture. The active involvement of students helped create a vibrant and inclusive atmosphere that encouraged cultural exchange and appreciation.\\n\\nOverall, Kannada Habba 2024 served as an important platform to strengthen cultural identity and foster unity within the college community. The event successfully highlighted the significance of regional culture while encouraging student participation, creativity, and organizational skills.\\n","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities – Kannada Sangha","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11–14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jDEkhqAojHrmzgeL2Pr1a","name":"Kannada Sangha – Buy a T-Shirt Activity","slNo":8,"place":"RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/xdWlWtBOePsa3QpL0HMxL.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed a stronger sense of cultural identity and appreciation for Kannada language and heritage. The experience encouraged me to actively participate in cultural initiatives and support community-driven activities.\\n\\nThe activity reinforced the importance of collective effort in promoting regional culture and helped me understand how small initiatives can contribute to larger cultural movements.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-05","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Kannada Sangha – Buy a T-Shirt Activity was organized as part of the Kannada Sangha initiatives at RV College of Engineering with the objective of promoting Kannada culture, unity, and identity among students. The activity encouraged students to actively participate in cultural movements by wearing and supporting Kannada Sangha merchandise, thereby fostering a sense of pride and belonging.\\n\\nThe initiative aimed to increase student involvement in cultural activities while spreading awareness about the importance of preserving and promoting the Kannada language and heritage. By participating in this activity, students demonstrated solidarity with the objectives of Kannada Sangha and contributed to strengthening cultural representation within the campus.\\n\\nAs a participant, I actively supported the initiative by engaging in the activity and promoting cultural awareness among peers. The activity, though simple in execution, played a significant role in reinforcing cultural identity and encouraging collective participation in cultural programs organized by the Kannada Sangha.\\n\\nOverall, the Buy a T-Shirt activity served as an effective means of engaging students in cultural promotion and enhancing visibility for Kannada Sangha initiatives within the college community.\\n","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities – Kannada Sangha","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"WMdV_rxOXu-whxpRzQUnW","name":"Mega Plantation Drive","slNo":9,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/ERZ3eK8PmgkvwFGE4Q9_u.jpeg"],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"Through participation in the Mega Plantation Drive, I gained a deeper understanding of environmental conservation and the significance of afforestation in maintaining ecological balance. The activity enhanced my awareness of sustainable practices and environmental responsibility.\\n\\nThe experience motivated me to adopt eco-friendly habits and actively participate in future environmental initiatives. It reinforced the importance of collective action in addressing environmental challenges and promoting a greener and healthier society.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-26","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Mega Plantation Drive was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) with the objective of promoting environmental sustainability, ecological balance, and awareness about the importance of afforestation. The activity aimed to encourage students to actively participate in environmental conservation efforts and to understand the role of trees in maintaining a healthy ecosystem.\\n\\nAs part of the drive, volunteers actively participated in planting saplings, preparing the soil, and ensuring proper watering and maintenance under guided supervision. The activity emphasized the importance of increasing green cover to combat environmental issues such as air pollution, climate change, and soil degradation. Participants were educated about the benefits of native plant species and the long-term impact of plantation drives on environmental health.\\n\\nAs a volunteer, I actively contributed to the plantation process and collaborated with fellow participants to ensure the smooth execution of the activity. The drive promoted teamwork, discipline, and responsibility towards nature while reinforcing the importance of individual contribution in large-scale environmental initiatives.\\n\\nOverall, the Mega Plantation Drive served as a meaningful initiative that combined environmental awareness with practical action. The activity successfully instilled values of environmental stewardship and social responsibility among students.\\n","aicteMapping":"NSS – Environmental Sustainability","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"16–17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Yo0sLoGOD2nAHetV08hyK","name":"Kannada Sangha –(Jagadvaha)","slNo":10,"place":"RV College of Engineering, Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/4d0317f2-7f73-472a-8d2a-9460146828e6/45PmhiBRHle9afv74aqwx.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-10","duration":62,"outcomes":"Through this activity, I developed a deeper appreciation for sustained cultural involvement and the importance of preserving linguistic heritage. The experience enhanced my sense of responsibility towards cultural organizations and encouraged active participation even in later semesters.\\n\\nThe activity helped me strengthen teamwork and leadership qualities while contributing to the continuity of cultural initiatives. It reinforced the value of consistent participation in community and cultural development activities.\\n","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-08-10","hoursSpent":30,"description":"The Kannada Sangha Student Participation activity during the 7th semester was conducted to encourage continued student involvement in cultural and linguistic initiatives organized by the Kannada Sangha at RV College of Engineering. The activity aimed to promote sustained engagement with Kannada language, culture, and traditions among senior students while fostering a sense of responsibility towards cultural preservation.\\n\\nAs a participant, I actively took part in Kannada Sangha activities and contributed to maintaining the continuity of cultural programs within the campus. The initiative emphasized the importance of student participation in cultural organizations beyond initial semesters, highlighting leadership, consistency, and commitment towards community-driven cultural activities.\\n\\nThe activity also provided an opportunity for senior students to support and guide junior members, thereby strengthening teamwork and collaboration within the Sangha. Through participation, students were encouraged to uphold cultural values and promote inclusivity and unity within the academic environment.\\n\\nOverall, the Kannada Sangha participation activity reinforced the significance of sustained cultural engagement and student responsibility in preserving and promoting regional heritage within the institution.\\n","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities – Kannada Sangha","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"18","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 19:17:34.171904+00', '2026-01-30 19:17:34.171904+00'), ('eb591ae3-caea-413b-9525-91b616c4e60d', 'c88f0904-14fa-4d83-adb4-f9aacd308727', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23CY400","name":"B TANUJ","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"6sD1xG0m1ybG1bz-Wd0F7","name":"Eco-Walk","slNo":1,"place":"EMPRI","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EEd0llomnvCIr7POcUSeg","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QYHpxRfTdxRQpTf-cMnDt","name":"Mera Phale Vote","slNo":3,"place":"MyGov Portal","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QFdv35G1CL3BDlzCXMk4d","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz","slNo":4,"place":"MyGov Portal","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AvNXAmM9irHDiay9ifkU4","name":"FistFull","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mkqgESFto9TY_nF2y_gq2","name":"Police Marshal","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6M8MyHhaN1opmqvLdKsSJ","name":"Paper Drive 2.0","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":14,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-20","hoursSpent":12,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"K7SWnlI7OYYt7V0lC3VUf","name":"Human Elephant Conflict","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":2,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"cBF9W8fikjBCNTHpmirdB","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-30","duration":4,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-27","hoursSpent":1,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"YBnJPwKbV6kWM1T08IHKm","name":"DD Chandana","slNo":10,"place":"Palace Ground","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-06-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-21","hoursSpent":4,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Minal Moharir","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 08:41:43.195315+00', '2026-02-01 08:56:00.887948+00'), ('eb721580-44a5-45c4-8cc4-23c8834cbd50', '7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS403","name":"Mohammed Faid","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"NYWUSyEkQcDIWD5lJPICB","name":"RVCE HAM CLUB","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/FPIgywmiIAcSPPJLT3PGK.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"Technical Skill Integration: Successfully bridge theoretical knowledge with practical application by participating in workshops involving SDR (Software Defined Radio) and MATLAB.\\n\\nEnvironmental Stewardship: Develop a proactive approach toward sustainability through the World Environment Day sapling plantation drive, moving beyond awareness to direct action.\\n\\nCommunity Impact and Physical Fitness: Contribute to social causes while promoting personal health and wellness by participating in the Utsarga Marathon 2025.\\n\\nAdministrative Responsibility: Learn the importance of formal documentation and reporting, such as submitting activity reports to the Dean of Student Affairs to validate participation and earn Activity Points.\\n\\nCollaboration and Leadership: Experience the value of student-led organizations (like the NSS or HAM Club) in organizing large-scale events that align with institutional goals and community needs.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-29","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Managed a significant environmental and technical initiative for students through a collaborative academic effort. Through a structured approach, the RVCE HAM Club, under the guidance of Dr. Usha Rani K R, demonstrated how student-led technical workshops can successfully integrate social responsibility with skill development. The project achieved high engagement by organizing a SDR + MATLAB Workshop, reflecting a strong commitment to technical excellence and collective environmental action within the RVCE ecosystem.\\n\\nThe initiative efficiently converted educational activities into measurable ecological impact. In observance of World Environment Day, the project transitioned from classroom learning to a Sapling Plantation drive, where participating teams were issued saplings to promote sustainability. This effort resulted in a formal request to the Dean of Student Affairs for the approval of 5 Activity Points for each student, rewarding their active participation in a green initiative that was both technically enriching and socially meaningful. By completing this activity and submitting the required reports, the students directly contributed to environmental awareness, ensuring that the project fostered not only technical growth but also a sense of dignity and responsibility toward the planet.","aicteMapping":"Automation of local activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/-C1JH2w3CrLWGmWwwOf_Q.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"GhO_08PKOhD5MArnoyc9H","name":"T shirt For Smile","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/XwXyE94G4cUd2eCp7eeya.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-09-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Technical Proficiency: Participants gained hands-on experience through the SDR + MATLAB Workshop.\\n\\nEnvironmental Impact: Students actively contributed to sustainability by planting and committing to nurture saplings.\\n\\nCivic Recognition: The project successfully integrated technical education with social meaningfulness, qualifying students for 5 Activity Points.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":7,"description":"Following an SDR + MATLAB Workshop, the RVCE HAM Club initiated an environmentally responsible project in observance of World Environment Day. Each participating student team was issued a sapling to plant and nurture, aiming to foster environmental awareness and sustainability alongside their technical learning. The initiative was formally documented and submitted to the Dean of Student Affairs to request the granting of 5 Activity Points for the participants.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/oQQp4Z7fyQST-6WfhRSDP.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Xe8fRwCrNBUbNr7ggn-QD","name":"Sparks of Service, Ripples of Change","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/5qH-khmeKgq9ekgU_ECnP.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"With official approval in place, the Rotaract Club of RVCE successfully executed Project Pustak in a structured and impactful manner. The authorization enabled smooth coordination with students, faculty, and external partners such as the Pranav Foundation, leading to strong participation and trust. As a result, the project progressed through its two phases—fundraising and distribution—achieving significant outcomes including the mobilization of over a thousand student contributors, the collection of substantial funds, and the large-scale distribution of educational kits to underprivileged children in government schools. The approval also ensured that participating students received due recognition in the form of activity points, thereby motivating engagement while translating institutional backing into meaningful social impact that helped bridge educational resource gaps.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-27","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The image shows an official approval letter issued to the Rotaract Club of RVCE by the Dean of Student Affairs, R.V. College of Engineering, granting permission and activity points for a social service initiative. This letter formally acknowledges the club’s request to conduct an AICF/NGO-based activity involving volunteers and participants, validating the event as part of the institute’s recognized extracurricular and service-oriented programs. The document reflects institutional support for the Rotaract Club’s outreach efforts and serves as an authorization for students to participate and earn activity points, reinforcing the college’s encouragement of community service, leadership, and social responsibility among its students.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/4iCkggDsDcql2ltLP8y0X.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LYNORhaxCuTsMezpg7JAX","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/BKwQZpdiM1qnbK0P32UIB.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"meaningful platform for community engagement. By organizing the event at R V College of \\nEngineering, the initiative motivated students and participants to adopt healthier lifestyles while \\ncontributing to a larger humanitarian cause. The marathon helped raise awareness and support \\nfor educational initiatives aimed at underprivileged children, reinforcing the idea that individual \\nparticipation can directly contribute to social development. The provision of AICTE activity \\npoints further encouraged active involvement, ensuring strong participation and institutional \\nrecognition of social responsibility.\\nThis initiative demonstrates that social causes can be effectively integrated with fitness and \\nrecreational activities to drive wider participation and impact. It highlights the value of \\nholistic development—balancing physical well-being with empathy and civic responsibility. \\nParticipants learn that social change does not always require complex interventions; consistent \\neffort and collective participation can make a tangible difference. The marathon also fosters \\ndiscipline, teamwork, and a sense of purpose, reinforcing the role of students as active \\ncontributors to societal progress while nurturing both body and mind","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-25","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is a social and fitness-oriented event organized at R V College of \\nEngineering on February 4th, 2024, from 6:00 AM to 10:30 AM. The marathon is designed \\nto promote physical well-being while fostering social responsibility among participants. More \\nthan just a running event, it carries a strong humanitarian message under the theme “Help a \\nChild Change the World.”\\nParticipants are encouraged to take part not only to celebrate health and fitness but also to \\ncontribute to a meaningful cause, as every step taken supports initiatives aimed at providing \\neducation to underprivileged children. By combining endurance, enthusiasm, and empathy, the \\nUtsarga Marathon creates a platform where students and participants actively engage in social \\nchange while earning 10 AICTE activity points for their involvement","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"TKPDTDuG7pwk7Qc0LsCaK","name":"Lakshya Air Rifle Shooting","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/6QG8gkCDkZCBoB3X2Yny7.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Lakshya shooting event served as a meaningful platform for promoting physical discipline, precision, and mental resilience among students. By recognizing participants with 10 AICTE Activity Points and associating the event with the NCC Plantation Drive through the presentation of a sapling, the initiative reinforced values of responsibility, environmental awareness, and national service. The event successfully motivated students to explore sports beyond conventional athletics while fostering confidence, self-control, and commitment. Overall, the initiative demonstrated how skill-based sports activities can be effectively combined with institutional recognition and social values, contributing to well-rounded personal and civic development among participants.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The image represents a Certificate of Appreciation issued by R V College of Engineering to Mohammed Faid for active participation in the 10m Air Rifle Shooting Event “Lakshya.” The event was organized by the NCC RVCE in collaboration with Kadamba Sports, aiming to promote discipline, focus, and sportsmanship among students. Conducted within the college campus, the event provided participants with an opportunity to engage in a structured shooting sport under professional guidance, encouraging skill development alongside mental concentration. The certificate formally acknowledges the participant’s involvement and highlights the institutional effort to integrate sports, co-curricular engagement, and holistic student development.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/TI2le1w_UtKRKvksbCzPq.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lEAAExhTW8BVpBFLVyUdN","name":"Project Pustak 2025(Rotract)","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/AZcu9IObNDYG-MCHWj22n.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":730486,"outcomes":"Project Pustak successfully translated collective goodwill into tangible educational support for \\nunderprivileged rural students. By mobilizing small but meaningful contributions of Rs. 100 \\nand Rs. 350 from donors, the initiative generated sufficient funds to procure essential school \\nsupplies such as textbooks, stationery, backpacks, and related learning materials. This directly \\nreduced the financial burden on economically disadvantaged families and improved students’ \\naccess to basic educational resources. The collaboration between the Rotaract Club of RVCE \\nand Pranav Foundation ensured transparent fund utilization and effective on-ground execution, \\nultimately fostering a more inclusive and supportive learning environment for rural students and \\nencouraging school attendance and engagement.\\nProject Pustak highlights the power of collective action, showing that modest individual \\ncontributions can create a significant social impact when pooled together. It demonstrates the \\nimportance of structured collaboration between student organizations and NGOs to achieve \\nefficient implementation and accountability. The project also reinforces key lessons in social \\nresponsibility, leadership, project planning, and resource management. Most importantly, it \\nemphasizes that education-focused interventions, even at a grassroots level, can play a crucial \\nrole in bridging inequality and empowering communities for long-term development.","semester":"3","startDate":"0024-05-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies \\nto underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was \\ncollected from each compassionate donor, which served as the foundation for procuring and \\ndonating much-needed supplies to these deserving students. The collected funds were efficiently \\nutilized to purchase educational materials such as textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and \\nother vital resources that contribute to a conducive learning environment. Through the generous \\ncontributions of donors who contributed either Rs 100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial \\nfunds. Rotaract Club of RVCE alongside Pranav Foundation will procure essential school \\nsupplies for the underprivileged students.","aicteMapping":"To assist the marketing of rural produce","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/saaM_HNcDN4fcvWx0Zn9l.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zD7yySM_pdB0jMx7XtN0Y","name":"Walk for her walk for change (Rotaract)","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/xdBnx-iljDJHpvq4F-deo.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE created \\nstrong social awareness around the critical issue of female foeticide and gender discrimination. \\nWith the participation of over 350 individuals—including students, faculty members, and \\nparents—the event successfully transformed a sensitive social concern into a collective public \\ndialogue. The walkathon, supported by impactful placards and slogans, helped spread a clear \\nmessage about the value of girl children and the urgent need to oppose gender-based violence \\nand discrimination before birth. The large turnout and visible solidarity amplified the reach of \\nthe message beyond the campus, reinforcing community engagement and social responsibility.\\nThis initiative highlights the effectiveness of peaceful public engagement in driving social \\nawareness and change. It demonstrates how collective participation can give voice to \\ncritical social issues and encourage reflection, discussion, and attitude change within society. \\nParticipants learned the importance of standing up against injustice, promoting gender equality, \\nand using community platforms to advocate for ethical and social values. The event also fostered \\nleadership, empathy, and civic responsibility among students, reinforcing the idea that educated \\nyouth play a vital role in shaping a more inclusive, just, and equitable society","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-14","hoursSpent":13,"description":"\\nDescription: On the occasion of Mother''s Day, 11th May 2025, the Rotaract Club of RVCE\\norganized a Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon with the aim of shedding light on the grave \\nissue of female foeticide and promoting the value of girl children in society. The event witnessed \\nan overwhelming participation of 350+ individuals, including enthusiastic students, dedicated \\nfaculty members, and supportive parents who came together to walk for a cause that truly \\nmatters. The walkathon began in the early hours of the morning from the RVCE campus and \\nwas marked by thought-provoking placards, powerful slogans, and an atmosphere of solidarity. \\nThe event served as a platform to educate and inspire change, urging everyone to take a stand \\nagainst gender-based violence and discrimination even before birth. The Rotaract Club of RVCE \\nextends heartfelt gratitude to all participants for their support and commitment to this impactful \\ncause.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/SS02FGdMnNX7UPsC_U4C1.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"aJnn46D5-fTzr-8oHncgS","name":"Utsarga-2025(NSS Marathon)","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/7c033d9b-5953-4f05-96be-cdb176da500a/m2NkkNSOGaQ6X4taTHw27.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"UTSARGA ’25 successfully served as a comprehensive platform that integrated fitness, social \\nresponsibility, and cultural celebration. By bringing together students and members of the wider \\ncommunity at RV College of Engineering, the marathon generated awareness and support for \\nunderprivileged children in the areas of education, healthcare, and welfare. The dual-distance \\nformat enabled inclusive participation, while the cause-driven nature of the event transformed \\nphysical effort into meaningful social contribution. The cultural elements associated with Ram \\nNavami further enhanced participant engagement and community bonding. Overall, the event \\nstrengthened collective commitment toward social upliftment while promoting healthy lifestyles \\nand active citizenship.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":10,"description":"UTSARGA ’25 is the flagship marathon organized at RV College of Engineering, dedicated \\nto the social cause “Help a Child, Change the World.” Scheduled on April 6, 2025, the event \\naims to mobilize students and the wider community to support underprivileged children through \\ninitiatives focused on education, healthcare, and overall welfare.\\nThe marathon features two categories—5 KM and 10 KM—encouraging participation \\nfrom individuals with varying fitness levels. By combining physical endurance with social \\ncommitment, the event promotes healthy lifestyles while fostering empathy and civic \\nresponsibility. Participants receive a comprehensive experience including a T-shirt, certificate, \\nmedal, breakfast, refreshments, and electrolyte juice, ensuring both motivation and well-being \\nthroughout the event.\\nIn addition, as the event coincides with Ram Navami, traditional refreshments such as \\nKosambari and Fruit Panaka are served, adding a cultural and celebratory dimension to the \\nmarathon. UTSARGA ’25 thus stands as a holistic initiative that blends fitness, social service, \\nand cultural values, while also recognizing participant involvement through the award of 15 \\nAICTE activity points.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 13:24:25.4084+00', '2026-01-31 09:21:07.563708+00'), ('ec3803b9-7350-401e-919d-c91269fc1ecb', 'a30b8d0f-fa1e-46d7-ab35-b05696dca5b2', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC028","name":"Avaneesh U Vasishta","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"o5GPhfd5knlGXI11WVGDi","name":"","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"","startDate":"","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":0,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 13:19:01.857263+00', '2026-02-02 06:07:28.179471+00'), ('ec6ea7c2-12c6-4c3a-a2e1-a0454db64469', '6a81e89c-78ac-4b75-a70f-fc7d7cb1d1cc', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC024","name":"Ashishkumar G Uppin","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"kLnXY0Gwe6syayid7HOUe","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2024","slNo":1,"place":"","photos":[],"endDate":"","duration":0,"outcomes":"","semester":"3","startDate":"2025-02-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":