tailedReportPageNo":"26-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"q9ttpj-XgSnorxXjQz1tP","name":"Hult Prize ","slNo":13,"place":"DTL Huddle, RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-02-18","duration":33,"outcomes":"","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Entrepreneurship/ Skill Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"28-30","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"P7ek6jRT4m-J-D2pHUApq","name":"Workshop: Blockchain and CBDC Applications","slNo":14,"place":"MCA Seminar Hall","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-04-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"","aicteMapping":"Innovation / Technical Skill","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"31-32","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 14:38:30.109822+00', '2026-01-30 15:23:28.973689+00'), ('edce18c5-89ef-43cf-97cc-95228b050cdb', '91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC017","name":"Ananya I Shirol","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"-2d-OoipS343uFqpmZQww","name":"Tanuja Screening","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus, Civil Seminar Hall","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/wUG6_kERbousfzix7-f4K.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/kc7c0FQ-pL_miYfDRyv6l.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The movie screening inspired students by emphasizing the importance of hard work, self-belief, and consistency in achieving academic success. It helped participants understand the realities of competitive exam preparation and motivated them to approach their studies with greater focus and determination. The activity also promoted positive discussions on mental strength, goal-setting, and overcoming challenges in the academic journey.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":3,"description":"A movie screening of Tanuja was organized to highlight the academic journey and challenges faced by a girl preparing for the NEET examination. The screening aimed to motivate students by portraying perseverance, dedication, and resilience in the pursuit of educational goals. Through the film, participants gained insight into the pressures, obstacles, and determination involved in competitive examinations. The activity encouraged students to relate to the character’s experiences and reflect on their own academic aspirations.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness and Value-Based Education Activity","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/z-tLQjrvy4x5WxQ1CPTsp.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"V5BtNLKU0IXNnMC6ldnxU","name":"Green Growth-One student One plant","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/kWAuVBeN9R0raMocU_b9m.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity resulted in the plantation of numerous saplings, contributing to a greener and healthier environment. It increased students’ awareness about environmental protection and sustainable living. The initiative also instilled a sense of responsibility, care for nature, and long-term commitment towards preserving natural resources.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-13","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The “Green Growth – One Student, One Plant” initiative was conducted to promote environmental awareness and encourage students to actively participate in plantation activities. Each student was motivated to plant and nurture at least one sapling, contributing towards increasing green cover and improving ecological balance. The activity aimed to educate participants about the importance of trees in maintaining air quality, conserving biodiversity, and combating climate change. Students took responsibility for planting, watering, and caring for their plants, making the initiative a hands-on environmental conservation effort.","aicteMapping":"Environment and Sustainability–related activities","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/nYqd7AJ4SpptV5wDh4qAM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hFZzK5tj7nD5gyNEozDka","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/zOHMETiRiIrgm-RD8AMKG.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative improved access to basic educational resources for underprivileged students, contributing to a better learning environment. It also fostered social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among student volunteers involved in planning and execution.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Project Pustak is a social initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged students in rural areas by providing essential school supplies. Funds collected through donor contributions of ₹100 or ₹350 were utilized to procure textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other learning resources. The project was carried out by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Pranav Foundation to promote equitable access to education.","aicteMapping":"Educational Support and Community Development Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/k6hUWfPZJdF0FM4eiWQOm.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NAy8fcTjcuDeuB_oYM4v9","name":"Biofuel Day Essay Competition","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/FoZmSewLmy3MZNqhVqsNM.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/sVDRQLAWF63cmro_DSZe9.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity significantly improved students’ understanding of renewable energy and sustainable fuel technologies. It enhanced their writing, research, and critical thinking skills. Participants became more aware of environmental conservation and the need to adopt eco-friendly energy practices. The competition also inspired students to spread awareness about clean energy solutions among peers and in the community, supporting long-term environmental sustainability.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-08","hoursSpent":3,"description":"An Essay Competition was organized in observance of Biofuel Day to spread awareness about renewable energy resources and their role in protecting the environment. The activity aimed to educate students about biofuels as an alternative to fossil fuels and their importance in reducing air pollution and carbon emissions. Participants wrote essays discussing different types of biofuels, their production methods, advantages, and how they contribute to sustainable development. The competition encouraged students to research current energy challenges and express innovative ideas for promoting clean and green energy solutions. It served as an effective platform to combine academic learning with environmental responsibility","aicteMapping":"Environmental Sustainability and Renewable Energy Awareness Activity","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/SWedgbbHNwzFnkxVq5_gn.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"L3UQ2TKFSUFsduDQD2QeP","name":"Fistfull","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/dmFkqWj2eQ53sKDKVNdo-.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/S_UPGfj1ye7Vx2m0Fyexj.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-30","duration":16,"outcomes":"Over 6700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor dal were collected, highlighting the strength of collective effort and the power of community support in addressing food insecurity. The event demonstrated how unified action, driven by empathy and a shared sense of purpose, can make a tangible impact in providing essential resources to those in need. More than just a charitable initiative, it instilled a sense of social responsibility among participants, inspiring many to continue engaging in philanthropic activities. By showcasing the transformative potential of community-driven efforts, the event reinforced the importance of sustained contributions and collaboration in building a more equitable and compassionate society.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, successfully launched the \"Fist Full of Rice & Dal\" initiative, a week-long charitable drive designed to cultivate the spirit of giving and provide much-needed support to underprivileged communities. This unique initiative encouraged the students and staff of RVCE to set aside a fistful of rice and dal during their daily meal preparation as a simple yet powerful gesture of generosity. The initiative embodied the principle that small, consistent acts of kindness, when multiplied across a large community, can create a profound and lasting impact. ","aicteMapping":"Community Service and Social Welfare Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/OqwywbywxhOXZ7ki_ZdPO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"HUmuMYoz4OguJPGiyTyoQ","name":"Plantation Drive","slNo":6,"place":"Kengeri, Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/z4lQCdjlWtgm_FbSK_1rs.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/PpcefcR2HCLk725yJOR4K.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-05-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"The plantation drive led to the successful planting of several saplings, contributing to improved greenery and environmental quality. It helped create awareness about the importance of trees and encouraged students to take responsibility for protecting nature. The activity fostered a sense of environmental stewardship and motivated participants to continue eco-friendly practices in their daily lives, supporting long-term sustainability efforts.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-26","hoursSpent":5,"description":"A Plantation Drive was organized to promote environmental conservation and enhance green cover in the surrounding area. Students actively participated in planting saplings within the campus and nearby open spaces, emphasizing the importance of trees in maintaining ecological balance. The activity aimed to raise awareness about climate change, air pollution, and the role of afforestation in sustainable development. Participants were educated on proper planting techniques and the need for regular care and maintenance to ensure healthy plant growth.","aicteMapping":"Environment and Sustainability–related activities","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/CgUzu-lLktHyEgglE0XeC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hPB1AP11UQ7PFnqcUh9y4","name":"Indi-Genius","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE, IEM Auditorium","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/-e6OaFT0NXeHALP00M1Il.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/2IVY9IR5ma4ie_AX9YCPq.png"],"endDate":"2023-07-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Awareness of Indian Knowledge Systems, Indian cultural heritage and diversity was created through this quiz.\\nThe quiz served as a platform to marvel at our nation and instill a sense of pride and the need to conserve the unique beauty of Indian culture and heritage.\\n","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-14","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Indigenius – The India Quiz was held as part of RV QuizCorp’s flagship annual quiz fest, Under the Peepal ’23. The quiz saw participation of students from premier colleges across India such as IITM, NITK, NITT, RVCE, BMS, PES.\\nThe event focused on showcasing the rich cultural heritage of India and the Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS). Participants were quizzed on their awareness of the various interesting facts about India.\\nRounds were dedicated to Indian art forms, Indian languages, Indian history, technology and the rich diversity of our nation. Participants were enriched with knowledge and a sense of pride towards our nation, its people, cultures, languages and diversity.\\n","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities by Quiz Corp","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/rfROvwE8Y3HmQpZyq3T9Q.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DUuWglCaPDeFu3SAXu_L2","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/9uWJ1LsesXIpv1PbmtA1l.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-03-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative improved access to basic educational resources for underprivileged students, contributing to a better learning environment. It also fostered social responsibility, empathy, and community engagement among student volunteers involved in planning and execution.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-30","hoursSpent":10,"description":"Project Pustak is a social initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged students in rural areas by providing essential school supplies. Funds collected through donor contributions of ₹100 or ₹350 were utilized to procure textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other learning resources. The project was carried out by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Pranav Foundation to promote equitable access to education.","aicteMapping":"Educational Support and Community Development Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/4RJfQFAWaILVMMTz61hhb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"v7yDkqz92DD8wX-yMEOAs","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth-SDG Photography Contest","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/yUZf0aE6Q5wEOlgisi5w-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"The contest resulted in the submission of several impactful photographs that effectively conveyed messages aligned with the Sustainable Development Goals. It enhanced students’ creative thinking and awareness of sustainability issues. The activity also promoted active engagement with global development initiatives and encouraged participants to use their skills to advocate for positive social and environmental change.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-20","hoursSpent":1,"description":"An SDG Photography Contest was organized to encourage students to creatively showcase the importance of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Participants captured photographs highlighting real-life issues and solutions related to sustainability, such as environmental conservation, social responsibility, and community development. The activity aimed to raise awareness about global challenges and inspire students to think critically about sustainable practices through visual storytelling. The second round qualified students were given a chance of live photography and then winners were announced.","aicteMapping":"SDG Awareness and Social Responsibility Activity","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/b3HdiS6Sm0rEApC3mzYyG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NwIWx9Ha2ZcO3n-IrFUvz","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/LS6DuOWM6GTXPkzRN0SAh.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/iG-kGfNSDrteGyBq37OxS.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/SqgPKUizMqVSRlvUSyLXF.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/N0WySIGuNYwGudjzCP1PV.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event fostered awareness of health and fitness while strengthening community engagement and social responsibility among participants. It also enhanced volunteers’ organizational, coordination, and leadership skills through large-scale event execution.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Utsarga Marathon was a community-focused outreach event aimed at promoting health, social responsibility, and collective participation. The marathon brought together students, volunteers, and members of the public to support a meaningful social cause while encouraging physical fitness and community bonding.","aicteMapping":"Health, Fitness and Well-being / Social Awareness Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/X1k1Q7CGKHJf4aL1wmh0H.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1YBIukWG5wQkQv9Y6p6MR","name":"Energy Literacy Training Program by Energy Swaraj Foundation","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus(Online)","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/Xf8MTo1V29swj47zVyXrt.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-31","duration":11,"outcomes":"The Energy Swaraj activity increased awareness among students about the importance of renewable energy and energy self-sufficiency. Participants gained a better understanding of sustainable energy practices, energy conservation, and the role of individuals in reducing carbon footprint. The initiative motivated students to adopt energy-efficient habits and support the use of clean energy sources such as solar power. Overall, the activity encouraged responsible energy consumption and strengthened commitment towards environmental sustainability and national clean energy goals.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-08-21","hoursSpent":22,"description":"The event enriched students’ perspectives by exposing them to interdisciplinary ideas, real-life \\nsuccess stories, and societal challenges. It fostered inspiration, self-reflection, and motivation \\nto pursue passion-driven and socially responsible career paths. Students gained insights into \\nleadership, creativity, mental well-being, governance, entrepreneurship, and the importance of \\nperseverance and innovation. The activity enhanced communication skills, critical thinking, \\nand cultural awareness while encouraging personal growth and lifelong learning. Overall, \\nTEDxRVCE 2023 contributed significantly to the holistic development of students and aligned \\nwith AICTE’s objectives of experiential learning and personality development.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness and Value-Based Education Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/srVlOs_h40HIX5pMHVWGZ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KOTDH36r4CkpKeqbBiS54","name":"Fistfull","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/bC92sqlrax43JSV3oq0SC.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/CoLnomEIv5ODuC6Z112-x.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in the “Fist Full” initiative, I became more aware of the issue of \\nhunger and the importance of contributing to community welfare. The activity strengthened my \\nsense of empathy and social responsibility, as I realized how small individual contributions can \\ncollectively create a significant impact. I gained satisfaction from being part of a large-scale \\nhumanitarian effort and was motivated to actively engage in future social service initiatives. \\nThis experience reinforced the value of compassion, unity, and responsible citizenship.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-20","hoursSpent":2,"description":"“Fist Full” was a social outreach and hunger-relief initiative organized by the Rotaract \\nClub of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th to \\n30th November 2025. The initiative aimed to combat hunger and support food security by \\nencouraging students to contribute essential food grains. As part of the drive, students were \\ninvited to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, with daily collections organized at the Civil \\nDepartment. The initiative witnessed an overwhelming response, resulting in the collection of \\nmore than 7000 kg of rice and 1000 kg of toor dal from over 2,050 students. The collected food \\ngrains were directed toward community welfare efforts, highlighting the impact of collective \\naction in addressing basic human needs.","aicteMapping":"Community Service and Social Welfare Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/95dYX_6tAipGUGq9jxp9r.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ehzoJ1YTOBQ9P5PAAqu_f","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":15,"place":"Vijayanagar, Attiguppe Residential Areas","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/P2AU7_obNt_rc62a7Vw82.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/tE7dH0udNLX3NWyZJtQyr.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully generated funds for charitable causes through recycling while promoting environmental sustainability. It also strengthened students’ teamwork, leadership, and community engagement skills, fostering a strong sense of social responsibility.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-25","hoursSpent":6,"description":"On 24th June 2023, the Rotaract Club of RVCE organized a large-scale community service initiative in Bengaluru focused on economic and community development. With the support of over 500 volunteers, the event involved collecting newspapers and recyclable paper materials from various localities to raise funds for social welfare, benefiting the Nele Narendra Foundation.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/WRHam7Vtv5u_y84_HFkjS.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"lTEuBcPe5z79BG2xKk3aW","name":"TedX RVCE","slNo":16,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/ipAZ6OM93_tJ-imjwoTK0.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event enriched students’ perspectives by exposing them to interdisciplinary ideas, real-life \\nsuccess stories, and societal challenges. It fostered inspiration, self-reflection, and motivation \\nto pursue passion-driven and socially responsible career paths. Students gained insights into \\nleadership, creativity, mental well-being, governance, entrepreneurship, and the importance of \\nperseverance and innovation. The activity enhanced communication skills, critical thinking, \\nand cultural awareness while encouraging personal growth and lifelong learning. Overall, \\nTEDxRVCE 2023 contributed significantly to the holistic development of students and aligned \\nwith AICTE’s objectives of experiential learning and personality development","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-08","hoursSpent":6,"description":"TEDxRVCE 2023, themed Resonating Chords, was a full-day intellectual and cultural event \\norganized on June 8, 2023, at the IEM Auditorium, RV College of Engineering. The event \\nfeatured an eminent lineup of speakers from diverse domains, each sharing unique life \\nexperiences, professional journeys, and ideas aimed at inspiring students and fostering holistic \\ndevelopment.\\nThe event commenced with an inspiring talk by Mr. Rishi Raghavan, who shared his journey \\nin local governance and community leadership, emphasizing the role of youth participation, \\ngrassroots initiatives, and responsible leadership in driving societal transformation. His talk \\nhighlighted how dedication and vision can bring meaningful change even without a traditional \\npolitical background.\\nMs. Andaleeb Wajid, a renowned author and self-published writer, spoke about her journey from \\nbeing a novice writer to a successful author with over forty published books. She provided \\ninsights into self-publishing, perseverance, and balancing personal responsibilities with \\nprofessional aspirations, motivating students to pursue creative passions despite challenges.\\nMr. Nishit Sharma, a travel filmmaker, self-taught cinematographer, and content creator, shared \\nhis experiences of choosing passion over conventional career paths. Through his journey as an \\nIIT graduate who embraced storytelling through cinematography, he emphasized authenticity, \\ncreativity, and the transformative power of visual media in shaping narratives and careers.\\nThe event also featured Mr. Krishna Setty, an acclaimed artist, art critic, printmaker, and former \\nChairman of Lalit Kala Akademi. He discussed the significance of art in society, creative \\ndiscipline, and cultural heritage, encouraging students to appreciate artistic expression as both \\na profession and a way of life.\\nDr. Padmakshi Lokesh, a distinguished doctor, clinical psychologist, and stress management \\nspecialist, delivered a session focused on mental well-being, stress management, and personal \\ngrowth. She shared practical techniques to manage stress, develop resilience, and cultivate a \\npositive mindset essential for academic and professional success.\\nThe artistic dimension of the event was further enriched by Vidwan Sujay Shanbhag, who \\nnarrated his life journey in the field of art and music. He spoke about the challenges and rewards \\nof pursuing art as a profession, highlighting the dedication, discipline, and perseverance required \\nto achieve self-sustainability through creative pursuits.\\nThe event concluded with an enlightening session by Shri D. P. Nagendra Kumar, a former \\ngovernment officer and key contributor to the implementation of the Goods and Services Tax \\n(GST) in India. His talk provided students with valuable insights into public policy, economic \\nreforms, and the importance of governance, helping them understand the rationale and impact \\nof GST on the Indian economy.\\nOverall, TEDxRVCE 2023 provided students with a rich platform to engage with \\nforward-thinking leaders, gain multidisciplinary exposure, and explore diverse career pathways, \\nthereby creating a meaningful and inspiring learning experience beyond the classroom.","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/JWEHydCIRmQ9uD9AyFRs1.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-31","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"AvIx2468IMy_mPlJRQzFA","name":"Vikshit Bharat Challenge","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE(online)","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/pxISok_WmsebJMm1f14QJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity improved participants’ awareness of India’s development initiatives and governance systems. It enhanced quick decision-making, digital literacy, and general knowledge skills. The quiz motivated students to remain updated on national progress and inspired a sense of responsibility towards contributing to a developed and empowered India","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-10-28","hoursSpent":0.2,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge was an online knowledge-based competition organized through the MyGov Quiz platform to promote awareness about India’s development goals, government initiatives, and the vision of a progressive and self-reliant nation. The quiz included questions related to national programs, economic growth, social welfare schemes, innovation, and India’s future roadmap. Participants actively engaged in the digital quiz format, testing their general knowledge and understanding of national development efforts. The activity encouraged students to stay informed about public policies and contribute towards building a knowledgeable and responsible society.","aicteMapping":"Quiz on National Vision and Public Policy Awareness","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/FbetTkaMLV9sce9Lv-Z8J.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"32-33","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"reF8C6evhsuxu6BVq-pmE","name":"Indi-Genius","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/zOmKkQDv6b_nry7OzCiig.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/nR6VIquQhj-QnFzTVVMRP.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Awareness of Indian Knowledge Systems, Indian cultural heritage and diversity was created through this quiz.\\nThe quiz served as a platform to marvel at our nation and instill a sense of pride and the need to conserve the unique beauty of Indian culture and heritage.\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-09","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Indigenius – The India Quiz was held as part of RV QuizCorp’s flagship annual quiz fest, Under the Peepal ’23. The quiz saw participation of students from premier colleges across India such as IITM, NITK, NITT, RVCE, BMS, PES.\\nThe event focused on showcasing the rich cultural heritage of India and the Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS). Participants were quizzed on their awareness of the various interesting facts about India.\\nRounds were dedicated to Indian art forms, Indian languages, Indian history, technology and the rich diversity of our nation. Participants were enriched with knowledge and a sense of pride towards our nation, its people, cultures, languages and diversity.\\n","aicteMapping":"Cultural Activities by Quiz Corp","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/5bcocTshhzWFniEsJfz-L.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"34-35","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NC9eMw_dpTHJox1bxMAw3","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth-SDG Photography Contest","slNo":17,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/i24k1cB8HctSxfmGXGm2A.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-08-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The contest received several meaningful and creative photograph submissions that effectively reflected the themes of the Sustainable Development Goals. It enhanced participants’ awareness of sustainability issues and improved their creative and observational skills. The activity encouraged students to actively engage with global sustainability initiatives and promote positive social and environmental responsibility.","semester":"4","startDate":"2023-08-19","hoursSpent":1,"description":"An SDG Photography Contest was organized to encourage students to creatively represent the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through photography. Participants captured photographs highlighting real-world issues and sustainable solutions related to environmental protection, social awareness, and community development. The activity aimed to increase awareness about global challenges and motivate students to express sustainability concepts through visual storytelling. Then the photographs were selected for second round and then the winners were announced.","aicteMapping":"SDG Awareness and Social Responsibility Activity","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/91364f68-a961-46c4-8c1c-709e5427eefa/JYjkQOnHlxvqUeu-ljg3J.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"36-37","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Rohini S Hallikar","designation":"Assistant Professor, Department of Electronics & Communication Engineering"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 15:11:38.459336+00', '2026-01-30 15:30:59.867981+00'), ('f0bd8dac-9887-4133-94a7-60b1f3efd812', 'f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS157","name":"Ramachandra Manjunath Rayakar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"C3jcg9hpWzAw9XDWetMDg","name":"Kannada Habba - Karnata","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/nMirTQZqu85lJrlwuMXp2.png"],"endDate":"2023-06-05","duration":22,"outcomes":"Promoted awareness and pride in Kannada language and culture among students.\\n\\nProvided a platform for students to showcase artistic and cultural talents.\\n\\nStrengthened cultural unity and inclusiveness on campus.\\n\\nEncouraged active participation in regional heritage activities.\\n\\nEnhanced appreciation of Karnataka’s traditions and values within the RVCE community.\\n\\nFostered teamwork and event management skills among Kannada Sangha volunteers.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-05-15","hoursSpent":16,"description":"Kannada Habba was a vibrant cultural celebration organized by the Kannada Sangha of RVCE to promote and preserve Karnataka’s rich language, heritage, and traditions. The event brought together students and faculty to celebrate Kannada literature, folk arts, music, and cultural pride.\\n\\nThe program featured various performances including classical and folk dance, music, poetry recitations, skits, and speeches highlighting the significance of the Kannada language and Karnataka’s cultural identity. Students actively participated in showcasing traditional art forms, costumes, and customs, creating an engaging and festive atmosphere across the campus.\\n\\nKannada Habba served as a platform to encourage linguistic pride, cultural awareness, and unity among students, while strengthening appreciation for regional heritage within the RVCE community.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/WZ2rlgNVlyxeyRlYfUKwM.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"qKLCZYV38QYi3M1j5LE-N","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":2,"place":"Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/QJJWn3n3Cn8FiYzR3FuOS.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Collected over 7 tonnes of newspapers and waste paper within nine hours.\\n\\nMobilized 500+ student volunteers for a large-scale community service activity.\\n\\nSuccessfully raised funds for the Nele Narendra Foundation supporting underprivileged communities.\\n\\nPromoted environmental responsibility through recycling of paper waste.\\n\\nStrengthened teamwork, leadership, and organizational skills among volunteers.\\n\\nReinforced the spirit of social service and empathy among RVCE students.\\n\\nDemonstrated the effectiveness of student-driven fundraising for social welfare.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-24","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE successfully organized a mega Newspaper Collection Drive to support orphanages and underprivileged communities by raising funds for social welfare. The event aimed to bring smiles to those in need while promoting student-driven community service.\\n\\nWith overwhelming support from 500+ volunteers, students collected more than 7 tonnes of newspapers in just over nine hours. Registered volunteers assembled at Kriyakalpa, RVCE at 8:00 AM and were transported by buses to various localities across Bengaluru to collect newspapers, books, magazines, and other waste papers.\\n\\nThe collected materials were sold to paper vendors, and the funds raised were donated to the Nele Narendra Foundation for the welfare of underprivileged individuals. This initiative showcased the power of collective student effort in driving meaningful community impact.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/4Gmeb02CUivcYvL2M8JWa.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vmf3uilJCgUUMNiY3RGJ9","name":"Campus Clean Up Drive Phase I","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced campus cleanliness and hygiene standards.\\n\\nCreated awareness about waste segregation and sustainable practices among students.\\n\\nEncouraged student participation in social and environmental service activities.\\n\\nDeveloped teamwork, leadership, and civic responsibility among NSS volunteers.\\n\\nReinforced the value of environmental conservation within the RVCE community.\\n\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS initiatives in promoting social responsibility.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-13","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Campus Clean-Up Drive to promote environmental awareness and encourage responsible waste management practices among students. The initiative aimed to maintain a clean, hygienic, and eco-friendly campus environment while fostering a sense of social and civic responsibility.\\n\\nVolunteers actively participated in collecting litter, segregating waste, and ensuring proper disposal across different areas of the RVCE campus. The drive also educated students on the importance of cleanliness, sustainability, and adopting environmentally friendly habits in daily life. Through enthusiastic participation, the event successfully conveyed the message that collective effort is essential in maintaining a green and healthy campus.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/5Iz56Jjcvqt90O5prGOnx.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eb8O1OpuME2sAGAq_t9kY","name":"Campus Clean Up Drive Phase II","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"Enhanced campus cleanliness and hygiene standards.\\n\\nCreated awareness about waste segregation and sustainable practices among students.\\n\\nEncouraged student participation in social and environmental service activities.\\n\\nDeveloped teamwork, leadership, and civic responsibility among NSS volunteers.\\n\\nReinforced the value of environmental conservation within the RVCE community.\\n\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS initiatives in promoting social responsibility.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-27","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Campus Clean-Up Drive to promote environmental awareness and encourage responsible waste management practices among students. The initiative aimed to maintain a clean, hygienic, and eco-friendly campus environment while fostering a sense of social and civic responsibility.\\n\\nVolunteers actively participated in collecting litter, segregating waste, and ensuring proper disposal across different areas of the RVCE campus. The drive also educated students on the importance of cleanliness, sustainability, and adopting environmentally friendly habits in daily life. Through enthusiastic participation, the event successfully conveyed the message that collective effort is essential in maintaining a green and healthy campus.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/QfHKSC7ru1qgWYcpaIabT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"zj3qqqQxM8joUqZGQBl9v","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus and Outskirts","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/YJujePHmFLDX4nTtAUT5_.webp"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Encouraged physical fitness and healthy lifestyle habits among students.\\n\\nPromoted social awareness and participation in community-oriented causes.\\n\\nDeveloped discipline, perseverance, and endurance through marathon participation.\\n\\nStrengthened student engagement in NSS initiatives.\\n\\nFostered a spirit of teamwork and motivation among participants.\\n\\nEarned 10 activity points for active participation and commitment.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RV College of Engineering organized the Utsarga Marathon to promote physical fitness, social responsibility, and awareness towards meaningful community causes. The marathon encouraged students to actively participate in a health-focused and service-oriented activity that combined endurance, discipline, and commitment to social welfare.\\n\\nParticipants took part in different distance categories, fostering enthusiasm for fitness and teamwork. I actively participated in the 5 KM category of the Utsarga Marathon, demonstrating commitment toward health, perseverance, and support for a worthy social cause.\\n\\nThe event successfully motivated students to adopt a healthy lifestyle while contributing to NSS’s mission of community engagement and social consciousness.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/iLo4RyeywvbkjUkJdNJVP.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0R217CUJUUUKAAjEogTQ8","name":"Mera Pehla Vote Desh Keliye","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/XeARE_z-iwte7LqYwZpzj.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/OtMB7LctjZUgatA9bLT-x.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Created awareness about the importance of voting among students.\\n\\nEncouraged active participation in the democratic process.\\n\\nPromoted responsible citizenship and national commitment.\\n\\nStrengthened civic consciousness among youth.\\n\\nReinforced the role of NSS in conducting awareness initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye was a voter awareness initiative conducted by the National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE to promote civic responsibility and educate students about the importance of voting in a democratic country. The program aimed to inspire young citizens to actively participate in the electoral process and understand their role in nation-building.\\n\\nThrough awareness sessions and pledge activities, participants were encouraged to register as voters, understand electoral procedures, and exercise their voting rights responsibly. The event successfully fostered a sense of patriotism and civic consciousness among students.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/cxjwCKl5LZVMmR8ySi6d9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uZQe88TxU4Jd6V0kM0kz0","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/sFQ69mTGoLT3j6K6P8Qee.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Collected financial contributions from donors to support underprivileged students.\\n\\nProcured and distributed essential school supplies including textbooks, stationery, and backpacks.\\n\\nSupported rural and underprivileged students in accessing quality education.\\n\\nEncouraged a strong sense of social responsibility and community service among volunteers.\\n\\nStrengthened collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Pranav Foundation.\\n\\nContributed to creating a better learning environment for deserving students.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak was a commendable and noble initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with the Pranav Foundation, aimed at providing essential school supplies to underprivileged students residing in rural areas. The primary objective of the project was to support students who lack access to basic educational resources and help create a conducive learning environment.\\n\\nUnder this initiative, donors generously contributed either Rs. 100 or Rs. 350, which formed the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed school supplies. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase textbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other educational materials. These supplies were then distributed to deserving students, ensuring they had the necessary tools to continue their education without financial constraints.\\n\\nThrough collective effort and compassionate participation, Project Pustak successfully extended educational support to underprivileged students and reinforced the spirit of social responsibility among RVCE students.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/wUri9jjTMCblOu6HVDEic.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Yq6wsnJz_dcdJLfXSya4z","name":"Mega Plantation Drive @Kanakapura Road","slNo":8,"place":"Kanakapura Road, Bengaluru","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-05-25","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased green cover in the elephant corridor region through sapling plantation.\\n\\nPromoted awareness about wildlife conservation and ecological balance among students.\\n\\nEncouraged active student participation in environmental service activities.\\n\\nDeveloped a sense of responsibility toward protecting natural habitats.\\n\\nContributed to long-term environmental sustainability and ecosystem restoration.\\n\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS environmental initiatives at RVCE.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-25","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Mega Plantation Drive at the Elephant Walking Corridor near Kanakapura Road, Bengaluru, as part of its environmental and community service initiatives. The event aimed to enhance green cover, support wildlife habitat restoration, and promote ecological conservation in regions critical for elephant movement.\\n\\nNSS volunteers actively participated in planting saplings in the corridor area, contributing to soil conservation, restoration of natural habitats, and long-term environmental sustainability. The drive also raised awareness among students about the importance of preserving wildlife pathways and maintaining harmony between urban development and natural ecosystems.\\n\\nThrough collective effort, the initiative successfully highlighted the role of students in environmental protection and wildlife conservation.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/IrGIm7aEZLQKoZmv0ugmf.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"33BWRpExVWKb-E9wTC1oH","name":"Adhamya Chetan Plantation @Kengeri","slNo":9,"place":"Kengeri","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/XgRwFZdGdcEwSWAm7AQl8.png"],"endDate":"2024-05-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"Contributed to increasing green cover in the Kengeri region.\\n\\nSupported Adhamya Chetana’s 439th consecutive Green Sunday plantation initiative.\\n\\nPromoted awareness about environmental conservation and tree nurturing.\\n\\nEncouraged active community participation in afforestation programs.\\n\\nContributed to long-term ecological sustainability and pollution reduction.\\n\\nDeveloped a sense of environmental responsibility and social commitment among participants.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-05-26","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Adhamya Chetana Plantation Drive was a tree planting and nurturing program conducted under Adhamya Chetana’s Green Sunday initiative at Kengeri, Bengaluru. The event aimed to promote environmental conservation by increasing green cover and encouraging public participation in afforestation activities.\\n\\nAs part of the 439th consecutive Green Sunday, volunteers actively participated in planting and nurturing saplings, contributing to long-term ecological sustainability. The initiative focused on restoring natural greenery, improving air quality, and spreading awareness about the importance of tree conservation in urban environments.\\n\\nI actively participated in this program on 26th May 2024, contributing to the plantation and supporting the mission of building a greener and healthier environment.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/IQ2MRAzzWOXL-8xAbh53B.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5nlI8QM3GCfINPt2oR-59","name":"Indi-Genius – The India Quiz (UTPT 2024)","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-06-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participated in a national-level quiz competition, gaining academic exposure beyond the college level.\\n\\nEnhanced general knowledge, logical thinking, and quick decision-making skills.\\n\\nEncouraged intellectual curiosity and competitive spirit among students.\\n\\nProvided experience in team-based and individual academic competitions.\\n\\nEarned 5 activity points for participation.\\n\\nStrengthened engagement in cultural and knowledge-based events at RVCE.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Indi-Genius: The India Quiz was a national-level quiz competition conducted as part of Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2024, organized by RVCE’s Cultural Activities Team. The event was held from 07th to 09th June 2024 and brought together students from various institutions across the country to test their knowledge of India’s history, culture, current affairs, science, and general awareness.\\n\\nThe quiz encouraged participants to think critically, respond quickly, and work under time constraints, making it both intellectually stimulating and competitive. I actively participated in this national-level quiz fest, gaining exposure to a large-scale academic competition and enhancing my knowledge and analytical skills.\\n\\nThe event successfully promoted intellectual engagement and academic enthusiasm among students.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/xXnRlPBck1J71ew3-ZG8U.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Y-zPz-ByqsoRQ0j1UQyBo","name":"Akshara","slNo":11,"place":"Government Model Primary School Kengeri","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/GtHg52FZu9OydCmPeniz5.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"Successfully reached and supported over 1000 underprivileged students across eight schools in Bangalore through academic and skill development sessions.\\n\\nEnhanced students’ foundational learning, subject understanding, and communication skills through interactive and curriculum-based teaching methods.\\n\\nIncreased student engagement and motivation toward education by introducing participatory and activity-oriented learning techniques.\\n\\nProvided practical teaching and mentoring experience to RVCE volunteers, improving their leadership, teamwork, and social responsibility skills.\\n\\nContributed to bridging educational disparities by extending quality learning support to students from financially modest backgrounds.\\n\\nStrengthened the bond between RVCE and local community schools, promoting long-term social outreach initiatives.\\n\\nReinforced the importance of volunteerism and accessible education, creating a positive impact on both students and volunteers.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE successfully conducted Akshara, a skill development and academic support initiative aimed at empowering underprivileged school students in Bangalore. The program was organized across eight schools, reaching and benefiting over 1000 students from financially modest backgrounds. The primary objective of Akshara was to enhance students’ academic understanding, strengthen foundational learning, and equip them with essential life and communication skills through interactive and engaging teaching methods.\\n\\nAs part of this initiative, I visited the Government Model Primary School, Kengeri, where I actively participated in teaching sessions and interacted with students to support their learning process. The schools covered under Akshara included BET Convent, Sai Sri Vidya Chethana, Vishwa Bharathi High School, Kengeri High School, Government Model Primary School, Nehru Memorial School, Priyadarshini Vidhya Kendra School, and Mount Carmel English School. Volunteers from RVCE served as mentors and instructors, adopting curriculum-based learning approaches to ensure effective knowledge transfer and student engagement.\\n\\nAkshara also provided volunteers with valuable teaching experience, fostering leadership, teamwork, and a deeper appreciation of the role of education in addressing social disparities. Overall, the initiative highlighted the impact of volunteerism in bridging educational gaps and reinforcing the importance of accessible quality education for all.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/JDzEnV0ZPk_ZxlqEExYJh.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"21-22","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mAZafiqB3KQlk0utTWrDF","name":"Mega Plantation @Hosadurga","slNo":12,"place":"Hosadurga","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/kc9Irkw6ed0-S3IPQT_cC.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased green cover in the Hosadurga region through large-scale plantation.\\n\\nPromoted environmental awareness among students and local residents.\\n\\nEncouraged active student participation in eco-friendly community service.\\n\\nDeveloped a sense of social and environmental responsibility among volunteers.\\n\\nContributed to long-term ecological sustainability and environmental restoration.\\n\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS environmental initiatives at RVCE.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-09","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Mega Plantation Drive at Hosadurga, as part of its environmental sustainability and community outreach initiatives. The primary objective of the event was to enhance green cover, promote afforestation, and create awareness about environmental conservation among students and local communities.\\n\\nNSS volunteers actively participated in planting saplings across identified areas in Hosadurga, contributing to soil conservation, ecological restoration, and long-term environmental improvement. The drive also encouraged students to take responsibility for protecting nature and emphasized the importance of tree plantation in reducing pollution and maintaining ecological balance.\\n\\nThrough collective participation, the initiative successfully demonstrated the role of youth in building a greener and healthier society.","aicteMapping":"Reduction in energy consumption","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/eanJlCaWiSkfg3wddW0Qq.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"23-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hqnM8yNa3EIuKkJ8OoNU2","name":"Kannada Habba - Gharjane","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/DRQodTU4fDAnsPEf8X4pS.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-20","duration":20,"outcomes":"Promoted Kannada language and cultural awareness among students.\\n\\nProvided opportunities for students to showcase artistic and creative talents.\\n\\nStrengthened cultural pride and unity within the RVCE community.\\n\\nEncouraged active participation in cultural and heritage programs.\\n\\nDeveloped event coordination and teamwork skills among Kannada Sangha members.\\n\\nEnhanced appreciation for Karnataka’s traditional art forms.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-01","hoursSpent":16,"description":"Gharjane was a grand cultural event organized by the Kannada Sangha of RVCE as part of Kannada Habba celebrations. The program was conducted to promote the Kannada language, heritage, and cultural traditions among students and faculty of RVCE.\\n\\nThe event featured a variety of performances including traditional folk dances, music, drama, poetry recitations, and cultural presentations that reflected the richness of Karnataka’s art and history. Students actively participated in showcasing their talents, wearing traditional attire and bringing vibrant energy to the celebration.\\n\\nGharjane served as a platform to instill pride in Kannada identity, strengthen cultural awareness, and create a sense of unity and inclusiveness on campus. The event successfully highlighted the importance of preserving regional culture in a modern academic environment.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/TCYSSWBNT2nILf7e_L-z8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"25-26","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"NkkrUJB-Oit2sv5srZ_Nf","name":"Paper Drive 2.0","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-01-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"Promoted awareness about reducing plastic usage and environmental protection.\\n\\nEncouraged adoption of eco-friendly paper bags among local vendors and community members.\\n\\nFostered active student involvement in sustainability and social service activities.\\n\\nDeveloped a sense of environmental responsibility among participants.\\n\\nContributed to reducing plastic waste in the surrounding community.\\n\\nStrengthened the impact of NSS initiatives in promoting green practices.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-02","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The National Service Scheme (NSS), RVCE organized a Paper Bag Distribution Drive as part of its environmental sustainability initiatives. The event aimed to promote the use of eco-friendly alternatives to plastic bags and create awareness about reducing plastic pollution.\\n\\nDuring the drive, NSS volunteers actively collected and submitted handmade paper bags, which were later distributed to local shops and vendors to encourage the adoption of sustainable packaging practices. The initiative also educated students and community members on the harmful effects of plastic on the environment and the importance of switching to biodegradable materials.\\n\\nThrough enthusiastic student participation, the event successfully contributed to environmental conservation while reinforcing the values of social responsibility and sustainable living.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/_ll5rB3v1bfgerlYGYhfz.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"27-28","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_qTIrqjLHCbh8HwW2qs65","name":"Say No to Drugs Pledge (Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan)","slNo":15,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"Created awareness about the dangers of drug and substance abuse among students.\\n\\nEncouraged participants to commit to a drug-free and healthy lifestyle through a formal pledge.\\n\\nStrengthened a sense of personal responsibility and self-discipline among youth.\\n\\nSupported the national vision of Nasha Mukt Bharat (Drug-Free India).\\n\\nPromoted mental and physical well-being through positive lifestyle choices.\\n\\nReinforced the role of students as responsible citizens contributing to a healthier society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":"As part of the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan, an awareness initiative by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, Government of India, a “Say No to Drugs” pledge program was conducted to promote a drug-free and healthy lifestyle among students.\\n\\nDuring this event, participants formally took a pledge to consciously stay away from drug abuse, remain sober, and adopt healthy habits in daily life. The program aimed to raise awareness about the harmful effects of substance abuse and to encourage youth to take responsibility for their personal well-being and societal health.\\n\\nI actively participated in this initiative and took the official pledge on 14th August 2025, committing myself to support the vision of a drug-free India","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/OrDimomsBTNhmi74J4Buk.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"29-30","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6IKjKXyCTiNk-WcWdCy_s","name":"Fist Full","slNo":16,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"Mobilized 2146 students to collectively address food insecurity.\\n\\nCollected and distributed 4370 kg of rice and 2516 kg of dal to care institutions.\\n\\nProvided sustained nutritional support to vulnerable groups.\\n\\nStrengthened student participation in social welfare initiatives.\\n\\nReinforced Rotaract’s mission of community service and volunteerism.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-27","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Fistful was a standalone community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, with support from Rotary Bangalore Spandana, under the Community Service Avenue focusing on Fighting Disease. The project aimed to combat food insecurity and support health and care institutions through collective student participation.\\n\\nEach participating student contributed either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of dal, resulting in the collection of 4370 kg of rice and 2516 kg of dal from 2146 students. The collected food grains were distributed to beneficiary institutions including Hanuman Temple mass feeding center, Pruthvi Foundation (Blind Boys Hostel, Chandapura), Amruthavani Vridh Seva Samithi, Sai Ashraya Hospital, Sai Satguna Sangraha Trust School, Neev Foundation, and nearby Anganwadis.\\n\\nThe initiative successfully transformed individual student contributions into large-scale nutritional support for children, elderly individuals, patients, and economically disadvantaged communities, highlighting the spirit of service and social responsibility among RVCE students.","aicteMapping":"Food preservation/packaging","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/f620046c-3b0d-4a59-b4bd-424489a2b00d/vLwkRYIvfrpzf8JEdTku9.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"31-32","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Prof. Apoorva Udaya Kumar Chate","designation":"Assistant Professor, Department of CSE"},"evaluator1":{"name":"Dr. Uma B V","designation":"Professor, Department of ECE"},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 04:03:29.412184+00', '2026-01-31 04:46:45.030648+00'), ('f1131b0e-9f59-4a81-beed-625f148821e7', 'b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY014","name":"Aryan Chaturvedi","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"JUr5b5X7T-iMWV2g7K1rj","name":"ACM Build with Gen AI Hackathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/Pxi7gp_Go7Xaj_6JNXmiZ.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":1,"outcomes":"As the organizer behind this hackathon, I gained firsthand experience in rapid-cycle project\\nmanagement and the nuances of fostering a specialized technical community. I had to navigate\\nthe logistics of a physical, offline venue while managing a partnership between ACM RVCE\\nand the Accelerate Club, which sharpened your ability to align different organizational goals\\ntoward a single vision.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-29","hoursSpent":20,"description":"The \"Build with GenAI\" Hackathon, organized by ACM RVCE and Accelerate Club at RV\\nCollege of Engineering, was a 6-hour offline event held on November 29, 2024, focused on\\ncreating AI-powered solutions. The competition encouraged teams of 2-4 members to develop\\ninnovative applications, such as agriculture assistants, with a ¹ 6,000 prize pool.","aicteMapping":"Technical / Professional Activity","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8ZpuryNEQdHSSAk1kxBQU","name":"TechTank Hackathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/DMmksNPyG-MxtbNb7SaZs.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-11","duration":5,"outcomes":"I learned that the real challenge of a 12-hour sprint isn''t the code, but the orchestration.\\nI mastered how to synchronize technical development with business viability by forcing a\\nbridge between developer grit and investor expectations. Managing this event taught me that\\n\"market-ready\" isn''t just a buzzword; it’s the result of rigorous time-boxing and facilitating the\\nright connections under pressure.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-07","hoursSpent":10,"description":"TechTank 2025 at RVCE was a 12-hour, Shark Tank-inspired hackathon held in April 2025, with\\nkey activities occurring around April 7th to April 11th, 2025. Organized by GDG RVCE and\\nACM RVCE, the event focused on innovation and entrepreneurship, featuring workshops and\\npitching sessions for student projects.","aicteMapping":"Technical / Professional Activity","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5IBypGZCVIY38n7Qcv7bU","name":"FEMALE FOETICIDE AWARENESS WALKATHON","slNo":4,"place":"Around RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/lA7X74Q0FDpspL3jpskUz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-05-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The event witnessed overwhelming participation with more\\nthan 350 participants, reflecting strong support and awareness\\nfor the cause. The walkathon successfully raised\\nconsciousness about female foeticide and gender equality\\namong the campus community. It encouraged participants to\\ntake a stand against gender based violence and discrimination\\nand reinforced the values of respect and equality. Overall, the\\nevent achieved its objective of fostering social awareness,\\ncommunity engagement and a sense of responsibility towards\\npromoting the dignity and rights of women and girls.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-14","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon was organised by\\nthe Rotaract Club of RVCE on the occasion of Mother’s Day,\\n11th May 2025, with the aim of spreading awareness about the\\nissue of female foeticide and promoting gender equality. The\\nwalkathon was conducted within the college campus and\\ninvolved active participation from students, teaching staff and\\nnon-teaching staff. The event focused on educating\\nparticipants about the importance of protecting the rights of\\nthe girl child and addressing societal issues related to gender\\nbased discrimination. The walkathon served as a platform to\\nencourage reflection, dialogue and collective responsibility\\ntowards creating a more inclusive and equitable society.","aicteMapping":"Social Awareness / Community Service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/56Ivz5xyAEHKpdT96ZDyI.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gqKClaAqlRNdDxHPkWK__","name":"UTSARGA MARATHON-5KM","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/pP_OAPaZ1dzAPSBx6UAeE.png"],"endDate":"0025-02-18","duration":-730484,"outcomes":"I learned that I’m capable of more than I thought, especially when there''s a good reason to keep\\nrunning. Pushing through the miles for a cause like \"Help a Child\" showed me that fitness is\\nway more rewarding when you''re running for someone else’s future, not just your own health.","semester":"3","startDate":"2025-02-18","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon 2024, organized by the NSS wing of RV College of Engineering (RVCE)\\nand sponsored by Elegant Builders & Developers, was a flagship charity event focused on\\nthe theme \"Help a Child, Change the World\". Held in early 2024, the event aimed to support\\nunderprivileged children through education, healthcare, and welfare initiatives.","aicteMapping":"NSS / Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/IImQrcUhP30_fNPFsq9VH.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vggvAnHSfsRrR5lgXuhYO","name":"FIST FULL ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE ","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/3mqmftbw5BSUwd39x4dH3.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":17,"outcomes":"The successful completion of both phases of the\\nFist Full Project by the Rotaract Club of RVCE\\nsignificantly contributed to addressing hunger\\nand supporting underprivileged communities.\\nThrough collective efforts, a substantial quantity\\nof food grains was collected and distributed to\\ncharitable organizations and schools, ensuring\\nnourishment for many in need. The initiative\\nfostered compassion, social responsibility, and\\ncommunity involvement among volunteers,\\ndemonstrating how small individual\\ncontributions can create a meaningful and lasting\\nsocial impact.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-01","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE has successfully\\ncompleted both Phase 1 and Phase 2 of the Fist\\nFull project. In collaboration with the Rotary\\nClub of Bangalore Spandana, District 3191. This\\ninitiative, centered around the simple yet\\nimpactful act of donating just a fistfull of rice and\\ndal. In Phase 1, we gathered 325 kg of rice, 115\\nkg of toor dal, 20 kg of wheat flour, and 15 kg of\\nMoong dal. The provisions were made at Advaya\\nEducational and Charitable Trust. Coming to the\\n2nd Phase, we collected and donated 1640 kg of\\nrice and 600 kg of toor dal, to the Sai Gurukul\\nSchool in Bengaluru, which provides free\\neducation, food, and other necessities to\\nunderprivileged children.","aicteMapping":"Social Service / NGO Activity","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/DH41gn061ho01TDtMAR25.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_Hkt6C_WRhxaDx8AX1JL-","name":"ACM India Chapter Summit","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE & BMS Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/1ZdckaXf1-idpTVBpHF1p.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-21","duration":3,"outcomes":"Leading a multi-institutional event of this scale likely taught me the complexities of high-stakes\\nstakeholder management and the art of cross-functional leadership. Ultimately, my role as\\nPresident and Event Head centered on community building, teaching you that the true success of\\nsuch an initiative lies in fostering long-term collaborative networks and driving a unified vision\\nacross the entire ACM India landscape.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-19","hoursSpent":35,"description":"B.M.S College of Engineering(Anchor Venue) and R.V. College of Engineering, Bangalore,\\nKarnataka, are excited to invite ACM Chapters from across India to the Annual ACM India\\nChapter Summit 2024. The event will be held on the 20th and 21st of December, 2024, in\\nBangalore.\\nThe summit aims to foster collaboration, exchange knowledge, and explore innovative solutions\\nto drive progress in computing. By bringing together ACM chapters across India, the event also\\nseeks to strengthen the community, inspire meaningful societal contributions, and build lasting\\nconnections among Student, Professional, SIG and ACM-W Chapters.\\nThe two-day event will feature technical talks, startup showcases, panel discussions, industry\\ninteractions, and various opportunities to network and engage.","aicteMapping":"Technical / Professional Activity","pointsEarned":25,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/Os8cI7iYBPwkBfGd21zYl.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LH7r05Fp4bSIai8OU526t","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/P1zojjDPwTqPIXT9s1t5N.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"I learned the power of targeted philanthropy and resource logistics. By contributing at a higher\\ntier, I saw firsthand how individual capital when efficiently managed directly removes the\\nphysical barriers to education for rural students, transforming a small donation into a complete\\ntoolkit for learning.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-14","hoursSpent":1,"description":" Project Pustak is a commendable and noble initiative aimed at bringing essential school supplies\\nt o underprivileged students residing in rural areas. A substantial amount of Rs 100 or 350 was\\ncollected from each compassionate donor, which\\nserved as the foundation for procuring and donating much-needed supplies to these deserving\\nstudents. The collected funds were efficiently utilized to purchase educational materialssuch as\\ntextbooks, stationery items, backpacks, and other vital resources that contribute to a conducive\\nlearning environment. Through the generous contributions of donors who contributed either Rs\\n100 or Rs 350, the project garnered substantial funds.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b87d3d1c-8e6b-428c-8aba-22de021af07a/g82_x88vtJqYOcIB8qq4U.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":" "},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 05:32:57.320166+00', '2026-01-31 06:41:18.012901+00'), ('f1be026e-e793-4386-970b-b72ceafe073b', 'ed85dd32-d01a-44db-ac7c-5cf22bbfa023', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI049","name":"Shashidhar A","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"63gIgQzX_-By0eFaaONu1","name":"NSS Utsarga 2023 ","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ed85dd32-d01a-44db-ac7c-5cf22bbfa023/Sxr_1XW03gJaHnzF1wUK2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed higher levels of discipline, perseverance and commitment. Gained a deeper understanding of the importance of sustained student involvement in social awareness and outreach programs.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":10,"description":"I participated as a volunteer  in the NSS UTSARGA Marathon – organized by the NSS unit with the objective of spreading awareness about social responsibility and encouraging youth participation in community service activities.","aicteMapping":"Social responsibility and awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ed85dd32-d01a-44db-ac7c-5cf22bbfa023/pVOUrtKmF_U8lxYFn8GWV.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"K7dC2gziixDFtcS14yb84","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2023","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ed85dd32-d01a-44db-ac7c-5cf22bbfa023/ZMLNqNOhkv1M8OSuzqJKR.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Developed a strong sense of social responsibility and awareness about public health services. Understood the importance of voluntary blood donation in saving lives and encouraging students to participate in community-oriented health initiatives.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-06","hoursSpent":20,"description":"I volunteered and actively participated in the Blood Donation Camp organized at the college campus. The objective of the camp was to support local blood banks and hospitals in meeting emergency medical requirements and to create awareness among students about the importance of voluntary blood donation. I assisted in the registration process and ensured proper coordination with medical staff during the donation drive.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ed85dd32-d01a-44db-ac7c-5cf22bbfa023/qSrb0RtK7x1qzThok7yeT.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fRJsRekcKyHb18M5GrEDh","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":3,"place":"Ramnagara Taluk","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ed85dd32-d01a-44db