nages and underprivileged communities.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/ed85dd32-d01a-44db-ac7c-5cf22bbfa023/lA7_z1FayCom46y4FfsCu.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-31 05:55:06.667542+00', '2026-02-01 17:49:17.440736+00'), ('f237e66b-f472-4e83-9eaf-455db1163eb6', '375a8703-03f3-433a-a75f-d49ecffb157e', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 09:55:18.269206+00', '2026-01-29 09:55:49.223559+00'), ('f3e52cec-8b86-4532-b9ce-77c8b7e2d689', '256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS219","name":"Tejas Ganesh Hegde","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"ab7h7vCBLFvKJFoDFqFoN","name":"Yoga day","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/KvgW9sO4Cf7IY1TFj8xPz.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-21","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness about the importance of yoga for physical and mental health\\n\\nImproved flexibility, posture, and breathing awareness among participants\\n\\nEnhanced concentration, relaxation, and stress management skills\\n\\nEncouraged participants to practice yoga regularly as part of daily routine\\n\\nPromoted a sense of harmony, self-discipline, and positive lifestyle habits\\n\\nStrengthened community participation and collective well-being","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-21","hoursSpent":3,"description":"International Yoga Day was observed with great enthusiasm to promote physical, mental, and spiritual well-being among participants. The program highlighted the importance of yoga as an ancient practice that helps in maintaining a healthy lifestyle and inner balance. The session began with a brief introduction explaining the significance of yoga and its role in stress management, flexibility, and overall fitness. Certified instructors guided participants through various yoga asanas, pranayama techniques, and meditation practices. Emphasis was placed on correct posture, breathing techniques, and mindfulness. The event encouraged individuals to adopt yoga as a daily habit for leading a disciplined, healthy, and balanced life.","aicteMapping":"Community development","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/C5NY-XOwyhwJlzuGynEV8.pdf","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"w5DGmgkx3TF_dym8iFNLq","name":"Mera Pehala vote Desh ke liye","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/dZbPfKrmb2SATdlFcclVN.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-03-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"The “Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye” initiative successfully encourages first-time voters to participate actively in the electoral process. It creates awareness about voting rights and strengthens democratic values among youth. The program helps reduce voter apathy and motivates young citizens to make informed choices. It also increases overall voter turnout by building confidence in RV college of Engineering® Bengaluru AICTE activity points new voters. Overall, the initiative promotes responsible citizenship and supports a stronger, more participatory Democracy The image shows an official First Time Voter pledge certificate (2024) by the Government of India. It encourages citizens to vote responsibly, featuring an inked finger over the Ashoka Chakra with the slogan “Mera Pehla Vote – Vote Desh Ke Liye.”","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-05","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The \"Mera Pehla Vote, Desh Ke Liye\" initiative by the Indian government is a significant campaign aimed at encouraging firsttime voters to actively participate in the democratic process and exercise their fundamental right to vote. Recognizing the importance of youth involvement in shaping the nation''s future, this program seeks to instill a deep sense of responsibility, civic duty, and national pride among young citizens who are eligible to vote for the first time. By engaging with the youth and educating them about the electoral process, the initiative emphasizes the power of voting in a democracy and the impact it has on governance, policy-making, and overall national development. As a part of this initiative, individuals take a pledge, committing themselves to vote responsibly, make informed choices, and support leaders who work towards the progress and well-being of the country. Awareness programs, workshops, and interactive sessions are often conducted to familiarize first-time voters with the importance of their participation and the role they play in strengthening democratic institutions. The campaign also leverages social media, educational institutions, and community engagement programs to reach a wider audience, ensuring that young voters are motivated and well-prepared to take part in the electoral process. By fostering a culture of informed and responsible voting, \"Mera Pehla Vote, Desh Ke Liye\" serves as a crucial step in empowering the youth and reinforcing the principles of democracy, ensuring that every vote contributes to the nation’s growth and stability. Outcome The “Mera Phale Vote Desh Keliye”","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/hklRBMF9G60fUiOZn_YdO.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6fTaSWERWDISzOgUEFqQy","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/-Z8DuXa32ghGlETqNndc2.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of RVCE, successfully blended fitness, community engagement, and philanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to contribute to a meaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With enthusiastic participation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful reminder of the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges. Runners contributed through their registration fees, which were directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to educational and environmental projects. The overwhelming response from participants highlighted the deep-rooted commitment of RVCE towards community service and social responsibility. Beyond the physical endurance required to complete the marathon, the event fostered a sense of camaraderie and unity among participants, reinforcing the spirit of teamwork and determination. The well-organized event featured structured routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance, ensuring a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Additionally, the marathon acted as an awareness campaign, encouraging individuals to embrace an active lifestyle while giving back to society. The initiative not only strengthened the bond between students and the community but also showcased how small contributions, when combined, can drive impactful social change.","semester":"1","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and social responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who participate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all the proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged communities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability projects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity and collective action among participants. Beyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes the spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute to meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a marathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement, as their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the marathon includes wellmarked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a smooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread support, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond.","aicteMapping":"Community development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/ZCcYR2hYDw6g-2GKRd1vU.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"gGdD0FrGIAQ3iRhpuh3t5","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/WQ81M3Pgm9U1YNCdVhlkN.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 was successfully conducted with enthusiastic participation and strong community spirit, creating a positive blend of health awareness and social service. The event motivated participants to adopt an active lifestyle while also contributing towards a noble cause through their registration fees. The marathon also served as a powerful awareness initiative, highlighting that individual efforts combined can lead to meaningful societal change. Overall, Utsarga Marathon 2024 reinforced the NSS vision of “Not Me, But You,” inspiring students to remain socially conscious while working towards personal and community well-being.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2024 is an annual flagship event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aimed at promoting fitness, unity, and social responsibility among students and the community. The marathon encourages participation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, bringing everyone together for a cause-driven initiative. Participants register for the event by paying a nominal fee, and the total amount collected is utilized for meaningful social welfare purposes such as supporting underprivileged communities, contributing to healthcare assistance, and funding community development initiatives. The event is not just a physical challenge but also a symbol of service and commitment towards society. Utsarga Marathon is planned and executed with proper route management, volunteer coordination, and safety measures such as hydration points and medical assistance, ensuring a smooth and safe experience for participants. Through this marathon, NSS emphasizes the values of discipline, determination, and empathy, inspiring individuals to lead healthier lives while contributing to a larger social impact.","aicteMapping":"Community development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/I2PeWaVaRnBJAYDdnQRox.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ptHC2vJRqagi6rg6Ju8sf","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/lA3ctQdXCz5dA_34udQLP.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 was successfully conducted with enthusiastic participation and strong community spirit, creating a positive blend of health awareness and social service. The event motivated participants to adopt an active lifestyle while also contributing towards a noble cause through their registration fees. The marathon also served as a powerful awareness initiative, highlighting that individual efforts combined can lead to meaningful societal change. Overall, Utsarga Marathon 2025 reinforced the NSS vision of “Not Me, But You,” inspiring students to remain socially conscious while working towards personal and community well-being.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 is an annual flagship event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering, aimed at promoting fitness, unity, and social responsibility among students and the community. The marathon encourages participation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, bringing everyone together for a cause-driven initiative. Participants register for the event by paying a nominal fee, and the total amount collected is utilized for meaningful social welfare purposes such as supporting underprivileged communities, contributing to healthcare assistance, and funding community development initiatives. The event is not just a physical challenge but also a symbol of service and commitment towards society. Utsarga Marathon is planned and executed with proper route management, volunteer coordination, and safety measures such as hydration points and medical assistance, ensuring a smooth and safe experience for participants. Through this marathon, NSS emphasizes the values of discipline, determination, and empathy, inspiring individuals to lead healthier lives while contributing to a larger social impact.","aicteMapping":"Community development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/mHu-J8KcQJCUEyDDUZ707.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BB03gcIFbREauF2doHtqQ","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/vNMEhG2_UFQ0tRi7h6skp.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-07-26","duration":5,"outcomes":"Project Pustak – Phase 2 successfully created a positive impact by distributing educational supplies to students who required support for their studies. The initiative strengthened the spirit of community service among participants and helped reduce resource gaps faced by underprivileged children. Through organized planning and efficient distribution, the drive ensured that contributions were effectively transformed into meaningful educational assistance. The drive also promoted awareness about the importance of education and equal learning opportunities, reinforcing the belief that every child deserves access to quality resources. By transforming small donations into practical educational support, the activity highlighted how collective contributions can bring significant change.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Project Pustak – Phase 2 is a donation drive organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, in collaboration with Pranava Foundation, to support education for underprivileged students. The initiative collected funds from donors and used them to procure and distribute essential school supplies such as notebooks, stationery kits, geometry boxes, and other learning materials. The drive aimed to ensure that students from rural and underserved communities had access to basic educational resources and better learning support. As a part of this drive, funds were collected through generous contributions from donors and volunteers. These contributions were carefully utilized to procure essential items such as notebooks, textbooks, stationery kits, pens, pencils, erasers, geometry boxes, backpacks, and other required study materials. The collected supplies were then distributed to school-going children who required support, ensuring that they could continue their education without financial barriers.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/V9FnKBghSDfWpXONNmvDB.pdf","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Mj8YG6Q8Bcc7nTMfLc2DY","name":"Plantation Drive","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/SY3l3aRSpvC85heId3RMm.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-07-12","duration":2,"outcomes":"The plantation drive resulted in increased awareness about environmental protection among the participants and highlighted the importance of trees in daily life. Several saplings were planted, contributing to greener and healthier surroundings. The activity helped improve air quality and supported ecological balance in the area. Participants developed a strong sense of responsibility toward nature and sustainability. The drive encouraged teamwork and active community involvement. It promoted eco-friendly habits and long-term care for plants. Awareness about climate change and conservation was strengthened. Overall, the initiative supported environmental conservation and sustainable development.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-07-11","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Plantation Drive was organized with the objective of promoting environmental awareness and encouraging sustainable practices among participants. The activity involved planting saplings of native and eco-friendly species in the designated area such as the campus premises, roadside, or community land. Participants actively took part in soil preparation, planting, watering, and fencing of saplings. The drive emphasized the importance of trees in maintaining ecological balance, improving air quality, conserving biodiversity, and combating climate change. Awareness was also created about proper plant care and long-term responsibility towards nature.","aicteMapping":"Social service","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0C3ax79AsafbboJ4e_WnA","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth – SDG Photography Competition 2025","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/CHo-kiRF1hYaJrC4UkYCa.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"The SDG Photography Competition 2025 was successfully conducted and created a strong impact by enhancing social awareness, sustainable thinking, and a sense of responsibility among participants. The event encouraged students to observe real-world issues through a creative lens and connect photography with global challenges such as environment, equality, education, and sustainability. Participants gained deeper understanding of SDGs and improved their skills in photography, observation, storytelling, and creative thinking. Overall, the initiative strengthened campus-level awareness on sustainability and demonstrated how creative expression can inspire action and positive change.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"“Through the Eyes of Youth” is a large-scale SDG Photography Competition 2025 organized by SPARK (IUCEE–RVCE Student Chapter) with the objective of spreading awareness and understanding of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) among students through creative visual storytelling. The event was conducted from 19th November 2025 to 2nd December 2025 at RV College of Engineering, receiving an overwhelming response with 830 registrations and 556 submissions, showing strong enthusiasm and engagement from students. In Round 1 (Online Submission), participants selected one SDG theme and submitted an original photograph along with a short writeup explaining the issue and its global impact. This round emphasized SDG knowledge, originality, visual storytelling, and photo quality. In Round 2 (On-Campus Photography Round), shortlisted participants were challenged to capture photographs in the campus environment within a given time frame, ensuring creativity under constraints and equal opportunity for all.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/IdBsN1i-9N6p_XKkFnLQa.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Zgsc7lGXs6PuOVXBDtMqR","name":"Plog Run along Vrishabhavathi Valley","slNo":9,"place":"Bangalore University","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/sZultDLw0Upt0F8zjHNZr.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Removal of significant quantities of plastic waste from the Vrishabhavathi Valley area\\n\\nIncreased awareness about plastic pollution and its impact on the environment\\n\\nEncouraged eco-friendly habits and responsible waste disposal practices\\n\\nPromoted physical fitness through an environmentally conscious activity\\n\\nStrengthened community participation in environmental conservation efforts\\n\\nContributed to the cleanliness and ecological preservation of the valley","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"A Plog Run was organized along the Vrishabhavathi Valley in Bengaluru with the objective of addressing plastic pollution and promoting environmental responsibility. The activity combined jogging with the collection of plastic waste, encouraging participants to contribute to environmental cleanliness while engaging in physical fitness.\\n\\nVolunteers actively collected plastic waste such as bottles, wrappers, carry bags, and other non-biodegradable materials discarded along the valley. The drive aimed to reduce plastic accumulation in the ecosystem and to create awareness about the harmful effects of plastic waste on water bodies, soil, and wildlife. The collected waste was segregated and handed over to authorized waste management agencies for proper disposal and recycling.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/AFX99S9vFk875QtN3oY0Q.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"fpW24vNgd7x8L8e5jWmAT","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/R43vv8ByroF_ys8LrSqmd.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The camp successfully collected a significant number of blood units, contributing to local blood banks and hospitals to support patients in need. The event increased awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and encouraged first-time donors to participate confidently. It fostered a sense of social responsibility, compassion, and community service among participants while strengthening the spirit of humanitarian support and public health awareness.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":2,"description":"Donated my blood to the blood bank for a social cause. Every drop counts — one pint of blood\\ncan save up to three lives. This was our chance to give someone a second chance at life, right\\nhere on campus.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/HnN3G2BieLLVxFD7ltM6S.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tLyOXKKy71dyTMtANYm-Y","name":"Kannada Sangha T-Shirt","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/ruRpzb_1rqyAt19hK_G8g.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":2,"outcomes":"The outcome of the activity was an increased sense of cultural awareness and pride in the Kannada language and heritage. It strengthened unity and participation within the Kannada Sangha, encouraged active involvement in cultural and social initiatives, and helped visibly represent and promote Kannada identity in the community.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-03","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The Kannada Sangha T-shirt distribution activity was organized to promote unity, cultural pride, and awareness of Kannada language and heritage. The initiative symbolized respect for Karnataka’s rich traditions and encouraged participants to actively identify with and support the values of Kannada Sangha. Receiving the T-shirt served as a mark of participation and belonging, fostering a sense of identity and togetherness among members.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/TAuGhty1l3uGl83INiAAa.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"XcTKwlhIrNflusT7m1SBk","name":"Paper Drive","slNo":12,"place":"Bangalore","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/gk8thp_Pi7whfMgeIgh7j.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-06-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"The paper drive successfully reduced paper waste through effective door-to-door collection, ensuring proper recycling of collected materials. It created strong awareness among residents about waste segregation and the importance of recycling. The activity encouraged active community participation and environmental responsibility. Volunteers developed teamwork, communication, and leadership skills while interacting with the public. The drive contributed to conserving trees, reducing landfill waste, and promoting sustainable environmental practices","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-23","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The Paper Drive event in Bangalore was organized with the objective of promoting recycling, waste reduction, and responsible environmental practices. Participants actively collected used and waste paper through a door-to-door collection process from households, offices, and educational institutions. This approach helped in reaching more people and encouraging direct participation from the community. The drive emphasized the importance of reducing paper consumption to conserve natural resources, especially trees. Volunteers also created awareness about waste segregation and recycling benefits. The event encouraged strong community participation and teamwork among volunteers, especially during the door-to-door paper collection activity, which made the initiative more impactful. All the collected paper was handed over to authorized recycling units for proper disposal. This effort helped reduce landfill waste and supported sustainable waste management practices. Participants gained practical knowledge about recycling and environmental responsibility. The drive played an important role in promoting eco-friendly habits among citizens.","aicteMapping":"Community development","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/ivKvX2_kecRZxMky4bFLJ.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"KLUeiT_0iPdcHORpIxdlf","name":"Viksit Bharat Quiz","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/OpHGHYMlYFkpTzAefllVW.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The outcome of participating in the quiz was improved understanding of the Viksit Bharat vision and increased awareness of national programs and developmental objectives. It promoted civic responsibility, encouraged informed citizenship, and motivated continued participation in government-led knowledge initiatives. The participation also added value to academic and co-curricular records by demonstrating involvement in educational and awareness-based activities.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Participation in The Viksit Bharat Quiz Challenge, organized through the MyGov platform, provided an opportunity to enhance awareness about India’s development initiatives, national vision, and governance-related topics. The quiz encouraged active learning and engagement with important information related to the progress, policies, and future goals of the country. Successfully completing the quiz reflected attentiveness, general awareness, and interest in nation-building initiatives promoted by the Government of India.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/mqdRDDfzQNI_-ECLsmQtm.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"24-25","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8KxhrRVh8hTatKnvdqjrD","name":"Eye Donation Fortnight","slNo":14,"place":"RVCE","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/R-vajHSpHzUxmOjAkFbdX.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-09-08","duration":12,"outcomes":"The outcome of the program was increased awareness and positive attitude towards eye donation among participants. Many individuals were motivated to pledge eye donation and share the message with family and friends. The activity helped promote social responsibility, compassion, and community service while contributing to the larger goal of reducing preventable blindness. Overall, the program strengthened awareness about organ donation and encouraged participation in life-saving initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-08-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Participation in the Eye Donation Awareness Program was aimed at educating individuals about the importance of eye donation and its role in restoring vision to visually impaired persons. The activity focused on spreading awareness about corneal blindness, the simple procedure of eye donation, and how a single donor can give sight to two individuals. Informational materials and messages were used to clear common myths and encourage people to pledge their eyes, emphasizing the humanitarian value of the act.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/I-U84Q21ADhKHCvIGMUi5.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"26-27","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5ItHqbcDsZpzwef7ZFHTS","name":"Blood donation camp","s