significant number of blood units, contributing to local blood banks and hospitals to support patients in need. The event increased awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and encouraged first-time donors to participate confidently. It fostered a sense of social responsibility, compassion, and community service among participants while strengthening the spirit of humanitarian support and public health awareness.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was organized with the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and creating awareness about the importance of saving lives. The camp was conducted in collaboration with qualified medical professionals, ensuring a safe and hygienic environment for donors. Participants were educated about the benefits of blood donation and the need for maintaining adequate blood supplies for emergency medical situations. Proper screening procedures were followed before donation, and donors were guided and supported throughout the process to ensure their comfort and safety.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/256b7b75-b243-4a17-9eaa-6b87ef960225/KAgsnc6vs4gm7XYRpinAT.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"30-31","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:09:50.117333+00', '2026-01-30 07:13:16.317654+00'), ('f6c000be-adbc-4aa3-ad76-05b1c03cf5e0', '74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY044","name":"Prabu Jayant","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"cbXVaPymPO3nrcLYpufKL","name":"Plog Run for Vrushabhavathi","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/r4t6-Hxtei102Lw9qvLi4.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"This cleanliness drive had a positive impact on the society and the\\nenvironment and created a sense of awareness of conserving rivers. It also proved the importance of teamwork","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Vrishabhavathi River is a minor river, a tributary of the Arkavathy, that flows through the south of the Indian city of Bangalore. The river was once so pristine that the water from it was used for drinking and used by the famous Gali Anjaneya temple but is now highly polluted due to pollutants from industrial, agricultural and domestic sources.\\nThe students started from college at 7 am and the buses took them to\\nNetaji Subhas Southern Centre in Bangalore University. The whole event was inaugurated by the principal and the other experts. They told the students and the NSS team about the importance of the cleanliness drive and the instructions of the cleanliness drive.\\nFrom 8 am to 10:30 am, the students, along with the NSS team, picked up jute waste bags and collected plastic waste using those bags. The students then stood for a photo along with the NSS team and the in charge professor Dr. Lokeshwari M. The students then had breakfast at around 11:00 to 11:30 am.\\n","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/ASkkNW8li895ghGXz5X4a.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9Un-g4Kisu5hTmBUSE_ov","name":" SWACHHATA PAKHWADA","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/NYCt1_9WMqZH1ITMA-sDw.png"],"endDate":"2024-10-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"This cleanliness drive had a positive impact on the society and the\\nenvironment and created a sense of awareness of conserving rivers. It also\\nproved the importance of teamwork","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-10-01","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Swachhata Pakhwada, held on October 1st, was a vital initiative aligned with\\nthe Swacch Bharat Abhiyan. The event featured the presence of the AlCTE\\nChairperson, who delivered an inspiring speech. Volunteers, including\\nRotaract members and students, collaborated to clean college premises and\\nits surroundings. This effort not only improved hygiene but also fostered a\\nsense of cómmunity responsibility and environmental stewardship. On\\nOctober 1st, Swachhata Pakhwada was organized, a vital initiative aligned\\nwith the Swachh Bharat Abhiyan. AICTE Chairperson graced the event as\\nthe chief guest, delivering an inspiring speech. Volunteers collaborated to\\nclean college premises, fostering cleanliness and community spirit.\\n","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/Fpi4bRyAJNrt11FwdSiKs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4IziRn1sIMwCLP-GxEdh-","name":"Utsarga 2023","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/VDkm6b7NMu4j9DkZxjZ65.png"],"endDate":"2023-01-19","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon, an annual event organized by the NSS of RVCE, successfully blended\\nfitness, community engagement, and philanthropy, creating a platform for individuals to\\ncontribute to a meaningful cause while promoting a healthy lifestyle. With enthusiastic\\nparticipation from students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts, the marathon served as a powerful\\nreminder of the importance of collective action in addressing societal challenges. Runners\\ncontributed through their registration fees, which were directed toward a noble cause, such as\\nsupporting underprivileged ","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-01-19","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Utsarga Marathon is an annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS)\\nof RV College of Engineering, aiming to promote fitness, community engagement, and\\nsocial responsibility. The event brings together students, faculty, and fitness enthusiasts who\\nparticipate in the marathon by paying a registration fee. This fee serves a greater purpose, as all\\nthe proceeds collected are directed toward a noble cause, such as supporting underprivileged\\ncommunities, funding healthcare initiatives, or contributing to environmental sustainability\\nprojects. The marathon not only encourages physical well-being but also fosters a sense of unity\\nand collective action among participants. Beyond just a race, Utsarga Marathon symbolizes\\nthe spirit of giving and service. The event provides a platform for individuals to contribute\\nto meaningful social initiatives while experiencing the thrill and satisfaction of completing a\\nmarathon. Participants take pride in knowing that their efforts go beyond personal achievement,\\nas their involvement directly aids those in need. Organized with meticulous planning, the\\nmarathon includes well marked routes, hydration stations, and medical assistance to ensure a\\nsmooth and safe experience for all runners. Over the years, this initiative has gained widespread\\nsupport, strengthening the values of empathy and community service within RVCE and beyond. ","aicteMapping":"Setting of the information imparting club for women leading to contributing in social and economic issues","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"QDAPXnNPep2VgWHhB4Di0","name":"Rush Hour 4.0","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/PeQ0X_GGCQ777f454BFJ8.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"This cleanliness drive had a positive impact on the society and the\\nenvironment and created a sense of awareness of conserving rivers. It also\\nproved the importance of teamwork.\\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":24,"description":"A community service and Professional development project which\\nwent on for 5 days and included a pre-event task to build interest among the\\nparticipants followed by 8 main tasks. The participants ran for their positions\\nas each task led to the elimination of a certain number of teams; with 250+\\nparticipants; participating actively, followed by regular updates through the\\nevent dashboard and leader board. The event was a huge success with the\\nparticipants contributing to society along with having fun in this process.\\nThe top 5 teams were rewarded with OTT subscriptions and other prizes","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":9,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"R6Rom_l3FaZkoV_NLA1g5","name":"Farmathon","slNo":5,"place":"Art of Living","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/Wpfcvp05xvlWnqb8czlSB.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"This cleanliness drive had a positive impact on the society and the\\nenvironment and created a sense of awareness of conserving rivers. It also\\nproved the importance of teamwork","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-07-09","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Farthathon event, organized in collaboration with The Art of Living\\nFoundation, focused on promoting environmental sustainability and holistic\\nwell-being through active participation. As a volunteer, I contributed to\\ncoordinating the marathon, managing participants, and spreading\\nawareness about environmental conservation and mindfulness. The initiative\\nencouraged individuals to adopt eco-friendly practices while fostering\\nphysical fitness and mental balance. Participants engaged in activities that\\ncombined environmental responsibility with the Art of Living’s principles of\\nharmony and positivity. Through this experience, I developed teamwork and\\nevent management skills while supporting a cause that emphasized health,\\nsustainability, and collective social.","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/HHvlEMNtgM_LpJRhwYR6z.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mHiV18bCt2zgw4Bs4hlQU","name":" Dengue Awareness","slNo":6,"place":"Govt Hospital","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/1GtfO_9g3B2hYTisnS6Tz.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"This cleanliness drive had a positive impact on the society and the\\nenvironment and created a sense of awareness of conserving rivers. It also proved the importance of teamwork.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-07","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Dengue Awareness campaign organized under the National Service\\nScheme (NSS) at RV College of Engineering aimed to educate students and\\nlocal communities about dengue prevention and control. As a volunteer, I\\nparticipated in conducting awareness drives, distributing informative\\npamphlets, and engaging with residents to emphasize cleanliness and\\nmosquito control measures. The initiative highlighted the importance of\\neliminating stagnant water, maintaining hygiene, and recognizing early\\nsymptoms of dengue. Through interactive sessions and community\\noutreach, the campaign successfully promoted public health awareness and\\ncollective responsibility. This experience strengthened my communication,\\nleadership, and social engagement skills while contributing to a healthier\\nenvironment.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/gamVW_SU3IYKIJLskb0RL.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ie2ncbcOnTYtjOrlcbvQp","name":"Fistfull 2024","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/FdX4kUf3x2oGCbrjMAm6j.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-12","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fist Full Drive successfully collected a significant quantity of rice through the contribution\\nof 5 kg from each participant. It helped provide food support to underprivileged communities\\nand addressed issues related to hunger and food insecurity. The drive created awareness about\\nthe importance of sharing and social responsibility among students. Participants developed\\nempathy, teamwork, and a strong sense of community service. Overall, the initiative made a\\nmeaningful social impact and strengthened the culture of volunteering and humanitarian service\\non campus.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-12","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Fist Full Drive was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the aim of supporting the\\nunderprivileged and promoting social responsibility among students. In this drive, students and\\nvolunteers contributed by donating 5 kg of rice, symbolizing the idea of giving a “fist full” of\\nfood to those in need. The initiative created awareness about food insecurity and hunger faced by\\nmany sections of society. It encouraged participants to share resources selflessly and develop a\\nhabit of giving back to the community. The drive also strengthened values of empathy, kindness,\\nand unity among the students. The collected rice was planned to be distributed to needy\\ncommunities through charitable organizations. The drive witnessed enthusiastic participation,\\nshowcasing strong teamwork and coordination among volunteers. It provided students with an\\nopportunity to actively engage in social service activities. The initiative highlighted how even\\nsmall contributions can collectively create a significant positive impact. Overall, the Fist Full\\nDrive successfully reinforced the spirit of service, compassion, and social responsibility within\\nthe campus","aicteMapping":"Preparing an actionable business proposal for enhancing the village income","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/dgd0YQ4VYAc-HLo3Fjl6L.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"z41aj9glszIsQzz0Ag-bI","name":"Fast trek 2.0","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/6rZNzFf6s3-FxloFdcizB.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Fast Trek 2.0 positively impacted participants by enhancing physical stamina, boosting confidence, and deepening appreciation for nature. It cultivated teamwork, leadership skills, and responsibility among volunteers and trekkers alike. The event also created lasting memories and strengthened bonds, encouraging students to embrace active, healthy lifestyles and step outside their comfort zones.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-28","hoursSpent":8,"description":"Fast Trek 2.0 was an exciting and invigorating trekking expedition organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of Engineering (RVCE). Held at the scenic Kaurava Kunda Hills near Chikkaballapur district on 28th December, the event brought together students and adventure enthusiasts to explore rugged trails, challenge their physical limits, and enjoy panoramic hilltop views in a refreshing outdoor environment. The trek was professionally coordinated with thorough planning covering route safety, hydration, and team organization. Participants were guided through varying terrains, fostering a spirit of resilience and camaraderie beyond the typical indoor activities. Fast Trek 4.0 emphasized not just adventure but also the importance of teamwork, physical fitness, and environmental appreciation.","aicteMapping":"Tourism approaches through innovative approaches","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/JCSgP0Davf-sBsy0KRd09.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"1HOJ0GNPSEfrCfWGlyM1k","name":"Utsarga 2024","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/1ETarv48pMdwkyRWju87d.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon created strong awareness about physical fitness, social responsibility, and community involvement. It strengthened teamwork among volunteers, improved leadership and coordination skills, and successfully fostered a sense of unity and purpose. The event left a positive impact on participants by inspiring them to stay active and socially conscious while contributing to a larger cause.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon organized by RV College of Engineering was a meaningful initiative aimed at promoting health, social responsibility, and community engagement among students and participants. The marathon brought together individuals from diverse backgrounds to run for a cause, emphasizing the importance of physical fitness while supporting social and humanitarian values associated with Utsarga.\\n\\nThe event was carefully planned and executed with active participation from volunteers and organizers, ensuring smooth registration, route management, safety arrangements, and crowd coordination. Through this marathon, participants were encouraged to adopt a healthy lifestyle and contribute towards a socially impactful cause, reinforcing the spirit of service and unity.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"a5SfmDlxc6wBRWOFksGQl","name":"Utsarga 2025","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/mPLVZneOGbj2PZ_PkYfZ4.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Utsarga Marathon created strong awareness about physical fitness, social responsibility, and community involvement. It strengthened teamwork among volunteers, improved leadership and coordination skills, and successfully fostered a sense of unity and purpose. The event left a positive impact on participants by inspiring them to stay active and socially conscious while contributing to a larger cause.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon organized by RV College of Engineering was a meaningful initiative aimed at promoting health, social responsibility, and community engagement among students and participants. The marathon brought together individuals from diverse backgrounds to run for a cause, emphasizing the importance of physical fitness while supporting social and humanitarian values associated with Utsarga.\\n\\nThe event was carefully planned and executed with active participation from volunteers and organizers, ensuring smooth registration, route management, safety arrangements, and crowd coordination. Through this marathon, participants were encouraged to adopt a healthy lifestyle and contribute towards a socially impactful cause, reinforcing the spirit of service and unity.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_Ruq9MwVLAXwOolpf1oKj","name":"Campus CleanUp ","slNo":11,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/mUjY-8rycxN-S9xX3LBzk.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The campus clean-up drive created awareness about hygiene, waste management, and environmental conservation. It strengthened teamwork and coordination among NSS volunteers and encouraged students to take ownership of their surroundings. The initiative contributed to a cleaner campus and reinforced the values of social responsibility and community service.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-06","hoursSpent":8,"description":"The Campus Clean-Up Drive was organized at the RVCE Ground by the National Service Scheme (NSS) unit of RV College of Engineering with the objective of promoting cleanliness, environmental responsibility, and civic sense among students.\\n\\nVolunteers actively participated in cleaning the campus ground by collecting waste, segregating biodegradable and non-biodegradable materials, and ensuring proper disposal. The activity emphasized the importance of maintaining a clean and healthy campus environment while instilling values of discipline, responsibility, and collective effort. The drive also served as a reminder of the role individuals play in sustaining cleanliness in shared public spaces.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/ZbMjZ0mwTt2hcRpXVEby8.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"tr-zw_kowqIN2v-Lt8Hzf","name":"Tech Tank","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/OKCBW7VCzU_S7ZnKYaAm3.png"],"endDate":"2025-10-06","duration":123,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully fostered\\ncreativity, teamwork, and a developer-focused learning environment,\\nempowering students to transform ideas into impactful tech solutions and\\nstrengthen the coding culture at RVCE.\\n","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-06-06","hoursSpent":24,"description":"The Tech Tank Hackathon conducted by the Google Developer Group\\n(GDG) Club at RV College of Engineering was an exciting 24-hour coding\\nmarathon that encouraged innovation and collaboration among aspiring\\ndevelopers. The event focused on solving real-world problems using\\ncutting-edge technologies such as AI, web development, and cloud\\ncomputing. As an organizer, I was involved in planning the event,\\ncoordinating participants, managing logistics, and ensuring the smooth\\nconduct of all hackathon activities. The initiative successfully fostered\\ncreativity, teamwork, and a developer-focused learning environment,\\nempowering students to transform ideas into impactful tech solutions and\\nstrengthen the coding culture at RVCE","aicteMapping":"Promotion of appropriate technologies","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/74e5c995-4faf-4db2-8e3f-eb3625c38d6f/RWdOVZTZoOBlOm4vYZeBz.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr Minal Moharir","designation":"Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 13:01:49.171326+00', '2026-01-30 14:29:56.594703+00'), ('f7069085-1495-455e-bfb3-db5027ed69f4', '07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22IS062","name":"Shashwath S H","period":"2022-2026","department":"Information Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"78jytiVkCscnziNCs7gIR","name":"Village Visit","slNo":1,"place":"Government Higher Primary School,Kulumepalya, Anekal, Bengaluru Urban","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/qFRPw5EJ17A-YUHieU1HG.png"],"endDate":"2022-12-02","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Improved cleanliness and hygiene in the school premises.\\n• Created awareness among children about basic hygiene and healthy habits.\\n• Strengthened foundational mathematics skills through interactive teaching.\\n• Encouraged learning through games and recreational activities.\\n• Brought joy and motivation to school children through meaningful interaction.\\n• Fostered empathy, teamwork, and social responsibility among volunteers.","semester":"1","startDate":"2022-12-02","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Village Visit was a community outreach activity carried out with the objective of supporting and engaging with a government school in a rural area. As part of the visit, students actively participated in cleaning the school surroundings to promote a hygienic and healthy learning environment. Volunteers interacted with school children by teaching basic hygiene practices, fundamental mathematics concepts, and engaging them in educational and recreational games. The activity aimed to improve awareness about cleanliness, enhance learning through interactive methods, and provide a joyful and motivating experience for the children while fostering a sense of social responsibility among the participants.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"H2dOVBeoFWBL-0UQzyGx6","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/z9OpzOMBnQzFa7-Gj7XVv.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully collected blood units to support hospitals and patients in need.\\n• Increased awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.\\n• Encouraged students to participate in life-saving humanitarian activities.\\n• Promoted a sense of social responsibility and empathy among participants.\\n• Strengthened collaboration between Rotaract Club of RVCE and Lions Club of Bangalore South.\\n• Recognized and motivated donors through certificates, appreciation badges, and AICTE activity points.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in association with the Lions Club of Bangalore South on 6th June 2023 at the RVCE campus. The event aimed to promote voluntary blood donation and create awareness about the importance of blood donation in saving lives. Students, staff, and volunteers actively participated in the camp, contributing to this humanitarian cause. Proper medical supervision and post-donation care were ensured, with refreshments provided to all donors. Participants were also recognized with certificates of participation and appreciation badges, and AICTE activity points were awarded as a mark of respect for their selfless contribution.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"k7t2cKoF27poF4csPbxHe","name":"Utsarga Marathon 2023","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/0Q6qsAsunHeg5GVGo4Y1o.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/zemQZ7UEWew4HwaMnWsh8.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully raised funds to support needy children and social welfare initiatives.\\n• Promoted awareness about child welfare and the importance of community contribution.\\n• Encouraged physical fitness and a healthy lifestyle among participants.\\n• Increased student and volunteer engagement in social service activities.\\n• Fostered a sense of empathy, responsibility, and collective effort among participants.\\n• Enhanced the visibility and impact of NSS RVCE’s flagship initiatives.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2023 was a flagship fundraising event organized by NSS RVCE with the theme “Help a child, change the world.” The marathon was conducted on 4th June 2023 and aimed to support needy children through funds raised from participant registrations. Participants were given the option to run either 5 km or 10 km, encouraging individuals of varying fitness levels to take part. The event combined physical fitness with social responsibility, motivating students and volunteers to contribute their time and effort toward a noble cause. All participants were provided with Utsarga T-shirts, certificates of participation, medals of recognition, and refreshments, making the event both meaningful and well-organized.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"F0lIAqZiun59WxF1Sm9Ts","name":"Fast Trek 2.0","slNo":4,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/1dkDl7UoViAJRv5QQGvDK.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/zd_pikEi567eDlwE5ps0o.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/yIFbVcx3mznb0xbIxLr8H.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/3M8mX8sZ4Xu06__LzSall.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully raised awareness about environmental cleanliness and sustainable practices among participants.\\n• Encouraged active student participation and fostered a sense of social responsibility.\\n• Strengthened teamwork, leadership, and coordination skills through group trekking activities.\\n• Promoted physical fitness, mental well-being, and stress relief among students.\\n• Enhanced the visibility and impact of the Rotaract Club’s community-oriented initiatives.\\n• Delivered a memorable and enriching outdoor experience, strengthening students’ connection with nature.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":null,"description":"FAST TREK 2.0 was a flagship trekking and social responsibility initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 28th January 2024. The event combined adventure with environmental consciousness through a cleanliness drive conducted during the trek. Participants assembled early in the morning and traveled to the trekking site after being briefed on safety protocols and event guidelines. The trek through the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills provided students with an opportunity to experience nature while actively contributing to its preservation. The event witnessed enthusiastic participation from over 750 students, creating a vibrant and energetic atmosphere while promoting teamwork, discipline, and environmental awareness.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RUX1LreplFoWIyUZD_xX1","name":"T-Shirt for Smiles","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/oDwhhm6MuQlip1AkstACi.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Brought happiness and emotional support to children residing in the orphanage.\\n• Encouraged students to actively participate in community service and social welfare activities.\\n• Strengthened values of empathy, compassion, and social responsibility among participants.\\n• Created awareness about the needs and challenges faced by underprivileged children.\\n• Fostered teamwork and a spirit of collective contribution among students.\\n• Successfully met the criteria for awarding AICTE activity points to participating students.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“T-Shirt for Smiles” and the Orphanage Visit was a community service initiative organized by Kannada Sangha on 07-07-2024. As part of this event, a group of students visited Prajakirana Seva Charitable Trust Orphanage located in Kumbalagodu, Bengaluru. The primary objective of the visit was to support underprivileged children and bring joy to their lives through meaningful interaction. Students actively engaged with the children by participating in various activities and contributing through donations and essential supplies. The initiative aimed to instill values of compassion, empathy, and social responsibility among students while encouraging active involvement in community service.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"dt6k9EwMxdcA-cYBgX4t0","name":"Indi – Genius: The India Quiz Under the Peepal Tree 2024","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/53m3XFVf8A4rDrqYdMnf_.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/5ZSuwz5RFo0IyP01WnKwV.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-09","duration":3,"outcomes":"• Provided exposure to a national-level quizzing platform.\\n• Enhanced general knowledge and analytical thinking skills.\\n• Encouraged teamwork and collaborative problem-solving.\\n• Offered an intellectually stimulating and competitive environment.\\n• Contributed to overall academic and extracurricular development.\\n• Awarded three AICTE activity points for first-day participation.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Under The Peepal Tree (UTPT) 2024 was a national-level quizzing festival organized by RV QuizCorp, the official quizzing club of R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE). Held from 7th to 9th June 2024 at the IEM Auditorium, RVCE, the event attracted participation from students representing multiple colleges across the country.\\n\\nThe festival featured six team-based quizzes covering a wide range of genres, with teams comprising up to three members and permitting inter-college participation. UTPT 2024 provided a highly competitive academic platform, offering a substantial prize pool along with academic incentives such as the allocation of three activity points for first-day participation. The event successfully fostered knowledge exchange, collaboration, and a strong competitive spirit among the participants.","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"G-NEQfZ_xO_K2Flsqh7Cm","name":"Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/z9QdlsMMETxUKLh-AEZVq.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/C_aL8Cyp81FhBzLzEFhCK.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Promoted environmental awareness and sustainable practices among students.\\n• Encouraged students to actively participate in tree plantation and conservation efforts.\\n• Fostered a sense of responsibility towards environmental protection.\\n• Increased student involvement in eco-friendly and socially responsible initiatives.\\n• Successfully distributed saplings with proper planting guidelines to participants.\\n• Strengthened the role of Kannada Sangha in organizing impactful community and environmental activities.\\n• Fulfilled the criteria for awarding AICTE activity points to participating students.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The “Buy a T-Shirt, Plant a Tree” event was a community and environmental awareness initiative organized by Kannada Sangha on 07-07-2025 at R V College of Engineering. The initiative aimed to promote environmental responsibility among students by encouraging active participation in tree plantation activities. As part of the event, every student who purchased a T-shirt was provided with a tree sapling along with guidelines on how and where to plant it. The program was designed to inspire students to take personal responsibility for environmental sustainability by planting and nurturing the saplings they received. The distribution of T-shirts and saplings was carried out within the college campus, ensuring wide student participation and effective execution of the initiative.","aicteMapping":"Developing Sustainable Water management system","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Eom6MuKnURQdxvYNgCGMA","name":"Fist full","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/R60gh-G9FlCgpOn1rLMwm.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/zaTqmqghoV6ae4F24EO1d.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-11-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Collected essential food grains to support individuals and families in need.\\n• Promoted the value of kindness, sharing, and social responsibility among students.\\n• Encouraged sustained participation through simple and practical contribution methods.\\n• Increased student involvement in community service initiatives.\\n• Created awareness about food insecurity and the importance of collective effort.\\n• Successfully motivated participants through the provision of 10 AICTE activity points.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"“” was a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE to support underprivileged communities through food grain collection. The event encouraged participants to set aside a fistful of rice or toor dal from every meal prepared between 15th November and 29th November, promoting a habit of mindful giving. Students contributed by donating either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, making a meaningful impact through small but consistent efforts. The initiative aimed to foster compassion, social responsibility, and community involvement among students while addressing food security needs in a simple yet effective manner.","aicteMapping":"Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uzWK6GB84RF3NvH7GZ7rf","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/D5KcaUa572Oay7WAmtwiE.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-26","duration":5,"outcomes":"• Provided essential stationery kits to underprivileged school-going children.\\n• Supported educational continuity and learning among economically disadvantaged students.\\n• Positively impacted the lives of over 5,500 children through community support.\\n• Encouraged social responsibility and active participation among contributors.\\n• Strengthened the Rotaract Club of RVCE’s commitment to education-focused service initiatives.\\n• Recognized and appreciated contributors for their meaningful involvement in the cause.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-07-22","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak 2025 was a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of supporting the education of underprivileged children. Through this project, essential stationery kits were distributed to school-going children from economically disadvantaged backgrounds. The initiative successfully reached over 5,500 children during the year, aiming to reduce barriers to education and encourage consistent learning. The project emphasized the importance of collective contribution and community involvement in empowering young minds and promoting educational equity.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"wh1UriRVZN67YhEZ46hwV","name":"Paper Bag Making Activity","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/eVd0ZiAe-O5UPFND6Hr-0.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/bhsqinlENA5l96q95-6Z9.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully produced and distributed over 4,000 handmade eco-friendly paper bags.\\n• Reduced dependency on single-use plastic during Kadlekai Parishe 2024.\\n• Raised environmental awareness among local vendors, visitors, and the community.\\n• Encouraged active student participation in sustainability-focused initiatives.\\n• Fostered teamwork, responsibility, and civic engagement among volunteers and participants.\\n• Provided practical exposure to environmental activism and community interaction.\\n• Received appreciation from local stall owners and fair organizers for the sustainable effort.\\n• Qualified the activity under Community Service / Environmental Awareness for AICTE activity points.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-11-04","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Paper Bag Making Initiative was an eco-conscious community service activity organized by the Department of Information Science and Engineering, RV College of Engineering, in November 2024 as part of Kadlekai Parishe 2024 at Basavanagudi. The initiative aimed to reduce the use of single-use plastic by designing, crafting, and distributing handmade paper bags to vendors and visitors at the fair. A total of 97 student participants and 5 volunteers collaborated to produce over 4,000 eco-friendly paper bags using recyclable materials. The activity aligned with sustainable development goals and provided students with hands-on exposure to environmental responsibility, teamwork, and community engagement while supporting a major local cultural event.","aicteMapping":"Developing and managing efficient garbage disposable system","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"PLcSB6V8gWTJfhtOr_6GO","name":"Har Ghar Tiranga","slNo":11,"place":"Home","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/ITHu6C90B9ChJ4LP_09yb.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/JBIFjknESKaEcnOGiyxaZ.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-08-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Strengthened patriotism and respect for the National Flag among participants.\\n• Encouraged active participation in national celebrations and civic responsibility.\\n• Promoted unity and a sense of belonging towards the nation.\\n• Increased awareness about the significance of Independence Day and Azadi Ka Mahotsav.\\n• Enabled widespread student involvement through a simple yet meaningful activity.\\n• Awarded 2 AICTE activity points to participating students.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Har Ghar Tiranga was a patriotic initiative conducted by NSS RVCE as part of Azadi Ka Mahotsav on 15th August 2025. The activity aimed to encourage citizens, especially students, to proudly hoist the National Flag at their homes, workplaces, or other suitable locations in celebration of India’s Independence Day. Participants were required to display the Tiranga and capture a photograph as per NSS guidelines, symbolizing unity, national pride, and respect for the nation. The initiative fostered a sense of patriotism and collective participation in commemorating the spirit of freedom.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"RO_89HajcC4EDg3t9baVT","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/PpuG1rZcb1VmDosyh74-6.jpeg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/W_00d-bpSAnxG78Ou6AT-.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully encouraged voluntary blood donation among students and the campus community.\\n• Contributed to saving lives by collecting blood units for medical emergencies.\\n• Raised awareness about the importance and impact of blood donation.\\n• Fostered a sense of social responsibility and humanitarian values among participants.\\n• Strengthened student participation in Rotaract Club’s service-oriented initiatives.\\n• Motivated donors through recognition in the form of 10 AICTE activity points.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The Blood Donation Camp was organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE as a pre-event for 8th Mile on 30th October 2025 at the Biotech Quadrangle, RVCE campus. The initiative aimed to encourage voluntary blood donation and create awareness about the life-saving impact of donating blood. Students, along with their friends and family members, were invited to actively participate in this noble cause. The event emphasized the message that a single pint of blood can save multiple lives, inspiring participants to contribute towards giving others a second chance at life. The camp was conducted in a well-organized manner with proper medical supervision, and donors were recognized with AICTE activity points for their selfless contribution.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"5bG1poMB5gnnIhNt-WKrZ","name":"Fist full","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/aEi9iD90aGt5uvAFtxTbB.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07b19bde-30e6-44c9-a91b-8c15a97317db/LXNyJ0iR3lKnmjn-JA_1s.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"• Successfully collected essential food grains from student contributors.\\n• Encouraged active student participation in social welfare activities.\\n• Promoted values of compassion, sharing, and social responsibility.\\n• Created awareness about food security and community support.\\n• Strengthened the role of Rotaract Club of RVCE in service-oriented initiatives.\\n• Fulfilled the criteria for awarding 10 AICTE activity points to contributing students.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fist Full was a flagship social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of supporting food security and encouraging community participation. The event was scheduled to commence on 1st November 2025, with the donation collection phase running from 17th November 2025. As part of the initiative, students voluntarily contributed either 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. The event aimed to promote empathy, social responsibility, and collective contribution among students while addressing the needs of underprivileged communities. Proper coordination and planning ensured smooth execution of the donation drive within the campus.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to any national level initiative of Government of India. For eg. Digital India, Skill India, Swachh Bharat Internship etc","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"22-23","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Kavitha S N","designation":"Associate Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 11:39:41.494749+00', '2026-01-30 06:55:20.129745+00'), ('f751177f-7a7d-4c0d-b18f-392592a0390c', 'ac7bdb3b-2dc4-41c8-8a27-0595c8521229', '{"student":{"usn":"","name":"","period":"2022-2026","department":"","totalPoints":0},"activities":[],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 11:09:16.834509+00', '2026-01-29 16:17:35.385567+00'), ('f7a4586a-062c-476b-8416-593e5dbe149b', 'e15d4a90-336d-4244-9ea2-a381dd3fca52', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CS235","name":"Vishwanath Ganesh Bhat","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"06QxLW_Ye3MVHjqwW3SGO","name":"Fist Full 2024","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/e15d4a90-336d-4244-9ea2-a381dd3fca52/nUwgKTvvOTb0w9gs59uVB.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The Fist Full initiative successfully addressed food insecurity\\nthrough active student participation, with the collected food\\ngrains contributing to hunger alleviation and supporting\\ncommunity welfare programs by Rotary Bangalore Spandana.\\nThe activity enhanced social awareness, compassion, and civic\\nresponsibility among participants while emphasizing the impact of small individual contributions. It also fostered teamwork, leadership, and unity among students, strengthening their involvement in organized community service initiatives. Overall, the initiative created a meaningful social impact by promoting empathy, generosity, and collective responsibility","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":0,"description":"The “Fist Full” initiative was a socially impactful food donation\\ndrive organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of\\nEngineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore\\nSpandana, conducted from 15th to 29th November. The primary\\nobjective of the initiative was to combat hunger and food\\ninsecurity by encouraging students to contribute essential food\\ngrains for the benefit of underprivileged communities.\\nThe drive focused on mobilizing student participation by inviting\\nindividuals to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal, symbolizing\\nhow small individual contributions could collectively lead to a\\nsignificant social impact. Daily collection counters were set up in\\nthe Civil Department, making it convenient for students to\\nparticipate consistently throughout the campaign period.\\nThe initiative received an overwhelming response from the\\nstudent community, reflecting a strong spirit of empathy,\\nsolidarity, and social responsibility. Over the duration of the\\ndrive, more than 1750 students actively participated, resulting in\\nthe collection of approximately 6700+ kg of rice and 800+ kg of\\ntoor dal. The collected food grains were intended for distribution\\nthrough Rotary Bangalore Spandana to support hunger relief\\nprograms and ensure food security for those in need.\\nThe “Fist Full” initiative successfully demonstrated the\\neffectiveness of community-driven efforts and reinforced the\\nvalues of service above self. It also strengthened collaboration\\nbetween student organizations and established service bodies,\\nshowcasing RVCE’s continued commitment to social welfare and\\nhumanitarian causes.","aicteMapping":"Rotaract","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Shanta Rangaswamy","designation":"Hod of CSE Department"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 15:14:23.935482+00', '2026-02-01 10:09:03.387354+00'), ('f7b29541-7764-456f-b6eb-4ff140ab36c8', '12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EI044","name":"Samarth Kulkarni","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"OkmUTzPiBPxWBoUAu3blP","name":"Anti-ragging (CARV-Hindi)","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/F7m2pkc2gGhUXBmzTZnng.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-08-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity successfully contributed to raising awareness on anti-ragging measures among students through a creative and impactful medium. Participants gained hands-on experience in teamwork, communication, and social responsibility while addressing an important campus issue. The initiative supported AICTE’s objective of fostering a safe and inclusive educational environment. In recognition of their contribution, participating students were awarded AICTE activity points.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-08-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"This activity involved the preparation of an anti-ragging skit video by students of CARV–Hindi, organized as part of the AICTE Anti-Ragging initiative. The skit was designed to spread awareness about the harmful effects of ragging, promote a safe campus environment, and communicate the importance of mutual respect among students. Through dramatization and social messaging, the activity effectively conveyed legal, ethical, and emotional aspects related to ragging. The completed video was officially uploaded to the AICTE portal as part of the nationwide awareness drive.","aicteMapping":"Promoting social awareness and ethical values","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/-mrWSjLsNahJ32qPtSWeb.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"D6ZP6IA11wLuVteezG-h1","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE","photos":[],"endDate":"2023-07-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation directly contributed to meeting the medical needs of patients requiring transfusions, potentially saving multiple lives. The activity reinforced the value of civic duty, empathy, and public health awareness among participants. It also helped encourage voluntary blood donation within the community, supporting a sustainable and reliable blood supply system. The blood bank formally recognized the contribution through a certificate of appreciation.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-07-18","hoursSpent":0,"description":"This activity involved voluntary blood donation at the Marathahalli Voluntary Blood Bank as part of a community health initiative. The objective of the activity was to contribute toward saving lives by ensuring the availability of safe blood for patients in need. By voluntarily donating blood, the participant supported emergency medical care and strengthened the healthcare system’s ability to respond to critical situations. The initiative also promoted awareness about the importance of regular blood donation and social responsibility.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to community service / social responsibility","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/Etfva2vi3xqR874N2pezV.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ltQNbUPZM71cBv8t1gQdY","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/YvvLXa8cxznDaT2mRzAMK.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-08-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"The project witnessed participation from 1,022 students, successfully raising approximately ₹3,50,000. The collected funds were utilized to distribute stationery kits and books to students of government schools, directly addressing educational resource gaps. Project Pustak created a tangible impact on school children while instilling social awareness and civic responsibility among participants, who were awarded AICTE activity points for their contribution.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-24","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Project Pustak was a flagship educational initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with the Pranav Foundation, aimed at supporting the education of underprivileged children. Conducted during April 2025, the project focused on raising funds from college students to provide essential learning materials. The initiative encouraged voluntary student contributions, fostering a spirit of generosity, collective responsibility, and commitment toward social upliftment through education.","aicteMapping":"Contribution to educational and social development initiatives","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/PIw920GMUjAbGa8oP3nDC.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"9YIFUEzOANa6_R1JwUjQh","name":"Nasha Mukta Bharat","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/a12jzEfGjFHvbcYFJwK5a.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-08-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity reinforced awareness about the harmful effects of drug abuse and encouraged conscious decision-making toward a sober and healthy lifestyle. By taking the pledge, the participant demonstrated social responsibility and personal commitment to the national objective of substance abuse prevention. The initiative contributed to spreading positive awareness within the community and supported the larger goal of building a drug-free society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-08-14","hoursSpent":0,"description":"This activity involved participation in the Nasha Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan, a national initiative by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment, Government of India, aimed at promoting a drug-free society. As part of the program, the participant took a formal “Say No to Drugs” pledge, committing to abstain from substance abuse and adopt a healthy, responsible lifestyle. The initiative focused on awareness, prevention, and personal accountability in combating drug abuse among youth.","aicteMapping":"Promoting social awareness and ethical values","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/cUQ-0PoyeGrh3ZEQ5LaBa.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"iGE0hVQ-m0wI3erSamaRw","name":"Fist Full 2025","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/7TRRELOYBi4RHXZDh0ATL.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/alrZN2zskUF2SHWGyaeQP.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/jDOPs52VDcMZ7ordsOkV_.png"],"endDate":"2025-11-17","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Fist Full initiative saw participation from 2146 students, leading to the collection of 4370 kg of rice and 2516 kg of dal. These food grains were distributed to seven beneficiary organizations, including mass feeding centers, hospitals, schools, and social welfare institutions. The initiative supported daily meal programs, healthcare nutrition, and child welfare services, directly benefiting underprivileged communities. It also strengthened collaboration between RVCE, the Rotaract Club, and Rotary Bangalore Spandana, while participants were awarded 10 AICTE activity points for their contribution.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-11-17","hoursSpent":0,"description":"Fist Full was a community service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE with the objective of addressing food insecurity through collective student effort. The activity encouraged students to voluntarily contribute essential food grains, where each participant donated either rice or dal. The initiative emphasized the idea that small individual contributions, when combined, can lead to a significant social impact. It was conducted as part of RVCE’s commitment to social responsibility and community engagement.","aicteMapping":"Community service and social responsibility initiative","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/12d8c697-fcd9-4797-a22d-7053f2a13b69/7LRH7g-ou2CTfMJNd0q4L.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 19:28:57.742827+00', '2026-02-02 07:37:33.644407+00'), ('f9349522-0207-43f3-88ff-61534e775ac0', 'c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC088","name":"Mahaling Kakamari","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"esuAUGtu-SOMHvmW1ubfn","name":"Utsarga 2024 – NSS Club, RVCE","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/lz6gI53JKW2q3hzKBmQ5_.png"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"This marathon celebration of health and fitness focused on a social mission to help reshape children''s \\nfutures by raising funds to provide education for underprivileged students. ","semester":"1","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":4.5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is an extraordinary event and a celebration of health, fitness, and making a \\ndifference, with a social mission to help reshape a child''s future by supporting education for those in \\nneed.","aicteMapping":"National Service  Scheme (NSS)","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/JbVbwXAZd6CL2Mqlun6gG.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"d_phUhb6kVu4F-jwtIKtu","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/4Y4-vVf5hQKgyFxU-riPR.png"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation initiative fostered a deep sense of social responsibility and community solidarity, \\ndirectly contributing to the local healthcare system''s life-saving resources. Through this activity, I gained \\npractical awareness of medical screening protocols and the critical importance of blood safety. \\nUltimately, the experience enhanced my organizational discipline and reinforced the impact of selfless \\nservice in driving significant societal welfare. ","semester":"2","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Rotaract Club of RVCE, in association with the Kidwai Hospital, organized the Blood \\nDonation Camp in the RVCE Campus. ","aicteMapping":"Social Service ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/oMrKyywYsln3IJxgjo43p.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"vnZgWm7Dq9XNtY1wQ7knj","name":"Utsarga 2025 – NSS Club, RVCE","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/rhRfHcPqizKITtN2xIs-r.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":" \\nThis marathon celebration of health and fitness focused on a social mission to help reshape children''s \\nfutures by raising funds to provide education for underprivileged students.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":4.5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon is an extraordinary event and a celebration of health, fitness, and making a \\ndifference, with a social mission to help reshape a child''s future by supporting education for those in \\nneed.","aicteMapping":"National Service  Scheme (NSS) ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/eFQG3NUxRrr4cfyhM2H2B.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"_mgZyC-fy0yAExlQG_Ke1","name":"Kannada Sangha T shirt","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/wh8MoWLmhv1neTgMNTirK.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"Students actively participated by planting saplings, helping promote green practices on and beyond campus. The event successfully increased environmental consciousness and community involvement, supporting AICTE’s objectives for student-led sustainability activities.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":1,"description":"The “Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” initiative organized by Kannada Sangha at R.V. College of Engineering encouraged students to contribute to environmental sustainability by purchasing a T-shirt and receiving a sapling, along with guidance on planting it. The activity aimed to build environmental awareness and personal responsibility among students.","aicteMapping":"Social Service","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/XhwcdWiJbl_YDEKwsovCC.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"yBNlGacJrHiyT9hR2J5_Z","name":"Project Pustak 2024 – Rotaract Club, RVCE ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/38Bp6mZTVLn6OReYrtQN4.png"],"endDate":"2024-07-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"This flagship fundraising phase successfully raised ₹3,50,000 from 1,022 students, allowing for the\\nwidespread distribution of books and stationery kits to government school children\\n","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-07-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a student-led initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged school children by collecting ₹100–₹350 from donors to provide essential educational materials such as textbooks, stationery, backpacks, and learning resources. The project, organized by Rotaract Club of RVCE with Pranav Foundation, focuses on improving access to education and creating a better learning environment for deserving students.","aicteMapping":"Social Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/qXY6oF5JvvJJ6pPWz0Qhf.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Fs_ZpMfgg7EWlUaGfV9_T","name":"Project Pustak 2025 – Rotaract Club, RVCE ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/ON-KAXY9w8d3PKQXdhubn.png"],"endDate":"2025-04-23","duration":1,"outcomes":"This flagship fundraising phase successfully raised ₹3,50,000 from 1,022 students, allowing for the \\nwidespread distribution of books and stationery kits to government school children","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-23","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Project Pustak is a student-led initiative aimed at supporting underprivileged school children by collecting ₹100–₹350 from donors to provide essential educational materials such as textbooks, stationery, backpacks, and learning resources. The project, organized by Rotaract Club of RVCE with Pranav Foundation, focuses on improving access to education and creating a better learning environment for deserving students.","aicteMapping":"Social Activities","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/cR1u9qx582sTaQgCvNFdx.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"nATncqneE0_hbRILH9TGV","name":"FistFull 2024 – Rotaract, RVCE ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/UBQCBw7__ES6L_Ja4Us3t.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-15","duration":1,"outcomes":"This large-scale hunger combat initiative successfully collected over 5,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor \\ndal from students to support community welfare and solidarity.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The “Fist Full” initiative by Rotaract Club of RVCE in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana encouraged students to donate rice or toor dal to support hunger relief. The drive collected significant contributions, highlighting student solidarity and RVCE’s commitment to community welfare.","aicteMapping":"Social Activities ","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/e1R68ecrxqBKe7KdnL35i.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-14","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ysnDPy2vauHZoQeKTTA82","name":"Paper Bag 1– NSS Club, RVCE ","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/gHNMm91GNx2Rk2pMsTofb.png"],"endDate":"2025-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"Continuing the sustainable collaboration with Youth For Seva, this workshop resulted in the creation of \\n200 newspaper bags by the student to reduce environmental waste. ","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-01-13","hoursSpent":8,"description":"NSS RVCE, in collaboration with Youth For Seva, is organizing a paper bag workshop. Go green by \\ncreating newspaper bags and contribute towards a sustainable environment!","aicteMapping":"National Service  Scheme (NSS) ","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/49wSPyWOgidw2j0EEa00b.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-I8-ZGjWn7rRWQVfCr61i","name":"Mera Phala Vote – NSS Club, RVCE ","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/cYCKRJfb-CquYqtyqp_0m.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"This online awareness event engaged young voters, resulting in participants taking a formal pledge to \\nexercise their democratic rights and encourage others to build a \"New India\".","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-05","hoursSpent":1,"description":"An Online Event organized by NSS RVCE with a focus on engaging young and aspiring voters.","aicteMapping":"National Service  Scheme (NSS)","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/kZ8HoHUrERLJY7xXmhG-0.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jTBhZVPuWE-fpuBTpDnFS","name":"Eye Donation Fortnight","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/eVAdKSIHSeB5V3chBUkUP.png"],"endDate":"2024-09-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Many students enrolled as Sight Ambassadors, strengthening awareness of eye donation across campus and beyond. The program successfully promoted social responsibility while supporting the national effort to increase eye-donor registrations.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-09-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Eye Donation Fortnight, organized by NSS RVCE, aimed to spread awareness about eye donation by encouraging students to register as Sight Ambassadors and pledge their eyes through a simple online process. The initiative focused on educating participants about the importance of corneal donation and motivating peer advocacy.","aicteMapping":"National Service  Scheme (NSS) ","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/A8EpBHZuO1jsVFTv7mtob.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ypnZaZVDqW3YRjLj50j5v","name":" Plantation Drive","slNo":11,"place":"Bengaluru University Bio-Park Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/sopOjYjP-Hwu4cn6tDpZR.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participants contributed directly to increasing green cover while gaining awareness about sustainable living. The program successfully completed 427 consecutive Green Sundays, demonstrating consistent community engagement and impact on urban environmental restoration.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-03","hoursSpent":5,"description":"Green Sunday is a tree-planting and nurturing program by Adamya Chetana that encourages citizens and students to actively participate in environmental conservation through regular plantation drives. The initiative focuses on building long-term responsibility toward nature by involving participants in planting and caring for saplings.","aicteMapping":"National Service  Scheme (NSS) ","pointsEarned":3,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/c8f35b7e-58e4-492b-a063-3b7878254926/3Sg9qalj0e_XEjmCDCOoW.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Rajasree P.M","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-29 18:12:01.857735+00', '2026-01-31 07:53:23.426672+00'), ('faff7000-1eca-4bdc-9476-fc5946d886f2', '125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY036","name":"Mahammad Rizwan","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"muMxKQywVwU1KKEuDMtH_","name":"Mere Pehele Vote Desh keliye","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/urOOjAS-IrLb80mfTKuSQ.png"],"endDate":"2023-03-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Increased awareness among students about the importance of voting and democratic values. \\nMotivation of first-time voters to actively participate in elections. Enhanced understanding of \\nelectoral rights, responsibilities, and the voting process. Development of a sense of patriotism \\nand social responsibility among participants. Encouraged students to become informed citizens \\nand contribute positively to nation-building. Strengthened the idea that every single vote matters \\nfor the future of the country","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-03-06","hoursSpent":2,"description":"The event “Mera Pehle Vote – Desh Ke Liye” was organized with the objective of creating \\nawareness among students and citizens about the importance of voting in a democratic nation. \\nThe program aimed to motivate first-time voters to actively participate in the electoral process \\nand understand their role in nation-building. The program successfully encouraged young voters \\nto be informed, responsible, and proactive citizens who contribute to strengthening democracy.","aicteMapping":"Awareness","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/MsOKGYupCIt6NARbOxWxJ.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"LhxCHko-yMJLmapeuC2oG","name":"Campus Cleanup-I","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/4DNCyCWHiBcCcz7O4jCyS.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improved cleanliness and hygiene across the campus premises.\\nIncreased awareness among students about environmental cleanliness and waste management. \\nEncouraged teamwork, discipline, and social responsibility. Developed a habit of maintaining \\ncleanliness in daily life. Promoted eco-friendly practices and reduced littering on campus. \\nStrengthened students’ commitment towards a clean and healthy environment.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-13","hoursSpent":4,"description":"The Campus Clean-Up Drive was organized with the objective of promoting cleanliness, \\nenvironmental responsibility, and community participation among students. The activity aimed \\nto create awareness about the importance of maintaining a clean and hygienic campus and \\nto encourage students to adopt cleanliness as a regular habit. Students actively participated \\nin cleaning classrooms, corridors, laboratories, gardens, and open areas of the campus. The \\ndrive included the collection and segregation of waste, proper disposal of litter, and spreading \\nawareness about reducing plastic usage. Through hands-on \\ninvolvement, participants understood the impact of cleanliness on health, environment, and \\noverall well-being .","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6Jk5qlMjMjEGcfvxD7jjk","name":"Campus Cleanup-II","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/H8fRA1NUcmgooQblYnQb6.png"],"endDate":"2024-01-27","duration":1,"outcomes":"Improved cleanliness and hygiene across the campus premises.\\nIncreased awareness among students about environmental cleanliness and waste management. \\nEncouraged teamwork, discipline, and social responsibility. Developed a habit of maintaining \\ncleanliness in daily life. Promoted eco-friendly practices and reduced littering on campus. \\nStrengthened students’ commitment towards a clean and healthy environment.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-27","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Campus Clean-Up Drive was organized with the objective of promoting cleanliness, \\nenvironmental responsibility, and community participation among students. The activity aimed \\nto create awareness about the importance of maintaining a clean and hygienic campus and \\nto encourage students to adopt cleanliness as a regular habit. Students actively participated \\nin cleaning classrooms, corridors, laboratories, gardens, and open areas of the campus. The \\ndrive included the collection and segregation of waste, proper disposal of litter, and spreading \\nawareness about reducing plastic usage. Through hands-on \\ninvolvement, participants understood the impact of cleanliness on health, environment, and \\noverall well-being .","aicteMapping":"Community   Development","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"d3M2qks_KawOWopRd-F9s","name":"Utsarga Marathon - Participant","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness among participants about the importance of physical fitness \\nand maintaining a healthy lifestyle while strengthening interaction and bonding between \\nstudents and the local community. It helped develop a strong sense of social responsibility, \\ndiscipline, and volunteerism among students. Through active involvement in planning and \\nexecution, students improved their organizational, leadership, andteamwork skills. Overall, \\nthe program contributed positively to community well-being and encouraged continued \\nparticipation in health-oriented and socially responsible activities.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized as a Community Development initiative with the \\nobjective  of promoting health awareness, social responsibility, and community participation \\namong  students and the general public. The event focused on encouraging physical fitness, \\ndiscipline, and a sense of social commitment while spreading awareness about healthy lifestyles \\nand community well-being. Students, faculty members, and local community participants \\nactively took part in the marathon. The program also aimed to instill values of teamwork, \\nleadership, and service towards society, aligning with the objectives of AICTE’s community \\nengagement and social outreach initiatives. ","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/B-kUk_eRp0fjH1PPSFst4.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"eMo8qD76-aK_zY8G7ptEu","name":"Utsarga Marathon - Participant","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness among participants about the importance of physical fitness \\nand maintaining a healthy lifestyle while strengthening interaction and bonding between \\nstudents and the local community. It helped develop a strong sense of social responsibility, \\ndiscipline, and volunteerism among students. Through active involvement in planning and \\nexecution, students improved their organizational, leadership, andteamwork skills. Overall, \\nthe program contributed positively to community well-being and encouraged continued \\nparticipation in health-oriented and socially responsible activities","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized as a Community Development initiative with the \\nobjective  of promoting health awareness, social responsibility, and community participation \\namong  students and the general public. The event focused on encouraging physical fitness, \\ndiscipline, and a sense of social commitment while spreading awareness about healthy lifestyles \\nand community well-being. Students, faculty members, and local community participants \\nactively took part in the marathon. The program also aimed to instill values of teamwork, \\nleadership, and service towards society, aligning with the objectives of AICTE’s community \\nengagement and social outreach initiatives","aicteMapping":"Community   Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/n-HyhpLkUAJEBH8TAFGQh.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"puY9atLIw0wBlQfnM92mT","name":"Project Pustak","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-07-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through Project Pustak, I learned the importance of social responsibility and community \\nengagement. The activity highlighted how small interventions, such as providing basic \\nstationery, can create a significant impact on a child’s education. I gained a deeper understanding \\nof the challenges faced by students from economically disadvantaged backgrounds and how \\nlack of resources can affect attendance and learning outcomes. This initiative strengthened my \\nsense of empathy, teamwork, and leadership, and reinforced the role of engineers and students \\nin contributing positively to society beyond academics.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-24","hoursSpent":3,"description":"Project Pustak is a joint initiative by the RV College of Engineering and the Pranav Foundation, \\naimed at supporting children in rural government schools. In 2024, the program made a \\nmeaningful impact by providing essential stationery like notebooks and geometry boxes \\nto students from underprivileged communities. Many of these children, from economically \\ndisadvantaged families, often missed classes due to a lack of basic supplies. Pustak helps bridge \\nthis gap, ensuring every child has the tools they need to participate in their education.","aicteMapping":"Community Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/LuPG2btFGEBQ427Adckex.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"kW6f4gko6LM-OfN6nvdlb","name":"Vikasit Bharath Quiz","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/G1lsH-IGiImBkVfQ7iH9G.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-01","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced participants’ understanding of India’s developmental roadmap and the \\nrole of citizens, especially youth, in nation-building. It improved awareness of government \\ninitiatives, current affairs, and socio-economic challenges. The quiz also helped develop critical \\nthinking, teamwork, and competitive spirit among students, while fostering a sense of patriotism \\nand responsibility towards contributing to a Viksit Bharat.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-01","hoursSpent":3,"description":"The Viksit Bharat Quiz Activity was organized to create awareness among students about \\nthe Government of India’s vision for a developed nation (Viksit Bharat). The quiz focused \\non key themes such as economic growth, digital transformation, innovation, sustainability, \\ninfrastructure development, and social inclusion. It encouraged participants to learn about \\nnational policies, flagship schemes, and India’s long-term development goals through an \\ninteractive and engaging format.","aicteMapping":"Community   Development","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/zae_Xsgu_Q_lMzQ2FJy2L.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"6vQbWEDW-KSM_wAqDkFDA","name":"Fist Full","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/DvKlSxde9JqHUNI37j427.png"],"endDate":"2024-11-29","duration":15,"outcomes":"The initiative received an overwhelming response, with over 6,700 kg of rice and 800 kg of toor \\ndal donated by more than 1,750 students. The collected food grains contributed significantly \\nto supporting underprivileged communities. The activity reinforced the impact of collective \\naction and demonstrated how small individual contributions can lead to meaningful societal \\nchange. Participants gained a deeper sense of compassion, teamwork, and civic responsibility, \\nstrengthening RVCE’s commitment to community welfare and social solidarity.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-11-15","hoursSpent":4,"description":"“Fist Full” is a social service initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RV College of \\nEngineering (RVCE) in collaboration with Rotary Bangalore Spandana, conducted from 15th \\nto 29th November. The initiative aimed to combat hunger and food insecurity by encouraging \\nstudents to donate 5 kg of rice or 2 kg of toor dal. Daily collections were carried out in the Civil \\nDepartment, ensuring smooth coordination and participation. The drive witnessed enthusiastic \\ninvolvement from students, reflecting a strong culture of empathy and social responsibility \\nwithin the campus.","aicteMapping":"Community   Development","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Z9WOhEWTHEvLbQLYYKNf9","name":"Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/k7YTT3NAWoowqGAUcyBvC.png"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The initiative successfully raised awareness about environmental protection and the importance \\nof afforestation. Students actively contributed to sustainability efforts by planting saplings, \\nfostering a sense of ownership and responsibility toward the environment. The activity \\nreinforced eco-friendly values, promoted green practices on campus, and highlighted the role \\nof individual actions in addressing environmental challenges. Participants developed greater \\nenvironmental consciousness and commitment to long-term ecological sustainability.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":5,"description":"“Buy a T-shirt, Plant a Tree” was a community service and environmental awareness initiative \\norganized by the Kannada Sangha to promote sustainability and individual responsibility among \\nstudents. As part of the initiative, students who purchased a T-shirt were provided with a tree \\nsapling along with clear guidelines on planting and maintenance. The distribution of T-shirts and \\nsaplings was conducted within the college campus, encouraging students to actively participate \\nin environmental conservation by planting and nurturing trees.","aicteMapping":"Community   Development","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"N5RRB4xY2-Y6XL1BSTZ_I","name":"Road Safety","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/YtreZ5nZWjxm_IfmHMgHg.png"],"endDate":"2024-03-06","duration":3,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness about traffic regulations, road safety norms, and responsible road usage among participants. Students gained practical knowledge of basic trauma care and emergency response techniques, improving their preparedness to handle accident situations. The program strengthened communication skills, civic sense, and social responsibility while contributing to public safety awareness. Overall, the initiative encouraged responsible citizenship and promoted a proactive approach toward accident prevention and life-saving interventions.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-03-04","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Jeevan Rakshak Program was a road safety awareness and basic trauma life support training program organized at RV College of Engineering by SaveLIFE Foundation as a CSR initiative of HDFC ERGO. The program aimed to promote safe road practices and enhance awareness about accident prevention and emergency response. The activity included sessions on traffic rules, pedestrian safety, responsible driving behavior, and the importance of using helmets and seat belts. In addition, participants were trained in Basic Trauma Life Support techniques, including the Stop the Bleed program by the American College of Surgeons, focusing on immediate first aid and life-saving measures during road accidents. Through demonstrations, interactions, and awareness messaging, the program educated students on road safety and the importance of timely response during emergencies.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/ZTHi8CHOLAT-oI3PSwsL-.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ESdodGznBIMrTf2qOR_h6","name":"Plog Run","slNo":11,"place":"Jnana Bharati Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/6T8goD-yxu96DJHKwGdJy.png"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity significantly increased awareness about environmental pollution and the need for river conservation among participants and the local community. Students developed a sense of environmental responsibility and civic duty by actively participating in cleanliness drives. The plog run promoted physical fitness, teamwork, and community engagement while contributing to the cleanliness of the Vrushabhavathi River area. Overall, the initiative encouraged sustainable behavior, responsible waste management, and active citizen participation in environmental protection.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":7,"description":"The Plog Run was an environmental and community development initiative conducted near Bangalore University, Jnanabharathi, focusing on the cleaning of the Vrushabhavathi River and its surrounding areas. The activity combined jogging with waste collection, encouraging participants to engage in physical activity while actively contributing to environmental conservation. Volunteers collected plastic waste, debris, and other pollutants from the riverbanks and nearby public spaces. The event aimed to create awareness about river pollution, improper waste disposal, and the importance of maintaining clean and sustainable urban ecosystems. Through hands-on participation, the program emphasized collective responsibility toward protecting natural water bodies and promoting eco-friendly practices.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"V2W_9Y6duF3BGuOTTHnDf","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":12,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-20","duration":1,"outcomes":"The blood donation drive at RVCE campus resulted in several meaningful outcomes. Most importantly, the donated blood will directly contribute to saving lives during medical emergencies, surgeries, and treatments. The initiative fostered a strong sense of social responsibility among students, encouraging them to actively participate in community welfare activities. It also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and inspired many to consider becoming regular donors. On a personal level, the experience brought a sense of fulfillment, empathy, and compassion, reinforcing the value of contributing to society in impactful ways .  \\n","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-03-20","hoursSpent":3,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at the RVCE campus. The event was conducted in a well-coordinated manner, with medical professionals ensuring safety and comfort throughout the process. It was a fulfilling experience to contribute towards saving lives and supporting the community. The initiative not only promoted social responsibility among students but also created awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation.","aicteMapping":"Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/_TuHeLCdSFw8DWCLtYtIE.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"mNyRoev-Q-Ph6ajVapagc","name":"Through the Eyes of Youth - SDG Photo Competition","slNo":13,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/7od5CtC0HWUloy7vAZLN8.png"],"endDate":"2023-08-13","duration":7,"outcomes":"The activity enhanced awareness about the Sustainable Development Goals, particularly the issue of poverty and social inequality. It helped develop observational skills, social sensitivity, and the ability to communicate powerful messages through visual storytelling. Participants gained a deeper understanding of real-world challenges faced by underprivileged communities and the importance of inclusive development. The competition encouraged youth engagement in social issues and reinforced the role of creativity and awareness in driving positive societal change.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-08-07","hoursSpent":7,"description":"Through the Eyes of Youth was a Sustainable Development Goals (SDG)–based photo competition aimed at encouraging students to visually interpret and highlight global social issues through photography. As part of the competition, participants were required to capture photographs aligned with one or more SDG goals. For this activity, a photograph depicting children affected by poverty was taken, aligning with SDG 1: No Poverty. The photograph aimed to portray the realities of socio-economic inequality and emphasize the importance of collective efforts toward poverty eradication. The competition promoted creative expression while fostering awareness of global challenges and the role of youth in addressing them.","aicteMapping":"Awareness Drive","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/125b158b-f3a6-4d5d-92e1-cc8aa24aeee9/86H4wpM14P6JtmXSCg7PE.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 08:29:45.115929+00', '2026-01-31 08:53:54.156519+00'), ('fbfdce31-4098-4765-8b31-17379ac0273e', 'b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22BT11","name":"Bhumika Mandolkar","period":"2022-2026","department":"Biotechnology","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"tv_AX4o_DXMzROxPGks1H","name":"FAST TREK 2.0","slNo":1,"place":"Kunagalu Betta Hills","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/K0b4vn0O7RckL1GtYT9Wx.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-01-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"Going on a trek results in improved physical fitness, increased stamina, and better overall health while also providing mental relaxation and stress relief. Being close to nature helps clear the mind, improve focus, and enhance emotional well-being. Completing a trek builds self-confidence, resilience, and a sense of achievement, while also encouraging teamwork and social bonding when done in a group. Overall, trekking leaves a person physically refreshed, mentally calm, and personally motivated.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-28","hoursSpent":10,"description":"The social cause behind the project was a cleanliness drive undertaken during the trek, with the primary objective of promoting environmental awareness and preserving the natural ecosystem. The initiative emphasized responsible tourism by encouraging participants to actively contribute to maintaining the cleanliness of the trekking trail and surrounding areas. The journey commenced early at 7:30 AM, as participants eagerly assembled and boarded the bus to the trekking site, filled with enthusiasm and anticipation for the day ahead. Before the trek began, detailed safety guidelines, rules of conduct, and event-related instructions were clearly communicated to ensure the well-being of all participants and the smooth execution of the activity.\\n\\nThe group then proceeded to the scenic Kunagalu Betta Hills, where the trek unfolded successfully, combining adventure with social responsibility. Along the route, participants engaged in collecting litter while enjoying the serene beauty of the hills, lush greenery, and panoramic views. The experience not only fostered teamwork and a sense of collective responsibility but also created lasting memories of a meaningful journey amidst breathtaking landscapes, reinforcing the importance of environmental conservation through action.","aicteMapping":"Preserving the environment","pointsEarned":12,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/LwlZ187tVIsJZPdhhVQzT.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"2-3","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"ma8vZYDy0ZK9KwYtTP1lH","name":"AKSHARA","slNo":2,"place":"Sai Sri Vidya Chethana","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/We7hIE_1X0cnFLOq6VXC9.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-08","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Akshara initiative yielded significant positive outcomes for both the student beneficiaries and the volunteers involved. Over 1,000 underprivileged students across eight schools in Bangalore gained improved clarity in academic concepts through interactive and activity-based learning methods. The sessions enhanced students’ interest in learning, classroom participation, and confidence, creating a more engaging and supportive educational environment.\\n\\nStudents benefited from strengthened foundational knowledge and exposure to essential life skills such as communication, problem-solving, and critical thinking, which contributed to their overall academic and personal development. The interactive approach helped bridge learning gaps and encouraged students to express themselves freely without hesitation.\\n\\nFor the volunteers, the project served as a meaningful experiential learning opportunity. Rotaractors developed skills in teaching, leadership, teamwork, communication, and social responsibility. The experience fostered empathy and a deeper understanding of grassroots educational challenges, reinforcing the importance of inclusive and accessible education.\\n\\nAt a broader level, the initiative strengthened the relationship between the Rotaract Club of RVCE and the local community, promoting a culture of volunteerism and social awareness. The project successfully contributed toward reducing educational disparities and reaffirmed the club’s commitment to quality education and community development, leaving a lasting and positive impact on all stakeholders involved.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-08","hoursSpent":6,"description":"The Rotaract Club of RVCE successfully organized and conducted a comprehensive skill development initiative titled “Akshara” on 8th June 2024, with the objective of improving academic understanding and essential life skills among underprivileged school students in Bangalore. The project was designed to address educational disparities faced by students from financially modest backgrounds by providing quality, interactive, and curriculum-aligned learning experiences.\\n\\nAs part of this initiative, Rotaract volunteers visited eight schools across Bangalore, reaching and benefiting over 1,000 students. The schools covered under this program included BET Convent, Sai Sri Vidya Chethana, Vishwa Bharathi High School, Kengeri High School, Government Model Primary School, Nehru Memorial School, Priyadarshini Vidhya Kendra School, and Mount Carmel English School. These institutions primarily cater to students from economically disadvantaged communities, making the intervention both timely and impactful.\\n\\nThe sessions were conducted using interactive and student-centric teaching methods, ensuring better engagement and understanding. Volunteers focused on strengthening core academic concepts while also emphasizing essential skills such as communication, problem-solving, and confidence-building. The use of activity-based learning helped create an inclusive classroom environment where students felt encouraged to participate actively and express themselves freely.\\n\\nIn addition to benefiting the students, the initiative also served as a valuable learning experience for the volunteers. Rotaractors gained hands-on exposure to teaching, classroom management, and community service, fostering a deeper appreciation for the role of educators and the importance of accessible education. The project promoted teamwork, leadership, empathy, and social responsibility among the volunteers.\\n\\nOverall, Akshara highlighted the transformative power of volunteer-driven educational outreach. The initiative reinforced the belief that consistent efforts in education can bridge learning gaps, empower young minds, and contribute to long-term social development. By addressing educational inequalities at the grassroots level, the project reaffirmed the Rotaract Club of RVCE’s commitment to community service and the vision of quality education for all.","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/dcGhvT9YdX1s893Zf9zdQ.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"4-5","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pnTRZvQ55EvEhzINGLmFP","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/-pgqpQwJfCue3Sgcuhx_L.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/rGu0iBBJyEFzbm_ljgoCZ.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Blood Donation Camp witnessed enthusiastic participation from the college community, resulting in the successful collection of a significant number of blood units. The donated blood contributed directly to meeting the requirements of nearby hospitals and blood banks, potentially saving numerous lives.\\n\\nThe camp helped create awareness among students about the importance of voluntary blood donation and motivated many first-time donors to take part confidently. It strengthened a sense of empathy, civic responsibility, and community service among participants. For volunteers and organizers, the event enhanced skills in coordination, teamwork, and event management.\\n\\nOverall, the initiative successfully reinforced the message that blood donation is a safe, simple, and impactful act of kindness, leaving a positive and lasting impression on the college community while contributing meaningfully to public health needs.","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":6,"description":"A Blood Donation Camp was successfully organized and conducted on the college campus with the objective of promoting voluntary blood donation and raising awareness about the importance of safe and timely blood availability. The camp was organized in collaboration with certified medical professionals and blood bank authorities, ensuring that all procedures were carried out in accordance with standard medical and safety guidelines.\\n\\nStudents, faculty members, and staff actively participated in the camp, demonstrating a strong sense of social responsibility and humanitarian concern. Prior to donation, donors were screened through basic health checks, including hemoglobin levels, blood pressure, and general health assessments, to ensure donor safety. The camp was conducted in a well-organized and hygienic environment, and volunteers assisted donors throughout the process to ensure comfort and smooth coordination.\\n\\nThe initiative aimed to encourage young individuals to become regular voluntary blood donors while dispelling myths and fears associated with blood donation. Awareness sessions and informational materials helped educate participants about the life-saving impact of blood donation and the continuous need for blood in medical emergencies.","aicteMapping":"Awareness about the importance of safe and timely blood availability","pointsEarned":14,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/RFUGcTHcgmuK_1aoN1geI.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"6-7","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"0Uu0xI2vVUBrlo5HCntHo","name":"Uptown Junk","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/XwVurDK6kr1cL4212IVYJ.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-14","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Uptown Junk event achieved its objective of providing an engaging platform for students to develop essential soft skills in an informal and enjoyable setting. Participants demonstrated improved teamwork, communication, and problem-solving abilities as they collaborated to decode riddles and follow clues within limited time frames.\\n\\nThe event generated high levels of enthusiasm and participation, contributing to a positive and energetic campus environment. It strengthened interpersonal connections among students from different backgrounds and promoted healthy competition. Many participants reported enhanced confidence, better logical thinking, and an increased appreciation for collaborative problem-solving.\\n\\nFor the organizing team and volunteers, the event served as an opportunity to develop planning, coordination, leadership, and crowd management skills. Overall, Uptown Junk was a successful blend of entertainment and intellectual challenge, leaving participants with memorable experiences while reinforcing the importance of creativity, teamwork, and strategic thinking.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-14","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Uptown Junk was a fun-filled, interactive event organized with the aim of fostering teamwork, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills among participants through an exciting series of riddles, clues, and challenges. Designed as a recreational yet intellectually stimulating activity, the event provided a refreshing break from routine academic life while encouraging collaboration and creative thinking.\\n\\nThe event followed a clue-based format where participants, usually in teams, were required to solve a sequence of riddles and puzzles to progress through different stages. Each clue led the teams closer to the final objective, demanding logical reasoning, observation, and quick decision-making. The challenges were strategically designed to test participants’ analytical abilities, presence of mind, and coordination under time constraints.\\n\\nVarious locations within the venue were utilized to enhance the thrill and immersive nature of the event, turning the campus into a dynamic playground of exploration and discovery. Volunteers and organizers ensured smooth execution by guiding participants, monitoring progress, and maintaining a lively and enthusiastic atmosphere throughout the event. The playful competitive spirit kept participants engaged while promoting sportsmanship and mutual respect.\\n\\nBeyond entertainment, Uptown Junk encouraged participants to step out of their comfort zones, communicate effectively within their teams, and approach problems from different perspectives. The event successfully blended fun with learning, making it an enjoyable and enriching experience for everyone involved.","aicteMapping":"Fostering teamwork, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/1WzMzkhwWPsln723CzkAs.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"8-9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"-4j5eKYk3fpY4-Wx-NOS0","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/8hzkjZJ1EvVT5o1xkpKVL.jpeg"],"endDate":"2023-06-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"As a participant in UTSARGA ’23, I actively contributed by completing a cumulative distance of 5,000 km, supporting the cause “Help a Child, Change the World.” Through consistent effort and dedication, each kilometer I ran symbolized a commitment toward improving the lives of underprivileged children by contributing to initiatives focused on education, healthcare, and child welfare.\\n\\nThis experience was both physically demanding and mentally rewarding. Maintaining discipline and consistency over the course of the event helped me develop greater endurance, time management, and self-motivation. Beyond personal fitness, the run gave me a deep sense of purpose, knowing that my efforts were part of a larger collective movement aimed at creating meaningful social impact.\\n\\nParticipating in the 5,000 km challenge strengthened my awareness of social responsibility and reinforced the idea that individual actions, when combined with a shared vision, can lead to transformative change. The experience instilled a sense of pride and fulfillment, as my contribution directly supported initiatives that strive to provide better opportunities and a brighter future for children in need.\\n\\nOverall, completing the 5,000 km run for UTSARGA ’23 was a powerful reminder that perseverance, compassion, and commitment can come together to make a lasting difference truly reflecting the spirit of “Help a Child, Change the World.”","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-04","hoursSpent":4,"description":"UTSARGA ’23 was organized as a flagship marathon event with the powerful theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The initiative was conceptualized with the vision of channelling collective community effort toward the upliftment of underprivileged children by supporting key areas such as education, healthcare, and overall child welfare. The marathon served as a platform to unite individuals from diverse backgrounds for a common humanitarian cause while promoting fitness, discipline, and social responsibility.\\n\\nThe event featured cumulative distance challenges of 5,000 km and 10,000 km, encouraging widespread participation and sustained commitment. Participants contributed by running, walking, or jogging, with every kilometre symbolizing a step toward creating a better future for children in need. The flexible and inclusive format allowed individuals of varying fitness levels to take part, reinforcing the idea that meaningful change can be achieved through collective effort rather than individual capacity alone.\\n\\nUTSARGA ’23 aimed not only to raise funds but also to spread awareness about the challenges faced by underprivileged children. The initiative highlighted the importance of access to quality education, timely healthcare, and a nurturing environment for holistic child development. Through consistent engagement, outreach, and awareness campaigns, the marathon inspired participants to recognize their role in driving social change.\\n\\nThe event was meticulously planned and executed with the support of volunteers and organizers who ensured smooth coordination, participant engagement, and effective tracking of cumulative distances. UTSARGA ’23 successfully combined the spirit of endurance with compassion, transforming physical effort into meaningful social impact.","aicteMapping":"To skill rural population","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/lwxxl740tPLYfmYzHQX6Z.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10-11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2d31Aw2A2sn8xb4NFAfFF","name":"Plog run along Vrushabhavathi Valley","slNo":6,"place":"Vrushabhavathi Valley","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/Sy0L1lyb1OjvNpxgYAPj6.jpeg"],"endDate":"2024-12-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"The plog run resulted in the successful removal of a significant amount of roadside waste from the Vrushabhavathi Valley, contributing to a cleaner and healthier environment. The collected trash was disposed of responsibly, reinforcing the importance of proper waste segregation and disposal practices.\\n\\nParticipants gained heightened awareness of environmental issues such as pollution, plastic waste, and urban neglect. The initiative encouraged individuals to adopt eco-conscious habits in their daily lives and inspired onlookers and local residents to take greater responsibility for maintaining cleanliness in public spaces.\\n\\nFor the volunteers, the activity promoted physical fitness, teamwork, and environmental stewardship, while also instilling a strong sense of social responsibility. Overall, the plog run successfully demonstrated how small, collective actions can lead to meaningful environmental impact, reinforcing the message that protecting natural spaces like the Vrushabhavathi Valley requires active and sustained community involvement.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-12-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"A Plog Run was successfully organized along the Vrushabhavathi Valley with the objective of promoting environmental awareness, physical fitness, and civic responsibility. The initiative combined jogging with plogging—an eco-friendly activity that involves collecting litter while running—thereby encouraging participants to contribute actively to environmental conservation while engaging in a healthy lifestyle.\\n\\nVolunteers and participants ran along the roadside stretch of the Vrushabhavathi Valley, collectively cleaning up waste that had accumulated in the area. Equipped with gloves, garbage bags, and safety gear, participants systematically collected plastic waste, wrappers, bottles, and other non-biodegradable trash discarded along the roadside and surrounding areas. The activity highlighted the growing issue of improper waste disposal and its harmful impact on local ecosystems.\\n\\nThe plog run fostered a sense of teamwork and community engagement as participants worked together to restore cleanliness and improve the visual and environmental quality of the valley. The initiative also served as a powerful awareness drive, drawing public attention to the importance of responsible waste management and sustainable practices. The event was conducted with proper coordination to ensure participant safety while maintaining efficiency in waste collection and segregation.","aicteMapping":"Promoting environmental awareness, physical fitness, and civic responsibility","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/WP3_VZkfgS1xAxNqP6MTH.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12-13","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"djG1_xeXH3U_0-6xmdWOD","name":"Gandhian Principles( Essay writing)","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/DyGRQIuu_m0ESm4Y3Tzqj.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-09","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Gandhian Principles Essay Writing event received enthusiastic participation and generated insightful and thought-provoking submissions. Participants demonstrated a strong understanding of Gandhian philosophy and its relevance in modern life, reflecting their ability to analyze social issues through an ethical lens.\\n\\nThe event enhanced participants’ writing, analytical, and critical thinking skills, while also instilling values of integrity, non-violence, and social responsibility. It encouraged students to engage in self-reflection and develop a deeper appreciation for ethical leadership and service-oriented living.\\n\\nAt a broader level, the event contributed to the promotion of Gandhian values within the academic community, inspiring students to apply these principles in their personal and professional lives. Overall, the initiative successfully reinforced the enduring significance of Mahatma Gandhi’s ideals and fostered a culture of thoughtful discourse, moral awareness, and responsible citizenship.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-12-09","hoursSpent":1,"description":"An Essay Writing Event on Gandhian Principles was organized with the objective of creating awareness and encouraging deeper understanding of the timeless values and philosophies propagated by Mahatma Gandhi. The event aimed to provide students with a platform to reflect upon and articulate their perspectives on Gandhian ideals such as truth (Satya), non-violence (Ahimsa), simplicity, self-reliance, social justice, and service to humanity.\\n\\nParticipants were invited to express their thoughts through well-structured essays, highlighting the relevance of Gandhian principles in contemporary society. The event encouraged critical thinking, creativity, and ethical reflection, allowing students to connect historical values with present-day social, political, and environmental challenges. By engaging in thoughtful writing, participants explored how Gandhi’s philosophy continues to offer solutions for issues such as conflict resolution, inequality, corruption, and sustainability.\\n\\nThe event was conducted in an organized and inclusive manner, fostering a scholarly environment that promoted respectful expression of ideas. It served not only as a literary activity but also as an educational initiative that strengthened moral awareness and civic responsibility among participants.","aicteMapping":"Encouraged critical thinking, creativity, and ethical reflection","pointsEarned":2,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/ygBPUBYvTfiqOgQJjbsJa.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"14-15","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"DJqBWEqv-iTzjQ7QKnIhl","name":"Police Marshal","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/Gxl3oPSQsEmcFWgEY_Eqo.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-12-18","duration":1,"outcomes":"The Police Marshal Awareness Program significantly enhanced students’ understanding of cyber crime and digital security. Participants became more aware of potential online threats and learned practical steps to safeguard their personal and financial information while using digital platforms.\\n\\nThe session helped reduce hesitation and fear associated with reporting cyber crimes by clarifying legal procedures and emphasizing the role of law enforcement in providing support. Students developed increased confidence to report incidents and contribute to a safer digital environment.\\n\\nOverall, the event fostered a sense of digital responsibility, vigilance, and cooperation with law enforcement. It successfully empowered students with knowledge and awareness, reinforcing the message that cyber safety is a shared responsibility and that timely reporting plays a crucial role in combating cyber crime.","semester":"6","startDate":"2024-12-18","hoursSpent":2,"description":"A Police Marshal Awareness Program was organized with the objective of educating students about the growing threat of cyber crime and the importance of digital safety. Officials from the local police department were invited to interact with students and provide first-hand insights into various forms of cyber crime, including online fraud, identity theft, cyber bullying, phishing, and financial scams.\\n\\nDuring the session, the police officials explained common cyber crime tactics and highlighted preventive measures that individuals can adopt to protect themselves online. Real-life case examples were shared to help students better understand how cyber criminals operate and the serious consequences of unsafe digital practices. Participants were also educated about safe usage of social media, protection of personal information, and the importance of strong passwords and secure online behavior.\\n\\nA key emphasis of the program was on timely reporting of cyber crime incidents. The police officials encouraged students to immediately report any suspicious activity or cyber crime they encounter, reassuring them that reporting helps authorities take prompt action and prevent further harm. Information regarding cyber crime helplines and reporting mechanisms was also shared to ensure students know where and how to seek help.","aicteMapping":"Awareness about cyber crime and importance of digital safety","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/PkoNiMQbTpjTJH8eHSEpO.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"16-17","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"uxYp8n6cMqdO78vNkFqes","name":"Kannada Sangha T-Shirt + Plant a Tree","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/Dgbls6WDQaEdXSb4pd6HY.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-07-07","duration":1,"outcomes":"The activity had several positive outcomes:\\n\\nEnvironmental Impact: The planted tree contributes to increasing green cover, improving air quality, and supporting local biodiversity.\\n\\nAwareness and Responsibility: Participating in tree planting fostered a sense of environmental responsibility and highlighted the importance of small actions in addressing global ecological challenges.\\n\\nClub Engagement: Purchasing the club T-shirt and participating in the plantation strengthened personal connection with the club, promoting teamwork, pride, and active involvement in club initiatives.\\n\\nPersonal Growth: The experience reinforced values of sustainability, commitment, and social responsibility, demonstrating how simple steps like planting a tree can create meaningful impact over time.\\n\\nOverall, this initiative successfully combined community engagement and environmental stewardship, leaving a lasting positive effect on both participants and the environment.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-07-07","hoursSpent":0,"description":"As part of an initiative to promote environmental sustainability and club engagement, I purchased the official club T-shirt and participated in a tree plantation activity. The initiative was designed to encourage members to demonstrate their commitment to both the club’s values and environmental responsibility.\\n\\nThe tree plantation activity involved planting a sapling in a designated area under the guidance of club volunteers or environmental coordinators. Proper care was taken to ensure that the sapling was planted correctly, including preparing the soil, providing adequate space, and watering it to support healthy growth. This simple yet impactful action aimed to contribute to increasing green cover, promoting biodiversity, and creating awareness about environmental conservation.\\n\\nBy combining club participation with environmental action, the activity symbolized the importance of personal responsibility, community involvement, and sustainable practices. It encouraged members to take small, consistent actions that can have a long-term positive impact on the planet.","aicteMapping":"Promote environmental sustainability","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/McD6HlKT1sumTmcpWVDy-.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"18-19","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ei88RRK4tdAbkdqqlRShL","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/VFYETSrour3JPh2g_LF-i.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/6IDSI-2IfvXNbpoRwebg6.png","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/0CbPyrfgtpMbibubzpVcR.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"As a participant in UTSARGA ’25, I actively contributed by completing a cumulative distance of 5,000 km, supporting the cause “Help a Child, Change the World.” Through consistent effort and dedication, each kilometer I ran symbolized a commitment toward improving the lives of underprivileged children by contributing to initiatives focused on education, healthcare, and child welfare.\\n\\nThis experience was both physically demanding and mentally rewarding. Maintaining discipline and consistency over the course of the event helped me develop greater endurance, time management, and self-motivation. Beyond personal fitness, the run gave me a deep sense of purpose, knowing that my efforts were part of a larger collective movement aimed at creating meaningful social impact.\\n\\nIn addition to participating in the marathon, I also volunteered to assist with registration and certificate distribution. This role allowed me to contribute to the smooth execution of the event, interact with fellow participants, and ensure that everyone’s efforts were properly recognized. Managing these responsibilities enhanced my organizational, teamwork, and communication skills, providing valuable experience in event coordination.\\n\\nParticipating in the 5,000 km challenge and volunteering strengthened my awareness of social responsibility and reinforced the idea that individual actions, when combined with a shared vision, can lead to transformative change. The experience instilled a sense of pride and fulfilment, as my combined contributions both on the track and behind the scenes directly supported initiatives that provide better opportunities and a brighter future for children in need.\\n\\nOverall, being part of UTSARGA ’25 was a powerful reminder that perseverance, compassion, and commitment can come together to make a lasting difference truly reflecting the spirit of “Help a Child, Change the World.”","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"UTSARGA ’25 was organized as a flagship marathon event with the powerful theme “Help a Child, Change the World.” The initiative was conceptualized with the vision of channelling collective community effort toward the upliftment of underprivileged children by supporting key areas such as education, healthcare, and overall child welfare. The marathon served as a platform to unite individuals from diverse backgrounds for a common humanitarian cause while promoting fitness, discipline, and social responsibility.\\n\\nThe event featured cumulative distance challenges of 5,000 km and 10,000 km, encouraging widespread participation and sustained commitment. Participants contributed by running, walking, or jogging, with every kilometre symbolizing a step toward creating a better future for children in need. The flexible and inclusive format allowed individuals of varying fitness levels to take part, reinforcing the idea that meaningful change can be achieved through collective effort rather than individual capacity alone.\\n\\nUTSARGA ’25 aimed not only to raise funds but also to spread awareness about the challenges faced by underprivileged children. The initiative highlighted the importance of access to quality education, timely healthcare, and a nurturing environment for holistic child development. Through consistent engagement, outreach, and awareness campaigns, the marathon inspired participants to recognize their role in driving social change.\\n\\nThe event was meticulously planned and executed with the support of volunteers and organizers who ensured smooth coordination, participant engagement, and effective tracking of cumulative distances. UTSARGA ’25 successfully combined the spirit of endurance with compassion, transforming physical effort into meaningful social impact.","aicteMapping":"","pointsEarned":22,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/b0c7cc1b-2542-4c3a-b896-6dbbf59bf861/x7Rs3E2z4jTeQOeMtbbEo.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"20-21","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-02-01 11:28:48.806017+00', '2026-02-02 06:59:03.670833+00'), ('fc62b80c-1d52-4eec-a58d-3d2019ccafe1', '07dff400-0808-41b9-aa17-8b27bb43b1be', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV23CY402","name":"Kapsha Suraj Singh","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"R2WZPe0L-uBamQqLWmN0r","name":"Campus Cleaning","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-01-13","duration":1,"outcomes":"to clean.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-01-13","hoursSpent":7,"description":"Cleaned the entire campus","aicteMapping":"Clearning College","pointsEarned":5,"certificateImage":"https://gsqeb