r technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07dff400-0808-41b9-aa17-8b27bb43b1be/dVWJa_UZt6f1WmvbGyGM6.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"2A4pObGmyH3MhrEPEb-zA","name":"Blood Donation","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-03-20","duration":-60,"outcomes":"blood saves lives","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-05-20","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Donated blood","aicteMapping":"Helping local schools to achieve good result and enhance their enrolment in Higher technical/vocational education","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07dff400-0808-41b9-aa17-8b27bb43b1be/1D0ZWZgG-U95uRqdzt50D.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"z4Q-NrNhI7wjYHXpA1VPO","name":"Blood Donation ","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2025-10-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"blood saves lives","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-10-30","hoursSpent":4,"description":"Donated blood","aicteMapping":"Blood Donation","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07dff400-0808-41b9-aa17-8b27bb43b1be/99N0p7Ow0S0sE_OLy6HjG.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"rzESBPTTxJavaTL41C-m_","name":"Paper Drive 2.0","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-12-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Plastic is harmful","semester":"4","startDate":"2024-12-30","hoursSpent":70,"description":"Made carry bags out of paper","aicteMapping":"Spreading public awareness under rural outreach program","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/07dff400-0808-41b9-aa17-8b27bb43b1be/E1yOx8cPKv_WOBVwE_Ual.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"12","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr. Minal Moharir","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 07:29:48.153651+00', '2026-01-30 07:31:27.680162+00'), ('ff5fa7c9-12b6-4a40-91c8-c51ac04da47a', 'df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22EC159","name":"Srujan Sateesh Kalagi","period":"2022-2026","department":"Electronics & Communication Engineering","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"sW7tjPcBTC2aOmgoEljXE","name":"Kannada Habba - KARNATA","slNo":1,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/n3TFeuY5HUnxEYSg6cO7y.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/XlND2vmoXPE8sA4UjzpZi.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-15","duration":32,"outcomes":"Through participating in Kannada Habba, I gained a deeper understanding of the richness and importance of the Kannada language and Karnataka’s cultural heritage. The event helped me appreciate traditional art forms, folk culture, and the historical values associated with them. It also emphasized the role of language in preserving cultural identity and connecting people across generations.\\n\\nAdditionally, the program enhanced my sense of cultural pride and encouraged me to respect and promote regional traditions. Participating alongside peers from diverse backgrounds improved my ability to collaborate effectively and strengthened my appreciation for cultural inclusivity within an academic environment.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-05-15","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Kannada Habba was celebrated with great enthusiasm at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) on 15 June 2023 to promote the richness of the Kannada language and the cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event was organized by the college’s Kannada Sangha with the objective of instilling pride in regional culture and encouraging students to connect with Karnataka’s traditions, literature, and values. Students and faculty from various departments actively participated, making the celebration vibrant and inclusive.\\n\\nThe program featured a variety of cultural activities that reflected the diversity of Kannada culture. Traditional folk dances, classical and light music performances, skits, and poetry recitations in Kannada were presented by students. These performances highlighted themes related to Karnataka’s history, social values, and linguistic beauty. The event also provided a platform for students to showcase their artistic talents while strengthening cultural unity among participants from different backgrounds.\\n\\nOverall, Kannada Habba at RVCE was a meaningful and memorable celebration that reinforced the importance of preserving and promoting the Kannada language and culture. The event fostered cultural awareness, enhanced student engagement, and encouraged respect for local traditions within the academic environment. It successfully fulfilled its objective of celebrating Karnataka’s heritage while strengthening the sense of community among students and faculty members.","aicteMapping":"Institutional Activity – Cultural & Social Engagement","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/MG4nWOoTQB3PCUHDXizHk.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"Ttp0B5H8P9BnwpUDQPP08","name":"Kannada Habba - GHARJANE","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/GPBO6YuOKPyxQM8rSEj0B.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-20","duration":32,"outcomes":"By participating in Kannada Habba – Gharjane, I gained a deeper appreciation for the richness and significance of the Kannada language and Karnataka’s cultural heritage. The event helped me understand how cultural programs play a vital role in preserving traditions and promoting a strong sense of cultural identity.\\n\\nI also learned the importance of teamwork and active participation in organizing and celebrating cultural events. Overall, the experience strengthened my cultural awareness and motivated me to respect, preserve, and promote regional traditions.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-05-20","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Kannada Habba – Gharjane was celebrated on 20 June 2024 at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) with the objective of promoting the Kannada language and the cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event aimed to foster cultural awareness and instill pride in regional traditions among students and faculty members. Participants from various departments came together, creating an inclusive platform to celebrate Karnataka’s rich linguistic and cultural legacy.\\n\\nThe program featured a variety of cultural performances, including traditional and contemporary dance forms, folk and classical music, skits, and Kannada poetry recitations. These activities highlighted the history, values, and artistic richness of Karnataka. The enthusiastic participation of students, complemented by vibrant stage decorations and traditional attire, created an engaging and authentic cultural atmosphere throughout the event.\\n\\nOverall, Kannada Habba – Gharjane served as a meaningful cultural celebration that strengthened unity and cultural appreciation within the college community. The event successfully encouraged student participation, promoted respect for regional culture, and reinforced the importance of preserving the Kannada language and traditions within an academic environment.","aicteMapping":"Institutional Activity – Cultural & Social Engagement","pointsEarned":20,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/P80WJrwLmvsPKKchjlBjI.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"jXDMfS5knY7jIsU89ZThU","name":"Kannada Habba - JAGADHVAHA","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/32W_x-1ycJeHUS4ptb2gi.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-12-04","duration":31,"outcomes":"By participating in Kannada Habba Jagadvaha 2025, held on 4 December 2025, I gained a stronger appreciation for the cultural richness and linguistic heritage of Karnataka. The celebration emphasized the importance of preserving and promoting the regional language through artistic expression and active community participation.\\n\\nWitnessing the enthusiasm of fellow students in various performances and cultural displays helped me understand how traditions bring people together and strengthen cultural identity. Overall, the event deepened my respect for Kannada culture and motivated me to remain connected to my roots while encouraging others to take pride in our shared heritage.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-11-04","hoursSpent":100,"description":"Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha 2025 was celebrated on 4 December 2025 at R.V. College of Engineering (RVCE) with great enthusiasm to honor the Kannada language and the cultural heritage of Karnataka. The event aimed to promote awareness, pride, and respect for Kannada traditions among students and faculty members. Organized as part of the college’s cultural initiatives, the celebration brought together participants from diverse backgrounds to collectively experience and appreciate the essence of Karnataka’s rich legacy.\\n\\nThe program featured a wide range of cultural activities showcasing the vibrancy of Kannada culture. Students performed traditional and contemporary dance forms, folk and classical music, skits, and poetry recitations in Kannada. These performances highlighted themes related to Karnataka’s history, social values, and linguistic beauty. The stage décor, traditional attire, and enthusiastic participation created an authentic cultural atmosphere, making the event engaging and memorable for the audience.\\n\\nOverall, Kannada Habba – Jagadvaha 2025 served as an effective platform for cultural expression and community bonding within the college. The event strengthened cultural awareness, encouraged student participation, and reinforced the importance of preserving regional language and traditions within a modern academic environment. It successfully fostered unity, cultural pride, and respect for Kannada heritage among the RVCE community.","aicteMapping":"Institutional Activity – Cultural & Social Engagement","pointsEarned":30,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/1c4kyM5xE-ba9jGZxZIDp.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"G0gOd62wm_kgx66Fbf7V5","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/BMPgo_WBfvUoIAhuNNonS.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the Utsarga Marathon enhanced awareness of social responsibility and the importance of community service among students. The event helped participants understand the role of collective action in addressing social causes while encouraging a positive attitude toward voluntary service. It also contributed to improved physical fitness and promoted the adoption of a healthy and active lifestyle.\\n\\nFurthermore, the activity strengthened essential life skills such as discipline, perseverance, teamwork, and time management. The experience motivated students to engage in future NSS and extension activities and reinforced a sense of civic duty and commitment toward societal well-being. Overall, the event contributed to the holistic development of students beyond academic learning.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The Utsarga Marathon was organized under the National Service Scheme (NSS) by R.V. College of Engineering as an extension and social outreach initiative aimed at promoting social responsibility and community engagement. The event encouraged students to actively participate in a cause-oriented physical activity that emphasized service to society while fostering awareness about important social issues. Students from various departments participated enthusiastically, reflecting a strong sense of collective responsibility.\\n\\nThe marathon served as a platform to integrate physical fitness with civic consciousness. By participating in the 5 km category, students demonstrated discipline, endurance, and commitment while contributing to a socially meaningful initiative. The event highlighted the importance of maintaining a healthy lifestyle alongside active involvement in community welfare programs, aligning well with the objectives of the National Service Scheme.\\n\\nAdditionally, the Utsarga Marathon promoted values such as teamwork, perseverance, and volunteerism. The collaborative nature of the event strengthened interpersonal interaction among participants and reinforced the role of youth in nation-building activities. Overall, the program successfully combined physical activity with social awareness, making it a purposeful and impactful outreach initiative within the academic environment.","aicteMapping":"Social Responsibility Activity (NSS)","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/-BQmabwcmbW4oATQSUinI.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"hhdDXtTTnfqND9Ffi4i6Q","name":"Blood Donation Camp","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/AJfmvRBYFfsgSqbiv1U90.JPG"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the blood donation activity enhanced awareness of public health issues and the critical role of voluntary blood donors in healthcare systems. The event encouraged a sense of civic duty and motivated students to contribute positively to society through responsible and ethical actions.\\n\\nFurthermore, the experience strengthened values such as empathy, social commitment, and community service. It inspired participants to engage in future outreach and health-related initiatives, contributing to their holistic development beyond academics while reinforcing the importance of giving back to society.","semester":"2","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The voluntary blood donation activity was conducted as a community service and social outreach initiative in collaboration with BGS Global Hospitals. The activity aimed to support healthcare services by encouraging voluntary blood donation and promoting awareness about the importance of safe and timely blood availability. Students willingly participated in the blood donation camp, demonstrating social responsibility and humanitarian values.\\n\\nThe program emphasized the role of youth in contributing to public health and saving lives through voluntary efforts. Participants were guided through proper medical screening procedures and educated on the significance of regular blood donation. The initiative helped create awareness about the continuous need for blood in hospitals and highlighted how individual contributions can make a meaningful impact on society.\\n\\nAdditionally, the activity fostered a spirit of compassion, empathy, and service among participants. By actively taking part in the blood donation drive, students reinforced the values of selflessness and community engagement. The program successfully aligned with the objectives of extension and outreach activities by integrating health awareness with social responsibility within the academic environment.","aicteMapping":"Health & Community Service","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/dSlA1-p9ZtltnLEElbL4U.jpg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pOkQ2pHwAJOB4mkxO5pvQ","name":"Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE , Bengaluru","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/iXKA1G7CrdtDCIvvfzElo.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-03-03","duration":1,"outcomes":"Participation in the voter awareness and pledge activity enhanced understanding of democratic rights and responsibilities. The initiative strengthened awareness about the significance of voting in nation-building and encouraged a sense of accountability toward the electoral process among first-time voters.\\n\\nFurthermore, the activity fostered civic consciousness, confidence, and a commitment to ethical participation in democracy. It motivated participants to promote voter awareness within their communities and reinforced the importance of active engagement in civic duties, contributing to their overall social and personal development.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-03-03","hoursSpent":5,"description":"The “Mera Pehla Vote – Desh Ke Liye” initiative was undertaken as a civic engagement and voter awareness activity aimed at encouraging first-time voters to actively participate in the democratic process. The program emphasized the importance of voting as a fundamental constitutional right and a vital responsibility of every citizen. As part of this initiative, participants pledged to exercise their right to vote and contribute to the democratic development of the nation.\\n\\nThe activity focused on creating awareness among youth about the role of elections in shaping governance and national progress. By engaging first-time voters, the program highlighted how informed and responsible participation strengthens democratic institutions. The pledge served as a reminder of the impact individual votes have on policy-making, leadership selection, and the overall future of the country.\\n\\nAdditionally, the initiative encouraged participants to act as ambassadors of democratic values by motivating peers and community members to participate in elections. It reinforced ethical citizenship, constitutional awareness, and social responsibility, aligning with national efforts to promote active civic participation among young citizens.","aicteMapping":"Electoral Awareness & Democratic Participation","pointsEarned":4,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/df631fc5-9dad-4b23-a555-ec1edf87ddf2/WNzpPcs0N0w0ssLlHknX2.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 20:16:40.063112+00', '2026-01-30 22:14:01.211379+00'), ('ffeccd52-02c4-474e-ba1a-6874cf2664bf', '5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f', '{"student":{"usn":"1RV22CY003","name":"Abhyuday Singh","period":"2022-2026","department":"Computer Science & Engineering - Cybersecurity","totalPoints":0},"activities":[{"id":"TWgEWcvZIGC-BlKoyzFye","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2023","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/uODbWsqGx1H3yowmlaCBu.jpg"],"endDate":"2023-06-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"1. Value of Humanitarian Service\\nI learned that donating blood is one of the simplest yet most powerful ways to help others and save lives.\\n\\n2. Responsibility Toward Public Health\\nThe drive helped me understand the importance of maintaining adequate blood supplies in government hospitals and supporting the healthcare system.\\n\\n3. Overcoming Fear and Building Courage\\nParticipating in the donation process helped me overcome hesitation and develop confidence in contributing to social causes.\\n\\n4. Health Awareness\\nI became more aware of my own health status through pre-donation screening and learned about healthy lifestyle practices.","semester":"3","startDate":"2023-06-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at my college in collaboration with a government hospital, with the aim of supporting patients in need of emergency and long-term medical care. This initiative was conducted to promote awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its role in saving lives. Students and faculty members actively took part in the drive, creating a strong sense of unity and social responsibility within the campus.\\n\\nThe event highlighted the critical shortage of blood in hospitals and the constant need for safe and timely donations. By contributing as a donor, I was able to directly support patients undergoing surgeries, accident victims, and individuals suffering from chronic illnesses. The drive also included medical screenings and guidance from healthcare professionals, ensuring that the donation process was safe and well-organized.\\n\\nParticipating in this blood donation camp was a deeply meaningful experience, as it allowed me to make a real and immediate impact on people’s lives. It strengthened my awareness of public health challenges and reinforced the importance of community participation in healthcare initiatives. The experience encouraged me to continue engaging in humanitarian and service-oriented activities in the future.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":6,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/2QEMQF4HPDc7Q1GvrO0Pj.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"1-2","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"EN1VfmwN77RNbLyReZeor","name":"Utsarga Marathon","slNo":2,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/1rsqyd3QcQ0EwXcIlk8j_.JPG"],"endDate":"2024-02-04","duration":1,"outcomes":"1. Social Responsibility\\nYou learn the importance of giving back to society and understanding the real-life challenges faced by underprivileged children. It helps you realize that even small actions can contribute to meaningful social change.\\n\\n2. Empathy and Awareness\\nThe event builds awareness about issues related to child welfare, education, and healthcare. It encourages you to be more empathetic and sensitive toward the needs of others.\\n\\n3. Discipline and Perseverance\\nTraining for and completing a 5K marathon teaches self-discipline, consistency, and mental strength. It shows you how dedication and effort lead to success.\\n\\n4. Goal Setting and Time Management\\nBalancing academics, training, and participation helps improve your ability to manage time and work toward set goals.","semester":"3","startDate":"2024-02-04","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I actively participated in a 5K marathon organized by RVCE College in support of the noble cause “Help a Child, Change the World.” This event was conducted with the objective of raising awareness about the importance of child welfare, access to quality education, healthcare, and overall development for underprivileged children. The marathon brought together students, faculty members, and staff in a collective effort to promote social responsibility and community engagement.\\n\\nThrough this initiative, participants were encouraged to reflect on the challenges faced by children from marginalized backgrounds and understand how small individual efforts can contribute to creating meaningful change. The event emphasized the values of empathy, compassion, and service, reminding everyone that supporting a child today can help shape a better and more sustainable future for society.\\n\\nParticipating in this marathon was not only a test of physical endurance and discipline but also an opportunity to contribute towards a socially impactful mission. It strengthened my sense of responsibility as a student and citizen, motivating me to actively engage in activities that promote inclusive growth and social development. The experience was both inspiring and fulfilling, as it combined personal fitness goals with a greater purpose of uplifting the lives of children and empowering them with better opportunities.\\n\\nOverall, the 5K marathon served as a powerful platform to spread awareness, encourage volunteerism, and inspire collective action toward building a more equitable and compassionate society.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/VYjbhscjd1EKX8iTY9lD1.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"3-4","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"w7r6djnNDL2Wzw_t2KGPJ","name":"Blood Donation 2024","slNo":3,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/8_Yg_41jSWcVx3C4Kp6At.jpg"],"endDate":"2024-06-28","duration":1,"outcomes":"1. Value of Humanitarian Service\\nI learned that donating blood is one of the simplest yet most powerful ways to help others and save lives.\\n\\n2. Responsibility Toward Public Health\\nThe drive helped me understand the importance of maintaining adequate blood supplies in government hospitals and supporting the healthcare system.\\n\\n3. Community Participation\\nI realized how collective efforts from students and institutions can address critical societal needs.\\n\\n4. Ethical and Civic Responsibility\\nThe experience reinforced my duty as a responsible citizen to contribute positively to society.\\n\\n5. Personal Growth and Selflessness\\nI learned the importance of putting others’ needs before my own and contributing selflessly for the greater good.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-06-28","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at my college in collaboration with a government hospital, with the aim of supporting patients in need of emergency and long-term medical care. This initiative was conducted to promote awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its role in saving lives. Students and faculty members actively took part in the drive, creating a strong sense of unity and social responsibility within the campus.\\n\\nThe event highlighted the critical shortage of blood in hospitals and the constant need for safe and timely donations. By contributing as a donor, I was able to directly support patients undergoing surgeries, accident victims, and individuals suffering from chronic illnesses. The drive also included medical screenings and guidance from healthcare professionals, ensuring that the donation process was safe and well-organized.\\n\\nParticipating in this blood donation camp was a deeply meaningful experience, as it allowed me to make a real and immediate impact on people’s lives. It strengthened my awareness of public health challenges and reinforced the importance of community participation in healthcare initiatives. The experience encouraged me to continue engaging in humanitarian and service-oriented activities in the future.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/SHu_DyD-FhYRjExKps0vw.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"5-6","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"OXfWZoo4UMei16Y-kLQvg","name":"Utsaraga Marathon 2025","slNo":4,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/VqcWJ7FiwExLhWGsjXqfl.jpeg"],"endDate":"2025-04-06","duration":1,"outcomes":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 was conducted successfully with high levels of enthusiasm and strong community participation, fostering a spirit of unity, fitness, and social service. The event encouraged participants to embrace a healthy and active lifestyle while simultaneously supporting a noble cause through their registration contributions. It also functioned as an effective awareness platform, demonstrating how collective individual efforts can create a significant positive impact on society.\\n\\nOverall, the marathon strongly reflected the NSS motto, “Not Me, But You,” motivating students to stay socially responsible while striving for personal growth and community development.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-04-06","hoursSpent":1,"description":"Utsarga Marathon 2025 is a flagship annual event organized by the National Service Scheme (NSS) of RV College of Engineering with the objective of promoting physical fitness, social responsibility, and community bonding among students and the public. The event brings together students, faculty members, and fitness enthusiasts to participate in a cause-driven initiative that supports meaningful social welfare activities. Participants register by contributing a nominal fee, which is collectively used to assist underprivileged communities, support healthcare initiatives, and fund various community development programs.\\n\\nBeyond being a test of physical endurance, the marathon represents a strong commitment to service and social awareness. The event is carefully planned and executed with efficient route management, dedicated volunteer support, and essential safety arrangements such as hydration stations and medical assistance, ensuring a safe and well-organized experience for all participants. Through Utsarga Marathon, NSS instills values of discipline, perseverance, and empathy, motivating individuals to adopt healthier lifestyles while actively contributing to positive social change.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/4ZRKWowz6Cdk1UQhWtqJn.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"7-8","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"8Q02vJ3XXJgSz4i_Ho-05","name":"GenAI Hackathon ACM ","slNo":5,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/5GRwUplSvsaikro_33hSL.JPG"],"endDate":"2024-11-24","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through volunteering at the GenAI Hackathon, I gained valuable practical experience in organizing and managing a large-scale technical event. I learned the importance of effective planning, coordination, and time management to ensure smooth execution. Working closely with organizers, mentors, and participants helped me improve my communication and interpersonal skills.\\n\\nThe experience enhanced my ability to work efficiently in a team, handle responsibilities under pressure, and adapt to dynamic situations. I developed problem-solving skills by addressing on-site challenges and responding promptly to participant queries. Additionally, exposure to Generative AI projects and discussions broadened my technical awareness and understanding of emerging technologies.\\n\\nVolunteering for this event also strengthened my leadership qualities, confidence, and sense of accountability. It reinforced the value of discipline, professionalism, and collaboration in achieving common goals. Overall, the experience contributed significantly to my personal and professional growth while motivating me to actively participate in future technical and social initiatives.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-11-24","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I volunteered for the GenAI Hackathon organized by EDDOCK on 29th November 2024 at the DTL Huddle, where I actively contributed to the successful planning and execution of the event. As a volunteer, I assisted in coordinating participants, managing registrations, and ensuring smooth communication between teams, mentors, and organizers.\\n\\nMy responsibilities included supporting logistical arrangements, facilitating access to technical resources, and helping maintain the event schedule. I also assisted in resolving on-site queries, guiding participants, and ensuring that the hackathon environment remained organized and productive throughout the event.\\n\\nVolunteering for this event provided me with valuable experience in event management, teamwork, and leadership. It enhanced my organizational and interpersonal skills while allowing me to contribute to a platform that promoted innovation and learning in Generative Artificial Intelligence. Overall, the experience strengthened my sense of responsibility and motivated me to take part in more academic and technical initiatives in the future.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/XH8A6Z-6N1U3UagMLTLie.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"9-10","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"4dUbD_qYE_z5S37WEUiSE","name":"Lakshya x Plantation Drive ","slNo":6,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/K8jifBkyp_6d24FARn9Pv.JPEG","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/_hwNhQglI2rawW1HhVoKo.JPEG"],"endDate":"2025-04-26","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through participation in the Lakshya Shooting Event 2025, I developed greater focus, patience, and self-discipline. The event helped me understand the importance of precision, consistency, and mental stability in achieving performance goals.\\n\\nI learned to follow safety protocols and work responsibly in a supervised environment, enhancing my sense of accountability and professionalism. The teamwork and peer interaction improved my communication and cooperation skills.\\n\\nThe environmental initiative associated with the event increased my awareness of sustainability and encouraged me to take personal responsibility for protecting the environment. Overall, the experience contributed to my personal growth by strengthening my confidence, resilience, and commitment to ethical and responsible conduct.","semester":"5","startDate":"2025-04-26","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in the “Lakshya” Shooting Event 2025 organized by the NCC at RV College of Engineering on 26th and 27th April 2025. The event was conducted under proper supervision and aimed at developing discipline, focus, teamwork, and precision among students. It provided a structured platform to practice shooting skills while emphasizing safety, responsibility, and sportsmanship.\\n\\nThe competition created a motivating environment where participants could enhance their technical abilities, concentration, and mental control. Along with skill development, the event promoted environmental awareness through a sapling distribution initiative, encouraging students to contribute towards sustainability and ecological responsibility.\\n\\nParticipating in Lakshya 2025 was a valuable experience that combined physical coordination, mental discipline, and social responsibility. It strengthened my confidence and motivated me to pursue continuous self-improvement while actively contributing to community and environmental welfare.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/bT53RqqxFoNcy-LZ8fcIe.JPEG","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"11-12","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"oPVrgGtR1y_2DccdHxtqx","name":"Blood Donation Camp 2025","slNo":7,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/UyVqpzx3OFr4Vpw5_945c.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/NAyHKtmjERdd-wHBOwqJt.jpg","https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/eWIKiXH0PcWNxhDINFLar.jpg"],"endDate":"2025-01-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"1. Health Awareness\\nI became more aware of my own health status through pre-donation screening and learned about healthy lifestyle practices.\\n\\n2.Empathy and Compassion\\nSeeing patients and medical staff working tirelessly increased my respect for healthcare workers and strengthened my sense of empathy.\\n\\n3.Community Participation\\nI realized how collective efforts from students and institutions can address critical societal needs.\\n\\n4. Ethical and Civic Responsibility\\nThe experience reinforced my duty as a responsible citizen to contribute positively to society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-01-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I participated in a blood donation drive organized at my college in collaboration with a government hospital, with the aim of supporting patients in need of emergency and long-term medical care. This initiative was conducted to promote awareness about the importance of voluntary blood donation and its role in saving lives. Students and faculty members actively took part in the drive, creating a strong sense of unity and social responsibility within the campus.\\n\\nThe event highlighted the critical shortage of blood in hospitals and the constant need for safe and timely donations. By contributing as a donor, I was able to directly support patients undergoing surgeries, accident victims, and individuals suffering from chronic illnesses. The drive also included medical screenings and guidance from healthcare professionals, ensuring that the donation process was safe and well-organized.\\n\\nParticipating in this blood donation camp was a deeply meaningful experience, as it allowed me to make a real and immediate impact on people’s lives. It strengthened my awareness of public health challenges and reinforced the importance of community participation in healthcare initiatives. The experience encouraged me to continue engaging in humanitarian and service-oriented activities in the future.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/dkqKmLsyjFNk3BhN1d_Lg.jpeg","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"13-24","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"BXx--YZpKnAwuvGMBTdvx","name":"Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon","slNo":8,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/M26JPp2mulWN6CnjT4ra4.png"],"endDate":"2025-05-11","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through participation in the Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon, I developed a deeper understanding of the social, ethical, and legal implications of gender discrimination and female foeticide. The event helped me recognize the importance of promoting equal rights and opportunities for girls from birth.\\n\\nI learned the value of collective action in creating awareness and influencing social attitudes. Engaging with diverse participants enhanced my communication skills and social sensitivity. The experience strengthened my sense of civic responsibility and encouraged me to actively support initiatives that promote social justice and human dignity.\\n\\nOverall, the walkathon contributed significantly to my personal growth by fostering empathy, social awareness, and a commitment to building a more inclusive and equitable society.","semester":"6","startDate":"2025-05-11","hoursSpent":2,"description":"I participated in the Female Foeticide Awareness Walkathon organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE on 11th May 2025, in observance of Mother’s Day. The event was conducted with the objective of raising awareness about the serious social issue of female foeticide and promoting the value and dignity of girl children in society.\\n\\nThe walkathon witnessed active participation from students, faculty members, and parents, creating a strong sense of unity and collective responsibility. Participants carried informative placards and raised impactful slogans, spreading awareness and encouraging social change. The early morning walk from the RVCE campus fostered a peaceful yet powerful atmosphere of solidarity and commitment towards gender equality.\\n\\nParticipating in this walkathon was a meaningful experience that allowed me to contribute to a socially relevant cause. It strengthened my awareness of gender-based discrimination and inspired me to advocate for equality, respect, and justice in both personal and social spheres.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":15,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"15-16","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"MLOROpyncIkK4vk0xe1oC","name":"Project Pustak 2025","slNo":9,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":[],"endDate":"2024-04-30","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through my participation in Project Pustak, I gained a deeper understanding of the challenges faced by underprivileged children in accessing basic educational resources. The initiative helped me realize how even small financial contributions can make a significant impact on someone’s learning journey.\\n\\nI learned the importance of social responsibility, empathy, and active citizenship. The experience encouraged me to become more conscious of educational inequalities and motivated me to support similar initiatives in the future.\\n\\nOverall, this project strengthened my sense of compassion, ethical responsibility, and commitment to contributing positively toward community development and social welfare.","semester":"5","startDate":"2024-04-30","hoursSpent":1,"description":"I actively participated in Project Pustak, an initiative organized by the Rotaract Club of RVCE, aimed at supporting the education of underprivileged children. The project focused on collecting donations to provide essential learning materials such as books, stationery, and educational resources to students in need.\\n\\nThrough this initiative, participants were encouraged to contribute towards improving access to quality education and reducing learning barriers faced by economically disadvantaged children. The project created awareness about the importance of educational equity and motivated students to take responsibility for social development.\\n\\nParticipating in Project Pustak was a meaningful experience that allowed me to contribute directly to the academic growth and well-being of children. It reinforced the value of generosity, social service, and collective action in building a better and more inclusive society.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":10,"certificateImage":"https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/a_CM-__KAq43C9dp4ii8S.png","certificateAttached":true,"detailedReportPageNo":"17-18","signatureOfCounsellor":""},{"id":"pmtFTWu5z7GWZIjMsOE3M","name":"PitchIt! - 8th Mile","slNo":10,"place":"RVCE Campus","photos":["https://gsqebbosjbvoeqfxocmu.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/activity-evidence/5d735eb2-a006-4bd2-aab3-d3537a13c95f/WOKX-RzHvipTvRuHvAdeT.png"],"endDate":"2025-12-05","duration":1,"outcomes":"Through volunteering at Accelerate PitchIT, I developed strong organizational and event management skills. I learned the importance of effective planning, coordination, and time management in conducting large-scale academic and professional events.\\n\\nThe experience enhanced my communication and interpersonal skills by interacting with participants, mentors, and judges. I also improved my ability to work efficiently under pressure and respond quickly to unexpected challenges.\\n\\nExposure to startup ideas and business presentations broadened my understanding of entrepreneurship, innovation, and problem-solving. The event strengthened my leadership qualities, sense of responsibility, and confidence in handling professional environments.\\n\\nOverall, this experience contributed significantly to my personal and professional growth and motivated me to actively engage in similar initiatives in the future.","semester":"7","startDate":"2025-12-05","hoursSpent":4,"description":"I volunteered for Accelerate PitchIT, an entrepreneurship and innovation-focused event organized to provide a platform for students to present and refine their startup ideas and business concepts. As a volunteer, I actively contributed to the planning and smooth execution of the event by assisting in participant coordination, registration management, and communication between organizers, mentors, and presenters.\\n\\nMy responsibilities included guiding participants, managing schedules, supporting technical arrangements, and ensuring that the pitching sessions were conducted in an organized and professional manner. I also assisted in coordinating with judges and mentors, helping to maintain a structured and productive environment throughout the event.\\n\\nVolunteering for Accelerate PitchIT allowed me to contribute to a learning-driven initiative that promoted creativity, innovation, and entrepreneurial thinking among students. The experience strengthened my commitment to supporting academic and professional development activities within the campus.","aicteMapping":"14","pointsEarned":8,"certificateImage":"","certificateAttached":false,"detailedReportPageNo":"19-20","signatureOfCounsellor":""}],"evaluations":[],"signatories":{"counsellor":{"name":"Dr Mohana ","designation":"Assistant Professor"},"evaluator1":{"name":"","designation":""},"evaluator2":{"name":"","designation":""}}}', '2026-01-30 06:12:33.385979+00', '2026-01-30 06:19:23.711073+00');